{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "#1 Stunna", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-1-stunna-lyrics", "genius_title": "#1 Stunna", "genius_id": 2478219, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "#23", "line": "Carol City nigga still duckin’ the RICO", "vault_lines": ["Carol City nigga still duckin' the RICO"], "meaning": "Carol City is the neighborhood where Ross grew up, while RICO refers to the federal law used in cases involving organized crime. The line connects his past street image with the success he built later in life.", "annotation_id": "40785483", "url": "https://genius.com/40785483", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "#23", "line": "Drip check, look at my diamonds, got her lips wet Blue ’59 Impala, where the Crips at? Chrome Heart, Jomo, nigga, Dipset Get ready, tryna show you how to get checks", "vault_lines": ["Drip check, look at my diamonds, got her lips wet", "Blue '59 Impala, where the Crips at?", "Chrome Heart, Jomo, nigga, Dipset", "Get ready, tryna show you how to get checks"], "meaning": "“Drip check” refers to showing off one’s style, while the diamonds represent wealth and success. The phrase “got her lips wet” is a playful exaggeration, suggesting his jewelry is so impressive that it draws attention.\n\nThe blue ‘59 Impala references the iconic 1959 Chevrolet Impala, a legendary car in American culture. The blue color connects to the visual identity associated with the Crips, making the line a nod to West Coast street imagery.\n\nChrome Hearts represents high-end fashion embraced by many artists, while Dipset references The Diplomats, the influential Harlem rap collective known for their signature style and impact on hip-hop culture.", "annotation_id": "40785447", "url": "https://genius.com/40785447", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
