{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "After bill, but I still pay respect to my city So much man you thought I was in debt for real", "vault_lines": ["After bill, but I still pay respect to my city"], "meaning": "This is a play on his hometown of Detroit filing for bankruptcy in 2013 when they were $18 billion in debt, the largest bankruptcy filing in history.", "annotation_id": "31115502", "url": "https://genius.com/31115502", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "I woke up workin’ like I’m Mexican", "vault_lines": ["I woke up workin' like I'm Mexican"], "meaning": "Mexicans are often referred to as some of the hardest workers that this world has ever seen. Sean is saying that he is on a fierce grind and is working hard", "annotation_id": "21092554", "url": "https://genius.com/21092554", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Raising Hell in my residence, godly presence with presidents", "vault_lines": ["Raising Hell in my residence, godly presence with presidents"], "meaning": "“Raising hell” and getting rowdy is how Travi$ turns up. He is saying that his presence is God like and even has the money to make it as such.\n\nTravi$ has not only produced but rapped for several tracks with Kanye West among other “presidents” of their respective labels (G.O.O.D Music and Grand Hustle among others) His flow can definitely be considered “godly” among them.", "annotation_id": "2531369", "url": "https://genius.com/2531369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "You gon’ pull up friend to friend, I’mma pull up Benz to Benz", "vault_lines": ["You gon' pull up friend to friend, I'mma pull up Benz to Benz"], "meaning": "Your gonna say you got a lot of friends, but that don’t matter becuase you aint ballin like Sean is. You might have 100 friends, but Sean could have 100 Benzes. Sean also have his entire fan base in which he considers his friends his family as he says in the Intro to Finally Famous:\n\nI never made the crowd fans\nI made ‘em all fam\n\nPossibly a reference to his line off of Ashley as well:\n\nYeah, I got a brand new Benz\nCrazy right, brand new BenzGot less miles on it than I do friends", "annotation_id": "2486453", "url": "https://genius.com/2486453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Some call it trickin’ cause this bitch thicker than Trina", "vault_lines": ["Some call it trickin' cause this bitch thicker than Trina"], "meaning": "This is a play on the Slip-n-Slide Records artist Trick Daddy and Trina. Trina has a very body frame.", "annotation_id": "2462143", "url": "https://genius.com/2462143", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "No off day just pay day", "vault_lines": ["no off day just pay day"], "meaning": "Sean’s net worth is $2.5 million, so I’m sure Sean is getting that mula!", "annotation_id": "2458850", "url": "https://genius.com/2458850", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "I’m higher than Day-Day,", "vault_lines": ["I'm higher than Day-Day,"], "meaning": "Mike Epps played the character Day-Day in the comedy Next Friday and its sequel, Friday After Next.  In the movies, Day-Day smoked a lot of weed.", "annotation_id": "2458357", "url": "https://genius.com/2458357", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Finally famous is a Detroit crew", "vault_lines": ["Finally famous is a Detroit crew"], "meaning": "Big Sean is a Detroit native and the group he made is called Finally Famous which was founded in Detroit", "annotation_id": "2458313", "url": "https://genius.com/2458313", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "All day about how Em ain’t the same Em And Hov ain’t the same Hov Some niggas never grew up, boy, they only grow old", "vault_lines": ["All day about how Em ain't the same Em", "And Hov ain't the same Hov"], "meaning": "Many people have accused older MCs like Eminem and Jay Z of having changed their style (sometimes for the better, sometimes for the worse). Sean says that this is simply those MCs finally maturing as both artists and people, and that the change is inevitable as life happens.", "annotation_id": "2457423", "url": "https://genius.com/2457423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "And college ain’t make no sense,", "vault_lines": ["And college ain't make no sense,"], "meaning": "Travis used to go to The University of Texas, but ultimately dropped out of college to explore musical pursuits, much like Kanye.\n\nTravis also may be touching on how college doesn’t make cents. College graduates nowadays are having a hard time finding jobs, despite their diploma.", "annotation_id": "2454768", "url": "https://genius.com/2454768", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Fuck am I sayin’, man, Jesus had Judas", "vault_lines": ["Fuck am I sayin', man, Jesus had Judas"], "meaning": "Judas was know as one of the 12 apostles of Jesus until he betrayed him and made a bribe with the devil to identify Jesus to the police and get him arrested. Varying account portray what happens afterwards, but Judas feels sorry and either commits suicide for his sin or is prosecuted.\n\nThe kiss was later known as a “Judas kiss”, which is know known as a kiss that seems to be meaningful from someone who is close to the person, but is later potently harmful to that person in the end.", "annotation_id": "2454750", "url": "https://genius.com/2454750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Mama please, I’m never comin’ home ’til I make a hundred G’s (Straight up!) Scratch that, ’til I make a hundred million, then I’ma stretch that ’til I make a hundred trillion", "vault_lines": ["Scratch that, 'til I make a hundred million, then", "I'ma stretch that 'til I make a hundred trillion"], "meaning": "Much like his mentor, Travis has goals of earning much more then just millions in his life, he wants trillions.\n\n\n\nFor reference, thats a trillion bucks looks like in hundreds. That red line on the left is a person", "annotation_id": "2454737", "url": "https://genius.com/2454737", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Did songs with Hov, now hallelujah, fell asleep the real McCoy", "vault_lines": ["Did songs with Hov, now hallelujah, fell asleep the real McCoy"], "meaning": "Travis was featured on JAY-Z’s “Crown” from his twelfth studio album, Magna Carta… Holy Grail.\n\nIn an interview, Travis explained the process behind his feature and how the track came about:\n\nJAY-Z let me rap on his album. He let me say ‘shit on me,’ like that’s what I’ve been wanting to say forever.\n\nTravis is referring to his lines said on the chorus, in which he raps:\n\nShit on me, these niggas tried to shit on me\nI was left for dead, they tried to wipe me out of your history\n\nHe also revealed that his verse was recorded a week before the album’s release.", "annotation_id": "2454690", "url": "https://genius.com/2454690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Fuck you know about night terrors, nightmares and night scares About not gettin’ that white money ’fore a young nigga get white hair", "vault_lines": ["Fuck you know about night terrors, nightmares and night scares", "About not gettin' that white money 'fore a young nigga get white hair"], "meaning": "Tell me what you know about them night terrors, every night\n\nBig Sean has a passion for music. So much in fact that before he made it, he had nightmares of not making it before he grew too old.\n\nNow, as Sean explains in “First Chain”, he wears a chain to motivate himself, and to remind him of the hard work he had to put in to make it.", "annotation_id": "2454588", "url": "https://genius.com/2454588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Bitch, I do what I do, I feel how I feel", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I do what I do, I feel how I feel"], "meaning": "Big Sean has his own type of flow. He doesn’t care about what other people think of him because he knows that his hustle is real. The people hating are the ones that are jealous. So Sean is doing what he feels is right in order to succeed. And Sean is making it clear to all his haters…\n\nGo against me, you won’t stop losin'", "annotation_id": "2454534", "url": "https://genius.com/2454534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Every day is a chase, every night is a thrill", "vault_lines": ["Every day is a chase, every night is a thrill"], "meaning": "During the daytime Sean does his job and recording, or writing songs. He chases the money because of course, “ain’t nothing more important than the mula”.\n\n\n\nBut, as Wiz Khalifa would put it you “Work Hard, Play Hard”. Because of the work Sean puts in, it allows him to enjoy his nights and party, or perform in front of thousands. Sounds pretty thrilling to me.", "annotation_id": "2454516", "url": "https://genius.com/2454516", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Everybody got haters, I swear we been through this Martin had Malcolm, Caesar had Brutus", "vault_lines": ["Everybody got haters, I swear we been through this", "Martin had Malcolm, Caesar had Brutus"], "meaning": "It is true, everyone does have haters, even those with smallest amounts of success. Get a compliment from your boss at work? It’s guaranteed that there’s coworker not too far away looking like…\n\nHere he also references the relationship between Martin Luther King Jr. and Malcolm X. A relationship in which some believe that Malcolm X may have been a little envious of MLK’s popularity, because they had differing views on how the civil rights movement should have been handled, as depicted in the video below.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AiinmLf3zA0", "annotation_id": "2454498", "url": "https://genius.com/2454498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Stack on my belt, double M we a cult Mastermind’s in control, so nigga fuck what you thought", "vault_lines": ["Stack on my belt, double M we a cult", "Mastermind's in control, so nigga fuck what you thought"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is the CEO and founder of the successful rap group MMG, or double M G. He is currently at the top of his game, and has an album dropping December 17, 2013 called Mastermind.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/statuses/402562404665810944", "annotation_id": "2454460", "url": "https://genius.com/2454460", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "You saying that I changed, yep, changed like I supposed While you at the same crib still wearin’ the same clothes Going to the same club, taking the same pose Pillow talkin’ with the same hoes", "vault_lines": ["You saying that I changed, yep, changed like I supposed", "While you at the same crib still wearin' the same clothes", "Going to the same club, taking the same pose", "Pillow talkin' with the same hoes"], "meaning": "To survive in the game, you’ve got to evolve. Artists continually get criticised for “changing”, with fans wanting them to go back to their “old selves”. Examples of this include Kanye West & Eminem.\n\nSean shouts out his haters who told him not to change – they’re still where they was 3 years ago, while Sean is on top of the game.", "annotation_id": "2454441", "url": "https://genius.com/2454441", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "And I done dropped “Control” just to show you hoes who done got controlled", "vault_lines": ["And I done dropped \"Control\" just to show you hoes who done got controlled"], "meaning": "Sean is implying he dropped the now infamous Control to rustle up the rap game. Essentially to show he could keep up with who everyone thinks is the best – Kendrick Lamar. But let’s be honest, he didn’t really do that…\n\nAlso, during this line Sean changes his flow and tone of voice to one that imitates (or maybe even mock) one of the voice’s Kendrick uses in his verse", "annotation_id": "2454438", "url": "https://genius.com/2454438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "16's of coke, all my verses be dope", "vault_lines": ["16's of coke, all my verses be dope"], "meaning": "Coke/dope are the same thing – cocaine. A 16 refers to a verse comprising of 16 bars. Rozay’s verses are fire!", "annotation_id": "2454418", "url": "https://genius.com/2454418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "My kilos on ice, my sneakers snow white", "vault_lines": ["My kilos on ice, my sneakers snow white"], "meaning": "He plays on the drug dealer character. Kilo’s on ice/snow white refer to the cocaine he’s sold to afford those dope sneakers.", "annotation_id": "2454397", "url": "https://genius.com/2454397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "They done fucked up now, ha-ha Mastermind...", "vault_lines": ["They done fucked up now, ha-ha"], "meaning": "Mastermind is Ross' sixth studio album, released on March 3, 2014.", "annotation_id": "2454390", "url": "https://genius.com/2454390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "G.O.O.D music or die ho, shout out to Ye-Ye", "vault_lines": ["G.O.O.D music or die ho, shout out to Ye-Ye"], "meaning": "Big Sean signed with Kanye’s GOOD. Music in 2007. Sean raps about the story of how he met and was recognized by Kanye in “Nothing is Stopping You.”.", "annotation_id": "2454372", "url": "https://genius.com/2454372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "line": "Fuck XXL ’cause I’m the source to these quotes", "vault_lines": ["Fuck XXL 'cause I'm the source to these quotes"], "meaning": "Interesting lyric from Ross, while there’s no apparent beef with XXL, it may just be Ross using the two hip hop magazines as a metaphor. The Source is the more respected of the two, it’s infamous “5 mic’s” is something every artist would strive for. Ross uses their name to imply he’s at the centre of the culture. He was featured on the Oct/Nov cover along with Pusha T.", "annotation_id": "2454361", "url": "https://genius.com/2454361", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 26, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Big-sean-10-2-10-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "10 2 10 (Remix)", "genius_id": 270814, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 Bricks", "line": "The watch on rocks, do this shit hard knocks", "vault_lines": ["The watch on rocks, do this shit hard knocks"], "meaning": "Birdman has a diamond encrusted watch\n\n\n\nBeing a hard knock means being a person who has made many mistakes and who has been able to learn from it. The term was most famously serenaded by Jay-Z", "annotation_id": "622558", "url": "https://genius.com/622558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 Bricks", "line": "Put on her mind, do it big time homie", "vault_lines": ["Put on her mind, do it big time homie"], "meaning": "A reference to the duo Big Tymers, consisting of Birdman and Mannie Fresh", "annotation_id": "622552", "url": "https://genius.com/622552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 Bricks", "line": "Dope boy fresh, made man getting tickets", "vault_lines": ["Dope boy fresh, made man getting tickets"], "meaning": "Comparing his rise to the top of the music business to that of the dope game – a made man refers to a member of the Sicilian mafia", "annotation_id": "622548", "url": "https://genius.com/622548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 Bricks", "line": "Tote it all the time, see my son did time on it", "vault_lines": ["Tote it all the time, see my son did time on it"], "meaning": "He carries a gun with him at all times. “My son did time on it” refers to how Lil Wayne, who is known as Birdman’s “son,” served a jail sentence for possessing a loaded gun on a tour bus.", "annotation_id": "558858", "url": "https://genius.com/558858", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 Bricks", "line": "Full grind, Cash Money all the time", "vault_lines": ["Full grind, Cash Money all the time"], "meaning": "Birdman is the founder of Cash Money Records, which has existed for more than 20 years. You could say that the company has proved to be a lasting force in music.\n\nIts also an obvious reference to the retarded amount of money Birdman is currently worth", "annotation_id": "388850", "url": "https://genius.com/388850", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "10 Bricks", "line": "Imitating Sammy Gravano", "vault_lines": ["Clapping at all you niggas imitating Sammy Gravano"], "meaning": "Sammy Gravano was a mobster for the Colombo crime family, and later for the Brooklyn faction of the Gambinos, who eventually turned informer. He caused John Gotti to receive a sentence of life imprisonment.", "annotation_id": "200326", "url": "https://genius.com/200326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
