{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Y’all niggas is old dog Y’all over the hill like you tryna race a soapbox", "vault_lines": ["Y'all over the hill like you tryna race a soapbox"], "meaning": "These old rappers are washed up and over the metaphorical “age” hill.\n\nSoapbox races start at the top of hills so the cart can be propelled by gravity.", "annotation_id": "397475", "url": "https://genius.com/397475", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Lyrically Aristotle, lyrically can’t see it", "vault_lines": ["Lyrically Aristotle, lyrically can't see it"], "meaning": "Aristostle was a Greek philosopher, so he did a lot of deep thinking.", "annotation_id": "397424", "url": "https://genius.com/397424", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "I spend it make it right back on a Monday", "vault_lines": ["I spend it make it right back on a Monday"], "meaning": "LIV is the top grossing club in the world. Almost anyone who’s anyone goes there to spend a lot of money. Jay-Z just spent 250,000 there and the Dallas Mavericks partied there after the NBA championship.", "annotation_id": "396454", "url": "https://genius.com/396454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Cover the building in green my nigga: Fred Segal", "vault_lines": ["Cover the building in green my nigga: Fred Segal"], "meaning": "Fred Segal is an upscale boutique located in West Hollywood and Santa Monica, CA. The West Hollywood location is covered in green vines.", "annotation_id": "396238", "url": "https://genius.com/396238", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Just to go to LIV on a Sunday", "vault_lines": ["Just to go to LIV on a Sunday"], "meaning": "LIV nightclub in Miami is America’s most famous nightclub, LIV on Sunday nights is ranked as the number two club scene in the world and mentioned in numerous raps. Meek Mill catches the jet just to be able to get to the club from where ever his touring.", "annotation_id": "395989", "url": "https://genius.com/395989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Self-made, 60K the first week I signed with Maybach, and we did that ish the 1st week", "vault_lines": ["I signed with Maybach, and we did that ish the 1st week"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Groups release self made sold 53,000 copies the first week.", "annotation_id": "395985", "url": "https://genius.com/395985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "I’m a double M-G nigga", "vault_lines": ["Off rip, I'm a double M-G nigga"], "meaning": "“Double M G” stands for Maybach Music Group, Rick Ross’s label (to which Wale just signed).", "annotation_id": "395893", "url": "https://genius.com/395893", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "I’m making movies: them Kill Bill’s and Tarantino’s", "vault_lines": ["I'm making movies: them Kill Bill's and Tarantino's"], "meaning": "He’s flossing so much he should be filmed.\n\nHe refers to the Kill Bill film series by Quentin Tarantino to put his excellence into perspective.", "annotation_id": "395835", "url": "https://genius.com/395835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Running this shit bet you lil’ niggas flea-flicker", "vault_lines": ["Running this shit bet you lil' niggas flea-flicker"], "meaning": "Wale runs (controls) shit. In football, running is a lot more physical than passing. Y'all would rather pass the ball than just take the hits like him.\n\nA flea-flicker a play where the running back gets the hand off and you think its a run play, but then he laterals back to the QB. The QB then throws it down field.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gY6wk_qDdP8", "annotation_id": "395830", "url": "https://genius.com/395830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "I dropped 2Pac Back and did it B.I.G", "vault_lines": ["I dropped 2Pac Back and did it B.I.G"], "meaning": "Reference to his song Tupac back which put big numbers on the board in terms of selling.", "annotation_id": "395828", "url": "https://genius.com/395828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Ha, okay that 90210 talk", "vault_lines": ["Ha, okay that 90210 talk"], "meaning": "Wale has a song titled “90210” talking about the stereotypical Beverly Hills chick. In this case, this is a reference to how much money he is making.", "annotation_id": "395824", "url": "https://genius.com/395824", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "2011 BET Hip Hop Awards - Maybach Music Group Cypher", "line": "Them bammas can’t see the bars, y’all some paralegals", "vault_lines": ["Them bammas can't see the bars, y'all some paralegals"], "meaning": "“Bamma” is Washington, DC slang for a whack person. Paralegals aren’t lawyers because they haven’t passed the Bar exam yet. Wale’s rhymes are lyrically way above other rappers so they “can’t see the bars”.", "annotation_id": "395817", "url": "https://genius.com/395817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
