{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Banksy, bitches, Basquiat", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Hov references a couple artists he enjoys the work of, including the secretive British graffiti artist Banksy and the iconic Jean-Michel Basquiat.\n\nHere is a photo of Hov dressed as Basquiat, standing next to a Basquait and Warhol piece entitled “GE (Alert)” that he owns:", "annotation_id": "11366235", "url": "https://genius.com/11366235", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "[Produced by Jake One]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "For this one Jake One used soulful vocals, piano melodies, hard hitting drums and tom rolls with some synth change ups. It contains one sample, which is multiple elements (including vocals) from “I’m So Grateful (Keep in Touch)” by Crowns of Glory:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IVB2mUXV-XE#t=121\nWhile allegedly failing to clear the rights – after being threatened to be sued they paid-up for the sample.\n\nIn an episode of Behind the Beat, Jake One also talked about producing “3 Kings”. The episode can be watched on YouTube by clicking here.", "annotation_id": "2787922", "url": "https://genius.com/2787922", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Real nigga’s dreams comin’ to fruition", "vault_lines": ["Real nigga's dreams comin' to fruition"], "meaning": "Rick considers himself a real nigga, maybe because he is doing a track with 2 legends. But basically just saying him, Jay, And Dre’s dreams have all came true.\n\nPerhaps one of his dreams was working with Dre, as he once called Dre his “biggest musical influence”. https://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/155831880070078464 https://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/155832273961361409 https://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/155832777722437633", "annotation_id": "944179", "url": "https://genius.com/944179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Fuck rap money, I’ve made more off grapes", "vault_lines": ["Fuck rap money, I've made more off grapes"], "meaning": "Grapes are an ingredient of champagne, and it is reported that Jay makes roughly $4 million a year from a deal he inked to promote Ace of Spades champagne.", "annotation_id": "937420", "url": "https://genius.com/937420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Taking her places that you can’t go with your per diem", "vault_lines": ["Taking her places that you can't go with your per diem"], "meaning": "A per diem, Latin for “each day,” is a daily allowance, typically handed out to professionals and musicians to pay for their expenses while they travel. With a $610 million net-worth Hov can afford to take your baby mother anywhere she wants – and not have her worrying about blowing an allowance.", "annotation_id": "937400", "url": "https://genius.com/937400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Till the white boys got him in that hot seat", "vault_lines": ["Till the white boys got him in that hot seat"], "meaning": "Dre has long had no love for authority figures\n\nNot only that, but Dr. Dre blew up because the “white boys” signed him to their record label, made him nationally popular.", "annotation_id": "934456", "url": "https://genius.com/934456", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Can’t be steppin’ on a nigga feet man (Hah!)", "vault_lines": ["Can't be steppin' on a nigga feet man (Hah!)"], "meaning": "In the dope game, when you step on someones toes like steal someones customer or deal, it’s like going behind someones back, it’s not acceptable with any dealer.\n\nThis goes along with the revenge theme of the album. Ross isn’t afraid to hurt someone stepping on his shoes, literally or figuratively.", "annotation_id": "926069", "url": "https://genius.com/926069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "The fuck you magazine niggas want from me? I rewrote the game, nigga, now talk money", "vault_lines": ["The fuck you magazine niggas want from me?", "I rewrote the game, nigga, now talk money"], "meaning": "The “magazine niggas” refer to the critics who always want/expect more from Dre. He already made his mark on hip-hop history the game so now these critics should start talking about the money Dre’s getting. Thus the play on “rewrote,” something of which would be commissioned if there were significant errors within a story or significant backlash for an article.\n\nAlso he launched Game to the stardom, being his mentor since Aftermath days.", "annotation_id": "925589", "url": "https://genius.com/925589", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "80 pair of sneakers came from the D game Cousin was a Crip, said it was a C thing", "vault_lines": ["80 pair of sneakers came from the D game", "Cousin was a Crip, said it was a C thing"], "meaning": "Ross uses some abecedarian wordplay, with “it’s a c[rip] thing” being a common phrase among Crips and “d” standing for “dope”.", "annotation_id": "924528", "url": "https://genius.com/924528", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "He wanted to shine at the swap meet", "vault_lines": ["He wanted to shine at the swap meet"], "meaning": "The Compton Swap Meet was a meme location in much of Dre’s early work\n\nAlso, Dr. Dre started his music career with the goal of being the respected and stand-out in his neighborhood, he never thought of it amounting to a national level.", "annotation_id": "922791", "url": "https://genius.com/922791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "I built a house, nigga, get your own shit", "vault_lines": ["I built a house, nigga, get your own shit"], "meaning": "Dre recently built a 13 million dollar house.\n\n\n\nAlso, he is quietly telling biters to get their own style, he has built and gathered so much wealth and luxury, he wants the people to stop copying him.", "annotation_id": "921397", "url": "https://genius.com/921397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Leanin’ on my pistol (Woo!)", "vault_lines": ["Stumble, but I never fall, leanin' on my pistol (Woo!)"], "meaning": "Ross paints the picture of a warrior on a battlefield. After defeating many foes and surviving fatal blows, the warrior plunges his sword into the ground and leans on it, supporting himself so he doesn’t stumble and fall, looking as if he were defeated.\n\nRick Ross symbolizes that, using his gun of course.", "annotation_id": "920829", "url": "https://genius.com/920829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Used to shop at TJ Maxx back in ’83 I don’t even know if it was open then", "vault_lines": ["I don't even know if it was open then"], "meaning": "https://twitter.com/tjmaxx/status/226352044963942403", "annotation_id": "920735", "url": "https://genius.com/920735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "All-black, on my Al Capone shit", "vault_lines": ["All-black, on my Al Capone shit"], "meaning": "He’s wearing all black like Al Capone, who was an American gangster who led a Prohibition-era crime syndicate in the early 1900s.\n\n\n\n\n\nThough the image of gangsters dressed in all black is a pervasive one, Capone was actually fond of more lavish, colorful suits.", "annotation_id": "920382", "url": "https://genius.com/920382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Number one for the last twenty years", "vault_lines": ["Number one for the last twenty years"], "meaning": "Dre has one of the longest and most succesful careers in rap, ever since N.W.A released Straight Outta Compton in 1988 Dre’s career has had an almost uninterrupted streak of commercial success.", "annotation_id": "920338", "url": "https://genius.com/920338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Brown bag money in a duffle bag", "vault_lines": ["Brown bag money in a duffle bag"], "meaning": "Brown bag money is the money earned by selling crack, the dealer puts his earnings in a brown bag to not look conspicuous carrying stacks around. The same goes for the duffle bag where the combined earnings end up on a higher level of the trade.\n\nAlso a possible reference to the DJ Khaled song “Brown Paper Bag”.", "annotation_id": "920328", "url": "https://genius.com/920328", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Fuck a gym, I am him, Andre Young", "vault_lines": ["Fuck a gym, I am him, Andre Young"], "meaning": "Dr. Dre’s government name is Andre Young. It’s also a play on words as he’s been in the rap game 20 years strong without need of a gym.\n\nIronically, he’s buff as hell, looking like the black terminator…", "annotation_id": "920159", "url": "https://genius.com/920159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Spray these niggas, baby, just like daddy taught ya [Outro] Young It’s just different", "vault_lines": ["Spray these niggas, baby, just like daddy taught ya"], "meaning": "He’s already teaching his daughter how to dominate the rap game, killing the competition by “spraying” them with “bullets”, the bullets being nothing but hot music. Her cries even appeared on his song “Glory” about B’s pregnancy, and at two days old, she became the youngest person ever on a Billboard chart.", "annotation_id": "920021", "url": "https://genius.com/920021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Close the curtains, fuckboy, out my face", "vault_lines": ["Close the curtains, fuckboy, out my face"], "meaning": "Stay out of his business! Jay could be referring to his house curtains mentioned in the prior line, but then again doesn’t his Maybach come with some too?\n\n\n\nOn the original “Maybach Music” Jay Z says\n\nThe curtains are drawn\nPerfectly like a Picasso, Rembrandts and Rothkos", "annotation_id": "920015", "url": "https://genius.com/920015", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "I ain’t know Oprah then", "vault_lines": ["I ain't know Oprah then"], "meaning": "Double entendre!\n\n\nHe wasn’t friends with Oprah then\nHe was not at the status he is now back then “I ain’t no Oprah then.” Oprah is an iconic black figure, just like Jay is now.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn 2009, Oprah interviewed Jay-Z and he appeared on her show.\n\nJigga had earlier referenced his new friend Oprah on “Murder To Excellence,” as well. He uses her as an example of the excellence that African-Americans should and must aspire to.\n\nNow please, domino, domino\nOnly spot a few blacks the higher I go\nWhat’s up to Will? Shout out to O\n That ain’t enough.. we gonna need a million more", "annotation_id": "919895", "url": "https://genius.com/919895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "The homie whippin’ chickens in his momma kitchen On the mission, said he get it for his son tuition (Ugh!)", "vault_lines": ["The homie whippin' chickens in his momma kitchen", "On the mission, said he get it for his son tuition (Ugh!)"], "meaning": "“Whippin' chickens” refers to cooking cocaine to turn it into crack. Ross' partner is doing whatever he has to do pay his son’s tuition, even if that means partaking in illegal activities. .", "annotation_id": "919840", "url": "https://genius.com/919840", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Had the XL 80 bike, loud motor, they be like, “Damn!” When I’m comin’ through, rrraaanngg", "vault_lines": ["Had the XL 80 bike, loud motor, they be like, \"Damn!\"", "When I'm comin' through, rrraaanngg"], "meaning": "Jay-Z claims he used to own a Honda XL 80 motorcycle, which he would rev up and down the Brooklyn streets.", "annotation_id": "919468", "url": "https://genius.com/919468", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Fuck show money, I spent that on drapes", "vault_lines": ["Fuck show money, I spent that on drapes"], "meaning": "This line Jay shows that the money he makes from shows is negligible, as he spends it on frivolous items like luxury drapes. Hov has no qualms spending large amounts of money to ensure he has the best there is to offer.\n\nThere is also an antithesis between show money as in showing his money and the fact that drapes are used for privacy, that is, stopping people from seeing something.\n\nThere are no lies in Hov’s verses:\nhttps://twitter.com/JustBlaze/status/232661280136257536", "annotation_id": "919392", "url": "https://genius.com/919392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Niggas couldn’t fuck with my daughter’s room Niggas couldn’t walk in my daughter’s socks", "vault_lines": ["Niggas couldn't fuck with my daughter's room", "Niggas couldn't walk in my daughter's socks"], "meaning": "Blue Ivy Carter: stuntin' on hoes since conception. As well as having Jay Z and Beyoncé as her parents, she is noted as the youngest person ever to appear on a Billboard chart.\n\nHer father’s socks are legendary, too:\n\nThese other rappers couldn’t wash my socks\nThat’s why I took the number one slot\nThe realest shit in rap comes from my voice box", "annotation_id": "919380", "url": "https://genius.com/919380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Millions on the wall in all my rooms", "vault_lines": ["Millions on the wall in all my rooms"], "meaning": "Double entendre alert! Jay Z has several RIAA-certified Gold and Platinum records hanging on his walls, which represents the tens of millions of records he’s sold worldwide.\n\nHe also owns multiple multi-million dollar valuable paintings on his walls as well – they even adorn his bathroom.", "annotation_id": "919366", "url": "https://genius.com/919366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "We started out mopping floors And now we front row at the awards", "vault_lines": ["And now we front row at the awards"], "meaning": "Dr. Dre, Rick Ross and Jay-Z went from rags (or dope dealing, as the case may be) to riches\n\nAlso, Dr. Dre was once part of the World Class Wrecking Cru. In a nightclub, a wrecking crew was always the group of DJ’s that performed last before closing. Other DJs could leave with only their crates but Wrecking Crews broke down the equipment at the end of the night. If you helped the club owner straighten up a bit, you made more money.", "annotation_id": "919362", "url": "https://genius.com/919362", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "You should listen to this beat through my headphones", "vault_lines": ["You should listen to this beat through my headphones"], "meaning": "Dr. Dre givin' a shout-out to his worldwide known headphones “Beats by Dr. Dre”.", "annotation_id": "919190", "url": "https://genius.com/919190", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Murder was the case that they gave me I killed the Hermès store, somebody save me", "vault_lines": ["Murder was the case that they gave me", "I killed the Hermès store, somebody save me"], "meaning": "This can be a reference to Jay’s case for attempted murder in 1999, except in this case, he’s going to be tried for the death of the Hermès store.\n\nLikewise, it can allude to Snoop Dogg’s classic song, “Murder Was The Case”. Hov has a career-long habit of quoting/referencing the Doggfather\n\n\n\nHermès is one of the most expensive luxury brands. The French company based in Paris specializes in “maroquinerie” and ready to wear clothing. It is most likely referencing the $350K Christmas Eve shopping spree he went on for this wife.", "annotation_id": "919170", "url": "https://genius.com/919170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "You ain’t gotta keep this, Khaled, it’s just a freestyle", "vault_lines": ["You ain't gotta keep this, Khaled, it's just a freestyle"], "meaning": "As usual, one-take Hov freestyled his verse.", "annotation_id": "919137", "url": "https://genius.com/919137", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Born broke, real nigga, straight outta Compton", "vault_lines": ["Born broke, real nigga, straight outta Compton"], "meaning": "Dr. Dre and many others like Game and Kendrick Lamar are all form the city of Compton, California, which has for reputation to be one of the roughest and most dangerous cities culminating with one of the highest crime rates in the U.S. He says here, he was basically born in poverty, in the ghetto and made it all the way up on his own.\n\nAdditionally, Dr. Dre was a part of the group N.W.A, whose classic proper debut album was called Straight Outta Compton.", "annotation_id": "919135", "url": "https://genius.com/919135", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "I only love her if her weave new I’m still a hood nigga, what you want me to do?", "vault_lines": ["I only love her if her weave new", "I'm still a hood nigga, what you want me to do?"], "meaning": "Beyonce’s weave game is on point. People often think it’s her real hair. Guys from the hood usually date women with weaves, so even with his wealth, Jay still has this tendency. Who can forget that he’s still “So Ghetto”?", "annotation_id": "919133", "url": "https://genius.com/919133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Play this shit while you play around with my crown", "vault_lines": ["Play this shit while you play around with my crown"], "meaning": "The crown refers to Jay’s near undeniable status as the King of Hip-hop (at least, if we’re talking about power moves, wealth, and influence). He’s even proclaimed himself “King Hov” and released a joint album with frequent collaborator Kanye West called Watch the Throne.", "annotation_id": "919118", "url": "https://genius.com/919118", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "I only love her if her eyes brown", "vault_lines": ["I only love her if her eyes brown"], "meaning": "Beyoncé’s eyes do things to us too, Jay…\n\n\n\nThe beginning of Jay’s verse continues the “only love if…” line that recurred throughout the song in both verses from Dre and Ross.", "annotation_id": "919104", "url": "https://genius.com/919104", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "I whip the coke, let the lawyer beat the case", "vault_lines": ["I whip the coke, let the lawyer beat the case"], "meaning": "Jay plays on the word “whip” and “beat,” as they (can) share the same meaning.\n\nJay could’ve taken the inspiration for this line from this Ross line from “Hustlin' (Remix),” a previous collaboration between the two.\n\nI’m whippin' the case like I’m whippin' the base.\n\n\n\nHe could be implying that he still sells drugs, but is not worried cause he knows his lawyer will somehow prove he is not guilty.\n\nCould Be reference To “Carlito’s Way”", "annotation_id": "919102", "url": "https://genius.com/919102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "I’ll take a Ace in the meanwhile", "vault_lines": ["I'll take a Ace in the meanwhile"], "meaning": "A reference to Hov’s champagne brand Armand de Brignac, known best as “Ace of Spades.” Hov reckons the bottle looks like a Golden Globe trophy:\n\nI’m on my Lupita Nyong'o\nStuntin' on stage, after 12 Years A Slave\nThis Ace of Spades look like an Oscar\n\n“ACE” could also be a reference to the “Award for Cable Excellence,” an award Robin Williams won in 1988 for the his legendary stand-up comedy special Robin Williams: An Evening at the Met.", "annotation_id": "919100", "url": "https://genius.com/919100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "H, shit! Oh, stuntin’ to the max, I’m so wavy", "vault_lines": ["Oh, stuntin' to the max, I'm so wavy"], "meaning": "To the listener, this could be assumed to be a Jay-Z freestyle.\n\nDepending on how you want to look at it, Jay may have messed up the previous bar. Then he says “Oh!” and repeats it better\n\nLikewise, “Oh shit” could be Jay assuming the position of the listener who is surprised at the Max B reference.\n\nAlso, Jay could have been surprised that he came up with a hot line out of nowhere. It’s very common to reflect back on your verse and say “Oh shit” “that was hot!”, although most do it after the fact.\n\nThis is Max B who coined the phrase “Wavy:”", "annotation_id": "919089", "url": "https://genius.com/919089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Ex-D-boy, used to park my Beamer Now look at me, I can park in my own arena", "vault_lines": ["Ex-D-boy, used to park my Beamer", "Now look at me, I can park in my own arena"], "meaning": "Back when he was moving drugs, he would have to search the NY streets for safe places to park his cars. Now that he’s a part owner of the Brooklyn Nets, he’s driving an even nicer car and he can safely park his whips in the VIP parking section of the billion dollar Barclays Center arena.\n\n\n\nJay is taking the listener back to a scene in “Regrets,” off Reasonable Doubt, where he describes a scene setting up a drug deal and watching it “from a remote location in the BM.” He has come a long way from that scene he describes on his debut album to his ownership stake in the Barclays Center today.", "annotation_id": "919087", "url": "https://genius.com/919087", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Been hoppin’ out the BM with your BM", "vault_lines": ["Been hoppin' out the BM with your BM"], "meaning": "We don’t drive X5s, we give ‘em to baby-mamas\n\nHov is riding in a BMW motor vehicle with the mother of his competition’s children.", "annotation_id": "919078", "url": "https://genius.com/919078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "They workin’ on another deal, they talkin’ two-hundred-fifty! I’m holdin’ out for three Two-seventy-five and I just might agree", "vault_lines": ["They workin' on another deal, they talkin' two-hundred-fifty!", "I'm holdin' out for three", "Two-seventy-five and I just might agree"], "meaning": "Upping the ante from the last deal, LiveNation is now prepared to pay Jay-Z $250M for his next contract. Even though this is already $100M more than his last, he wants to double his previous contract, but may be willing to settle for a mere $125M more.\n\nBut Jay, do you really want to negotiate with yourself in public like this?", "annotation_id": "919064", "url": "https://genius.com/919064", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Had the grill in ’88, y’all niggas is late", "vault_lines": ["Had the grill in '88, y'all niggas is late"], "meaning": "Once again, Jay refers to 1988, as in “Dead Presidents II”, and “Takeover.” He is supposed to have made a lot of money off drugs that year.\n\nAs usual, the rest of the rap game is playing catch up to Jay. He’s been off that.", "annotation_id": "919061", "url": "https://genius.com/919061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "I ran through that buck fifty Live Nation fronted me", "vault_lines": ["I ran through that buck fifty Live Nation fronted me"], "meaning": "LiveNation paid Jay-Z $150M to fund his Roc Nation record label, and he’s ran through all of that money already.", "annotation_id": "919049", "url": "https://genius.com/919049", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Stuntin’ to the max like, wavy", "vault_lines": ["Stuntin' to the max like, wavy"], "meaning": "Double entendre! Incarcerated Harlem rapper Max B coined the term “wavy” and Jay is paying homage. He is also referring to the fact that Max B is currently incarcerated at New Jersey State Prison in a maximum security unit.", "annotation_id": "919044", "url": "https://genius.com/919044", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "Screamin’ “Carpe diem!” until I’m a dead poet Robin Williams shit, I deserve a Golden Globe, bitch!", "vault_lines": ["Screamin' \"Carpe diem!\" until I'm a dead poet", "Robin Williams shit, I deserve a Golden Globe, bitch!"], "meaning": "Robin Williams played English teacher John Keating in a movie called Dead Poets Society. John wanted his students to shout “carpe diem,” a Latin aphorism which means “Seize the day!” Some would say that it’s a grown-up version of “YOLO.”\n\nThough Robin Williams was nominated for the “Best Performance by an Actor” Golden Globe for Dead Poet’s Society, he did not win. But he eventually got four Golden Globes, so whatevs! Apparently, King Hov wants one too.", "annotation_id": "919032", "url": "https://genius.com/919032", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "G5s to 6-4s, Dre got ’em", "vault_lines": ["G5s to 6-4s, Dre got 'em"], "meaning": "The Gulfstream V (as known as G5) is very expensive business jet. Dre still has the ‘64 Impala though. He hasn’t lost his roots.", "annotation_id": "919022", "url": "https://genius.com/919022", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "line": "We should listen to this track in my Maybach (Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": ["We should listen to this track in my Maybach (Maybach Music)"], "meaning": "Ross has quite an affinity for the now-defunct Maybach brand of luxury cars, having named his crew after the vehicle.", "annotation_id": "919019", "url": "https://genius.com/919019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3 Kings", "status": "done", "targets": 45, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-3-kings-lyrics", "genius_title": "3 Kings", "genius_id": 80548, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "30 for 30 Freestyle", "line": "Good news, they just let me off house arrest", "vault_lines": ["Good news, they just let me off house arrest"], "meaning": "Ross was ordered to stay put at home in the case where he allegedly pistol-whipped a man.\n\nA judge ruled Friday Rozay’s home confinement wasn’t necessary since the alleged victim didn’t live anywhere near him.\n\nThe judge said Ross has to stay clear of where the alleged victim lives, and he has to notify officials before leaving the state of Georgia.\n\nRead more: http://www.tmz.com/2015/11/01/rick-ross-house-arrest-pistol-whipping/#ixzz3qRBVFe1M", "annotation_id": "8099527", "url": "https://genius.com/8099527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "30 for 30 Freestyle", "line": "Write you niggas rhymes, they should call me ghost face", "vault_lines": ["Write you niggas rhymes, they should call me ghost face"], "meaning": "Rick Ross used to allegedly ghostwrite for Trina and Trick Daddy – his fellow label mates at slip-n-slide, before he became famous.\nHe has also allegedly written for Diddy and Dr Dre, and also claims to write for a lot of rappers – but he hasn’t disclosed any identities as of yet.\n\nHe was also tied for 10th in XXl’s 2012 Hip-Hop’s 10 Greatest Ghostwriters [Poll]", "annotation_id": "8099416", "url": "https://genius.com/8099416", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "30 for 30 Freestyle", "line": "LA Reid and Steel calling back to back", "vault_lines": ["LA Reid and Steel calling back to back"], "meaning": "Like he said on the Breakfast club\n\nBlack Market is his last album with Def Jam, so he is currently in the process of negotiations with top hip hop labels, such as LA Reid’s Epic for a new deal.", "annotation_id": "8099341", "url": "https://genius.com/8099341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
