{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3Hunna (Album Version)", "line": "Drivin’ a Bentley through the battlefield (Huh?)", "vault_lines": ["Drivin' a Bentley through the battlefield (Huh?)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross isn’t shy about revealing his car collection- he owns several Bentleys, and even purchased a white Bentley Bentayga SUV for his daugher’s 16th birthday, costing him around $229,000.\nRoss isn’t afraid to drive one of his Bentleys through a “battle field” of his enemies mentioned in the previous line, since he has so many Bentleys, getting one damaged isn’t an issue to him.", "annotation_id": "22018603", "url": "https://genius.com/22018603", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3Hunna (Album Version)", "line": "My dog died, they put him in a plastic bag (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["My dog died, they put him in a plastic bag (Oh)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross mentions that his dog (a loyal friend of his) died. When the body was found, the authorities placed it in a plastic bag for the coroner.", "annotation_id": "22018586", "url": "https://genius.com/22018586", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3Hunna (Album Version)", "line": "O’Block,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“O-Block” is a set on the 0600 block in Englewood Chicago where Chief Keef, Lil Reese, Fredo Santana etc. all the GBE boys are from. They represent LAMRON which is Normal spelled backwards because OBlock starts on 63rd & Normal.\n\n\n\nLamron gang is a set of the criminal gang knows as the Black Disciples. This set of the BDs is located in Normal Ave in Chicago. This particular faction of the BDs has seen its popularity rise due to Lil Durk and Lil Reeese, both whom are members of Lamron.\n\n“O-Block” is also dubbed one of Chicago’s most dangerous blocks", "annotation_id": "4755397", "url": "https://genius.com/4755397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3Hunna (Album Version)", "line": "Need 250 more, double M, this shit for real", "vault_lines": ["Need 250 more, double M, this shit for real"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is shouting out his group, Maybach Music Group, or MMG for short", "annotation_id": "1431137", "url": "https://genius.com/1431137", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3Hunna (Album Version)", "line": "Fuck a Tooka gang, bitch, I’m 3Hunna (Bang, bang, bang)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck a Tooka gang, bitch, I'm 3Hunna (Bang, bang, bang)"], "meaning": "“Tooka” and “3hunna” are gang references. Tooka is GD (Gangsta Disciple) And 3hunna is BD (Black Disciple). Both gangs are in the southside of Chicago. The song is very catchy, but you might wanna be careful where you sing it", "annotation_id": "1316598", "url": "https://genius.com/1316598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "3Hunna (Album Version)", "line": "Sosa baby,", "vault_lines": ["I'm Sosa, bitch, Chief Keef, yeah (Sosa baby)"], "meaning": "Chief Keef often refers to himself as Chief Keef Sosa, which is most likely a reference to Tony Montana’s Nemesis in Scarface, Alex Sosa.\n\nAlternatively, Keef’s nickname comes from Chicago Cubs player Sammy Sosa. keef is from Chi-town after all.", "annotation_id": "1316548", "url": "https://genius.com/1316548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
