{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "In Denver", "vault_lines": ["And I sever my opponents, bitch I'm cold like it's in Denver"], "meaning": "Should be “in Denver”", "annotation_id": "14913274", "url": "https://genius.com/14913274", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "Life’s a bitch and I feel her", "vault_lines": ["Life’s a bitch and I feel her"], "meaning": "Jadakiss is not suggesting that he’s into bestiality, but he’s indicating that regardless of how unfair life can be sometimes he still accomplishes what he sets out to do.  Where most people views life’s misfortunes, Jadakiss views the “bitch” as just another necessity that he has to learn how to operate with.", "annotation_id": "2588347", "url": "https://genius.com/2588347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "I get that work on my face", "vault_lines": ["I get that work on my face"], "meaning": "In the underbelly of the drug trafficking world, believe it or not…at the end of the day Drug Dealers are businessmen.  Rick Ross is demonstrating that he is so well known that his reputation proceeds him.  When it’s time for him to re-up, he doesn’t even have to give anything up front to get drugs to distribute because his face is enough credit and collateral.", "annotation_id": "2588329", "url": "https://genius.com/2588329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "Rozay told me, “Keep on working shawty, you’ll be rich forever” Ever", "vault_lines": ["Rozay told me, \"Keep on working shawty, you’ll be rich forever\""], "meaning": "Ross told Wale as long as he continues to work, it will pay off and he’ll always have money.\n\nThis line inspired the usernames for Ross' instagram and tumblr, and the title of his classic 2012 mixtape.", "annotation_id": "536089", "url": "https://genius.com/536089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "600 Benz, house six hundred grand That was six years ago, whips come from Japan I get that work on my face I get that work on my face, ay", "vault_lines": ["I get that work on my face", "I get that work on my face, ay"], "meaning": "He has a Mercedes 600 Benz.\n\n\n\nRoss is stuntin' on owners of Asian imported vehicles. Here he boasts of his possession of a flagship European vehicle asserting his preference for luxury cars by expressing his ignorance that a second world country actually makes cars.\n\nMost people need some sort of credibility or someone to vouch for them in order to do business.\n\nBut Ross is so well known, he gets work without any pre-requisites other than his face.", "annotation_id": "205845", "url": "https://genius.com/205845", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "To mash on assholes with petty badges Tell them niggas we throwed, but they never gon’ catch us", "vault_lines": ["To mash on assholes with petty badges", "Tell them niggas we throwed, but they never gon' catch us"], "meaning": "Play on the word throwed. He means they’re “throwed” as in high/drunk but the police won’t ever catch them, like they are throwed in the air and need to be caught.", "annotation_id": "184626", "url": "https://genius.com/184626", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "The dilemma is, you think I got no conscience", "vault_lines": ["The dilemma is, you think I got no conscience"], "meaning": "Some people will judge Wale because of some of his songs, but in reality he’s quite articulate", "annotation_id": "178115", "url": "https://genius.com/178115", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "Keep the digital ruler in arm’s length of the Ruger", "vault_lines": ["Keep the digital ruler in arm's length of the Ruger"], "meaning": "Digital Ruler = scale to weigh drugs, particularly coke\n\n\n\nRuger is a type of handgun. Also “arms length” is a clever play on words. The term “arms” also refers to weapons.\n\nRuger P95", "annotation_id": "176226", "url": "https://genius.com/176226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "Where I’m from is a circus, hope you don’t expect a fair one Dropping hundreds like it ain’t nothin’ Really it was but you know I’m never sayin’ nothin’", "vault_lines": ["Where I'm from is a circus, hope you don’t expect a fair one", "Dropping hundreds like it ain't nothin'", "Really it was but you know I'm never sayin' nothin'"], "meaning": "D.C., where Wale’s from, is a tough place to live, where not everything is fair (in D.C. you see some of the wealthiest politicians with their huge mansion and eveything in one neighborhood, and 15 minutes down the road you see some of the poorest and toughest neighborhoods)\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso, a “fair” might feature a circus if it were one of your better fairs", "annotation_id": "164487", "url": "https://genius.com/164487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "I’m a rare one, camos and some rare ones", "vault_lines": ["I'm a rare one, camos and some rare ones"], "meaning": "smart wordplay: Wale is a “rare one” or unique, meaning they don’t make ‘em like him anymore… He’s rocking camo shorts and some RARE ONES (AIR JORDAN 1s)\n\n\n\n#wordplay", "annotation_id": "164483", "url": "https://genius.com/164483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "I’m Polamalu, 600 the newest model", "vault_lines": ["I'm Polamalu, 600 the newest model"], "meaning": "Pro-Bowl strong safety, Troy Polamalu.\n\n\n\nHe’s comparing himself to Polamalu, who is one of the best safetys in the NFL.", "annotation_id": "163057", "url": "https://genius.com/163057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "My newest motto to use a condom with newest models Uhh, got a hundred on the dash, young Y’all ain’t killers, y’all got hundred yard dash guns", "vault_lines": ["My newest motto to use a condom with newest models", "Uhh, got a hundred on the dash, young"], "meaning": "No one has ever killed anyone with the starting gun that is used at track meets, it looks like a gun, sounds like a gun, but is completely harmless.", "annotation_id": "163055", "url": "https://genius.com/163055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "Ain’t nobody iller Perico Godzilla", "vault_lines": [", ain't nobody iller"], "meaning": "Perico is Spanish for cocaine. Godzilla = Monster. Therefore, Jada is dealing some Monster Coke.", "annotation_id": "162707", "url": "https://genius.com/162707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "If I am pulled over, I know they gon’ be on it Cause it’s hot in here and I got no L like the ’7-2 Dolphins", "vault_lines": ["If I am pulled over, I know they gon' be on it", "Cause it's hot in here and I got no L like the '7-2 Dolphins"], "meaning": "The ‘72 Dolphins went undefeated through the regular season and playoffs.\n\nHe means if he gets pulled over by the cops he knows the police will be on arresting him because it’s hot in his car (from the weed smoke) and he has no L (License) like the 72' Dolphins (only team to ever be undefeated in NFL history).", "annotation_id": "162650", "url": "https://genius.com/162650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "All black everything, this shit like a HBCU", "vault_lines": ["All black everything, this shit like a HBCU"], "meaning": "Wale’s Benzo has black paint, black tints, black rims, “all black everything.”\n\nHBCU stands for ‘Historically Black College or University’ such as Howard, Hamptom, Clark Atlanta, etc. Historical black colleges? All black? Why, yes indeed.", "annotation_id": "162638", "url": "https://genius.com/162638", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "You think I’m just here flossing on raw shit about car shit", "vault_lines": ["You think I'm just here flossing on raw shit about car shit"], "meaning": "“You think I simply adore shoes?”\n\nHere is where Wale subtly critiques his haters: “You think I\"m just here talking about ‘ car shit on that Ross shit” – his haters say he sold out for signing with Rick Ross – but if you pay attention – 600 Benz is simply a metaphor for Wale’s drive and ambition. unbelievable how much of this shit goes over people’s heads.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0Gip9m8__M", "annotation_id": "162526", "url": "https://genius.com/162526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "You only half a W without a second V", "vault_lines": ["You only half a W without a second V"], "meaning": "A “V” is a NY slang term for car, more specifically a luxury or exotic car like a Lotus, Ferrari, Maserati, Maybach, etc. “V” is also literally half of a W. V could refer to Volkswagen as well, which is a much cheaper car.\n\nWale claims that just because you have one of them (You probably bought yours used anyways), doesn’t mean you are a winner, you gotta have at least two V’s to show you balling. This corresponds to the previous “One whip just aint enough” line.", "annotation_id": "162523", "url": "https://genius.com/162523", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "600 Benz", "line": "I got twelve hundred kicks, them bitches straight from Japan", "vault_lines": ["I got twelve hundred kicks, them bitches straight from Japan"], "meaning": "It’s true that Nikes in Japan are far cooler than those sold in the U.S.\n\n\n\nStill.. 1200 pairs?! Is this Wale or the chick from Sex & The City?\n\nHowever, Wale is easily the biggest sneakerhead in the rap game. Dating back to 2006’s 100 Miles and Running Mixtape where he raps about his dunks, J’s, etc. on the song “Kicks,” Wale has proven that he has the dopest kicks in the game. He has been known to rock foamposites MONTHS before they drop, as well as mad other exclusive Jordans, Nikes, Pennys, ETC.\n\nI would guess he has 3000 pairs.", "annotation_id": "162505", "url": "https://genius.com/162505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
