{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9 Piece", "line": "Fuck you mean I’m talking keys like Ray Charles", "vault_lines": ["Fuck you mean I’m talking keys like Ray Charles"], "meaning": "Not piano keys, but kilos of cocaine (which Ray Charles, the famous blind pianist, loved! His eyes didn’t work, but his nostrils did..)", "annotation_id": "161414", "url": "https://genius.com/161414", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9 Piece", "line": "Automatic leave ’em dead in the living room Get it? Leave ’em dead in the living room", "vault_lines": ["Automatic leave 'em dead in the living room", "Get it? Leave 'em dead in the living room"], "meaning": "Weezy will kill you in the living room just to make a dead/living pun (it’s like starving someone to death in the dining room..)\n\nThis line bears extreme similarity to a line from Eminem’s “Underground”.", "annotation_id": "161413", "url": "https://genius.com/161413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9 Piece", "line": "I’m talking white girl; Marilyn Monroe", "vault_lines": ["I’m talking white girl; Marilyn Monroe"], "meaning": "“White girl” is 70’s slang for cocaine (as opposed to heroin which is called “boy”)\n\nMarilyn Monroe had some junk in the trunk, just like Weezy’s got a fat sack of yayo..", "annotation_id": "161409", "url": "https://genius.com/161409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9 Piece", "line": "It’s Lil Tunechi, what up doe?", "vault_lines": ["It’s Lil Tunechi, what up doe?"], "meaning": "Tune was the name that Weezy was given by his grandmother. He added the “chi” on the end there. He added the Chi on the end, because of Gucci. Similar sounds.\n\nFind him on Twitter @LilTunechi", "annotation_id": "161408", "url": "https://genius.com/161408", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
