{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "line": "Two Russian twins suck while I drive fast", "vault_lines": ["Two Russian twins suck while I drive fast"], "meaning": "Action has the privilege of two Russian twins giving him a blowjob at the same time while he speeds in his car. He also raps a similar line on “La Luna,” the second track from the album:\n\nChampagne drippin' down the beard hair\nSupermodel suckin' while I steer the long pink Fleetwood\n\nAction is also heard rapping about getting sucked at the wheel on “The Don’s Cheek” from Blue Chips 2:\n\nRoll up, looking like Sinbad with the earring\nLightskin sucking my penis while I’m steering", "annotation_id": "13013744", "url": "https://genius.com/13013744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "line": "[Intro 1]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The intro/outro part is only heard one time in the song. On the version put on streaming services like Spotify and iTunes, it can be heard at the very beginning of the song, while on the version released on Action Bronson’s official Youtube page, it can be heard at the end of the song.", "annotation_id": "12658107", "url": "https://genius.com/12658107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "line": "I’m the label owner, I’m the only one can shelf me", "vault_lines": ["I'm the label owner, I'm the only one can shelf me"], "meaning": "Rick Ross founded Maybach Music Group in 2009 with Atlantic Records as a distributor. As the CEO of his record label, Rick Ross is the only one who can decide if he doesn’t want a project or track to be released.", "annotation_id": "12634919", "url": "https://genius.com/12634919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "line": "All my niggas down, we lookin’ like Fu-Schnickens", "vault_lines": ["All my niggas down, we lookin' like Fu-Schnickens"], "meaning": "Fu-Schnickens were an American hip-hop trio who were active in the 90’s.", "annotation_id": "12598195", "url": "https://genius.com/12598195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "line": "I’m the one that takes the wolf head, wears it on my own head", "vault_lines": ["I'm the one that takes the wolf head, wears it on my own head"], "meaning": "Action Bronson references the cover art for his 2012 mixtape Rare Chandeliers.", "annotation_id": "12584232", "url": "https://genius.com/12584232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "line": "Shit, sweep you off your feet Like Ryu in the corner", "vault_lines": ["Like Ryu in the corner"], "meaning": "This is a Street Fighter reference as well as Bronson boasting about how good this song is gonna be; it’s gonna make you fall head over heels as if you’ve been hit by a leg sweep.\n\nhttps://i.imgur.com/Z78fhsI.gifv\n\nBronson also references Street Fighter on “La Luna,” the album’s second track:\n\nAsian shooter with the blonde hair, Street Fighter character\nFuck around and suplex ‘em through the salad bar", "annotation_id": "12559709", "url": "https://genius.com/12559709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "line": "Yo, if I didn’t say it’s me, you would probably think it’s Sting", "vault_lines": ["Yo, if I didn't say it's me, you would probably think it's Sting"], "meaning": "Action Bronson is known for introducing his verses by saying “It’s me!”. His raspy voice may be as elegant and smooth as Sting, but the comparison may also refer to the song (especially the bassline) sounding like “Wrapped Around Your Finger” by the Police, which had Sting on bass and lead vocals.\n\nComparing himself to pop culture personalities is classic humor by Action, for example:\n\nYo it’s the rap Scott Disick", "annotation_id": "12559181", "url": "https://genius.com/12559181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "9-24-7000", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Action-bronson-9-24-7000-lyrics", "genius_title": "9-24-7000", "genius_id": 3122685, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Hustle while niggas gossip, hatin’, that switch the topic", "vault_lines": ["Hustle while niggas gossip, hatin', that switch the topic"], "meaning": "“Hustle while niggas gossip, hate and I’ll switch the topic”.. Ross maintains his boss status by avoiding the habits of losers. People who gossip usually talk negative about others to feel better about themselves and their insecurities.\n\nWhile they gossip, he outworks, outperforms, out-hustles and outshines everyone. He can’t contribute the conservation of a hater/loser. He didn’t become a boss with the habits of losers.", "annotation_id": "15567667", "url": "https://genius.com/15567667", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Can I let my top down in my 911?", "vault_lines": ["Can I let my top down in my 911?"], "meaning": "“Letting the top down” refers to a vehicle being a convertible. Many manufactures have different names and forms of a convertible, such as a spyder, cabriolet, targa and roadster. Being that Ross is referring to Porsche who produce cabriolet as well as targa models, he’s most likely referring to the cabriolet seeing as he’s letting the top down and targa’s only remove the upper front portion of the vehicle’s roof instead of completely retracting to the rear.", "annotation_id": "13484387", "url": "https://genius.com/13484387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "In my 911? In my 911? In my 911? In my 911?", "vault_lines": ["Jump in my 911, 2 bricks in my compartment"], "meaning": "This line is repeated multiple times throughout the hook to emphasize his fondness of the illustrious German automaker Porsche’s flagship and most successful model, the 911. The Porsche 911 is the cornerstone of Porsche. Recently Porsche have incorporated it’s sleek, easily recognizable and appealing body style in the form of the 911’s rear headlights to their mid-size luxury crossover SUV, the Cayenne, as well as the newly redesigned Panamera.", "annotation_id": "13484304", "url": "https://genius.com/13484304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Fuck your investigation, study my elevation", "vault_lines": ["Fuck your investigation, study my elevation"], "meaning": "Ross wants people to stop asking questions about his personal life, and marvel at how he has risen like hot magma at Pompei—only to harden into the Rap State of Liberty.\n\nThe American spirit in the soul of a hustler.\n\n\n\nAlso, “study my elevation” refers to his elevation to the top of the rap game. Ross started out as a highly-sought free agent after his hit single “Hustlin”, and has now become one of the biggest names in hip-hop. Like Ross wrote in the liner notes of the GFID booklet:", "annotation_id": "1349662", "url": "https://genius.com/1349662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "400K in my baggage, 80 round automatic", "vault_lines": ["400K in my baggage, 80 round automatic"], "meaning": "This could be seen as a double entendre:\n\n\nRoss rides around with $400,000 cash in his luggage.\nRozay has $400,000 worth of bullets in his suitcase.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUsually, AK-47’s have a standard magazine of 30 rounds. So having an AK with 80 rounds would probably cause Ricky to pray to God and ask for help to hold his chopper.\n\n\n\nIt’s all apart of Bawseology.", "annotation_id": "1349661", "url": "https://genius.com/1349661", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Secret indictments,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "An indictment in the common law system, is a formal accusation that a person has committed a crime.\n\nA Rozay indictment on the other hand is like a regular indictment except it’s secret—meaning Ross won’t tell you that he’s accusing you of a crime, Ross will just deal with himself. Justice is handed out without the discretion of a jury. Ross is your judge, jury, and executioner.\n\nGod Forgives, Rozay Don’t", "annotation_id": "1349643", "url": "https://genius.com/1349643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Boom boom boom boom!", "vault_lines": ["Boom boom boom boom!"], "meaning": "Gun noises are very popular in dirty southern hip-hop. These uncredited adlibs throughout the song are performed by MMG lieutenant Gunplay.", "annotation_id": "1274611", "url": "https://genius.com/1274611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "I remember pickin’ watermelons Now the Porsche cost me a quarter million", "vault_lines": ["I remember pickin' watermelons", "Now the Porsche cost me a quarter million"], "meaning": "A rise from rags to riches type of lyric, Ross recollects how at one point he used to pick watermelons—either to eat or sell. Now however, he is at the top of the rap game, and is able to afford cars worth $250,000.\n\n\n\nIn a Rolling Stone article about Ross, reporter asks if his Porsche really did cost a quarter million, but Ross said that it was rented for $400 because that wouldn’t sound as good in a song.", "annotation_id": "1158067", "url": "https://genius.com/1158067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Cherry red 911, straight to my destination", "vault_lines": ["Cherry red 911, straight to my destination"], "meaning": "This gets Ross where he needs to go – the millions, Heaven, etc.", "annotation_id": "1058581", "url": "https://genius.com/1058581", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "911: 100 miles and runnin’", "vault_lines": ["911: 100 miles and runnin'"], "meaning": "MMG labelmate Wale has a song named “911” and also a mixtape called 100 Miles and Running (it should be noted though that the song is not on the mixtape). He uses these allusions to refer back to theme of the song, Porsche 911s. .", "annotation_id": "1019310", "url": "https://genius.com/1019310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "God forgives, I don’t In other words, retaliation is a must!", "vault_lines": ["In other words, retaliation is a must!"], "meaning": "God forgives peoples' transgressions but Ross says he doesn’t have that type of quality in him—so if you do wrong by him he’s gonna do wrong by you. Revenge is necessary when you’re the Boss.", "annotation_id": "965347", "url": "https://genius.com/965347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Fired the stylist, went and bought a big and tall", "vault_lines": ["Fired the stylist, went and bought a big and tall"], "meaning": "Big & Tall is a retail store than specializes in clothing made for men of Rozay’s size. Just like in the dope game, it’s more beneficial to ‘cut the middle man’ in order to obtain more income, so he fired his personal stylist then bought the store and turned that into his closet.\n\n\n\nThis is also a reference to Rick Ross announcing a “Big and Tall” Reebok Line. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j-PC1A-ZHFA", "annotation_id": "955390", "url": "https://genius.com/955390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Gucci Pucci money long, he got 20 cars", "vault_lines": ["Gucci Pucci money long, he got 20 cars"], "meaning": "​Alex Bethune aka “Gucci Pucci” is Ross' longtime manager and CEO of MMG, He is rarely in the public eye, but you can read a few interview excerpts here.\n\nPucci is an extremely well respected manager that helped start up the Poe Boy Entertainment record label. Pucci’s wealth allows him to afford many luxuries, such as a copious amount of cars.", "annotation_id": "950724", "url": "https://genius.com/950724", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Mayweather got a fight, make me some reservations", "vault_lines": ["Mayweather got a fight, make me some reservations"], "meaning": "50 Cent used to promote Floyd Mayweather, but after a falling out, Rozay stepped up as Floyd Mayweather’s Hip Hop representative. Although at one point Ross and Mayweather had beef, they have since squashed it. Ross has announced that he is now apart of the new Money Team, where as Mayweather touts Rozay as one of the principal figures in hip-hop today.\n\n\n\n https://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/264100725175513089 https://twitter.com/FloydMayweather/status/264579388341891072 https://twitter.com/FloydMayweather/status/264615634258767872 https://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/264744773699645440", "annotation_id": "950715", "url": "https://genius.com/950715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "If I die today, on the highway to heaven", "vault_lines": ["If I die today, on the highway to heaven"], "meaning": "Ross, who was born in 1976, is just the right age to remember the 1984-9 TV drama Highway to Heaven, which starred Michael Landon as an angel helping people with their problems.", "annotation_id": "950657", "url": "https://genius.com/950657", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "911", "line": "Ain’t no more off days, my crib look like a mall", "vault_lines": ["Ain't no more off days, my crib look like a mall"], "meaning": "Rick Ross refuses to slow down his grind—there will be no breaks, he’s got a goal to accomplish!\n\nAlso referencing his MMG member Wale’s movement and song, called “No Days Off”.\n\nDue to his constant grind, he’s earned a lot of money, and as his prize, he is able to afford a MASSIVE crib!", "annotation_id": "946293", "url": "https://genius.com/946293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
