{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "A GEOMETRY’S DASH", "line": "Adamant that you never click, there’s a bug shit You will never win", "vault_lines": ["Adamant that you never click, there's a bug shit", "You will never win"], "meaning": "Hundreds of levels officially endorsed via the ratings system by the developer of Geometry Dash include “bugs” in their gameplay due to the old nature of the levels staying the same as updates still occur. Things like physics updates don’t always retain their original logic and can cause old levels to become unbeatable. This can also be caused due to different FPS values that the game runs at, making the physics more reliable at different speeds. This effect usually doesn’t occur on newer levels due to the fact that auto is usually relegated to short stories rather that just automatic gameplay.", "annotation_id": "40071542", "url": "https://genius.com/40071542", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
