{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "A Miracle", "line": "You’ll think I’m Biggie, I’m bumping Juicy with several groupies", "vault_lines": ["You'll think I'm Biggie, I'm bumping Juicy with several groupies"], "meaning": "Christopher George Latore Wallace, best known as The Notorious B.I.G. or Biggie Smalls, was an American rapper.\nWallace was raised in the Brooklyn borough of New York City.\n\n“Juicy” is a single by American hip hop artist The Notorious B.I.G. and his solo debut single from his 1994 debut album Ready to Die.", "annotation_id": "1874632", "url": "https://genius.com/1874632", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "A Miracle", "line": "I surely didn’t believe in magic, but I knew I had it in Savage", "vault_lines": ["I surely didn't believe in magic, but I knew I had it in Savage"], "meaning": "He didn’t expect that it would happen easily or without effort (magically) but he believed in his vision for using rap to create a better life for himself (going by the nickname ‘Young Savage’ and titling his major label debut album Savage Life)", "annotation_id": "1411617", "url": "https://genius.com/1411617", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
