{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Above The Law", "line": "One billion, two billion, three billion, four", "vault_lines": ["One billion, two billion, three billion, four"], "meaning": "Khaled is interpolating Jay-Z’s legendary line on “U Don’t Know” off The Blueprint where the Brooklyn superstar raps,\n\nI tell you the difference between me and them\nThey tryin' to get they ones, I’m tryin' to get them M’s\nOne million, two million, three million, four\nIn just five years, forty million more\nYou are now lookin' at the forty million boy\nI’m rapin' Def Jam ‘til I’m the hundred million man", "annotation_id": "30041401", "url": "https://genius.com/30041401", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Above The Law", "line": "So postin’ guns on the internet, we don’t condone It’s like snitchin’ on yourself Doin’ crimes on the camera, you like a witness to yourself", "vault_lines": ["So postin' guns on the internet, we don't condone"], "meaning": "Meek Mill discourages the act of sharing images or posts of guns on the internet, emphasizing that it’s not something to support. He likens it to snitching on oneself, suggesting that broadcasting illegal activities online is akin to acting as a witness against oneself, making it easier for law enforcement to track or build a case.", "annotation_id": "30040692", "url": "https://genius.com/30040692", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
