{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "Beef for dinner, pill for breakfast", "vault_lines": ["Beef for dinner, pill for breakfast"], "meaning": "Using  dinner and breakfast to signal times of days as dinner is the last meal and breakfast is the first.\n\nHe gives her his (raw) meat for dinner and in the morning she has to take the pill.", "annotation_id": "3289175", "url": "https://genius.com/3289175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "Throwing jabs like four Zab Judah’s", "vault_lines": ["Throwing jabs like four Zab Judah’s"], "meaning": "Gunplay is talking about Zab Judah. Zabdiel “Zab” Judah is an American professional boxer. Judah has won five world titles between the light welterweight and welterweight divisions and is a former Undisputed World Welterweight Champion. If Gunplay is able to embody this strength and more, you know you don’t stand a chance.", "annotation_id": "3225590", "url": "https://genius.com/3225590", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "My nigga Gun got my back He went on trial for his life", "vault_lines": ["He went on trial for his life"], "meaning": "Gunplay was\n\n\n\n faced a second charge of aggravated assault with a firearm. According to the rapper’s attorney, Gunplay could have faced life in prison if convicted on both counts.", "annotation_id": "3225374", "url": "https://genius.com/3225374", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "She want a thug nigga, she a little choosey Beat a life sentence, feel like Lil’ Boosie", "vault_lines": ["She want a thug nigga, she a little choosey", "Beat a life sentence, feel like Lil’ Boosie"], "meaning": "The woman Gunplay is associating with only likes men who fit her definition of a “thug nigga”, which is great news for Gunplay considering that in 2012 he proved his status by narrowly escaping life in prison for his participation in an armed robbery against his own accountant. Gunplay also thanks Rick Ross for helping him dodge this jail time.\n\n\n\nGunplay is relating his incident with the law as being similar to that of Lil' Boosie’s story. In 2009, Lil Boosie was arrested on his ‘participation’ in the murder of Terry Boyd. While still incarcerated, Lil Boosie admitted to an attempt to smuggle drugs into the prison he was housed in, further extending his sentence.\n\nIn March 5th 2014, cries from fans and fellow rappers stating Free Boosie were finally heard and he was released from prison.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fL8o0oMdfeQ", "annotation_id": "3224546", "url": "https://genius.com/3224546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "Aight, aight, aight, aight, aight", "vault_lines": ["Aight, aight, aight, aight, aight"], "meaning": "Repetition is an incredibly effective literary device that allows Rick Ross to emphasize his previous points regarding the sexual dilemma facing his latest woman", "annotation_id": "3224539", "url": "https://genius.com/3224539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "Aight, she wanna fuck a dope dealer Aight, or keep fuckin’ with them broke niggas", "vault_lines": ["Aight, she wanna fuck a dope dealer", "Aight, or keep fuckin’ with them broke niggas"], "meaning": "These lines allude to the hook of Meek Mill’s “Dope Dealer” track:\n\nWanna fuck with a dope dealer?\nOr keep fuckin’ them broke niggas?", "annotation_id": "3224440", "url": "https://genius.com/3224440", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "You pulled a gun on my homie you better have one for me", "vault_lines": ["You pulled a gun on my homie you better have one for me"], "meaning": "If someone pulls out a gun on one of Rozay’s boys, Ricky is strapping himself up and coming at you with a gang of miscreants to avenge his boy.\n#Don’t play no games with Rozay", "annotation_id": "3224404", "url": "https://genius.com/3224404", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "line": "Boobie got with the work what Dre just got for his Beats", "vault_lines": ["Boobie got with the work what Dre just got for his Beats"], "meaning": "This is an allusion to Ross’s connection with the notorious street gang the Boobie Boys and Ross is stating that by putting in work (selling drugs and participating in other illicit activtieis) he and his associates were able to make nice amounts of money.\n\nHow nice? Well on May 9th 2014, Dr. Dre announced a deal with Apple to purchase his style of headphones named Beats by Dre, for $3.2 Billion dollars. Its suffice to say that Ricky Rozay is alluding to having tons of money.\n\nDr.Dre even made a video upon this announcement calling himself the “First billionaire in Hip Hop”.", "annotation_id": "3224285", "url": "https://genius.com/3224285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aiight", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gunplay-aiight-lyrics", "genius_title": "Aiight", "genius_id": 434337, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "AintNuttin", "line": "Bron bringing back the title, it ain’t nothin’ nigga", "vault_lines": ["Bron bringing back the title, it ain't nothin' nigga"], "meaning": "French Montana likes to keep his songs in the vault for awhile before release, as seen with Lose It’s “Cash Money till I die” reference by Weezy.This is a reference to the 2014 NBA Championships were the Miami Heat, Ross’s team, played off against the San Antonio Spurs. Rick Ross was hoping for 3-peat championship thanks to Lebron James, unfortunately that’s not how it happened.", "annotation_id": "7336489", "url": "https://genius.com/7336489", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "AintNuttin", "line": "AP balenciagas it ain’t nothin’ nigga", "vault_lines": ["AP balenciagas it ain't nothin' nigga"], "meaning": "French is referring to Audemars Piquets, which is a very expensive Swiss watch, made with the world’s thinnest calibers.\n\nHe is also talking about the designer Balenciaga, a European fashion house founded by Cristóbal Balenciaga, which is famous for its leather shoes, and bags.", "annotation_id": "7196758", "url": "https://genius.com/7196758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "AintNuttin", "line": "All they jewelry gold plated", "vault_lines": ["All they jewelry gold plated"], "meaning": "Gold plating is a method of depositing a thin layer of goldonto the surface of another metal, most often copper or silver (to make silver-gilt), by chemical or electrochemical plating. In other words it’s not Authentic\n\n\n\nAn example of fufu jewelry", "annotation_id": "6605744", "url": "https://genius.com/6605744", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
