{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ain’t Worried About Nothin (Remix 2)", "line": "Started on the first floor, my apartments just rose", "vault_lines": ["Started on the first floor, my apartments just rose"], "meaning": "Rozay uses an analogy of an apartment here to illustrate his rise to success, as well as literally describe how his living situation has changed. He uses “first floor” as an analogy for his poor beginnings, and he’s now risen above and is at the opposite side of the spectrum as a millionare.\n\n\n\n“My apartments just rose” may also mean that the apartments in which he used to live have risen in cost now that he’s famous, since they were once home to a superstar.", "annotation_id": "3391508", "url": "https://genius.com/3391508", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ain’t Worried About Nothin (Remix 2)", "line": "All my goons in grey and blue", "vault_lines": ["All my goons in grey and blue"], "meaning": "As stated a few lines before, Snoop is a member of the “Rollin' 20’s Crips”, whose trademark color is blue.", "annotation_id": "3383432", "url": "https://genius.com/3383432", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ain’t Worried About Nothin (Remix 2)", "line": "Worried about nothing cause I’m still counting that money I ain’t even made yet", "vault_lines": ["Worried about nothing cause I'm still counting that money I ain't even made yet"], "meaning": "Why would Diddy worry about something ?\nIn 2014 he reached a worth of 700 million dollars , and he is still rising up. He is counting the money he ain’t even made yet , because he surely will gain it.", "annotation_id": "3269142", "url": "https://genius.com/3269142", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
