{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Albert Pujols", "line": "Three strikes like a muh-fucking C.C", "vault_lines": ["Three strikes like a muh-fucking C.C"], "meaning": "In baseball, 3 strikes earns you one strikeout. Pitchers, earn the strikeout. Wale shouts out the famous and successful pitcher C.C Sabathia of the New York Yankees.", "annotation_id": "567485", "url": "https://genius.com/567485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Albert Pujols", "line": "Three strikes put a muh-fucking K up", "vault_lines": ["Three strikes put a muh-fucking K up"], "meaning": "As is keeping with baseball tradition, fans will often put up large letter “K\"s to symbolize the amount of strikeouts the given pitcher has. Every strike out earns one K. Wale’s verse was \"another strikeout”, and a K (or one thousand dollars) Wale has earned.\n\nWale continues the next four lines with a similarly letter-oriented theme.", "annotation_id": "567482", "url": "https://genius.com/567482", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Albert Pujols", "line": "I’m tryna knock that out the park, Albert Pujols)", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna knock that out the park, Albert Pujols)"], "meaning": "Wale is referring to St. Louis Cardinals first baseman Albert Pujols. But, the only thing Wale wants to knock out the park is that p*****y.", "annotation_id": "567460", "url": "https://genius.com/567460", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Albert Pujols", "line": "Schematic, hold the fuck up nigga Bring that shit the fuck back", "vault_lines": ["Schematic, hold the fuck up nigga", "Bring that shit the fuck back"], "meaning": "In “Concrete Jungle”, Juelz Santana gives DJ Drama a similar order. In the case of Lil Wayne and Juelz' effort, the track was exclusive. Here, Ross wants everyone to know that he is not playing a game and has a clear message about MMG.\n\nHold up Drama\nWhere you get that shit from nigga\nMan, that’s exclusive\nRun that shit the fuck back", "annotation_id": "567455", "url": "https://genius.com/567455", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Albert Pujols", "line": "You wife ain’t shit, we G’d her", "vault_lines": ["You wife ain't shit, we G'd her"], "meaning": "Wale is saying your wife is nothing to him because him and his crew had sex with her. He also continues the baseball theme of the song by referring to Derek Jeter(G’d her) the New York Yankees player.\n\n\n\nDerek Jeter with latest flame.", "annotation_id": "567411", "url": "https://genius.com/567411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Albert Pujols", "line": "Be a snitch? No way, Jose Canseco", "vault_lines": ["Be a snitch? No way, Jose Canseco"], "meaning": "Jose Canseco is a former MLB Player and Star who played from 1985-2001. At the end of his storied career, he co-authored the book “Juiced” where he admitted and accused numerous former teammates of using steroids. Or, snitching on fellow players. Fab will never be a snitch like Jose.\n\n\n\nAlso nice play on words “No way José” by itself is another way of saying absolutely not.", "annotation_id": "567409", "url": "https://genius.com/567409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Albert Pujols", "line": "From turning white into cream, powdered milk", "vault_lines": ["From turning white into cream, powdered milk"], "meaning": "He turned white (cocaine) into cream (the acronym for Cash Rules Everything Around Me originated by Wu-Tang Clan)", "annotation_id": "567404", "url": "https://genius.com/567404", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
