{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Fuck y’all mad at me for, ’cause my belt got two G’s on it? Her bag got two C’s on it?", "vault_lines": ["Fuck y'all mad at me for, 'cause my belt got two G's on it?", "Her bag got two C's on it?"], "meaning": "The Game sports belts by the high-end brand Gucci, whose logo consists of two interlocking G’s. Similarily, Chanel’s logo consists of two interlocking C’s, and The Game evidently buys his women nice bags.", "annotation_id": "15283871", "url": "https://genius.com/15283871", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "If them niggas pussy, we douche ’em, we clean ’em out", "vault_lines": ["If them niggas pussy, we douche 'em, we clean 'em out"], "meaning": "A douche is a device used to introduce a stream of water into the body for medical or hygienic reasons, and usually refers to a rinsing of the vagina (“pussy”). A pussy can also be a coward, creating a double entendre, as 2 Chainz suggests he will get you should you prove to be a weakling", "annotation_id": "15283821", "url": "https://genius.com/15283821", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Disrespect my nigga Boss and I’m flashin’ the chrome", "vault_lines": ["Disrespect my nigga Boss and I'm flashin' the chrome"], "meaning": "Possibily a reference to among others 50 Cent, as Fiddy has been involved in a notorious beef with both Rick Ross (i.e. “Boss”) and The Game. Game is saying that he is riding with Rick Ross, and should you insult him, he will take his side.", "annotation_id": "15283814", "url": "https://genius.com/15283814", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "I like clubs where all the women workin’ naked", "vault_lines": ["I like clubs where all the women workin' naked"], "meaning": "2 Chainz showed his love for strip clubs by starting a fashion collection, Strip Club Veteran. He has rapped extensively about his love for strippers and strip clubs throughout his catalogue of music.\n\nHit the strip club in the day shift\nGive a lil' bitch a donation", "annotation_id": "11628079", "url": "https://genius.com/11628079", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Like a little nigga in Africa, I was born totin’ that K", "vault_lines": ["Like a little nigga in Africa, I was born totin' that K"], "meaning": "An estimated 120,000 African children take part in armed conflict, some as young as 7 years old.\n\nGame says he was born holding a ‘K, short for the soviet-made AK-47 – a weapon commonly used by child soldiers.", "annotation_id": "11570413", "url": "https://genius.com/11570413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "[Verse 2: The Game]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Along with referencing one of Jay Z’s lines from HAM, Game also uses the same type of flow that Jay used on his verse in that song. This is just one of many allusions Game has made to Jay in his music over the years.", "annotation_id": "3057637", "url": "https://genius.com/3057637", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Free Big Meech, free Boosie and C-Murder", "vault_lines": ["Free Big Meech, free Boosie and C-Murder"], "meaning": "Big Meech is the co-founder of the “Black Mafia Family” and was sentenced to 30 years for running an international cocaine distribution ring.\n\n\n\nLil Boosie was sentenced to eight years in prison after pleading guilty to drug charges and was released March 5, 2014.\n\n\n\nC-Murder was convicted of murder in 2003 and is currently serving a life sentence.", "annotation_id": "2654927", "url": "https://genius.com/2654927", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "And my AR see murders, that’s beef, nigga; no burgers", "vault_lines": ["And my AR see murders, that's beef, nigga; no burgers"], "meaning": "Game’s ArmaLite Rifle has seen some cold nights and bloody days.\n\nA little beef word play. Game clarifies that his AR related beef has nothing to do with a damn cheeseburger.", "annotation_id": "1466494", "url": "https://genius.com/1466494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Got coke swimmin’ in that glass jar, bitch, go turn on them burners!", "vault_lines": ["Got coke swimmin' in that glass jar, bitch, go turn on them burners!"], "meaning": "In contrast to the previous line, these ain’t no metaphorical burners: Game’s cooking up a batch of crack. He’s already got the coke (cut with baking soda) swimming in water in a jar, now he’s just waiting for his girl to turn on the stove to get it started.", "annotation_id": "1448559", "url": "https://genius.com/1448559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Ali Bomaye! Ali Bomaye!", "vault_lines": ["Ali Bomaye! Ali Bomaye!"], "meaning": "A chant during the Rumble in the Jungle in 1974 between Muhammad Ali and George Foreman. It means “Ali, Kill Him\"\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AF65FrX0dKY", "annotation_id": "1390907", "url": "https://genius.com/1390907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Got a chopper and a bottle—fuck it, let ’em spray!", "vault_lines": ["Got a chopper and a bottle—fuck it, let 'em spray!"], "meaning": "The Game’s livin up to his name (Mr. Spades) and got his bottle\n\n\n\nand an AK so let the niggas come at him in this fight\n\n\n\nIt is also common to use a bottle as a homemade silencer, which Game could also be talking about. That would make spray a double entendre for spraying bullets and spraying water.", "annotation_id": "1328005", "url": "https://genius.com/1328005", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Skateboard on a nigga track", "vault_lines": ["Skateboard on a nigga track"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is probably talking about how he raps on tracks.  2 Chainz doesn’t just flow on the track, he skateboards on it and pulls off “lyrical” tricks.\n\nA possible reference to Lil Wayne, who loves skateboarding, and who released a remix of No Lie Remix on Dedication 4 mixtape.\nGame already talked about him (as “Tune”) in the verse just before. Skateboard P (a.k.a Pharrell Williams), would later go on to produce 2 Chainz’s track Feds Watching\n\n2 Chainz is possibly also referring to the fact that he’s a feature artist, more famous for hopping on other people’s tracks than his own.  2 CHAINZ!!!", "annotation_id": "1321472", "url": "https://genius.com/1321472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Thank God that a nigga seen another day", "vault_lines": ["Thank God that a nigga seen another day"], "meaning": "Continuing on the line before, thank God Ali didn’t literally kill George Foreman.\n\n\n\nSecond meaning, Game is thanking God for keeping him alive, especially in Compton where a lot of people die everyday", "annotation_id": "1317025", "url": "https://genius.com/1317025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Weigh the mothafuckas in, made another mil", "vault_lines": ["Weigh the mothafuckas in, made another mil"], "meaning": "Speaking on the process of weigh-ins before a boxing match, where you only get paid if you make the weight requirements. Same with coke.\n\nAlso notice the homonym meal/mill. After he weighed the word he made another MEAL on the grill and MILL in his pockets", "annotation_id": "1313289", "url": "https://genius.com/1313289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Put my hands up? Fuck you sayin’, bruh? ’Cause I’m a black man in a Phantom Or is it ’cause my windows tinted?", "vault_lines": ["Or is it 'cause my windows tinted?"], "meaning": "Cops that see a black man in a Phantom will automatically assume that he’s a drug dealer or a criminal of some sort.\n\n\n\nAlso note that tinted windows, once they reach a certain degree, are actually criminal. Game wonders if he’s being pulled over for this legit reason, or because he’s a black man with riches.", "annotation_id": "1308938", "url": "https://genius.com/1308938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "If you got work Go to work, don’t work at your residence", "vault_lines": [". If you got work", "Go to work, don't work at your residence"], "meaning": "As stated by The Notorious B.I.G. in “Ten Crack Commandments”:\n\n“Never sell no crack where you rest at\nI don’t care if they want a ounce, tell ‘em 'bounce!’”", "annotation_id": "1307733", "url": "https://genius.com/1307733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "And that’s real shit, no Will Smith and no Nona Gaye But they yellin’…", "vault_lines": ["And that's real shit, no Will Smith and no Nona Gaye"], "meaning": "Will Smith and Nona Gaye starred as Muhammad & Belinda Ali in the movie Ali. In the movie the kids in Africa were yelling “Ali Bomaye”. He is saying that they are yelling for real and not in a movie.", "annotation_id": "1301219", "url": "https://genius.com/1301219", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Word to Muhammad, that triple beam is heaven-sent", "vault_lines": ["Word to Muhammad, that triple beam is heaven-sent"], "meaning": "A triple beam is a balance scale used to measure chemicals or streetdrugs. He says that a triple beam is sent from heaven, so he gives thanks to the Prophet Muhammad. Going by the other references in the song, he’s most likely also referring to Muhammad Ali, the prophet of boxing. In context of the following line, the fight where “ali bomaye!” was shouted was called “the rumble in the jungle.”\n\nThis also can be a reference to the Notorious BIG in “Mo' Money Mo' Problems”:\n\nTriple beam lyrical dream", "annotation_id": "1300791", "url": "https://genius.com/1300791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "You know I got that work on the foreman grill", "vault_lines": ["You know I got that work on the foreman grill"], "meaning": "Great metaphor here by Game. The “Work” he’s referring to is a “chicken” (slang for coke), and you cook chickens on grills. A reference to George Foreman who fought Muhammed Ali in the Rumble in the Jungle, and became famous for his cooking grills.", "annotation_id": "1294430", "url": "https://genius.com/1294430", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Car cost 300 thou’ and I blow Indo in it (2 Chainz!)", "vault_lines": ["Car cost 300 thou' and I blow Indo in it (2 Chainz!)"], "meaning": "His car costs 300,000 and he smokes weed in it, looks like the cops were partially correct…\n\nAlso notice that Game has a “fuck it” attitude towards the cops stopping him, the real reason they stopped him was because he was black but they are using what they found to justify the stop. But, The Game is like fuck it, he will do what he wants in his car because he will be stopped whether it is legal, or not.", "annotation_id": "1293732", "url": "https://genius.com/1293732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "This the voice of ghetto intelligence", "vault_lines": ["This the voice of ghetto intelligence"], "meaning": "2 Chainz represents the peak of sophisticated ignorance. He was raised on the streets, so his streets smarts are extremely high. He also graduated from ASU with a 4.0 GPA. This proves 2 Chainz has both street and book smarts.", "annotation_id": "1293384", "url": "https://genius.com/1293384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Get my people out them chains, nigga I mean handcuffs, time to man up", "vault_lines": ["I mean handcuffs, time to man up"], "meaning": "Game suggests racism still exists. African-Americans aren’t in chains anymore but they end up in handcuffs due to racial profiling.\n\nHandcuffs are the modern reincarnation of chains from the slave days.\n\n\n\nHe later refers to “Free Big Meech, Boosie and C-Murder” in the song", "annotation_id": "1291758", "url": "https://genius.com/1291758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Ali Bomaye! Ali Bomaye!", "vault_lines": ["Ali Bomaye! Ali Bomaye!"], "meaning": "A chant in Lingala, the language that is spoken in the Republic Democratic of Congo, that was screamed by the supporters of Muhammad Ali during the Rumble in the Jungle in 1974 against George Foreman. It means “Ali, Kill Him\"", "annotation_id": "1290998", "url": "https://genius.com/1290998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 157, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Gentleman attire, in threads that won’t expire", "vault_lines": ["Gentleman attire, in threads that won't expire"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is notorious for wearing Louis Vuitton and Versace clothes. These clothing lines never go out of style due to the fact that unsold items are burned causing the value to never decrease.", "annotation_id": "1290184", "url": "https://genius.com/1290184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "I’m on the block like D12, I got the white; no B-12", "vault_lines": ["I'm on the block like D12, I got the white; no B-12"], "meaning": "This two-part line is crazy. The Game tosses around two metaphors to amazing effect:\n\n\nGame is on his block like NBA center Dwight (“da white” = Dwight) Howard, whose nickname is D-12 since he wears #12. A low post player, he commonly operates on “the block”.\n\n\n\n\n\n-Thus Game is using the sound of Dwight, which sounds very similar to “The White” to imply that he has has cocaine on his block.\n\n-Eminem, a white rapper, was considered the leader of the rap group, D12. The group has more or less fallen apart with the death of Proof.", "annotation_id": "1289918", "url": "https://genius.com/1289918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 113, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": ", I smack niggas; Sprewell", "vault_lines": ["You a bitch nigga; no female, I smack niggas; Sprewell"], "meaning": "Refers to Latrell Sprewell’s volatile behavior off the court, when he choked his coach and was suspended for 68 games.\nSpree was a bad dude with an even badder jumpshot\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=edtCa8O0hiM\nOn a Hip Hop side note, he was also the inspiration behind the legendary Spinning Spree basketball shoes:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tMpodB2Rc9o", "annotation_id": "1288539", "url": "https://genius.com/1288539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Got a call from Skateboard, pick ’em up at LAX", "vault_lines": ["Got a call from Skateboard, pick 'em up at LAX"], "meaning": "Skateboard P a.k.a Pharrell\n\n\n\nHe’s worked on numerous songs with Game and even called him the most underrated MC at one point.\n\nLAX is Game’s third studio album, but he refers to the airport in Los Angeles in this line.", "annotation_id": "1288519", "url": "https://genius.com/1288519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Ridin’ through the jungles in that mothafuckin’ elephant That’s a gray Ghost, with the ears on it", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' through the jungles in that mothafuckin' elephant", "That's a gray Ghost, with the ears on it"], "meaning": "Game is ridin' round the gang areas of LA in a grey Rolls Royce Phantom ( recalling the Rumble in The Jungle match)\n\n\n\n“Ears” refers to the suicide doors.", "annotation_id": "1288488", "url": "https://genius.com/1288488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Niggas tough on them blogs and never did nothin’ at all", "vault_lines": ["Niggas tough on them blogs and never did nothin' at all"], "meaning": "People talk shit on the internet (blogs, twitter, etc.) but don’t apply that same tough guy act in real life. Plus, those sample people usually haven’t done anything meaningful in their own life.\n\nThis line is intended for the people on the internet who call Ross fake & pelt him with insults about his weight, while he is a millionaire and well aware of himself.", "annotation_id": "1288479", "url": "https://genius.com/1288479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "I got rifles with lasers, swing it just like the majors", "vault_lines": ["I got rifles with lasers, swing it just like the majors"], "meaning": "Putting a laser on a rifle gives you better accuracy on hitting targets.\n\n\n\n“Majors” is short for the Major League (baseball) by “swing it” he means gun butting.\n\nSo he swings it like a baseball bat.", "annotation_id": "1288468", "url": "https://genius.com/1288468", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "I got a bitch that look like Laila Ali sittin’ in my lap", "vault_lines": ["I got a bitch that look like Laila Ali sittin' in my lap"], "meaning": "Laila Ali is the daughter of Boxing legend, Muhammed Ali.", "annotation_id": "1288459", "url": "https://genius.com/1288459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Like New Orleans, like Baltimore, come to Compton you’ll see murders", "vault_lines": ["Like New Orleans, like Baltimore, come to Compton you'll see murders"], "meaning": "Game is comparing Compton’s murder rates with the likes of Baltimore and New Orleans.\n\nAlso ‘See murders’ is a play on C-Murder’s name.\n\nIt isn’t the first time that Game uses this wordplay", "annotation_id": "1288435", "url": "https://genius.com/1288435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "From the P houses, did it from the wee hours", "vault_lines": ["From the P houses, did it from the wee hours"], "meaning": "“P” standing for projects.\n\n2 Chainz was born in College Park, Georgia", "annotation_id": "1288420", "url": "https://genius.com/1288420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "In my four-door, lookin’ real photogenic", "vault_lines": ["In my four-door, lookin' real photogenic"], "meaning": "He’s looking really good while ridin' around and gettin' it in his four door vehicle\n\n\n\nPlay on words: “four door” (pronounced fo-doe) and “photogenic” (pronounced fo-doe-genic)", "annotation_id": "1288413", "url": "https://genius.com/1288413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "You mad ’cause your daughter fuck with me on spring break Well, I’ma fuck her till the springs break", "vault_lines": ["Well, I'ma fuck her till the springs break"], "meaning": "Spring break is known for college students partying and having fun; Lots of outdoor concerts and shit. Game’s saying that the cop is hating on him because his daughter is coming out to see him perform on Spring break and he’s gonna fuck the cops daughter so hard that the bed is gonna break.\n\n\n\nClever wordplay with “spring break” and “fuck her ‘til the springs break”\n\nGame is really ‘bout that spring break wordplay life\n\nIn a lot of ways this is similar to what Jay Z touched on in Somewhereinamerica, when he mentions Miley Cyrus twerking. Game is commenting on how hip-hop and “gangsta rappers” such as himself have been accepted by the mainstream, and as a result, even suburban white girls come to his shows. The cop is mad because he doesn’t want his daughter associating with what he considers to be “low class” or “ghetto.”", "annotation_id": "1288346", "url": "https://genius.com/1288346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": ", 2 Chainz!", "vault_lines": ["Car cost 300 thou' and I blow Indo in it (2 Chainz!)"], "meaning": "Game is saying 2 Chainz' popular catchprase to introduce him since his second verse is about to follow this line. 2 Chainz shouts it in the majority of the tracks he is in.\n\nWatch 2 Chainz Say His Name 50 Times In 3 minutes..", "annotation_id": "1288342", "url": "https://genius.com/1288342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Speakin’ skateboards, where Tune at?", "vault_lines": ["Speakin' skateboards, where Tune at?"], "meaning": "Game is referring to Lil Wayne aka Young Tune aka Lil Tunechi. Wayne loves to skateboard.", "annotation_id": "1288057", "url": "https://genius.com/1288057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Gold medals on my neck, I call it Michael Phelps", "vault_lines": ["Gold medals on my neck, I call it Michael Phelps"], "meaning": "Micheal Phelps is the most decorated olympian of all time with a total of 28 medals, 23 of which are golds.\n\n\n\nRick has just as many gold chains around his neck (also a reference to how much he’s winning)\n\nThe Michael Phelps reference is also keeping with the same theme of swimming previous line.\n\nRoss' gold medals are his ten jesus pieces of course.", "annotation_id": "1288040", "url": "https://genius.com/1288040", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "No lie, “No Lie” already got a plaque", "vault_lines": ["No lie, \"No Lie\" already got a plaque"], "meaning": "As of November 2012, “No Lie” was certified platinum, only 6 months after its release. .", "annotation_id": "1287819", "url": "https://genius.com/1287819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "I take my case to trial, hire the Dream Team Robbie Kardashian, Johnnie Cochran; I seen things", "vault_lines": ["Robbie Kardashian, Johnnie Cochran; I seen things"], "meaning": "The Dream Team most commonly refers to the 1992 US Men’s Olympic basketball team, but Ross uses it here to refer to a group of lawyers who were skillful in a different kind of court.\n\nRobert Kardashian and Johnnie Cochran were among the legal Dream Team of lawyers who defended OJ Simpson during his infamous murder case. They aren’t cheap either, but Ross has the dough to afford it.\n\n\n\nIf they can make OJ look innocent in the situation he was in, they can make anyone look innocent. It’s funny that Ross uses this in the present tense when both of the lawyers are dead.\n\nRoss could possibly be referring to his trial with the real “Freeway” Ricky Ross, who was suing him for copyright infringement for using his name. Rozay beat the case.", "annotation_id": "1287780", "url": "https://genius.com/1287780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Versace outfit cost me 3,000", "vault_lines": ["Versace outfit cost me 3,000"], "meaning": "Most likely refering to the Versace outfit he wore to the VMA’s. .", "annotation_id": "1286550", "url": "https://genius.com/1286550", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "I’m insane and you Usain, nigga better turn on them burners", "vault_lines": ["I'm insane and you Usain, nigga better turn on them burners"], "meaning": "Game is crazy; you’re so scared of him, you’ll run as fast as Usain Bolt (the fastest man in the world). .\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=By1JQFxfLMM\n\nThis could also be a refernce to a Comcast Xfinity commercial:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RJCGEr_usXc", "annotation_id": "1286318", "url": "https://genius.com/1286318", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Sellin’ that chicken; no lemon pepper, no sweet and sour", "vault_lines": ["Sellin' that chicken; no lemon pepper, no sweet and sour"], "meaning": "“Chicken” is drug slang derived from kilos of cocaine being called “birds.” This line is a pun as lemon pepper and sweet and sour are two flavors of chicken. Extending the pun, lemon pepper and sweet and sour could be slang for tainted forms of cocaine.\n\n\n\nRick Ross (also on this track) owns several Wing Stops.", "annotation_id": "1285319", "url": "https://genius.com/1285319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "My lawyer threw them gloves on and beat another case", "vault_lines": ["My lawyer threw them gloves on and beat another case"], "meaning": "With reference to The Rumble in the Jungle from the previous line. Game uses a boxing metaphor to explain how his lawyers got him off the hook on another court case.\n\n\n\nThis could also be a reference to the OJ Simpson trial where OJ’s lawyer Johnnie Cochran had Simpson put the gloves on in the courtroom, only to find out that they didn’t fit, with Cochran famously saying “if it doesn’t fit, you must acquit” eventually leading to Simpson never being found guilty.\n\n2 Chainz also used this line in “Spend It:”\n\nI’m ridin round my side of town, boxing gloves, I beat the trial", "annotation_id": "1284936", "url": "https://genius.com/1284936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "I’m ’bout to rumble in the jungle in these new Kanye’s Ali Bomaye! Ali Bomaye!", "vault_lines": ["Ali Bomaye! Ali Bomaye!", "I'm 'bout to rumble in the jungle in these new Kanye's"], "meaning": "Refers back to the Rumble in the Jungle in 1974 between Muhammad Ali and George Foreman.\n\nHe’s saying he’ll fight/kill anybody out here while wearing his new Air Yeezy 2’s", "annotation_id": "1284425", "url": "https://genius.com/1284425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Fuck y’all mad at me for?", "vault_lines": ["Fuck y'all mad at me for?"], "meaning": "Reference to Jay-Z’s opening line in the second verse of “HAM”\n\nFuck y'all mad at me for? Y'all don’t even know what I’ve been through", "annotation_id": "1283855", "url": "https://genius.com/1283855", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "Got two chains, they two-tone, two hundred racks, no lie", "vault_lines": ["Got two chains, they two-tone, two hundred racks, no lie"], "meaning": "REFERENCE OVERLOAD\n\nGot two chains\n\nShout-out to 2 Chainz (who’s featured on the song).\n\nGot two chains, they two-tone\n\nRefers to Game’s chains. He actually has a “Jesus Piece” for his “Jesus Piece”!\n\n\n\nTwo hundred racks\n\nReferencing Kanye’s nod that 2chainz verses are now 100k a piece. His one necklace has two chains, therefore it is worth $200K\n\n\n\nNo lie\n\nHe finishes off with a reference to No Lie, which is a name of one of 2 Chainz’s more popular songs featuring Drake", "annotation_id": "1272400", "url": "https://genius.com/1272400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "line": "[Verse 1: 2 Chainz]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "2 Chainz' verse for this track leaked a while back and was actually named “Twilight Zone.” Some people thought it was going to end up on his debut album, Based on a T.R.U. Story.", "annotation_id": "1269916", "url": "https://genius.com/1269916", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ali Bomaye", "status": "done", "targets": 48, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/The-game-ali-bomaye-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ali Bomaye", "genius_id": 97993, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "Theres no limit to Gucci money just ask Silkk the Shock & them", "vault_lines": ["Theres no limit to Gucci money just ask Silkk the Shock & them"], "meaning": "No Limit was a huge rap movement and label in the 90’s started by Master P, whose roster included his brother Silkk the Shocker.", "annotation_id": "15487255", "url": "https://genius.com/15487255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "A Geto Boy like ’Face and them", "vault_lines": [", a Geto Boy like 'Face and them"], "meaning": "Geto Boys are a rap group who were amongst some of the most popular rap acts of the ‘90’s. Scarface, nicknamed 'Face, is perhaps their most famous member.", "annotation_id": "15487252", "url": "https://genius.com/15487252", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "Cause like R. Kelly “I’m a Flirt”", "vault_lines": ["Cause like R. Kelly \"I'm a Flirt\""], "meaning": "A reference to one of R&B singer R. Kelly’s many hit songs, “Im A Flirt.”", "annotation_id": "15487245", "url": "https://genius.com/15487245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "Just like the New Boys “I’m a jerk”", "vault_lines": ["300K, my paper work just like the New Boys \"I'm a jerk\""], "meaning": "New Boyz were a popular rap duo in the early 2010’s who capitalized off of the “jerking dance movement” with their hit song, “You’re A Jerk.”", "annotation_id": "15487243", "url": "https://genius.com/15487243", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "Hottest boys out Drake and him", "vault_lines": ["Hottest boys out Drake and him"], "meaning": "Him is Scarface, you can tell this because Gucci Mane was talking about him 2 lines before. In Gucci Mane’s opinion, the hottest rappers out back when he made this song were Drake and Scarface.\n\n\n\nFun fact: Gucci Mane released this album 3 months after Drake had dropped his EP So Far Gone, which was his breakthrough into the mainstream.\n\nGucci Mane has worked with Drake in the past, on the song “Believe It Or Not” 2 months before this song was released. He later worked with Scarface on the song “Scarface” in 2012.", "annotation_id": "3315276", "url": "https://genius.com/3315276", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "I can make a Hummer flip", "vault_lines": ["I can make a Hummer flip"], "meaning": "Double entendre: He can cause a Hummer SUV to overturn with his waves of gunfire, but also can sell or “flip” a Hummer’s worth of cocaine. The Hummer H2’s MSRP is around 53,000, which is almost exactly three times the street price of a kilo of cocaine: $17,500.", "annotation_id": "495085", "url": "https://genius.com/495085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "I’m on my way to see my P.O I ain’t talking about probation officer", "vault_lines": ["I ain't talking about probation officer"], "meaning": "At first gucci makes you think he’s on his way to see parole officer or his probation officer because he is recently released from prison. But really he is on his way to his post office box to pick up money from his record label and other ways hes making that guap.\nGucci is being playful with the fact that he’s a known criminal.", "annotation_id": "228215", "url": "https://genius.com/228215", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "Gucci, pass the other clip", "vault_lines": ["Gucci, pass the other clip"], "meaning": "While it’s possible that Ross and Gucci are using M1 Garands or other WWII-vintage battle rifles, it seems more likely that they would stick to something modern and efficient.\n\nThe gun in the picture is an SKS, but Waka Flocka is not with them, so we can assume it’s not one of those.\n\nAn AK-47, for example, is quite commonly used and is loaded with magazines. Magazines look like this:\n\n\n\nAK’s are sometimes called “choppers,” and we know Rick Ross has one of those in his car.", "annotation_id": "174892", "url": "https://genius.com/174892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "Talking about my P.O. box, they just sent me 3 million dollars", "vault_lines": ["Talking about my P.O. box, they just sent me 3 million dollars"], "meaning": "Gucci is referring to the fact that his commercial success has given the initials “P.O.” a new meaning, and he’s getting paid.", "annotation_id": "174889", "url": "https://genius.com/174889", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "More check than a check-o-slovin", "vault_lines": ["More check than a check-o-slovin"], "meaning": "Gucci is explaining that he makes a lot of money (checks) with a double entendre on the word Czech, an adjective referring to people from the Czech Republic. “Check-o-slovin” is simply a bastardization of “Czechoslovakian,” altered to fit the rhyme-scheme.", "annotation_id": "103147", "url": "https://genius.com/103147", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "line": "I got work like babe and them", "vault_lines": ["I got work like babe and them"], "meaning": "Baby had an album by the Big Tymers called I Got That Work\n\n\n\nGucci Mane is similarly industrious", "annotation_id": "101208", "url": "https://genius.com/101208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All About The Money", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gucci-mane-all-about-the-money-lyrics", "genius_title": "All About The Money", "genius_id": 724, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Away", "line": "Still with these niggas that I started with", "vault_lines": ["Still with these niggas that I started with"], "meaning": "They often say money changes people, but it didn’t change Elhae, he is still the same thug he always was. And he still hangs with the same crew because he knows that they will always have his back, while new “friends” are just fakes that would leave the second his money ran out.", "annotation_id": "2899233", "url": "https://genius.com/2899233", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Away", "line": "Bitch is a dime a dozen, I get dimes by the bundle (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch is a dime a dozen, I get dimes by the bundle (Huh)"], "meaning": "Wordplay using two definitions of the word dime:\n\nBecause Ross is a rap star, getting bitches is easy (making them a dime a dozen), so easy, that he has bundles of dimes (or 10/10 girls).", "annotation_id": "2899229", "url": "https://genius.com/2899229", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Away", "line": "Bag full of money, uh, heart full of hate (Uh) Club full of bitches, I’ma ball ’til I can’t (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Bag full of money, uh, heart full of hate (Uh)", "Club full of bitches, I'ma ball 'til I can't (Woo)"], "meaning": "This entire song is about living in the now, and this line epitomizes that. He might have things hurting him in his heart, but all of that goes away when steps into the club, all that matters then is having a good time (or balling), because you don’t know when you will die.", "annotation_id": "2899227", "url": "https://genius.com/2899227", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Away", "line": "My niggas ride, I pray to God we never die (Right) ’Cause it ain’t a game, ain’t no such thing as extra lives (Lives)", "vault_lines": ["My niggas ride, I pray to God we never die (Right)", "'Cause it ain't a game, ain't no such thing as extra lives (Lives)"], "meaning": "He knows that this is real life, not a video game, so you aren’t going to get a second chance when you die. That is why he prays so hard for his crew to stay alive, he doesn’t want to lose his homies forever.", "annotation_id": "2899101", "url": "https://genius.com/2899101", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Away", "line": "My niggas gon’ forever ride (Yeah) I pray to God we never die (Uh) I’m tryna blow it all today ’Cause we won’t know who’s ’bout to fall today (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["I pray to God we never die (Uh)", "I'm tryna blow it all today", "'Cause we won't know who's 'bout to fall today (Uh)"], "meaning": "Even though he prays that him and his homies will never die, he knows that it is still likely that they will as they are living the dangerous life of a G.\n\nSo, since he knows they could die any day, he blows his money on nice things, as his money will have no use to him after he’s dead.", "annotation_id": "2122638", "url": "https://genius.com/2122638", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Away", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Elhae-all-away-lyrics", "genius_title": "All Away", "genius_id": 145125, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Birds", "line": "Wanna shoplift? Come and boost this", "vault_lines": ["Wanna shoplift? Come and boost this"], "meaning": "Ross alludes to the classic Ancient Greek expression of defiance: Molan Labe (English: Come and Take [Them]).\n\nIf you want what he has, you’ll have to come and take it from him!", "annotation_id": "17501381", "url": "https://genius.com/17501381", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Birds", "line": "Say the word on the street is that my man got him", "vault_lines": ["Say the word on the street is that my man got him"], "meaning": "Ross is talking about how he been helping other artist to  make to the main stream and if he couldn’t sign them to his record label then they could still be unknown.", "annotation_id": "15737755", "url": "https://genius.com/15737755", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Birds", "line": "No clothes in the closet, it’s all birds (Hah) No sneakers in the sneaker box, it’s all birds (Hah) No luggage in the trunk, man, it’s all birds (Hah)", "vault_lines": ["No clothes in the closet, it's all birds (Hah)", "No sneakers in the sneaker box, it's all birds (Hah)", "No luggage in the trunk, man, it's all birds (Hah)"], "meaning": "Birds is slang on the street for kilos of cocaine. So everywhere he just mentioned, is filled with kilogram of cocaine.", "annotation_id": "911870", "url": "https://genius.com/911870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Birds", "line": "My red bottoms", "vault_lines": ["Cargo pants and my red bottoms"], "meaning": "He wears Louboutin shoes, known for their red bottom.", "annotation_id": "888694", "url": "https://genius.com/888694", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Birds", "line": "Double MG this little thing of ours", "vault_lines": ["Double MG this little thing of ours"], "meaning": "‘MMG’ a popular music group, named Maybach Music Group was established by Rick Ross and the current roster includes (Febuary 2012) French Montana, Triple C’s, Torch, Gunplay, Rick Ross, Omarion, Rockie Fresh, Meek Mill, Wale, Magezeen and many more!\n\n\n\nThe Sicilian Mafia calls itself “La Cosa Nostra” or literally translated, “This little thing of ours”. Rozay is comparing MMG to the mafia.\n\nAlso a reference to another song on the album, “This Thing of Ours”.", "annotation_id": "888692", "url": "https://genius.com/888692", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
