{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All Birds", "line": "I’m a John Gotti, got my own army", "vault_lines": ["I'm a John Gotti, got my own army"], "meaning": "Reference to the American mobster who became the Boss of the Gambino crime family in New York City. John Gotti’s nickname was “The Teflon Don”. He was called this because a series of charges and court cases didn’t stick like he was Teflon, a non-stick chemical developed by Dupont\n\n\n\nRicky Rozay has an album called Teflon Don and often refers to himself as such. Rick Ross took the nick name because he was able to maintain his momentum and success while being able to withstand the barrage of many efforts to discredit him", "annotation_id": "859469", "url": "https://genius.com/859469", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
