{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "(Up, down, up, down, up, down)", "vault_lines": ["Keep your hands up, get 'em in the sky for the homies that didn't make it and my folks locked down (Woo)"], "meaning": "T – pain states, “and every time i step up in the building everybody hands go up, and they stay there”, this implies that the hands stay permanently  up, strangely, the next line in the song implies something that completely changes the story, is the complete opposite of what is previously stated, T – pain beautifully sings, in the adlib technically “up down, up down, up down.” this could imply that in reality it is difficult to keep ones hand up for a prolonged period of time. This could possibly be interpreted as a metaphor, as the themes of the song is that they always win, but in reality, this is statistically impossible, and they don’t always win and sometimes experience failure.", "annotation_id": "28191755", "url": "https://genius.com/28191755", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Yellow bone passenger, they see it they say, “Oh boy”, tell Khaled ”Back it up”", "vault_lines": ["Yellow bone passenger, they see it they say, \"Oh boy\", tell Khaled \"Back it up\""], "meaning": "Rick Ross shows off the reliquary he procured from a contact in Venice.", "annotation_id": "21196687", "url": "https://genius.com/21196687", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Hit the trick, jump the track, bitch, I want my money back", "vault_lines": ["Hit the trick, jump the track, bitch, I want my money back"], "meaning": "Snoop Dogg references a familiar children’s rhyme\n\nEngine, engine number nine,\nGoing down Chicago line,\nIf the train goes off the track,\nDo you want your money back?", "annotation_id": "15430296", "url": "https://genius.com/15430296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "DJ Khaled (Hey; Nasty Beatmakers)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "DJ Khaled has a habit of screaming his name on the tracks he puts on his album (but doesn’t always produce the tracks he puts on his album). This has caused criticism at the apparent lack of contribution on Khaled’s part. As the meme goes:", "annotation_id": "14627474", "url": "https://genius.com/14627474", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "And every time I step up in the building, everybody hands go up And they stay there (Yeah) And they say, “Yeah” (Yeah), and they stay there", "vault_lines": ["And they stay there (Yeah)", "And they say, \"Yeah\" (Yeah), and they stay there"], "meaning": "For years, fans of this song have been singing “and they stay there” until T-Pain revealed on Twitter that the actual lyrics are “and they say yeah”:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/TPAIN/status/377794577475702784\n\nReaffirmed in a since-deleted 2017 tweet as well:", "annotation_id": "13154506", "url": "https://genius.com/13154506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "My niggas call me loco, down for armed trafficking", "vault_lines": ["My niggas call me loco, down for armed trafficking"], "meaning": "Arms trafficking is selling guns without a Federal Firearms License as a commercial business. Generally associated with the criminal underworld that Ross constantly refers to being the boss of.\n“Automatic weapons on the floor but who can you call?”", "annotation_id": "346515", "url": "https://genius.com/346515", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "I been runnin’ this rap game since I was twenty years old (What? What?)", "vault_lines": ["I been runnin' this rap game since I was twenty years old (What? What?)"], "meaning": "Snoop’s first appearance was on Dr. Dre’s “Deep Cover” back in 1992. Snoop brags about his history to make it clear he isn’t going anywhere.", "annotation_id": "42374", "url": "https://genius.com/42374", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Hardaway, cross ’em up", "vault_lines": ["Floss 'em up, toss 'em up, Hardaway, cross 'em up"], "meaning": "The crossover is a move used in basketball to outmaneuver the competition, just as Snoop is doing in his line of work. Tim Hardaway is credited for the “killer crossover” back in his Golden State Warrior days.", "annotation_id": "38541", "url": "https://genius.com/38541", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Blame it on that conjure (Ha), the hood call it Luda ’gnac", "vault_lines": ["Blame it on that conjure (Ha), the hood call it Luda 'gnac"], "meaning": "Conjure Congac is Ludacris' very own brand.\n\n\n\nAlso hinting at the Jamie Foxx hit “Blame It”", "annotation_id": "27488", "url": "https://genius.com/27488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "I hung with the worst of ’em, bust ’til I burst ’em up", "vault_lines": ["I hung with the worst of 'em, bust 'til I burst 'em up"], "meaning": "Snoop actually has one of the longest rap sheets in the game.\nCheck it: Snoop’s Legal Issues", "annotation_id": "27321", "url": "https://genius.com/27321", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Al Davis said it best, “Just win baby, win”", "vault_lines": ["Al Davis said it best, \"Just win baby, win\""], "meaning": "Al Davis is the owner of the Oakland Raiders who uttered the famous quote “Just win, baby.”\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0RAlrzcdfRY\n\nThe phrase has become so attached to his name that Glenn Dickey found it fitting to use as the title for his 1991 biography of Davis.", "annotation_id": "25351", "url": "https://genius.com/25351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Don’t mess with us, we like the U in the ’80s Back to back, set a trap, hit the lick, hit it back", "vault_lines": ["Don't mess with us, we like the U in the '80s", "Back to back, set a trap, hit the lick, hit it back"], "meaning": "“The U” is The University of Miami, specifically the football team.\nIn the 1980’s they were a NCAA Football powerhouse, although they never actually won “back-to-back” National Championships as Snoop says.\n\nThey won in 1987 and 1989 and believed they were robbed in 1988. They were also a notoriously “tough team” who fought and bullied other teams to the point that Notre Dame refused to schedule any further games against them.", "annotation_id": "25346", "url": "https://genius.com/25346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Last time on the Khaled remix, now I’m on the original version", "vault_lines": ["Last time on the Khaled remix, now I'm on the original version"], "meaning": "On the “I’m So Hood (Remix)” Ludacris says:\n\nI’m so hood that Ludacris should have been on the original version\n\nApparently, Ludacris is now “hood” enough to do that..", "annotation_id": "24872", "url": "https://genius.com/24872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "You know serving me’s a no-no", "vault_lines": ["You know serving me's a no-no"], "meaning": "Nobody can hand Rick his ass in a lyrical battle. Your mileage may vary\n\nThis and the beginning of the next line could also mean that there are no outstanding arrest warrants for Rick (thus he can’t be served with one, and he is “clean as a whistle”)", "annotation_id": "24174", "url": "https://genius.com/24174", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Swervin’ in my lo-lo, head on the swivel", "vault_lines": ["Swervin' in my lo-lo, head on the swivel"], "meaning": "Rick Ross calls himself The Boss and swerves in his low-riding luxury car, which sits lower to the ground than your average Honda, SUV, or minivan.", "annotation_id": "24173", "url": "https://genius.com/24173", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "We all strapped in all black, it’s like fuck life (Fuck life) (All we do is win)", "vault_lines": ["We all strapped in all black, it's like fuck life (Fuck life) (All we do is win)"], "meaning": "Rick refuses to let life’s hardships like a beef with 50 Cent get him down, that’s why he and his crew are armed (“strapped”)\n\n“All black dressing” can signify mourning too, like you’d see on  people attending a funeral. It’s one of the many “fuck life” moments that we have to be put through.", "annotation_id": "24171", "url": "https://genius.com/24171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Do Is Win", "line": "Clean as a whistle as I pull out in my Rolls Royce", "vault_lines": ["Clean as a whistle as I pull out in my Rolls Royce"], "meaning": "The Rolls Royce has a clean (fresh, new, bright) finish.\n\nRick claims that he ain’t “Riding Dirty” a-la Chamillionare. He isn’t packing any drugs, the car ain’t stolen, and the cops got no reason to pull him over.", "annotation_id": "24169", "url": "https://genius.com/24169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
