{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Have in This World", "line": "Okay, I’m reloaded (Ain’t expect this)", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I'm reloaded (Ain't expect this)"], "meaning": "Reminiscent of the intro on Jay-Z’s Brooklyn’s Finest, which in turn was  inspired by Carlito’s Way.", "annotation_id": "30561870", "url": "https://genius.com/30561870", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Have in This World", "line": "Sippin’ on that Remy outside of the club Got me trippin’ like I’m Remy outside of the club", "vault_lines": ["Sippin' on that Remy outside of the club", "Got me trippin' like I'm Remy outside of the club"], "meaning": "Remy takes on two meanings here:\n\n\nRozay’s drinking Rémy Martin brand cognac\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlcohol consumption causes people to act out of character and unreasonably, which is known as “trippin”. Some might say fellow rapper Remy Ma was tripping when she got into a gith outside a club, eventually catching assault, illegal weapon possession and attempted coercion charges related to the fight.", "annotation_id": "2912623", "url": "https://genius.com/2912623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All I Have in This World", "line": "The homey, Elvis Freshly (Uh, Huuh) and Rick Ross-teen (Nigga)", "vault_lines": ["The homey, Elvis Freshly (Uh, Huuh) and Rick Ross-teen (Nigga)"], "meaning": "Mannie Fresh has dubbed himself “Elvis Freshly”, a play on the name of the ultra-famous musician & cultural icon, “Elvis Presley”.\n\nAdditionally, he has labeled Rick Ross as “Rick Ross-teen”, a play on the other “Boss”, Bruce Springsteen.", "annotation_id": "1446924", "url": "https://genius.com/1446924", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
