{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All the Money In the World", "line": "Tryna figure out where I’m goin’ with my life As I’m steppin’ on the brake and hangin’ a sharp right", "vault_lines": ["Tryna figure out where I'm goin' with my life", "As I'm steppin' on the brake and hangin' a sharp right"], "meaning": "Ross uses “steppin on the brake and hangin' a sharp right” as a visual metaphor for making confident decisions that change the course of his life.", "annotation_id": "3488638", "url": "https://genius.com/3488638", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All the Money In the World", "line": "That time never felt so good Can’t forget about you, man I never would", "vault_lines": ["That time never felt so good", "Can't forget about you, man I never would"], "meaning": "Reminiscing on the past makes him feel so good. He finds it funny that even if certain things happened to him in the past, they feel like they just happened at the moment and it brings the exact feelings back to him. He wouldn’t trade any of his memories for anything in the world, not for even all the money in the world.", "annotation_id": "1002924", "url": "https://genius.com/1002924", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All the Money In the World", "line": "Passed in ’99, cancer all in his liver Shit different since we last spoke, his son’s a lil’ richer I’d never rap again if I could tell him that I miss him", "vault_lines": ["Passed in '99, cancer all in his liver", "Shit different since we last spoke, his son's a lil' richer"], "meaning": "Liver cancer took Ricky’s father in 1999, preventing him from witnessing Ross’s musical success. In the lines below, Ross questions the very merit of wealth if it can’t be shared with those who were so essential to his upbringing.\n\nRoss would gladly stop rapping just to tell his father, in person, that he’s dearly missed.", "annotation_id": "166223", "url": "https://genius.com/166223", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "All the Money In the World", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-all-the-money-in-the-world-lyrics", "genius_title": "All the Money In the World", "genius_id": 5988, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Almighty Black Dollar", "line": "Burnt down Black Wall Street", "vault_lines": ["Burnt down Black Wall Street"], "meaning": "In 1921, a racist white mob burned down “Black Wall Street”, a burgeoning African American entrepreneurial community in Tulsa, Oklahoma’s Greenwood District. The reverberations of that hateful destruction is still felt today.\n\nhttps://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/jun/19/tulsa-1921-massacre-trump-violence-legacy", "annotation_id": "21415600", "url": "https://genius.com/21415600", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Almighty Black Dollar", "line": "Fuck them bottles ain’t Puff, it ain’t Jay’s Ciroc, D’USSÉ, Bellaire, let’s get paid", "vault_lines": ["Fuck them bottles ain’t Puff, it ain’t Jay’s", "Ciroc, D'USSÉ, Bellaire, let's get paid"], "meaning": "Jeezy is tired of his money going to people that don’t care about his community.\n\nCiroc, D’USSÉ, and Luc Bellaire are respectively partnered with: Sean “Puffy” Combs, Jay Z (Shawn Carter), and Rick Ross.\nIf you’re going to buy the bar, Jeezy would rather see those dollars go to black entrepreneurs.", "annotation_id": "21415493", "url": "https://genius.com/21415493", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Almighty Black Dollar", "line": "Gucci don’t like Black people In my Boosie Badazz voice", "vault_lines": ["Gucci don't like Black people", "In my Boosie Badazz voice"], "meaning": "Jeezy makes reference to a June 2020 video in which Boosie Badazz told shoppers who were lined up at the Gucci store, “Gucci don’t like Black people, I don’t know why all y’all in that line”. The video can be viewed here.", "annotation_id": "21404598", "url": "https://genius.com/21404598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
