{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Long as your mama love you, don’t ever love a woman", "vault_lines": ["Long as your mama love you, don’t ever love a woman"], "meaning": "As long as your mama loves you, that’s all the love you need. Love from other women might be temporary, but a mother’s love for her child(ren) is forever.", "annotation_id": "19859629", "url": "https://genius.com/19859629", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Girls wanna have fun", "vault_lines": ["Girls wanna have fun"], "meaning": "Tie to the previous line where he uses “Cyndi Lauper” as a metaphor for drugs. He now plays with the title of Cyndi Lauper’s hit song “Girls Just Want To Have Fun”", "annotation_id": "16506467", "url": "https://genius.com/16506467", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Easy to dream a dream, though it’s harder to live it", "vault_lines": ["Easy to dream a dream, though it's harder to live it"], "meaning": "Its easy to dream about an idea- but to implement and to follow through all the way is a bit more difficult. Most cant follow through all the way.", "annotation_id": "15444927", "url": "https://genius.com/15444927", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "My ambition to win, just to get me some ends", "vault_lines": ["My ambition to win, just to get me some ends"], "meaning": "“Getting ends” initially means making ends meet, but he quickly develops more ambition.", "annotation_id": "503451", "url": "https://genius.com/503451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Servin’ raw and, fiends was calling, we was dot com", "vault_lines": ["Servin' raw and, fiends was calling, we was dot com"], "meaning": "Meek Mill was serving crack to fiends. “Dot com” relates to them being well connected – having many contacts in the streets. The internet is one giant information highway connected at many points. .", "annotation_id": "466116", "url": "https://genius.com/466116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "But I’m limitless mentally, I’m lyrically ZMT", "vault_lines": ["But I’m limitless mentally, I’m lyrically ZMT"], "meaning": "Wale’s intellectual ability is what defines him as a rapper, unlike Ross, who’s defining attributes are ambition and toughness. ZMT is a drug that cures migraine headaches; Wale’s flow is relief to the listener’s head\n\nWale could also be making a reference to NZT which is a drug that makes you use your brain to its fullest capacity from the movie “Limitless”.", "annotation_id": "453897", "url": "https://genius.com/453897", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "I got nothing against them, they got fucking potential", "vault_lines": ["I got nothing against them, they got fucking potential"], "meaning": "Wale isn’t tryin to be cocky or anything and he is saying that is rap opponents basically have as much potential as himself. Wale and J. Cole have been friendly rivals ever since they became friends.", "annotation_id": "433311", "url": "https://genius.com/433311", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "You know you real you don’t say it You know you real, we gon feel it", "vault_lines": ["You know you real you don’t say it", "You know you real, we gon feel it"], "meaning": "Anyone could go around saying they’re real, but the people who know they’re real don’t brag about it. Real recognize real, so Wale is saying if you’re real he’s going to feel it and know who’s real. This also plays into Mirrors, another song on Attention Deficit “real recognize real you need id to be noticed”.", "annotation_id": "423094", "url": "https://genius.com/423094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Life was diggin’ me deeper, I kept on coming up short", "vault_lines": ["Life was diggin’ me deeper, I kept on coming up short"], "meaning": "He’s saying life keeps on putting him in a deeper and deeper hole so he keeps up coming up short this pic should explain it more better:\n\n\n\nThe kid is shorter as he was put in a deep hole. Also coming up short means to fall short of succeeding.", "annotation_id": "422789", "url": "https://genius.com/422789", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Painting pictures that be my vision", "vault_lines": ["Beautiful music, painting pictures that be my vision"], "meaning": "Wale is going to set his own destiny, this is also a reference to one of his early mixtapes, Paint a Picture.", "annotation_id": "422498", "url": "https://genius.com/422498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Ralph!", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Wale’s real name is Olubowale, but one other name he goes by is Ralph Folarin. Folarin isn’t his last name, but more of a pen name. From the start Wale used “Ralph” because Folarin sounds like “Lauren”, feeding into an allusion to the revered clothing brand Ralph Lauren.", "annotation_id": "422494", "url": "https://genius.com/422494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "You niggas probably cop a plea before you cop a pistol", "vault_lines": ["You niggas probably cop a plea before you cop a pistol"], "meaning": "Wale suggests these other guys would go for a plea bargain before they bought a gun, suggesting that they are not as tough as they make themselves out to be.", "annotation_id": "422000", "url": "https://genius.com/422000", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Niggas reside where all the lions and killers be And I ain’t spend a minute up in the streets", "vault_lines": ["And I ain't spend a minute up in the streets"], "meaning": "Wale never claimed he was hood – he has lived both in D.C. and suburban Maryland as a youth – but he can relate with people from there cause he came from the same circumstances.", "annotation_id": "421996", "url": "https://genius.com/421996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "My father was missing, War Lord Oliver North", "vault_lines": ["My father was missing, War Lord Oliver North"], "meaning": "Rick Ross makes a reference to his father being missing, much like the gold and arms given to Iran in the Iran-Contra Scandal, which Oliver North, retired U.S. Marine, was the center of\n\nLord of War is a 2006 movie starring Nicolas Cage about an international arms dealer.  The main character is a conflation of several notorious real-life weapon sellers", "annotation_id": "421489", "url": "https://genius.com/421489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Me and Folarin MMG gon’ bring that Warner back", "vault_lines": ["Me and Folarin MMG gon' bring that Warner back"], "meaning": "Don’t make a mistake, Meek Mill and Wale are going to take the few mistake rappers make back and score (hits, money, etc.)\n\nMMG is also signed to Warner Brothers Records and will help bring that company back to success, like a cornerback who takes an interception back for a touchdown\n\n\n\nAlso a double entendre in reference to the Super Bowl interception by the Steelers' James Harrison off of Cardinals' quarterback Kurt Warner. Harrison ended up bringing the interception back 100 yards for a touchdown.", "annotation_id": "421197", "url": "https://genius.com/421197", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Cause chances are never given they tooken like interceptions So throw that pass, I’ll be the cornerback", "vault_lines": ["Cause chances are never given they tooken like interceptions", "So throw that pass, I’ll be the cornerback"], "meaning": "Given his rather rough childhood, he doesn’t view himself as someone in a position to receive (i.e. wide receiver) the same types of chances that more affluent people have. Therefore, with his plan to “move with aggression”, he’ll seize opportunities, similar to the way a cornerback (who is never purposely the target of a pass) often baits quarterbacks into making dangerous throws (“use my mind as a weapon”). He’ll manage to put himself into positions to be successful. Nice job of tying in the song’s title through rhyme scheme. .", "annotation_id": "421016", "url": "https://genius.com/421016", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Waking up in the dark Who cut my power off? it’s time to move that powder soft", "vault_lines": ["Who cut my power off? it’s time to move that powder soft"], "meaning": "Time for Rick Ross to sell some dope and get money to get his lights back on.  Young Jeezy faced this same dilemma on “Go Crazy”:\n\nIt’s kinda hard to be drug-free\nWhen Georgia Power won’t give a nigga lights free\n\nAlso it’s a sense of urgency that his lights got cut off, so it’s time to sell the drugs pure, no time to cook it up because that will take too long for his immediate issues", "annotation_id": "420811", "url": "https://genius.com/420811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Oh, I was raised by the stop sign", "vault_lines": ["Oh, I was raised by the stop sign"], "meaning": "Being \"raised by the stop sign\" interpreted literally implies \"on the street corner,\" where the stop sign is and where dope is sold, people are robbed, etc.", "annotation_id": "420263", "url": "https://genius.com/420263", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Uh, only hope I had was selling dope", "vault_lines": ["Uh, only hope I had was selling dope"], "meaning": "In “Self-Made,” Meek Millz dropped a line saying “Dropped out of school/ Never made it to the 12th grade”. I guess it’s safe to say this is a continuation to that line. The only way forward in the hood for him was to sell white..\n\n\n\nAlso “No hope in dope” is a famous anti-drug slogan of the 90’s. Popularized through bumper stickers and a ‘Saved by the Bell’ episode. Being raised ‘by the stop sign’ (street corner) selling dope became the his only hope to reach his ambitions.", "annotation_id": "420081", "url": "https://genius.com/420081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "But I got that green on my eyes And that ain’t no Donnie Simpson", "vault_lines": ["But I got that green on my eyes", "And that ain’t no Donnie Simpson"], "meaning": "“Green on my eyes” refers to being determined to earn money. This is a reference to the great Donnie Simpson, who hosted the most popular morning show in the DC Metro area on WPGC 95.5. His eyes are famously green:", "annotation_id": "419882", "url": "https://genius.com/419882", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Beautiful music, painting pictures that be my vision", "vault_lines": ["Beautiful music, painting pictures that be my vision"], "meaning": "His music paints pictures in the listeners head. His music is an art form, and he is metaphorically ‘painting pictures’ of his visions. Paint a Picture is also one of Wale’s early mixtapes", "annotation_id": "419642", "url": "https://genius.com/419642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Lebron shit, I was in that 6 after 23", "vault_lines": ["Lebron shit, I was in that 6 after 23"], "meaning": "Wale’s ambition is what lead him to owning a 600 Benz (or a 6 figure salary) at such a young age.\n\nAlso, Lebron James started his career off as #23 when he was with he Cleveland Cavaliers. He then changed his # to 6 when he went to the Miami Heat.", "annotation_id": "419503", "url": "https://genius.com/419503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ambition", "line": "Sittin’ in the trap now you moving Cyndi Lauper", "vault_lines": ["Sittin’ in the trap now you moving Cyndi Lauper"], "meaning": "Cyndi Lauper is a white female pop singer. So this is a reference to selling cocaine or “white girl”.  See Young Jeezy’s “White Girl” for the meme cocaine-as-white-female-pop-star tune. The Cyndi Lauper metaphor continues in the next line.", "annotation_id": "419501", "url": "https://genius.com/419501", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
