{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amore", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Bebe-rexha-amore-lyrics", "genius_title": "Amore", "genius_id": 6013023, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Lamborghini, middle of the ghetto", "vault_lines": ["Lamborghini, middle of the ghetto"], "meaning": "Some nice alliteration between Laborghini and ghetto. Makes sense since both words originate from Italian.\n\nA bit of a paradox since you won’t find a Lambo in most ghettos. Probably a figure of speech meaning he’s good in the hood.", "annotation_id": "30549018", "url": "https://genius.com/30549018", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "These boys goin’ blind they just happy bein’ free In a world of so many, I just wanted me a ki’", "vault_lines": ["These boys goin' blind they just happy bein' free", "In a world of so many, I just wanted me a ki'"], "meaning": "“Ki” has two meanings: 1) short of a “kilo” of cocaine (https://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=ki); and 2) a “key” to set him free (as per the previous line)", "annotation_id": "14340762", "url": "https://genius.com/14340762", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Wrists on chill", "vault_lines": ["Billionaire bid, wrists on chill"], "meaning": "This is another way of saying he has ice on his wrists (https://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=ice%20on%20my%20wrist)", "annotation_id": "14340758", "url": "https://genius.com/14340758", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Open fire when you see me", "vault_lines": ["Open fire when you see me"], "meaning": "Rozay isn’t scared of you, he dares you to try and assassinate him. Of course, this eventually happened for real when his car was wrecked during an assassination attempt.", "annotation_id": "2901393", "url": "https://genius.com/2901393", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "[Intro: Teedra Moses]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This intro and adlibs throughout the track are sung by ‘The Lioness’ Teedra Moses, who made history by becoming the first female to ever sign with MMG.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/356200174273572864", "annotation_id": "1318831", "url": "https://genius.com/1318831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "All stainless steel, quick to match it with my tool", "vault_lines": ["All stainless steel, quick to match it with my tool"], "meaning": "The watch he mentions in the above line is stainless steel, and his gun matches it in it’s quality.\n\n“Steel” is another term for gun, so if his “tool” (more slang for “gun”) is of stainless steel quality, you can bet that it’s gonna cause some pretty noticeable damage. By “pretty noticeable” I, of course, mean “it’s gonna blow your head off”.\n\nAnother rapper to have used the term “steel” and referring to a gun is the infamous Eminem, in his song “If I Had”, off of his The Slim Shady LP:\n\nTired of not having a deal,\nTired of having to deal with the bullshit without grabbing the steel", "annotation_id": "949116", "url": "https://genius.com/949116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "These boys snort lines, I’m fine just sippin’ wine", "vault_lines": ["These boys snort lines, I'm fine just sippin' wine"], "meaning": "Reference to them inhaling “cocaine”, whilst Ross sip wine.\n\nA shoutout to his MMG bretherin Gunplay & his coke snortin' habits.", "annotation_id": "948811", "url": "https://genius.com/948811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Nothin’ to lose, I was starvin’ from the start", "vault_lines": ["Nothin' to lose, I was starvin' from the start"], "meaning": "Ross continually alludes to, in his music, his rags-to-riches story, how he was one day struggling, and now is one of the wealthiest yearly earners in the game as according to the piece written by RG’s own Zack Greenburg.", "annotation_id": "948521", "url": "https://genius.com/948521", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "I’m speakin’ on unwritten laws, the code of the streets", "vault_lines": ["I'm speakin' on unwritten laws, the code of the streets"], "meaning": "the law of the streets is now the law of the government..you can listen to the government but in the streets…this is the law\n\nRoss is a student of hip hop, so you know this line is a shout-out to the original Code of the Streets.", "annotation_id": "948144", "url": "https://genius.com/948144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "It’s the red light district, nigga this Amsterdam", "vault_lines": ["It's the red light district, nigga this Amsterdam"], "meaning": "Prostitution in the Netherlands is legal and regulated.\nAmsterdam has a red light district where brothels are concentrated.", "annotation_id": "946606", "url": "https://genius.com/946606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Burnin’ Amsterdam green where it falls like a leaf", "vault_lines": ["Burnin' Amsterdam green where it falls like a leaf"], "meaning": "Amsterdam, and the Netherlands in general, have by United States standards pretty liberal drug laws.  Amsterdam is famously full of so-called “coffee shops” that offer the opportunity to get high.", "annotation_id": "946583", "url": "https://genius.com/946583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "The club that I’m a member, they’ll be gone by November", "vault_lines": ["The club that I'm a member, they'll be gone by November"], "meaning": "Ross continues the Wyclef reference above with this line.  One of Jean’s biggest solo hits was the 1997 song “Gone ‘Til November”.", "annotation_id": "946572", "url": "https://genius.com/946572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Refugees runnin’ wild, Wyclef with a SIG Sauer", "vault_lines": ["Refugees runnin' wild, Wyclef with a SIG Sauer"], "meaning": "Wyclef Jean was one of the members of the group The Fugees, who always made it clear that their name was short for “refugees”.  SIG Sauer is a German-based firearms company.", "annotation_id": "946563", "url": "https://genius.com/946563", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Standin’ in the field of dreams, tryna see a hundred mil", "vault_lines": ["Standin' in the field of dreams, tryna see a hundred mil"], "meaning": "1 million dollars simply isn’t the goal of hustlers. 10 million is hardly an acceptable net-worth if you’re really about your business. 100 million dollars.\n\nWALL STREET:\n\nWake up, will ya, pal? If you’re not inside, you’re outside, okay? And I’m not talking a $400,000 a year working Wall Street stiff flying first class and being comfortable, I’m talking about liquid. Rich enough to have your own jet. Rich enough not to waste time. Fifty, a hundred million dollars, buddy. A player, or nothing. Now, you had what it took to get into my office; the real question is whether you got what it takes to stay.\n\n\n\nAlso, Ross is alluding to the Kevin Costner movie about a baseball field in the middle of Iowa where dead ballplayers emerge out of the cornfields to play.\n\n“If you build it, they will come.” is a famous line from the film—this is comparable to the Maybach Music Empire that Ross has built. Make quality music, and people will buy it.", "annotation_id": "946004", "url": "https://genius.com/946004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Now the same cat drivin’ Jaguars", "vault_lines": ["Now the same cat drivin' Jaguars"], "meaning": "A play on words;\n\nHe’s a cat that used to hustle, that now drives a Jaguar, which is a BIG cat.", "annotation_id": "936601", "url": "https://genius.com/936601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "Amsterdam state of mind:", "vault_lines": ["Amsterdam state of mind:"], "meaning": "Shoutout to Nas, whose 1993 Illmatic features the track “New York State of Mind”. Also shoutout to Jigga, who’s Blueprint III contains “Empire State of Mind”.\n\nAn Amsterdam state of mind will quite probably involve women and drugs, since those are often associated with Amsterdam (and Holland as a whole).", "annotation_id": "934600", "url": "https://genius.com/934600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "I’m Berry Gordy to the streets", "vault_lines": ["I'm Berry Gordy to the streets"], "meaning": "Berry Gordy is the founder of Motown Records, and has cultivated such acts as The Jackson Five.", "annotation_id": "934594", "url": "https://genius.com/934594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Amsterdam", "line": "The Hublot’s cool but my Terminator’s foolish", "vault_lines": ["The Hublot's cool but my Terminator's foolish"], "meaning": "Hublot is a Swiss luxury watch maker while Terminator is a model of watch maker Audemars Piguet:\n\n\n\nRozay simply shows his watch preferences but also implies that he has the means to buy both even though they are very expensive.\n\nHe makes the same argument in Cigar Music.", "annotation_id": "933206", "url": "https://genius.com/933206", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
