{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Anything (To Find You)", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Monica-anything-to-find-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "Anything (To Find You)", "genius_id": 63129, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "Just had a seizure at the Super Bowl Woke up in the third quarter lookin’ for the smoke", "vault_lines": ["Just had a seizure at the Super Bowl", "Woke up in the third quarter lookin' for the smoke"], "meaning": "This line is in reference to a seizure that Ross suffered at Super Bowl 49, which took place weeks before the release of “Rather You Than Me”\n\nRick Ross has a documented history of seizures. Suffering at least two in October of 2011. He also mentions episodes of seizures in his 2019 memoir Hurricanes: A Memoir.", "annotation_id": "36370413", "url": "https://genius.com/36370413", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "Travelin’ the world, I’m just reppin’ my city But rarely do I hear that this nigga done did it", "vault_lines": ["Travelin' the world, I'm just reppin' my city", "But rarely do I hear that this nigga done did it"], "meaning": "Ross a Carol City/Miami repper (although he was born in Mississippi) feels some kind of way when he doesn’t get the respect he deserves in his hometown.", "annotation_id": "30427465", "url": "https://genius.com/30427465", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "Tears runnin’ down a nigga face", "vault_lines": ["Tears runnin' down a nigga face"], "meaning": "Ross is likely referring to the common teardrop face tattoo, rather than physical tears running down ones face.\n\nA teardrop tattoo can symbolize numerous events in a persons life.\n\nThe tattoo shows that the person has committed murder, served a lengthy jail sentence and/or an attempted murder.", "annotation_id": "12617940", "url": "https://genius.com/12617940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "Just bein’ somebody that the neighborhood respected And my mama could be proud of was the apple of my eye", "vault_lines": ["And my mama could be proud of was the apple of my eye"], "meaning": "Ross states that above all else, the two things that mean the most to him in life, are being someone his neighborhood could respect, while also becoming something his mama could be proud of.\n\n“Apple of my eye” is a an English idiom located in the bible from the King James Version, translated in 1611. It has widely been used in pop culture, most notable in the song “You Are the Sunshine of My Life,” by Stevie Wonder, where he used the phrase to potray the feelings he had for the woman he cherished.", "annotation_id": "11549209", "url": "https://genius.com/11549209", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "But like I’d rather be a killer than be a statistic", "vault_lines": ["But like I'd rather be a killer than be a statistic"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to Meek’s propensity to “Jump out the window” or be erratic, which in itself may be a defense mechanism, preempting any attack that may leave him harmed. To be a statistic is usually a negative connotation referring to a victim (as denoted in crime statistics).", "annotation_id": "11525279", "url": "https://genius.com/11525279", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "If it’s more than a quarter million, I’ll count it twice Pucci broke my heart, shit, I call it life And never will I call it right", "vault_lines": ["If it's more than a quarter million, I'll count it twice", "Pucci broke my heart, shit, I call it life", "And never will I call it right"], "meaning": "Alexander “Gucci Pucci” Bethune was Rick Ross' manager and former A&R of Maybach Music Group.\n\nWhile nothing was ever reported in the media, it appears the two have had a fallout in recent years; Ross is clearly alluding to an incident that caused a break up between the two that can never be fixed, however what actually happened is  currently unknown.", "annotation_id": "11522489", "url": "https://genius.com/11522489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "We all make mistakes, let’s not be too ’pecific", "vault_lines": ["We all make mistakes, let's not be too 'pecific"], "meaning": "Continuing from the last bar, this seems to indicate that Ross thinks it was a mistake for Meek to beef with Drake; but Ross doesn’t fault him for it, because all humans make mistakes.", "annotation_id": "11521619", "url": "https://genius.com/11521619", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "Real shit, look at me inside the White House With a pocket full of weed inside the White House", "vault_lines": ["Real shit, look at me inside the White House", "With a pocket full of weed inside the White House"], "meaning": "Barack Obama invited several entertainers to the White House for a “youth empowerment” program.\n\nThe various musicians invited by Obama included Rick Ross, Alicia Keys, Busta Rhymes, Ludacris, Chance the Rapper, Nicki Minaj, Wale, DJ Khaled, J. Cole, and Janelle Monae.", "annotation_id": "11521596", "url": "https://genius.com/11521596", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "I told Meek I wouldn’t trust Nicki Instead of beefin’ with your dog, you just give ’em some distance", "vault_lines": ["I told Meek I wouldn't trust Nicki", "Instead of beefin' with your dog, you just give 'em some distance"], "meaning": "Meek Mill referenced this lyric in an Instagram post a week before this song released:\n\n\n\nRoss told Wendy Williams that he has nothing against Nicki. He was giving Meek general advice he would give him for any woman. Now that Meek and Nicki are broken up, it’s easier for Meek to accept that big brother advice.\n\nRoss chose not to interfere with Meek’s relationship. It was best for him to keep his distance and not cause tension.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/bhbGogC1Pns?t=11m26s", "annotation_id": "11521591", "url": "https://genius.com/11521591", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "I’m happy Donald Trump became the president Because we gotta destroy before we elevate", "vault_lines": ["I'm happy Donald Trump became the president", "Because we gotta destroy before we elevate"], "meaning": "Donald J. Trump was a candidate for the 2016 United States Presidential Election. He subsequently won the Republican party’s nomination and sucessfully won the general election on November 9, 2016 in a stunning upset against former Secretary of State Hillary Clinton.\n\nOn the campaign trail Trump has been riddled with controversy. Since entering the oval office this controversy has only gotten worst with the debate over a new healthcare bill to the firing of FBI director James Comey. Trump’s views and actions have many questioning his qualification for a position of power.\n\nRick Ross has been very vocal about his views of Trump. His album Black Market was pulled from Walmart shelves due to a lyric about assassinating Trump on the song “Free Enterprise”:\n\nAssassinate Trump like I’m Zimmerman\n\nNumber 8 in the Supreme Mathematics is Build/Destroy and GZA left a strikingly similar annotation:\n\nIn order to build you must destroy", "annotation_id": "11521569", "url": "https://genius.com/11521569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "US Treasury addressing me, mad at my address Own the biggest residential pool in the US Drake and Kanye can invite every bitch they ever met Finger-fuckin’ bitches in the holy water", "vault_lines": ["US Treasury addressing me, mad at my address", "Own the biggest residential pool in the US", "Drake and Kanye can invite every bitch they ever met", "Finger-fuckin' bitches in the holy water"], "meaning": "Ross knows that as a black man, the white government doesn’t want him winning and that his success angers the higher ups. In 2014, Ross purchased Evander Holyfield’s former mansion for about $5.8 million. It is noteworthy for having the largest residential pool in the country.\n\nRoss name-drops his close friends and collaborators as a direct response to Drake’s line on “Summer Sixteen” addressing his and Kanye’s pool size:\n\nNow I got a bigger pool than Ye\nAnd look man, Ye’s pool is nice, mine’s just bigger’s what I’m saying\n\nDrake and Ye can argue over who has a bigger pool, but the reality is that both have smaller pools than Yung Renzel!", "annotation_id": "11521498", "url": "https://genius.com/11521498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Apple of My Eye", "line": "Dead presidents tattooed on a nigga chest", "vault_lines": ["Dead presidents tattooed on a nigga chest"], "meaning": "Ross isn’t lying – he has George Washington and Abraham Lincoln tatted on his chest.", "annotation_id": "11521497", "url": "https://genius.com/11521497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
