{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Inherit no riches, Jehovah’s my witness", "vault_lines": ["Inherit no riches, Jehovah's my witness"], "meaning": "Using the Lord’s Prayer (Matthew 6:9:13) as one possible perspective context… Old records [testament] will show that there wasn’t anything passed down to him that he was able to build his estate on.", "annotation_id": "13309146", "url": "https://genius.com/13309146", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "See I live by the code that the mafia wrote", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A code he learned from mob themed movies.\n\nAn excerpt from page 63 of the Rolling Stone article on Rozay:\n\nHe flips over to the History Channel, where there’s a documentary on the Godfather movies. “Mario Puzo!” says Ross, a student of the genre. “The greatest.” Later, they cut to the scene where Michael Corleone is talking to a senetor aobut getting a gaming license, and Ross leans in close. “My offer is this: nothing”, He says.\n“My offer is this: nothing,” says Al Pacino on the TV.", "annotation_id": "1343455", "url": "https://genius.com/1343455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "When he ran his mouth, me? I’d rather smoke", "vault_lines": ["When he ran his mouth, me? I'd rather smoke"], "meaning": "Rick Ross on his marijuana use from a Rolling Stone article:\n\n I’m most definitely an avid user, a pothead, however you want to look at it. I call it green caviar. It’s like a short vacation – it helps me chill out. And people really love it when I chill out, because I can really be a dickhead.", "annotation_id": "1341973", "url": "https://genius.com/1341973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Physical fitness,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross could also be referring to “moving weight”, which of course is slanging drugs.", "annotation_id": "1341721", "url": "https://genius.com/1341721", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "I was callin’ them plays, you were still in the bleaches", "vault_lines": ["I was callin' them plays, you were still in the bleaches"], "meaning": "A metaphor of the drug game & a sports game. Ross is like a coach, he calls the plays on how the drugs should be dealt. You are on the outside, and watching the game. People who watch sports game are usually sitting in bleachers.", "annotation_id": "1310323", "url": "https://genius.com/1310323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Wearing Bally’s and gold", "vault_lines": ["Wearing Bally's and gold"], "meaning": "Rozay is rocking Bally Shoes and thick gold chains which we commonly wore by dope boys. The look was popularized by the famous rap group, Run-D.M.C..", "annotation_id": "1310317", "url": "https://genius.com/1310317", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "They wanna know names, they totin’ them thangs", "vault_lines": ["They wanna know names, they totin' them thangs"], "meaning": "“They” is perhaps referring to the Feds – they wanna know the names of the dope dealers, and they carry guns (toting on thangs).\n\nAnd here is the answer to the question posed by the previous line. Rozay carries a weapon because the police do, not because criminals do.\n\nPolice are the real crooks.", "annotation_id": "1310310", "url": "https://genius.com/1310310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Until then, I’ma be a D-boy, I’m ashamed to say Until then, I’ma be a D-boy, I’m ashamed to say", "vault_lines": ["Until then, I'ma be a D-boy, I'm ashamed to say", "I'm ashamed to say"], "meaning": "This song is perhaps the counterpart to one of the standout tracks off Teflon Don, “Tears of Joy”.\n\nWhile Tears of Joy is a celebration of Ross' life, Ashamed is the complete opposite – it’s a condemnation on how he’s made it out of the gutter.", "annotation_id": "1310265", "url": "https://genius.com/1310265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Honey, it’s shameless Shameless, what you’ve done", "vault_lines": ["Shameless, what you've done"], "meaning": "This sampled from “Shameless” by Wilson Pickett. It refers back to the theme of the song – it’s shameless that Ross made money in a sleazy way.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&v=dqyOK673ayI", "annotation_id": "1310262", "url": "https://genius.com/1310262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "It’s the home of the brave", "vault_lines": ["In the coupe with the Tec, it's the home of the brave"], "meaning": "Home of the Brave, a phrase from “The Star Spangled Banner”, refers to the act of carrying a tec with him in his coup. Rozay will defend what he has worked for with his life.\n\nBut is true bravery showing love to the ones that try to destroy you as Ghandi suggests?\n\nA coward is incapable of exhibiting love; it is the prerogative of the brave.", "annotation_id": "1310260", "url": "https://genius.com/1310260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Home economics", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Home Economics is the profession and field of study that deals with the economics and management of the home and community. One major part of home economics is cooking.\n\nIn this case, Ross' home economics is perhaps referring to the cooking of crack cocaine, as this song is a drug anthem.", "annotation_id": "1310251", "url": "https://genius.com/1310251", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "These emotional niggas, and most of them killas", "vault_lines": ["These emotional niggas, and most of them killas"], "meaning": "This line is foreshadows one of the main themes in track 12 off GFID, “Ice Cold”. Despite the outward appearance a killer/dope boy portrays, they too have feelings and are usually emotional despite never showing it to the outside world.", "annotation_id": "1267812", "url": "https://genius.com/1267812", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Not a crack in my voice, this young nigga so poised", "vault_lines": ["Not a crack in my voice, this young nigga so poised"], "meaning": "A person’s voice cracks usually when under pressure, but Ross portrays himself to be a dignified person, despite his internal struggle for feeling ashamed of becoming rich off drugs.", "annotation_id": "1267796", "url": "https://genius.com/1267796", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Cut the noose off my neck, black runaway slave", "vault_lines": ["Cut the noose off my neck, black runaway slave"], "meaning": "Comparing his situation of getting out of the hood, Rick Ross likens his story to that of the runaway slaves once they escaped from their chains to run to freedom. In the same way, Ross ran from the chains of the hood and went on to become successful in the game of hip hop.", "annotation_id": "1253620", "url": "https://genius.com/1253620", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "I needed some change, mama needed a raise She stayed in a rage, hated minimum wage I’m feelin’ the same, all these criminals paid", "vault_lines": ["I needed some change, mama needed a raise", "She stayed in a rage, hated minimum wage", "I'm feelin' the same, all these criminals paid"], "meaning": "In his Rolling Stone story, Ross talked about how his mother Tommie was a hustler just like a him, working numerous jobs. However, she was still barely paid which infuriated her. Ross felt the same way, why work hard and be barely paid, especially when all he saw was criminals getting Rich of Cocaine.", "annotation_id": "1062296", "url": "https://genius.com/1062296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Shinin’ bright, who am I for you to criticize?", "vault_lines": ["Shinin' bright, who am I for you to criticize?"], "meaning": "Ross is one of the most criticized rappers out, but he’s been one of the best rappers since 2010, and was even recently named the Hottest Rapper in the Game.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/252891407583420417", "annotation_id": "1062294", "url": "https://genius.com/1062294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "I mean look at my features, educated my teachers", "vault_lines": ["I mean look at my features, educated my teachers"], "meaning": "Ross starts this line off as though his leadership skills are visible, but ends up alluding to his ability to steal an artist’s thunder on their own song.\n\n\n\nWhen Ross recites this line during this song’s video, the camera cuts to a spread of magazines he’s covered, where he’s provided the magazines with feature stories.\n\n\n\n\n\nThis could also be a reference to his extensive list of guest appearances, in which Complex once detailed.", "annotation_id": "962641", "url": "https://genius.com/962641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Until the day I’m slain, the commission remains", "vault_lines": ["Until the day I'm slain, the commission remains"], "meaning": "A nod here to the shoulda-been supergroup The Commission.  The group, dreamed up by Biggie before his untimely death, was initially supposed to include Big, Charli Baltimore, and Jay-Z. It was extended to include Puff Daddy, Lil' Cease, and producer Lance “Un” Rivera.  Jay would pay tribute in his song “The City is Mine”\n\n You held it down long enough, let me take those reigns\nAnd just like your spirit, The Commission remains", "annotation_id": "958119", "url": "https://genius.com/958119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "line": "Boobie gave me the game, change to give me some sneakers", "vault_lines": ["Boobie gave me the game, change to give me some sneakers"], "meaning": "Kenneth “Boobie” Williams, leader of the infamous Boobie Boys drug gang, was known to be a “friend and mentor” of Rozay.  The real nature of their relationship, both past and present, remains ambiguous, though Ross reps it frequently – see the “Boobie Boys” t-shirt in the photo below:", "annotation_id": "958107", "url": "https://genius.com/958107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashamed", "status": "done", "targets": 19, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-ashamed-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ashamed", "genius_id": 80549, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashes To Ashes", "line": "So ghetto but she turned me onto Jean-Michel", "vault_lines": ["So ghetto but she turned me onto Jean-Michel"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION: So ghetto but she turned me onto Jean-Michel\n\nI think Ross is probably referring to Jean-Michel Basquiat famous neo-expressionist artist in the 70s/80s.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Could also mean Jean Michel Jarre the musician", "annotation_id": "945146", "url": "https://genius.com/945146", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashes To Ashes", "line": "Opa-locka airport talking G6", "vault_lines": ["Opa-locka airport talking G6"], "meaning": "Opa-Locka is a 4.2 Mile radius of hood in Miami. Slightly south of Carol City, which is home of the BO$$ himself (Rick Ross). Opa-Locka is the home of american rapper Brisco.\n\nG6 is slang for the Gulfstream G650, a twin-engine jet airplane\n\n\n\nThe Opa-Locka Airport is primarily used for military vehicles but Ross is so high-profile that he uses it even though he isn’t allowed to.", "annotation_id": "926070", "url": "https://genius.com/926070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ashes To Ashes", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-ashes-to-ashes-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ashes To Ashes", "genius_id": 82094, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "Fuck maintain, boy: I gotta keep ballin", "vault_lines": ["Fuck maintain, boy: I gotta keep ballin"], "meaning": "Instead of keeping a consistent balance of money Rick Ross decided to keep increasing his money.", "annotation_id": "21236602", "url": "https://genius.com/21236602", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "Yeah, you gotta own it if you want it Kisses all on her body, she tells me live in the moment", "vault_lines": ["Kisses all on her body, she tells me live in the moment"], "meaning": "He’s reflecting on the times he had with this girl (specifically Paris) when they were together getting intimate.\n\n\n\nAs he serenaded her body in kisses: Drake questioned whether or not he should go as far as sexual intercourse, and she told him to forget everything else, and to just live in the moment.\n\nParis Morton, who Drake dedicated the title of a song to twice; Part 2 being on Nothing Was The Same in the form of the second half of “Pound Cake/ Paris Morton Music”, actually has a “Live In The Moment” tattoo.", "annotation_id": "13443801", "url": "https://genius.com/13443801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "Listening to the Aston Martin Music, Music", "vault_lines": ["Listening to the Aston Martin Music, Music"], "meaning": "Aston Martin is a British manufacturer of luxury cars, perhaps most famously the DBS that appeared in Casino Royale.\n\nThe idea is that you would listen to this song in your Aston Martin two seater with your girl and just ride out. Similarly to how Maybach Music is about stunting hard with your crew, this one is about that Bonnie and Clyde feel.\n\nIt could also be referring to the beautiful ‘music’ the Aston Martin’s engine produces.", "annotation_id": "264404", "url": "https://genius.com/264404", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "I don’t drink every bottle I own, I be agin’ shit", "vault_lines": ["I don't drink every bottle I own, I be agin' shit"], "meaning": "On 2016’s “You Know You Know,” Drake described his extensive wine collection:\n\nWhy has every woman never dined here before?\nAm I the only 23 year old wine connoisseur?\nThe Rothschild’s, the Krug’s, the Goya’s and the Opus’s\nIt’s always nice when you’re out with someone that notices\n\n\n\nThis also implicates a double meaning; Drake’s saving bottles of alcohol but is also saving songs or verses up to hit you all at once with a great combination.", "annotation_id": "73451", "url": "https://genius.com/73451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "I’m on some Marvin Gaye shit, a bunch of distant lovers", "vault_lines": ["I'm on some Marvin Gaye shit, a bunch of distant lovers"], "meaning": "“Distant Lover” is the 1973 song by R&B legend Marvin Gaye. The song desrcibes a rocky relationship with Marvin and his woman.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U9BSjRCN0cQ\n\nThis may also be a foreshadowing of Drake’s 2011 hit single “Marvin’s Room”, which was named after Marvin Gaye’s Studio.", "annotation_id": "73440", "url": "https://genius.com/73440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "I’m urgin’ all daughters to kiss they mothers With those lips that all that lipstick covers You’re never too grown up to miss and hug her", "vault_lines": ["I'm urgin' all daughters to kiss they mothers", "With those lips that all that lipstick covers", "You're never too grown up to miss and hug her"], "meaning": "Many mothers don’t know how to teach their daughters how to be a lady – but Drake wants them to be gal pals anyways\n\nDrake probably got the idea to include a parenting-related Public Service Announcement from RZA\n\nAfter all, showing respect to mothers is a recurring theme in hip hop, ranging from Rozay’s “Smile, Mama, Smile” and Ye’s “Hey Mama”, to Pac’s iconic “Dear Mama”. With all these figures and role models paying tribute to those that birthed them, Drake believes all women should take part.", "annotation_id": "73439", "url": "https://genius.com/73439", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "I never threw away that paper with my Grammy speech Because I haven’t hit the pinnacles I plan to reach", "vault_lines": ["I never threw away that paper with my Grammy speech", "Because I haven't hit the pinnacles I plan to reach"], "meaning": "Drake was nominated for 2 Grammys in 2010 for “Best I Ever Had” – but lost to Jay-Z’s “D.O.A.” in both categories\n\nBut he kept his victory speech saved! (On Google Docs) – because surely he’ll win some award sooner or later", "annotation_id": "69305", "url": "https://genius.com/69305", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "A lot of quiet time, pink bottles of rose", "vault_lines": ["A lot of quiet time, pink bottles of rose"], "meaning": "Rosé wine, pronounced “rozay” not “rose” as Ross does here, is “a type of wine that has some of the color typical of a red wine, but only enough to turn it pink”\n\n\n\nRoss has fancied calling himself “Rozay” lately after his penchant for the variety", "annotation_id": "45873", "url": "https://genius.com/45873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "VVS’s in the watch", "vault_lines": ["Mr. KFC, VVS's in the watch"], "meaning": "VVS diamonds are “very very slightly included” and have minute inclusions that only a jeweler can see with a microscope at 10x; the highest quality diamonds\n\n\n\nAlternately, Ross could’ve said “DBS is in the watch”, a reference to the exclusive Aston Martin watch that you can use as a remote key to lock / unlock.", "annotation_id": "28377", "url": "https://genius.com/28377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "Pull up on the block in a drop-top chicken box", "vault_lines": ["Pull up on the block in a drop-top chicken box"], "meaning": "A coop is an enclosure or ‘box’ used to contain poultry\n\n“Chickenheads” are girls who like to give head because their heads make an up-and-down motion during the act (like a chicken). See definition #2 here.\n\nSo “chicken box” means his drop-top is used to transport chickenheads, not literal chickens or poultry.", "annotation_id": "28371", "url": "https://genius.com/28371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "line": "When I’m alone in my room, sometime I stare at the wall", "vault_lines": ["When I'm alone in my room, sometime I stare at the wall"], "meaning": "Ricky recycled LL Cool J’s line from his 1987 hit “I Need Love”, which was also recycled by Common in “Sum Shit I Wrote”", "annotation_id": "24376", "url": "https://genius.com/24376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Aston Martin Music", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-aston-martin-music-lyrics", "genius_title": "Aston Martin Music", "genius_id": 765, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Audio Meth", "line": "Got a nigga down the street down to murk somethin’ (Murk somethin’) Couldn’t have nothin’, shit, now he work or somethin’", "vault_lines": ["Got a nigga down the street down to murk somethin' (Murk somethin')", "Couldn't have nothin', shit, now he work or somethin'"], "meaning": "This coincides with the previous line about the “white men sucking black folks dicks,” in that before, Ross' men would have to be out on the streets trying to get theirs by any means. Now, due to the heavy interest in “black music and culture,” more and more men are having the opportunity to flourish in the job market.", "annotation_id": "1813520", "url": "https://genius.com/1813520", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Audio Meth", "line": "Paint artist, lace you with scars, and tarnish everythin’ on you", "vault_lines": ["Paint artist, lace you with scars, and tarnish everythin' on you"], "meaning": "An expert painter can blend colors perfectly and place certain characteristics in the right place, Raekwon does the opposite. He uses his preciseness to place scars in the right spot on a person and mess up their entire physique.", "annotation_id": "1761808", "url": "https://genius.com/1761808", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
