{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BCGMMG (Remix)", "line": "Started off with that .oz and tried to flip that bitch to a whole ki’", "vault_lines": ["Started off with that .oz and tried to flip that bitch to a whole ki'"], "meaning": "Meek started out with a small amount of dope (an ounce) and successfully hustled until he was able to make enough to buy and distribute a kilogram (35 ounces).", "annotation_id": "701207", "url": "https://genius.com/701207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BCGMMG (Remix)", "line": "Someone pass me the Mont Blanc, I got somethin’ to say boy", "vault_lines": ["Someone pass me the Mont Blanc, I got somethin' to say boy"], "meaning": "Mont Blanc“ is a company that makes expensive pens.\n\nStalley compares the quality of his rhymes to that of his writing implement. The idea behind Like Mike shares a similar sentiment, in that the shoes make the player.\n\n\n\nYou tough now Lil Bow Wow huh?", "annotation_id": "701031", "url": "https://genius.com/701031", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BCGMMG (Remix)", "line": "BCGMMG, yea that be my only crew BCGMMG, yea that be my only crew BCGMMG, yea that be my only crew BCGMMG, yea that be my only crew", "vault_lines": ["BCGMMG, yea that be my only crew"], "meaning": "BCGMMG stands for Blue Collar Gang and Maybach Music Group. They are Stalley’s crew and he will only be loyal to them.\n\n\n\n\n\nIs it possible to have “only” (meaning singular) of 2 things? The mysteries of the universe.\n#ohio elevate", "annotation_id": "674207", "url": "https://genius.com/674207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BCGMMG (Remix)", "line": "Drag racin’, left the game behind me I’m zoomin’ on these niggas and I don’t see nobody", "vault_lines": ["I'm zoomin' on these niggas and I don't see nobody"], "meaning": "“I don’t see nobody” is a reference to a Fabolous' song by the same name Stalley follows with a reference to “There’s No Competition”, a Fabolous mixtape series.\n\nStalley also references Aretha Franklin’s 1985 single and album “Who’s Zoomin' Who”. To “zoom” on someone is to examine them, but Stalley’s car is moving too quickly to make note of the people he passes.", "annotation_id": "674202", "url": "https://genius.com/674202", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
