{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIG TYME", "line": "I just got a crib in Chile to chill a few summers (God damn) Or catch me out in Haiti, still running up numbers (God damn) If I look into your eyes then I made you a promise", "vault_lines": ["I just got a crib in Chile to chill a few summers (God damn)", "Or catch me out in Haiti, still running up numbers (God damn)", "If I look into your eyes then I made you a promise"], "meaning": "Ross has so many houses away from the united states which includes some in South America. The boss would get a holiday and chill in those houses but the business never ceases.", "annotation_id": "19801883", "url": "https://genius.com/19801883", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIG TYME", "line": "Be stackin’ them tickets, I’m tryna sit with Hov’ (Oh) I be stackin’ my tickets, I’m tryna sit with Hov’ (A billi’)", "vault_lines": ["I be stackin' my tickets, I'm tryna sit with Hov' (A billi')"], "meaning": "He’s trying to make a Billion Dollars Just like Jay z", "annotation_id": "17810118", "url": "https://genius.com/17810118", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIG TYME", "line": "I pray somebody tell you ’bout these bumpy roads (Woo) Only maps to follow is your bible quotes (Yes)", "vault_lines": ["I pray somebody tell you 'bout these bumpy roads (Woo)", "Only maps to follow is your bible quotes (Yes)"], "meaning": "There’s something spectacular about these lines and it speaks on different levels. First, it highlights the road to success and how it usually filled with bumpy roads. But the bumpy roads are usually characterised by rejections, set-backs and so many unfathomable events. Ross here tries to reminds his listeners that the success he portrays on daily comes with a lot of story hence why he pronounces that “I pray somebody tell…” Ross statement aligns in the same vein as Matshona Dhliwayo’s statement when he says  “The road to success is paved with doubters and haters.”  Second, is simple as it sounds.  argues that the only maps to follow to success are in bible quotes. However, some might frown at this statement as some listeners  are non-Christians or atheists. But, some bible quotes comes to mind and one can find them here:  Philippians 4:13 “I can do everything through him who gives me strength.” Proverbs 16:3 “Commit to the Lord whatever you do, and your plans will succeed.”", "annotation_id": "17708939", "url": "https://genius.com/17708939", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIG TYME", "line": "Miami Heat, I rep like my name was Udonis (Damn)", "vault_lines": ["Miami Heat, I rep like my name was Udonis (Damn)"], "meaning": "Rozay’s loyalty to Miami is akin to that of Miami Heat player, and personal friend, Udonis Haslem- who has played his entire career for the Heat", "annotation_id": "17512939", "url": "https://genius.com/17512939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIG TYME", "line": "Surviving R. Kelly, registered pedophiles", "vault_lines": ["Surviving R. Kelly, registered pedophiles"], "meaning": "Rick Ross appears to be commenting on the current climate of artists being pedophiles and sex offenders. (Tekashi 6IX9INE, R. Kelly etc.)", "annotation_id": "17508816", "url": "https://genius.com/17508816", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIG TYME", "line": "Penal systems come to the Source, Benzino of C-notes", "vault_lines": ["Penal systems come to the Source, Benzino of C-notes"], "meaning": "Benzino was a co-owner of The Source magazine. Rick Ross is using wordplay to say he’s “The Source” of money making (c-notes).", "annotation_id": "17508808", "url": "https://genius.com/17508808", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIG TYME", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-big-tyme-lyrics", "genius_title": "BIG TYME", "genius_id": 4671351, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "Butterfly doors keep the birds chirpin’ (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["Butterfly doors keep the birds chirpin' (Oh)"], "meaning": "Butterfly doors is mainly on expensive sports cars, there is no purpose for butterfly doors besides them being flashy.\n\n\n\nThe birds could be the general public talking about Denzel when he pulls up in a new car with butterfly doors.\n\nChirping is a smart wordplay with bird because birds chirp, which is used as a metaphor instead of saying “Butterfly doors keep the people talking”\n\nBird is also a british slang for “girl”, which could also be a reference to all the girls talking about Denzel.", "annotation_id": "20619486", "url": "https://genius.com/20619486", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "We was able to sell it, now my city serve ’caine", "vault_lines": ["We was able to sell it, now my city serve 'caine"], "meaning": "“My city” is Denzel Curry repping Carol City, which is in Miami Florida.\n\nMiami is known for Cocaine or as short ‘Caine especially because of the drug trafficking from the Northern areas of South America, and Middle America to Miami.\n\nDenzel Curry is saying that Miami is hugely influensed by Cocaine. Especially young black folks selling cocaine as a way of getting by and earning money.\n\nIt might also be a reference to Cain and Abel", "annotation_id": "20619464", "url": "https://genius.com/20619464", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "I got lil’ homie with me, city on our backs (Denzel)", "vault_lines": ["I got lil' homie with me, city on our backs (Denzel)"], "meaning": "When asked about this line by Rob Markman in a 2019 Genius interview, Denzel expressed admiration and respect for Rick Ross. He explained his belief that the two are likely the most well-known artists to hail from Carol City, Florida:\n\nWe represent Carol City… we putting on for Carol City. We’re probably the most well known out of the city.", "annotation_id": "17753455", "url": "https://genius.com/17753455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "FnZ Well damn", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This robotic noise, followed by Denzel’s voice, is the producer tag for FnZ (Finatik N Zac), an Australian production duo most known for his collaborative work with A$AP Rocky.\n\nUsed for the first time on ZUU and first heard on “RICKY,” this sound can be heard frequently throughout ZUU, for example pitched up on “WISH.”\n\nThe duo are frequent collaborators of Denzel Curry, and for example handles the production of Curry’s famous 2016 song “ULT”. FnZ contributed to seven tracks on Imperial, produced nine on TA1300, and produced 8 songs out the 12 tracks of ZUU.\n\nDenzel sowed appreciation for the australian duo in a 2018 tweet:\nhttps://twitter.com/denzelcurry/status/1067643987454918656\n\nAs HighSnobiety points out, Finatik N Zac first connected with Curry back in 2015 during an auspicious first recording session that yielded the creation of Curry’s classic “Knotty Head.”\n\nA few times after the release of ZUU, Fanatik discussed the creative process that led to the recording of the album and compared it to the recording of the highly conceptual TA1300:\n\nThe process for ZUU was the complete opposite to the process of TA1300. They’re two polar opposites. On TA1300, we took a really meticulous approach. ZUU was going straight off feel. There was not a lot of overthinking at all.\n\nDenzel also hinted at forthcoming collaborations between the three artists, and expressed their common willingness to explore new grounds:\n\nThey’re willing to take it to any avenue, and I’m willing to take it to any avenue.", "annotation_id": "17605670", "url": "https://genius.com/17605670", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "Everybody thinking that they know me for real ’Cause they only seen me on a poster for real", "vault_lines": ["Everybody thinking that they know me for real"], "meaning": "A parasocial relationship refers to psychological relationship experienced by an audience member in relation to their encounters with a well-known figure in the media.\n\nAkin to a real relationship, upon acquiring information about the life of, or consuming media featuring the well-known person, the “audience member” develops a sense of closeness to the well-known person which is based on a incomplete or false picture (a persona) of what that person is really like.\n\nDenzel here implies that people can’t really know him just by consuming his media (seeing him on a poster) and that he is much more than just his artist persona. A sentiment also expressed in his song SWITCH IT UP.", "annotation_id": "17340530", "url": "https://genius.com/17340530", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "Eye of Jehovah Come take a look at my city and its culture City full of vultures, city full of Zoes City full of gangsters that’s stickin’ to the code", "vault_lines": ["Come take a look at my city and its culture", "City full of vultures, city full of Zoes", "City full of gangsters that's stickin' to the code"], "meaning": "The Eye of Jehovah is all seeing and understanding. These next few lines can be interpreted in two ways:\n\n\n\nFirstly, that Denzel claims to have the Eye of Jehovah as he sees and understands everything in his city. He then asks the listener to see his city for what it truly is.\n\nOr secondly, that he is asking the Eye of Jehovah to see his city for what it truly is and help him. Denzel mentioned that his mother was a Jehovah’s Witness on his Genius interview explaining his song “RICKY”.\n\nThe Zoes referred to here by Denzel are members of Zoe Pound, one of the biggest, if not the biggest, street gangs in Florida.", "annotation_id": "17290719", "url": "https://genius.com/17290719", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "Fuck a Pop-Tart, we carry toasters for real", "vault_lines": ["Fuck a Pop-Tart, we carry toasters for real"], "meaning": "Pop-Tarts are toaster pastries which are manufactured by the Kellogg’s Company. While Pop-Tarts can be eaten without being toasted, they are more commonly toasted in a toaster. Denzel isn’t toasting Pop-Tarts but is carrying toasters which is slang for a gun.", "annotation_id": "17289411", "url": "https://genius.com/17289411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "My pastor making dollars like he Erick Sermon", "vault_lines": ["My pastor making dollars like he Erick Sermon"], "meaning": "A sermon is the oratory or lecture a pastor preaches on church day.\n\nOn the other hand, legendary producer and rapper Erick Sermon is one half of EPMD, the iconic hip-hop duo formed along Parrish Smith, also known as PMD, which stands for “Parrish Mic Doc.”\n\nEPMD is a concatenation of both of their names, “E” and “PMD,” which is an acronym for “Erick and Parrish Making Dollars.”", "annotation_id": "17288144", "url": "https://genius.com/17288144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "Long live my nigga Nipsey, light another candle", "vault_lines": ["Long live my nigga Nipsey, light another candle"], "meaning": "Nipsey Hussle was a respected West Coast MC who unfortunately was shot and killed on March 31, 2019. Rick and Nipsey have collaborated on multiple tracks, including “Fountain of Youth” and “Mark My Words”.\n\nIn honor of the late Crenshaw legend, Rick Ross got a tattoo of Nipsey’s face on the back of his leg.", "annotation_id": "17286281", "url": "https://genius.com/17286281", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "line": "Big top back like I’m in the circus (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Big top back like I'm in the circus (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A “big top,” is the tent that is commonly seen at circuses.\n\n\n\nCurry’s previous record, TA13OO, had many themes revolving around him being a circus act. In all three music videos from the album, Curry is dressed as a clown in a circus after signing a deal with an agency. After signing, Curry is essentially the deal owner’s slave, until he revolts in the final act of the album. The album’s cover even features Curry with the same makeup and outfit on.", "annotation_id": "17283900", "url": "https://genius.com/17283900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BIRDZ", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Denzel-curry-birdz-lyrics", "genius_title": "BIRDZ", "genius_id": 4572531, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Damn right, a nigga black but he sellin’ white", "vault_lines": ["Damn right, a nigga black but he sellin' white"], "meaning": "Black men are prospering selling white, which is somewhat ironic, since black people suffered a significant amount of injustice from the white race and they even still shoot them down til this day for no reason (i.e. Mike Brown), and through all this they are still being successful and making money like many black people out there.\n\nWhich gives this line potential to be a play on the words black and white.", "annotation_id": "4041611", "url": "https://genius.com/4041611", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Hangin’ out the window screaming “F the police”", "vault_lines": ["Hangin' out the window screaming \"F the police\""], "meaning": "Classic real nigga move #2.\n\nIt is known that for you to join the Real Nigga Squad ye needs to scream out the window of ye’s car: Fuck the police!. It is known.", "annotation_id": "4041607", "url": "https://genius.com/4041607", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
