{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Ridin’ Cutlass Classics", "vault_lines": [", ridin' Cutlass Classics"], "meaning": "The Oldsmobile Cutlass is a line of automobiles made by the Oldsmobile division of General Motors. It’s popularity in the 70’s and 90’s made it a cool and cheap car to own in the 90’s (you would know if you ever played GTA San Andreas).", "annotation_id": "4041447", "url": "https://genius.com/4041447", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "The coupe roofless, the nine is near", "vault_lines": [", the coupe roofless, the nine is near"], "meaning": "He’s riding through the hood in a convertible foreign sports car, you think he finna get jumped or what?\n\n\n\nThat’s why he keeps a 9mm handgun nearby, probably under the seat or in the glove compartment.", "annotation_id": "4041400", "url": "https://genius.com/4041400", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "The streets ruthless", "vault_lines": ["The streets we mastered, in BAs and AKs"], "meaning": "The street is unforgiving. This is because of constant violence among gangs. You have to cautious at all times because you never know if it’s your day to meet your maker.", "annotation_id": "4030506", "url": "https://genius.com/4030506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Smoked a ounce for my dog on the day he died Sprayed yo’ name on the walls in the project hall", "vault_lines": ["Smoked a ounce for my dog on the day he died", "Sprayed yo' name on the walls in the project hall"], "meaning": "Ross pays his respect to his homie that passed away by rolling a fat blunt and smoking it. Also, when someone from the projects gets killed or dies, their friends and family usually spray paint their name in the staircase and hallway of the projects.\n\nIt is usually to keep their name alive even though they aren’t with you anymore.", "annotation_id": "4015706", "url": "https://genius.com/4015706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Tear gas all through the night Niggas thuggin’ out in Ferguson so get it right", "vault_lines": ["Niggas thuggin' out in Ferguson so get it right"], "meaning": "After the shooting of Michael Brown, riots broke out in Ferguson. It got so bad they eventually had to bring out the National Guard. Tear gas was thrown, people were beaten, arrested, and even shot.", "annotation_id": "4015698", "url": "https://genius.com/4015698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Coming from nothin’, I had to hustle up somethin’ I had to get me some paper,", "vault_lines": ["Coming from nothin', I had to hustle up somethin'", "I had to get me some paper,"], "meaning": "Before his record deal, Gunplay was dirt poor and had no money so the only way for him to make some quick cash was too sell drugs and hustle.", "annotation_id": "4015678", "url": "https://genius.com/4015678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "The situation wack, we need a moment of silence", "vault_lines": ["The situation wack, we need a moment of silence"], "meaning": "The tragic deaths of both Trayvon Martin and Michael Brown were very horrific and death should not have been the result.", "annotation_id": "4015665", "url": "https://genius.com/4015665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Wanna gun me to the ground like Michael Brown", "vault_lines": ["Wanna gun me to the ground like Michael Brown"], "meaning": "Michael Brown was a teenager from Ferguson, Missouri who was tragically gunned down by a Ferguson police officer on August 9th, 2014.\n\n\n\nIn this case Rick has enemies that envy him and want to shoot and kill him just like the cop did to Michael.", "annotation_id": "4015649", "url": "https://genius.com/4015649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "BLK & WHT (Remix)", "line": "Word to Trayvon and Mike Brown Them pigs’ll gun you down and call it standin’ they ground", "vault_lines": ["Word to Trayvon and Mike Brown", "Them pigs'll gun you down and call it standin' they ground"], "meaning": "Stalley references two black men who have lost their lives unjustly in the last few years. Trayvon Martin was killed by George Zimmerman, even though he was an unarmed teenager. Mike Brown was also unarmed, and was shot and killed by a police officer.\n\nPigs is usually a slang term for police, but Stalley also just means that the killers were terrible people.\n\nGeorge Zimmerman infamously was acquitted of murder under the Stand-Your-Ground law in Florida, which made it legal to kill Martin.\n\nObviously, Stalley doesn’t think he was actually standing his ground, but instead was actively trying to start something.", "annotation_id": "4014015", "url": "https://genius.com/4014015", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
