{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Now we got so many cars, we just leave ’em on the grass", "vault_lines": ["Now we got so many cars, we just leave 'em on the grass"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is not one to have few cars and this leads to little parking space on his big piece of land thus the following is evidence to what he’s talking about.", "annotation_id": "7878484", "url": "https://genius.com/7878484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "My uncle wanna know if I’m still fucking with dope Lyrics say we livin’ like the movie Blow", "vault_lines": ["My uncle wanna know if I'm still fucking with dope", "Lyrics say we livin' like the movie Blow"], "meaning": "Rozay’s uncle wants confirmation as to whether indeed he is still pushing to the level since his lyrics state that he and his crew is living life quite like the drug dealing themed movie of blow", "annotation_id": "7878448", "url": "https://genius.com/7878448", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Niggas sentenced to death by a sentence in the text", "vault_lines": ["Niggas sentenced to death by a sentence in the text"], "meaning": "Rick Ross simply makes reference to the popular way in which rappers state of how they finish off people, one simple phone call. However Rick Ross is takes it to a point where niggas get cleared off the map with a single sentence on the phone. A text.\n\nThe Double entendre here is seen with the play to the word “sentence which in one means death sentence and another meaning a text sentence.", "annotation_id": "7878371", "url": "https://genius.com/7878371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Like my partner Lil Reese Trigger man beat the case we’ll deal with that in the streets", "vault_lines": [", like my partner Lil Reese", "Trigger man beat the case we'll deal with that in the streets"], "meaning": "In an interesting case of street wars in which some beefs end Rick Ross references to Lil Reese’s case versus Lil Marc which Lil Marc ended up dead after dissing Lil Reese and a couple of dead gang members.\nFor more on the story visit here", "annotation_id": "7878369", "url": "https://genius.com/7878369", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Smoke one for the deceased", "vault_lines": ["Smoke one for the deceased"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is known to smoke weed in memory of the dead from Michael Jackson to other various people showing respect for them.\n\n ‘The only time in my life I smoked angel dust was by accident and it was on a double date with Andy Warhol and Michael Jackson,’ laughs Mothersbaugh. ‘We all went to Studio 54 and people were passing drugs all over the place.\n“Michael Jackson had just finished doing the movie The Wiz and still looked like Michael Jackson back then – he had an Afro and he was still black. He passed me a joint and I thought, well OK, we don’t have marijuana in Ohio so I’ll try it.’\n\nMinutes later Mothersbaugh found himself on the dancefloor as pillars of light were swirling around ‘like weedcutters’ knocking people over and cutting them up. He turned to his date in horror, only to hear her say: ‘You didn’t smoke any of that angel dust did you?’", "annotation_id": "7878361", "url": "https://genius.com/7878361", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Bitches been known to relapse", "vault_lines": ["Bitches been known to relapse"], "meaning": "A relapse refers to a deterioration in someone’s state of health after a temporary improvement.In this case Rick Ross hasn’t finished his drug references by stating that his drugs are so good he will have ladies back to him after being clean for a while.\n\nIn this line lies a Double entendre in which he states women may be clean after saying they will never mess around with men from previous wrecked relationships until they meet the biggest boss they ever seen thus far.", "annotation_id": "7878331", "url": "https://genius.com/7878331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Come and see me for a hit and I shoot it right in your arm", "vault_lines": ["Come and see me for a hit and I shoot it right in your arm"], "meaning": "Rick Ross speaks of drugs and thus being the plug he definitely has what you need.\n\nIn this case however he has what you need in two ways. Whether you want to kill him or get a drug fix of heroine which is most commonly shot in the arm.He will give you each of these in the arm. With a bullet or a needle.", "annotation_id": "7878317", "url": "https://genius.com/7878317", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Balling without a bond, Def Jam’s only Lebron", "vault_lines": ["Balling without a bond, Def Jam's only Lebron"], "meaning": "Rick Ross speaks of his extravagant lifestyle which he can definitely afford while cleverly joining his recent kidnapping and assault stint to state he is definitely the rooster’s biggest playing star. This is similar to Lebron who in 2015 has been known to have outstanding performance as well as years before.\n\n\n\nWhile this bears some truth to it, you cannot claim Rozay to be the only powerful star lyrically in this rooster", "annotation_id": "7878249", "url": "https://genius.com/7878249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "Bitches applaud the hustle , the recipe of a Russel", "vault_lines": ["Bitches applaud the hustle , the recipe of a Russel"], "meaning": "Women definitely love a man who can hustle and this shows in the attraction they have towards rich men.\n\n\n\nThis thus is the recipe for the likes of successful rich men like Russel Simmons, who along with Rick Rubin are the founders and chairmen of one of HipHop’s biggest and historical stables, Def Jam which Rick Ross is signed to", "annotation_id": "7878218", "url": "https://genius.com/7878218", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "I was blessed with a wonderful sister Never vulnerable cause she know how these niggas’ll kick it", "vault_lines": ["Never vulnerable cause she know how these niggas'll kick it"], "meaning": "He is referring to Tawanda Roberts, his sister and assistant for the past few years. She has played a major role in setting up several business ventures like his Wingstop food chain, DGK clothing, Mcigs….\n\nShowing that she is smart and business saavy, he understands that she isn’t a “valunerable” woman, because she knows how men act.", "annotation_id": "7856195", "url": "https://genius.com/7856195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Babies Cry", "line": "So when I see these niggas cry, tell ’em wipe your eyes So many shots through the night, you know a nigga died First you hear the screams, then your hear the sirens Then the helicopter, a life lost to violence A life lost to violence", "vault_lines": ["So when I see these niggas cry, tell 'em wipe your eyes", "So many shots through the night, you know a nigga died", "First you hear the screams, then your hear the sirens", "Then the helicopter, a life lost to violence", "A life lost to violence"], "meaning": "Painting a vivid picture of what takes place too often in the hood, line by line. He sees someone crying, and tells them to wipe their eyes as a way of expressing sympathy, then explains what took place during the night, screams, sirens, helicopters, and a confirmed death.", "annotation_id": "7856177", "url": "https://genius.com/7856177", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
