{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "The streets introduced me to money, nice to meet ya (What’s up?)", "vault_lines": ["The streets introduced me to money, nice to meet ya (What's up?)"], "meaning": "When Jeezy met the streets, he met the money that came along with it. The streets introduced him to money b.c in the street he started to drug deal\n\n\n\nAlso in the street the dealers has a dream to become a rapper.", "annotation_id": "3914892", "url": "https://genius.com/3914892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Bricks, they was beautiful, yeah, Mona Lisa", "vault_lines": ["Bricks, they was beautiful, yeah, Mona Lisa"], "meaning": "Jeezy ain’t talking about the clay bricks you build houses with; he’s referring to the snow bricks you build empires with! Cocaine bricks\n\n\n\nMona Lisa is the famous portrait of an Italian woman by artist Leonardo da Vinci; Jeezy is implying that his bricks are as beautiful as the Mona Lisa", "annotation_id": "3914882", "url": "https://genius.com/3914882", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Yokohamas, no Vogues, man, that bitch beautiful", "vault_lines": ["Yokohamas, no Vogues, man, that bitch beautiful"], "meaning": "“Parked outside and it’s sittin' on Vogues”\n\nA well known line from Jeezy, he takes us back to the past with this bar. Only this time around his whip is sporting Yokohama tires.\n\nEither way, that Lambo is sitting pretty.\n\nBelow, Jeezy can be seen riding in the green Lambo from his “I Luv It” music video.", "annotation_id": "3914323", "url": "https://genius.com/3914323", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Execute a nigga, Abe Lincoln", "vault_lines": ["Execute a nigga, Abe Lincoln"], "meaning": "A reference to the assassination of Abraham Lincoln in 1865. The assassination occurred five days after the commander of the Confederate Army of Northern Virginia surrendered to Lieutenant General Ulysses S. Grant and the Union Army of the Potomac.", "annotation_id": "3914201", "url": "https://genius.com/3914201", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Pull up at the The Mirage", "vault_lines": ["Pull up at the The Mirage"], "meaning": "The Mirage is a hotel and casino resort located on the Las Vegas Strip in Nevada. Built by Steve Wynn, the resort is currently owned and operated by MGM Resorts International. The marquee sign in front of the resort is the largest free standing marquee in the world.", "annotation_id": "3914060", "url": "https://genius.com/3914060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "I ain’t talkin’ Sprite when I say I need soda", "vault_lines": ["I ain't talkin' Sprite when I say I need soda"], "meaning": "When most people talk about soda they mean soda pop, but not in Jeezy’s world; he be talking about baking soda.\n\n\n\nTo make crack, powder cocaine is dissolved in a mixture of water and either ammonia or sodium bicarbonate (baking soda)", "annotation_id": "3913304", "url": "https://genius.com/3913304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Came a long way from a nigga first advancement Test drive the new Bugatti, hold that bitch for ransom (That’s right)", "vault_lines": ["Came a long way from a nigga first advancement", "Test drive the new Bugatti, hold that bitch for ransom (That's right)"], "meaning": "An advancement is a payment artists receive prior to being paid for their product. Game’s first advancement was most likely before his first album 10 years ago (2004). As another reminder of Game’s present day wealth, he lets us know that he recently test drove a Bugatti which is a hyper-car with a starting price over one million dollars.", "annotation_id": "3913223", "url": "https://genius.com/3913223", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Murci’ in my garage, course it is supercharged", "vault_lines": ["Murci' in my garage, course it is supercharged"], "meaning": "“Murci” is short for Murciélago, a sports car produced by Lamborghini. The term became famous after the hit single “Mercy” by Kanye West.\n\nSpeed enthusiasts usually fit or design an internal combustion engine with a “supercharger” on their cars to add horsepower.", "annotation_id": "3912758", "url": "https://genius.com/3912758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Front yard like a soccer field, and we kickin’ it", "vault_lines": ["Front yard like a soccer field, and we kickin' it"], "meaning": "Soccer field is the playing surface for the game of soccer made of turf. Its dimensions and markings are defined by Law 1 of the Laws of the Game, “The Field of Play”.\nMinimum length: 100 yards (90 meters)\nMinimum width: 50 yards (45 meters)\n\nGame describes his front yard as one of these fields, and how rich he is to afford a large yard, where he just Just lay back and chill.", "annotation_id": "3912526", "url": "https://genius.com/3912526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "I got a bad bitch from Vogue,", "vault_lines": ["I got a bad bitch from Vogue,"], "meaning": "Vogue is a globally recognized fashion and lifestyle magazine that is published monthly in 23 different national and regional editions by Condé Nast. He states that his partner is a model or celebrity who has appeared on the cover of the magazine.", "annotation_id": "3912107", "url": "https://genius.com/3912107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "R.I.P. to Camoflauge Just drove through Savannah, Georgia", "vault_lines": [", R.I.P. to Camoflauge", "Just drove through Savannah, Georgia"], "meaning": "Camoflauge was a rapper from Savannah, Georgia who was shot & killed on May 19, 2003 while walking with his baby daughter.", "annotation_id": "3912098", "url": "https://genius.com/3912098", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Jeezy like Versace so we rented out the mansion", "vault_lines": ["Jeezy like Versace so we rented out the mansion"], "meaning": "Jeezy likes Versace so much that he and Game rented out the entire Versace Mansion.\n\nThe Versace Mansion is located in Miami, FL, and Suites start at $795 per night with the Villa Suite going from $2,200 per night – Jeezy and Game are gonna have a big tab.", "annotation_id": "3911654", "url": "https://genius.com/3911654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Mirror, mirror in my garage Tell me which Lambo’ I should park at the L’Ermitage", "vault_lines": ["Mirror, mirror in my garage", "Tell me which Lambo' I should park at the L'Ermitage"], "meaning": "The Game does a little bit of bragging with these first couple lines. His net worth is approximately between $20-$25 million dollars, so I think it’s fair to say he has earned some bragging rights!\n\nIn his fancy lifestyle, it’s always a tough decision when it comes to choosing which of his many Lamborghini’s to take out for a drive. The Game looks strait ahead into his mirror panel-lined garage and asks himself which one he should take, kind of a pompous way of reminding himself how hard he’s worked and how much he deserves his fortune.\n\n\n\nAs if that not being enough, he has to add how he will be parking his Lamborghini at the nicest hotel/spa in all of Beverly Hills, where even staying one night alone will cost you over $500.", "annotation_id": "3910823", "url": "https://genius.com/3910823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "Bottle of Avion", "vault_lines": [", bottle of Avion"], "meaning": "Aside from Jeezy’s love for Avion tequila, which he has shown through multiple shotouts, he is also a Multicultural Advisor to the founder and chairman of Avion – Ken Austin.\n\nJeezy has mentioned Avion on his songs “4 What,” “Me OK,” and “Damn Liar” – to name a few.", "annotation_id": "3910767", "url": "https://genius.com/3910767", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Beautiful", "line": "My Chevrolet a seven trey", "vault_lines": ["My Chevrolet a seven trey"], "meaning": "A seven trey Chevrolet is a 1973 chevy impala. A car that is commoly used as a lowrider. Ross is in a seven trey Chevrolet, which isn’t surprising because everyone already knows how much he loves his Box Chevy.", "annotation_id": "3910727", "url": "https://genius.com/3910727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
