{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Been That", "line": "Put my dogs on salary, you see we all be blowing loud", "vault_lines": ["Put my dogs on salary, you see we all be blowing loud"], "meaning": "Ross was not always a boss. MMG was founded in 2009, and Ross promptly began signing up cohorts like Meek Mill.\n\n\n\n“Loud” is a type of high quality marijuana.", "annotation_id": "7193582", "url": "https://genius.com/7193582", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Been That", "line": "Have these niggas playing on me, devils wish it was a hearse", "vault_lines": ["Have these niggas playing on me, devils wish it was a hearse"], "meaning": "A deeper line than it first appears. The centrepiece to Ross' 2014 album Mastermind, was a track entitled “The Devil Is A Lie,” an incredible collaboration with JAY-Z.\n\nThe devil does not actually exist, so Ross' enemies are non-existent. No-one is wishing death upon him.", "annotation_id": "7193509", "url": "https://genius.com/7193509", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Been That", "line": "No shirt, baking soda standing at the sink Swerving in my Wraith, I should just pull up at the church", "vault_lines": ["No shirt, baking soda standing at the sink", "Swerving in my Wraith, I should just pull up at the church"], "meaning": "Two of Ross' favourite subjects: selling drugs and purchasing the Rolls Royce Wraith, which he has placed in more verses than you could imagine.\n\nBaking Soda is used to cut cocaine, and also used primarily in the manufacture of crack cocaine, something the “real Rick Ross” was well versed in.", "annotation_id": "7193505", "url": "https://genius.com/7193505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Been That", "line": "I got bitches out in Paris that be texting “Ooh la la”", "vault_lines": ["I got bitches out in Paris that be texting \"Ooh la la\""], "meaning": "A reference to the Grace Potter and the Nocturnals song “Paris (Ooh La La)”, which is about a woman desiring sex in a very decadent way.\n\nMeek got women around him.", "annotation_id": "7193478", "url": "https://genius.com/7193478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Been That", "line": "I used to mop the floors now who the motherfucking boss?", "vault_lines": ["I used to mop the floors now who the motherfucking boss?"], "meaning": "As Dr. Dre began on the collaboration “3 Kings”, Ross repeats here, describing a typical rags to riches tail. It also completes the link with his earlier line as Jay Z was featured on both of the records referenced.\n\nIt’s also a direct response to his correctional officer days, as it is the prisoners, not the employees, who mop floors behind bars.", "annotation_id": "7192718", "url": "https://genius.com/7192718", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
