{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bel Air", "line": "At the Kings game but I got the heat with me", "vault_lines": ["At the Kings game but I got the heat with me"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to the Los Angeles Kings ice hockey team (and not the Sacramento Kings basketball team) since he is rapping about Bel Air, Los Angeles.\n\nHe is saying that he is at Kings game but he has the Miami Heat basketball team with him all the time. He has given shout outs of the Heat as it is his hometown that he has represented from day one.\n\n\n\nSeriously though, props to him for staying loyal and tattooing the team’s logo on his face even after LeBron went back to Cleveland last season.", "annotation_id": "7750306", "url": "https://genius.com/7750306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bel Air", "line": "Shout out to young Hov, my first deal The transaction, my first meal Island Def Jam, paradise", "vault_lines": ["The transaction, my first meal", "Island Def Jam, paradise"], "meaning": "Young Hov (Jay-Z) gave Rozay his first record deal with Def Jam, after Ross debuted his first single, Hustlin'. Rick Ross sees Jay-Z as his role model and without him, his hip hop career wouldn’t have been as affluent and successful.\n\n\n\nThis isn’t the first time Rozay mentions Young Hov in Black Dollar. In Icon, he talks of Jay-Z being his icon.", "annotation_id": "7745170", "url": "https://genius.com/7745170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bel Air", "line": "Elevators in the crib on the intercom", "vault_lines": ["Elevators in the crib on the intercom"], "meaning": "Rozay talking about his prosperous life, having a house which he invested his wealth into which features elevators and an intercom, alluding to the fact that he has multiple floors in the mansion.", "annotation_id": "7745151", "url": "https://genius.com/7745151", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bel Air", "line": "Tripping if you think I’m slipping, lil nigga, please", "vault_lines": ["Tripping if you think I'm slipping, lil nigga, please"], "meaning": "He’s not slipping up and screwing up his life, he’s doing his thing making money. If you think otherwise, you’re wrong, Rozay is living the life.", "annotation_id": "7744461", "url": "https://genius.com/7744461", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bel Air", "line": "Tank tops, young niggas living fabulous Cali hills, Cali weed Nipsey give a nigga tree by the OZ", "vault_lines": ["Cali hills, Cali weed", "Nipsey give a nigga tree by the OZ"], "meaning": "He lives a lavish lifestyle in Cali  is cool with Nipsey Hu$$le, who gives him weed to smoke, Cali’s finest.\n\nNipsey Hussle is a Cali rapper who is good friends with Ricky. They have featured on songs together.", "annotation_id": "7744454", "url": "https://genius.com/7744454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
