{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I stand tall, no Eiffel", "vault_lines": ["I stand tall, no Eiffel"], "meaning": "Meek is a tall guy, as evidenced by being taller than his boss Rozay, who is 6'2. But obviously Meek’s not as tall as the Eiffel Tower, which is over 1000 ft.\n\n\n\nThe phrase “no Eiffel” is used as a double entendre – “no I fall” – he has experienced both success and failure, but his crew sticks with him.", "annotation_id": "1236870", "url": "https://genius.com/1236870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I said I be on my way, break a brick down in all zones", "vault_lines": ["I said I be on my way, break a brick down in all zones"], "meaning": "A zone is one ounce. So, a kilo broke down into “all zones” is approximately 35 separate ounces.", "annotation_id": "1236869", "url": "https://genius.com/1236869", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "And I got pills, and I got purp", "vault_lines": ["And I got pills, and I got purp"], "meaning": "Pills is a very broad description\n\n\n\n…but purp (for you under 15 folk) is purple marijuana. It is usually harvested later in season, so the tiny flowers (which bud essentially is) are starting to bloom.\n\n\n\nPurp could also refer to purple drank.", "annotation_id": "1208184", "url": "https://genius.com/1208184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I (h)ate that pussy can you keep a secret", "vault_lines": ["I (h)ate that pussy can you keep a secret"], "meaning": "This line has two possible interpretations:\n\nI ate that pussy can you keep a secret\n\nThis would refer to Rozay fooling around with a girl already in a  relationship or a girl that was off limits. He doesn’t want the word out. He could also be’s referring to the fact that he doesn’t want people to know he went down on a woman, because some believe it is demeaning.\n\n\n\nAlternately, the line could be as the lyric video states:\n\nI hate that pussy can you keep a secret\n\nThis would refer to the fact Ross is just fucking some girl, but he hates her pussy. Regardless, pussy is pussy so Ross will continue to fuck her despite the fact he isn’t enjoying the sex.\n\nRoss is not calling Bieber a pussy – this isn’t a Justin Bieber diss as they are friends, and Ross has a Lambo named after Justin Bieber.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/justinbieber/status/224476231964434432\n\n\n\nNote: Both interpretations of this line are included despite the fact the official lyric video states the lyric is “hate”. The video itself is not 100% correct and has its issues itself – in the beginning of the video, the lyrics say “Play that music”, despite the fact the lyric is clearly the world famous “Maybach Music” adlib.", "annotation_id": "1192350", "url": "https://genius.com/1192350", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I’m ridin’ clean and I’m fuckin hoes (hah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm ridin' clean and I'm fuckin hoes (hah)"], "meaning": "This line is similar to the hook of his smash hit, MC Hammer. “Riding clean,” refers to the fact that there are no drugs in his car. Despite that, he still gets hoes.\n\n\n\nClean is another name for powder, he could be using this term to throw people off.", "annotation_id": "1189963", "url": "https://genius.com/1189963", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "Hector my amigo straight", "vault_lines": ["Hector my amigo straight"], "meaning": "He gets his dope from the main source. He is saying his amigo because his connect is hispanic & he’s straight because drugs are available.\n\nAlso ‘Hector’ is mentioned to be a connect in a song from A1FBG Colombia where Scooter says he makes bricks with Hector.\n\nSo i guess this is one good amigo. Get it?", "annotation_id": "1181990", "url": "https://genius.com/1181990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "Spend Iguodala on my Rolly", "vault_lines": ["Spend Iguodala on my Rolly"], "meaning": "He spent 80k on his Rolex, and wordplay with Andre Iguodala, who was a member of the Philadelphia 76ers at the time the record was recorded.", "annotation_id": "1173565", "url": "https://genius.com/1173565", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "Hammers and the fucking vogues", "vault_lines": ["Hammers and the fucking vogues"], "meaning": "Ever the cross-promoter, Ross gives nod here to a song by MMG’s Stalley called, natch, “Hammers & Vogues”", "annotation_id": "1171666", "url": "https://genius.com/1171666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I got that Justin Bieber, please believe it", "vault_lines": ["I got that Justin Bieber, please believe it"], "meaning": "With reference to the previous line regarding Griselda Blanco, this line refers to Justin Bieber as “cocaine” – because he’s white.\n\nIn addition, it can also mean Rozay has the ability to continually churn out hits. Ross simultaneously has both then, since many of hits hits are about the distribution of cocaine. This creates a homonym on “believe”:\n\n\nA plea for you to believe him\nJustin Biebers fourth and most recent album was titled; Believe\n\n\n\n\n\nAlternately, this line could actually refers to possession of heroin. Dating back to the early 60s, many dealers and users have referred to heroin and cocaine as “boy” and “girl”, respectively. As a play on words, many rappers have used a famous white female entertainer’s name to describe cocaine. Therefore, in this context, Miley Cyrus' name is being used as slang for cocaine and Justin Bieber’s name is being used as slang for heroin.", "annotation_id": "1165623", "url": "https://genius.com/1165623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I got a a bad bitch in my Chevy Selling Miley Cyrus in my brand-new Monte Carlo I got that Justin Bieber, please believe it", "vault_lines": ["I got that Justin Bieber, please believe it"], "meaning": "Miley Cyrus is a “white girl” (cocaine) and Justin Bieber is “white boy” (heroin) – this is slang for drugs dating back to the 70s\n\n\n\nHe is also using word play with the word “believe” which is the name of Bieber’s last album", "annotation_id": "1164402", "url": "https://genius.com/1164402", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "Niggas sellin’ that China white Fuck around with that Yao Ming", "vault_lines": ["Niggas sellin' that China white", "Fuck around with that Yao Ming"], "meaning": "China White is a very pure form of heroin and Yao Ming is a fair-skinned Chinese NBA player.", "annotation_id": "1163200", "url": "https://genius.com/1163200", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I let go of my eggo", "vault_lines": ["I let go of my eggo"], "meaning": "Talking about going out to sell the crack and “letting it go”.\n\nAlso a reference to Eggo Waffles, as he had referred to his “toaster” on the previous line.", "annotation_id": "1163180", "url": "https://genius.com/1163180", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "I’m screaming rest in peace, Griselda Blanco", "vault_lines": ["I'm screaming rest in peace, Griselda Blanco"], "meaning": "Griselda Blanco aka The Cocaine Godmother was a drug lord for the Medellín Cartel and a pioneer in the Miami-based cocaine drug trade and underworld during the 1970s and early 1980s. As a drug lord (in his music) himself, Ross respects what she has done. Griselda recently was gunned down in Columbia, hence “I’m screaming rest in Peace.” .", "annotation_id": "1161989", "url": "https://genius.com/1161989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "And Rozay D-Wade nigga", "vault_lines": ["And Rozay D-Wade nigga"], "meaning": "LeBron, Rick Ross, and Dwyane Wade are all ballers and great at what they do. Meek balls similar to them.\n\n\n\nDwyane Wade is the captain of the Miami Heat and Rick Ross is the captain of Maybach Music.", "annotation_id": "1161978", "url": "https://genius.com/1161978", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "line": "Straight chips, Frito Lay", "vault_lines": ["Straight chips, Frito Lay"], "meaning": "“Chips” is slang for money. Frito-Lay is a snack brand that produces many well-known snacks but not limited to Doritos, Cheetos, and Fritos.  Meek previously referenced the brand on his Drake-assisted song “Amen”:\n\nAnd all I get is Frito Lay", "annotation_id": "1161977", "url": "https://genius.com/1161977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Believe It", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Meek-mill-believe-it-lyrics", "genius_title": "Believe It", "genius_id": 93312, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Belly", "line": "Mon fils a déjà Rolex, plus tard il fera jamais d’crédit", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Guy2Bezbar exprime ici une fierté de réussite matérielle transmise à sa descendance. Offrir une Rolex à son fils symbolise une forme de réussite, de luxe et de statut social. En affirmant qu’il “fera jamais d'crédit”, il souligne qu’il souhaite le voir vivre dans l’abondance, sans avoir besoin de s’endetter pour atteindre ses objectifs.\nC’est une vision où la richesse est héritée, et où la lutte économique qui a marqué la génération du rappeur n’aura pas à être répétée par ses enfants. Une forme de vengeance sociale douce, qui passe par la transmission du confort et de la dignité.", "annotation_id": "35414053", "url": "https://genius.com/35414053", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Belly", "line": "T’es par terre comme la montre à Ace Hood (C’est fort), appelle ton équipe, tu sais qu’j’en ai rien à foutre (Coco)", "vault_lines": ["T'es par terre comme la montre à Ace Hood (C'est fort), appelle ton équipe, tu sais qu'j'en ai rien à foutre (Coco)"], "meaning": "C’est Ace Hood, rappeur qui était dans le label We The Best Music de DJ Khaled et a fait « Hustle Hard ».\nIci, Guy2Bezbar fait référence à un tapis rouge où le rappeur a fait tomber le cadran de sa montre et a cherché à le remettre en place…\n\nhttps://youtu.be/DHTAaDBKwOE?si=isR72_USN9vyxTF4", "annotation_id": "34650852", "url": "https://genius.com/34650852", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
