{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Benediction", "line": "People dying all around me", "vault_lines": ["People dying all around me"], "meaning": "Growing up in the streets of both New Orleans and Houston, he has seen many people die – including his father and his brother. He goes into detail about these incidents of deaths in his hit record Downtown, featuring Kidd Kidd.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5ViSMGCqsvE", "annotation_id": "2960217", "url": "https://genius.com/2960217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Benediction", "line": "Now that I got your attention Let us end with the benediction", "vault_lines": ["Now that I got your attention", "Let us end with the benediction"], "meaning": "Benediction is the bestowing of a blessing, usually occurring at the end of a religious service. Which makes sense because this is the last song on the album (not including the two bonus tracks which have already been released).", "annotation_id": "2950679", "url": "https://genius.com/2950679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
