{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "100 karat diamond chain make them hoes blink", "vault_lines": ["100 karat diamond chain make them hoes blink"], "meaning": "Meek’s 100 karat diamond chain makes hoes blink for 2 reasons:\n\n\nIt’s so new, it shill shines, so they need to blink\nThe hoes are so surprised by such a beautiful chain", "annotation_id": "1320740", "url": "https://genius.com/1320740", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "Cake my birthday, blow them candles Baby please don’t blow my high", "vault_lines": ["Cake my birthday, blow them candles", "Baby please don't blow my high"], "meaning": "A mixed interpretation of blowing something out. Getting cake implies getting money. At a birthday party, the birthday boy/girl would blow out their candles on their birthday cake. Pill’s birthday party consist of his rising to fame and getting money would be the cake and haters blowing his high (or ruining his good time) would blowing out his own candles.", "annotation_id": "1221786", "url": "https://genius.com/1221786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "I fuck four bitches, I got eight balls I’ll finish your career, nigga: eight bars", "vault_lines": ["I'll finish your career, nigga: eight bars"], "meaning": "Nice double entendre. French is having sex with four girls at once, as if he had four penises (eight testicles.) An 8 ball is also 3 ½ grams of cocaine. While a crack/cocaine addiction could certainly end a man’s rap career, French could also be saying “8 bars,” as in it would only take him a few lines to off someone in a rap battle, making them quit rapping. Frenchie came to fame partially due to his success on the battle-rap scene:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SwfdV0ctszo", "annotation_id": "788583", "url": "https://genius.com/788583", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "I say Benji after Benjamin", "vault_lines": ["I say Benji after Benjamin"], "meaning": "Meek Mill is counting his one hundred dollar bills out loud.\n\n\n\nOne hundred dollar bills are also known as Benji’s. The reason  for this is that Benjamin Franklin is on the front of the bill.", "annotation_id": "622814", "url": "https://genius.com/622814", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "Aaron Rodgers, I quarterback the pack, Torch", "vault_lines": ["Aaron Rodgers, I quarterback the pack, Torch"], "meaning": "Aaron Rodgers is the Quarterback of the Green Bay Packers. Ross uses this as a metaphor as in drugs, which is another word for pack.", "annotation_id": "577250", "url": "https://genius.com/577250", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "It go ”vroom, vroom, skrrt”, that bitch cost like seven birds", "vault_lines": ["It go \"vroom, vroom, skrrt\", that bitch cost like seven birds"], "meaning": "His Rolls Royce probably has a nice engine in it. When he steps on the gas the sound is ‘vroom, vroom’ and when he skids it makes the loud pitched sound ‘scrrrt’.\n\n\n\nHow did I figure out it was a Rolls Royce?\n\n7 birds = 7 bricks of cocaine.\n1 brick of cocaine = 2.2 pounds.\n7 bricks X 2.2 pounds = 15.4 pounds\n1 gram of coke goes for about 55-65 USD. I’ll use 60.\nThere is 453.952 grams in a pound.\n60$ X 453.952 grams = 27,237.12\nBut, if you buy in bulk you get wholesale price. 25K.\n25K X 15.4 pounds = $385,000\n\nAccording to http://www.famelycars.blogspot.com, a Rolls Royce goes for about 385,000 USD.", "annotation_id": "557692", "url": "https://genius.com/557692", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "Hundred clip for the payback", "vault_lines": ["62 in the Maybach, hundred clip for the payback"], "meaning": "Probably a 100 round magazine for a MAC-10, and he’s going to use it for payback. Seeing as you can empty a MAC-10 in about 3 seconds, he’ll probably just walk into a joint and spray the room Chinese Triad style (gun sideways so the recoil pushes the gun across the room).", "annotation_id": "493818", "url": "https://genius.com/493818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "You know I coach them niggas like Phil up in that paint", "vault_lines": ["You know I coach them niggas like Phil up in that paint"], "meaning": "He’s coaching niggas like Phil Jackson ( a basketball coach), learning them how to grind.", "annotation_id": "493811", "url": "https://genius.com/493811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "Big bank take little bank", "vault_lines": ["Big bank take little bank"], "meaning": "Refers to a game played in the hood.\nWhoever got the most money in there pockets between two people, would get all the money.\nSimilar game as Fat Bank Take Skinny Bank.\n\nThis also could be a possible reference to Paul Beatty’s first book of poetry, Big Bank Take Little Bank.", "annotation_id": "493780", "url": "https://genius.com/493780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "My hands dirty, my face clean", "vault_lines": ["My hands dirty, my face clean"], "meaning": "Comitting crimes is considered as doing ‘dirt’ as you hear many rappers say in songs e.g. Torch.\nSo he uses this metaphorically and says that his hands are dirty (due to the crimes he has comitted) and his face is clean as he does not do his own dirt himself, he pays people to do his dirt for him (which is considered to be more gangster).\nBasically his dirt means dirty money earned through an illegal way (drug dealing).\n\nPeep the wordplay between dirty/clean.", "annotation_id": "479700", "url": "https://genius.com/479700", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Bank", "line": "Drop a X pill in the fish tank Got the sharks on lean Fishscale for the whole team", "vault_lines": ["Fishscale for the whole team"], "meaning": "Rick Ross here uses a lot of metaphors to describe a situation.\nX pills are exctasy pill. A fish tank is the club. The sharks are Ross and his homies. Fish Scale means coke for his team.\nSo Ross drugged the girls in the club, and they are looking at the girls for sex. They are also under the influence of coke.", "annotation_id": "443355", "url": "https://genius.com/443355", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
