{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Boy Talk", "line": "Love this money making like Mitch, can’t leave the game (Can’t)", "vault_lines": ["Love this money making like Mitch, can't leave the game (Can't)"], "meaning": "Jeezy references Mekhi Phifer’s character Money Making Mitch from the 2002 film Paid in Full. One of the most iconic quotes of the film said by Mitch is\n\nA nigga like me man, I love the game, I love the hustle. You be feeling like one of them ball players niggas you know? Like Bird or Magic or some. Yeah you know, a nigga got dope, a nigga can leave the league. But if I leave, the fans still gone love me my nigga?\"", "annotation_id": "17192815", "url": "https://genius.com/17192815", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Boy Talk", "line": "Hope Shakir Stewart see me balling down from heaven", "vault_lines": ["Hope Shakir Stewart see me balling down from heaven"], "meaning": "Shakir Stewart was a VP for Def Jam who was found dead in April 2008 in the bathroom of his Atlanta home. The cause of Stewart’s death was by gunshot. Stewart’s death was determined to be suicide. Stewart was thirty-four years old and Jeezy has been signed to Def Jam since 2004.", "annotation_id": "17192803", "url": "https://genius.com/17192803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Boy Talk", "line": "All black hoodie just like I’m Trayvon (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["All black hoodie just like I'm Trayvon (Uh)"], "meaning": "Trayvon Martin was an unarmed black teenager killed in Florida by George Zimmerman in 2012. He was wearing a black hoodie when shot.", "annotation_id": "17191330", "url": "https://genius.com/17191330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
