{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Big Fish", "line": "I took an oath when I was young, said I would never tell", "vault_lines": ["I took an oath when I was young, said I would never tell"], "meaning": "The timing of Gucci’s feature on “Big Fish” is nothing short of unfortunate, as he faced “snitching” allegations in April 2026 after the news broke that he was robbed, kidnapped, and forced to sign a recording contract release in January by his artist Pooh Shiesty and several of his associates. Gucci gave a written statement to the FBI about the incident, describing what happened and identifying those who robbed him.\n\n\n\nA video showing Gucci being pressured to sign Shiesty's contract release from 1017\n\n\n\nThe criticism of Gucci became more abundant after he dropped “CRASH DUMMY,” a diss track towards Shiesty that included descriptions of what transpired during the robbery and kidnapping. Many figures in the hip-hop industry interpreted this as Gucci “snitching” on Shiesty and his crew in the song.\n\nThe heavy criticism of Gucci is partly due to the fact that he has denounced snitching several times over the course of his career, such as on his June 2021 track “How I See It”:\n\nA snitch gon' be a snitch, and like a rat, they should be treated (Rule)", "annotation_id": "40700945", "url": "https://genius.com/40700945", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
