{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "Get a bitch some Xannys, ain’t no Bill Cosby", "vault_lines": ["Get a bitch some Xannys, ain’t no Bill Cosby"], "meaning": "Xanax is a drug which acts as a central nervous system depressant. Wayne gives them to his girl so she can get high, but he does not do it with the intention of drugging her to have sex with her such as comedian Bill Cosby was accused of doing by many women.\n\nIn a sworn deposition pertaining to the 2006 civil lawsuit filed by Andrea Constand, Cosby was asked if he intended to use Quaaludes he had gotten to drug women he wanted to have sex with and he replied yes. Quaaludes are a different drug than Xanax, but it is also a central nervous system depressant.", "annotation_id": "11264489", "url": "https://genius.com/11264489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "I’ve been popping all these pain pills and still hurting Popping all these Percs, call me Lil Wayne Perkins Lil Tunechi, you can call me Pill Gates", "vault_lines": ["I’ve been popping all these pain pills and still hurting", "Popping all these Percs, call me Lil Wayne Perkins", "Lil Tunechi, you can call me Pill Gates"], "meaning": "Percocet is the brand name of the pain killer consisting of Acetaminophen and Oxycodone. Despite taking a bunch of Percs his pain will not go away, perhaps he has built up a tolerance to the drug due to abuse. Wayne also interpolates his name into the name of Rock and R&B singer, guitarist, and songwriter David Wayne Perkins and drops a pill pun using philanthropist Bill Gates' name.", "annotation_id": "11264465", "url": "https://genius.com/11264465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "Sipping out my GRAMMY, Best Hip Hop Artist", "vault_lines": ["Sipping out my GRAMMY, Best Hip Hop Artist"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has been nominated for 21 GRAMMYS and has won 4. He won all 4 in 2008 during the 51st annual GRAMMY awards:\n\nBest Rap Solo Performance for “A Milli', Best Rap Performance By A Duo Or Group for “Swagga Like Us, Best Rap Song for Lollipop, and Best Rap Album for Tha Carter III.", "annotation_id": "11264429", "url": "https://genius.com/11264429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "I live in Miami, I see real dolphins", "vault_lines": ["I live in Miami, I see real dolphins"], "meaning": "A clever double entendre by Weezy. He lives in Miami, Florida where he owns an $18 million mansion. He watches dolphins swim through the waters of Miami beach and also watches the Miami Dolphins of the NFL play their games.", "annotation_id": "11264419", "url": "https://genius.com/11264419", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "All you niggas real fake, I like my kill laced", "vault_lines": ["All you niggas real fake, I like my kill laced"], "meaning": "Kill is slang for marijuana which is densely packed and very potent. Weezy does not just prefer his weed strong, he also likes it mixed with other drugs such as cocaine to give it even more of a kick.", "annotation_id": "11264411", "url": "https://genius.com/11264411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "Take your bitch she can’t be found, I’m talking milk carton", "vault_lines": ["Take your bitch she can’t be found, I’m talking milk carton"], "meaning": "The back of milk cartons have been used as a means to spread awareness of a missing person. When Wayne steals your girl she goes missing from your life and never comes back.", "annotation_id": "11264408", "url": "https://genius.com/11264408", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "Smoking all this fucking loud, I mean it’s real noisy", "vault_lines": ["Smoking all this fucking loud, I mean it’s real noisy"], "meaning": "Loud is a popular nickname for high quality marijuana. Wayne drops a metaphor in this line and says the weed is so strong that it has a very noticeable smell.", "annotation_id": "11264383", "url": "https://genius.com/11264383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "line": "Taking all this fucking Adderall, I’m sleep walking", "vault_lines": ["Taking all this fucking Adderall, I’m sleep walking"], "meaning": "The first of many clever puns in this verse. Adderall is the brand name of a combination of the central nervous stimulants Amphetamine and Dextroamphetamine. Adderall is taken to treat attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) and narcolepsy, but it is also misused by others to stay up for extended periods of time. The most prevalent case of this is college students who use it to pull all nighters to study. Wayne has been abusing Adderall to stay up and feels like a zombie at this point.", "annotation_id": "11264368", "url": "https://genius.com/11264368", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bill Gates Remix", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-bill-gates-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Bill Gates Remix", "genius_id": 2971579, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Haters want to murder me and I can smell a hit So it’s music to my ears every time I fill a clip", "vault_lines": ["Haters want to murder me and I can smell a hit", "So it's music to my ears every time I fill a clip"], "meaning": "Possible double entendre. A “hit” is usually when someone plans an attack on someone, usually an assassination. Rick Ross says he can smell a hit, he sees signs for a hit so he gets ready with his countermeasure – filling up gun clips. Rick Ross has been attacked and has survived a few hits in the past.\n\nHowever, Rick Ross doesn’t actually retaliate with violence but with releasing a hit in the form of music. It’s music to his ears i.e. the music he is creating through him filling up a clip – a money clip.", "annotation_id": "15645836", "url": "https://genius.com/15645836", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Jay-Z what up nigga", "vault_lines": ["Jay-Z what up nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross & Jay-Z have been good friends ever since Rozay has touched the spotlight.\n\nJay-Z wrote a verse to Rick Ross’s first radio single “Hustlin'” & has been on every one of his albums ever since besides Deeper Than Rap & Black Dollar.\n\nIn 2017 Jay-Z shouted out Ross in a tweet thanking over 90 rappers for helping him be in the song writing hall of the fame.", "annotation_id": "8627160", "url": "https://genius.com/8627160", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Hit me up on the 3-0-5 or the 7-8-6", "vault_lines": ["Hit me up on the 3-0-5 or the 7-8-6"], "meaning": "Both 305 and 786 are area codes associated with Miami-Dade County of the state of Florida.", "annotation_id": "4525352", "url": "https://genius.com/4525352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Told y’all niggas in ’95 I was worth ten million Now it’s ’08 and I got ten in the bank nigga", "vault_lines": ["Told y'all niggas in '95 I was worth ten million", "Now it's '08 and I got ten in the bank nigga"], "meaning": "Ross is saying that in March 2008, at the time of Trilla’s release, his net worth was $10 million dollars. This is conceivable in part because his debut album, Port of Miami sold  187,000 copies its first week in 2006, before become certified gold later that year.", "annotation_id": "4525333", "url": "https://genius.com/4525333", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Triple C, we unstoppable", "vault_lines": ["Triple C, we unstoppable"], "meaning": "Founded by Ross in 2005, Triple C, also known as “Carol City Cartel”, is a trio that includes Gunplay, Torch, and Young Breed.", "annotation_id": "4525304", "url": "https://genius.com/4525304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Snow white Range, let my partner park it", "vault_lines": ["Snow white Range, let my partner park it"], "meaning": "Ross insists on having his entourage park his vehicles for him, in this case, a white Range Rover. Rozay is too busy making money to do it himself.\n\nAlso, white Range can have an underlying meaning. The car is white, just like the cocaine Ross deals. The car has been bought with the money Ross made off the cocaine.", "annotation_id": "490893", "url": "https://genius.com/490893", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Niggas want to kidnap Leave me in the trunk, walk away with big stacks", "vault_lines": ["Niggas want to kidnap"], "meaning": "Ross believes his enemies are plotting to kidnap him in order to extort his family for money, even though they’ll likely kill him, and leave him in the trunk of a car.\n\nThis could also be seen metaphorically: rappers want to steal Ross' style (kidnapping him) and then Ross will fall off as rapper (leave him in the trunk) and the biters will eventually be more successful than him (walk away with big stacks).", "annotation_id": "490891", "url": "https://genius.com/490891", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "See I got on my Tom Ford shades nigga I got a new outlook on life y’know", "vault_lines": ["See I got on my Tom Ford shades nigga I got a new outlook on life y'know"], "meaning": "This is a metaphor: Ross' new Tom Ford designer sunglasses have changed his perspective on life. This actually means he lives different (new outlook on life) because of all the money (Tom Ford shades) he got right now.", "annotation_id": "490886", "url": "https://genius.com/490886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "I won’t let the roof up", "vault_lines": ["I won't let the roof up"], "meaning": "Likely due to threats on his life, Ross is opting to keep the roof of his car closed.", "annotation_id": "490876", "url": "https://genius.com/490876", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "I’m a card shark up in the Hard Rock", "vault_lines": ["I'm a card shark up in the Hard Rock"], "meaning": "Ross goes to his local Hard Rock Cafe – most likely Miami – and wins multiple card games there.", "annotation_id": "490875", "url": "https://genius.com/490875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Whip that white girl just like K-Fed", "vault_lines": ["Whip that white girl just like K-Fed"], "meaning": "Like Kevin Federline has controlled Britney Spears, Ross controls his own white girl: pure Colombian cocaine.", "annotation_id": "490873", "url": "https://genius.com/490873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "In the Phantom on that 2Pac Ridin’ Thru The Ghetto like I’m lookin’ for a new spot", "vault_lines": ["In the Phantom on that 2Pac", "Ridin' Thru The Ghetto like I'm lookin' for a new spot"], "meaning": "Ross is rolling through your neighborhood in his Phantom, listening to 2Pac – likely a reference to the album All Eyez on Me.\nTo the unsavvy passer-by, Ross might look like he is looking for a new crack spot.\n\nAlso a reference to the song Ridin' Thru The Ghetto, the only bonus track on this album.", "annotation_id": "490863", "url": "https://genius.com/490863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "In the game like Tony Parker", "vault_lines": ["In the game like Tony Parker"], "meaning": "Two meanings are possible here:\n\n\nRoss is involved in the dope game to the same degree as Tony Parker (Point Guard, San Antonio Spurs) is involved in the NBA.\nRoss is as good as a rapper (game means rap industry here) like Tony Parker is an NBA-player.", "annotation_id": "490711", "url": "https://genius.com/490711", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Kingdom come, Prince of Zamundah", "vault_lines": ["Kingdom come, Prince of Zamundah"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to Akeem Joffer, the character played by Eddie Murphy in the 1988 hit-comedy Coming to America, where Murphy plays the often unintentionally hilarious Prince of Zamunda.\n\n\n\nKingdom Come is also the name of Jay-Z’s 2006 comeback album.", "annotation_id": "490701", "url": "https://genius.com/490701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "It’s all the same gang, posted up in front of Popeye’s in the Maybach, nigga", "vault_lines": ["It's all the same gang, posted up in front of Popeye's in the Maybach, nigga"], "meaning": "Many rap stars aren’t too proud to be seen in front of Popeye’s. Here we can see Cam'ron and Clipse posted-up inside a Popeye’s enjoying some chicken and fries for the video Popular Demand. Ross is stating that neither is he too proud to visit Popeye’s, a low-income restaurant, in his million dollar Maybach sedan, because he too enjoys their fine herbs and spices.", "annotation_id": "490697", "url": "https://genius.com/490697", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Billionaire", "line": "Bugatti, the Gotti of Morocco", "vault_lines": ["Bugatti, the Gotti of Morocco"], "meaning": "Ross is claiming to be the John Gotti, a notorious mafia boss, of Morocco.\n Probably not the model Ross meant, but here is an exquisite Bugatti in Morocco:\n\n\n\nRoss relates in a lot of ways to John Gotti. Teflon Don is the nickname of Gotti, and also the name of Ross' fourth studio album.", "annotation_id": "490693", "url": "https://genius.com/490693", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
