{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Black Man’s Dream", "line": "Terminator X, I’m a public enemy", "vault_lines": ["Terminator X, I’m a public enemy"], "meaning": "Norman Rogers is retired DJ “Terminator X” and was known for his time with rap group “Public Enemy.” More here.\n\n\n\nA possible connection to the Terminator series as well, Ross could be implying that he’s out to kill, a threat to the public.", "annotation_id": "5112622", "url": "https://genius.com/5112622", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Black Man’s Dream", "line": "Middle of December I will melt your fucking snow", "vault_lines": ["Middle of December I will melt your fucking snow"], "meaning": "Rozay’s so hot in the drug game, that his mere presence will melt all your snow, even during the middle of the winter (December).\n\n\n\nThis continues the “frozen” wordplay he used two liens prior.", "annotation_id": "2869597", "url": "https://genius.com/2869597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Black Man’s Dream", "line": "Chrome lips all on the whip and yeah that bitch be blowing kisses", "vault_lines": ["Chrome lips all on the whip and yeah that bitch be blowing kisses"], "meaning": "The lips of a car are the parts that stick out of the wheel, and the farther out the lips are, the nicer the car usually looks.\n\nLuda’s car might act differently than Wayne’s", "annotation_id": "2759517", "url": "https://genius.com/2759517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Black Man’s Dream", "line": "Check me out, it go one for the money Two for the hoes Three to put that sticky green scent up to my nose", "vault_lines": ["Check me out, it go one for the money", "Two for the hoes", "Three to put that sticky green scent up to my nose"], "meaning": "What is always played as “one for the money, two for the show” is now used in hip-hop a lot but many artists replace “show” with “hoes.”\n\nI’m sure you know what the sticky green scent is.", "annotation_id": "2759473", "url": "https://genius.com/2759473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Black Man’s Dream", "line": "Got 3 bricks headed straight for your nose", "vault_lines": ["Got 3 bricks headed straight for your nose"], "meaning": "A brick is a pound of any drug.\n(Brick usually referring to cocaine)\n\nRoss telling you that you have some fucked up habits now.", "annotation_id": "2759455", "url": "https://genius.com/2759455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
