{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Black Opium", "line": "Dreamchasers you fuck with Meek, you gotta fuck with Coon", "vault_lines": ["Dreamchasers you fuck with Meek, you gotta fuck with Coon"], "meaning": "Ross refers to rapper Meek Mill’s track “Dreamchasers”, off his well received mixtape of the same name. The two have had a close bond since Meek signed to his label MMG in 2011.\n\n\n\nRozay’s threats about messing with Meek did indeed come into play when he had something to say about Meek’s 2017 prison sentence.", "annotation_id": "13830556", "url": "https://genius.com/13830556", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Black Opium", "line": "[Chorus: Spliff Star and Baby Sham] I do this for us Stuck on the grind trying to elevate I’ma stand as a man never above ya", "vault_lines": ["I'ma stand as a man never above ya"], "meaning": "Spliff Star recites “Stuck on the grind trying to elevate” at the end of his guest verse in Busta Rhymes‘ “I Know What You Want”.\n\nBaby Sham spitd “I'mma stand as a man, never above ya” later in the song.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/WDaNJW_jEBo?t=94", "annotation_id": "8354575", "url": "https://genius.com/8354575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
