{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "A nigga wit’ a attitude, take it outta’ context", "vault_lines": ["A nigga wit' a attitude, take it outta' context"], "meaning": "Ricky sure does have an attitude that can get him into trouble, but we love him anyway.\n\n\n\nRoss references the original Niggaz Wit Attitudes, NWA, who were often taken out of context within the media who portrayed them as misogynistic, promoting gun violence, and gangsters (ironically all things that the media has portrayed Ross as over the years). In reality we know that NWA was just delivering a social commentary about the state of their city, but God forbid we attempt to contextualize the “horrible” things rappers are talking about.\n\n\n\nRozay hanging out with OG NWA member Dr. Dre among others.", "annotation_id": "2775726", "url": "https://genius.com/2775726", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "Afghan in a bomb vest", "vault_lines": ["Bin Laden beard, Afghan in a bomb vest"], "meaning": "A continuation of his Bin Laden reference in the previous line. He makes it sound as if he is wearing a suicide vest that serves as a bomb, when instead he is wearing a vest that is “the bomb” – like the awesome sweater vest below.", "annotation_id": "1906505", "url": "https://genius.com/1906505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "Cool & Dre", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Cool & Dre are a team of hip hop producers from Miami, Florida, consisting of Marcello “Cool” Valenzano and Andre “Dre” Christopher Lyon who produced this song.", "annotation_id": "921608", "url": "https://genius.com/921608", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "Lease apartments to get kicked out it Next day, buy a condo to get a kick out it", "vault_lines": ["Lease apartments to get kicked out it", "Next day, buy a condo to get a kick out it"], "meaning": "Many Drug Dealers Lease multiple apartments under Anonymous or Assumed names to deal drugs out of, or use ass stash houses or safe houses.  They know they will get kicked out of many if not all of them.\n\nRoss Says that he makes so much money in the Drug-game that the day after he gets kicked out of one of his many apartments he will legitimately purchase a condominium just for fun.\n\nCheck out his condo on the rap map.", "annotation_id": "416380", "url": "https://genius.com/416380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "Way up in them Cali Hills, burnin’ like the sunset", "vault_lines": ["Way up in them Cali Hills, burnin' like the sunset"], "meaning": "First, Ross is up in the cali hills (a reference to rollin thru the hills of northern california, Most likely the Oakland Hills)\nNow he’s burning like a sunset (Smoking Northern California Marijuana (Dank Weed or Purple Flowers, Purple Haze, Etc ) as intensely as a burning Sunset.\n\n\n\n\n\n#WHUHH", "annotation_id": "416373", "url": "https://genius.com/416373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "We came for trigga’ play, kill a nigga for a dime I’m tryna’ chill today, I got a million on my mind", "vault_lines": ["We came for trigga' play, kill a nigga for a dime", "I'm tryna' chill today, I got a million on my mind"], "meaning": "Ross is the Teflon Don.  He always ready for trigga' play (Gun play)  and he’d kill someone for Ten Thousand Dollars (a dime) without thought.  (or possibly even a dime bag of weed or coke etc.) Even though he was a cop…\n\n\n\nRoss then says hes trying to be more level headed (chill) these days (today) because he has projects or deals worth millions of dollars that he is working on or thinking about. (on his mind)", "annotation_id": "416371", "url": "https://genius.com/416371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "Carol City Cartel", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A shoutout to his Triple C’s.\n\n\n\nCould be a reference to the network of cocaine trafficking and illegal activity in Dade County, FL. Ross maintains affiliated although several members are now incarcerated.", "annotation_id": "374540", "url": "https://genius.com/374540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Blow", "line": "Ha, they say life’s a bitch", "vault_lines": ["Ha, they say life's a bitch"], "meaning": "A popular pessimistic phrase to explain the unfair plight of life and the best case scenario means you eventually pass on.\nLife’s a bitch and then you die", "annotation_id": "374528", "url": "https://genius.com/374528", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
