{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bo$$", "line": "48 laws of power", "vault_lines": ["48 laws of power"], "meaning": "48 Laws Of Power is a book written by Robert Greene and demonstrates that today’s elite shared similar traits with powerful figures throughout history. It’s popular with inmates and celebrities.", "annotation_id": "4469789", "url": "https://genius.com/4469789", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bo$$", "line": "Ever seen a presidential suite before? So come on in, in the mornin’ I be John and you be Marilyn Monroe", "vault_lines": ["Ever seen a presidential suite before?", "So come on in, in the mornin'", "I be John and you be Marilyn Monroe"], "meaning": "Omarion sees himself as President John F. Kennedy while his girl is portrayed as Marilyn Monroe. For a bit of insight, rumors have been going on for 50 years about John F. Kennedy & Marilyn Monroe since they first met and whether or not JFK had an affair with her.\n\nAlso, Omarion refers to the presidential suite when playing off of the JFK line.", "annotation_id": "4469709", "url": "https://genius.com/4469709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bo$$", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Omarion-bo-lyrics", "genius_title": "Bo$$", "genius_id": 601709, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Body Count", "line": "Then we cook em up, and let ’em dry We break it down, and let em fly Send em to the hood, and tell em bye", "vault_lines": ["We break it down, and let em fly", "Send em to the hood, and tell em bye"], "meaning": "Meek’s cousin Knock told him not to teach people exactly how to do it, but he gives a little insight on how it goes down.\n\nFirst, they cook up the crack in the kitchen. Next step, they let the crack dry after cooking it. Then, he breaks it down in weight increments to be sold. Finally, he lets the bird fly and sells it real fast.", "annotation_id": "762460", "url": "https://genius.com/762460", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Body Count", "line": "Whole bird on my desk, bag it up by ounce", "vault_lines": ["Whole bird on my desk, bag it up by ounce"], "meaning": "A bird is slang for a kilo of coke. He divides them individually on his desk into 1 ounce bags, which not only makes it easier, but also quicker to distribute.", "annotation_id": "391788", "url": "https://genius.com/391788", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Body Count", "line": "Murder after murder, nigga you ain’t heard ‘Cause when it come to beef, I’m puttin’ bread all on my burger Man them shooters be so hungry", "vault_lines": ["Murder after murder, nigga you ain't heard", "'Cause when it come to beef, I'm puttin' bread all on my burger", "Man them shooters be so hungry"], "meaning": "Having beef is another word for having an issue with someone. We know Meek’s body count is double digits, all it is is murder after murder.\n\nMeek will eat up the beef just like a juicy hamburger. The shooters are hungry for money, and the “hunger” also makes sense with the previous burger bar.", "annotation_id": "389875", "url": "https://genius.com/389875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
