{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born Stunna (Remix)", "line": "Bitch, I’m Tuco, I’m too cold,", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm Tuco, I'm too cold,"], "meaning": "This line is actually: “Bitch I’m Tuco, I’m too cold.”\n\nTuco is a character from the television show Breaking Bad", "annotation_id": "8141819", "url": "https://genius.com/8141819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born Stunna (Remix)", "line": "I show you bitches how to put together punchlines", "vault_lines": ["I show you bitches how to put together punchlines"], "meaning": "Nicki demonstrates her lyricism to other female rappers. There’s an art and a science to the punchline rap, and Nicki has mastered both. Nicki’s trademark and clever punchlines/fire verses are part of the reason she’s winning.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GHzLrMgolg0", "annotation_id": "2150688", "url": "https://genius.com/2150688", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born Stunna (Remix)", "line": "Used to have Trina but I still got Nina", "vault_lines": ["Used to have Trina but I still got Nina"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne used to date Trina. He doesn’t anymore but he still has nina, his gun. Nina = 9mm.\n\nThey’re still on good terms, as she turned up (out of nowhere) on Wayne’s Wowzers from I Am Not A Human Being II.", "annotation_id": "882959", "url": "https://genius.com/882959", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
