{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born to Kill", "line": "So many verts outside, call it Candy Land", "vault_lines": ["So many verts outside, call it Candy Land"], "meaning": "He’s talking about old-school convertibles (usually from the 70s and referred to as “donks”) that are upgraded with huge wheels and a shiny, bright colored, “candy” looking paint job.", "annotation_id": "17781622", "url": "https://genius.com/17781622", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born to Kill", "line": "So many hundreds in my pocket like some Hammer pants (Hammer pants)", "vault_lines": ["So many hundreds in my pocket like some Hammer pants (Hammer pants)"], "meaning": "Jeezy’s referring to pop-rap one hit wonder MC Hammer’s iconic style of pants, which came to be known as “Hammer pants” because of his use of them in the music video for his most famous song, “U Can’t Touch This.” The pants have a thin but baggy look, similar to that of sweatpants.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=otCpCn0l4Wo\n\nJeezy has stuffed so much physical cash into his pants that they stretch out and have a baggy appearance just like Hammer pants.", "annotation_id": "17780296", "url": "https://genius.com/17780296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
