{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "Llamar el babalao pregunta le por un depojo", "vault_lines": ["Llamar el babalao pregunta le por un depojo"], "meaning": "Call a Santeria priest (babalao) to give you a spiritual cleansing and protection (despojo). Pitbull’s saying his crew is so tough you’ll need street and spiritual protection.", "annotation_id": "2778706", "url": "https://genius.com/2778706", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "Trick, Pitbull, DJ Khaled, 305 M-I Yayo", "vault_lines": ["Trick, Pitbull, DJ Khaled, 305 M-I Yayo"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is shouting out his fellow dade rappers in the song\n\n305 – miami’s area code\n\nM-I-Yayo is a play on M-I-A which represents miami and saying it is a city of yayo (cocaine)", "annotation_id": "1639041", "url": "https://genius.com/1639041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "You try me and I’ma get 20 tonight", "vault_lines": ["You try me and I'ma get 20 tonight"], "meaning": "basically if you try to punk/play me IM gonna get 20 to life just like my road dawgs. and when you talkin crime and punishment, 20 years is the going rate for murder charges nation wide. So what we can take from this is, “you try me & im gonna kill yo ass”", "annotation_id": "932364", "url": "https://genius.com/932364", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "I’m Mr. 305 put that on a triple beam I bet it weigh out more than a boatload of keys", "vault_lines": ["I'm Mr. 305 put that on a triple beam", "I bet it weigh out more than a boatload of keys"], "meaning": "305 is the an area code for Miami/Dade county. Pitbull says hes important man in miami. Hes mr 305. and if you were to  put that on a triple beam. ( a scale used for weighing large amounts of drugs) its weight (importance) we be more then a whole boat full of keys of cocaine.", "annotation_id": "416468", "url": "https://genius.com/416468", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "Pero final de todo tu no puede con los lobos", "vault_lines": ["Pero final de todo tu no puede con los lobos"], "meaning": "But in the end you cant hang (or keep up) with the wolves", "annotation_id": "416447", "url": "https://genius.com/416447", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "We ain’t just hitting you buddy, we Warren Sapp’n you", "vault_lines": ["We ain't just hitting you buddy, we Warren Sapp'n you"], "meaning": "They hit hard lke Warren Sapp in his prime.\n\nWarren Sapp – After playing college football at the University of Miami, where he was a defensive standout, Sapp was drafted into the NFL by the Tampa Bay Buccaneers in the first round of the 1995 draft (12th pick overall). Sapp ran the fastest defensive tackle forty time, recording a 4.69 time. Upon joining Tampa Bay, Sapp was almost immediately given the starting job at the position of right defensive tackle and finished his rookie season with 27 tackles and one interception. Sapp continued to be a prolific, intimidating tackler for the Buccaneers, tallying 51 tackles and nine sacks in 1996 and 58 tackles and 10.5 sacks in 1997. In 1997, Sapp was named to his first Pro Bowl. It was the first of seven straight selections. Sapp was named 1999 NFL Defensive Player of the year.", "annotation_id": "416432", "url": "https://genius.com/416432", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "I been born and raised in the county of Dade Land of the haze, the cocaine capital", "vault_lines": ["I been born and raised in the county of Dade", "Land of the haze, the cocaine capital"], "meaning": "Once again Pitbull makes reference  to his home – Miami/ Dade County. Where they have a lot of Haze ( Purple Haze , A great purple Sativa strain of marijuana) and they claim to be the cocaine capital.", "annotation_id": "416427", "url": "https://genius.com/416427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "Bass stay bumpin’, make the trunk rattle, rearview shake", "vault_lines": ["Bass stay bumpin’, make the trunk rattle, rearview shake"], "meaning": "Many people will put big speaker boxes in the trunk of their old style cars.  Because of the age of the vehicle there are  usually many rattles when the bases goes boom. Loose trim, License plate frames, etc.  Te rear-view mirror will often shake violently as well in sync to the base.", "annotation_id": "416420", "url": "https://genius.com/416420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "It’s dat lil’ chico Pitbull", "vault_lines": ["It's dat lil’ chico Pitbull"], "meaning": "Chico – Term used mostly for male Latinos residing on the east coast. but also used around the US.\n\nLatino heritage rappers from the east coast called themselves chico or lil' chico, and include this term in the songs where a chicano rapper might had included ese or an African American might had included nigga", "annotation_id": "416410", "url": "https://genius.com/416410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "Cuz everywhere I go they be like ya-yo!", "vault_lines": ["Cuz everywhere I go they be like ya-yo!"], "meaning": "Everywhere in Dade County that Trick Daddy frequents often people will often be selling drugs on the corner,  They will say Ya-Yo (An old school term used to describe cocaine. Popularized by the urban folk hero Tony Montana in the Hip Hop classic film Scarface.  Also spelled llello.) as u pass to see if u are interested in what they are selling.", "annotation_id": "416405", "url": "https://genius.com/416405", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Born-N-Raised", "line": "And when I take off its like I took off And when I ride by its like I fly by", "vault_lines": ["And when I take off its like I took off", "And when I ride by its like I fly by"], "meaning": "Continuing with the previous few lines his car is very fast! From a stop it accelerates so fast it as if hes in a plane taking off.  When he drives by hes actually in a plane flying by.", "annotation_id": "416400", "url": "https://genius.com/416400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
