{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Boss Talk", "line": "I put elbows on the ‘lac", "vault_lines": ["I put elbows on the ‘lac"], "meaning": "“Bows”, short for ‘elbows’, is another street term for Cadillac ’84 model spoke rims. The term originates from the style of the spokes that poke out like elbows.", "annotation_id": "13263239", "url": "https://genius.com/13263239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Boss Talk", "line": "Put on Ferragamo on clothes", "vault_lines": ["Put on Ferragamo on clothes"], "meaning": "“Ferragamo” (Salvatore Ferragamo) is an Italian designer brand known for its prestige and high-end quality.", "annotation_id": "13263200", "url": "https://genius.com/13263200", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Boss Talk", "line": "Black doors on fours", "vault_lines": ["Black doors on fours"], "meaning": "“4’s” short for “Four-Four’s” is the street term for the 1984 model spoke wheels, made popular by Mike Jones’ “Still Tippin’, and a car trend originating in Houston, TX since the early 2000’s.", "annotation_id": "13263142", "url": "https://genius.com/13263142", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Boss Talk", "line": "We ride Forgies in Florence clothes", "vault_lines": ["We ride Forgies in Florence clothes"], "meaning": "Slim Thug is conveying he leads a luxurious and sophisticated life.\n\n“Forgies” is the street term for custom wheels made by the wheel company Forgiato. Slim Thug’s Cadillac Escalade features a set of chrome Forgiato Lavarato ECL wheels.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z_2Q9Oc2-u0\n\nFlorence, the capital of Tuscany, Italy, is historically famous for its rich influence in Italian fashion, clothing and culture.\n\nhttps://s3.amazonaws.com/filepicker-images-rapgenius/VqSB5caFQRK0Yh1BXZMh_g2ssz1SSD4g9w6jAtaAQ_d413de55ed6d0d8113d5e52190eb66d2", "annotation_id": "13263051", "url": "https://genius.com/13263051", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Boss Talk", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Slim-thug-boss-talk-lyrics", "genius_title": "Boss Talk", "genius_id": 3369199, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bossy Lady", "line": "Come in late night, so I’m airportin’ As I take fright, I’m your Air Jordan We the world champs, come and ball with us", "vault_lines": ["As I take fright, I'm your Air Jordan", "We the world champs, come and ball with us"], "meaning": "These 3 lines use clever puns with basketball and flight.\n\nAirporting means he’s so important that he has his own private planes. He links this with the Air in Air Jordan. Going of the new Jordan theme he goes on to rap about basketball and perhaps loosely ties it in with travelling the world.\n\nAlso the last line is possibly once again talking about the couple’s importance. They are both world champ just as they are like the presidential couple.\n\nHaving a ball is a double-entendre. Have a ball like the game ball after a match or literally party and have a ball celebrating the fact that you both are world champs and a very important and powerful couple.", "annotation_id": "1116768", "url": "https://genius.com/1116768", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bossy Lady", "line": "Take you parasailin’, straight to Jamaica Your man a batty boy, what the bumbaclot?", "vault_lines": ["Take you parasailin', straight to Jamaica", "Your man a batty boy, what the bumbaclot?"], "meaning": "Batty boy in Jamaican Patois means a homosexual person.\nBumbaclot translates literally as asswipe.\nIts real meaning is more like what we would call a motherfucker.\nIt is used regularly in Jamaican swearing.\n\nRoss cleverly ties both these lines in linking with the brief Jamaican theme.", "annotation_id": "1116750", "url": "https://genius.com/1116750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bossy Lady", "line": "These moves that we’re making Got us on top of the world", "vault_lines": ["These moves that we're making", "Got us on top of the world"], "meaning": "This could mean two things:\n\n\nThe way they are moving up in the world. They’re becoming one of the most important people in the world.\nThe move they are making during sex got them have fantastic orgasms that have them on top of the world.", "annotation_id": "1116407", "url": "https://genius.com/1116407", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bossy Lady", "line": "Smoke junkie kush funkier than Parliament", "vault_lines": ["Smoke junkie kush funkier than Parliament"], "meaning": "Parliament is a groundbreaking 70’s funkadelic band fronted by the brilliant and eccentric George Clinton.", "annotation_id": "1116395", "url": "https://genius.com/1116395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bossy Lady", "line": "Baby, you You shine just like I do", "vault_lines": ["You shine just like I do"], "meaning": "He’s a shining star, and his girl is shining just like he is. Shining could also be seen in the meaning of shining jewelry. Ross is known for his massive amount of jewelry, and because of Ross, his girl now also has a lot of jewelry.", "annotation_id": "1116390", "url": "https://genius.com/1116390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bossy Lady", "line": "My kicks brown, now I’m lookin’ for Rihanna and ’em", "vault_lines": ["My kicks brown, now I'm lookin' for Rihanna and 'em"], "meaning": "Pun about Chris Brown and Rihanna.\nAt around the time this song was made they where the perfect couple. He is looking for his Rihanna now.\nI really don’t think he would be saying this right now though.", "annotation_id": "1116376", "url": "https://genius.com/1116376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bossy Lady", "line": "To deal with a dude like me, baby, you gotta be the HBIC", "vault_lines": ["To deal with a dude like me, baby, you gotta be the HBIC"], "meaning": "To be able to deal and handle a man like Rick Ross you have to be the ‘Head Bitch In Charge’ as the next line of the verse will tell us.\n\nThis line might also mean that the girl has to be the number one girl because he has plenty following him.", "annotation_id": "1116359", "url": "https://genius.com/1116359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
