{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bottles and Rocking J’s", "line": "This DJ Khaled, We The Best", "vault_lines": ["Shit, them hoes love it too, this DJ Khaled, We The Best"], "meaning": "DJ Khaled’s record label, motto, and two of his studio albums feature this phrase in their title: We The Best and We The Best Forever.", "annotation_id": "260968", "url": "https://genius.com/260968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bottles and Rocking J’s", "line": "Pictures of Boston George", "vault_lines": ["Fifty floors, marble walls, pictures of Boston George"], "meaning": "George Jacob Jung was instrumental in the cocaine trade during the 1970s and 80s.  Ross has a penchant for naming old school criminals in his songs so this is just another addition to the list.\n\n\n\nThe 2001 movie Blow was based on his life and it stars Johnny Depp as George Jung.", "annotation_id": "246494", "url": "https://genius.com/246494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bottles and Rocking J’s", "line": "Young Moula, baby", "vault_lines": ["WHOOO! Young Moula, baby"], "meaning": "Moula is another word for money.  Wayne is just saying “Young Money” which is the name of his record label.", "annotation_id": "246429", "url": "https://genius.com/246429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bottles and Rocking J’s", "line": "But tonight we on that Red Berry and Cranberry", "vault_lines": ["But tonight we on that Red Berry and Cranberry"], "meaning": "Fab has developed a penchant for creating drinks with CÎROC vodka, here he mixes Red Berry CÎROC with Cranberry juice which is also called the “Tiger Blood”.", "annotation_id": "246403", "url": "https://genius.com/246403", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bottles and Rocking J’s", "line": "Raise a glass for erry’body that’s done something from nothin’", "vault_lines": ["Raise a glass for erry'body that's done something from nothin'"], "meaning": "A slick reference to Fab’s fourth album From Nothin' To Somethin', released in 2007.", "annotation_id": "239839", "url": "https://genius.com/239839", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bottles and Rocking J’s", "line": "Sippin’ on that purp", "vault_lines": ["Sippin' on that purp"], "meaning": "Wayne uses “purp” to refer to the color of the drink he usually sips on that contains prescription-strength cough syrup (which has the powerful drugs codeine and promethazine) which is added to Sprite or Mountain Dew along with Jolly Ranchers and is most often purple in Hue.", "annotation_id": "239334", "url": "https://genius.com/239334", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
