{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Chad and Evelyn evidence, just a block away", "vault_lines": ["Chad and Evelyn evidence, just a block away"], "meaning": "Chad Johnson and Evelyn Lozada were married for 41 days before Chad headbutted her in their car after she mentioned she wanted to have kids and he did not.", "annotation_id": "9024864", "url": "https://genius.com/9024864", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "10 mil’ in a duffle, make a nigga shiver", "vault_lines": ["10 mil' in a duffle, make a nigga shiver"], "meaning": "10 million dollars in front of anybody would make you shiver", "annotation_id": "4029974", "url": "https://genius.com/4029974", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "You makin’ wack songs with the nice titles", "vault_lines": ["You makin' wack songs with the nice titles"], "meaning": "#Shots fired?!\n\nMaybe a reference to 2Chainz, as his songs do have some very nice titles, such as Beautiful Pain, and Black Unicorn. Some of them even resemble the Ebonics way 2Pac named his songs, like You Da Realest, and Wut We Doin?. 2Chainz even calls himself 2Pac with out a nose ring, but he does seem to compare himself to other great rappers as well. Rick Ross continues with “All chains, no rings, never see the finals”. With the fact that 2Chainz wear all chains, this very well may be a diss.\n\nHowever, 2Chainz has “rings”, like a Soul Train award for best rap song, “Mercy”, but that was a feature. Also he has seen “finals” such as many nominates for Grammies and BET Hip Hop awards. Then again, it may be a jab at his failed basketball career.", "annotation_id": "2625955", "url": "https://genius.com/2625955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Scott Dis’nick,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Scott Ryan Disick is an American reality television personality, model and businessman. Disick is best known for appearing on the TV series Keeping Up With the Kardashians by dating Kourtney Kardashian. This could also be a reference to the original “Bound 2” song where Yeezy is talking about his fiance Kim Kardashian.", "annotation_id": "2619530", "url": "https://genius.com/2619530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "She ready for this dope boy dialect", "vault_lines": ["She ready for this dope boy dialect"], "meaning": "Rick Ross poses like a drug kingpin in his raps. Drug dealers use words such as “yeyo”, “lines” etc. in relation to drugs. The girl i s ready for that.\n\nFor further reference :http://www15.uta.fi/FAST/GC/drugslan.html", "annotation_id": "2619236", "url": "https://genius.com/2619236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Run in your home, put your infant in a blender Sip on a smoothie, or give it up smoothly", "vault_lines": ["Run in your home, put your infant in a blender", "Sip on a smoothie, or give it up smoothly"], "meaning": "Clever wordplay and references. A smoothie is made by mixing several ingredients such as fruits, milks, yogurts, ice, and more into a blender.\n\nAs you come home, you fight with your baby mother, making your child cry in the process, putting them in a blender of feelings.\n\nSippin' on a smoothie can be that you are cheating on her with someone younger, which may have been the reason you two were fighting.\n\nIn the end, you may choose to leave, giving up smoothly. Although it is an easy choice for you, you’re putting your offspring into a bad predicament by walking out on your family. This may lead to a string of bad choices, hatred for you, and a sense of being unloved. In regardless, your child is still growing, “in the blender”. Maybe he or she might grow up to be a smoothie?", "annotation_id": "2619129", "url": "https://genius.com/2619129", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Do the bitches love you when you out the league? Will my car still crank when I hit the keys?", "vault_lines": ["Do the bitches love you when you out the league?", "Will my car still crank when I hit the keys?"], "meaning": "When you’re no longer Superman, at least you know you got Lois Lane\n\nIt’s a rhetorical question. Rick Ross is comparing a woman’s love to turning on your car using keys. Obviously, your car will turn on. Even though you may leave the “league” and retire from the fame, fortune, and money, your women will still love you. That includes hoes and side bitches too.", "annotation_id": "2619097", "url": "https://genius.com/2619097", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Black bottle boy, nigga blazin’ peach", "vault_lines": ["Black bottle boy, nigga blazin' peach"], "meaning": "Referring to his endorsement of Belaire Rosé. which is dubbed France’s most exquiste rosé. This also paved way for the MMG mixtape series Black Bottle Boys.\n\n\n\nAlso he is imbiding in Peach Kush, which gets its name from smelling like a Peach, and having the aftertaste in your throat being that of a peach.\n\n\n\nTo further cement this, the lifestyle brand @blackbottleboys was created for all those who live the life and want to celebrate in style, like Rick Ross and Diddy.", "annotation_id": "2618363", "url": "https://genius.com/2618363", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Rich Forever", "vault_lines": ["May we live long, rich forever"], "meaning": "Clearly a reference to Rozay’s song and mixtape of the same name.\n\n\n\nHowever, considering that Rozay is using one of Kanye’s songs, it could also be a reference to lyrics by Kanye on Chris Brown’s “Deuces Remix” where Kanye, referring to Amber Rose says: “You gonna be hot a little while, I’mma be rich forever.”", "annotation_id": "2618335", "url": "https://genius.com/2618335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "All chains, no rings, never see the finals", "vault_lines": ["All chains, no rings, never see the finals"], "meaning": "This line continues off Rozay’s earlier basketball reference. In the NBA, when a team wins it all, every player on the winning team is rewarded with championship rings. You only have the chains that you bought for yourself and don’t own a single ring, in fact you’re so wack, you don’t even get a chance to compete for the ring! Basically, to Rozay you’re all flash and talk, with little critical success to show for it.\n\n\n\nIt’s likely that Rozay implies he has plenty of rings, like basketball legend Michael Jordan.", "annotation_id": "2618318", "url": "https://genius.com/2618318", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Let me rewind that, G-shit, let me rewind that Check, I just wanna know your mindset Here starin’ at your fine ex Damn, this where you put your time at Unappreciated like that Timex", "vault_lines": ["Let me rewind that, G-shit, let me rewind that"], "meaning": "Especially during freestyled verses, rappers will call upon the mixer to “rewind” what they’ve said so as to start the verse over with a better flow, or to regain their lyrics. Check Action Bronson’s usage of this on “Pouches of Tuna”, the opener to his mixtape Blue Chips.", "annotation_id": "2618314", "url": "https://genius.com/2618314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Ruthless Records, next Eazy to be", "vault_lines": ["Ruthless Records, next Eazy to be"], "meaning": "Ruthless Records was a label founded by rap legend and N.W.A. member Eazy-E. N.W.A. is easily considered one of the most prolific groups in rap and therefore the label as a whole held a high pedigree for its signees. Rozay is comparing his label MMG or Maybach Music Group to this label, foreshadowing MMG’s continuing success with Rozay as the front-man (like Eazy-E was) for the label. In addition, Rick Ross' stage persona is that of a ruthless gangster, a descendant of Eazy’s style.", "annotation_id": "2618300", "url": "https://genius.com/2618300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Got a thing for Khloe, Lamar lost his feet", "vault_lines": ["Got a thing for Khloe, Lamar lost his feet"], "meaning": "Rozay is interested in Khloe Kardashian who is (but soon won’t be) married to Lamar Odom a basketball player for the LA Clippers. Rozay likely has a chance too, since they are getting divorced, likely due to Lamar’s constant substance abuse (with both crack and alcohol). You could definitely say he’s lost his feet in the relationship and somewhat in his life lately, which also plays nicely with the fact that he is a basketball player–a job where keeping your feet planted is important.\n\n\n\nThis is an interesting line, considering Bound 2 is a love song that Kanye wrote for Kim Kardashian, Khloe’s sister.\n\nFunnily enough, not many dudes are into her, as Eminem put it in “Berzerk”: she is “The ugly Kardashian”.", "annotation_id": "2618287", "url": "https://genius.com/2618287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Standin’ on my own, Anderson Silva Break a bone, nigga gone ’til November", "vault_lines": ["Standin' on my own, Anderson Silva", "Break a bone, nigga gone 'til November"], "meaning": "This was written shortly after UFC fighter Anderson Silva broke his leg in a gruesome looking incident when fighting in a match in late December 2013:\n\n\n\n\n\n#COLD ROZAY", "annotation_id": "2618266", "url": "https://genius.com/2618266", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Damn, this where you put your time at Unappreciated like that Timex", "vault_lines": ["Unappreciated like that Timex"], "meaning": "Rozay creates a homonym on Timex and doing so, plays off “time”:\n\n\nTimex as in the watch brand. Hence others don’t appreciate time.\nTimex referring to the bathroom scales, Ross implies the drug dealing game is unappreciated.", "annotation_id": "2618260", "url": "https://genius.com/2618260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "The East Coast meets Kanye West", "vault_lines": ["The East Coast meets Kanye West"], "meaning": "For this track, Rozay (a rapper from Carol City, Florida) is remixing a track made by the Chi-town legend, Kanye West. The two have built an impressive collaboration record:\n\n\nKanye’s “Monster”\n\nKanye’s “Devil in a New Dress”\n\nRozay’s “Live Fast, Die Young”\n\nRozay’s “Maybach Music II”\n\n\nDJ Khaled’s “I Wish You Would”", "annotation_id": "2618253", "url": "https://genius.com/2618253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "Death Row reeks underneath my breath", "vault_lines": ["Death Row reeks underneath my breath"], "meaning": "Death Row was a record label that was arguably the biggest rap label in the 1990’s. It’s signees included 2Pac, Dr. Dre, and Snoop Dogg. It’s worth noting that while Ross compares himself to the likes of the fabled Death Row Records, he has compared himself to 2Pac in multiple songs, even having a verse on “I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie”:\n\nFour chains, big studs, a nigga too fly \nTop down, tank top, I think I’m 2Pac", "annotation_id": "2618247", "url": "https://genius.com/2618247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bound 2 Freestyle", "line": "[Bridge: Charlie Wilson]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "All of this is borrowed from the original version. Check out the original annotations here!", "annotation_id": "2618245", "url": "https://genius.com/2618245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
