{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "MMG, cut that check", "vault_lines": ["MMG, cut that check"], "meaning": "MMG or Maybach Music Group is a music label headed up by Rick Ross. So Kutta is obviously stating that he is signed to MMG and that he will be receiving a check for his verse soon", "annotation_id": "3377377", "url": "https://genius.com/3377377", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Dying, always on my mind for real", "vault_lines": ["Dying, always on my mind for real"], "meaning": "When you are a target you always have to expect someone trying to off you. This is especially true for Rick Ross, since the Gangsta Disciples have a hit out on him for the “B.M.F. song” about him not giving them loyalties for mentioning Larry Hoover (The founder of GD) in the song.", "annotation_id": "2252278", "url": "https://genius.com/2252278", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Now everybody ridin’ dirty like it ain’t no soap", "vault_lines": ["Now everybody ridin' dirty like it ain't no soap"], "meaning": "Very funny and clever: when you are riding illegal (without driver license, insurance, or registration) it is referred to as riding “dirty”. So he is using the soap to make reference to an actual physical state of being dirty.", "annotation_id": "2231313", "url": "https://genius.com/2231313", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Sky Dweller my watch", "vault_lines": ["Sky Dweller my watch"], "meaning": "Torch claims to have a Rolex Sky-Dweller, which runs around 45-50k. A very expensive watch, for someone about that life.", "annotation_id": "2229241", "url": "https://genius.com/2229241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "[Intro: Ric Flair] It’s so hard for me to sit back here, in this studio Looking at a guy out here, hollering my name When last year I spent more money on spilt liquor In bars from one side of this world to the other, than you made You’re talking to the Rolex wearing Diamond ring wearing, kiss stealing, woo! Wheeling dealing, limousine riding, jet flying son of a gun And I’ma have a hard time, holding these alligators back", "vault_lines": ["And I'ma have a hard time, holding these alligators back"], "meaning": "“The Nature Boy” Ric Flair aka “the dirtiest player in the game” was a legendary wrestler for NWA, WCW, WWF, WWE, and more. He was famous for his in-ring antics such as strutting and his catchphrase, “Wooooooo!” He also actually lived the lavish lifestyle he talked about, with his stylish looks, jewelry, pricey cars and many women.\n\nThis is sampled from Ric Flair’s What Dreams Are Made of Speech, which was also used in reference Pusha T’s “What Dreams Are Made of”, who is also a very big fan of Ric Flair.\n\nFrench Montana also gives Ric Flair a shout out in his verse in this song.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oESVMyJ20Ik", "annotation_id": "2219316", "url": "https://genius.com/2219316", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "[Leaked Verse 1: Diddy]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Note that neither Ross nor Diddy’s verses are included on the album version of this song.", "annotation_id": "2211639", "url": "https://genius.com/2211639", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "That bitch you lovin’ we popped that", "vault_lines": ["That bitch you lovin' we popped that"], "meaning": "He even made love to your chick, along with his team.", "annotation_id": "2202453", "url": "https://genius.com/2202453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "That price tag you ain’t bout that", "vault_lines": ["That price tag you ain't bout that"], "meaning": "French spends money on things that others can’t even dream of buying, because of his large bank account.", "annotation_id": "2201226", "url": "https://genius.com/2201226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Anybody wanna act loco? Who you with? Numerous shots from the .44", "vault_lines": ["Who you with? Numerous shots from the .44"], "meaning": "This is a line borrowed from the Jay-Z classic “Nigga What, Nigga Who (Originator ‘99)”, where Jay says a similar line:\n\nMotherfuckers wanna act loco, hit em with numerous shots with the fo'-fo'\n\nBasically if you start acting crazy, he isn’t going to put up with it.", "annotation_id": "2201168", "url": "https://genius.com/2201168", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "That nigga right there, that nigga right there Look at that nigga right there That bitch right there, that bitch right there Look at that bitch right there You ain’t bout that life, you ain’t bout that", "vault_lines": ["Look at that nigga right there", "That bitch right there, that bitch right there", "Look at that bitch right there", "You ain't bout that life, you ain't bout that"], "meaning": "French is calling out those who are clearly not about that life.\n\n\n\nThis could also be a reference a song he is featured in called “Right There”, the hook goes:\n\nBitch right there, look at that bitch right there, look at that bitch right there X3", "annotation_id": "2201147", "url": "https://genius.com/2201147", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Empire, always what I want to build", "vault_lines": ["Empire, always what I want to build"], "meaning": "Although Rick Ross formerly claimed that he was “rich off cocaine” and had connections in the game, he has since come clean about his past.  Still, it shows how focused he’s been from the beginning on building something powerful.  Nowadays he really is building a musical empire with his Maybach Music Group.", "annotation_id": "2196145", "url": "https://genius.com/2196145", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Them Self Made niggas, Volume 3", "vault_lines": ["Them Self Made niggas, Volume 3"], "meaning": "The third installment of the Self Made series by Rick Ross’s Maybach Music Group (MMG), available September 17, 2013.", "annotation_id": "2195984", "url": "https://genius.com/2195984", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Bike life on your bitch nigga Pop a wheelie all in that pussy, she switchin’ gears on this dick nigga", "vault_lines": ["Pop a wheelie all in that pussy, she switchin' gears on this dick nigga"], "meaning": "Meek is an avid biker, so it’s no surprise that he’s comparing bike riding to him fucking your girl.\n\nWhen you switch gears on a bike, you change the speed. His girl is going wild!", "annotation_id": "2194881", "url": "https://genius.com/2194881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Rollie gold, I’m Michael Corleone Scarface bitch I got it goin’ on", "vault_lines": ["Rollie gold, I'm Michael Corleone", "Scarface bitch I got it goin' on"], "meaning": "Michael Corleone was the main character of The Godfather trilogy, and Scarface was a drug kingpin, both of which were portrayed by Al Pacino.", "annotation_id": "2194863", "url": "https://genius.com/2194863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Shorty got that Ric Flair pussy like woo", "vault_lines": ["Shorty got that Ric Flair pussy like woo"], "meaning": "French really emphasizes the “woo” he says, sounding a lot like the WWF legend “The Nature Boy” Ric Flair.\n\n\n\nThe word French uses to describe his womans hoo ha is woo, meaning great.\n\nAlso a reference to the hook, where Ric Flair is featured.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/FrencHMonTanA/status/380083392895025152", "annotation_id": "2194073", "url": "https://genius.com/2194073", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bout That Life", "line": "Ho shut your mouth when you in the presence of kings I ball like LeBron but I got a couple more rings", "vault_lines": ["Ho shut your mouth when you in the presence of kings", "I ball like LeBron but I got a couple more rings"], "meaning": "LeBron James (King James) is known as the best basketball player in the game today, he’s won 2 NBA Finals, giving him 2 rings.\n\n\n\nDiddy is a king of the rap game, and he compares his “balling” to that of LeBron’s. But instead, he balls in the sense of living a rich, upper class life. Diddy actually has the most money of any rapper, currently having a net worth of 580 million dollars!\n\nYou better believe he has more than 2 rings to his collection..", "annotation_id": "2194033", "url": "https://genius.com/2194033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
