{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "T-Street’s my brother", "vault_lines": [", FeFe's my brother"], "meaning": "T-Streets was one of the first people to sign to now classic label Young Money Entertainment, an imprint of Cash Money Records. This wasn’t Lil Wayne’s last time mentioning T-Streets as he mentions his name again in “Rollin' on Sorry 4 The Wait.", "annotation_id": "35387720", "url": "https://genius.com/35387720", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "I go into the booth and just change like Clark Kent", "vault_lines": ["I go into the booth and just change like Clark Kent"], "meaning": "This is just like his line on “I’m A Beast” which is a song on the same mixtape where he says “The door close to the booth I feel like a caged lion.”\nIn this line he claims he changes in the booth every time he goes in there and transforms into rapping Lil Wayne just like how fictional person Clark Kent changes into fictional hero Superman.", "annotation_id": "35387648", "url": "https://genius.com/35387648", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "Miami", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Lil Wayne said “Miami” for what appears to be no reason, he said this to make his previous line, ending with dolphin a bar. Miami Dolphins are a football team.", "annotation_id": "35387632", "url": "https://genius.com/35387632", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
