{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "Definition of that brown paper bag money", "vault_lines": ["Definition of that brown paper bag money"], "meaning": "Fat Joe is using a Double Entendre to great effect here, the first being that he sold drugs making his money handling brown paper bags. The other being that since the bags aren’t transparent you can’t its contents, Joe is saying know one knows what is inside of him", "annotation_id": "74549", "url": "https://genius.com/74549", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "I’m by myself cause niggas run they mouths like auctions", "vault_lines": ["I'm by myself cause niggas run they mouths like auctions"], "meaning": "He doesn’t trust anybody because people talk shit. He uses the idiom “running your mouth” to compare them to people who go back and forth offering a higher bid on an item.", "annotation_id": "57958", "url": "https://genius.com/57958", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "Practice make perfect, I’m relaxing at rehearsal I’m a mothafuckin’ professional, like Herschel Walker, the talk of the game, is I But I wonder will they still be talkin’ after I die", "vault_lines": ["Practice make perfect, I'm relaxing at rehearsal", "I'm a mothafuckin' professional, like Herschel", "Walker, the talk of the game, is I"], "meaning": "Herschel Walker is a Hall of Fame player. Former running back for the Dallas Cowboys. Lil' Wayne is referring to his legendary status and if he will remain important even after his death.", "annotation_id": "31289", "url": "https://genius.com/31289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "They used to call me the Pyrex kid (Who?) A.K.A. Young Arm & Hammer (Young) In the kitchen with the pots, yeah I worked the glass", "vault_lines": ["They used to call me the Pyrex kid (Who?)", "A.K.A. Young Arm & Hammer (Young)", "In the kitchen with the pots, yeah I worked the glass"], "meaning": "Pyrex is a company that sells no-stick glass products, which is ideal for people who want to cook crack.\n\nArm & Hammer is one of more well-known brands of baking soda (the primary ingredient to make crack).\n\nI don’t know the recipe; I’m just sayin'…\n-Katt Williams", "annotation_id": "31284", "url": "https://genius.com/31284", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Brown Paper Bag", "line": "Try front and I’ll zip you in a bag, money", "vault_lines": ["Try front and I'll zip you in a bag, money"], "meaning": "Joey is saying that if you front on him, he’ll kill you and “zip you” in a body bag. Money is a term that is used like “bro” or “homie” in some areas.", "annotation_id": "31140", "url": "https://genius.com/31140", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
