{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "I come lookin’ for you with Haitians", "vault_lines": ["I come lookin' for you with Haitians"], "meaning": "Future intends to track you down with his Haitian associates, surely for no benevolent purpose.\n\nThis may imply that Future is affiliated with Zoe Pound, a fearsome Haitian-American gang native to south Florida. Zoe Pound members are alleged to practice voodoo (Vodun) and kill their enemies in gruesome ways.", "annotation_id": "31992062", "url": "https://genius.com/31992062", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "Give me a pistol, then run with the K’s", "vault_lines": ["Give me a pistol, then run with the K's"], "meaning": "Ace Hood is assuring you even with just a pistol (a small firearm) that he could hold his own in an environment where every other goon has a ‘K’, which is a slang name for an “AK-47”, an automatic assault rifle much more deadly than a handgun.\n\n\n\nK’s could also be referring to a kilo(gram) of cocaine- approximately 2.2 pounds of weight. This double entendre suggest that in the drug industry you don’t need any significant weaponry to manage to make it back home safe.", "annotation_id": "2024624", "url": "https://genius.com/2024624", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "I woke up in a new Bugatti (Yeah, yeah, yeah) I woke up in a new Bugatti (Woah, skrrt) I woke up in a new Bugatti (Woah, turn up) I woke up in a new Bugatti (Woah) I woke up in a new Bugatti (Woo, woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["I woke up in a new Bugatti (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5237520692001", "annotation_id": "1890124", "url": "https://genius.com/1890124", "state": "verified", "votes": 156, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "Millionaire nigga, no rumor, livin’ my life off of tuna", "vault_lines": ["Millionaire nigga, no rumor, livin' my life off of tuna"], "meaning": "Unlike other rappers who claim to be millionaires but can’t back up the talk, Ace is worth approximately $5 million. The success of this song only helped him out even more.\n\nNot bad for a guy who was at one point broke even after putting out two albums.", "annotation_id": "1737004", "url": "https://genius.com/1737004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "Super, Future", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A reference to Future’s Super Future mixtape, which was supposed to come out on 10/23/13 but was postponed so that he could work on Pluto 3-D and his sophomore album, Future Hendrix, which comes out this year.\n\n\n\nThe album has since been renamed Honest and was released on April 22, 2014.", "annotation_id": "1630239", "url": "https://genius.com/1630239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "Signin’ bonus, hit that man that’s from thirty feet (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Signin' bonus, hit that man that's from thirty feet (Woo)"], "meaning": "Ross follows up on the basketball metaphor in the previously line.\n\nIn basketball, a signing bonus is guaranteed money. In the D-League, most players don’t get signing bonuses, however Ross' shooters do get guaranteed money because they are guaranteed to kill.\n\nRozay awards signing bonuses to his gun shooters that can hit a target from 30 feet away, much like a D-League shooter might earn a bonus as their next 10 day contract from an NBA team if they can hit open shots. 30 feet is a bit of a stretch though, as an NBA three is 22 feet to 23.75 feet.", "annotation_id": "1522648", "url": "https://genius.com/1522648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "That’s why I hustle for half a key, that’s twelve G’s (G)", "vault_lines": ["That's why I hustle for half a key, that's twelve G's (G)"], "meaning": "Following up on from the previous line, Ross explains he sells cocaine in order to let his mother retire comfortably, as he was tired of watching her struggle.\n\nIn Miami, a kilo of coke is worth of 20K-28.5K, so when Ross is selling $12K for a half a kilo, he might be asking for too much.", "annotation_id": "1508526", "url": "https://genius.com/1508526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "You gotta love me, I got shooters out the D-League (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["You gotta love me, I got shooters out the D-League (Woah)"], "meaning": "An extended basketball metaphor. A shooter is a basketball player that can make long-range buckets, usually 3 pointers. In this case, Ross' shooters are killers.\n\nThe NBA Developmental League or D-League is the NBA’s official minor league basketball organization, which refers back to the original basketball metaphor. When Ross mentions “D-League”, he’s probably referring to a dope league of some sort.\n\nNBA teams usually go to the D-League to find a new role player or bench player for their team. Ross is saying that he has players on his team who’s sole purpose is to shoot and fulfill that role, because those type of soldiers are rarely the famous, successful ones; instead, they are known more for their effort and hustle.\n\nYet in rare cases they do sometimes win games for you:", "annotation_id": "1421132", "url": "https://genius.com/1421132", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bugatti", "line": "Ricky Rozay and Ace Hood, we hella Trill Yeah", "vault_lines": ["Ricky Rozay and Ace Hood, we hella Trill"], "meaning": "‘Trill’ is a slang word/lifestyle popularized by duo UGK, a portmanteau of “true” & “real”. Ross and Ace are close friends like both UGK members, and have worked numerous times, from “Cash Flow”, to “Get Money”, to “The Realist Livin”, “Hustle Hard Remix”, this song, etc.", "annotation_id": "1421120", "url": "https://genius.com/1421120", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
