{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bury Me a G", "line": "They told me it’s never too late for prayer (M-M-Maybach Music) Well Lord, pray for us niggas Cause we ready to die bout this shit", "vault_lines": ["Cause we ready to die bout this shit"], "meaning": "Bury Me a G concludes Self Made Vol. 2, the next time we hear from Rick Ross on a label release is God Forgives I Don’t which begins with the prayer that Ross requests.", "annotation_id": "1299954", "url": "https://genius.com/1299954", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bury Me a G", "line": "Should I die, lay me next to my daughter Lelah and my partner", "vault_lines": ["Should I die, lay me next to my daughter Lelah and my partner"], "meaning": "Two important people in T.I.’s life have already passed on – his daughter Lelah, who was miscarried, and his lifelong friend Philant Johnson, who was murdered in 2006", "annotation_id": "862115", "url": "https://genius.com/862115", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bury Me a G", "line": "Every gun I had was one the home invaders couldn’t use", "vault_lines": ["Every gun I had was one the home invaders couldn't use"], "meaning": "Tip went into more detail with the Daily Beast about the circumstances surrounding his arrest:\n\n\n The Daily Beast: I’ve always been curious about the initial weapons arrest, and why you needed this heavy arsenal of automatic machine guns with silencers on them.\n\n T.I.: Well, to understand that, you need to understand my specific circumstances. An attempt was made on my life, and the life of a friend [Philant Johnson] was taken. Those people had never been brought to justice. They were still out there and I was getting anonymous threats. They were identifying themselves as the ones who initiated that first attack, saying, “We’re going to finish the job … We know where you live,” so I was advised by my security to upgrade the equipment. Quite naturally, I was paranoid and concerned about mine and my family’s safety.", "annotation_id": "862103", "url": "https://genius.com/862103", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bury Me a G", "line": "Know that ATF listening, I’m just playing, I’m just playing", "vault_lines": ["Know that ATF listening, I'm just playing, I'm just playing"], "meaning": "T.I. ran into some real-life trouble in 2007 when the ATF raided his house and found stockpiles of weapons. He knows the ATF is probably listening to everything he says so he defers all if his marksman talk by adding the line “I’m just playing”. Better watch out, TIP..", "annotation_id": "861146", "url": "https://genius.com/861146", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bury Me a G", "line": "Machine gun man, seen him on the news", "vault_lines": ["Machine gun man, seen him on the news"], "meaning": "T.I. did some jail time for very serious automatic weapons charges after a 2007 arrest.  He claimed that the guns (and silencers!) he bought were for self-defense\n\nCheck out the sick collection of weapons the federal agents found in T.I.’s home here", "annotation_id": "859929", "url": "https://genius.com/859929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bury Me a G", "line": "If I die tonight, I pray I get buried in clean drawers Line us all up, just bury me with my dawgs If I die tonight, I pray I get buried in clean drawers Line us all up, just bury me with my dawgs Bury me with my dawgs, bury me with my dawgs Line us all up, bury me with my dawgs Bury me with my dawgs, bury me with my dawgs Line us all up, bury me with my dawgs", "vault_lines": ["If I die tonight, I pray I get buried in clean drawers", "Line us all up, just bury me with my dawgs", "Bury me with my dawgs, bury me with my dawgs", "Line us all up, bury me with my dawgs"], "meaning": "Rick Ross isn’t concerned about death. But, should he die he wants to be wearing clean, fresh clothes and to be buried in a group, lined up with his homies. It’s all about respect and family.\n\n\n\nReminiscent of the “John” hook:\n\nIf I die today, remember me like John Lennon\nBuried in Louis, I’m talking all brown linen, huh\n\nIt is also reminiscent of Boots Riley’s touching reminder to his daughter to wear clean draws", "annotation_id": "859409", "url": "https://genius.com/859409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Bury Me a G", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-bury-me-a-g-lyrics", "genius_title": "Bury Me a G", "genius_id": 78674, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "And I know how to pitch, so I’ma get your bitch to drive", "vault_lines": ["And I know how to pitch, so I'ma get your bitch to drive"], "meaning": "In 2011, Gucci Mane was accused of pushing a woman out of a moving vehicle during an argument. Safe to say women are safer in the driver’s seat when Gucci is in the vehicle. Over the years, Gucci Mane has worked on personal growth, addressing his past behavior and legal issues.", "annotation_id": "33080951", "url": "https://genius.com/33080951", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Been bought my mama a crib", "vault_lines": ["Been bought my mama a crib"], "meaning": "2 Chainz had recently purchased a new home for his mother.\n\n\n\nHe later says in his song 4 AM:\nhttps://genius.com/11938660", "annotation_id": "15781932", "url": "https://genius.com/15781932", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Sellin’ dope just like dunkin’ to niggas, uh This is a windmill, I smell like 10 mil’", "vault_lines": ["Sellin' dope just like dunkin' to niggas, uh", "This is a windmill, I smell like 10 mil'"], "meaning": "2 Chainz stands at 6'5\", making it fairly easy for him to slam dunk a basketball. Selling dope to him is just as easy. 2 Chainz compares how smooth, and simple it is for him with the “Windmill Dunk”, a classic dunk with 1 simple move. This is where the dunker takes the ball from the waist with his arm fully extended and slams the ball in the hoop by making a half circle motion with his arm.", "annotation_id": "14229729", "url": "https://genius.com/14229729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "We got Gucci Mane, 2 Chainz and Rick Ross And we’re here for the “Buy Back the Block” movement Where we raise up the community and support and love us", "vault_lines": ["Where we raise up the community and support and love us"], "meaning": "The ‘Buy Back The Block’ movement is a movement that has been gaining traction in most economically depressed areas in the U.S.A.\n\n‘Buy Back The Block’ means to be so successful to the point when a man can buy an entire neighborhood.\n\n‘Buy Back The Block’ also means to eradicate black on black violence in economically depressed areas.", "annotation_id": "13033473", "url": "https://genius.com/13033473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Hey it’s your girl Super Cindy reporting live From the corner of 183rd Street and 27th Avenue At Checkers, in Miami Gardens", "vault_lines": ["At Checkers, in Miami Gardens"], "meaning": "Before Rick Ross was “The Boss,” he was posted up at a local car wash at 13 years old, making a mere $30 per day for every 12-hour shift he religiously worked. Since then, the 40-year-old Maybach Music Group mogul has secured several Wingstop locations across the nation and also recently finalized a deal with Checkers restaurant franchise\n\n  “At age 13, I made 30 dollars a day 8am to 8pm plus tips at the shell car wash on 183rd St and 27th avenue in Carol City. We now own 30 Wingstop franchises.”\n\n\n\nsources:- http://www.hiphopdx.com\n                - Rick Ross' snapchat (ferrarifatboy)", "annotation_id": "11661420", "url": "https://genius.com/11661420", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "I’m goin’ live, I’m, I’m still alive", "vault_lines": ["I'm goin' live, I'm, I'm still alive"], "meaning": "Gucci Mane told the hosts of Highly Questionable that he was scared that someone was coming for his life before his most recent stint in prison. Gucci is happy to still have his life despite the chaos before being locked up.\n\nI just kinda, in my mind I felt like someone was going to try to hurt me, try to rob me, do something to force my hand and defend myself and hurt them.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/5gmN0GuTZS8", "annotation_id": "11226540", "url": "https://genius.com/11226540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Been had the Rollie, been ate bologna", "vault_lines": ["Been had the Rollie, been ate bologna"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is a true rags to riches story. He came from a one bedroom apartment with his mother in College Park, Georgia all the way to rap fame. He has highlighted his struggles by stating that he used to ride public transportation, struggle to put food on the table, and even sell drugs to his own mom. Bologna is a typical cheap food that 2 Chainz ate when he was poor, but now he has a nice watch to show for his success.", "annotation_id": "11226513", "url": "https://genius.com/11226513", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Nigga no treadmill, you niggas just stand still", "vault_lines": ["Nigga no treadmill, you niggas just stand still"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is making moves while everyone else just sits and does nothing. Tit implies that you need to work hard in order to accomplish the things that he has, rather than just sitting around, thus the “no tredmill” reference.", "annotation_id": "11226501", "url": "https://genius.com/11226501", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Just closed on a Cali crib, ’round the corner from Kobe", "vault_lines": ["Just closed on a Cali crib, 'round the corner from Kobe"], "meaning": "2 Chainz just bought a $2 million dollar Hollywood Hills home in October of 2016. This house was previously owned by guitarist Steve Vai. Conveniently, the house is in close proximity to Kobe, one of 2 Chainz' favorite basketball players.", "annotation_id": "11226447", "url": "https://genius.com/11226447", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Just bought two studios ’cause I got so much shit to say", "vault_lines": ["Just bought two studios 'cause I got so much shit to say"], "meaning": "Gucci is using hyperbole when saying he bought 2 studios (because it’s physically impossible to record in two studios at once). Gucci is saying that while locked up he wasn’t able to tell the world anything, so he is going to use his newfound freedom to share everything he’s been waiting to say.\n\nThis sentiment is echoed on the first track off of “Everybody Looking”, Gucci’s first album since being released from prison, https://genius.com/Gucci-mane-no-sleep-intro-lyrics", "annotation_id": "11091364", "url": "https://genius.com/11091364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "[Music Video Skit]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Gucci:\nBro I’m gettin' tired of washing these mo'fuckin' cars man. Bro you gettin' tired of this shit?\n\nRoss: I been tired, but I told you what we gotta do is buy something that’s going to make us some money.\n\nGucci: We need to come up with a plan then mane.\n\nRoss: I told you I saw this lil [?] spot up the street  for sale. We might need to do it, it’s a lil' jugg, even if it’s a—\n\nGucci:\nHow we gon' get the money?\n\nRoss:\nWhat happened to the lick you said we was gone hit?\n\nGucci:\nI fucked around and lost $1200 gambling yesterday.\n\nRoss:\nThe dice game got you?  $1200?\n\nGucci: Fucked me over mane.\n\nRoss: Oooh, that’s how I know you toast, you ready to go from eight dollars a wash to seventeen.\n\nGucci:\nShit I might go motherfucka' down to five dollars a wash how my pockets lookin' right now man.\n\nRoss:\nFive dollars a peel for the wax. [Laughs.]\n\nRoss: You got the text this morning I sent you right.\n\nGucci: Yeah I got it.\n\nRoss: He talking ‘bout he finna go out of town two months early and he need his rent.\n\nGucci: He need his rent now?\n\nRoss: Man he acting like we god damn charging a hundred a wash and we doing 100 cars I told that boy I mean like shit how many cars do you think we washing man? I said I ain’t with that we ain’t washin' all that many cars\n\nGucci: Ay, who is buddy mane?\n\n[Tom Cat] Who the fuck is me?\nNigga I’m Tom Cat, down south car wash right here man. Where you at, where you workin'? Listen here fellas, hate to break the news..man. This what wrong with you young niggas. Get the window man, look at the window.\n\nGucci: Man fuck the window\n\n[Tom Cat] Let me tell you something, you young niggas don’t listen. But I'mma tell you something today, I gotta get outta town. Y'all got two months. $2500, you know what it is.", "annotation_id": "10968079", "url": "https://genius.com/10968079", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "These niggas fallin’ off, only the strong survive", "vault_lines": ["These niggas fallin' off, only the strong survive"], "meaning": "The artist’s referring to the Mobb Deep’s song “Survival of the fittest”.\n\nHere Prodigy spits: https://genius.com/1850310", "annotation_id": "10967328", "url": "https://genius.com/10967328", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Time to buy back the block, talkin’ one brick at a time", "vault_lines": ["Time to buy back the block, talkin' one brick at a time"], "meaning": "A play on words involving Brick Blocks which are usually made of cement\n\nhttp://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/fantendo/images/6/63/Brick_Block.png/revision/latest?cb=20120718183930\n\nBut here the “bricks” are kilograms of drugs, and put together they make up the “block” ie the crime-infested slum from which Rozay sells these drugs.", "annotation_id": "10951704", "url": "https://genius.com/10951704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Put all my chains on, I cause a wind chill", "vault_lines": ["Put all my chains on, I cause a wind chill"], "meaning": "Diamond-encrusted chains are referred to by rappers as “froze” or “ice”, two things which definitely cause chills.", "annotation_id": "10951692", "url": "https://genius.com/10951692", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Property, property, property, property, nigga I’m tryna invest Talking monopoly, I’m tryna encourage a nigga to run up a check", "vault_lines": ["Property, property, property, property, nigga I'm tryna invest", "Talking monopoly, I'm tryna encourage a nigga to run up a check"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is trying to create himself a monopoly which means that he is the only supplier of a product or service which can make him a big profit.\n\nMonopoly can also refer to the board game where the goal is to own as much properties as possible.\n\n\n\nEither way, 2 Chainz is investing in property’s or other products/services from which he can profit.", "annotation_id": "10943205", "url": "https://genius.com/10943205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "I used to sell the reefer, now I just sell Adidas", "vault_lines": ["I used to sell the reefer, now I just sell Adidas"], "meaning": "‘'Reefer’‘ is street slang for marijuana that 2 Chainz used to sell back before his fame.\n\nSports brand Adidas did a collaboration in 2014 with 2 Chainz creating his own version of the Top Ten Hi sneaker which goes by the name of 2 Good To Be T.R.U.", "annotation_id": "10943140", "url": "https://genius.com/10943140", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Cut it to 50 Cent, I got a job for your father", "vault_lines": ["Cut it to 50 Cent, I got a job for your father"], "meaning": "A play on words with the previous line suggesting he will have a huge sale at Family Dollar after he buys the company, but also subtly calls out 50 Cent (Curtis Jackson) by suggesting that his father would be an ideal Family Dollar employee.\nThe long standing beef between Rick Ross and 50 Cent is apparently still alive and well.", "annotation_id": "10890891", "url": "https://genius.com/10890891", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "Yes I feed lemon pepper, angel wings with the feathers", "vault_lines": ["Yes I feed lemon pepper, angel wings with the feathers"], "meaning": "Ross made it clear that his all time favorite meal from Wingstop, a franchise which he is an owner, is their lemon pepper wings. As he says in “Thug Cry,”\n\nCame from the hood, ain’t nothing changed\nStill lemon pepper on my mothafuckin' wangs!", "annotation_id": "10867137", "url": "https://genius.com/10867137", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "I sold a few records, I bought me a Checkers", "vault_lines": ["I sold a few records, I bought me a Checkers"], "meaning": "In May, Ross was posting on Snapchat from a meeting with the Checker’s team, and extremely recently, at the end of September, a video was released showing Rozay with the CEO of Checker’s announcing that he had purchased a location.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I2sID0unScg", "annotation_id": "10867120", "url": "https://genius.com/10867120", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "God thank you for my punishment, it made me wise", "vault_lines": ["God thank you for my punishment, it made me wise"], "meaning": "Since his release, Guwop has been very outspoken about his drug addiction which played a huge role in his downward spiral in 2013.\n\nIn one of his first interviews since being released from prison Gucci said this about overcoming his addiction:\n\nI was on drugs so bad, I talked different, When I was smoking damn near a pound of weed every other day, I was congested. When I was drinking lean like crazy every day, I was out of my mind\n\nNow that he is free and completely sober, Gucci thanks God for sentencing him to prison, where he realized his issues and turned his life around.", "annotation_id": "10867106", "url": "https://genius.com/10867106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "I made 10 million dollars, man and I was on house arrest", "vault_lines": ["I made 10 million dollars, man and I was on house arrest"], "meaning": "Between the time that Gucci got out of prison (May 26, 2016) and got off of house arrest (September 26, 2016), he released a full length studio album, Everybody Looking, along with a slew of features and shows, while gearing up to release another album, Woptober, in October. He reportedly made $10 million during this time, and couldn’t even leave his house!\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BKlK48vBYcJ/", "annotation_id": "10867065", "url": "https://genius.com/10867065", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "I sold ten bricks a day but now I need ten Chick-Fil-A’s", "vault_lines": ["I sold ten bricks a day but now I need ten Chick-Fil-A's"], "meaning": "Gucci used to be selling drugs, but now that he’s a successful rapper and multi millionaire, he wants to follow in the footsteps of many other celebrities celebrities and rappers by investing in franchises, perhaps a Chick-Fil-A. Or he’s just hungry…\n\n\n\nRoss continues this theme in the next verse, naming franchises that he has already bought or is considering purchasing.", "annotation_id": "10867043", "url": "https://genius.com/10867043", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Buy Back the Block", "line": "I hit up Renzel, went over details", "vault_lines": ["I hit up Renzel, went over details"], "meaning": "“Renzel” is one of the many nicknames of Rick Ross, and currently is part of his Twitter handle, Yung Renzel.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/799429035524767744", "annotation_id": "10867007", "url": "https://genius.com/10867007", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
