{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "Mini fourteen stuffed in my denim jeans", "vault_lines": ["Mini fourteen stuffed in my denim jeans"], "meaning": "Ross walking around with a 36\" Ruger Mini 14.", "annotation_id": "30429799", "url": "https://genius.com/30429799", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "On my deen", "vault_lines": ["I'm on my deen"], "meaning": "Deen ( دين ) means something similar to “religion” and “duty” in Arabic. In the Quran, God explains that the true “deen” incumbent upon humanity is Islam (3:19) – revealed to all prophets throughout all of human history.\nThe metaphor Wale is striking here is that he is on his religion – but his references to selling crack and other things that are contrary to Islam, insinuate that his “deen” is about getting rich … “by any means.”", "annotation_id": "27746627", "url": "https://genius.com/27746627", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "Inshallah", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In shaa Allah (إن شاء أللّه ) means “if God wills” in Arabic.", "annotation_id": "27746610", "url": "https://genius.com/27746610", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "It’s hard when starvin’, Marcus Garvey mixed with Malcolm Little", "vault_lines": ["It's hard when starvin', Marcus Garvey mixed with Malcolm Little"], "meaning": "Marcus Garvey was a major and one of the first proponent of Pan-Africanism in America. Garvey and Malcolm were viewed as being “pro-black”. Pill is implying that he supports and loves his black people.", "annotation_id": "846963", "url": "https://genius.com/846963", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "Several rallies mask Allah’s teachings through Shabazz That’s Malik, Omaha, Nebras", "vault_lines": ["Several rallies mask Allah's teachings through Shabazz", "That's Malik, Omaha, Nebras"], "meaning": "When Malcolm converted to Islam, he changed his name to El-Hajj Malik El-Shabazz. He was born in Omaha, Nebraska May 19, 1925.", "annotation_id": "846944", "url": "https://genius.com/846944", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "And we ain’t land on it, Mr. Reagan", "vault_lines": ["And we ain't land on it, Mr. Reagan"], "meaning": "On Easter Sunday night, 1964, Malcom X recited one of his most famous lines.“We are Africans, and we happen to be in America. We are not Americans. We are a people who formerly were Africans who were kidnaped and brought to America. Our forefathers weren’t the Pilgrims. We didn’t land on Plymouth Rock; the rock was landed on us.“ So this quote ties in with the 2 lines before this one.\nAnd in this context the Crack cocaine landed in the hood,  not the other way around.", "annotation_id": "221483", "url": "https://genius.com/221483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "By any means, if ya like it or not", "vault_lines": ["By any means, if ya like it or not"], "meaning": "“By any means” is a reference to a speech Malcolm X gave in the last year of his life.\n\nMalcolm X, who changed his name to El-Hajj Malik El-Shabazz, famously said “By any means necessary” in that speech and it is generally considered to leave open all available tactics for the desired ends, including violence; however, the “necessary” qualifier adds a caveat—if violence is not necessary, then presumably, it should not be used.", "annotation_id": "211320", "url": "https://genius.com/211320", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "Malcolm X, get your hand out my pocket", "vault_lines": ["Malcolm X, get your hand out my pocket"], "meaning": "“Get your hand out of my pocket!” Those words were echoed in the film “Malcolm X” while Malcom X was giving his last lecture, where he was assassinated, one of the conspirators jumped up and yelled “Get your hand out of my pocket!” to the guy sitting next to him (who had done nothing) to create a distraction while the gunmen pulled out their firearms to kill X.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qSm1t3Uv9QI", "annotation_id": "204234", "url": "https://genius.com/204234", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "Shout out to this Pyrex that bought this Audemeer Oops, I meant Audemar,", "vault_lines": ["Shout out to this Pyrex that bought this Audemeer", "Oops, I meant Audemar,"], "meaning": "A Pyrex pot used to cook cocaine and the fact that he sells cocaine is providing money for his Audemar Piguet watch", "annotation_id": "204211", "url": "https://genius.com/204211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "I’m a field nigga, you a house nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm a field nigga, you a house nigga"], "meaning": "Malcolm X had a great speech about House Negroes and Field Negroes.", "annotation_id": "200095", "url": "https://genius.com/200095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "She kneel down every Friday and then go to Jummah", "vault_lines": ["She kneel down every Friday and then go to Jummah"], "meaning": "Wale’s saying she gives head but then goes to Jummah prayers, which is Friday prayers at the mosque which are important to Muslims and Muslims should go every Friday to the mosque to perform these prayers unless they have an excuse to miss it. Jummah prayers are the prayers done by practicing Muslims on Fridays. During this prayer, they go to their knees. He’s saying that she gives him head, on her knees, then goes to Jummah, which is also done on the knees.", "annotation_id": "199974", "url": "https://genius.com/199974", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "On the Bible, you can run but you can’t hide", "vault_lines": ["On the Bible, you can run but you can't hide"], "meaning": "Wale is playing cleverly off the pronunciation of the Qu'ran (Koran or however you choose to spell it). Sticking with the theme of the track, Wale throws in popular Muslim references and phrases. This one is particular is juxtaposed with the Bible in the form of the popular saying “you could run but you can’t hide”", "annotation_id": "199620", "url": "https://genius.com/199620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "No pork on the fork, but it’s white in the pot", "vault_lines": ["No pork on the fork, but it's white in the pot"], "meaning": "Meek Mill tries to clear up Rick Ross' dietary error (good luck!)\n\nIn the Islamic belief, people are forbidden to eat pork, but Meek puts a spin on the idea. Contrary to Ross, Meek has no food on the table so he’s cooking up drugs to fix that. .", "annotation_id": "199564", "url": "https://genius.com/199564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "As-salāmu ’alaykum, wa ’alaykum-salām", "vault_lines": ["As-salāmu 'alaykum, wa 'alaykum-salām"], "meaning": "“As-Salāmu Alaykum” is a traditional Islamic greeting meaning “Peace be upon you”. “Wa Alaikum Assalam” is the traditional response, meaning “And upon you be peace”.", "annotation_id": "199562", "url": "https://genius.com/199562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "By Any Means", "line": "Malcolm X, by any means", "vault_lines": ["Malcolm X, by any means"], "meaning": "The song is named after a famous Malcolm X speech:\n\nWe declare our right on this earth…to be a human being, to be respected as a human being, to be given the rights of a human being in this society, on this earth, in this day, which we intend to bring into existence by any means necessary. Our objective is complete freedom, justice and equality by any means necessary", "annotation_id": "199561", "url": "https://genius.com/199561", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
