{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "CUT EM IN", "line": "Foc-focusin’ on me, way from Tel-Aviv", "vault_lines": ["Foc-focusin' on me, way from Tel-Aviv"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has visited Israel numeorous times, and even performed in Tel Aviv in 2022", "annotation_id": "33782506", "url": "https://genius.com/33782506", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "CUT EM IN", "line": "Sometimes I need a check (Check) Not the sneakers but the ones that make you watch your step", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes I need a check (Check)", "Not the sneakers but the ones that make you watch your step"], "meaning": ".Paak doesn’t need Nikes, which all feature the iconic swoosh, or ‘check,’ but he does need to get paid. When he gets his check, he’s going to ‘watch his step’ so to speak, and make sure that he isn’t putting himself in danger on the way to the bank, as having a big check puts a target on his back. Also note the word association between ‘sneakers’ and ‘step’.", "annotation_id": "22516538", "url": "https://genius.com/22516538", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "CUT EM IN", "line": "Men gon’ lie (Oh), women gon’ lie (Oh) You lookin’ for the truth, then the numbers don’t hide (Oh) Lookin’ for the root of all evil, then you need to go Open up the briefcase, see it with your eyes (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["Men gon' lie (Oh), women gon' lie (Oh)", "You lookin' for the truth, then the numbers don't hide (Oh)", "Lookin' for the root of all evil, then you need to go"], "meaning": "These lines are about the measurement of success. The numbers of success most bragged about by rap artists are usually record sales and money earned.\n\nThe first two lines are a variation of what Jay-Z said in “Reminder”:\n\nBack-to-back, double plat', I did what you won’t\nMen lie, women lie, numbers don’t\n\nMoney is also referred to as “the root of all evil” in the Bible’s First Epistle To Timothy:\n\nFor the love of money is the root of all evil\n\nAnderson is displaying his wealth by carrying large sums of cash money in his briefcase.", "annotation_id": "20944884", "url": "https://genius.com/20944884", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "CUT EM IN", "line": "You know I sat down with my accountant He said, “I got good news and I got bad news” (Okay) I said, “What’s the good news?” He said, “The good news is you made a lot” (Whoa, okay) I said, “What’s the bad news?” “The bad news is you spent more” Okay, oh, shit, look", "vault_lines": ["You know I sat down with my accountant", "He said, \"I got good news and I got bad news\" (Okay)", "I said, \"What's the good news?\""], "meaning": ".Paak talks about his wasteful spending. His 2019 album, Ventura, sold 55,000 album equivalent sales.\nHis album also won the Grammy’s for The Best R&B Album, so it was commercially successful.\nThe consecutive verses goes on to talk about how it is important have faith in these hard times with no money.", "annotation_id": "20678978", "url": "https://genius.com/20678978", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "CUT EM IN", "line": "Shoot like the Golden Boy, but ain’t from the Bay (I make it rain)", "vault_lines": ["Shoot like the Golden Boy, but ain't from the Bay (I make it rain)"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Steph Curry, who is plays in the NBA for San Francisco, home to the Golden State Warriors. Curry is widely renowned for his ability to shoot the basketball from almost anywhere on the basketball court. He is also a 3x NBA Champion ( 2015, 2017, 2018) , 2× NBA Most Valuable Player ( 2015, 2016) and a 6× NBA All-Star (2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019)", "annotation_id": "20604245", "url": "https://genius.com/20604245", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
