{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Camel Meat", "line": "Lord Vader, uh", "vault_lines": ["Lord Vader, Star Wars"], "meaning": "In an Architectural Digest home tour, Rick Ross gives viewers a look inside his $100 million mansion on Star Island, Miami. While showing off the bar in one of the rooms, he says:\n\n“When I’m behind the bar, I don’t go by Rick Ross. I go by Lord Vader, I repeat, Lord Vader.”\n\nHere, “Lord Vader” is a clear nod to Darth Vader from Star Wars. Ross intentionally says Lord Vader instead of the character’s official name, using it as an alter ego that reinforces his larger-than-life, commanding persona behind the bar. It’s less about accurately referencing the character and more about leaning into the powerful, boss-like image that’s long been part of the Rick Ross brand.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/BoJPDNbCnBc?si=Doo9aJgrpnM3GOWr&t=228", "annotation_id": "40785155", "url": "https://genius.com/40785155", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Camel Meat", "line": "Lemon pepper", "vault_lines": ["Ravioli, marinara, lemon pepper"], "meaning": "Rick Ross owns dozens of Wingstop franchise locations, where lemon pepper wings are considered one of the chain’s signature menu items.", "annotation_id": "40785098", "url": "https://genius.com/40785098", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Camel Meat", "line": "Got me dancin’ like Khaled", "vault_lines": ["Money all in the attic, got me dancin' like Khaled"], "meaning": "DJ Khaled is well known for his signature dance moves, which reflect his carefree attitude and his ability to enjoy the moment.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/shorts/HTfIE4IWdlE", "annotation_id": "40785073", "url": "https://genius.com/40785073", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Camel Meat", "line": "Camel meat in Dubai", "vault_lines": ["Camel meat in Dubai"], "meaning": "In September 2025, Rick Ross returned to Dubai, UAE, for one of his regular performances. Before flying back to the U.S., he was offered a rare local delicacy (camel meat).\n\nRoss was genuinely surprised to learn that camel meat is commonly served in the UAE. He even posted several Stories, asking his followers and friends whether he should give it a try. Keeping things lighthearted, he joked that he was a little hesitant, not out of disrespect for the local culture, but because he’d never eaten camel before and had no idea how his stomach would handle it.\n\nAcross the Gulf region, including the UAE, camel meat carries cultural significance that goes far beyond its role as a traditional dish.\n\nIt represents:\n\nBedouin heritage. For centuries, camels were essential to life in the desert, providing transportation, milk, and wool. They were only slaughtered for meat on special occasions.\n\nHospitality and generosity. Serving camel meat has long been considered a gesture of great respect toward guests, especially during weddings, religious celebrations, and major family gatherings.\n\nProsperity and social status. Because camels were highly valuable animals, slaughtering one was a rare occasion. As a result, camel meat became associated with wealth, generosity, and life’s most important celebrations.", "annotation_id": "40784810", "url": "https://genius.com/40784810", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Camel Meat", "line": "Living like I’m a Saudi, run up in it and out it Living with my two wives, fifty Ms on the palace", "vault_lines": ["Living like I'm a Saudi, run up in it and out it", "Living with my two wives, fifty Ms on the palace"], "meaning": "Saudi Arabia practices under Islamic Sharia law, which allows their Muslim men to have up to four wives concurrently. Also, it’s common for Saudi Arabian people to live in extravagant palaces.", "annotation_id": "40695071", "url": "https://genius.com/40695071", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Camel Meat", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-and-deon-cole-camel-meat-lyrics", "genius_title": "Camel Meat", "genius_id": 13448861, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "Smoke in the air like LeBron James", "vault_lines": ["Smoke in the air like LeBron James"], "meaning": "During the first 8 years of his career, LeBron James' on-court pregame ritual included pouring talcum powder into his hands and tossing it up into the air.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7rnDJvd419Y\n\nLil Wayne, a personal friend/fan of LeBron and die-hard sports fan, compares his athlete friend’s ritual to what it looks like when he’s smoking weed.", "annotation_id": "12954369", "url": "https://genius.com/12954369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "I’m beyond, I pee on you peons for eons", "vault_lines": ["I'm beyond, I pee on you peons for eons"], "meaning": "Here, Wayne is referencing “B-Boy Document ‘99”, by The High & Mighty, featuring Mos Def, Mad Skillz and Mr. Eon.\n\nMr. Eon says in his verse:\n\nWackest MC’s, we pee on those\n\nGame, who is featured on this track, later references this line in “Bitch, Don’t Kill My Vibe (Remix)”:\n\nPee on you peons for eons and eons", "annotation_id": "2220753", "url": "https://genius.com/2220753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
