{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "If 32 Seville when that all black Hummer run", "vault_lines": ["If 32 Seville when that all black Hummer run"], "meaning": "a Seville is a discontinued line of Cadillacs.  Travis Barker is a Cadillac fanatic and collects many styles of them.  He has an all black Seville and game has an all black hummer so they must be riding out in separate cars.\n\nSome sevilles have 32-valve engines, that is where the “32” comes from.  Here’s a Seville…", "annotation_id": "128299", "url": "https://genius.com/128299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "Can a drummer get some? Can a drummer get some? Can a drummer get some? Can a drummer get some? Can a– can a drummer get Can a– can a drummer get Can a– can a drummer get (Can a drummer get some?)", "vault_lines": ["Can a– can a drummer get"], "meaning": "It can either means\n\n\nHe want the drummer to finally be acknowledged, because the drummer is usually the most ignored member of a band.\nHe makes it seem as if he is saying can he get some sex from a female.\n\n\n\n\n\nCould be also a reference to this Jigga’s line, the first rapper who seems to acknowledge the drummers", "annotation_id": "116920", "url": "https://genius.com/116920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "Make money with Ruff Ryders, homie, that’s Swiss cheese", "vault_lines": ["Make money with Ruff Ryders, homie, that's Swiss cheese"], "meaning": "Cheese is referring to money, Swizz is referring to Swizz Beatz, a member of the Ruff Ryders, which makes the money Swizz Cheese (like Swiss Cheese, if you stil don’t get it)", "annotation_id": "108900", "url": "https://genius.com/108900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "Iller than most MCs ‘cause I be killin’ ’em Most emcees turn into ghost emcees", "vault_lines": ["Iller than most MCs 'cause I be killin' 'em", "Most emcees turn into ghost emcees"], "meaning": "He is meaning that he lyrically kill all the rappers. He is so ill that he gets a lot of space. He is referring to the fact that when you kill someone… they become ghosts. And usually, you don’t hear a lot about ghosts and you don’t even see them. So he takes so much place in the rap industry because he is the illest.\n\nAlso they’ll become ghostwriters", "annotation_id": "108881", "url": "https://genius.com/108881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "Face/Off, Nicolas Cage with a gauge", "vault_lines": ["Face/Off, Nicolas Cage with a gauge"], "meaning": "Movie called Faceoff starring Nicholas Cage\n\n\n\nTyler had a similar line in Earl’s Pidgeons:\n\nThis bitch is underage\nBut I’ll have her face off tied and Nicholas caged", "annotation_id": "102990", "url": "https://genius.com/102990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Can A Drummer Get Some", "line": "Weezy F, I’m a F’ing star, haha Get it? F and star", "vault_lines": ["Weezy F, I'm a F'ing star, haha", "Get it? F and star"], "meaning": "Travis Barker owns the popular clothing company ‘Famous Stars and Straps’ – the logo is an F with a star in it.\n\n\n\nGet it?\n\nAnother possible meaning ( attempt to triple entendre): The star reference is the 5-point star of the bloods, of which Wayne consistently shouts out in his ryhmes.", "annotation_id": "102717", "url": "https://genius.com/102717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
