{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Caviar Bumps", "line": "It’s so expensive, I know you can see the pink flamingos once you hear my voice", "vault_lines": ["It's so expensive, I know you can see the pink flamingos once you hear my voice"], "meaning": "Pink flamingos are one of Miami’s most iconic symbols, synonymous with the city’s tropical glamour and sun-soaked excess. Here, Rick Ross uses the image to make a statement about his brand: his voice alone is enough to transport you there. The moment he speaks, you’re not just hearing a rapper. You’re seeing the flamingos, feeling the heat, living in the luxury he’s built his entire identity around.", "annotation_id": "40784523", "url": "https://genius.com/40784523", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Caviar Bumps", "line": "Miami’s Martin Scorsese", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In recent years, Miami has cemented itself as a cultural hub of the United States — home to major film festivals, art exhibitions, and movie productions. With that backdrop, Rick Ross draws a parallel between himself and legendary director Martin Scorsese, positioning himself as the undisputed boss of the city.", "annotation_id": "40784478", "url": "https://genius.com/40784478", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Caviar Bumps", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-caviar-bumps-lyrics", "genius_title": "Caviar Bumps", "genius_id": 13894584, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "What is this", "vault_lines": ["Ain't no love or sympathy, what the fuck is a friend?"], "meaning": "The phrase “What is this” is usually played as an intro in many of Rick Ross' songs, throughout his entire discography. It first appeared in “Maybach Music” featuring Jay-Z. A small skit plays between two girls (informally known as the MMG girls) in which they listen to Maybach Music.", "annotation_id": "17987793", "url": "https://genius.com/17987793", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "Eyes open cause them broke niggas still snatchin’ chains", "vault_lines": ["Eyes open cause them broke niggas still snatchin' chains"], "meaning": "Ross is perhaps confirming a rumoured incident which occurred on a visit to London when his chain got snatched. The image below appears to show Ross being held down.\n\n\n\nRoss is saying telling people that he was caught slipping once but it won’t happen again, his eyes are now open. Tinie Tempah was asked about Ross getting robbed in his interview on The Breakfast Club (watch from 5:20 onwards) and he explains his thoughts on why he thinks the incident occurred. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FCtgLDplfd4", "annotation_id": "8271755", "url": "https://genius.com/8271755", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "Still blowing money fast, Lizzie’s in that duffle bag", "vault_lines": ["Still blowing money fast, Lizzie's in that duffle bag"], "meaning": "Here Ross is still referring to his verse about the English lifestyle.\n\nIn England, on the notes, they have the picture of the Queen, whos name is Elizabeth. He’s saying he’s blowing a lot of money that he’s carrying in his bag.", "annotation_id": "7254674", "url": "https://genius.com/7254674", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "My car stick in your memory, that’s what I call a flash drive", "vault_lines": ["My car stick in your memory, that's what I call a flash drive"], "meaning": "Wordplay – a flash drive is another name for a USB memory stick that you plug into a computer. Flash(y) can also mean cool or good-looking so he’s saying his car’s a flash drive.\n\nTo add a second level of wordplay to the bar, “stick in your memory” is saying that his car’s unforgettably good while also embedding the phrase memory stick.", "annotation_id": "6587418", "url": "https://genius.com/6587418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "Tell the waiter more cheese on my bolognese", "vault_lines": ["Tell the waiter more cheese on my bolognese"], "meaning": "Reference to rolling a spliff, where weed is mixed with tobacco to create a smokable joint. Here Konan wants more cheese (slang for weed), in his bolognese (the tobacco).\n\n\n\nAlso, a sign he can tell people to do what he wants now that he’s “certified”", "annotation_id": "5151871", "url": "https://genius.com/5151871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "In the club you see we banging like it’s Scotland Yard", "vault_lines": ["In the club you see we banging like it's Scotland Yard"], "meaning": "Scotland Yard is used to describe the headquarters of the Metropolitan Police Service, the police force responsible for policing most of London.", "annotation_id": "5140663", "url": "https://genius.com/5140663", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "Take a picture of me, that’s an ice pic", "vault_lines": ["Take a picture of me, that's an ice pic"], "meaning": "“An ice pic”, sounds like ‘a nice pic’ so he’s saying if you take a picture with him it’ll turn out nice. Also ice pic refers to the jewellery he has.", "annotation_id": "5126070", "url": "https://genius.com/5126070", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
