{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "Feds stopped me like “Did you see the crime?” Sorry officer, I’m legally blind", "vault_lines": ["Feds stopped me like \"Did you see the crime?\"", "Sorry officer, I'm legally blind"], "meaning": "A reference to a popular video where a guy who gets arrested claims he’s legally blind.\n\nThis bar shows how Krept would rather lie to the boydem than snitch on someone.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S0I9JAYuCYs", "annotation_id": "5121743", "url": "https://genius.com/5121743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "Broom broom, but this ain’t my mum’s car", "vault_lines": ["Broom broom, but this ain't my mum's car"], "meaning": "Based on this meme, Konan assures the listener that he’s paid for his car himself.", "annotation_id": "5121740", "url": "https://genius.com/5121740", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "I swear the ass was enormous The last time we all seen it, it was August", "vault_lines": ["I swear the ass was enormous", "The last time we all seen it, it was August"], "meaning": "“All seen it” sounds like Alsina – this is a play on words referring to August Alsina.\n\nWorth noting that fellow Play Dirty artist Yungen had a very similar pun on “Ain’t On Nuttin'”:\n\nMet her in July, flew her out in August\nShe gonna tell you that she loved this shit", "annotation_id": "5114991", "url": "https://genius.com/5114991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "When I park up, that’s your bae gone", "vault_lines": ["When I park up, that's your bae gone"], "meaning": "This is play on the driving term “bay parking”\n\n\n\nHe’s saying if he gets comfortable with your bae (girl) then he’ll steal her from you.", "annotation_id": "5114977", "url": "https://genius.com/5114977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "All these red bottoms getting silly nigga More pairs than Ricky", "vault_lines": ["All these red bottoms getting silly nigga", "More pairs than Ricky"], "meaning": "More like Creps & Konan!\n\nHere Krept is talking about his large collection of expensive Louboutin shoes, renowned for their red bottoms.\n\nHe plays on the homonym of pairs/pears – he’s got a lot of pairs of the shoes. Rick Ross’s love of pears (the fruit) became a meme in late 2014 following an interview with Tim Westwood about them.", "annotation_id": "5112208", "url": "https://genius.com/5112208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Certified", "line": "So don’t ever leave your bitch lonely Cause I’m a young thug getting rich, homie Rap life", "vault_lines": ["So don't ever leave your bitch lonely", "Cause I'm a young thug getting rich, homie"], "meaning": "Slick reference to Young Thug and Rich Homie Quan who are two famous artist who Collaborate under Birdman’s ‘Rich Gang’.\n\nHence Konan gives an explicit warning to other men to watch their girls as his influence as a rapper may compel her to cheat. This take on the “rap life” is something alluded to on the track ‘Lifestyle’ by the same Rich Gang and as such, may be adding another layer to the reference", "annotation_id": "5111566", "url": "https://genius.com/5111566", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
