{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Chain of Command", "line": "In the trap, keep yay with me and two young niggas that stay with me Metal-grain strap when you see me, 7.62s fly, Chopper City, B.G.", "vault_lines": ["In the trap, keep yay with me and two young niggas that stay with me", "Metal-grain strap when you see me, 7.62s fly, Chopper City, B.G."], "meaning": "The New Orleans rapper, B.G. uses the moniker “Choppa City” to refer to the murders in city (at the time was the murder capitol of US in 1995 – most likely when the album was recored as the album debuted in 1996).\n\nThe album cover displays ammunition for assault riffles (AK-47’s which are often refered to as “Choppas”) which ties into the caliber 7.62s.\n\nHe mentions 2 young gangsters with him in the trap and BG means “Baby Gangster” (and could also be referring to Young Turk, as his trap was “ran up in” by the police in 2004.)", "annotation_id": "40685626", "url": "https://genius.com/40685626", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
