{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Look me right in my face, he beginnin’ to shake", "vault_lines": ["Look me right in my face, he beginnin' to shake"], "meaning": "Based on the context of Rick Ross’s lyrics and persona, the line “Look me right in my face, he beginnin' to shake” from his verse on “Stay Schemin'” (featuring Drake and French Montana) is a demonstration of intimidation, dominance, and a call-out to a rival", "annotation_id": "39395523", "url": "https://genius.com/39395523", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "[Intro]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In an interview with PANDA CHOP! News, underground rapper Poe Rilla revealed that Rick Ross remixed the beat to rapper Cuban Link’s posse cut “Nos Tienen Miedo 2” and sampled it into his diss track “Champagne Moments”. “Nos Tienen Miedo 2” is the sequel to “Nos Tienen Miedo” which was released in 2008.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vf60GEhQngM&t=202s", "annotation_id": "34670418", "url": "https://genius.com/34670418", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
