{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Let you get on my songs, it was good for your face Now, bitch nigga, it’s on, ain’t no room for debate", "vault_lines": ["Let you get on my songs, it was good for your face", "Now, bitch nigga, it's on, ain't no room for debate"], "meaning": "Collaborating with Rick Ross early on did well for Drake’s reputation, or “face”.\n\nIt’s possibly another dig at the plastic surgery rumors surrounding Drake. Ross claims he’s had a nose job, among other procedures.\n\nDrake has denied the allegations in an instagram story, posting a screenshot of a conversation with his mother.", "annotation_id": "32092399", "url": "https://genius.com/32092399", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "I got pictures to paint", "vault_lines": ["I could shoot up the block, I got pictures to paint"], "meaning": "Possibly a response to Drake’s line on Push Ups – “I know my picture on the wall when y'all cook up” meaning that it’s Drizzy’s picture he wants to paint with blood", "annotation_id": "31547585", "url": "https://genius.com/31547585", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "That wasn’t the same white boy that I seen, nigga, when we were makin’ them early records, nigga", "vault_lines": ["That wasn't the same white boy that I seen, nigga, when we were makin' them early records, nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross and Drake collaborated on lots of big hits, most notably “Aston Martin Music”, “Money in the Grave” and “Stay Schemin”.", "annotation_id": "31489874", "url": "https://genius.com/31489874", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Give Rap-A-Lot some more money, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Give Rap-A-Lot some more money, nigga"], "meaning": "Referring to Rap-A-Lot Records which is founded by J. Prince who helped Drake get signed to the record label Young Money. Drake had mentioned J. Prince in his and 21 Savage’s song “Circo Loco”:\n\nLinking with the opps, bitch, I did that shit for J. Prince\nBitch, I did it for the mob ties", "annotation_id": "31463856", "url": "https://genius.com/31463856", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
