{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Give Weezy some more money, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Give Weezy some more money, nigga"], "meaning": "Referring to Lil Wayne who’s Drake’s mentor and close friend. Drake was also signed to Lil Wayne’s record label Young Money until leaving in 2018.", "annotation_id": "31463752", "url": "https://genius.com/31463752", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Niggas pussy, don’t want to push me, I’m like, “Really, would he?”", "vault_lines": ["Niggas pussy, don't want to push me, I'm like, \"Really, would he?\""], "meaning": "“Would he” sounds like “Woody”. In Pixar’s first animated film, Toy Story (1995), Woody famously pushes Buzz out the window. This alludes to Drake being the “white boy” (Woody in this context), which is reinforced by Ross' repeated taunts. It also hints at the jealousy Drake might feel towards Ross, resulting in pushing and shoving. However, Rick Ross labels him a pussy and doubts Drake is street enough to get physical.", "annotation_id": "31462412", "url": "https://genius.com/31462412", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Maybach Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross confirmed on Instagram on August 29, 2023, that Jessica Gomes is the voice behind the Maybach Music Group. The Australian model was born in Sydney to a Chinese father and a Singaporean mother of Chinese descent.", "annotation_id": "31459090", "url": "https://genius.com/31459090", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Fish tanks and marble floors, livin’ big and bad Niggas laugh until they hit with my official jab Crack smoke is the exhaust from my pen and pad", "vault_lines": ["Crack smoke is the exhaust from my pen and pad"], "meaning": "Similar to Nas' “My Way” which begins with: “Gateways, marble floors, chandeliers\nJacuzzi’s, Gucci soap, throwin' cash in the air\nThough I still feel broke with millions in the bank\nAnd deals on the table, I focus to stay afloat\nAnd just to think some would die to get what I got\nThey think it’s a lot, in the blink of an eye you could get shot.”", "annotation_id": "31456942", "url": "https://genius.com/31456942", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "“Got more money than you,” fuck you want me to say?", "vault_lines": ["\"Got more money than you,\" fuck you want me to say?"], "meaning": "Ross is imitating Drakes bar from “Push Ups” here, where he tells Ross to “spend that little check you got”\n\nRoss mocks Drakes bar that he has more money than Ross, stating that he lives in a 50 million dollar mansion so what does having more money than that really count for?", "annotation_id": "31456660", "url": "https://genius.com/31456660", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Do the job, better known as the Charles Schwab", "vault_lines": ["Do the job, better known as the Charles Schwab"], "meaning": "Its also a continuation to the previous line. Charles R. Schwab is one good inverster and now a shareholder of the largest discount of securities in the United States\n\nhttps://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSzeyesVqmRldZyr_yrCkNruby3tPl-aHpqLBF-qIV0Ug&s", "annotation_id": "31451724", "url": "https://genius.com/31451724", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Get to mine, tell by my watch, this a different time", "vault_lines": ["Get to mine, tell by my watch, this a different time"], "meaning": "“get to mine” references the previous line about Drake’s record label OVO- when you “get to” Rick’s label, it’s way better than drakes. He says that you can tell by his watch that it’s a different time. this is a double entendre.\nfirst of all, you can tell by his watch that he is making more money at his record label than Drake is at his, therefore it’s a different time, or the “different time” could be a new time period, saying that Drakes’ time is over.", "annotation_id": "31451475", "url": "https://genius.com/31451475", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Livin’ fine, I’m gettin’ high as your shit decline", "vault_lines": ["Livin' fine, I'm gettin' high as your shit decline"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is referring to the famous clip of Drake’s credit card getting declined on stream.\nhttps://streamable.com/69fihb", "annotation_id": "31446035", "url": "https://genius.com/31446035", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "You owe motherfuckin’ Stunna your life, nigga", "vault_lines": ["You owe motherfuckin' Stunna your life, nigga"], "meaning": "Stunna is a nickname of Cash Money Records founder Birdman.\n\nIn 2009, Drake secured a recording contract with Young Money Entertainment that it’s a label imprint of Cash Money Records. Ross is saying that Drake owes Birdman so much for everything in Drake’s career.\n\nBirdman and Rick Ross have their own personal beef stemming from 2017.\n\nIn the same year, Ross dissed the Cash Money Records boss in the song Idols Become Rivals.\n\nIn 2022, Birdman has called out Ross for copying his style.\n\nAfter “Champagne moments” dropped, Birdman posted an Instagram story supporting Drake.\n\n\n\nRoss replied through the same plataform, mocking the late Ms. Gladys, Birdman’s mother that was shot and killed in 1975.", "annotation_id": "31445935", "url": "https://genius.com/31445935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Another white boy at the park wanna hang with the crew", "vault_lines": ["Another white boy at the park wanna hang with the crew"], "meaning": "Ross is once again drawing attention to Drake’s relationship with the black community. Ross is claiming that Drake is only using hip hop and black culture for his own clout, and he’s really an outsider.", "annotation_id": "31439563", "url": "https://genius.com/31439563", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Like his moves, but he never had to fight in school", "vault_lines": ["Like his moves, but he never had to fight in school"], "meaning": "Once again Ross is pointing out a contradiction between the subjects in Drake’s music and his actual lifestyle.\n\nRoss is saying Drake likes to portray himself as being hard, when in reality he’s lived a sheltered life and doesn’t know what it’s like for rappers who grew up on the streets.", "annotation_id": "31439555", "url": "https://genius.com/31439555", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Who believes he movin’ keys in his Louis V’s?", "vault_lines": ["Who believes he movin' keys in his Louis V's?"], "meaning": "Ross is pointing out the contradiction between the themes in Drake’s music and Drake’s actual lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "31439507", "url": "https://genius.com/31439507", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Ghostwriters, they get to floss what you could’ve had", "vault_lines": ["Ghostwriters, they get to floss what you could’ve had"], "meaning": "Drake has long been accused of using ghostwriters to write his songs. This is a big faux pas in hip-hop, as authenticity has been a major theme in the genre since its inception.\n\nHere, Rick Ross is mocking Drake for using ghostwriters, saying he’s making his ghostwriters rich when he could have written his own songs and saved the money.", "annotation_id": "31439455", "url": "https://genius.com/31439455", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Gettin’ bullied, don’t walk up on me ’cause the clip is fully", "vault_lines": ["Gettin' bullied, don't walk up on me ’cause the clip is fully"], "meaning": "Full clip could refer to Drake taking shots at several artists on Push Ups. Ross feels it was uncalled to bring his name up like he wouldn’t respond.\n\nApparently, Push Ups leaked via Drake’s camp so it wasn’t a thought out strategy. Fans even speculated about the track being AI-generated for the unexpected release and its lyrical content.\n\nHowever, the song was recorded and that alone is enough for Ross to think it was a reckless mistake by Drake.", "annotation_id": "31437209", "url": "https://genius.com/31437209", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "You ain’t never want to be a nigga anyway, nigga That’s why you had an operation to make your nose smaller than your father nose, nigga", "vault_lines": ["You ain't never want to be a nigga anyway, nigga", "That's why you had an operation to make your nose smaller than your father nose, nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross here takes a shot at Drake for being insecure about his prominent black/Afro-American features. To the point in which Drake took matters in to his own hand to get it surgically innovated. Using the term “father nose” to get the point across.\n\nAs Drake’s father (Dennis Graham) is a black man with significantly large nose.\n\n\nIf you look closely you can see that Drake’s nose was a bit more plum and stubby in 2011 [1st image] than it is now in 2024, where’s it’s a bit more narrow and longer [2nd image].\n\n\n\n Which gives Rick Ross artillery for the rest of the verse, going to taunt Drake various other times for being “white.” Due to Drake embracing and changing himself to fit white standards, instead of staying to true to what he once was.", "annotation_id": "31435148", "url": "https://genius.com/31435148", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Fifty mil’ for the crib, where you want me to stay?", "vault_lines": ["Fifty mil' for the crib, where you want me to stay?"], "meaning": "Ross is the proud owner of one of the largest private homes in America.", "annotation_id": "31434255", "url": "https://genius.com/31434255", "state": "pending", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Pulitzer Prize winner switchin’ up like dyed denim", "vault_lines": ["Pulitzer Prize winner switchin' up like dyed denim"], "meaning": "Likely a reference to Kendrick releasing the Future feature after being taunted for years by Drake.\n\n\nKendrick receiving his Pulitzer\n\nRoss could also be suggesting that Drake is winning the awards (Pulitzer Prize) for his writing skills. Meanwhile, his ghostwriters are riding rentals because they aren’t being paid when they are making the hits (doing the killings). Dyed denim shows the original color beneath. Ross would be implying that Drake is fake and see-thru.", "annotation_id": "31434165", "url": "https://genius.com/31434165", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "You got it and you keep it tucked if you be by me", "vault_lines": ["You got it and you keep it tucked if you be by me"], "meaning": "Whether it’s guns or jewelry, Drake will normally have to stay put in front of a senior of his like Ross.\n\nMore than a brag, this line could be interpreted as an example of their past relationship as Ross would take care of anything Drake needed. In the sense Ross would’ve probably taken smoke for him if need had been.", "annotation_id": "31434101", "url": "https://genius.com/31434101", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Double R’s spread through the yard, and I swear to God", "vault_lines": ["Double R's spread through the yard, and I swear to God"], "meaning": "Double Rs refers to the Rolls Royce logo which has a double R\n\nAlso a possible nod to a track on his Rich Forever mixtape.", "annotation_id": "31434087", "url": "https://genius.com/31434087", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Flow is copy-and-paste, Weezy gave you the juice", "vault_lines": ["Flow is copy-and-paste, Weezy gave you the juice"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is claiming Drake’s flow on his songs are a copy-and-paste of Lil Wayne’s flow and that without Lil Wayne he would be nowhere.\n\nDrake started writing rap music whilst he was an actor for Degrassi in 2001. He self-published his first mixtape Room for Improvement in 2006 but it wouldn’t be until the release of his third mixtape So Far Gone in 2009 that Drake would see an international level of fame, even landing him a signing to Lil Wayne’s Young Money Entertainment label. After that Drake went on to having seventy-seven top ten songs and sixteen top ten albums, with thirteen being number one songs and thirteen being number one albums on the Billboard Hot 100 and Billboard 200 charts at the time of this song.\n\nRick Ross uses this line to show that without Lil Wayne, Drake’s career would have likely never taken off or have been nowhere the same as it is now.", "annotation_id": "31433594", "url": "https://genius.com/31433594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Yeah, you had that surgery, that six-pack gone That’s why you wearin’ that funny shit at your show, you can’t hide it, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you had that surgery, that six-pack gone", "That's why you wearin' that funny shit at your show, you can't hide it, nigga"], "meaning": "In late 2015, Drake exhibited a significant body transformation in the span of 3 months seen below:\n\n\nWith such a rapid transformation, rumors of Drake’s penchant for plastic surgery arose, but seem to stem from Joe Budden and Drake’s 2016 feud, in which Joe Budden mentioned Drake visiting Dr. Miami, a popular celebrity plastic surgeon, in one of his 4 Drake diss tracks, titled Afraid:\n\nYeah Aubrey that’s the one we trusted\nNot this new Aubrey with his stomach sculpted\n\nJoe Budden also tweeted about Drake allegedly having liposuction twice:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/JoeBudden/status/754711702676054016\n\nAt the time Joe Budden didn’t provide proof of this, but these lyrics fueled speculation that Drake had had procedures done. Similarly, speculation in 2016 existed around Drake’s having a nose job as well.\n\nAround 2019, when Drake was seen shirtless in an IG post, people began to speculate that he had plastic surgery, which rapper and close friend, DJ Carnage seemingly confirmed:\n\n\n\n\n\nDuring his recent “It’s All a Blur Tour”, people noticed Drake’s wardrobe included many outlandish outfits that appear to have padding over his abs, which Rick Ross claims Drake is wearing to hide that he does not have the surgical abs he used to–an attempt Ross says has failed:", "annotation_id": "31433518", "url": "https://genius.com/31433518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Let you DM my ho, but got bitches you can’t", "vault_lines": ["Let you DM my ho, but got bitches you can't"], "meaning": "Following the release of Future & Metro Boomin’s WE DON’T TRUST YOU, Rick Ross unfollowed Drake on Instagram. Rick Ross was featured on “Everyday Hustle” on WE DON’T TRUST YOU and on the song dissed his baby mama.\n\nBaby mama still the biggest opp\n\nFour days after the release of WE DON’T TRUST YOU, Drake invited Rick Ross' ex Cristina Mackey to his concert.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/shannonsharpeee/status/1772824116246274144", "annotation_id": "31432860", "url": "https://genius.com/31432860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Told you niggas “Stay schemin’,” I predicted my fate", "vault_lines": ["Told you niggas \"Stay schemin',\" I predicted my fate"], "meaning": "“Stay Schemin'” is Rick Ross' collaboration with Drake and French Montana which released as a single for Ross' mixtape Rich Forever in 2012. Rick Ross seemingly makes reference to the song’s chorus when claiming “I predicted my fate”.\n\n I ride for my niggas, dawg\nI ride for my niggas\nI slide for my niggas, dawg (Dawg)\nI ride for my niggas\nStay schemin', niggas tryna get at me, dawg\nI ride for my niggas\nStay schemin', niggas tryna get at me, dawg\nI ride for my niggas\n\nTowards the outro of Champagne Moments, Rick Ross claims Drake sent a cease-and-desist to French Montana. Rick Ross is showing his loyalty towards French Montana not switching up on him and staying by his side.\n\nI unfollowed you, nigga, ‘cause you sent the motherfucking cease-and-desist to French Montana, nigga\nYou sent the police, nigga, hatin’ on my dog project", "annotation_id": "31432766", "url": "https://genius.com/31432766", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Either you niggas gettin’ money or ready to die B-I-G or give a fuck if you Chi-Ali", "vault_lines": ["Either you niggas gettin' money or ready to die", "B-I-G or give a fuck if you Chi-Ali"], "meaning": "Homage to Biggie’s Classic Album: Ready to Die, as well as his song “Get Money” with Junior M.A.F.I.A.\n\n\n\nRoss points out once again the contradiction between Drake’s lifestyle and his gangster lyrics.\n\nChi-Ali is a rapper who was a member of the Native Tongues. He went to prison for murdering his girl’s brother. Ross implies here that he doesn’t care if Drake is a murderer, he still wouldn’t be able to be harmed by him.\n\nIt is also worth mentioning that an early leaked version of Drake’s “Push Ups” samples the “Get Money” line from Junior M.A.F.I.A. in the background. Given the very quick response from Ross, it is likely that he was responding to that version originally.", "annotation_id": "31432751", "url": "https://genius.com/31432751", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Record label takin’ a loss, are you in your bag? You a worker wantin’ to chart, don’t make me laugh", "vault_lines": ["You a worker wantin' to chart, don’t make me laugh"], "meaning": "In 2022, Drake signed a multi million dollar deal with Universal Music Group. According to Variety, the label earns an estimated “50 or 70 million dollars” from the rapper’s music.\n\nMedium did a rundown of OVO artits careers up until 2017.\n\nWhen it comes to the signings, In the five years the label has been active, the label has signed PartyNextDoor, Majid Jordan, ILoveMakonnen, Roy Woods, DVSN, Baka, Plaza and OB O’Brien. Excluding ILoveMakonnen because he left the label in 2016, all of these acts have had dismal success on their own. (…)\nThe acts that have toured, Roy Woods, PartyNextDoor, Majid Jordan and DVSN have all gone on successful tours and continue to do so, but if their records don’t really start to sell.\n\nRoss’s record label Maybach Music Group has had successful artists in the rap scene such as Meek Mill, French Montana, Wale.\n\nThe rapper accuses Drake of being the reason that some of the artists didn’t perform as expected. On the song “Summer Sixteen”, Drake talks about his contribution to the label referencing Jay-Z, the Roc-A-Fella director as an example of what he wanna be like.\n\nI used to wanna be on Roc-A-Fella then I turned into Jay", "annotation_id": "31432736", "url": "https://genius.com/31432736", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Always ran, another nigga had to write your grooves", "vault_lines": ["Always ran, another nigga had to write your grooves"], "meaning": "Drake has had allegations of not writing his own rhymes and having ghostwriters instead.\n\nThis was used by Pusha T in the 2018 track Infrared, that dissed Drake.\n\nIt was written like Nas, but it came from Quentin\n\nQuentin is a reference to Quentin Miller, a writer that used to send songs to DJ Drama and Drake. According to the writer, one of the raps that was used was the verse on Meek Mill’s song “Rico”. In an interview to VladTV, Miller told how he found out that his lyrics were on a Drake’s song.\n\nI had a super tight relationship with Drama at the time, so I sent him that. Just on some, ‘Check me out. […] Then one random day in a club with Drama in L.A., he’s like, ‘Yo, you know Meek got on that joint.’ And I’m like, ‘What joint?’ He’s like, ‘The “R.I.C.O.” joint.’” And at the time, I hadn’t heard Drake’s version of ‘R.I.C.O.’ I didn’t even know that Drake did it. So by the time I found out, we were already in it. We were in the thick of this shit.\n\nQuentin is not credited as a collaborator in R.I.C.O. That is not the case for the work in the 2015’s project If You’re Reading is Too late where he co-wrote Legend, 10 Bands, Know Yourself, No Tellin', Used to and 6 Man,    .\n\nIn the same year in a interview to Verge cleared the rumours.\n\nI am not and never will be a ‘ghostwriter’ for Drake.. I’m proud to say that we’ve collaborated.. but I could never take credit for anything other than the few songs we worked on together", "annotation_id": "31432676", "url": "https://genius.com/31432676", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Run up on you and snatch your chain, watch you bitches bleed", "vault_lines": ["Run up on you and snatch your chain, watch you bitches bleed"], "meaning": "Rick Ross responds to Drake’s diss track “Push Ups”:\n\nYou won’t ever take no chain off of us\n\nDrake was originally responding to Kendrick Lamar’s diss from his verse on “Like That” by Future & Metro Boomin:\n\nGot 2TEEZ with me, I’m snatchin' chains and burnin' tattoos, it’s up\n\nRick Ross sides with Future, Metro Boomin and Kendrick Lamar over Drake, stating that they will be snatching chains no matter what Drake says. Rick Ross was featured on Future & Metro Boomin’s collaborative album WE DON’T TRUST YOU on the song “Everyday Hustle”.", "annotation_id": "31432667", "url": "https://genius.com/31432667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "By the way, I got a lot of respect for a lot of rappers, but I got one guy He’s my favorite person to rap with on any song, his name is Rick Ross", "vault_lines": ["He's my favorite person to rap with on any song, his name is Rick Ross"], "meaning": "Rick Ross sampled a clip of Drake speaking at his It’s All a Blur tour.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/lHccXD1Ky9k?t=7", "annotation_id": "31432654", "url": "https://genius.com/31432654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "Niggas leakin’ they records when we speakin’ directly If we keepin’ it gangster, when you see me, you check me", "vault_lines": ["If we keepin' it gangster, when you see me, you check me"], "meaning": "On April 13, 2024, Drake’s diss track “Push Ups,” directed towards multiple artists who were against him — including Rick Ross —  leaked.  Ross claims either Drake or someone in his camp leaked the record on his behalf as he was too scared to speak directly.", "annotation_id": "31432640", "url": "https://genius.com/31432640", "state": "accepted", "votes": 90, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "I unfollowed you, nigga, ‘cause you sent the motherfuckin’ cease-and-desist to French Montana, nigga You sent the police, nigga, hated on my dog project", "vault_lines": ["You sent the police, nigga, hated on my dog project"], "meaning": "Rick Ross could be alluding to the song “Big Pun” featuring Drake that was rumoured to be on French Montana’s “Mac & Cheese 5”. A snippet of this song was leaked in May 2023 and then in full in December.\n\nHe may also be referring to “Splash Brothers”, another leaked track with Montana and Drake initially scheduled for Montana’s album “They Got Amnesia”. The song was then finally released on “Mac & Cheese 5” with Rick Ross and Lil Wayne replacing Drake.\n\nThe reasons for the cease and desist are still unclear.", "annotation_id": "31432631", "url": "https://genius.com/31432631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Champagne Moments", "line": "White boy, I see you, I see you Yeah, check", "vault_lines": ["White boy, I see you, I see you"], "meaning": "Drake, being the child of a white mother and a black father, is considered biracial and therefore “light-skinned.”\n\nRick Ross takes jabs at Drake’s complexion in a similar fashion as Pusha T on May 2018’s “The Story of Adidon”:\n\nConfused, always felt you weren’t Black enough\nAfraid to grow it ‘cause your 'fro wouldn’t nap enough", "annotation_id": "31432548", "url": "https://genius.com/31432548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
