{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Let him go check the stats, cause all I want is the racks", "vault_lines": ["Let him go check the stats, cause all I want is the racks"], "meaning": "In reference to the previous line in which he mentions being close to the action for the Miami Heat game.\n\n\n\nthe HIM Ross is referring to is LEBRON (‘Bron). Ross is only concerned when money is involved, not so much the statistics of the basketball game.", "annotation_id": "3441269", "url": "https://genius.com/3441269", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "MCM on my luggage,", "vault_lines": ["MCM on my luggage,"], "meaning": "MCM is a very high end expensive luggage and accessories brand.  Mode Creation Munich, commonly known as MCM, is South Korean luxury brand of leather goods, apparel and footwear.  Its' range of products included luxury handbag collection and vintage briefcases, as well as its men’s bag products and gloves.", "annotation_id": "1498758", "url": "https://genius.com/1498758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "I’m talking the facts of life, can I just have a slice?", "vault_lines": ["I'm talking the facts of life, can I just have a slice?"], "meaning": "Referring to Slice of Life, a literary genre that follows a small section of a character’s life, sometimes not having a progressive plot, but usually having an underlying meaning.\n\n\n\n“Facts of life” refers to the last four lines, that described Ross' own life.\n\nIn the last four lines Ross gave you a slice of life by describing his life, though not including a particular plot.\n\n\n\nFAT JOKE\n\nWho would have guessed, Rick Ross wants a slice.", "annotation_id": "1498741", "url": "https://genius.com/1498741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Even in my everyday ride I be stuntin’", "vault_lines": ["Even in my everyday ride I be stuntin'"], "meaning": "Spitta has a ride for every day of the week, and they’re all flyer than your average automobile. There’s no need to bring out anything “special” because all his cars are already top of the line.", "annotation_id": "1476141", "url": "https://genius.com/1476141", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "I don’t hide bitch, I’m high when I’m in public", "vault_lines": ["I don't hide bitch, I'm high when I'm in public"], "meaning": "Most amateur smokers don’t like to be high in public because they might feel awkward, paranoid, or anti-social, but Curren$y is obviously a pro at this.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/CurrenSy_Spitta/status/305910804715298817\n\nNotice the wordplay between “hide” and “high” due to his southern drawl.", "annotation_id": "1475262", "url": "https://genius.com/1475262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "This is nothing really, you should see me Sunday", "vault_lines": ["This is nothing really, you should see me Sunday"], "meaning": "People often ride out in their best clothes and whips on Sunday (sometimes for church), so if he’s stunting every day of the week, imagine what he does on Sundays.", "annotation_id": "1475077", "url": "https://genius.com/1475077", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Double M, we the hottest on the fucking turf", "vault_lines": ["Double M, we the hottest on the fucking turf"], "meaning": "“Double M” is relating to Rick Ross' record label “Maybach Music Group” (Maybach Music for short, or M.M.G.).", "annotation_id": "1470454", "url": "https://genius.com/1470454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Behike Cuban cigars bombaclot he think he Dudus", "vault_lines": ["Behike Cuban cigars bombaclot he think he Dudus"], "meaning": "Christopher “Dudus” Coke was a Jamaican drug lord who lived extravagantly. He was the leader of the Shower Posse Jamaican gang since he was 21 up until his capture in 2010.\n\nBehike Cohiba are like the Rolls-Royce of cigars. They’re pretty expensive and are being marketed as the most exclusive Cuban cigars produced by Cohiba (which is Castro’s favorite brand). People often try to make fakes.\n\n\n\nJust because this bombaclot is smoking the exclusive cigars, he thinks he’s a big time drug dealer like Dudus. The use of the jamaican insult refers to Dudus' origin of Jamaica. Pretty clever, Rozay.", "annotation_id": "1458683", "url": "https://genius.com/1458683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "My Cuban was Spanish gold, so vintage as my Cazals", "vault_lines": ["My Cuban was Spanish gold, so vintage as my Cazals"], "meaning": "Cazal sunglasses have been popular since the days of Run-D.M.C.\n\n\n\nRoss even has the company’s logo tatted below his eye.\n\n\n\nThe frames, paired with his Cuban link chain, give him an old school appearance.", "annotation_id": "1456794", "url": "https://genius.com/1456794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Bust your head that’s a concussion", "vault_lines": ["bust your head that's a concussion"], "meaning": "“Bust your head” means Wiz wont hesitate to put a bullet in your head.\nConcussion is the most common injury to your brain. Especially common in sports with hitting like football and hockey.\n\n\n\nHe uses a simple wordplay with the two, when he shoots you in the head he’s going to do a little more damage than just a concussion.", "annotation_id": "1456327", "url": "https://genius.com/1456327", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Uh, daytime lights on Hell yeah I’m frontin’ but you love it", "vault_lines": ["Hell yeah I'm frontin' but you love it"], "meaning": "Spitta is riding his whip with the daytime running lights on, acting cocky, but you know you love it regardless.\n\n\n\nThis is also a quote word for word from Jay-z’s song “Show You How”\n\nspitta is known for recycling classic lines from his favorite rappers.", "annotation_id": "1456314", "url": "https://genius.com/1456314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Bitch, I’m from the Burg so you know that I be thuggin’", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm from the Burg so you know that I be thuggin'"], "meaning": "Wiz represents his hometown, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.", "annotation_id": "1456176", "url": "https://genius.com/1456176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Choppers like the Russians,", "vault_lines": ["Choppers like the Russians,"], "meaning": "A ‘chopper’, better known as an AK-47, is a Russian assault rifle, one of the most reliable assault rifles ever manufactured.", "annotation_id": "1456166", "url": "https://genius.com/1456166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Black & Yellow, Black & Yellow, something out of nothing", "vault_lines": ["Black & Yellow, Black & Yellow, something out of nothing"], "meaning": "“Black and Yellow” was his breakthrough hit into the mainstream.\nIn an interview for a radio station he once said that song just came to him out of no where sitting in the studio just messing around, explains something out of nothing.", "annotation_id": "1456158", "url": "https://genius.com/1456158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Choosin’", "line": "Pull up, pushing buttons blowing OG like it’s nothing", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, pushing buttons blowing OG like it's nothing"], "meaning": "Wiz is known for his “push to start/ pushing buttons” line where he’s talking about the new cars that dont require turning a key, that start at a push of a button.\n\nBlowing OG, he is smoking OG Kush, a popular strain of marijuana\n\n\n\nIn addition to having a “push-to-start” car, he is also “pushing the buttons” of haters (ties in with the hook about haters ‘losing it’ when curren$y drives off in his nice car) Khalifa also references how “It’s Nothing”, a common theme for Young Khalifa.", "annotation_id": "1456124", "url": "https://genius.com/1456124", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
