{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "Tryna shine like Birdman teeth glitters", "vault_lines": ["Tryna shine like Birdman teeth glitters"], "meaning": "Ross speaks on his desire to shine as bright as rap mogul Birdman. His opinion of the Cash Money head has soured in recent years, however.", "annotation_id": "17018668", "url": "https://genius.com/17018668", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "My loose cheese scooped up the Gucci", "vault_lines": ["My loose cheese scooped up the Gucci"], "meaning": "Gucci, an Italian fashion brand, is noted for being very expensive. With a net worth of over $30 million, Ross’s loose cheese (change) can buy Gucci clothing.", "annotation_id": "17018660", "url": "https://genius.com/17018660", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "I touched her with the second hand stroke Got her mind racin’ quicker than a Lambo", "vault_lines": ["I touched her with the second hand stroke", "Got her mind racin' quicker than a Lambo"], "meaning": "Funny wordplay by Rozay, as his girl is getting more and more nervous as Ross gets closer to her.\n\nShe got so many thoughts on her mind that moment, the thoughts are racing even faster than a Lamborghini.", "annotation_id": "2968306", "url": "https://genius.com/2968306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "Biggest boss in the game, chatter, I never mind that Cause if it mattered, C-Murder would go diamond", "vault_lines": ["Biggest boss in the game, chatter, I never mind that", "Cause if it mattered, C-Murder would go diamond"], "meaning": "Perhaps the greatest and realest shit Ross has ever wrote.\n\nRoss first begins by reminding us who he is exactly – the biggest Boss that we’ve seen thus far. Ross has had numerous Boss-titled songs throughout his career: “Boss”, “The Boss”, “I'ma Boss”, “You The Boss”, etc. Three years after this song was released, Ross was even named GQ’s Bawse of the Year in 2012.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/44928899796307968\n\nRoss then goes on to defend himself from the harsh criticism he has received throughout his career, from 50 Cent and the rest of his critics and haters.\n\nThis song was released in Spring 2009, during the prime of the Rozay-50 Cent beef. Just before their beef, it was revealed that Ross had been employed as a correctional officer for 18 months. Throughout their ordeal, Fif poked fun at Ross because of gangsta image he portrays in his raps, despite his CO stint.\n\nRoss’s response to 50 and the rest of his haters was simple: If being real and living out your lyrics truly mattered the way that Ross' critics claim, then C-Murder would have had a diamond certified album. Ross insinuates that “keeping it real” has no true merit on sales or legacy – the only thing that truly matters in the rap game is to make extremely tantalizing music, which Ross has continued to do throughout his career.\n\nC-Murder is a New Orleans rapper who, as his stage name would suggest, was convicted of murder. C-Murder is often thought of one of the realest rappers ever, if not the realest rapper ever. He sold relatively well throughout his career, but never came close to a diamond certification (an achievement for selling 10 million copies), verifying Rozay’s point.", "annotation_id": "2175865", "url": "https://genius.com/2175865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "But I’m sellin’ records, everything I touch gold", "vault_lines": ["But I'm sellin' records, everything I touch gold"], "meaning": "Despite his previous history in drug dealing, Ross no longer needs to sell dope because of his status in the music industry. Ross is one of the better selling artists of the 2000’s era, as he goes on to explain his 3 million worldwide sales in the next line.\n\nEach one of Ross' albums except for Deeper Than Rap (ironically, the album that this song was featured on) and Mastermind (on its way to gold though) have been certified Gold by the RIAA. One might say that Rozay has the Midas Touch, the ability to turn everything he touches into gold.", "annotation_id": "2076236", "url": "https://genius.com/2076236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "Better yet, check the record, three milli’ sold", "vault_lines": ["Better yet, check the record, three milli' sold"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has had his fair share of criticism over the years. In response to the haters and critics, Ross' rebuttal is his album sales: he has sold over three million albums worldwide, which is quite the accomplishment.", "annotation_id": "2076229", "url": "https://genius.com/2076229", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "Down to go toe-to-toe before Tecmo Bowl", "vault_lines": ["Down to go toe-to-toe before Tecmo Bowl"], "meaning": "Ross was always down to settle beefs by scrapping it out with whomever, even before the arcade game was released – which was in 1988.", "annotation_id": "1513254", "url": "https://genius.com/1513254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "As I recline, cut ’em like key lime", "vault_lines": ["As I recline, cut 'em like key lime"], "meaning": "Cut em is reffering to the aforementioned Foreign Felines as him having sex with a girl because he follows up with We both came as in he has sex with the chick till they both came.", "annotation_id": "828061", "url": "https://genius.com/828061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "Two handguns on the riders for the shows", "vault_lines": ["Two handguns on the riders for the shows"], "meaning": "On his list of demands when he comes to a venue to perform, aside from the usual rapper accoutrements (ie. Champagne, Weed, Blunts, Hoes, Green M&M’s, etc.), Ross needs the promoters to supply two handguns as well.", "annotation_id": "828060", "url": "https://genius.com/828060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "Black flaggin’, just braggin’, I’m a street nigga", "vault_lines": ["Black flaggin', just braggin', I'm a street nigga"], "meaning": "Gangster Disciples is a gang that is known for having black flags. Ross reps them cause he’s a street nigga and inspired by their founder, Larry Hoover.\n\nHowever, in late 2012, Ross ran into some trouble with the GDs.", "annotation_id": "796724", "url": "https://genius.com/796724", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "I’m the down south Nas, click so firm Ridin’ with a fox as the cigar burn", "vault_lines": ["I'm the down south Nas, click so firm", "Ridin' with a fox as the cigar burn"], "meaning": "A reference to the hip group, The Firm, which consisted of Nas, Nature, Cormega, AZ, and Foxy Brown.", "annotation_id": "796645", "url": "https://genius.com/796645", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "This cigar got me buzzin’ like a beehive", "vault_lines": ["This cigar got me buzzin' like a beehive"], "meaning": "Ross compares the buzz he gets from smoking to the buzzing sound bees make. This could be a reference to the Beehive Cigar shop in Utah.", "annotation_id": "613353", "url": "https://genius.com/613353", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "I reflect as I’m ridin’ in a Rolls Royce Get respect cause I give these hoes no choice", "vault_lines": ["I reflect as I'm ridin' in a Rolls Royce", "Get respect cause I give these hoes no choice"], "meaning": "Ross reflects on his life in the music biz as he cruises in his Rolls Royce and he gets respect from people who may not really like him because the moves he’s made in the industry & life in general have made it impossible to feel otherwise.\n\nAlso note the alliteration with letter R in the first line.", "annotation_id": "361248", "url": "https://genius.com/361248", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "Most wanted, I’m Bin Laden on a beat nigga", "vault_lines": ["Most wanted, I'm Bin Laden on a beat nigga"], "meaning": "Rozay compares other artists' desires for a Ross feature to the USA’s want for terrorist Osama Bin Laden, who topped their most wanted list for quite some time.", "annotation_id": "255545", "url": "https://genius.com/255545", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cigar Music", "line": "See the Audemar? It’s call a terminator The exact watch Arnold wore in Terminator", "vault_lines": ["See the Audemar? It's call a terminator", "The exact watch Arnold wore in Terminator"], "meaning": "A reference to the Audemar Piguet Terminator T3 watch. Arnold Schwarzenegger wore this watch in the third Terminator film.\n\n\n\nRick Ross bought the exact same watch.\n\n\n\nBAWSE.", "annotation_id": "255540", "url": "https://genius.com/255540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
