{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "I’m still mo’ fire", "vault_lines": ["I’m always going higher, I’m still mo' fire"], "meaning": "You A Lie was the song that caught MMG’s attention, and Rick Ross even hopped on the remix. “I’m mo' fire” was part of the chorus. Rockie’s saying that even though he’s signed to a major label he’s still going to remain the same guy", "annotation_id": "1250491", "url": "https://genius.com/1250491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "And new Olympic sevens I need rings and the medal", "vault_lines": ["And new Olympic sevens I need rings and the medal"], "meaning": "Olympic 7’s are Jordans that just came out around the time of this song. Jordan wore them during the 1992 Olympics and won a gold medal with “The Dream Team”. Also, he won an NBA Championship that year, giving him a ring.", "annotation_id": "1250485", "url": "https://genius.com/1250485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "Holes in the roof, hardly had a door", "vault_lines": ["Holes in the roof, hardly had a door"], "meaning": "He’s referring to the house he grew up in. It was so beat up there were holes in the roof, and barely had doors.", "annotation_id": "1131800", "url": "https://genius.com/1131800", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "Just hope that she never fall off like Kreayshawn", "vault_lines": ["Just hope that she never fall off like Kreayshawn"], "meaning": "After San Francisco rapper Kreayshawn dropped her debut song Gucci Gucci, many had high hopes for her.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately her debut album, Somethin' ‘Bout Kreay was a colossal failure.", "annotation_id": "1127744", "url": "https://genius.com/1127744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "Telephone lines ringing, calling Angie Martinez", "vault_lines": ["Telephone lines ringing, calling Angie Martinez"], "meaning": "Angie “The Voice of New York” Martinez is a host on the popular New York radio station Hot 97", "annotation_id": "1127680", "url": "https://genius.com/1127680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "Now it’s the double M dream team doing something special Bout to kill the shit so get the casket and the shovel", "vault_lines": ["Now it's the double M dream team doing something special", "Bout to kill the shit so get the casket and the shovel"], "meaning": "MMG is going to be doing big things, so a casket and shovel will be needed to bury the competition\n\nRockie also has a song on the Electric Highway mixtape called Something Special", "annotation_id": "1127100", "url": "https://genius.com/1127100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "Yeah I’m talking gunplay, yeah I walk it too Yeah that nigga ratted, yeah that depo true Yeah I’m really ’bout it, yeah I out anybody", "vault_lines": ["Yeah I'm talking gunplay, yeah I walk it too", "Yeah that nigga ratted, yeah that depo true", "Yeah I'm really 'bout it, yeah I out anybody"], "meaning": "A play on Jay’s verse from Clique :\n\nYeah, I’m talking Ye, yeah, I’m talking Rih\nYeah, I’m talking B, nigga, I’m talking me\n\nDepo refers to deposition which is an out-of-court oral testimony of a witness that is reduced to writing for later use in court.", "annotation_id": "1126850", "url": "https://genius.com/1126850", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "John Legend flow the magnificent me", "vault_lines": ["John Legend flow the magnificent me"], "meaning": "Ricky did a song with John Legend off his album “Deeper Than Rap” called “Magnificent”", "annotation_id": "1126835", "url": "https://genius.com/1126835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "Kanye shoes sorry No ID,", "vault_lines": ["Kanye shoes sorry No ID,"], "meaning": "Kanye West makes shoes for Nike, such as the Air Yeezy and Air Yeezy II.\n\nNo ID is a double entendre:\n\n\nNot customizable shoes, as Nike offers some customizable shoes\n\n\n\n\n\n\nReference to producer No ID who is, Kanye’s mentor. Maybe suggesting Kanye is to Ross for pumps what No ID was to Kanye for beats.", "annotation_id": "1125863", "url": "https://genius.com/1125863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clique", "line": "Hottest niggas in the game MMG, tour starts in a few weeks If you fucking with it, fuck with me Ha ha", "vault_lines": ["If you fucking with it, fuck with me"], "meaning": "Ross is exalting his crew, Maybach Music Group.\nThey stared an MMG Tour on Friday, November 2, 2012\n\nSome of the boys\n\n\n\nThis is one of the most blatant examples of self-promotion ever.", "annotation_id": "1125758", "url": "https://genius.com/1125758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
