{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clouds", "line": "We’ll just refer to her as alpine", "vault_lines": ["We'll just refer to her as alpine"], "meaning": "Alpine climate is the average weather (climate) for a region above the tree line. This climate is also referred to as mountain climate or highland climate.\n\nAlpines can be generally covered in snow.\n\nIn the same way, he’s got mountains of coke, just as an alpine is a giant mountain of white.\n\n\n\nTyrone’s vacation spot.", "annotation_id": "1107371", "url": "https://genius.com/1107371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clouds", "line": "You only second to my first love, haha", "vault_lines": ["You only second to my first love, haha"], "meaning": "A pie is a kilo of coke.\n\nDo you wanna make pies? Yes, I wanna make pies\nLet me see it in your eyes, I wanna make pies", "annotation_id": "1107370", "url": "https://genius.com/1107370", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clouds", "line": "Close enough to see the gates open", "vault_lines": ["Close enough to see the gates open"], "meaning": "Playing on the words of ‘close’ and ‘open’ Push infers a metaphorical gate. She is ‘close’, (aka near enough) to see them open but they could ‘close’ (aka shut), just as quickly. Nice use of a homonym.\n\nThis also ties in with the previous line refering to the gates of heaven.", "annotation_id": "1106405", "url": "https://genius.com/1106405", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Clouds", "line": "We in the God ceilings, cathedral-style homes Rosaries in my Rolls Royce, God put me on", "vault_lines": ["We in the God ceilings, cathedral-style homes", "Rosaries in my Rolls Royce, God put me on"], "meaning": "The conflict between God and Mammon is an ongoing theme with many rappers.  Here, Curren$y neatly solves the problem Prosperity Gospel-style, by proclaiming that not only is the Big Guy on his side, but is actually directly responsible for his rap success.  We’re looking forward to the sure-to-be-a-smash collaboration record!", "annotation_id": "1091435", "url": "https://genius.com/1091435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
