{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Peep this Rollie fugazy, I’m sellin’ game to a pimp", "vault_lines": ["Peep this Rollie fugazy, I'm sellin' game to a pimp"], "meaning": "Rollie is slang for Rolex which  is a high end Swiss luxury watchmaker often regarded as one of the best watchmakers by rappers.\n\nFugazi or Fugazy is Italian slang for fake/false.\n\nRoss is bragging about how he can sell a fake watch to a pimp, someone who would be able to tell the difference between a fake and a real Rolex.\n\nInterestingly in 2014, the same year as the song came out Ross was sued $90,000 by Rolex for not paying for three Rolex watches he ordered in August the previous year.", "annotation_id": "13251016", "url": "https://genius.com/13251016", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "John Doe nigga, you know that convo, nigga", "vault_lines": ["John Doe nigga, you know that convo, nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross compares himself to serial killer John Doe from the movie Se7en", "annotation_id": "4918083", "url": "https://genius.com/4918083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "A mil’ in the hole is every real nigga goal", "vault_lines": ["A mil' in the hole is every real nigga goal"], "meaning": "Either broke, living in poverty or being an average person with an average income, everyone wants to live in luxury and to become successful– as well as not having to worry about wasting/retaining money.", "annotation_id": "4614347", "url": "https://genius.com/4614347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "All white nigga, Big Ike nigga", "vault_lines": ["All white nigga, Big Ike nigga"], "meaning": "In same Rick Ross fashion he continues to refer to infamous drug lords and traffickers,now Leslie ‘Ike’ Atikson. USA Army master sergeant that moved heroin (smuggled in dead soldiers coffins) from 1968 to 1975,with the partership of frank lucas (Danzels charecter from American Gangster)", "annotation_id": "4499601", "url": "https://genius.com/4499601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Conch fritters", "vault_lines": ["Get these conch fritters"], "meaning": "Pronounced as “Konk Fritters”, Theses are a deep fried breaded nugget consisting of sliced bits of Conch meat, which is typically pull out of the shell.\n\nConch fritters are a delicacy of The Bahamas, and other West Indian countries.", "annotation_id": "4483926", "url": "https://genius.com/4483926", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Her man wanted a line, so I sold ’em a verse", "vault_lines": ["Her man wanted a line, so I sold 'em a verse"], "meaning": "This line could have a different meaning far as more or less but first part:\n\nHer man wanted a line\n\n\n\nCould possibly mean that her boyfriend, husband or whatever wanted a line, as in a line of coke, which lots of people did in the 80’s, snorted lines of coke.\n\nSecond part where Ross says:\n\nso I sold ‘em a verse\n\nNow this could metaphorically mean he sold 16 lines of coke as there are 16 bars or 16 lines in a standard rap verse.", "annotation_id": "4474207", "url": "https://genius.com/4474207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Get that paper, my plug, he sent that pack from Bahamas It’s uncut like the 80's, 17 still my number", "vault_lines": ["Get that paper, my plug, he sent that pack from Bahamas", "It's uncut like the 80's, 17 still my number"], "meaning": "A plug is a supplier. Ross gets his pure cocaine through the Florida Keys – Bahamas to Miami. Each kilo costs him $17,000.", "annotation_id": "4453442", "url": "https://genius.com/4453442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "It is what it is, I left the vest at the crib Extended the clip, I’ma give ’em the biz Catch you jackin’ your dick, now you fucked in the game Leave you flat on your back, where you lay was a stain", "vault_lines": ["It is what it is, I left the vest at the crib", "Extended the clip, I'ma give 'em the biz", "Catch you jackin' your dick, now you fucked in the game", "Leave you flat on your back, where you lay was a stain"], "meaning": "Ross goes literal comedy rap while describing shooting his enemy in the dick. He caught you nappin' (masturbating) so now you’re really fucked with not just a stain on your pants – there’s probably a pool of blood on your bed…and you’re most likely dead!\n\nReminds us of 21 Jump Street…\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5DDyciFBmo8", "annotation_id": "4444956", "url": "https://genius.com/4444956", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Bo Diddley nigga, oh really nigga? Bunche Park hot, block full of killas Lil’ Trav, nigga, the bad nigga Execution upcomin’, ‘bout that lil’ tab nigga River City they slide, aka homicide Rest in peace to the Goonies, one day we’ll be eye to eye", "vault_lines": ["Bo Diddley nigga, oh really nigga?", "Bunche Park hot, block full of killas", "Lil' Trav, nigga, the bad nigga", "Execution upcomin', 'bout that lil' tab nigga", "River City they slide, aka homicide", "Rest in peace to the Goonies, one day we'll be eye to eye"], "meaning": "Ross shouts out his local hustlers, dead and alive for still keeping it real. Bunche Park is close to where Ross grew up in Carol City, while Ross still runs with the killers in River City – another hot block about 30mins south of Bunche Park.", "annotation_id": "4444942", "url": "https://genius.com/4444942", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Get you that weed and white, want you a combo nigga Checkmate with the sticks, identify by your kicks Welcome home to Skinner, already bought him a brick", "vault_lines": ["Get you that weed and white, want you a combo nigga", "Checkmate with the sticks, identify by your kicks"], "meaning": "A primo is a blunt sprinkled with cocaine. Ross has the best weed & coke out – his homie Skinner just got out of the penitentiary so he bought him a kilo!", "annotation_id": "4444937", "url": "https://genius.com/4444937", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Carol City the set, 183rd still the route We live in the jungle, fishtanks in the house", "vault_lines": ["Carol City the set, 183rd still the route", "We live in the jungle, fishtanks in the house"], "meaning": "Ross was born and raised in Carol City. 183rd St runs right through the block. Fishtanks is a nod to kilo’s of cocaine – “fishscale” is a common term to describe the drug.\n\n\n\n Not only does Ross describe his living conditions as a concrete jungle, but juxtaposes the difference in his life experience. Instead of having real fishtanks in the house, he’s literally got bricks of cocaine.", "annotation_id": "4444931", "url": "https://genius.com/4444931", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "It’s that Dade Country yayo shit Double MOB I’m finny take these pussy niggas down Beat Billionaire", "vault_lines": ["It's that Dade Country yayo shit", "I'm finny take these pussy niggas down"], "meaning": "Dade County is in Miami where Ross used to deal cocaine (yayo).\n\nHe also shoutsout producer Beat Billionaire", "annotation_id": "4436385", "url": "https://genius.com/4436385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Boobie Gang was the clique, forever changed the game Bunky Brown was a legend, Wayne Parker the mane (Vonda)", "vault_lines": ["Boobie Gang was the clique, forever changed the game", "Bunky Brown was a legend, Wayne Parker the mane (Vonda)"], "meaning": "I studied Kenneth Williams, I’m one hell of a student\n\nThe “Boobie Boys” were one of Miami’s most violent gangs during the late 80’s and early 90’s. Miami Dade Police Department estimates they were responsible for more than 100 killings during an eight year run. Rick Ross is rumoured to have been an inside man for the gang while he was a C.O.\n\nHowever Bunky Brown and Vonda (otherwise known as Avonda Dowling or the “Black Girl”) were in an opposing gang to the “Boobie Boys”. Their turf war ultimately bought both gangs down as the FBI got involved and caught up with them.\n\nRoss is most likely just name dropping them and showing respect to both sides.", "annotation_id": "4431511", "url": "https://genius.com/4431511", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "Welcome home George Jung (RIP McBride) The real Boston George", "vault_lines": ["The real Boston George"], "meaning": "Ross shouts out George Jung aka Boston George. Jung was part of the Medellin cartel and a major drug smuggler during the 1980s American crack epidemic, what this song is about.\n\nGeorge Jung was released from prison on June 2, 2014 which is why Rozay welcomes him back.", "annotation_id": "4400061", "url": "https://genius.com/4400061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "I got coke like the 80's I got coke like the 80's, in my coke white Mercedes I got coke like the 80's I got coke like the 80's, I got coke like the 80's I got coke like the 80's, I got coke like the 80's I got coke like the 80's, I got coke like the 80's I got coke like the 80's I got coke like the 80's, in my coke white Mercedes", "vault_lines": ["I got coke like the 80's, in my coke white Mercedes", "I got coke like the 80's, I got coke like the 80's"], "meaning": "A reference to the crack epidemic, a period in the 1980s to early 90s (also known as the “Ronald Regan Era”) which saw a major surge of crack cocaine use in cities.\n\nIt was the Boobie Boys that ran the drug scene in Miami during the crack epidemic, the cartel that Ross was a prominent member of.", "annotation_id": "4399849", "url": "https://genius.com/4399849", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Coke Like the 80's", "line": "[Sample] Okay last time, this is drugs This is your brain on drugs Any questions?", "vault_lines": ["This is your brain on drugs"], "meaning": "This sample is from an 80’s anti-drug commercial that compares the effects that drugs have on the brain to the frying an egg.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3FtNm9CgA6U", "annotation_id": "4395582", "url": "https://genius.com/4395582", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
