{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Full confrontation, home invasion for the quarter key", "vault_lines": ["Full confrontation, home invasion for the quarter key"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION: This is a continuation from the line before where Ross suggests 100k will cover everything he has been talking about. Now he is suggesting he can send the dogs to run up in your house in exchange for giving them a quarter key. As simple as that.", "annotation_id": "8320157", "url": "https://genius.com/8320157", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Sell a lot of record but I make a brick jump", "vault_lines": ["Sell a lot of record but I make a brick jump"], "meaning": "Rick Ross didn’t actually sell a lot of copies of his latest record Black Market—it only sold 34,000 copies in the first week. But in the grand scheme of his career, he has sold a lot of records—his 2014 record Mastermind was his fifth No. 1.", "annotation_id": "8580286", "url": "https://genius.com/8580286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Catch a flight to Paris, time to get some other money", "vault_lines": ["Catch a flight to Paris, time to get some other money"], "meaning": "Ross also talks about spending time in Europe on his song “Lay Back,”, DJ Khaled’s “I’m On One,” and Jay Z’s “FuckWitMeYouKnowIGotIt.” His lavish video for “Rich Is Gangsta” was also filmed in Paris.\n\nIn 2013, Ross told Time:\n\nIf you want it to be different, you stop. Move to Paris. I want to do this.", "annotation_id": "8545210", "url": "https://genius.com/8545210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "The red ring, nigga looking like a fed case", "vault_lines": ["The red ring, nigga looking like a fed case"], "meaning": "Baby aka Birdman, who Ross called out in the last verse is known for flashing an oversized ruby ring, consistent with his alleged Blood gang affiliation.\n\n\n\nA federal case is tougher to beat than a state case, so Rozay’s implying that Birdman’s financial transgressions could be a big deal.", "annotation_id": "8379631", "url": "https://genius.com/8379631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "If you real, all we kill for is color money Fuck where you from, ’cause all we deal with is color money", "vault_lines": ["If you real, all we kill for is color money", "Fuck where you from, 'cause all we deal with is color money"], "meaning": "The phrase “color money” comes from a viral video of rapper Plies getting body-slammed at a show—\"color money\" was the code word his DJ yelled for security.\n\n“Color money” could also refer to modern hundred dollar bills, which have blue security ribbons—they started circulating in 2013.", "annotation_id": "8353739", "url": "https://genius.com/8353739", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Red rubies on, they can’t believe a nigga rap Color money still feed niggas in the trap", "vault_lines": ["Red rubies on, they can't believe a nigga rap", "Color money still feed niggas in the trap"], "meaning": "This is reference to the Hood Billionaire cover art which has Ross showing off among many jewelry his red ruby chain.", "annotation_id": "8322866", "url": "https://genius.com/8322866", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Got her selling pussy for the love of the money", "vault_lines": ["Got her selling pussy for the love of the money"], "meaning": "The girl he’s mentioning in this line is a prostitute.\n\nShe’s “selling her pussy,” or in other words: she’s getting paid for sex.\n\n\n\n‘'For the love of money’‘ is an interesting wordplay. Sex is related to love most of the time, but in the girl’s case it’s not about love for the other person, but love for the money she gets from him.", "annotation_id": "8321833", "url": "https://genius.com/8321833", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Fuck all these rappers, real talk, ’cause I ain’t fucking with ’em", "vault_lines": ["Fuck all these rappers, real talk, 'cause I ain't fucking with 'em"], "meaning": "Ross uses the word “Fuck” as a pun over here.\n\n\n\nHe tells us to “Fuck all these rappers” because he won’t feel them and so, can’t fuck with them.", "annotation_id": "8320217", "url": "https://genius.com/8320217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Put it down quarter key in every category", "vault_lines": ["Put it down quarter key in every category"], "meaning": "A “quarter key” is slang for a quarter kilogram of cocaine—250 grams.", "annotation_id": "8320069", "url": "https://genius.com/8320069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Get it down even if a nigga momma know me", "vault_lines": ["Get it down even if a nigga momma know me"], "meaning": "This line could mean two things\n\n\nRick Ross will get any female to “get down” on him even if it’s your mom.\nOr Ross is saying he’ll get down to hurting you, referring to the above bars, even if he’s close with you and your family, and knows your mom.\n\n\n\nBoth interpretations demonstrate how unrelentless and unforgiving Rick Ross can be. I guess he’s living up to the name of his fifth album, “God Forgives, I Don’t”.", "annotation_id": "8320004", "url": "https://genius.com/8320004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Rob a nigga close to me, you better bring it back", "vault_lines": ["Rob a nigga close to me, you better bring it back"], "meaning": "This line refers to an incident during the 2012 BET awards when MMG artist Gunplay was jumped by 50 cent and his security team for his MMG chain.\n\nIt’s near certain that 50 never brought the chain back—he famously bragged about wearing in a video taken at a bowling alley.", "annotation_id": "8319255", "url": "https://genius.com/8319255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Miami niggas got ’em changing all the gun laws", "vault_lines": ["Miami niggas got 'em changing all the gun laws"], "meaning": "Ross could be referring to a proposal in the Florida legislature, which if passed would allow for the “open-carry” of firearms in the state.", "annotation_id": "8319253", "url": "https://genius.com/8319253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Only nigga that you know with two NASCARs", "vault_lines": ["Only nigga that you know with two NASCARs"], "meaning": "Ross likes fast cars, but he doesn’t own two NASCARS. In 2013 he customized Maybach Music Group’s Ferrari 458 Italia with stock car logos.\n\nhttp://imgur.com/DBS4Aa0", "annotation_id": "8319233", "url": "https://genius.com/8319233", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "You still alive ’cause you niggas still running from me", "vault_lines": ["You still alive 'cause you niggas still running from me"], "meaning": "The only way these “niggas” can stay alive is to run from Rozay – Ross leaves it up to the listener’s imagination, as to how he will kill them, either literally or metaphorically in the rap game. Notice the rhyme scheme here too, which conflates “me” and “money,” continually throughout the verse. Ross is in the $$money$$.", "annotation_id": "8319228", "url": "https://genius.com/8319228", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Indictments coming and I really think they coming for me Tinted box Chevy, pussy nigga gunning for me", "vault_lines": ["Indictments coming and I really think they coming for me", "Tinted box Chevy, pussy nigga gunning for me"], "meaning": "Firstly, Ross references his origin story, namely: selling coke out the back of a Box Chevy, which he even wrote a song about.\n\nSecondly, Ross compares his drug trafficking to his cowardly enemies trying to gun him off his rap throne. Despite their constant presence, neither charges nor enemies will be able to catch him.\n\nhttps://genius.com/1444864", "annotation_id": "8319174", "url": "https://genius.com/8319174", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "I got a duffle bag that I wanna shop with Or get another double R to cut the top with Or hit the booty club and go and get some pussy wit I might buy a bitch a Benz if I’m pussy whipped", "vault_lines": ["I got a duffle bag that I wanna shop with", "Or get another double R to cut the top with"], "meaning": "Ross’s money stacks can’t fit in his pocket so he carries them in a duffle bag. He has so much money that he doesn’t know what to do with all of it, but he knows he wants to spend it. Maybe buy a Rolls-Royce (“double R”), or rent some hookers, or even get one of the hookers a Mercedes-Benz, depending on how good the sexual experience is.", "annotation_id": "8317645", "url": "https://genius.com/8317645", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Blackjack, black bottles with the black cards", "vault_lines": ["Blackjack, black bottles with the black cards"], "meaning": "This line expresses Rozay’s extensive wealth. The Blackjack part of this line could have multiple meanings:\n\n\nRoss could be referring to physically playing blackjack—high stakes, of course.\nBlackjack could also refer to Armand de Brignac (Ace of Spades) Champaign.\n\n\n\nBlack Bottles refers to Luc Belaire, a French Rosé  company for which Ross is a brand ambassador.\n\nBlack Cards refers to the American Express Centurion card. The annual spending minimum for this card is 250k, a symbol of the Boss’s immense wealth.", "annotation_id": "8317078", "url": "https://genius.com/8317078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Call him a C.O. but you better not go call police", "vault_lines": ["Call him a C.O. but you better not go call police"], "meaning": "Ross is throwing shade at his longtime rival 50 Cent. In an interview with Tim Westwood, 50 said the reason he and Ross have never had a physical confrontation is because his rival’s past as a Florida Corrections Officer in the 1990s.\n\n\n\nRoss acknowledges his past, but he argues that 50’s is actually worse. He told the Breakfast Club that 50 Cent is basically the police himself, referencing an incident when GS9 members tried to confront 50 outside of an NYC nightclub, but were unable to because he had called for a police escort.", "annotation_id": "8315885", "url": "https://genius.com/8315885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Bottles in the club got me screaming, “Color money”", "vault_lines": ["Bottles in the club got me screaming, \"Color money\""], "meaning": "New hundred dollar bills have a blueish color to them. Ross uses these hundreds to pay for bottles in the club.\n\n“Color money” might also be Ross referencing his being rich and a man of color.", "annotation_id": "8315658", "url": "https://genius.com/8315658", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "If you wanna get a block, then you should see the man", "vault_lines": ["If you wanna get a block, then you should see the man"], "meaning": "“Block” is slang for the kilogram of cocaine that Ross starts the verse by trying to sell to you.", "annotation_id": "8315623", "url": "https://genius.com/8315623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Make her sign a prenup just to get my dick sucked", "vault_lines": ["Make her sign a prenup just to get my dick sucked"], "meaning": "A prenup is a legal agreement before marriage, usually to protect the assets of the wealthier partner. Kanye made it famous in “Gold Digger”:\n\nIf you ain’t no punk, holla, “We want prenup!”\n“We want prenup!” (Yeah!)\n\nHowever, Drake flipped the gender norms by suggesting that rap’s leading lady, Nicki Minaj, could use one too in “Back to Back”:\n\nAnd shout-out to all my boss bitches wifin' niggas\nMake sure you hit him with the prenup\nThen tell that man to ease up\n\nRick Ross is so careful with his money, he needs the protection of a prenup before he even gets to third base!", "annotation_id": "8315472", "url": "https://genius.com/8315472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Double M, we balling way harder than Puff and them It ain’t no love loss, I only see one boss", "vault_lines": ["Double M, we balling way harder than Puff and them", "It ain't no love loss, I only see one boss"], "meaning": "Ross is solidifying his label, Maybach Music Group’s spot above all other rappers and labels in the game by taking a light jab at business partner and good friend Sean Puffy Combs of Bad Boy records.\n\nRoss' statement is more of a sparing match between friendly competitors. He means no personal disrespect, he just views himself as the only Boss and Double M as the top crew.\n\nThis may also be a sly response to Drake’s “besides Ricky Ross, Aubrey the biggest boss here” line.", "annotation_id": "8312464", "url": "https://genius.com/8312464", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "I got more money than that pussy that you’re signed to", "vault_lines": ["I got more money than that pussy that you're signed to"], "meaning": "In defending his protege Meek Mill, Ross directed these lyrics towards Drake, and thus as an extension, this lyric is a jab at Birdman. This was confirmed as a shot at Birdman as Ross appeared on Power 105’s “the Breakfast Club” two days following the release of this song, to discuss these lyrics, and stated he is in full support of Lil Wayne and the line is directed at Birdman:\n\nI don’t have [a relationship] with Birdman. What Wayne’s going through as an artist, him being a boss. Me idolizing Birdman at a time, me looking up to Wayne… for me to see the way things are transpiring I don’t respect that.\n\nThis comes as no surprise, as Wayne made a guest appearance on the Renzel Remixes tape and attended Ross' album release party at Club LIV.", "annotation_id": "8310408", "url": "https://genius.com/8310408", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Diamonds all through the watch and you should see the band", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds all through the watch and you should see the band"], "meaning": "Ross is no stranger to flossing his jewelry. His watch has diamonds throughout. “The band” refers to the band of his watch as well as the band that holds his stack of money.", "annotation_id": "8310078", "url": "https://genius.com/8310078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Aye, call lil’ homie to the stage The one got that color money Trappin’ for the color money Make it happen for the color money 305, nigga You know what it is", "vault_lines": ["Make it happen for the color money"], "meaning": "Color Money refers to the incident from April 2015, when a fan body-slammed Plies off of a stage. “Color money” was the code word Plies' DJ yelled for security\n\nhttps://youtu.be/siMHAZJmmR8?t=20s\n\nBy referencing this event, Young Renzel lets his friends (like Meek Mill) know he’ll be there for them if they get in trouble.\n\n\n\nColor Money is mainly money from different nations like European Euros and Japanese Yen, which have different colors on them. Ross is  making money worldwide, not just in the U.S.", "annotation_id": "8309025", "url": "https://genius.com/8309025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "So run Forrest, got some shooters and they dying too", "vault_lines": ["So run Forrest, got some shooters and they dying too"], "meaning": "“Run, Forrest” is subtle reference to Drake’s “0-100” lyric:\n\n“I run this shit, they like ‘Go, Forrest’.”\n\nDrake was of course referencing a key scene in the 1994 film Forrest Gump, where the title character found himself on the run from a gang of bullies.\n\nRoss appears to be on the offensive now, with a team of gunmen willing to die for him.\n\nWhen asked if lines in “Color Money” were directed at Drake during a Power 105 “The Breakfast Club” interview, Ross didn’t confirm, but he didn’t deny:\n\nEverybody who knows Rozay, knows how I get down, and when I come, I come. Let’s see how it unfolds.", "annotation_id": "8307893", "url": "https://genius.com/8307893", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "We back to back and down to whack a nigga unborn", "vault_lines": ["We back to back and down to whack a nigga unborn"], "meaning": "Playing off of the last line, Ross directly references Drake’s “Back to Back” here, showing that he’s down to ride for Meek Mill, who he signed to MMG in 2011.\n\nRozay is willing to go to great lengths to protect his people; he’s so serious that he’ll even murder an unborn child.\n\nWe’re sure The Boss is taking great poetic license here, because this sounds terrifying.", "annotation_id": "8307849", "url": "https://genius.com/8307849", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "line": "Color money got your bitch out on a world tour My lil’ homie made a million on his girl tour", "vault_lines": ["Color money got your bitch out on a world tour", "My lil' homie made a million on his girl tour"], "meaning": "Rick Ross uses these two bars to remix Drake’s “Back to Back” Meek Mill diss:\n\nIf you love her then you gotta give the world to her\nIs that a world tour or your girl’s tour?\n\nThe first half of Ross' couplet finds him bragging about taking some poor sap’s girlfriend on trips around the world, but on the second half he comes to Meek’s defense.\n\nYes, Meek was an opening act on Nicki Minaj’s The Pinkprint tour, but according to Ross he made a million dollars performing.", "annotation_id": "8307791", "url": "https://genius.com/8307791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Color Money", "status": "done", "targets": 30, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-color-money-lyrics", "genius_title": "Color Money", "genius_id": 2381771, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "Miami have colors, colors, colors, colors, colors (Californ-i-a) Jamaica have colors, colors, colors, colors, colors (All the way to Dade County) My jewels have colors, colors, colors, colors, colors My people die over colors, colors, colors, colors, colors", "vault_lines": ["My people die over colors, colors, colors, colors, colors"], "meaning": "Miami, Jamaica, Jewels, and Sean Kingston’s people (who live in Jamaica) all have something in common: colors. The people in Miami and Jamaica are gang members that each rep their respective colors, whereas the jewels are things like rubies with the same colors.\n\nGang violence also leaves Kingston’s people to die over the colors they wear.", "annotation_id": "7259010", "url": "https://genius.com/7259010", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "Certain dudes get one in the head Certain places you wear certain colors you dead", "vault_lines": ["Certain dudes get one in the head", "Certain places you wear certain colors you dead"], "meaning": "Certain people get a head shot simply for wearing the wrong colors in the wrong places, i.e., wearing the Bloods' red in a Crip (Blue) neighborhood.", "annotation_id": "1006902", "url": "https://genius.com/1006902", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "And what I didn’t get from her I picked up watchin colors", "vault_lines": ["And what I didn't get from her I picked up watchin colors"], "meaning": "While he learned some aspects of the gang banging lifestyle from his mother, other aspects he learned from watching the 1988 movie “Colors” starring Sean Penn.", "annotation_id": "1006882", "url": "https://genius.com/1006882", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "Some get smoked others smoke chronic out of philly papers", "vault_lines": ["Some get smoked others smoke chronic out of philly papers"], "meaning": "Those fake Bloods wouldn’t last long before being killed. While the real Bloods smoke weed like a boss.", "annotation_id": "1006878", "url": "https://genius.com/1006878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "Some authentic some niggas Milli Vanilli bangers", "vault_lines": ["Some authentic some niggas Milli Vanilli bangers"], "meaning": "Some of the rappers claiming to be bloods are legit (maybe he’s talking about his friend Lil' Wayne here), but some are bullshitting, like Milli Vanilli, a 1980’s pop group who, it turned out, had been lip syncing during shows and hadn’t actually recorded the music in their catalogs.", "annotation_id": "834586", "url": "https://genius.com/834586", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "I said blood one on a Dr. Dre track Now the world is affiliated", "vault_lines": ["Now the world is affiliated"], "meaning": "Around the time of this song there had recently been an uptick in rappers claiming affiliation with the bloods, Game thinks some of them are just biting his style.", "annotation_id": "834583", "url": "https://genius.com/834583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "A couple red tops while the feds watchin", "vault_lines": ["A couple red tops while the feds watchin"], "meaning": "red tops being a reference to the caps on the vials that hold the drugs he’s selling.\n\n#The Red Tops\n\n\n\n#The Feds", "annotation_id": "834577", "url": "https://genius.com/834577", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "Let it be known, I reign Supreme like Kenneth McGriff Reincarnated put me in Queens and give me a strip", "vault_lines": ["Let it be known, I reign Supreme like Kenneth McGriff", "Reincarnated put me in Queens and give me a strip"], "meaning": "Kenneth McGriff (aka Supreme) was a well-known drug kingpin in Jamaica, Queens during the 1980’s.", "annotation_id": "834575", "url": "https://genius.com/834575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "I’m the Bastard Of The Party", "vault_lines": ["Check it! I'm the Bastard Of The Party"], "meaning": "Taking form the title of the HBO documentary “Bastards of the Party”, a documentary about how today’s popular gangs (bloods and crips particularly) grew out of the Black Panther Party when it was taken down by the government. Game himself is a Blood.", "annotation_id": "834558", "url": "https://genius.com/834558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "I’m from a world of different colors different faces Different slang different races different gangs different places", "vault_lines": ["I'm from a world of different colors different faces", "Different slang different races different gangs different places"], "meaning": "Nobody in this world is the same, people are different in so many ways and every has different interests. Kingston is showing these interests in relation to color (gangs, races, etc. these can also relate to himself)", "annotation_id": "690614", "url": "https://genius.com/690614", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "Kingston boy I rep like no other Black, yellow and green I bleed the Jamaican colors", "vault_lines": ["Kingston boy I rep like no other", "Black, yellow and green I bleed the Jamaican colors"], "meaning": "Sean Kingston was born Miami but moved to Kingston, Jamaica and still loves his origin.\n\n#Black, Yellow and Green.. Jamaican flag.", "annotation_id": "690602", "url": "https://genius.com/690602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "Beluga Heights", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Beluga Heights Records is a Los Angeles based record label founded by super-producer J. R. Rotem. The label has worked with Rihanna, Leona Lewis, Lil Kim, Ne-Yo, Rick Ross as well as developing/discovering new talent such as Sean Kingston, Jason DeRulo, Iyaz, Mann, Auburn, and Livvi Franc.", "annotation_id": "619202", "url": "https://genius.com/619202", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Colors", "line": "I’m the bloods to what Pac was to thugs What Snoop is to crips I’m the California king", "vault_lines": ["I'm the bloods to what Pac was to thugs", "What Snoop is to crips I'm the California king"], "meaning": "Pac was the king of thugs, Snoop Dogg is the most well know crip, and may i say when he says California king, i think it would have sounded better if he said I', the California blood\n\n#Snoop Dogg\n\n\n\n#2Pac", "annotation_id": "346700", "url": "https://genius.com/346700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
