{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Come Back to Me", "line": "Lookin’ like another game of show and tell (Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh, ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Lookin' like another game of show and tell (Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh, ooh)"], "meaning": "Ross likens the “game of show and tell” to him trying to prove his wealth to the ‘ponytail’ lady through material items; which involves the aspect of individuals trying to one-up each other (as previously juxtaposed with the vehicles), and possibly insinuating the idea that his actions may have been somewhat childish (show and tell being associated with elementary school)", "annotation_id": "20159172", "url": "https://genius.com/20159172", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Come Back to Me", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Teyana-taylor-come-back-to-me-lyrics", "genius_title": "Come Back to Me", "genius_id": 4995895, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Comfortable Freestyle", "line": "I’m the biggest rapper, Google me, Expedia", "vault_lines": ["I'm the biggest rapper, Google me, Expedia"], "meaning": "This line is famous for Ross’s obvious slip-up.\n\nWhat Ross would of been meaning to say was\n“I’m the biggest rapper google me Wikipedia”.\n\nWikipedia is a massive internet encyclopedia that millions of people use everyday.\n\nAlthough this isn’t that impressive in the late 2010s, this was a big brag back in 2009 as you would have to be very famous to have Wikipedia page dedicated to you.\n\nSadly for Ross as it is a freestyle he messes up and says “Expedia” instead of “Wikipedia”.\n\nThis is a strange brag as Expedia is an American travel website so it wouldn’t make sense for someone to find Rick Ross on there.", "annotation_id": "13280299", "url": "https://genius.com/13280299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Comfortable Freestyle", "line": "Bust a pussy nigga head you can sue me", "vault_lines": ["Bust a pussy nigga head you can sue me"], "meaning": "In 2008, YouTube entertainer DJ Vlad filed a lawsuit against Ross for assault and battery. Vlad claimed Ross organized an ambush on him at the 2008 Ozone Awards in Houston, Texas for asking questions about his past as a correctional officer", "annotation_id": "626710", "url": "https://genius.com/626710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Comfortable Freestyle", "line": "For the record pussy far from a c.o", "vault_lines": ["For the record pussy far from a c.o"], "meaning": "The ‘pussy’ he is referring to is DJ Vlad for his hand in exposing Ross as a former prison guard. Lord knows Ricky makes more than $12,000 a year these days.", "annotation_id": "626684", "url": "https://genius.com/626684", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Comfortable Freestyle", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-comfortable-freestyle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Comfortable Freestyle", "genius_id": 59012, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "Yeah, hit a button on that new don and watch it transform (transform)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, hit a button on that new don and watch it transform (transform)"], "meaning": "New Dawn*, a convertible Rolls Royce, that transforms when the roof disappears or appears.", "annotation_id": "16413094", "url": "https://genius.com/16413094", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "Drop Rolls Royce, that’s a don nigga", "vault_lines": ["Drop Rolls Royce, that's a don nigga"], "meaning": "Could be referring to a Rolls Royce Dawn. A convertible Rolls Royce. Hence the “drop”.", "annotation_id": "16413084", "url": "https://genius.com/16413084", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "We CMG grizzly, we just sold out the forum", "vault_lines": ["We CMG grizzly, we just sold out the forum"], "meaning": "Yo Gotti and his CMG label are originally from Memphis. The Memphis Grizzlies play home games at the FedEx Forum. Here, Yo Gotti is comparing himself and CMG to the Grizzlies because he can sell out the FedEx Forum.", "annotation_id": "14060585", "url": "https://genius.com/14060585", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "This that raw, this that raw, bitch I ball like Chris Paul I switch it to Blake Griffin, they gon’ bang that shit on y’all", "vault_lines": ["This that raw, this that raw, bitch I ball like Chris Paul", "I switch it to Blake Griffin, they gon' bang that shit on y'all"], "meaning": "Chris Paul and Blake Griffin were a superstar duo for the Los Angeles Clippers from 2011 until 2017.\n\nSince Meek balls Chris Paul, who is one of the best players in the NBA, he is saying that he is one of the best rappers in the game.\n\nBlake Griffin is also a top player in the NBA, along with being one of the best dunkers in the league. “they gon' bang that shit on y'all” refers to a powerful dunk on the defense.\n\nSince Blake Griffin and Chris Paul can do an equal amount of damage on the court, Meek is comparing the dynamic duo of Griffin and Paul to himself and his mentor, Rick Ross, who signed Meek to Maybach Music in 2011.", "annotation_id": "13002666", "url": "https://genius.com/13002666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "White come straight from ’cross the border, you can never overcook it", "vault_lines": ["White come straight from 'cross the border, you can never overcook it"], "meaning": "“White” references cocaine and Meek’s letting it be known that this particular cocaine is coming from across the Mexican border. Meek also speaks to its high grade and potency based on being unable to over cook the substance.", "annotation_id": "12408480", "url": "https://genius.com/12408480", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "All about the timing and I’m feeling so correct Got all these diamonds, bitches say I seem possessed", "vault_lines": ["All about the timing and I'm feeling so correct", "Got all these diamonds, bitches say I seem possessed"], "meaning": "The word “possessed” has a double meaning here. On one hand, Ross is saying how females is saying he’s controlled (possessed) by something, in this case, diamonds. But also, Ross is speaking of how he literally possesses a wide number of diamonds, and even labeled himself the “King of Diamonds.”", "annotation_id": "12402576", "url": "https://genius.com/12402576", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "Who you fadin’? Pussy boy, go get a body bag Renzel records with your Tina Turner contracts", "vault_lines": ["Who you fadin'? Pussy boy, go get a body bag", "Renzel records with your Tina Turner contracts"], "meaning": "In this line, Rick Ross is taking an aim at Birdman and his Label.\n\nBirdman said he was pulling up on all the people that were down talking him about his situation with Lil Wayne, but he never did.\n\n\n\nHe also compares Cash Money to Ike and Tina Turner’s violent relationship", "annotation_id": "12376678", "url": "https://genius.com/12376678", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "They gave him life for living life, that boy was sauce", "vault_lines": ["They gave him life for living life, that boy was sauce"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Bobby Shmurda’s song ‘Living Life’ Featuring Ty Real. Although Bobby himself only got 7 years many of his affiliates got over 100 years for their crimes.", "annotation_id": "12373799", "url": "https://genius.com/12373799", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "Link with the connect and we collect them blocks (That white perico)", "vault_lines": ["Link with the connect and we collect them blocks (That white perico)"], "meaning": "“Perico” is a spanish word for bird, and is used as a slang term for uncut cocaine.", "annotation_id": "12372150", "url": "https://genius.com/12372150", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Connect the Dots", "line": "You looked up to Jordan, we looked up to Meech", "vault_lines": ["You looked up to Jordan, we looked up to Meech"], "meaning": "Unlike others who dreamt of having careers in the basktetball, Yo Gotti looked up to Black Mafia Family leader “Big Meech.”\n\nFounded in the 1980s with the his brother Terry Flenory, the BMF organisation had established cocaine distribution throughout the U.S. by the 2000s—and by 2005 the organisation had allegedly made over $270million.", "annotation_id": "12367606", "url": "https://genius.com/12367606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
