{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Got a crib in my closet, hustle every day, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Got a crib in my closet, hustle every day, nigga"], "meaning": "Ross had to grind and hustle everyday to achieve such a big closet which includes over 4000 pairs on sneakers as he claims in this verse.\n\nAlso a reference to the hook of his debut smash hit single “Hustlin'” which featured on his 2006 album Port of Miami.", "annotation_id": "14108239", "url": "https://genius.com/14108239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "You should see me in Lennox, I shop ‘til I drop", "vault_lines": ["You should see me in Lennox, I shop ‘til I drop"], "meaning": "Lennox is a giant shopping mall in Atlanta, which is 2 Chainz hometown.", "annotation_id": "3169242", "url": "https://genius.com/3169242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Raised down the street from a crack house", "vault_lines": ["Raised down the street from a crack house"], "meaning": "Growing up in a very poor environment in Georgia, 2 Chainz' life in the hood has been well documented throughout his songs. If you’re a 2 Chainz fan, you’re probably well aware that he used to cook and sell crack, just to make a living.\n\nI’m all that and then some, my trap house is my income\nAnd it’s booming\n\nThe street 2 Chainz lived on, had it’s very own crack house, meaning the street is a very dangerous one. Just once again showing how dangerous his life was growing up.", "annotation_id": "3167221", "url": "https://genius.com/3167221", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "I’m in Vogue, this winter, the runway, no in store", "vault_lines": ["I’m in Vogue, this winter, the runway, no in store"], "meaning": "Rocky was featured on the cover of Vogue this winter.  The runway is real fashion shit that you won’t find in any store.\n\n\n\nThe line could also be seen as “I’m in vogue; this Wintour,” as a reference to Anna Wintour, who is the editor-in-chief of Vogue.", "annotation_id": "3166183", "url": "https://genius.com/3166183", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Pull her hair weave ’til the track out", "vault_lines": ["Pull her hair weave 'til the track out"], "meaning": "Weaves are held in by a track that’s glued on or woven into the natural hair.  He’s rough enough with this chick that he’s gonna end up pulling her hair till the track comes off.", "annotation_id": "3166170", "url": "https://genius.com/3166170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Fuck it, I said it, I’m winning, downsouth MC Ren", "vault_lines": ["Fuck it, I said it, I'm winning, downsouth MC Ren"], "meaning": "MC Ren is a Compton-rapper and member of the legendary hiphop group N.W.A with the likes of Dr. Dre, Eazy-E, Ice Cube, and DJ Yella.\n2 Chainz is the Atlanta-version of MC Ren.\n\nPreviously he has called him and Kanye West for the new Snoop Dogg & Dr. Dre on “Birthday Song”:\n\nDeuce and Ye\nWe like Snoop and Dre", "annotation_id": "3166157", "url": "https://genius.com/3166157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "A nigga wearing a Versace shirt, man that’s a motherfucking throwback", "vault_lines": ["A nigga wearing a Versace shirt, man that's a motherfucking throwback"], "meaning": "The high fashion brand, Versace, was popularized in hip-hop when Tupac and Biggie started wearing the clothing.\n\n\n\n2 Chainz refers to this as a throwback, he could also possibly be saying this in a negative way, seeing as 2 Chainz doesn’t JUST wear Versace anymore.\n\nTity Boy’s Versace game is hard.", "annotation_id": "3166155", "url": "https://genius.com/3166155", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "If you work with them people, I’m unavailable, nigga You smell like pork in a Mecca, Lord be my protector", "vault_lines": ["If you work with them people, I’m unavailable, nigga", "You smell like pork in a Mecca, Lord be my protector"], "meaning": "“Pork in Mecca” is actually in reference to the holiest city in Islam – Mecca, Saudi Arabia.\n\nEating pork is looked down upon in the Muslim religion, so smelling like pork in Mecca would be borderline sacrilegious. Ross doesn’t fuck with snitches and in this case, he can smell the snitch on the guy, just like a Muslim would be able to smell pork on another’s breathe.", "annotation_id": "3166149", "url": "https://genius.com/3166149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "I got Dolce, I ain’t even worn yet, codeine I ain’t even po’ yet", "vault_lines": ["I got Dolce, I ain't even worn yet, codeine I ain't even po' yet"], "meaning": "He’s got some Dolce & Gabana (which is an expensive clothing line) he has already purchased but hasn’t even used\n\n\n\n& codeine\n\n\n\nthat he hasn’t even poured yet", "annotation_id": "3166127", "url": "https://genius.com/3166127", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Larry Merchant my nigga, I got Holyfield money", "vault_lines": ["Larry Merchant my nigga, I got Holyfield money"], "meaning": "Continuing with the boxing theme, Larry Merchant is a former sportswriter, telecaster for HBO Boxing, and is widely considered to be the greatest television boxing analyst of all time.\n\nIn February 2014, Ross bought former boxer Evander Holyfield’s 109 room mansion for 5.8 million dollars!", "annotation_id": "3166061", "url": "https://genius.com/3166061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Spanish chick in my casa", "vault_lines": ["Got a crib in my closet, Spanish chick in my casa"], "meaning": "“Casa” means “home” in Spanish. Flacko’s banging a hispanic bitch at his house. He also demonstrates his fine knowledge of the Spanish language.", "annotation_id": "3165855", "url": "https://genius.com/3165855", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "If ye ain’t got it then you bragging, that’s automatic I see no need for me to Tweet, these bitches know my status", "vault_lines": ["If ye ain't got it then you bragging, that's automatic", "I see no need for me to Tweet, these bitches know my status"], "meaning": "The people who brag about what they have, often times don’t have as much. Rocky doesn’t need to brag, he’s built up his reputation and everyone already knows what he’s about.\n\n\n\nNotice the wordplay though? On Twitter, to tweet means to make a status for everyone to see.", "annotation_id": "3165750", "url": "https://genius.com/3165750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "I’m the shit, all designer shit, got all kinds of shit Got Prada, Raf from 1999 and shit, bet you won’t find the shit", "vault_lines": ["I'm the shit, all designer shit, got all kinds of shit", "Got Prada, Raf from 1999 and shit, bet you won't find the shit"], "meaning": "Rocky is flexing and claiming he’s got items for Prada’s 1999 line. If you go out looking for it you won’t find it because it’s so rare.", "annotation_id": "3165731", "url": "https://genius.com/3165731", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Second row at the fight, bitch get on my level", "vault_lines": ["Second row at the fight, bitch get on my level"], "meaning": "Ross and 2 Chainz both escorted boxer Floyd Mayweather to his big fight against Marcos Maidana on May 3rd, 2014.\n\n\n\nThis fight was huge, and anyone who attended is most likely a big deal. Which explains why Rozay was there.", "annotation_id": "3165547", "url": "https://genius.com/3165547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crib in My Closet", "line": "Tryna make a yellow ho tap out", "vault_lines": ["Tryna make a yellow ho tap out"], "meaning": "A “yellow ho” refers to either an Asian, or a light skin black woman. Chainz is feeling him some Asian action tonight.\n\n\n\nTapping out refers to a wrestling match, where the loosing wrestler taps out:\n\n\n\nIn other words Tity Boi is about to fuck his Asian girl real hard!\n\nACCEPTED SUGGESTION:\nReferring to the previous line about the game, Chainz might be alluding to the The Simpsons: Tapped Out game, with Simpsons obviously yellow.", "annotation_id": "3165497", "url": "https://genius.com/3165497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
