{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Love at large", "vault_lines": ["You know, love at large"], "meaning": "The lyric “love at large” most commonly refers to love that is free, unrestrained, and unconfined by typical societal rules, boundaries, or monogamous expectations. It can describe a general, overarching feeling of love for humanity (often called universal love) or the philosophy of ethical non-monogamy.", "annotation_id": "40250060", "url": "https://genius.com/40250060", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "I’m holding you closest, that’s ’til the day I rest", "vault_lines": ["I'm holding you closest, that's 'til the day I rest"], "meaning": "This lyric expresses a deep, unwavering commitment to cherish and hold someone close for a lifetime.", "annotation_id": "40250044", "url": "https://genius.com/40250044", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Her words be so potent, scribbled ’em on my chest", "vault_lines": ["Her words be so potent, scribbled 'em on my chest"], "meaning": "This lyric is a poetic or metaphorical expression of deep emotional impact. It means the speaker is so profoundly moved, influenced, or struck by someone’s words he writes- or tattoos them onto their chest—the area closest to the heart—to keep them forever close and visible to themselves.", "annotation_id": "40250023", "url": "https://genius.com/40250023", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "It feels like we floating when we really having sex", "vault_lines": ["It feels like we floating when we really having sex"], "meaning": "When people describe feeling like they are “floating” during sex, it usually refers to a state of deep physical and emotional disconnection from reality, often driven by intense intimacy, pleasure, or the physiological effects of arousal.", "annotation_id": "40250018", "url": "https://genius.com/40250018", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "An angel in the flesh", "vault_lines": ["Criminal thoughts (Boss), an angel in the flesh"], "meaning": "The phrase “an angel in the flesh” is a poetic, metaphorical expression used to describe a living human who displays extraordinary kindness, purity, or unselfishness. Bringing heavenly qualities to earthly life.", "annotation_id": "40250014", "url": "https://genius.com/40250014", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Taking you to places selfies get taken the least", "vault_lines": ["Taking you to places selfies get taken the least"], "meaning": "The phrase “places selfies get taken the least” refers to secluded, remote, or highly restricted locations where photography is either physically impossible, discouraged, or forbidden. These destinations usually demand extreme effort, specialized skills, or security clearance to reach.", "annotation_id": "40250005", "url": "https://genius.com/40250005", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Every day she had to find a way to find a way", "vault_lines": ["Every day she had to find a way to find a way"], "meaning": "This lyric means she was forced to constantly innovate, problem-solve, or push through obstacles simply to figure out how to accomplish a task or survive a difficult situation.", "annotation_id": "40249960", "url": "https://genius.com/40249960", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "He did her like a dirty rug", "vault_lines": ["Stepping on her, said he did her like a dirty rug"], "meaning": "The phrase means someone treated another person with extreme disrespect, ruthlessly taking advantage of them or casting them aside without a second thought. It equates the person to a throwaway object—something you wipe your feet on, abuse, or easily discard when it gets dirty.", "annotation_id": "40249957", "url": "https://genius.com/40249957", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "It’s so good it feels criminal", "vault_lines": ["Oh, it's so good it feels criminal"], "meaning": "The phrase “it’s so good it feels criminal” is a hyperbolic expression used to describe something so incredibly delightful, satisfying, or beautiful that it seems like it should be illegal or morally wrong. It highlights a sense of extreme indulgence, pleasure, or guilt-inducing appeal.", "annotation_id": "40249955", "url": "https://genius.com/40249955", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "I know it’s dicey", "vault_lines": ["I know it's dicey"], "meaning": "The adjective dicey means slightly dangerous, unpredictable, or uncertain. It is an informal term used to describe situations where the outcome is unclear, risky, or potentially troublesome.", "annotation_id": "40249946", "url": "https://genius.com/40249946", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "I’m close ties that you shouldn’t cut loose", "vault_lines": ["I'm close ties that you shouldn't cut loose"], "meaning": "The phrase “close ties that you shouldn’t cut loose” refers to valuable personal, professional, or familial relationships you should maintain. It means you have strong, meaningful bonds with people that provide support or opportunity, and severing those connections would be a mistake.", "annotation_id": "40249939", "url": "https://genius.com/40249939", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Volatile", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Volatile generally means something that is likely to change suddenly, unexpectedly, or uncontrollably. Depending on the context, it refers to a rapidly shifting situation, an unpredictable emotional state, a fast-fluctuating market, or a substance that evaporates easily.", "annotation_id": "40249932", "url": "https://genius.com/40249932", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Vigilante", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A vigilante is a person who takes the law into their own hands. They act as self-appointed enforcers to prevent crime or punish suspected criminals without possessing official legal authority, often because they feel official law enforcement is failing or inadequate.", "annotation_id": "40249931", "url": "https://genius.com/40249931", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Got a mind full of TNT", "vault_lines": ["Got a mind full of TNT"], "meaning": "Having a “mind full of TNT” means your brain is filled with explosive, volatile, or chaotic thoughts.", "annotation_id": "40249930", "url": "https://genius.com/40249930", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "5150 and lawless hearts", "vault_lines": ["5150 and lawless hearts"], "meaning": "5150, also known as the involuntary psychiatric hold, is a California law enforcement term for a mentally disturbed person (a reference to Section 5150 of the California Welfare and Institutions Code).\n\nThe Cali police use it as code for a “crazy”, someone who is a danger to themselves.\n\nTo continue the criminal/danger metaphors, Miguel is saying that he is so insane that he is a danger to everyone around him, including himself.", "annotation_id": "13467455", "url": "https://genius.com/13467455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "I need a lunatic just like me", "vault_lines": ["I need a lunatic just like me"], "meaning": "Miguel says he is a Lunatic (a mentally ill person) and he need a another lunatic just like him. It’s like finding a friend, some one to relate to, the whole nine yards.\n\nHe is saying that he is a psycho and finding some like that is really hard because those people like to hide away from the general public for obvious reason’s.", "annotation_id": "13248038", "url": "https://genius.com/13248038", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Just plead the fifth if you’re ever questioned, girl", "vault_lines": ["Just plead the fifth if you're ever questioned, girl"], "meaning": "Miguel wants someone who is ever interrogated about their love, criminal activities to stay quiet.\n\nPleading the fifth will also protect an individual from self-incrimination. By not answering, Miguel wants to protect her from anything he might have done in the past.\n\nIt is also a metaphor for not answering questions from the tabloids, paparazzi, and media about their relationship.", "annotation_id": "13237785", "url": "https://genius.com/13237785", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Pain is heaven, call it 9/11", "vault_lines": ["Pain is heaven, call it 9/11"], "meaning": "On September 11, 2001,  four airplanes were hijacked by Al-Qaeda, two of which crashed into the two world trade center buildings killing nearly 3,000 people in total.\n\nConversely, Heaven is considered a place of religious cosmology and never ending peace and paradise.\n\nMiguel is paradoxical enough to compare the two to exhibit the criminal side of his thoughts. Although most people would consider this line ludicrous, Miguel embraces it.", "annotation_id": "13189964", "url": "https://genius.com/13189964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "I pick and choose like Duck Duck Goose", "vault_lines": ["I pick and choose like Duck Duck Goose"], "meaning": "Duck Duck Goose is a childhood game in which all players sit in a circle while the ‘picker’ taps each player’s head until one is chosen with the exclamation of “goose!\"–he or she must chase the picker to avoid becoming the next picker.\n\n\n\nMiguel sings as though he is ‘picker’ when selecting women to say that he is choosy.", "annotation_id": "13189815", "url": "https://genius.com/13189815", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "I got a mind like Columbine, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I got a mind like Columbine, yeah"], "meaning": "The Columbine Massacre happened in 1999. During the tragic event, 12 students and 1 teacher lost their lives when Dylan Klebold and Eric Harris decided to shoot up Columbine High School.\n\nMiguel feels that he is becoming dangerously unhinged in this song, and references many tragic events throughout this song to put his plight into perspective.", "annotation_id": "13167440", "url": "https://genius.com/13167440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "5150 and lawless hearts", "vault_lines": ["5150 and lawless hearts"], "meaning": "5150, also known as the involuntary psychiatric hold,  is a California law enforcement term for a mentally disturbed person (a reference to Section 5150 of the California Welfare and Institutions Code).\n\nThe Cali police use it as code for a “crazy”, someone who is a danger to themselves.\n\nTo continue the criminal/danger metaphors, Miguel is saying that he is so insane that he is a danger to everyone around him, including himself.", "annotation_id": "13165793", "url": "https://genius.com/13165793", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Kaepernick of my city, lil homie, take a knee", "vault_lines": ["Kaepernick of my city, lil homie, take a knee"], "meaning": "Colin Kaepernick was the San Francisco 49ers quarterback who sparked a movement in the NFL when he started sitting and then later taking a knee against racial injustice during the National Anthem in the 2016 season. While Kaepernick has been blackballed from the league for the 2017 season because of his action, many current players have continued the protest he started to the dismay of President Donald Trump. For his influence, GQ magazine named Kaepernick as their 2017 Citizen of the Year.\n\n\n\nRoss feels that he is the leader of the movement to further Miami’s position in the rap game and that his position gives him influence on the residents to follow his lead.", "annotation_id": "13160884", "url": "https://genius.com/13160884", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Criminal", "line": "Feeling played, underpaid, like she was Satchel Paige", "vault_lines": ["Feeling played, underpaid, like she was Satchel Paige"], "meaning": "Leroy “Satchel” Paige was a pitcher in the Negro League before playing with Major League Baseball’s Cleveland Indians as a 42-year-old rookie in 1948. Many have declared Satchel Paige as the greatest pitcher of all time but due to the segregated era in which he played, he was grossly underpaid for his worth—a feeling the girl Rozay is talking about can understand.", "annotation_id": "13160872", "url": "https://genius.com/13160872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
