{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Took my Rolex and gave me an ankle monitor", "vault_lines": ["Took my Rolex and gave me an ankle monitor"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to an event that took place in 2015 that got Rick Ross in trouble with the law.\n\nIn August of 2015 Ross got into an argument with his groundskeeper about guests he’d invited over the night before. The argument took a violent turn and Ross is said to have dragged the man inside his mansion where he locked him in a spare bedroom and assaulted him causing severe injury to both the ground keeper’s neck and jaw.\n\nRoss had to pay 2 Million in bail and was given an ankle monitor to wear while on bail. After his trial Ross accepted a deal to erase his conviction that gave him 60 months of probation in addition to having to pay $10,000 in fines.", "annotation_id": "12908790", "url": "https://genius.com/12908790", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "I gave so much, I got nothing to lose in these streets", "vault_lines": ["I gave so much, I got nothing to lose in these streets"], "meaning": "In 2010, Rick Ross decided to host a blood drive to help Haiti after their horrifying earthquake.\n\nAlso, in 2012, Rozay donated Reeboks & iPads to Miami Carol City Senior High school, the high school he graduated from.\n\nAlso on “Live Fast Die Young” from his 2010 album Teflon Don; Ross said this\n\n Look at Haiti, children dyin' round the clock, nigga\nI sent a hundred grand, but that’s a decent watch, nigga", "annotation_id": "8627170", "url": "https://genius.com/8627170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "[Produced by Jahlil Beats & Antman Wonder]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "As stated in the song’s credits, Kahlil’s production of “Crocodile Python” samples Antman Wonder’s instrumental track “Sleeping Giant” from his 2015 album Memories of the Fewture:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=czIOAKo2EJA&spfreload=10", "annotation_id": "8357674", "url": "https://genius.com/8357674", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Renounced my citizenship and move to Singapore Couple tax breaks, all accounts offshore", "vault_lines": ["Renounced my citizenship and move to Singapore", "Couple tax breaks, all accounts offshore"], "meaning": "This refers to Eduardo Saverin, one of the co-founders of Facebook, who renounced his U.S. citizenship and moved to Singapore to save an estimated $700 million capital gains tax.", "annotation_id": "8347953", "url": "https://genius.com/8347953", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "They want to own every thing I own They sends drones to survey my home Zeus and Zion to protect my wealth Bloody Glock 40 to protect myself", "vault_lines": ["They want to own every thing I own", "They sends drones to survey my home", "Zeus and Zion to protect my wealth", "Bloody Glock 40 to protect myself"], "meaning": "Ross got “some enemies, got a lot of enemieswho wanna drain him of his energy” so he does what he can and that’s protect himself while looking fly. He also carries something to return fire with when they come shooting.", "annotation_id": "8347834", "url": "https://genius.com/8347834", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Beat twenty cases like John Gotti", "vault_lines": ["Beat twenty cases like John Gotti"], "meaning": "Rick Ross, an avid fan of the Teflon Don’s work even named his 2010 album, Teflon Don.\n\nHere he once again shows his love for the deceased Gambino Family mob boss to say he has beat many cases (20 to be exact), just like the mob boss beat his cases with documented underhand means.", "annotation_id": "8347753", "url": "https://genius.com/8347753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Skip your name, now they want to know your tax bracket Tell ’em that you with me and the pussy’s automatic", "vault_lines": ["Skip your name, now they want to know your tax bracket", "Tell 'em that you with me and the pussy's automatic"], "meaning": "With a rich man around, people always briefly ask a little about the man’s name but want to know much about his money. Something Ross is saying he has faced.\n\nRoss here is much more like the Vincent Chase of his team. He attracts all the ladies to him to a point he even has the ability to attract more for his hommies. This means more girls in the bedroom.\n\nBAWSE!", "annotation_id": "8347697", "url": "https://genius.com/8347697", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Have your ass in a church before I end the verse", "vault_lines": ["Have your ass in a church before I end the verse"], "meaning": "Ross has spoken before of dealing with beefs in a less amicable manner. This is just but an echo on where you will be and best believe you won’t be singing hymns too.", "annotation_id": "8347575", "url": "https://genius.com/8347575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Jahlil Beats, holla at me!", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "One of the most identifiable ad-libs in the rap game this era from the Roc Nation in-house producer.", "annotation_id": "8347562", "url": "https://genius.com/8347562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Fayette county prosecutor want to take a nigga house", "vault_lines": ["Fayette county prosecutor want to take a nigga house"], "meaning": "In June of 2015 Ross was arrested in his home for aggravated assault, aggravated battery, and kidnapping. The charges stemmed from an incident in which Ross and his bodyguard allegedly pisol-whipped Ross’s groundskeeper and questioned him at gunpoint while not allowing him to leave the residence.\n\nRoss was originally denied bail. When he went back to court, his lawyer was able to convince the judge to grant him a $2 million bail.\n\nRoss paid the $2 million bail with $500,000 bond, $500,000 cash and $1 million equity from his Fayetteville, Georgia home. Additionally, Ross promised to hand over his entire estate if he violated the conditions of his bail by intimidating the witness or obstructing justice. This is specifically what the line is referencing.\n\nThis is an image of Rick Ross’s estate in Fayetteville, Georgia worth roughly $5 million. The property originally belonged to Evander Holyfield. It is the largest single-family home in the entire state of Georgia.", "annotation_id": "8333002", "url": "https://genius.com/8333002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Family asked me, am I in Illuminati?", "vault_lines": ["Family asked me, am I in Illuminati?"], "meaning": "Ross, and many other rappers, have been accused of being in the notorious government run group the ‘illuminati’\n\nBecause of Ross' sudden flux of wealth his family don’t believe you can make all that money singing, he must be a part of something higher", "annotation_id": "8311559", "url": "https://genius.com/8311559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Damn, why they want to stick me for my paper? They want the deeds to my fruit of labor Every time I turn around Lawsuits put a lean on a king crown", "vault_lines": ["Damn, why they want to stick me for my paper?", "They want the deeds to my fruit of labor", "Every time I turn around", "Lawsuits put a lean on a king crown"], "meaning": "Rick Ross borrows this question from the edited version of Biggie Smalls' classic 1994 song “Warning.” While B.I.G. was apprehensive of burglars raiding his home, Rozay is wary of a legal shakedown.\n\n“Lean on a king crown” could be a reference to Barron Claiborne’s iconic photo of Biggie wearing a crown cocked to the side.", "annotation_id": "8282589", "url": "https://genius.com/8282589", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "My son’s mother don’t know when or where to start All the years that I known her, trick never had a job Unemployed, that’ll get a bitch depressed But unlike them other boys, she watched me kill ’em with finesse", "vault_lines": ["But unlike them other boys, she watched me kill 'em with finesse"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has had a couple of twists and turns with his baby mama, Tia Kemp, which have gone from this, which happened at the height of his 50 Cent beef to this, which happened after the sex tape. Apparently she still seeks child support which Ross doesn’t pay from this info here not to mention this, which happened much much later.\n\nAll this happening there is something Rick Ross hints to us, she has no job, thus she’s easily allured by the money.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_rBxSF7y5Bk\n\nRoss however returns the spotlight to him by speaking of his flair and his ability to have her hooked to him up to date.", "annotation_id": "8281982", "url": "https://genius.com/8281982", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "And ain’t nobody fucking with me while the mics on", "vault_lines": ["And ain't nobody fucking with me while the mics on"], "meaning": "Rick Ross could be meaning two things here.\nOne:\nNobody can outmatch his rapping skills.\n\nTwo:\nHe is a drug boss of course so you can assume nobody will want to snitch on him using a wire which comes with a microphone strapped to the skin too otherwise this will happen.", "annotation_id": "8271774", "url": "https://genius.com/8271774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Crocodile Python", "line": "Cubans on my neck, looking like a python", "vault_lines": ["Cubans on my neck, looking like a python"], "meaning": "The Cuban links are known to be pretty heavy when they are many, something Plies can testify to. Pythons have the ability to weigh heavily on it’s prey with 350 pounds being its weight\n\nThis could also be a reference to how many Cuban links look like when they are together which looks like a thick snake not just in colour (gold) but thickness. The thickest snake in the planet is a python.", "annotation_id": "8271463", "url": "https://genius.com/8271463", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
