{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cross That Line", "line": "See the voodoo priest, then the coke gon’ come", "vault_lines": ["See the voodoo priest, then the coke gon' come"], "meaning": "Ross alludes to the movie “City of God”, where a scene takes place in which eventual main character Lil Zeke, visits a vodou priest and shortly after becomes the head nigga in charge.\n\n\n\nSimilar to a Rain Dance in Native American culture, Ross asks the spirits for assistance in lifting the dry spell. Let the coke wave fall.", "annotation_id": "2857209", "url": "https://genius.com/2857209", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cross That Line", "line": "No mask on", "vault_lines": ["I gets my mash on (Ross) no mask on"], "meaning": "Ross doesn’t use a ski mask (or any type of mask for that matter) when robbing people, he shows his face. Usually, if a robber lets you see his face, he’s probably not planning on letting you live to testify against him.", "annotation_id": "1425517", "url": "https://genius.com/1425517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cross That Line", "line": "Walk in the 40-40, I’ma score, bet it", "vault_lines": ["Walk in the 40-40, I'ma score, bet it"], "meaning": "The 40-40 Club is a chain of sports bars and lounges owned by hip hop mogul Jay-Z and partners Desiree Gonzalez and Juan Pérez.\n\nWhen Ross goes, he will leave the club with a beatiful female, you can bet your money on that.", "annotation_id": "717968", "url": "https://genius.com/717968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cross That Line", "line": "I’m glorifyin’ knights and regals", "vault_lines": ["I'm glorifyin' knights and regals"], "meaning": "Knights are royal soldiers, and the word regal refers to things belonging to a higher class, such as royalty.\n\nHence, Ross knew as child despite growing up in povery: “I’m gonna make it!”", "annotation_id": "717952", "url": "https://genius.com/717952", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Cross That Line", "line": "But what made it worse every first is a packed house", "vault_lines": ["But what made it worse every first is a packed house"], "meaning": "On the first of the month, people receive welfare checks. With that welfare money, many drug addicts choose to go to the crack house and buy drugs. Ergo, a packed house.", "annotation_id": "717948", "url": "https://genius.com/717948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
