{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Presidents", "line": "Fully loaded .60s smokin’ on a seven (All ready)", "vault_lines": ["Fully loaded .60s smokin' on a seven (All ready)"], "meaning": "Fully loaded sixes [6-series BMW (SUV)], smoking on a seven [gram blunt].", "annotation_id": "20882891", "url": "https://genius.com/20882891", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Presidents", "line": "Poor attitude and got rich nigga calisthenics (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Poor attitude and got rich nigga calisthenics (Woah)"], "meaning": "Calisthenics: gymnastic exercises to achieve bodily fitness and grace of movement.\n\nSuggesting a poor attitude develops an elegant ‘rich’ composure.", "annotation_id": "20882875", "url": "https://genius.com/20882875", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Presidents", "line": "Keep the blocks over there, we call it Legoland", "vault_lines": ["Keep the blocks over there, we call it Legoland"], "meaning": "A ‘block’ is slang for a brick of cocaine. Lego is a building toy that has elements that resemble blocks. So when Jeezy says ‘Legoland’ he is alluding to the ‘block’ imagery and also the amusement park based on the popular toy. Amusement parks are large venues, so the image of ‘Legoland’ suggests that Jeezy has a large drug hoard; He has stacks of ‘blocks’ akin to the way Lego bricks stack.", "annotation_id": "11517063", "url": "https://genius.com/11517063", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Presidents", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-dead-presidents-lyrics", "genius_title": "Dead Presidents", "genius_id": 3019833, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Slim Dunkin", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Slim Dunkin was a rapper signed to Waka Flocka’s label Brick Squad Monopoly who was murdered in 2011. Ross was featured on the remix of Waka’s hit single O Lets Do It in 2010 and most likely knew Slim through him.\n\nMany other rappers have shown respect to Slim Dunkin in their lyrics, including Waka, Kodak Black, and a full song dedicated to his memory by Gucci Mane, who owns Brick Squad Monopoly.\n\nRIP DUNK", "annotation_id": "20424745", "url": "https://genius.com/20424745", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Lost Boyz, Freaky Tah, we were four deep", "vault_lines": ["Lost Boyz, Freaky Tah, we were four deep"], "meaning": "Freaky Tah was 1 of 4 members of the rap group Lost Boyz who was murdered in 1999. Here Ross is relating to the Lost Boyz struggle of losing one of their close friends, and going from a crew of 4 to 3.\n\nRIP Tah", "annotation_id": "20424707", "url": "https://genius.com/20424707", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Jam Master Jay one day I’m gon’ meet", "vault_lines": ["Jam Master Jay one day I'm gon' meet"], "meaning": "Jam Master Jay (Real name Jason Mizell)  was the DJ of the popular rap group Run-D.M.C.\n\nOn October 30, 2002, at 7:30 pm, an unknown assailant shot Master Jay in a Merrick Boulevard recording studio in Jamaica, Queens. Sadly he did not survive being shot.\n\nThough the theme of the song is to pay tribute to dead rappers, Ross is paying tribute to a non rapper who had helped the culture so much.\n\nBeing a christian man Ross is going to meet Jay when he goes to heaven.", "annotation_id": "13277453", "url": "https://genius.com/13277453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Bandanas and rags, wave them for Soulja Slim", "vault_lines": ["Bandanas and rags, wave them for Soulja Slim"], "meaning": "Soulja Slim was an American rapper known for his appearance on the  hit song “Slow Motion” by rapper Juvenile.\n\nHe is one of the many deceased rappers Ross pays tribute to in this song.\n\nSadly he was killed on November 26, 2003, after an assailant shot him four times, three in the chest and once in the face, on the front lawn of the home of his mother and stepfather.\n\nWaving a bandanna is a way of paying tribute to a dead person.", "annotation_id": "13271658", "url": "https://genius.com/13271658", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "They say I’m a scholar, but I want a key", "vault_lines": ["They say I'm a scholar, but I want a key"], "meaning": "This could mean one of two things;\n\n1.) He got the aforementioned degrees he wanted from school and now people are calling him a scholar. But this wasn’t his plan, he went to go study because he wanted to run his city/wherever (with a key to the city, or in other words become the smartest most powerful man around).\n\n2.) Throughout his life people have told him that he’s great at researching and/or finding things out. But he foresaw himself already knowing everything he would ever need to know (touching on the idea of having the “key to life”).", "annotation_id": "8722766", "url": "https://genius.com/8722766", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Here’s a toast to the dead rappers", "vault_lines": ["Here's a toast to the dead rappers"], "meaning": "This song is his homage to the late-greats, all the way to those who’ve passed away recently (Tupac to Lil Snupe). Also the entire song is kind of a testament to the trials of becoming a big name rapper, as well as to the dangers and responsibilities that come with making it.", "annotation_id": "8722740", "url": "https://genius.com/8722740", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Yes, I’m flawed, these walls will leave you traumatized", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I'm flawed, these walls will leave you traumatized"], "meaning": "Here Rick Ross elaborates on his previous line and confirms that within the relationship he is the root cause of the issues that plague their bond. Unfortunately in return for bringing numerous problems, with the sheltered heart he holds, into the relationship he consequently ruins the girls mindset leaving her with numerous doubts and insecurities when it ends.\n\n\n\nThis could also be a nod to his mental well being from the “killers” constantly after him.", "annotation_id": "8043743", "url": "https://genius.com/8043743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "I apologize to these women, I keep on telling lies", "vault_lines": ["I apologize to these women, I keep on telling lies"], "meaning": "As a man of success Ross meets plenty of women, the phrase “running through these hoes” comes into play here.\n\nRoss is displaying remorse for the females who may have believed what they had was special, but in the end their relationship may not have worked out even if he told them it would.", "annotation_id": "8043638", "url": "https://genius.com/8043638", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Doe B", "vault_lines": [", and peace to Doe B"], "meaning": "Doe B, also known as Glenn Thomas was a rapper who passed away in 2013.\n\nStarlito and Don Trip also paid homage to the legend on the track G.Thomas", "annotation_id": "8017991", "url": "https://genius.com/8017991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Mac Dre", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j8Szl_JyCUQ\nBay Area Legend died at age 34 he was shoot in a van after his show in Kansas in Missouri.\nFat Tone who was suspected of killing him, was later killed by Mac Minister a friend of Mac Dre.", "annotation_id": "7924248", "url": "https://genius.com/7924248", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dead Rappers", "line": "Lil Snupe’s in my prayers, I still can hear him laughing", "vault_lines": ["Lil Snupe's in my prayers, I still can hear him laughing"], "meaning": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bJZYdWIlHJI\n\nHe was killed one week after his 18th Birthday tragic R.I.P he was the little homie of Meek Mill something like a Birdman Lil Wayne relationship without the kissing.", "annotation_id": "7924241", "url": "https://genius.com/7924241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
