{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Deeper Than Rap (Lost Intro)", "line": "I always had a plan to let your grand wizard", "vault_lines": ["I always had a plan to let your grand wizard"], "meaning": "I always had a plan to “lynch” a grand wizard. With the millions of power accessible to the boss, he all but incriminates himself by stating he is willing to turn a klan leader into strange fruit.", "annotation_id": "32187457", "url": "https://genius.com/32187457", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Deeper Than Rap (Lost Intro)", "line": "Pretty cars, I slept with pistols all under the pillow Shotty all in the kitchen, heard over a bowl of cereal", "vault_lines": ["Pretty cars, I slept with pistols all under the pillow", "Shotty all in the kitchen, heard over a bowl of cereal"], "meaning": "What’s beef?\n\nBeef is when you need two gats to go to sleep!\n\n\n\nHe keeps the shotguns (shotties) on deck. His kitchen must be loud.", "annotation_id": "678611", "url": "https://genius.com/678611", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Deeper Than Rap (Lost Intro)", "line": "Let me tell you about the last beef Ak-47 seven times seven feet Gave that bitch a bloodbath", "vault_lines": ["Let me tell you about the last beef", "Ak-47 seven times seven feet", "Gave that bitch a bloodbath"], "meaning": "The last person to get on Ross’s bad side got shot and might’ve been buried 49 (7 x 7) feet in the ground.\n\nThis person was literally bathing in their own blood. He should’ve stayed dirty…", "annotation_id": "678601", "url": "https://genius.com/678601", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Deeper Than Rap (Lost Intro)", "line": "Momma go to church and shit’s so far from heavenly (Lord!)", "vault_lines": ["Momma go to church and shit's so far from heavenly (Lord!)"], "meaning": "Ms. Rozay is an avid churchgoer (she probably contributes to the collection plate, as well), but her life isn’t getting any better.\n\nNotice the wordplay between “church” and “heavenly.” Ross’s word choice there is no accident.", "annotation_id": "678599", "url": "https://genius.com/678599", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Deeper Than Rap (Lost Intro)", "line": "Lord forgive me for my sin but I have to serve (Lord!) Starin’ out of a Benz is what I deserve", "vault_lines": ["Lord forgive me for my sin but I have to serve (Lord!)", "Starin' out of a Benz is what I deserve"], "meaning": "Ross puns on “serve.” He both served his time in jail and served crack rocks to fiends.\n\nRoss understands that drug pushing isn’t exactly a holy thing to do, but the Mercedes-Benz is calling his name.", "annotation_id": "678578", "url": "https://genius.com/678578", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Deeper Than Rap (Lost Intro)", "line": "Took me to Dade County for a short stay It was somethin’ small, but chickens was my forte", "vault_lines": ["Took me to Dade County for a short stay", "It was somethin' small, but chickens was my forte"], "meaning": "After the police raided his parents' home, they arrested Ross and took him to Miami-Dade County Jail. It was for a relatively minor offense.\n\nRoss was born to move chickens (cocaine rocks). Someone’s “forte” is a thing that they’re exceptionally good at.", "annotation_id": "678570", "url": "https://genius.com/678570", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
