{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diamonds", "line": "Duckin’ the devil, you could say I live my life in limbo", "vault_lines": ["Duckin' the devil, you could say I live my life in limbo"], "meaning": "Limbo has 2 meainings here:\n\n\nThe game where you duck under a pole.\nThe place people supposedly go before hell.\n\n\n\nBy duckin the devil, you could see how Cole would be stuck in limbo, but at the same time he’s duckin as if he’s playin the game of limbo. Pretty clever.\n\nOne of Cole’s idols, Kanye West, uses a different “limbo” pun in his song The Glory.", "annotation_id": "1236580", "url": "https://genius.com/1236580", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diamonds", "line": "Her pops is into the opera Well, look here, my dear, I’m the Pavarotti of rhymers", "vault_lines": [", her pops is into the opera", "Well, look here, my dear, I'm the Pavarotti of rhymers"], "meaning": "Luciano Pavarotti was known as one of the best opera singers. Cole draws a parallel between him and Pavarotti, stating they are both the best at their respective genres.", "annotation_id": "1236127", "url": "https://genius.com/1236127", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diamonds", "line": "She a bougie chick, seen every flick at the Oscars", "vault_lines": ["She a bougie chick, seen every flick at the Oscars"], "meaning": "Bougie, short for “bourgeois” is French in origin and originally referred to the middle class. These days however, it’s more commonly used to denote a female in a high social class, an applicant for said position, or a very good poser who knows they may never quite reach those social heights. She’s high class because she has seen many of the obscure and tasteful films that the Oscar ceremonies often feature.\n\nAlso lines up with the previous line, in that the movie The Hurt Locker won the Best Film Oscar in 2009.", "annotation_id": "1234499", "url": "https://genius.com/1234499", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
