{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "She never wrote a song, but I know that she’s a star", "vault_lines": ["She never wrote a song, but I know that she's a star"], "meaning": "Alluding to people with fame in a different area i.e. sex workers.\n\nThe woman he’s talking is a pornstar, hence “she’s a star\"", "annotation_id": "23894480", "url": "https://genius.com/23894480", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Her uniform Isabel Marant, when you on the team", "vault_lines": ["Her uniform Isabel Marant, when you on the team"], "meaning": "Isabel Marant is a women’s designer brand made by French designer, Isabel Marant. Ross alludes to the fact that whoever is with him, will dress in the best clothes that money can buy, as a uniform is an outfit someone is obliged to wear when they are part of a group.\n\n\n\nPictured: Isabel Marant", "annotation_id": "22366294", "url": "https://genius.com/22366294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Double MG", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group, or its initials MMG (Double M G), is the music label Rick Ross founded.", "annotation_id": "19774835", "url": "https://genius.com/19774835", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Pop bottles, make love, Thug Passion", "vault_lines": ["Pop bottles, make love, Thug Passion"], "meaning": "Thug Passion is a mixture of Alize and Cristal. The drink was popularized by the 1996 song “Thug Passion” by West Coast legend 2Pac.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mcjL8w7p1Xc", "annotation_id": "1703562", "url": "https://genius.com/1703562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Hate when they be too anxious though, hate when they be too dull", "vault_lines": ["Hate when they be too anxious though, hate when they be too dull"], "meaning": "Wale wants a balanced passionate lover—not one that is too dull & lazy, but not a sex crazy slut either.\n\nAlso, note the brilliant use of wordplay: Wale was continuing with the pineapple references by [possibly] saying “hate when they be too Dole” which sounds like dull.\n\nDole Food Company Inc is an American-based agricultural multinational corporation headquartered in Westlake Village, California. Dole markets such food items as bananas, pineapples (what they are perhaps most famous for), grapes, strawberries, salads, and other fresh and frozen fruits and juices.\n\nThis interpretation would make sense because there is indeed better diced pineapples out there then those from Dole.", "annotation_id": "1120353", "url": "https://genius.com/1120353", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "When I peek into your nature And I promise you, my goals will exceed any physical pleasure", "vault_lines": ["When I peek into your nature", "And I promise you, my goals will exceed any physical pleasure"], "meaning": "“Peek” is a double entendre as its playing off the previous line “I can make you reach things unobtainable.” Wale is saying he can elevate her to the peak of her nature (i.e highest point her life) thus allowing to attain certain things she once deemed unreachable.\n\nFurthermore peek is also referring to sex—“peek into her nature.”  Wale is saying that when he gets inside her he is going to make her feel an emotional or spiritual connection.", "annotation_id": "1042193", "url": "https://genius.com/1042193", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Diced pineapples, talking diamonds by the jar", "vault_lines": ["Diced pineapples, talking diamonds by the jar"], "meaning": "JAR is a very high-end French jeweler.\n\nAlso could be Ross calling his yellow diamonds, diced pineapples.", "annotation_id": "1042145", "url": "https://genius.com/1042145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Diced pineapple", "vault_lines": ["Shorty get it together, hah, diced pineapple"], "meaning": "When I got out of the hospital — you know, I had a seizure last year — when I was leaving, the doctor told me, ‘You gotta eat some more fruit, drink you some water, eat fruit and just relax for a little while.’ My fruit of choice was pineapples.\n\nFor the next three weeks, I woke up every morning and ate diced pineapples, and I put the concept together,“ he continued. \"Drizzy came in, as well as Wale, and it’s kinda like, ‘She could be my diced pineapple. This special lady, she could be what I wake up to every morning and help me get by every day.\n\n\n-Rick Ross", "annotation_id": "1004944", "url": "https://genius.com/1004944", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Hol’ up, showing off some Agent Provocateur", "vault_lines": ["Hol' up, showing off some Agent Provocateur"], "meaning": "Agent provocateur could either refer to a:\n\n\nBritish lingerie retailer, or;\nSpecial kind of agent that is an agent employed by the police or other entity to act undercover to entice or provoke another person to commit an illegal act.", "annotation_id": "940505", "url": "https://genius.com/940505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Let me redefine foreplay ’til you need five and", "vault_lines": ["Let me redefine foreplay 'til you need five and"], "meaning": "Wale’s so good at foreplay (“four”-play), she’s gonna need a five minute break because she can’t handle his sex game. .\n\nYou can also take it as “five” meaning, one more level higher than four (“four”-play). He is gonna make foreplay so good that she is going to want “fiveplay.” .", "annotation_id": "935217", "url": "https://genius.com/935217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "I ain’t no connoisseur but I’m, kinda sure you will admire my taste", "vault_lines": ["I ain't no connoisseur but I'm, kinda sure you will admire my taste"], "meaning": "Connoisseurs are, so to speak, professional tasters. Wale may not be a professional taster but he is sure that she will like his taste in cars, clothes, jewelry, fine dining, etc. Could also refer to the fact she would love it when Wale eats her.\n\nThe sexual pun here is pretty obvious—Wale’s “taste”, i.e. the taste of his semen.", "annotation_id": "934735", "url": "https://genius.com/934735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "And I won’t ever rest, we meet at the peak of your mountain", "vault_lines": ["And I won't ever rest, we meet at the peak of your mountain"], "meaning": "Wale puns here on the name of perhaps the world’s most famous mountain, Mount Everest.\n\nWale is talking about him embarking tirelessly on the task of ensuring that they both reach their climax together.", "annotation_id": "933933", "url": "https://genius.com/933933", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "Crib on the water, got LeBron up the block", "vault_lines": ["Crib on the water, got LeBron up the block"], "meaning": "This line shows how wealthy Rick Ross is, as he lived near LeBron since they both lived in Miami. It continues the basketball metaphor with “shots” from the previous line, because block could also be referring to the basketball statistic:\n\n\n\nLeBron & Ross are friends.", "annotation_id": "931573", "url": "https://genius.com/931573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Diced Pineapples", "line": "I’ma trip, go to Cannes, France to catch a flick", "vault_lines": ["I'ma trip, go to Cannes, France to catch a flick"], "meaning": "Cannes, France is known for its incredibly prestigious film festival. The decadence of flying all the way to the Riviera just to take in a single film speaks to both Rick’s immense wealth and his familiarity with the highbrow world of art cinema.", "annotation_id": "931327", "url": "https://genius.com/931327", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
