{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do What I Do", "line": "See I come from them cuts for real Much long before this rap came, fuck the deal I survived the game of life, nigga, fuck some skills", "vault_lines": ["See I come from them cuts for real", "Much long before this rap came, fuck the deal", "I survived the game of life, nigga, fuck some skills"], "meaning": "Before the rap game, Scarface was hustling to make his money in the streets. Now that he’s making money in a legal way, he’s survived the game of life.\n\nThis is also a reference to the last lines of his 2002 song “Sellout”:\n\nI survived the game of life nigga, fuck some skills", "annotation_id": "8829412", "url": "https://genius.com/8829412", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do What I Do", "line": "The prison industrial complex a fuckin’ set up", "vault_lines": ["The prison industrial complex a fuckin' set up"], "meaning": "A confluence of factors turn American prisons into a massive industry that largely targets black and latino men. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u51_pzax4M0\n\nOne important factor is the for-profit prison lobby, whereby the increase of private prisons reward expanding prisons and exploiting prison labor.  For a sustained defense of the view that mass incarceration is a discriminatory practice, see The New Jim Crow by Michelle Alexander.\n\n\n\nAs Nas puts it:“a fuckin' set up”.", "annotation_id": "8528170", "url": "https://genius.com/8528170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do What I Do", "line": "Selassie eye in the ghost, thousand bales of that diesel", "vault_lines": ["Selassie eye in the ghost, thousand bales of that diesel"], "meaning": "Selassie I is (according to rastafarians) returned messiah of the bible. The Rastafarian lifestyle includes the spiritual use of cannabis.\n\nRoss could be saying that he’s riding in the Ghost, a luxury car made by Rolls Royce, with Selassie I and a thousand bales of marijuana.\n\nHe could also be saying that he has a thousand bales of marijuana, which is actually Selassie I in the form of a ghost.", "annotation_id": "7834314", "url": "https://genius.com/7834314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do What I Do", "line": "My Atlantic star, not a Notre Dame Not a student loan, tried to motivate", "vault_lines": ["My Atlantic star, not a Notre Dame", "Not a student loan, tried to motivate"], "meaning": "Impressive wordplay that ties together religion, college, 1980s R&B, and cruise ships.\n\nNotre Dame means ‘Our Lady’ in french.\n\nAn ancient title for the Virgin Mary is ‘Our Lady, Star of the Sea.’\n\nSo when Ross says “My Atlantic Star, not a Notre Dame” he is actually referring to a cruise ship! The Atlantic Star is the name of a commercial cruise ship.\n\nRoss is saying since he never graduated college when he does things like buy expensive yachts he’s trying to motivate people by showing them how far he’s come.", "annotation_id": "7833793", "url": "https://genius.com/7833793", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do What I Do", "line": "We were secret lovers, had to get a beeper", "vault_lines": ["We were secret lovers, had to get a beeper"], "meaning": "“Secret Lovers” is a 1985 single by R&B group Atlantic Starr. This continues the 1980s musical references from the previous lines. It also sets up the next line with the Atlantic Starr reference.\n\nHe’s comparing his secret relationship with “Lisa Lisa” (a girl) to his relationship with his secret drug connect.", "annotation_id": "7833721", "url": "https://genius.com/7833721", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do What I Do", "line": "New editions, Lisa Lisa", "vault_lines": ["New editions, Lisa Lisa"], "meaning": "New Edition – An R&B group formed in Boston, Massachusetts in 1982. Founding members include: Bobby Brown, Michael Bivins and Ricky Bell.\n\nLisa Lisa – Referring to the group Lisa Lisa and Cult Jam who toured with New Edition in the ‘80s.\n\nHe’s saying he went from selling weed (Bobby Brown) to cocaine (Lisa Lisa).", "annotation_id": "7833713", "url": "https://genius.com/7833713", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do What I Do", "line": "Riskin’ 25 years just to see another first", "vault_lines": ["Riskin' 25 years just to see another first"], "meaning": "Z Ro is risking twenty-five years of prison time selling drugs just to see another first of the month—when rent is usually due.", "annotation_id": "7796808", "url": "https://genius.com/7796808", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
