{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "No need to hesitate, I need it, impatient (Yeah) I’m not used to waitin’ (Yeah, yeah) I want you to give it to me", "vault_lines": ["No need to hesitate, I need it, impatient (Yeah)", "I'm not used to waitin' (Yeah, yeah)", "I want you to give it to me"], "meaning": "These lines reference Jeremih’s hit 2015 single “Impatient.”", "annotation_id": "11836809", "url": "https://genius.com/11836809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "I want a dude that still kiss me when he mad Type to cop me diamonds, he can miss me with them bags", "vault_lines": ["I want a dude that still kiss me when he mad", "Type to cop me diamonds, he can miss me with them bags"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj & Meek Mill have been romantically involved since 2014.\n\nAccording to Nicki, “this boy that likes her,” is going to get her 3 rings before they become officially engaged. Since Meek is dealing with a platinum chick, it’s only a given that he would cop her diamonds & other expensive jewelry, eschewing the usual “make up” gift of expensive bags.", "annotation_id": "10258896", "url": "https://genius.com/10258896", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Fell out with your peoples, so you took the pictures down (Yeah) Instagram ain’t been the same since you so distant now (Woo!)", "vault_lines": ["Fell out with your peoples, so you took the pictures down (Yeah)", "Instagram ain't been the same since you so distant now (Woo!)"], "meaning": "Ross references the breakup he  had with his ex-fiancée Lira Galore. Allegedly, the two split due to an old photo of a topless Lira with Meek Mill. Ross deleted pics of Lira off his Instagram.", "annotation_id": "10221791", "url": "https://genius.com/10221791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Seen the two G-wagons in my driveway (Woo!)", "vault_lines": ["Seen the two G-wagons in my driveway (Woo!)"], "meaning": "G-wagon is the nickname given to the vehicles in the Mercedes Benz G class. 10 days before Major Key dropped, Rick Ross actually bought a G65 that costs $230k.", "annotation_id": "10171542", "url": "https://genius.com/10171542", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "(Man, with all this red carpet shit, baby)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Future’s not humble about his fame when appealing to women, openly comparing himself to the world-famous guitar player Jimi Hendrix.\n\n\n\nIn an interview with Elle Magazine, Future revealed he is inspired by Jimi Hendrix:\n\nMan, just for being able to take a risk and for being able to step outside his comfort zone. For just being a black artist in rock n’ roll and be able to step outside and create, and make great music. And just be different. Just a different breed. And that’s what I love about Jimi Hendrix’s music—the way he plays the guitar is so different. He’s just an icon all around.", "annotation_id": "10170824", "url": "https://genius.com/10170824", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Ooh, just in case you need me I don’t mind, uh Yo, tell them what to do, tell them what to do Tell them what to do when you see a bad bitch in front of you, baby Yeah, assume the position", "vault_lines": ["Ooh, just in case you need me", "Yo, tell them what to do, tell them what to do", "Tell them what to do when you see a bad bitch in front of you, baby", "Yeah, assume the position"], "meaning": "Nicki’s echoing The Pinkprint’s sex-themed cut “Get On Your Knees”. Her lovers know they have to get on their knees to perform oral sex on her when they see Nicki or any other “bad bitch”.", "annotation_id": "10170258", "url": "https://genius.com/10170258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "(Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": ["We the best and I told you this back in '05 (Maybach Music)"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group or MMG is the record label founded by Rick Ross.  Other popular artists like Meek Mill, Wale, Omarion and French Montana all are signed to this record label.\n\n“Maybach Music” is a regular ad-lib for Rozay.", "annotation_id": "10164783", "url": "https://genius.com/10164783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Eat the cake and he suck on my toes, yes Hittin’ them home runs, I be like “Go Mets”", "vault_lines": ["Hittin' them home runs, I be like \"Go Mets\""], "meaning": "Nicki possibly reveals some Meek Mill bedroom secrets. “Cake” is booty; he’s adept at eating that and sucking toes. A “home run” usually refers to intercourse.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BNLFfE0hkar/\n\nThe New York Mets baseball team play in Nicki’s hometown of Queens and also score home runs. Nicki cheers them on the same way she (possibly) cheers Meek on in the bedroom.", "annotation_id": "10164711", "url": "https://genius.com/10164711", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "I can hold you down, be your friend and your lover (Brrrp)", "vault_lines": ["I can hold you down, be your friend and your lover (Brrrp)"], "meaning": "Future will do everything in his power to keep his girl satisfied, not only sexually but also mentally. He will always have her back. This is a far cry from his attitude towards women on tracks such as “In Her Mouth.”\n\nThis line is also a reference to the DJ Khaled song “Hold You Down” that has a similar message and also features Future.\n\n\n\nThis is also a reference to the song’s sample, Lil Jon’s “Lovers and Friends,” hence the “friend and lover” line.", "annotation_id": "10164513", "url": "https://genius.com/10164513", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "You want watches, new Versaces, you want Céline (Ugh!) Top back, screamin’, “Money ain’t a thing” (Boss)", "vault_lines": ["You want watches, new Versaces, you want Céline (Ugh!)", "Top back, screamin', \"Money ain't a thing\" (Boss)"], "meaning": "Future buys his women whatever they want, like designer goods from luxury brands Versace or Céline.\n\nFuture also interpolates Jay Z and Jermaine Dupri’s “Money Ain’t a Thang” in the last line of his verse:\n\nIn the Ferrari or Jaguar, switchin' four lanes\nWith the top down screamin' out, money ain’t a thang", "annotation_id": "10164325", "url": "https://genius.com/10164325", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Yo, he ain’t messin’ with no average chick, pop, pop He got Nicki, he know that he hit the jackpot", "vault_lines": ["He got Nicki, he know that he hit the jackpot"], "meaning": "Nicki is a woman who enjoys the luxuries of life. The “pop, pop” could signify the popping of champagne bottles, or Nicki’s status as a popstar.\n\nHer boyfriend Meek Mill attempted to win the Powerball in January 2016. Nicki implies he’s already hit the jackpot by being with her.", "annotation_id": "10163970", "url": "https://genius.com/10163970", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Took you shoppin’ in other places that I won’t name (Boss) First time your friends really got to see Balmain (Woo!) Twenty million cash, seen that there with my two eyes (Ugh!)", "vault_lines": ["Took you shoppin' in other places that I won't name (Boss)", "First time your friends really got to see Balmain (Woo!)"], "meaning": "Balmain is a Parisian fashion house that has designed for, and been worn by, many notable names—from Audrey Hepburn to\nKanye West and members of the Kardashian family—who became the face of Balmain’s 2016 Fall Collection.\n\n\n\nThis line may be a reference to Rick Ross’s recent romantic relationships. At the 2015 BET Awards, Ross’s now ex-fiance Lira Galore wore a Balmain dress.  For Ross’s 40th birthday, two women that Ross had been romantically linked with showed up to the party in the same Balmain dress.", "annotation_id": "10163900", "url": "https://genius.com/10163900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Two cups of styrofoam, excuse me, lil’ mama", "vault_lines": ["Two cups of styrofoam, excuse me, lil' mama"], "meaning": "Styrofoam cups are used to keep Future’s favorite concoction, lean, cold.  Lean is a mixture of a soda, like Sprite or Fanta, with promethazine and codeine cough syrup. Sometimes Jolly Ranchers or other candy is added for extra flavor.\n\nAlso known as Dirty Sprite, Future’s adoration of these codeine cocktails inspired the titles of his popular mixtape Dirty Sprite and the 2015’s sequel album DS2.", "annotation_id": "10163755", "url": "https://genius.com/10163755", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Another one We The Best Music!", "vault_lines": ["We The Best Music!"], "meaning": "These are DJ Khaled’s ad-libs. We The Best is the name of his music group.", "annotation_id": "10163659", "url": "https://genius.com/10163659", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Do You Mind", "line": "Every baller tryna score, check them shot clocks But I hit them with them ‘Bron-Iguodal’ blocks", "vault_lines": ["But I hit them with them 'Bron-Iguodal' blocks"], "meaning": "In the NBA, a 24 second shot clock counts down possession of the ball. When it reaches zero, possession changes hands.\n\nWith less than two minutes remaining and the score tied at 89 during Game 7 of the 2016 NBA Finals, LeBron James emphatically blocked Andre Iguodala’s fast-break layup attempt. “The Block” helped the Cavaliers to victory.\n\n\n\nNicki will block any man that tries to make a move on her—she’s committed to Meek Mill.", "annotation_id": "10163608", "url": "https://genius.com/10163608", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
