{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dog Food", "line": "Throw the white in the pot, my future look bright Did my wrongs in the dark, long as that paper look right", "vault_lines": ["Throw the white in the pot, my future look bright", "Did my wrongs in the dark, long as that paper look right"], "meaning": "Referring back to Rozay’s “past” of being a drug dealer; selling crack cocaine as his source of income.\n\nHowever, selling the drug brought Ross some complication – this is brought up frequently in the track, Nickel Rock.\n\nAlso, not to mention Ross' track about the positives of him selling coke – Rich Off Cocaine.", "annotation_id": "5194577", "url": "https://genius.com/5194577", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
