{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "M-cig, let it vape so we liftin’ off", "vault_lines": ["M-cig, let it vape so we liftin' off"], "meaning": "M-cig is a small herbal vaporizer. It is used  to vaporize marijuana, hence Ross is saying “we lifting off”, meaning they get high on cannabis.\n\nRoss is the ultimate brand ambassador, he recently announced he signed an endorsement deal with the M-Cig company and thus name drops them. Ross is known for name dropping his businesses ventures; he has a long standing history of referencing his Wingstop restaurants in his records.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/mCigs/status/501463165088321536", "annotation_id": "3932472", "url": "https://genius.com/3932472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "Hit the corner, burnin’ rubber like a stunt driver", "vault_lines": ["Hit the corner, burnin' rubber like a stunt driver"], "meaning": "Hit the corner refers to him selling cocaine before he made it into the rap game, and when a race car driver or a stunt drivers swerves on a corner you can smell the burning rubber of the tires as it passes by.\n\nBurning rubber also means having sex with a condom so when Ross says he is stopping at a corner it can refer to a corner store where he is getting condoms for his night.", "annotation_id": "3932468", "url": "https://genius.com/3932468", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "Snow white yacht in my red Yeezys", "vault_lines": ["Snow white yacht in my red Yeezys"], "meaning": "Ross juxtaposes the colors red and white in this line by referencing Snow White from Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs and Kanye West’s signature sneaker, the Air Yeezy Red Octobers – which Ross owns a pair of.\n\n\n\nAuthentic Yeezys fetch thousands of dollars on eBay, so the fact that Ross can afford both a yacht and the sneakers shows he’s on a serious cash flow.", "annotation_id": "3931938", "url": "https://genius.com/3931938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "It’s such a pretty thing, life is such a bitch Went to sleep as friends, waking up to this", "vault_lines": ["It's such a pretty thing, life is such a bitch", "Went to sleep as friends, waking up to this"], "meaning": "A reference to the classic song “Life’s a Bitch” by Nas, Ross makes the best of a bad situation. However strong of a hold life’s hardships has on him, he knows it’s meaningless compared to his current luxurious lifestyle.\n\n\n\nRoss has kept the “bitch” known as life close as friends, but once he made his move he awoke to a new start and a feel of accomplishment. This is also the same way one would act waking up after tapping an attractive women.", "annotation_id": "3931658", "url": "https://genius.com/3931658", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "With a weapon, go to steppin’ like I’m Kevin Spacey", "vault_lines": ["With a weapon, go to steppin' like I'm Kevin Spacey"], "meaning": "This is referring to Kevin Spacey’s role as Roger ‘Verbal’ Kint in the movie The Usual Suspects. His character is crippled due to cerebral palsy which gives him a lame foot making him step differently. Here Rozay plays with the word ‘'stepping’‘ as in walking and the act of moving up on someone with a weapon.", "annotation_id": "3931599", "url": "https://genius.com/3931599", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "[Verse 2: Ed Sheeran] I met this girl late last year She said “don’t you worry if I disappear” I told her “I’m not really looking for another mistake” I called an old friend thinking that the trouble would wait But then I jumped right in a week later, returned I reckon she was only looking for a lover to burn But I gave her my time for two or three nights Then I put it on pause until the moment was right I went away for months until our paths crossed again She told me ”I was never looking for a friend Maybe you could swing by my room around ten Baby, bring the lemon and a bottle of gin We’ll be in between the sheets till the late AM” Baby, if you wanted me then should have just said, she’s singing [Hook: Ed Sheeran] Don’t fuck with my love That heart is so cold All over my arm I don’t wanna know that babe Don’t fuck with my love I told her she knows Take aim and reload I don’t wanna know that babe [Verse 3: Ed Sheeran] And for a couple weeks I only wanna see her We drink away the days with a takeaway pizza Before a text message was the only way to reach her Now she’s staying at my place and loves the way I treat her Singing out Aretha, all over the track like a feature And never wants to sleep, I guess that I don’t want to either But me and her, we make money the same way Four cities, two planes, the same day And those shows have never been what it’s about But maybe we’ll go together and just figure it out I’d rather put on a film with you and sit on a couch But we should get on a plane or we’ll be missing it now Wish I’d have written it down, the way that things played out When she was kissing him, how I was confused about Now she should figure it out, while I’m sat here singing [Hook: Ed Sheeran] Don’t fuck with my love That heart is so cold All over my arm I don’t wanna know that babe Don’t fuck with my love I told her she knows Take aim and reload I don’t wanna know that babe [Verse 4: Ed Sheeran] (Knock knock knock) on my hotel door I don’t even know if she knows what for She was crying on my shoulder, I already told ya Trust and respect is what we do this for I never intended to be next But you didn’t need to take him to bed, that’s all And I never saw him as a threat Until you disappeared with him to have sex, of course It’s not like we were both on tour We were staying on the same fucking hotel floor And I wasn’t looking for a promise or commitment But it was never just fun, and I thought you were different This is not the way you realised what you wanted It’s a bit too much, too late if I’m honest And all this time, God knows I’m singing [Hook: Ed Sheeran] Don’t fuck with my love That heart is so cold All over my arm I don’t wanna know that babe Don’t fuck with my love I told her she knows Take aim and reload I don’t wanna know that babe Don’t fuck with my love That heart is so cold All over my arm I don’t wanna know that babe Don’t fuck with my love I told her she knows Take aim and reload I don’t wanna know that babe", "vault_lines": ["I met this girl late last year", "She said \"don't you worry if I disappear\""], "meaning": "These lyrics are from the original Ed Sheeran track “Don't” that was featured on his 2014 album x.\n\nYou can find the original lyrics and annotations here.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iD2rhdFRehU", "annotation_id": "3931458", "url": "https://genius.com/3931458", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
