{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Panic", "line": "2 birds in the kitchen; 1 brick, 1 desert Eagle", "vault_lines": ["2 birds in the kitchen; 1 brick, 1 desert Eagle"], "meaning": "Meek plays with the meaning of the word bird. In slang/drug terms bird usually stands for a “brick of drugs usually cocaine” – a brick stands for a kilo. The gun Desert Eagle contains the word Eagle – a bird – therefore he describes it as a bird.\n\nSo when he says,that he has 2 birds in the kitchen it stands for one kilo of drugs (probably cocaine) and a gun.", "annotation_id": "397195", "url": "https://genius.com/397195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
