{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Seen the pictures, feel the pain, scandalous how they murder son", "vault_lines": ["Seen the pictures, feel the pain, scandalous how they murder son"], "meaning": "There is a very graphic image of Mike Brown in the road after he was killed. Game is hurt by looking at the picture, and shocked by the incident.", "annotation_id": "3983116", "url": "https://genius.com/3983116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Tired of them killing us, I’m on my way to Ferguson", "vault_lines": ["Tired of them killing us, I'm on my way to Ferguson"], "meaning": "https://twitter.com/JColeNC/statuses/499615515779035136\nGame, like many black men, is tired of cops killing blacks. Game is taking his own journey out to Ferguson, as he states later in the verse: “I seen Cole out there, felt I should go out there”", "annotation_id": "3982848", "url": "https://genius.com/3982848", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "People stressing, protesting, unity is a blessing", "vault_lines": ["People stressing, protesting, unity is a blessing"], "meaning": "Gotti is saying that all this stressing and protesting is a blessing because we all are bonded together by this tragedy.", "annotation_id": "3982298", "url": "https://genius.com/3982298", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "And who cares who ain’t on our side ’cause we on our own", "vault_lines": ["And who cares who ain't on our side 'cause we on our own"], "meaning": "Problem is saying that so what and who cares who is with us. Because we are all we have. We are all we got, each other and if we protest we are on own.", "annotation_id": "3981058", "url": "https://genius.com/3981058", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Ferguson, rest in peace Mike Brown And all the young soldiers out there God help us", "vault_lines": ["And all the young soldiers out there"], "meaning": "Ferguson is the city in St. Louis County, Missouri where the killing of unarmed teenager Michael Brown took place. Protests, violence, and police brutality filled the streets trying to bring justice for Mike Brown.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GO1SKC6dK7o", "annotation_id": "3979208", "url": "https://genius.com/3979208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "It’s going down, Armageddon right here Right now, not on TV but right here", "vault_lines": ["It's going down, Armageddon right here", "Right now, not on TV but right here"], "meaning": "Armageddon is a 1998 sci-fi movie about deep core drillers that travel into space to stop an asteroid from colliding with Earth. In the bible, it’s also the sight of a battle during the end times. In this case, Swizz Beatz is referring to both definitions of Armageddon.\n\n\n\nAt the peak of chaos, Ferguson looked similar to a war zone that would be located on the other side of the world. Because of the racial tension that is currently going on between peaceful Ferguson protesters and the police stationed there, the situation escalated from a simple protest to a modern day battlefield.\n\n\n\nAt one point, the situation in Ferguson was so bad, the FAA set a no-fly-zone over the town.", "annotation_id": "3978664", "url": "https://genius.com/3978664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "[Verse 10: JasonMartin]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Problem marks this song’s last verse, and also has the angriest verse. If you pay attention, you will realize that as this song progresses, it gets more and more aggressive. While Game’s opening verse is compassionate, by the end Problem is on a rage, and Problem is also the one that curses the most, to represent anger.", "annotation_id": "3978561", "url": "https://genius.com/3978561", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "As we keep our hands up high and scream for justice", "vault_lines": ["As we keep our hands up high and scream for justice"], "meaning": "Hundreds participated in peaceful marching and picketing to protest the situation surrounding the death of Michael Brown. At an August 11th press conference, Brown’s parents said:\n\nWe don’t want no violence. Michael would have wanted no violence. We need justice for our son.\n\nIn reference to the circumstances of the shooting, during which Brown is said to have been unarmed with his hands in the air, many demonstrations feature protestors with their hands in the air, shouting, “Hands up, don’t shoot!”", "annotation_id": "3978536", "url": "https://genius.com/3978536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Stole by the system, black men we pay the toll", "vault_lines": ["Stole by the system, black men we pay the toll"], "meaning": "Ross is saying the system is stealing these inoccent teens lifes. In which he is correct. In a country like America with a pro-gun system, this is an inevitable outcome. He continues this statement but adds to it that he thinks the black minority is the one who pays the toll for this. The price of the toll is a black man’s life.", "annotation_id": "3977881", "url": "https://genius.com/3977881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I am Michael Brown, ’cause I stand for what he stand for", "vault_lines": ["I am Michael Brown, 'cause I stand for what he stand for"], "meaning": "During the protests in Ferguson many people showed symbolic identification with Michel Brown by saying “I am Michael Brown”.", "annotation_id": "3977581", "url": "https://genius.com/3977581", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Man that sound absurd Matter fact to me that sound like murder", "vault_lines": ["Man that sound absurd", "Matter fact to me that sound like murder"], "meaning": "As the last line just said, Mike Brown already surrendered, putting his hands up, but still was shot and that’s apparently unreasonable. But you know what it sounds more like? It sounds like murder.", "annotation_id": "3977319", "url": "https://genius.com/3977319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "[Chorus: The Game’s Daughter]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This last hook is sung by Game’s daughter, with Diddy saying “Stand up” after the hook. Since these rappers all have many younger fans, it symbolizes that their belief and their stand has passed on to these fans.", "annotation_id": "3977294", "url": "https://genius.com/3977294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "[Verse 3: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This verse isn’t the first time Ross has been speaking on this sort of matter. In his 2013 song “I Wonder Why”, he laments about the shooting of Trayvon Martin.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ISnHMvX0lt8", "annotation_id": "3977252", "url": "https://genius.com/3977252", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Television broadcasts, a confused country", "vault_lines": ["Television broadcasts, a confused country"], "meaning": "Often times, the news chooses to twist stories into favoring their viewers and to not shed too much light on the actual, exact event that occurred.", "annotation_id": "3976727", "url": "https://genius.com/3976727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "What’s done is done,", "vault_lines": ["What's done is done,"], "meaning": "Michael Brown is dead, and no matter how regretful and sorry his shooter, the media, the government, or the police is, the damage has been done and Brown is gone.\n\nCurren$y emphasizes the gravity of what officer Darren Wilson has done as even if he is proven not guilty by the legal system, he will feel the guilt of what he has done forever and the public will feel the guilt for not addressing the issues of racial discrimination and police misuse of power before it was too late for Brown to be saved.", "annotation_id": "3976709", "url": "https://genius.com/3976709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I’m sure the general population trying to be more active", "vault_lines": ["I’m sure the general population trying to be more active"], "meaning": "While most famous celebrities choose to ignore the police brutality that is insanely hard to miss and not be aware of, regular, everyday people are doing everything in their power to stop the police. So basically most civilians are doing more than most celebrities, which is saddening due to the fact that celebrities can reach out to more people throughout the world to help spread awareness of the high rate of police brutality/murder in the United States itself.\n\nProtester showing a sign telling police to help kill a extremist group ISIS, also known as Islamic State because they are the real threat, they have beheaded an American Journalist recently, yet the police chose to shoot tear gas at its own people. Keep in mind, they have been firing tear gas for more than just that one day, though as of now, the tension has eased and there is not so much craze going on.", "annotation_id": "3976703", "url": "https://genius.com/3976703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Don’t point your weapons at me", "vault_lines": ["Don't point your weapons at me"], "meaning": "Many of the police officers in Ferguson have been reported as pointing their high-powered rifles on peaceful civilians during the protests in an effort to intimidate them, some even verbally threatening to shoot.\n\n\n\nSeveral military veterans responded to these reports, stating that they followed stricter rules of engagement in places such as Afghanistan and Iraq, and raising weapons is the wrong way to handle them, as it aggravates the situation.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/AlexHortonTX/statuses/499943287579742209", "annotation_id": "3976656", "url": "https://genius.com/3976656", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "So it’s time we come together Use our voice as a weapon", "vault_lines": ["So it's time we come together", "Use our voice as a weapon"], "meaning": "People are the most powerful and influential when they are unified behind a certain cause. In this case the cause happens to be fighting police brutality/militarization and police misuse of authority to discriminate against certain communities.\n\nWhen divided, the public does not have a good chance to improve the issue, but when united, its voice can be powerful enough to make a change.", "annotation_id": "3976643", "url": "https://genius.com/3976643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Where does it end? I got my hands up, what else am I supposed to do? Rest in peace to Mike Brown Where does it end? And all the other fallen soldiers Tell me, where’s the love for everything we’re going through? That will not be on the news or televised, ah Mercy, mercy, mercy, mercy me Hope that God can save us Mercy, mercy, mercy, mercy me As we lead in peace", "vault_lines": ["Where does it end?", "I got my hands up, what else am I supposed to do?", "Rest in peace to Mike Brown"], "meaning": "The whole bridge summarizes the frustration of many citizens (specifically the African-American community) when it comes to its relationship with the police.\n\nDue to the negative stereotypes associated towards the black community and the tendency for people to give the benefit of the doubt to police officers in other controversial encounters similar to the Michael Brown case, pockets of Americans tends to grasp for reasons to justify over-the-top discrimination and punishment against blacks (particularly young black males). In the Michael Brown case, the unarmed Brown allegedly raised his hands in surrender, thus posing no threat to officer Darren Wilson, who shot him numerous times and eventually killed him.\n\nThe African-American community is now impatiently questioning what more it must do to avoid such severe treatment from the police. It believes the attention should no longer be on solely on how blacks can avoid instigating police officers, but also on what police officers can do to avoid these situations.", "annotation_id": "3976522", "url": "https://genius.com/3976522", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "A lot of motherfuckers need to act more worried", "vault_lines": ["A lot of motherfuckers need to act more worried"], "meaning": "Curren$y is most likely advising people that they shouldn’t feel comfortable around police due to the their violent actions on innocent citizens with the Michael Brown shooting being the most publicized and recent.", "annotation_id": "3976300", "url": "https://genius.com/3976300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "My brodie Game just banged my line like “We gotta do something”", "vault_lines": ["My brodie Game just banged my line like \"We gotta do something\""], "meaning": "Compton OG, Game, called up Problem, a young rapper from Compton, to drop a verse on this song as he is doing right now in order to take a stand.", "annotation_id": "3976270", "url": "https://genius.com/3976270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "How do you preach peace to a family that just lost they own?", "vault_lines": ["How do you preach peace to a family that just lost they own?"], "meaning": "Despite the riots in Ferguson also being a terrible act of violence, Problem understands that Michael Brown’s family(and in extension all black people) have a right to be angry about the situation and retaliate", "annotation_id": "3976265", "url": "https://genius.com/3976265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "News say we’re looting Paint pictures like we some animals", "vault_lines": ["News say we're looting", "Paint pictures like we some animals"], "meaning": "Yo Gotti feels that the media is portraying the situation in Ferguson poorly. When news outlet report about the lootings and the riots it makes the town of Ferguson look unpleasant when in reality they’re protesting to seek justice for Michael Brown.", "annotation_id": "3976246", "url": "https://genius.com/3976246", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Fuck that, we have arrived", "vault_lines": ["Fuck that, we have arrived"], "meaning": "As you can see these rappers aren’t just standing around and doing nothing, like said in the previous line, they made a song about it", "annotation_id": "3976241", "url": "https://genius.com/3976241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Fuck it, my moms, sorry I’m ready to rage", "vault_lines": ["Fuck it, my moms, sorry I'm ready to rage"], "meaning": "Problem is apologizing to his mother (who would most likely not want him to resort to force) for the anger he is about to release through violence, like a solider writing about the horrible things he’s done and is going to do.", "annotation_id": "3976062", "url": "https://genius.com/3976062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "[Verse 1: The Game]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Seeing another young black male shot down in the prime of his life probably hit close to home for Game as his older brother was gunned down at a gas station at the tender age of 17.\n\n\n\nAbove: Game honored his late brother by making him the cover to Game’s west coast classic, Jesus Piece.", "annotation_id": "3976009", "url": "https://genius.com/3976009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "We want justice", "vault_lines": ["As we keep our hands up high and scream for justice"], "meaning": "A common theme of the Ferguson Riots has been the quote “No Justice, No Peace!”. The people of Ferguson want justice for the shooting of Mike Brown, and so does Fab.", "annotation_id": "3975985", "url": "https://genius.com/3975985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Mothers crying ”Stop the riots”, we ain’t got to chalk the city", "vault_lines": ["Mothers crying \"Stop the riots\", we ain't got to chalk the city"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the riots that erupted in Ferguson after the shooting of Mike Brown.\n\n\n\nMany on the side of peaceful protest decry the riots, considering them pointless overkill and actually detrimental to the Michael Brown cause.\n\nThe chalk here is that which homicide detectives outline the bodies of murder victims with. The meaning of this line seems to be that rioting is not necessary, and causes more harm than good.", "annotation_id": "3975975", "url": "https://genius.com/3975975", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Heard another brother slain up in St. Louis Sure the mother feel the pain, but what you famous doing", "vault_lines": ["Heard another brother slain up in St. Louis", "Sure the mother feel the pain, but what you famous doing"], "meaning": "The shooting sparked unrest in Ferguson, a suburb of St. Louis, Missouri, in part due to racial tensions between the majority-black community and the majority-white city government and police. Protests, vandalism, looting, and other forms of social unrest continued for more than a week, with occurrences of escalating violence and night curfews being imposed.\n\nNobody can feel the loss of somebody as much as a mother can do. Wale also states how the mainstream artists partially ignored that incident, or have not suffered as his family did.", "annotation_id": "3975926", "url": "https://genius.com/3975926", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "All that marching and that peace ain’t gonna fucking do nothing", "vault_lines": ["All that marching and that peace ain't gonna fucking do nothing"], "meaning": "A rather cynical way of looking at it. Problem feels – maybe rightly so – that peacefully protesting isn’t going to change anything, and police brutality is bound to occur anyway.", "annotation_id": "3975920", "url": "https://genius.com/3975920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Heard it’s a lotta rotten eggs in the crow’s nest", "vault_lines": ["Heard it's a lotta rotten eggs in the crow's nest"], "meaning": "2 Chainz uses this line to make a metaphor about the corruption and the inclusion of personal feelings of police judgment.\n\nThe “Crows Nest” is a symbol of an overseer. The police are supposed to be protective of the people and oversee to make sure we are safe.\n\n2 Chainz is pointing out that the people who are supposed to be watching and protecting us are rotten and corrupt.", "annotation_id": "3975900", "url": "https://genius.com/3975900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Got us tryna protest, it’s a slow process", "vault_lines": ["Got us tryna protest, it's a slow process"], "meaning": "There is a phrase that says “Rome wasn’t built in a day”, meaning it takes a long time to do things that important.\n\nProtesting against police brutality is definitely an important thing, so naturally it will take time to finally stop police brutality.", "annotation_id": "3975866", "url": "https://genius.com/3975866", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Shot down with his hands up, that’s what occurred", "vault_lines": ["Shot down with his hands up, that's what occurred"], "meaning": "Forensic pathologist Shawn Parcells, who assisted former New York City chief medical examiner Dr. Michael Baden during the private autopsy, said a bullet grazed Brown’s right arm. He said the teen may have had his back to the shooter, or he could have been facing the shooter with his hands above his head or in a defensive position.\n\nProtesters use hands-up gesture defiantly after Michael Brown shooting:", "annotation_id": "3975848", "url": "https://genius.com/3975848", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "They left that boy for hours in the cold out there They killin’ teens, they killin’ dreams (It’s murder)", "vault_lines": ["They left that boy for hours in the cold out there", "They killin' teens, they killin' dreams (It's murder)"], "meaning": "A reference to the Michael Brown case in which a cop shot him 6 times, and just left his corpse lying there for about 4 hours.\n\nAnd Game goes on to underlay the countless atrocities committed by law enforcement to young people all over the U.S. These aren’t cases that have the police protecting and serving citizens, these are cases in which they outright murder people wrongly; hence, those people’s dreams and the dreams of anybody else that involve them vanish along side with them.\n\nThe killing dreams part possibly references the fact that Michael Brown had hip-hop related dreams for his future", "annotation_id": "3975803", "url": "https://genius.com/3975803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Put your flags in the air if you don’t really care (Wave it)", "vault_lines": ["Put your flags in the air if you don't really care (Wave it)"], "meaning": "The lines and variations of “Put your hands in the air if you don’t care” are quite common in hip-hop. Perhaps Swizz Beatz is patronizing other artists who glorify being ignorant or unaware of important real-world issues and instead encourages people to pay attention to these issues. Instead of putting hands in the air if you really don’t care, express your freedom by waving your flag.\n\nThis is also a modified version of Swizz Beatz Chorus on Kanye West’s “So Appalled”.", "annotation_id": "3975800", "url": "https://genius.com/3975800", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Rather use my brain than throw a cocktail through a window", "vault_lines": ["Rather use my brain than throw a cocktail through a window"], "meaning": "Diddy is referring to the turmoil nights as protesters hurled bottles and Molotov cocktails through windows. He would rather get revenge mentally than physically, and he is against the idea of stopping violence by being violent.", "annotation_id": "3975741", "url": "https://genius.com/3975741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Our Lord, grant us good in this world And good in the life, to come keep us safe from the torment of the fire", "vault_lines": ["And good in the life, to come keep us safe from the torment of the fire"], "meaning": "This is a dua'a (Engligh translation: invocation) from the Quran – the central Islamic religious text.\n\n\n\nAs a Muslim, DJ Khaled is calling out to Allah for help with this difficult situation.", "annotation_id": "3975732", "url": "https://genius.com/3975732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "But they ain’t respecting Jesse up out here", "vault_lines": ["But they ain't respecting Jesse up out here"], "meaning": "Reference to Jesse Jackson, an American civil rights activist and Baptist minister. Jackson has been known for commanding public attention since he first started working for Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr..\n\nThe eulogy came as relatives and supporters including Jesse Jackson said goodbye to the young man, remembering him as a ‘gentle soul’.\n\nLook around you. The absence of noise isn’t the presence of justice.", "annotation_id": "3975696", "url": "https://genius.com/3975696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Throwing up our hands don’t let them shoot us ’Cause we all we got, we all we got", "vault_lines": ["Throwing up our hands don't let them shoot us"], "meaning": "According to Brown’s friend and another eye witness, a police officer arguing with Brown and his friend about walking in the street eventually began shooting at the teens, and Brown was killed with his hands in the air, after he stopped running and showed he was unarmed.\n\n“Hands up, don’t shoot!” has become a slogan and a campaign, and protestors of the incident are commonly seen with their hands in the air.\n\n\n\nWith these protests, there has been a call for people across the country, especially those of color, to push for change and justice through a united effort, through events such as Reverend Al Sharpton’s Unity Rally, which brought thousands together, including Brown’s parents and civil rights leaders.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/TheRevAl/statuses/501057112383184897", "annotation_id": "3975684", "url": "https://genius.com/3975684", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "’Cause action speaks louder than words, that’s what I heard", "vault_lines": ["'Cause action speaks louder than words, that's what I heard"], "meaning": "Fabolous is viewing a look at this old famous saying, “actions speak louder than words,” is as a guide for how to live life. Actions should meet verbal obligations or sentiments, and they should not contradict them. If a person constantly talks about the rights of black men, but never thinks of taking a stand or joining a riot, their words have a hollowness or empty quality.", "annotation_id": "3975657", "url": "https://genius.com/3975657", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "And they don’t really respect Obama out here", "vault_lines": ["And they don't really respect Obama out here"], "meaning": "Many Americans believe that due to President Obama’s race, people are disrespecting him more than any other president. The link contains a video of Oprah talking about the disrespect he gets because of his race.  http://youtu.be/H7Jpt8bWAas?t=3m23s", "annotation_id": "3975653", "url": "https://genius.com/3975653", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "If I sit here and do don’t do nothing, homie, that’s genocide", "vault_lines": ["If I sit here and do don't do nothing, homie, that's genocide"], "meaning": "If you see the injustice happening in front of you and ignore it, you’re part of it too.", "annotation_id": "3975650", "url": "https://genius.com/3975650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I’m a resident of a nation that don’t want me", "vault_lines": ["I'm a resident of a nation that don't want me"], "meaning": "Curren$y is, like most rappers, a black man. But because of the racial inequality and the black persons that are killed everyday, is clear that Curren$y is not living in a nation that wants him or any black person.", "annotation_id": "3975641", "url": "https://genius.com/3975641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "’Cause everybody care for a minute, then stop People only there for a minute, then stop And what’s the point of giving if you ain’t giving your all We never getting ahead, might as well give up your heart", "vault_lines": ["'Cause everybody care for a minute, then stop", "People only there for a minute, then stop", "And what's the point of giving if you ain't giving your all", "We never getting ahead, might as well give up your heart"], "meaning": "Tragedys and bad things happen all the time and they are everywhere on the TV, news and internet. People start saying that they will fight forever and won’t stop until justice is made, but most of the times that is not truth. Saying that you’ll do something and only being there for the moment won’t help, so if you are going to do something, stay there from the start to the end until everything is finished.", "annotation_id": "3975629", "url": "https://genius.com/3975629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "God ain’t put us on the Earth to get murdered, it’s murder God ain’t put us on the Earth to get murdered, it’s murder", "vault_lines": ["God ain't put us on the Earth to get murdered, it's murder"], "meaning": "“All we wanna do is take the chains off\nAll we wanna do is break the chains off\nAll we wanna do is be free\nAll we wanna do is be free”\n\nYoung teenager Mike Brown was shot in the town of Ferguson, MO on August 9th, 2014. Brown had allegedly stolen cigarettes from a convenience store, and a few minutes later, 6+ shots were fired at him. He was killed.\n\nThis shooting has received lots of attention from the rap community. Many rappers have made songs about this shootings, such as J. Cole’s “Be Free”, T.I.’s “New National Anthem”, as well as this song.\n\n\n\n“Hands Up, Don’t Shoot!”\n\nThis shooting confirms the sad fact that has haunted America for many years – African Americans are still treated with unfairness and prejudice.", "annotation_id": "3975625", "url": "https://genius.com/3975625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "And I know they hate to hear me screaming, “I’m a Boss!”", "vault_lines": ["And I know they hate to hear me screaming, \"I'm a Boss!\""], "meaning": "Rick Ross is commonly referred to as “Boss”, and has a song titled The Boss.\n\nThis line’s a reference to Meek Mill’s breakout single featuring himself, Ima Boss.", "annotation_id": "3975613", "url": "https://genius.com/3975613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Now we throwing Molotovs in this holocaust", "vault_lines": ["Now we throwing Molotovs in this holocaust"], "meaning": "Comparing the current state of discrimination in America to the genocide of Jewish people in the Holocaust, Ross touches on the severity of the situation.\n\nIt was reported that some Ferguson protesters used Molotov cocktails – a type of homemade fire bomb – during the protests.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/stlcountypd/status/501628755836559360", "annotation_id": "3975596", "url": "https://genius.com/3975596", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Time to take a stand and save our future Like we all got shot, we all got shot", "vault_lines": ["Like we all got shot, we all got shot"], "meaning": "The racism and violence is pretty obvious, but only when someone gets shot to death, people start doing something. Here, all these rappers are trying to tell you save our future like we all got shot, so no one will need to actually be shot for someone to do something.", "annotation_id": "3975582", "url": "https://genius.com/3975582", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "But when the light finally catches you, you’re ice challenged Okay, and I support the ALS just like the rest of them", "vault_lines": ["Okay, and I support the ALS just like the rest of them"], "meaning": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mcGwCnMN2Bc\n\nOrlando Jones pretty much hit the nail on the head, just like what Wale is saying here.\n\nAs important as funding for ALS research is as good as the now, extremely viral Ice Bucket challenge has helped to raise millions of dollars for it. It has taken away attention desperately needed for the events in Ferguson, as well as young black males being shot by cops and acquitted for it.", "annotation_id": "3975576", "url": "https://genius.com/3975576", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "The town erupts in fury", "vault_lines": ["the town erupts in fury"], "meaning": "Spitta is referring to the Ferguson Riots that occurred after the death of Michael Brown.\n\nSeveral riots broke over the course of two weeks after the shooting. Businesses were looted and vehicles and other property were vandalized. Rocks, bricks and bottles were thrown at police officers. Officers used tear gases and rubber bullets to disperse violent protesters on several occasions. Missouri’s State Senate, Maria Chappelle-Nadal joined protesters at one time and she among others, was tear gassed. About 155 arrests were made and 12 businesses were destroyed, including a gas station set on fire.", "annotation_id": "3975575", "url": "https://genius.com/3975575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "And I’m already hearing ’bout this lopsided jury Three faces like his, the rest another story", "vault_lines": ["And I'm already hearing 'bout this lopsided jury", "Three faces like his, the rest another story"], "meaning": "Darren Wilson (the police officer who murdered Michael Brown), is facing a jury that is 75% white, made up of  one black man, two black women, six white men, and three white women\n\n\n\nThis lopsided jury makes it unlikely that justice will be served in such a racially heated case", "annotation_id": "3975574", "url": "https://genius.com/3975574", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "People praying on they feet, police holding on they heat", "vault_lines": ["People praying on they feet, police holding on they heat"], "meaning": "While the people are peacefully protesting and praying for the loss of Michael Brown, police are brandishing their weapons and treating the crowds as if they were rioting", "annotation_id": "3975564", "url": "https://genius.com/3975564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "America’s a glass house and my revenge is mental", "vault_lines": ["America's a glass house and my revenge is mental"], "meaning": "Referring to the famous idiom: People who live in glass houses, shouldn’t throw stones. This phrase means that if you are a type of person who is easily offended, do not go around offending people unless you can handle being offended yourself.\n\nDiddy is depicting the U.S in a glass house, which is in a vulnerable position that could be easily attacked or rebuked if riots were real.", "annotation_id": "3975560", "url": "https://genius.com/3975560", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I’m talking ’bout Ezell Ford", "vault_lines": ["I'm talking 'bout Ezell Ford"], "meaning": "Ezell Ford was a young man making a rap video when some police unjustly killed him. He had a mental illness that the police knew well, autopsy, however they said he was “high on PCP” and shot him.", "annotation_id": "3975550", "url": "https://genius.com/3975550", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "’Cause right now, I challenge you to use your talents to Speak up, and don’t you ever let ’em silence you", "vault_lines": ["'Cause right now, I challenge you to use your talents to", "Speak up, and don't you ever let 'em silence you"], "meaning": "This a play on the word challenge – referencing the ALS Ice Bucket Challenge in the previous line, but challenging his fans to speak up about the shooting rather than dump water on their heads.", "annotation_id": "3975531", "url": "https://genius.com/3975531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I got the keys to the city still we left in the cold", "vault_lines": ["I got the keys to the city still we left in the cold"], "meaning": "The keys to the city is referring to two different topics:\n\n– Kilos of cocaine otherwise known as keys which Ross is notoriously known for selling.\n\n– Earlier this month he was presented with the key to the city of Memphis.\n\nBut an honor like this is not enough for him to be treated fairly; his skin color remains the ultimate stumbling block.", "annotation_id": "3975530", "url": "https://genius.com/3975530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I heard he surrendered, but we all saw how they did him", "vault_lines": ["I heard he surrendered, but we all saw how they did him"], "meaning": "According to several witnesses of the shooting, Mike Brown had surrendered, but was still gunned down. Also, Brown did not have any weapons on him.", "annotation_id": "3975527", "url": "https://genius.com/3975527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Talked to TIP, I talked to Diddy, them my brothers walking with me", "vault_lines": ["Talked to TIP, I talked to Diddy, them my brothers walking with me"], "meaning": "All three rappers have spoken out about the Michael Brown shooting. Game posted pictures supporting Brown through his Instagram.\n\nDiddy, along with his appearance on this song, also spoke out on the issue through his Instagram.\n\nThough T.I. isn’t featured on this song, he has released his own track decrying the shooting and others like it: “New National Anthem.”", "annotation_id": "3975526", "url": "https://genius.com/3975526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "The revolution has been televised", "vault_lines": ["The revolution has been televised"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the classic Gil Scott-Heron poem/song “The Revolution Will Not Be Televised”. In the original poem, Scott-Heron hinted that an American revolution against racism would not be something you could watch happen on your TV, it would be something that everyone has to participate in if it were to succeed.\n\nBut Problem is pointing out that the revolution was televised thanks to the spread of social media. News regarding Ferguson has spread across the country and is being given massive media attention. This still isn’t something that you should sit back and idly watch, but Problem is just making it clear that the revolution that changes this country could very well be televised thanks to the age we live in.", "annotation_id": "3975514", "url": "https://genius.com/3975514", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Hands in the sky, still was left in the road", "vault_lines": ["Hands in the sky, still was left in the road"], "meaning": "Michael Brown had surrendered and put his hands in the sky, but was still left dead on the road after Officer Darren Wilson murdered him", "annotation_id": "3975512", "url": "https://genius.com/3975512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I’m talking ’bout Emmett Till,", "vault_lines": ["I'm talking 'bout Emmett Till,"], "meaning": "Emmett Till was an African-American boy who was murdered, and severely beaten in Mississippi after he was allegedly flirting with a white women in 1955. He was just 14 years old.\n\n\n\nHe was also referenced in a very controversial Lil Wayne line.", "annotation_id": "3975509", "url": "https://genius.com/3975509", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "If excessive force was a drug, then they overdosed", "vault_lines": ["If excessive force was a drug, then they overdosed"], "meaning": "Overdosing is the excessive use of a drug\n\nThat being said if force was a drug and used excessively it would in fact be overdose.", "annotation_id": "3975498", "url": "https://genius.com/3975498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Martin Luther King had a dream", "vault_lines": ["Martin Luther King had a dream"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Martin Luther King Jr.’s legendary speech from his March on Washington, which included the famous lines:\n\nI have a dream that my four little children will one day live in a nation where they will not be judged by the color of their skin but by the content of their character", "annotation_id": "3975494", "url": "https://genius.com/3975494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "On my NWA CMG Hollerin’ “Rest in peace Eazy and fuck the police”", "vault_lines": ["On my NWA CMG", "Hollerin' \"Rest in peace Eazy and fuck the police\""], "meaning": "N.W.A  was an American hip hop group from Compton, California, widely considered one of the seminal acts of the gangsta rap and west coast hip hop sub-genres. The original lineup consisted of Arabian Prince, DJ Yella, Dr. Dre, Eazy-E, and Ice Cube.\n\nCMG, also known for Collective Music Group, is a record label founded by Yo Gotti. CMG used to stand for Cocaine Muzik Group, however Yo Gotti changed the title because he felt like Cocaine Muzik Group was more of an underground street name.\n\n“Fuck tha Police” is a protest song by the gangsta rap group N.W.A.\n\nBut don’t let it be a black and a white one\nCause they’ll slam ya down to the street top\nBlack police showing out for the white cop", "annotation_id": "3975491", "url": "https://genius.com/3975491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "But you have yet to pay your debt So you just flexing then", "vault_lines": ["But you have yet to pay your debt", "So you just flexing then"], "meaning": "People are forgetting that you must donate to the ALS foundation as well and not just do the ice bucket challenge to fit in.", "annotation_id": "3975489", "url": "https://genius.com/3975489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Tired of the okie-dokie, lying you Pinocchio", "vault_lines": ["Tired of the okie-dokie, lying you Pinocchio"], "meaning": "The police department claims that Michael Brown physically assaulted officer Darren Wilson before the fatal shooting and that Wilson “feared for his life.”\n\nDue to the large amount of evidence to the contrary, 2 Chainz doesn’t believe Wilson’s side of the story, instead claiming the department is lying like Pinocchio – a fictional puppet who has become a symbol for lying due to the fact that his nose would grow every time he lied.\n\nThe “okie dokie” is either:\n\n\nAn old phrase meaning “okay,” used in the early 20th century, the time of prevalent racism in America – a way for him to point out that this systematic racism is not okay.\n\nSlang for being played a fool, or believing a scam – something he refuses to do anymore, as he can see the truth that racial profiling is a widespread problem in the country.\n\n\n\nCam'ron uses a similar rhyme in “Family Ties”", "annotation_id": "3975487", "url": "https://genius.com/3975487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Driving while black, tell me, where am I supposed to go?", "vault_lines": ["Driving while black, tell me, where am I supposed to go?"], "meaning": "“Driving while black” is a phrase used to African Americans getting racially profiled and pulled over by the police for no real reason other than their skin color.\n\n\n\nJay Z most famously outlined this scenario in 99 Problems:\n\n“Son do you know why I’m stopping you for”\nCause I’m young and I’m black and my hat’s real low", "annotation_id": "3975476", "url": "https://genius.com/3975476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Gun shots hit the car, now I got the holy ghost", "vault_lines": ["Gun shots hit the car, now I got the holy ghost"], "meaning": "This line line has a double meaning centered around the phrase “holy ghost”:\n\n\nHis Rolls Royce Ghost getting shot and littered with bullet holes\n\nDying and becoming a ghost after being shot, alluding to seeing the Holy Ghost (of the Christian Trinity) in heaven.", "annotation_id": "3975471", "url": "https://genius.com/3975471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "History keeps repeating itself, like a Biggie instrumental", "vault_lines": ["History keeps repeating itself, like a Biggie instrumental"], "meaning": "Notorious B.I.G was one of the biggest rappers in 90’s hip hop and an icon for modern day rappers. His instrumentals are constantly re used in  other rappers tracks because they are just that good. Like the repetitive use of Biggies music the police have not changed much over the years. There are still crooked cops out there who are racist and kill for no reason. They give the american justice a bad name and cause the people they are crooked to to act unkindly towards them, resulting the same cops to be even more crooked.\n\n\n\nWhen Tupac was arrested during his deposition he was asked why he hated cops. The interviewer said it meant a cop, but Tupac reviewed it and first of all:\n\n\nthe song never actually said cops, the reviewer wrote that in, it just said the word “them”\nthe word them did in fact mean a cop\n\nThem meant racist, unjust, crooked cops who which Tupac despised.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9DBAcZpY90k", "annotation_id": "3975465", "url": "https://genius.com/3975465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Turned on the news and seen a tank rolling down the street", "vault_lines": ["Turned on the news and seen a tank rolling down the street"], "meaning": "The police response to the peaceful protest of the people of Ferguson has been unnecessarily forceful, with innocent people being tear gassed, journalists being threatened with guns, and even tank-like Mine Resistant Ambush Protected Vehicles, or MRAPs rolling down the streets", "annotation_id": "3975451", "url": "https://genius.com/3975451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Police taking shots and I ain’t talkin’ ’bout Ciroc", "vault_lines": ["Police taking shots and I ain't talkin' 'bout Ciroc"], "meaning": "A play on the two meanings of shots: gunshots and shots of alcohol to reference both the police shooting of Mike Brown and Ciroc vodka.\n\nDiddy is an ambassador for the luxury vodka company, and doesn’t waste any opportunities to promote the product…", "annotation_id": "3975445", "url": "https://genius.com/3975445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I’m talking ’bout Sean Bell, they never go to jail for", "vault_lines": ["I'm talking 'bout Sean Bell, they never go to jail for"], "meaning": "Sean Bell was the name of an incident in New York, Diddy’s home state, in which three innocent black men were shot at 50 times by 5 undercover cops.\n\nBell was killed and his friends were injured in the shooting, which took place on his wedding day. Although the three of the officers were taken to trial, they were found not guilty.", "annotation_id": "3975441", "url": "https://genius.com/3975441", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "I seen Cole out there, felt I should go out there", "vault_lines": ["I seen Cole out there, felt I should go out there"], "meaning": "In the most notable approach, J. Cole not only made an impactful track days after the shooting, (“Be Free”), but he also visited the town to show his support and pay respects. As he told Complex:\n\nThis is a beautiful thing, people here are saying it: ‘Don’t let them tell you otherwise.’ We’ve been here five hours walking through the streets, and it ain’t no violence, everything is love. Yeah, you got a lot of people that are mad, and rightfully so, of course. Then you got some people — a lot of people — that, yes they’re mad but they see the perspective that violence don’t bring peace. This is love, that’s why we out here.\n\nhttps://vine.co/v/M39ZOq0Oqhe", "annotation_id": "3975425", "url": "https://genius.com/3975425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Yeah, I seen a lot of ice water tossed and I know it’s for a cause My only question is, what we doing for the loss Of Mike Brown?", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I seen a lot of ice water tossed and I know it's for a cause", "My only question is, what we doing for the loss"], "meaning": "Fab is calling out the recent public infatuation with the ALS Ice Bucket Challenge, which has been done by seemingly every celebrity from Bill Gates to Katy Perry to Cristiano Ronaldo.\n\n\n\nThough the Ice Bucket challenge is for a great cause, Fabo questions whether it should be drawing attention away from the situation in Ferguson, Missouri caused by the shooting of 18 year-old Michael Brown by Officer Darren Wilson.", "annotation_id": "3975411", "url": "https://genius.com/3975411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "line": "Trayvon over Skittles, Mike Brown Cigarillos", "vault_lines": ["Trayvon over Skittles, Mike Brown Cigarillos"], "meaning": "Skittles are the symbol of black teenager Trayvon Martin who died in a police shooting. This was the only thing that this poor young man was carrying in his pocket during the incident. He was the neighborhood watch coordinator for the gated community in which he lived in where Martin was temporarily staying and where the shooting took place. He was not armed but the police claimed he was.\n\nAnother young black teenager, Michael Brown, was killed by the police for “stealing cigars”. He grabbed several packages of Swisher Sweets cigars and tried to leave without paying them,   however in a video it shows he left money on the counter and left calmly, however police claim it was an “armed robbery” and shot him dead.\n\nThese are both examples of the racist police brutality that go on to this day and Diddy is speaking out against. How some police are unjust after everything this country has gone through towards to stopping these sort of thing.", "annotation_id": "3975410", "url": "https://genius.com/3975410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Shoot", "status": "done", "targets": 75, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/The-game-dont-shoot-lyrics", "genius_title": "Don’t Shoot", "genius_id": 507496, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Don’t Tell Em (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "Stalley drop pills, double M we get it done", "vault_lines": ["Stalley drop pills, double M we get it done"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is referring to his signed artist, Stalley, who is part of Maybach Music Group, music label founded by Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "4242483", "url": "https://genius.com/4242483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
