{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "I can feel it", "vault_lines": ["I can feel it"], "meaning": "This line is sampled from The Undisputed Truth’s “(I Know) I’m Losing You”, in a similar fashion to how it was sampled on Dr. Dre and Snoop Dogg’s classic “Deep Cover”, which is also the song “Dope” samples its whole grove from.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&v=2jtnCeV3rEk\n\nKanye also samples this on TLOP’s “Fade”.", "annotation_id": "2452267", "url": "https://genius.com/2452267", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Wes, west up, hot temper", "vault_lines": ["Wes, west up, hot temper"], "meaning": "Our boy Tyga hails from Gardena, CA.\n\n\n\nWestside Connection has a song called West Up", "annotation_id": "1709206", "url": "https://genius.com/1709206", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Tell her to pull them things out ’cause my car topless", "vault_lines": ["Tell her to pull them things out 'cause my car topless"], "meaning": "Convertibles with the top down are referred to as “topless” although Nas would rather you call it something else…\n\nBut don’t say my car’s topless,\nsay the titties is out\n\n\n\nOr you could read this line as a rule for riding in Tyga’s whip: it doesn’t have a top on so you can’t either.", "annotation_id": "1555760", "url": "https://genius.com/1555760", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "You niggas stay in your lane no playing ain’t nothing changed", "vault_lines": ["You niggas stay in your lane no playing ain't nothing changed"], "meaning": "Portraying life as a highway is a common cliche in rap music. Don’t cross Tyga, or you’ll regret it (he ain’t playin'). Best stay on the straight and narrow.\n\nTyga, on the other hand, can switch lanes in his insane whips.", "annotation_id": "1539354", "url": "https://genius.com/1539354", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "So sincere in her belly, that’s that Nas shit", "vault_lines": ["So sincere in her belly, that's that Nas shit"], "meaning": "Referencing hip hop legend Nas' first acting role in the movie Belly, where he stared as a power-hungry thug named Sincere.", "annotation_id": "1539333", "url": "https://genius.com/1539333", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Crown on the watch, young niggas still thuggin’", "vault_lines": ["Crown on the watch, young niggas still thuggin'"], "meaning": "Rolex is a very luxurious watch company whose logo is a crown.", "annotation_id": "1539295", "url": "https://genius.com/1539295", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "H on the Buckle, Hermes and the hustle", "vault_lines": ["H on the Buckle, Hermes and the hustle"], "meaning": "Hermes is a popular clothing brand whose logo is a “H”. One of their best selling products, their belts, showcases this logo with a giant H for the buckle. Funny, Rick Ross must be custom-ordering these belts to fit his waistline.\n\n\n\nRoss could also be alluding to his mixtape with Cash Money CEO Birdman “The H” which was recorded in 2008 but not released until 2013 (same year as this song/album).", "annotation_id": "1539291", "url": "https://genius.com/1539291", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Bitch, nigga you don’t want no drama, I’m worth a couple commas", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, nigga you don't want no drama, I'm worth a couple commas"], "meaning": "The commas Tyga are referring to are those shown in his money. After every three digits a comma should be placed in the number. To have more than one comma, he must be worth at least $1,000,000.\n\nOr if you’d prefer a less academic explanation:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rs6kT_0H1MI", "annotation_id": "1539277", "url": "https://genius.com/1539277", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Last King come sign up, all my shit be designer", "vault_lines": ["Last King come sign up, all my shit be designer"], "meaning": "Last Kings is Tyga’s very own apparel brand. Besides that, he only wears designer clothes.\n\n\n\nA possible reference to Tyga’s song, “Designer”", "annotation_id": "1539268", "url": "https://genius.com/1539268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Another triple got me tripping like it’s angel dust", "vault_lines": ["Another triple got me tripping like it's angel dust"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has another triple platinum single, which gets him tripping as if he were on angel dust, one of the most dangerous and addicting drugs there is.\n\nRick Ross could also be referring to Ice Cube’s hit film, Friday(1995).\nWhen smokey starts trippin' real hard.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5UKm6C4EmqI\n\nStart At 0:19", "annotation_id": "1469956", "url": "https://genius.com/1469956", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Hands clap like a nigga in the stadium", "vault_lines": ["Hands clap like a nigga in the stadium"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is applauded like NFL, NBA, NHL, etc. players on the stadium.\n\n\n\n(Mainly black players are applauded, since they are often the best athletes, Rick Ross is making a reference to the superior race here, can’t disagree with him “Niggas” run the rap- and sportsgame)", "annotation_id": "1469955", "url": "https://genius.com/1469955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "I (Pop, pop) wish a nigga would call Thomas", "vault_lines": ["I (Pop, pop) wish a nigga would call Thomas"], "meaning": "Nod to the song “I Wish” by Carl Thomas\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rhHIPx6FnVA", "annotation_id": "1457025", "url": "https://genius.com/1457025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Murder was the case all the kids say that nigga T-raw", "vault_lines": ["Murder was the case all the kids say that nigga T-raw"], "meaning": "A reference to the song “Murder Was The Case” by Snoop Dogg:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Do4fA8tONY4\nAnd that everyone on the street is claiming that it was Tyga (T-Raw).\n\nAdditionally, Tyga is using a play on words with both his name and the name of his new show line. Tyga is letting it be known that all of his listeners are talking about how good (or “raw”) he is and the fact that he has attracted significant street credit. As for the shoe reference, he calibrated with Reebok to create his own shoe line; he called it “T-Rawws” (referenced earlier in the song).", "annotation_id": "1455570", "url": "https://genius.com/1455570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Say my name say my name nigga say my name Hundred million dollar nigga, nigga say my name", "vault_lines": ["Say my name say my name nigga say my name", "Hundred million dollar nigga, nigga say my name"], "meaning": "A possible nod to Beyoncé, but almost certainly aimed at Byran Cranston’s line, “Say my name”, from the season 5 episode of Breaking Bad. The name of the episode also happens to be “Say My Name.”\n\nWalter White was a “Hundred million dollar nigga” while Rick Ross wasn’t even half-way there when he spit this line.", "annotation_id": "1455569", "url": "https://genius.com/1455569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Scottie Pippen on the dribble I just laid ’em up", "vault_lines": ["Scottie Pippen on the dribble I just laid 'em up"], "meaning": "Scottie Pippen was a basketball player for the Bulls. This continues the ___ up series from the last line with a play on laid (laid out/hustled) and laid up (layup in basketball). Dribble also means both drooling(not in his zone) and dribble (actually basketball). Back to back double entedres, get this man a title.", "annotation_id": "1431710", "url": "https://genius.com/1431710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "OK the day you beating me bitch no day", "vault_lines": ["OK the day you beating me bitch no day"], "meaning": "Two important points about this line:\n\n1) Tyga plays on OJ by turning to OK, the next letter in the alphabet\n\n2) This line references the previous about OJ killing his wife, and comments that his bitch will never beat him which fits with the theme of killing hoes (figuratively)", "annotation_id": "1431678", "url": "https://genius.com/1431678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Pardon this good regime, I make your girl David Blaine", "vault_lines": ["Pardon this good regime, I make your girl David Blaine"], "meaning": "David Blaine is a magician, he’s more known for his levitation acts and card tricks more than his disappearing acts. Either way, Tyga says he’ll make your girl disappear before your own eyes.\n\nOn a skit on “General Patton” off of OutKast rapper Big Boi’s solo debut album Sir Lucious Left Foot… Son of Chico Dusty, he describes a sex move called the David Blaine.\n\nThe David Blaine is when you fucking a girl from the back or somebody from the back, right, and goddam, you let your friend slide in without her even knowing, right, goddam, and you run around and bang on the window and wave at her, and, its called the David Blaine", "annotation_id": "1427716", "url": "https://genius.com/1427716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Bitch, I’m the bomb call me the unabomber", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm the bomb call me the unabomber"], "meaning": "“The Bomb” is a way of saying he is the coolest or most popular guy around. Comparing that term bomb with the literal term bomb, really stressing it to the point of bringing up the Unabomber.\n\nTed Kaczynski (A.K.A The Unabomber) was a serial killer that targeted victims by sending bombs in packages to their homes during the late 70s to mid 90s. He killed 3 people and injured 14 others before being caught and sent to prison.", "annotation_id": "1427696", "url": "https://genius.com/1427696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "We taking your dollars creflo no white collar", "vault_lines": ["We taking your dollars creflo no white collar"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the televangelist pastor Creflo Dollar.  He has been subject to controversy because he used all the money he earned from his religious empire on private jets and Rolls-Royces.\n\n\n\nThe white collar reference is also a reference to pastors in general, who are usually pictured wearing a black gown with a white collar. White-collar crime is the embezzlement of cash over time. Both hustles accumulate money slow, but Tyga is just taking your money now.", "annotation_id": "1427691", "url": "https://genius.com/1427691", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Still pop ace king shit, I’m with Rozay", "vault_lines": ["Still pop ace king shit, I'm with Rozay"], "meaning": "Ace of Spades Champagne has became a very popular drink in hip-hop after Jay-Z boycotted Cristal, due to it’s racist owner.\n\n\n\nTyga is obsessed with Kings from Egypt. He named his son King Cairo and started a clothing line, Last Kings, in which the symbol is an Egyptian Pharaoh.\n\nOf course,  Ricky Rozay is on this track with Tyga. He could also be referring to Rosé, seeing how Armand de Brignac does offer a Rosé. Strangely, Hov later goes on to say:\n\nLet’s celebrate, no red champagne, we don’t play that", "annotation_id": "1427687", "url": "https://genius.com/1427687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "AK get a full clip not a soundwave", "vault_lines": ["AK get a full clip not a soundwave"], "meaning": "This right here is what you call a full 30-round 62x99mm AK-47 magazine. (A.K.A Banana clip)\n\n\n\nThis right here is about a 30 second clip from a song. (A.K.A Soundwave)\n\n\n\nNow what makes a fatality? Direct shots from a subliminal diss song? Or direct shots from an AR?", "annotation_id": "1427684", "url": "https://genius.com/1427684", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Bath Salt Boss, got insurance on the beard", "vault_lines": ["Bath Salt Boss, got insurance on the beard"], "meaning": "If you haven’t read the news, the sales of bath salts has skyrocketed in terms of drugs, and so has the people using it as hallucinogens and then later turning into real-life zombies. Rick Ross be moving Bath Salts, but he has to make sure his beard’s safe before getting his face ate out by someone under the influence of bath salts.\n\n\n\nFun Fact: One of the victims of bath salt zombies used to have a beard.", "annotation_id": "1427683", "url": "https://genius.com/1427683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Get wet up she give me head not neck up She clean the mess up", "vault_lines": ["Get wet up she give me head not neck up", "She clean the mess up"], "meaning": "Tyga’s girl gives him straight up brain, nothing lower than that (e.g. neck) then cleans the mess.\n\n“She clean the mess up” could mean Tyga’s girl swallowed his load after performing her duties.", "annotation_id": "1427678", "url": "https://genius.com/1427678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "T-Rawws rock my own kick game", "vault_lines": ["T-Rawws rock my own kick game"], "meaning": "About a couple months ago Tyga worked with Reebok to create his own line of sneakers called T-rawws:\n\n\n\nNow of course Tyga’s going to get a lot of “sneakerheads” rocking his kicks only because they’re “popular”.", "annotation_id": "1427674", "url": "https://genius.com/1427674", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Aviator crew, we flyest ’round here", "vault_lines": ["Aviator crew, we flyest 'round here"], "meaning": "Aviator sunglasses are what Rick Ross is known for wearing, 90% of the time you don’t see him without them. At the same time an aviator, is a person that is piloting an aircraft, hence the reason he’s saying he’s fly. Along with him bragging about that in other songs.\n\nHOWEVER:", "annotation_id": "1426930", "url": "https://genius.com/1426930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Went gold in a month so it ain’t no budget", "vault_lines": ["Went gold in a month so it ain't no budget"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' fifth studio album God Forgives, I Don’t was released on July 31, 2012. On September 12, it was certified gold by the RIAA, for shipments of 500,000 copies in the US.", "annotation_id": "1426919", "url": "https://genius.com/1426919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Bandz a make her dance that’s thousand dollar foreplay", "vault_lines": ["Bandz a make her dance that's thousand dollar foreplay"], "meaning": "The term “bands” is referring to a stack of bills (i.e. $1,000). Tyga is indicating that the money spent on fine women dancing is foreplay. Also a reference to Juicy J’s club smash, “Bandz A Make Her Dance”.", "annotation_id": "1426898", "url": "https://genius.com/1426898", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "Black Maybach leather gloves on that OJ", "vault_lines": ["Black Maybach leather gloves on that OJ"], "meaning": "American football star and actor O. J. Simpson was tried on two counts of murder following the June 1994 deaths of his ex-wife Nicole Brown Simpson and her friend Ronald Goldman. The evidence was sketchy and everything was pointing towards OJ, except one large piece of evidence; a bloody glove that the murderer used which couldn’t fit OJ’s hand. He deemed innocent and was released.\n\nTyga is comparing the sleek black leather in his Maybach to that of the glove that OJ Simpson couldn’t fit into.", "annotation_id": "1426889", "url": "https://genius.com/1426889", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "line": "I’m dope (All) all my shit dope (All) all my shit dope ’Cause it’s 187 how I killing these hoes (All) all my shit dope (All) all my shit dope ’Cause it’s 187 how I killing these hoes", "vault_lines": ["(All) all my shit dope", "'Cause it's 187 how I killing these hoes"], "meaning": "The original title of this song was 187, which is the police code for murder. Tyga is clearly referencing the re-occuring Snoop Dogg line from, “Deep Cover”, but adds a different twist. Instead of killing undercover cops, he killing hoes. Not murdering prostitutes, but easily getting with lots of women. Lady killer is slang for someone who bangs a lot of women.\n\nWhy the name change? It’s probable that Tyga changed the name to focus on how dope he looks, to promote his Last Kings clothing line and T-Rawws shoe line.", "annotation_id": "1426232", "url": "https://genius.com/1426232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope", "status": "done", "targets": 29, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Tyga-dope-lyrics", "genius_title": "Dope", "genius_id": 110781, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Bitch (Skit)", "line": "Call up George Condo. Make me a fucking one of a kind", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "She’s asking for a one of a kind bag, referencing the one of kind Birkin bag that Kanye West gave Kim Kardashian. The bag was hand-painted by George Condo, the same artist that did the cover of his My Beautiful Dark Twisted Fantasy album.", "annotation_id": "3183836", "url": "https://genius.com/3183836", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Bitch (Skit)", "line": "You wanna know what basic bitches do? They wash their hair with shampoo. You know what we wash our hair with? I wash my hair with fucking champagne, baby. (All day) Champagne. (All day) I hope it’s Belaire Rosé I bathe in Belaire Rosé. I have people wash me in Belaire Rosé. People fucking throw rose petals at me when I walk by. They throw Belaire Rosé", "vault_lines": ["I wash my hair with fucking champagne, baby. (All day) Champagne. (All day)", "I hope it's Belaire Rosé"], "meaning": "A champagne that has its own Wikipedia page! Check it out here (it’s not really complete). But what she’s saying is that her money so tall she can cleanse herself in this champagne.\n\n\n\nRoss himself enjoys this champagne and claims it’s his favorite although he reps that Ciroc.\n\nCiroc Boy forever\nBut this Belaire Rosé\nHas to be the world’s finest\n\nRoss also calls himself Rozay which is based of the name of this champagne. They’re are both pronounced the same way.\n\nRozay, that’s my nickname\n\nShe uses its name to explain how people praise her wherever she goes by throwing pedals at her.", "annotation_id": "2884948", "url": "https://genius.com/2884948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Bitch (Skit)", "line": "I’m gon’ show you. If you’re a boss, this stack right here falls out of your pocket, you don’t even got time to pick it up. (You keep walking) You don’t got time. You keep going. It’s probably not worth your time. (Your minutes cost more than the stack.) Keep it moving.", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Proving the classic telling, ‘Time is money’. These chicks stack so much a single stack of cash falling doesn’t concern them.\n\nRick Ross himself has even said this himself.\n\nTime is money (mula)\n\n\n\nIf we don’t use our time working, we are not making our money which in turn is losing money.", "annotation_id": "2884852", "url": "https://genius.com/2884852", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
