{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Make her bust that pussy open in Singapore", "vault_lines": ["Make her bust that pussy open in Singapore"], "meaning": "Nicki obviously likes to spoil bitches with good pussy by taking them on vacation and making them bust it open for her. Gay asf.", "annotation_id": "32405249", "url": "https://genius.com/32405249", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "I got all these dope dealers serving Cut the work up, they surgeons", "vault_lines": ["I got all these dope dealers serving", "Cut the work up, they surgeons"], "meaning": "Dope dealers are mostly men who frequently or habitually uses illicit drugs.\n\n\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj is stating that they are serving. Could it be that are serving drugs to their buyers? To make a deal with them.\n\nThese dope dealers are cutting the work up. A drug addict learns to expect the drugs they buy to be cut.\n\n\n\nProfit is the reason why dealers cut the drugs.\n\nShe compares the dope dealers to surgeons.\n\nSurgeons are doctors who treats injuries or diseases by operations in which the body sometimes has to be cut open to remove a diseased part.", "annotation_id": "26847073", "url": "https://genius.com/26847073", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "So go get off my testicle, pardon my decimal, bitch!", "vault_lines": ["So go get off my testicle, pardon my decimal, bitch!"], "meaning": "To get off someone’s testicle or dick, is a way of asking them to stop hounding you or continuously involving themselves in your business.\n\n\n\nWhen someone tells you pardon them, it is a term to forgive or excuse (a person, error, or offense):\n\nIn 2011, NM had a networth of 6.5 million dollars.\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj is telling these female rappers or anyone who rains on her parade every chance they get, to excuse her for being worthy because they aren’t.", "annotation_id": "26846945", "url": "https://genius.com/26846945", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Cause you’re outta your element; I am your fear", "vault_lines": ["Cause you're outta your element; I am your fear"], "meaning": "If someone is out of their element, they are in place or situation that is not suitable for them aka the music industry and the game of hiphop.\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj is stating that they are scared of her because they know she is her element.", "annotation_id": "26828170", "url": "https://genius.com/26828170", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "No, they can’t see me, they’re never my peers", "vault_lines": ["No, they can't see me, they're never my peers"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj is stating that these female rappers can’t see her because she is untouchable and unstoppable because of her skills.\n\nA peer is someone who a person of the same age, status, or ability as another specified person.", "annotation_id": "26828143", "url": "https://genius.com/26828143", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "In the pool rockin’ polo, Marco", "vault_lines": ["In the pool rockin' polo, Marco"], "meaning": "Marco Polo is a call and reponse game that people play in swimming pools.\n\n\n\nThe game is based off the merchant and adventurer “ Marco Polo ” who traveled from Europe to Asia in 1271–95, remaining in China for 17 of those years.\n\n\n\nPay close attention to what she says Marco Polo in the bar.", "annotation_id": "26828067", "url": "https://genius.com/26828067", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Wetter than a lake, that’s Ricki!", "vault_lines": ["Wetter than a lake, that's Ricki!"], "meaning": "Ricki Lake is an American actress and producer, who is known for her role in the 1988 film Hairspray. Nicki uses “wet” as an adjective for her vagina—which she later used the term in her 2016 feature “Froze”:\n\nPussy wet, Swiffer jet, come through on that bigger jet\n\nNicki referenced the American icon Ricki Lake before, in her 2011 feature “Till the World Ends (The Femme Fatale Remix)”:\n\nYou was hot when? Ricki Lake!", "annotation_id": "19699671", "url": "https://genius.com/19699671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Rollie yellow like Homer Simpson", "vault_lines": ["Rollie yellow like Homer Simpson"], "meaning": "Rollie, also known as a Rolex, is a high-end Swiss luxury watchmaker. Meek compares his gold Rolex to the iconic cartoon character Homer Simpson from The Simpsons, who has yellow skin.\n\nMeek compares his jewelry to the cartoon character similarly, in his 2009 track “Forever”:\n\nDiamond studded yellow Breitling\nLooking like Corona, or Homer", "annotation_id": "14427131", "url": "https://genius.com/14427131", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "That’s dope, nigga!", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He made enough money to buy a Rollie by sellin' dope. Also a play n words to reference homer simpson when he says “d'oh” and a double entendre for dough (money).\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vD_ZKcfZxbs", "annotation_id": "2698248", "url": "https://genius.com/2698248", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "[Verse 2: Nicki Minaj]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Nicki starts her verse with a flow similar to Meek’s:\n\nHer’s:\n\n“I got all these dope dealers serving\nCut the work up, they surgeons\nI don’t want y'all bitches ‘round me\nWhack bitches make curve 'em”\n\nMeek’s:\n\n“I got all these bad bitches twerkin’\nWaves on swim, shit surfin’\nI don’t wanna yall niggas ‘round me\nBroke niggas make me nervous”", "annotation_id": "2304444", "url": "https://genius.com/2304444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Philly brothers, sometimes they call me Ock! (call me Ock!)", "vault_lines": ["Philly brothers, sometimes they call me Ock! (call me Ock!)"], "meaning": "“Ock” — noun. an Americanized version of the Arab word “Ahkhee” which means “my brother”. “Ahkhee” is difficult to say unless you are a native Arabic speaker and thus it is pronounced “Ock-kee”, which then gets shortened to “Ock.“\nIt is a term used mostly by African Americans and African American Muslims in urban areas.", "annotation_id": "2304440", "url": "https://genius.com/2304440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "On the corner Pac-Man Jones,", "vault_lines": ["On the corner Pac-Man Jones,"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is referring to Cincinnati Bengals' Adam “Pac-Man” Jones.\n\n\nThis could just be a clever play on Pac-Man’s position as cornerback for the Bengals. Ross is saying he is “on the corner”, like “Pac-Man” Jones. But, of course Ross is talking about selling drugs, not defending the receivers.\n\n\n\nOr\n\n\nRoss could be referring to when a Cadillac with Jones' nickname “Pac-Man” stitched in the headrests was seized during an April 2006 cocaine bust, which would go along with the “dope dealer” theme of the song. The car was not registered to Jones then, but Jones told a TV reporter that it was his car and that he had loaned it to Darryl Jerome Moore for a music video.", "annotation_id": "2275750", "url": "https://genius.com/2275750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "We drink Belaire like St. Ides", "vault_lines": ["We drink Belaire like St. Ides"], "meaning": "Belaire Rosé is a fancy French wine—Ross went to Cannes, France to present the wine himself. Ross' nickname, “Rozay” is also a play on Rosé.\n\nSt. Ides is a brand of malt liquor first launched in the 1980s. It became popular through endorsements by many rappers including Ice Cube, 2Pac, Dr. Dre, Snoop Dogg, Scarface, The Notorious B.I.G., and Method Man & Redman.", "annotation_id": "2275727", "url": "https://genius.com/2275727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "My sneaker deal like A.I.’s", "vault_lines": ["My sneaker deal like A.I.'s"], "meaning": "A.I. is referring to former NBA star Allen Iverson.\n\nRozay is speaking of Iverson’s $30 million trust fund, which was created for him by Reebok, at the peak of his NBA career. Coincidentally, A.I. has had so many financial woes in the past couple of years that he is over a million dollars in debt and has went bankrupt. Although this would be the right time to tap in to that fund, Iverson can’t touch it til' 2030. He will be 55 years old then.\n\nEven though Ross lost his Reebok deal due to his molly rape line on “UOENO”, he continues to show the shoe brand love. He has stated before:\n\n“I’m still supporting Reebok. I’m still wearing Reebok,”…“It’s nothing more than that. I’ve been wearing Reebok my whole life…Still got nothing but love for Reebok.”", "annotation_id": "2275672", "url": "https://genius.com/2275672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "From Monte Carlo to Los Muchachos", "vault_lines": ["From Monte Carlo to Los Muchachos"], "meaning": "From Monte Carlo, Las Vegas, NV to Mexico could be Ricky’s route to his drug cartel connect.\n\nAlso, the previously mentioned duo, “Sal” Magluta and “Willy” Falcon were known as “Los Muchachos”, which means “The boys” in Spanish.", "annotation_id": "2269613", "url": "https://genius.com/2269613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Talkin’ Al Capone", "vault_lines": ["Flamboyant dough boy, talkin' Al Capone"], "meaning": "“The Boss” Rick Ross is comparing himself to Brooklyn gangster Al Capone.\n\nAl Capone was an original gangster, who led a Prohibition-era crime syndicate. His life was dedicated to many illegal acts from smuggling and bootlegging liquor to prostitution. He died on January 25, 1947, only 8 days after his 48th birthday.\n\nEven though they both are known thugs, they aren’t all bad. Capone donated to many charitable groups with the money he had from his cartel success.\n\nThey have alot in common, including the fact that they both enjoy cigars.", "annotation_id": "2269596", "url": "https://genius.com/2269596", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "“Sal” Magluta, “Willy” Falcon", "vault_lines": ["\"Sal\" Magluta, \"Willy\" Falcon"], "meaning": "Ross is sticking with the theme of the song by mentioning, and comparing himself to, a couple of the most notorious drug dealing masterminds in Florida’s history.\n\nSalvador “Sal” Magluta and Augusto “Willy” Falcon operated one of the most significant cocaine trafficking organizations in South Florida history. They were accused of importing and distributing over 75 tons of cocaine, or over 68,181 kilograms (150,000 lbs).", "annotation_id": "2269592", "url": "https://genius.com/2269592", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Millionaires, never do leers", "vault_lines": ["Millionaires, never do leers"], "meaning": "She is a millionaire, so she never has to take “lears” or learjets. Learjets are used by civilians and businesses, she takes private G6 jets.", "annotation_id": "2268927", "url": "https://genius.com/2268927", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "I’m the shit, coming down Broad Street", "vault_lines": ["I'm the shit, coming down Broad Street"], "meaning": "Ross is playing off the previous lines of Philly.\n\nHe says he is riding down Broad Street, which is one of the main streets in Philadelphia. This street plays host to many of Philly’s land marks such as the Wells Fargo Center and the Avenue of the Arts. It goes through many different neighborhoods and connects to highways. It also leads to City Hall.", "annotation_id": "2257752", "url": "https://genius.com/2257752", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Mastermind", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“Mastermind” is the name of Ricky Rozay’s upcoming 6th album.\n\n\n\nHe released the first official single on September 5, 2013 titled “No Games”, which features Future.", "annotation_id": "2257411", "url": "https://genius.com/2257411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "DC, Double M", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "DC stands for Dream Chasers Records, Meek’s own record label which he founded in 2012. It is a subsidiary under MMG.\n\n\n\nDouble M is of course Maybach Music, Ross' imprint.", "annotation_id": "2257374", "url": "https://genius.com/2257374", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Imported rug, that’s Persian", "vault_lines": ["Imported rug, that's Persian"], "meaning": "Persian rugs are made in Northwest Iran. They are thought of to be works of art and can range from $3,000 all the way up to $100,000.", "annotation_id": "2256932", "url": "https://genius.com/2256932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "I ride in my hood in a Bently like it’s a Crown Vic", "vault_lines": ["I ride in my hood in a Bently like it’s a Crown Vic"], "meaning": "A Bentley is worth a Crown Victoria to Meek, and it’s nothing for him to ride around his hood in one. He just wants to stunt and show his haters what he is working with. Also, he rides around in his hood so frequently in a Bentley, just like the cops ride around the his hood frequently in a Crown Vic.\n\n(Meek and his Bentley)\n\n\n\nCrown Vic", "annotation_id": "2256811", "url": "https://genius.com/2256811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Check up my resumé, I’m upper echelon rich", "vault_lines": ["Check up my resumé, I'm upper echelon rich"], "meaning": "“Echelon” is a level of rank, achievement or reputation.\n\n\n\nNicki is saying that not only is she rich, but she is gettin' money with the best of them.\n\n\n\nCheck the Forbes' Cash Kings list, where Nicki is the only “king” with a vagina. She made more money this year than her two Young Money labelmates, Lil Wayne & Birdman. Not to mention Kanye West.", "annotation_id": "2256769", "url": "https://genius.com/2256769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Waves on swim, shit surfin’", "vault_lines": ["Waves on swim, shit surfin’"], "meaning": "Waves is a hair style for males with short hair. Meeks waves are on 360 degrees.\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj also said In “Your Love”, Nicki says:\n\nAnd he keep a doo-rag, keep the wave on swim\nW-waves on swim so they hate on him", "annotation_id": "2256700", "url": "https://genius.com/2256700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Fruits of my labor, go get me my pears", "vault_lines": ["Fruits of my labor, go get me my pears"], "meaning": "Continuing from the line above, she’s saying those rap chicks who can’t see her are the fruits of HER labor. Then she tells them to go get her pears.\n\nAlmost like in her ‘Itty Bitty Piggy’ & ‘Grindin’ freestyles where she tells these basic bitches to start picking her fruit out because she is the QUEEN.\n\nAncient Egyptian Queens were fed grapes and fanned with leaves while they sat on their throne. http://kittythedreamer.hubpages.com/hub/Ancient-Egyptian-Queens", "annotation_id": "2256683", "url": "https://genius.com/2256683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Green, and I ball Like Rondo", "vault_lines": ["55 hundo, pop green, and I ball"], "meaning": "Meek is comparing himself to NBA player Rajon Rondo.\n\nRajon Rondo is the Boston Celtic’s Point Guard. Rondo is definitely a baller. He is known to put up big number in assists and steals. He has even lead the league in most assists in both 2012 and 2013. Green is the Celtic’s team color.\n\n\n\nRondo balling: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vNpQCbHHdUc", "annotation_id": "2256621", "url": "https://genius.com/2256621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "One wheel up and we swervin’", "vault_lines": ["One wheel up and we swervin'"], "meaning": "Nicki, her hype man SB, and Meek Mill like riding motorcycles.\n\nCheck them three out riding through New York boroughs, Brooklyn and Queens (Nicki’s hometown), before shooting their ‘I B On Dat’ video: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iDb9OFsdHPk", "annotation_id": "2256453", "url": "https://genius.com/2256453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "Now they call me Young Oprah; Harpo", "vault_lines": ["Now they call me Young Oprah; Harpo"], "meaning": "Oprah Winfrey is the richest talk show host. In 2011, it was estimated that her Net Worth was $2.7 billion. Her studio’s name is Harpo Studios which is “Oprah” backwards. Nicki compares herself to Oprah because Nicki is making a ton of money. In 2013, she was on the Forbes' Hip Hop Cash Kings List as the only woman. She made an estimated $29.9 million which is nearly double from her 2012 Forbes' Listing at $15.5 million.", "annotation_id": "2256258", "url": "https://genius.com/2256258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "My clothing line is out in them stores and I’m sipping a Myx, bitch!", "vault_lines": ["My clothing line is out in them stores and I'm sipping a Myx, bitch!"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj released her clothing line, “The Nicki Minaj Collection”, in the Fall of 2013 to K-Mart stores around the world.\n\n\n\nNicki also teamed up with Moscato for her “Myx Fusions” drink. She recently hosted a cruise to promote the drink. Minaj would not only front the campaign, but also shares ownership of the company.", "annotation_id": "2256232", "url": "https://genius.com/2256232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "line": "30 million though, Forbes list", "vault_lines": ["30 million though, Forbes list"], "meaning": "Nicki made the 2013 Forbes Cash King list, coming in at #4, bringing in $29 Million just in 2013. The only female Hip Hop artist to ever do so.", "annotation_id": "2256170", "url": "https://genius.com/2256170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dealer", "status": "done", "targets": 31, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Meek-mill-dope-dealer-lyrics", "genius_title": "Dope Dealer", "genius_id": 229614, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dick", "line": "Went from slice and dice pineapple and now it’s pear (Haha)", "vault_lines": ["Went from slice and dice pineapple and now it's pear (Haha)"], "meaning": "Reference to his song “Diced Pineapples”", "annotation_id": "36954250", "url": "https://genius.com/36954250", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dick", "line": "Post memes I got the toaster and the beam on yah", "vault_lines": ["Post memes I got the toaster and the beam on yah"], "meaning": "Referencing the Meek/Drake beef. Twitter (and other social media outlets) played a vital role in the back in forth, providing memes for comedic effect. Drake cleverly used the memes during his OVO Fest concert while performing “Back To Back”\n\n\n\nRoss is proposing that while others are entertaining the jokes, that he is prepared to take it to another level", "annotation_id": "8327645", "url": "https://genius.com/8327645", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dick", "line": "3 pointer, Harold Miner when I lean on yah", "vault_lines": ["3 pointer, Harold Miner when I lean on yah"], "meaning": "He’s characterizing his balling to Harold Miner shooting a 3: an NBA player who played for the Miami Heat from 1992-1995.", "annotation_id": "8325950", "url": "https://genius.com/8325950", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dick", "line": "100 room mansions, I paid all of the tax No shots, but I write all of my raps", "vault_lines": ["100 room mansions, I paid all of the tax", "No shots, but I write all of my raps"], "meaning": "He wants you to know that there is no tax evasion charge on deck, he payed for everything when it comes to his property.\n\nHe is also addressing Drake in this line. Earlier in the year, Meek Mill called out Drake because he found out that he was using ghostwriters on some his songs– specifically R.I.C.O. and 10 Bands– this fueled the event that scorched the Summer, Meek and Drake trading shots back to back (pun intended).\n\nRoss has chosen to stay neutral since the conception of the beef, but now he’s choosing to be vocal about it saying that he writes his own raps, despite what methods other rappers may use.", "annotation_id": "8325834", "url": "https://genius.com/8325834", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dick", "line": "Wrote the rules on how to ball without a bodyguard Learn to move or get hit with the John Gotti charge I pray you niggas never lose a minute to a cell Or lose your manhood in a yard, painted nails", "vault_lines": ["Wrote the rules on how to ball without a bodyguard", "Learn to move or get hit with the John Gotti charge", "I pray you niggas never lose a minute to a cell", "Or lose your manhood in a yard, painted nails"], "meaning": "Ross wrote the handbook on how to stunt without the need of a bodyguard to protect his neck. He has his own shooters who will do that for him. In that game, you have to know how to maneuver around, or else you’ll get charged like the infamous mob boss John Gotti, who was sentenced to life in prison without possibility of parole in 1992.\n\n\n\nRoss has been to jail before, so he would never wish his fellow man to have to go through that pain. He also prays that if you do, you won’t get turned out in the penitentiary.", "annotation_id": "8325802", "url": "https://genius.com/8325802", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dope Dick", "line": "Get Rich or Die Tryin’, yeah that was 50 plan Filed the chapter 11, guess the nigga kidneys failed", "vault_lines": ["Get Rich or Die Tryin', yeah that was 50 plan", "Filed the chapter 11, guess the nigga kidneys failed"], "meaning": "Get Rich or Die Trying is 50 Cent’s debut studio album and his motto. Ross pokes fun by insinuating that 50 did the latter – died trying. They have been taunting each other for a while.\n\nRick Ross alluded to this lyric in a recent interview with the Breakfast Club.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/oI51YhKkOHo?t=340\n\nKidney failure occurs when waste cannot be filtered from the blood because of lack of water. This could be a jab at 50 Cent’s venture with vitamin water. The water (money) stopped flowing/coming, so his kidneys (bank account) failed.", "annotation_id": "8325686", "url": "https://genius.com/8325686", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
