{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Dopechella", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yo-gotti-dopechella-lyrics", "genius_title": "Dopechella", "genius_id": 5218373, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Here", "line": "If you’ve been through New Orleans, you’ve been through hell and back Boy", "vault_lines": ["If you've been through New Orleans, you''ve been through hell and back"], "meaning": "Not only is there a lot of crime where Wayne Carter grew up in  Hollygrove. But, Hurricane Katrina was the deadliest and most destructive Atlantic hurricane of the 2005 Atlantic hurricane season. It was the costliest natural disaster, as well as one of the five deadliest hurricanes, in the history of the United States. Among recorded Atlantic hurricanes, it was the sixth strongest overall. At least 1,833 people died in the hurricane and subsequent floods, making it the deadliest U.S. hurricane since the 1928 Okeechobee hurricane; total property damage was estimated at $81 billion, nearly triple the damage brought by Hurricane Andrew in 1992", "annotation_id": "1874758", "url": "https://genius.com/1874758", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Here", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Petey-pablo-down-here-lyrics", "genius_title": "Down Here", "genius_id": 76570, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "line": "Had to hit that follow button like, ohh And I never read your bio, baby", "vault_lines": ["Had to hit that follow button like, ohh", "And I never read your bio, baby"], "meaning": "She’s so good looking that he didn’t even take the time to read her biography. He went straight to the pics", "annotation_id": "8555763", "url": "https://genius.com/8555763", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "line": "I tell ’em, Snapchat me that pussy Snapchat me that pussy if it’s cool Snapchat me that pussy Snapchat me that pussy if it’s cool", "vault_lines": ["I tell 'em, Snapchat me that pussy", "Snapchat me that pussy if it's cool", "Snapchat me that pussy"], "meaning": "While the song is primarily about DMing on Instagram, Gotti’s also ready to take his convos with women to the next level via the ephemeral sexting app Snapchat or Apple’s FaceTime video chat app.\n\n\n\nGotti’s use of “mood” is likely a reference to the popular “#mood” hashtag, which could be used as a caption for a sexy photo to denote that someone is feeling horny.", "annotation_id": "8490894", "url": "https://genius.com/8490894", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "line": "And I just followed Angela Simmons Boy I got a crush on Angela Simmons they like “damn gotti you bold” fuck it ima let the world know Goals", "vault_lines": ["and I just followed Angela Simmons"], "meaning": "Gotti let the world know about his crush on Angela Simmons (the daughter of hip-hop icon Rev Run) on October 8, 2014, when he posted this “Woman Crush Wednesday” photo on Instagram:\n\n\n\nAnd just in case that wasn’t bold enough, Gotti posted another #WCW photo of Simmons in July 2015.\n\nIt’s unclear if they have any relationship outside of the ’Gram (the two shared the 106 & Park stage in summer 2013), but Simmons still hasn’t followed Gotti back.", "annotation_id": "8490887", "url": "https://genius.com/8490887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "line": "I love tha gram I love tha gram (I love tha gram) im addicted to it I know I am (I know I am)", "vault_lines": ["I love tha gram I love tha gram"], "meaning": "Gotti’s Instagram obsession is getting a little out of control. Your man might need an intervention:\n\n\n\nWhile social media “addiction” doesn’t function exactly like drugs, many rehab programs (like California’s Alternatives Addiction) have started offering treatment for extreme internet dependency. In 2014, a UK teen made headlines after his “selfie addiction” drove him to attempt suicide.", "annotation_id": "8490866", "url": "https://genius.com/8490866", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "line": "I tell her, dont you hate when you get screenshot (petty) Bitch that dm wasn’t for everybody (rules)", "vault_lines": ["I tell her, dont you hate when you get screenshot (petty)", "Bitch that dm wasn't for everybody (rules)"], "meaning": "Private conversation on social media are private…until one person takes a screenshot and shares it with their friends. Gotti considers this a violation of the unwritten “rules” of DM etiquette.", "annotation_id": "8490862", "url": "https://genius.com/8490862", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "line": "It goes down in the Dm (it go down) it go down in the dm (it go down, it go... down) It goes down in the dm (it go down) it go down in the dm (it go down, it go... down)", "vault_lines": ["It goes down in the Dm (it go down) it go down in the dm (it go down, it go... down)"], "meaning": "The private Direct Messenger (DM) function on Instagram (as well as Twitter and Snapchat) has enabled all kinds of secret flirtation to go down.\n\nGotti (@yogottikom) isn’t the only guy seeing a lot of action in his DMs—everyone from Drake to James Franco has had their flirty private conversations leaked to the public.\n\nBut if there’s one celebrity who’s name is synonymous with kicking game in the DM, it would have to be NBA player J.R. Smith, whos “you trying to get the pipe?” pickup line will forever live in infamy:", "annotation_id": "8490805", "url": "https://genius.com/8490805", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-down-in-the-dm-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Down In The DM (Remix)", "genius_id": 2344165, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Always come through with a bee (Yeah) Got to do a lot to trouble me (Yeah) Visionary still won’t tunnel me (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Always come through with a bee (Yeah)", "Got to do a lot to trouble me (Yeah)", "Visionary still won't tunnel me (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In a Genius interview, KSI explained:\n\nMy vision is always just to prove people wrong, like, you know, that’s always been my life, like, I was in a car with my mum and this girl that I was seeing and I was telling them all about my YouTube videos and they were both clownin' me! They were like, “Yo, like, this YouTube thing ain’t gon' go anywhere, you’re wasting your time, you should just study, blah, blah, blah,” and obviously now, like, yeah, I’m poppin', and, you know, I proved everyone wrong, and that’s just me, I always like proving people wrong, that’s my vision and you will never be able to tunnel me. You will never be able to, like, put me in a box.\n\nAt the beginning of the video, KSI also explained:\n\nI’m always uppin' the levels, and people don’t know what to expect. They were just, like, all right, “you’re never gonna be able to beat Joe Weller,” I beat Joe Weller. “You’re never gonna be able to fight Logan Paul,” you know, like, “Logan Paul is huge,” blah, blah, blah. All right, we got a draw, but then we had a pro fight, people were like, “it’s a pro fight, against Logan Paul? It’s over, it’s done.” And I was the underdog, like, people band against me, saying, like, I got no chance, and then I come through and win, so, like.. Time and time and time again, proving people wrong and that’s just me, man.", "annotation_id": "18703482", "url": "https://genius.com/18703482", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Fuck up the system, make it shut down", "vault_lines": ["Fuck up the system, make it shut down"], "meaning": "In a Genius interview, KSI explained:\n\nI guess some people thought me saying “shut down” was, like, a shoutout to Skepta. No, it was just me wanting to shut down his brain when I punched him. Logan’s brain, for those of you wondering, yeah.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/Fm6N4IADc9s?t=121", "annotation_id": "18703393", "url": "https://genius.com/18703393", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "(M-M-Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group is a record label imprint of Atlantic Records, founded by Rick Ross himself. The tagline, which is voiced by Australian Model Jessica Gomes, is heard on Ross' songs, alongside artists such as Meek Mill and Wale, who are also signed to record label.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4vOExWDh9KQ", "annotation_id": "18511491", "url": "https://genius.com/18511491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "You know I fuck with Ross, I even went and bought the block", "vault_lines": ["You know I fuck with Ross, I even went and bought the block"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Rick Ross’s song “Buy Back the Block” featuring 2 Chainz and Gucci Mane.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BUu8u7fX8Pc", "annotation_id": "18507623", "url": "https://genius.com/18507623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Championship belt, them VVS’s spark", "vault_lines": ["Championship belt, them VVS's spark"], "meaning": "This is a possible allusion to KSI’s ‘YouTube Boxing Belt’ which he won on February 3rd 2018 when he defeated Joe Weller through technical knockout.\nLogan Paul was unable to win it after drawing with him on August 25th of the same year, and KSI ultimately retained it after he defeated him in a rematch on 9th November 2019.\nhttps://youtu.be/CA9g2XHGhPs?t=481", "annotation_id": "18462041", "url": "https://genius.com/18462041", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Devilish views when they’re aiming at the prophet", "vault_lines": ["Devilish views when they're aiming at the prophet"], "meaning": "JJ likens himself to a prophet using religious imagery to paint himself as the hero in his boxing match with Logan Paul on November 9th 2019 which he ultimately won.\nLogan is portrayed to have ‘devilish views’ possibly due to his many controversies.", "annotation_id": "18462014", "url": "https://genius.com/18462014", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Yeah, yeah, I want that knockdown", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, yeah, I want that knockdown"], "meaning": "This refers to KSI’s boxing match against Logan Paul on 9th November 2019.\n\nIronically, though the song was released before the fight, it can be applied to this situation, where many fans believe that he should have scored a knockdown, though the referee believed otherwise, as shown here.\nhttps://youtu.be/PPvarI256eU?t=172\nNevertheless, KSI was winner of the fight by split decision.", "annotation_id": "18461998", "url": "https://genius.com/18461998", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Remember what I said when that pussy tried moving with the opps? (Woo) Now he back with the blocks, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Now he back with the blocks, nigga"], "meaning": "This is a reference to KSI’s NetNobody diss track, “Adam’s Apple.” NetNobody is also known as SkyDoesMinecraft on YouTube but he had said that he was done with Minecraft and focusing on music, but after his beef with KSI he went back to it.\n\nThe line also has a double meaning as the phrase “opp’s” (opposite gang) is a U.K term, and the blocks is where they reside to live, as in a block of flats.", "annotation_id": "18424964", "url": "https://genius.com/18424964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Helicopter pad the home of Sammy Sosa (Biggest) Still stealing all the bases, I’m the ladies token (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Helicopter pad the home of Sammy Sosa (Biggest)", "Still stealing all the bases, I'm the ladies token (Woo)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross name-drops Sammy Sosa, a professional baseball player who broke many records while playing for the Chicago Cubs.\n\n\n\nRoss also explains in baseball metaphors that whenever he engages with a girl, he gets what he wants.\n\n\n\nAll in all, Ross subtly connects his ability to ‘steal bases’ sexually to the legendary hitter Sammy Sosa.", "annotation_id": "18399028", "url": "https://genius.com/18399028", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Phantoms in my yard, so ring around the Rolls (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["Phantoms in my yard, so ring around the Rolls (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "In a clever play of words, Rick Ross refers to the ultra-luxury vehicle Rolls-Royce Phantom, and connects the car to the common nursery rhyme: Ring Around the Rosie.\n\nHe may also be playing on the fact that one of his nicknames is Rozay, adding another layer to this bar.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GdeauBTMYJY", "annotation_id": "18398817", "url": "https://genius.com/18398817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Wanna backstab like Frieza (Mm)", "vault_lines": ["Wanna backstab like Frieza (Mm)"], "meaning": "KSI refers to Frieza, one of the most prevalent antagonists in Dragon Ball Z.\n\n\n\nIn the popular anime Dragon Ball Z, Goku must fight the most powerful, evil villain in the universe, Frieza. Goku defeats Frieza and shows mercy on him by giving him some of his last remaining energy to escape the planet. But as soon as Goku’s back is turned, Frieza instead uses the energy to fire one last blast at Goku in hopes to kill him.", "annotation_id": "18398170", "url": "https://genius.com/18398170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Down Like That", "line": "Dictate death like Caesar (Mm)", "vault_lines": ["Dictate death like Caesar (Mm)"], "meaning": "KSI alludes to Julius Caesar, the iconic dictator that ruled the Empire of Rome from 49 to 44 B.C.\n\nCaesar was a ruthless military leader, taking over the region of Gaul, to later become the first self-declared dictator of the Roman Empire.", "annotation_id": "18398072", "url": "https://genius.com/18398072", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
