{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drive a Nigga Crazy", "line": "Money calls in the morning, death threats through the night", "vault_lines": ["Money calls in the morning, death threats through the night"], "meaning": "Double entendre, “money calls” could mean business deals on the phone, but it also could mean money is calling him. And “death threats through the night” could mean actual death threats, or death itself threatening Ross.", "annotation_id": "7990248", "url": "https://genius.com/7990248", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drive a Nigga Crazy", "line": "Marble on the ceiling cause this crib I wanna flip", "vault_lines": ["Marble on the ceiling cause this crib I wanna flip"], "meaning": "Rozay loves his marble and the glossy stone makes for great decor. Ross puts his marble on the ceiling so when he “flips” or sells the house the new owners can have marble floors.", "annotation_id": "7909486", "url": "https://genius.com/7909486", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drive a Nigga Crazy", "line": "Me likkle, but me tall at war", "vault_lines": ["Me likkle, but me tall at war"], "meaning": "She maybe small but when it’s game time she’s the biggest threat. Which is different, because usually people talk a big game but in reality don’t live up to it, much like Earl Sweatshirt says in his song “Quest/Power”.\nhttps://genius.com/4932921", "annotation_id": "7766576", "url": "https://genius.com/7766576", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drive a Nigga Crazy", "line": "If Afeni he had a genie, Machavelli would be near me", "vault_lines": ["If Afeni he had a genie, Machavelli would be near me"], "meaning": "If Tupac (aka Makaveli)’s mother had a genie, she would obviously wish for her son to be alive.  Ross is saying if this were to happen, pac would be hangin with him at the Bawse’s estate.", "annotation_id": "7763680", "url": "https://genius.com/7763680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drive a Nigga Crazy", "line": "My hustle is supreme nigga, like Supreme nigga Biggie on the wall, Nicki on the team nigga", "vault_lines": ["My hustle is supreme nigga, like Supreme nigga", "Biggie on the wall, Nicki on the team nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is comparing his hustle in rap to the street hustle of convicted drug boss Kenneth “Supreme” McGriff.\n\nMcGriff was the head of the infamous Queens, New York crew, The Supreme Team, back in the 1980s. Supreme is currently serving a life sentence in federal prison after he was convicted in 2007 on charges related to murder.\n\n\n\nThe MMG boss also brags about having paintings of the late Notorious B.I.G. hanging on his wall and having Nicki Minaj on his team. Though Nicki isn’t signed to Ross' label, she is currently dating his artist Meek Mill and has collaborated with Rozay on a number of occasions.", "annotation_id": "7744794", "url": "https://genius.com/7744794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drive a Nigga Crazy", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-drive-a-nigga-crazy-lyrics", "genius_title": "Drive a Nigga Crazy", "genius_id": 2297251, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drop Top Music", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Boosie-badazz-drop-top-music-lyrics", "genius_title": "Drop Top Music", "genius_id": 1889601, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "He put Wi Fi in his cell Middle of the night, my nigga wanna Skype I just count money for him, that shit just get him hype", "vault_lines": ["He put Wi Fi in his cell", "Middle of the night, my nigga wanna Skype", "I just count money for him, that shit just get him hype"], "meaning": "Inmates in prisons have extremely limited access to the internet, and the access they do have is monitored. The person mentioned in the previous line was so wealthy that he was able to get wifi access in his cell.\n\nHe then used that access for personal communications such as Skype to video chat with Ross. Ross counting his money for him only motivated the inmate.", "annotation_id": "26875694", "url": "https://genius.com/26875694", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Nigga vision the clearest, I get shooters on clearance", "vault_lines": ["Nigga vision the clearest, I get shooters on clearance"], "meaning": "Ross has shooters ready to handle his dirty work for him, and he doesn’t even have to pay them full price for the hit job.", "annotation_id": "26875679", "url": "https://genius.com/26875679", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "I seen a rich nigga go to jail", "vault_lines": ["I seen a rich nigga go to jail"], "meaning": "This vers is about Bobby Shmurda, when in 2014 go to jail", "annotation_id": "22462537", "url": "https://genius.com/22462537", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Son of Osama", "vault_lines": ["Mighty Muhammad, son of Osama"], "meaning": "Muhammad’s father’s name was actually Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, so the lyric doesn’t make any sense", "annotation_id": "16767663", "url": "https://genius.com/16767663", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Aggravated with hoes, distracted all of my foes", "vault_lines": ["Aggravated with hoes, distracted all of my foes"], "meaning": "Women keep calling Rick Ross with his money in their interest.  This likely refers to prostitutes or women Ricky finds annoying in general.\n\nWhen he says “distracted all of my foes,” it means that he has expanded so much as a drug lord that it’s hard to keep track of him.  He has given problems to his enemies that they are busy dealing with while he gets his paper.  For instance, Pablo Escobar, once an extremely powerful drug lord, was so powerful that governments around the world would not even try to touch him.", "annotation_id": "2983770", "url": "https://genius.com/2983770", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "This on everything I love I done came too far to look back Lord protect my soul, you heard me? Check", "vault_lines": ["Lord protect my soul, you heard me?"], "meaning": "Ross came a long way, from being a correctional officer to releasing 6 studio albums. he founded  MMG and is the first artist to be signed on Diddy’s management company Ciroc Entertainment. He was named the hottest MC in the game in 2012 to being shot at Biggie and Pac style in 2013. He also owns the biggest mansion in the whole state of Georgia.\n#RichForever", "annotation_id": "2955772", "url": "https://genius.com/2955772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "See me as a promotion, tax charges, etcetera", "vault_lines": ["See me as a promotion, tax charges, etcetera"], "meaning": "Continuing from the previous line, Rozay sees the feds promoting Ross' life in a negative light and using him as a scapegoat. Not only the feds, but also the media as well. Whether through the news or portrayals through movies. Also, when a police detective the case of a major drug dealer, they may get a promotion if they bust the criminal. Example: Eliot Ness from The Untouchables.", "annotation_id": "2882467", "url": "https://genius.com/2882467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Labelled a hustler, look at my Benz", "vault_lines": ["Labelled a hustler, look at my Benz"], "meaning": "A reference to Wale’s 600 Benz, off Self Made Vol.1.\n\nThough Ross was not a drug dealer, he has been associated with drug hustling and it is a common theme throughout his music. HOWEVER, Ross has also worked extremely hard throughout his career. Prime examples of this: MMG with 3 Gold Albums, Wing Stop outlets, a partnership with Reebok. So fuck a nigga, he’s self made. He’s hustling, everyday.", "annotation_id": "2882431", "url": "https://genius.com/2882431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Dope boy tatted on my neck", "vault_lines": ["Dope boy tatted on my neck"], "meaning": "Rick Ross\n\ncalls himself a dope boy because he distributes illicit substances such as hard drugs (ex. cocaine, crack) as well as the standard marijuana and prescription pills in Miami\n\nRick Ross is just another hood entrepreneur.\n\nTHE REAL DRUG DEALER!!!", "annotation_id": "2881481", "url": "https://genius.com/2881481", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Mansion on the water, home in the hills", "vault_lines": ["Mansion on the water, home in the hills"], "meaning": "Big Living.\n\nHaving a house in the middle of a lake or a river is a symbol of wealth. Most houses built on hilltops are for the rich like this mansion:\n\n\n\nRich people also built houses in water only accessible by  Yacht\n\n\n\nRoss is giving people an insight into the drug dealer’s dream, which involves living a lavish lifestyle. Ross may also be drawing comparisons from famous drug dealer’s who have portrayed this e.g. Tony Montana from Scarface, Ace Rothestein from Casino, Henry Hill from Goodfellas and Frank Lucas from American Gangster to name a few.", "annotation_id": "2881369", "url": "https://genius.com/2881369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "No you didn’t see it but I know you bitches heard it", "vault_lines": ["No you didn't see it but I know you bitches heard it"], "meaning": "Ross is often criticized for his lack of a criminal record despite his own lyricism that glorifies his supposed criminal activity as a young man.\n\nWhat Ross is saying here is that criminals don’t always have to get caught. Ross claims to have committed some pretty grimy felonies; just because the authorities didn’t catch him and document these felonies doesn’t mean they never took place.\n\nNo one will ever see the alleged crimes he committed as a young man. Through his music, and various mystery affiliations with gangs, you can hear about these felonies.\n\nAnother way of saying “Things I did in the dark, will it ever see the light?”", "annotation_id": "2867710", "url": "https://genius.com/2867710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Blood on the corner, damn I miss my dawg", "vault_lines": ["Blood on the corner, damn I miss my dawg"], "meaning": "P-Nut, one of Ross' fallen comrades.\n\n\n\nNotable to mention that it can be a recycled line from the hook of Lil Wayne’s song I Miss My Dawgs off of Tha Carter.", "annotation_id": "2867683", "url": "https://genius.com/2867683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Tats on my back, tats on my face", "vault_lines": ["Tats on my back, tats on my face"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is known around for being covered in ink. Along with Wiz Khalifa, Birdman, Lil Wayne, Waka Flocka Flame and many more, Rozay’s whole body is tattooed.\n\nInk my whole body,\nI don’t give a motherfuck", "annotation_id": "2864158", "url": "https://genius.com/2864158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "He wanted him a degree but got him a ki", "vault_lines": ["He wanted him a degree but got him a ki"], "meaning": "The rich man in jail wanted to lead a normal life, getting a college degree, and then eventually joining the workforce. Instead of leading a normal life he ended up selling cocaine instead.\n\nNote that the homophone between “ki” and “key” created wordplay with the next line. The ki opened up the door to the drug world for the man in jail.", "annotation_id": "2860497", "url": "https://genius.com/2860497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Eatin’ out of the trash, shit would make you a killer", "vault_lines": ["Eatin' out of the trash, shit would make you a killer"], "meaning": "Ross has said before that “being dead broke is the root of all evil.”\n\nThis line continues the well-documented history of Ross admiring and then contradicting his own lifestyle and past with religion. Christian teachings – and other Judaic religions – condemn the greed and selfishness that play a role in wealth and success. This line, along with many others, directly defies religion and God.\n\nRoss has done this before, and takes a harder look at this than most of his fellow rappers. While part of this contradiction is present in other rappers' desire for money, women and drugs, Ross analyzes the inconsistencies between religion and reality. This is especially true for someone of Ross' socioeconomic background; religion inspires the poor, but do its teachings advocate the qualities needed to move past the ghetto? Does it encourage the desire for a better life? Ross doesn’t seem to think so.", "annotation_id": "2860490", "url": "https://genius.com/2860490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "They say it’s hard to smile with a double life", "vault_lines": ["They say it's hard to smile with a double life"], "meaning": "When you live a double life you are being dishonest with yourself and a lot of people around you.  You really have to do a lot of acting.  “It’s hard to smile,” but as a famous rapper, Rick Ross swallows his guilt and smiles for his fans.\n\nThis also has another interpretation, by double-life he also means that his friend in jail is serving two life-times in jail.", "annotation_id": "2856583", "url": "https://genius.com/2856583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Barely fit in a Lambo but did it for the appearance", "vault_lines": ["Barely fit in a Lambo but did it for the appearance"], "meaning": "Rozay is over 6 feet tall and over 300 lbs – he is quite the gargantuan fellow. Lamborghinis are pretty compact cars, and aren’t really built for a person as massive as Ross.\n\nThus, Ross admits that he doesn’t really care to have a Lambo – he just purchased one in order to post it on his Instagram account and stunt on fuck niggaz. Ross is known to show off his car collection on his Instagram.", "annotation_id": "2855874", "url": "https://genius.com/2855874", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Lord forgive these bitches, gettin’ their money strippin’ Chasin’ this fast money, next time we’ll do it different", "vault_lines": ["Lord forgive these bitches, gettin' their money strippin'", "Chasin' this fast money, next time we'll do it different"], "meaning": "Ross asks the Lord to forgive him and others in the hood committing sinful acts in order to get money.\n\nThe men typically earn it by selling crack while the women have to sell their bodies via stripping or prostitution. Since they had no other opportunities, Ross asks for forgiveness and promises that if he got another chance, he’d do things differently.\n\n\n\nOther rappers have expressed similar sentiments in their songs as well:\n\nI know that there’s a better way cause I’ve seen it lord\nBut this faster money is so convenient\nAnd I need it, say I need it", "annotation_id": "2855552", "url": "https://genius.com/2855552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Shoutout to KOD, shoutout to Onyx nigga", "vault_lines": ["Shoutout to KOD, shoutout to Onyx nigga"], "meaning": "“KOD” is short for King of Diamonds, an opulent Miami strip club, which both Ross and his occasional collaborator Drake have referenced before. Ross even had his birthday there!\n\nOnyx is also a strip club, and was made most famous, perhaps, by rapper Trinidad James' mention of it in his 2013 smash “All Gold Everything”.\n\n\n\nRozay loves them strippers!", "annotation_id": "2854597", "url": "https://genius.com/2854597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "Shoutout to MMG, cause we the hottest nigga", "vault_lines": ["Shoutout to MMG, cause we the hottest nigga"], "meaning": "MMG stands for Maybach Music Group, which is Rick Ross’s clique. Ross is known to frequently boast how MMG stands atop the Rap Himalayas.", "annotation_id": "2854297", "url": "https://genius.com/2854297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Drug Dealer’s Dream", "line": "One time for Black, nigga, one time for Nut, nigga One time for Gucci, nigga, one time for Cano, nigga One time for Bizzle, nigga, these my realest niggas One time for Trav, nigga, and all them dope dealers", "vault_lines": ["One time for Black, nigga, one time for Nut, nigga", "One time for Gucci, nigga, one time for Cano, nigga", "One time for Bizzle, nigga, these my realest niggas", "One time for Trav, nigga, and all them dope dealers"], "meaning": "Black refers to Kenneth “Black” Williams, of the former Boobie Boys gang – someone Ross has been paying tribute to since his first single\n\nThe “Nut” here is Raymond Adderly, or P-Nut, a close friend of Ross who was killed in a home invasion in 2010\n\n\n\n“Gucci” is Ross' longtime manager Alex “Gucci Pucci” Bethune.  More info here\n\nWe’re unclear about the rest – suggest in comments below!\n\nUnlikely that the “Bizzle” is the Christian rapper who recently dissed him, although anything’s possible\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Bizzle is a South Florida rapper who was murdered in October 2013.", "annotation_id": "2853930", "url": "https://genius.com/2853930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
