{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Memph-ghanistan, shoot them rifles long like African Got them young boys shootin’ shit up like Africans", "vault_lines": ["Memph-ghanistan, shoot them rifles long like African", "Got them young boys shootin' shit up like Africans"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nThis in keeping with the war theme of the line ‘Memph-gan-istan’ references the contrast to American street warfare,\nin the war torn parts of Africa pistols are not as prevalent.\n\nIllegal ammunitions whether held by child soldiers, rebels, private armies or national armies; are in the form of the long automatic rifle.", "annotation_id": "4085602", "url": "https://genius.com/4085602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I been that nigga, I been that nigga", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross has been rapping for a while now, and he’s always been dropping hit songs and has stayed relevant over the years. He’s been that nigga that everyone knows about, especially for his classic ad-lib, the ‘UGH’", "annotation_id": "4451914", "url": "https://genius.com/4451914", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I’m ridin’ down Elvis Presley BLVD I’m ridin’ down Elvis Presley BLVD", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' down Elvis Presley BLVD"], "meaning": "Elvis, the king of rock (who also loved his uppers) has an album titled: ‘From Elvis Presley BLVD, Memphis Tennessee’.\n\nRoss also recorded this song in Memphis, TN, home of the famous Graceland Mansion:", "annotation_id": "4447053", "url": "https://genius.com/4447053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I’m ridin’ down Elvis Presley BLVD Ridin’ down Elvis Presley BLVD Got the boy, got the girl and I got the heart Tell them pussy crackers they can bring the dogs", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' down Elvis Presley BLVD", "Got the boy, got the girl and I got the heart", "Tell them pussy crackers they can bring the dogs"], "meaning": "Boy and girl refer to heroin and cocaine respectively. The ending is very similar to the last hook, except this time the addition of ‘pussy’ lets us know he’s  talking about cops and K-9 units while adding some mild  wordplay between cat and dogs.", "annotation_id": "4432439", "url": "https://genius.com/4432439", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I’m stackin’ scrilla", "vault_lines": ["I bend that corner, I'm stackin' scrilla"], "meaning": "Scrilla here means money, paper, fetti, chedda. You name it.\n\nPhrase coined by E-40: “doin dirt fo tha scrilla maine”", "annotation_id": "4089531", "url": "https://genius.com/4089531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Nigga mouth was full of slugs, left these bodies full of slugs", "vault_lines": ["Nigga mouth was full of slugs, left these bodies full of slugs"], "meaning": "Slugs are a type of ammunition in shotguns, however when bodies are dead and buried in the earth they will be covered in slugs and worms.", "annotation_id": "4085607", "url": "https://genius.com/4085607", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Nigga need that quinine", "vault_lines": ["Nigga need that quinine"], "meaning": "Just like baking soda is used to cut cocaine into crack, quinine is used to stretch heroin. Ross has been making a lot more references to this lately! Like in War Ready:\n\nHeroin and quinine\nCut that bitch a thousand times", "annotation_id": "4074830", "url": "https://genius.com/4074830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Iced ’em with the heater, took his shit, it’s a cold game", "vault_lines": ["Iced 'em with the heater, took his shit, it's a cold game"], "meaning": "Putting someone “on ice” means killing them, but as guns are referred to as “heat” the result becomes…\n\nWORDPLAY!", "annotation_id": "4074826", "url": "https://genius.com/4074826", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I got vanilla, boy, I got vanilla", "vault_lines": ["I got vanilla, boy, I got vanilla"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is stating he has the possession of benzoylmethylecgonine, in other words “Cocaine.”", "annotation_id": "4068534", "url": "https://genius.com/4068534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Bumpin’ Playa Fly until a player die", "vault_lines": ["Bumpin' Playa Fly until a player die"], "meaning": "Rick Ross gives a shout out to Playa Fly, a Memphis rapper, and ex Three 6 Mafia member.\n\n\n\nFun fact: His original name was Lil' Fly while he worked for Three 6 Mafia, but quit due to monetary disputes, and gained attention when he released a diss song, “Triple Bitch Mafia”", "annotation_id": "4065059", "url": "https://genius.com/4065059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Hood Billionaire", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross announced via twitter on September 14th that his next project will be titled “Hood Billionaire” which will be released November 24th.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/512307127738982401", "annotation_id": "4063262", "url": "https://genius.com/4063262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Charged ’em for the nine gram, but I gave em five", "vault_lines": ["Charged 'em for the nine gram, but I gave em five"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is cheating customers out of their money by charging them for 9 grams while only giving them 5 grams. This is a smart move for Ross because he will be able to sell less and still gain a huge profit for himself. The implication might also be that he’s cut the coke with baking soda (or the heroin with quinine), so that while they’re getting 9 grams of something, there’s only 5 grams of actual drugs in it.", "annotation_id": "4063241", "url": "https://genius.com/4063241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Me gold in me mouth, ’round my neck like leprechaun", "vault_lines": ["Me gold in me mouth, 'round my neck like leprechaun"], "meaning": "Leprechaun’s are very fond of gold, so when Project Pat wear’s his gold grill and his gold chains he feels like a leprechaun.", "annotation_id": "4062331", "url": "https://genius.com/4062331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Run up in the trap, I push the panic button", "vault_lines": ["Run up in the trap, I push the panic button"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is known from his previous trap days, the reason why he’s pushing the panic button is most likely because the feds are on to Ross and his trap. So he has to make sure he can get away from the feds.", "annotation_id": "4062311", "url": "https://genius.com/4062311", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Hard work pays off, get more if you sellin’ soft", "vault_lines": ["Hard work pays off, get more if you sellin' soft"], "meaning": "Project Pat is probably stretching his cocaine what might be a hard work but is good for a better profit, because you don’t use as much from the expensive substance. Through this process the drug will lose it’s ‘rocky’ texture and become “powdery'.", "annotation_id": "4062230", "url": "https://genius.com/4062230", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I got Priscilla, I got Priscilla", "vault_lines": ["I got Priscilla, I got Priscilla"], "meaning": "Priscilla Presley was Elvis Presley’s wife for 6 years. Colloquially a slang for cocaine is “Old White Lady.”", "annotation_id": "4060179", "url": "https://genius.com/4060179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "His niggas know I done it, now it’s rumors they want my head Got my Russian bitch sleepin’ with me right in the bed", "vault_lines": ["His niggas know I done it, now it's rumors they want my head", "Got my Russian bitch sleepin' with me right in the bed"], "meaning": "Double entendre! He’s got a Russian woman and/or an AK47 assault rifle with him in bed. Anyone with a hit out on their head would do well to sleep with a weapon.", "annotation_id": "4057302", "url": "https://genius.com/4057302", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I could fly Priscilla, send her in the mail She got Meek Milly cellphone in the county jail", "vault_lines": ["I could fly Priscilla, send her in the mail", "She got Meek Milly cellphone in the county jail"], "meaning": "Meek Mill was recently arrested, following the trending and famous hashtag “#FreeMeekMill”. Ross means that the white girl he’s referring to as “Priscilla” smuggled a cell phone into the prison where Meek Mill is being held. The sample of Mill talking on a phone in the background is used to lend credence to this claim.", "annotation_id": "4056216", "url": "https://genius.com/4056216", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "Half a milli for the whip, this bitch’ll hurt your feelings", "vault_lines": ["Half a milli for the whip, this bitch'll hurt your feelings"], "meaning": "He has $500,000 to spend on either upgrading, customizing, or redoing his car. When you’re driving by in your 98 Honda Civic, you’re probably gonna  get butthurt looking at Rozay’s fly ride.", "annotation_id": "4056209", "url": "https://genius.com/4056209", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "My face familiar, my face familiar", "vault_lines": ["My face familiar, my face familiar"], "meaning": "Niggas know Rozay face because he so damn rich and famous .", "annotation_id": "4055981", "url": "https://genius.com/4055981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "line": "I’m makin’ more with the bakin’ soda, don’t hate on me", "vault_lines": ["I'm makin' more with the bakin' soda, don't hate on me"], "meaning": "Baking soda is used to cook crack cocaine; Ross is making more money with his cocaine exploits than his heroin endeavors. Illegal activities frequently occur in Ross' songs, in fact, his debut single Hustlin' which made him very famous, was exactly about this.\n\nOf course, with success comes envy, just like he said in the first promotional song of his previous album, Mastermind. We shouldn’t hate him because of all the money he’s making with hustling, it’s all he does.", "annotation_id": "4055162", "url": "https://genius.com/4055162", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-elvis-presley-blvd-lyrics", "genius_title": "Elvis Presley Blvd.", "genius_id": 519200, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Empire", "line": "The deal got signed and my split’s all good", "vault_lines": ["The deal got signed and my split's all good"], "meaning": "Drake’s verse recycles lyrics used back in 2009, around the same time he signed to Young Money Records.\n\nI am very happy in my situation now, which is signed to Cortez [Bryant] and Gee Roberson at Young Money and management through ‘Hip Hop Since 1978.’ The most important thing for me is being around my team – they are stronger than any label.", "annotation_id": "8576174", "url": "https://genius.com/8576174", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Empire", "line": "And don’t listen to anybody that knew me Cause to have known me would mean that there’s a new me And if you think I changed in the slightest could’ve fooled me Yeah, and to my city I’m the two-three Drug dealers live vicariously through me", "vault_lines": ["And don't listen to anybody that knew me", "Cause to have known me would mean that there's a new me", "And if you think I changed in the slightest could've fooled me", "Yeah, and to my city I'm the two-three"], "meaning": "These lyrics also appear on Drake’s “Say What’s Real,” off his mixtape So Far Gone, which was released back in 2009. Although the lyrics are identical, there’s a distinct difference in the way the bars are delivered. In this track, Drake adopts a more laid back cadence opposed to the aggressive and emotive flow that was featured on the previous cut.", "annotation_id": "8575402", "url": "https://genius.com/8575402", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Empire", "line": "And these other lames is hardly mentioned I bet that with this pen I could draw attention But you can tell by my strut I’m just chillin’ in the cut, nigga what, and I’m feelin’ like", "vault_lines": ["And these other lames is hardly mentioned", "I bet that with this pen I could draw attention", "But you can tell by my strut", "I'm just chillin' in the cut, nigga what, and I'm feelin' like"], "meaning": "Drake apparently can’t draw in the traditional sense, but he sure knows how to draw a crowd. This was written in 2011, around the time he was prepping a November release for his sophomore, Take Care, which to date is his best-selling album with 2,260,000+ copies sold. Since then, he has only made a bigger name for himself, becoming hip hop’s biggest player, and breaking into the pop-o-sphere. He pretty much predicted his success, and did it with ease.", "annotation_id": "8575003", "url": "https://genius.com/8575003", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Empire", "line": "[Intro: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick reuses his verse and the hook from “Addicted,” from his collab album with Birdman.", "annotation_id": "8574702", "url": "https://genius.com/8574702", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Empire", "line": "Olympic pools of money, I’m just glad I learned to swim", "vault_lines": ["Olympic pools of money, I'm just glad I learned to swim"], "meaning": "The volume of an Olympic-size swimming pool is 2,500 cubic meters, or 88,000 cubic feet. WolframAlpha places the volume of a dollar bill at 0.06943 cubic inches. Therefore, to fill an Olympic-sized swimming pool with American bills, you would need 2,190,200,000 such bills of any denomination to do so. You could use only $1s and still have a cool couple of billion, or upgrade to $100s and nearly triple the wealth of the world’s richest man.", "annotation_id": "8574649", "url": "https://genius.com/8574649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Empire", "line": "No bench time, nickname Starter Drake Franchise player, I don’t even get a water break", "vault_lines": ["No bench time, nickname Starter Drake", "Franchise player, I don't even get a water break"], "meaning": "Reminiscent of a line from “Tuscan Leather”:\n\nBench players talkin' like starters, I hate it\n\nA franchise player is a team’s most talented, recognizable player—think LeBron James or JJ Watt. Drake views himself as the rap game’s franchise player, and it’s a full-time job.\n\nIf he doesn’t work on his long-range game, he might see some bench time.", "annotation_id": "8574646", "url": "https://genius.com/8574646", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
