{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Errday", "line": "I hit the booth, no suit and tie I’m Superman, my bitch is super fly", "vault_lines": ["I'm Superman, my bitch is super fly"], "meaning": "Meek is talking about the studio when he says booth. A studio is where he records his music.\n\n\n\nSuperman was known from switching to Clark Kent, into Superman inside a phone booth.\n\n\n\nBasically, once Meek hits that studio, he turns into SuperMeek. This is the version of Meek Mill you hear on the radio where he goes straight H.A.M. Of course along with SuperMeek, he has a super fly bitch with him.", "annotation_id": "1999076", "url": "https://genius.com/1999076", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Errday", "line": "Jumpin’ off the jet, like sayonara to ya honor", "vault_lines": ["Jumpin' off the jet, like sayonara to ya honor"], "meaning": "This line has a curious reference to D.B. Cooper, who hijacked a Boeing 727 jet, jumping out of it with over $200,000. He’s never been caught.", "annotation_id": "800343", "url": "https://genius.com/800343", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
