{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "Leaving things, I had a bucket full of Maybelline (Ha) I had a bucket in my favorite green", "vault_lines": ["Leaving things, I had a bucket full of Maybelline (Ha)", "I had a bucket in my favorite green"], "meaning": "Maybelline is a popular inexpensive makeup brand. Ross is using this to mean that the women he was seeing in his early days left behind their makeup  cosmetics at his place because they were spending the night.\nThe second line with green could be a reference to money or simply the he really liked a shade of green that women would leave.", "annotation_id": "41198321", "url": "https://genius.com/41198321", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "Mulsanne run ya half a ticket", "vault_lines": ["Mulsanne run ya half a ticket"], "meaning": "Referring to the Bentley Mulsanne. A car that starts at over $300k and can easily reach $500k (Half a ticket)", "annotation_id": "20294552", "url": "https://genius.com/20294552", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "I see my niggas scramble chickens by the twos", "vault_lines": ["I see my niggas scramble chickens by the twos"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n- His niggas are selling dope in the packs of two\n\n\n\n\nHis niggas are actually making breakfast for him and are serving him two scrambled eggs.", "annotation_id": "1817769", "url": "https://genius.com/1817769", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "Every bitch was born to break a man", "vault_lines": ["Every bitch was born to break a man"], "meaning": "Note the excellent use of alliteration\n\nEvery bitch was born to break a man\n\nRick is playing off of the saying, “Behind every man is a woman”, but he’s saying that every woman was made to bring men down.\n\nPrime example : Adam and Eve", "annotation_id": "1817758", "url": "https://genius.com/1817758", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "I know the feeling, gotta re-align your wills to life Or better yet, maybe should write your will tonight", "vault_lines": ["I know the feeling, gotta re-align your wills to life", "Or better yet, maybe should write your will tonight"], "meaning": "Playing off of the word “will”. Rozay is saying that you have to change your focus on how you want to live your life. A better decision would be to start writing your will , because you’re most probably gonna die soon.", "annotation_id": "1817732", "url": "https://genius.com/1817732", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "I’m talking S&M, but got her screaming A to Z", "vault_lines": ["I'm talking S&M, but got her screaming A to Z"], "meaning": "Sadomasochism (often abbreviated as “S&M”) is the practice of receiving sexual pleasure from physical pain and humiliation.", "annotation_id": "1729176", "url": "https://genius.com/1729176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "Money grew like grass Money grew like grass Money grew like grass", "vault_lines": ["Money grew like grass"], "meaning": "A reference to a classic Kool G. Rap line:\n\nThe cash was coming fast/money grew like grass\n\nAs originator of mafioso rap, Ross owes G. Rap a great debt. They collaborated on the track “Knife Fight” off of Ross' Albert Anastasia EP.", "annotation_id": "1723946", "url": "https://genius.com/1723946", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "Cîroc in my margarita in Mexico", "vault_lines": ["Cîroc in my margarita in Mexico"], "meaning": "Ciroc is a brand of vodka that Diddy is the spokesperson for.\n\n\n\nMargarita’s are a delicious alcoholic cocktail (consisting of tequila mixed with lime or lemon juice) that were invented in Mexico.\n\nJust so happens that Ross is in Mexico.", "annotation_id": "932479", "url": "https://genius.com/932479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Even Deeper", "line": "Got on my Vacheron", "vault_lines": ["Got on my Vacheron"], "meaning": "He’s referring to a Vacheron Constantin watch.\n\n\n\nVacheron Constantin is a brand of watches which is regarded as a sign of richness and nobility.\n\nAlso, their watches are limited editions so they run unique and valuable.", "annotation_id": "932458", "url": "https://genius.com/932458", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
