{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "Look at the poverty strike Look at the bombings at night Look at the parents of infants Never knowing if they will abide Punched out and get shot and just die Huh", "vault_lines": ["Look at the poverty strike", "Look at the bombings at night", "Look at the parents of infants", "Never knowing if they will abide", "Punched out and get shot and just die"], "meaning": "Groves seems to be referring to the infamous feuds between Israel and Palestine, as well as the war between Ukraine and Russia. Bringing up parents of children that are uncertain of their future ties in nicely to the overall theme.", "annotation_id": "30427242", "url": "https://genius.com/30427242", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "[Outro: Spencer Groves & Rick Ross] I’m the greatest alive (and enjoy it) I know you know (go hard and enjoy it) If you’re praying for me to leave (push yourself those extra reps) I swear you’ll never know", "vault_lines": ["I’m the greatest alive (and enjoy it)", "If you’re praying for me to leave (push yourself those extra reps)", "I swear you’ll never know"], "meaning": "A very solemn outro provided by a veteran rapper, and a rising star.", "annotation_id": "30427239", "url": "https://genius.com/30427239", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "Why was this not in the book? Two stars, one North, South You afraid you all doubt Me I’m all faith that’s how I am not afraid of what’s out there Everyone lookin’ at rivers but I’m looking up at the sky Cause I’m wondering what’s next cause the river is dry (Who knew)", "vault_lines": ["Why was this not in the book?", "Two stars, one North, South", "You afraid you all doubt", "Me I’m all faith that’s how", "I am not afraid of what’s out there", "Everyone lookin’ at rivers but I’m looking up at the sky", "Cause I’m wondering what’s next cause the river is dry (Who knew)"], "meaning": "Making a comment about his Unreleased album ‘Euphrates’. And how the river is drying up which is a biblical symbol of Revelations and the second coming of Christ.", "annotation_id": "30427219", "url": "https://genius.com/30427219", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "Me and the Bible Tell you my one goal Why are you flexing? I just wanna know? What you’re livin’ for? How’d you find the door? How’d you make it out alive when the lights were off?", "vault_lines": ["Me and the Bible", "Tell you my one goal", "Why are you flexing?", "I just wanna know?", "What you’re livin’ for?", "How’d you find the door?", "How’d you make it out alive when the lights were off?"], "meaning": "As heard on “Halo (feat. Lil Wayne)”, Groves is reflecting on his past of hiding his true feelings by “flexing” or boasting his accomplishments to mask insecurity.", "annotation_id": "30427199", "url": "https://genius.com/30427199", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "Damn Woah", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "With over 7 seconds runtime by these 2 words, the tone of Groves' voice sound reflective and apologetic. Perhaps alluding to his long awaited 2nd drop, and time away from the music scene.", "annotation_id": "30427193", "url": "https://genius.com/30427193", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "Every minute every hour I need Thee You’re the only one who can save me Every minute every hour (every hour) I need Thee I need Thee (I need)", "vault_lines": ["You’re the only one who can save me"], "meaning": "Kingston comes back with the second rendition of the Chorus, this time accompanied by the first Spencer Groves vocals on the track.", "annotation_id": "30427190", "url": "https://genius.com/30427190", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "I’m lookin’ in the Phantom, bitch you know that I’m the mobb", "vault_lines": ["I’m lookin’ in the Phantom, bitch you know that I’m the mobb"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s love for cars is no secret. He hosts a car show that hosts over 7,000 people every year.", "annotation_id": "30427186", "url": "https://genius.com/30427186", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "Hundred stacks on the watch Hundred blocks on the dot Ricky Ross new whip, tennis shoes and the socks", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "As quoted from his verse on Kanye West’s “Devil in a New Dress” ‘Excess is just my character’. Ross starts his 16 bar verse flexing on everyone who ever doubted him.", "annotation_id": "30427180", "url": "https://genius.com/30427180", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "I accept reality There’s fuckin trillionaires being developed Before our eyes right now Are you feeling Ricky Ross I get a million a month Maybach Music", "vault_lines": ["There’s fuckin trillionaires being developed", "Before our eyes right now"], "meaning": "Ross again provides narration over the track as a segue into his verse. The notorious “Maybach Music” tag is heard just before the drop.", "annotation_id": "30427173", "url": "https://genius.com/30427173", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Every Hour", "line": "Every minute every hour I need Thee You’re the only one who can save me Every minute every hour I need Thee I need Thee", "vault_lines": ["You’re the only one who can save me"], "meaning": "A hymn originally arraigned by Annie Sherwood Hawks is interpolated by Kingston. Hawks had a love for writing poetry, and her poems were published in local newspapers while she was still in her youth.", "annotation_id": "30427161", "url": "https://genius.com/30427161", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
