{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "I blaze J’s, fuck the Dutch slave trade", "vault_lines": ["I blaze J's, fuck the Dutch slave trade"], "meaning": "Dutch Masters (Better known as Dutches) are a brand of cigars. They are usually gutted to remove the tobacco inside and refilled with weed (known as a blunt). Here Ross is saying he does not smoke blunts, but rather refers to smoke Joints, which are different to blunts as they are rolled with rolling papers rather than a tobacco leaf. He also condemns the Dutch slave trade, which took place in the Southern Caribbean, cleverly tying this in with his dislike for blunts, specifically Dutches.", "annotation_id": "4936751", "url": "https://genius.com/4936751", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Your paper chasin’, can’t see that it’s runnin’ from you", "vault_lines": ["Your paper chasin', can't see that it's runnin' from you"], "meaning": "Possibly an unintentional reference to a Paradox of Motion, explaining how the closer you get to something, the more difficult it becomes to reach that thing:\n\nSuppose Atalanta wishes to walk to the end of a path. Before she can get there, she must get halfway there. Before she can get halfway there, she must get a quarter of the way there. Before traveling a quarter, she must travel one-eighth; before an eighth, one-sixteenth; and so on.\n…\nThis description requires one to complete an infinite number of tasks, which Zeno maintains is an impossibility.", "annotation_id": "21138656", "url": "https://genius.com/21138656", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Tennessee, I felt like Mr. Wendal", "vault_lines": ["Tennessee, I felt like Mr. Wendal"], "meaning": "A reference to 90s hip-hop group Arrested Development’s track “Mr. Wendel”", "annotation_id": "7509986", "url": "https://genius.com/7509986", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Belaire Rose", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross endorsed the French sparkling wine Luc Belaire Rose in 2013 and he has been heavily promoting it ever since. Ross also formed a group called the Black Bottle Boys, which consists of other rappers who promote the wine.", "annotation_id": "4936773", "url": "https://genius.com/4936773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Speakin’ in native tongues, me, myself and I", "vault_lines": ["Speakin' in native tongues, me, myself and I"], "meaning": "“Me,Myself and I” was a song by “De La Soul”, a legendary hip hop group. They were part of a huge hip hop collective by the name of “Native Tongues” which contained many other rappers and hip hop groups like Common, A Tribe Called Quest, Brand Nubian, Leaders of The New School, Black Sheep, Queen Latifah, and (lesser known at the time) Mos Def\n\nWhat Ross means is he’s speaking in a language only, in his words, “me, myself and I” can understand.\n\nVery nice line in my opinion.", "annotation_id": "4856283", "url": "https://genius.com/4856283", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Through Michael Rapaport eyes, it’s just a lost tribe", "vault_lines": ["Through Michael Rapaport eyes, it's just a lost tribe"], "meaning": "Michael Rapaport played as Donald “Don” Self on the show prison Break. Don Self was a ICE Homeland Security Investigations special agent. He he studied law before work for ICE Homeland Security in 2002. Practiced law in Long Island New York from Approx 1980’s to Early 2000; New York was infested with crime such as Coke like in the 80’s. It is a lost trial to a very trained professional of law.\n\nSo moral is never give up, I guess", "annotation_id": "4782396", "url": "https://genius.com/4782396", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Butterball, Magic City, so you know it’s him, me", "vault_lines": ["Butterball, Magic City, so you know it's him, me"], "meaning": "Mitch Glazer produced a pool ulnar show called “Magic City” Rick Ross made a guest appearance  as Butterball. So you should know that’s Rick Ross", "annotation_id": "4782371", "url": "https://genius.com/4782371", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Francis Ford", "vault_lines": ["Francis Ford films budget, double-forty M's"], "meaning": "The title of this track, “Family Ties”, is a reference to organized crime. Francis Ford Coppola is an American film director, producer and screenwriter known for directing The Godfather trilogy, which is a film series that tells the story of the fictional Corleone crime family. Ross mentions The Godfather and Corleone family in the second and third verses of this song.", "annotation_id": "4490792", "url": "https://genius.com/4490792", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "How she fuck on the back, that’s to keep food on her stomach", "vault_lines": ["How she fuck on the back, that's to keep food on her stomach"], "meaning": "Here Ross is seemingly talking about a prostitute or a gold digger, though the line could certainly apply to all women..\n\nShe has sex with the man face-up, on her back, refusing to let the man turn her over. She does this to “keep food in her stomach,” or to keep from starving. Not only does this represent the struggle to make ends meet but the power struggle between man and woman that comes with that endeavor.\n\nReminiscent of this classic line by Rozay: https://genius.com/2855552/Rick-ross-drug-dealers-dream/Lord-forgive-these-bitches-gettin-their-money-strippin-chasin-this-fast-money-next-time-well-do-it-different", "annotation_id": "4432375", "url": "https://genius.com/4432375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "It was written, Mr. Jones, a different picture", "vault_lines": ["It was written, Mr. Jones, a different picture"], "meaning": "Here Rozay shouts out a legend, Nasir Jones. Nas' second album, It Was Written, was considered the breakthrough album for Mafioso-style of rap. Ross has collaborated with Nas before, most notably on “God Forgives, I Don’t” and Nas' “Life Is Good.”\n\n\n\nRoss might be suggesting that the album gave him a different perspective on life. It wouldn’t be the first time Ross has paid homage to Nas' poetry.", "annotation_id": "4426921", "url": "https://genius.com/4426921", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Fuckin’ with them hoes you niggas still can’t afford", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' with them hoes you niggas still can't afford"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is messing around and have all sorts of sex with girls that no average person could get because he’s a Hood Billonare. These women aren’t cheap and will only be with a man if she notices that he’s a big spender.", "annotation_id": "4395667", "url": "https://genius.com/4395667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Made so many mistakes I know that my niggas relate Just to rattle my cage, so much shit they sat on my plate", "vault_lines": ["Just to rattle my cage, so much shit they sat on my plate"], "meaning": "Growing up in a do-or-die environment, and then being thrust onto the national stage where every move is scrutinized, you can be sure Ross never forgets his missteps. He knows his fellow dawgs can relate.", "annotation_id": "4395636", "url": "https://genius.com/4395636", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Double-M, fuckin’ G", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Ross was waiting until the end of “Family Ties” to rhyme the hook, “Look at me” with his label, MMG.\n\n\n\nBy pausing between the “Double-M” and “fuckin' G,” Ross is saying he’s a “fuckin' G” making many millions.", "annotation_id": "4395630", "url": "https://genius.com/4395630", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Niggas own Versace, don’t know Nikki Giovanni", "vault_lines": ["Niggas own Versace, don't know Nikki Giovanni"], "meaning": "Nikki Giovanni is one of the world’s most well-known African American poets. She has won numerous awards, including the Langston Hughes Medal, the NAACP Image Award, and has been nominated for a Grammy Award,for her Nikki Giovanni Poetry Collection. Giovanni gained initial fame in the late 1960s as one of the leading authors of the Black Arts Movement.\n\n\n\nRappers nowadays are obsessed with fashion and designer labels like Versace and Armani. Maybe Rick is imploring to listen to a wider range of art, especially since she was nominated for a grammy award once for best spoken word album and some rappers haven’t even produced the quality of music to be nominated.", "annotation_id": "4395622", "url": "https://genius.com/4395622", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Had a few seizures, nigga refused to get me some sleep", "vault_lines": ["Had a few seizures, nigga refused to get me some sleep"], "meaning": "In late 2011, Ross had two seizures in one day which was due to lack of sleep.", "annotation_id": "4395614", "url": "https://genius.com/4395614", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Family Ties", "line": "Shots fired, man expired in his Jordan 3's Small talk, turn that page, that’s all they ever read", "vault_lines": ["Shots fired, man expired in his Jordan 3's"], "meaning": "In Rick Ross' neighborhood, reading an article in the newspaper of a man getting shot is nothing new to them. It’s so common in the papers that people start to consider it small talk and turn the page to read a more interesting story. Because violence is in the news so much, we start to become less sensitive to each new tragedy.", "annotation_id": "4395554", "url": "https://genius.com/4395554", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
