{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "And when they love you to death, just never die on ’em”", "vault_lines": ["And when they love you to death, just never die on 'em\""], "meaning": "Clever word play, when someone loves you “to death,” it means that they are really in love with you. So Drake says to not “die on them” or let them down.", "annotation_id": "410906", "url": "https://genius.com/410906", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "[Verse 4: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This verse is not on the single version, due to Wayne not being able to make the music video shoot. This verse only appears on the album version of the record.", "annotation_id": "105529", "url": "https://genius.com/105529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "I keep a red flag, in case I get penalized", "vault_lines": ["I keep a red flag, in case I get penalized"], "meaning": "In American football, a yellow flag is thrown if there is a penalty. A red flag is thrown to challenge a referee’s decision. He uses a red flag instead of a yellow one as a reference to his gang affiliation, blood. Blood in, blood out.\n\nAlso, if one’s team is called for a penalty, the coach can challenge the call by throwing his red flag. Weezy is saying that he won’t back down to those who are attacking him.", "annotation_id": "105077", "url": "https://genius.com/105077", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "Got a chest full of heart, no Tin Man", "vault_lines": ["Got a chest full of heart, no Tin Man"], "meaning": "Wayne actually portrayed L.Frank Baum’s Tin Man in a school rendition of The Wizard of Oz when he was 12.", "annotation_id": "97178", "url": "https://genius.com/97178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "It was all a dream, now we the Dream Team", "vault_lines": ["It was all a dream, now we the Dream Team"], "meaning": "Hiphop has gone from the “fad” it was supposed to be with people claiming it would be over in a few years like disco to now where people like Wayne are among the most successful and acclaimed artists in all of music.\nWe’ve gone from the era of “Juicy” to the era where Young Money and Lil Wayne are at the top of the charts.\nYoung Money’s succes was something Wayne dreamt about and it’s come to fruition.", "annotation_id": "97172", "url": "https://genius.com/97172", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "That’s why I’m higher than the Star Trek Enterprise", "vault_lines": ["That’s why I’m higher than the Star Trek Enterprise"], "meaning": "The flagship of Starfleet.  Star Trek: Enterprise the show, however, was supposed to serve as a prequel series for the franchise but it was met with middling reviews and lukewarm fan reaction and was canceled after only five seasons making second shortest of the live-action television series after the original.  Thus Wayne’s line works on two levels: First, he’s high as fuck and in “outer space” mentally. Secondly all the hatred has fueled his monumental success so far which has given him a longer run than the bedraggled show.", "annotation_id": "97164", "url": "https://genius.com/97164", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "I’m so sick and tired of being sick and tired", "vault_lines": ["I'm so sick and tired of being sick and tired"], "meaning": "This line comes from American voting rights activist and civil rights leader Fannie Lou Hamer. She ran for Congress in 1964 and 1965, showing people that a Black woman can run for office.\n\nIn a speech, she states, “All my life I’ve been sick and tired. Now I’m sick and tired of being sick and tired.”\n\n\n\nAnthony Hamilton’s chorus on the Nappy Roots‘ “Sick and Tired” also quotes this line.", "annotation_id": "97152", "url": "https://genius.com/97152", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "Stop playin’, I hit Drizzy with the give-and-go", "vault_lines": ["Stop playin', I hit Drizzy with the give-and-go"], "meaning": "A give-and-go is a fundamental maneuver in many team sports which involves two players passing the ball or puck back and forth. The player who has the ball or puck passes to a teammate and then repositions in order to receive a return pass and a scoring opportunity.", "annotation_id": "90183", "url": "https://genius.com/90183", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "That’s why I go hard like A.C. Slater", "vault_lines": ["That’s why I go hard like A.C. Slater"], "meaning": "A character from Saved By The Bell (an American television sitcom that aired between 1989 and 1993), played by Mario Lopez. He’s a ‘jock’, usually sporting the most up to date fashion items and greasey mullet to boot.", "annotation_id": "90178", "url": "https://genius.com/90178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "line": "And when they give ya they shoulders, never cry on ’em", "vault_lines": ["And when they give ya they shoulders, never cry on 'em"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre. It refers to:\nA shoulder shrug (meaning that if people feel “iffy” about what you do), don’t “cry” or feel negative…\nAnd to the common phrase “a shoulder to cry on”. When someone gives a person their shoulder, they’re expressing sympathy for the person.\n\nEither way, Drake is saying to stay strong and independent…", "annotation_id": "79011", "url": "https://genius.com/79011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fed Up", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-khaled-fed-up-lyrics", "genius_title": "Fed Up", "genius_id": 2687, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Feds Takin’ Pictures", "line": "Certified plat, you think I’d rather make hits? Between me and you, yeah I’d rather flip bricks", "vault_lines": ["Certified plat, you think I'd rather make hits?", "Between me and you, yeah I'd rather flip bricks"], "meaning": "While some people may be certified platinum or gold, Jeezy is saying here that he is “certified plastic”, potentially meaning that he’d rather be famous selling mixtapes or cds (made from plastic) on the street than to sell a lot of official albums. he follows this line by saying he’d “rather flip bricks” than make hits. This could mean two things: either that he’d rather sell bricks of cocaine or that he’d rather sell mixtapes (which are brick shaped as well.)", "annotation_id": "24660561", "url": "https://genius.com/24660561", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Feds Takin’ Pictures", "line": "900 for the zip, what you think I’m smoking, homie? (haha)", "vault_lines": ["900 for the zip, what you think I'm smoking, homie? (haha)"], "meaning": "A “zip” is a slang for a ounce and if you pay $900 for weed it must be a high potent strain, e.g. OG Kush etc.", "annotation_id": "1574638", "url": "https://genius.com/1574638", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Feds Takin’ Pictures", "line": "Young, rich, and famous with a pistol, you can call me Chi Ali", "vault_lines": ["Young, rich, and famous with a pistol, you can call me Chi Ali"], "meaning": "Chi Ali is a rapper who was young (just 14 years old) when he recorded his debut album The Fabulous Chi Ali. He went from rich and famous to infamous when he shot and killed his girlfriend’s brother.\n\n\n\nWeapons charges have been an issue for T.I.", "annotation_id": "1574518", "url": "https://genius.com/1574518", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Feds Takin’ Pictures", "line": "And FBI, they talk about the G I be", "vault_lines": ["and FBI, they talk about the G I be"], "meaning": "Things the Feds are doing:\n1. Taking pictures\n2. Talking about T.I.\n3. Making dinner reservations for their anniversary on Tuesday\n\n\n\nG.I.B. is also a play on words – GIB is the name of the Georgia Bureau of Investigation", "annotation_id": "1574489", "url": "https://genius.com/1574489", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Feds Takin’ Pictures", "line": "Whether you know me as T.I. or you call me T.I.P", "vault_lines": ["Whether you know me as T.I. or you call me T.I.P"], "meaning": "T.I.? T.I.P? Clifford Harris? It doesn’t matter what you call him.\n\n\n\nRG Fact TI was originally known as TIP. But to avoid lawsuits he changed his name to TI because there was already a rapper named TIP. And so what he means is that if you knew him before he became famous or after the feds have always been on him.", "annotation_id": "1574441", "url": "https://genius.com/1574441", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
