{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "I live down south, right on the last avenue", "vault_lines": ["I live down south, right on the last avenue"], "meaning": "He lives in Carol City down in Miami. It’s a very small city near the edge of Florida.\n\nFun fact: Gunplay’s rap group, Triple C’s, is named after Carol City (Carol City Cartel, three C’s.)", "annotation_id": "533391", "url": "https://genius.com/533391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "Riding in a wheels a fortune, then I made a vow", "vault_lines": ["Riding in a wheels a fortune, then I made a vow"], "meaning": "His cars cost a fortune because they’re so rare. So he swears (vows) that other rappers will never be like him or take his style.\n\nThis could also be a reference to the tv show Wheel of Fortune.", "annotation_id": "533358", "url": "https://genius.com/533358", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "I bring it straight to your door, do you like it, Manolo?", "vault_lines": ["I bring it straight to your door, do you like it, Manolo?"], "meaning": "Manolo (from the movie Scarface) was shot at his front door by Scarface for having an affair with his younger sister.\n\nRoss will do the same to you niggas!", "annotation_id": "476169", "url": "https://genius.com/476169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "You running with me, nigga, or you better run", "vault_lines": ["You running with me, nigga, or you better run"], "meaning": "Wordplay with running: either you are supporting him and his team or you better run away out of fear.", "annotation_id": "476154", "url": "https://genius.com/476154", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "I’m triple A; arrogant ass attitude", "vault_lines": ["I'm triple A; arrogant ass attitude"], "meaning": "[A]rrogant [A]ss [A]ttitude – Triple A.\nThis is also a play on his rap group Triple C’s since it also has 3 words with the same letter at the beginning, Carol City Cartel in this case.", "annotation_id": "455340", "url": "https://genius.com/455340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "When I get the gooking, only 3 note is the dial now", "vault_lines": ["When I get the gooking, only 3 note is the dial now"], "meaning": "Gookin is a term from Miami meaning when someone’s high and starts tripping hard they start acting crazy, aka gookin'. When Gunplay starts gookin' you only have to dial 3 numbers now (911) because he’s going to start killing people.", "annotation_id": "455339", "url": "https://genius.com/455339", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "Two times for you pussies ’cause you know who number one", "vault_lines": ["Two times for you pussies 'cause you know who number one"], "meaning": "Since this whole song is about Miami Heat, Gunplay is referring to Miami’s supposedly second championship against the Dallas Mavericks. Eventually, Miami didn’t win.\n\nPeep the wordplay between two/one.", "annotation_id": "421878", "url": "https://genius.com/421878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "Got birds flying around, like Mr. 23 himself", "vault_lines": ["Got birds flying around, like Mr. 23 himself"], "meaning": "This could mean two things:\n\n\nHe’s talking about his birds (drugs) flying out of the trap house the same way jordan (Mr. 23) used to ‘fly’ on the court.\nHe is referring Lebron James pre-game ritual. His coke just flying around (he sells them fast) just like LeBron’s pre-game ritual.", "annotation_id": "387490", "url": "https://genius.com/387490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "Lou-Louie Vutton kicks, they my ball sneaks 30 pair Michael Jordans what they cost me Lou-Louie Vutton kicks, the-they my ball sneaks 30-30 pair Michael Jordans what they cost me", "vault_lines": ["Lou-Louie Vutton kicks, they my ball sneaks", "30 pair Michael Jordans what they cost me", "Lou-Louie Vutton kicks, the-they my ball sneaks"], "meaning": "Louboutins are shoes that MMG refer to frequently. 30 pairs of Michael Jordans are easily $4500, so they are probably around that price.", "annotation_id": "307976", "url": "https://genius.com/307976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "My hard so hard, the cookie need a pile-drive", "vault_lines": ["My hard so hard, the cookie need a pile-drive"], "meaning": "Hard as in crack, which is shaped into a cookie shape. The size of the cookie is so big it needs a pile-driver, a mechanical device used to drive poles into soil to provide foundation support for buildings or other structures.", "annotation_id": "280898", "url": "https://genius.com/280898", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "I got cheerleaders too, and everyone a hood bitch And a whip the color the yayo, and that mothafucka foreign Whi-whi-whip the color yayo, and that mothafucka foreign", "vault_lines": ["I got cheerleaders too, and everyone a hood bitch", "And a whip the color the yayo, and that mothafucka foreign", "Whi-whi-whip the color yayo, and that mothafucka foreign"], "meaning": "Gunplay does not mean cheerleaders as in the ones you would find at your local high school, but rather that he has women who cheer for him while his fame rises in the rap game. Every one of these females come from impoverished areas around Miami, known as ‘hoods’.\n\nGunplay also drives a cocaine (white) colored foreign car. The fact that he chooses to repeat this line just enforces the seriousness of the statement.", "annotation_id": "280884", "url": "https://genius.com/280884", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "This a ten million flip, so nigga, fuck what you talk", "vault_lines": ["This a ten million flip, so nigga, fuck what you talk"], "meaning": "Due to Ricky Rozay’s rise from poverty to straight baller status, when he re-ups for his heroin industry, ten million dollars now changes hands.\nMr. Rozay is able to buy in bulk so he receives a much more economic value on his beloved drug.\nSo unless more than 10 million is changing hands at your drug deals, then shut the fuck up and let Rozay run shit.", "annotation_id": "280878", "url": "https://genius.com/280878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "This the dead end, gotta kill to fit in", "vault_lines": ["This the dead end, gotta kill to fit in"], "meaning": "Gunplay grew up in the dangerous hood where catching a stray bullet is all in a days work. Once he reached the age of eight and experienced drugs and being strapped up, he realized he would have to kill anyone who could possibly be scheming on him.", "annotation_id": "280567", "url": "https://genius.com/280567", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "With the heron, nigga I’m Lebron (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["With the heron, nigga I'm Lebron (Huh)"], "meaning": "Just like Lebron is one of the best in the NBA in Miami, Ross is the best in the business of selling Heroin. The HUH enforces the seriousness of his statement.", "annotation_id": "280546", "url": "https://genius.com/280546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "I’m posted with that china white, the smokers say it’s Yao", "vault_lines": ["I'm posted with that china white, the smokers say it's Yao"], "meaning": "China White is a slang term for the specific type of opium α-Methylfentanyl. China White can be anywhere from 10-1000 times more potent then heroin!\nSo, it’s safe to say that he has the best product in the streets, and like Rick Ross said earlier: he is also Lebron with the heroin.", "annotation_id": "277936", "url": "https://genius.com/277936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals", "line": "Quarter millie for my car, and that’s on the Quran", "vault_lines": ["Quarter millie for my car, and that's on the Quran"], "meaning": "He spent $250.000 on his car, and it’s not drug money, he mean it’s Hallal (legal money, money he made with rapping), that’s why he refers to the Quran (Muslim Religious book).", "annotation_id": "277932", "url": "https://genius.com/277932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
