{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I’m like a hundred Hannibal Lectors", "vault_lines": ["Yayo, I'm like a hundred Hannibal Lectors"], "meaning": "Hannibal Lecter is a serial killer, well known for his habit of consuming his victims\n\n\n\nIf Gunplay is like a hundred Hannibals, then he eats up his competition very quickly", "annotation_id": "3294637", "url": "https://genius.com/3294637", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I just let her blow, in a moment she gon’ be home", "vault_lines": ["I just let her blow, in a moment she gon' be home"], "meaning": "Another reference to Lance Stephenson; he lets the girl blow him. He further alludes to Lance’s and Pacers' playoff exit after being defeated by the Miami Heat.", "annotation_id": "3289467", "url": "https://genius.com/3289467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I’m just tryna get a buck, nigga Like Milwaukee,", "vault_lines": ["Stuntin' hard, I'm just tryna get a buck, nigga"], "meaning": "Wordplay on “buck”.\n\n\nBuck in the sense of money.\nThe basketball team of Milwaukee are the Bucks.", "annotation_id": "3288286", "url": "https://genius.com/3288286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Montana, but tonight I’m Tony Parker", "vault_lines": ["Montana, but tonight I'm Tony Parker"], "meaning": "Tony Parker is the playmaker of the San Antonio Spurs.\n\n\n\nThe frenchman, who won the European Championship in 2013 and got the MVP-trophy of the final game, is knwon as one of the best point guards in the NBA.", "annotation_id": "3288256", "url": "https://genius.com/3288256", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Like Ray Allen with shots, cheerleaders, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Like Ray Allen with shots, cheerleaders, bitch"], "meaning": "Tracy compares his accuracy with his gun to Ray Allen’s accuracy from beyond the three point line.\n\nRay is one of the game’s most prolific three point shooters in NBA history, and has been very clutch during his time with the Miami Heat, especially known for his clutch three point shot in Game 6 of the 2013 NBA Finals, which helped propel Miami to a repeat championship.", "annotation_id": "3288175", "url": "https://genius.com/3288175", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Team full of heat, I’m talkin’ Erik Spoelstra Yeah bitch, Erik Spoelstra and a nigga post up", "vault_lines": ["Team full of heat, I'm talkin' Erik Spoelstra", "Yeah bitch, Erik Spoelstra and a nigga post up"], "meaning": "Rick Ross often compares his Maybach Music squad to the Miami Heat, because they are both the best squads of their respective sports.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/238062847496704000\n\nTracy is piggybacking off the Heat-MMG comparison while shouting out Eric Spoelstra, the head coach of the Miami Heat.", "annotation_id": "3288148", "url": "https://genius.com/3288148", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "And you know I watch more green than like floor season tickets in Boston", "vault_lines": ["And you know I watch more green than like floor season tickets in Boston"], "meaning": "Wale plays on the fact that The Boston Celtics' uniforms are green. Of course is Wale talking about that money, but he continues the theme of NBA themed lines.", "annotation_id": "3287960", "url": "https://genius.com/3287960", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I come through in the clutch, I’m like Ray Allen at 40", "vault_lines": ["I come through in the clutch, I'm like Ray Allen at 40"], "meaning": "Rockie is comparing himself to Ray Allen as he feels he’s as clutch as Ray.\n\nEven at age 38, Ray Allen is one of the clutchest in the game, notably for hitting a clutch three pointer in Game 6 of last year’s NBA Finals which propelled Miami to a second straight NBA title.", "annotation_id": "3287772", "url": "https://genius.com/3287772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Now I seen the scenery, can’t seem to get the cigar", "vault_lines": ["Now I seen the scenery, can't seem to get the cigar"], "meaning": "This is off the phrase\n\nClose but no cigar. At carnivals you would win cigars as a prize. This also means almost but not quite.\n\nWale is just coming up in the rap game so even though he has come to a little success, he is still grinding.", "annotation_id": "3287399", "url": "https://genius.com/3287399", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "And double M, that be the best", "vault_lines": ["And double M, that be the best"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is giving a shout out to his label Maybach Music Group, as the majority of the MMG label is featured on this song.", "annotation_id": "3287365", "url": "https://genius.com/3287365", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Niggas ain’t playin’, they commentatin’ like Shaq", "vault_lines": ["Niggas ain't playin', they commentatin' like Shaq"], "meaning": "Shaquille O'Neal is one of basketballs greats. He’s won many championships and awards over his basketball career including being MVP three years in a row during the playoff finals on the LA Lakers. In 2013 Shaq retired his jersey and has gone one to do a couple other ventures. Most notably he became an commenter along with Charles Barkley, Ernie Johnson, and Kenny Smith on TNT.\n\n“Niggas ain’t playin'” refers to the people who don’t fight but just talk. They’ll just run their mouth but won’t be about the action just like a commentator is.", "annotation_id": "3287356", "url": "https://genius.com/3287356", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "All y’all niggas claim to know me well", "vault_lines": ["All y'all niggas claim to know me well"], "meaning": "People act like they are cool with Rick Ross since he is famous, but Rozay can tell the difference between his real homies and fake friends. Like Drake says in “No New Friends”:\n\nFuck all y'all niggas except my niggas\nFuck all y'all niggas except my niggas\nOne more time\nFuck all ya’ll niggas except my niggas\nFuck all ya’ll niggas, stay down from day one so I say", "annotation_id": "3287352", "url": "https://genius.com/3287352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Yeah they tell me that these ain’t the streets to floss on", "vault_lines": ["Yeah they tell me that these ain't the streets to floss on"], "meaning": "Ricky’s hood isn’t the type of place you want to floss your stuff. You will get robbed as soon as you pull out whatever you are showing off.", "annotation_id": "3287343", "url": "https://genius.com/3287343", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "So I double back for that encore", "vault_lines": ["So I double back for that encore"], "meaning": "In show business, fans who enjoy a show often call for an encore (a repeat performance), in this case the NBA finals rematch between Timmy Duncan’s Spurs and Bron’s Miami Heat is the encore.", "annotation_id": "3287299", "url": "https://genius.com/3287299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Yayo comin’ out my pores, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Yayo comin' out my pores, nigga"], "meaning": "Always the dope dealer, Ross is producing so much cocaine that he’s sweating the stuff.", "annotation_id": "3287205", "url": "https://genius.com/3287205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "She never been to Tom Ford, nigga", "vault_lines": ["She never been to Tom Ford, nigga"], "meaning": "She ain’t never been to Rodeo Drive, and she sure ain’t never been in the Tom Ford store there, where only the most luxurious clothes and accessories are sold.\n\n…cause somebody  couldn’t afford it.\n\n\n\nMaybe she pops Molly instead…?", "annotation_id": "3287201", "url": "https://genius.com/3287201", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I keep a bomb, I drop it like a compilation", "vault_lines": ["I keep a bomb, I drop it like a compilation"], "meaning": "Compilation albums are usually released when an artist really just needs the money, and isn’t too inspired to put together a whole album’s worth of material.\n\n\n\nRozay on the other hand, has a stash of solid material that he can drop whenever he likes – as carelessly as one would a compilation album.", "annotation_id": "3287196", "url": "https://genius.com/3287196", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Just know the Bulls been the shit, wait ’til D Rose back", "vault_lines": ["Just know the Bulls been the shit, wait 'til D Rose back"], "meaning": "Rockie Fresh’s hometown is chicago so repping his home team the Chicago Bulls was expected. Derrick Rose is a point gaurd for the Bulls, Before he got injured again in the 13/14 season he was averaging about 15 points. Before getting injured this season he sat out a full year in the 12/13 season due to the injury he received in the 11/12 playoffs. D. Rose returned at the start of the 13/14 season but got injured in late November.\n\nD. Rose showed great potential in his earlier years, he has slowed a bit due to his injuries but Fresh still holds hope and believes the Bulls will be stronger than ever with the return of D. Rose, then maybe go on to win a couple more championships.", "annotation_id": "3287195", "url": "https://genius.com/3287195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I put your bitch on my list, and it’s not long", "vault_lines": ["I put your bitch on my list, and it's not long"], "meaning": "Your girl has been official added to Rick Ross’s To-Do list – but no worries – she won’t be on there for long, seeing as how he seems to accomplish his goals pretty quickly.  No girl stays on the hit list for too long before having her name crossed out.", "annotation_id": "3287185", "url": "https://genius.com/3287185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "And we show off like Dolph Ziggler, let raw bitches get tossed out", "vault_lines": ["And we show off like Dolph Ziggler, let raw bitches get tossed out"], "meaning": "Wale is comparing himself to Dolph Ziggler, a WWE superstar whose gimmick revolves around his ego and tendency to show off, his mantra is “It isn’t showing off, if you can back it up”. Wale has also made it known that he is a fan of Ziggler’s in the past:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Wale/status/473821668738363392\n\nThe second half of this line is a play on words, referencing WWE’s weekly wrestling show – Monday Night Raw. Women not up to standard cannot hang around Wale, they have to go… One way or another:", "annotation_id": "3287170", "url": "https://genius.com/3287170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Like a Euro step, them niggas nearly walkin’", "vault_lines": ["But we know their set, like a Euro step, them niggas nearly walkin'"], "meaning": "A Eurostep is a move in basketball where you lean heavily on one foot and switch directions by hopping to the other one. This move originated in Europe and it’s probably about as close as you can get to travelling in the NBA without it being called (Which is also called “walking”)\n\nSo basically Wale is saying these dudes are so close to walking away from the game", "annotation_id": "3287151", "url": "https://genius.com/3287151", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I tried to let you pussy niggas eat", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Fat Trel is not only Ross' artist, but he is a huge Rick Ross fan.\n\nTherefore, it is not a surprise that he is he recycling Ross' lines from his “Box Chevy” banger.\n\nI try to let you pussy niggas eat\nIt’s time to put your pussy boys to sleep\nPussy niggas always wanna talk\nI’m busy getting pussy like a fucking boss", "annotation_id": "3287108", "url": "https://genius.com/3287108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I’m on the finals on the floor and that boy strapped 50 stacks for the seat, bring the popcorn", "vault_lines": ["50 stacks for the seat, bring the popcorn"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is known for being a loyal Heat fan, from even before Miami’s Big Three era. Ross frequently goes to Heat games, and has been spotted courtside numerous times.\n\nBy the time this song was released, courtside Heat tickets were going for $27K, but Ross is well-prepared to drop $50,000 on courtside tickets if need be.", "annotation_id": "3287099", "url": "https://genius.com/3287099", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Rich niggas don’t test drive", "vault_lines": ["Rich niggas don't test drive"], "meaning": "Before buying a car, most people will test drive it to see if it is worth purchasing. It is not easy for the average person to buy a car because of the price, so a person wants to be absolutely sure of what they’re buying.\n\nRoss is insinuating that money ain’t a thang for him, so he does not bother wasting his time testing driving a car. Even if Ross is not happy with his purchase, it doesn’t matter because it’s not as if the purchase hurt him financially.", "annotation_id": "3287087", "url": "https://genius.com/3287087", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Put all her naked photos in my laptop", "vault_lines": ["Put all her naked photos in my laptop"], "meaning": "As Ricky Rozay once detailed, he does NOT send dick pics but he will gladly takes women’s nudes!\n\nChicks send me pictures. And I appreciate it! I love all of them. But I don’t do that shit. I’m the Boss. Real niggas don’t send dick flicks.", "annotation_id": "3287079", "url": "https://genius.com/3287079", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "She wash her hair with Belaire, that pussy sweet as cake", "vault_lines": ["She wash her hair with Belaire, that pussy sweet as cake"], "meaning": "As noted on Ross' “Dope Bitch Skit”, dope bitches wash their hair with champagne as opposed to shampoo. Saucy.", "annotation_id": "3287067", "url": "https://genius.com/3287067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "2014 and them boys back", "vault_lines": ["2014 and them boys back"], "meaning": "The original version of this track was released in 2011, when Miami’s Big Three made the NBA Finals for the first time as a group.\n\nNow in 2014, this same core has lead Miami to the NBA Finals for the fourth straight year, becoming one of four NBA teams to reach the Finals for 4 straight years.", "annotation_id": "3287048", "url": "https://genius.com/3287048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Thank God for this hip-hop cause on ESPN I bombed it", "vault_lines": ["Thank God for this hip-hop cause on ESPN I bombed it"], "meaning": "Here Wale refers to how terrible he is at basketball:\n\n During the 2014 NBA All-Star festivities, Wale came in and played during the Celebrity All-Star Game… and absolutely sucked. He has been constantly ridiculed for his performance during that game ever since it aired on ESPN.\n\nSo, Wale is grateful that he was blessed with the skills to be a great rapper, because he had no chance at making it as a basketball player.", "annotation_id": "3287012", "url": "https://genius.com/3287012", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "We them niggas at the park, we just wanna ball Sellin’ dope to get a car and don’t know what it’s called Niggas foul but the referees don’t get involved It’s the finals and my dogs came to take it all", "vault_lines": ["It's the finals and my dogs came to take it all"], "meaning": "These parts are taken from the original track. Check out the annotations here!", "annotation_id": "3287010", "url": "https://genius.com/3287010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "My palms itchy, I coulda swore I just hit the lotto Safe house in Cabo, my Spanish bitch related to Blanco", "vault_lines": ["My palms itchy, I coulda swore I just hit the lotto", "Safe house in Cabo, my Spanish bitch related to Blanco"], "meaning": "According to old superstition if your right palm is itchy you will be losing money in the near future, if it is your left palm you will be receiving money. Following this line of thinking, Trel is feeling lucky by getting lucky with this woman.\n\nFat Trel is showing off exactly how much of a thug he is by explaining that he has a place to hide from police (safe house) in Cabo, Mexico. Here, he has a Spanish girl, and he is solidifying her aggressive nature by saying she is related to Blanco. This “Blanco” was Griselda Blanco one of the richest drug dealers in the world. She hailed from Columbia and was often called the “Godmother of Cocaine” – this is ironic as blanco means white in Spanish, which is a term for cocaine.\n\nhttp://imgur.com/YcSiZaQ", "annotation_id": "3286997", "url": "https://genius.com/3286997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Fuck Donald Sterling, fuck him, fuck Donald Sterling Fuck him, fuck Donald Sterling, screamin’ fuck Donald Sterling", "vault_lines": ["Fuck Donald Sterling, fuck him, fuck Donald Sterling, fuck him", "Fuck Donald Sterling, screamin' fuck Donald Sterling"], "meaning": "With an entire track centered around the NBA, who wouldn’t expect a reference to Clippers owner Donald Sterling, widely known for his racist remarks about Magic Johnson and the black community.\n\nWhile some have accepted and moved on, Gunplay has taken it as a serious hit, and expressed it in song, (he’s not alone).\n\nNote: Gunplay kept it PG compared to Snoop Dogg’s response.", "annotation_id": "3286993", "url": "https://genius.com/3286993", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "Pop champagne like I won a championship game", "vault_lines": ["Pop champagne like I won a championship game"], "meaning": "This is a re-phrasing of a line from the Birdman and Lil’ Wayne song titled “Pop Bottles”.\n\nOkay we poppin' champagne like we won a championship game\n\nTracy is also referencing his own single, “Champagne”, which was featured on his most recent mixtape, Wolf Of All Streets.\n\nhttp://imgur.com/wATzWDA", "annotation_id": "3286992", "url": "https://genius.com/3286992", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Finals 2", "line": "I keep that powder on me, nigga, like Lebron James", "vault_lines": ["I keep that powder on me, nigga, like Lebron James"], "meaning": "NBA Superstar LeBron James is famous for throwing up talcum powder prior to every game he plays. So, just like LeBron keeps the talcum powder on him to throw, Tracy T keeps cocaine powder on him at all times to sell.", "annotation_id": "3286990", "url": "https://genius.com/3286990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
