{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foolish (Remix)", "line": "When you hear that “Trilla” (Trilla, Trilla), niggas back it up (Back it up)", "vault_lines": ["When you hear that \"Trilla\" (Trilla, Trilla), niggas back it up (Back it up)"], "meaning": "A reference to Rick’s second album “Trilla”, which had recently been released", "annotation_id": "2252366", "url": "https://genius.com/2252366", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foolish (Remix)", "line": "Ayy, cross your T’s and dot your I’s (Yeah) I’m the real Bankhead, man, that’s no lie", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, cross your T's and dot your I's (Yeah)", "I'm the real Bankhead, man, that's no lie"], "meaning": "This verse was written during a feud with fellow Atlanta rapper T.I. over his roots in Lo’s hometown Bankhead. This is a shot at him, and is censored in the television version.", "annotation_id": "720940", "url": "https://genius.com/720940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
