{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "The white man call us stupid niggas We spend it all, nothing for our children", "vault_lines": ["The white man call us stupid niggas", "We spend it all, nothing for our children"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to the current state of a black man, we seem to not want to contribute towards generational wealth, we use up all the money we earn living rich and flashy forgetting about our children (The future, or the next generation)\nmajority of white people are where they are due to the wealth passed down from their forefathers. hence white people call us stupid, we get all this money but save nothing for the future. its vicious cycle throughout", "annotation_id": "7724134", "url": "https://genius.com/7724134", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Death Row, fast life", "vault_lines": ["Death Row, fast life"], "meaning": "Two meaning in this line. Death row refers to figuratively being on death row based on your decisions of how you spend money and the lack of longevity it brings. The other meaning is Death Row records which is notorious for allegedly cheating artists. Both are fast lives which will catch up with you.", "annotation_id": "7765679", "url": "https://genius.com/7765679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Pistol to your ear, this that level I’m on I apologize, woadie, but this all I got", "vault_lines": ["Pistol to your ear, this that level I'm on", "I apologize, woadie, but this all I got"], "meaning": "“Pistol to your ear” describes the intensity of his message. Equating it to a life or death situation.\n\nHe chooses to say ear instead of forehead or temple, etc., as a metaphor of firing his message from his weapon (this song) to your mind via your ear.\n\n“I apologize, woadie, but this all I got” explains how this is the only platform he can reach you to get his message across by using his weapon.", "annotation_id": "7765598", "url": "https://genius.com/7765598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Made niggas respect my hustle on both coasts", "vault_lines": ["Made niggas respect my hustle on both coasts"], "meaning": "Rick Ross made people respect his music hustle on both the east and west coast, who are known to have beef with each other. Rozay is referring to himself as a character who doesn’t care about the conflict, just the relationships and good music that comes from each coast.", "annotation_id": "7742103", "url": "https://genius.com/7742103", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "We both come from those humble beginnings Still can’t believe we never followed each other on Twitter", "vault_lines": ["We both come from those humble beginnings", "Still can't believe we never followed each other on Twitter"], "meaning": "Ross is speaking about a long time friend who he’s now doing business with. They’re pretty close, with a real life bond, but for some reason they never took bothered to connect online.\n\nThis shouldn’t come as too much of a surprise. Despite having over three million followers, Ross was only following 366 people on Twitter when his Black Dollar mixtape dropped in September 2015.", "annotation_id": "7741521", "url": "https://genius.com/7741521", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Buying belts you seen on other niggas waists", "vault_lines": ["Buying belts you seen on other niggas waists"], "meaning": "The previous bar -“Young niggas, time to act your age” – means build your knowledge. BECOME someone instead of trying to BE someone who has all the required experience under their belt (Get it?). This bar transitions from that one and tells us that he keeps seeing up-and coming rappers, businessmen and really just anyone trying to make something of themselves trying to copy successful people in any of the respective fields. Instead of going their own path, they try to copy and walk a road that isn’t theirs.", "annotation_id": "7721813", "url": "https://genius.com/7721813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Ever seen a rich nigga go broke?", "vault_lines": ["Ever seen a rich nigga go broke?"], "meaning": "Perhaps a subliminal shot at Ross' former rival, 50 Cent.\n\nIn July 2015, 50 Cent filed for bankruptcy, and admitted that his flashy lifestyle was all fake, despite that fact that 50 was once estimated to be worth upwards of $100 million.\n\nRoss poked fun at 50’s financial woes in a 2015 verse.", "annotation_id": "7721773", "url": "https://genius.com/7721773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Funny thing is the animosity money brings", "vault_lines": ["Funny thing is the animosity money brings"], "meaning": "According to motivational posters, magazine articles and other media outlets – Money is “supposed” to bring a person wealth in the form of happiness and of course money.\nHere, Rick Boss is saying that money truly makes someone more greedy, power hungry and they won’t let anyone get in the way of them making more money", "annotation_id": "7721620", "url": "https://genius.com/7721620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "You reap what you sow, and they speaking repossessions To the culture itself, these are powerful lessons", "vault_lines": ["You reap what you sow, and they speaking repossessions", "To the culture itself, these are powerful lessons"], "meaning": "Rappers & the culture of Hip Hop are known for their flamboyant lifestyle, & over the top spending which is aided by them amassing huge amounts of debts. And there comes a point when some can no longer pay their mortgages, and loan interest, and that’s when the repo man comes to collect. In the end, all that debt & bad financial planning has come to haunt you. MC Hammer is the truest example of this. Ross just feels it’s something that shouldn’t be happening again as there are so many lessons to learn from.\n\nRoss could be directing this verse to 50 Cent, who filed for bankruptcy on July 13, 2015. “You reap what you sow” eulogizes Curtis – known for polarizing many members of the hip-hop community. Ross has built a movement based on collaboration and cooperation with other artists (many of whom were also attached by 50). Thus Ross still eats. Hence the “powerful lessons” to the culture itself.", "annotation_id": "7721060", "url": "https://genius.com/7721060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "That paper it get funny when publishing is involved Mechanicals never mattered because that was your dog Now you hands-on, but things don’t ever seem right You make a call to give your lawyer the green-light He look into it then hit you up with the bad news It’s so familiar, he did the same with the last dudes", "vault_lines": ["That paper it get funny when publishing is involved", "Mechanicals never mattered because that was your dog"], "meaning": "Ross feels that publishing contracts are never in the artist’s favor. When most artists are coming up they don’t really pay attention to the details of their contracts.\n\nRoss feels that even now when he is hands on & getting his lawyers on it, it’s still the same old thing — bad news; terrible contract with little payout for him. He feels he is being ripped off.\n\nHe isn’t happy about being ripped off by these publishers & good for nothing, money grabbing lawyers, because these guys aren’t his homies. They wasn’t there when he was pushing in the gym, and these same lawyers probably did the same thing to previous clients.\n\nMechanicals refers to Mechanical Licensing which a way that artists make money from music which is different from publishing.", "annotation_id": "7720919", "url": "https://genius.com/7720919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "I never met an artist who fully recouped", "vault_lines": ["I never met an artist who fully recouped"], "meaning": "Artists usually take advances from record companies at the start of their record contracts. These advances are sometimes a endless web of debt.\n\nAs explained in the Rolling Stone article regarding the Economics of the Music Business, typical record contracts give artists 12 to 20 percent of sales assuming the artist has made enough to “recoup” the expenses for their album – otherwise, their share contributes to paying off debt to the record company.", "annotation_id": "7719586", "url": "https://genius.com/7719586", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Young niggas, time to act your wage", "vault_lines": ["Young niggas, time to act your wage"], "meaning": "A flip on the saying “act your age…”\nRoss cautions young up-and-comers to act their wage, meaning they should know their financial limitations and spend accordingly. (Which he expands upon in the following line.)", "annotation_id": "7719449", "url": "https://genius.com/7719449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Can’t be writing checks with your eyes closed While you living out of homes in different time zones", "vault_lines": ["Can't be writing checks with your eyes closed", "While you living out of homes in different time zones"], "meaning": "Eye’s closed means you’re signing a deal blindly – Not knowing everything the contract entails. You need to pay attention and keep on your toes always if you want to keep your riches, or make your own fortune.", "annotation_id": "7719426", "url": "https://genius.com/7719426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "It’s still double M still making mills", "vault_lines": ["It's still double M still making mills"], "meaning": "Double M is a reference of Maybach Music, Rick Ross' record label. Many fans have claimed that MMG has fallen off a bit, but Ross puts those claims to rest, as everyone in MMG has seen success. In the last year:\n\n\nRick Ross released his seventh studio album, Hood Billionaire, and released his eighth studio album, Black Market.\nMeek Mill released his highly anticipated sophomore album Dreams Worth More Than Money following a few delays, due to his incarceration.\nWale released his long awaited fourth studio album, The Album About Nothing.\nStalley and Gunplay both released their debut studio albums, Ohio and Living Legend, respectively.\nOmarion released his MMG debut, Sex Playlist and has begun working on its follow-up. Reasons.", "annotation_id": "7719421", "url": "https://genius.com/7719421", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "One bullet, one target, one choice You can take an L or take the shell", "vault_lines": ["One bullet, one target, one choice", "You can take an L or take the shell"], "meaning": "You have two choices when opposing Rozay:\n1) you can take the loss or “L” in this feud\n  2) you can take the [bullet] shell from his gun\n\nSimply put, you can accept the loss or he is going to kill you.", "annotation_id": "7719413", "url": "https://genius.com/7719413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "Just drove the numbers all the way back up at retail", "vault_lines": ["Just drove the numbers all the way back up at retail"], "meaning": "A continuation from the previous line about Meek’s loss from going back to prison.\n\nMeek’s sophomore effort Dreams Worth More Than Money was originally scheduled for release on September 9, 2014; but was delayed when Meek’s parole was revoked.\n\nInstead of letting MMG take an L, Ross announced his second album of the year, Hood Billionaire which released in November, in place of Meek’s missing album.", "annotation_id": "7719409", "url": "https://genius.com/7719409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "You still digging through ashtrays killing the roaches", "vault_lines": ["You still digging through ashtrays killing the roaches"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has a clever double entendre here with roaches. In marijuana culture, roaches are the very end of a blunt or joint, typically put in an ashtray after the smoke session. To kill a roach is to smoke the entire thing, whether that be by putting it in a pipe, or using tweezers to hold it so you don’t burn your fingers.\n\n\n\nTo go digging through an ashtray to smoke the roaches is generally considered a desperate way to get high. Rozay is frowning upon this desperate act.\n\nAlternatively, roaches can refer to the slang term for fake friend that asks for money and favors when you’re rich. In this way, the implication would be that the crew you run with is nasty and fake, while Ross’s crew is stacked up and ready to roll.", "annotation_id": "7719241", "url": "https://genius.com/7719241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "line": "And I never took an L back when Meek fell", "vault_lines": ["And I never took an L back when Meek fell"], "meaning": "Ross is probably alluding to Meek’s jail stint in July 2014, in which his probation was revoked. The sound of a prison cell closing can be heard in conjunction with this line, making this interpretation more plausible.\n\n\n\nAlternatively, Ross could be making a reference to Meek’s feud with Drake.\n\nIn July 2015, Ross' artist Meek Mill ignited a feud with Drake. The night that Meek initially called Drake out on Twitter, even Ross seemed to side with Drizzy, but did end up backing Meek.\n\nMany fans and companies alike chimed in on Twitter, and overwhelmingly declared Meek the loser in his feud. It seems that even Meek’s own Boss agrees with the sentiment that Meek lost against Drake.\n\nRoss affirms that even though Meek took L’s in the feud against Drake, he did not, as he mostly stayed out of the situation.", "annotation_id": "7719236", "url": "https://genius.com/7719236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Foreclosures", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-foreclosures-lyrics", "genius_title": "Foreclosures", "genius_id": 2293385, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Forever (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Mario-forever-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Forever (Remix)", "genius_id": 2493170, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "R.I.P to Mr. Shakur, this one is for you", "vault_lines": ["R.I.P to Mr. Shakur, this one is for you"], "meaning": "Second reference to Pac in this verse.\n\nWith the references to Cali and a West Coast feature in Nipsey, Rozay decorates this song as a tribute to Pac.\n\nRAP GENIUS EXPLANATION ON 106 & PARK: this verse also followed Suge Knight blasting Ross for comparing himself to Pac.", "annotation_id": "30441409", "url": "https://genius.com/30441409", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Makaveli to the max, never turn it down", "vault_lines": ["Makaveli to the max, never turn it down"], "meaning": "Makaveli was one of Tupac’s aliases.\n\n\n\nAlso a play on loud (smoke) from the previous line and music volume.", "annotation_id": "30441375", "url": "https://genius.com/30441375", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "I made a promise, give me options and I cold turk’", "vault_lines": ["I made a promise, give me options and I cold turk'"], "meaning": "Cold turkey, hardcore way to stop an addiction. Meaning Nips would drop his hurtful habits in a heartbeat should he be given a way out of the dope game, like a career in rap.", "annotation_id": "30441333", "url": "https://genius.com/30441333", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Never vocalize my visions, actions was my spokespers’", "vault_lines": ["Never vocalize my visions, actions was my spokespers'"], "meaning": "👑", "annotation_id": "26662818", "url": "https://genius.com/26662818", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "My nigga did a dime, didn’t learn a thing from it", "vault_lines": ["My nigga did a dime, didn't learn a thing from it"], "meaning": "In 1998, a good friend of Ross, Jabar Delancy served 10 years (a dime) in prison on narcotic charges. Just a year after Jabar was released from prison, he was convicted again.", "annotation_id": "15905804", "url": "https://genius.com/15905804", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Recurring dream, tryna scream but ain’t had no voice", "vault_lines": ["Recurring dream, tryna scream but ain't had no voice"], "meaning": "He is referring to sleep paralysis, a phenomenon where one is conscious during falling asleep or awakening, but unable to move or speak.\n\n\n\nThis is referred to as sleep paralysis", "annotation_id": "1140209", "url": "https://genius.com/1140209", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "From the trenches I rose, only loving the dough From the Chevy to Rolls, now it’s fur on the floor", "vault_lines": ["From the trenches I rose, only loving the dough", "From the Chevy to Rolls, now it's fur on the floor"], "meaning": "Being that he is a known sinner, Ross might spend a lot of time confessing and/or attending funerals of fallen comrades/enemies (explains the ‘rose’ reference).\nThe 2nd part alludes to the famed Biggie and Hov song “I love the Doough”.\nPart 3 explains his transition from the lower end car models to the high-end luxury vehicles.\n\n\n\n\n\nPart 4 illustrates how lavish the upholstery in his new car is. The material most people align with opulence is what Ross’s Nikes rest on while he’s driving/being driven.", "annotation_id": "963383", "url": "https://genius.com/963383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "So what they did with cocaine and a couple spoons Had the whole hood acting like goons", "vault_lines": ["So what they did with cocaine and a couple spoons", "Had the whole hood acting like goons"], "meaning": "A subtle and rather sad touch by Stalley here.  He points out the relatively innocuous nature of the tools that were used to create the crack epidemic, which had such disastrous consequences", "annotation_id": "862547", "url": "https://genius.com/862547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Staring at my Rollie bezel as I soul search", "vault_lines": ["Staring at my Rollie bezel as I soul search"], "meaning": "The bezel is the rim encompassing the lens of the watch face on his Rolex", "annotation_id": "860210", "url": "https://genius.com/860210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Claim to be balling, end up like Len Bias", "vault_lines": ["Claim to be balling, end up like Len Bias"], "meaning": "Len Bias was the 2nd overall pick to the Boston Celtics in the 1986 NBA draft. The day after he was selected, Bias died of a cocaine overdose. He never got to play in the big leagues\n\n\n\nCheck out the ESPN 30 for 30 on Len Bias, Without Bias.", "annotation_id": "859434", "url": "https://genius.com/859434", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Came home in two weeks, got him a 600", "vault_lines": ["Came home in two weeks, got him a 600"], "meaning": "The semantics of the line allows for two interpretations:\n-The 600 Benz could be a welcome home gift that Ross bought him.\n\n\n\nOR\n-The car was the result of his homey not learning from his mistakes, going back to the drug trade and grinding to earn a 600 Benz in two weeks time.", "annotation_id": "859314", "url": "https://genius.com/859314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Get a text from the boss: you know them bricks coming", "vault_lines": ["Get a text from the boss: you know them bricks coming"], "meaning": "Referring to himself as Boss, Rozay refuses to speak on the phone (for wire tapping reasons) so he texts his custies about the new shipment.\n\n\n\nAlso, since he says “you know them bricks coming”, Ross is emphasizing that if he says it, it’ll happen. You can take his word on the work.", "annotation_id": "859248", "url": "https://genius.com/859248", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fountain of Youth", "line": "Laces in my blue Chucks, represent my bros first", "vault_lines": ["Laces in my blue Chucks, represent my bros first"], "meaning": "Chucks referring to Converse Chuck Taylor brand of shoes.  He, like all of MMG, reps his family and close associates to the fullest.\n\n\n\nNipsey is also a self-proclaimed Crip, hence the color of his sneaks", "annotation_id": "859237", "url": "https://genius.com/859237", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
