{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Freaks (Remix)", "line": "“Haile Selassie I” “Haile Selassie I!”", "vault_lines": ["Biggest of the boss, say \"Haile Selassie I\""], "meaning": "Former king of Ethiopia venerated by Rastafarians as the true son of God.", "annotation_id": "1771379", "url": "https://genius.com/1771379", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Freaks (Remix)", "line": "Shout-out to Toronto where I know a couple Habeshas", "vault_lines": ["Shout-out to Toronto where I know a couple Habeshas"], "meaning": "Habesha is an ethnic group from Ethoipia or Eritrea who speak Semitic languages, and include the aforementioned Haile Selassie.", "annotation_id": "1771368", "url": "https://genius.com/1771368", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Freaks (Remix)", "line": "Showered them posse Vivian Blake", "vault_lines": ["Showered them posse Vivian Blake"], "meaning": "Vivian Blake was a Jamaican drug kingpin who founded and operated the American operations of the Jamaican Shower Posse.", "annotation_id": "1720420", "url": "https://genius.com/1720420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Freaks (Remix)", "line": "Murder for coke, rev, rev Murder for coke Murder for coke, rev, rev Murder for coke", "vault_lines": ["Murder for coke, rev, rev"], "meaning": "This song contains a sample of Murder She Wrote by Chaka Demus and Pliers and here Ricky does his own Dope Boy rendition.\nAlso “Rev” is Jamaican slang for full blast which is another way of saying the cliched “Turn Up”.", "annotation_id": "1720382", "url": "https://genius.com/1720382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Freaks (Remix)", "line": "A yah suh nice, a yah suh nice", "vault_lines": ["A yah suh nice, a yah suh nice"], "meaning": "Reference to Dancehall artist Potential Kidd’s “A Yah Suh Nice.” “Yah suh” can refer to anywhere – parties, clubs, etc.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AD_YeUXRMes", "annotation_id": "1710318", "url": "https://genius.com/1710318", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Freaks (Remix)", "line": "Talkin’ J-A, V-I, straight Trinny", "vault_lines": ["Talkin' J-A, V-I, straight Trinny"], "meaning": "Jamaica, the birthplace of Mavado, and the Virgin Islands. Both Rick Ross and Mavado have performed at both locations.\n\nHe’s bragging about taking luxury vacations to Jamaica, the United States Virgin Islands, or Trinidad; and hearing the local dialects.", "annotation_id": "1710043", "url": "https://genius.com/1710043", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
