{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "Riding with the chopper, like it’s my friend", "vault_lines": ["Riding with the chopper, like it's my friend"], "meaning": "“Chopper” is a common rap slang for an AK-47 automatic rifle. In this sense Chainz has his right in the car (Rick Ross grunt), in the passenger seat.", "annotation_id": "535830", "url": "https://genius.com/535830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "Just do it like Bo Jackson", "vault_lines": ["My girl is bow-legged, just do it like Bo Jackson"], "meaning": "Star 1980’s and 90’s multi-sport athlete Bo Jackson was involved in one of Nike’s most successful ad campaigns of all time, the famed “Bo Knows” series of ads featuring tons of celebrities including, most memorably, rock and roll legend Bo Diddley.  Nike’s age-old corporate slogan is, of course, “Just do it”.  See the first and most famous “Bo Knows” ad below:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bjpSH8qJ7c4", "annotation_id": "533239", "url": "https://genius.com/533239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "On a note, I’ma talk that jazz Jungle fever for the night, horny and white, that’s Anglo-Sax", "vault_lines": [", on a note, I'ma talk that jazz", "Jungle fever for the night, horny and white, that's Anglo-Sax"], "meaning": "Wale is gonna spit game to get in bed with a white girl\n\nJungle fever is a term used to describe a black male in an intimate relationship with a white woman. Anglo Saxons were a tribe that settled in Great Britain in the 5th century, and many Caucasians have Anglo Saxon in their blood. Wale uses the jazz saxophone (a horn instrument) to play off of “Anglo Sax”, and of course pronounces “sax” so it could easily be mistaken for a different three-letter word that starts with “s” and ends with “x”. Many vikings were Anglo Saxon and wore horned helmets, which would also account for “horny” wordplay.", "annotation_id": "532267", "url": "https://genius.com/532267", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "Corvette so clean, you’ll think Bruce Springsteen rent that", "vault_lines": ["Corvette so clean, you'll think Bruce Springsteen rent that"], "meaning": "A young Springsteen and his fresh (& so clean) whip. Look at the shine on that ‘vette! Ross has a more modern model.\n\n\n\nThis reference seems fitting since Bruce’s nickname was “The Boss” as well. .", "annotation_id": "532249", "url": "https://genius.com/532249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "I live next to Denzel", "vault_lines": ["Roll up and inhale, I live next to Denzel"], "meaning": "Ross is so rich, he lives next to esteemed (and presumably rich) actor Denzel Washington – an actor, who, like Ross, has convincingly played a gangster\n\nAs Denzel’s main residence seems to be NYC’s elite building of elite buildings 15 Central Park West, where the cheap places go for almost $6 million, and Ross appears to live in Davie, FL, this is likely an exaggeration", "annotation_id": "531786", "url": "https://genius.com/531786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "C-note after C-note,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A C-note is slang for a hundred dollar bill. Ross has a lot of these.", "annotation_id": "531782", "url": "https://genius.com/531782", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "A police siren, woop woop, nah, that’s just Diplo", "vault_lines": ["A nigga tree fire, a police siren, woop woop, nah, that's just Diplo"], "meaning": "A reference to the Diplo-produced Wale hit Slight Work which featured a unique array of police sirens in the beat", "annotation_id": "531720", "url": "https://genius.com/531720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "Smoke that Mark McGwire strong, Oakland A no basic smoke", "vault_lines": ["Smoke that Mark McGwire strong, Oakland A no basic smoke"], "meaning": "The West Coast is known to have the best, or strongest weed– much as former Oakland A’s ball player Mark McGwire was one of the strongest players in the game (steroids can do that for ya…..)\n\n\n\nThis isn’t the first time Wale has name-dropped McGwire in a song", "annotation_id": "531714", "url": "https://genius.com/531714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "Ironic since my drive increased, my driver see the profit", "vault_lines": ["Ironic since my drive increased, my driver see the profit"], "meaning": "As Wale’s drive, or Ambition increased, so did his bankroll. Naturally, as he gets more money, the more money he has to spend on things like his chauffeur.\n\nThis is ironic because the more drive (ambition) Wale has gained, the less he actually drives, but still gets paid more", "annotation_id": "531709", "url": "https://genius.com/531709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "Riding five deep and I’m as dirty as them congressmen", "vault_lines": ["Riding five deep and I'm as dirty as them congressmen"], "meaning": "A reference to the oh-so-appropriately-named congressman Anthony Wiener, made infamous through a scandal involving him sending nude pictures of himself to at least six girls.\n\n\n\nWale isn’t talking politics when he says this, he’s talking about riding dirty in the UGK sense, meaning with illegal contraband. .", "annotation_id": "531701", "url": "https://genius.com/531701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "line": "Thought I wouldn’t make it, now I’m winning, Timothy Tebow", "vault_lines": ["Thought I wouldn't make it, now I'm winning, Timothy Tebow"], "meaning": "Many people thought that Tim Tebow wouldn’t make it in the NFL, especially after he was demoted to Denver’s 3rd string QB. He was moved to 1st string and has led the Broncos to many astonishing wins.\n\n\n\nIronically, Tebow has quickly fallen off and has since been cut by the Denver Broncos, New York Jets, and New England Patriots.", "annotation_id": "531647", "url": "https://genius.com/531647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Em", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-fuck-em-lyrics", "genius_title": "Fuck Em", "genius_id": 63016, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up Some Commas (Remix)", "line": "I’m a empire her to my empire, big as Empire, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm a empire her to my empire, big as Empire, nigga"], "meaning": "To make something an Empire makes Big Sean the Emperor. Often rappers refer to the Roman Empire which was ruled by Julius Ceasar. He then completes this reference in the next line.\n\n\n\nSide note, Empire is an American drama television series which debuted on Fox on January 7, 2015. It centers on a hip hop music and entertainment company, Empire Entertainment, and the drama among the members of the founders' family as they fight for control of the company.", "annotation_id": "6586711", "url": "https://genius.com/6586711", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up Some Commas (Remix)", "line": "I don’t bop, I do the money dance, nah, I call it that Robert Kraft", "vault_lines": ["I don't bop, I do the money dance, nah, I call it that Robert Kraft"], "meaning": "Robert Kraft is the owner of the New England Patriots. When his team won the Super Bowl, Kraft joined the fun by dancing with Rick Ross, who was also present.\nhttps://youtu.be/pNfaA9C1qAo?t=56s\n\nThe first part of the line is recycled from his verse on Jay-Z’s Fuckwithmeyouknowigotit", "annotation_id": "6586289", "url": "https://genius.com/6586289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up Some Commas (Remix)", "line": "I was born in ’88, but I been ready since ’87", "vault_lines": ["I was born in '88, but I been ready since '87"], "meaning": "This line can be taken two ways:\n\n\nSean was born in March 1988, so he was conceived in 1987. He could be stating he has been ready for the fame since the moment he was ever conceived.\nIt’s also possible that, since he’s so ready, he’s one step ahead of everything, even his own birth.\n\n\n\nThe line itself is a reference to a similar one by Lil Wayne on his Dedication 2 cut Spitter:\n\nI’ve been ready since ‘81 and I was born in '82", "annotation_id": "6582806", "url": "https://genius.com/6582806", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up Some Commas (Remix)", "line": "Yeah, just know I’m livin’ single on some young Khadejah shit", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, just know I'm livin' single on some young Khadejah shit"], "meaning": "Big Sean recently ended his high-profile relationship with singer and collaborator Ariana Grande, so now he’s back living the single life.\n\nHe makes this clear while referencing the sitcom ‘Living Single’, which starred Queen Latifah as Khadejah, the woman looking for a man.", "annotation_id": "6582525", "url": "https://genius.com/6582525", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up Some Commas (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-fuck-up-some-commas-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Fuck Up Some Commas (Remix)", "genius_id": 1914390, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up the Club", "line": "Got on my Vacheron, Belair, my bottles come", "vault_lines": ["Got on my Vacheron, Belair, my bottles come"], "meaning": "Rozay is name-dropping two of his favourite, expensive brands.\n\nFirstly, he mentions Vacheron, an expensive watch manufacturer he adores so much, he titled his 2013 mixtape Vacheron Don after the brand.\n\nSecondly, he also refers to Belaire, an expensive champagne manufacturer, which Rick Ross has previously endorsed and is often credited with propelling the sparkling rosé to fame.\n\n\n\nPictured: Rick Ross pictured holding a Belaire bottle.", "annotation_id": "10210843", "url": "https://genius.com/10210843", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up the Club", "line": "Yeah! This that ’63 AMG Ghost music It’s that Ace of Spade, girl – and it’s toast music Nigga, let’s toast to it DJ Khaled!", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, let's toast to it"], "meaning": "Two cars are mentioned here, the Rolls Royce Ghost, and a Mercedes Benz 63 AMG badged vehicle, likely an S63. Both are opulent, expensive vehicles.  Both makers have been featured on Future’s Instagram.\n\nAce of Spades is the nickname of Armand de Brignac Champagne, a brand endorsed by Jay Z. Bottles cost around $300 a piece.", "annotation_id": "10206753", "url": "https://genius.com/10206753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up the Club", "line": "Bello’s at Wimbledon, hell of a gentleman", "vault_lines": ["Bello's at Wimbledon, hell of a gentleman"], "meaning": "Bello Cigars are made by Don Bello in Little Havana, a Cuban neighborhood in Miami. Ross was spotted with owner Dan Bello in 2016.\n\nWimbledon is the oldest tennis tournament in the world but also regarded as the most elite and prestigious. One of the events is the gentleman’s singles and doubles tournament.", "annotation_id": "10172479", "url": "https://genius.com/10172479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up the Club", "line": "We just gon’ fuck up the club, baby, fuck up the club, baby We just gon’ fuck up the club, baby, fuck up the club, baby We just gon’ fuck up the club, baby, fuck up the club, baby And you better bring your whole crew We just gon’ fuck up the club, baby, fuck up the club, baby We just gon’ fuck up the club, baby, fuck up the club, baby We just gon’ fuck up the club, baby, fuck up the club, baby Yes, any time you want to", "vault_lines": ["And you better bring your whole crew", "Yes, any time you want to"], "meaning": "The hook is similar to “Fuck Up Some Commas.” Future has a number of strip club anthems including “Magic” “Plastic Bag” & “100it Racks.”\n\nFuture is such a fan of frequenting strip clubs and throwing some racks that he was featured in a GQ strip club documentary.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-RfRclWgIOg", "annotation_id": "10166784", "url": "https://genius.com/10166784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up the Club", "line": "West Coast, that’s my shit, 4Hunnid, that’s my clique", "vault_lines": ["West Coast, that's my shit, 4Hunnid, that's my clique"], "meaning": "YG represents the West Coast & Tree Top Piru gang and his block 400 Spruce St. in Compton.\nYG’s brand called 4hunnid also being named after his block", "annotation_id": "10166706", "url": "https://genius.com/10166706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up the Club", "line": "A nigga still sellin’ weight Still tippin’ them scales, I’m Ross, fit in the Wraith", "vault_lines": ["Still tippin' them scales, I'm Ross, fit in the Wraith"], "meaning": "A reference to Ross' inherited drug dealing past, and his weight loss, which stands at around 100 pounds. The money from dealing, and his shrinking waistline allow, him to fit in the new Rolls Royce Wraith.\n\n\n\nDespite his weight loss, he’s still heavy in the game, and still pushing “drugs” (music) on his fans, hence “tipping scales.”", "annotation_id": "10165293", "url": "https://genius.com/10165293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Fuck Up the Club", "line": "I be tearin’ clubs up like Three 6 I be tearin’ plugs up, that’s that street shit", "vault_lines": ["I be tearin' clubs up like Three 6", "I be tearin' plugs up, that's that street shit"], "meaning": "Gotti makes a reference to  the song “Tear Da Club Up” by fellow Memphis rappers Three 6 Mafia to express how wild the club gets when he appears. This song actually got the group banned across several venues in the country, because it reportedly started fan riots.\n\nAdditionally Gotti not only causes mayhem in the club, but also in the streets, when he robs plugs/drug suppliers off their money.", "annotation_id": "10165119", "url": "https://genius.com/10165119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
