{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GOD IS REAL", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Kanye-west-god-is-real-lyrics", "genius_title": "GOD IS REAL", "genius_id": 13695946, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Guess what? I just made a porno in the booth", "vault_lines": ["Guess what? I just made a porno in the booth"], "meaning": "On December 2019’s hit, “BEST ON EARTH,” Russ also mentioned filming sexual content:\n\nShe know I got cameras, she say, “We should vlog it”\n\nThen again, in “3AM” with Ty Dolla $ign, Russ suggested recording similar acts:\n\nI like a freak, type to ask, “When we droppin' the porn?” (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "20967938", "url": "https://genius.com/20967938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "My throwaways are hits for you, one day I might be merciful", "vault_lines": ["My throwaways are hits for you, one day I might be merciful"], "meaning": "Russ' “throwaways” are his songs he keeps and stores on his computer, occasionally previewing and teasing them on Instagram Lives—even dropping songs.  Russ alludes he’ll be merciful to his fans and release the songs, which he stated doing so in an Instagram Live:\n\nI'ma drop [all the throwaways] at some point, on my computer. These songs need to go. I got too much heat.\n\nRuss even gave his opinion on the idea of releasing a throwaway album in the same Instagram Live:\n\nThe only problem with [releasing a throwaway album] is the context of dropping a project and labeling it as “throwaways,” ‘cause I feel like people’ll listen to it less excited. But, it’s interesting, it’s a way for me to just get rid of shit.\n\nInterestingly, Russ' 2019 hit, “BEST ON EARTH” was a throwaway project—which was soon released after his part-time producer convinced him to do so:\n\nI learned to stop overthinking shit when Best On Earth blew up. That song was a throwaway sittin on my computer. I liked it but I didn’t love it enough to even consider dropping it. Boi1da called me and convinced me to drop and then boom lol", "annotation_id": "20640967", "url": "https://genius.com/20640967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "McLaren’s a convertible, my Porsche’s name is Percival", "vault_lines": ["McLaren's a convertible, my Porsche's name is Percival"], "meaning": "McLaren and Porsche are both automobile manufacturers, both ranging up to $300k—roughly a quarter of a million.\n\nOn July 3rd, 2020, Russ took to Twitter to show off the names of his vehicles—in which, he named one “Percival.”\nhttps://twitter.com/russdiemon/status/1279231833671184385\n\nRuss standing in front of his opulent cars — middle car is “Percival.”", "annotation_id": "20640789", "url": "https://genius.com/20640789", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Parents’ marriage crumbled, so I told my mama pack it up", "vault_lines": ["Parents' marriage crumbled, so I told my mama pack it up"], "meaning": "Russ makes it clear his parents' marriage wasn’t great or ideal and shares another sentiment on his 2018 track, “Parkstone Drive”:\n\nYeah, my parents' marriage in shambles, I won’t lie, it hurts\nI thought money would fix it, but it just made it get worse\nSee my dad was the man, ‘til his job cut ties\nHe went broke, I got rich, that shit fucked with his pride\nYeah, I recognize it was disturbing to see\nThe family stopped turnin’ to him and started turnin' to me\nGoing through it, I know he tried to hide the pain\n\nInterestingly, “September 16” is a dedicated track from Russ to his parents, detailing the perspectives of his parents during their complicated marriage.", "annotation_id": "20494319", "url": "https://genius.com/20494319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Eatin’ ’til I’m fat enough, rise again like Lazarus", "vault_lines": ["Eatin' 'til I'm fat enough, rise again like Lazarus"], "meaning": "In the New Testament of the Bible, Lazarus—a close friend to Jesus Christ,  brother of Martha and Mary Magdalene, and child of Cyrus and Eucharis—died from the severe illness of leprosy. Soon after his passing, Jesus went to his tomb miraculously resurrecting him from the dead—hence “rise again.”\n\nAs recorded in the chapter of John 11, Jesus performed the supernatural miracle:\n\n41 So they took away the stone. Then Jesus looked up and said, “Father, I thank you that you have heard me. 42 I knew that you always hear me, but I said this for the benefit of the people standing here, that they may believe that you sent me.” 43 When he had said this, Jesus called in a loud voice, “Lazarus, come out!”", "annotation_id": "20463611", "url": "https://genius.com/20463611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Guess what? I just put my logo in my pool", "vault_lines": ["Guess what? I just put my logo in my pool"], "meaning": "Captioned “Live your raps,” Russ took to Twitter shortly after “GUESS WHAT”’s release on February 8, 2020, to announce that his backyard pool had his logo engraved in the bottom of it:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/russdiemon/status/1226185177149444101?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw", "annotation_id": "19015376", "url": "https://genius.com/19015376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Ooh, this pussy’s good as fuck, it’s temptin’ not to wrap it up", "vault_lines": ["Ooh, this pussy's good as fuck, it's temptin' not to wrap it up"], "meaning": "Here, Russ makes a double entendre with “wrap it up,” which means to wear a condom. As well as “wrap it up” means to finish something quickly.\n\nThe pussy is so good that he doesn’t want to wear protection, while he also doesn’t want the sexual intercourse to end.", "annotation_id": "18982887", "url": "https://genius.com/18982887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Heavy chest, when Nipsey didn’t Make it through, give me a minute, damn", "vault_lines": ["Make it through, give me a minute, damn"], "meaning": "Russ reflects on the event of Nipsey Hussles passing.\n\nNipsey was a huge inspiration to Russ, and Russ constantly stated that. Russ was deeply affected by the loss and even got a tattoo of Nipsey on his arm posthumously to honor him.\n\nIn his song Outlaw he raps\n“I never listen to the churches.\nI listen to Kanye, Eminem, Nipsey, J Cole, Kendrick, Drake and Jay Z verses.”", "annotation_id": "18976107", "url": "https://genius.com/18976107", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Maybach Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group is a record label imprint of Atlantic Records, founded by Rick Ross himself.\n\nThe tagline is voiced by Australian Model Jessica Gomes and is heard on Rick Ross' songs, alongside artists such as Meek Mill and Wale, who are also signed to record label.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4vOExWDh9KQ", "annotation_id": "18950873", "url": "https://genius.com/18950873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "Money every Friday, indie catalog, I’m versatile", "vault_lines": ["Money every Friday, indie catalog, I'm versatile"], "meaning": "Throughout his career in his interviews, Russ has discussed his use of TuneCore – a digital music distribution site for independent artists.\n\nPrior to partnering with Columbia Records in 2016, Russ had released 11 mixtapes independently – as well as hundreds of singles via TuneCore, between 2011 and 2014.\n\nSpeaking at a 2018 Forbes Under 30 event in Boston, Russ discussed his experience with TuneCore:\n\nSo I’ve been doing that (TuneCore) since 2011, and even since being signed to the label, every Friday I still get payed for my independent catalogue. So whilst most artists have to sit around and wait for the label to cut them the check..I’m out here getting mailbox money every Friday.", "annotation_id": "18946325", "url": "https://genius.com/18946325", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "GUESS WHAT", "line": "I want roses when I’m livin’, not just roses when I die", "vault_lines": ["I want roses when I'm livin', not just roses when I die"], "meaning": "While celebrities often receive outpourings of affection when they die, Russ would prefer to be loved while he can still enjoy it. Russ stresses this statement again on his 2019 song, “RENT FREE”:\n\nYeah, y'all ain’t showin' love until I die\nSo I don’t want it anyway then, goodbye\n\nThen again, he has another lyric resembling a similar meaning, in his song “Some Time”:\n\nBut I’m gonna try ‘til the casket closes\nUntil they give me my roses\n\nAnother possible reference comes from Rick Ross‘ 2019 hit, “Gold Roses,” where the same idea is expressed in the chorus:\n\nBefore I’m gone outta this place, yeah\nPut some flowers in my vase, won’t you?\nLet me know that I did okay, yeah\nDon’t wait ‘til some other day, no, no\nThey love to wait 'til it’s too late, it’s too late", "annotation_id": "18945948", "url": "https://genius.com/18945948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
