{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "Bitch you bad and I know it, in your Honda Accord You gon’ be strippin,’ sellin’ pussy ’til you make it to the Forbes", "vault_lines": ["Bitch you bad and I know it, in your Honda Accord", "You gon' be strippin,' sellin' pussy 'til you make it to the Forbes"], "meaning": "This is one of the realist lines in Self Made 3.\n\n\n\nGotti comes at this girls LIFE – she is in a VERY grey 2006 Honda Accord, loving these rap dudes for shoes, bags, and a photo till she rich forever like them. Right.", "annotation_id": "3073154", "url": "https://genius.com/3073154", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "Them monkey niggas some Care Bears", "vault_lines": ["Them monkey niggas some Care Bears"], "meaning": "Some rappers look like they act wild when in fact they really sweet like the Care Bears. The Care Bears are bears that shoot love out of their chest who have a special mission to help people share their feelings.\n\nThis episode of their tv series could be a metaphor for Gunplay’s battle with tear gas and real molly that look like real glass:", "annotation_id": "2799638", "url": "https://genius.com/2799638", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "Arrivederci", "vault_lines": ["Plus that Beamer dot ya, arrivederci"], "meaning": "Arrivederci is Italian for “goodbye”:\n\n\n\nHow to pronounce Ariva-derche in American:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4aXIFFaWNjM", "annotation_id": "2788859", "url": "https://genius.com/2788859", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "Try fuckin with me and my shit? Nah, that’s that Vietnam shit", "vault_lines": ["Try fuckin with me and my shit? Nah, that's that Vietnam shit"], "meaning": "The Vietnam War was a war that pit North Vietnam against South Vietnam and the United States, lasting from 1956-1975.\n\nAs the war progressed, many Americans became anti-Vietnam War due to its length and high casualties as well as the US involvement in various massacres such as My Lai. The United States withdrew from the war in 1973, therefore losing the conflict.\n\n\n\nGunplay’s saying that if you fuck with him, you’ll end up losing.", "annotation_id": "2657179", "url": "https://genius.com/2657179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "Don’t call it your house until you paid it off", "vault_lines": ["Don't call it your house until you paid it off"], "meaning": "Ricky Rosay is reffering to the rap game. There are alot of rappers who claim they run the rap game or in other words, “own” it, but Ross is saying you can’t claim shit until you’ve paid your dues.\n\nThis actually could be taken as a small jab at Kendrick Lamar’s “Control” verse, in which he says:\n\n“I heard the barbershops be in great debates all the time\nBout who’s the best MC? Kendrick, Jigga and Nas\nEminem, Andre 3000, the rest of y'all\nNew niggas just new niggas, don’t get involved”\n\nKendrick has only been “mainstream” since the release of “Swimming Pools (Drank)”, which dropped on July 31, 2012, so it could be considered a big deal for him to claim the top spot, when he has only been in the game for a year and some change.", "annotation_id": "2274643", "url": "https://genius.com/2274643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "May run for state attorney just to free my dawgs", "vault_lines": ["May run for state attorney just to free my dawgs"], "meaning": "As a state attorney, you can choose who to prosecute and choose to make sentences lighter on individuals. Interestingly though, Florida does not have a state attorneys office, so maybe he will run for District Attorney of Dade County?", "annotation_id": "2240673", "url": "https://genius.com/2240673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "I pay up four a mouth just like a round of golf I try to stay in shape, I’m standing counting ones", "vault_lines": ["I pay up four a mouth just like a round of golf", "I try to stay in shape, I'm standing counting ones"], "meaning": "A play on the golf term “hole-in-one”.\n\nHe is comparing buying blowjobs (mouth) like playing a round of golf – and he stays in good shape, he always get his “hole in one” – if you know what that means? ;)", "annotation_id": "2204547", "url": "https://genius.com/2204547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "I got me a ki, I’m out’chea", "vault_lines": ["Fuck that BMI shit, I got me a ki, I'm out'chea"], "meaning": "Gunplay is out trapping, selling coke in the streets.\nA ki (key) is a kilo of coke and “outchea” is slang for “out here”, meaning he is in the streets.\n\nA reference to Ace Hood & Lil Wayne’s “We Outchea”.", "annotation_id": "2204502", "url": "https://genius.com/2204502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "Pimpin’ on them Cleopatras", "vault_lines": ["Body count, real caskets, pimpin' on them Cleopatras"], "meaning": "Gunplay is making them girls.\nRick Ross has previously called his girl Cleopatra.\n\nUsually the pimp preys on vunerable women, but Gunplay is on a whole notehr lever with the shit and pimps the girls who are in positions of power like Cleopatra did Egypt.", "annotation_id": "2204491", "url": "https://genius.com/2204491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "line": "Doors going up, hoes going HAM Doors going up, hoes going HAM", "vault_lines": ["Doors going up, hoes going HAM"], "meaning": "Lamborghini cars often got scissor doors, what Kanye would call suicide doors, and when these doors go up, the girls go crazy – HAM Hard As a Motherfucker…\n\nThat’s what Tyga would call an automatic bang", "annotation_id": "2204484", "url": "https://genius.com/2204484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gallardo", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gunplay-gallardo-lyrics", "genius_title": "Gallardo", "genius_id": 213370, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Ain’t Based On Sympathy", "line": "Showed us Tony Montana, teachers couldn’t care less A young prince in Miami,", "vault_lines": ["Showed us Tony Montana, teachers couldn't care less", "A young prince in Miami,"], "meaning": "Scarface was filmed and set in Miami.\n\nRoss can relate as a Miami native. Tony Montana had to make due with the little chances he had as an immigrant and Ross feels he faced similar predicaments AND in the same city.", "annotation_id": "30808494", "url": "https://genius.com/30808494", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Ain’t Based On Sympathy", "line": "This is deeper than raps", "vault_lines": ["This is deeper than raps"], "meaning": "Name drop of his 3rd studio album, Deeper Than Rap.", "annotation_id": "30561825", "url": "https://genius.com/30561825", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Ain’t Based On Sympathy", "line": "Reminiscing on that, uh I remember they used to give us that free cheese A big block of that shit, hehe Yo, hehe, man I’m glad y’all ain’t gotta get that cheese Man, I thank God my kids ain’t gotta see that cheese, yo (M-M-M-M-Maybach Music) You know what I’m saying? You gotta feed it to them raw, feel me?", "vault_lines": ["You know what I’m saying?", "You gotta feed it to them raw, feel me?"], "meaning": "Ross is remembering his experience with the Temporary Emergency Food Assistance program aka “Government Cheese Program”. The program distributed processed cheese to welfare, food stamp and social security recipients in the United States.\n\nHip hop rags to riches stories often visit this hood trope as a means to authenticate the “struggle” that rappers experienced as youths prior to their success.\n\nRoss is thankful to God that he is financially stable and in a position that doesn’t require the assistance of such programs. Thus his children will never that particular experience in common with him.", "annotation_id": "11547487", "url": "https://genius.com/11547487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Ain’t Based On Sympathy", "line": "Niggas shoot for the Magic, never heard of Mutumbo", "vault_lines": ["Niggas shoot for the Magic, never heard of Mutumbo"], "meaning": "Mutumbo was a Center in the NBA who was a notorious shot blocker. He’s using “shoot for the Magic” (The Orlando NBA Franchise) as a metaphor for young men aiming for goals without even knowing about the pitfalls and obstacles that await.", "annotation_id": "11589367", "url": "https://genius.com/11589367", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Ain’t Based On Sympathy", "line": "Uh, gang violence ongoin’, let’s fight our own wars Chicago been out of hand, the city lost its soul Funeral every weekend or either you cremated Homie’s son, he been murdered, he didn’t seem faded", "vault_lines": ["Chicago been out of hand, the city lost its soul", "Funeral every weekend or either you cremated", "Homie's son, he been murdered, he didn't seem faded"], "meaning": "Ross is taking a swipe at America’s interventionist tendencies by using Chicago as an example of one of the many “war zones” or areas that could use more attention or resources from the government versus fighting in foreign lands.\n\nHe adds, that Chicago in particular has gotten so bad that the residents are becoming numb to all of the funerals that result of the violence that currently plagues the city.", "annotation_id": "11555206", "url": "https://genius.com/11555206", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Ain’t Based On Sympathy", "line": "Holdin’ guns on the ’Gram, out of my league baby Real killers and hitters would rather live nameless I got a homie I know with a twenty body count Maybe only once or twice a month he leave the house Older brother, type to get a curly perm Pappy Mason type, respect for holdin’ thirty birds", "vault_lines": ["Holdin' guns on the 'Gram, out of my league baby", "Real killers and hitters would rather live nameless", "I got a homie I know with a twenty body count", "Maybe only once or twice a month he leave the house", "Older brother, type to get a curly perm", "Pappy Mason type, respect for holdin' thirty birds"], "meaning": "Ross doesn’t understand the desires of some people to pose with weapons on social media. Specifically Instagram in this line.\n\n\n\nHe continues to assert that true hit men would rather not receive publicity for their deeds. He gives an anecdote about one such older gentlmen with an out of fashion hairstyle who is rarely see outside of his home. He likens this OG to the legendary drug trafficker and Supreme Team top Lieutenant Howard “Pappy” Mason from Queens NYC.", "annotation_id": "11555111", "url": "https://genius.com/11555111", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Ain’t Based On Sympathy", "line": "If it was her, she had to kiss my feet and lick my ass", "vault_lines": ["If it was her, she had to kiss my feet and lick my ass"], "meaning": "He has no respect for Stacy Dash as a person. She is known for her coonery such as her opinions on the BLM movement and her brief stint on FOX News. The black delegation will not accept her", "annotation_id": "11525767", "url": "https://genius.com/11525767", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
