{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Over", "line": "They want to take a nigga chain ain’t they?", "vault_lines": ["They want to take a nigga chain ain't they?"], "meaning": "Could be referencing 50 Cent as he was seen with Gunplay’s MMG Chain in the video to his hit single ‘Major Distribution’", "annotation_id": "3175453", "url": "https://genius.com/3175453", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Over", "line": "M’s, Double M’s I’m entitled to a hundred M’s", "vault_lines": ["M's, Double M's I'm entitled to a hundred M's"], "meaning": "Fat Trel is part of Maybach Music Group (double M’s), and like every other member he is about to make millions from the rap game so he is entitled with 100 millions.", "annotation_id": "2792932", "url": "https://genius.com/2792932", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Over", "line": "Niggas at me like I’m 2Pac at a Vegas lobby", "vault_lines": ["Niggas at me like I'm 2Pac at a Vegas lobby"], "meaning": "On September 7, 1996, 2Pac and Suge Knight left a boxing match they had attended that was hosted in Las Vegas at the MGM Grand hotel. One of Knight’s associates saw a Crip named Orlando Anderson in the hotel lobby. Anderson robbed a Death Row affiliate earlier that year so after Knight told Pac that Anderson was there, Pac and his entourage attacked Anderson.\n\nLater that night after Pac and Suge left to head to a club, a car pulled up at a light and opened fire on their vehicle, killing Pac.\n\nFootage of the MGM lobby brawl:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lMyMyYfd9Gc\n\nThis line has two possible meanings:\n\n\nRick Ross is making the point that he isn’t scared to confront people in the same sense Pac wasn’t scared to confront Anderson.\nAlternatively, it could be interpreted that Ross is saying that “niggas at him” like they were at 2Pac, both Pac and Ross had haters wanting to see their downfall.\n\n\n\nRicky Rozay actually fought with Jeezy at the BET Awards in 2012. Starting backstage, it eventually spilled out into the parking lot. Gunshots were fired, but not by an affiliate of either rapper.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BUuqbFww_sM", "annotation_id": "2704857", "url": "https://genius.com/2704857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Over", "line": "Fuck the state penn, I’m fuckin’ hoes at Penn State", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the state penn, I'm fuckin' hoes at Penn State"], "meaning": "Wordplay\n\nPenn State is a university in Pennsylvania.\n\nRicky Rozay says fuck going to jail–he’d rather FUCK BITCHES.\n\n\n\nRick Ross also referenced Penn State in “Maybach Music IV”:\n\nNiggas get abused like boys at Penn State\n\nMMG also stopped to perform at Penn State’s Bryce Jordan Center last year:", "annotation_id": "2704829", "url": "https://genius.com/2704829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Game Over", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Young-breed-game-over-lyrics", "genius_title": "Game Over", "genius_id": 345907, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gang Related", "line": "I sold fake dope in my own complex", "vault_lines": ["I sold fake dope in my own complex"], "meaning": "This is a diss to me, I think (pretty sure— or a “Back handed complement)??– for being– to Rick’s judgement some how- not \"authentic”, as if somehow we were peddling “fake dope” (fake heroin, or cocaine, etc.) out of the Marc Ecko Enterprises building that Complex operated inside of in 2009.\n\nIn 2008-2009, Ross had beef with 50.\n\nHonestly I don’t know all the details– and really was unaware of this at that time. But one of the shots fired by Rick was a diss that somehow G-Unit & my then partnership with 50 cent was the reason for problems in my business in 2008-09.\n\nThe rise and subsequent constriction of G-Unit clothing definetly created pain in my business during those years– but in no way did that alone result in our businesses down turn. The banking industries implosion– and the company having massive debt from all the retail store growth that we deficit funded– was the root to our pain.  So contrary to the conjecture, 50 didn’t fuck it up…we did.\n\nWe (the executive team) made our own mess.  Despite all of the random internet rumors— none of the business’s I have ever operated have went bankrupt.  I am proud of that fact– and having survived a shit storm by landing a burning plane in 2009.\n\nLater in 2009 (after this 50 beef) Rick actually came through “the Complex” and gave me a pound. Which was cool because his man also dapped me with a fat purple bud in a amber plastic bottle.\n\nIn May of 2011 he was featured on the cover of Complex magazine– with Andy Samberg.", "annotation_id": "2197378", "url": "https://genius.com/2197378", "state": "verified", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gang Related", "line": "I’m so Complex", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick is referring to Complex Media…the Magazine and network of sites I am the founder of.  Complex actually was goingto be called “climate”, and the first issue was a mini-DVD that used to be a hang tag on my Ecko Unlimited clothing line.\n\nInternet sort of made the mini-dvd rom thing irrelevant. So we went DOT.COM.", "annotation_id": "2197309", "url": "https://genius.com/2197309", "state": "verified", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gang Related", "line": "I’m Marc Ecko", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "No actually, I am.  But I am hyped as fucked that ROSS acknowledged this OG.", "annotation_id": "2197307", "url": "https://genius.com/2197307", "state": "verified", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
