{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "Ex-slave, proud field nigga", "vault_lines": ["Ex-slave, proud field nigga"], "meaning": "Ross plays off the house vs field slave motif – and as is common in his style – flips the motif upon itself by embracing the role of the field slave. He’s in the field, and he’s embracing the hustle & hard work it took to get there.", "annotation_id": "7922631", "url": "https://genius.com/7922631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "Get up on my level you say you a boss Everybody seen it we know that you’re soft (Boss) Heard you went and got a lawyer, you niggas is lost (Is lost)", "vault_lines": ["Get up on my level you say you a boss", "Everybody seen it we know that you're soft (Boss)", "Heard you went and got a lawyer, you niggas is lost (Is lost)"], "meaning": "These lines seem to be Rick Ross making fun of 50 Cent’s recent files for bankruptcy after being sued by Rick Ross' baby mother. Fifty has been to court several times since then in attempts to fight the case, while reviving the feud between him and Ross. https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/style-blog/wp/2015/07/14/behind-the-scenes-of-50-cent-vs-rick-ross-how-a-lucrative-rap-beef-may-end-up-costing-fiddy/", "annotation_id": "7874808", "url": "https://genius.com/7874808", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "My family mean the world although I’m never there (Weird)", "vault_lines": ["My family mean the world although I'm never there (Weird)"], "meaning": "Although he doesn’t get to spend as much time with his family as he likes, he loves them dearly.\n\nThis line also sets up the one that follows it. One observing from the outside would expect him to spend more time with his family if they meant the world to him – hence, “these days, nothing makes sense.”", "annotation_id": "7823946", "url": "https://genius.com/7823946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "Geechi Liberace,", "vault_lines": ["True G, Geechi Liberace (Uh)"], "meaning": "Basically a black version of Librace.\n\nGeechi: a favorite slang term of the MMG crew, is a person of Gullah origin. The Gullahs are black people living in the Lowcountry region of Georgia and South Carolina, who have preserved their links to Africa arguably more than any other African-American group.", "annotation_id": "7816184", "url": "https://genius.com/7816184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "Holy Ghost reading through the book of Job (Lord)", "vault_lines": ["Holy Ghost reading through the book of Job (Lord)"], "meaning": "Holy Ghost as in riding in Rolls Royce. Reading the chapter of Job in the bible. In this chapter Job God directly allows Satan to attack Job. Job’s friends give him bad advice and lead him astray. In the end God restores Job and BLESSED him with 2x as much as he started out with. Rick Ross feels that in his current situation he can relate to Job. Growing up in Mississippi, Ross knows the bible.", "annotation_id": "7816176", "url": "https://genius.com/7816176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "I once made love to a princess For security reasons let’s call her Empress (Haha)", "vault_lines": ["I once made love to a princess", "For security reasons let's call her Empress (Haha)"], "meaning": "Ross claims to have had relations with royalty, but for public reasons chooses to keep her name concealed and use something that rhymes instead.", "annotation_id": "7816154", "url": "https://genius.com/7816154", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "No cracks for the Task Force", "vault_lines": ["Glass slippers, no cracks for the Task Force"], "meaning": "References another “Freeway Ricky Ross” fact, that Freeway Ricky Ross a notorious crack dealer in the 80’s had a task force dedicated to catching him in LA.", "annotation_id": "7816130", "url": "https://genius.com/7816130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Geechi Liberace", "line": "Out in L.A. Freeway Ricky Ross (Racks) Testified on over 40 dudes (What?) I seen the documents, I’m who he wanna sue (Woo) He testifies for a state allowance (Bank) Then does a blog like your favorite coward (Fuck)", "vault_lines": ["Out in L.A. Freeway Ricky Ross (Racks)", "Testified on over 40 dudes (What?)", "I seen the documents, I'm who he wanna sue (Woo)", "He testifies for a state allowance (Bank)", "Then does a blog like your favorite coward (Fuck)"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the pending law suit between Rick Ross (rapper) and Freeway Ricky Ross the renowned drug trafficker.  Rapper Ross is saying that due the pending lawsuit, he has privy information that Freeway Ricky Ross is a snitch and a federal informant.", "annotation_id": "7742815", "url": "https://genius.com/7742815", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
