{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go Mode", "line": "My young niggas, they on go mode shit I know the shooters, they on go mode shit", "vault_lines": ["My young niggas, they on go mode shit", "I know the shooters, they on go mode shit"], "meaning": "Ace Hood’s songs like,  “100 Foreva” and “Buss Guns” show great insight on his shooters and what they will do if there is conflict.", "annotation_id": "10053254", "url": "https://genius.com/10053254", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go Mode", "line": "I told you niggas I’m in beast mode, shit", "vault_lines": ["I told you niggas I'm in beast mode, shit"], "meaning": "I’m in beast mode, I’m talking Marshawn, talkin Ronda Rousey, nigga Lebron James\n\nAce Hood’s work flow is coined as “beast mode,” this ethic consists of dedication, hard work and passion. Ace implies he is a beast in the rap game because his rap skills are exemplary from others. Also, he is a beast in the gym as well.\n\nhttps://instagram.com/p/BG42sDWlywn/", "annotation_id": "10053237", "url": "https://genius.com/10053237", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go Mode", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Ace-hood-go-mode-lyrics", "genius_title": "Go Mode", "genius_id": 2814566, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go To Hell", "line": "The Don Shula", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Don Shula (Donald Francis Shula) was a legend of American football and one of the most successful coaches in NFL history. He is best known as the head coach of the Miami Dolphins, with whom he won two Super Bowls.", "annotation_id": "37723850", "url": "https://genius.com/37723850", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go To Hell", "line": "Uh", "vault_lines": ["All the real niggas clique up, let's get rich tonight, uh"], "meaning": "Meek Mill puts his own spin on Rick Ross' signature grunt.", "annotation_id": "30044511", "url": "https://genius.com/30044511", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go To Hell", "line": "I’m doin’ anything I want, I’m havin’ lunch with Tom Brady Talkin’ ’bout his girl problems, I can’t lie, I related", "vault_lines": ["I'm doin' anything I want, I'm havin' lunch with Tom Brady", "Talkin' 'bout his girl problems, I can't lie, I related"], "meaning": "Despite being considered by many as the greatest player in NFL history, Tom Brady has faced some challenges in his romantic life. He dated actress Bridget Moynahan for three years before they split in December 2006 — the same month Brady began dating Brazilian supermodel Gisele Bündchen.\n\nTwo months into Brady and Bündchen’s relationship, Brady found out Moynahan was pregnant with his first son, Jack, who was born August 22, 2007. Brady and Bündchen were married on February 26, 2009 after being engaged for one month. The pair welcomed son Benjamin on December 8, 2009 and daughter Vivian on December 5, 2012 before they finalized their divorce in October 2022 after thirteen years of marriage.\n\nAround the time of the song’s release, rumors of Brady’s possible relationship with Russian model Irina Shayk were circulating, although TMZ claimed their relationship had “fizzled out.”\n\nThough never married, Meek Mill’s dating life could certainly also be considered tumultuous. He has three children and has been romantically involved with at least five women, most notably dating Nicki Minaj between 2015 and 2017.\n\nBrady and Meek Mill were spotted together in early October 2023 at a Casino Night event hosted by JAY-Z. Given both their histories, it is certainly possible that “girl problems” would have been a topic of conversation.\n\nMeek Mill and Brady pictured at JAY-Z’s charity Casino Night", "annotation_id": "30038113", "url": "https://genius.com/30038113", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go To Hell", "line": "These are the things I can do without, come on I’m talking to you, come on", "vault_lines": ["I'm talking to you, come on"], "meaning": "The vocal samples were taken from Tears for Fears‘ number one hit “Shout,” the first track on their 1985 album Songs from the Big Chair.\n\n“Shout” has been sampled across a multitude of genres, and appears in at least seventy different songs according to WhoSampled.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ye7FKc1JQe4", "annotation_id": "30038076", "url": "https://genius.com/30038076", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go To Hell", "line": "Laugh now, cry later", "vault_lines": ["Laugh now, cry later"], "meaning": "This clip led fans to believe that. Drake would be featured on the album. Meek Mill references the title of a Drake song released in 2020. In a clip, Meek Mill expressed his strong support for Drake, suggesting that Drake would be featured on his new album. However, upon listening to the album, Drake is not actually featured on any track. The reference to the title of Drake’s song can be seen as a shoutout, highlighting the significance of acknowledging someone’s music on your own album.\n\nhttps://youtube.com/clip/UgkxH2eIu8Yd32Fn3nzH2UQflGbPrjXvBuND?si=8o-nCW9HT540B9y4", "annotation_id": "30036380", "url": "https://genius.com/30036380", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go To Hell", "line": "Rich nigga, name in Wikipedia (Boss)", "vault_lines": ["Rich nigga, name in Wikipedia (Boss)"], "meaning": "All the rich and famous personalities of our planet have a page on Wikipedia which traces their lives and their careers.\n\nRick Ross who is a famous and rich rapper also has one.\n\nThis is what he is trying to say through this passage.", "annotation_id": "30033412", "url": "https://genius.com/30033412", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Go To Hell", "line": "Now we ride double M’s through the whole city (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Now we ride double M's through the whole city (Huh)"], "meaning": "They ridin' Mercedes-MayBach through the city.", "annotation_id": "30033335", "url": "https://genius.com/30033335", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
