{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Alpinas", "line": "Your body like a eighty-eighty I said your body like a eighty-eighty", "vault_lines": ["Your body like a eighty-eighty", "I said your body like a eighty-eighty"], "meaning": "Dom is referring to the 1988 Ford Mustang. The fox body style is popular on the west coast. Dom owns one that he raps about in “5.0 | Conversations” and can be seen below:\n\nhttp://instagram.com/p/MkCMuTg5_b/\n\nThe girl’s body is sleek and sexy like the appearance of his Mustang. .\n\nDom could also be referring to the actual shape of the number 88, as it has curves like the girl’s body. .", "annotation_id": "869256", "url": "https://genius.com/869256", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Alpinas", "line": "And these Chucks is so fucking geechi", "vault_lines": ["And these Chucks is so fucking geechi"], "meaning": "“Geechi” is a term popularized by the rap group Camp Lo.\n\nSimply put, it means “cool”.", "annotation_id": "867417", "url": "https://genius.com/867417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Alpinas", "line": "I rub it like a fucking genie I said I rub it like a fucking genie", "vault_lines": ["I rub it like a fucking genie", "I said I rub it like a fucking genie"], "meaning": "ACCEPTED COMMENT: The first Time he says it is because he relates him rubbing “clitoris” to a genie in a lamp. The second time he says it and laughs is because he relates a genie and “genitalia”.", "annotation_id": "867410", "url": "https://genius.com/867410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Alpinas", "line": "Girl I know you’re ready for it But I’mma make you beg me for it You want me, I already know it She tell me I can fill that void", "vault_lines": ["You want me, I already know it", "She tell me I can fill that void"], "meaning": "The girl wants to have sex with Dom, but Dom is making her wait. She is quite desperate for it at this point.", "annotation_id": "867399", "url": "https://genius.com/867399", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Alpinas", "line": "Chromed out Bimmers Gold Alpinas Chromed out Bimmers Chromed out Bimmers, chromed out Bimmers", "vault_lines": ["Chromed out Bimmers, chromed out Bimmers"], "meaning": "Alpina BMWs are made by a separate manufacturer that works with BMW. Their vehicles come with a unique set of rims (which is what Dom is referring to) that don’t come on standard Bimmers. .", "annotation_id": "864314", "url": "https://genius.com/864314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Alpinas", "line": "You know we run this rap game I couldn’t run a lap on the track mane Run the rap game like a trap mane Fat nigga, fast money, just the facts mane Run the rap game like a trap mane Fat nigga, fast money, just the facts", "vault_lines": ["You know we run this rap game", "I couldn't run a lap on the track mane", "Run the rap game like a trap mane", "Fat nigga, fast money, just the facts mane", "Fat nigga, fast money, just the facts"], "meaning": "Ross knows he’s pretty fat and out of shape, but it’s okay because he still “runs” the rap game. His money does the running for him. .\n\nIf someone were to run the trap, they would be making a lot of money from drug sales in that area. The rap industry is Ross' trap, and music is the drug he pushes. .", "annotation_id": "864303", "url": "https://genius.com/864303", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Alpinas", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dom-kennedy-gold-alpinas-lyrics", "genius_title": "Gold Alpinas", "genius_id": 78780, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Medals", "line": "You got the Richard Millie with the flooded dial", "vault_lines": ["You got the Richard Millie with the flooded dial"], "meaning": "In this line Ross is refers to the RM 27-04 Manual Winding Tourbillon Rafael Nadal that marks the 10th anniversary of the partnership between 14-time French Open winner Rafael Nadal and Richard Mille. The “floating dial” is the Cable-Suspension Mechanism inspired by the process used to string a tennis racket and designed to stay in suspension within its case.", "annotation_id": "30102188", "url": "https://genius.com/30102188", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Medals", "line": "R.I.P. to Juice WRLD, he had the world to see (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["R.I.P. to Juice WRLD, he had the world to see (Woo)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross pays homage to the late rapper Juice WRLD who passed on the 8th of December, 2019.\n\nJuice’s private jet was alerted to authorities on the ground after they were informed by the pilot flying the jet that Juice’s entourage had guns on them, when Juice landed the police were waiting for him. It was reported that in an attempt to hide pills from the police, Juice swallowed them which lead to an accidental overdose causing Juice to suffer a seizure and pass away. Many people debate on whether this report is true or false but in the documentary Juice WRLD: Into the Abyss, which was released in 2021, Juice is shown developing a severe drug addiction leading up to him overdosing on the day he passed away.", "annotation_id": "30044798", "url": "https://genius.com/30044798", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Medals", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-meek-mill-and-jeremih-gold-medals-lyrics", "genius_title": "Gold Medals", "genius_id": 9712628, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "“I gotta get the most of everything” is the axis on which it sit and twirls", "vault_lines": ["\"I gotta get the most of everything\" is the axis on which it sit and twirls"], "meaning": "The axis is the center that something spins around.\nHe’s saying his entire ambition is built around one core belief: “I have to get the most out of life.”\nThat means making the most money, having the biggest success, and not settling for less.", "annotation_id": "40874394", "url": "https://genius.com/40874394", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Lot of lives lost, but I never panicked Lot of lines crossed, I never did a Xanny", "vault_lines": ["Lot of lives lost, but I never panicked", "Lot of lines crossed, I never did a Xanny"], "meaning": "Ross remains calm during during a period of conflict, where death occurs regularly. This may allude to his childhood in Carol City, a poverty-stricken neighborhood in California.\n\nThe second bar is a double entendre with Ross comparing figurative “lines ” being crossed, as in someone escalating a situation , with “lines” of cocaine.\n\n This leads to his assertion of never doing a “Xanny”, a shortened term used to describe Xanax (alprazolam), a drug often used to relieve anxiety.", "annotation_id": "38336485", "url": "https://genius.com/38336485", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "‘Cause they’ll get to poppin’ out of place like they double jointed", "vault_lines": ["'Cause they'll get to poppin' out of place like they double jointed"], "meaning": "People that are double jointed experience bones popping out irregularly.", "annotation_id": "29608371", "url": "https://genius.com/29608371", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "And what I got for sale just sit on the scale Triple beam dream", "vault_lines": ["And what I got for sale just sit on the scale"], "meaning": "Ross has a song featuring Nas called Triple Beam Dreams, which is basically about growing up dreaming of being a rich drug dealer, when in reality Ross made those dreams come true but through a different method.", "annotation_id": "24054753", "url": "https://genius.com/24054753", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Paid the cost to be the boss wasn’t even my most expensive purchase", "vault_lines": ["Paid the cost to be the boss wasn't even my most expensive purchase"], "meaning": "A popular phrase.\n“Pay the cost to be the boss.” – Meaning that you have to sacrifice time, likeness and anything potential to be the leading figure in your own niche.\nDrake is claiming that although he is the boss, everything sacrificed for becoming his own boss doesn’t match whatever he’s spent in real life (or even the biggest sacrifice he made.)", "annotation_id": "20828400", "url": "https://genius.com/20828400", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "(Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group (abbreviated as MMG) is an American record label founded in 2009 by Rick Ross. A number of solo albums and three compilation albums have been released under the label.", "annotation_id": "18512522", "url": "https://genius.com/18512522", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Before I’m gone outta this place, yeah Put some flowers in my vase, won’t you? Let me know that I did okay, yeah Don’t wait ’til some other day, no, no They love to wait ’til it’s too late, it’s too late", "vault_lines": ["Before I'm gone outta this place, yeah", "Put some flowers in my vase, won't you?", "Let me know that I did okay, yeah", "Don't wait 'til some other day, no, no", "They love to wait 'til it's too late, it's too late"], "meaning": "Speaking to Megan Ryte on Hot 97, Ross gave an explanation for the “Gold Roses” song title, saying:\n\nMe and him (Drake) were just conversating, and you know – Nipsey came up in our conversation, and we were just saying.. I wish he had an idea of the impact that he had and made on these streets, I pray he just had an idea.\n\nThis then led the conversation to a point where Drake stated:\n\nMan, I hope I can smell my flowers whilst I’m here.\n\nWhat Drake means by this is that whilst he’s still alive, he wants his fans and supporters to give him his dues and respects for the work he has put in before it’s too late.", "annotation_id": "17722069", "url": "https://genius.com/17722069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Fly you out to Cannes, ménages with bitches", "vault_lines": ["Fly you out to Cannes, ménages with bitches"], "meaning": "Ross is known to take vacation in Cannes, France. He mentioned it before on his August 2012 track, “Diced Pineapples,” which is another collaboration with Drake:\n\nI'ma trip go to Cannes, France to catch a flick\n\nThe word “ménage” is short for the French word “Ménage à Trois,” which is three people having sex together.", "annotation_id": "17705247", "url": "https://genius.com/17705247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Ten years in and y’all yet to hear my most impressive verses", "vault_lines": ["Ten years in and y'all yet to hear my most impressive verses"], "meaning": "While Drake released his first mixtape, Room for Improvement, well over a decade ago in 2006, it was 2009’s So Far Gone that put Drake on the Hip-Hop radar and well into mainstream success.\n\nDespite having 4 Grammy awards, having eight songs reach septuple platinum or better, and being the highest-certified digital singles artist ever in the US, Drizzy still believes his best is yet to come.", "annotation_id": "17703579", "url": "https://genius.com/17703579", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Still a part of shorty even if we’ve been livin’ apart", "vault_lines": ["Still a part of shorty even if we've been livin' apart"], "meaning": "The “shorty” in this line may be Drake’s son, Adonis Graham, who was born on October 11th, 2017, which is also the same month as Drake’s birthday. Adonis lives in France with his mom, Sophie Brussaux.", "annotation_id": "17690650", "url": "https://genius.com/17690650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Tales about me are like corridos in Culiacán", "vault_lines": ["Tales about me are like corridos in Culiacán"], "meaning": "The Corrido is a Mexican musical genre developed in the 18th century, whose origins date back to the Spanish middle ages. One of its most popular subgenres is the Narcocorrido, songs that focus on drug smugglers, the lyrics refer to particular events and include real dates and places and also tend to speak approvingly of illegal activities, mainly drug trafficking. While Culiacán is the capital of the Mexican state, Sinaloa and is also one of the places where this genre is most heard and produced.\n\nDrake is likely comparing his legacy to notorious drug lords like, Joaquín Guzmán Loera, AKA El Chapo, Miguel Ángel Félix Gallardo or Rafael Caro Quintero, and the stories told of their legacies.", "annotation_id": "17690047", "url": "https://genius.com/17690047", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "A hundred room mansion but I felt abandoned", "vault_lines": ["A hundred room mansion but I felt abandoned"], "meaning": "In January 2014, Ross bought a 109 room mansion in Georgia from former heavyweight boxing champion, Evander Holyfield for $5.8 million.", "annotation_id": "17684539", "url": "https://genius.com/17684539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Coming to America, really the set I’ll let your soul glow, I’m keepin’ you wet", "vault_lines": ["Coming to America, really the set", "I'll let your soul glow, I'm keepin' you wet"], "meaning": "Soul Glo is a fictional hair product from the 1988 movie, Coming to America. The product is applied to hair, particularly Jheri curl, in order to keep it shiny and moisturized.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o4AiHmhJGzw", "annotation_id": "17679787", "url": "https://genius.com/17679787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "She got a thing for Chanel vintage that dropped before she could speak English", "vault_lines": ["She got a thing for Chanel vintage that dropped before she could speak English"], "meaning": "Chanel is a high fashion house founded by Coco Chanel in 1909 in Paris, France.\n\n\n\nDrake seems to imply that his romantic interest prefers Chanel accessories that were released before she was born.", "annotation_id": "17677669", "url": "https://genius.com/17677669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Postcard from Grace Bay, sendin’ my distant regards", "vault_lines": ["Postcard from Grace Bay, sendin' my distant regards"], "meaning": "Grace Bay is a beach in Turks and Caicos. It has won countless awards for being the World’s best beach and accommodation destination.", "annotation_id": "17676551", "url": "https://genius.com/17676551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "I’m all for spiritual liftin’, but I don’t fly Spirit", "vault_lines": ["I'm all for spiritual liftin', but I don't fly Spirit"], "meaning": "Spirit Airlines has consistently been ranked amongst the worst airline carriers in the world, primarily due to it charging for carry-on baggage, frequent cancellations and minimal leg room. In 2017, Spirit was named “the worst airline in America” by Consumeraffairs.com.\n\nIn May 2019, Drake was gifted a Boeing 767 plane from Canadian airline Cargojet, which is estimated to be worth around $200 million. That same month, Drake gave a tour of his plane.", "annotation_id": "17675696", "url": "https://genius.com/17675696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "I know they love to rock a check, but who gon’ do it really? Really?", "vault_lines": ["I know they love to rock a check, but who gon' do it really? Really?"], "meaning": "The Nike logo, called the “swoosh,” resembles a checkmark symbol, and one of their slogans is “Just Do It.”\n\nDrake has been signed to Nike’s Jordan Brand since December 2013, and has released six official collaboration sneakers.", "annotation_id": "17674753", "url": "https://genius.com/17674753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "The one that’s rebuildin’ schools and feedin’ the homeless", "vault_lines": ["The one that's rebuildin' schools and feedin' the homeless"], "meaning": "In the January 2018 music video for “God’s Plan”, Drake uses the $1 million budget in Miami to pay people’s college tuition, or buy them clothes or groceries. Drake’s philanthropy also extends to his hometown of Toronto, where he partnered with the Raptors and donated $1 million to Welcome Toronto, a basketball, fashion and arts initiative.", "annotation_id": "17674392", "url": "https://genius.com/17674392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Roxx’ll do you filthy for me soon as I give him the nod Meanin’ he’ll blast for me like puttin’ the 6 with the God", "vault_lines": ["Roxx'll do you filthy for me soon as I give him the nod", "Meanin' he'll blast for me like puttin' the 6 with the God"], "meaning": "Johnny Roxx is a member of Drake’s crew and his personal trainer. Driz shouted him out before on September 2015’s “Change Locations”:\n\nRoxx got a case but they get off again\n\nAccording to Roxx, he and Drake have been friends for over 10 years.\n\n\n\nDrake pronounces ‘blast for me’ similar to blasphemy. He follows-up with his popular 6God nickname, which was birthed around the time he released his February 2015 album, If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late.", "annotation_id": "17674136", "url": "https://genius.com/17674136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Hop on a float to show the city the one they appointed", "vault_lines": ["Hop on a float to show the city the one they appointed"], "meaning": "Drake celebrated the Toronto Raptors' 2019 NBA championship by riding around the city on the team’s parade float. He also dropped two songs to commemorate the win, including ”Money in the Grave” featuring Rick Ross and Omertà.", "annotation_id": "17674119", "url": "https://genius.com/17674119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Sashimi from Saito, you know that man two Michelin Star", "vault_lines": ["Sashimi from Saito, you know that man two Michelin Star"], "meaning": "Masaki Saito is the founder, owner and lead executive chef at Sushi Masaki Saito. He relocated his restaurant to Toronto from New York in February 2019. Sashimi is usually a thinly sliced, raw fish.\n\nDrake has a history of rapping about his taste for luxury food and restaurants. For example, on March 2013’s “5AM in Toronto” he says:\n\nEatin' like I’m seated at Swish, Sotto, and Joso’s\n\nMichelin Stars are a mark of quality awarded to a restaurant, or individual chefs, by anonymous reviewers. According to trip savvy, a two rating means:\n\nA restaurant worth a detour, indicating excellent cuisine and skillfully and carefully crafted dishes of outstanding quality\n\nInterestingly, there is a chef named Takashi Saito, who is the head chef at Sushi Saito in Tokyo, which is ranked number 26 of the 50 best restaurants in Asia, and holds a Michelin rating of 3.", "annotation_id": "17674002", "url": "https://genius.com/17674002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Mentally I’m already on next year, that’s some 20/20 clear vision", "vault_lines": ["Mentally I'm already on next year, that's some 20/20 clear vision"], "meaning": "“20/20 vision” or ‘normal vision,’ is a term used in ophthalmology, where a person can see clearly up to 20 feet away.\n\n\n\nAdditionally, since “Gold Roses” dropped in 2019, Drake’s making a slick play on next year being 2020. It highlights how Drizzy’s always plotting his next move and future success, a mindset that’s played a major role in keeping him at the top.", "annotation_id": "17673990", "url": "https://genius.com/17673990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Chanel in the mail, FedEx from Pharrell", "vault_lines": ["Chanel in the mail, FedEx from Pharrell"], "meaning": "In March 2019, Pharrell Williams collaborated with Chanel and released his iteration of Chanel glasses, sweatshirts, t-shirts, hoodies and tote bags. Some of the pieces can be seen in a GQ interview, and he also posted a snippet of the collection to his Instagram.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BvUXUIdBqxz/?utm_source=ig_embed", "annotation_id": "17673951", "url": "https://genius.com/17673951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "I was nominated, never won a Grammy", "vault_lines": ["I was nominated, never won a Grammy"], "meaning": "As of this song’s release, Ross has been nominated for four Grammys:\n\n\nDJ Khaled’s “I’m On One” — Best Rap Collaboration (2012)\n\nGod Forgives, I Don’t — Best Rap Album (2013)\nChris Brown’s “New Flame” — Best R&B Song (2015)\n\n“Purple Lamborghini” — Best Song Written for Visual Media (2017)\n\n\n\nDrake, on the other hand, has been nominated a total of 42 times. The 6 God has won 4 awards, with his most recent being January 2018’s “God’s Plan.”\n\nOn November 20th, ‘Gold Roses’ itself was nominated for a Grammy.", "annotation_id": "17673946", "url": "https://genius.com/17673946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "All smiles, Kevin Durant trials Had to blow it on the court, I must have blew a milli’ I’m walkin’ on all charges, that’s my new Achilles", "vault_lines": ["Had to blow it on the court, I must have blew a milli'", "I'm walkin' on all charges, that's my new Achilles"], "meaning": "Drake uses wordplay to compare his legal court battles to Kevin Durant’s “trials” and tribulations on the basketball court. The former Golden State Warriors forward ruptured his right Achilles’ tendon during Game 5 of the 2019 NBA Finals. Drake attended the game courtside and was seen consoling KD as he walked off the court from the injury.\n\n\n\nDrake may also be playing on the Greek hero, Achilles, who was virtually invincible until an arrow struck his achilles heel.\n\nDrake has battled numerous court cases, from his July 2011 case where Ericka Lee claimed she was not compensated for helping write June 2011’s “Marvin’s Room,” to a 2017 case where Layla Lace falsely accused him of raping and impregnating her. Drake acknowledges the uphill challenge facing Durant, who is currently recovering from surgery and aiming to make a strong return back to the NBA.", "annotation_id": "17673930", "url": "https://genius.com/17673930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Tanenbaum know the logo on the jersey, it’s gettin’ purchased", "vault_lines": ["Tanenbaum know the logo on the jersey, it's gettin' purchased"], "meaning": "Drake intends to purchase the sponsorship rights to the NBA’s Toronto Raptors jerseys when the team’s current deal with Sun Life Financial is over. He also gives a shout out to Raptors co-owner Larry Tanenbaum.\n\nDrake and October’s Very Own won the logo spot on the Raptors training jerseys during the team’s 2019 championship season:", "annotation_id": "17673910", "url": "https://genius.com/17673910", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Vision wasn’t mine, told my niggas the vision was ours", "vault_lines": ["Vision wasn't mine, told my niggas the vision was ours"], "meaning": "Drake has chosen to work closely with his DJ, Future The Prince, and his childhood friend, manager, and producer, Oliver El-Khatib. Together, they run the October’s Very Own clothing line and label and have established lucrative deals with Nike’s Jordan Brand, the Toronto Raptors, Apple Music, and in July 2019, Sirius Radio.\n\nDrake mentions both Future and Oliver on June 2018’s ”Nonstop”:\n\nFuture took the business and ran it for me\nI let Ollie take the owl, told him brand it for me\n\n\n\nThis could also be a play on Canadian R&B duo dvsn (pronounced “division”), who signed to OVO in February 2016.", "annotation_id": "17673801", "url": "https://genius.com/17673801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Point blank period, like a City Girl and then I bring it back to 50 world", "vault_lines": ["Point blank period, like a City Girl and then I bring it back to 50 world"], "meaning": "“Point blank period” is a popular phrase used to signify the end of an argument. Incidentally, the term “Periodt” developed into a meme when rap group, City Girls, whose vocals are featured on Drake’s June 2018 track, “In My Feelings,” dropped their debut mixtape Period in May 2018, which included a track of the same name. The first usage of “Periodt” on Twitter dates back to May 2009.\n\n50 is Drake’s friend “Fif,” whose real name is Anthony Soares—he was shot to death in September 2017. Drake plans to take his money to 50 in the afterlife, perhaps by being buried with it, as the title of his June 2019 track with Rick Ross, “Money In The Grave,” suggests.", "annotation_id": "17673769", "url": "https://genius.com/17673769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
