{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Got Me Crazy", "line": "Rosetta", "vault_lines": ["Money talks, niggas need Rosetta"], "meaning": "Rosetta Stone is a computer software used to learn languages.\n\nThe software gets it’s name and logo from an ancient stone slab on which the Decree of Memphis was inscribed in three writing systems. It was instrumental in deciphering Egyptian hieroglyphs for the first time.\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosetta_Stone_(software)", "annotation_id": "11685851", "url": "https://genius.com/11685851", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Got Me Crazy", "line": "Wingstop", "vault_lines": ["in the drive-thru (Wingstop"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is the owner of over 20 Wingstop chains. He frequently raps about his franchise ownership and his love for lemon pepper wings.\n\nSee:\n\n\nWingstop owner, lemon pepper aroma― Rick Ross – BLK & WHT", "annotation_id": "11685844", "url": "https://genius.com/11685844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
