{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Down", "line": "She be in my double R and I’m just runnin round", "vault_lines": ["She be in my double R and I'm just runnin round"], "meaning": "Double R refers to the two R’s on the logo of the luxury British car manufacturer Rolls-Royce. Ross himself owns a Rolls-Royce Wraith.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BLSA1dbjtPH/?taken-by=richforever", "annotation_id": "11414542", "url": "https://genius.com/11414542", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Down", "line": "Post lil homie bond, now watch him do the Shmurda dance", "vault_lines": ["Post lil homie bond, now watch him do the Shmurda dance"], "meaning": "Rapper Bobby Shmurda’s “shmoney dance”  featured in the video for his song “Hot Nigga,” became a sensation in 2014. It’s appropriate to Rick’s lyric because the shmoney dance made the obscure Bobby Shmurda a star and got him paid; conversely, Rick’s friends who get money, do the dance.", "annotation_id": "9131328", "url": "https://genius.com/9131328", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Down", "line": "He usually do the redbone, tonight he want a brown", "vault_lines": ["He usually do the redbone, tonight he want a brown"], "meaning": "The term “Redbone,” considered by some to be a slur, has been used as a general term for a multi-racial person, but also specifically refers to a Louisiana ethnic group, perhaps of white, black and Native American origins,  who dwell in the southern states, especially Louisiana. With this lyric, Remy asserts that her lover prefers her dark skin to the (probably) lighter skin of a multi-racial woman; while he has a “thing” for  light-skinned women he finds Remy’s brown complexion admirable as well.", "annotation_id": "8953964", "url": "https://genius.com/8953964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Down", "line": "Fuck with Shaka Zulu in dem in Zimbabwe", "vault_lines": ["Fuck with Shaka Zulu in dem in Zimbabwe"], "meaning": "In the 19th century, Shaka Zulu was a military leader for the Zulu tribe in Southern Africa, and thanks to his conquests, ruled over much of the lands that now form parts of South Africa, Swazliland and Zimbabwe . He is considered one of the greatest military leaders of all time. Rick would have to bring his A game to compete on that level with Shaka Zulu.", "annotation_id": "8392822", "url": "https://genius.com/8392822", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Down", "line": "Doors up, doors down When I’m in the club, bitch, it’s going down Shorty thick as fuck, hands down Hands up, pants down Down, down, shorty fucking head down I see my phone blowing up, I know it’s going down Once I busted at the rapper, then it hit the town Chiefin’ numbers in the city, boy, it going down", "vault_lines": ["Hands up, pants down", "Down, down, shorty fucking head down", "I see my phone blowing up, I know it’s going down", "Once I busted at the rapper, then it hit the town", "Chiefin' numbers in the city, boy, it going down"], "meaning": "Gotti used the same lyrics in his 2013 song King Shit ft T.I.", "annotation_id": "8389417", "url": "https://genius.com/8389417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Down", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Remy-ma-hands-down-lyrics", "genius_title": "Hands Down", "genius_id": 2390346, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "A-A-Ain’t going no where like horses in a stable Bitch I’m in the mansion, flossing, clickin’ cable", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I'm in the mansion, flossing, clickin' cable"], "meaning": "In this section of bars, Nicki is alluding to one’s career being stagnant by comparing their progress to the liking of a horse in its stable.", "annotation_id": "29141468", "url": "https://genius.com/29141468", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Uhn, you my son, no daddy you a bastard", "vault_lines": ["Uhn, you my son, no daddy you a bastard"], "meaning": "Nicki is referring to female rappers trying to be her while dissing her at the same time. She refers to them as her sons,and Nicki influenced them alone, no man included, so they are fatherless.", "annotation_id": "25023093", "url": "https://genius.com/25023093", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "I jack a nigga queen, I don’t play cards", "vault_lines": ["I jack a nigga queen, I don't play cards"], "meaning": "I jack (the lowest face card/jerking) a nigga queen (dame card/someone’s girl)", "annotation_id": "23799997", "url": "https://genius.com/23799997", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Rozay! (M-M-Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Famous Rick Ross ad-libs! Ross’s nickname is Ricky Rozay, and he makes reference to it all the time in his songs/guest appearances.\n\nThe “M-M-Maybach Music” thing is a staple of Rick Ross’s record label, Maybach Music Group. It’s customary that this ad-lib makes it on almost every song featuring an MMG artist… And I mean almost EVERY SONG!", "annotation_id": "2189970", "url": "https://genius.com/2189970", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Bullet-proofin’ the truck (hah)", "vault_lines": ["Blocka they better duck, bullet-proofin' the truck (hah)"], "meaning": "Probably a reference to how his car got shot at in Miami in January of 2013. He now feels the need to bullet proof his vehicles to avoid being shot.", "annotation_id": "2149024", "url": "https://genius.com/2149024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Tatted like a Navajo,", "vault_lines": ["Tatted like a Navajo,"], "meaning": "The Navajo are America’s largest Native American Tribe, and they are known for having vibrant tatoos.", "annotation_id": "2136526", "url": "https://genius.com/2136526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Bitches sweatin’ me like they been in the desert for days", "vault_lines": ["Bitches sweatin' me like they been in the desert for days"], "meaning": "Women approach Wayne all the time because he’s popular.  But as he’s mentioned before, he doesn’t like these chicas coming up and asking him ridiculous questions.  Here he uses the two meanings of sweat (interrogate/perspire) to reiterate this point while tying in some desert heat imagery.", "annotation_id": "2135936", "url": "https://genius.com/2135936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Now it’s Bugattis,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Bawse has moved up in the world, from driving a run-of-the-mill SUV in the past to now a high-end exotic sports car.  He likes his new ride so much he even raps about it.", "annotation_id": "2135844", "url": "https://genius.com/2135844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Got my leather on lookin’ like Thunderdome", "vault_lines": ["Got my leather on lookin' like Thunderdome"], "meaning": "Kind of an obscure reference to an 80s movie starring Mel Gibson and Tina Turner.", "annotation_id": "2135594", "url": "https://genius.com/2135594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "N-N-Now where my bad bitches? W-W-Where #PrettyGang T-T-T-Twerk that ass and let dem titties hang!", "vault_lines": ["N-N-Now where my bad bitches? W-W-Where #PrettyGang", "T-T-T-Twerk that ass and let dem titties hang!"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj recently held the Pretty Gang Twerk Contest where fans could upload videos of themselves twerking.", "annotation_id": "2134907", "url": "https://genius.com/2134907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Ayo pass the crown to the real queen", "vault_lines": ["Ayo pass the crown to the real queen"], "meaning": "Similar start to Lil Wayne verse, but this time Nicki is asking for the crown.The crown to become the Hip-Hop queen\n\nNot the first time she called herself the queen of hip-hop.", "annotation_id": "2134264", "url": "https://genius.com/2134264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "From the Dirty South, muzzle on my mouth Roof, I’m a dog, I’m in it", "vault_lines": ["From the Dirty South, muzzle on my mouth", "Roof, I'm a dog, I'm in it"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is from Atlanta which is part of the Dirty South. Muzzle on his mouth, basically means that he always has a firearm. He also uses muzzle as he compares himself to a dog, or a beast, a muzzle goes on a dogs mouth to protect it.", "annotation_id": "2133529", "url": "https://genius.com/2133529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Let me see your hands up like a gun in your face", "vault_lines": ["Let me see your hands up like a gun in your face"], "meaning": "Typically when a gun is pointed at you, hands up means you are surrendering and/or defenseless. Weezy is using this in two ways… First, he wants to see your hands up because this shows him that you are feeling the song… think in “concert” terms. Also, he wants you to surrender because he is self-proclaimed still… “The best rapper alive”", "annotation_id": "2133507", "url": "https://genius.com/2133507", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Nah, I can’t work with none of them", "vault_lines": ["Nah, I can't work with none of them"], "meaning": "Nicki is too good to work with any other female rapper than she sees as her competition.\n\nAgain this can be seen as a reference to Iggy Azalea, who has a single entitled “Work” and has constantly expressed her desire to collaborate with Minaj.", "annotation_id": "2133392", "url": "https://genius.com/2133392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "I’m smoking on strong, this is that steroid era", "vault_lines": ["I'm smoking on strong, this is that steroid era"], "meaning": "STRONG WEED = GOOD WEED\nSTEROIDS = STRONG BODY\n\nIt’s no secret that Tity 2 Necklace likes to smoke his pot, he’s actually been arrested for possession of the drug. Clearly, he has that loud weed, in No Lie he says:\n\nI smoke strong, that Popeye\n\n\n\nYou can’t turn on SportCenter without seeing something about PED’s. The MLB is seriously cracking down on a issue with steroids. They recently had the biggest drug bust in sports history. Taking down huge names such as:\n\n\nAlex Rodriguez\nRyan Braun\n\n\n\nThe past 10 years of baseball is now known as the steroid era.", "annotation_id": "2133364", "url": "https://genius.com/2133364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Tell by the jewels, I’m a hundred grand dude (dude) Really a lot more, I’m talkin’ channel 4 news (woo)", "vault_lines": ["Tell by the jewels, I'm a hundred grand dude (dude)", "Really a lot more, I'm talkin' channel 4 news (woo)"], "meaning": "TAKE A GLANCE\n\n\n\nTHE DUDE HAS A CHAIN WITH HIS OWN FACE ON IT!\n\nIf you can’t tell that he’s rich, than maybe you are blind. Rick is clearly rich, worth a big 28 million. Like he said, he is worth A LOT more than “a hundred grand”.\n\nChannel 4 news is a big news station, you may hear Rick’s name time to time. They don’t name off any average Joe either.\n\nJay-Z has a similar line on “Crown”:\n\nSee my name come across on CNN\n‘bout 6 minutes, you gonna see it again", "annotation_id": "2133357", "url": "https://genius.com/2133357", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Gimme her combination I’mma put my tongue in her safe", "vault_lines": ["Gimme her combination I'mma put my tongue in her safe"], "meaning": "Wayne doesn’t just like to get head, it’s well established that he likes to give it too.  This example is just another one of his euphemisms for it.", "annotation_id": "2133329", "url": "https://genius.com/2133329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "And that TrukFit shit is all we wear", "vault_lines": ["And that TrukFit shit is all we wear"], "meaning": "TrukFit is Lil Wayne’s clothing line. To respect Lil Wayne and his clothing line and also to promote others on buying it, her and the crew (YMCMB), will wear it.\n\n\n\nNot the first song Tunch has mentioned his clothing line in a song.", "annotation_id": "2133304", "url": "https://genius.com/2133304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Two doors in the air", "vault_lines": ["Two doors in the air"], "meaning": "Swizz Beats is the VP of Global Design at Lotus.  They didn’t invent doors that open straight up, but that’s not to say they can’t make ‘em!", "annotation_id": "2133242", "url": "https://genius.com/2133242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "I got your girl at home, she got that Thunderdome", "vault_lines": ["I got your girl at home, she got that Thunderdome"], "meaning": "The Trop (aka Tropicana Field) in St. Pete, FL used to be called the Thunderdome.  2 Chainz uses each part of this compound word as a creative way to say your girl gives great (thunder) head (dome).", "annotation_id": "2133156", "url": "https://genius.com/2133156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Roll down on her when I used to have a Cherokee", "vault_lines": ["Roll down on her when I used to have a Cherokee"], "meaning": "A clever play on “Cherokee” as the name of a Native American tribe as well as a Jeep model.\n\n\n\nRicky Rozay is also no stranger to ending a line with the same word twice in a row – he’s even been a little creative with it, rhyming the next-to-last word instead.", "annotation_id": "2133122", "url": "https://genius.com/2133122", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Every interview yes I am their focal, point", "vault_lines": ["Every interview yes I am their focal, point"], "meaning": "Whenever any other female rapper is in an interview, Nicki is always brought into the conversation. They are often asked how they feel about her, and if they like her or not.\n\nFellow female rapper Iggy Azalea mentions and praises Nicki Minaj regularly in her interviews by expressing her desire to meet and possibly collaborate with her in the future.", "annotation_id": "2132996", "url": "https://genius.com/2132996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Diamond sparkle in my mouth, bluetooth homie", "vault_lines": ["Diamond sparkle in my mouth, bluetooth homie"], "meaning": "His diamond grill makes his teeth look blue. Also a play on “bluetooth” (wireless technology used for sending data from cellphone to cellphone)", "annotation_id": "2132939", "url": "https://genius.com/2132939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Plus you got mad miles on your vag card", "vault_lines": ["Plus you got mad miles on your vag card"], "meaning": "Nicki’s trying to say that her female competitors have had sex with a lot of people to get where they are so their “vag card”, in the same vein as race card, their vagina, has a lot of mileage on it, sort of like an old car.", "annotation_id": "2132929", "url": "https://genius.com/2132929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "And my homies got that work, they Alicia’n them keys (woo)", "vault_lines": ["And my homies got that work, they Alicia'n them keys (woo)"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne’s friends deal kilos of drugs on the streets. The second part sounds like “unleashin' them keys”; it’s a play on singer Alicia Keys, Swizz Beatz’s wife.", "annotation_id": "2132923", "url": "https://genius.com/2132923", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Weezy F is the grade", "vault_lines": ["Make your woman a slave, Weezy F is the grade"], "meaning": "Adding to Lil Wayne’s long list of nicknames.", "annotation_id": "2132900", "url": "https://genius.com/2132900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "New crib lookin’ like Kim Dotcom (HUH)", "vault_lines": ["New crib lookin' like Kim Dotcom (HUH)"], "meaning": "Paying homage to another large and wealthy man, Ross name-drops Kim Dotcom, the computer hacker who rose to prominence and affluence with the websites Megaupload and Mega. His extreme wealth from these websites fed into his big-spending habits, much like those rappers exhibit in their songs and lives. Ross' house, with the money he’s accrued from rap, looks like that of the mansion owned by Mr. Dotcom (shown below).\n\nCoincidence that he name-drops Kim on Swizz’s track? I think not. Swizz was officially listed on Megaupload’s website as CEO prior to the site’s shutdown.", "annotation_id": "2132894", "url": "https://genius.com/2132894", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "Your girl is my biggest fan, windmill nigga", "vault_lines": ["Your girl is my biggest fan, windmill nigga"], "meaning": "Play on the meaning of fan.\n\nA windmill a like a big fan. sorta", "annotation_id": "2132891", "url": "https://genius.com/2132891", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "You know the girl get it poppin’ like a pill fiend", "vault_lines": ["You know the girl get it poppin' like a pill fiend"], "meaning": "To pop pills is a way of taking drugs like ecstasy or any other drug that you can take as a pill. If you feind something, then you are addicted to that. So the girl (aka Nicki Minaj) gets it poppin'.", "annotation_id": "2132700", "url": "https://genius.com/2132700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "I got little bunny rabbits in my backyard So fuck a funny style fraud, tryna act hard", "vault_lines": ["So fuck a funny style fraud, tryna act hard"], "meaning": "#SHOTS FIRED?\n\nThis is a possible reference to Iggy Azalea and the bunny ears she sometimes sports; Iggy’s rise to success has coincided with the reign of Nicki Minaj, a reign that she wishes to keep for years to come.\n\nNicki is diminishing Iggy’s emergence on the scene – saying she’s a fraud with funny style (i.e. the bunny ears) and mere annoyance, like a rabbit digging up a garden in her backyard.\n\nThe metaphor goes deeper considering that Iggy’s native Australia has dealt with a massive rabbit overpopulation problem since the invasive species was introduced in 1859.  Nicki might be arguing that Iggy is an invasive species in the American rap scene.\n\nIggy regularly cites 1996-animated film Space Jam’s character Lola Bunny as one of her inspirations.\n\n“Bunny” is also slang for white girl.", "annotation_id": "2132630", "url": "https://genius.com/2132630", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hands Up", "line": "I don’t do Barnes but yes I am noble", "vault_lines": ["I don't do Barnes but yes I am noble"], "meaning": "Nicki is giving a double entendre. She has made several allusions to royalty and regalia in the past:\n - You can be the king but watch the queen conquer\n\nAnd I will retire with the crown, yes!\n\nBitch, I’m queen, ‘lizabeth\n\nSo it’s off with your heads, decapitation\n\n\n\n…so it would only make sense that she would allude to her competition as MEDIEVAL TIMES (How’s THAT for old school?) peasants (who were called serfs, the lowest of the social order). She’s calling them farm animals, while she is highest, beating a king, with classless nobility (get it? She has no class, even though she’s at the top). Apparently she’s also too cool for public/local libraries, so she goes to the bookstore chain Barnes & Noble.", "annotation_id": "2132200", "url": "https://genius.com/2132200", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
