{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Exactly what the game’s been missin’", "vault_lines": ["Exactly what the game's been missin'"], "meaning": "This is an old rap adage that has colloquially come to mean, “I’m a high quality rapper that elevates the game.” This  is how he is using it here. The line doesn’t apply literally to Pusha, in fact it is the opposite. This is his third solo album and before that he released 3 albums with his brother as Clipse, plus about a half dozen mixtapes and EP’s, so he’s been in the game for a long time, which makes this an ironic turn of phrase as well.", "annotation_id": "32936463", "url": "https://genius.com/32936463", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "It’s flesh and blood ’til I’m fresh as fuck", "vault_lines": ["It's flesh and blood 'til I'm fresh as fuck"], "meaning": "This likely refers to some of Ross' friends and family who previously considered him “flesh and blood” switching up on him after he found success.\n\nThis also ties in with the line “Watchin' my success, for some, is bittersweet” earlier in the verse.", "annotation_id": "31644844", "url": "https://genius.com/31644844", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
