{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Never trust a bitch who finds love in a camera She will fuck you, then turn around and fuck a janitor", "vault_lines": ["She will fuck you, then turn around and fuck a janitor"], "meaning": "Girls who find love in appearances do not care about you and will not see your worth. She will leave you for a janitor because all she cares about are appearances.", "annotation_id": "27305805", "url": "https://genius.com/27305805", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "This fire burns hot as Hell’s Kitchen", "vault_lines": ["This fire burns hot as Hell's Kitchen"], "meaning": "Hell’s Kitchen is a British cooking show hosted by famed chef Gordon Ramsey.\n\n\n\nPush is comparing his rap game to the show, named after Gordon Ramsey’s fiery attitude and difficult nature, and giving it a new meaning in this song.", "annotation_id": "25785400", "url": "https://genius.com/25785400", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Still do the Fred Astaire on a brick", "vault_lines": ["Still do the Fred Astaire on a brick"], "meaning": "Stepping on a brick means cutting cocaine.\n\nFred Astaire was, among other things, a very famous and talented dancer and actor who mastered his dance steps. Push reestablishes his status as a trap chef and witty MC with this line.", "annotation_id": "14758679", "url": "https://genius.com/14758679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Look at my new digs The rooftop can host a paint-and-sip for, like, forty", "vault_lines": ["Look at my new digs", "The rooftop can host a paint-and-sip for, like, forty"], "meaning": "“Paint and sips” refers to parties in which paying customers attend art lessons while drinking wine and other beverages.\n\nPusha T’s new house is so big that he could host a 40-person lesson on his roof.", "annotation_id": "14688197", "url": "https://genius.com/14688197", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Diamonds drippin’ on me via Tiffany’s", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds drippin' on me via Tiffany's"], "meaning": "Tiffany & Co. is one of the world’s most famous luxury jewelry retailers. Based in New York City, Tiffany has been a staple of American high-end culture since the first half of the 19th century.\n\n\n\nWhen Rick Ross says that he’s wearing diamonds from Tiffany’s, he’s saying that he’s reached the highest level of luxury. Ross has spoken more of his habit of buying expensive jewelry, for example here, where he’s accompanied by two other G.O.O.D. legends.", "annotation_id": "14678253", "url": "https://genius.com/14678253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "I’m dyin’ to find a way to get a Grammy from it (Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": ["I'm dyin' to find a way to get a Grammy from it (Maybach Music)"], "meaning": "While he has been nominated four times over the course of his career, to date Rick Ross has never won a Grammy Award, presented annually by The Recording Academy. Despite continued commerical success, Ross is bothered by this lack of recognition and is looking for new ways to reach this end, possibly involving his ‘amputated homie’ from the previous line.\n\n\n\nRoss has had his issues with the Grammy’s in the past. In a 2015 interview with Billboard, Ross spoke on their out-of-touch award selections:\n\nThe rap community doesn’t feel like the rap Grammy is in touch. Not at all…This is music that powers from the streets up…If anything, in the rap categories, that’s what should be most recognized.\n\nMaybach Music is the name of Ross' record label, founded in 2009. Notable artists also signed to the Maybach Music Group (MMG) include Meek Mill, Wale, and Omarion.", "annotation_id": "14652122", "url": "https://genius.com/14652122", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "My homie amputated but gon’ stand for somethin’", "vault_lines": ["My homie amputated but gon' stand for somethin'"], "meaning": "Some clever wordplay here. Amputation refers to the removal of a limb from the body. Ross is likely talking specifically about the amputation of his homie’s leg, in which case he would have more trouble standing—nevertheless, his homie continues to “stand for something”.\n\nRoss could also be referencing the amputation of Quentin Miller, Drake’s alleged ghostwriter, which would be consistent with the shots fired at Drake throughout the album. He might be stating that Drake can’t stand for himself; he needs a ghostwriter.", "annotation_id": "14648372", "url": "https://genius.com/14648372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "I keep the coldest flows on the hot seat (M-M-M—)", "vault_lines": ["I keep the coldest flows on the hot seat (M-M-M—)"], "meaning": "In rap, a “cold flow” is a rhyme that is effortless and top-notch with some punchlines/word plays.\n\nA hot seat is a metaphor for a position (in an organization) that comes with a lot of stress or pressure to perform at your best.\n\nRick Ross is referencing the fact that he has rappers with the best lines (coldest flows) and he keeps them spitting these flows by continually putting them under pressure (hot seat).", "annotation_id": "14646572", "url": "https://genius.com/14646572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "All these K-9 units still sniffin’ me", "vault_lines": ["All these K-9 units still sniffin' me"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the police department’s K-9 Unit that specializes in using trained dogs (canines/k-9) to perform people/suspects tracking and drug searches.\n\n\n\nRoss feels he’s still being treated like a drug dealer with these dogs sniffing searches even though he’s been a legitimate businessman/rapper for a long time now.", "annotation_id": "14644874", "url": "https://genius.com/14644874", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Now that’s how the ting go, I’m back from Santo Domingo That’s where the kings go, down in Santo Domingo Now that’s how the ting go, I’m back from Santo Domingo This for the sneaker hoarders and coke snorters ’Cause that’s where the kings go, down in Santo Domingo", "vault_lines": ["Now that's how the ting go, I'm back from Santo Domingo", "That's where the kings go, down in Santo Domingo", "This for the sneaker hoarders and coke snorters", "'Cause that's where the kings go, down in Santo Domingo"], "meaning": "Santo Domingo, the capital city of the Dominican Republic, is a media-described ‘Drug Mecca’. In 2008 alone, 661 Kilos of cocaine were confiscated within the city. Given his drug dealing past, it comes as no surprise that Pusha would be familiar with this area.\n\nThe word, “King,” has a specific purpose within these lines as it could be referencing Kingpins who travel to the city to obtain the product, or Pusha T himself, who has been given the nickname King Pusha.", "annotation_id": "14644397", "url": "https://genius.com/14644397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 108, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Your bustdown is bust-down and don’t match the metal Lower level’s where you settle at I’m the pot callin’ the kettle black", "vault_lines": ["Your bustdown is bust-down and don't match the metal", "Lower level's where you settle at", "I'm the pot callin' the kettle black"], "meaning": "Push here is degrading materialistic people.\n\nHe begins by stating people own diamond encrusted(bustdown) timepieces which ironically bust down and/or broken with inadequate metals incomparable to Push’s. Potentially a metaphor for how genuine Push and his watch are in contrast with the people who he is speaking on.\n\n\n\nPush then references an old saying of “the pot calling the kettle black” with the notable irony being that both utensils are black, whomsoever he is speaking towards must have much in common with Push but whosoever he is speaking of is ignorant to Push’s accomplishments but prideful of their own.", "annotation_id": "14644004", "url": "https://genius.com/14644004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Art Basel-in’ the bezel", "vault_lines": ["Art Basel-in' the bezel"], "meaning": "“Art Basel stages art shows for Modern and Contemporary works, sited annually in Basel, Miami Beach and Hong Kong”\n\n\n\nWhat Pusha means here is how out-smarting the game or those who think they got him. It matches the following line “your bust down is a bust down…” meaning he is two steps ahead of those who think they will get him.", "annotation_id": "14641066", "url": "https://genius.com/14641066", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Tap-tap, throw the phone if you hear it click", "vault_lines": ["Tap-tap, throw the phone if you hear it click"], "meaning": "“Tap, tap” is a continuation of the Fred Astaire reference, seeing as Mr. Astaire was renowned for his tap dancing. To step on a brick of cocaine is to cut it with something else.\n\n\n\nHowever “tap” also refers to the act of tapping phones in order to intercept calls and listen to the conversations secretly. This interception is common practice by the FBI, DEA and other [opps]. People often discover that their phone has been tapped by a light static or clicking sounds in the background of phone calls. This is why Push instructs to “throw the phone if you hear it click” (because it’s being tapped by the feds).", "annotation_id": "14640543", "url": "https://genius.com/14640543", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "From Honda Accords to Grammy awards, yo", "vault_lines": ["From Honda Accords to Grammy awards, yo"], "meaning": "Ross seems to be referencing The Game’s 2006 track “Wouldn’t Get Far,” where at the end of the first verse, The Game rapped:\n\nAnd all these new video bitches tryin to be Melyssa Ford\nBut they don’t know Melyssa Ford drive a Honda Accord\nShe a video vixen, but behind closed doors\nShe do whatever it take to get to the Grammy Awards, ha ha\n\nHonda Accords are rather basic cars that “kings” such as Kanye West and Pusha T wouldn’t drive now that they have Grammy awards.", "annotation_id": "14639863", "url": "https://genius.com/14639863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "It’s double-M, baby, money monopolies (Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": ["It's double-M, baby, money monopolies (Maybach Music)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross refers to double M’s as in “money monopolies,” his income and cash flowcash as well as “Maybach Music,” Rick’s music record label he founded back in 2009.", "annotation_id": "14639306", "url": "https://genius.com/14639306", "state": "pending", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "It’s not the temperature for you in Timberlands", "vault_lines": ["It's not the temperature for you in Timberlands"], "meaning": "Timberland is a popular footwear manufacturing company known for their iconic tan waterproof boots.\n\nRick Ross compares the critical heated temperature and his status to a literal hot day, too hot for Timberlands.", "annotation_id": "14639273", "url": "https://genius.com/14639273", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Chillin’ in a condo full of ready-rock", "vault_lines": ["Chillin' in a condo full of ready-rock"], "meaning": "Ready rock is drug slang for crack. Ironically, the term was coined by a drug dealer named “Freeway” Rick Ross. Freeway Rick is also credited as being the main component in the introduction and spread of cocaine across America in the early 80s.\n\nIn 2010, Freeway Rick filed a lawsuit against Rick Ross, born William Leonard Roberts II, claiming that Roberts was using his identity as a drug kingpin to earn a profit. When the case was settled, Roberts was awarded ten million dollars, for lawyers and fees, and permission to keep the name.", "annotation_id": "14639055", "url": "https://genius.com/14639055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "I’m too rare amongst all of this pink hair, ooh!", "vault_lines": ["I'm too rare amongst all of this pink hair, ooh!"], "meaning": "Push sees himself in direct contrast to the newer wave of rappers, particularly the lot with colored hair. He’s also making a reference to rare meat, which is pink in color.\n\nIn a 2018 Vulture interview, Pusha T revealed the meaning behind this line:\n\nThere’s a lot of pink hair … Oh! Ye was like, ‘Hey, man, what do you think about that? You think you should change that? Not just because I have pink hair.’ I said, ‘Oh, do you have pink hair today?’ He was like, ‘It’s blond …’ I was like, ‘Oh.’ He said, ‘One of my best friends, he dyes his hair, too.’ I said, ‘I want you to understand the two types of people out here. You have guys that do [the pink hair]. And you have rap fans and rappers that I admire and look up to — those young guys, the A Boogies, the Don Qs, the Meek Mills — that speak for another section. I feel like my energy leans towards more of that side, the elder of that side.’ If you’re a rager, if you like to rage and go ‘Aaaaah!’ [shakes his fists skyward] Jump out, and you do all that … I feel like that’s for your side. And, I feel like your side is making a lot of noise. So, ‘I’m too rare in a world full of pink hair’ means ‘I feel like there’s more of you guys than there are of us.’", "annotation_id": "14638989", "url": "https://genius.com/14638989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Confront my problems like I’m Ralo in the bluff", "vault_lines": ["Confront my problems like I'm Ralo in the bluff"], "meaning": "Atlanta rapper Ralo was arrested on Sunday, April 15th for transporting nearly $2 million worth of marijuana. Additionally, Atlanta police raided Ralo’s apartment complex, known as “Lil Pakistan” and agents confiscated illicit substances.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lcl5inKORSQ", "annotation_id": "14638832", "url": "https://genius.com/14638832", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "The Warhols on my wall paint a war story Had to find other ways to invest ’Cause you rappers found every way to ruin Pateks", "vault_lines": ["Had to find other ways to invest", "'Cause you rappers found every way to ruin Pateks"], "meaning": "Andy Warhol is one of the most famous contemporary artists of all time. His paintings sell for millions—in 2013, the “Silver Car Crash (Double Disaster)” Andy Warhol painting sold for $105.4 million at auction.\n\nPusha’s “war story” refers to his time in the music industry. From seeing his debut Clipse album Exclusive Audio Footage shelved in 1999, to record label Jive delaying Hell Hath No Fury in the mid ‘00s, to suddenly having to become a solo artist in 2010, Pusha’s career has been a rollercoaster of highs and lows.\n\nPatek Philippe is a Swiss watchmaker. “Patek” references in hip-hop have increased dramatically since 2013 leading to the oversaturation of the brand in rap lyrics.\n\n\n\nPush addresses ruining watches again later in this verse, rapping:\n\nYour bustdown is bust down and don’t match the metal\n\nThis refers to adding diamonds to the bezel of the watch. Seems Push likes his watches Plain Jane.", "annotation_id": "14638177", "url": "https://genius.com/14638177", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "Still hands-on, sucker, press your luck (M-M—)", "vault_lines": ["Still hands-on, sucker, press your luck (M-M—)"], "meaning": "Press Your Luck was a 80’s game show where contestants had to keep their hands on a button to win cash and prizes.\n\nRoss is letting folks know that things can go really bad for them if they try to take his kindness as a weakness.", "annotation_id": "14637499", "url": "https://genius.com/14637499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "So why debate my case vs. a Nancy Grace?", "vault_lines": ["So why debate my case vs. a Nancy Grace?"], "meaning": "Nancy Grace is an American legal commentator who is best known for her self titled talk show where she would regularly discuss high profile criminal cases. Ross wouldn’t let anybody tread on his name like that.", "annotation_id": "14637488", "url": "https://genius.com/14637488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hard Piano", "line": "I won’t let you ruin my dreams or Harvey Weinstein the kid Good mornin’, Matt Lauer—can I live?", "vault_lines": ["Good mornin', Matt Lauer—can I live?"], "meaning": "Both Harvey Weinstein and Matt Lauer were accused of sexual misconduct during the #MeToo movement, with both of them accused of taking advantage of people who worked for them.\n\nPush is saying he won’t let any industry bigwigs try to fuck him over or take advantage of him.\n\nOn the morning of this song’s release, Weinstein actually turned himself in to the New York Police Department in order to face his criminal charges as part of the probe into his sexual assaults.\n\nAlso, Matt Lauer was a host of The Today Show on NBC, hence the “good morning” line.\n\nThis could also be a reference to Jay-Z’s 1996 song “Can I Live,” as the track is used to express frustration and the unwillingness to conform to societal pressures, whether it be from the music industry or the struggles of hustling on the streets.\n\nIn the recent interview on Red Bull Music Academy Pusha T spoke about this line, saying:\n“When I’m talking about Matt Lauer, and I’m talking about Harvey Weinstein is like man, I’m talking about not falling into any of those wild weird sexual deviant behaviours, and I’m also talking about just my growth like I got different things to brag about”.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oamsbwuCves&list=WL&index=19&t=0s", "annotation_id": "14637471", "url": "https://genius.com/14637471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 100, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
