{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Harsh", "line": "I’m like a Rothschild with money, that’s why I’m (harsh)", "vault_lines": ["I'm like a Rothschild with money, that's why I'm (harsh)"], "meaning": "The Rothschilds is the wealthiest family in the world  with an estimated net worth on $350 billion – $2 trillion\n\n\n\nBusta is describing his desire for more money to become as rich as a Rothschild one day.", "annotation_id": "14329703", "url": "https://genius.com/14329703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Harsh", "line": "Yo, I rub stones together and cast a spell quick Like a Zo hittin’ voodoo blessings ’fore I move bricks", "vault_lines": ["Like a Zo hittin' voodoo blessings 'fore I move bricks"], "meaning": "Zo is slang for the Haitian gang “Zo Pound”. Voodoo is a popular form of religion in Haiti.\nSo when Busta moves his bricks of coke, he practices voodoo rituals to gain blessings of success.", "annotation_id": "384811", "url": "https://genius.com/384811", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Harsh", "line": "I beat you like the number eleven with two sticks", "vault_lines": ["I beat you like the number eleven with two sticks"], "meaning": "The image here is that if you had two sticks side by side it’d show the number eleven. Busta will proceed to use these sticks to beat down his opponents, because well, he’s harsh.", "annotation_id": "384808", "url": "https://genius.com/384808", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Harsh", "line": "Hard like when Cus D’Amato was trainin’ Tyson", "vault_lines": ["Hard like when Cus D'Amato was trainin' Tyson"], "meaning": "Cus D'Amato is famous for finding a young Mike Tyson and training him to unleash his beast mode. Under Cus' tutelage, Mike earned the nickname “Iron” Mike Tyson for being such a hard hitter.", "annotation_id": "384717", "url": "https://genius.com/384717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Harsh", "line": "Beef never settle, I’m Lyor to the ghetto (Huh) Russell with the hustle, Rick Rubin with the metal", "vault_lines": ["Beef never settle, I'm Lyor to the ghetto (Huh)", "Russell with the hustle, Rick Rubin with the metal"], "meaning": "Referencing Lyor Cohen, Russell Simmons and Rick Rubin, three of the world’s most influential music execs from Def Jam.\nRozay is the Lyor Cohen of the Ghetto, as he’s steadily begun to create the unstoppable Maybach Music Empire, putting Meek Mill into the spotlight from the ghetto, the Russell Simmons of the hustle because he is transforming the career of another rapper Wale and the Rick Rubin of the “metal” because:\n\n“When it comes to tools, fool I’m a Pep Boy”.\n\nMetal refers to guns, but in regards to Rick Rubin, it references his forays into metal/rock sounds when producing hip-hop songs for the likes of The Beastie Boys and Jay-Z (99 Problems)", "annotation_id": "384704", "url": "https://genius.com/384704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Harsh", "line": "Cash too green, it’s taped to the toilet Like I’m Michael Corleone in the bathroom scene Young black Vito, chopped and wrapped kilos", "vault_lines": ["Cash too green, it's taped to the toilet", "Like I'm Michael Corleone in the bathroom scene"], "meaning": "In a move consistent in hip-hop culture, Styles alludes to thepopular theme of the rap game being akin to the mafia.\nHe references the scene from the Godfather where Michael Corleone goes to the bathroom to retrieve a gun from the stall in order to perform a hit. In this case, Styles is getting money left hidden in the stall after a drug transaction.\nVito refers to Michael’s father, Vito Corleone, or the Godfather. So Styles is a young, black Godfather in charge of the drug game.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=876CZk5r7IM", "annotation_id": "384689", "url": "https://genius.com/384689", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Harsh", "line": "Like Audio Two, yeah, the crew is “Top Billin’”", "vault_lines": ["Like Audio Two, yeah, the crew is \"Top Billin'\""], "meaning": "Audio Two was an old school rap group from Brooklyn who scored fame with their hit single “Top Billin”\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0wbWPyhW7fE\n\nStyles and his crew, The Lox, are “top billin”, or in other words, well paid", "annotation_id": "384679", "url": "https://genius.com/384679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
