{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Haterz", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Bob-haterz-lyrics", "genius_title": "Haterz", "genius_id": 480331, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "Your son called you a dead beat", "vault_lines": ["Your son called you a dead beat"], "meaning": "This is most likely a reference to 50 Cent with whom Rick Ross had an ongoing beef. 50 is known to have a rocky relationship with his son.", "annotation_id": "17481022", "url": "https://genius.com/17481022", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "Couple niggas got killed at my show last weekend But how am I to blame if they were already beefing When they first started shooting man we was just leaving", "vault_lines": ["Couple niggas got killed at my show last weekend", "But how am I to blame if they were already beefing", "When they first started shooting man we was just leaving"], "meaning": "Two men were shot outside of a Gucci concert in California in 2010. Many were quick to blame Gucci’s street affiliations and violent lyrics for the incident, but here Gucci explains he can’t be held responsible for what his concertgoers do at his shows.\n\nAgain in 2016, one man was killed and two others were injured in a shooting outside of a St. Louis Gucci Mane concert.", "annotation_id": "16028406", "url": "https://genius.com/16028406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "Glock 40 on my hip, it was just me and Mac Bre-Z", "vault_lines": ["Glock 40 on my hip, it was just me and Mac Bre-Z"], "meaning": "Mac Bre-Z is a singer who dated Gucci for a while, and appeared on his hit track “Pills.”", "annotation_id": "16028380", "url": "https://genius.com/16028380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "AR in the car the first day I met Jeezy When I first started dissing niggas it was just teasing", "vault_lines": ["AR in the car the first day I met Jeezy", "When I first started dissing niggas it was just teasing"], "meaning": "Jeezy and Gucci Mane have had a long-running beef since the release of “So Icy,” a song which both Atlanta rappers claim as their own.\n\nThe beef turned deadly in 2005 when Jeezy offered $10,000 for someone to snatch Gucci Mane’s chain in his diss track “Stay Strapped.” Five Jeezy-affiliates attempted to claim the bounty on Wop’s chain, breaking into a home he was staying at. The incident resulted in Gucci shooting and killing Pookie Loc, a rapper signed to Jeezy.\n\nGucci claims here that, even before the beef, when he met Jeezy to record “So Icy,” he was packing an AR-15 assault rifle in his car.", "annotation_id": "16028343", "url": "https://genius.com/16028343", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "Baby says she never seen a nigga so freezy But these VVS diamonds make me feel like Meech", "vault_lines": ["Baby says she never seen a nigga so freezy", "But these VVS diamonds make me feel like Meech"], "meaning": "In rap music it’s common for rappers to boast about the diamonds in their jewelry to be “icy” or “freezing”, so in Gucci fashion he plays on this by creating his own word: freezy.\n\nVVS diamonds (which stand for very very slighty) in terms of clarity are some of the highest grades you can get, and because of this they can be very expensive.\n\nDemetrius Flentory otherwise known as Big Meech was one of the heads of the Black Mafia Family, which was a drug trafficking operation founded in Detroit.\n\n\n\nThey started a record label titled “BMF Entertainment” and helped rappers like Young Jeezy with their careers. The family was known for their flashy and high-profile lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "14077286", "url": "https://genius.com/14077286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "I had a pistol in the club the first day I met Weezy", "vault_lines": ["I had a pistol in the club the first day I met Weezy"], "meaning": "When Gucci met Lil Wayne, like everyone in the industry he was cautious of him. Although they have collaborated multiple times and are affiliated with each other, Gucci’s too street smart to ever not have his pistol with him", "annotation_id": "1271710", "url": "https://genius.com/1271710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "I got them Robin jeans saggin’ and I ain’t even bragging", "vault_lines": ["I got them Robin jeans saggin' and I ain't even bragging"], "meaning": "“Robin Jeans” is a clothing company. Gucci probably looks hella good in them but he doesn’t even need to brag verbally; his sagging pants make a statement already\n\n\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: The braggadocio is probably due to the fact that Robin Jeans cost $500-$900 a pair.", "annotation_id": "1164289", "url": "https://genius.com/1164289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "I still remember the first day that I ain’t have to serve smokers", "vault_lines": ["I still remember the first day that I ain’t have to serve smokers"], "meaning": "Another triple entendre from Gucci Mane:\n\n\nThe day when he was rich enough off rapping that he didn’t have to slang drugs to make ends meet anymore.\nThe day that he first started selling cocaine. Selling coke is a lot more profitable than selling weed to smokers.\nThe day that he started selling to dealers rather than smokers. A huge step up in the drug game.", "annotation_id": "1160669", "url": "https://genius.com/1160669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "Holding on to my dick, Michael Corleone, bitch Head shot like Fredo,", "vault_lines": ["Head shot like Fredo,"], "meaning": "A reference to The Godfather characters Michael Corleone and Fredo Corleone. Michael was the Godfather, and Fredo was his traitorous younger brother. Fredo was killed on Michael’s orders, shot in the back of the head on the family lake as Michael watched from afar.\n\n\n\nFredo Santana also has a song called “Head Shots.”", "annotation_id": "1151279", "url": "https://genius.com/1151279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "line": "Gucci Mane the CEO, I feel like Eazy", "vault_lines": ["Gucci Mane the CEO, I feel like Eazy"], "meaning": "Gucci is the boss and CEO of his 1017 Bricksquad record label, just as Eazy-E was the CEO for his label Ruthless Records.", "annotation_id": "1148911", "url": "https://genius.com/1148911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Head Shots", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gucci-mane-head-shots-lyrics", "genius_title": "Head Shots", "genius_id": 92664, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Headache", "line": "Gettin’ money, never cared that LeBron left Cause I thought that gettin’ wealthy was the concept I just want to be the richest, they say I’m the nicest", "vault_lines": ["Gettin' money, never cared that LeBron left", "Cause I thought that gettin' wealthy was the concept", "I just want to be the richest, they say I'm the nicest"], "meaning": "On July 11th, 2014 LeBron James announced via Sports Illustrated that he was leaving the Miami  Heat and going back home to the Cleveland Cavaliers.\n\nRoss could really care less that LeBron left because the only goal he is trying to accomplish is to get as rich as he can.", "annotation_id": "4459515", "url": "https://genius.com/4459515", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Headache", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-headache-lyrics", "genius_title": "Headache", "genius_id": 589950, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heads Up Eyes Open", "line": "It’s the facts versus the facts simile,", "vault_lines": ["It's the facts versus the facts simile,"], "meaning": "Should be ‘the facts versus the facsimile , though there is a fairly obvious etymological link to the  word  'simile’ …\n\nHere though the comparison is between the original,  bona fide article and copies made by a fax machine  (facsimiles):", "annotation_id": "14087754", "url": "https://genius.com/14087754", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heads Up Eyes Open", "line": "I celebrated with a bottle I just brought back from Italy And some loud, I got super packs like I backed Hillary", "vault_lines": ["And some loud, I got super packs like I backed Hillary"], "meaning": "Italy is famous for expensive fine  wines,  and also  Prosecco-   fairly cheap (at  least compared   to  its French rival Champagne) but  associated with celebrations. The bottle is likely one of  these.\n\nThere is   no  doubt  as  to what accompanies it:  high-grade pot,   denoted by both  ‘loud’ and its  coming  in a   ‘super  pack’ …\n\n\n\n…  a  play  on the super  PACs,  or  unlimited-funds political action committees, that  have influenced  U.S. politics extensively  since the Citizens  United  decision gutted  campaign finance restrictions. While  super  PACs exist to  support  both  major parties, the chief organization  of this  kind   backing  Hillary Clinton  in 2016 was Priorities USA (which had its roots in pro-Obama activism.)", "annotation_id": "14087687", "url": "https://genius.com/14087687", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heads Up Eyes Open", "line": "So you might as well believe in you", "vault_lines": ["so you might as well believe in you"], "meaning": "An affirmation from Talib: If all people are  manifestations of the Divine, we all have infinite inherent worth  and so  it  is  appropriate to practice  self-love rather than doubting our  usefulness to the  world.", "annotation_id": "14087646", "url": "https://genius.com/14087646", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heads Up Eyes Open", "line": "God is what I see in you", "vault_lines": ["God is what I see in you"], "meaning": "Panentheism: the belief that  God is an  immanent life-force found within living  beings and through the universe, as opposed to traditional (mono)theism’s  positing of a personal God who brought the universe into existence  but stands independent of their creation.\nPerhaps   inspired  by  ‘namaste’, a  common greeting in spiritually conscious  circles; loosely translates as ‘I  see the divine in you’", "annotation_id": "14087622", "url": "https://genius.com/14087622", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heads Up Eyes Open", "line": "A righteous man walks the earth without judgment And loves his enemies enough to deliver justice", "vault_lines": ["A righteous man walks the earth without judgment"], "meaning": "A righteous person knows they aren’t righteous on their own but only through God.  So, the righteous person can’t judge but only love everybody.  The righteous person even loves others who would set themselves up to be enemies of the righteous person.  However, that love pushes the righteous person to speak truth to their enemies and seek justice against those enemies should it come to that.  Justice is good for everyone, including the offending enemies, and ‘love’ isn’t love unless it holds everyone accountable for their actions.", "annotation_id": "13010338", "url": "https://genius.com/13010338", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heads Up Eyes Open", "line": "A wise man know what he know, and what he doesn’t", "vault_lines": ["A wise man know what he know, and what he doesn't"], "meaning": "This is a saying by Lao Tzu, the legendary Chinese philosopher. It’s a statement from his works Tao Te Ching.", "annotation_id": "12799497", "url": "https://genius.com/12799497", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
