{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heartless", "line": "Growin’ up, my mama explained the difference between fame and notoriety See fame is when people know you Notoriety is when people know your work And notoriety leave a legacy", "vault_lines": ["And notoriety leave a legacy"], "meaning": "Bigga Rankins' mother drops some serious knowledge on this one. Growing up, Rankins mom taught a very insightful lesson to him. She discussed the difference between the words “fame” and “notoriety”. Fame is simply people being familiar with you. There is no saying whether you’re important whatsoever or not. People just know your name (ex: the “Cash Me Ousside” girl, Bhad Bhabie). However, notoriety is people being familiar with what you do and how it is relevant. In notoriety, you aren’t the main focus of the popularity, you’re actions are (ex: Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr.).", "annotation_id": "12771147", "url": "https://genius.com/12771147", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
