{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "Heavyweight, Don King Robin Givens, big dreams", "vault_lines": ["Robin Givens, big dreams"], "meaning": "Don King was part of Mike Tyson heavyweight Dream. Robin Givens had high standards for success she aimed high she had big Dreams and now she is an entrepreneur selling books. She dropped out of Harvard an IVY League College/University to be on “The Cosby Show” if that’s not following your dream then what is. Also Robin Givens starred in Boomerang with Eddie Murphy.\nTo show how high Givens was one of her quotes reads\n\nMy mother never acknowledged my strength, I wondered, I could ever Be enough. I had no love for my self\n-Robin Givens\n\nProof http://annecarolinedrake.com/2011/10/22/robin-givens-grace-will-lead-me-home-book-review-more/", "annotation_id": "4782449", "url": "https://genius.com/4782449", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "License suspended, ridin’ with the yay (Slab) I shit where I eat, I trap where I stay (Slab)", "vault_lines": ["License suspended, ridin' with the yay (Slab)", "I shit where I eat, I trap where I stay (Slab)"], "meaning": "Chef in the kitchen, cooking up with the crimies\n\nSince Slab got his drivers licence for drug dealing out of his car, he stays at home and cooks crack.", "annotation_id": "4453614", "url": "https://genius.com/4453614", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "Shout out Mally Mall, I got a few bitches I don’t get my dick sucked unless it’s two bitches", "vault_lines": ["Shout out Mally Mall, I got a few bitches", "I don't get my dick sucked unless it's two bitches"], "meaning": "Slab doesn’t get into bed without two women with him. Mally Mall got him the hook up. Hopefully it came before his home was recently raided by the FBI on corruption charges.", "annotation_id": "4453570", "url": "https://genius.com/4453570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "And I don’t give a fuck what pussy niggas say (Fuck ’em) Michelangelo of this trap game Traded fifteen bags of mid for a half a thang (Flip) Remix that eighteen, now it’s thirty-six (Flip) Turned that midget to a brick, that’s a pretty flip (Slab)", "vault_lines": ["Michelangelo of this trap game", "Traded fifteen bags of mid for a half a thang (Flip)", "Remix that eighteen, now it's thirty-six (Flip)", "Turned that midget to a brick, that's a pretty flip (Slab)"], "meaning": "Whole Slab draws parallels between himself and Michelangelo – one of the greatest artists of all time. He flipped 15 pounds of marijuana to half a kilo of cocaine, then cooked it as crack and made a brick (kilo). Stab’s on top of the hustle game!", "annotation_id": "4453540", "url": "https://genius.com/4453540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "Bulletproof the Lincoln, there go Ricky Rizzle", "vault_lines": ["Bulletproof the Lincoln, there go Ricky Rizzle"], "meaning": "Considering Ross was the target of a drive by shooting in 2013, it’s no surprise his ride is now bulletproof.", "annotation_id": "4432402", "url": "https://genius.com/4432402", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "I been touchin’ the sack, I made my way to a ki’ I’m so in love with the trap, I bought a house ’cross the street Quarter key got me livin’ like I’m Don King Heavyweight, I’m in the ring nigga, ding ding Nigga, ding ding Nigga, ding ding Don’t make me hit you ’cross your head, nigga, ding ding Runnin’ off with all your things, ding ding", "vault_lines": ["I'm so in love with the trap, I bought a house 'cross the street", "Quarter key got me livin' like I'm Don King", "Heavyweight, I'm in the ring nigga, ding ding", "Don't make me hit you 'cross your head, nigga, ding ding", "Runnin' off with all your things, ding ding"], "meaning": "Rozay lives large – like famous boxing promoter Don King. Selling keys of cocaine means he was able to afford former heavyweight Evander Holyfield’s $5.8 million, 109 room mansion.", "annotation_id": "4428020", "url": "https://genius.com/4428020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "For this cocaine, they standin’ in this cold rain (Woo) In pneumonia weather tryna move that whole thing (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["For this cocaine, they standin' in this cold rain (Woo)", "In pneumonia weather tryna move that whole thing (Woo)"], "meaning": "Rain, sleet, hail, or snow… even if its cold enough to catch pneumonia, Ross will make the sales. As Clipse said…", "annotation_id": "4427956", "url": "https://genius.com/4427956", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "My trap Mike Tyson, nigga, heavyweight (Woo) I’m sleepin’ in the trap, we open every day", "vault_lines": ["My trap Mike Tyson, nigga, heavyweight (Woo)", "I'm sleepin' in the trap, we open every day"], "meaning": "Slab compares the superiority of his trap house to Mike Tyson’s boxing legacy. Tyson was a undisputed heavyweight boxing champion from the years 1985-2005.\n\nSlab’s trap house is moving heavy weight to supply his hood. His drug dealing is as successful as Tyson’s boxing tenure (which is really impressive).", "annotation_id": "4417372", "url": "https://genius.com/4417372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "Diamonds on my pinky, women on my dizzle", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds on my pinky, women on my dizzle"], "meaning": "Rozay has a pink diamond on his pinky, and some women bouncing on his dick. Ross uses the -izzle slang popularized by Snoop Dogg to replace the word “dick”.", "annotation_id": "4395719", "url": "https://genius.com/4395719", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "Snortin’ powder, poppin’ Belaire Rose (Slab)", "vault_lines": ["Snortin' powder, poppin' Belaire Rose (Slab)"], "meaning": "Belaire Rose is a french sparkling wine produced in the south of France. The brand gained its popularity from none other than Rick Ross when he endorsed it in early 2013.", "annotation_id": "4395712", "url": "https://genius.com/4395712", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Heavyweight", "line": "’88 Mike Tyson, that’s with the gold teeth", "vault_lines": ["'88 Mike Tyson, that's with the gold teeth"], "meaning": "Mike Tyson fought three times in 1988, defeating Larry Holmes, Tony Tubbs, and Michael Spinks.\n\nTyson later lost a gold tooth after being headbutted by his pet tiger.", "annotation_id": "4395631", "url": "https://genius.com/4395631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
