{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hell’s Angels (American Heathens)", "line": "Pull up, hop out, shoot up this bitch like Jonathan Mannion", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, hop out, shoot up this bitch like Jonathan Mannion"], "meaning": "Ross is going to jump out of his car and open fire on his haters. Jonathan Mannion is a photographer who “shoots” photos, hence the reference. Mannion is most known for his work being the photographer of Jay-Z’s Reasonable Doubt photoshoot:", "annotation_id": "674338", "url": "https://genius.com/674338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hell’s Angels (American Heathens)", "line": "Bought me a Corvette motor, put a supercharger on it From the bus stop it’s sounding like a damn train rollin’", "vault_lines": ["Bought me a Corvette motor, put a supercharger on it", "From the bus stop it's sounding like a damn train rollin'"], "meaning": "While your broke ass is waiting at the bus stop for a ride, you can hear Rick’s ride, which sounds like a train because of the supercharger he put on it.\n\nIf it sounds like a train, why not put a train horn on it?", "annotation_id": "674334", "url": "https://genius.com/674334", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hell’s Angels (American Heathens)", "line": "I’m a star in the ghetto I swear C-Murder my neighbor", "vault_lines": ["I'm a star in the ghetto I swear C-Murder my neighbor"], "meaning": "Ross solidifies himself as an iconic figure in the hood, comparing his status in the ghetto to that of C-Murder, a notorious rapper from the gritty streets of New Orleans, LA. The hood loves him because he was really ‘bout that life. (He’s currently serving life in jail for a murder charge.)", "annotation_id": "674329", "url": "https://genius.com/674329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hell’s Angels (American Heathens)", "line": "I got a star on my sneakers, they go by Chuck Taylor", "vault_lines": ["I got a star on my sneakers, they go by Chuck Taylor"], "meaning": "Ross may not be be a star, but he’s wearing converse sneakers, which have stars on them.", "annotation_id": "674326", "url": "https://genius.com/674326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hell’s Angels (American Heathens)", "line": "It’s the boss bitch, so go tell your boss bitch", "vault_lines": ["It's the boss bitch, so go tell your boss bitch"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is the Boss, so he wants you to go and tell your boss, that he is the Boss of all bosses!", "annotation_id": "674323", "url": "https://genius.com/674323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
