{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Big body Benzes while the bitch niggas starve", "vault_lines": ["Big body Benzes while the bitch niggas starve"], "meaning": "In one of Ross' toughest lines ever, he contrasts his successes to his haters' failures using EXCELLENT alliteration with the letter B.\n\nBig body Benzes while the bitch niggas starve", "annotation_id": "13129841", "url": "https://genius.com/13129841", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Put a number on your helmet like it’s Notre Dame 5 grand’ll get you whacked, won’t even know your name", "vault_lines": ["Put a number on your helmet like it's Notre Dame", "5 grand'll get you whacked, won't even know your name"], "meaning": "“Putting a number on your helmet” refers to putting a price on your head. In the following line, Ross illustrates that he only has to put up $5000 to get a bounty on a fuckboi’s head.\n\nHowever, the metaphor in this line makes no sense. Ross is trying to say that he can put a price (number) on your head like there’s a number on the Notre Dame football team’s helmets…. but there are no numbers on Notre Dame’s helmets..", "annotation_id": "13129826", "url": "https://genius.com/13129826", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "And the Lord is my witness we making major moves", "vault_lines": ["And the Lord is my witness we making major moves"], "meaning": "Like most drug dealers, Ross relies on the Lord to watch his back and forgive him for future infractions.\n\nAlso could be a reference to all the power moves he made in 2012. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o-ziL7r8Lh8", "annotation_id": "763323", "url": "https://genius.com/763323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Road to the riches until I’m paid in full", "vault_lines": ["Road to the riches until I'm paid in full"], "meaning": "The obvious point is that he’s going to keep making money until he’s seriously rich sure, but more importantly the the statement specifically references  two legendary Rap albums: Kool G Rap’s Road to the Riches and Rakim’s Paid in Full", "annotation_id": "544301", "url": "https://genius.com/544301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Look at this stuff, this is history here...you’re history This is garbage...I can say I bled for garbage So this is meaningless... No, at one time it meant a lot. When you’re just a young kid this is everything to you, but then you realize your priorities change. And you just want your children to be happy and do nice things and that makes you happy. This is nothing. This is just nothing, man...", "vault_lines": ["So this is meaningless..."], "meaning": "Ross used this intro to draw a parallel between his life and Mike Tyson’s, by comparing Mike’s championship belts to his albums and accomplishments in his rap career.", "annotation_id": "536518", "url": "https://genius.com/536518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Got the forty by my dick I keep on pissin’ on the hammer", "vault_lines": ["Got the forty by my dick I keep on pissin' on the hammer"], "meaning": "Double Entendre Alert!\nTrue gangstas carry the 40 cal in their pants close to their peen. “40” also meaning a 40 oz malt liquor, alcohol notoriously makes everyone urinate more frequently, hence the “I keep on pissin'” – his dick being the hammer.", "annotation_id": "535653", "url": "https://genius.com/535653", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "On the road to the riches until I’m paid in full And the Lord is my witness, I got a AK to pull", "vault_lines": ["On the road to the riches until I'm paid in full", "And the Lord is my witness, I got a AK to pull"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is currently in pursuit of riches and won’t stop until he has achieved what he believes he is worth; toting an AK47 for protection which he is ready to fire if he needs to.\n\nThis is also a play on two classic albums by New York MCs Eric B and Rakim (Paid in Full) and Kool G Rap and DJ Polo (Road To The Riches)", "annotation_id": "533423", "url": "https://genius.com/533423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "[Skit: Bill Whitaker & Mike Tyson]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is taken from a recent interview done by CBS news anchor Bill Whitaker in which Mike Tyson claims all his champion belts mean nothing to him anymore. It’s not the same as it used to be.", "annotation_id": "533387", "url": "https://genius.com/533387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Diamonds on my neck call it the ghetto’s guillotine", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds on my neck call it the ghetto's guillotine"], "meaning": "Probably Rick Ross' most Jay-Z esque line ever…A guillotine is this.\n\n\n\nBasically you put your neck in the hole and it decapitates you. The Bawse is saying that people strive for the diamonds, which we wear around our necks, and in pursuit of that we go so far that we die for it.\nWe go for the diamonds and we die for it. It takes our head in two ways. We wear it around our heads and we die for it (aka lose our heads which is death).", "annotation_id": "532266", "url": "https://genius.com/532266", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "When they talkin’ slick I double back with that banana", "vault_lines": ["When they talkin' slick I double back with that banana"], "meaning": "Some gun magazines get the nickname “banana clip” because of the shape of the case. Don’t talk shit about Ross, or he’ll be glad to give you a healthy serving of his “fruit”…", "annotation_id": "531379", "url": "https://genius.com/531379", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Pacquiao purse, boy I took another belt", "vault_lines": ["Pacquiao purse, boy I took another belt"], "meaning": "In boxing, a “purse” refers to the payout scheme to the boxers which includes sources of income from: PPV sales, live ticket sales, and a guaranteed sum from the promotor(s) and venue of the fight.  “Pacquiao purse” refers to the purse / amount of money that world-class boxer Manny Pacquiao  recieves from his bouts.  Ross claims to have a comparable amount (I mean, he named his mixtape Rich Forever).\nHe continues to to use this boxing theme to say he took (bought) another belt (probably something luxury like Louie Vatton), while still referencing the amount of championship title belts that Manny Pacquiao has.", "annotation_id": "531287", "url": "https://genius.com/531287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "High Definition", "line": "Crucifix on my neck I pray it never melt", "vault_lines": ["Crucifix on my neck I pray it never melt"], "meaning": "Among his array of jewelry that he flaunts on his neck, there is a crucifix (sign of the Christian cross w/ Jesus on it) piece.", "annotation_id": "531285", "url": "https://genius.com/531285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
