{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hit U from the Back", "line": "Flippin’ chickens for the sushi", "vault_lines": ["Flippin' chickens for the sushi"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is delving into some clever wordplay using two different types of food.\n\nChickens here means cocaine, a drug commonly referred to as birds. In rap you’ll hear the term slangin' birds or flip a bird a lot. Hell, a rapper named himself after it\n\nAnyway, he’s selling cocaine so he can enjoy the high life. Being poor, he is unable to afford the finer things, here the finer things are characterized as “sushi”, a fancy Japaneese food.", "annotation_id": "998661", "url": "https://genius.com/998661", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hit U from the Back", "line": "Don P every glass", "vault_lines": ["Don P every glass"], "meaning": "Short for Don Perignon, a fancy champagne that would be typical of the Teflon Don to drink every glass.", "annotation_id": "458642", "url": "https://genius.com/458642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
