{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "Chunk a deuce, sip a deuce", "vault_lines": ["Chunk a deuce, sip a deuce"], "meaning": "Chunking up a deuce is throwing up a “Peace sign with your hand ✌️ (“deuces”)\n\nDeuce or deuces usually correlate with the number 2. In a peace sign you throw up 2 fingers. You “chunk up a deuce”", "annotation_id": "3324645", "url": "https://genius.com/3324645", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "Dade County Big Cheese", "vault_lines": ["Smoking on the (Mint leaves), Dade County Big Cheese"], "meaning": "Dade County is the most popular county in Miami, Florida. Big Cheese is a popular restaurant in Dade County where many Miami athletes visit. Rick Ross is shouting out his county.", "annotation_id": "7894280", "url": "https://genius.com/7894280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "I’m a GRiT Boy looking for a ass like Ki Toy", "vault_lines": ["I'm a GRiT Boy looking for a ass like Ki Toy"], "meaning": "GRiT stands for Ghetto Reality in Texas, coined by the Houton rap crew the GRiT Boys\n\nPaul Wall wasn’t in the group, but uses the phrase GRiT boy to identify himself as a fellow Houstonian hustler.\n\nKi Toy Johnson is a model/actress with a rather large booty.", "annotation_id": "3324503", "url": "https://genius.com/3324503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "Nigga, I ain’t Will Smith, nah, I ain’t a Fresh Prince (Uh-uh) Nigga, I’m a young king, nigga, I’m a Bun B (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, I ain't Will Smith, nah, I ain't a Fresh Prince (Uh-uh)", "Nigga, I'm a young king, nigga, I'm a Bun B (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Wayne distances himself from Will Smith’s squeaky clean image.\n\nWill Smith rapped as The Fresh Prince in the duo DJ Jazzy Jeff & The Fresh Prince and starred as The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air.\n\n\n\nRather than a prince, Wayne suggests he’s a king.\n\nBun B was a member of rap duo UGK (Underground Kingz).", "annotation_id": "3324323", "url": "https://genius.com/3324323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "It’s Cash Money, baby (Yeah), It’s Young Money, bitch (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["It's Cash Money, baby (Yeah), It's Young Money, bitch (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Wayne founded the label Young Money Entertainment as an imprint of Cash Money Records, which was founded by Baby (aka Birdman)", "annotation_id": "3143226", "url": "https://genius.com/3143226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "It’s— Paul Wall, baby, Swishahouse club rocker", "vault_lines": ["It's— Paul Wall, baby, Swishahouse club rocker"], "meaning": "Paul Wall was signed to the Houston-based record label Swishahouse", "annotation_id": "3143218", "url": "https://genius.com/3143218", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "I owe my future: the last name Campbell, first name Luther", "vault_lines": ["I owe my future: the last name Campbell, first name Luther"], "meaning": "Luther Campbell’s Luke Records signed Pitbull to his first record deal in 2001, and Pitbull’s first break came in the form of appearing on Campbell’s single “Lollipop.” (YouTube link – not on RG yet)\n\nLuther Campbell aka Luke Skywalker aka Uncle Luke is the quintessential Miami rapper and headed the group 2 Live Crew", "annotation_id": "2479376", "url": "https://genius.com/2479376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holla at Me", "line": "You got the right one (Yeah), it’s Weezy Fuckin’ Baby (Yeah) And if your woman looking (Yeah), I’ll let the woman taste me (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["And if your woman looking (Yeah), I'll let the woman taste me (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne starts the track off right, letting everyone know that their women can all get free samples of his downstairs mixup", "annotation_id": "2166308", "url": "https://genius.com/2166308", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
