{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "Even my lawyer be askin is it dope", "vault_lines": ["Even my lawyer be askin is it dope"], "meaning": "Double entendre!\n\n\nRoss' defense attorney is asking if Ross really does sell cocaine probably because Ross' networth is so high the lawyer can’t believe it all comes from rap (especially when the DA is trying to bring Ross up on drug related charges).\nThe lawyer wonders how dope the pussy is that Ross is fucking (referring back to the previous line).", "annotation_id": "938707", "url": "https://genius.com/938707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "I’m forever dope, touched by the Holy Ghost", "vault_lines": ["I'm forever dope, touched by the Holy Ghost"], "meaning": "“I’m forever dope” is Ross telling the listeners that much like his bank roll will always be large, he’s also going to be the shit until the end of time.\n\n“Touched by the Holy Ghost” (or Holy Spirit)) is a common expression used in various languages, more popularly in Catholicism.", "annotation_id": "618946", "url": "https://genius.com/618946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "Talking to the Holy Ghost, in my Bugatti He knockin’ on the do’ don’t let the Devil in He knockin’ on the do’ don’t let the Devil in", "vault_lines": ["Talking to the Holy Ghost, in my Bugatti", "He knockin' on the do' don't let the Devil in"], "meaning": "The Holy Ghost is the smoke that Rick Ross is blazing in his car. It is so thick and clowdy he refers to it as the Holy Ghost. The devil is the cops like when they knock on your door window when you do something wrong like speeding or smoking weed in your car. Rick compares the two like a religious experience. Also if the ‘devil’ comes in then the Holy Ghost will leave…he doesn’t want that.\n\nOh… And this is a Bugatti:", "annotation_id": "588159", "url": "https://genius.com/588159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "They say I’m gettin’ money, must be Illuminati", "vault_lines": ["They say I'm gettin' money, must be Illuminati"], "meaning": "Some people (mostly paranoid and irrational idiots) believe that rappers have joined the devil-worshiping Illuminati when they start making a lot of money. This line is similar to Jay-Z’s line in Usher’s “Hot Tottie”:\n\nBig balling is my hobby\nSo much so they think I’m down with the Illuminati\n\n\n\nAnd for those of you who are still wondering (Like Kanye) “What the FUCK is the Illuminati… READ THIS", "annotation_id": "540564", "url": "https://genius.com/540564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "I got the calico, I got the dynamite They wanna do it big? Pick a time tonight", "vault_lines": ["I got the calico, I got the dynamite", "They wanna do it big? Pick a time tonight"], "meaning": "Rozay invites his enemies to bring tha muthafuckin' ruckus. He’ll willingly catch a body.\n\nThe Calico M960 is a 9mm semi-automatic gun. Dynamite = bombs.", "annotation_id": "539083", "url": "https://genius.com/539083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "Work! That’s all my niggas workin’ with Work! That’s all my niggas lurkin’ with", "vault_lines": ["Work! That's all my niggas workin' with", "Work! That's all my niggas lurkin' with"], "meaning": "Besides being one of Wale’s new ad-libs, work here is associated with crack cocaine. That’s all his boys work and move with.\n\nRoss has a history of whippin' up work.", "annotation_id": "532175", "url": "https://genius.com/532175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "Touch him with the Holy Ghost, can you hear me Father?", "vault_lines": ["Touch him with the Holy Ghost, can you hear me Father?"], "meaning": "Ross pleads for God to hear him out.\n\nAdditionally, “Father” might also mean Rick Ross’s father, who died of liver cancer in 1999.\"\n\nPassed in ‘99 cancer all in his liver\nShit different since we last spoke; his son’s a lil richer\nI’d never rap again if I could tell him that I miss him\n\nIf so, the Holy Ghost would be conduit linking Ross to his dead father.", "annotation_id": "532159", "url": "https://genius.com/532159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "Got the phone tapped, I think I’m being followed", "vault_lines": ["Got the phone tapped, I think I'm being followed"], "meaning": "Ross, being the yayo-pushing kingpin he is, has his phone tapped.\n\nApparently, his car’s OnStar is also tapped.\n\nHe also sarcastically plays on “followed,” continuing the Twitter allusion in the line above.", "annotation_id": "532157", "url": "https://genius.com/532157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "Being dead broke is the root of all evil", "vault_lines": ["Being dead broke is the root of all evil"], "meaning": "People do wrong because they are poor. Ross seems to believe a bit different from 1 Timothy 6:10:\n\nFor the love of money is the root of all evil: which while some coveted after, they have erred from the faith, and pierced themselves through with many sorrows.\n\nThen again, this absence of money might make someone love it even more than they normally would.", "annotation_id": "531937", "url": "https://genius.com/531937", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Holy Ghost", "line": "Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do", "vault_lines": ["Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do"], "meaning": "This line bears an eery similarity to one Diddy had on Biggie’s “Notorious Thugz”\n\nWe forgive you, for you know not what you do.\n\nIn both instances, he biting a phrase that Jesus said on the cross.\n\nThen said Jesus, Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do.", "annotation_id": "531907", "url": "https://genius.com/531907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
