{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "305 niggas, we gon’ get it right", "vault_lines": ["305 niggas, we gon' get it right"], "meaning": "Ross is from Miami, Florida, and 305 is the area code for Miami.", "annotation_id": "4445059", "url": "https://genius.com/4445059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Philly niggas, know we gon’ get it right Dreamchasers, we gon’ get it right Shoot and run, we gon’ get it right", "vault_lines": ["Philly niggas, know we gon' get it right", "Dreamchasers, we gon' get it right", "Shoot and run, we gon' get it right"], "meaning": "Ross shoutsouts label mate Meek Mill’s city Philadelphia.\n\nDream Chasers is Meek’s own label, which is distributed under Ross' MMG imprint.", "annotation_id": "4444843", "url": "https://genius.com/4444843", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Make the most in the Ghost, fuck Huffington Post Young brother Rolls, Belaire Rose, I’m makin’ a toast At the Heat game, talkin’ all cash Still tweetin’ while ya’ll eatin’ out of our trash", "vault_lines": ["Make the most in the Ghost, fuck Huffington Post", "Young brother Rolls, Belaire Rose, I'm makin' a toast", "At the Heat game, talkin' all cash"], "meaning": "Once again Ross mentions one of his rides, this time the Rolls Royce Ghost. While he makes a toast with expensive champagne at the Miami Heat game, he’s tweeting and hating on Huffington Post.\n\nAs far as the Huffo shoutout, it could for a number of negative articles – Rick Ross Arrested After Concert In North Carolina, Rick Ross Date Rape or their continued coverage of his arch nemesis Freeway Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "4444835", "url": "https://genius.com/4444835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Let me show you how to get right, whip an ounce of that white Fast forward to a brick, now you livin’ that life", "vault_lines": ["Let me show you how to get right, whip an ounce of that white", "Fast forward to a brick, now you livin' that life"], "meaning": "Rozay alludes to cooking crack cocaine. One must whip the product over a stove mixed with water and baking soda.\n\n\n\nThis waters down the product, but flips it from an ounce to a kilo (brick).", "annotation_id": "4444812", "url": "https://genius.com/4444812", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "All I talk is that cash, Versace all in my bag Dope all in my vein, hoes hollin’ my name White T still pimpin, Lenox Mall in a Bentley He a fuckboy, that’s simple, I ain’t into what he into Hoes wave to my window, keep a pile of that endo I always got bond money, you don’t know what I’ve been through", "vault_lines": ["He a fuckboy, that's simple, I ain't into what he into", "Hoes wave to my window, keep a pile of that endo", "I always got bond money, you don't know what I've been through"], "meaning": "My bitch bad, looking like a bag of money\nThat bitch bad, looking like a bag of money\n\nRoss keeps things fresh with Versace,  a white tee, blunts and some cash in Lenox Mall, Georgia.\n\nWhite tees are synonymous with street culture, while Versace and Bentley are traditionally upper class. Along with a reference to bail bonds,  this defines Ross' concept as a Hood Billionaire.", "annotation_id": "4444786", "url": "https://genius.com/4444786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "20 for the bird, better get it right Got a bag of money, nigga get it right", "vault_lines": ["20 for the bird, better get it right", "Got a bag of money, nigga get it right"], "meaning": "Rozay is getting top dollar for his product! 20k is a few thousand more than most people would expect to pay for a kilo of coke. He doesn’t just carry money in pockets, wallets, or on a plastic card; he carries them in bags. Moneybags Ross, how G is that?", "annotation_id": "4442666", "url": "https://genius.com/4442666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "30 franchises, show you what this pot make", "vault_lines": ["30 franchises, show you what this pot make"], "meaning": "Adding to claims of material wealth in the lines above he states his wealth came from cooking crack cocaine, often done in a pyrex pot.\n\nThis line highlights his rags to riches story in where he went from selling crack to owning 30 franchises. He owns various Wing Stop franchises, that sell chicken wings. It costs between $200,000 – $650,000 to start a Wing Stop restaurant per the company’s website – he’s made it big.", "annotation_id": "4438943", "url": "https://genius.com/4438943", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "All white me gusta, oh hallelujah Oh hallelujah, oh I maneuver", "vault_lines": ["All white me gusta, oh hallelujah", "Oh hallelujah, oh I maneuver"], "meaning": "“Me gusta” in Spanish translates to “I like it”. Ross really likes the color white. Ross also emphasizes the  purity of the color by using another ethnic term: “Hallelujah”– “Praise the Lord”.", "annotation_id": "4438896", "url": "https://genius.com/4438896", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Pull up with 20 bitches on the hundred footer", "vault_lines": ["Pull up with 20 bitches on the hundred footer"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to a 100 foot yacht:\n\n\n\nHaving 20 bitches on a 100 foot yacht is an opulent status symbol; considering they retail around $8-10 million dollars.", "annotation_id": "4438887", "url": "https://genius.com/4438887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Opa Locka’ niggas, still got them quarters Overtown niggas (billionaire), still movin’ water", "vault_lines": ["Opa Locka' niggas, still got them quarters", "Overtown niggas (billionaire), still movin' water"], "meaning": "Opa-Locka is a hood in Miami-Dade County, Florida not far south of where Ross was raised. Opa-Locka hustlers had the quater pounds of “what you need” when Ross was a young hustler. All these years later nothing has changed.\n\nOvertown is also a neighborhood in the greater Miami area, which was once titled “Colored Town”, because of its prominent colored population.\n\nContinuing off the previous lines, Ross is simply shouting out all his hustlers in all the various hoods of Miami.", "annotation_id": "4429703", "url": "https://genius.com/4429703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Nigga, tell your pops I got a million dollar watch All you fake watch bustas, I’m the one to watch Rolls Royce fake and my two yachts fake", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, tell your pops I got a million dollar watch", "All you fake watch bustas, I'm the one to watch", "Rolls Royce fake and my two yachts fake"], "meaning": "According to the Instagram account fakewatchbusta, Rick Ross was spotted wearing a fake Audemars Piguet watch in the Veteran’s Day music video:\n\n\n\nRoss is mocking these allegations. Yachts are something that you can’t fake the production of; they separate the ultra rich from the rich.", "annotation_id": "4428568", "url": "https://genius.com/4428568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Carol City niggas, still 187 Lil’ Haiti niggas, still 211", "vault_lines": ["Carol City niggas, still 187", "Lil' Haiti niggas, still 211"], "meaning": "Rozay was raised in Carol City, Florida. 187 is the police code for homicide, while 211 is for robbery. Little Haiti is a few blocks from Carol City.\n\nHis homies are still committing crimes. Whether that is figuratively or metaphorically – that’s up to you.\n\nRoss begins to shout out his Miami hustlers in this line, and continues in the next few lines.", "annotation_id": "4428529", "url": "https://genius.com/4428529", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "I went and bought your bitch a washer and a dryer Seen it in your son’s face, I’m who he admires", "vault_lines": ["Seen it in your son's face, I'm who he admires"], "meaning": "Ross is a real Hood Billionaire, like the great Bunkie Brown, former “Mayor” of Overtown, MI-YAYO.\n\nBunkie would provide for the whole community:\nhttps://youtu.be/cCHcInJ3Mfg?t=59m50s\n\nRoss learned from Bunkie and others like him that the Hood Billionaire provides for his people.\n\nThis girl’s son now respects Ross more than his own father because of Ross' generosity.", "annotation_id": "4416333", "url": "https://genius.com/4416333", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "I done fucked all these bitches, I can’t even name ’em But if the bitch is bad, bring her, yellow stone on my finger Mink coat, mine cheetah, before I fuck I’m gon’ eat her", "vault_lines": ["Mink coat, mine cheetah, before I fuck I'm gon' eat her"], "meaning": "Ross has had so many high status relationships that even if he wanted to remember the girls names, he wouldn’t due to un-wanted publicity.\n\nDespite this he’s not slowing down  - he’s more than happy to entertain more bad bitches in mink coats to go down on.", "annotation_id": "4416302", "url": "https://genius.com/4416302", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Kilo at the telly, bitch it’s Makiaveli", "vault_lines": ["Kilo at the telly, bitch it's Makiaveli"], "meaning": "Top down, tank top, I think I’m 2Pac\nSo I’m labeled the rebel, nigga get on my level\n\nRozay draws an comparison between himself and 2Pac – he insists he’s as real as one of the greats. Rozay also expresses this by telling us he’s dealing cocaine in a hotel room. The feds know about dealing or trading drugs in a motel so it is the most obvious thing you can do.", "annotation_id": "4403398", "url": "https://genius.com/4403398", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Now I think I’m Don Shula", "vault_lines": ["Now I think I'm Don Shula"], "meaning": "First he thinks he’s Big Meech, now he thinks he’s Don Shula.\n\nDon Shula is a legendary football coach, who is most famous for his tenure with Ross' hometown Miami Dolphins.\n\nShula is the winningest coach in Miami Dolphins and football history, having complied an NFL record 328 wins (257 with Miami). He coached the Dolphins to the franchise’s only two Super Bowl wins, including the 1972 Dolphins; the only team to win the Super Bowl following a perfect season. The 17-0 Fins are often considered one of the greatest, if not the greatest NFL team of all time.", "annotation_id": "4400245", "url": "https://genius.com/4400245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Icy on the court at the basketball games", "vault_lines": ["Icy on the court at the basketball games"], "meaning": "Rozay is a huge fan of the Miami Heat – he’s even willing to bet $100k that they’ll finish with a better record than the Cavaliers for the 2015 NBA season. He can frequently be seen sitting courtside at Heat games, flashing the bling and posing for the jumbotron.", "annotation_id": "4400122", "url": "https://genius.com/4400122", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "I can get you that in my hood, I’m a billionaire in my hood Tryna buy a piece of the Dolphins, 5% and I’m good", "vault_lines": ["Tryna buy a piece of the Dolphins, 5% and I'm good"], "meaning": "Rick Ross mentioned he had a conversation about purchasing a stake with the Miami Dolphins ownership back in October, in an interview with Angie Martinez. It’s possible he was referencing this line.\n\nI went and sat down with the Miami Dolphins, we discussed a few things. You know I’ve been interested in trying to buy a small percentage of the Dolphins for a long time and they finally invited me into the office and I sat with some people. It was a real positive conversation, and when we left, they offered me to walk out through the field. It was sprayed for the game the following day, and I walked out on the field, I was excited. I put it on the table and there was a few things they wanted to ask and discuss and so forth. But it was a positive situation…. They ultimately decide if the time is now, or does it happen at all. I just wanted to let them know I’m a huge supporter. I would bring them a positive energy to the set, ya dig?", "annotation_id": "4400104", "url": "https://genius.com/4400104", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "Double M empire, I know these niggas fear me", "vault_lines": ["Double M empire, I know these niggas fear me"], "meaning": "Ross shouts out his MMG brethren. The label is known as the double M empire and more commonly Maybach Music group. Ross' partners in crime like Wale, Meek Mill & Gunplay have been at the top for a minute now.", "annotation_id": "4396917", "url": "https://genius.com/4396917", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hood Billionaire", "line": "I’m already rich, I’m tired of bein’ famous", "vault_lines": ["I'm already rich, I'm tired of bein' famous"], "meaning": "Like DJ Khaled said – Rozay is Suffering from Success. He’s already filthy rich! and tired of the paparazzi and the lack of privacy.", "annotation_id": "4395475", "url": "https://genius.com/4395475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
