{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "How We Do It", "line": "Killing the game damn I think I need my lawyer here (2x)", "vault_lines": ["Killing the game damn I think I need my lawyer here (2x)"], "meaning": "Since he commited homicide, Ross is gonna need his lawyer to defend him; to keep him away from his ex-boss and coworkers.", "annotation_id": "683832", "url": "https://genius.com/683832", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "How We Do It", "line": "I used to fail math as an adolescent", "vault_lines": ["I used to fail math as an adolescent"], "meaning": "Math is a very difficult subject to master.\nRoss admitted this in a Rolling Stone interview:\n\n“I got through high school on my popularity and shit,” Ross says. “But my grades was never good. I was never good at math.”\n\nIronically, he requires that math now to count his ever mounting cash.", "annotation_id": "683529", "url": "https://genius.com/683529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "How We Do It", "line": "Bummy clothes hoes used to laugh at us Now I close deals like I’m athletic", "vault_lines": ["Bummy clothes hoes used to laugh at us", "Now I close deals like I'm athletic"], "meaning": "Back in the day, Ross was raised in poverty and probably couldn’t afford fine clothing. He even had to be a corrections officer just to make ends meet. Even the less-stylish girls used to mock him.\n\nA couple years later, he’s the successful rapper who’s making deals and endorsements on a daily basis. The women who used to shun him now find his success attractive. A perfect rags to riches story.", "annotation_id": "683504", "url": "https://genius.com/683504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
