{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hungry", "line": "Well maybe conflict made it the new flavor in your ear", "vault_lines": ["Well maybe conflict made it the new flavor in your ear"], "meaning": "Never sleep on Fergie’s talent. She can drop some bars! “Flavor in your Ear” by Craig Mack was released in 1994. The remix went on to feature heavy hitters Notorious B.I.G., LL Cool J & Busta Rhymes. The video pays homage to the Warriors movie with Puff Daddy himself\n\n\n\n smacking bottles together saying, “Bad Boy come out and play..”", "annotation_id": "13363505", "url": "https://genius.com/13363505", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hungry", "line": "El Chapo", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Joaquín “El Chapo” Guzmán is one of the most notorious drug lords from Mexico. He rose up the ranks of the drug cartels in the 80s and 90s before affirming his position as the number 1 crime boss in 2003. He has been arrested several times, and also escaped several times. He was most recently extradited to the US in January 2016, and is awaiting trial.\n\nRick references El Chapo’s success and hunger to become a boss rather than a mere sicario or drug mule.", "annotation_id": "12579879", "url": "https://genius.com/12579879", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hungry", "line": "I fuck up money like I’m Escobar", "vault_lines": ["I fuck up money like I'm Escobar"], "meaning": "Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949 – 1993) was the most powerful drug trafficker in the Colombian mafia and leader of the Medellin cartel in the late 80s-early 90s. Once he consolidated his criminal empire he became the most powerful man in the country let alone the Colombian mafia. He accumulated an immense fortune, estimated around $25-30 billion USD, thus confirming him as one of the richest men in the world. He even made the 1987 Forbes list of world’s richest men.\n\n\n\nRick aligns himself with Escobar’s success and notoriety, a common analogy for rappers to make. Pablo Escobar’s story has increased in popularity recently due to the success of Netflix’s Narcos series (Season 3 was released around the same time as Double Dutchess).", "annotation_id": "12588896", "url": "https://genius.com/12588896", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
