{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hurt Nobody", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-dred-hurt-nobody-lyrics", "genius_title": "Hurt Nobody", "genius_id": 3393281, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle", "line": "I pray so long, He sees my faults", "vault_lines": ["I pray so long, He sees my faults"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is open about his faith in a lot of his bars and here is another  example of his expression of faith. He states that he spends so much time in prayer because He (capitalized when referring to God) considers prayer as a form of communication. Prayer is the most common way a religious person can communicate with God. While talking to God, He is passing judgement onto Rick Ross' actions and points out the fault in these actions for Rick Ross to notice, understand, and ultimately repent", "annotation_id": "16124099", "url": "https://genius.com/16124099", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle", "line": "I act so frio", "vault_lines": ["Packaged like fritos I act so frio"], "meaning": "As mentioned in a previous annotation, Rick Ross uses the spanish word for “cold” here.\nHe says I act so ‘cold’. Frio is the spanish word for cold.\n\nhttps://www.google.com/search?q=frio+to+english&oq=frio+to+english&aqs=chrome.0.0l6.3318j1j7&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8", "annotation_id": "16124093", "url": "https://genius.com/16124093", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle", "line": "I beep my plug , Javi got me", "vault_lines": ["I beep my plug , Javi got me"], "meaning": "Classic Rick Ross drug dealer talk. In this bar, he raps about having to page his latino drug dealer likely named Javier who he abbreviates as “Javi”. We can assume his drug dealer is latino because Javier is a common latino name and Rick Ross adds a spanish word to one of his bars soon after this one.", "annotation_id": "16124079", "url": "https://genius.com/16124079", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle", "line": "’ricans", "vault_lines": ["Knew a few 'ricans"], "meaning": "‘ricans is shorthand for Puerto Ricans. It isn’t a derogatory term at all, its just used to abbreviate the title of Puerto Ricans.", "annotation_id": "16124072", "url": "https://genius.com/16124072", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Camron-and-vado-hustle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Hustle", "genius_id": 4196297, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Swagger just dumb, call it Kelly Bundy", "vault_lines": ["Swagger just dumb, call it Kelly Bundy"], "meaning": "Kelly Bundy was the on screen name for actress  Christina Applegate, for the TV series “Married…With Children” that ran from 1987 to 1997.  It was about what a steriotypical low income family lives like.  The dad is a heavy drinker who displays anti-social characteristics, a lazy wife who doesnt do any of the submissive tasks around the house like was expected of woman back then (cleaning, cooking, laundry.  They used her lack of doing this as laugh tracks when the dad would get upset by it.  A son who isnt very good with women ( I guess this was a huge unspoken fear of many fathers back then.  That their son would be gay/suck with women). And finally Kelly, the slutty extra stupid daughter.", "annotation_id": "23994767", "url": "https://genius.com/23994767", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "I eat these rappers, Anthony Hopkins", "vault_lines": ["Young money we poppin', I eat these rappers, Anthony Hopkins"], "meaning": "Anthony Hopkins played Hannibal Lecter in The Silence of the Lambs and its spin offs, as a super genius (people who are freakishly smart, they make genius’s look like average intelligence) who eats people – cannibalism.", "annotation_id": "23994753", "url": "https://genius.com/23994753", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Riding round in that ’Gatti", "vault_lines": [", riding round in that 'Gatti"], "meaning": "“gatti” is slang for a Bogatti super car.", "annotation_id": "23994751", "url": "https://genius.com/23994751", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Ok, now, black card in my pocket", "vault_lines": ["Ok, now, black card in my pocket"], "meaning": "A ‘Black Card’ is the level of credit card that companies offer that have no spending/credit limit.  You can buy a multi-million dollar house with one, etc.  It is usually offered to either the super rich or perfect credit holders.", "annotation_id": "23994734", "url": "https://genius.com/23994734", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Choppers only thing free niggas (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["No, you bitches can't hit my weed, choppers only thing free niggas (Huh)"], "meaning": "A ‘Chopper’ is an AK47 assault rifle. They are saying only violence/gun deaths free the black person.", "annotation_id": "23994692", "url": "https://genius.com/23994692", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "19 in my nina (woo), red dot when I ride up", "vault_lines": ["19 in my nina (woo), red dot when I ride up"], "meaning": "Nina, or Nina Ross, is a slang term for a 9mm pistol.  19 either references the Glock 19 which has an ideal shorter barrel then the Glock 17.  Or it means how many rounds the pistol has, indicating an extended clip is being used, along with a red dot sight attachment for precision aim.", "annotation_id": "23994676", "url": "https://genius.com/23994676", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "24's on my Bimmer (woo)", "vault_lines": ["24's on my Bimmer (woo)"], "meaning": "“The correct term for a BMW automobile is “bimmer” – “beemer” and “beamer” actually only refer to a BMW motorcycle. ”\nSource:\nhttps://www.bmw.com/en/automotive-life/bimmer-beamer-nickname-origin.html", "annotation_id": "23994656", "url": "https://genius.com/23994656", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Closed mouths don’t get fed on this boulevard", "vault_lines": ["Closed mouths don't get fed on this boulevard"], "meaning": "The ‘Closed mouths don’t get fed’ means if you do not ask for what you want/need, you will not get it.  If you wanna smash, ask to smash, or you may miss a chance at sex kinda thing. Or drugs.  It rarely actually means food/eating.", "annotation_id": "23994635", "url": "https://genius.com/23994635", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Got a red bone, she look tropic", "vault_lines": ["Got a red bone, she look tropic"], "meaning": "Red bone means light skin and tropic meaning she is exotic looking like Brazillian.\n\nThis line and the next were sampled for the hook to “Redbone” by Timbaland, Petey Pablo and Sebastian.", "annotation_id": "107413", "url": "https://genius.com/107413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Hundred deep in that K.O.D, King Of Diamonds, that’s me, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Hundred deep in that K.O.D, King Of Diamonds, that's me, nigga"], "meaning": "He’s in the strip club King of Diamonds with hundreds of people throwing money.\n\nRoss was named the actual “King Of Diamonds” for throwing 1 million in 1’s at his birthday party.", "annotation_id": "105863", "url": "https://genius.com/105863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Bitch, my league too major I’m hip-hop Derek Jeter", "vault_lines": [", bitch, my league too major", "I'm hip-hop Derek Jeter"], "meaning": "Ace hood is a veteran in the game and a household name #thatswhathesaysanyway\n\nOn another note, Derek Jeter is one of the biggest names in Major League Baseball today. He recently achieved a milestone that only 27 players did before him: collect 3,000 career hits. Now he can officially be called Mr. 3000.\n\n\n\nIf Ace Hood is calling himself the “Mr. 3000” of hip-hop, I don’t think this guy would agree, to say the least.", "annotation_id": "104566", "url": "https://genius.com/104566", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "They want that Carter IV, bitch, it’s coming soon", "vault_lines": ["They want that Carter IV, bitch, it’s coming soon"], "meaning": "During the time Wayne was recording this, Wayne’s long awaited album Tha carter IV is going to be released shortly: August 29, 2011, to be exact.\n\nFact: Weezy began the process of making this album in October 2008… which shows how long people have been waiting for this.", "annotation_id": "101749", "url": "https://genius.com/101749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "And I’m all about the new Franklins (franklins) Ain’t talkin’ Aretha", "vault_lines": ["And I'm all about the new Franklins (franklins)"], "meaning": "Franklins, in this instance refer to US $100 bills, as Benjamin Franklin features on them, not to be confused with, the singer, songwriter, Aretha Franklin\n\n\n\nThere’s also a new 100 dollar bill that’s gone into circulation as of February 2011 which includes a 3D Security Ribbon and a color-changing inkwell! Oooohh!", "annotation_id": "100689", "url": "https://genius.com/100689", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Hustle Hard (Remix)", "line": "Grilled up like Ocho", "vault_lines": ["See that V-neck? That's Polo, grilled up like Ocho"], "meaning": "NFL wide receiver Chad “Ochocinco” Johnson, shortened to “ocho”, had a mean grill when he played for the Cincinnati Bengals. Check them teeth.\n\n\n\nChad and Wayne are very good friends by the way.\n\n\n\nThe line also refers to OCHO’s Mexican Grill Restaurant in LA.", "annotation_id": "100668", "url": "https://genius.com/100668", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
