{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Got No Time", "line": "Dunk Ryder but none of my niggas suffering", "vault_lines": ["Dunk Ryder but none of my niggas suffering"], "meaning": "A shot fired at Ross' former mentor, Trick Daddy regarding the label situation of Iceberg.\n\n\n\nThe Dunk Ryders are rap group from Miami founded by Trick Daddy, Iceberg, and Fella. They have since grown to include numerous rappers.\n\n\n\nIceberg is signed to Trick Daddy, who refuses to put him on, or let him out of his contract. Ross has made it clear he wishes to sign Iceberg to MMG, however he is still under contract with Trick and can’t jump ship due to all the restrictions that Trick’s brother, Charles Young Jr aka Chuck, has set forth.\n\n\n\nWhile Trick Daddy’s artist suffer, Ross' artists clearly don’t.\n\n\nGunplay has recently signed a solo deal with Def Jam and is prepping his debut studio album.\nMeek Mill has released several mixtapes which have toppled download records and his debut album Dreams & Nightmares, debuted high on the Billboard charts.\nWale released his MMG debut album Ambition, which has been certified gold and Wale was nominated for a Grammy award as well.\nOmarion has released a Care Package EP and has announced his MMG debut studio album, Love & Other Drugs.\nStalley & Rockie Fresh have put out mixtapes – Savage Journey To The American Dream & Electric Highway as well, and are both prepping their MMG debut studio albums too.\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/309145497120165890", "annotation_id": "1559462", "url": "https://genius.com/1559462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Got No Time", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Ice-billion-berg-i-aint-got-no-time-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Ain’t Got No Time", "genius_id": 124160, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Worried", "line": "Ain’t no game, this ain’t Nintendo", "vault_lines": ["Ain't no game, this ain't Nintendo"], "meaning": "This line is similar to the line Eminem stated in his song “Love The Way You Lie”:\n\n“You don’t get another chance, life is no Nintendo game”\n\nAce Hood doesn’t play around because life doesn’t always give second chances. Ace will do whatever he has to do to provide for his family. This moral has been seen in several rap songs such as “100 Foreva” and “No Games”.", "annotation_id": "8038448", "url": "https://genius.com/8038448", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Worried", "line": "Ferrari doin’ donuts", "vault_lines": ["All my nerves best rolla, Ferrari doin' donuts"], "meaning": "As a matter of fact, Ace Hood owns a Ferrari.\n\n\n\nI doubt Ace Hood won´t be pullin some donuts on his Ferrari.", "annotation_id": "8038060", "url": "https://genius.com/8038060", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Worried", "line": "I ain’t worried, I ain’t worried Every time I jump on a beat, these niggas get nervous Ho naw, I ain’t worried, just know I ain’t worried Rap game that’s mine due time ain’t lyin’, y’all gotta be worried Ho naw, I ain’t worried, these niggas ain’t worthy Long as my family straight, you know homeboy I ain’t worried Ho naw, I ain’t worried, ain’t worried bout ’em Ain’t worried bout ’em, naw", "vault_lines": ["Rap game that's mine due time ain't lyin', y'all gotta be worried", "Ho naw, I ain't worried, these niggas ain't worthy", "Long as my family straight, you know homeboy I ain't worried", "Ho naw, I ain't worried, ain't worried bout 'em", "Ain't worried bout 'em, naw"], "meaning": "Ace Hood shares the same concept as French Montana in his song, “Ain’t Worried About Nothin”. Ace is the new guy in the rap industry and puts fear into the competition. Ace won’t worry about the opposition because he doesn’t interact with them.", "annotation_id": "8033685", "url": "https://genius.com/8033685", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Worried", "line": "Ain’t worried bout a damn thing, young nigga big nuts, ha!", "vault_lines": ["Ain't worried bout a damn thing, young nigga big nuts, ha!"], "meaning": "What has Ace Hood got to worry about? His young, got big nuts, lots of money and everything he could wish for.", "annotation_id": "8033197", "url": "https://genius.com/8033197", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Worried", "line": "Laughing at all you rap niggas out tryna sound like Hood You can keep that flow, hope it tastes good", "vault_lines": ["Laughing at all you rap niggas out tryna sound like Hood", "You can keep that flow, hope it tastes good"], "meaning": "Ace Hood is laughing at all these rappers because they are trying to sound like him. Ace doesn’t care because he is always improving and getting better and moves on before that style gets ‘old’.", "annotation_id": "8033194", "url": "https://genius.com/8033194", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Worried", "line": "This We the Best Music, WTB", "vault_lines": ["This We the Best Music, WTB"], "meaning": "We the Best Music (Group) is a record label that was founded by DJ Khaled in 2008. Members of this record label include: Ace Hood, Mavado, Vado, and Khaled himself.\n\nKhaled can be heard yelling “We the Best!” in most of his songs, such as “I’m So Hood”:\n\nDJ Khaled, we the best\nWho, we nigga? We the best", "annotation_id": "8023977", "url": "https://genius.com/8023977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Ain’t Worried", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-khaled-i-aint-worried-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Ain’t Worried", "genius_id": 2329498, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am The Streets", "line": "Me and Trae flying through Houston like Von Wafer You niggas ain’t balling, you T-Mack, you stay hurt", "vault_lines": ["Me and Trae flying through Houston like Von Wafer", "You niggas ain't balling, you T-Mack, you stay hurt"], "meaning": "Von Wafer is a basketball player, who was active for the Houston Rockets in 2009 and took the starting spot of Tracy McGrady (T-Mac). He was able to do so because Mac had to fight several injuries and he was performing well. But after one season he left the Rockets to play in Europe.\n\nLike the aforementioned events, Game and Trae ball in the city of Houston while others aren’t able to do so, which means to prosper financially.", "annotation_id": "6393665", "url": "https://genius.com/6393665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am The Streets", "line": "This the National Hood Geographics, call it bird watching", "vault_lines": ["This the National Hood Geographics, call it bird watching"], "meaning": "Like National Geographic makes documentaries about birds, you could see in Trae’s hood documentary worthy material about an other sort of birds – cocaine bricks.", "annotation_id": "6393640", "url": "https://genius.com/6393640", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am The Streets", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Trae-tha-truth-i-am-the-streets-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Am The Streets", "genius_id": 371278, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "I body bitches, go get the bandages", "vault_lines": ["And yes, I body bitches, go get the bandages"], "meaning": "Here, Minaj is saying she is thoroughly dominating and outperforming all of the other females in the rap game with “I body bitches.” ‘Bodying’ someone, in a more physical sense, can mean to beat them up, in which case the “bitches” would need bandages to heal.", "annotation_id": "40162627", "url": "https://genius.com/40162627", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Saint Nick, Ross, hey, Rick I just got a toy, cost eight fifty Now I’m in the hood, niggas is gettin’ woodies", "vault_lines": ["Saint Nick, Ross, hey, Rick", "I just got a toy, cost eight fifty", "Now I'm in the hood, niggas is gettin' woodies"], "meaning": "Seemingly an extended allusion to The Beach Boys: first to their classic Christmas single “Little Saint Nick” (1963), then to their beloved slang term “woodie” (a station wagon with a wooden exterior), used in various songs including “Boogie Woodie” (also 1963)—which makes sense since the “toy” she gets in the previous line is ostensibly a car", "annotation_id": "36999929", "url": "https://genius.com/36999929", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Yo, when I fly, it’s one letter and one number", "vault_lines": ["Yo, when I fly, it's one letter and one number"], "meaning": "When she flies as in traveling on a plane it’s one letter and one number as in a private jet which is named a G4", "annotation_id": "35527042", "url": "https://genius.com/35527042", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "After that, the Queen’ll still reign here", "vault_lines": ["After that, the Queen'll still reign here"], "meaning": "Reign is a homophone is this line. Previously mentioned, other rappers will only be “hot” for a short period of time, and once that time is over, Minaj will still reign as the Queen. “Reign”, can also be interpreted as “Rain,” tying more weather elements to the bar.", "annotation_id": "31277539", "url": "https://genius.com/31277539", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "You wack hoes could get hot for one summer", "vault_lines": ["You wack hoes could get hot for one summer"], "meaning": "Minaj states that other rappers don’t have longevity, and they are only popular for a short period of time.", "annotation_id": "31277532", "url": "https://genius.com/31277532", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Now I need a Aspirin; she said, “You’re only Cameron” Girlfriend, you don’t know Cameron from nowhere so don’t go tampering (Watch ya mouth)", "vault_lines": ["Girlfriend, you don't know Cameron from nowhere so don't go tampering (Watch ya mouth)"], "meaning": "This references Eminem’s lines in the third verse of his song “Superman”\n\nI don’t see what the big deal is anyway, you’re just plain old Marshall to me\n\nAnd the lines\n\nFirst off, you don’t know Marshall\nAt all, so don’t grow partial", "annotation_id": "30744125", "url": "https://genius.com/30744125", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "I am your leader, yes, I am your leader", "vault_lines": ["I am your leader, yes, I am your leader"], "meaning": "Reference to her line in Big Sean’s song “Dance [A$$] Remix”:\n\nBad bitches, I’m your leader\n\nWhich is what most likely inspired the name of this song.", "annotation_id": "29182633", "url": "https://genius.com/29182633", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Street fighter, bitches, this the up-cut-uh", "vault_lines": ["Street fighter, bitches, this the up-cut-uh"], "meaning": "A street fighter is a referance to Nicki Minaj alter ego Chun Li that alter ego made an apperance on Fire Ball and her hit song on her album Queen\n\n\n\nChun Li is also a game character", "annotation_id": "21967763", "url": "https://genius.com/21967763", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Go to Harlem and get Cam", "vault_lines": ["Go to Harlem and get Cam"], "meaning": "Featured artist Cam'ron hails from Harlem, New York. The two rejoined forces in 2013, on Cam'ron’s “So Bad.”", "annotation_id": "17703584", "url": "https://genius.com/17703584", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "I bought a couple nines, plus the Ks with me", "vault_lines": ["I bought a couple nines, plus the Ks with me"], "meaning": "Minaj uses her word play to refer to a canine dog, saying she bought her “dogs” with her a.k.a. her homies.\n\nWhen rappers say “9” they’re referring to The Intratec TEC-9, a blowback-operated semi-automatic pistol. And in this line Minaj uses “K” which is another gun, the AK-47, officially known as the Avtomat Kalashnikova.\n\nWatch out for her!", "annotation_id": "17228872", "url": "https://genius.com/17228872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Hit up Hot Topic, Nicki Minaj hoodies", "vault_lines": ["Hit up Hot Topic, Nicki Minaj hoodies"], "meaning": "Hot Topic is a retailer focused on selling pop culture merchandise and memorabilia. In the past, they’ve sold items like Nicki Minaj sweatshirts and physical copies of Pink Friday: Roman Reloaded.\n\n\n\nOne of the sweatshirts Hot Topic sold promoting Minaj.", "annotation_id": "17043919", "url": "https://genius.com/17043919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "You not a believer, suck a big dick", "vault_lines": ["You not a believer, suck a big dick"], "meaning": "If you don’t believe that Nicki Minaj is the Queen, then go fuck yourself!\n\n“You can suck my dick” is a common variation of a vulgar phrase (like fuck off or “kiss my ass”) used to express disdain or refusal. It’s interesting that Nicki, as a female rapper in a male-dominated game, chooses to appropriate this very masculine language.\n\nAlmost in an act of Freudian castration, Nicki subverts the misogynistic language of oppression and lets everyone know that women can perform this role just as well.", "annotation_id": "1965456", "url": "https://genius.com/1965456", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Monday night with the RAW, I’m Vince McMahon with a beat Power-slamming them hammers, I get you handled for free (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Monday night with the RAW, I’m Vince McMahon with a beat", "Power-slamming them hammers, I get you handled for free (Uh)"], "meaning": "Ricky Rozay not only looks like he could easily be mistaken for a black, bald Yokozuna, but he knows a little something about modern wrestling. Vince McMahon is of course the owner of World Wrestling Entertainment – the biggest wrestling promotion over the last decade – whose flagship show is Monday Night Raw. When he gets on any track, he owns the beat. As for “power-slamming hammers”, let’s just say he doesn’t need to hire any gunmen to get rid of you\n\nHughh!", "annotation_id": "1462230", "url": "https://genius.com/1462230", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "I’m on my Russell Simmon,", "vault_lines": ["I'm on my Russell Simmon,"], "meaning": "Russell Simmons is one of the four big rap and hip-hop moguls, being the third richest of them. Unlike other moguls, though, he has little to no experience as an artist himself. He is also Nicki’s Queens compatriot.\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj is “on” her Russell Simmons, meaning she is on his game, playing with the same level of success and entrepreneurship. She’s winning!", "annotation_id": "775281", "url": "https://genius.com/775281", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Rolls Royce wood,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rolls Royce Wood can mean two things here: 1) A vintage model of the Rolls Royce or 2) A Rolls Royce with a wooden finish interior", "annotation_id": "691469", "url": "https://genius.com/691469", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Lookin’ like a shark, the nose, call it Pinocchio (No lie)", "vault_lines": ["Lookin' like a shark, the nose, call it Pinocchio (No lie)"], "meaning": "Cam is probably referring to the Mercedes-Benz SLR McLaren. Both Mercedes-Benz and McLaren are European, and the front of the car does resemble a hammerhead shark.", "annotation_id": "685938", "url": "https://genius.com/685938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Heartbreak hotel, I’m in the A-Rod suite", "vault_lines": ["Heartbreak hotel, I'm in the A-Rod suite"], "meaning": "Heartbreak Hotel: a phrase that is interpolated here to mean that women get their hopes up only to find out that they will be dumped fairly quickly.\n\n\n\nHe symbolizes it as the “A-Rod suite”, as the phrase “heartbreak hotel” coincides well with A-Rod’s “romantic relationship” arena:\n\n\n\n(He’s no longer with Cameron Diaz anymore, either… and this fails to mention the women that he was “secretly” with during this time span.)\n\n\n\n*On top of that, the A-Rod suite itself could also mean that the suite is top-dollar since he is being paid a LOT of money to play baseball", "annotation_id": "684950", "url": "https://genius.com/684950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Know that boy busy balling, I like to play all week", "vault_lines": ["Know that boy busy balling, I like to play all week"], "meaning": "Word play on “balling” & “play”: balling is often referred to as playing basketball.", "annotation_id": "684670", "url": "https://genius.com/684670", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Y-Y-Y-Young Yummy, fuck you got for me?", "vault_lines": ["Y-Y-Y-Young Yummy, fuck you got for me?"], "meaning": "Wordplay on Young Money: similar to the idiom, “eating somebody for breakfast”.\n\nIn other words, she is a beast. (Feed her rappers, or feed her beats.)", "annotation_id": "683010", "url": "https://genius.com/683010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Big fat pussy wit’ a icy watch", "vault_lines": ["Big fat pussy wit' a icy watch"], "meaning": "This lyric interpolates Rick Ross’s verse on Lil Wayne’s 2011 track “John”:\n\nBig black nigga in a icy watch", "annotation_id": "677795", "url": "https://genius.com/677795", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "I’m Santa Claus to these hoes without a reindeer", "vault_lines": ["I'm Santa Claus to these hoes without a reindeer"], "meaning": "This is a clever line because Santa says “Ho, Ho, Ho!”\n\nNicki is like Santa to these broads for gifting them the light of day in the music world just for giving them the chance to diss her and get away with it. Nicki’s dope raps are enough of a gift to bring everyone good cheer.\n\n\n\nAnd she does’t even need a reindeer!\n\nNote that Cam'ron also references Santa in his verse.", "annotation_id": "677793", "url": "https://genius.com/677793", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Boarded a big jet and got a big check", "vault_lines": ["Boarded a big jet and got a big check"], "meaning": "Talking about her Pepsi endorsement to which she flew in a private jet to Argentina to film a commercial.\n\nThe parallels between this song and “Baby Girl” continue:\n\nBaby girl we gettin them big checks", "annotation_id": "677788", "url": "https://genius.com/677788", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Am Your Leader", "line": "Sign of the cross, ’cause this is her last supper", "vault_lines": ["Sign of the cross, 'cause this is her last supper"], "meaning": "The Last Supper is a famous Biblical event, where soon after Jesus Christ was betrayed and crucified on the cross soon after.\n\n\n\nYou better make a sign of the cross with your fingers, because you won’t be gettin' a resurrection.\n\nMetaphorical more than allegorical, Nicki’s saying her enemies' careers are going to end soon, like the Last Supper, so they better eat up and prepare to die, before it’s too late for them to back out from Nicki’s onslaught", "annotation_id": "669170", "url": "https://genius.com/669170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
