{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Tired of countin money bitch I went and bought a scale", "vault_lines": ["Tired of countin money bitch I went and bought a scale"], "meaning": "this could mean 2 things:\n1. he bought a scale to weigh his money instead of count it because he has so much\nor 2, before he became famous he was tired of having to count all of his money because funds were too tight so he bought a scale so he could sell drugs and make a better profit", "annotation_id": "8616200", "url": "https://genius.com/8616200", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Rims on the jeep sittin higher than Khalifa", "vault_lines": ["Rims on the jeep sittin higher than Khalifa"], "meaning": "Ace is metaphorically comparing how tall his rims on his Jeep are to how high (as in drug use) Wiz Khalifa can get.\nWiz Khalifa is known as a frequent drug consumer, he is even pictured using drugs on his third album cover, Rolling Papers:", "annotation_id": "2606664", "url": "https://genius.com/2606664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Highway to life, need a hundred mill exit", "vault_lines": ["Highway to life, need a hundred mill exit"], "meaning": "As Rascal Flatts stated so well:\n\n\n\nOn a highway (evidently including the highway of life), there are exits which allow the driver to leave the highway.\nFrench just hopes that when he gets off at his exit (when he dies), he will have made at least one hundred million dollars – to be remembered as a successful man.", "annotation_id": "1911959", "url": "https://genius.com/1911959", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Play with my paper, run up in your offices", "vault_lines": ["Play with my paper, run up in your offices"], "meaning": "This line and the line below refer to Ice Cube because Ice Cube destroyed a Priority Records office with a baseball bat because he was owed money.\nFrench is warning everyone to not fuck with him.\n\nMore info here:\nhttp://youtu.be/rPt2YjHBqrw", "annotation_id": "1399492", "url": "https://genius.com/1399492", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Hundred bottles send ‘em to the vip, ballin’", "vault_lines": ["Hundred bottles send ‘em to the vip, ballin’"], "meaning": "Play on the Drake and Chris Brown situation as Chris Brown had a bottle sent to Drake’s VIP booth.", "annotation_id": "1068655", "url": "https://genius.com/1068655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Nickel-plated Ruger have you in a box on Worldstar", "vault_lines": ["Nickel-plated Ruger have you in a box on Worldstar"], "meaning": "A Nickel plated ruger is a type of gun.\n\nRoss could be referring to two things right here:\n\n\nWorldstar is a hip hop site with violent videos (in boxes) relating to music and all things considered. Ross is talking about how he’s going to put you on there.\nWorldstar is also a packaging regulation company. So Ross is also saying he can put you in a packaging box (coffin).", "annotation_id": "1068646", "url": "https://genius.com/1068646", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Sittin’ on them M’s, mad shit is gettin realer", "vault_lines": ["Sittin’ on them M’s, mad shit is gettin realer"], "meaning": "Meek Mill is telling us as his money continues to grow to millions, everything around him is turning into something more serious and surreal.\n\nAlso, M’s could refer to MMG, the label founded by Ross and the label Meek is signed to.\nSo Meek Mill says as long as MMG is making music, the industry is staying real and competitive.", "annotation_id": "1058308", "url": "https://genius.com/1058308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "I’mma die fly, Rest in Peace Aaliyah", "vault_lines": ["I’mma die fly, Rest in Peace Aaliyah"], "meaning": "Meek Mill will die in some expensive ass clothing, because he achieved so much success in the rap industry.\n\nAaliyah was a famous R&B singer, who died in a plane crash back in 2001 (Rest In Peace). Meek is metaphorically saying he’s going to die fly just like Aaliyah did.", "annotation_id": "1012743", "url": "https://genius.com/1012743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "What’s a death sentence cause we all gotta die", "vault_lines": ["What’s a death sentence cause we all gotta die"], "meaning": "Why fear a death sentence? We will all die one day anyway. Living with this mentality is one way to stay motivated to keep selling drugs.\nRoss told us something similar to this in his song Usual Suspects featuring Nas & Kevin Cossom off of his album Deeper Than Rap:\n\nI run with niggas who destined to get a life sentence", "annotation_id": "1012741", "url": "https://genius.com/1012741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Staring at the ceiling when I wake up in the morning My dawg doing life, try to see him ‘fore he hit the coffin’", "vault_lines": ["Staring at the ceiling when I wake up in the morning", "My dawg doing life, try to see him ‘fore he hit the coffin’"], "meaning": "He wakes up in the morning thinking if he will ever see his friend in jail before he dies. French is referring to Max B here, a long time friend of his.\nMax B is currently serving a 75-year long sentence in jail, charges are murder and robbery among others.\nEven though he was in jail, he was able to collaborate with French Montana on the song Once In A While, off of French’s debut album, Excuse My French.", "annotation_id": "1012193", "url": "https://genius.com/1012193", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Started with a Bonne now I’m sittin’ in a Porsche", "vault_lines": ["Started with a Bonne now I’m sittin’ in a Porsche"], "meaning": "The Bonne Meek refers to is a Pontiac Bonneville. In Philly that’s a hood car, most people that hustle drive Pontiac Bonneville’s or similar vehicles that they call ‘Squadders/Squaddas’.\n\nAfter amounting the wealth and success that Mill has experienced he has upgraded his whip to a Porsche.", "annotation_id": "1004319", "url": "https://genius.com/1004319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "It’s the ’012 Ice Cube nigga with the Raider hat", "vault_lines": ["It’s the ’012 Ice Cube nigga with the Raider hat"], "meaning": "French is comparing himself to Ice Cube. Back in the early 90’s Cube and N.W.A. Were known for there Love for the Oakland Raiders.", "annotation_id": "1003188", "url": "https://genius.com/1003188", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Did It for My Dawgz", "line": "Ricky’s diesel got my hood looking like it’s Thriller", "vault_lines": ["Ricky's diesel got my hood looking like it's Thriller"], "meaning": "Meek is implying Rick Ross has hooked him up with some very high grade sour diesel marijuana. The people in Meek’s hood have been smoking it and are so high they look like zombies (like in the Thriller video).", "annotation_id": "1003169", "url": "https://genius.com/1003169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
