{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "Rich nigga rituals, Rolls Royces and residuals Residue in my residence, revenue was so plentiful Rumors Rozay still be runnin’ with all you criminals Ransom notes and repercussions follow my ridicule", "vault_lines": ["Rich nigga rituals, Rolls Royces and residuals", "Residue in my residence, revenue was so plentiful", "Rumors Rozay still be runnin' with all you criminals", "Ransom notes and repercussions follow my ridicule"], "meaning": "This is a new flow. He went lyrical with alliteration with all the Rs, but it’s a vibe because it’s straight through with no breath kind of. It’s called evolving.\n\nRoss, when he sent me that verse; that’s my brother and that’s somebody that I’ve seen grow and grow into a number one MC. So when he sends me a verse, I know what it is. Especially when it’s a Khaled record, he’s not only gonna give me his best, he cares about it. This shit means something to him.", "annotation_id": "8029295", "url": "https://genius.com/8029295", "state": "verified", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "[Chorus: Future]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Future went in there and if he loves something he’ll go from the beginning of the record to the end of the beat and spit all types of different shit: flows, chants, breakdowns, bridges, verses, bars. Just so much shit.\n\nI just let him go two or three times and then I’m like we’re good. And I’ll put it together and take the best moments of his writing skills, delivery and cadence. I love that record.\n\nFuture recorded more parts, but I only put what I felt made sense for the record.", "annotation_id": "8029288", "url": "https://genius.com/8029288", "state": "verified", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "[Intro: DJ Khaled]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Beat Bully gave me this beat and I said it was so hard and I put it aside.\n\nMe and Future were in the studio, I played him that beat. Future got a special way of recording and if you’re a real producer, you know how to really get the best out of Future because Future says so much dope shit.", "annotation_id": "8029276", "url": "https://genius.com/8029276", "state": "verified", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "Got a flood on my wrist, I wear Mello Yello Had a flood on my wrist, I wear yellow mellow", "vault_lines": ["Got a flood on my wrist, I wear Mello Yello", "Had a flood on my wrist, I wear yellow mellow"], "meaning": "‘Mello Yello’ is a citrus-flavored softdrink, which is distributed by Coca-Cola since 1979. Sometimes Future uses this drink instead of Sprite to mix lean. He mentioned this in his verse on the track “Big Rings” from the collabo mixtape What a Time to Be Alive with Drake.\n\nSince ‘Mello Yello’ is filled in yellow cans, he uses this image to refer to his watches, which are provided with big amount of yellow diamonds. So his wrist is literally flooded by them, what confirms the fact that diamonds are dancing on him.\n\nEven when this watch might be a beaut, it’s only a watch in Future’s rotation. Since he owns a lot watches, it’s obvious that Future switches them up sometimes.\n\n\n\nIf you take a look at Future’s Instagram profile, you will also see that he’s a big fan of accessoires and jewelry.", "annotation_id": "8024179", "url": "https://genius.com/8024179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "Got a flood on my wrist, I wear Mello Yello Had a flood on my wrist, I wear yellow mellow", "vault_lines": ["Got a flood on my wrist, I wear Mello Yello", "Had a flood on my wrist, I wear yellow mellow"], "meaning": "‘Mello Yello’ is a citrus-flavored softdrink, which is distributed by Coca-Cola since 1979. Sometimes Future uses this drink instead of Sprite to mix lean. He mentioned this in his verse on the track “Big Rings” from the collabo mixtape What a Time to Be Alive with Drake.\n\nSince ‘Mello Yello’ is filled in yellow cans, he uses this image to refer to his watches, which are provided with big amount of yellow diamonds. So his wrist is literally flooded by them, what confirms the fact that diamonds are dancing on him.\n\nEven when this watch might be a beaut, it’s only a watch in Future’s rotation. Since he owns a lot watches, it’s obvious that Future switches them up sometimes.\n\n\n\nIf you take a look at Future’s Instagram profile, you will also see that he’s a big fan of accessoires and jewelry.", "annotation_id": "8023813", "url": "https://genius.com/8023813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "When I fuck on these bitches, no lovey-dovey", "vault_lines": ["When I fuck on these bitches, no lovey-dovey"], "meaning": "He doesn’t do lovey dovey – meaning getting sentimental and things like “Netflix and Chill”. Future stated in his verse on the track “Scholarships”, from his mixtape What a Time to Be Alive which he made  with Drake:\n\nShoot out the car man, no lovey dovey\n\nThis shows that Future doesn’t show any emotions and just wants to have sex with her.", "annotation_id": "7991938", "url": "https://genius.com/7991938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "I put the racks and the goons on ’em I got a MAC with a drum on ’em Soon as the drought hit, we laid on ’em", "vault_lines": ["I put the racks and the goons on 'em", "I got a MAC with a drum on 'em", "Soon as the drought hit, we laid on 'em"], "meaning": "A goon is a person who’s hired to maltreat someone.\nSince Future often claims to be a trapper and has lot of money, it’s not suprising that he put a bounty on people, who misplease him.\n\nThe fact that he has a MAC on him, shows that Future doesn’t flinch from taking care of this buisness on his own.\n\nThe Military Armament Corporation Model 10 or just ‘MAC-10’ is a light, subcompact machine pistol produced since 1970. Due to his compactness, this weapon was really popular in the 80’s.\nBy using of a drum magazine he has more ammunition, what consequently means that Future can fire a lot more bullets on those people.\n\n\n\nTo hit dry means to smoke a e-cigarette, which is often considered being lame.", "annotation_id": "7976653", "url": "https://genius.com/7976653", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "Check on that chick out the melo", "vault_lines": ["Check on that chick out the melo"], "meaning": "The term ‘melo’ usually appears in last names of people with Portuguese roots.\n\nSince Future only got exotic bitches, it’s not suprising that he’s checking out a girl from Portugal, which often look similar to latin women.\n\nCinderella is a princess of the same-named folk tale, which became really popular after being made to a Disney movie in 1950. By comparing this girl to Cinderella, Future shows his affection for her. Even when princesses are often considered to be spoiled, Future only might be attracted by her glamourous appearance.", "annotation_id": "7966575", "url": "https://genius.com/7966575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "I got that white on that white on the Panamera", "vault_lines": ["I got that white on that white on the Panamera"], "meaning": "‘White on white’ means that the interior and the exterior of a vehicle, be it a car or a jet, is white. When you buy the Porsche “Panamera” 970, whose baseprice amounts to 141,300$, you can personalize the design of this car, which is generally only black outside, for extra money.\n\nSo, when Future hits the roads with his Panamera, which can reach a maximum speed of 162 mph (261 km/h), he always drives really fast, so you can literally see fire come out of the exhaust pipes. He uses a similar wordplay on “Digital Dash”:\n\nSee the fire come out the ass on the Lamborghini\n\nOn the remix of Rick Ross’s  track Hustlin', Jay-Z mentions a similar thing.", "annotation_id": "7966326", "url": "https://genius.com/7966326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "Percocet roxies, we stay on ’em Them Percocet roxies, we stay on ’em", "vault_lines": ["Percocet roxies, we stay on 'em", "Them Percocet roxies, we stay on 'em"], "meaning": "Percocet is a trade name for its main ingredient, oxycodone and is highly addictive.\n\nLike heroin and morphine, Percocet affects the brain and the central nervous system, changing the way the brain perceives pain. Abuse of it can lead to the same dangerous problems of dependence and addiction as the illicit street drugs that share its origin. When taken in large doses or when the prescription tablet is crushed to destroy the time-release mechanism, Percocet can cause a “high” similar to heroin that is characterized by:\n\n\nEuphoria\nFeelings of claim and relaxation\nHeightened pleasure\n\n\n\nPercocets are generically known by their street names:\n\n\n\nPercs\nPaulas\n\nRoxicotten & Roxies (from their brand name Roxane Laboratories)\n\nBlue dynamite (the 15-30 Percocet with no Tylenol)\n\n512s (refers to the generic brand that prints 512 on the round white 5mg Percocet pill).", "annotation_id": "7964415", "url": "https://genius.com/7964415", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "Soon as I turn out the Ghost they was mad at me I can see jealousy written on they face when they looked at me They know I don’t play about that paper They know I don’t play about that paper They know I don’t play about that paper They know I don’t play about that paper They know I don’t", "vault_lines": ["I can see jealousy written on they face when they looked at me", "They know I don't play about that paper", "They know I don't"], "meaning": "Future and Rick Ross are known for not playing games with their money and will show remorse with this matter. If one does not give them their money, conflict will come into play. Of course people will get mad at them for their fame and fortune. With Rozay’s Wingstop success  and Future’s great music success they will be focused on getting some commas.", "annotation_id": "7962642", "url": "https://genius.com/7962642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "line": "Sippin’ my cup with this muddy muddy", "vault_lines": ["Sippin' my cup with this muddy muddy"], "meaning": "Actavis is a pharmaceutical company that’s well known for manufacturing cough syrup that contained Promethazine with Codeine, which was taken off the shelves in April of 2014 because they became aware that people were using it to make Lean – a narcotic consisting of cough syrup, any kind of soda and Jolly Rancher Candy.\n\nMuddy is a term to describe a cup of Lean that contains more cough syrup than soda. When mixed, the narcotic usually turns to a dark purple.", "annotation_id": "7962224", "url": "https://genius.com/7962224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "status": "done", "targets": 12, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-khaled-i-dont-play-about-my-paper-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Don’t Play About My Paper", "genius_id": 2328748, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "I feel like Biggie", "vault_lines": ["I feel like Pac (Yeah!), I feel like Biggie"], "meaning": "In this line “Biggie” is sampled from the intro from “Kick In The Door”.", "annotation_id": "3363758", "url": "https://genius.com/3363758", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Ayo, how you gon’ compare yourself to greatness If you ain’t ready to be great man? Ain’t no more to it", "vault_lines": ["Ayo, how you gon' compare yourself to greatness", "If you ain't ready to be great man? Ain't no more to it"], "meaning": "The whole song is about feeling like Pac and Biggie, two of hip-hops bests. Everyone is always rapping or talking about these two because of their amazing music style and ability to connect with their fan-base. Diddy is stating how can you compare yourself to these two when you haven’t accomplished anything to be on their level. Once you’ve done something worthy, you can be deemed as one of the best, A “Pac” or “Biggie”.", "annotation_id": "2361544", "url": "https://genius.com/2361544", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Got my mind made up,", "vault_lines": ["Got my mind made up,"], "meaning": "Playing on 2Pac’s “Got My Made Mind Up ” is a song featuring Kurupt, Method Man, Redman, Daz Dillinger, and Inspectah Deck on the original. Essentially, it’s 3 Eastside rappers and 3 Westside rappers capitalizing on their lyrical ability and trying to prove they’re the best. A battle to each other and wack MC’s one track, very clever.", "annotation_id": "2347939", "url": "https://genius.com/2347939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "You know this shit don’t stop,", "vault_lines": ["You know this shit don't stop,"], "meaning": "Shit Don’t Stop is a song by Tupac’s rapgroup Thug Life.", "annotation_id": "2347888", "url": "https://genius.com/2347888", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Take my case to trial, my juror Paula Deen", "vault_lines": ["Take my case to trial, my juror Paula Deen"], "meaning": "Paula Deen, a famous celebrity chef, ruffled feathers in 2013 when she announced she used the N-word and saw no problem with it. Obviously, she was hit with much backlash and some have labeled her as a racist that hates black people.\n\nWhen Ross goes to court, he feels like the jurors are against him. Obviously, Paula Deen herself is not Ross' juror, but Ross feels as if his juror(s) represents what she represents – racist bigotry. Ross has said before how feels people wanna see him locked up.", "annotation_id": "2343005", "url": "https://genius.com/2343005", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Kick in your door", "vault_lines": ["See a kid around around in your town kick in your door"], "meaning": "Another Biggie reference, this time to The Mad Rapper-featured Kick In The Door", "annotation_id": "2340290", "url": "https://genius.com/2340290", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Why you complaining? And you wonder why we call you bitch", "vault_lines": ["Why you complaining? And you wonder why we call you bitch"], "meaning": "Reference to the Tupac song Wonda Why They Call You Bitch of the All Eyez On Me album.", "annotation_id": "2328252", "url": "https://genius.com/2328252", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "And when we ride on, no more pain, we go hard as shit", "vault_lines": ["And when we ride on, no more pain, we go hard as shit"], "meaning": "“When We Ride” and “No More Pain” are both 2Pac songs, while “we go hard” is a reference to “Brooklyn Go Hard” as performed by Jay Z as the theme song of the Notorious soundtrack.", "annotation_id": "2328227", "url": "https://genius.com/2328227", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "305 the realest", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "305 is the primary area code for Miami, Florida – where Rick Ross is from and lives.", "annotation_id": "2326051", "url": "https://genius.com/2326051", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Ricky Ross the richest", "vault_lines": [", Ricky Ross the richest"], "meaning": "Though he claims to be the richest, as of March 2013 Rick Ross is actually the 25th richest rapper alive according to  http://www.celebritynetworth.com/articles/entertainment-articles/the-richest-rappers-2013/ .  Diddy on the other hand could make this claim and it would be correct as he is in fact the richest rapper.", "annotation_id": "2318377", "url": "https://genius.com/2318377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "We cradle to the grave, ride when my homie call", "vault_lines": ["We cradle to the grave, ride when my homie call"], "meaning": "“Cradle to the Grave” was the single off of Tupac’s ‘94 album “Thug Life Vol. 1” and one of his more underrated music videos:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEw4eypIaQQ\n“If My Homie Calls” is the second single off “2Pacalypse Now”", "annotation_id": "2295150", "url": "https://genius.com/2295150", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "It’s unbelievable suicidal thoughts you would get Said fuck me warning and the gun don’t blast", "vault_lines": ["It's unbelievable suicidal thoughts you would get", "Said fuck me warning and the gun don't blast"], "meaning": "“Suicidal Thoughts” and “Warning” are both Biggie songs off his 1994 album Ready To Die.", "annotation_id": "2292033", "url": "https://genius.com/2292033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Somebody gotta die", "vault_lines": ["When somebody gotta die"], "meaning": "A reference to big’s track Somebody Gotta Die off 1997’s Life After Death", "annotation_id": "2288582", "url": "https://genius.com/2288582", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Belaire on my table, I talk it then I live it", "vault_lines": ["Belaire on my table, I talk it then I live it"], "meaning": "Luc BELAIRE Rose is a champagne that sponsors Rick Ross. Ross proudly promotes and sponsors the champagne brand on his instagram.\n\n\n\nIf Rick says something then it’s true, so you best believe that Belaire is on his table.", "annotation_id": "2287086", "url": "https://genius.com/2287086", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "A paid thug nigga, that’s why shorty wanna be me", "vault_lines": ["A paid thug nigga, that's why shorty wanna be me"], "meaning": "This is a nod to 2Pac’s song Shorty Wanna Be a Thug.", "annotation_id": "2286909", "url": "https://genius.com/2286909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "It’s an everyday struggle nigga, me and my bitch", "vault_lines": ["It's an everyday struggle nigga, me and my bitch"], "meaning": "T.I. is referring to The Notorious B.I.G.’s songs “Everyday Struggle” and “Me And My Bitch” from Ready To Die.", "annotation_id": "2286875", "url": "https://genius.com/2286875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Down south nigga,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross was born in Coahoma County, Mississippi, where Nate Dogg spent his childhood.", "annotation_id": "2286261", "url": "https://genius.com/2286261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "I feel like Pac and Biggie, love the dough more than you know", "vault_lines": ["I feel like Pac and Biggie, love the dough more than you know"], "meaning": "Referring to Biggie’s song “I Love The Dough”\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G6HLi4oCebc", "annotation_id": "2286060", "url": "https://genius.com/2286060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
