{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "[Verse 3: T.I.]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Throughout the whole verse, T.I. neatly uses the title of the track and works in many, many references to Tupac and Biggie songs and albums.\n\nIt’s also one of four T.I./Khaled collaborations, the others being a DJ Khaled song called “Dip, Slide, Rideout”, Make It Rain (Remix), We Takin' Over and Bitches & Bottles (Let’s Get It Started).", "annotation_id": "2286025", "url": "https://genius.com/2286025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "We pour out a little liquor, thug life, straight balling", "vault_lines": ["We pour out a little liquor, thug life, straight balling"], "meaning": "“Pour Out A Little Liquor”\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cBons6TRxic\n\n“Thug Life”\n\n“Straight Ballin'”\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p6pepmOEoho\n\nAll references to 2Pac.", "annotation_id": "2286007", "url": "https://genius.com/2286007", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Hollerin’ only God can judge me shawty, I ain’t mad at ya", "vault_lines": ["Hollerin' only God can judge me shawty, I ain't mad at ya"], "meaning": "Referencing to two Tupac Shakur records :“Only God Can Judge Me” and “I Ain’t Mad At Ya”. Two amazing tracks by one of the greatest Hip Hop Artists of all time… Only god can judge me is a common idiom. T.I could be saying that even though you judged him he isn´t mad, since he would be judging him then, Catch 22!", "annotation_id": "2285999", "url": "https://genius.com/2285999", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Talking Jam Pony", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Jam Pony Express is a DJ crew from Fort Lauderdale, Florida.", "annotation_id": "2285828", "url": "https://genius.com/2285828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Rest in Peace to Uncle Al,", "vault_lines": ["Rest in Peace to Uncle Al,"], "meaning": "DJ Uncle Al was a DJ in Miami, which is where Rozay is from.", "annotation_id": "2285825", "url": "https://genius.com/2285825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "My ambitions as a rider got me ready to die", "vault_lines": ["My ambitions as a rider got me ready to die"], "meaning": "T.I. is down to ride for his people and for what he believes in. Even if he has to die for it.\n\nThis line also references one Tupac’s most famous songs, Ambitionz Az a Ridah. Which was on his incredibly successful album, All Eyez On Me Which went 5X platinum in just 2 months!\n\nAlso references The Notorious B.I.G’s album Ready To Die which was his debut studio album.", "annotation_id": "2285441", "url": "https://genius.com/2285441", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "They said Brenda had a baby but she left it in the alley One shot that playa hater now we going back to Cali", "vault_lines": ["They said Brenda had a baby but she left it in the alley", "One shot that playa hater now we going back to Cali"], "meaning": "This line references Brenda’s got a baby a song written and performed by Tupac Shakur. The song about a twelve year-old girl named Brenda who lives in a ghetto, has a baby, and is incapable of supporting it.\n\nT.I. also references Biggies songs Playa Hater and Going back to Cali – about Biggie going back to Los Angeles and the West Coast, where, coincidentally, he was subsequently gunned down.", "annotation_id": "2285398", "url": "https://genius.com/2285398", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "My OG said, “Strap up and don’t lay your head where you do dirt”", "vault_lines": ["My OG said, \"Strap up and don't lay your head where you do dirt\""], "meaning": "We all know the fifth “Crack Commandment” –\n\nNever sell no crack where you rest at\nI don’t care if they want a ounce, tell ‘em “bounce!\n\nDon’t do your dirty work where you sleep. Shout out to Meek’s “old g”, Biggie.", "annotation_id": "2285308", "url": "https://genius.com/2285308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Man they hit Big in the passenger, hit Pac in the passenger So I’m riding ’round with this Mac on me And a bunch of shooters in back of us Roll up, you a dead man, headshots when we clap at ya", "vault_lines": ["So I'm riding 'round with this Mac on me", "And a bunch of shooters in back of us", "Roll up, you a dead man, headshots when we clap at ya"], "meaning": "Ironically, both Biggie and Tupac were riding in the passenger seats during each of their murders.\n\nBecause of this, Meek keeps his commonly referenced Mac 11 by his side in case someone wants to roll up on him. Dare get to close, and you’re a dead man because he aims for the head.", "annotation_id": "2285056", "url": "https://genius.com/2285056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "line": "Feel like it’s me against the world, bury me a G My middle finger to the world, I’m gon’ forever be a G", "vault_lines": ["Feel like it's me against the world, bury me a G", "My middle finger to the world, I'm gon' forever be a G"], "meaning": "T.I. pays homage to the great Tupac by referencing three of his pieces. Tupac is one of the two main subjects of this song.\n\n\n“Me Against the World” – is Tupac’s third studio album, and went double platinum.\n“Bury Me a G” – is a song by Pac.\n“Fuck the World” – is a song from Pac off of the album that was just mentioned, “Me Against the World”.\n\n\n\n\n\nBut, T.I. doesn’t come out and say it’s a reference. He puts it in his own words describing how he is actually feeling. Like it’s him against the world.\n\nT.I. and Rick Ross also have their own song called Bury Me a G.", "annotation_id": "2285020", "url": "https://genius.com/2285020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "status": "done", "targets": 29, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-khaled-i-feel-like-pac-i-feel-like-biggie-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie", "genius_id": 233980, "source": "api"}
