{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Pray", "line": "Wake up out a coma, frozen in the moment You could have the biggest clique, but you gon’ die a loner Tubes down my throat, rules that I broke All these quotes that I wrote and never cared to vote", "vault_lines": ["Wake up out a coma, frozen in the moment", "You could have the biggest clique, but you gon' die a loner", "Tubes down my throat, rules that I broke", "All these quotes that I wrote and never cared to vote"], "meaning": "In March 2018 Rick Ross was hospitalized due to a potential heart attack and was briefly on life support. Although he ended up pulling through, this near-death experience made him look back on his personal relationships and decisions he’s made.", "annotation_id": "24051066", "url": "https://genius.com/24051066", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Pray", "line": "Rick Ross was reportedly hospitalized early Friday morning Sources close to Rick Ross tell **** that he’s been hooked up to a machine that’s taking over the function of his heart and lungs He’s reported getting treatment in the cardiac unit, which is a strong sign that he could’ve suffered a heart attack that started as a respiratory problem early Thursday morning He’s hooked up to an ECMO, which is a form of life support This story is still developing", "vault_lines": ["This story is still developing"], "meaning": "This a reference to a March 2018 incident in which Rick Ross was hospitalised after being found unconscious at his home.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JgRCp_DBnZw", "annotation_id": "17777991", "url": "https://genius.com/17777991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Pray", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-i-still-pray-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Still Pray", "genius_id": 4767762, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "Learn from O.G.’s, Alfa Romeos and Sterlings", "vault_lines": ["Learn from O.G.'s, Alfa Romeos and Sterlings"], "meaning": "Studied Original Gangsterology.\n\nAlfa Romeo 164 S & Sterling 825 should have been pictured of the 80’s and early 90’s model that’s what some of the hustlers use to drive back then that’s why he said updated that upgraded that saying he watched and learned from the OG’s he just got the newer ones.\n\n\n\nAlfa Romeo 164 S\n\n\n\nSterling 825", "annotation_id": "759425", "url": "https://genius.com/759425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "It’s like an itch you can’t scratch It’s like a bitch you can’t shake I still wanna", "vault_lines": ["It's like a bitch you can't shake"], "meaning": "Selling crack is something you can’t stop doing easily, earning that much money becomes addictive.\nThe line is also an allusion to drug fiends that consume crack cocaine. They are often portrayed as scratching a non-existent itch.\n\nPusha uses that imagery to propel the song into the next line in which he makes clear that he is, in fact, using the term as an idiom.", "annotation_id": "394549", "url": "https://genius.com/394549", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "Powder falls, smoke clears through the walking dead", "vault_lines": ["Powder falls, smoke clears through the walking dead"], "meaning": "A nod to the ubiquitous scene from every zombie movie ever that has a huge cloud of smoke or steam and a horde of the undead coming through. Here Liva name checks Robert Kirkman’s  comic series The Walking Dead (which has been adapted for television on AMC).\n\nRappers have long compared coke heads to zombies going all the way back to P.E.’s “Night of the Living Baseheads” and Pusha compared them to the zombies in “Thriller” in “What Happened to that Boy?”", "annotation_id": "161578", "url": "https://genius.com/161578", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "Sparkles to the table, got him feeling like he’s Merlin", "vault_lines": ["Sparkles to the table, got him feeling like he’s Merlin"], "meaning": "It’s a common practice at expensive nightclubs to bring out bottles with sparklers to draw attention to the person(s) ordering them. This ostentatious display is a surefire method of attracting more than one gold digger\n\n\n\nAll the sparkles at the table got them feeling like there Merlin the magician/wizard.", "annotation_id": "157739", "url": "https://genius.com/157739", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "You know what pain is? Flushing two bricks and trying to have a nigga strain it out the drainage", "vault_lines": ["You know what pain is?", "Flushing two bricks and trying to have a nigga strain it out the drainage"], "meaning": "Remember near the end of Goodfellas when Henry finds out his wife Karen (see below) flushed all the coke down the toilet during the police raide? That’s exactly how angry and frustrated Push would feel\n\n\n\nNote – 2 bricks is rought $20k.\n\nAnd people involved in the drug trade have been known to transport cocaine by ingesting it so they can pass it out later.\nSo Imagine you’ve got someone with a massive shipment and while shitting the bricks, they flush it.", "annotation_id": "153543", "url": "https://genius.com/153543", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "In this climate I’m Kareem Burke tied-in The Roc’s silent partner, I ain’t throwing up the diamond", "vault_lines": ["The Roc's silent partner, I ain't throwing up the diamond"], "meaning": "Kareem “Biggs” Burke (seen on right in the photo below) was the co-founder of Roc-A-Fella records who was arrested for for a drug bust (Marijuana though!). Burke’s drug dealing was referenced by Pusha on Number On The Board:\n\n“Mix drug and show money, Biggs Burke on tour”\n\n\n\nKareem was known as the silent parter because unlike Dame Dash he wasn’t dancing around in the music videos and constantly doing interviews.", "annotation_id": "150600", "url": "https://genius.com/150600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "Security blanket of cocaine, I am Linus", "vault_lines": ["Security blanket of cocaine, I am Linus"], "meaning": "Linus is a character from the newspaper comic strip “Peanuts” who always carries a blanket around. Coke (and the money that comes with it) gives Pusha a sense of security.. it’s his “yayo blankie”\n\nThe reason Push may find it as an item of comfort is that even if his rap records don’t sell, he’s always got coke money. After all, he ain’t spend one rap dollar in three years, holla.", "annotation_id": "150566", "url": "https://genius.com/150566", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "Bell Biv DeVoe, push poison like a copperhead", "vault_lines": ["Bell Biv DeVoe, push poison like a copperhead"], "meaning": "Bell Biv DeVoe is an R&B group, “Poison” was one of the groups most successful singles–it reached the nation. Similarly, Liva pushes poison (in this case, cocaine) to the masses. The reference to the copper head is both an allusion to the snake that tempts otherwise good hearted men (from the Garden of Eden) and a useful analogy of what, essentially, a drug dealer is: a snake.", "annotation_id": "150554", "url": "https://genius.com/150554", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "Feds listening to conversations through my OnStar", "vault_lines": ["Feds listening to conversations through my OnStar"], "meaning": "OnStar is a security and communication system in certain cars. Rick’s saying that the government has modified his OnStar to record him talking about the drug game.", "annotation_id": "150544", "url": "https://genius.com/150544", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Still Wanna", "line": "When we talking business, talking on the phone cease", "vault_lines": ["When we talking business, talking on the phone cease"], "meaning": "Because the phone is probably tapped. On his album Hood Billionaire, Ross has a track titled “Phone Tap.”", "annotation_id": "150543", "url": "https://genius.com/150543", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
