{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "And it’s thin", "vault_lines": ["Got the .22 on me, and it's thin"], "meaning": "Should be “got a .22 on me, Anderson”. CJ Anderson was a running back for the Denver Broncos who wore #22 and was the starter when this song came out", "annotation_id": "21800649", "url": "https://genius.com/21800649", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "You witnessing greatness..", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Khaled has had a great run, releasing national hits annually and semi-annually, from We Takin Over to No New Friends. He has worked with all of the big names in hip hop, and is linked to the biggest two imprints in rap history. All that and he doesn’t appear to be stopping anytime soon.", "annotation_id": "2052779", "url": "https://genius.com/2052779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Voom, voom, oh yeah,", "vault_lines": ["Voom, voom, oh yeah,"], "meaning": "A references to a Song by Nicki Minaj who is also featured in this song.", "annotation_id": "2051787", "url": "https://genius.com/2051787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Shoot movies, Jennifer Aniston", "vault_lines": ["Shoot movies, Jennifer Aniston"], "meaning": "Nicki was shooting a movie with Cameron Diaz & Kate Upton named, The Other Woman, due out April 25th, 2014.\n\nPicture below is Nicki filming the movie on set in New York.\n\n\n\nThis builds on the previous .22 reference since movies involve clips of scenes and guns require clips filled with bullets.\n\n\n\nAniston is one of the biggest names in Hollywood, this ties into the wordplay.", "annotation_id": "2044257", "url": "https://genius.com/2044257", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Got a big billboard out in Madison", "vault_lines": ["Got a big billboard out in Madison"], "meaning": "Nicki has a billboard in Madison promoting her new moscato drink, “Myx”.", "annotation_id": "2044240", "url": "https://genius.com/2044240", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Nah, I ain’t gotta shoot, I got mad assists", "vault_lines": ["Nah, I ain't gotta shoot, I got mad assists"], "meaning": "Like Steve Nash she doesn’t need to put up a lot of points when she sets other people up as well as she does (by being featured in numerous songs).\n\n\n\nAlternately, if something went down she wouldn’t have to shoot anybody because she has friends who would handle that for her.", "annotation_id": "2043864", "url": "https://genius.com/2043864", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Phantom cost like four dollar", "vault_lines": ["Phantom cost like four dollar"], "meaning": "Rozay is referencing his white Rolls Royce Phantom. He’s saying that compared to the money he’s got, the expensive purchase merely seems like four dollars.\n\n\n\nHe’s also crashed his White Phantom during a gun shooting.", "annotation_id": "2043842", "url": "https://genius.com/2043842", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Car paint like tar,", "vault_lines": ["Car paint like tar,"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s car is painted so black that it looks like tar.\n\nRoss could be talking about two cars since he owns two different black cars. He is most likely talking about his Rolls Royce since he has referenced it being really black before.\n\n\n\nHe could also be talking about his Maybach car that inspired his group name “Maybach Music Group” (MMG)\n\n\n\nEither way both cars are as black as tar.", "annotation_id": "2043770", "url": "https://genius.com/2043770", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Underground with this pimp shit so smoke one for Port Arthur", "vault_lines": ["Underground with this pimp shit so smoke one for Port Arthur"], "meaning": "Using the terms “underground” and “pimp” in the same sentence can only mean one thing; a shout-out to the late, great Pimp C, of the Underground Kingz, UGK (alongside Bun B). Ross is showing his respect to the H-Town legend by smoking one for the hometown of the southern duo; Port Arthur, Texas.", "annotation_id": "2043761", "url": "https://genius.com/2043761", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Blow the roof back - Kurt Cobain", "vault_lines": ["White tee and these rope chains, blow the roof back - Kurt Cobain"], "meaning": "Similar to his line from “Free Mason”:\n\nMy top back like JFK\nThey wanna push my top back like JFK\n\nHowever, this time he’s comparing collapsing the roof on his convertible car to Kurt Cobain’s suicide via shotgun blast to the head.", "annotation_id": "2043652", "url": "https://genius.com/2043652", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I Wanna Be With You", "line": "Saw the High School video now he wanna play hookie", "vault_lines": ["Saw the High School video now he wanna play hookie"], "meaning": "Nicki referring to her “High School” single and to high school in general – students often play “hooky” and skip class.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&v=e5j6GKKZa2k", "annotation_id": "2043523", "url": "https://genius.com/2043523", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
