{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "Fuckin’ to the rhythm, got her singin’ like she Jill Scott", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' to the rhythm, got her singin' like she Jill Scott"], "meaning": "Jill Scott is an American singer, songwriter, model, poet and actress.", "annotation_id": "20092438", "url": "https://genius.com/20092438", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "Anythin’ other than to ride is out of character", "vault_lines": ["Anythin' other than to ride is out of character"], "meaning": "This is perhaps the most “real” line from Rozay in his lyric history.\n\nRoss alludes to his character of “Rick Ross” while making a statement about maintaining his work ethic, to ride.\n\nIf you were not already aware, The Biggest Boss is playing a character. William Roberts II was a High School football star, corrections officer, & family man. Rick Ross is the biggest music & drug peddling Bawse in the world of Hip Hop.\n\nRick Ross is the Stephen Colbert of Hip Hop\n\nTheir shameless self promotion, prolific output, and cult-like fan following is a function of playing a character.\n\n\nThe shameless self promotion: every single album he has released has his face on the physical CD. Evidence from Port of Miami, Teflon Don, & GFID – In the Rolling Stone article on him, the reporter wrote that he tweeted for “5 hours about his upcoming album” after he awoke one morning.\nStephen Colbert, amongst other things, spent a week on a US Aircraft Carrier and peddled Pepsi\n\n\n\n\n\nTo spend a week on a ship that even looks huge in Battleship is worth major boss points. Both Ross & Colbert are undeniable and unstoppable Bosses.\n\n\nWhen you play a character, you never run out of material. See Colbert’s regular literary output & Rick Ross' never ending flow of mixtapes & albums as evidence.\nRoss & Colbert’s ability to entertain comes from the mastery of their characters. Colbert studied Bill O'Riley, & Rick Ross studied Golden Era Hip Hop.\n\n\n\nAlso, Ross is a student of the Mafioso genre so it should not come as a surprise that he can rap about being a coke dealing gangster with proficiency. Rozay is a learned student.", "annotation_id": "1299283", "url": "https://genius.com/1299283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "As I run away from my obituary", "vault_lines": ["As I run away from my obituary"], "meaning": "An obituary is a news article that reports the recent death of a person, so Ross is saying he runs away from death.", "annotation_id": "1267900", "url": "https://genius.com/1267900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "A.P’s for the whole team", "vault_lines": ["A.P's for the whole team"], "meaning": "Audemar Piguet watches is MMG’s offical watch apparently. Ross also dropped a mixtape named after the watch.", "annotation_id": "1267894", "url": "https://genius.com/1267894", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "Baselines shooters nigga, act wisely", "vault_lines": ["Baselines shooters nigga, act wisely"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre. In basketball, the baseline is the out-of-bounds area under the hoop. Really good 3 point shooters in basketball can nail the 3 right next to the baseline. The Miami Heat (who’s president Pat Riley was just named dropped in the previous line) have really good 3 point shooters.\n\nBut Ross is also saying he has shooters on the payroll (because of the mafioso lifestyle he lives), so act wisely or they will kill you.", "annotation_id": "1267886", "url": "https://genius.com/1267886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "Earnin’ revenue through different avenues", "vault_lines": ["Earnin' revenue through different avenues"], "meaning": "Ross has many different ways of making money. He is a rapper, owns several Wingstop restaurants, has an endorsement deal with Reebok Classics, is signed to Ciroc Boys/managed by Diddy, etc. Simply put, Ross is an entrepreneur.", "annotation_id": "1267881", "url": "https://genius.com/1267881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "One of my soldiers died in Attica", "vault_lines": ["One of my soldiers died in Attica"], "meaning": "The Attica Prison riot occurred at the Attica Correctional Facility in Attica, New York, United States in 1971. The riot was based in part upon prisoners' demands for better living conditions.\n\nSeeing as how Ross wasn’t alive for the Attica Prison riot, it’s a good bet that one of Ross' boys didn’t die during the Attica prison riot, he could have either died during a prison riot, or just have died while serving time at Attica Correctional Facility.", "annotation_id": "1267870", "url": "https://genius.com/1267870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "She sheds tears for that dope boy Shit, it is what it is for that dope boy", "vault_lines": ["She sheds tears for that dope boy", "Shit, it is what it is for that dope boy"], "meaning": "A “Dope Boy” is hardly around and barely has the time to spend with her because he out getting that money or either in Jail. So She cry because its nothing she can do, she misses him amd needs him.\n\n“It is what it is” because that is the Lifestyle he lives and cant stop because he knows that’s the quickest way for him to bring in the money to provide for them.", "annotation_id": "1076438", "url": "https://genius.com/1076438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ice Cold", "line": "Callate la boca", "vault_lines": ["Come to the coca, callate la boca"], "meaning": "Spanish for “close your mouth” or simply, “shut up”.", "annotation_id": "992205", "url": "https://genius.com/992205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
