{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "line": "Crack dealers need me as their motivation", "vault_lines": ["Crack dealers need me as their motivation"], "meaning": "Most people can listen to popular mainstream music about love or family to bring up their motivation and happiness levels but crack dealers can’t relate to that stuff. Rick Ross has finally given people with troubled pasts an icon to look up to to prove that it’s still possible to get millions of dollars.", "annotation_id": "7789717", "url": "https://genius.com/7789717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "line": "[Produced By: J.U.S.T.I.C.E. League]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Track samples “Song Cry” by Jay-Z\nhttps://youtu.be/w5srnNrICJo", "annotation_id": "7762555", "url": "https://genius.com/7762555", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "line": "I did it by myself so it took me some time No Dr. Dres, no Eminems, no Neptunes, no Timbalands", "vault_lines": ["No Dr. Dres, no Eminems, no Neptunes, no Timbalands"], "meaning": "Having a big-time co-sign has been essential for a number of rap careers. Eminem had Dr. Dre in his corner, 50 Cent had Eminem, Clipse had The Neptunes and newcomer Tink has Timbaland.\n\nHere Rick Ross wants to point out that he built his Maybach Music Empire with no backing from any of hip-hop’s heavyweights.\n\nWhile this may be true, it’s important to point out that Ross used to write for Trina back when he was signed to Slip-N-Slide Records. He also appeared on her 2002 single “Told Y'all,” though Trina wasn’t officially backing him.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NEu03bmxiZk\n\nRoss also signed to Def Jam while Jay Z served as the label’s president, but he’s right, he built his empire off the strength of his own name.", "annotation_id": "7744620", "url": "https://genius.com/7744620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "line": "I can’t see ’em running down my eyes So I gotta make the song cry", "vault_lines": ["So I gotta make the song cry"], "meaning": "Rick Ross sets this song off using lyrics from Jay Z’s 2001 single “Song Cry” from his classic The Blueprint LP.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w5srnNrICJo\n\nBefore “Song Cry,” Jay Z rarely showed emotion, especially when it came to women; but on this track Hov opened up about a past love and the heartbreak that he suffered. On the hook he rapped “I can’t see ‘em coming down my eyes, so I gotta make the song cry.”\n\nNotice how Ross simply changed “coming” to “running.”", "annotation_id": "7744544", "url": "https://genius.com/7744544", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "line": "Too many bitches, the homies could fuck ’em for me Winning in real estate, opening restaurants", "vault_lines": ["Too many bitches, the homies could fuck 'em for me", "Winning in real estate, opening restaurants"], "meaning": "Rozay is so successful that he can’t be with all the women with him, so what better thing to do to get your homies to do it for you. He’s also so successful that he owns multiple houses and restaurants around the world.", "annotation_id": "7744471", "url": "https://genius.com/7744471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "line": "Young Hov, I see you nigga I got the Blueprint in my back pocket nigga I did what you told me nigga [Verse 1: Rick Ross] Look at me nigga, I got so much fucking money", "vault_lines": ["Young Hov, I see you nigga", "I got the Blueprint in my back pocket nigga", "I did what you told me nigga", "Look at me nigga, I got so much fucking money"], "meaning": "One of Jay-Z’s many nicknames is “Young Hov”, who back in the late 90’s, early 00’s, was an icon of hip hop. Jay-Z and Rozay have featured in songs together. https://genius.com/Jay-z-fuckwithmeyouknowigotit-lyrics\n\nJay-Z gave Ross his first record deal with Def Jam after Ross' first single Hustlin'. Without Jay, where would Rozay be?\n\nOne of Young Hov’s most successful albums is The Blueprint. Rozay is using this as a double entendre, talking about him following Jay-Z as a mentor and icon, and using his album as a blueprint for shaping his own hip hop career.", "annotation_id": "7744411", "url": "https://genius.com/7744411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "line": "I just came to get the millions I just came for the millions", "vault_lines": ["I just came for the millions"], "meaning": "Rick Ross only got into the music lifestyle for the money, and look where it got him.", "annotation_id": "7744401", "url": "https://genius.com/7744401", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Icon", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-icon-lyrics", "genius_title": "Icon", "genius_id": 2296438, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Iconic", "line": "The gold Presidential (I got it)", "vault_lines": ["The gold Presidential (I got it)"], "meaning": "The Gold Presidential Rolex is one of the most recognizable models of the Swiss brand Rolex, officially called the Rolex Day-Date.\n\nMaterial: often made of gold (yellow, white, or rose), emphasizing luxury.\n\nIn hip-hop culture, the Presidential Rolex is a symbol of success, wealth, and high status, which is why rappers often mention it in lyrics and show it in photos.", "annotation_id": "37723949", "url": "https://genius.com/37723949", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Iconic", "line": "Giuliani next (Haha), Renzel wrote it", "vault_lines": ["Giuliani next (Haha), Renzel wrote it"], "meaning": "Rudolph William Louis Giuliani is an American lawyer and politician who served as the Mayor of New York City from 1994 to 2001, representing the Republican Party.", "annotation_id": "37723923", "url": "https://genius.com/37723923", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
