{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "I used to see niggas on TV, man I used to be like, “Yo, them niggas so blessed”", "vault_lines": ["I used to be like, \"Yo, them niggas so blessed\""], "meaning": "In the early 2000s, it must have been a common occurrence to catch Big Tymers and other Cash Money associates' videos on TV. A young Rozay on the come up would’ve naturally looked up to them as an aspiring MC from the South.", "annotation_id": "30429625", "url": "https://genius.com/30429625", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Stunna", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In one final dig at Birdman, Ross ends the song with Birdman’s signature adlib. “Stunna” or “#1 Stunna” is also one of Birdman’s many nicknames.\n\nInterestingly enough, Ross was featured on Birdman’s successful single, Born Stunna.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DTmwGXP2c6Q", "annotation_id": "16857613", "url": "https://genius.com/16857613", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Fast money comin’ slow, you better think quick", "vault_lines": ["Fast money comin' slow, you better think quick"], "meaning": "A reference to Birdman’s 2005 album, Fast Money", "annotation_id": "16569102", "url": "https://genius.com/16569102", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "I handed over records, never charged a coin", "vault_lines": ["I handed over records, never charged a coin"], "meaning": "DJ Khalid was on Cash Money Records for 3 albums. During his tenure at Cash Money, he made compilation albums and all three of them heavily featured Rick Ross. Rick Ross was also featured on a handful of other Cash Money artists albums. Rick Ross is stating he handed over those records and Never asked for a cent in return, and it appears Cash Money decided not to pay him after either, no act of good faith was put forward by Cash Money Records.", "annotation_id": "16141700", "url": "https://genius.com/16141700", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Publishin’ is a sin, repent, forgive me, Lord", "vault_lines": ["Publishin' is a sin, repent, forgive me, Lord"], "meaning": "Publishing is what percentage an Artist owns his song and the artist gets paid royalties accordingly. Birdman owns Cash Money Master Recordings and owns his artists Publishing and pays them according to what ever contract he has negotiated with them. While Ross hints that Birdman commits sin with artists publishing money, in plain language Birdman has commonly been accused of not pay his Cash Money Artists from Wayne, to Juve to Mannie Fresh and dozens of others.", "annotation_id": "16141670", "url": "https://genius.com/16141670", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "How the fuck, nigga, you touch half a billion, nigga And your team starvin’, nigga?", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck, nigga, you touch half a billion, nigga", "And your team starvin', nigga?"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is confronting Birdman over the fact that while he’s enjoyed financial success as the head of Cash Money Records, many of the artists signed to his label have struggled to flourish creatively and financially.\n\n\n\n$500 million is a bit of an exaggeration of Baby’s wealth. As of 2017, his net worth was a reported $180 million, which is impressive but 320 million shy of “touching half a billion.”", "annotation_id": "15025255", "url": "https://genius.com/15025255", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "This little thing of ours, not the ones to tattle on", "vault_lines": ["This little thing of ours, not the ones to tattle on"], "meaning": "The Italian Mafia is often referred to as “La Cosa Nostra” which translates to “our thing/this thing of ours.” This line is a reference to that, as well as an implied threat to those who would snitch on the family.", "annotation_id": "11793518", "url": "https://genius.com/11793518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "I’ma bring my niggas with me if I lose or win", "vault_lines": ["I'ma bring my niggas with me if I lose or win"], "meaning": "Unlike Birdman, Rick Ross is always with his team, never leaves a man behind no matter what the consequences are.\n\nBirdman can’t say the same, with many criticisms towards him as Birdman is known for his unloyalty to his team at Cashmoney Records, with not paying his team such as Wayne and being selfish and taking success to uplift himself and only himself", "annotation_id": "12687477", "url": "https://genius.com/12687477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "You on an island, nigga, you came to my city, nigga I let you in my city, nigga", "vault_lines": ["You on an island, nigga, you came to my city, nigga", "I let you in my city, nigga"], "meaning": "Before buying a mansion on Palm Island in Miami and setting himself in the city, Birdman made his business in New Orleans, where Wayne is also from and where they knew each other. As many people know, Ross is from Dade County.\n\nRoss may imply that being on an island, Birdman is not aware of the problems surrounding his label.", "annotation_id": "11677748", "url": "https://genius.com/11677748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Shootin’ dope, usin’ coke, movin’ like you the Folks", "vault_lines": ["Shootin' dope, usin' coke, movin' like you the Folks"], "meaning": "Rumors about Cash Money and especially Birdman trying to influence and “trap” artists by getting them addicted to heroin have been circulating for many years. This is most likely what Ross is referring to here.\n\nWhile it is a known fact that both Turk and B.G. were addicted to heroin and cocaine, Turk has since denied allegations of Birdman having gotten them hooked. Much rather, Turk said that it was a common thing in N.O. at the time, and that pretty much his entire circle of friends were shooting as well as snorting heroin. Turk even admitted that it was him who got B.G. involved with the substance in a 2003 HipHopDX interview:\n\nTurk: Nah. Actually man, I was shooting heroin and cocaine, and I introduced B.G. to shooting heroin and cocaine. We was on the Cash Money/Ruff Ryders tour. B.G. had been getting high; I had been getting high. In New Orleans, Uptown, that’s the drug of choice, heroin. You got kids, 12, 13-years-old on heroin. As I was coming up, people glorified it like they do mollies today. They say “pop a molly, I’m sweating,” they rap about it and this and that. Soulja Slim, who was Magnolia Slim at the time, used to rap about heroin all the time.\nPartners-N-Crime also had a song about heroin. And that was the song. And the girls used to always say they want the dope dick. So [I was like], “Shit, let me go on ahead and snort me a bag of heroin and fuck this bitch all night.” That’s what influenced us to do it.\n\nhttp://hiphopdx.com/interviews/id.2048/title.turk-revisits-birdmans-ruthless-business-compares-heroin-battle-to-ray-charles#\n\n“Movin like the Folks” is another way of saying Birdman and his brother/associates think they’re the shit.", "annotation_id": "11609409", "url": "https://genius.com/11609409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Tyga, chinchilla, really ain’t no penny pinchin’", "vault_lines": ["Tyga, chinchilla, really ain't no penny pinchin'"], "meaning": "Tyga is the only one that got out of Cash Money clean and not in debt. Although he also was not paid for most of his work. Now he is on a space where he is reaping the rewards and now wearing Chinchilla coats.\n\n\n\nPenny-pinching is the act of unwillingness to spend money. Tyga does not know the concept of penny-pinching.\n\nInteresting enough Pusha T also said:\n\nThe illusion of money we don’t believe in\nYou ask me, Tyga looking like a genius\n\nand Pusha further explained that line by saying:\n“I felt he was looking like a genius simply because it takes a lot for you to leave a situation at Cash Money— a label of prominence, with a large history of success… To me, Tyga stepped out there and said, “I ain’t have a royalty check in God knows when.”\n\nHe wasn’t looking to be more famous than rich, and he was open to the world about it.\n\nhttps://genius.com/8343820", "annotation_id": "11584257", "url": "https://genius.com/11584257", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Never slippin’, got relationships with the trillest niggas", "vault_lines": ["Never slippin', got relationships with the trillest niggas"], "meaning": "Before starting his own label, Ross was signed to Miami-based record label, Slip-N-Slide Records, where he would release his first and second album. He eventually cut ties with the label in 2009.\n\nSlip-N-Slide Records was the label home for Miami artists Trina and Trick Daddy. Plies was also a sign-ee to Slip-N-Slide Records who Ross collaborated with on DJ Khaled’s “Out Here Grinding,” and “I’m So Hood.”", "annotation_id": "11555223", "url": "https://genius.com/11555223", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Fuck a skateboard, I went and got a Wraith, boy", "vault_lines": ["Fuck a skateboard, I went and got a Wraith, boy"], "meaning": "This line correlates with the previous line about Wayne’s brand Trukfit. Lil Wayne is known for skateboarding.\n\nWayne also launched a mobile skateboarding game last year.\n\n\n\nOn the other hand, Ross alludes the fact that he can afford an expensive Wraith and implicates a “skateboard” as a cheap “waste of his time”.\n\nRozay isn’t all words either. In 2013, he brought a Rolls Royce Wraith for $400,000.", "annotation_id": "11555163", "url": "https://genius.com/11555163", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Omerta the code, Met Ball, parties with Vogue", "vault_lines": ["Omerta the code, Met Ball, parties with Vogue"], "meaning": "Omerta is the Sicilian “code of silence.” Basically, no matter what – no snitching to the police. It’s referenced in the Godfather movies and book.\n\nThe Met Ball is an annual fundraiser put on to support to the Metropolitan Museum of Art, and its guests are an invite-only list of mostly high class, A-list celebrities. Parties thrown by Vogue Magazine are made up of the same sort of people.\n\nRozay is juxtaposing his gangster and bougie lifestyles in this line.", "annotation_id": "11536945", "url": "https://genius.com/11536945", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "(Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music is Rick Ross' infamous ad-lib that you hear in many of his songs.\n\nMaybach Music Group (MMG) is a record label imprint that was founded by Ross in 2009. It’s members include well-known rappers, Wale, and Meek Mill, and R&B singer Omarion.", "annotation_id": "11536241", "url": "https://genius.com/11536241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "You can’t handle this, nigga, you can’t handle, sit down in the corner, shut the fuck up and take notes, bitch. Just take notes", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Chris using his powerful voice and commanding presence prepares people for what’s about to happen in the song. Real knowledge is going to be dropped, and you are going to learn some realness.", "annotation_id": "11536239", "url": "https://genius.com/11536239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Hard to point a finger when you live a life of sin", "vault_lines": ["Hard to point a finger when you live a life of sin"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is claiming that pointing out Birdman’s flaws is hypocritical of himself. He feels since he has sinned (e.g. his legal troubles) in his life that he’s no one to judge someone else.\n\nTo paraphrase the Bible: “Let he who is without sin cast the first stone.”", "annotation_id": "11536167", "url": "https://genius.com/11536167", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "[Skit: Chris Rock] Yo this Chris Rock! I’m in here with my man Ricky Rozay.", "vault_lines": ["Yo this Chris Rock! I'm in here with my man Ricky Rozay."], "meaning": "Before the album was released, Ross hinted at a “surprise feature”. It would seem that Chris Rock was that surprise feature.\n\nRock called Rick Ross “the greatest rapper in the world” when he was chosen to unveil the release date for Rather You Than Me in an Instagram video.\n\nRock and Ross have not always seen eye to eye; in 2014 Ross called the comedian “washed up” after Rock made a Ross fat joke at the BET awards. In 2016, Ross called Rock a “cornball” following his Oscars monologue. However, with two Rock skits on this album, it appears the two have buried all hatchets.", "annotation_id": "11530091", "url": "https://genius.com/11530091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Plenty killers and I know that Diddy with it", "vault_lines": ["Plenty killers and I know that Diddy with it"], "meaning": "Alluding to Jimmy Henchmen here to be specific.  In 2015 while already serving a life sentence for cocaine trafficking and other charges, Henchmen would be charged and sentenced to a second term of life.\n\nThis time for the murder-for-hire and conspiracy to commit murder of Lowell “Lodi Mack” Fletcher, a G-Unit affiliate.", "annotation_id": "11529530", "url": "https://genius.com/11529530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Tony Draper, J Prince and every Jimmy Henchmen", "vault_lines": ["Tony Draper, J Prince and every Jimmy Henchmen"], "meaning": "All three of these men were praised figures in the music industry, highlighting Ross' high-profile connections he mentions in the previous line.\n\nDraper, founded Draper Inc. Records managing artists such as Eddie Kane and Scoe.\n\nJ Prince is the current CEO of Rap-A-Lot Records and former boxing manager to Andre Ward and Floyd Mayweather.\n\nJimmy Henchmen was the CEO of Czar Entertainment when it managed artists such as Akon, The Game, and Sean Kingston.\n\nIt can be noted that J Prince took Lil Wayne’s side in the Baby VS Lil Wayne feud.", "annotation_id": "11529465", "url": "https://genius.com/11529465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "We in here drinkin’ this Belaire Rosé. That’s how we do it. That’s all we do, Belaire Rosé!", "vault_lines": ["We in here drinkin' this Belaire Rosé. That's how we do it. That's all we do, Belaire Rosé!"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is part owner of Luc Belaire, a French sparkling wine that is frequently featured by rappers akin to Ross.", "annotation_id": "11528799", "url": "https://genius.com/11528799", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Shots fired, home invasion out on Palm Isle Red beam detonators, who the bomb now?", "vault_lines": ["Shots fired, home invasion out on Palm Isle", "Red beam detonators, who the bomb now?"], "meaning": "Palm Isle is where Birdman’s mansion is located. In September of 2012, Birdman bought a mansion on 70 Palm Avenue, located on the exclusive Palm Island in Florida. The mansion was previously owned by record producer and former The Roots keyboardist Scott Storch.", "annotation_id": "11528364", "url": "https://genius.com/11528364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "And then I met you out on LiveNation dates Came to the realization that your watch was fake", "vault_lines": ["And then I met you out on LiveNation dates", "Came to the realization that your watch was fake"], "meaning": "Live Nation is a global entertainment company. It owns venues and organizes concerts and tours for big time artists.\n\nRoss was a supporting act for Lil' Wayne from 2008 to 2009, when he first met Stunna on the I Am Music tour.  Lil' Wayne extended the tour in 2011. It was during this time that Ross suggests he caught Birdman wearing fake jewelry.\n\nHe told Wendy Williams that Birdman’s watch wasn’t right:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/bhbGogC1Pns?t=12m22s", "annotation_id": "11526853", "url": "https://genius.com/11526853", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "That’s why this .45 in my Trukfit trunks", "vault_lines": ["That's why this .45 in my Trukfit trunks"], "meaning": "The .45 ACP (Automatic Colt Pistol), or .45 Auto is a handgun cartridge designed by John Browning in 1905, for use in his prototype Colt semi-automatic pistol.\n\n\n\nTrukfit is a premium apparel brand from the mind of Lil Wayne. Ross' mention of the apparel reaffirms that he is siding with Wayne in this feud.", "annotation_id": "11525819", "url": "https://genius.com/11525819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "I really thought you niggas really owned them cars", "vault_lines": ["I really thought you niggas really owned them cars"], "meaning": "In May 2011, Birdman bought a one-of-a-kind Maybach Excelero coupe for $8 million. But three months later, information surfaced that he hadn’t actually paid for the vehicle.", "annotation_id": "11524821", "url": "https://genius.com/11524821", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Hug Barack Obama, whisper, “As-salāmu ʿalaykum”", "vault_lines": ["Hug Barack Obama, whisper, \"As-salāmu ʿalaykum\""], "meaning": "Barack Obama served as the 44th President of the United States. He is a Protestant Christian, but is often mistaken for being Muslim because of his Arabic middle name, Hussein. He claims his religious views developed in his adult life.\n\nAs-salāmu ʿalaykum is a greeting in Arabic that means “peace be upon you.” It’s a standard salutation among Muslims.\n\nRoss likely whispered this greeting to Obama during their meeting at the White House.\n\nhttp://images.genius.com/861f7e3f61228767233e1da889a19837.564x564x1.jp", "annotation_id": "11524728", "url": "https://genius.com/11524728", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Leased whips, bad blood, that shit’ll sink ships", "vault_lines": ["Leased whips, bad blood, that shit'll sink ships"], "meaning": "This is a play on the idiom “Loose lips sink ships,” a warning against speaking carelessly. The phrase first appeared on propaganda posters in World War II which discouraged US citizens from divulging security information that could be used by enemy spies.\n\nRoss claims the Cash Money ship is sinking due to internal feuds and poor money management—leasing cars is considered one of the worst investments a person can make.", "annotation_id": "11523400", "url": "https://genius.com/11523400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "And pray that Mannie Fresh’ll get to see the light", "vault_lines": ["And pray that Mannie Fresh'll get to see the light"], "meaning": "Mannie Fresh is a rapper, producer, and DJ who produced just about all of the Cash Money classics from the late 1990s and early 2000s before leaving the label in 2004.\n\nOn SMACK DVD’s The Album Vol. 1, Mannie said:\n\nI left Cash Money because of money, scratch, moola. … I move on if something’s not right. I had to do my thing, because it wasn’t right.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/DMej_9-hEjE?t=130", "annotation_id": "11523387", "url": "https://genius.com/11523387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Damn, I grew up on that Cash Money Bling bling, was well known to flash money", "vault_lines": ["Bling bling, was well known to flash money"], "meaning": "Rozay was a teenager when Cash Money Records formed in 1991. The label signed B.G., Turk and Lil' Wayne in 1995. BG and Wayne formed the Hot Boys in 1997.\n\n“Bling Bling” is a classic BG song, which became a popular term used in hip-hop to imitate the supposed sound of jewelry when it’s hit by light.\n\nRoss entered the music industry in 2000, but claims he sold drugs and had lots of money before that happened. Cash Money motivated him to make money and be a flashy person.", "annotation_id": "11522708", "url": "https://genius.com/11522708", "state": "accepted", "votes": 71, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "A thug holiday is where your body lay Me and Trick Daddy come from a common place", "vault_lines": ["A thug holiday is where your body lay", "Me and Trick Daddy come from a common place"], "meaning": "Trick Daddy, Rozay’s label mate and fellow Floridian rapper, also had a fallout with Birdman. In a 2015 interview with The Breakfast Club, he said:\n\nI’ve done business with Birdman. Some was good, some was bad. I just think when you try and be a CEO … I just think, had Baby been more of a businessman… Like, for instance, somebody tell me what’s Cash Money address. You ever saw a Cash Money office? You ever saw a picture? There ain’t one.\n\nTrick Daddy had a 2002 album titled Thug Holiday, which featured a song of the same name. He was also involved in Rick Ross’s past beef with 50 Cent.", "annotation_id": "11521878", "url": "https://genius.com/11521878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "I pray you find the kindness in your heart for Wayne His entire life, he gave you what there was to gain I watched this whole debacle so I’m part to blame", "vault_lines": ["I pray you find the kindness in your heart for Wayne", "His entire life, he gave you what there was to gain"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne and Birdman were once close friends, but their relationship started unravelling in 2014 when Wayne first took shots at Birdman and Cash Money Records. In 2015, Wayne filed a $51 million lawsuit against Cash Money, claiming Birdman was violating the terms of his contract by withholding Tha Carter V. Later that year, Birdman sued Jay Z and Tidal for $50 million for streaming the Free Weezy Album.\n\nIn May 2016, Lil Wayne cursed out Cash Money during a live performance, encouraging the crowd to say, “Fuck the bullshit” and “Fuck Cash Money.” Wayne also took shots at C.M. in his verse on “Changed It,” his collaboration with Nicki Minaj that came out a week before this song.\n\nHowever, in January 2017, Birdman appeared on Travis Scott’s Beats 1 Radio show .wav radio, and claimed the album would be released later that year. He also commented on his relationship with Weezy:\n\nThe situation with me and my son—I’m going to put it all behind us and just let it move forward. Wayne is one of the best artists ever to do the game, and I want to see him continue to do what he been doing, and I’m going to support whatever he’s doing.\n\nTha Carter V was later released in September 2018 after Lil Wayne was released from Cash Money and started putting out music through Universal.", "annotation_id": "11521615", "url": "https://genius.com/11521615", "state": "accepted", "votes": 93, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Cigars in the Oval Office, Ronald Reagan", "vault_lines": ["Cigars in the Oval Office, Ronald Reagan"], "meaning": "The Oval Office is the office of the President of the United States. Presidents have been smoking cigars in the Office for over 200 years.\n\nAlthough some presidents attempted to ban smoking in the White House, Ronald Reagan actually endorsed several vintage cigarette brands, even though he didn’t smoke. White House doctor T. Burton attempted to convince Reagan to ban smoking, but he resisted.", "annotation_id": "11520744", "url": "https://genius.com/11520744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Damn, Stunna I loved you, nigga Hate it came to this", "vault_lines": ["I loved you, nigga", "Hate it came to this"], "meaning": "In 2000, when Birdman was still one half of the duo Big Tymers with Mannie Fresh, he released a song called “#1 Stunna.” He also has a 2007 album titled 5 Star Stunna, which featured a track called “I’m A Stunna,” and a 2012 song called “Born Stunna.”\n\nRozay once looked up to Birdman—they even released a mixtape together in 2013 called The H: The Lost Album Vol. 1. But Ross lost respect for him after his mistreatment of Lil Wayne. In a 2015 interview with The Breakfast Club, he said:\n\nRight now, really me just seeing what Wayne going through as an artist, me idolizing Birdman at a time, me looking up to Lil Wayne … For me to see the way things are transpiring, I can’t respect that, and I don’t respect that.", "annotation_id": "11520669", "url": "https://genius.com/11520669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Knew that you would never visit BG Turk came home, take that boy a three piece", "vault_lines": ["Knew that you would never visit BG", "Turk came home, take that boy a three piece"], "meaning": "Like Wayne, B.G. and Turk were signed to Cash Money as teenagers in the 1990s. BG left the label in the early 2000s over financial disputes. In 2002, he told MTV:\n\nI looked up to them and respected them. I felt like they wouldn’t do me like that, but I was wrong. [Baby] calls himself the Birdman, but he wants to birdfeed me.\n\nIn 2012, B.G. was sentenced to 14 years for witness tampering and gun possession. Although there are no reports that he wasn’t visited by Birdman, there was already bad blood between them after he left Cash Money and founded Chopper City Records in 2002.\n\nIn 2004, Turk was arrested for attempted murder and spent eight years in jail. Ross brought him a “three piece,” which is either a three piece chicken meal or a three piece suit or both.\n\nIn February of 2015, three years after his release, he filed a lawsuit of $1.3 million for unpaid royalties against Cash Money Records.", "annotation_id": "11520612", "url": "https://genius.com/11520612", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Last request, can all producers please get paid?", "vault_lines": ["Last request, can all producers please get paid?"], "meaning": "Ross alludes to the producers who worked for Cash Money, but have since spoken out against the label because after not being compensated for their work. Notable examples include Bangladesh who didn’t receive payment for his production on Lil Wayne’s 2008 hit single “A Milli,” and Jim Jonsin, who sued Wayne for “Lollipop” royalties. The same situation occurred with the Bangladesh-produced “6 Foot 7 Foot.”\n\nBangladesh took Cash Money to court over unpaid royalties for both songs, but settled the case in March 2012 and later signed a contract with Cash Money.\n\nRoss may also be referencing Mannie Fresh, who produced the majority of Ca$h Money’s music from 1993-2005, until he left over financial mismanagement.", "annotation_id": "11520030", "url": "https://genius.com/11520030", "state": "accepted", "votes": 80, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "All Miami issues, Rozay handle for him Same way Big Ducky do for me in California", "vault_lines": ["All Miami issues, Rozay handle for him", "Same way Big Ducky do for me in California"], "meaning": "Ross claims that he used his power in his hometown Miami to smooth over unnamed problems Birdman had there—presumably these were “street” issues with local criminals.\n\nBig Ducky is an associate of Ross' from California, pictured here in a 2016 Instagram photo with the caption “My family Big Duck @ Maybach Estates.”\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BMcofKiDwg_/\n\nIn 2010, rumors circulated about Rick Ross having problems with members of the Crips gang in California.", "annotation_id": "11519716", "url": "https://genius.com/11519716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "And what hurt me the most, nigga Is how you did my brother Khaled, nigga Khaled was loyal to you, nigga The pain I seen in my brother’s eye, nigga FaceTimin’ my nigga, nigga, he took that to the chin, nigga That’s why my nigga blessed! That’s why my nigga Khaled blessed! You put my nigga in the hole, homie I don’t feel you for that, my nigga That shit hurt me, you under-dig? Umm", "vault_lines": ["And what hurt me the most, nigga", "Is how you did my brother Khaled, nigga"], "meaning": "“In the hole,” means “in debt.”  Ross told Billboard about how the contract that Khaled signed with Birdman resulted in financial loss.\n\nFor [Khaled] to owe someone millions of dollars and act like this is a normal business practice? It’s not.  Just to see the way [Birdman] did [Khaled’s] family, that’s unacceptable…\n\nDJ Khaled signed to Cash Money in 2010 and left in 2015. A lot of other artists were leaving Cash Money during this time, including Busta Rhymes, Bow Wow and Limp Bizkit.\n\nPeople were under the impression he was still with Cash Money until he went on the Breakfast Club and said he isn’t signed to the label at all.  He offered no explanation why he left, but he did say Wayne and Birdman are family, likely since he’s not the type to dwell on negativity.\n\nKhaled spoke in a Genius interview about his longstanding relationship with Birdman and Cash Money Records.  He has moved forward and is known for always using the word “blessed.” He went into more detail about the Birdman situation in a 2017 interview with Hot 97, revealing that he took his own risks and takes responsiblity for what happened:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/_jE1OgNyvIg?t=34m10s", "annotation_id": "11519516", "url": "https://genius.com/11519516", "state": "accepted", "votes": 141, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Bible on the dash, kilos on the seat", "vault_lines": ["Bible on the dash, kilos on the seat"], "meaning": "From vending drugs to reciting with God, Ross is showing the juxtaposition of being righteous and a sinner.\n\n“Bible on the dash” is also a reference to MMG rapper and Rick Ross protege Gunplay’s 2013 single “Bible on the Dash.”", "annotation_id": "11519431", "url": "https://genius.com/11519431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "Eatin’ Wingstop, what you know about Wingstop, nigga? You don’t know nothin’ about no Wingstop.", "vault_lines": ["Eatin' Wingstop, what you know about Wingstop, nigga? You don't know nothin' about no Wingstop."], "meaning": "Rick Ross is a franchise owner of Wingstop, operating at least 25 restaurants.", "annotation_id": "11519254", "url": "https://genius.com/11519254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "line": "You stole them boys’ pub’ and bought a foreclosure Scott Storch demons in it, which is more poison", "vault_lines": ["You stole them boys' pub' and bought a foreclosure", "Scott Storch demons in it, which is more poison"], "meaning": "In 2012, Birdman purchased the Miami mansion of producer Scott Storch out of foreclosure for $14.5 million, after Storch lost it in a bankruptcy filing caused by his severe cocaine addiction. Ross claims that Birdman used his Cash Money artists' publishing money to make the purchase.\n\n\n\nThe law of karma eventually turned against Birdman, and the house was foreclosed on due to unpaid loans.", "annotation_id": "11519082", "url": "https://genius.com/11519082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 168, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Idols Become Rivals", "status": "done", "targets": 40, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-idols-become-rivals-lyrics", "genius_title": "Idols Become Rivals", "genius_id": 3019831, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Life amazin’, wake up in new places Big faces stuffed in suitcases", "vault_lines": ["Life amazin', wake up in new places", "Big faces stuffed in suitcases"], "meaning": "Life is amazing, he’s undergone the transformation from having close to nothing to being a successful, extremely wealthy rap star (“big faces” refers to high dollar-denomination bills) who has the means to travel all over the world.", "annotation_id": "4490762", "url": "https://genius.com/4490762", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Played the hand I was dealt, few aces", "vault_lines": ["Played the hand I was dealt, few aces"], "meaning": "To “play the hand you are dealt” is to make the best out of a situation despite difficult circumstances that are out of your control.  In a game of cards, you must use the cards that you are dealt the best you can to win, even if the cards are not favorable.  In many card games the “ace” is the best card to have, so Rick saying that he had “few aces” implies that life’s circumstances often didn’t make things easy.", "annotation_id": "4490659", "url": "https://genius.com/4490659", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "She in love with the life, champagne and all the lights Chanel sneakers and scarves, I want you to be my wife We can run around the world and tuck with no fear G4, G5, whole team here Call ourselves friends, but we holdin’ hands", "vault_lines": ["She in love with the life, champagne and all the lights", "Chanel sneakers and scarves, I want you to be my wife", "We can run around the world and tuck with no fear"], "meaning": "Rozay officially extends an invitation into his lifestyle, allowing her to meet up with the rest of the MMG crew members. There’s something inherently romantic about being 35,000 feet in the air in G4 (Gulfstream 400) and G5 (Gulfstream 500) private airplanes.", "annotation_id": "4442385", "url": "https://genius.com/4442385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Biggest boss in the business and really that’s to infinite", "vault_lines": ["Biggest boss in the business and really that's to infinite"], "meaning": "Rick runs things, and here he puts it into perspective for us.  He is the biggest; there’s no one more powerful that him, however in his instance, it could also be taken literally.\n\nRegardless of meaning, he has no limits – his power is infinite.", "annotation_id": "4416613", "url": "https://genius.com/4416613", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Green Goyard bag, it got the tool in it", "vault_lines": ["Green Goyard bag, it got the tool in it"], "meaning": "Goyard Bags are sophisticated and luxurious handbags that are a symbol of wealth and power.\n\n\n\nThese probably aren’t used to conceal many guns; Rozay’s just classy and wouldn’t use a normal duffel bag.", "annotation_id": "4407235", "url": "https://genius.com/4407235", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "She not a side chick, she all in my lane", "vault_lines": ["She not a side chick, she all in my lane"], "meaning": "Rick doesn’t treat his girl like a side chick that he’d call for quick satisfaction whenever he needs it, but treats her like his main chick and gets her included in anything that involves him. She’s “ride or die” and probably carrying out tasks that only those closest to him could perform. She’s now an integral part of the operation.", "annotation_id": "4407178", "url": "https://genius.com/4407178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "She from a lovin’ home, I’m from a troubled home One bedroom, didn’t have a telephone", "vault_lines": ["She from a lovin' home, I'm from a troubled home", "One bedroom, didn't have a telephone"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is from a troubled home where love was scarce and his girl is from a home where love was abundant. Its hard to be with someone who doesn’t know what you’ve been through, but as the saying goes: “opposites attract”.\n\n\n\nOne bedroom, didn’t have a telephone is a clever way of referring to a jail cell.", "annotation_id": "4407166", "url": "https://genius.com/4407166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Small waist, red weaves", "vault_lines": ["Small waist, red weaves"], "meaning": "Ross is probably referring to K. Michelle who’s featured on the song, has a nice waist, and is usually seen with red hair.", "annotation_id": "4407117", "url": "https://genius.com/4407117", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "It will never last but it feels so good, guess I gotta deal with it This is so all bad, this is so all bad", "vault_lines": ["This is so all bad, this is so all bad"], "meaning": "For the time being K. Michelle is enjoying every moment she’s having with her lover, but she sees  signs in their relationship that all the sweetness won’t last forever. She feels as if the train has derailed, it’s only a matter of time before it crashes.", "annotation_id": "4407065", "url": "https://genius.com/4407065", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Sweet but sad, I don’t know love ruins a relationship", "vault_lines": ["Sweet but sad, I don't know love ruins a relationship"], "meaning": "Love either tends to be a blessing or a curse  depending on the issues the lovers experience in their relationship. Love is sparked by the fires of passion, but often consumes itself.", "annotation_id": "4407047", "url": "https://genius.com/4407047", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Got alot of questions, am I a controllin’ man? I run the streets but I’m well known in Japan As a G, a boss, the money coming fast", "vault_lines": ["Got alot of questions, am I a controllin' man?", "I run the streets but I'm well known in Japan", "As a G, a boss, the money coming fast"], "meaning": "Are you mad cause I’m asking you 21 questions?\n\nRoss ponders if he’s being overbearing when he asks his girl questions to find out as much as possible about her. It’s interesting that ‘am I a controlling man?’ is a question in and of itself.\n\nRoss asserts that the only thing controlling about him is his boss-like nature. Running the game where he lives and known around the world.", "annotation_id": "4273262", "url": "https://genius.com/4273262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Please believe in niggas that’s still schemin’", "vault_lines": ["Please believe in niggas that's still schemin'"], "meaning": "You should trust in those who remain on their hustle.\n\nReference to Stay Schemin'.", "annotation_id": "4273253", "url": "https://genius.com/4273253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "I’m gettin’ high, I’m above the law", "vault_lines": ["I'm gettin' high, I'm above the law"], "meaning": "Even though smoking marijuana is illegal, Ross gets away with it because he doesn’t follow those rules.\n\n\n\nDope wordplay on getting ‘high’, and escalating ‘above’ the law.", "annotation_id": "4273244", "url": "https://genius.com/4273244", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "Black car, keep it flyer than them Red Wings", "vault_lines": ["Black car, keep it flyer than them Red Wings"], "meaning": "Rozay at his best. The Detroit Red Wings (NHL) club emblem is – yeah, you guessed it – a red, flying wing. He will keep it flyer than this though.", "annotation_id": "4272845", "url": "https://genius.com/4272845", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "This is so all bad, nothin’ good can come from this", "vault_lines": ["This is so all bad, nothin' good can come from this"], "meaning": "She is saying her relationship with whoever she’s with is not good because of their life of crime and nothing good can come from it if they continue to date.", "annotation_id": "4272762", "url": "https://genius.com/4272762", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "If They Knew", "line": "She a quiet chick, may let her see some things", "vault_lines": ["She a quiet chick, may let her see some things"], "meaning": "Rozay’s girl is quiet in that he knows she won’t snitch or rat him out, she’s loyal. So, he might let her see some parts of the drug kingpin he put together as he will have no worries about her busting him.", "annotation_id": "4272389", "url": "https://genius.com/4272389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
