{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ima Boss (Remix)", "line": "The world is an asshole and we the next big shit", "vault_lines": ["The world is an asshole and we the next big shit"], "meaning": "Shits come out of assholes, so wayne is saying that they are the next big thing to come out of this world. This could also just be wayne calling everyone assholes.", "annotation_id": "32874659", "url": "https://genius.com/32874659", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ima Boss (Remix)", "line": "I just fucked an Avatar, now I got a blue dick", "vault_lines": ["I just fucked an Avatar, now I got a blue dick"], "meaning": "the avatar is blue….. he fucked the avatar… now he has a blue dick", "annotation_id": "28755555", "url": "https://genius.com/28755555", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ima Boss (Remix)", "line": "And I got the gats, Gilbert Arenas", "vault_lines": ["And I got the gats, Gilbert Arenas"], "meaning": "Gilbert Arenas is a retired NBA player who is mostly remembered for his performance with Washington Wizards in mid 2000s. This line is a reference to his infamous gun incident with another former Wizards player Javaris Crittenton. The two were reported to bring unloaded guns to Wizards' locker room regarding gambling debts in 2010. Arenas then pretended he was shooting his teammates surrounding him during a pregame introductions to make fun of the situation. Eventually, both ended up getting suspended for the rest of that season after meeting with the NBA commissioner back then David Stern. The criminal investigation also took place and punishments were given to each.", "annotation_id": "16982640", "url": "https://genius.com/16982640", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ima Boss (Remix)", "line": "I was shining every summer", "vault_lines": ["When I came up in this bitch I was shining every summer"], "meaning": "An obvious reference to lyrics from “Stuntin' like my Daddy” one of Birdman’s most popular songs (which also featured Lil' Wayne):\n\n“You know we shine every summer, we grind every summer, and this is how we spend money”\n\nStuntin' like my Daddy was released 6 years prior to the recording of this song. He most likely thinks of this song as when he finally came up because “Like father, Like son” (his collaboration album with Lil' Wayne) was his highest ranking studio album peaking at number 3 on the Billboard 200 in 2006, which beat his first two albums, Baby aka the #1 Stunna (no. 24) & Fast Money (no. 9) that featured hits such as: “What Happened to that Boy”, “Get your Shine on”, and “Neck of the Woods”", "annotation_id": "14535104", "url": "https://genius.com/14535104", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ima Boss (Remix)", "line": "I still whip it like it’s Anna Mae", "vault_lines": ["I still whip it like it's Anna Mae"], "meaning": "Referring to Tina Turner, real name Anna Mae Bullock, and how her husband Ike used to physically beat her.\n\nRoss uses a similar line to this on Drake’s Lord Knows.", "annotation_id": "1703585", "url": "https://genius.com/1703585", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ima Boss (Remix)", "line": "Niggas really be fraud (huh), I’ma keep it a C-note (Huh) Got shooters down in Miami, they throw it like Dan Marino", "vault_lines": ["Niggas really be fraud (huh), I'ma keep it a C-note (Huh)", "Got shooters down in Miami, they throw it like Dan Marino"], "meaning": "Dan Marino was the legendary quarterback for the Miami Dolphins. Meek Mill is saying that he has the best jewelers in Miami making jewelry for him, similar to how Dan Marino is one of the greats.", "annotation_id": "457253", "url": "https://genius.com/457253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
