{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "They scream Maybach on the cell blocks", "vault_lines": ["They scream Maybach on the cell blocks"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s label is named MMG, standing for Maybach Music Group.\n\nHe’s also released 5 songs in his Maybach Music series.\n\nRoss is also a lover of Maybachs, owning a few himself.", "annotation_id": "2852617", "url": "https://genius.com/2852617", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Now our bond deep, deeper than the rap", "vault_lines": ["Now our bond deep, deeper than the rap"], "meaning": "Rick Ross again talking about his lavish lifestyle, the use of the word ‘balling’ used frequently throughout this record. However, Ross now balls outside of the rap game too—he’s become one of the biggest entrepreneurs in the game! He owns several Wingstop franchises and has a few endorsement deals.\n\nThis also refers back to his 3rd studio album, Deeper Than Rap .", "annotation_id": "2851149", "url": "https://genius.com/2851149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Don’t apologize, I quite enjoy messy I see that bottle after bottle got you goin’ crazy And doin’ shows after shows got me so lazy So ride it out for me, and take it off for me", "vault_lines": ["So ride it out for me, and take it off for me"], "meaning": "She’s probably trying to keep up with the XO Gang after a show (typical Abel) but can’t hang. It’s okay, though – he’s no stranger to getting dirty, even if you’re white girl wasted!\n\n\n\nThis verse also notes how Abel is tired after doing all these shows and worldwide tours (hence why he got so lazy after the shows). He tells the girl to ride him because he’s too tired to fuck her any other way. Sounds pretty familiar.", "annotation_id": "2850894", "url": "https://genius.com/2850894", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Gotta grind ’till your eyes close", "vault_lines": ["Gotta grind 'till your eyes close"], "meaning": "#DOUBLE ENTENDRE\n\n\nBeing “on the grind” means to be working hard towards some sort of goal you have in life. This goal could be a grind to the top of the rap game, or a grind to be the top hustler on your block. This would make the line interpreted as “grind until you die.” Instead of referring to death, Ross could also be saying he’s on his grind all day; he only stops to catch some Z’s, once his eyes are open/he awakens, it’s back to the grind.\nRoss could also be referring to grinding (the dance), since he was talking about fucking and getting head in the previous lines. This interpretation would cause this part of the line to be interpreted in a sexual light, rather than a determined, “trying to make it to the top” tone.", "annotation_id": "2850505", "url": "https://genius.com/2850505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Stay strapped ’till the trap close", "vault_lines": ["Stay strapped 'till the trap close"], "meaning": "Ross was affiliated with the Boobie Boys back in the 90’s, they are notorious for their drug trafficking. Ross most likely dealt Crack Cocaine while he was affiliated with the Boobie Boys.\n\nIn this line, Ross uses the word “trap”, which is referring to a drug deal, or a location where drugs are being dealt. He also refers to “being strapped”, which means you’re packing heat, in other words your bringing guns with you.\n\n#KEEP YOUR GUNS ON YOU AND READY TILL YOU CLOSE THE DEAL!", "annotation_id": "2850504", "url": "https://genius.com/2850504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Twenty-five mil’, I’m doing twenty-five-to-life", "vault_lines": ["Twenty-five mil', I'm doing twenty-five-to-life"], "meaning": "By 25 mil, Ross is referring to his net worth, which according  to Celebrity Net Worth is 25 million dollars.\n\n“25-to-life” is a term for the standard prison sentence for murder, which is between 25 years to life imprisonment. This phrase has also been used by Eminem in his song of the same name.", "annotation_id": "2850471", "url": "https://genius.com/2850471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "I’m the champ, baby, Real Deal Holyfield", "vault_lines": ["I'm the champ, baby, Real Deal Holyfield"], "meaning": "Ross, of course, recently purchased the real Real Deal Holyfield’s 109-room repossessed mansion.", "annotation_id": "2850311", "url": "https://genius.com/2850311", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Private elevator goin’ straight to my unit", "vault_lines": ["Private elevator goin' straight to my unit"], "meaning": "Whether or not Abel has a permanent place of residence, he is about that penthouse life. Note also the glaringly obvious sexual connotation of this line; she’s giving him a private show.", "annotation_id": "2850202", "url": "https://genius.com/2850202", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "I don’t got a single sober vein in my body", "vault_lines": ["I don't got a single sober vein in my body"], "meaning": "Abel constantly uses weed, ecstasy and percocets so he’s always high. He hasn’t got a single “sober” vein in his body because he’s high non-stop.\n\n\n\nAdding off of the previous line, no one can stop him from taking this path, which he probably can afford to do now since he needs some way to exhale the stresses of life.\n\nHe’s made many songs about being high before.", "annotation_id": "2850197", "url": "https://genius.com/2850197", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Bitches runnin’ wild gettin’ faded in the bathroom", "vault_lines": ["Bitches runnin' wild gettin' faded in the bathroom"], "meaning": "Getting “faded” is a popular term for getting high, in the context of bathroom, The Weeknd is most likely referring to cocaine. Doing drugs is widely considered as a wild activity, and doing it in the bathroom of a party probably enhances that experience.\n\nThe Weeknd may also very well be saying that the women are running around the house with little to no clothes on, relating that line to the adult entertainment company, Girls Gone Wild.\n\n\n\nThis line is also reminiscent of this line from Loft Music and also seems like a nod to the House of Balloons album art. Of course, being the sexually adventurous man he is, Abel is no stranger to having sex in the bathroom.", "annotation_id": "2850186", "url": "https://genius.com/2850186", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Tour bus like a National Geographic", "vault_lines": ["Tour bus like a National Geographic"], "meaning": "The Weeknd just recently finished touring the North American leg of his Fall Tour and also headlined for Justin Timberlake. He is now on Drake’s Would You Like a Tour in Europe. His tour bus has been around the world, similar to the National Geographic (magazine).\n\n\n\nWhen looking at the next line with this one, it can be seen this line sets up the next: his tour bus is like National Geographic because “bitches [are] runnin' wild,” like animals.\n\nThere could also a lot of topless women in his Tour Bus. You may find lots of tribal nudity in a National Geographic magazine. Even more likely, since National Geographic covers the exotic, the analogy could be everything on his tour bus is too. Exotic women, exotic clothing, exotic drugs.", "annotation_id": "2850166", "url": "https://genius.com/2850166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "Can’t nobody stop me, used to be homeless (Used to be homeless) Now that penthouse at the Ritz where my home is", "vault_lines": ["Can't nobody stop me, used to be homeless (Used to be homeless)", "Now that penthouse at the Ritz where my home is"], "meaning": "Around the time that Kiss Land was released fans that called the number 647-794-9223 received a message from The Weeknd which revealed his previous homelessness.\n\nIf it wasn’t for you I wouldn’t be able to write music. From being homeless to travelling the world in such a short time, it’s made me realize I’ll never stop going, and I do it all for you.\n\nWe know that Abel is a hard worker that refuses to quit grinding, and now that he is far from homeless, with a net worth of an estimated 50 million dollars, he fully takes advantage of his monetary gains to live in the most expensive rooms in the Ritz-Carlton Hotel.", "annotation_id": "2850109", "url": "https://genius.com/2850109", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "She give me brain, she a mastermind to be exact She a mastermind to be exact", "vault_lines": ["She give me brain, she a mastermind to be exact", "She a mastermind to be exact"], "meaning": "Ties into the previous line where he mentions his previous album title Deeper Than Rap and here he mentions this album’s title Mastermind. Notice the wordplay with brain and mastermind, mind is another word for brain:\n\nTo give brain is to give someone a blow job. So, she gave him such great brain, that he thinks she is a mastermind (or master at giving head).", "annotation_id": "2850091", "url": "https://genius.com/2850091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "That’s when she went and tatted double M G", "vault_lines": ["That's when she went and tatted double M G"], "meaning": "Referring to Ross' record label, Maybach Music Group. After just a short experience with Ross, she fell in love with him and wanted to become his girl, as symbolized by her getting a tattoo of his label.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to Drake’s line in “Free Spirit”\n\nTat my name on you girls so I know it’s real\nTat my fuckin' name on you so I know it’s real", "annotation_id": "2850085", "url": "https://genius.com/2850085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "In Vein", "line": "She wanna buy a dream, I said I don’t sell it But she can rent it for a night, I don’t mind, open wide ’Cause all this fame, I earned it, I might as well use it", "vault_lines": ["But she can rent it for a night, I don't mind, open wide", "'Cause all this fame, I earned it, I might as well use it"], "meaning": "She wants to get with him so that she can live out the dream with his money, she is a Gold Digger, but he is aware of this and tells her straight off the bat he isn’t going to get into a long term relationship with her (or that he doesn’t sell dreams).\n\n\n\nDespite him not selling dreams, he will rent her a dream sexual experience for one night, because he doesn’t mind fucking her (as shown by him telling her to open her legs wide) and because that’s what fame’s for, isn’t it?", "annotation_id": "2849968", "url": "https://genius.com/2849968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
