{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Inkredible", "line": "Then I pull your card, then I deal with you", "vault_lines": ["Then I pull your card, then I deal with you"], "meaning": "Here, Wayne uses card games (such as poker or blackjack) as a metaphor to demonstrate how he handles fake people.\n\nTo “pull someone’s card” means to expose, challenge, or call out someone for acting like a fraud. Just like how a card dealer pulls cards from the pile and deals them to players at the table, Wayne pulls fake people’s cards and deals with them.", "annotation_id": "41549070", "url": "https://genius.com/41549070", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
