{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Paranoid, I’m walkin’ ’round I’m butt naked with my chopper, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Paranoid, I'm walkin' 'round", "I'm butt naked with my chopper, nigga"], "meaning": "Here, Ross is referring to General Butt Naked. He was an African soldier and leader in the First Liberian Civil War who killed thousands of men, women, children. He fought naked because he believed it made him fight stronger.\n\nRoss is comparing his strength with his gun, to General Butt Naked’s strength in battle.", "annotation_id": "3225141", "url": "https://genius.com/3225141", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "A psycho, God made me that ’Cause I fade to black, I gets down like a plane attack", "vault_lines": ["A psycho, God made me that", "'Cause I fade to black, I gets down like a plane attack"], "meaning": "Reference to the plane attack of 9/11. During this attack the Twin Towers collapsed (or got down), and faded to black by the black smoke.\n\nMac also fades to black: a dark side in his head is taking over, he’s a psycho, and there’s nothing he can do about it.", "annotation_id": "3192304", "url": "https://genius.com/3192304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Done doin’ promo", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "From a business perspective, Mac has taken a very different approach to promotion ever since his second LP, Watching Movies With The Sound Off.\n\nHe wants to let the music talk for itself rather than surround it with hype, as he describes in this interview with Forbes:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0pfhcJjKCpA", "annotation_id": "3190377", "url": "https://genius.com/3190377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "M-M-M-M-M-M", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group is Rick Ross' record label, which he founded himself.", "annotation_id": "3189702", "url": "https://genius.com/3189702", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Think it’s fake? Bitch, test me", "vault_lines": ["Jet skis and the best weed, think it's fake? Bitch, test me"], "meaning": "Ever since 50 Cent revealed that Ross used to work at a prison, people started questioning whether Ross was a real gangster or not, or if he has ever even sold any drugs in his life.\n\nRoss of course knows the truth – insinuating that everything he raps about is legit, that he really is a drug kingpin. If you don’t believe him and think he’s soft, you’re welcome to fight him and prove him wrong. But since he’s already survived an assassination attempt, he knows you are too scared to fight him – in your heart you know he’s legit.", "annotation_id": "3188897", "url": "https://genius.com/3188897", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "White girl in a black Phantom", "vault_lines": ["California, Atlanta, white girl in a black Phantom"], "meaning": "Rozay either literally has a white girl with him in his Phantom, or he moved his cocaine from his Monte Carlo to the Rolls Royce\n\n\n\nRozay seems to have an affinity for RR’s, since he frequently raps about them, and even became the first nigga with a (2014) Wraith soon after they were put on the market\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lrds0ju1qNM", "annotation_id": "3188339", "url": "https://genius.com/3188339", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "And I don’t sleep at all", "vault_lines": ["And I don't sleep at all"], "meaning": "Mac Miller doesn’t sleep at all, thus him being an insomniac. He also has a song titled “Up All Night”, so he probably doesn’t sleep because he is too busy partying.\n\n\n\nAlso, another reason as to why he doesn’t sleep is probably because sleep is the cousin of death.", "annotation_id": "3187224", "url": "https://genius.com/3187224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Bought the estate from a boxer nigga", "vault_lines": ["Bought the estate from a boxer nigga"], "meaning": "Rozay recently purchased former boxing champion, Evander Holyfield’s 109-room foreclosed Georgia mansion for a reported $5.8 Million.", "annotation_id": "3187072", "url": "https://genius.com/3187072", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "(How does it feel?)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This snippet is taken from D'Angelo’s “Untitled (How Does It Feel)”, a sexually-themed ballad.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&v=SxVNOnPyvIU#t=86\n\nMac uses this snippet in a different way – asking how it feels to know that he’s getting money.\n\nAlso, this sample is used for the same purpose as the sample Kanye used on “On Sight”: contrast. Both songs have a raw, hard-hitting beat. The very suddenly interrupting and surprisingly soulful sample emphasizes the “ugliness” of the song. After the weird sample has finished, the song goes on like nothing has happened.", "annotation_id": "3187033", "url": "https://genius.com/3187033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "The don, Ricky Farrakhan, huh?", "vault_lines": ["The don, Ricky Farrakhan, huh?"], "meaning": "On the phone Farrakhan gave me my first Quran\nWe joined hands, said a prayer, may Allah bless the don\n\nHere Rozay is flipping the name of Louis Farrakhan,\n\nFarrakhan is a controversial black american religious leader and activist. As well as being an ex-minister of major Islamic mosques in Harlem and Boston, Farrakhan is most known for being the leader of the political and religious group “Nation of Islam”.\n\nPictured Rick Ross and Louis Farrakhan:\n\n\n\nJay Electronica called himself Farrakhan as well:\n\nI’m the Farrakhan of rap and I get it from the wheel", "annotation_id": "3186658", "url": "https://genius.com/3186658", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Pants sag, Jimmy Fallon", "vault_lines": ["I'm jet-lagged, don't need a stylist, pants sag, Jimmy Fallon"], "meaning": "Here Rozay uses Jimmy Fallon’s name to tell us his pants are hanging low.\n\n‘Fallon’ sounds very similar to ‘falling’.\n\nIt’s also good to note that he performed “Devil is a Lie” on Jimmy Fallon’s late night talk show.\n\n\n\nCheck out the performance here.", "annotation_id": "3186601", "url": "https://genius.com/3186601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "He’s self made, Mac Miller my real nigga", "vault_lines": ["He's self made, Mac Miller my real nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross mentions Self Made a lot and it’s also a album compilation series.\n\n\n\nMac Miller is also self made\n\n\nHe’s independent and his debut album Blue Slide Park sold 145,000 copies in its first week which is a lot for a independent album\nHe has his own Television Series\nHe produces the Majority of his own songs\n\n\n\nThe list continues…….\n\nSelf Made", "annotation_id": "3186289", "url": "https://genius.com/3186289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "See a muh’fucker like me gettin’ money", "vault_lines": ["See a muh'fucker like me gettin' money"], "meaning": "Mac now has a net worth of $6 million. His debut album Blue Slide Park sold nearly 400.000 units, and since the album was released through an independent label, Mac made more money out of it. He also has an MTV reality TV show, a clothing line and a budding record label.", "annotation_id": "3080454", "url": "https://genius.com/3080454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Bitch, you better have my money", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, you better have my money"], "meaning": "A reference to fellow rapper Ol' Dirty Bastard, or ODB for short. His song “Got Your Money” has always been a cult classic, spawning songs from rappers such as Tyga.\n\nMore recently, though, this song was boosted to fame by  Drake’s “Worst Behavior”, which Mac literally just mentioned a few bars ago on this track.", "annotation_id": "3070253", "url": "https://genius.com/3070253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Treat her like a dog how I do that bitch, uh", "vault_lines": ["Treat her like a dog how I do that bitch, uh"], "meaning": "Dogs have a good life: they are just eating, playing and especially chilling. Mac is doing the exact same thing.\nA bitch is not just a unpleasant woman, but also a female dog! Staying in the ‘dog-theme’, Mac is a dog: chilling and fucking bitches.\nSo how is mac doing that bitch? doggystyle.\n\nMac also recently got himself a dog: Ralphie!\n\nhttp://instagram.com/p/j-Lo2jwa0p/", "annotation_id": "3063790", "url": "https://genius.com/3063790", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Bought a brand new crib, yeah, I move that brick", "vault_lines": ["Bought a brand new crib, yeah, I move that brick"], "meaning": "At an age of only 22 years old, Mac already owns his mansion! In this mansion, his own reality show takes place.\n\nAlso a possible double entendre:\n\n\n“moving bricks” means “selling drugs”\nMac moved from Pittsburgh to California, so you could say he moved his own bricks\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ref16TzzOow", "annotation_id": "3063555", "url": "https://genius.com/3063555", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "I’m an insomniac, a muh’fuckin’ insomniac (Look bitch, don’t try and speak around me) I’m an insomniac, a muh’fuckin’ insomniac (Bitch I don’t speak French, look bitch, don’t try and speak around me) I’m an insomniac, a muh’fuckin’ insomniac (Oh, hello, Q)", "vault_lines": ["I'm an insomniac, a muh'fuckin' insomniac"], "meaning": "An insomniac is someone who has insomnia, which is a sleep disorder in which there is an inability to fall asleep or to stay asleep as long as desired.\n\nMac might refer to the fact that he’s always making music – even at night – and because of that he never sleeps. Another take could be that Mac doesn’t sleep much as a result of a life full of partying.\n\nThis track was played live by Mac, and hasn’t been released yet. Mac always plays songs live before releasing them as a single to promote an upcoming album or single. This track will probably be on one of the four (!) albums/projects Mac has made, ready to drop in 2014. Mac is a true workaholic.\n\n\n\nMac’s also shouting out his Most Dope teammate, Quentin", "annotation_id": "3063542", "url": "https://genius.com/3063542", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Insomniak", "line": "Muh’fuckers never loved us Comin’ for your money, muh’fucker, don’t trust us (Nah)", "vault_lines": ["Muh'fuckers never loved us"], "meaning": "Another nod to fellow Jewish rapper, Drake, as Mac takes a concept of his track “Worst Behavior” and puts a twist on it.\n\nOn my worst behavior, no? They used to never want to hear us\nRemember? Mothafucka never loved us\n\nMac’s competition has never been fond of him, Mac takes that as motivation to takeover your bank account and that’s why Mac is never trusted.", "annotation_id": "3060089", "url": "https://genius.com/3060089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
