{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Instagram That H**", "line": "Andy Warhol on my wall so all yall heard the bitch scream", "vault_lines": ["Andy Warhol on my wall so all yall heard the bitch scream"], "meaning": "Andy Warhol was a famous artist that has a painting named the Scream.\n\n\n\nOf course it was actually based on a painting by Edvard Munch also by the same name.\n\n\n\nFat Joe is just bragging that he can afford expensive artwork and he can please a woman.", "annotation_id": "1179305", "url": "https://genius.com/1179305", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Instagram That H**", "line": "Instagram that jet", "vault_lines": ["Instagram that ho, Instagram that ho"], "meaning": "Due to the lifestyle rappers are able to afford private jets, also known as “PJ’s”.  What Fat Joe is infering is that he should take a picture to show that he is doing something that most people are unable to do.", "annotation_id": "1128361", "url": "https://genius.com/1128361", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Instagram That H**", "line": "Instagram that ho, Instagram that ho Instagram that ho, Instagram that ho", "vault_lines": ["Instagram that ho, Instagram that ho"], "meaning": "Instagram is a social network program where you mobile upload pictures.  It was acquired by facebook in 2012, for 1 Billion dollars.  Founded by Kevin Systrom it is a popular app used by rappers to show off their illustrius lifestyle.\n\nWhat Juicy J is insinuating is that this certain female is very attractive and that a picture should be taken of her.\n\nRick Ross is also notorious for having one of the best Instagram accounts, documenting his lavish lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "1128355", "url": "https://genius.com/1128355", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Instagram That H**", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Fat-joe-instagram-that-h-lyrics", "genius_title": "Instagram That H**", "genius_id": 92166, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Intro (Mastermind)", "line": "Even your own success", "vault_lines": ["Even your own success"], "meaning": "The outro is a preparation to the following track of the album, Rich is Gangsta.", "annotation_id": "13837741", "url": "https://genius.com/13837741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Intro (Mastermind)", "line": "Now there is something you need to know about the mastermind In order to understand the overall concept and the prior to achieve success in all that you do You must know that you can borrow other people knowledges, achievements, life experiences, and even their personal ressources in order to execute your own life goals By adapting this one idea, you can achieve more in a short time than you could in a lifetime otherwise", "vault_lines": ["Now there is something you need to know about the mastermind"], "meaning": "Napoleon Hill is defining what a mastermind is—someone who not only sets out to accomplish a task, but completes said task as well.\n\nIt can be assumed that this speech is what inspired Ross to title his sixth album as such. Rozay himself was asked on the MasterMind album title, and his definition of a mastermind is similar to Hill’s:\n\nIt’s all about coming from wherever you come from and take it wherever you want to go to. And the minute you do that that’s when you can consider yourself a mastermind", "annotation_id": "2777319", "url": "https://genius.com/2777319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Intro (Mastermind)", "line": "“Push it to the-” “Everyday I’m-” “Ten years later-for me to cash out”", "vault_lines": ["\"Ten years later-for me to cash out\""], "meaning": "These lines are all taken from various songs from Rozay’s debut album, Port of Miami. Ross begins this album with lines from his debut album in order to portray the evolution his career has taken.\n\nThe first line is taken from “Push It”, the second single. The second line is taken from “Hustlin'”, the song that really jumpstarted his career, and is certified 5x platinum.\n\nThis third line is from “It’s My Time”, another track on Ross' debut album. Ross perhaps included this line in the intro because MasterMind marks nearly ten years since Ross broke onto the rap scene—his debut album came out in 2006. And now, nearly ten years later, Ross has truly hit his stride and releasing the best music of his career.", "annotation_id": "2776946", "url": "https://genius.com/2776946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Intro (Mastermind)", "line": "[Interlude: Napoleon Hill]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This segment is taken from Napoleon Hill in his philosophy of “The Mastermind Principle”.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LDHCoNnuqUI", "annotation_id": "2776934", "url": "https://genius.com/2776934", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Intro (Mastermind)", "line": "We all know that you cannot get something for nothing There is a price tag to everything", "vault_lines": ["We all know that you cannot get something for nothing", "There is a price tag to everything"], "meaning": "Napoleon Hill is addressing the philosophy that for every output, there must be some input. To become successful and be a “Mastermind”, you must be willing to put in the effort for the success you wish to attain.\n\nSuccess is something that must be earned, and that even luck is something that you must create for yourself by giving yourself the right opportunities.", "annotation_id": "2776907", "url": "https://genius.com/2776907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
