{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Remix, remix, remix Remix, remix, remix Remix, remix, remix Remix (Remix)", "vault_lines": ["Game got at me about the remix, it's a honor, my nigga"], "meaning": "The Game is letting all of us know that this is indeed, a remix…", "annotation_id": "33214952", "url": "https://genius.com/33214952", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "A hundred forty thousand the first week? Ughhh", "vault_lines": ["A hundred forty thousand the first week? Ughhh"], "meaning": "The Game disses the first week sales of Lloyd Bank$’s second album Rotten Apple, as it sold 143,000 copies the first week. The Game had previously mocked the albums first week sales in his “Show Me What You Got Freestyle”\n\nCome on, you ain’t done yet?\nFuckin' hundred forty thousand, nigga\n\nAnd he made fun of the album’s second week sales in the intro of his song “SoundScan”\n\nSkip the bullshit, Lloyd Banks in at number 16: 48,000, ha ha\n\nIn November 2006, The Game mentioned this in his One Man Riot interview with AllHipHop.com\n\nAnd, at the end of the day, you check SoundScan, you check the clothing store, you check and see what I’ve done to G-Unit as a whole. And 50, he’ll probably never admit it, but he’s sitting somewhere, that nigga knows what’s up. Lloyd Banks flopped. Don’t try to blame it on the climate [of the music industry]. Last time, he sold 400,000 the first week. I was there for that and this time he comes out and sell 140,000 [his first week], the 40,000 [his second week], then 25. That nigga’s gone, he’s done with. Yayo sold more than Banks and Yayo flopped.\n\nAlso the “Ughhh” part is a reference to his line in the original version of his song “It’s Okay (One Blood)”\n\nYou 38 and you still rappin'? ughhh\n\nWhich he used again in his song “SoundScan” but bumps up Tony Yayo’s age to 39\n\nI got two words for Tony Yayo\nOne Blood\nYou 39 now and you still rappin'? Ughhh", "annotation_id": "28890759", "url": "https://genius.com/28890759", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "But sadly gets torn between one Crip and one (Blood!)", "vault_lines": ["But sadly gets torn between one Crip and one (Blood!)"], "meaning": "Despite all being “One Blood” (as in family), the black community sadly gets split red and blue.", "annotation_id": "27067042", "url": "https://genius.com/27067042", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I got these corny wannabe diss song kings on the radio Talk about how they gon’ spray and take me away But I’m the true living legend, I’m not to be questioned", "vault_lines": ["I got these corny wannabe diss song kings on the radio", "Talk about how they gon' spray and take me away", "But I'm the true living legend, I'm not to be questioned"], "meaning": "Nas might be taking subliminal shots at Jeezy, who was dissing Nas at the time and claiming he would outsell him.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NIsL_VMCLwA\nThe reason why was Nas was releasing his “Hip Hop is Dead” album and has taken shots at Southern hip hop. Nas refutes this by claiming he is the true living legend.", "annotation_id": "18965977", "url": "https://genius.com/18965977", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "The king comin’ – no, I’m not Jay-Z", "vault_lines": ["The king comin' – no, I'm not Jay-Z"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Jay Z’s ninth studio album Kingdom Come which released in 2006. The Game is known for having an on and off again beef with Jay Z and goes out of his way to tell the audience he’s the king and not Jay Z.", "annotation_id": "16503208", "url": "https://genius.com/16503208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Hip-Hop ain’t dead, it just took a couple shots", "vault_lines": ["Hip-Hop ain't dead, it just took a couple shots"], "meaning": "Around the time Game blew up, there was alot of comments about how dull the Hip-Hop scene has become and that it died. Even Nas ,who is featured in this Remix, released an album by the Name Hip Hop is Dead, but Game claims otherwise, Actually the amount of iconic featured artists recruited by the game on this remix claims otherwise like he is trying to keep the game alive.", "annotation_id": "14785082", "url": "https://genius.com/14785082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Nasir signin’ with Jigga", "vault_lines": ["I made rap one blood, Nasir signin' with Jigga"], "meaning": "Around the end of 2005, to be exact, in October, Jay-Z (Jigga) and Nas squashed the long time beef between them, they aswell performed together, and even Nas decided to sign with Def Jam at the start of 2006, where Jay-Z was president at that time.", "annotation_id": "14784958", "url": "https://genius.com/14784958", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "It’s Dipset Capo", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A Capo is short for Caporegime, a mafia term describing a rank, which is usually the Second or Third in command after the Boss. Jim Jones calls himself the second command of The Diplomats, right after the boss Cam'ron.", "annotation_id": "14784919", "url": "https://genius.com/14784919", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Yeah, classic shit, we mastered this Left for dead, I’m back,", "vault_lines": ["Left for dead, I'm back,"], "meaning": "A reference to not only their coke rap classic, Hell Hath No Fury, but also their passed label Jive Records, which screwed them over and shelved them for 4 years.", "annotation_id": "11377023", "url": "https://genius.com/11377023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Slauson Swap Meet", "vault_lines": ["Del Amo to Compton, Slauson Swap Meet"], "meaning": "Slauson Swap Meet refers to Slauson Supermall located in LA.", "annotation_id": "9179144", "url": "https://genius.com/9179144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Nigga, one Crip, one Blood,", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, one Crip, one Blood,"], "meaning": "Actually… there are several Bloods and several Crips on this track, from Snoop Dogg to Game. But in the end, it isn’t the gang they used to rep that matters, they are all brothers in the rap game and will always have each other’s backs regardless of what goes down.", "annotation_id": "3185091", "url": "https://genius.com/3185091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Game got at me about the remix, it’s a honor, my nigga", "vault_lines": ["Game got at me about the remix, it's a honor, my nigga"], "meaning": "Nas and Game have been friends for quite a while, from having an unofficial collab album together to featuring each other on their albums. But, before all that, Nas was featured here, on this track, which really honored him because at the time Game was one of the biggest names in West Coast Hip-Hop.", "annotation_id": "3185046", "url": "https://genius.com/3185046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "New York, get the Blood money (Dirty cash!), still sweet", "vault_lines": ["New York, get the Blood money (Dirty cash!), still sweet"], "meaning": "Continuation from the opening line in the song Bloody Money by Capone-N-Noreaga (N.O.R.E.’s first group) from their debut album The War Report\n\nNew York get the bloody money, dirty cash", "annotation_id": "2998409", "url": "https://genius.com/2998409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Game said he made room for Jeezy, I had to make room for me, G", "vault_lines": ["Game said he made room for Jeezy, I had to make room for me, G"], "meaning": "Reference to this line from the original track", "annotation_id": "1092426", "url": "https://genius.com/1092426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 23: Ja Rule]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It was notable that Ja appeared on this remix because it was in the immediate aftermath of his career pretty much being destroyed by mainly 50 Cent, but also Eminem, D12, G-Unit, Busta Rhymes, Obie Trice, and DMX.  Game, after having several other people 50 had beefed with (Fat Joe, Jadakiss, and Nas) on the remix, decided to end it with 50’s biggest enemy of all\n\n\n\nHowever, it was also notable that Game included Ja Rule on this remix after saying on the clean version of “One Blood” that “You got a beef with me, if you beefin' with Dre”. Ja Rule was beefing with Dre along with Em and 50, so despite his beef with 50, Game should have had a beef with Ja too.", "annotation_id": "106421", "url": "https://genius.com/106421", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Shark meat to Pappadeaux,", "vault_lines": ["Shark meat to Pappadeaux,"], "meaning": "That would be Houston’s Pappadeaux Seafood Kitchen", "annotation_id": "105641", "url": "https://genius.com/105641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "L.A., New York", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Game is the L.A. half of this equation, and Queens native Ja Rule is the NY half", "annotation_id": "105639", "url": "https://genius.com/105639", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Ask the Hundreds,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Hundreds is a streetwear brand that Bun B has become close friends with.", "annotation_id": "97762", "url": "https://genius.com/97762", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Neon green outta Flight Club off of Fairfax", "vault_lines": ["Neon green outta Flight Club off of Fairfax"], "meaning": "Flight Club is a sneaker reseller with a location on Fairfax Ave in Los Angeles.", "annotation_id": "97759", "url": "https://genius.com/97759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Mic check, one two, one two (Check!)", "vault_lines": ["Mic check, one two, one two (Check!)"], "meaning": "Reference to his first single “Mic Check” from his album What The Game’s Been Missing.", "annotation_id": "83910", "url": "https://genius.com/83910", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I do it for my Folks, Vice Lords and Kings", "vault_lines": ["I do it for my Folks, Vice Lords and Kings"], "meaning": "“Folks” is not the innocuous word it might seem here.  In gang terminology, the Folk Nation is a slew of non-Blood or Crip gangs.  Slim Thug, ever mindful of shouting out all sides, also mentions the Vice Lords and Latin Kings, who belong to a rival collective, the People Nation", "annotation_id": "76647", "url": "https://genius.com/76647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "(Ballin’!)", "vault_lines": ["And we ballin', foreign toys what we hoppin' out (Flossing!)"], "meaning": "Cribbed from his own song “We Fly High”, Jimmy Jones never misses an opportunity to reference the only hit he’s ever had", "annotation_id": "67422", "url": "https://genius.com/67422", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Like Eric, they think it’s Eazy", "vault_lines": ["Like Eric, they think it's Eazy"], "meaning": "A reference to NWA founder Eric “Eazy-E” Wright", "annotation_id": "26823", "url": "https://genius.com/26823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I’m from Long Beach City, a Crip next to Compton", "vault_lines": ["I'm from Long Beach City, a Crip next to Compton"], "meaning": "Daz and the rest of the Dogg Pound have long repped Long Beach City (the LBC). There was even briefly a Snoop-affiliated group called the LBC Crew", "annotation_id": "26822", "url": "https://genius.com/26822", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I’m New York’s king, I’m New York’s hardest nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm New York's king, I'm New York's hardest nigga"], "meaning": "Jada styles himself as “top 5, dead or alive” as a rapper, and Styles P, playing up his gangster cred, has long claimed the title of “New York’s hardest”", "annotation_id": "26819", "url": "https://genius.com/26819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "My celebrated presence, like the return of Rayful", "vault_lines": ["My celebrated presence, like the return of Rayful"], "meaning": "The Clipse compare themselves to notorious drug dealer Rayful Edmond, the guy who introduced crack to Washington, D.C. Edmond’s gang committed over 400 murders prior to his arrest in 1989", "annotation_id": "24864", "url": "https://genius.com/24864", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "And you ain’t gotta go overseas to see Iraq shit You can come to Lefrak, Queens, and get jacked quick", "vault_lines": ["And you ain't gotta go overseas to see Iraq shit", "You can come to Lefrak, Queens, and get jacked quick"], "meaning": "Every rapper likes to brag their hood is tougher, usually by inviting people to go there to get robbed, carjacked or shot. NORE’s hood is LeFrak City, Queens. NORE and others have long referred to LeFrak as “Iraq” because of its warzone-like status", "annotation_id": "24372", "url": "https://genius.com/24372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "On the Eastside Of New Orleans, where the Bloods at the B-hive", "vault_lines": ["Of New Orleans, where the Bloods at the B-hive"], "meaning": "The Eastside of New Orleans, which is heavy with Blood activity, is sometimes referred to as the “B-hive” for this reason. If you can, wade through this comment thread for an in-depth discussion of N.O. gangbanging, which specifically references this line", "annotation_id": "24238", "url": "https://genius.com/24238", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Clean your clock, open your can of tuna (Doot-doot-doot!)", "vault_lines": ["Clean your clock, open your can of tuna (Doot-doot-doot!)"], "meaning": "E-40 is known, more than anything, for his inventive slang. “Open your can of tuna” here is his way of saying “shoot you in the head”", "annotation_id": "24225", "url": "https://genius.com/24225", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Get your chest ate out with the FN 57 (Bo! Bo! Bo!)", "vault_lines": ["Get your chest ate out with the FN 57 (Bo! Bo! Bo!)"], "meaning": "The Fabrique-Nationale FN 5-7 pistol is a high capacity semi-automatic which fires a 5.7mm armor piercing round.", "annotation_id": "24222", "url": "https://genius.com/24222", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "They hold cards down, nigga, like spades and pinochle (Nigga)", "vault_lines": ["They hold cards down, nigga, like spades and pinochle (Nigga)"], "meaning": "A pun – spades and pinochle are card games, and claiming a particular Crip set is sometimes called “holding a card”", "annotation_id": "24181", "url": "https://genius.com/24181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Got two tiny locos ready to take trips", "vault_lines": ["Got two tiny locos ready to take trips"], "meaning": "The Tiny Locos are a LA street gang, their name means “Little Crazies”. Here they’re ready to sell Kurupt’s drugs", "annotation_id": "24175", "url": "https://genius.com/24175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Where them killers throw that third letter up", "vault_lines": ["Where them killers throw that third letter up"], "meaning": "The “third letter” being C, for Crip", "annotation_id": "24055", "url": "https://genius.com/24055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Like Raymond Washington and Tookie Williams", "vault_lines": ["Like Raymond Washington and Tookie Williams"], "meaning": "Raymond Washington was the original founder, in 1969, of the gang that came to be known as the Crips. They were originally called the “Baby Avenues”, then the “Avenue Cribs” (because of their youth), then the Crips\n\nStanley Tookie Williams met Washington in 1968 and was another founder of the Crips. Later in life, he authored several anti-gang books and worked against violence, ultimately getting a Nobel Prize nomination. His activism spurred calls for clemency on the death sentence he was facing for murders he committed in 1979. Clemency was denied, and Williams was executed on December 12, 2005", "annotation_id": "24052", "url": "https://genius.com/24052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Who the riders shooting through the gutter lane? Trued up in them Carolina blue Hurricanes (What up, Blood?)", "vault_lines": ["Who the riders shooting through the gutter lane?", "Trued up in them Carolina blue Hurricanes (What up, Blood?)"], "meaning": "Hurricanes are Game’s shoe line. WC’s are blue because he likes blue. No, just kidding! It’s because he’s a Crip!\n\nThe “Carolina blue” is because it’s the same shade of blue worn by the University of North Carolina’s Tarheels", "annotation_id": "24035", "url": "https://genius.com/24035", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Y.G.’s and B.G.’s, O.G.’s – it’s time to ride!", "vault_lines": ["Y.G.'s and B.G.'s, O.G.'s – it's time to ride!"], "meaning": "G[angsters], B[aby] G[angsters], and O[riginal] G[angsters] – basically, gangbangers of all ages", "annotation_id": "24034", "url": "https://genius.com/24034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "It’s one blood if you Blood or Cuz", "vault_lines": ["It's one blood if you Blood or Cuz"], "meaning": "It doesn’t matter if you are Crip (cuz) or Blood because we are all one blood/people/etc. This has historically been a West Coast idea (though Slim Thug himself is from Houston), as you can see in this all-star West Coast 1990 anti-gang song “We’re All in the Same Gang”\n\n\n\nSnoop and Pac famously engaged in “Blood/Cuz gangbangin” on “2 Of Amerikaz Most Wanted”", "annotation_id": "23913", "url": "https://genius.com/23913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Draped in blue, notorious gangsta crew", "vault_lines": ["Draped in blue, notorious gangsta crew"], "meaning": "Blue is the traditional color of the Crip gang, with whom Daz (and Snoop) have aligned themselves publicly", "annotation_id": "23911", "url": "https://genius.com/23911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Hurt him in that cherry ’6-4", "vault_lines": ["Hurt him in that cherry '6-4"], "meaning": "‘64 Chevrolet Impala (the meme West Coast gangster car), cherry colored. Note that the car is red, the color of the Bloods. In Snoop’s classic “Ain’t No Fun”, Warren G drives a “6-4 Chevy, red to be exact” for the same reason (Death Row Records head Suge Knight had an affiliation with the Bloods that went back to his childhood)", "annotation_id": "23849", "url": "https://genius.com/23849", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Chi got them ballers and hustlers, show me where them figures at", "vault_lines": ["Chi got them ballers and hustlers, show me where them figures at"], "meaning": "Rather than the generic term for drug dealer, when Twista says “hustlers” he is likely referring to the long-running Chicago gang the Four Corner Hustlers", "annotation_id": "23845", "url": "https://genius.com/23845", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "(What it look like?) All I say, at most Shooters waitin’ on the word, “Just say it, ’Los!”", "vault_lines": ["(What it look like?) All I say, at most"], "meaning": "Loso is Fabolous' nickname (From Faboloso), and he has a room of gunmen waiting on his word. “What it look like?” is one of his most common catchphrases", "annotation_id": "23828", "url": "https://genius.com/23828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "D-B-L-O-C-K, he spray", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "D-Block is the record label/extended crew of The LOX, a group composed of Jadakiss, Styles P and Sleek Louch. You might know them from their collaboration with Biggie, Last Day", "annotation_id": "23821", "url": "https://genius.com/23821", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "”Def Jam, they gon’ flop him And Reggaeton ain’t hot in the building no more” It’s okay, I get it poppin’", "vault_lines": ["\"Def Jam, they gon' flop him", "And Reggaeton ain't hot in the building no more\"", "It's okay, I get it poppin'"], "meaning": "NORE thinks Def Jam didn’t promote his 2006 reggaeton album N.O.R.E. Y La Familia… Ya Tu Sabe enough, so he left the label in 2007\n\nNORE is one of the artists most closely associated with the mid-00s reggaeton boom, thanks to his single Oye Mi Canto\n\nThis is also a slightly altered quote of the original “One Blood” The original being:\n\nThe Math gon' drop him, and 50 ain’t rocking with him no more, It’s okay I get it popping\n\nThe delivery is also nearly the same as Game’s.", "annotation_id": "23807", "url": "https://genius.com/23807", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "We the Black Wall Street, by the swap meet with heat", "vault_lines": ["We the Black Wall Street, by the swap meet with heat"], "meaning": "NORE associates with The Game’s group, Black Wall Street, who apparently carry guns by Compton’s famous Slauson Indoor Swapmeet", "annotation_id": "23806", "url": "https://genius.com/23806", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Call me Goldie, I’ll smack a bitch too", "vault_lines": ["Call me Goldie, I'll smack a bitch too"], "meaning": "Goldie is a character from 1973 blaxploitation classic The Mack. He was a pimp, and pimps have a reputation for slapping women", "annotation_id": "23804", "url": "https://genius.com/23804", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Somebody go and get this nigga a pine box And I ain’t just talkin’ ’bout a measly nine shots", "vault_lines": ["Somebody go and get this nigga a pine box", "And I ain't just talkin' 'bout a measly nine shots"], "meaning": "Oh, that’s right! For some inscrutable reason, 50 Cent started a beef with Joe (supposedly because he recorded a verse with Ja Rule, with whom 50 was beefing with). This allows Joe to bite some lines from  Ether. Since 50 famously got shot nine times and survived, Joe wants to shoot him even more and put him in a coffin (the Ether-bite “pine box”)", "annotation_id": "23802", "url": "https://genius.com/23802", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "My fair Eastside, where we ride And we all fly high in the Lear G5s", "vault_lines": ["And we all fly high in the Lear G5s"], "meaning": "Lear is a company that produces private jets, but the Gulfstream V is actually produced by…Gulfstream\n\nAnother reference to his only hit “We Fly High”\n\n“My Fair East Side” is a reference to the school song of east side high school in the movie Lean On Me", "annotation_id": "23782", "url": "https://genius.com/23782", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Japanese thread, brought flavor to these bums", "vault_lines": ["Japanese thread, brought flavor to these bums"], "meaning": "Prior to starting their own clothing line, The Clipse had an oft-stated affinity for the Japanese clothing brand BAPE, or A Bathing Ape", "annotation_id": "23642", "url": "https://genius.com/23642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Ain’t nothin’ sweet, unless it’s Presidential ’Cause that is where I sleep, now give me my key", "vault_lines": ["Ain't nothin' sweet, unless it's Presidential", "'Cause that is where I sleep, now give me my key"], "meaning": "A clever homophone pun by Weezy – nothing about him is sweet (soft, homo, un-gangster, etc.) except the suite he stays in when traveling, which is always the Presidential Suite (because he’s so rich, and also the President of Young Money Records)", "annotation_id": "23592", "url": "https://genius.com/23592", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "504 gangsta, New Orleans solja", "vault_lines": ["504 gangsta, New Orleans solja"], "meaning": "504 is the area code for most of New Orleans. Lil Wayne is from there.  The “soldier” image is huge in N.O., dating back to hood legend-turned-rapper Soulja Slim, who started the trend when he was only a teen", "annotation_id": "23590", "url": "https://genius.com/23590", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Bangin’ underwater, fuck around and soak ya", "vault_lines": ["Bangin' underwater, fuck around and soak ya"], "meaning": "Weezy refers to his New Orleans hometown as “the water” (likely due to Katrina-induced flooding), also he’s affiliated with the Bloods, and thus he “bangs” (abbreviation of gangbanging, basically being part of a gang and representing it on the street). Also a pun on “wetting you up”, or shooting someone, and on soaking their shirt with blood", "annotation_id": "23589", "url": "https://genius.com/23589", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I Press Play like Puff, no pause at all", "vault_lines": ["I Press Play like Puff, no pause at all"], "meaning": "T.I “presses play” (shoots), much like Puff Daddy’s 2006 album Press Play", "annotation_id": "23584", "url": "https://genius.com/23584", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "With two-twos, you can call me Quick Draw McGraw (Haha!)", "vault_lines": ["With two-twos, you can call me Quick Draw McGraw (Haha!)"], "meaning": "T.I draws his .22 pistol as fast as Hanna-Barbera cartoon character Quick Draw McGraw", "annotation_id": "23583", "url": "https://genius.com/23583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I got rappers gettin’ mad at me I got these new jack rappers tryin’ to clap at me", "vault_lines": ["I got rappers gettin' mad at me", "I got these new jack rappers tryin' to clap at me"], "meaning": "“New Jack” is an old expression for new, fresh, with a different mindset, also implies that they’re different from the old guard and a bit phony (due to the New Jack Swing implications)", "annotation_id": "23577", "url": "https://genius.com/23577", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Ha, you know what it is When you see me two twelvin’ you, homie (That’s right) You fuck niggas keep triple ninin’ (Eastside) Have some integrity, bitch ’Fore it be a 1090 out here, smell me?", "vault_lines": ["'Fore it be a 1090 out here, smell me?"], "meaning": "“212” is Blood slang for “Let me holla at you”, and “tripling nining” is slang for snitching\n\nNot snitching is a big concern for Jones. In a 2007 interview, he explains what he means by “integrity” here:\n\n\nYou mention integrity on your intro to The Game’s “One Blood” remix, is that what you were talking about?\n\nOh yeah you mean when I’m talking, when I’m telling these niggas, stop triple nining, before it be 1090 [set-tripping, or gang members attacking other members of the same gang], have some integrity.  Exactly, I’m telling niggas stop snitching and shit like that, keep your mouth closed if you want to be in this game, or don’t gangbang.", "annotation_id": "23568", "url": "https://genius.com/23568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "ByrdGang, bitch!", "vault_lines": ["(Blood hunt) Dipset, ByrdGang, bitch!"], "meaning": "Byrdgang is the other Jim Jones group, with other members  Max B, Mel Matrix and Stack Bundles\n\nThe name is inspired by the many meanings of “Bird” in drug dealing lingo (see JR Writer’s “Byrd Call”)", "annotation_id": "23559", "url": "https://genius.com/23559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "And Kings, show me where them killas at", "vault_lines": ["and Kings, show me where them killas at"], "meaning": "While there are several Chicago gangs with “Kings” in their name, Twista likely means the infamous Latin Kings, who are among the largest gangs in the city", "annotation_id": "23556", "url": "https://genius.com/23556", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Chi got Lords and Gangsters, show me where them niggas at", "vault_lines": ["Chi got Lords and Gangsters, show me where them niggas at"], "meaning": "The two main gangs in Chicago are the Gangster Disciples and the Vice Lords", "annotation_id": "23555", "url": "https://genius.com/23555", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Chi got Two Sixes", "vault_lines": ["Chi got Two Sixes"], "meaning": "The Gangster Two Six Nation are a notoriously violent Latino gang in Chicago (who have been around since 1964 – props for longevity, guys!)", "annotation_id": "23552", "url": "https://genius.com/23552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I’m bickin’ back, bein’ bool,", "vault_lines": ["I'm bickin' back, bein' bool,"], "meaning": "Wayne here adopts common Bloods slang by replacing the hard “c” sounds in words (as found in the word “Crip”) with “b” sounds (as found in “Blood”). So he is actually saying, “I’m kicking back, being cool”", "annotation_id": "23551", "url": "https://genius.com/23551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I’m comin’ straight up outta P-A-T, like Compton, in all black But when we say “What it do?” – they never say, “Holla back!”", "vault_lines": ["I'm comin' straight up outta P-A-T, like Compton, in all black", "But when we say \"What it do?\" – they never say, \"Holla back!\""], "meaning": "Bun is from Port Arthur, Texas (PAT), and much like NWA during their Straight Outta Compton phase, he is wearing all black", "annotation_id": "23549", "url": "https://genius.com/23549", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "I’m a heavy better, I’m a heavy seller (Tell ’em) Keep white in the office, call it Jerry Heller", "vault_lines": ["Keep white in the office, call it Jerry Heller"], "meaning": "Ross jokingly refers to his (white) cocaine that he keeps in his place of business as “Jerry Heller”, NWA’s former (white, Jewish) manager and Eazy-E’s longtime mentor and confidant", "annotation_id": "23548", "url": "https://genius.com/23548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": ",", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is Game’s mocking reference to the first-week sales of the album Rotten Apple, by his enemy Lloyd Banks of G-Unit. After many of the tracks leaking, the album sold a disappointing-by-2006-standards 143,000 copies the first week", "annotation_id": "23547", "url": "https://genius.com/23547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "So twist your fingers up and bang, motherfucker, bang! (Nine-Trey!)", "vault_lines": ["So twist your fingers up and bang, motherfucker, bang! (Nine-Trey!)"], "meaning": "Gangbangers often twist their fingers up to make gang signs. Jay-Z poked fun at this in “The Watcher 2”:\n\nAll of these rap singers claiming they bangers\nDoing all sorts of twisted shit with they fingers\n\nSome different gang signs used by Bloods sets can be found here", "annotation_id": "23546", "url": "https://genius.com/23546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "And Nine-Trey is what I fuckin’ claim (Ugh!)", "vault_lines": ["And Nine-Trey is what I fuckin' claim (Ugh!)"], "meaning": "The Nine Trey Gangsters are an East Coast subset of the Bloods gang. In 2007, 46 of their alleged members were indicted in New Jersey and Michael Smart, a reputed “Four Star General”, got sentenced to 70 years", "annotation_id": "23545", "url": "https://genius.com/23545", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "What duo you know Get XXL kudos while coppin’ off Julio?", "vault_lines": ["What duo you know", "Get XXL kudos while coppin' off Julio?"], "meaning": "The Clipse second album, Hell Hath No Fury, famously got the top “XXL” review from XXL magazine. Read it here. The Thornton brothers claim that they manage to make critically-acclaimed rap while still dealing coke. This claim was given extra credibility in 2009 when their former manager was arrested for running a $10 million a year drug ring", "annotation_id": "23539", "url": "https://genius.com/23539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "This ain’t a movie, dawg (Nope!) not Waist Deep I’m not a actor but I’ll show your bitch big meat", "vault_lines": ["This ain't a movie, dawg (Nope!) not Waist Deep", "I'm not a actor but I'll show your bitch big meat"], "meaning": "Waist Deep was a 2006 movie that Game starred in as a character called “Big Meat” – thus the pun on his “big meat”\n\n\n\nAlso, in Jay-Z’s song, “Public Service Announcement” (which Game referenced in the previous line) Jay-Z says,\n\nShoot at you actors like movie directors.\n\nThis is another shot taken by The Game towards Jay.", "annotation_id": "23537", "url": "https://genius.com/23537", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "line": "Twenty-one, twenty Crips and all of us is Crippin’, cuz", "vault_lines": ["Twenty-one, twenty Crips and all of us is Crippin', cuz"], "meaning": "Despite being on a song called “One BLOOD”, in which at least a few artists are repping the Bloods, Snoop here reps his former set, the Rollin 20’s Crips, likely from his home turf of 21st Street. “Cuz” is a common Crip salutation", "annotation_id": "23533", "url": "https://genius.com/23533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 68, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/The-game-its-okay-one-blood-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "It’s Okay (One Blood) (Remix)", "genius_id": 706, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s On", "line": "Went from crumbs to brick (lay down), the other shit", "vault_lines": ["Went from crumbs to brick (lay down), the other shit"], "meaning": "Peep Da WordPlay Cuh….\n\n-…“from crumbs to brick…” means to go from small portions of crack rocks to a bigger league of copping full kilos of cocaine\n\n-“lay down” refers to laying bricks to build something. Something like an empire or a cartel.", "annotation_id": "3130393", "url": "https://genius.com/3130393", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
