{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s a Tower Heist", "line": "Born in NYC beastin’", "vault_lines": ["Born in NYC beastin'"], "meaning": "Nas has been spitting fresh rhymes since birth! After all, he snuffed Jesus at age 12.\n\nAdditionally, “beastin',” used to boast of his infantile mic prowess, might connect with the religious namedrops in the next line, which would also hint at The Beast, mentioned especially in The Book of Revelation.", "annotation_id": "549509", "url": "https://genius.com/549509", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s a Tower Heist", "line": "Islamic thoughts", "vault_lines": ["Christian pendants, Islamic thoughts"], "meaning": "This line shows Nas’s spiritual complexity. He wears a cross but has the thoughts and beliefs of a member of the Nation of Gods & Earths (5%ers), who practice a quasi-Islamic religion.\n\nNas was hella influenced by the 5% Nation in his youth.", "annotation_id": "484745", "url": "https://genius.com/484745", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s a Tower Heist", "line": "I feel amaz-on, it’s a jungle in these streets", "vault_lines": ["I feel amaz-on, it's a jungle in these streets"], "meaning": "This is what happens when you force “amazing” to rhyme with “shades on” and “J’s on.”\n\n“Amaz-on” amazon, alludes to the rainforest of the same name.\n\nThis line also connects with Ross’s comparison of urban neighborhoods to jungles, due to their violence and exoticness.", "annotation_id": "396236", "url": "https://genius.com/396236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s a Tower Heist", "line": "Live 100 years like crocodiles", "vault_lines": ["Count it in warehouses, leave town and live 100 years like crocodiles"], "meaning": "Nas must really be watching a lot of Wild Planet like he mentioned recently on the “Outro” track on Lil' Wayne’s Tha Carter IV.", "annotation_id": "396221", "url": "https://genius.com/396221", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s a Tower Heist", "line": "I wanna die like Godfather did", "vault_lines": ["Father forgive, I wanna die like Godfather did"], "meaning": "Vito Corleone (The Godfather) died of a heart attack at an old age.\n\n\n\nNas is saying he wants to live long and die of natural causes rather than be killed by his criminal lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "396205", "url": "https://genius.com/396205", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "It’s a Tower Heist", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Nas-its-a-tower-heist-lyrics", "genius_title": "It’s a Tower Heist", "genius_id": 57132, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Dippin’ and I’m rollin’, rollin’ and I’m dippin’", "vault_lines": ["Dippin’ and I’m rollin’, rollin’ and I’m dippin’"], "meaning": "Dipping is a term which is used to describe the action of consuming MDMA straight from the bag, something which can only be done with the higher purity MDMA and not the low grade molly which other rappers use.\n\nRolling is a term used to describe being high on MDMA, which is a euphoric experience.\nRolling could also mean rolling joints/blunts.\nSo Chinx is doing MDMA and he’s getting high.", "annotation_id": "2966130", "url": "https://genius.com/2966130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "A lot of clean money, I just bought me 30 bitches", "vault_lines": ["A lot of clean money, I just bought me 30 bitches"], "meaning": "He uses the word clean meaning that money was made legally, compared to dirty money which is made illegally.", "annotation_id": "1708391", "url": "https://genius.com/1708391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Homie, matter of fact - I’m a motherfucking coke boy Keep wiggling baby, I’m a motherfucking coke boy Keep wiggling baby, I’m a motherfucking coke boy Keep wiggling baby, I’m a motherfucking coke boy Keep wiggling baby, I’m a motherfucking coke boy", "vault_lines": ["Homie, matter of fact - I'm a motherfucking coke boy", "Keep wiggling baby, I'm a motherfucking coke boy"], "meaning": "A reference to LL Cool J’s classic Jingling Baby chorus.\n\nHe could perhaps also be talking about people trying to change him (wiggling) but he remains a coke boy.", "annotation_id": "1566754", "url": "https://genius.com/1566754", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Could’ve been a battle rapper, havin’ lunch with Lux", "vault_lines": ["Could’ve been a battle rapper, havin’ lunch with Lux"], "meaning": "Loaded Lux is a popular battle rapper from Smack/URL series, who caught alot of peoples attention after his battle with Calicoe.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2dPwBIl8Wwk", "annotation_id": "1405020", "url": "https://genius.com/1405020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
