{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Could’ve put an extra .2 up in the baggie And had them niggas from the other side feelin’ aggy", "vault_lines": ["Could’ve put an extra .2 up in the baggie", "And had them niggas from the other side feelin’ aggy"], "meaning": "He does this draw more customers, leaving the other dealers mad they lost people to him.", "annotation_id": "1405011", "url": "https://genius.com/1405011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Got me livin’ lavish, mansions,", "vault_lines": ["Got me livin’ lavish, mansions,"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' home offers seven bedrooms, four bathrooms, balcony, swimming pool, three-car garage, and 4,771 square feet.\nBiggest house in Georgia.", "annotation_id": "1405010", "url": "https://genius.com/1405010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Jesus piece swingin’, causin’ havoc on the corner", "vault_lines": ["Jesus piece swingin’, causin’ havoc on the corner"], "meaning": "Even in the hood, Rozay wears his Jesus Pieces while on the block. He stays true to his faith.", "annotation_id": "1405009", "url": "https://genius.com/1405009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Could’ve been a ball player, but I’m still ballin’", "vault_lines": ["Could’ve been a ball player, but I’m still ballin’"], "meaning": "Rozay graduated from Carol City Senior High School and later attended historically black college Albany State University in Albany, Georgia on a football scholarship.\nEven though Ross didn’t end up playing football professionally, he still ended up ballin'. Nice use of homonyms there.", "annotation_id": "1405004", "url": "https://genius.com/1405004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m A Coke Boy (Remix)", "line": "Leanin’ toward Obama but I could’ve went for Romney", "vault_lines": ["Leanin’ toward Obama but I could’ve went for Romney"], "meaning": "Liked what Obama had to offer but he could have chosen to vote for Romney.\n\nHe’s implying that he’s successful enough that he considered voting for Romney in order to maintain lower tax rates, etc.", "annotation_id": "1404993", "url": "https://genius.com/1404993", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
