{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Good Remix", "line": "[Chorus] You can find me in the streets, even in the drought My mattress is full Why shouldn’t I be out Hey buddy, I’m good (what they tell you?) I’m good (what they tell you?) I’m good (what she tell you?) I’m good (what you see?) Two hundred dolla jeans with my favorite patch Pullin up my ride hell yea the rims match! What they tell you? I’m good (what they tell you?) I’m good (what they tell you?) I’m good (what she tell you?) I’m good (what you see?)", "vault_lines": ["Two hundred dolla jeans with my favorite patch", "Pullin up my ride hell yea the rims match!", "What they tell you? I'm good"], "meaning": "See the original for notes pertaining to this portion of the song.", "annotation_id": "1840996", "url": "https://genius.com/1840996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Good Remix", "line": "I made Forbes 6 point M letter", "vault_lines": ["I made Forbes 6 point M letter"], "meaning": "In 2009, Ross placed number 20 on Forbes Cash Kings of hip-hop, where his net worth was 6 million dollars that year.", "annotation_id": "1840958", "url": "https://genius.com/1840958", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Good Remix", "line": "Extended clip in the fog, ya gotta air it out He’s so flamboyant, put a fan on him", "vault_lines": ["Extended clip in the fog, ya gotta air it out", "He's so flamboyant, put a fan on him"], "meaning": "A play on words: to ‘air out’ means to fire a gun, and since the image Ross has set up is foggy, he’ll need to air out his clip.\n\nThe metaphor is continued in the next line with the inclusion of a fan, another device used to air things out – it’s necessary because this dude’s acting way too weird.", "annotation_id": "1840877", "url": "https://genius.com/1840877", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Good Remix", "line": "I couldn’t tell, I thought a kilo meant I finally made it Then came 10, 20 came quick Walked out the kitchen, face white as Taylor Swift’s", "vault_lines": ["I couldn't tell, I thought a kilo meant I finally made it", "Then came 10, 20 came quick", "Walked out the kitchen, face white as Taylor Swift's"], "meaning": "Pusha was dealt a look of shock upon his face when he saw exactly how big his coke business was growing, thus, his face went white.\n\nThis could be a reference to one of two things:\n\n\nComparing his face to Taylor Swift’s pasty complexion\nMimicking Taylor’s shock when Kanye West went up and grabbed Taylor Swift’s award at the VMA’s.", "annotation_id": "1810263", "url": "https://genius.com/1810263", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Good Remix", "line": "Yo! Mo’ money mo’ problems, that’s what Big said But we ain’t care, we was all about that quick bread", "vault_lines": ["But we ain't care, we was all about that quick bread"], "meaning": "Even when The Notorious B.I.G. taught them that more money leads to more problems, they still went after the cash because they were willing to risk it  enough to live a lavish life.", "annotation_id": "1784115", "url": "https://genius.com/1784115", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
