{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "Not even worth a shower, just grab me a stick of D-O", "vault_lines": ["Not even worth a shower, just grab me a stick of D-O"], "meaning": "Not even worth a shower, just grab me a stick of DEO-\nIn other words, it was just a quickie, so what’s the point in completely freshening up in the shower, all he needs is a couple slicks of a deodorant stick and it’s back to business.", "annotation_id": "32444395", "url": "https://genius.com/32444395", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "Diddy negotiates, send the paperwork to Theo", "vault_lines": ["Diddy negotiates, send the paperwork to Theo"], "meaning": "Ricky is talking about his production/management team. Sean “Diddy” Combs has worked with Ross on many songs and most likely handles some negotiations for the Maybach Music Group. Ross also credits Theo Sedlmayr, his lawyer. Funny fact: at one point he was also 50 Cent’s lawyer.\n\n\n\nRoss and Diddy at a Miami Heat game", "annotation_id": "750822", "url": "https://genius.com/750822", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "Am I my brother’s keeper? Motherfucker, take my hand (Me)", "vault_lines": ["Am I my brother's keeper? Motherfucker, take my hand (Me)"], "meaning": "Reference to the Bible, Genesis IV 9: “And the Lord said unto Cain, where is Abel thy brother? And he said, I know not: Am I my brother’s keeper?”\n\nExcept Rick Ross would never kill his brother. That’s wack. Also a reference to New Jack City, as he used in the second verse", "annotation_id": "500068", "url": "https://genius.com/500068", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "Black card", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Ross is referring to the American Express Centurion card. Black Card has a minimum spend of 150k per year and 5000 per year renewal membership fee.\n\n\n\nRoss has a black card but he’s spending 100’s at the bar. His using cash because that’s what drug dealers do, they can’t buy assets with credit, or else the IRS will get them (it was an accountant that got Al Capone after all). So, Ross stunts at the club and gets street love. Ross could use his black card but he prefers to spend his cash earned from his side game at the club. Plus, if they find the kilo in his car that was mentioned in the last line, he has no name on file and can claim that someone stole his car and took it to the club.", "annotation_id": "151033", "url": "https://genius.com/151033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "Monday for ménages", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Menage – Having sex with two or more people.\n\nFrom the French – Ménage à trois – literally “the mixing of three”.\n\n\n\nTop tip – when having a menage with two girls try to know them (in the biblical sense) individually before you introduce them to each other so you don’t get sidelined in the action.", "annotation_id": "151020", "url": "https://genius.com/151020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "It come alive Never feed it after dark, gotta treat it like a Gremlin (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Never feed it after dark, gotta treat it like a Gremlin (Woo)"], "meaning": "Here’s referense to film “Gremlins”. It’s about strange cute creature called mogwai as a pet. They have a feature: If you feed their after dark, or make them wet – they will turn to monsters.", "annotation_id": "134621", "url": "https://genius.com/134621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "I’m not a star I’m not a star I’m not a star I’m not a star", "vault_lines": ["I'm not a star"], "meaning": "Ross doesn’t feel like he’s famous but he is a star. The stark contradiction of this statement with reality emphasizes the point by forcing the listener to disagree. The power of this statement is that the listener makes his point for him.", "annotation_id": "129862", "url": "https://genius.com/129862", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "And I’m quick to blow a milli in a minute (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["And I'm quick to blow a milli in a minute (Woo)"], "meaning": "Blowing money is spending it on things as strippers, hoes, cars, or just throwing it up in the air to show that your rich. Another song from this album (Teflon Don) is B.M.F. which means Blowin' Money Fast and is a shout-out to the Black Mafia Familly.", "annotation_id": "129861", "url": "https://genius.com/129861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "But a nigga spendin’ c-notes at the bar", "vault_lines": ["but a nigga spendin' c-notes at the bar"], "meaning": "C-notes are another name for 100 dollar bills, that gets its name from Roman Numerals as C = 100.", "annotation_id": "84049", "url": "https://genius.com/84049", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "Trunk full of work, yeah, this nigga think he Nino (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["Trunk full of work, yeah, this nigga think he Nino (Ugh)"], "meaning": "Nino was a character in the film New Jack City\n\n\n\nIt’s gonna take more than that to own a Carter!", "annotation_id": "69856", "url": "https://genius.com/69856", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "If I die today, remember me like John Lennon (Ha)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Strawberry Fields Memorial to John Lennon in Central Park, New York\n\nAlthough John Lennon himself was very much opposed to the idea of mortals being worshipped as if they were Gods.", "annotation_id": "69843", "url": "https://genius.com/69843", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "I’m not a star (Me), somebody lied I got a pistol in the car (Ha), a .45", "vault_lines": ["I'm not a star"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' message in this song is that he is truly a gangster first, rapper second. Hence “I’m not a [super]star”. He affirms this by stating that he carries automatic weapons in his vehicle and intends to use them in the conduct of criminal/gangworld related activities.", "annotation_id": "69842", "url": "https://genius.com/69842", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "My niggas never sing, if I need ’em, I go to Ne-Yo", "vault_lines": ["My niggas never sing, if I need 'em, I go to Ne-Yo"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s boys never sing on tracks. Ross calls up Ne-Yo to take care of the singing.  Like on “Super High”\n\n\n\nSinging is another word for snitching he uses wordplay because Ne-Yo is an R&B singer. In other words the boss doesn’t hang with snitches.\n\nWell, we did catch Ross singing once.", "annotation_id": "65823", "url": "https://genius.com/65823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m Not a Star", "line": "Buried in Louie, I’m talkin’ all brown linen", "vault_lines": ["Buried in Louie, I'm talkin' all brown linen"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s all brown Louis Vuitton suit, will be the last thing he sleeps in and what moves over to the other side with him.\n\nPretty boss threads to rock up to heaven in or hell for that matter, but you wouldn’t think people really give much of a thought to fashion brands there though.", "annotation_id": "53602", "url": "https://genius.com/53602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
