{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "I pray to God I look my killer in his eyes Snatch his soul out his shirt, let’s take him for that ride (For that ride)", "vault_lines": ["I pray to God I look my killer in his eyes", "Snatch his soul out his shirt, let's take him for that ride (For that ride)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is saying that he prays to god that his soul will haunt the person that killed him.", "annotation_id": "24841012", "url": "https://genius.com/24841012", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "No love, cry when only babies die", "vault_lines": ["No love, cry when only babies die"], "meaning": "No love refers to Rick’s loss for love. In the rapper lifestyle, love is rare as thousands of women are available. This is also a reference towards the loss of his heart as he continued the street life.\n\nHowever, although Ross has no heart, he still cries when babies die, but only then. This is a nod towards his Pro-Life beliefs.", "annotation_id": "22784453", "url": "https://genius.com/22784453", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "A boss is one who guarantee we gon’ eat (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["A boss is one who guarantee we gon' eat (Huh)"], "meaning": "Rick contrasts an OG with a true boss; while an OG is capable of surviving in a challenging environment, a boss finds a way to survive and help other people. The boss can provide for his whole team: he can guarantee they have food to eat and money to spend.", "annotation_id": "20870285", "url": "https://genius.com/20870285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "Jerry Jones money, nigga, you a running back (You a running back)", "vault_lines": ["Jerry Jones money, nigga, you a running back (You a running back)"], "meaning": "Jerry Jones is the owner of the Dallas Cowboys, with a net worth estimated at $6.8 billion. While many can only dream of having the wealth of an NFL running back, earning a few million a year, Jones buys and sells them on a regular basis. Those running backs labor every day to make a tiny fraction of what Jones holds.", "annotation_id": "17163413", "url": "https://genius.com/17163413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "OG is one who standin’ on his own feet", "vault_lines": ["OG is one who standin' on his own feet"], "meaning": "The term O.G. is the acronym for Original Gangster with the roots dating back to 1972 when Original was used by the Crips. It was used to insinuate that “we’re first”, the Originals. Two years later the word “Gangster” was added to form the Original Gangster Crips and they only used the term “O.G.” when writing their name or their neighbourhood.\n\nSince then, the term O.G. has been widely used in hip-hop and hood culture in reference to original individuals within a certain area or just someone successful or highly skilled in any given area.\n\nRick Ross shares more of his wisdom with us in his verse on Ima Boss where he mentions how an O.G. is someone who can take care of themselves, who can achieve success in a certain field. Whereas a boss (pronounced “bawse” by Rick Ross) is someone who guarantees all their boys eat.\n\nTo expand this further, the term eat is used to describe success in such a way that everyone reaps and benefits from it. The prime example of this as always is a figure such as Jay-Z, who throughout the years has guaranteed quite a few people gon’ eat.\n\nTo quote him on this from his verse on “Pound Cake”:\n\nI’ve done made more millionaires than the lotto did\nDame made millions, Biggs made millions\nYe made millions, Just made millions\nLyor made millions, Cam made millions\nBeans’a tell you if he wasn’t in his feelings", "annotation_id": "15692488", "url": "https://genius.com/15692488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "If you say I don’t run my city, you a muh’fuckin liar", "vault_lines": ["If you say I don't run my city, you a muh'fuckin liar"], "meaning": "Meek Mill has a history with his hometown Philadelphia, having been influenced by Beanie Sigel, whom he worked with on the song “Dreamchasers”. Also, fellow Philadelphia rapper Cassidy, who has beef with Meek respects him despite their beef:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_zmte9lvGg&t=1m37s\n\nMeek is by far the most successful mainstream rapper in Philly at the moment, with the possible exception of Black Thought. His album sales, whilst funny to Drake, are admirable from an area that produces few gold selling artists.", "annotation_id": "7700449", "url": "https://genius.com/7700449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "Bitch, I’m a boss! (I’m a boss) Bitch, I’m a boss! (I’m a boss)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm a boss! (I'm a boss) Bitch, I'm a boss! (I'm a boss)"], "meaning": "No doubt, Rick Ross is a boss, he has many other songs that are related to the word “BOSS”, such as “Boss”, “The Boss”, “You The Boss” and Meek is also a boss like his man Ricky Rozay.", "annotation_id": "1358377", "url": "https://genius.com/1358377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "I’m a Boss", "line": "If I ever go broke, I’mma take yo’ money I ain’t never dropped a dime, you ain’t take none from me", "vault_lines": ["I ain't never dropped a dime, you ain't take none from me"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5237852082001", "annotation_id": "1135823", "url": "https://genius.com/1135823", "state": "verified", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
