{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jam On It", "line": "Mr. 305, to Mr. Worldwide To Mr. Take Something Make something, that’s right", "vault_lines": ["Mr. 305, to Mr. Worldwide", "To Mr. Take Something", "Make something, that’s right"], "meaning": "Pitbull has gone through a lot in order to get where he is today. He first started off as Mr.305, and was very popular in Miami. His song “Calle Ocho” was the first internationally successful single, which eventually create the moniker Mr. Worldwide (which Pit first used on the album Planet Pit).\n\nAfter his success with “Calle Ocho”, he’s had several hits, such as “Give Me Everything” and “Timber”.", "annotation_id": "10483607", "url": "https://genius.com/10483607", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
