{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Ain’t it funny, mama only son be bakin’ cakes", "vault_lines": ["Ain't it funny, mama only son be bakin' cakes"], "meaning": "Ross thinks it’s ironic that as the only male child in his family, he’s also the only one who cooks. Keep in mind, though, that he means this\n\n\n\nand probably not this", "annotation_id": "216383", "url": "https://genius.com/216383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "It’s a cold world, I need a bird to cuddle up", "vault_lines": ["It's a cold world, I need a bird to cuddle up"], "meaning": "Bird has many meanings in the rap world.\nRoss is possibly saying he needs a woman to keep him [physically] warm.\n\n\n\nOr, he needs a brick of cocaine (or the money he makes from it) to comfort him when times are hard.", "annotation_id": "214935", "url": "https://genius.com/214935", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "The money don’t sleep, so Weezy can’t rest", "vault_lines": ["The money don't sleep, so Weezy can't rest"], "meaning": "Wayne’s motivations are well known. He’s prepared to stalk his prey day and night\n\n\n\nWeezy can’t sleep/rest until he gets everything in control\n\nWeezy often takes expressions like this very literally. For instance, he says married to the money, fuck the world that’s adultery in “6 Foot 7 Foot.”", "annotation_id": "214915", "url": "https://genius.com/214915", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Well connected, got killers off in Chicago", "vault_lines": ["Well connected, got killers off in Chicago"], "meaning": "Reference to his song BMF & The Gangster Disciples Chief Larry Hoover (sometimes Rick thinks he’s Larry Hoover..)", "annotation_id": "167541", "url": "https://genius.com/167541", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
