{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "That banana clip, let Chiquita speak", "vault_lines": ["That banana clip, let Chiquita speak"], "meaning": "30 round magazines for AK-47s are curved in a silimar fashion to a banana and Chiquita is popular brand of bananas.\n\n\n\nThe word “chiquita” could be a homonym, meant to also mean “your heater”", "annotation_id": "156206", "url": "https://genius.com/156206", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "I got that Esther, bitch, I’m Redd Foxx", "vault_lines": ["I got that Esther, bitch, I'm Redd Foxx"], "meaning": "Redd Foxx’s hit TV show Sanford and Son featured Foxx as Fred Sanford and LaWanda Page as Sanford’s sister-in-law, Esther Anderson, with whom he has a (very funny) antagonistic relationship\n\n\n\nWhen he says, “I’ve go that Esther bitch, I’m Red Foxx” he’s obviously using Red Foxx as an allusion, with which to make a pun on the word Eshter. There are several slang definitions for the word Esther. The most prominent of which is “a good girl, especially one who may bitch sometimes, but only for good reason.”  Also the word Esther can be a shortened form of the word Polyester, as in the fabric.  In this particular case, it’s difficult to determine exactly which one of these two slang versions of the word Wayne is implying, as he has spoken previously in the song about his “good girl” that let him “call her collect,” and also about how he wishes to be buried in “brown linen.”", "annotation_id": "151634", "url": "https://genius.com/151634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Double M,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s label is Maybach Music (two M’s).\n\nIs it a coincidence that there are two M’s in Y(M)C(M)B, as well?", "annotation_id": "150898", "url": "https://genius.com/150898", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
