{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Red on the wall, Basquiat when I paint", "vault_lines": ["Red on the wall, Basquiat when I paint"], "meaning": "One would think that gunfire-fueled blood spatter would look more like a Pollock\n\nRick Ross says he is to rap what Basquiat is to painting…a genius.\n\n\n\nAccording to his recent article in XXL, Ross has a tattoo of Basquiat on his leg (somewhere).", "annotation_id": "150870", "url": "https://genius.com/150870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Yeah, load up the choppers like it’s December 31st", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, load up the choppers like it's December 31st"], "meaning": "New Year’s Eve is a popular time to shoot off guns\n\nSome people like to ring in the New Year with gunplay (a “chopper” is a gun)\n\nPersonally, I prefer making a resolution that I won’t keep more than a week..", "annotation_id": "150868", "url": "https://genius.com/150868", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Dark shades, Eazy E", "vault_lines": ["Dark shades, Eazy E"], "meaning": "R.I.P. to the man who could pull off the Jheri Curl.\n\n\n\nHe was also a member of N.W.A.", "annotation_id": "150848", "url": "https://genius.com/150848", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Drop palmolive in a nigga dope Make it come back even harder than before (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Drop palmolive in a nigga dope", "Make it come back even harder than before (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Palmolive is a brand that is known for making hand soap. He is mixing it with pure cocaïne to make a stronger variation of it for his fiends.\nJust a drop of soap when making cocaine into crack will make it harder like a soap rock, thus making it less pure but the hard texture is liked better.", "annotation_id": "150838", "url": "https://genius.com/150838", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Buried in Louis, I’m talking all brown linen, huh", "vault_lines": ["Buried in Louis, I'm talking all brown linen, huh"], "meaning": "Wayne wants to be buried in Louis Vuitton which is made with brown linen.\n\n“Louis” is also short for Louisiana.", "annotation_id": "150784", "url": "https://genius.com/150784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "If I die today, remember me like John Lennon", "vault_lines": ["If I die today, remember me like John Lennon"], "meaning": "John Lennon died but he will live on forever in everyone’s memory, “John” is also the name of the song.\n\nHe was also an iconic rockstar – a mantra to which Weezy aspires..\n\n\n\n“If I Die Today” was also the original name of the song\n\n\n\nAlso said by Rick Ross in “I’m Not A Star”", "annotation_id": "150783", "url": "https://genius.com/150783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "The guns are drawn and I ain’t talking ’bout a sketch", "vault_lines": ["The guns are drawn and I ain't talking 'bout a sketch"], "meaning": "“Drawing” a gun is pulling it out, not literally drawing it with a pencil, or sketching it\n\nBut let us not forget: Wayne went to art school..", "annotation_id": "150763", "url": "https://genius.com/150763", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "The flight too long, I got a bed on the jet", "vault_lines": ["The flight too long, I got a bed on the jet"], "meaning": "Gulfstream jets feature Tempurpedic™ matresses\n\n\n\nThis suggest that he flies a lot over long distances, but also that hes so pimp that he can afford to fit a bedroom in his private jet. In all probability, he is likely using this line as a way to suggest sex to whatever lucky gal is on the jet with him.", "annotation_id": "150762", "url": "https://genius.com/150762", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "Top down, it’s upset", "vault_lines": ["Top down, it's upset"], "meaning": "The roof of his car is down. Down can also mean upset in a different context\n\nEssentially, Weezy “turns that frown upside down” by taking the top off his convertible\n\nThis line can also be an extension of the sports metaphor earlier, saying that the top dog has been defeated by someone lower. In sports, this is called an upset if a weaker opponent defeats a stronger opponent.", "annotation_id": "150759", "url": "https://genius.com/150759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": "When I was in jail, she let me call her collect But if she get greedy, I’ma starve her to death", "vault_lines": ["When I was in jail, she let me call her collect", "But if she get greedy, I'ma starve her to death"], "meaning": "During Weezy’s recent stint in jail, a woman paid the fee to talk to him on the phone. Now that he’s out, if she tries to get a lot in return, he’s not giving her anything!\n\nThis can also refer to hip hop.The calling part is referring to when Wayne was in jail he called into hot 97 in NY. And if hip hop gets “greedy” and demands to much music from him, he will stop releasing it.", "annotation_id": "150758", "url": "https://genius.com/150758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "John", "line": ".44 bulldog, my motherfuckin’ pet I point it at you and tell that motherfucker, “Fetch”", "vault_lines": ["I point it at you and tell that motherfucker, \"Fetch\""], "meaning": "The .44 Bulldog is a popular revolver\n\n\n\nAlso, Wayne shooting is like playing fetch with a dog. The dog is the bullet, and the stick is you\n\n\n\nsidenote wayne has made a very similar reference to his beloved .44 in the past!", "annotation_id": "150750", "url": "https://genius.com/150750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
