{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumping Out the Gym", "line": "I’m mobbing in the streets like my name is Capone", "vault_lines": ["I'm mobbing in the streets like my name is Capone"], "meaning": "Rick Ross pulls up with his gang, doing something not illegal, not like Al Capone which  traffiked alcohol in the early 1900,figure  which was modified in the movie  “Scarface” to Tony Montana, a cocaine dealer.", "annotation_id": "15140620", "url": "https://genius.com/15140620", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumping Out the Gym", "line": "Fuck the rap game, soon as my niggas come home", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the rap game, soon as my niggas come home"], "meaning": "When my partners get home, we’ll be selling so many drugs I won’t need the rap game.\n\nTill then, Rozay will continue to stack.", "annotation_id": "652792", "url": "https://genius.com/652792", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumping Out the Gym", "line": "Got that A-1 Yellow to jumping out the gym, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Got that A-1 Yellow to jumping out the gym, nigga"], "meaning": "A1 Yellow is a type of ecstasy pill, another one of the COUNTLESS drugs that Ross has rapped about. He’s saying that he has new drugs, so come buy it while it fresh so Rozay can watch his profits jump out of the gym.", "annotation_id": "652785", "url": "https://genius.com/652785", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumping Out the Gym", "line": "Balling like I’m Michael Jackson, I’m a psychopath", "vault_lines": ["Balling like I'm Michael Jackson, I'm a psychopath"], "meaning": "Michael Jackson had so much money he made his own house into an amusement park, but some people thought he was a little crazy.\n\n\n\nRest in peace doe!\n\nSmoke on for the King of Pop!", "annotation_id": "652776", "url": "https://genius.com/652776", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumping Out the Gym", "line": "Lebron whaddup, D. Wade whaddup", "vault_lines": ["Lebron whaddup, D. Wade whaddup"], "meaning": "LeBron James and Dwayne Wade are two NBA superstars that play together on the Miami Heat. This is a pun on the name of the song, because they are known for jumping so high the game has to be stopped momentarily because Lebron & Dwayne need to be allowed time to get back in the area, for having jumped out of it.\n\nThis song was released around the time of ‘The Decision’, so Ross is saluting his Miami comrades.\n\n\n\nYou can catch Rozay courtside at Heat games, especially during the playoffs.", "annotation_id": "643143", "url": "https://genius.com/643143", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
