{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumpman (Remix)", "line": "Bentley Spurs and Phantom, Jordan fadeaway", "vault_lines": ["Bentley Spurs and Phantom, Jordan fadeaway"], "meaning": "Future’s Bentley Flying Spur has the same colorway as the San Antonio Spurs: black, white, and silver.\n\n\n\nHe also owns a Rolls Royce Phantom, so you can never catch up to him like defenders couldn’t stop Michael Jordan’s fadeaway jumpshot.", "annotation_id": "8445440", "url": "https://genius.com/8445440", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumpman (Remix)", "line": "Trapping is a hobby, that’s the way for me Money coming fast, we never getting sleep I just had to buy another safe", "vault_lines": ["Trapping is a hobby, that's the way for me", "Money coming fast, we never getting sleep", "I just had to buy another safe"], "meaning": "Future’s relationship with dealing is storied and extensive, and it is a persona he is unwilling to part with.  He’s earned enough money to leave the trap life alone, but it’s a hobby and a passion for him, so he keeps his hand in the game.\n\nIf Future has the means to drop $60k on a Monday at a strip club, he no longer requires his trap house income.", "annotation_id": "8445439", "url": "https://genius.com/8445439", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumpman (Remix)", "line": "Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu I just throwed a private dinner in LA", "vault_lines": ["I just throwed a private dinner in LA"], "meaning": "Nobu is worldwide chain of high quality Japanese restaurants, with this particular reference to the West Hollywood location, designed by world renowned architect David Rockwell. Renting one of the dining rooms out for a private dinner is a sure sign of wealth. Their website doesn’t list a price. If you have to ask…\n\n\n\nAdditionally, Nobu sounds like “no boo”, and could be considered a continuation of the previous line, suggesting Future doesn’t like to take women on dates.\n\nNobu gets a solid following with the hip-hop crowd. Drake referenced it on “Who Do You Love”:\n\nAnd man shout my nigga Game he just rolled through / Eatin' crab out in Malibu at Nobu", "annotation_id": "8445437", "url": "https://genius.com/8445437", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumpman (Remix)", "line": "She was tryna join the team I told her wait Chicken wings and fries, we don’t go on dates", "vault_lines": ["She was tryna join the team I told her wait", "Chicken wings and fries, we don't go on dates"], "meaning": "Drake’s treatment of the lower classes is picked up by Future, who plays with the basketball theme of the track, and vetoes this girl’s attempt to join his entourage. Don’t forget Future has incredibly high standards. If you’re lacking, you won’t be put on rotation.", "annotation_id": "8445436", "url": "https://genius.com/8445436", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumpman (Remix)", "line": "Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman I just seen the jet take off, they up to something Them boys just not bluffing, them boys just not bluffing Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, them boys up to something", "vault_lines": ["Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman", "I just seen the jet take off, they up to something", "Them boys just not bluffing, them boys just not bluffing", "Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, them boys up to something"], "meaning": "Air Jordan’s logo is the Jumpman, and its namesake, Michael Jordan, wore #23 during his NBA career. When Drake posted a picture of himself with Future on Instagram, speculation about a collaboration between the two artists began.\n\n\n\n“Up to something,” coupled with leaving the country, implies some kind of illegal activity. In the What A Time to Be Alive vlog, Drake and Future’s crews are in Atlanta. Since Drake’s Canadian, it’s likely he really did spend a few weeks in the United States to record the project. The felony? Dropping this tape on the rap game unannounced.", "annotation_id": "8445433", "url": "https://genius.com/8445433", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Jumpman (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-jumpman-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Jumpman (Remix)", "genius_id": 2392611, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just Business", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Wires-fl-just-business-lyrics", "genius_title": "Just Business", "genius_id": 8642841, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "Open up my window again (Yeah) Open up my window again (Yeah) I can hear death calling my name (It’s calling) I can hear death calling again (It’s calling)", "vault_lines": ["Open up my window again (Yeah)", "I can hear death calling my name (It's calling)", "I can hear death calling again (It's calling)"], "meaning": "The hook likely references the iconic photo of Malcolm X by Don Hogan Charles. Published in March 1964 issue of Life magazine, it portrays Malcolm X peering out his window holding an M1 Carbine with an extended clip. Actor Nigél Thatch’s stars as Malcolm X in the Godfather of Harlem tv show.", "annotation_id": "27554413", "url": "https://genius.com/27554413", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "The kilos come in like they new pianos", "vault_lines": ["The kilos come in like they new pianos"], "meaning": "‘Kilos’ is a size used to measure objects, but in this case, Rick Ross is talking about the drug known as Cocaine, which the show is partly about. But another name to say Kilos when talking about cocaine is ‘keys’ and as you should know, there are keys on pianos.", "annotation_id": "24107483", "url": "https://genius.com/24107483", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "You can’t be lucky like you Luciano", "vault_lines": ["You can't be lucky like you Luciano"], "meaning": "Lucky Luciano was an Italian-born gangster. He went to prison for 30 years, but got back out and continued doing drug & rum runs.\n\n\n\n The show ‘Godfather Of Harlem’, which this song is based off stars Forest Whitaker as the main gangster ‘Bumpy Johnson’ who was against drugs after he got out of prison. He also got out of prison and continued mafia work.", "annotation_id": "24107411", "url": "https://genius.com/24107411", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "Skull and bones ’til I die, nigga, well paid (Damn)", "vault_lines": ["Skull and bones 'til I die, nigga, well paid (Damn)"], "meaning": "This is a Freemason and bragging reference highlighting the stereotype that Freemasons are all rich and powerful.\n\nWhen becoming a Master Mason (3rd degree) the significance of the skull and cross bones is made clear.", "annotation_id": "23231251", "url": "https://genius.com/23231251", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "Dutch Schultz", "vault_lines": ["Snow White mink like I'm Dutch Schultz"], "meaning": "Dutch Schultz was an NYC German-Jewish-American mobster of the 20s and 30s. He made his fortune in organized crime, with activities such as bootlegging, and the numbers racket.\nHis network was $7M.\nThere were rumors of buried treasure in the Catskill Mountains in upstate NY. Apparently, there is a steel box filled with millions of dollars on the banks of the waterway.", "annotation_id": "18136725", "url": "https://genius.com/18136725", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "Rolls Royce down Malcom X boulevard", "vault_lines": ["Rolls Royce down Malcom X boulevard"], "meaning": "Malcolm X Boulevard, also known as Lenox Avenue, is the primary north-south route through Harlen in the upper portion of NYC Manhattan.\nThe avenue was the heart of Harlem during the Harlem Renaissance in the 30s, bringing together African Americans, Latinos, West Indians and Spaniards in the common interest of jazz and food.\nHarlem became established as the world capital of jazz and African-American culture, that black cinema films like “Harlem is Heaven” were playing on big screens.\nIt is thought t be one of the most important streets for African American culture.", "annotation_id": "18136711", "url": "https://genius.com/18136711", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "I seen your bitch through my Cazal shades", "vault_lines": ["I seen your bitch through my Cazal shades"], "meaning": "Ross has been known to wear designer sunglasses, such as Cazal, Dita, and Gucci.\n\n\n\nCazal can be seen as really expensive, as prices can be seen going as high as £641.00", "annotation_id": "18136699", "url": "https://genius.com/18136699", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Just In Case", "line": "Tryna touch ten figures, uh Lay on my back watching the ceiling fan I had a dream to touch a kilo gram", "vault_lines": ["I had a dream to touch a kilo gram"], "meaning": "Whilst Rozay was born in Mississippi, he was raised in Carol City, Florida, which was an impoverished area of Miami. Due to this background, Ross dreamed of wealth and luxury, to get out of the projects and succeed in life, while he was still in such a situation.\nWhen Ross first started writing rap lyrics, he romanticized drug dealing, which was he saw regularly as a child.\nThis may be a bit of a “nature vs nurture” case, in which the environment that Ross grew up in, has heavily shaped his mindset.\nRoss, before he became successful, aspired to be a successful drug dealer, but in the environment, he grew up in, this may have been the only way out of the hood.\nDepending on the purity, where you live and who you know, the price of 1kg of cocaine can fluctuate. Some sources indicate that in CA, pure cocaine goes for $26K, whereas shitty, garbage cocaine can go for $12K.\nYears ago in Atlanta, a kilo was around $30K.\nSource:https://www.quora.com/How-much-does-a-kilo-of-cocaine-cost", "annotation_id": "18136680", "url": "https://genius.com/18136680", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
