{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Justice", "line": "Call some don king,.. jay z", "vault_lines": ["Call some don king,.. jay z"], "meaning": "Double meaning,\n\n\n\nDon King is a Boxing Promoter who promoted Thriller In Manilla and The Rumble In The Jungle, probably two of his most famous fights.\n\nRoss is shouting out Jay-Z here by calling him a Don King\n\nDon – meaning the best or the greatest\n\n\n\nThese 2 have collaborated on a few records including – FuckWithMeYouKnowIGotIt, Free Masons, Maybach Music", "annotation_id": "2206395", "url": "https://genius.com/2206395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Justice", "line": "Coming up a nigga had to fight for erything Now I’m at the fight 3 rows from the ring", "vault_lines": ["Coming up a nigga had to fight for erything", "Now I'm at the fight 3 rows from the ring"], "meaning": "Ross was saying he was born poor, had to fight for food, education, his life.\n\nNow he is rich he has the luxury to afford the best seats in a boxing match.\n\n\n\nBoxing connection made with Fight and Ring in the 1st and 2nd verse.", "annotation_id": "2206384", "url": "https://genius.com/2206384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
