{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Keys to the Crib", "line": "I see no nigga in these clear Cazals", "vault_lines": ["I see no nigga in these clear Cazals"], "meaning": "Cazal is a brand of luxury sunglasses. It is Ross' main pair of choice:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHe indicates that he sees nobody with these, which indirectly means he has no competition around him.", "annotation_id": "13787849", "url": "https://genius.com/13787849", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Keys to the Crib", "line": "I’m riding in a 6 like this bitch for sale", "vault_lines": ["I'm riding in a 6 like this bitch for sale"], "meaning": "A six usually refers to a top of the line Mercedes S Class (i.e. an S600) although it could refer to a BMW 6 series coupe. With the Maybach no longer in production, the S-Class will be the highest end sedan produced by Mercedes Benz\n\nRegardless of it’s a Bimmer or Benz, it’s showroom clean, as if it could be for sale", "annotation_id": "540248", "url": "https://genius.com/540248", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Keys to the Crib", "line": "That boy Meek Mill squeeze clips for real", "vault_lines": ["That boy Meek Mill squeeze clips for real"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group member Meek Mill is a real gangsta\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to Hip Hop duo Clipse who often works with Pharrell.\n\n\nClipse is a homophone for clips\nPharrell is a homophone for “for real”", "annotation_id": "540247", "url": "https://genius.com/540247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Keys to the Crib", "line": "For the love of the game", "vault_lines": ["For the love of the game"], "meaning": "The actual name of the baseball film is “For Love of the Game”, but it’s often misconstrued like Styles P does here. He loves the drug game, not baseball", "annotation_id": "540241", "url": "https://genius.com/540241", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Keys to the Crib", "line": "I put a ribbon on the pie", "vault_lines": [", I put a ribbon on the pie"], "meaning": "Continuing Rick Ross' reference on the hook, Styles P will decorate his pie of crack cocaine with a ribbon.\n\nAlso a reference to Stevie Wonder’s “Ribbon in the Sky”", "annotation_id": "540239", "url": "https://genius.com/540239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Keys to the Crib", "line": "Homie holding a nina, could sneeze him a brick", "vault_lines": ["Homie holding a nina, could sneeze him a brick"], "meaning": "“Nina” or a “Nina Ross” refers to a pistol, specifically a 9mm. His homie is about to rob someone’s brick of cocaine with the gun", "annotation_id": "540214", "url": "https://genius.com/540214", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Keys to the Crib", "line": "I’m a guru in the kitchen, whipping mass appeal", "vault_lines": ["I'm a guru in the kitchen, whipping mass appeal"], "meaning": "Rick Ross satisfies the masses with his crack concoctions like Paula Deen or something.\n\n\n\nReference to the late MC Guru of rap group Gang Starr who had a hit called “Mass Appeal”.", "annotation_id": "540208", "url": "https://genius.com/540208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
