{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "King of Diamonds", "line": "Can’t even drop your top, because your ass so paranoid", "vault_lines": ["Can't even drop your top, because your ass so paranoid"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is basically saying that the “fuck boy,” or whomever is being referred to, won’t put down his convertible roof because he’s afraid of getting attacked, JFK style. Kennedy was fatally shot while traveling with his wife Jacqueline, Texas Governor John Connally, and Connally’s wife Nellie, in a presidential motorcade.", "annotation_id": "731904", "url": "https://genius.com/731904", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "King of Diamonds", "line": "Drop a chicken in that grease and make one into two", "vault_lines": ["Drop a chicken in that grease and make one into two"], "meaning": "“Chicken”, like almost every word Ross says, serves as drug slang here – this is his description of watering down and stretching his product\n\nMaybe Rozay wanted another excuse to talk about food.", "annotation_id": "533224", "url": "https://genius.com/533224", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "King of Diamonds", "line": "Twenty million, nigga -- look in my face", "vault_lines": ["Twenty million, nigga -- look in my face"], "meaning": "Surprisingly, this $20 million figure seems to be the one aspect of Ross' persona that is not exaggerated.  While reliable information about private fortunes is of course hard to come by, several sources have reported Ross' net worth at $20 million", "annotation_id": "532620", "url": "https://genius.com/532620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "King of Diamonds", "line": "All these rides in my yard, my shit a carnival", "vault_lines": ["All these rides in my yard, my shit a carnival"], "meaning": "Ross puns here on the colloquial meaning of “ride”, as in car, and on ride in the amusement park sense.  It should be noted that Ross hilariously pronounces “carnival” as “car-ni-VOO” in order to fit the rhyme scheme", "annotation_id": "531769", "url": "https://genius.com/531769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "King of Diamonds", "line": "Somebody call the Brinks truck The boss back, somebody call the Brinks truck The boss back, somebody call the Brinks truck The boss back, somebody call the Brinks truck", "vault_lines": ["The boss back, somebody call the Brinks truck"], "meaning": "Brinks is a security and protection company that has armored trucks to transfer large amounts of money from point A to point B. Ross announces his return by saying that he will be making so much money they will need a Brinks truck to transfer it all.\n\n\n\nRoss is also alluding to the events of his birthday bash. After Ross and Diddy allegedly blew a million dollars at the King of Diamonds strip club, an armored truck had to be called to transfer the money.\n\nWhich makes no sense at all. A Brinks truck delivers money which comes from a bank. If he had the money in the bank to start with he could have paid on a card.", "annotation_id": "531754", "url": "https://genius.com/531754", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "King of Diamonds", "line": "Love my daughter to death, ten karats in her ear", "vault_lines": ["Love my daughter to death, ten karats in her ear"], "meaning": "Ross loves his daughter so much, that he bought her ten karat diamond earrings. This line pays homage to an old Biggie line.\n\nAlso, Ross uses a play on words here with ‘death’, suggesting conflict diamonds. He loves his daughter so much he bought her Sierra Leone jewelry.", "annotation_id": "531748", "url": "https://genius.com/531748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
