{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Kiss My Pinky Ring, Curly (50 Cent Diss)", "line": "‘In Da Club’ heard Banks wrote the chorus", "vault_lines": ["'In Da Club' heard Banks wrote the chorus"], "meaning": "Former G-Unit member Bang Em Smurf said that 50 Cent got the chorus for his song “In Da Club” from a Lloyd Banks song.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QglrdNQFvz8&t=125s\n\nSha Money XL, who is one of the executive producers of 50 Cent’s album Get Rich Or Die Tryin', also said that 50 Cent took the chorus from one of Lloyd Banks’s songs:\n\nTruth be told Lloyd Banks wrote that hook. That whole part was a verse in one of Banks’ songs. “Find me in the club, bottle full of Bubb…” Fifty heard it and knew how to make it a hook and make it hot.\n\nInterestingly enough 50 Cent had rapped the chorus in a freestyle that G-Unit did on Hot 97 in 2002.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MTpWQj6DxNM&t=619s", "annotation_id": "36934277", "url": "https://genius.com/36934277", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
