{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "It’s the lazy eyed gangsta kid G. Giancana", "vault_lines": ["It's the lazy eyed gangsta kid G. Giancana"], "meaning": "The “G” in Kool’s name stands for both Genius and Giancana, which he takes from Sicilian Chicago mob boss Sam Giancana.\n\n\n\nDaz Dillinger, Rick Ross, and Capone continue the tradition by taking mob inspired names as well.\n\nSee BET’s list here\n\nIn someone afflicted with lazy eye sindrom, one eyeball is cockeyed, permanently stuck, glancing at objects unknown. But for Kool G. Rap, having a lazy eye means he can look at what is in front of him as well as to his side without having to turn his head. A trait most gangsters wish they had.\n\nThe lazy eye:\n\n\n\nT-Mac from 2K8\n(skip to 0:30)\n\nKeep an eye on the haters.", "annotation_id": "1365882", "url": "https://genius.com/1365882", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "The past of the present tense", "vault_lines": ["The past of the present tense"], "meaning": "Past events constitute your present reality.\n\nStudy them, know what happenings brought things to their current state and why.\n\nEvident in the appearances of Biggie’s voice and Kool G. Rap on this track, Ross is connecting himself with the history of Hip Hop and giving it the respect it deserves.\n\nWithout Kool G. Rap and may other hip hop forefathers, there would be no Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "1362335", "url": "https://genius.com/1362335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "Pastors lie is my testament", "vault_lines": ["Pastors lie is my testament"], "meaning": "Ross is insinuating that [Pastor Troy] was lying about getting the all clear from Roy Jones Jr. to walk him out to the ring in his 2008 bout verses Felix Trinidad.\n\nTroy walked Roy Jones Jr. out to the ring, but Hip Hop’s Biggest Bawse followed right behing while performing The Boss.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T-8IS94GFyY\n\nSource #1\nSource #2", "annotation_id": "1362334", "url": "https://genius.com/1362334", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "Kool G’s back nigga MMG,", "vault_lines": ["Kool G's back nigga MMG,"], "meaning": "You were fooled!\n\nKGB stands for Kool G. Rap, a Hip Hop forefather who might as well be Isaac, son of Abraham, (Big Daddy Kane),  on the flow-e-tree in terms of the number of rappers he has influenced.\n\nFor his return see verse 2.", "annotation_id": "1349821", "url": "https://genius.com/1349821", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "Swerving thorough the streets it’s the KGB", "vault_lines": ["Swerving thorough the streets it's the KGB"], "meaning": "“KGB agents are as tough as they come. Not only are they physically prepared, but their mental training takes them far beyond the capabilities of a regular human being.\n- Pavel Ksendz, KGB operator descendent\n\nRoss' music and influence moves like the Soviet Secret Service, the KGB. Also, the KGB are in pursuit of Ross so he swerves in his Maybach through traffic.\n\nFocus, intensity, and toughness are all characteristics that Rozay & the KGB have in common.\n\nBonus:\nWho would win in a match between the CIA & the KGB?", "annotation_id": "1349610", "url": "https://genius.com/1349610", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "Lord forgive me I’m a sinner Still smoking Bible paper Revelations getting thinner", "vault_lines": ["Lord forgive me I'm a sinner", "Still smoking Bible paper Revelations getting thinner"], "meaning": "Ross, continuing the Christian theme, begins by paraphrasing a general confession recited by many Christian denominations, including the Church of the Street to which Ross belongs:\n\nMost merciful God, I confess that I have sinned against you in thought word and deed by what I have done, and by what I have left undone…\n\nThe 2nd part of the line gives the listener a prime example of “sin”, smoking weed wrapped in pages from the Bible. Curious behavior, because Rozay not only has his own joint roller, but twists pearls himself.\n\n\n\nMarijuana is a contemplative drug. To smoke the Book of Revelation to absorb it’s essence and ponder its meaning. Revelation is the final book in the Bible and apocalyptic in nature. By inhaling holy joints that on describe the end of the world, Rozay is metaphorically coming to terms with his own mortality while renewing his resolve to act as the great hustling profit we have come to know and love.\n\nBut is smoking Bible paper healthy or practical?", "annotation_id": "1341863", "url": "https://genius.com/1341863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "All black all my cars I call them Amistad", "vault_lines": ["All black all my cars I call them Amistad"], "meaning": "The Amistad was a Spanish slave ship that, in 1839 while sailing from Havana to Puerto Principe was captured by the slaves on board. Led by Sengbe Pieh aka Joseph Cinqué, their bravery, re-capture, trial, and return to Africa was immortalized in the 1997 film the Amistad.\n\n\n\nA portion of Rising Up: Hale Woodruff’s Murals from the High Museum of Art in Atlanta.\n\nBut how does a fleet of black Maybach’s owed by Rick Ross relate to a slave revolt?\n\n\n\nRoss is validating the sacrifices made and hardships endured by his enslaved ancestors by naming the cars he earned after the famed ship. A quote from Joseph Cinqué from the film explains this sentiment best:\n\n I meant my ancestors. I will call into the past, far into the beginning of time, and beg them to help me at the judgment. I will reach back and draw them into me. And they must come…for at this moment I am the whole reason they have existed at all.", "annotation_id": "1333854", "url": "https://genius.com/1333854", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "Hallelujah, women holler, somebody plotting Got ’em leaking holes in his medulla oblongata", "vault_lines": ["Hallelujah, women holler, somebody plotting"], "meaning": "The medulla oblongata is a section at the base of the brain that controls automatic bodily functions (ie breathing).\n\nRoss, always one for the dramatic, albeit fictional, mob hit conjures the image of a group people screaming at the sight of a man with a bullet whole in the lower back part of his head.\n\nRoss is somewhere where he was able to see the hit go down, and with a breath as he exhales smoke from his lungs, he exclaims, “Hallelujah”.\n\nAlso, when women see Ross they scream, “Hallelujah” which means “God be praised.” They praise the god of sex because of moves like this.", "annotation_id": "1286156", "url": "https://genius.com/1286156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "Four piece chicken box Birdman dinner", "vault_lines": ["Four piece chicken box Birdman dinner"], "meaning": "This is perhaps Ross' deepest fried entendre:\n\n\nHe is a “bird man” in that he loves chicken. Eating chicken is his favorite chicken activity. Forget about MMG, he is building the Untouchable Wing Stop Empire.\nHe has four attractive girls, aka chickens, with him in his Maybach, another foreshadowing of his life as the Teflon Don.\nHe is bringing Birdman, head of YMCMB, a four piece chicken box for dinner – Ross is all about label executive cooperation.\nChicken as drug terminology: It’s going to be a succulent dinner because Ross has raised his chickens to be juicy through abundant consumption of anabolic steroids.", "annotation_id": "1285604", "url": "https://genius.com/1285604", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "They nailed Jesus to the cross My jeweler nailed a piece 30 g’s for me to floss", "vault_lines": ["They nailed Jesus to the cross", "My jeweler nailed a piece 30 g's for me to floss"], "meaning": "Rozay is well versed in scripture and that knowledge is reflected in his deft word play.\n\nJudas sold Jesus to the Romans for 30 pieces of sliver (the modern equivalent of $5000):\n\nMatthew 26:14-16 –\n\nThen one of the Twelve—the one called Judas Iscariot—went to the chief priests 15 and asked, “What are you willing to give me if I deliver him over to you?” So they counted out for him thirty pieces of silver. 16 From then on Judas watched for an opportunity to hand him over.\n\n\n\nJudas Returning The Thirty Pieces of Silver – Rembrandt\n(Judas is the kneeling figure on the lower right)\n\nThe symbolism is pristine: Judas was paid 30 pieces of silver to betray his teacher while Ross paids $30,000 for his Jesus Piece, a reward for his output in the Rap game. The 30 pieces of silver denote worldly wealth, and Ross is known for his lavish spending. But his spending habits are a celebration of the blessings God has bestowed on him. Where once greed led to the death of Jesus, Rozay’s gold chain bearing his likeness celebrates his sacrifice.", "annotation_id": "1282280", "url": "https://genius.com/1282280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "My Masonic Lodge the second nation under God", "vault_lines": ["My Masonic Lodge the second nation under God"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' mansion is so illustrious that it is second to the United States of America, specifically the White House.\n\n\n\nOur pledge of allegiance:\n\nI pledge allegiance to the Flag of the United States of America, and to the Republic for which it stands, one Nation under God, indivisible, with liberty and justice for all.\"\n\nFor validation of Rozay’s claim, see his episode of MTV Cribs.\n\nHighlights include a motorcycle named Madonna, a cameo appearance from [GUNPLAY] at 2:34, and the quotes:\n\nDiet sodas… they’ve been in there for over a year. I don’t drink diet sodas ya feel me?\n\nas well as\n\nWhen I come home, I put my ice on. I hate global warming.\n\nThis line is also a prelude to what listeners will find on Teflon Don, specifically the song Free Mason.", "annotation_id": "1276656", "url": "https://genius.com/1276656", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knife Fight", "line": "That’s why I bust back, it don’t phase me When he drop take his Glock and I’m Swayze", "vault_lines": ["When he drop take his Glock and I'm Swayze"], "meaning": "Sampled from the Biggie & 2Pac joint Runnin' (Dyin to Live)\n\nBiggie busts back at the police because he is too fat", "annotation_id": "1276474", "url": "https://genius.com/1276474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
