{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Curry, what’s up? Double M (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Curry, what's up? Double M (Uh)"], "meaning": "Ross shouts out Denzel Curry. Double M refers to his record label Maybach Music.", "annotation_id": "31254612", "url": "https://genius.com/31254612", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Bumpin’ Speaker Knockerz, “Rico Story” when I see the coppers, damn", "vault_lines": ["Bumpin' Speaker Knockerz, \"Rico Story\" when I see the coppers, damn"], "meaning": "Speaker Knockerz was a young South Carolina artist who died tragically in 2014 at the age of 19. He was an early pioneer of the autotuned rap sound that would become mainstream a few years after his death as well as an extremely accomplished producer.\n\nOne of Speaker Knockerz' most popular songs is “Rico Story,” which tells the tale of a Rico, a man who sets out to rob a bank and ultimately shoots a police officer. With this reference, Denzel pays homage to a young legend as well as reaffirms his attitude towards police.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=alx4oFnkotk", "annotation_id": "26170093", "url": "https://genius.com/26170093", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Golds in my mouth and my dreads lookin’ like a palm tree", "vault_lines": ["Golds in my mouth and my dreads lookin' like a palm tree"], "meaning": "Gem golds in his mouth are meaning his grills and his dreads actually looked like a palm tree the way they were styled during the time recording the song.", "annotation_id": "22552773", "url": "https://genius.com/22552773", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Tell my mama that I love her ’cause tomorrow not for sure", "vault_lines": ["Tell my mama that I love her 'cause tomorrow not for sure"], "meaning": "This is most likely a reference to another track on Imperial, “If Tomorrow’s Not Here.”", "annotation_id": "20025743", "url": "https://genius.com/20025743", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Call me knotty head ’cause I don’t give a fuck", "vault_lines": ["Call me knotty head 'cause I don't give a fuck"], "meaning": "Knotty Hair and large locks are very culturally tied to\npeople from Florida, and being that this song is with Rick Ross, he is embracing his Florida roots by acknowledging his “Knotty Head”, and taking pride in those roots through his hair.", "annotation_id": "19855018", "url": "https://genius.com/19855018", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Fuck karate, I got me a shotty", "vault_lines": ["Fuck karate, I got me a shotty"], "meaning": "In this line, Curry states that any fight with opposition would not lead to physical contact (karate) as he would use a firearm. The firearm in this case is a shotgun.\n\nThe fact that he won’t engage physically is reinforced in the pre-chorus, through the line “Bitch I can’t be touched”.", "annotation_id": "18504734", "url": "https://genius.com/18504734", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Yeah, uh (Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A reference to Ross’s label Maybach Music Group, which has also signed artists like Meek Mill and Wale.\n\n\n\nThis audio clip can be heard on other Ross-assisted tracks, like Drake’s “Lord Knows” and DJ Khaled’s “No New Friends”", "annotation_id": "17969750", "url": "https://genius.com/17969750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Dolphin Gang, Bello cigars on the sideline (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Dolphin Gang, Bello cigars on the sideline (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Both Denzel Curry and Rick Ross are from Miami Dade County, Florida where the pro-football team the Miami Dolphins play. Since they’re rich, they can afford to both be on the sidelines for NFL games and to smoke Bello Cigars, which is a very expensive brand of Cuban Cigar.", "annotation_id": "14022377", "url": "https://genius.com/14022377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Monday to Sunday all you niggas, we slangin’ like Pistol Pete, peace", "vault_lines": ["Monday to Sunday all you niggas, we slangin' like Pistol Pete, peace"], "meaning": "Now you might think that Denzel is referring to ‘Pete Maravich’ the famous NBA legend. However, he is actually talking about: ‘Peter “Pistol Pete” Rollack’, the murderous kingpin from the Bronx. Pete has been serving a life sentence since 1995 at the age of 20. He is also the leader of: “Sex Money Murder” a blood set in the east.", "annotation_id": "13343690", "url": "https://genius.com/13343690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Educated, reading books, I’m talkin’ Art of War", "vault_lines": ["Educated, reading books, I'm talkin' Art of War"], "meaning": "The Art of War is an ancient Chinese military text written by Sun Tzu. It is known for its diverse knowledge on warfare as Sun Tzu was a military strategist.\n\nRick Ross basically saying he is getting educated in strategizing how he will take down his enemies.", "annotation_id": "9040395", "url": "https://genius.com/9040395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Life is melancholy, sellin’ flock when they think it’s molly", "vault_lines": ["Life is melancholy, sellin' flock when they think it's molly"], "meaning": "Denzel reflects on his life as being sad and dark since he’s always selling drugs, some of which are not the actual product but “flock”, short for flakka, a very potent designer drug comparable to bath salts that is common in southern Florida where Curry is from.", "annotation_id": "8904521", "url": "https://genius.com/8904521", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Calm nigga, when I’m lit up, I get Von Miller (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Calm nigga, when I'm lit up, I get Von Miller (Huh)"], "meaning": "Von Miller is one of the best outside linebackers in the NFL, and is known for his impressive ability to chase down the quarterback.\n\nRick is most of the time calm and chill, but if you provoke him, he might let you feel his anger in a similar way.", "annotation_id": "8820263", "url": "https://genius.com/8820263", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Pullin’ into Risco Park in the richest cars (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Pullin' into Risco Park in the richest cars (Woo)"], "meaning": "Ross grew up in Carol City, Florida, an area mainly consisting of projects a little north of Miami. Risco Park is located within the Miami Gardens, a ghetto hood within Carol City. He’s talking about how he made it out the hood and is coming back after making it out with his rapping, and now with success and money backing him.", "annotation_id": "8798384", "url": "https://genius.com/8798384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Found another body in the lake (Huh) Same day, another tattoo on his face (Huh) Obituary on his mother’s fireplace", "vault_lines": ["Found another body in the lake (Huh)", "Same day, another tattoo on his face (Huh)", "Obituary on his mother's fireplace"], "meaning": "It’s very common for gang members, and sometimes non-affiliated individuals, to get a tattoo – typically a teardrop – to represent each life they’ve taken.\n\n\n\nThe obituary on a mother’s fireplace refers to the obituary of the individual murdered.", "annotation_id": "8798334", "url": "https://genius.com/8798334", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "211's broad day, I had to live a life of crime", "vault_lines": ["211's broad day, I had to live a life of crime"], "meaning": "A 211 is the police code for a robbery/burglary.\n\nAlso a reference to Steel Reserve which is stylized with a 211 on the front of the can. He needs to drink during the day to get through his life of crime.", "annotation_id": "8741675", "url": "https://genius.com/8741675", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Hair is nappy, knotty", "vault_lines": ["Hair is nappy, knotty"], "meaning": "Denzel’s hair is tightly coiled and unbrushed, Like a lot of people in Carol City. Notice the homophone between knotty and naughty: unbrushed hair is knotty.", "annotation_id": "8700649", "url": "https://genius.com/8700649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Buddy got jacked like MK4", "vault_lines": ["Buddy got jacked like MK4"], "meaning": "Denzel is comparing how he throws his enemies off a cliff to the way Jackson Briggs threw his own opponent off at the end of the fighting video game, Mortal Kombat 4.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UNkRvcUn6VM\n\nDenzel uses Jackson’s nickname, Jax, as a homophone to tie into the relation to the first mentioned video game.\n\nHe has utilized a fighting game known as Yu Yu Hakusho: Dark Tournament in the past, using half of the game’s title for another title of a 2012 song and also gameplay for the music video.", "annotation_id": "8699099", "url": "https://genius.com/8699099", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "I’ma tote a stick until they send me to the pen’ This the way it is, I gotta get it how I live", "vault_lines": ["This the way it is, I gotta get it how I live"], "meaning": "“Stick,” is a term used to refer to a gun, usually an AK-47. The term is commonly used in South Florida, which is where Curry is from.\n\nCurry is saying that where he is from means he has to carry a gun on him, even if that means going to the “pen,” which is short for penitentiary, or prison, because has to be able to protect himself.", "annotation_id": "8692785", "url": "https://genius.com/8692785", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Sub-Zero, put a nigga on, so Iced out This the price I gotta pay because I wanna be iced out", "vault_lines": ["Sub-Zero, put a nigga on, so", "This the price I gotta pay because I wanna be iced out"], "meaning": "Denzel is “iced out”, which is a slang for wearing diamonds/chains around his neck, but it’s also a reference to the Mortal Kombat character Sub-Zero, who’s able to form ice.", "annotation_id": "8692400", "url": "https://genius.com/8692400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Knotty Head", "line": "Bitches be givin’ me sloppy, my pockets on Andy Milonakis", "vault_lines": ["Bitches be givin' me sloppy, my pockets on Andy Milonakis"], "meaning": "Denzel has enough money to enjoy the sweeter things of life and compares his pocket size to that of the comedian Andy Milonakis, who is overweight – his pockets are fat.\n\nAlso is Andy’s net worth at a respectable value of $2 million.", "annotation_id": "8688540", "url": "https://genius.com/8688540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
