{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Know What I’m Doin’", "line": "Nigga I mack hard, bitch, I’m a bad boy", "vault_lines": ["Nigga I mack hard, bitch, I'm a bad boy"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to Craig Mack, who was one of the original Bad Boy Records artists.", "annotation_id": "18946592", "url": "https://genius.com/18946592", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Know What I’m Doin’", "line": "Bitch, what you tryna do? I haven’t spent a check yet off Tha Carter II", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, what you tryna do?", "I haven't spent a check yet off Tha Carter II"], "meaning": "Wayne has already made so much money from his previous record sales and hustling in the streets, he hasn’t spent a single dollar he made off of his most recent album, Tha Carter II yet.\n\nLike Father, Like Son was released around a year after Carter II, so Wayne is clearly set for life.\n\n\n\nThis has a very similar sentiment to this Jay-Z line.", "annotation_id": "2718196", "url": "https://genius.com/2718196", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Know What I’m Doin’", "line": "My mama didn’t know, and Stunna ain’t know ’bout it ’Til the day I got shot, they found some money in my pocket", "vault_lines": ["My mama didn't know, and Stunna ain't know 'bout it", "'Til the day I got shot, they found some money in my pocket"], "meaning": "Not even his mama or mentor Birdman (aka Baby, aka Stunna) knew he was selling drugs until the day he accidentally shot himself and there was an inexplicable amount of money in his pocket.\n\nWhen Lil Wayne was 12, he was home alone playing with a gun and accidentally shot himself two inches from his heart. A heroic off-duty cop came to save him and Wayne nearly died on the ride to the hospital.\n\nListen to Wayne tell the story:\n\nhttp://youtu.be/84U1I5e7I54?t=13s", "annotation_id": "113270", "url": "https://genius.com/113270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Know What I’m Doin’", "line": "And if they ever play with me I’m gettin’ another teardrop", "vault_lines": ["And if they ever play with me I'm gettin' another teardrop"], "meaning": "Birdman is referring to his teardrop tattoos, which signify that you have killed someone (at least it does in the context Birdman is using it here- for other meanings click here)\n\n\n\nOne of Birdman’s teardrops is widely rumored to be for his alleged arrangement of the murder of the rapper Yella Boy, which Birdman has hinted on in a song before.\n\nIf you mess with Birdman, he will have to get another teardrop tattoo because he will kill you.", "annotation_id": "56820", "url": "https://genius.com/56820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Know What I’m Doin’", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Birdman-and-lil-wayne-know-what-im-doin-lyrics", "genius_title": "Know What I’m Doin’", "genius_id": 1475, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Kobe or Ginobili (Remix)", "line": "No what’s the difference between a real fan and a fake groupie?", "vault_lines": ["No what's the difference between a real fan and a fake groupie?"], "meaning": "Mack ushers in a verse of euphoric ambiance and this line is his pilgrim – the first of many miraculously astonishing bars. At first glance Mr. Maine seems to be posing a simple question. A mild conundrum with a relatively easy answer; for what is a fake groupie if not the antithesis of a real fan? Mack dares you to hear deeper into the words. He uses the grammatical version of “no” as opposed to “know” because he says “no” to listeners who are less than authentic. Firmly establishing that his face is in fact his warrent.", "annotation_id": "3426654", "url": "https://genius.com/3426654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
