{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "My pockets fat enough to catch a nigga if I fall", "vault_lines": ["My pockets fat enough to catch a nigga if I fall"], "meaning": "Ross alludes that he has enough money to survive if he were to be prosecuted or arrested.\n\nactually, he means it in all contexts of life. He means if any issue occurs he will be able to tackle it with his money.", "annotation_id": "12695928", "url": "https://genius.com/12695928", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "My nigga had on yellow Balenciagas, ha ha ha ha", "vault_lines": ["My nigga had on yellow Balenciagas, ha ha ha ha"], "meaning": "A statement Rick makes in regards to Meek’s sense of fashion. The rapper attended The Hip-Hop Inaugural Ball II where he received the Community Activist Award at the Harman Center for the Arts in Washington, DC.\n\n\n\nHis statement piece garnered a lot of media attention, and definitely some mixed reactions from his fan base.", "annotation_id": "12632743", "url": "https://genius.com/12632743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "To ridin’ under stars, the life we lived for", "vault_lines": ["To ridin' under stars, the life we lived for"], "meaning": "Referencing the Rolls Royce Wraith, Meek owns the vehicle with the stars on its roof", "annotation_id": "12629502", "url": "https://genius.com/12629502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "So when my nigga Meek caught his case, I went to visit him", "vault_lines": ["So when my nigga Meek caught his case, I went to visit him"], "meaning": "In 2014, Meek Mill was sentenced to a 3-6 month sentence in the slammer due to violating his parole from a drug and gun conviction in 2008. Ross is letting it be known that he visited Meek Mill while he was locked up.", "annotation_id": "12629469", "url": "https://genius.com/12629469", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "These helicopters rise for the one in charge If I sentence you to die, well that’s a hundred shots", "vault_lines": ["These helicopters rise for the one in charge", "If I sentence you to die, well that's a hundred shots"], "meaning": "Police helicopters circle around the scene of the crime at night and the ones in charge are the feds.\nWhen Ross says hundred shots he is figuratively referring to how many young black lives are lost and then shot at multiple times by the ignorant cop who has taken away an innocent life since he is the one in charge.\n17 year old Laquan Mcdonald was shot dead multiple times by a police officer in Chicago in late 2014.", "annotation_id": "11594815", "url": "https://genius.com/11594815", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Judge bangin’ like a blood, show a nigga love", "vault_lines": ["Judge bangin' like a blood, show a nigga love"], "meaning": "The corrupt judge is on Ross' payroll and will make sure Ross gets off easy.\n\n“Bangin' like a blood” correlates with the way the judge bangs his gavel.", "annotation_id": "11581061", "url": "https://genius.com/11581061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Time to set a date for trial, we never settle out (bring it)", "vault_lines": ["Time to set a date for trial, we never settle out (bring it)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross went through legal issues that stemmed from Ross assaulting Johnathan Zamudio. Zamudio was Ross' gardener and he allegedly invited people to Ross' home without permission. Ross was charged with assault and kidnapping. He would rather fight the case and spend money through legal fees instead of paying off Zamudio.", "annotation_id": "11581024", "url": "https://genius.com/11581024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Now it’s stones on my hands, Roberto Durans", "vault_lines": ["Now it's stones on my hands, Roberto Durans"], "meaning": "This line refers to Panamanian boxer Roberto Duran whose nickname was “Hands Of Stone\"—a name he earned because of his punching power. Duran played in Rocky II as a sparring partner for Balboa and had a small role in Harlem Nights.\n\n\n\nRappers commonly call diamond-embedded jewelry “rocks.” Ross plays on the nickname given to Duran, to express his love for jewelry.", "annotation_id": "11580965", "url": "https://genius.com/11580965", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Watch your dog die as my gun bark", "vault_lines": ["Watch your dog die as my gun bark"], "meaning": "This is a play on the words, “dog” and “bark,” Ross expresses how he will shoot and kill one of your friends, or associates.\n\nHe would use this terminology later on in the track.", "annotation_id": "11580905", "url": "https://genius.com/11580905", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "And before I had that bag, I used to bag them bitches", "vault_lines": ["And before I had that bag, I used to bag them bitches"], "meaning": "To “bag” a woman is to win her over and date her exclusively.  A “bag” is also slang for money. Meek uses the wordplay to express collecting different women even before the money and the fame.\n\nThis may also be a reference to his song, “In My Bag,”", "annotation_id": "11580857", "url": "https://genius.com/11580857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Love to see a pretty bitch rollin’ a wood leaf", "vault_lines": ["Love to see a pretty bitch rollin' a wood leaf"], "meaning": "Ross loves seeing a pretty girl rolling up a fresh “backwood” aka wood leaf with fresh marijuana.\n\n\n\nOn a side note, back in 2014 Ross announced he was going to fly a girl out from LA to Miami once a month to roll his weed for three day periods because of her incredible talent and impeccable rolling techniques.", "annotation_id": "11550442", "url": "https://genius.com/11550442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Me and all my dogs sell a lot of that food", "vault_lines": ["Me and all my dogs sell a lot of that food"], "meaning": "Before rapping, this line most likely would’ve been referring to drugs. However, the food in question could be metaphorically speaking about Meek’s music. Note the play on “dog food.”\n\nDog food is also a slang term used for heroin as that’s what the drug looks like in its raw form. According to an USA Today report, there was a drug found in actual dog food prompting a recall.\n\nPresently, Meek’s labelmate and boss, Rick Ross is known for owning several franchises of Wing Stop Restaurants where he would actually be selling food.\n\n\n\nSide note: Rick Ross even has a song called “Dog Food.”", "annotation_id": "11549378", "url": "https://genius.com/11549378", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Chad was sippin’", "vault_lines": ["I been tippin' since Scottie was Pippen, Chad was sippin'"], "meaning": "This refers to the late Pimp C, who was known for sipping lean which contributed to his death on December 4, 2007. Chad Lamont Butler was his real name. Rick Ross also collaborated with Bun B, Pimp C’s bandmate in the tribute “You’re Everything.”", "annotation_id": "11549323", "url": "https://genius.com/11549323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Make me shoot a rapper like my name was Benny Boom", "vault_lines": ["Make me shoot a rapper like my name was Benny Boom"], "meaning": "Meek Mill plays on literally “shooting a rapper,” by shouting out Benny Boom.\n\nBenny Boom is a prominent hip-hop video director, who is from Philly like Meek. Benny has worked with Meek Mill in past. He directed videos for Meek’s 2011 hit “Ima Boss,” and 2015 “All Eyes On You”.", "annotation_id": "11541293", "url": "https://genius.com/11541293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "line": "Corners wanna check him like Odell Beckham", "vault_lines": ["Corners wanna check him like Odell Beckham"], "meaning": "Odell Beckham Jr is a Wide Receiver who plays for the New York Giants. In football, a Cornerback is a position on defense and they often match up with the Wide Receivers and attempt to, of course, stop them. Odell has had various run-ins and battles with some of the NFLs top cornerbacks including Washington Redskins' CB Josh Norman\n\nIn a game between the Carolina Panthers and New York Giants on December 20, 2015, Odell and Josh Norman, then a member of the Panthers, went at one another on and off the field. They shoved and even threw punches at one another. In addition Norman pointed a Baseball Bat at Beckham Jr’s head before the game.\n\nIt seemed that the panache, confident and fan favorite second year player, Odell Beckham, was put in check by Josh Norman and learned how cruel and violent opposing players could be just less than two years into his career.", "annotation_id": "11522967", "url": "https://genius.com/11522967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lamborghini Doors", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-lamborghini-doors-lyrics", "genius_title": "Lamborghini Doors", "genius_id": 3018284, "source": "api"}
