{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Last Breath", "line": "Money, power, respect, I took your bitch with finesse", "vault_lines": ["Money, power, respect, I took your bitch with finesse"], "meaning": "The Lox, a hip hop group from New York, released a song called “Money, Power, Respect” in 1998, which features DMX and Lil Kim.\n\nTaking somebody’s girl with finesse takes skill and composure. His high status and healthy bank account also helps the cause.", "annotation_id": "5089261", "url": "https://genius.com/5089261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Last Breath", "line": "Chickens jumping like checkers, but this game is chess", "vault_lines": ["Chickens jumping like checkers, but this game is chess"], "meaning": "Ross plays chess, generally considered a more complex, more strategic game than checkers, but his enemies aren’t thinking 7 moves ahead, unlike Ross.\n\nRoss seems to be revising a line he had on an earlier song where he confused chess with checkers.", "annotation_id": "544336", "url": "https://genius.com/544336", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
