{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Hold up, hurdles in life, I hop in a Turbo and roll around ’em", "vault_lines": ["Hold up, hurdles in life, I hop in a Turbo and roll around 'em"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION: Furthermore, the fact that he’s hopping in a Turbo to avoid the hurdles conveys how he’s so rich now that he doesn’t have to go through average person hardships – he can just pay for an easier alternative.", "annotation_id": "9098216", "url": "https://genius.com/9098216", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "I’m an artist, drug dealer, foreign car keys", "vault_lines": ["I'm an artist, drug dealer, foreign car keys"], "meaning": "A theme of the luxuriant lifestyle from the gutter is painted on one end and another end also brings out the same luxuriant lifestyle.\nBeing an artist brings about money from the tour life and sales while being a drug dealer brings you money from the drug sales.\nA brief example here is the lifestyle of famous new-era drug dealer El Chapo and Pusha T.\nBoth love the fast life and as such El Chapo’s kids can live lavishly like the video below entails.\nPusha T also is able to ride around in expensive foreign cars.\nPoint is if Pusha stops being an artist some foreign car keys will still be dangling from his finger.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a1QSdT0rDtY", "annotation_id": "9218318", "url": "https://genius.com/9218318", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Look at you, no pleasure in creative thinking, because you don’t think creatively anymore The real joy of being a human being is to be able to use your mind in the manner that the Almighty God has designed the human mind to do", "vault_lines": ["Look at you, no pleasure in creative thinking, because you don't think creatively anymore"], "meaning": "The overall theme of the speech is that Americans have become stupid and ignorant and things need to change. Citizens are no longer using their minds to the fullest potential, instead, they are letting them get bogged down by various other things. For example: mass media and television could be creating this problem or a poor education system could also be at fault. The speech does not blame drug and alcohol use alone but the entire system the country is build on as a whole. If Royce chose this audio fragment to solely criticize drug use it would be a bit hypocritical when the first verse is done by Pusha T who just dropped a song titled “Drug Dealers Anonymous” with Jay-Z. So, it can be inferred that Royce is evoking the overall message and not that one specific part of it. Other songs on this album criticize the United States of America so it is more reasonable that if he were to choose one thing to take away from this intro it would be that the American Government is fucking over its people.\n\nThis song shares the title “Layers” with the album so the two obliviously connect. One of the messages behind the title “Layers” is that Royce has layers to his writing and raps more than just shallow bars. One could argue that there is a second meaning to the title: Royce is a complex person with layers to him. Both are acceptable. Choosing to name your album and song in a way that can be interpreted different ways  goes to show how there are “layers” to a lot of what Royce does. Royce is a recognized lyricist and because he chose this speech for the intro to his main single he obviously thinks the problem Farrakhan spoke on is still a problem today but also a problem in the rap game. Meaning that other rappers can only spit basic lines. New and modern emcees cannot compete on the level Royce is at. Royce has made claims like this before so that’s not a stretch by any means.\n\nIt is unfortunate that Royce’s entire verse is recycled from his BET Backroom Freestyle ruining  the impact of a speech by proving that he cannot even think creatively enough to come up with a new verse for the track that matters most. It is so hypocritical it could almost be possibly that Royce did it ironically.\n\nLouis Farrakhan, the gentleman who wrote and recited the speech used for this introduction, is the leader of the religious group Nation of Islam. He is an outspoken and affluent man whose words have inspired masses. He is frequently surrounded by controversy. https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=SQHrqZ6Sc3Q\n\nSome of his most famous quotes:\n\n“They call them terrorists, I call them freedom fighters.”\n\n“There really can be no peace without justice. There can be no justice without truth. And there can be no truth, unless someone rises up to tell you the truth.”\n\nAlso the fact that “Tabernacle” and “Wait” were originally on his “Trust The Shooter” mixtape.", "annotation_id": "9135328", "url": "https://genius.com/9135328", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Yeah, God hearin’, but I’m gone fishin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, God hearin', but I'm gone fishin'"], "meaning": "He hears God but he refuses to bow down to anyone.  “God hearin” is a perversion of the phrase God fearing.  Pusha has no fear of so called authority figures, not even God Himself.\n\nHearin' is a homophone for herring, a type of fish.  Pusha T plays with the concept by saying that he has “gone fishin.”  This plays right into the religious theme of the song as the fish is a Christian symbol.\n\n\n\nIn the Book of Mark, Jesus says “Come ye after me, and I will make you to become fishers of men.”", "annotation_id": "9098211", "url": "https://genius.com/9098211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Underground locomotive man", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is a multi-layered reference to The Underground Railroad, a term used to describe the various secret passageways, safe-houses, and people dedicated to freeing the American slaves in the 19th century.\n\n\n\nAs Royce references Tupac many times on this album, this may also be a nod to “Violent”, a song off the 2pacalypse Now album in which Shakur raps:\n\nThe Underground Railroad on an uprise\nThis time the truth’s getting told, heard enough lies\"\n\nFurthermore, the reference may go deeper into what is known as Tupac’s Underground Railroad.  In a 1991 interview with Davey D, ‘Pac explains the intent of his Underground Railroad:\n\n\nI have a crew called the Underground Railroad and a program called the Underground Railroad…I want to build all this up, so that by next year you will know the name Underground Railroad.\n\nThe concept behind this is the same concept behind Harriet Tubman, to get my brothers who might be into drug dealing or whatever it is that’s illegal or who are disenfranchised by today’s society-I want to get them back into by turning them onto music. It could be R&B, hip hop or pop, as long as I can get them involved. While I’m doing that, I’m teaching them to find a love for themselves so they can love others and do the same thing we did for them to others.", "annotation_id": "9020807", "url": "https://genius.com/9020807", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Was a water boy, but balling always in my genes", "vault_lines": ["Was a water boy, but balling always in my genes"], "meaning": "A reference to Adam Sandler’s 1998 Film The Waterboy.\n\n\n\nRoss is saying that despite starting out small, he was always destined for greatness.", "annotation_id": "9005940", "url": "https://genius.com/9005940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "I philosophize with wise words from learned lessons", "vault_lines": ["I philosophize with wise words from learned lessons"], "meaning": "Reffering to the previous Pusha T line:\n\nI philophize for them Pitchfork scholars\n\nRoyce’s philosophies are words inspired by his own life, therefore they are learned lessons.", "annotation_id": "8952420", "url": "https://genius.com/8952420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Burner on my waist, yet I’m saying “Stop the violence”", "vault_lines": ["Burner on my waist, yet I'm saying \"Stop the violence\""], "meaning": "Something which is common in rap is the double standards which it represents. Lately has been the Black Lives Matter which has seen rappers such as The Game take part in it. The point to note is that The Game like Pusha T has indulged in some heavy black-on-black violence themed tracks which is pretty hypocritical.\n\n\n\nKendrick Lamar recently pointed this out in his 2015, The Blacker The Berry and explains why its pure hypocrisy", "annotation_id": "8952082", "url": "https://genius.com/8952082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Paranoid of poverty, hustle was the philosophy I seen a kilo, I swear it became a part of me", "vault_lines": ["I seen a kilo, I swear it became a part of me"], "meaning": "Ross explains the struggle of being broke, and how it lead him to a life of drug dealing. Ironically, he served as a correctional facilities officer for a year and a half.\n\n\n\nThe opening line also creates a link in the philosophies of Pusha, Royce and Ross. For Push, his is addressing critics, whilst Royce uses “wise words from learned lessons” for his audience: Ross’s is hustling.", "annotation_id": "8943728", "url": "https://genius.com/8943728", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "You players can jump if you want, but you half-stepping like Paul George", "vault_lines": ["You players can jump if you want, but you half-stepping like Paul George"], "meaning": "Royce uses basketball as a comparison to the rap game. In basketball, the half-step is a hesitation move used to trick your opposition. It is often used to fake the act of making a jump-shot. If your opponent falls for the trick play, it could open up space for you and your teammates.\n\nRoyce is giving his opponents to opportunity to jump him and try to push him out the game. Rather than taking him up on his offer, Royce' competitors are hesitating to make a step. NBA small forward Paul George is known for his half-step dribble move.", "annotation_id": "8943365", "url": "https://genius.com/8943365", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "God fearin’, but I’m Guy Fisher", "vault_lines": ["God fearin', but I'm Guy Fisher"], "meaning": "Pusha gives the glory to God for enhancing his ability and increasing his efficiency, with the portmanteau of “godficient”.  He believes that with the strength of God anything is possible — a view expressed in Matthew 19:26:\n\nJesus looked at them and said, “With man this is impossible, but with God all things are possible.”\n\nand again in Jeremiah 32:17:\n\nAh Lord God! behold, thou hast made the heaven and the earth by thy great power and stretched out arm, and there is nothing too hard for thee:\n\nPusha has also dropped two albums named Fear of God and Fear Of God 2. The fear of God is described in Proverbs 8:13 as the hatred of evil.", "annotation_id": "8939386", "url": "https://genius.com/8939386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "In my world, mistakes turn to blessings, The hate turned to destiny", "vault_lines": ["In my world, mistakes turn to blessings,", "The hate turned to destiny"], "meaning": "In life, we as humans are subjected to thinking in our own human wisdom that mistakes have nowhere else to take us but a dead end. However, in Royce, he is so optimistic that whatever he sees going grim is highly a blessing in disguise.\n\nRoyce could be pointing out to his drinking problem here which he had gotten deep into to a point his rapping gift dipped a little. This is what took him two years to cleanse off and when he came back he forged two great unions, Bad Meets Evil and PRhyme to make some of the illest music in the rap game right now. To add on to that guidance from one of the illest rappers in the game too.", "annotation_id": "8938774", "url": "https://genius.com/8938774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "I live by a code of demonic – Illuminati, Obama, Hovanomics", "vault_lines": ["I live by a code of demonic – Illuminati, Obama, Hovanomics"], "meaning": "Living by codes such as these combined must represent the biggest influential evil known to man.\n\n\nDemonic code is engraved in the Eleven Satanic Rules on earth which could easily explain why Royce doesn’t want to be bothered by whoever for whatsoever.\nThe Illuminati is a powerful group which is known the world over for its heavy influence on populations around the world\nBarrack Obama on the other hand was one of the most powerful men on the planet when this was written. He of course was the president of the United States for eight years. That’s tremendous power and influence once again.\nHovanomics refers to Jay-z and his intriguing effect on the rap game which seems to change tide in any direction he chooses.\n\n\n\nTo combine these four concepts would result in immeasurable power and influence.", "annotation_id": "8938665", "url": "https://genius.com/8938665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "All I got time to do is go back in time and pose with the Unabomber Just so I can go back in time a second time to photobomb it", "vault_lines": ["All I got time to do is go back in time and pose with the Unabomber", "Just so I can go back in time a second time to photobomb it"], "meaning": "Talk about time travelling.\nThe Unabomber, whose real name is Ted Kaczynski, was notorious for sending bombs to universities and airlines between 1978 and 1995, which resulted in three people dead and 23 people injured.\n\nThe idea of taking a selfie with a bomber recently hailed from the Egypt Air hijacking in which Ben Innes took a photo with the hijacker who wanted to go see his ex-wife and profess his love to her.\n\n\n\nCheck out the video clip of how the selfie was taken.\n\nAn interesting fact which also emerged after this selfie was taken was that Ben is a criminal too.\n\nRoyce states that he is fearless enough to go taking photos with criminals who might pose a threat to him too while being a bad guy himself.", "annotation_id": "8938529", "url": "https://genius.com/8938529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Sitting on that white horse, look at Prince Valiant", "vault_lines": ["Sitting on that white horse, look at Prince Valiant"], "meaning": "Push continues the theme of Greek mythology in his verse by using the image of a white horse, referring to Pegasus from his earlier mention of Clash of The Titans and stature on quoting.\n\n\n\nThis is likely a metaphor for his drug dealing skill, its colour white synonymous with cocaine. His signature subject matter, Push has also used birds to represent the craft. His self-depiction of a “valiant prince” relates to royalty, suggesting his superiority in the trade.\n\nPush may also be alluding to the logo for a Porsche luxury car, having shown appreciation for the brand before on “Numbers On The Boards”:\n\nCan’t a bitch living say I bought her Michael Kors\nEvery car driven was decided by the horse\n\n\n\nPrince Valiant is also the name of the longest running comic strip, started in 1937. Push may be using this reference to suggest his longevity in the game.", "annotation_id": "8935877", "url": "https://genius.com/8935877", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Tug of war and my mind’s like a clash of the titans Thoughts contrast, so it’s layers to my writin’", "vault_lines": ["Thoughts contrast, so it's layers to my writin'"], "meaning": "Clash of The Titans is a film adaptation of the myth of Perseus. The story follows Perseus (son of Zeus) in his battles against Medusa and the Kraken monster.\n\nPusha likens his internal struggle as the “drug dealer dichotomy” to good vs evil. He regularly refers to his state of mind as a double edged sword—on one hand he’s a notorious drug dealer, while on the other he’s a street preacher. Like his state of mind, his lyrics are littered with references to both worlds. He has previously described himself as a “conscious dopeboy.”\n\nHe used similar imagery on “Alone In Vegas”:\n\nThe tug of war opens the door, entrada\nRip me apart and see what’s inside of this piñata\n\nAnd more recently on the “Intro” of Darkest Before Dawn.", "annotation_id": "8935062", "url": "https://genius.com/8935062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Devil on my shoulder and the pitchfork follows Poking at my problems, I know how to solve ’em With a ski mask, automatic or revolver", "vault_lines": ["Devil on my shoulder and the pitchfork follows", "Poking at my problems, I know how to solve 'em", "With a ski mask, automatic or revolver"], "meaning": "The devil on his shoulder represents the two sides of each persons conscious, moral righteousness vs. evil tempation.\n\nPusha T solves his problems using a Ski Mask and automatic or revolver handgun.", "annotation_id": "8934416", "url": "https://genius.com/8934416", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "I philosophize for them Pitchfork scholars", "vault_lines": ["I philosophize for them Pitchfork scholars"], "meaning": "Pusha T spits his prophetic message in the form of bars, Pitchfork, is a online music magazine devoted to music journalism, news, and album reviews.\n\nPitchfork Album Reviews for Pusha T\n\nPitchfork reviewed Pusha T’s My Name is My Name a 8.0 and his latest Album Darkest Before Dawn a 8.2 saying\n\nPusha T’s sophomore studio album is an exercise in pure craft for everyone involved. The beats sound like money..", "annotation_id": "8934026", "url": "https://genius.com/8934026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "[Verse 2: Royce Da 5'9\"]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Royce' verses on this song were recycled verses from PRhyme’s BET Backroom Freestyle. Days after PRhyme released their debut album,  the group stopped by BET’s 106 & Park, to participate in their  freestyle segment “The Backroom”.\n\nSince audio and visual are prohibited for use outside of BET’s website, check out the freestyle here.", "annotation_id": "8933920", "url": "https://genius.com/8933920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "They say misery loves company, no, I don’t", "vault_lines": ["They say misery loves company, no, I don't"], "meaning": "Royce is implies that he doesn’t like the company of unhappy people. He also states that he is misery, obviously meaning he’s unhappy.\n\nThe idiom “misery loves company” is used to explain the feeling when someone who’s unhappy gets comfort from  knowing that others are unhappy too.\n\nRoyce used the same phrase in his song “Apologize”:\n\nShe hates when I drink\nMy miserable company don’t know her\nWon’t bring us closer", "annotation_id": "8933895", "url": "https://genius.com/8933895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Ain’t got no time for you to try on no Manolo Blahniks", "vault_lines": ["Ain't got no time for you to try on no Manolo Blahniks"], "meaning": "Manolo Blahnik is a high end shoe company self-titled by its founder Manolo Blahnik. Blahnik has worked wholeheartedly on shoes throughout his entire life. He not only personally designs the shoes, but also hand-crafts them.", "annotation_id": "8933863", "url": "https://genius.com/8933863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "I’m Doug E. Fresh in the flesh, I beat box I “boo-boo-du-du” between the sheets to seek the G-spot", "vault_lines": ["I'm Doug E. Fresh in the flesh, I beat box", "I \"boo-boo-du-du\" between the sheets to seek the G-spot"], "meaning": "Doug E. Fresh is rapper, record producer, and  exceptional  beatboxer. So exceptional, that he was nicknamed the Human Beat Box. He is able to manipulate his voice to accurately imitate drum machines and various special effects.\n\nIn Ice T’s documentary Something from Nothing: The Art of Rap, Doug E. Fresh explains how beatboxing has an influence in hip hop.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZaEmpL5C_nI", "annotation_id": "8933856", "url": "https://genius.com/8933856", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Birds in the trunk so these keys, now they homin’ Letters and numbers on the Coupe like it’s Roman", "vault_lines": ["Birds in the trunk so these keys, now they homin'"], "meaning": "Continuing the bird talk, Pusha T turns to his cocaine — also called birds or keys — and explains he’s got a large number of kilos in the trunk of his car.\n\nKing Push then plays on the number with the Roman numeric system, which consists of letters from the Latin alphabet. With this system, MMXVI, for example, would equal 2016.", "annotation_id": "8933180", "url": "https://genius.com/8933180", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Woo, all black like ‘The Omen’ Kim said it, yup, BIG wrote it", "vault_lines": ["Woo, all black like 'The Omen'", "Kim said it, yup, BIG wrote it"], "meaning": "On Puff Daddy’s “It’s All About The Benjamins (Remix)”, Lil Kim rapped:\n\nDressed in all black like The Omen\n\nPusha refers this line and also Biggie’s activity as a ghostwriter for her.“Queen Bitch”, for example, is written by the passed legend.\n\nAlso, Pusha loves the suit and tie attire, that is present in the horror movie The Omen.", "annotation_id": "8932844", "url": "https://genius.com/8932844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Drop jewels so these falcons like the Maltese", "vault_lines": ["Drop jewels so these falcons like the Maltese"], "meaning": "“Drop jewels” is a typical hip-hop term meaning to educate someone — which is exactly what Push does with his lyrics. The phrase owes its origins to the Five-Percent Nation, an organization that believes in the Twelve Jewels.\n\nFurther illustrating his lyrical wisdom, Pusha references The Maltese Falcon, a 1929 novel by Dashiell Hammett. The stories center around a falcon statue encrusted with several gems worth a lot a money – even off screen!", "annotation_id": "8932791", "url": "https://genius.com/8932791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Season ticket holder, nigga sitting with the team", "vault_lines": ["Season ticket holder, nigga sitting with the team"], "meaning": "Continuing the sports metaphor of the previous line, Ross is not only working for the “team” but is now a part of it. After all he’s now the boss of Maybach Music.\n\nThis could be also a reference to his love for the NFL-team Miami Dolphins; in 2015 he declared that wants to be a part owner of the team.\n\nOn “Hood Billionaire”, he rapped about it as well:\n\nI can get you that in my hood, I’m a billionaire in my hood\nTryna buy a piece of the Dolphins, 5% and I’m good", "annotation_id": "8932664", "url": "https://genius.com/8932664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "First in science, first in technology, wealthiest country on Earth, most powerful country on Earth is 26th in Education.", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The United States of America is the dominant leader in science and technology worldwide, according to a RAND Corporation study.\n\nThe United States accounts for 40 percent of the total world’s spending on scientific research and development, employs 70 percent of the world’s Nobel Prize winners and is home to three-quarters of the world’s top 40 universities.\n\nU.S.A also has the highest GDP per capita in the world with $53,041.18.\n\nDespite the leadership in science, technology, and wealth America is far from a leader in Education.  It ranks 26th in school performance in the world.", "annotation_id": "8932645", "url": "https://genius.com/8932645", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "I’m in bed with three major labels And I ain’t talkin’ ’bout wearing clothing brands", "vault_lines": ["I'm in bed with three major labels", "And I ain't talkin' 'bout wearing clothing brands"], "meaning": "All the rappers on this song come from three major record labels. Ross comes from his own label, Maybach Music Group; Pusha comes from GOOD Music, the same label that he is president of; and lastly, Royce—although releasing this album independently via his own label, Bad Half Entertainment—he is affiliated with Interscope Records under the  Slaughterhouse group and the Bad Meets Evil duo, respectively.", "annotation_id": "8932587", "url": "https://genius.com/8932587", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "line": "Labeled a mastermind, I positioned every move", "vault_lines": ["Labeled a mastermind, I positioned every move"], "meaning": "Rick Ross strategically thinks out each move like a game of Chess so he could become a Mastermind, the name of his sixth album.", "annotation_id": "8932546", "url": "https://genius.com/8932546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Layers", "status": "done", "targets": 29, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Royce-da-59-layers-lyrics", "genius_title": "Layers", "genius_id": 2419639, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Legend", "line": "I finally made it out the hood, now I ain’t got no neighbors", "vault_lines": ["I finally made it out the hood, now I ain't got no neighbors"], "meaning": "Joyner purchased a property with so much land he has no immediate neighbors in the traditional sense\n\nThis line may also be a call back to the line “I live in a skyscraper, I ain’t got no neighbors” from Dom Kennedy’s “She Ain’t In Love\"", "annotation_id": "23395061", "url": "https://genius.com/23395061", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Legend", "line": "Shot her in the foot, what pussy-boy, you rockin’ skirts (Gang)", "vault_lines": ["Shot her in the foot, what pussy-boy, you rockin' skirts (Gang)"], "meaning": "Probably alluding to the recent shooting of rapper Megan Thee Stallion in which rapper Tory Lanez was charged for shooting her in the foot after an argument the two had.\n\nTory had been the target of media, fans and artist since, with multiple artist publicly cutting ties with him.", "annotation_id": "21129028", "url": "https://genius.com/21129028", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Legend", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Joyner-lucas-legend-lyrics", "genius_title": "Legend", "genius_id": 6077985, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemme See", "line": "[Verse 1: Usher] Hey girl, I’m debating if I should take you home Should I take you home?", "vault_lines": ["Hey girl, I'm debating if I should take you home", "Should I take you home?"], "meaning": "In the start of this verse Usher is wondering if he should bring a girl to his house with him and asks her for her thought of the idea", "annotation_id": "35159053", "url": "https://genius.com/35159053", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemme See", "line": "She on my wanted poster", "vault_lines": ["She on my wanted poster"], "meaning": "Just like in the west, people with cases of crimes and needed by the state government were placed in posters with a certain amount for their capture a.k.a bounty.\nClearly this lady has rick Ross' interest and as such he has her in his wanted poster", "annotation_id": "4732028", "url": "https://genius.com/4732028", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemme See", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Usher-lemme-see-lyrics", "genius_title": "Lemme See", "genius_id": 73091, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "One truck in front of me, one behind me to follow", "vault_lines": ["One truck in front of me, one behind me to follow"], "meaning": "Drake rarely travels anywhere without security, especially by road. He tends to have multiple groups of bodyguards at his disposal in case anything bad occurs. He suggests that he’d normally have a truck both in front AND behind him to cover him from any possible attacks, acts of terrorism, etc.\n\nDrake’s typical security movement can be seen here", "annotation_id": "23398187", "url": "https://genius.com/23398187", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "G-Wagen for my bitch, now, girl, go live it up", "vault_lines": ["G-Wagen for my bitch, now, girl, go live it up"], "meaning": "The Mercedes-Benz G-Class, sometimes called G-Wagen (short for Geländewagen, “terrain vehicle”), is a mid-size four-wheel drive luxury SUV manufactured by Magna Steyr (formerly Steyr-Daimler-Puch) in Austria and sold by Mercedes-Benz. In certain markets, it has been sold under the Puch name as Puch G. The G-Class starts at around $132,000. Though most features are standard, a wide range of optional trim packages add everything from extra-cost paint (as much as $6,500), AMG styling bits, massaging seats, softer leather, and more can easily add $20,000 to that.\n\nMore info on the G-Wagen can be found here\n\n\n\nRoss suggests that he bought his girl a G-Wagen; a subtle flex to how wealthy he is.", "annotation_id": "23398169", "url": "https://genius.com/23398169", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Three-sixty up front, it all comes full circle", "vault_lines": ["Three-sixty up front, it all comes full circle"], "meaning": "Many artists who start out are baited into signing a predatory “360 deal,” an exclusive arrangement with a record label, where the label provides a range of platforms, outlets and services while taking a cut of everything the artist touches.\n\n\n\nBuilding off the “purple heart” line, Drake is battle-hardened in the music industry now—and “three-sixty up front” may be giving listeners insight into how he structures his fees for guest verses ($360k upfront, the other half on completion, so approx. $750k for a verse… fudging the numbers to make the poetics work).\n\nIn essence, his life has come “full circle” by avoiding the predatory deals at first, controlling what he creates and setting his own exorbitant prices for verses.", "annotation_id": "22563617", "url": "https://genius.com/22563617", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Courtroom soundin’ like I’m in an opera", "vault_lines": ["Courtroom soundin' like I'm in an opera"], "meaning": "To “sing” in a courtroom or trial means that one is providing a judge with incriminating information about another individual or group, or as some would put it, “snitching”. In this line Ross suggests that an individual in the courtroom that he is in is taking part in said act.", "annotation_id": "22393352", "url": "https://genius.com/22393352", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Everybody that survive got survivor’s guilt", "vault_lines": ["Everybody that survive got survivor's guilt"], "meaning": "Survivor’s guilt is a phenomenon where a person feels as if they have done something wrong by surviving a traumatic experience when others did not.\n\nDrake is thinking about his own career and various points where he could not have made it, perhaps he didn’t sell an album as well as he wanted or deliver the project that fans were expecting. With this, he’s solidified himself as one of the most successful entertainers of all time, and many have speculated that Drake’s “too big to fail,” which has affected the criticism surrounding his projects, and personal life. Drake’s calling himself a “survivor” because he’s managed to push past controversies and low points in his career surprisingly well, and seemingly feels guilty for it at the same time.", "annotation_id": "22393042", "url": "https://genius.com/22393042", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "“The number’s all good, just pay me, I’m at the Rhino”", "vault_lines": ["\"The number's all good, just pay me, I'm at the Rhino\""], "meaning": "The Rhino is in reference to Las Vegas, Nevada based gentleman’s club Spearmint Rhino. Spearmint Rhino is located on the Las Vegas strip and is less than a mile from the Wynn Las Vegas. Drake signed a residency deal with the Wynn in 2019.", "annotation_id": "22372157", "url": "https://genius.com/22372157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Matthew Maddox called in the pit boss, double checkin’", "vault_lines": ["Matthew Maddox called in the pit boss, double checkin'"], "meaning": "Matthew Maddox is the CEO of Wynn Resorts, which notably includes a large hotel and casino in Las Vegas.  When you’re winning a lot of money gambling, the owner will oftentimes call in the pit boss to look over your shoulder and make sure you’re not cheating in any way.  Drake uses the symbol of a pit boss watching his moves to emphasize the degree to which he’s winning.", "annotation_id": "22370106", "url": "https://genius.com/22370106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "I sent her the child support, she sent me the heart emoji", "vault_lines": ["I sent her the child support, she sent me the heart emoji"], "meaning": "On his May 2018 single, “I’m Upset,” Drake denounced paying child support and made a connection to his dad not paying child support when Drake himself was still a child:\n\nCan’t go fifty-fifty with no ho\nEvery month\nI’m supposed to pay her bills and get her what she want\nI still got like seven years of doin' what I want\nMy dad still got child support from 1991 (One, one, one)\n\nThese lines came at an interesting time as the song was released the day after Drake released his Pusha T diss track, “Duppy Freestyle.” Four days later, Pusha released his response, “The Story of Adidon,” where he exposed Drake for “hiding” Adonis, his son, from the public eye.\n\nNowadays, with Drake three years into fatherhood at the time of this song’s release, his perspective has child support has changed. This line shows that he and Adonis' mother, Sophie Brussaux, are in a good place and have a good co-parenting relationship with each other.", "annotation_id": "22366478", "url": "https://genius.com/22366478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Spinnin’ vinyl, Teddy P, or is it Lionel?", "vault_lines": ["Spinnin' vinyl, Teddy P, or is it Lionel?"], "meaning": "Teddy Pendergrass was a popular artist in the 80s and 90s, known for hits like July 1980’s “Love T.K.O.”. On the other hand, Lionel Richie is another 80s ballad powerhouse, known for hits like October 1983’s “Hello” and “All Night Long (All Night),” and is one of the best selling artists of all time.\n\nThe line is a callback to a line Ross said on Kanye West’s November 2010 song, “Devil in a New Dress”:\n\nSpinnin' Teddy Pendergrass vinyl as my J burns", "annotation_id": "22365612", "url": "https://genius.com/22365612", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Yeah, make a set sail in Croatia to get the leverage", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, make a set sail in Croatia to get the leverage"], "meaning": "Croatia is a country that’s located in the northwestern part of the Balkan Peninsula. It’s a popular destination for many celebrities during the summer due to its beautiful shores and islands.", "annotation_id": "22364394", "url": "https://genius.com/22364394", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Patty Mahomes, ’bout to fall short a couple hunnid", "vault_lines": ["Patty Mahomes, 'bout to fall short a couple hunnid"], "meaning": "Patrick Mahomes is the starting NFL quarterback for the Kansas City Chiefs. The young QB has proven to be one of the most talented players in his league. In the 2018 NFL season—his first season as a starter—Mahomes broke several passing records and won the NFL MVP award, the first Chief player to do so.\n\nDuring the 2019 season, Mahomes took the Chiefs to Super Bowl LIV, the team’s first appearance since 1970, and won against the San Francisco 49ers. Following the win, the Chiefs and Mahomes agreed to a ten-year contract extension worth $477 million with another $26 million in potential bonuses. At the time, this made Mahomes the first athlete with a half-billion-dollar contract and the first NFL player to be the highest-paid athlete in the sports world.\n\nDrake playfully notes here that his contract may be worth more than Mahomes', seeing that Drake is one of the most commercially successful artists in the world. However, he could also be making a nod to Mahomes' loss against the Tampa Bay Buccaneers in Super Bowl LV during the 2020 season, as he likely lost incentive money because of it. The event took place a few weeks prior to this song’s release.\n\nMahomes jokingly reacted to the name-drop via Twitter a few hours after the song’s release:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/PatrickMahomes/status/1367808727450062853", "annotation_id": "22364189", "url": "https://genius.com/22364189", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Livin’ in the 6ix, eight weeks, sun blazin’ After that, the killies just go into hibernation", "vault_lines": ["Livin' in the 6ix, eight weeks, sun blazin'", "After that, the killies just go into hibernation"], "meaning": "“The 6” is a nickname for Toronto, which comes from the 416 and 647 area codes in the city. Also, at one point, Toronto was broken up into six areas, Old Toronto, Scarborough, East York, North York, Etobicoke, and York, giving the nickname more significance.\n\nIn the summer, the crime rate tends to go up. This is due to the increase in temperatures, which makes people uncomfortable, causing them to be more aggressive and violent. Toronto is no different—during the summer of 2018, the city had 109 shootings alone.", "annotation_id": "22363626", "url": "https://genius.com/22363626", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Me and Chubbs drive by, shorty heart racin’", "vault_lines": ["Me and Chubbs drive by, shorty heart racin'"], "meaning": "Nessel “Chubbs” Beezer is one of Drake’s closest friends and his OVO head of security. Drake frequently name-drops him in his music—for example, on his June 2016 song, “4PM in Calabasas,” he raps:\n\nCameras pointing every time I look up\nThat’s why I gotta duck behind Chubb’s shoulder just to hit the kush up", "annotation_id": "22363578", "url": "https://genius.com/22363578", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Ross sittin’ on two hunnid thirty-five acres", "vault_lines": ["Ross sittin' on two hunnid thirty-five acres"], "meaning": "Drake gives a nod to Rick Ross' 235-acre mansion in Georgia. The house is listed as the largest residence in the state of Georgia and boasts a lavish interior, including a bowling alley and swimming pool. The mansion was showcased for a January 2020 edition of Complex Closets:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/JfQ22aiYddU", "annotation_id": "22363526", "url": "https://genius.com/22363526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Dockin’ jet skis in the Florida Keys", "vault_lines": ["Dockin' jet skis in the Florida Keys"], "meaning": "Florida Keys are a coral key island chain located in southern Florida. Drake partially recorded his June 2018 album Scorpion and songs such as May 2020’s “From Florida With Love” in Miami.\n\nIn the music video of Drizzy’s August 2020 song, “Laugh Now Cry Later,” he rides a jet ski at Nike World Headquarters in Beaverton, Oregon.", "annotation_id": "22363224", "url": "https://genius.com/22363224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Class photographs, Sandi had me on my Urkel", "vault_lines": ["Class photographs, Sandi had me on my Urkel"], "meaning": "Drake makes reference to his childhood class photographs in which he sported rather large glasses that he likens to the Steve Urkel character from the tv series Family Matters. The Urkel character was played by Jaleel White and was renown for his high-water pants, suspenders and forenamed large glasses. In 2014, Drake parodied the Urkel character on Saturday Night Live in this skit by incorporating his style and apparel with the imagery of Lil Wayne. Drake and White met in 2017 for the first time after Drake had parodied the Urkel character on Saturday Night Live. Sandi refers to Drakes mother, Sandra Graham.", "annotation_id": "22362367", "url": "https://genius.com/22362367", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Damn, rest in peace Dolla Bill", "vault_lines": ["Damn, rest in peace Dolla Bill"], "meaning": "On September 15, 2020, Drake posted a photo on his Instagram account captioned,\n\nKnown you for so many years and since day one you came around with a smile and positive words for me and your main priority was ALWAYS your family and the guys…you will be missed dearly brother RIP DOLLA BILL @repsupdolla\n\nDolla Bill worked for the graphic design company Dreamwork in Toronto, Canada and collaborated with Drake and the OVO Sound crew throughout the past decade. Chubbs and Baka Not Nice also paid tribute to Dolla Bill upon his passing.", "annotation_id": "22362268", "url": "https://genius.com/22362268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Yeah, heart just turned purple", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, heart just turned purple"], "meaning": "A Purple Heart is a military medal awarded to those wounded or killed while serving – in this context however, Drake means to say he is in his element. This line is also follow-up to his lines in his October 2016 song “Sneakin”, where he raps:\n\nFaceTime with my shawty on tour,\nAnd she textin' purple hearts ‘cause she know that we at war, yuh", "annotation_id": "22362258", "url": "https://genius.com/22362258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "And that’s facts, Hamdan Mohammed like my third cousin (Facts) Mansoor Mohammed like my real brother (Facts) Dubai embrace me like a Emirati (Facts)", "vault_lines": ["And that's facts, Hamdan Mohammed like my third cousin (Facts)", "Mansoor Mohammed like my real brother (Facts)", "Dubai embrace me like a Emirati (Facts)"], "meaning": "Sheikh Hamdan bin Mohammed Al Maktoum and Sheikh Mansoor bin Mohammed Al Maktoum are the Crown Princes of the Emirate of Dubai.\n\nHere, Drake expresses a special sense of kinship with Dubai and its leadership, comparing himself to an Emirati or native of the United Arab Emirates. During his first visit to Dubai in 2015, Drake connected with the royal family of Dubai. He went on to post the following photo with Sheikh Mansoor bin Mohammed  on his Instagram page, with the caption:\n\nFinally found my long lost brother", "annotation_id": "22362068", "url": "https://genius.com/22362068", "state": "accepted", "votes": 99, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Big Boi got me tryna buy the Braves", "vault_lines": ["Big Boi got me tryna buy the Braves"], "meaning": "Rick Ross speaks on his desire to buy a sports franchise and in particular the MLB’s Atlanta Braves. Ross purchased the former Atlanta home of boxer Evander Holyfield in 2014. Ross has previously spoken on his desire to purchase a sports franchise- in 2014 he discussed minority ownership of the Miami Dolphins with the Dolphins brass and in 2019 he spoke on his desire to own an NFL team with former NBA great Dwyane Wade.", "annotation_id": "22362011", "url": "https://genius.com/22362011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "We want everything galore, not just Lira Galore", "vault_lines": ["We want everything galore, not just Lira Galore"], "meaning": "Drake references model and influencer Lira Mercer a.k.a. Lira Galore. Galore previously dated rapper Rick Ross and the two were engaged in 2015. The engagement ended up only lasting for two months before the couple split. Galore appeared on the OWN talk show Iyanla, Fix My Life in 2016 to speak on the couple’s split. The full episode can be viewed here. Drake also has history with Galore and retired her jersey in July of 2017 at the Houston gentlemen’s club Dreams. Drake desires things in abundance, like the Galore surname.", "annotation_id": "22361886", "url": "https://genius.com/22361886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Godfather with a garden full of snakes", "vault_lines": ["Godfather with a garden full of snakes"], "meaning": "A reference to the Garden of Eden, where the Devil, incarnated as a snake, persuaded Eve to bite an apple from the tree that was forbidden by God.\n\n\n\nRozay uses this religious imagery to portray himself as the Godfather as in the criminal organisation (like the movies) surrounded by traitors. This is particularly relevant in The Godfather II when Fredo Corleone betrays the family.", "annotation_id": "22361515", "url": "https://genius.com/22361515", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "All my Rolls-Royces got a different body (Facts) Mansory, kitted out with every option (Facts)", "vault_lines": ["All my Rolls-Royces got a different body (Facts)", "Mansory, kitted out with every option (Facts)"], "meaning": "Rolls-Royce is a popular British brand of luxury cars. In November 2019, Drake bought a custom-made, one of a kind Rolls-Royce Phantom for a reported $700,000.\n\nThe custom changes include a Bushukan yellow finish with a signature two-tone paint scheme, courtesy of Mansory—a luxury car modification company. Aside from that, the Rolls-Royce’s signature Spirit of Ecstasy bonnet ornament was replaced with a gold owl, which has two large diamonds that make up the owl’s eyes, that has Drake’s full name—Aubrey Drake Graham—engraved in it.\n\nThe brain-child behind the design was none other than Drake’s friend and vehicle designer, Tony Bet, who unveiled the car on his Instagram.", "annotation_id": "22361452", "url": "https://genius.com/22361452", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Air Canada Centre nigga when I die Y’all gon’ have to fly in and do your fake cry First couple rows, you gon’ see the real guys", "vault_lines": ["Air Canada Centre nigga when I die", "Y'all gon' have to fly in and do your fake cry", "First couple rows, you gon' see the real guys"], "meaning": "Air Canada Centre is home to the Toronto Raptors. Drake’s history with the team is deep—he became their global ambassador in 2013, and has raked in a lot of revenue for them, so his idea of being commemorated by the Raptors after death is not unlikely.\n\nDrake explored themes of false admiration from his peers on October 2016’s “Fake Love,” and memorably denounced fake people mourning him on The Game’s June 2015 track, “100”:\n\nY'all better not come to my studio with that fake shit\nY'all better not come to my funeral with that fake shit\n\nHaving his funeral in a sports arena would follow late legends such as Michael Jackson, Nipsey Hussle, and Kobe Bryant, who each had their memorial services at Staples Center in downtown Los Angeles.\n\n\n\nDrake on sidelines during the 2019 NBA playoffs", "annotation_id": "22361272", "url": "https://genius.com/22361272", "state": "accepted", "votes": 94, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Of course Pull up to the front in a fleet of Suburbans Flooded French immersion with the Secret Service Shit is so obvious, it defeats the purpose", "vault_lines": ["Pull up to the front in a fleet of Suburbans", "Flooded French immersion with the Secret Service", "Shit is so obvious, it defeats the purpose"], "meaning": "French immersion is a form of bilingual education where kids who don’t speak French as a first language will receive their learning in French through completion of the standard curriculum classes in French. Drake’s son, Adonis Graham, attends Toronto French School, a private French immersion school.  He’s half-French since his mother, Sophie Brussaux, is from France, which makes this an ideal school for him.\n\nThe United States Secret Service is a federal law enforcement agency under Homeland Security, elected to protect U.S. politicians and their families. They transport U.S. presidents in motorcades, using Surburban vehicles, to ensure their safety. Drake travels Adonis to school in a similar fashion, while also joking that the large motorcade defeats the purpose of having a “secret” service—meaning his security—since it won’t be much of a secret anymore.\n\n\n\n\nA Presidential Motorcade", "annotation_id": "22361244", "url": "https://genius.com/22361244", "state": "accepted", "votes": 97, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "We all grateful for Weezy, but no one more than me", "vault_lines": ["We all grateful for Weezy, but no one more than me"], "meaning": "Weezy, or Lil Wayne, is an American rapper hailing from New Orleans. His indisputable impact on music credits his reputation of often being cited as one of the greatest rappers of all time. He has been consistently mentioned numerous times as a core influencer for many artists, such as Kendrick Lamar, Lil Uzi Vert, and of course Drake.\n\nKnown for founding Young Money Entertainment, Lil Wayne signed Drake to his label in 2009. Under the label, eight of Drake’s albums landed a number one spot on the Billboard 200 chart.\n\n\n\nDrake previously addressed his connection with Weezy on his 2015 track “6PM in New York”:\n\nLil Wayne could not have found him a better successor", "annotation_id": "22361185", "url": "https://genius.com/22361185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 99, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Real life, the whole fam’ goons like Ralo", "vault_lines": ["Real life, the whole fam' goons like Ralo"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out the Atlanta rapper Ralo, whose social media handle is @ralofamgoon. On Ralo’s January 2017’s Young Thug, Lil Uzi Vert and Lil Yachty assisted “Young Nigga,” Yachty raps:\n\nRalo fam goon, don’t nobody go harder\n\n\n\nRalo’s fam goon merch hoody", "annotation_id": "22361043", "url": "https://genius.com/22361043", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Yeah, dropped him off at school, big day for my lil’ man Recess hits, daddy prolly made another M School bell rings and I’m out there to get him again", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, dropped him off at school, big day for my lil' man", "Recess hits, daddy prolly made another M", "School bell rings and I'm out there to get him again"], "meaning": "On September 9, 2020, Adonis Graham, Drake’s son, started attending school. Drake and Adonis' mother, Sophie Brussaux both shared pictures on Instagram to commemorate their child’s first day of school.\n\n\n\nSince Drake is a superstar, he might get asked quite frequently whether he knows certain artists or not, using Beyoncé and Nicki Minaj as examples.", "annotation_id": "22361033", "url": "https://genius.com/22361033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 121, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "How I’m so famous, gotta live where they hide the hills?", "vault_lines": ["How I'm so famous, gotta live where they hide the hills?"], "meaning": "Drake is alluding to the exclusive, gated California neighborhood Hidden Hills. Business Insider reported on his 2012 purchase of a 7.7 million dollar house in Hidden Hills. Like other celebrities who live there, such as Miley Cyrus, Kylie Jenner, and The Weeknd, Drake now values the perks that come with esoteric living.\n\nDrake references the same property in his 2016 song Summer Sixteen:\n\nNow I got a house in LA, now I got a bigger pool than Ye.\nAnd look man, Ye’s pool is nice, mine’s just bigger’s what I’m saying", "annotation_id": "22360779", "url": "https://genius.com/22360779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Foot Locker, twenty deep, a nigga spend a dub", "vault_lines": ["Foot Locker, twenty deep, a nigga spend a dub"], "meaning": "Foot Locker is a popular American retail store that sells shoes and sports clothing. A “dub” is usually slang for $20 worth of weed but in Ross' case, he means a lot of money.\n\n\n\n\nA Foot Locker store", "annotation_id": "22360756", "url": "https://genius.com/22360756", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Tryin’, tryin’, tryin’, tryin’", "vault_lines": ["Tryin', tryin', tryin', tryin'"], "meaning": "The intro, break, and outro of “Lemon Pepper Freestyle” sample the live version of Danish duo Quadron’s March 2010 track, “Pressure”:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ILPNhmg3geM&t=101s", "annotation_id": "22360680", "url": "https://genius.com/22360680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 241, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Ushered a generation in, these are where my confessions live", "vault_lines": ["Ushered a generation in, these are where my confessions live"], "meaning": "Drizzy and his OVO Sound label have inspired a new generation of musicians in both hip-hop and R&B over the last decade. Artists such as The Weeknd, PARTYNEXTDOOR, and Popcaan all started at OVO.\n\nDrake uses clever wordplay to compare the success and influence of his music to that of Usher’s 2004 fourth studio album Confessions, which is one of the most influential and critically acclaimed R&B albums of our time, and quite literally “ushered” in a new generation of musicians, including Drake himself.", "annotation_id": "22360662", "url": "https://genius.com/22360662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 83, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Practicin’ social distance with all these snitch niggas", "vault_lines": ["Practicin' social distance with all these snitch niggas"], "meaning": "Social distancing is a health practice that involves standing six feet, or about two arms length, away from another person.\n\nThis strategy became widely used during the COVID-19 pandemic as one way to mitigate the spread of the deadly virus from person to person.\n\nRick Ross reapplies this to his life, staying away from  “snitches,” which are people who tattletale.", "annotation_id": "22360598", "url": "https://genius.com/22360598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "For real, and my city love me like DeMar DeRozan", "vault_lines": ["For real, and my city love me like DeMar DeRozan"], "meaning": "DeMar DeRozan is a professional basketball player in the NBA. He currently plays for the San Antonio Spurs, but spent the first nine years of his career on the Toronto Raptors, the team of Drake’s hometown.\n\n\n\nDeRozan was a beloved player by the Raptors fanbase, co-leading the team with fellow star Kyle Lowry for most of the 2010s. The duo lead the Raptors five playoff runs and multiple Eastern Conference Regular Season titles, but consistently ran into problems in the NBA Playoffs, getting knocked out by LeBron James‘ Cleveland Cavaliers in DeRozan’s last three years with the team. On July 18, 2018, following the team’s third straight playoff exit at the hands of James, DeRozan was traded out of San Antonio.\n\nIn the weeks after the trade, the city of Toronto and DeRozan expressed their mutual love for each other in many forms. DeRozan took to Instagram just days after the trade to express what his time in the city meant to him:\n\nWords could never express what you’ve meant to me. I was just a 19 year old kid from Compton when we first met, but you took me in and embraced me as one of your own. I am so grateful for the Love and Passion that you’ve given me over the past 9 years. All I ever wanted to do was duplicate it 10x over just to show my appreciation. Thank you Toronto, thank you Canada. #Comp10 #ProveEm.\n\nDrake himself even took to social media to express his admiration for DeRozan after the trade:\n\nTo my brother @demar_derozan I want to say 10 million thank you’s on behalf of YOUR city. You are a fixture in Toronto forever and you gave everything you had[…] Through your leadership we had the most exciting years in franchise history. I am grateful to have witnessed your combination of skill, persistence, and loyalty from the same seats every night. Thank you for being an incredible captain and an even better friend\n\nDeRozan’s trade to San Antonio gave the Raptors future hall of famer Kawhi Leonard, which culminated in the first-ever championship for the franchise. DeRozan commented on the finals victory and his trade, saying\n\nI was happy. Good for them. Happy for them. I spent a lot of time with a few of them guys this offseason. It was good for them. I spent nine years of my basketball career there. Even at times when I see pictures seeing my jersey in the crowd, you are there some way somehow. You got to be happy with that.", "annotation_id": "22360449", "url": "https://genius.com/22360449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "(M-M-M-Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": ["Biggest, you feel me? (M-M-M-Maybach Music)"], "meaning": "This is the tag for Rick Ross’s record label Maybach Music Group. It is often prominently featured in the mix of songs by or featuring Ross, and also appears on songs by artists who are signed to the label.\n\nThe woman heard saying the tag is Jessica Gomes, an Australian model. She told the story behind the tag’s origin in a 2012 feature with DJcityTV:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4vOExWDh9KQ", "annotation_id": "22360427", "url": "https://genius.com/22360427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lemon Pepper Freestyle", "line": "Death Row, that’s for these niggas, I’ma hit ’em up Makaveli, it’s all eyes on me Pinkie rings, it’s still M.O.B.", "vault_lines": ["Death Row, that's for these niggas, I'ma hit 'em up", "Makaveli, it's all eyes on me", "Pinkie rings, it's still M.O.B."], "meaning": "Rick Ross pays homage to Death Row Records signee, 2Pac, referencing some of his most influential work in the past: from Shakur’s June 1996 diss track, “Hit ’Em Up,” to his February 1996 album, All Eyez On Me, and his November 1996 posthumous album, The Don Killuminati: The 7 Day Theory, which was released under his stage name, Makaveli and is commonly shortened to Makaveli. Both projects peaked at #1 on the Billboard 200 chart.\n\n\n\nRoss continues the Tupac references with “M.O.B.”, which Pac tattooed on the back of his right arm. Standing for “Money Over Bitches,” “M.O.B.” is also one of 2Pac’s most frequent phrases used in his music, for example, on “Blasphemy,” the fifth track off of Makaveli, he spits the following lines:\n\nNow, rule one: get your cash on, M.O.B.\nThat’s Money Over Bitches, ‘cause they breed envy\n\nMoreover, “pinkie rings” are often associated with organized crime and affiliation, which could be an allusion to 2Pac’s gangsta rap style and his gang-member-involved drive-by murder.", "annotation_id": "22360372", "url": "https://genius.com/22360372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 120, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
