{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let Me Tell Ya", "line": "Better have my ready, Fab Five Freddy", "vault_lines": ["Better have my ready, Fab Five Freddy"], "meaning": "Fab Five Freddy is a legendary NYC Hip Hop figure from the late 80s known for his involvement in the fashion, graffitti and videography advancements in Hip Hop. He’s referenced in the first ever Hip Hop song to be played on MTV Blondie’s “Rapture” in 1980. He went on to host YO! MTV Raps.", "annotation_id": "27534384", "url": "https://genius.com/27534384", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
