{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let Me Tell Ya", "line": "V.V.S. rims", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It’s BBS rims, for BBS Kraftfahrzeugtechnik AG, a high-performance automobile wheel design company headquartered in Schiltach, Germany.", "annotation_id": "27025194", "url": "https://genius.com/27025194", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let Me Tell Ya", "line": "Heltah Skeltah means war, I’m on my rock ruckus", "vault_lines": ["Heltah Skeltah means war, I'm on my rock ruckus"], "meaning": "Heltah Skeltah was a Hip-Hop duo consisting of rappers Rock and the late Sean Price, who performed under the name Ruckus.\n\nThey debuted on Smif-N-Wessun’s album Dah Shinin' in 1995, appearing on the tracks “Wontime,” “Cession at da Doghillee,” and “Let’s Git It On.”\n\nAlso, they were members of the supergroup Boot Camp Click which consisted of Buckshot from Black Moon, both Steele and Tek from Smif-N-Wessun and Starang Wondah, Louieville Sluggah and Top Dog from the Originoo Gunn Clappaz.\n\nThey took their name after “Helter Skelter,” a 1968 song by The Beatles, off their self-titled ninth studio album, also known as “White Album.”\n\nCult leader Charles Manson believed that several White Album songs were a part of a coded prophecy, which he named “Helter Skelter,” an apocalyptic racial war between black and white people.\n\nHeltah Skeltah released their debut album Nocturnal in 1996, which contained the song “Undastand”:\n\nUndastand Heltah Skeltah only mean war\nUndastand the war’s with everything outside your door\nUndastand he be R-O, I be R-U\nUndastand it can happen to you", "annotation_id": "16583949", "url": "https://genius.com/16583949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let Me Tell Ya", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Smif-n-wessun-let-me-tell-ya-lyrics", "genius_title": "Let Me Tell Ya", "genius_id": 4309101, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let’s Get It", "line": "I’m cookin’ up blow, I’m cookin’ up blow, I’m cookin’ up blow", "vault_lines": ["I'm cookin' up blow, I'm cookin' up blow, I'm cookin' up blow"], "meaning": "With this line, Ca$h Out states that he is manufacturing crack cocaine by mixing high grade blow, with a solution of boiling water and a cutting ingredient such as baking soda, minerals, which causes the cocaine to solidify, thereby degrading its quality and allowing for an increase in profit margins.", "annotation_id": "4574753", "url": "https://genius.com/4574753", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let’s Get It", "line": "Keep red bottoms on the bottom my shoe, they like how we kick it", "vault_lines": ["Keep red bottoms on the bottom my shoe, they like how we kick it"], "meaning": "Christian Louboutin is an expensive French brand, which is known for their shiny, red-lacquered soles.", "annotation_id": "4210489", "url": "https://genius.com/4210489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let’s Get It", "line": "China Connect, Bruce Leroy (Bruce Leroy)", "vault_lines": ["China Connect, Bruce Leroy (Bruce Leroy)"], "meaning": "His diamonds glow like Bruce Leroy from The Last Dragon.\n\n\n\n\n\nBasically the same thing.", "annotation_id": "3870906", "url": "https://genius.com/3870906", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
