{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let’s Talk", "line": "Cîroc got me loose but your dress fit tight", "vault_lines": ["Cîroc got me loose but your dress fit tight"], "meaning": "O does some “loose”/“tight” wordplay here while promoting Diddy’s favorite vodka.  The use of opposites (wrong/right, cold/fire, smartest/fool) continues throughout this verse", "annotation_id": "859106", "url": "https://genius.com/859106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let’s Talk", "line": "Rev Run bubble bath", "vault_lines": ["Now double that, Rev Run bubble bath"], "meaning": "Joseph Simmons aka Rev Run was notorious for starting and ending episodes of his series “Run’s House” in a bubble bath going over his agenda for the day.", "annotation_id": "809713", "url": "https://genius.com/809713", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Let’s Talk", "line": "All the chicks came like we at a Knicks game Carmelo numbers first and the fifteenth", "vault_lines": ["All the chicks came like we at a Knicks game", "Carmelo numbers first and the fifteenth"], "meaning": "Rozay knows how to throw a party. His crib is so packed its starting to resemble MSG(where the Knicks play). It also refers to MMG having the popularity and appeal similar to professional basketball players. He also claims to make Carmelo Anthony-type money (about $20 million) every two weeks, during the meme dope sale days", "annotation_id": "809673", "url": "https://genius.com/809673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
