{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "Consider me a Caterpillar crane, gift-wrapped", "vault_lines": ["Consider me a Caterpillar crane, gift-wrapped"], "meaning": "Continuation from the previous line: Because they put the city on your back, and you weren’t strong enough to support it (i.e. your back cracked), people are giving Rockie the torch now and passing him a caterpillar crane to help take the load off of you fuck niggas that can’t represent.", "annotation_id": "2570919", "url": "https://genius.com/2570919", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "Shout-out my Crenshaw niggas", "vault_lines": ["Shout-out my Crenshaw niggas"], "meaning": "Crenshaw is a city in Los Angeles. Ice Cube and Nipsey Hussle are from there. Many rappers have referenced the area or the street, Crenshaw Boulevard. Among them are 2Pac, Nas, Dr. Dre and Game.", "annotation_id": "1435150", "url": "https://genius.com/1435150", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "Lookin’ like a Westside Crip, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Lookin’ like a Westside Crip, nigga"], "meaning": "Very reminiscent of another westside crip.", "annotation_id": "1432287", "url": "https://genius.com/1432287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "I plan to live my life a rich nigga That’s known to always keep a clip with him Talkin’ on the Bluetooth in the 6, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I plan to live my life a rich nigga", "That’s known to always keep a clip with him", "Talkin’ on the Bluetooth in the 6, nigga"], "meaning": "He never wants to be broke again. He stays high all the time (financially and off of marijuana), so he keeps a clip with him at all times. A clip holds a joint from where you smoke so you’ll be able to smoke it till the roach without getting your lips or fingers burnt (clever, huh?).\n\n\n\nAnd he doesn’t use his cellphone while driving his BMW 6 series.\n\n\n\nBut he can’t miss them calls, so he uses bluetooth earphones while driving.", "annotation_id": "1411948", "url": "https://genius.com/1411948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "I pray I never die a broke nigga Terrell Owens, owing all the dope dealers", "vault_lines": ["Terrell Owens, owing all the dope dealers"], "meaning": "Terrell Owens was a star wide receiver in the NFL from 1996-2010. In early 2012 it was revealed that T.O. was broke due to bad investments and child support.", "annotation_id": "1411346", "url": "https://genius.com/1411346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "Them Satchel Paige diamonds, yeah, them bitches pitch black", "vault_lines": ["Them Satchel Paige diamonds, yeah, them bitches pitch black"], "meaning": "Satchel Paige is a Hall of Fame pitcher that was great in the Negro Leagues  and MLB for many years. Like Satchel Paige’s skin, Rockie’s diamonds are black. Similarly, they look like the “diamond” field that baseball is played on.", "annotation_id": "1411198", "url": "https://genius.com/1411198", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "Collect calls from Gunplay I pray one day I get to see some peace But I’mma ride until the wheels won’t Anything Double-M I will kill for", "vault_lines": ["Collect calls from Gunplay", "I pray one day I get to see some peace", "But I’mma ride until the wheels won’t", "Anything Double-M I will kill for"], "meaning": "Gunplay recently got in some trouble with the law; he was thrown in jail before being released on $150,000 bond. He kept contact with his label boss through phone calls. Although he was bailed out, he’s still on house arrest. .\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cHLHKtPB94Y\n\nRick Ross is praying all of this will be over soon so they can fully concentrate on making good music and enjoying the positives of their lives, but one thing he won’t do is leave his friend until he’s free because it’s his team MMG and he rides with them to death. .", "annotation_id": "1410741", "url": "https://genius.com/1410741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "Money way taller than the average height", "vault_lines": ["Money way taller than the average height"], "meaning": "Metaphor – he’s way richer than average person\n\n\n\nJust look at him. I can hear him quote 2 Chainz’s lyrics,\n\nSo much money on me that it won’t fit in my wallets\nAnd these are Rock & Republics so it won’t fit in my pockets", "annotation_id": "1410709", "url": "https://genius.com/1410709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "Survivin’ even though I’m sick, Magic Johnson money shit", "vault_lines": ["Survivin’ even though I’m sick, Magic Johnson money shit"], "meaning": "Magic Johnson has lived with HIV since 1991; he’s worth over $500 million, so he can easily afford the medication.\n\n\n\nBut, Rockie Fresh, ask Steve Jobs if billions can save you…", "annotation_id": "1410023", "url": "https://genius.com/1410023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "line": "So self-made", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Two compilations and countless mentions in various songs…if you still haven’t got it, Rick Ross is self made! Nothing inherited in his case, just hard work. .", "annotation_id": "1409977", "url": "https://genius.com/1409977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Life Long", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rockie-fresh-life-long-lyrics", "genius_title": "Life Long", "genius_id": 109374, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lifestyles of the Rich & Hated", "line": "Some want the new me, some want this, some want the old me But I thought I told you all you can’t control me (M-M)", "vault_lines": ["Some want the new me, some want this, some want the old me", "But I thought I told you all you can't control me (M-M)"], "meaning": "His old music is not coming back and fans should deal with it, He is going forward.", "annotation_id": "25286883", "url": "https://genius.com/25286883", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lifestyles of the Rich & Hated", "line": "Y’all keep lookin’ for shortcuts, lookin’ for cheat codes, lookin’ for hacks", "vault_lines": ["Y'all keep lookin' for shortcuts, lookin' for cheat codes, lookin' for hacks"], "meaning": "Avid gamers will recall the novelty of cheat codes coded into popular franchises—notably GTA—where a specific input is required to activate these, leading to character boosts or changes to the game.\n\n\n\nG-Eazy alludes to people seeking real-life equivalents instead of working hard as he did, which he elaborated on in the song “Eazy,” released in December 2017:\n\nI literally sold all my shit\nI moved out of my place in New Orleans\nI was bouncing around, living out of a suitcase\nCrashing on friends' couches\nLiving at AirBnb’s and hotels\nTrying to make the album\nTrying to make When It’s Dark Out\nIf I could take it there, that’d be great", "annotation_id": "21714380", "url": "https://genius.com/21714380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
