{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Light Years", "line": "I’m pro-Black, my cloth top look like Kente though", "vault_lines": ["I'm pro-Black, my cloth top look like Kente though"], "meaning": "Kente cloth is a Ghanaian textile, made of handwoven cloth, strips of silk and cotton.\n\nIt’s very vibrant, loud and colorful so Folarin is saying that his clothes are as loud and vibrant as kente cloth, which you can see the imagery he’s painting.", "annotation_id": "30105604", "url": "https://genius.com/30105604", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
