{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lights Get Low", "line": "Right about now, you’re about to be possessed by the sounds of Cool N Dre and Freeway", "vault_lines": ["Right about now, you're about to be possessed by the sounds of Cool N Dre and Freeway"], "meaning": "This song borrows the intro from Rob Base and DJ EZ Rock’s song “It Takes Two” using a similar altered deep voice, with Freezy beginning the song with “Hit it!”", "annotation_id": "23428373", "url": "https://genius.com/23428373", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lights Get Low", "line": "I took four years off I went to Mecca paid respect", "vault_lines": ["I took four years off", "I went to Mecca paid respect"], "meaning": "In response to his crisis of faith, Freeway went on hiatus for a few years, making his Hajj, a journey to the holy city of Mecca, required by every Muslim at least once in his or her lifetime if they are able.", "annotation_id": "20152593", "url": "https://genius.com/20152593", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lights Get Low", "line": "The feds tappin out and they fucking with figure fours I dont wanna wrestle I wet em and then they froze", "vault_lines": ["The feds tappin out and they fucking with figure fours", "I dont wanna wrestle I wet em and then they froze"], "meaning": "The “figure four leg-lock” is a submission move made famous by the professional wrestler Ric “The Nature Boy” Flair.  It involves the wrestler twisting his legs with the opponents legs in such a way that ends up resembling the number 4.  If done correctly the opponent will give up (i.e. “tap out”) due to extreme pressure on their knee and shin.\n\n(I’m assuming Rick Ross has some kind double meaning of “figure fours”, but I don’t know, suggestions welcome).\n\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VKrNGKO47ss", "annotation_id": "4883623", "url": "https://genius.com/4883623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lights Get Low", "line": "Put homes together like I’m the Great Lakes", "vault_lines": ["Put homes together like I'm the Great Lakes"], "meaning": "DOUBLE ENTENDERE ALERT\n\nThe Great Lakes are Lake Huron, Lake Ontario, Lake Michigan, Lake Erie and Lake Superior-as a mnemonic device, schoolchildren learn to remember the names of the lakes by the acronym “HOMES”.\n\nJust as “HOMES” together form the Great Lakes, Freeway makes sure his homies stay united.", "annotation_id": "3303581", "url": "https://genius.com/3303581", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
