{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lipstick", "line": "Closet full of labels like Carrie on Sex in the city, but just me, though", "vault_lines": ["Closet full of labels like Carrie on", "Sex in the city, but just me, though"], "meaning": "Brian alludes to the American rom-com TV series Sex and the City and one of the series' main characters, Carrie Bradshaw—portrayed by Sarah Jessica Parker. In the series, Bradshaw is a devoted fashionista and is known for her extensive closet, which boasts many high-end fashion brands.\n\n\n\nBradshaw’s closet in her New York City apartment.", "annotation_id": "21310491", "url": "https://genius.com/21310491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lipstick", "line": "She bad, shawty bad like the Michael Jackson song", "vault_lines": ["She bad, shawty bad like the Michael Jackson song"], "meaning": "Brandon and Brian open their respective verses by comparing the object of their affection to two of pop legend Michael Jackson’s songs: September 1987’s “Bad” and the Paul McCartney-assisted, October 1982’s “The Girl Is Mine.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dsUXAEzaC3Q", "annotation_id": "21310470", "url": "https://genius.com/21310470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
