{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Little Havana", "line": "Did you cry for the man or did you cry for the fame?", "vault_lines": ["Did you cry for the man or did you cry for the fame?"], "meaning": "When Kobe died, many people online paid respects just to get online attention. TheDream is calling out those people exploiting a tradgety for online clout which means nothing.", "annotation_id": "26167699", "url": "https://genius.com/26167699", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Little Havana", "line": "I released Omarion, he began to fizz", "vault_lines": ["I released Omarion, he began to fizz"], "meaning": "R&B singer Omarion was signed to Ross' music label Maybach Music Group from 2012 to 2017. Things apparently didn’t end well between Omarion and MMG/Ross, and according to a 2019 interview with VladTV, Omarion stated that “they [MMG] never helped promote his music”:\nhttps://youtu.be/WXL6FSKbbdE\n\nFurthermore, “He began to fizz” can be also be a reference to Omarion’s former B2K bandmate Lil Fizz.", "annotation_id": "24559739", "url": "https://genius.com/24559739", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Little Havana", "line": "My name is Willie Falcon I was the undisputed king in the cocaine industry From the mid ’70s through the ’80s and into the ’90s If you snort cocaine back in those days There was 85% chance it was my cocaine I helped build Miami skyline into what it is today Twenty billion dollars got me twenty-seven years in federal prison I always live by the code of honor That’s why my best days are ahead of me I am richer than I’ve ever been I would like to send my love to my friend Rick Ross Rick, I’m immensely appreciated in giving me love And keeping my name in your music for the past two decades It rocks me that I had your support for so many years", "vault_lines": ["My name is Willie Falcon", "I am richer than I've ever been", "I would like to send my love to my friend Rick Ross", "Rick, I'm immensely appreciated in giving me love", "And keeping my name in your music for the past two decades", "It rocks me that I had your support for so many years"], "meaning": "https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSUDmAeJEU-lCIiEO8AWPnpbj91z5Oq0SJiyADBArVUuqDW3FCWgb8BxxbePQe1SHbfKYg&usqp=CAU\n\nWillie Falcon is a former drug kingpin who, along with his partner Sal Magluta, operated one of the most significant cocaine trafficking organizations in South Florida history.\n\nAlong with his partner, Falcon was indicted by a federal grand jury in April 1991 for a plethora of drug trafficking crimes, including operating a continuing criminal enterprise accused of importing and distributing over 75 tons of cocaine but both were found not guilty after a lengthy trial.\n\n\n\nFollowing the 1996 trial, the United States Attorney’s Office directed an investigation into Falcon’s and his partners finances that ultimately revealed that members of their jury – including the jury foreman – had been bribed. Falcon, his partner, several of the jurors, their associates and even some of their lawyers were ultimately charged with various criminal offenses arising from the conduct.\n\n\n\nIn 2003 he pled guilty to a single count of money laundering in a plea deal with the government for a reduced 20 year sentence. After his 2017 release he was transferred to ICE custody. He was deported to the Dominican Republic.", "annotation_id": "24555920", "url": "https://genius.com/24555920", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Little Havana", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-little-havana-lyrics", "genius_title": "Little Havana", "genius_id": 7452613, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Litty", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Bruno-mali-kidd-litty-lyrics", "genius_title": "Litty", "genius_id": 3167176, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Peter Piper pickin’ peppers, Rick pitch poems", "vault_lines": ["Peter Piper pickin' peppers, Rick pitch poems"], "meaning": "Peter Piper pickin' peppers\n\nThis is a reference to a famous nursery rhyme (Peter Piper picked a peck of pickled peppers). It’s often used to show someone who is skilled at saying tricky words quickly.\n\nRick pitch poems\n\nHere Rick Ross compares himself to Peter Piper, but with a twist:\n\nPeter Piper → picks peppers\n\nRick Ross → pitches poems\n\n“Pitch poems” means delivering or throwing out powerful rap lyrics.\n\nHe’s basically saying:\n\nJust like Peter Piper was good at picking peppers, Rick Ross is good at delivering rhymes.", "annotation_id": "38973505", "url": "https://genius.com/38973505", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Three bad bitches, don’t come concurrent", "vault_lines": ["Three bad bitches, don't come concurrent"], "meaning": "Geometry line, concurrent lines are 3+ lines that intersect with each other at one point, the point of concurrency. With Rick Ross being the point of concurrency and the 3 girls being the lines", "annotation_id": "38707700", "url": "https://genius.com/38707700", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Well we gon’ be livin’ like this for the rest of tonight", "vault_lines": ["Well we gon' be livin' like this for the rest of tonight"], "meaning": "This could be a hint to the title, “Live Fast, Die Young”. As the line implies, they (Rick Ross and Kanye most likely) won’t be “living like this” for long, making it so that they’re “living like this” fast, thus “Liv[ing]e Fast”. (Though many other lines in the song would already hint to this)", "annotation_id": "35348875", "url": "https://genius.com/35348875", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "And I wanna show you how you all look like beautiful stars tonight", "vault_lines": ["And I wanna show you how you all look like beautiful stars tonight"], "meaning": "This was sampled from the Rick James 1981 live performance of “Mary Jane” in Long Beach, California:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/XDMEVBFvAus?t=370\n\nThe “beautiful stars” line comes in at 6:10 and the “sounding good” line comes in at 9:14.", "annotation_id": "33705608", "url": "https://genius.com/33705608", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "[Chorus: Kanye West, Tony Williams & Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The hook of this song was also used on the unreleased Kanye version of this song ‘Hard Horn Nightmare,’ meant for his scrapped 2009 album Good Ass Job.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z5tmmNcqZeM", "annotation_id": "29746141", "url": "https://genius.com/29746141", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "And if I see Biggie tonight, I loved every minute", "vault_lines": ["And if I see Biggie tonight, I loved every minute"], "meaning": "Kanye is referencing Biggie Smalls (A.K.A. The Notorious B.I.G.), who died on March 9, 1997. Kanye is saying that if he died and went to Heaven tonight, he would have appreciated every moment of his life.", "annotation_id": "28780492", "url": "https://genius.com/28780492", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "And I know they tryna get they cool back", "vault_lines": ["And I know they tryna get they cool back"], "meaning": "=the people in question want they cool back. cool can mean alot, but in this context i think cool is a methapor for fame", "annotation_id": "28546579", "url": "https://genius.com/28546579", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Hoppin’ out the van, screams from the fans “Yeezy, always knew you’d be on top again!”", "vault_lines": ["Hoppin' out the van, screams from the fans", "\"Yeezy, always knew you'd be on top again!\""], "meaning": "that werent wrong", "annotation_id": "28541600", "url": "https://genius.com/28541600", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "They say we can’t be livin’ like this for the rest of our lives", "vault_lines": ["They say we can't be livin' like this for the rest of our lives"], "meaning": "people tell kanye that he cant live his lifestyle since its self desrtuctive", "annotation_id": "28541596", "url": "https://genius.com/28541596", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "I’m back by unpopular demand ‘Least we still poppin’ in Japan, shoppin’ in Milan", "vault_lines": ["I'm back by unpopular demand", "'Least we still poppin' in Japan, shoppin' in Milan"], "meaning": "At the time of this release (Teflon Don dropped in July 2010), Kanye’s public perception was at an all time low because of his stage-crashing at the September 2009 VMAs.\n\nAs he revealed in a 2010 interview with Ellen, after the massive backlash, he fled the US and hid out temporarily in Japan for two months, then moving to Italy in November 2009, where he interned at Fendi with Virgil Abloh, indulging his interest in fashion while contemplating whether to quit music or not.\n\nBut then by early 2010, he was back in the US, where he moved to Hawaii and began assembling a super team of hip hop producers and rappers to make music. Those now-legendary Hawaii recording sessions were for My Beautiful Dark Twisted Fantasy, and this track was originally slated for that project before Kanye decided to give it to Ross for Teflon Don.\n\nSo ‘Poppin in Japan’ might refer to his period living in Japan away from paparazzi, while ‘shoppin in Milan’ might just refer to him being in Italy afterwards, even if he was actually interning in Rome. This is backed up by paparazzi photos catching him and then-GF Amber Rose shopping in Rome in November 2009 during that exile period.", "annotation_id": "20932866", "url": "https://genius.com/20932866", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "You can go ’head and sneeze cause my presence blessed you", "vault_lines": ["You can go 'head and sneeze cause my presence blessed you"], "meaning": "“God Bless You” is a common response to someone sneezing. Kanye is comparing himself to God by saying that just his presence is enough to bless you. This is not uncommon in Kanye’s music. Another example of this comparison is on the track “I Am A God” off of his “Yeezus” album.", "annotation_id": "15593513", "url": "https://genius.com/15593513", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Niggas done mistook me for my stylist", "vault_lines": ["Niggas done mistook me for my stylist"], "meaning": "It’s certainly no surprise that people have mistaken Kanye West for his stylist.. He doesn’t need one anyway, he is plenty stylish on his own.", "annotation_id": "5055474", "url": "https://genius.com/5055474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Got the club rockin’ like a fuckin’ boat", "vault_lines": ["Got the club rockin' like a fuckin' boat"], "meaning": "The Rock Boat is an annual floating rock music festival. It occurs on a cruise ship that sails from Miami (Ross' hometown) or other places in Florida every winter.", "annotation_id": "2190213", "url": "https://genius.com/2190213", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Seems like we gettin’ money for the wrong things Look around, Maseratis for the whole team", "vault_lines": ["Seems like we gettin' money for the wrong things", "Look around, Maseratis for the whole team"], "meaning": "Here Rick Ross gets a bit conscious and introspective, he juxtaposes how he and his Maybach family are enjoying the luxuries of life(such as buying expensive Maserati’s) while the children in Haiti are suffering and starving. He believes the money that he spends on such expensive material things could be put to better use, he further goes into detail in the next lines.", "annotation_id": "2098751", "url": "https://genius.com/2098751", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Every time we hit the charts, niggas shoot up like a fiend", "vault_lines": ["Every time we hit the charts, niggas shoot up like a fiend"], "meaning": "A play on words. Whenever Ross or one of his label mates gets on a song, that song will shoot up the music and Billboard charts. A fiend is a term for drug abusers, those known for ‘shooting up’ drugs.", "annotation_id": "2097380", "url": "https://genius.com/2097380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Let my convertible marinate on the avenue Mami, that’s half a million, I’m livin’ la vida rapido", "vault_lines": ["Let my convertible marinate on the avenue", "Mami, that's half a million, I'm livin' la vida rapido"], "meaning": "Ross is pointing out to the girl that he’s with that his car is worth so much because he’s living the ‘fast life’ (translated to ‘la vida rapido’ in Spanish); the term ‘mami’ is generally used in the Spanish language as well.\n\nRick Ross is a Miami native, and Florida generally has a large Cuban/Spanish-speaking population, which explains the dialect in these lines.", "annotation_id": "2097361", "url": "https://genius.com/2097361", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Young and radical, methods are mathematical I’m multiplyin’ my money through different avenues", "vault_lines": ["I'm multiplyin' my money through different avenues"], "meaning": "Referring to the drug hustling business; he’s selling dope on different streets and raising his money. Note the math/multiplying wordplay.\n\nThis could also speak to him being a multi-faceted businessman, making money through rap, hustling, endorsements, etc.", "annotation_id": "2028445", "url": "https://genius.com/2028445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Dr. Martin Louis the King, Junior", "vault_lines": ["Dr. Martin Louis the King, Junior"], "meaning": "Kanye West “changed” his name to this back in 2009 as a part of the lead-up to his Grammy performance that year.", "annotation_id": "1837157", "url": "https://genius.com/1837157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "And I’mma never let the dream turn to Kruegers", "vault_lines": ["And I'mma never let the dream turn to Kruegers"], "meaning": "Kanye will never let anyone turn his dreams of success (which he’s now achieved) into nightmares and failures, here called Kruegers – referencing Freddy Krueger from Nightmare on Elm Street, who haunted dreams and turned them into nightmares.", "annotation_id": "1814020", "url": "https://genius.com/1814020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Twenty-four karat gold, eighty carats worth of ice", "vault_lines": ["Twenty-four karat gold, eighty carats worth of ice"], "meaning": "Refers to jewelry, 24 carat gold is the purest and finest gold sold and eighty carat diamonds is the closest you get to the 100 carat pureness in diamonds.", "annotation_id": "408997", "url": "https://genius.com/408997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "And if I die today bury me in a dope-ass watch", "vault_lines": ["And if I die today bury me in a dope-ass watch"], "meaning": "If Ross somehow dies today living his fast and furious life he wants to be buried in an amazing and expensive watch.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to his lines on I’m Not a Star, first track of the same album. Remember him like John Lennon..", "annotation_id": "394674", "url": "https://genius.com/394674", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Look at Haiti, children dyin’ round the clock, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Look at Haiti, children dyin' round the clock, nigga"], "meaning": "This song was put out around the time of the 2010 Haiti earthquake", "annotation_id": "159473", "url": "https://genius.com/159473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "I live for the moment, and put a bullet on that", "vault_lines": ["I live for the moment, and put a bullet on that"], "meaning": "A reference to the line before fuck life insurance, he lives for the moment not worrying about the next day. Putting a bullet on it is gambling your life as we all know a bullet kills.\n\nRoss is leading a risky life.", "annotation_id": "116487", "url": "https://genius.com/116487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Hard-headed, but my top peelin’ back", "vault_lines": ["Hard-headed, but my top peelin' back"], "meaning": "Double entendre referring to his hard-topped convertible as well as himself.\n\n‘Hard-headed’ refers to his stubborn attitude as well. So ‘top peeling back’ just might refer to a receding hairline. Sounds implausible, but Pusha T recently dropped a similar line in ‘Mercy’, referencing George Jefferson.", "annotation_id": "103910", "url": "https://genius.com/103910", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "I’m gettin’ better, cause it woulda leased a drop, nigga I’mma get my money right, just watch, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm gettin' better, cause it woulda leased a drop, nigga", "I'mma get my money right, just watch, nigga"], "meaning": "Ross is admitting that sending $100k isn’t really going to do much to aid Haitians suffering in the wake of the 2009 Earthquake but the fact that he donated at all means he’s becoming more aware of his responsibilities as someone with a lot of money and fame.  That money he sent to Haiti would have probably gone to add to his stable of cars in the past.\n\nThe second line implies that once he achieves a greater level of success he’ll make it a point to do more, larger, charitable acts.  It also references the hook of Kanye’s “Can’t Tell Me Nothing”", "annotation_id": "93820", "url": "https://genius.com/93820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "For my mother I applaud Ms. Afeni Shakur", "vault_lines": ["For my mother I applaud Ms. Afeni Shakur"], "meaning": "Afeni Shakur was the mother of late rapper Tupac Shakur. Two had a close relationship growing up despite Afeni being addicted to crack. Tupac dedicated his 1995 song “Dear Mama” to Afeni.", "annotation_id": "70776", "url": "https://genius.com/70776", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "She came to party like it’s 1999", "vault_lines": ["She came to party like it's 1999"], "meaning": "To “party like it’s 1999” refers to the entering of a new millenium. Also 1999 was prodominantly large year for rap music with the release of The Notorious B.I.G.’s posthumous album “Born Again”.\n\nThere was a widespread belief that the world would end in 2000, so people were going to have wild parties before they died.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to the 1982 Prince song titled 1999 where in the hook he says “Tonight were going to party like it’s 1999.”", "annotation_id": "69049", "url": "https://genius.com/69049", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "When she walked up out the dressing room, the store just froze", "vault_lines": ["When she walked up out the dressing room, the store just froze"], "meaning": "“The store just froze” is a double entendre. Meaning that the store “froze” because everybody stood still, staring at her because of her beauty and everybody “froze” because of the loads of ice (jewelery) that she was wearing.", "annotation_id": "53854", "url": "https://genius.com/53854", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Young and radical, methods are mathematical", "vault_lines": ["Young and radical, methods are mathematical"], "meaning": "An interesting line using two contrasting phrases. First Ricky brings up the idea that he makes radical moves in order to make money, but follows the thought by reassuring that his decisions are all carefully and precisely calculated.", "annotation_id": "32866", "url": "https://genius.com/32866", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "And I know it’s superficial and you say it’s just clothes But we shoppin’ in that motherfucker and they just closed", "vault_lines": ["And I know it's superficial and you say it's just clothes", "But we shoppin' in that motherfucker and they just closed"], "meaning": "Kanye clearly cares alot about clothing and he is so famous that he can shop in any store, even after its closed, because ‘Ye can just use his (African-) American Express Black Card.", "annotation_id": "30045", "url": "https://genius.com/30045", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "I sent a hundred grand, but that’s a decent watch, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I sent a hundred grand, but that's a decent watch, nigga"], "meaning": "Ross donated one hundred thousand dollars to the aforementioned poor children affected by the earthquake, but still laments that he didn’t do more for the people of Haiti.  The few lines before set it up: he’s not using his money the right way. Now he’s admitting a hundred grand can only buy a decent watch, it’s really not much money to help those in need. He could do more, but at least he’s making an effort, as the next few lines point out.", "annotation_id": "28649", "url": "https://genius.com/28649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "For all my young ladies that drivin’ Miss Daisy", "vault_lines": ["For all my young ladies that drivin' Miss Daisy"], "meaning": "A reference to the 1989 film Driving Miss Daisy\n\nYeezy is also making a dedication to all the coke-using Miami females.\n\nA reference to the movie Driving Miss Daisy, the line alludes to the use of cocaine – often referred to in hip-hop as “white girl”. Miss Daisy was a white woman driven around by chauffeur.", "annotation_id": "27892", "url": "https://genius.com/27892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "Like Mike, my Spikes stay all white", "vault_lines": ["Like Mike, my Spikes stay all white"], "meaning": "Like Michael Jordan, Ricky keeps his Spizikes cocaine white.\n\nHe’s also referencing Spike Lee, since the Spizikes' name is taken from “Spike.”", "annotation_id": "27887", "url": "https://genius.com/27887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "And we ’bout to hit Jacob the Jeweler", "vault_lines": ["And we 'bout to hit Jacob the Jeweler"], "meaning": "Jacob Arabo, aka Jacob the Jeweler, is famous for selling jewelry and expensive watches for artists, especially rappers. He had his name shouted-out in various songs by different artists", "annotation_id": "26437", "url": "https://genius.com/26437", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "So I can be like Slick Rick, and rule ya", "vault_lines": ["So I can be like Slick Rick, and rule ya"], "meaning": "Kanye refers to another version of Slick Rick’s name; Rick the Ruler, he also has a song called “The Ruler’s Back”\nRick’s also known for wearing extreme amounts of jewelry, like a King perhaps.", "annotation_id": "26436", "url": "https://genius.com/26436", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Live Fast, Die Young", "line": "What you see me wavin’, Vacheron Constantine", "vault_lines": ["What you see me wavin', Vacheron Constantine"], "meaning": "Vacheron Constantin is a very expensive Swiss watch, so you already know Rozay has one!", "annotation_id": "24271", "url": "https://genius.com/24271", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
