{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Living Large", "line": "Startin’ hearing voices, so I gave away the Ghost (Ghost)", "vault_lines": ["Startin' hearing voices, so I gave away the Ghost (Ghost)"], "meaning": "In this line, the Ross uses a double entendre with the word “Ghost.” After saying he’s “starting hearing voices,” he claims he gave away the Ghost — a reference that can be interpreted both as a literal ghost and as a Rolls-Royce Ghost, a luxury car that has become a major status symbol in hip-hop culture.\n\nThe bar blends a supernatural image with a symbol of wealth, turning a luxury item into something unsettling as if the success and lifestyle attached to it have started to haunt him.", "annotation_id": "40785182", "url": "https://genius.com/40785182", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
