{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "When I get them goons, you in the afterlife by afternoon (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["When I get them goons, you in the afterlife by afternoon (Uh)"], "meaning": "Freddie gibbs musclemen will deliver a swift and potentially fatal beatdown", "annotation_id": "34160881", "url": "https://genius.com/34160881", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "Rappers wanna play sports, athletes caught in the courts", "vault_lines": ["Rappers wanna play sports, athletes caught in the courts"], "meaning": "Could be a reference to J. Cole who played for the Scarborough Shooting Stars during the summer of 2022 in the Canadian Elite Basketball League, tying in with wordplay about courts.\n\nhttps://www.thestar.com/sports/basketball/analysis/2022/05/26/rap-icon-j-cole-draws-a-crowd-for-scarborough-shooting-stars-debut-and-a-loss-feels-like-a-win.html", "annotation_id": "27150388", "url": "https://genius.com/27150388", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "Broken hearts and empty pockets", "vault_lines": ["Broken hearts and empty pockets"], "meaning": "Freddie used this line on Bandana , the track Soul Right.\n\n“Empty stomach, broken heart, and empty pocket\nThree things that occur to show you if you and your niggas solid”", "annotation_id": "26942093", "url": "https://genius.com/26942093", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "But I’m whoopin’ with them ’Rus (Suwoop, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["But I'm whoopin' with them 'Rus (Suwoop, yeah)"], "meaning": "In direct contrast to the previous line, Freddie implies that despite counting up blue notes on the regular, he still fucks heavy with the Pirus, a subset of the Bloods gang- infamous for their red insignia and disdain for their blue-wearing rivals- the Crips", "annotation_id": "26910311", "url": "https://genius.com/26910311", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "I’m addicted to diamonds, such a fiend for them watches", "vault_lines": ["I'm addicted to diamonds, such a fiend for them watches"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is known for purchasing expensive jewelry, including diamonds and Audemars Piguet watches. In fact, he is known for being the owner of the most expensive chain ever– with the price set at a whopping $1.5 million dollars.\n\nIn this line, Ross makes an honest confession: he simply cannot stop purchasing high-end jewelry and flaunting his wealth.", "annotation_id": "26829328", "url": "https://genius.com/26829328", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "Bel-Air bottles in Venice", "vault_lines": ["Bel-Air bottles in Venice"], "meaning": "Luc Belaire is the sparkling wine brand promoted by Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "26817399", "url": "https://genius.com/26817399", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "On the West Coast countin’ blues", "vault_lines": ["On the West Coast countin' blues"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Wes Montgomery’s ‘West Coast Blues’. The track begins with a jazz guitar playing octaves, a technique which Wes Montgomery is known for.\nThis is also referring to ‘blues’ as in $100 bills.", "annotation_id": "26813015", "url": "https://genius.com/26813015", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lobster Omelette", "line": "And folks and them was stealin’ my Starter jacket and my shoes", "vault_lines": ["And folks and them was stealin' my Starter jacket and my shoes"], "meaning": "Starter is a sports clothing brand that was very popular in the 90’s, the decade Gibbs (born 1982) grew up in.\n\nThe brand had licensing deals with a lot of sports teams and is thus synonymous with sports jackets of the era:\n\n\n\n\n\nRappers have often rapped about the difficulty of growing up in the hood and having priced items stolen from them or someone they know.\n\nThe Game – Hate It Or Love It:Been bangin since my lil nigga rob got killed for his barkleys\n\n50 Cent – Hate It Or Love It: Woke up the next morning, niggas had stole my bike", "annotation_id": "26811073", "url": "https://genius.com/26811073", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
