{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "I’m off papers, I heart paper, no short paper, better get the point Cause I’m point-shaven with a sharp razor, get buck like a horse stable", "vault_lines": ["I'm off papers, I heart paper, no short paper, better get the point", "Cause I'm point-shaven with a sharp razor, get buck like a horse stable"], "meaning": "Wayne uses paper with two different meaning\n- Wayne has recently finished his supposed to be a year long sentence after 8 months serving in Rikers Island http://www.mtv.com/news/1651483/lil-wayne-released-from-prison/ (hence the “off papers”).\n- With his legal issue done, he’s back on the grind with his eyes on the money (the second and third “paper”)\nAfter stating all the above, he makes sure you get the point clear (understand him) like\n\n\n\nTo end the quadrane, Wayne plays on the word buck to say he gets money like a stable, where bucks (male horses) are kept.", "annotation_id": "10854615", "url": "https://genius.com/10854615", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Coulda been San Quentin on lock", "vault_lines": ["Coulda been San Quentin on lock"], "meaning": "San Quentin State Prison is a prison in California, which is one of the largest and most notorious prisons in the nation. French Montana was about to get locked", "annotation_id": "7170930", "url": "https://genius.com/7170930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "You know I pop-pop-pop-pop-pop-pop, at your head, my nigga", "vault_lines": ["You know I pop-pop-pop-pop-pop-pop, at your head, my nigga"], "meaning": "Popping sounds are gunshots. It could be .22 rifle, a 9mm handgun or a 12 gauge shotgun. Lil Wayne is imitating the sound of a firearm, which happens when he is shooting at your head.", "annotation_id": "7169778", "url": "https://genius.com/7169778", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Too street smart, I’m a geek, I put my niggas on they feet", "vault_lines": ["Too street smart, I’m a geek, I put my niggas on they feet"], "meaning": "We usually consider geeks to be book smart, but Lil Wayne is so cunning in his street smarts, he is technically a geek too.\n\nWeezy helped out his niggas get out of struggles they were in, and guided them to make their dreams come true. He had a similar line in “Rollin'”, which is off of the Sorry 4 The Wait mixtape:\n\nI put some real niggas on their feet, boy", "annotation_id": "7163789", "url": "https://genius.com/7163789", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "I can’t see none of you niggas, and I can see the future man", "vault_lines": ["I can’t see none of you niggas, and I can see the future man"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is saying that you are going to be gone in the future. He sees the future and you are not in it!\n\nHe is also referencing to one of his older songs “I Can See The Future” featuring Mack Maine.", "annotation_id": "7163785", "url": "https://genius.com/7163785", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "So if we fall, it be that lean that make a nigga fall asleep", "vault_lines": ["So if we fall, it be that lean that make a nigga fall asleep"], "meaning": "The only way Lil Wayne and his crew are going to fall is from codeine cough syrup, a recreational drink popular to make the user sleepy. They’re not degrading from their high positional place.", "annotation_id": "7163779", "url": "https://genius.com/7163779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "I am your ruler, no measurements", "vault_lines": ["I am your ruler, no measurements"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n\nLil Wayne is the ruler of the world! Not the type of ruler you use in school, but the ruler who would rules or commands. Additionally, there is “no measurement” that could compare him to anyone else.", "annotation_id": "7163776", "url": "https://genius.com/7163776", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Out the sewer, now my crib the size of Cuba", "vault_lines": ["Out the sewer, now my crib the size of Cuba"], "meaning": "The nation of Cuba is 42,426 square miles in land area; by contrast, the largest “house” in the world is the entire complex of China’s Forbidden City, which spans 0.05792 square miles.\n\nGenius' Politifact-esque truth grader gives French a “Pants on Fire” rating for this boast.", "annotation_id": "7163599", "url": "https://genius.com/7163599", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Gin with no tonic", "vault_lines": ["Lately so sick I could vomit, Gin with no tonic"], "meaning": "A gin and tonic is a highball cocktail made with gin and tonic water poured over ice. It is usually garnished with a slice or wedge of lime.\n\nUsually, people drink Gin with tonic water like Schweppes tonic water, but French prefer the pure flavor of Gin so he drinks it without tonic water.", "annotation_id": "7163597", "url": "https://genius.com/7163597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "I be riding around with that blocka We them Brick Squad, ask Flocka", "vault_lines": ["I be riding around with that blocka", "We them Brick Squad, ask Flocka"], "meaning": "French Montana shouts out Waka Flocka Flame’s record label. Brick Squad includes Waka Flocka Flame, Gucci Mane, Chief Keef, and Young Thug.", "annotation_id": "7163474", "url": "https://genius.com/7163474", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "I’m in here, now who let the Devil in? I ain’t been taking my medicine My trigger finger ain’t never been hesitant", "vault_lines": ["I’m in here, now who let the Devil in?", "I ain’t been taking my medicine", "My trigger finger ain’t never been hesitant"], "meaning": "Wayne is referring to himself as the devil when he isn’t on his “meds” This is a play on Rick Ross’s and Diddy’s song “Holy Ghost”, where the hook includes following lines:\n\nTalking to the Holy Ghost, in my Bugatti\nHe knockin' on the do' don’t let the Devil in\n\n\n\nWayne then alludes to his track “Trigger Finger” and says he is not hesitant to pull the trigger on someone.", "annotation_id": "7163447", "url": "https://genius.com/7163447", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "I be floor seats by that coach", "vault_lines": ["I be floor seats by that coach"], "meaning": "French went to the Raptors vs. Clippers game in December 2014 and had floor seats with his homies. He Instagrammed this picture with the caption, “Put me in coach !!!! Lol”", "annotation_id": "7163389", "url": "https://genius.com/7163389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Still-a in that trap getting GuWop", "vault_lines": ["Still-a in that trap getting GuWop"], "meaning": "Even though Montana would be rich enough to quit selling drugs, he’s still doing it because of the money.\n\nFun Fact: “Guap” is slang for a high amount of money. But it also sounds like “GuWop”, that’s one of Gucci Mane’s aliases.", "annotation_id": "7163337", "url": "https://genius.com/7163337", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Run shit like a Greyhound", "vault_lines": ["Run shit like a Greyhound"], "meaning": "Greyhounds are a dog breed typically used in racing. In fact, greyhounds are the second fastest land animal capable of going speeds up to 43 miles per hour.", "annotation_id": "7163301", "url": "https://genius.com/7163301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "I think I’m bout to lose it, mayne Said I’m ’bout to go Gucci Mane", "vault_lines": ["I think I'm bout to lose it, mayne", "Said I'm 'bout to go Gucci Mane"], "meaning": "Ross is about to lose it all and end up like Gucci Mane who is currently in prison until 2016-2017. Gucci is one of the most influential rappers in the Atlanta trap scene.\n\nHe was charged on September 30th, 2014, for carrying a concealed weapon, possession of marijuana, and disorderly conduct. He eventually plead guilty to possession of a firearm by a convicted felon and was sentenced until late 2016 or early 2017.\n\n\n\nRoss must have been serious because he was recently sent to prison for kidnapping and assault charges.", "annotation_id": "7163130", "url": "https://genius.com/7163130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Uh, get down or lay down Shoot everything up but a school or a playground", "vault_lines": ["Uh, get down or lay down", "Shoot everything up but a school or a playground"], "meaning": "This bar is the exact same as Birdman used in his single “Y.U. Mad” which Lil Wayne featured on with Nicki Minaj.\n\n\nShoot up anything except a school or playground― Birdman (Ft. Lil Wayne & Nicki Minaj) – Y U Mad\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nA code of the streets.\n\nWayne is saying he will shoot anything up as long as it isn’t a school or a playground. I guess old folks homes and hospitals are fine though.", "annotation_id": "7162996", "url": "https://genius.com/7162996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "Cash Money ’til I die, even if I go broke, I still wouldn’t beg to differ", "vault_lines": ["Cash Money 'til I die, even if I go broke, I still wouldn't beg to differ"], "meaning": "Not exactly the best thing for Weezy to claim considering his recent ongoing public squabbles with his former label, Cash Money.\n\nBut this is just down to the fact the verse and the song was recorded several months before his issues with Birdman started.\n\nIgnoring the current beef, Wayne is saying how he is and always will be loyal to Cash Money even if he didn’t have money which is basically all they’re about.\n\n\n\nIn the official version, they cut the Cash Money shout out. With silence replacing ‘cash’.", "annotation_id": "7162157", "url": "https://genius.com/7162157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Lose It", "line": "What’s Gucci, my nigga? What’s Louis, my killer?", "vault_lines": ["What’s Gucci, my nigga? What’s Louis, my killer?"], "meaning": "Sampled from Kanye West’s “Niggas in Paris” from the album Watch The Throne.\n\nhttps://genius.com/319273", "annotation_id": "7159687", "url": "https://genius.com/7159687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
