{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Loss 4 Wrdz", "line": "Burnin’ weed in the Benjamin", "vault_lines": ["Burnin' weed in the Benjamin"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is part owner of Empire Rolling Papers, famous for distributing rolling paper printed to look like the hundred dollar bill, commonly referred to as “Benjamins” because the banknote features the portrait of Benjamin Franklin", "annotation_id": "12181065", "url": "https://genius.com/12181065", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Loss 4 Wrdz", "line": "I’m feelin’ like I took a Perc’, I’m at a loss for words It’s like I smoked a pound of herbs, so please do not disturb Feel like I drunk a pound of syrup and snorted up half a bird Can’t even find the words, I’m so at a loss for words I’m feelin’ like I took a Perc’, I’m at a loss for words It’s like I smoked a pound of herbs, so please do not disturb Feel like I drunk a pound of syrup and snorted up half a bird Can’t even find the words, I’m so at a loss for words", "vault_lines": ["Can't even find the words, I'm so at a loss for words"], "meaning": "The hook describes the feelings derived from using different drugs, such as: smoking weed, popping Percocet pills, drinking lean, and snorting cocaine.\n\nSide effects of lean include a rough, raspy voice, and slow, slurred speech. This would make sense as Gucci Mane has a loss for words since he feels like he is under heavy side effects of drugs.\n\n\n\nThe phrase “snorted up half a bird” refers to doing a large amount of cocaine; “bird” is a slang word for a brick of cocaine.\n\nDespite the way Gucci is feeling, he has actually been sober since being released from prison in May 2016.", "annotation_id": "11912747", "url": "https://genius.com/11912747", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Loss 4 Wrdz", "line": "Mary J, they reminisce", "vault_lines": ["Mary J, they reminisce"], "meaning": "Mary J. Blige is an American singer who is well-known in the R&B community.\n\nThis is a reference to her third 1992 single “Reminisce” off her debut album What’s the 411?\n\n\n\n“Mary J” is also popular slang for marijuana.", "annotation_id": "11912618", "url": "https://genius.com/11912618", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Loss 4 Wrdz", "line": "Wanna kill just like Tony did When Manny fucked his sister", "vault_lines": ["Wanna kill just like Tony did", "When Manny fucked his sister"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the movie character Tony Montana from the 1983 movie Scarface. He was a drug lord and a hitman who killed many people in the movie. His best friend Manny helped Tony throughout the movie, but Montana finds him and Gina together. Tony realizes that Manny had sex with his sister, which eventually ends in him killing Manny in a cocaine-fueled rage. It is later revealed that Gina and Manny were married.", "annotation_id": "11912331", "url": "https://genius.com/11912331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Loss 4 Wrdz", "line": "Metro Boomin want some more, nigga", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The sample from “Some More” by Young Thug has become a very common production tag for Metro Boomin. This line is sang by Young Thug.", "annotation_id": "11912309", "url": "https://genius.com/11912309", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Loss 4 Wrdz", "line": "Drinkin’ lean like I’m Pimp", "vault_lines": ["Drinkin' lean like I'm Pimp"], "meaning": "A reference to Pimp C, one half of rap duo UGK, who was big a fan of sizzurp. Sadly, an overdose on lean resulted in Pimp C’s untimely death.  RIP Pimp C.", "annotation_id": "11910943", "url": "https://genius.com/11910943", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
