{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Luxury Tax", "line": "”Gangsta’s Paradise”, and I ain’t talkin’ ’bout Coolio", "vault_lines": ["\"Gangsta's Paradise\", and I ain't talkin' 'bout Coolio"], "meaning": "Jeezy is referencing the legendary rap song “Gangsta’s Paradise” by Coolio released in 1995. He could also be referencing Coolio’s 1995 album of the same name.", "annotation_id": "13822596", "url": "https://genius.com/13822596", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Luxury Tax", "line": "And we ain’t tryna see the Pen Like a needle in a haystack, we ain’t tryna see the ‘pin’", "vault_lines": ["And we ain't tryna see the Pen", "Like a needle in a haystack, we ain't tryna see the 'pin'"], "meaning": "Nobody wants to go to prison (the Penitentiary).  And if you live a luxurious, baller lifestyle jail would be an even harsher downgrade.\n\nIn a signature Weezy turn of phrase, he likens “the pen” (prison) to “the pin” (from the saying “needle in a haystack”).", "annotation_id": "10571818", "url": "https://genius.com/10571818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Luxury Tax", "line": "And they say you ain’t great until someone assassinate And I feel like MLK Yeah, “I Have a Dream” to be your worst nightmare", "vault_lines": ["And they say you ain't great until someone assassinate", "And I feel like MLK", "Yeah, \"I Have a Dream\" to be your worst nightmare"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has heard  that someone is not truly great until their works have caused some individuals to attempt to murder them.\n\nMr. Carter then says he feels like Martin Luther King Jr, a civil rights activist who was assassinated by James Earl Ray because of MLK’s belief that Black Americans should have the same rights as White Americans.\n\nLil Wayne then alludes to MLK’s ‘I Have A Dream’ speech, saying that he also has a dream, but instead of furthering civil rights, Wayne wants to strike fear into his enemies.", "annotation_id": "7199029", "url": "https://genius.com/7199029", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Luxury Tax", "line": "Boss", "vault_lines": ["Now meet The Boss of The Cartel, Ross"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' uses this adlib many times in his music.\n\nHe even has a song dedicated to his Bosshood on his studio album Trilla called The Boss.", "annotation_id": "2869229", "url": "https://genius.com/2869229", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Luxury Tax", "line": "Black-flaggin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm gettin' money and my swag, black-flaggin'"], "meaning": "“So the black flag is representing the struggle, cuz that’s what we’re living. I’m a black flag bastard. I don’t want people to think it’s gang-banging, because we hang with niggas who represent red flags. We’re gangstas for real.”\n\n\nTrick Daddy\n\n\n\nhttp://www.miaminewtimes.com/2008-06-19/music/trick-daddy-bids-farewell-to-slip-n-slide/full/", "annotation_id": "1640244", "url": "https://genius.com/1640244", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
