{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "I never borrowed jewelry,", "vault_lines": ["I never borrowed jewelry,"], "meaning": "Gucci buys all of his jewelry, he never borrows it. Unbeknownst to many people, a lot of jewelry draped on celebrities is rented. A New York Time Article from 2003 titled All That Glitters Has Most Likely Been Borrowed talks about jewelry houses that specialize in lending jewelry to celebrities for publicity:\n\nFor exclusive jewelry houses, the risk to the jaw-dropping ‘'loaners’‘ that drape the stars as they stroll the red carpet is minor compared with the potential reward in free publicity. Not only does a vast audience see Halle and Nicole and J. Lo scintillate in megacarat eye candy, but the photographs splashed across the globe are recycled for years. What’s more, some of the pieces are sold right off a star’s back, so to speak. The $490,000 Chanel diamond comet necklace worn by Celine Dion in 1997 and the Fred Leighton 19th-century diamond-and-pearl necklace Madonna wore the same year were snapped up afterward.\n\nMaybe Gucci watches the Oscars to see what his next purchase will be?\n\n\n\nProbably not.", "annotation_id": "750917", "url": "https://genius.com/750917", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "Ambulance, ambulance, 9-1-1, 9-1-1", "vault_lines": ["Ambulance, ambulance, 9-1-1, 9-1-1"], "meaning": "911 is an emergency phone number which will could trigger ambulances or other emergency vehicles.\n\n\n\n911 is also the most popular type of Porsche.", "annotation_id": "671888", "url": "https://genius.com/671888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "You gotta judge a man by his principles", "vault_lines": ["You gotta judge a man by his principles"], "meaning": "Rick offers advice on making a fair assessment of someone’s character.\n\nThis is pretty ironic as for most of the song he is talking about drug dealing. Then again if you ask most investment bankers what their most important value is they will say “integrity”.", "annotation_id": "161577", "url": "https://genius.com/161577", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "Gucci!", "vault_lines": ["Gucci Pucci money long, now we call him Alex"], "meaning": "“Gucci!” is what Gucci Mane yells at the beginning and/or end of his verses in songs that he is in", "annotation_id": "116701", "url": "https://genius.com/116701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "Teflon Don, I am invincible", "vault_lines": ["Teflon Don, I am invincible"], "meaning": "Teflon is a nonstick surface that is put on lots of cooking materials. Rick is implying that he’s “too slick” to get caught, and that he cannot be touched.\n\nFor the originator of the term, see famed mobster John Gotti", "annotation_id": "116700", "url": "https://genius.com/116700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "Had to move from Davie,", "vault_lines": ["Had to move from Davie,"], "meaning": "Davie, FL is a town in Broward County, Florida, United States. Perhaps Ross had to leave the town because he had it on lock due to his drug dealing.", "annotation_id": "116698", "url": "https://genius.com/116698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "I got 30 cars, whole lot of dancers I take them everywhere, I’m MC Hammer", "vault_lines": ["I got 30 cars, whole lot of dancers", "I take them everywhere, I'm MC Hammer"], "meaning": "This entire song is a tribute to Hammer’s lifestyle in the early 90s, in which he was partly known to travel with large entourages and in circles of celebrities.", "annotation_id": "70335", "url": "https://genius.com/70335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "It’s an occasion, a celebration, at Central Station", "vault_lines": ["It's an occasion, a celebration, at Central Station"], "meaning": "Central Station, a premier nightclub in atlanta, GA", "annotation_id": "45872", "url": "https://genius.com/45872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "Diamonds movin’ on my chest, wanna Hammer dance", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds movin' on my chest, wanna Hammer dance"], "meaning": "When a person’s diamonds are “dancing” it means the clarity of the diamonds are of the highest quality and they are extremely bright, in this case gucci mane’s diamonds are doing the hammer dance that’s alot of dancing, heres a picture of Gucci Mane", "annotation_id": "45868", "url": "https://genius.com/45868", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "Gucci Pucci money long, now we call him Alex", "vault_lines": ["Gucci Pucci money long, now we call him Alex"], "meaning": "Alex “Gucci Pucci” Bethune is Ross' long time manager and CEO of MMG. This line refers to the fact that Pooch got so much money now that people call him Alex because he is renowned.\n\n\n\nHow is Gucci Pucci aka Alex doing now?", "annotation_id": "45857", "url": "https://genius.com/45857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "My top back, uncircumcised I pull it back, just to go inside", "vault_lines": ["My top back, uncircumcised", "I pull it back, just to go inside"], "meaning": "Rick is all about convertibles, he is large so he has to drop the top on his car before he can get in. the scrunching effect the softtop makes as it folds away resembles that of the foreskin of an uncircumcised penis.", "annotation_id": "34763", "url": "https://genius.com/34763", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "One button like an Atari", "vault_lines": ["It's called Scaglietti, one button like an Atari"], "meaning": "Modern supercars rarely require you to turn a key in the ignition, preferring a solution from race cars: a single button that stops and starts the car. Just like the Atari 2600 systems of yore", "annotation_id": "34760", "url": "https://genius.com/34760", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "I’m at the car lot, I’m goin’ broke I pay for 5, they front a couple mo’", "vault_lines": ["I'm at the car lot, I'm goin' broke", "I pay for 5, they front a couple mo'"], "meaning": "Rick Ross buys cars with such consistency that the dealers know he’s good for the money, thus he gets fronted whips. He “gets that work on his face”.\n\n“Going broke” is a reference to the titular MC Hammer, who had to declare bankruptcy after spending away his fortune frivolously. Rick is comparing his spending habits to Hammer’s, but the implication is that he isn’t actually going broke.", "annotation_id": "34756", "url": "https://genius.com/34756", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "I’m too legit to quit When it’s hammer time,", "vault_lines": ["When it's hammer time,"], "meaning": "Too Legit To Quit is the title of MC Hammer’s second best selling album, while Hammertime is the name of his A&E talk show.\n\n“Hammer” is also used as a euphemism for guns, so Ross will fire if necessary.\n\nRoss is also “too legit to quit” in the sense that his prowess as a kingpin is so great that he’ll never completely quit pushing kilos.", "annotation_id": "34754", "url": "https://genius.com/34754", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "Bitch, I’m MC Hammer,", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm MC Hammer,"], "meaning": "MC Hammer was one of the most commercially successful rappers in history\n\nRoss should be careful, as Hammer is remembered these days largely as a cautionary example", "annotation_id": "34753", "url": "https://genius.com/34753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "My dick clean She talk dirty, but her mouth clean", "vault_lines": ["She talk dirty, but her mouth clean"], "meaning": "A classical example of hip-hop’s madonna/whore complex\n\nRoss insists that his dick is clean which therefore would make her mouth clean too.. right? Also she has a potty mouth hence its why she talks dirty", "annotation_id": "34751", "url": "https://genius.com/34751", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "line": "I’m ridin’ dirty,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Driving a car containing goods or in such a manner that would allow the police to arrest the driver\n\nNot to be confused with driving a dirty car.  Nobody ever drives a dirty car–car-detailing is a popular enterprise among ex-cons, high-school dropouts, money launderers and other small business owners\n\nRiding dirty is so common that Chamillionaire wrote a song about it", "annotation_id": "34750", "url": "https://genius.com/34750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MC Hammer", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-mc-hammer-lyrics", "genius_title": "MC Hammer", "genius_id": 1157, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "I want you to ride, definition of honor Honor thy brother, but murder these hoes", "vault_lines": ["I want you to ride, definition of honor", "Honor thy brother, but murder these hoes"], "meaning": "Ross puts his twist on the popular expression “bros before hoes”—meaning how men should not abandon their male friends in order to pursue relationships with women. It was popularized by the American sitcom How I Met Your Mother where Barney Stinson wrote a book named The Bro Code, a book on what “bros” should or shouldn’t do.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GDctKgcN1K0", "annotation_id": "12821918", "url": "https://genius.com/12821918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Your life and your wrist got the wrong timing, you hate me", "vault_lines": ["Your life and your wrist got the wrong timing, you hate me"], "meaning": "Metaphor: You have the wrong time on your watch just like you were never able to make it and become some type of mogul celebrity due to the wrong timing just like that of your watch due to this you hate people like Pharell who have become succsessful and are envious of what they have and you wish you were them.", "annotation_id": "4439035", "url": "https://genius.com/4439035", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "I put mirror tint all on the Ghost, I’m screaming, “Bloody Mary” Nigga, Bloody Mary, Bloody Mary, Bloody Mary", "vault_lines": ["I put mirror tint all on the Ghost, I'm screaming, \"Bloody Mary\"", "Nigga, Bloody Mary, Bloody Mary, Bloody Mary"], "meaning": "There is a ghost tale about a woman named Mary. According to legend, if you say ‘Bloody Mary’ three times in front of a mirror, she comes out of it and kills you.\n\nThis could actually mean two things:\n\n\nSo the ghost means the one in the tale, but it also means a Rolls Royce Ghost. The mirror tint is in the Rolls Royce Ghost, and because it is reflective (like a mirror) Meek Mill jokingly is saying the bloody Marry chant, proving that he can not die within the vehicle, probably because it is bullet proof. In other words he is saying he has transcended the level of being murdered on the street like an average drug.\nHe’s saying he doesn’t fear anything. He turned his windows into mirrors and is tempting death by screaming Bloody Mary everywhere he goes. After everything he has witnessed: death friends, death family members, probably even a near death experience, he ain’t scared of shit, he’s seen it all.", "annotation_id": "3417550", "url": "https://genius.com/3417550", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "I’m on my Convertible Burt shit", "vault_lines": ["I'm on my Convertible Burt shit"], "meaning": "Convertible Burt Simmons was a Miami based drug deal whom Ross admires. He mentioned him in the 3rd verse of “Hustlin'”:\n\n*I touch work like I’m Convertable Burt", "annotation_id": "3207796", "url": "https://genius.com/3207796", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "My nigga Peanut, rest in peace See you would felt this right here", "vault_lines": ["My nigga Peanut, rest in peace"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s best friend Ramond Adderly, a.k.a P-Nutt, was shot and killed back in 2010. he was also an aspiring rapper who was on the come up with Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "2743092", "url": "https://genius.com/2743092", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "This shit feel like, some Carol City shit right here", "vault_lines": ["This shit feel like, some Carol City shit right here"], "meaning": "Rozay shouts out his hometown, Carol City, which is also the home to several other big-name artists:\n\n\nFlo Rida\nDenzel Curry\nGunplay", "annotation_id": "2743086", "url": "https://genius.com/2743086", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Uhh! Geechi Liberace", "vault_lines": ["Geechi Liberace, put diamonds in everything"], "meaning": "Geechi, a favorite slang term of the MMG crew, is a person of Gullah origin.\nThe Gullahs are black people living in the Lowcountry region of Georgia and South Carolina, who have preserved their links to Africa arguably more than any other African-American group, so he means freedom to geechie.", "annotation_id": "1050852", "url": "https://genius.com/1050852", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "But when I had a quarter, they had four and the baby It was a whole different story, but fuck, them niggas is shady", "vault_lines": ["But when I had a quarter, they had four and the baby", "It was a whole different story, but fuck, them niggas is shady"], "meaning": "The phrase four and a baby refers to 1/8 of a kilo of cocaine. Approximately 125 grams which breaks down to four full ounces in addition to 13g which is just short of a half ounce. The baby refers to the short half ounce. Here Meek is comparing his amount of drugs to his other homies.", "annotation_id": "1050849", "url": "https://genius.com/1050849", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Black boy scoring his life, I’m scoring the Oscars", "vault_lines": ["Black boy scoring his life, I'm scoring the Oscars"], "meaning": "The black boy is procuring drugs (“scoring”) to maintain his way of life. Pharrell along with Hans Zimmer (film composer of The Dark Knight and Inception fame) scored the 84th Academy Awards (or Oscars) on February 26th, 2012, shortly after this mixtape was released", "annotation_id": "737619", "url": "https://genius.com/737619", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "I’m noble dog like Drew Ali", "vault_lines": ["I'm noble dog like Drew Ali"], "meaning": "Noble Drew Ali founded The Moorish Science Temple of America as a sect of Islam. He is sometimes credited as being the first American Muslim, he drew inspiration from Buddhism, Christianity, Freemasonry, Gnosticism and Taoism.\n\nStalley compares himself to this historical figure because he’s muslim himself.", "annotation_id": "731885", "url": "https://genius.com/731885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Remember I used to want a Pasha and eat some lobster But now I eat the apple with my AP", "vault_lines": ["Remember I used to want a Pasha and eat some lobster", "But now I eat the apple with my AP"], "meaning": "Double entendre right here:\n\nHe thinks back to the days when he had nothing and wanted to go to pasha to eat lobster but couldn’t afford it, whereas now on the other hand he eats an apple with the same hand as his very expensive AP (Audemar Piguet) watch is on.\nThis lyric is also a play on words as apple, the famous Macintosh computers, are also famous for their apps which is similar to the word AP.", "annotation_id": "638278", "url": "https://genius.com/638278", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Old heads told me, “Young fella, this ain’t the game to play” Had to take the chance, told the dealer, “Deal my hand”", "vault_lines": ["Old heads told me, \"Young fella, this ain't the game to play\"", "Had to take the chance, told the dealer, \"Deal my hand\""], "meaning": "He intertwined taking chances in gambling in a card game and hustling in this one line.\n\nThe older hustlers warned him that hustling isn’t something he should be doing, especially at his age, he took his chances and did it anyway and asked the dealer for a front.\n\nJust as someone would tell you not to get carried away at the casino.", "annotation_id": "589568", "url": "https://genius.com/589568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Yeah, they villains But I’m chilling", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A play on the phrase chillin' like a villain.", "annotation_id": "583083", "url": "https://genius.com/583083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "But now I pull up in that thing Them niggas gon’ need some Tylenol", "vault_lines": ["But now I pull up in that thing", "Them niggas gon' need some Tylenol"], "meaning": "Funny wordplay here:\n\nMeek is now so rich, he can afford everything he ever wanted. People are jealous and they need Tylenol to heal of the jealousy.", "annotation_id": "575575", "url": "https://genius.com/575575", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "God forgives and I don’t, unforgettable dude", "vault_lines": ["God forgives and I don't, unforgettable dude"], "meaning": "Double entendre in which Ross implies that only god forgives and he doesn’t because he never forgets (and thus never forgives) and the fact that he’s so great as a rapper he won’t be forgotten (unforgettable).\n\nAlso a shout out to his (at the time) upcoming album, God Forgives, I Don’t.", "annotation_id": "568076", "url": "https://genius.com/568076", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Now I’m self-made, self-paid, and I give myself a raise", "vault_lines": ["Now I'm self-made, self-paid, and I give myself a raise"], "meaning": "Meek controls his own salary because it depends on how hard he pushes himself.\n\nAlso a reference to the MMG album Self Made.", "annotation_id": "543551", "url": "https://genius.com/543551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Making deals, squeezing the life out of them Nextel chirps", "vault_lines": ["Making deals, squeezing the life out of them Nextel chirps"], "meaning": "During the mid 2000’s, Nextel released a line of cell phones which featured “push to talk” walkie talkie type calling. The push to talk button made a chirping sound when pressed. Many drug dealers used these phones to make drug deals because A) It was quick and B) It was harder to record and trace.", "annotation_id": "542388", "url": "https://genius.com/542388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Went from Spaghetti-O’s to a new set of Vogues", "vault_lines": ["Went from Spaghetti-O's to a new set of Vogues"], "meaning": "This is an illustrated line, meaning he came from being small to doing it big.\n\nSpaghetti-O’s is a cheap food brand and Vogues are expensive tires.\n\nNote that Spaghetti-O’s is a small ‘O’ shaped spaghetti pasta and vogues are tires. You do the math.", "annotation_id": "535050", "url": "https://genius.com/535050", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Had them birds but we ain’t fuck with Larry", "vault_lines": ["Had them birds but we ain't fuck with Larry"], "meaning": "A “bird” is slang for cocaine. Larry Bird is an American basketball executive and president of the NBA team, Indiana Pacers.  Larry was a former NBA player himself—he played for the Boston Celtics before retiring in 1992.", "annotation_id": "534048", "url": "https://genius.com/534048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Young Bonaparte,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Stalley compares himself to Napoleon Bonaparte because he has the same ambitions to conquer many things.", "annotation_id": "533070", "url": "https://genius.com/533070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "My Tribe Called Quest, shit was nice dawg Gucci was Q-Tip, I was Phife Dawg On awards tours", "vault_lines": ["My Tribe Called Quest, shit was nice dawg", "Gucci was Q-Tip, I was Phife Dawg"], "meaning": "Q-Tip and Phife Dawg are members of the hip-hop collective, A Tribe Called Quest.\n\nRick Ross is comparing himself to Phife and Atlanta Rapper Gucci Mane to Q-Tip.\n\nWorld Tours refers to ATCQ’s song “Award Tour”.", "annotation_id": "532511", "url": "https://genius.com/532511", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "line": "Here we are The world is ours", "vault_lines": ["The world is ours"], "meaning": "A nod to the phrase “the world is yours”, as seen in and popularized by the movie Scarface, a movie that has served as inspiration for Rick Ross' work throughout the years.\n\nThis hook has a celebratory tone, as Ross and his crew are living out their [American] dream and feel that they’ve made it and that the world is theirs.", "annotation_id": "531296", "url": "https://genius.com/531296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG The World Is Ours", "status": "done", "targets": 22, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-mmg-the-world-is-ours-lyrics", "genius_title": "MMG The World Is Ours", "genius_id": 62995, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "Just beat another charge, made ’em drop that case", "vault_lines": ["Just beat another charge, made 'em drop that case"], "meaning": "Perhaps a reference to his lawsuit with Freeway Ricky Ross, in which Ross was sued for $10 million. Ross ended up beating the case, as the lawsuit was thrown out.", "annotation_id": "1449769", "url": "https://genius.com/1449769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "I got that green with me, Gucci got those blocks", "vault_lines": ["I got that green with me, Gucci got those blocks"], "meaning": "Two double entendres!\n\nThe first double entendre is about the green, which refers to:\n\n\nMoney\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMarijuana\n\n\n\n\n\nThe second double entendre is about Gucci, which refers to both Gucci Mane & Ross' manager, Gucci Pucci. Either way, Gucci has cocaine.", "annotation_id": "731820", "url": "https://genius.com/731820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "I’m talking trigger play (Woo), never safe for lames", "vault_lines": ["I'm talking trigger play (Woo), never safe for lames"], "meaning": "Ross is saying the games he referred to in  the previous line are shooting lame dudes\n\nRick Ross is referring to drug dealing as “trigger play” which is “never safe for lames”. A “lame” is a disabled person or Ross could referring to less brilliant people, who can be easily caoght. For those people, its not a safe job to do drug trafficking.", "annotation_id": "599570", "url": "https://genius.com/599570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "Greenhouse on the couch, niggas seeing me toast (Toast)", "vault_lines": ["Greenhouse on the couch, niggas seeing me toast (Toast)"], "meaning": "Ross smoking so much jane that he hotboxed the shit outta himself, similar to a greenhouse that keeps all the moisture and air inside to refresh and nurture plants\n\n\n\nHe could also be referring to club Greenhouse in NYC.  He’s standing on the couches and popping bottles. That’d be the reason the aforementioned “niggas” are able to see him toast.", "annotation_id": "536503", "url": "https://genius.com/536503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "Panamera parade (Okay)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Panamera: Luxury sports cars made by German car company, Porsche\nRoss gotta enough of these that he could ride down the street and make it look like a parade (full of Porsches)", "annotation_id": "536478", "url": "https://genius.com/536478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "A nigga cheese dripping (Yeah), I like my nachos hot", "vault_lines": ["A nigga cheese dripping (Yeah), I like my nachos hot"], "meaning": "Cheese drippin – Cheese being slang for money, Ross is saying that he is splurging with the cash. Cheese starts to melt and drip, when it gets hot. There are cheese on nachos, so when he says he like hot nachos that explains why the cheese is dripping.", "annotation_id": "536459", "url": "https://genius.com/536459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "They standing in line, they all suffer from vapors (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["They standing in line, they all suffer from vapors (Woo)"], "meaning": "People who used to hate him now line up to see him. “Vapors” is a term that describes taking a newfangled and opportunistic liking to someone only after that person became successful. The term first entered the rap lexicon in Biz Markie’s 1988 The Vapors. Those who used to turn up their noses “catch the vapors” of fame and flyness and change their tune.\n\n“Vapors” is also an archaic diagnosis of dizzyness, fainting, etc. Interestingly, the vapors can be triggered by standing for too long.", "annotation_id": "532174", "url": "https://genius.com/532174", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "I’m running the city like a pair of new J’s Maybe the patent 11s, I got these hoes in a daze (Okay)", "vault_lines": ["I'm running the city like a pair of new J's", "Maybe the patent 11s, I got these hoes in a daze (Okay)"], "meaning": "Rozay runs the streets like a pair of Jordans (shoe pun). He wears the much-anticipated retro Air Jordan 11’s that were released. The pair sported some iconic patent leather styling.\n\nRoss also refers to reports that riots broke out over the scarce shoes", "annotation_id": "531824", "url": "https://genius.com/531824", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "MMG Untouchable", "line": "My lawyers going hard (Yeah), a nigga versus the state", "vault_lines": ["My lawyers going hard (Yeah), a nigga versus the state"], "meaning": "When it’s The State of Florida vs. William L. Roberts II aka Rick Ross, his lawyers aren’t allowed to slack off! On a more serious note, Ross has had his own share of legal problems at the hands of government, other entertainers, and even an ex-convict.", "annotation_id": "531326", "url": "https://genius.com/531326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
