{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "Me and my niggas came out the basement (out the basement) We been trapping, make sure they can’t trace it (hey)", "vault_lines": ["Me and my niggas came out the basement (out the basement)", "We been trapping, make sure they can't trace it (hey)"], "meaning": "Jay Critch has made several references to the ‘basement’ and how he has made it out and is in better surroundings such as in ‘Ego’ where he said :\n“I’m in the penthouse but I came from the basement” which he later explained in a Genius Lyric Breakdown.\nTrapping refers to drug dealing or moving drugs and Critch did it in such a manner that it’s not traceable hence his clean record.", "annotation_id": "22417371", "url": "https://genius.com/22417371", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "I just signed a contract like a Laker (swish)", "vault_lines": ["I just signed a contract like a Laker (swish)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross owns his own label called ‘Maybach Music’ and in this line he is talking about just having signed a contract which he contrasts to signing a contract in basketball like the team Los Angeles Lakers.  The Lakers are considered to be one of the best teams in the NBA and signing a contract with them is a big deal.", "annotation_id": "22417321", "url": "https://genius.com/22417321", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "The darker her skin (yes), the more I get off (queen)", "vault_lines": ["The darker her skin (yes), the more I get off (queen)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is discussing his love for black women.  He feels that for black women, “the darker” their “skin” is, the more beautiful they are to him. This is on the contrary to the colorist norm of light skin women being more beautiful than darker skinned women. He also does not have a history of choosing women based on the tone of their skin considering the variety of shades his baby mamas are, shown in the image below:", "annotation_id": "20244284", "url": "https://genius.com/20244284", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "Hood fave with the clutch like game six (hey)", "vault_lines": ["Hood fave with the clutch like game six (hey)"], "meaning": "Jay critch shouts out his nickname ‘Hood fave’ and declares he’s clutch and will deliver like a top basketball player in a game six\n\n\n\nA game six is the game that precedes the elimination game in a basketball series", "annotation_id": "14986159", "url": "https://genius.com/14986159", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "With the killers like Freddy and Jason (Freddy and Jason) How I ran up them racks it’s amazing (it’s amazing)", "vault_lines": ["With the killers like Freddy and Jason (Freddy and Jason)", "How I ran up them racks it's amazing (it's amazing)"], "meaning": "Jay is referring to the fictional horror-slasher movie characters Freddy Krueger and Jason Vorhees.\n\nFreddy Krueger is from the movie series Nightmare on Elm Street. While Jason Vorhees is from the movie series Friday the 13th. In 2003, a crossover between these 2 characters was created known as Freddy vs Jason.\n\n\n\nCritch is also referring to songs from 21 Savage, Offset, and Metro Boomin’s collaboration Without Warning.\n\nJay also says “ran up them racks” which is directly referring to the song “Run Up the Racks”.\n\nAlso, Jay Critch could potentially be referring to 2 songs from the project. Being “My Choppa Hate Niggas” and “Nightmare”.\n\nNear the end of the song “My Choppa Hate Niggas”, 21 Savage raps:\n\nA Nightmare on Elm Street\nFeel like Jason, Friday 13th\nHockey mask with the .223\nIssa Nightmare on Elm Street\n\nThe outro to “My Choppa Hate Niggas” is also the intro to the song “Nightmare”. In the song, “Nightmare”, Offset raps:\n\nFreddy Kruger, give ‘em a nightmare\nSoon as you close your eyes, nigga, we right there", "annotation_id": "14204299", "url": "https://genius.com/14204299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "Niggas singin’ Rich Forever, so you know we related (huh) (M-M-M-) So you know we related (huh) (M-M-M-) Yeah, you know we related (woo)", "vault_lines": ["Niggas singin' Rich Forever, so you know we related (huh) (M-M-M-)", "So you know we related (huh) (M-M-M-)", "Yeah, you know we related (woo)"], "meaning": "The phrase “Rich Forever” is one that is associated with both Rick Ross and Rich The Kid.\n\nRick Ross' second mixtape as well as his Instagram account share names with the phrase.\n\nRich The Kid named his record label Rich Forever Music. He constantly repeats the phrase throughout his music, using it on this song and throughout the album.", "annotation_id": "14201522", "url": "https://genius.com/14201522", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "Blue and yellow diamonds like Jacob (woo)", "vault_lines": ["Blue and yellow diamonds like Jacob (woo)"], "meaning": "Jacob & Co. is a jewellery company, located in Manhattan, who specialise in luxury wristwatches.\n\nThey are known for their incorporation of multi-coloured diamonds into their watches.\n\nOne of their signature products is the Five Time Zone Watch,  a version of which is made with blue and yellow diamonds.", "annotation_id": "14201483", "url": "https://genius.com/14201483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "My water, my wrist is on Fiji", "vault_lines": ["My water, my wrist is on Fiji"], "meaning": "Fiji Water is self-branded artisan water, which has grown in popularity due to its association with class and affluence.  Rich compares the class and complexity of Fiji with the jewelry on his wrist.  He also raps about Fiji water on “No Question” where he raps\n\nFiji water, don’t slip (Fiji water)", "annotation_id": "14200659", "url": "https://genius.com/14200659", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "Santorini Greece where I’ma take her (woo)", "vault_lines": ["Santorini Greece where I'ma take her (woo)"], "meaning": "Santorini is a greek island located in the Aegean Sea. The island is about 200 km southeast of Greece’s mainland and is a popular tourist attraction and location for holidays.\n\n\n\nOn Ross’s 9th studio album Rather You Than Me released in 2017  the second track was titled “Santorini Greece”. The music video for the track was filmed in Santorini.", "annotation_id": "14199166", "url": "https://genius.com/14199166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "Whole team Rich Forever, that’s my word (huh)", "vault_lines": ["Whole team Rich Forever, that's my word (huh)"], "meaning": "Rich Forever is the name of Rich The Kid’s record label.  Currently, Famous Dex, Jay Critch and YBN Almighty Jay are signed to it.\n\nPossibly a coincidence but could also be a reference to rapper Rick Ross, who features on this track. @richforever is his Instagram handle and he also named his critically acclaimed 2012 mixtape Rich Forever.", "annotation_id": "14196883", "url": "https://genius.com/14196883", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It", "line": "La música de Harry Fraud", "vault_lines": ["(La música de Harry Fraud"], "meaning": "“La Música de Harry Fraud” is the producer tag of Harry Fraud. The tag is simply Spanish for “Harry Fraud’s music”.\n\nFraud is known for working with French Montana and Action Bronson but has produced beats for a variety of artists including Pusha T, Hopsin, Playboi Carti and The Weeknd.", "annotation_id": "14196881", "url": "https://genius.com/14196881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
