{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It from Nothing", "line": "No better feelin’ seein’ lil Papi talkin French to me", "vault_lines": ["No better feelin' seein' lil Papi talkin French to me"], "meaning": "Meek is talking about his son Rihmeek “papi” Williams, he is able to afford education for papi and hence he can speak french, this makes meek feel good that he is able to provide for his son", "annotation_id": "19578301", "url": "https://genius.com/19578301", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It from Nothing", "line": "Nigga, put some respect up on my last name", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, put some respect up on my last name"], "meaning": "On April 22, 2016, Birdman, one of Meek’s mentors, visited The Breakfast Club for an interview, in which he stated:\n\nPut some respek on my name\n\nAfter the interview aired, the quote went viral and hundreds of memes were made in its honor.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/4jLT7GQYNhI?t=1m30s", "annotation_id": "12400947", "url": "https://genius.com/12400947", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It from Nothing", "line": "Uh, North Philly in my bloodstream, nigga South Philly from my dad genes, nigga I could wear my dad jeans Bought my mom and sister a new crib when that cash came", "vault_lines": ["South Philly from my dad genes, nigga", "I could wear my dad jeans", "Bought my mom and sister a new crib when that cash came"], "meaning": "Meek was born in South Philly and grew up in North Philly. His dad was killed when he was five years old. He rapped about it on his 2012 song “Traumatized”:\n\nWhen I find the nigga that killed my daddy know I'mma ride\nHope you hear me, I'mma kill you nigga\nTo let you know that I don’t feel you nigga\n\nNow that he’s successful, he can fill in for his dad and provide for his family. “Dad jeans” are also a fad amongst middle aged men with no sense of fashion.", "annotation_id": "12380430", "url": "https://genius.com/12380430", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made It from Nothing", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Meek-mill-made-it-from-nothing-lyrics", "genius_title": "Made It from Nothing", "genius_id": 3156917, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "And I’m running straight up in the culo My wrist always on frío", "vault_lines": ["And I’m running straight up in the culo", "My wrist always on frío"], "meaning": "Some very entry level Spanish from Ross here, who has lived in Miami, Florida his entire life.\n\n“Culo” is basically a curse word that means ass/butt/behind\n“Frio” = cold", "annotation_id": "40932360", "url": "https://genius.com/40932360", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "S65, I call it “Rihanna” It got a red top, but it’s white like Madonna", "vault_lines": ["S65, I call it \"Rihanna\""], "meaning": "Ross compares the appearance of his Mercedes Benz S65 AMG Cabriolet to two female pop superstars, Rihanna and Madonna.\n\nHis car has a red convertible top – at the time of this songs release, Rihanna famously had her hair dyed red.\n\n\n\nHowever, Rihanna is from Barbados – the body of Ross’s car is white, like the Queen of Pop, Madonna, who is from Michigan and is very pale.", "annotation_id": "40932314", "url": "https://genius.com/40932314", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Made man, also known as “Papi Chulo” (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["Made man, also known as \"Papi Chulo\" (Ugh)"], "meaning": "Papi chulo can mean a lot of things translated, main ones being pimp daddy or a real cool dude, Ross is reminding you that he is a boss in Spanish", "annotation_id": "31053713", "url": "https://genius.com/31053713", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
