{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "I say shout my driver, Lauren; that ’62 with curtains", "vault_lines": ["I say shout my driver, Lauren; that '62 with curtains"], "meaning": "Drake is in the back of a Maybach 62, a luxury automobile manufactured by Daimler ( Mercedes Benz ) from 2002 to 2012", "annotation_id": "31053669", "url": "https://genius.com/31053669", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Michael Jackson: Let it moonwalk", "vault_lines": ["Michael Jackson: Let it moonwalk"], "meaning": "MJ’s signature dance move was the moonwalk, referring back to the previous line about Ross' yayo “dancing”:", "annotation_id": "2870064", "url": "https://genius.com/2870064", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Got on my blue Dickie, shout out my nigga Roccett", "vault_lines": ["Got on my blue Dickie, shout out my nigga Roccett"], "meaning": "Roccett is a West Coast rapper and known member of the Crips. He was briefly signed to Jeezy’s CTE Word record label, but is now a Rick Ross/MMG affiliate. At the present time, Ross and Jeezy do not like each other.\n\nDickies is a clothing brand that is traditionally associated with gang attire on the West Coast.", "annotation_id": "89232", "url": "https://genius.com/89232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Ashes to ashes, me, Rozay and Khaled", "vault_lines": ["Ashes to ashes, me, Rozay and Khaled"], "meaning": "Ashes to Ashes is the name of Rick Ross' mix tape that he released on Dec. 24, 2010.", "annotation_id": "88293", "url": "https://genius.com/88293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Spending tomorrows money, I call it “Mañana”", "vault_lines": ["Spending tomorrows money, I call it \"Mañana\""], "meaning": "Following on Rozay’s Spanglifications:\n\nDrake knows he’s going to make it big in the game, so he’s spending money he doesn’t have yet (did The Great Recession teach him nothing?!)\n\n(for the non-Spanish speakers, “mañana” means “tomorrow”)\n\nHe pronounces it as “moneyana” bc he said “tomorrow’s money” and tmrw is “mañana” in spanish.", "annotation_id": "88165", "url": "https://genius.com/88165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "I’m Damon Wayans, just know that homie don’t play that", "vault_lines": ["I’m Damon Wayans, just know that homie don’t play that"], "meaning": "“Homie don’t play that” was the catchphrase of Homie D. Clown in the Wayans Brothers sketch show In Living Color. He was played by Damon Wayans.", "annotation_id": "88158", "url": "https://genius.com/88158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Got my revolver, too, I call it “Ving Rhames” You still a baby boy, we doing big things", "vault_lines": ["Got my revolver, too, I call it \"Ving Rhames\"", "You still a baby boy, we doing big things"], "meaning": "Ving Rhames starred in the film Baby Boy. His character snatches a gun away from someone trying to commit suicide.\n\nRevolver is also the aforementioned T-Pain’s fourth studio album.\n\n\n\nRoss is known to name his inanimate objects, such as having a Benz named after Bieber, and continues that trend by naming his gun after Rhames.\n\nRoss is also pointing out the fact that while you are essentially doing nothing, Ross keeps making mogul moves.", "annotation_id": "88046", "url": "https://genius.com/88046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "line": "One of my baddest women ever, I call her “Rihanna” But that’s ’cause her name is Rihanna", "vault_lines": ["One of my baddest women ever, I call her \"Rihanna\"", "But that's 'cause her name is Rihanna"], "meaning": "Hah! Making fun of Rozay’s earlier metaphor!\n\n\n\nDrake was trying to trick us making us think “oh there’s another Rihanna?” (or as if he’s using the name “Rihanna” to represent an ideal, like Dante’s Beatrice)\n\n…but it was actually the singer Rihanna!\n\nUPDATE: Rihanna and Drake are now dating exclusively\n\nUPDATE 2 UPDATE: They broke up!", "annotation_id": "87813", "url": "https://genius.com/87813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made Men", "status": "done", "targets": 12, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-made-men-lyrics", "genius_title": "Made Men", "genius_id": 3091, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made N*GGAZ", "line": "Pillsbury dopeboy, I-I I know all about an oven", "vault_lines": ["Pillsbury dopeboy, I-I I know all about an oven"], "meaning": "Classic double entendre. Game is saying as a drug dealer (dopeboy), he knew all about an oven, because he used to cook cocaine into crack using it.\n\nIt’s also a play on words, of Pillsbury Dough, a type of pre-made dough mix for making crescent rolls. i.e. Game was the chef! Dough is also a slang term for money. As in, Game was caking up.", "annotation_id": "11103019", "url": "https://genius.com/11103019", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made N*GGAZ", "line": "I AM, like Nas’ album cover", "vault_lines": ["I AM, like Nas' album cover"], "meaning": "I AM… is the name of Hip-Hop legend, Nas’s 1999 album. The cover art depicts Nas' face morphed into a Pharaoh’s casket cover.\n\nGame is saying he is a legend like Nas, and also that he is a king, like a Pharaoh of ancient Egypt (Kemet).", "annotation_id": "11100494", "url": "https://genius.com/11100494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Made N*GGAZ", "line": "They speak my name like a myth, when they got me a ghost", "vault_lines": ["They speak my name like a myth, when they got me a ghost"], "meaning": "Someone’s ghostwriting talents are infamous across the industry… See Ghostwriter:\n\nAlso double entendre, contrasting between myth and ghost, as fantasy themes. How, can they speak of him as a myth, if he is a true ghost?…", "annotation_id": "11100420", "url": "https://genius.com/11100420", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
