{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Even once had a job pourin’ tar up on a roof That boy had it hard, no facade, it’s the truth", "vault_lines": ["That boy had it hard, no facade, it's the truth"], "meaning": "Ross is reminiscing on having a job on top of Roof working.", "annotation_id": "40350450", "url": "https://genius.com/40350450", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Look up at the stars, she like, “Honey, where the roof?”", "vault_lines": ["Look up at the stars, she like, \"Honey, where the roof?\""], "meaning": "Ross and his girl are driving around in his Rolls-Royce. The British luxury automobile company offers a Starlight Headliner option for around $13,000. The headliner can be custom ordered to any design; his mimics the night sky so well that she mistakes the roof for the stars.", "annotation_id": "12777077", "url": "https://genius.com/12777077", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "But I thought about my future and the loops I could pin", "vault_lines": ["But I thought about my future and the loops I could pin"], "meaning": "He though about his future, mistakes that he have done.. and awards that if he will work hard he can get.\n\nBy “loops,” Ross probably means loopholes in the system that he could exploit to keep his ill-begotten wealth.\n\nIt’s a double entendre as he is talking about loops in the industry with the upper class but describes it as loops sewed up in clothes by sewing pins. The money he makes is the sewing pin.", "annotation_id": "514389", "url": "https://genius.com/514389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "These hoes so excited, so they catchin’ every drop", "vault_lines": ["These hoes so excited, so they catchin' every drop"], "meaning": "As Rick Ross masturbates, his women like to catch every bit of semen he ejaculates.\n\n\n\nIf the lyric is “the room has turned him on”, this refers to him masturbating at the top of rap game, so hoes (rap listeners) are so excited, they are catch every drop (they like the albums he is “dropping” from the top).", "annotation_id": "487239", "url": "https://genius.com/487239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "I flip my middle finger, I’m chillin’ on twenty million", "vault_lines": ["I flip my middle finger, I'm chillin' on twenty million"], "meaning": "“Fuck you haters; I’ve got 20 million dollars!”—Rozay\n\nWhat a deft, masterfully concise rebuttal. Ross should have a permanent debating spot during the Presidential debates. Hopefully this sort of argumentative mastery will show up, again.\n\nRoss doesn’t care about his haters, he’s rich forever.", "annotation_id": "284342", "url": "https://genius.com/284342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "You eat from the bowl while your dog need a fork", "vault_lines": ["You eat from the bowl while your dog need a fork"], "meaning": "This is basically him just comparing his opponent negatively to himself. It’s a possible continuation of the last line, in which case “pause on the pork” would have also been a homophone rhyme “paws on the pork” meaning he thinks of him as a dog. The line is made wittier by his subtly ironic reference to himself as “your dog,” meaning in this case simply “your boy” or “this guy.”\n\nThis line is a popular saying mostly in other European languages, it means that you, who makes the money and is feeding everybody, is the one not living really extravagant but just eating from a bowl, while his dog, his lower man who might also work for him, are being excessively flashy and spending too much for their standards and what they have accomplished in the game.\n\nIn essence, if you have alot of money you need to train your people to make money too otherwise they’ll just be waiting for handouts and that doesn’t breed loyalty.", "annotation_id": "221525", "url": "https://genius.com/221525", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "A Farrakhan aura, pause on the pork", "vault_lines": ["A Farrakhan aura, pause on the pork"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is comparing his “aura” or demeanor to that of Louis Farrakhan, the leader of the Nation of Islam. Muslim law forbids the consumption of pork. He also uses this line to express his distrust of the law (the “pigs”).", "annotation_id": "221520", "url": "https://genius.com/221520", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Beef I’ll make you thinner, take a seat so we can eat", "vault_lines": ["Beef I'll make you thinner, take a seat so we can eat"], "meaning": "What he means by that is simple.  In the mob, beef = war.  When there is war in the mob, everyone loses lives and money.  Thus gangs become thinner.  “beef / war will make you thinner.”\n\nWhat he means by “take a seat so we can eat” is simply, wars can be avoided when gentleman come together like scenes in the Godfather to come to mutual understandings.", "annotation_id": "190220", "url": "https://genius.com/190220", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "That boy get salad", "vault_lines": ["That boy get salad"], "meaning": "Salad = lettuce = green = money. Ross rolls in cash.\n\nRoss is dabbling in some salad wordplay; blue cheese, from the previous line, is a popular salad topping.", "annotation_id": "190218", "url": "https://genius.com/190218", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "We boys in the hood, and nigga, you lil’ Tre", "vault_lines": ["We boys in the hood, and nigga, you lil' Tre"], "meaning": "Ross is comparing his opponent to Cuba Gooding’s character in the 1991 classic hood drama Boys N The Hood.\n\n\n\nCuba Gooding plays Lil' Tre, a good kid, who is still a virgin, lies about his sexual history, and cries when confronted with the conflicts that arise from dealing with gangsters and criminals in the hood.\n\nTre wasn’t hard, and Ross is Doughboy.", "annotation_id": "112939", "url": "https://genius.com/112939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Smokin’ on a blunt in my own restaurant People lookin’ from a distance think I’m Big Daddy Conch Reincarnated, spirit of a G", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' on a blunt in my own restaurant", "People lookin' from a distance think I'm Big Daddy Conch", "Reincarnated, spirit of a G"], "meaning": "Big Daddy Conch’s is a restaurant in Key West, Florida with a mythical figurehead similiar to Wendy from Wendy’s, though people still question his existence.\n\nWhen tourists see Ross, a rotund fellow, they might think he’s Big Daddy Conch.", "annotation_id": "99391", "url": "https://genius.com/99391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "The bluest of weed Trunk full of white, car smell like blue cheese", "vault_lines": ["Trunk full of white, car smell like blue cheese"], "meaning": "Ross partakes in some color wordplay here.\n\nOf course, “white” = cocaine. “Blue Cheese” is a weed strain, not a dairy product.", "annotation_id": "99383", "url": "https://genius.com/99383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "BMWs on them big thangs lookin’ foolish", "vault_lines": ["BMWs on them big thangs lookin' foolish"], "meaning": "The “big thangs” are huge-ass rims. “Foolish,” which is used to describe his car, is also the title of a Shawty Lo song that Ross refers to in the next line.", "annotation_id": "90704", "url": "https://genius.com/90704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "That Mayweather money lookin’ funny in the light But who really cares? We just throw it in the air Celebratin’ wealth", "vault_lines": ["That Mayweather money lookin' funny in the light", "But who really cares? We just throw it in the air"], "meaning": "Floyd Mayweather is known for posing in photos with his money. Ross suspects that the cash is fake.\n\n\n\nRoss don’t care if the money’s fake, though; he’s finna make it rain.\n\n\n\nRick Ross is dissing Floyd Mayweather because one of the videos that 50 Cent filmed with Ross' baby mama Tia Kemp and his kids was in Mayweather’s mansion.\n\n\n\nRick Ross is also friends with Manny Pacquiao, Mayweather’s main rival in boxing.", "annotation_id": "90701", "url": "https://genius.com/90701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Shawty sitting low, big thangs popping Tip on the Glock from a Crip up in Compton", "vault_lines": ["Shawty sitting low, big thangs popping", "Tip on the Glock from a Crip up in Compton"], "meaning": "He plays with the names of Shawty Lo and T.I. AKA Tip who were beefing at the time of this song’s recording.\n\n“Big Things Poppin'” was one of T.I’s hit songs.\n\nRoss seems to side with T.I. on this one, besides their past beef.", "annotation_id": "49913", "url": "https://genius.com/49913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Mike Vick paid", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is a double entrendre.\n\nMichael Vick is a professional NFL quarterback. At one point, he set the record for highest paid NFL player ever when he signed a $130 million dollar contract with the Falcons. He became the first NFL player to get two $100 million contracts, when he signed a second one with the Eagles in 2011, two years after this song’s release.\n\nHowever, Vick eventually went bankrupt because he was convicted of operating an illegal dogfighting ring, including financing the project and personally executing between six and eight dogs.  He served 21 months on a two-year sentence and has since returned to the NFL.\n\nErgo, Ross could be referring to the fact that Vick is one of the highest paid NFL athletes, or the fact that Vick paid for his crimes.", "annotation_id": "30052", "url": "https://genius.com/30052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "I came up with a strategy to come up mathematically", "vault_lines": ["I came up with a strategy to come up mathematically"], "meaning": "If one purchases coke at price x, then steps it down by factor y…\n\nDon’t get it twisted–just because he says ‘mathematics’ doesn’t mean Ross is a five-percenter\n\nRick Ross admits that he came up with a way to make money by stealing a drug dealers name and rapping about his life. Hence the next line “I did it for my city, now everybody mad at me” Fans are angry that he lied about his past regardless of how good his music is.", "annotation_id": "29905", "url": "https://genius.com/29905", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Kimbo Slice on the pad when I write", "vault_lines": ["Kimbo Slice on the pad when I write"], "meaning": "Despite achieving YouTube immortality, Kimbo Slice has attained only limited success as an MMA fighter.", "annotation_id": "29752", "url": "https://genius.com/29752", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Pull up, hear the dogs, Canaries, they gon’ woof", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, hear the dogs, Canaries, they gon' woof"], "meaning": "The Presa Canario is a Spanish breed, similar to a mastiff, that originated in the Canary Islands.", "annotation_id": "29745", "url": "https://genius.com/29745", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Creflo prayed", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Creflo Dollar is a minister and entrepreneur who preaches Prosperity theology from churches in Georgia and NYC and on a syndicated television show.\n\n\n\nIn response to requests from watchdog group Ministry Watch (and a Senate investigation), he has refused to either disclose his salary or reveal whether he personally profits from donations to his church.\n\nThere may be a prayed/preyed pun here as well.", "annotation_id": "29623", "url": "https://genius.com/29623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "I’m dodgin’ debacles like potholes in Jamaica", "vault_lines": ["I'm dodgin' debacles like potholes in Jamaica"], "meaning": "There are a lot of potholes in Jamaica—it’s a poor country with a lot of infrastructure problems and institutional corruption.\n\n(\n\n\n\nRoss skirts around debacles (failures). Keeping with the driving simile, Ross is a cautious mutha.\n\nNote the mention of “pot” and “Jamaica”.", "annotation_id": "26071", "url": "https://genius.com/26071", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Listenin’ to niggas like whistlin’ at Wendy Williams", "vault_lines": ["Listenin' to niggas like whistlin' at Wendy Williams"], "meaning": "Wendy Williams is a media personality and the host of the syndicated Wendy Williams Show. Before television, she had radio shows on, among other stations, NYC’s Hot 97, where she focused on celebrity gossip.\n\n\n\nThis refers to the fact that listening to haters is as pointless as whistling at Wendy Williams, because she’s unattractive.\n\nAlso note the tremendous alliteration of the letter W.", "annotation_id": "26070", "url": "https://genius.com/26070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Burn the house down (Nigga), you gotta buy another Don’t forget the gas can, jealous stupid motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["Burn the house down (Nigga), you gotta buy another", "Don't forget the gas can, jealous stupid motherfucker"], "meaning": "Reference to 50 Cent’s house mysteriously burning down while only 50’s baby’s mother was in the house. This song (specifically, this line) led to the beef between Ross and 50.", "annotation_id": "26065", "url": "https://genius.com/26065", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Curtis Jackson baby mama, I ain’t askin’ for a cent", "vault_lines": ["Curtis Jackson baby mama, I ain't askin' for a cent"], "meaning": "50 Cent, Curtis Jackson, wanted his baby mama to pay rent for his house that she was leaving in. So Ross is saying he loves to pay her bills and she cant wait to pay her rent, and unlike 50 cent he aint asking for a cent.\n\nNotice the word play with “Cent”, Curtis Jackson is Mr. Cent.\n\nThis song led to 50 Cent vs Rick Ross Beef.", "annotation_id": "25540", "url": "https://genius.com/25540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mafia Music", "line": "Love my handgun, but my choppa still the shit Banned in 1994, but I’m too legit to quit", "vault_lines": ["Love my handgun, but my choppa still the shit", "Banned in 1994, but I'm too legit to quit"], "meaning": "Ross boasts of owning a “choppa” (i.e. an “assault weapon”), even though Congress outlawed their sale in 1994.\n\nBy 2009, when Rick Ross released these rhymes, the Federal Assault Weapons Ban had expired.  Ross implies that he (in contrast with noted non-gangsta, M.C. Hammer) was hard enough to keep his semi-autos in defiance of the law.", "annotation_id": "23416", "url": "https://genius.com/23416", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
