{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Magnificent", "line": "I’m the magnificent with a sensational style", "vault_lines": ["I'm the magnificent with a sensational style"], "meaning": "Ross begins all three of his verses paying homage to Special Ed’s chorus on “I’m The Magnificent” off his 1989 album, Youngest in Charge when he said:\n\nI’m the magnificent with the sensational style\nAnd I can go on and on for like a mile, a minute\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vEMDWdhyrz0", "annotation_id": "20161800", "url": "https://genius.com/20161800", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Magnificent", "line": "Allan Zamren on the case, so you know what you could suck", "vault_lines": ["Allan Zamren on the case, so you know what you could suck"], "meaning": "Allan Stephen Zamren is an attorney in Miami, Florida who represents Rick Ross", "annotation_id": "1962793", "url": "https://genius.com/1962793", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Magnificent", "line": "Nigga, you a clown, here’s the number you should dial Yeah, it start with 305, but we end at four pound", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, you a clown, here's the number you should dial", "Yeah, it start with 305, but we end at four pound"], "meaning": "(305) is Miami’s area code. Ross uses a phone number metaphor to describe how there’s no escaping him. You might start dialing for help, but you won’t be able to finish because Ross will come at you with his Desert Eagle\n\n“Four pound” is common slang used to describe a Desert Eagle .50 cal handgun, which typically weighs four pounds when loaded", "annotation_id": "1962759", "url": "https://genius.com/1962759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Magnificent", "line": "Gold emblem with two M’s in it", "vault_lines": ["Gold emblem with two M's in it"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group’s abbreviation is MMG. Rick Ross wears a necklace with the MMG logo, which has 2 M’s in it", "annotation_id": "1962594", "url": "https://genius.com/1962594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Magnificent", "line": "Sak pase to Zoe Pound, for lifers in O-Town", "vault_lines": ["Sak pase to Zoe Pound, for lifers in O-Town"], "meaning": "“Sak pase” is Creole for “what’s up”. Zoe pound is a street gang in Miami Florida founded by Haitians. O-Town is a reference to Overtown, a town in Dade County (which Ross reps heavily)", "annotation_id": "293274", "url": "https://genius.com/293274", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Magnificent", "line": "I made a transition from the thieves To the biggest executive Def Jam’s ever seen", "vault_lines": ["I made a transition from the thieves", "To the biggest executive Def Jam's ever seen"], "meaning": "He used to be a drug dealer and a bad man but now he’s the biggest boss.\n\nAlso a possible Jay-Z swipe. Jay-Z was famously the president of Def Jam, so Ross might be saying that he’s topping Hova.", "annotation_id": "283107", "url": "https://genius.com/283107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Magnificent", "line": "In memory of Shakir, boss gotta shout Oakland", "vault_lines": ["In memory of Shakir, boss gotta shout Oakland"], "meaning": "Shakir Stewart was a Def Jam executive who committed suicide in 2008 from a self-inflicted gunshot wound.", "annotation_id": "84693", "url": "https://genius.com/84693", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
