{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mahogany Caskets", "line": "She can hit me in the DM or just ask for me [Outro: Rick Ross] @richforever", "vault_lines": ["She can hit me in the DM or just ask for me"], "meaning": "In hip-hop, this lyric means the rapper is so desirable, wealthy, or famous that women do not need to wait in line or go through intermediaries. They can either privately message them (DM) or directly ask them out.The handle “@richforever” is the famous Instagram handle and longtime moniker of rap mogul Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "40206362", "url": "https://genius.com/40206362", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mahogany Caskets", "line": "Was born to be up since a fetus, I kick my feet up", "vault_lines": ["Was born to be up since a fetus, I kick my feet up"], "meaning": "“Born to be up since a fetus”: “Up” in hip-hop slang means being successful, wealthy, or highly motivated. By saying he has been “up since a fetus,” he is claiming that greatness and hustling were in his DNA even before he was born.“I kick my feet up”: This represents ultimate relaxation, luxury, and being stress-free. It means he has built so much wealth and power that he can now sit back comfortably, enjoy his success, and let his money work for him.Combined, it is a way of bragging that his success isn’t new—he was destined for it, and now he is in a position to relax and enjoy the fruits of his labor.", "annotation_id": "40206327", "url": "https://genius.com/40206327", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mahogany Caskets", "line": "I make you rap niggas come and rap for me Helicopters comin’, all my niggas deep", "vault_lines": ["Helicopters comin', all my niggas deep"], "meaning": "Ross’s massive wealth, asserting his dominance in the music industry to the point where he can hire other “rap niggas” to work for him, while simultaneously acknowledging the high-risk, federal-scrutiny reality of his inner circle.", "annotation_id": "40206313", "url": "https://genius.com/40206313", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mahogany Caskets", "line": "I spent a lot on my chain, so send the condiments", "vault_lines": ["I spent a lot on my chain, so send the condiments"], "meaning": "The Chain: Refers to expensive, icy diamond necklaces or jewelry worn by rappers to show wealth and status.\n\nThe Condiments / Sauce: In hip-hop slang, having “sauce” or “condiments” means having style, swag, confidence, and drip.\n\nThe Phrase: It essentially means, “I am showing off expensive jewelry, so I need an equally excessive amount of swag/style to match.", "annotation_id": "40206289", "url": "https://genius.com/40206289", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
