{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Rain (Remix)", "line": "Yeah, I’m in this bitch with the Terror Got a handful of stacks Better grab an umbrella (Remix!) I make it rain, I make it rain", "vault_lines": ["Better grab an umbrella (Remix!)"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne showed up for his feature with Terror Squad, who he refers to as “the Terror”. Terror Squad is a Bronx, New York hip-hop collective that was founded by rapper Fat Joe in 1998 and had various hits going through the 2000s like this song. Wayne obviously has a bunch of money and is about to throw it to make it rain and is potentially also referencing Rihanna’s smash hit “Umbrella” that dropped the same year a couple months earlier and was dominating airwaves in the pop world at the time.", "annotation_id": "39952675", "url": "https://genius.com/39952675", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Rain (Remix)", "line": "I take a chick to my room like caveman", "vault_lines": ["I take a chick to my room like caveman"], "meaning": "Now we know, Kellz.\nThis didn’t age well.", "annotation_id": "24926150", "url": "https://genius.com/24926150", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Rain (Remix)", "line": "If the head right, Ricky there e’ery night", "vault_lines": ["If the head right, Ricky there e'ery night"], "meaning": "This line is an interpolation of The Notorious B.I.G’s “Hypnotize”. In the original song, the lyrics are “Dead right, if the head right, Biggie there e’ry night”. This line has also been interpolated by many other artists such as Ice Cube, Jeezy, Fabolous, and J. Cole.", "annotation_id": "23336137", "url": "https://genius.com/23336137", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Rain (Remix)", "line": "I be drillin’ these chicks like Major Payne", "vault_lines": ["I be drillin' these chicks like Major Payne"], "meaning": "R. Kelly is referring to the Damon Wayans character from the 1995 movie of the same name. Major Payne is a no-nonsense Marine Major placed in charge of a bunch of misfits at a junior ROTC programme who whips them into shape and turns them into winners through intense physical training. Kelly is saying he’s as tough on women sexually", "annotation_id": "14903497", "url": "https://genius.com/14903497", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Rain (Remix)", "line": "Woo! Roxanne!", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "These lines are very similar to the pre-chorus of The Police’s 1978 hit “Roxanne”.\n\nRoxanne\nYou don’t have to put on the red light\n\nIn the Police song, lead singer Sting attempts to convince a prostitute he is in love with to leave her work in the red light district. R. Kelly is parodying those lines, asserting that he doesn’t care what happens to the hooker he has sex with after he uses her services.", "annotation_id": "13461167", "url": "https://genius.com/13461167", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Rain (Remix)", "line": "You see, I order one bottle, then I fuck with one model Then I order more bottles; now, I got more models", "vault_lines": ["You see, I order one bottle, then I fuck with one model", "Then I order more bottles; now, I got more models"], "meaning": "R. Kelly is observing a correlation in the natural world: when he is at the club and purchases a single bottle, he usually has a single model to take home. However — as he observes — when he orders more bottles, he is able to obtain more models.\n\nIt is a logical fallacy to assume that correlation implies causation. However, in this case, we might assume that R. Kelly has an extensive sample size and is able to control for confounding variables (club quality, bottle quality, model quality, etc.) and therefore implying that the bottles are indeed leading to the models.\n\n\n\nNote: R. Kelly does not explicitly imply that there is a linear relationship between models and bottles. In all likelihood there are decreasing returns to scale: at some point, each incremental full bottle ordered will result in less than an full additional model fornicated with.", "annotation_id": "2759", "url": "https://genius.com/2759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Rain (Remix)", "line": "“Skeet-skeet-skeet-skeet, weatherman ’bout to make it rain!”", "vault_lines": ["\"Skeet-skeet-skeet-skeet, weatherman 'bout to make it rain!\""], "meaning": "The phrase “make it rain” has two definitions; one of which is the more common usage, and, “less explicit.” Here, R. Kelly is using what is considered to be the “more explicit” definition: Ejaculating on a woman.\n\nR. Kelly has also called himself a “weatherman” in his aptly titled song, “Weatherman.”", "annotation_id": "2749", "url": "https://genius.com/2749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
