{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Meanin’ I cut and leaf a nigga", "vault_lines": ["Meanin' I cut and leaf a nigga"], "meaning": "A continuation of the previous line, Wale weaves the celebrities' names into a marijuana reference.\n\nA Dutch Master is a cigar that is often cut open and emptied of its tobacco leaves in order to turn it into a blunt.\n\n\n\nWale is saying that if you get in his way, he’ll cut you open and disembowel you just like a blunt.", "annotation_id": "9890551", "url": "https://genius.com/9890551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "But my niggas drinkin’ like them Black Ink niggas Hah, Dutch Ceaser nigga", "vault_lines": ["But my niggas drinkin' like them Black Ink niggas", "Hah, Dutch Ceaser nigga"], "meaning": "Black Ink Crew is a reality television show about tattoo artists in Harlem, New York. The series focuses on Ceaser and Dutchess, the owner and his fiancé.\n\n\n\nWale’s reference is topical, in that several members of the cast have gone to rehab for drinking problems. He’s implying that his friends drink recklessly, and he really couldn’t care less.", "annotation_id": "9890430", "url": "https://genius.com/9890430", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I used to really want that hoe until she hopped on my dick", "vault_lines": ["I used to really want that hoe until she hopped on my dick"], "meaning": "Meek Mill has mentioned numerous of times in the past that one of his goals is to be with Nicki Minaj dating back to 2010.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/meekmill/status/28806530083?lang=en-gb\n\nAs he exclaimed on the Mr. Philadelphia track “Miss Me”,\n\nI love Nicki Minaj, I swear ya’ll I admit it I hope one day I can fuck her just to say I fucking hit it And girl I’m fucking serious I lick it ‘fore I stick it If you ever hear this verse I’m on your top just like a fitted\n\nThe two have been seen together quite regularly in 2014 but never confirmed the rumours. April 2015 Meek Mill confirms the rumours that have been circling that Meek and Nicki was in a relationship.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BGSVdDrL8V8/?taken-by=nickiminaj\n\nSince April 2016 there have been rumors that their relationship is on the rocks. Nicki decided she doesn’t want to be responsible for any man, and this could be Meek’s way of saying he’s already over it.", "annotation_id": "9333280", "url": "https://genius.com/9333280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I used to want a quarter bird ’til I got me a brick I used to want that SRT until I hopped in the Benz", "vault_lines": ["I used to want that SRT until I hopped in the Benz"], "meaning": "A ‘quarter bird’ refers to an ounce of cocaine, while a “brick”  may amount to a pound or kilo of product –  both are a visual of Meek’s old hustle.\n\nA Dodge SRT Viper, commonly referred to as a ‘SRT,’ is a relatively expensive sports car, typically priced at almost $90,000.\n\n\n\nThe Mercedes Benz, a classy, more reputable luxury vehicle, is more often found above the $100,000 price range.\n\n\n\nMilly insinuates that, after spending so much time in the game, his youthful ambitions pale in comparison to all the success he’s achieved. As the next line states, this is especially the case with some women he entertains.", "annotation_id": "9333272", "url": "https://genius.com/9333272", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "And if a nigga step to me, I’ll break the law", "vault_lines": ["And if a nigga step to me, I'll break the law"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has been on tag for a while now for  alleged kidnapping and assault charges. Both Ross and his bodyguard were accused for forcing a lands keeper into a guesthouse and beating him in the head with a handgun, allegedly over money he owed Ross.\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/7gTSbxBvN5/?taken-by=richforever\n\nMeek Mill recently got of tag & house arrest for violating his probation which meant he was not able to release music. Which stopped Meek Mill from releasing any music during the fude with Meek and Drake. The judge allowed Meek to release FREE music as it would of affected his brand.\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BE9aduUikN-/?taken-by=meekmill", "annotation_id": "9333007", "url": "https://genius.com/9333007", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Sellin’ that dope, I went through hell bein’ broke", "vault_lines": ["Sellin' that dope, I went through hell bein' broke"], "meaning": "Before Meek Mill’s singing with Grand Hustle or Maybach Music Meek Mill had to sell dope to get some funds. Most of his funds went to studio sessions in the making of Flamerz 1,2 &3 which was the hottest mixtapes out in Philly at the time.\n\n2005 Meek was arrested for illegally possessing a firearm and assaulting the police when he was 18 years old. He was put on probation. Since then, he has been arrested four times for parole violation. Another violation will result in him being imprisoned.\n\nIn 2008, Mill was convicted of drug dealing and gun possession and was sentenced to 11 to 23 months in prison.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BBMIHUiCkOU/?taken-by=meekmill", "annotation_id": "9332883", "url": "https://genius.com/9332883", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I gotta think of some more shit to want, nigga Oh!", "vault_lines": ["I gotta think of some more shit to want, nigga"], "meaning": "In the last year Meek Mill has not only gotten with the “Baddest Bitch” in the game, Nicki Minaj, but has also managed to score his first No. 1 on the Billboard 200 chart for his album, Dreams Worth More Than Money. With an estimated net worth of $4 million dollars, what else could he ask for?", "annotation_id": "9315317", "url": "https://genius.com/9315317", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Now follow me, front your boy and I’ma make you work", "vault_lines": ["Now follow me, front your boy and I'ma make you work"], "meaning": "To ‘front’ a person typically means to give them a n advanced payment or supply in hopes of being reimbursed later on. Ross is a boss, so he’ll make sure you have the money, but you’ll surely have to “work”  for it.", "annotation_id": "9310662", "url": "https://genius.com/9310662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Now follow me, Balenciagas like they’re Nikes, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Now follow me, Balenciagas like they're Nikes, nigga"], "meaning": "Balenciaga is a luxury, European fashion line by  Cristóbal Balenciaga, a Spanish designer. The shoes are typically priced well into the high hundreds, but Ross bags them like they’re the average pair of Nike’s.\n\n\n\nNotice how Rozay flows with the repetition of the phrase “Now follow me.” He does so almost as if he was personally giving a tour through his extravagant home for the hit TV show, MTV Cribs.", "annotation_id": "9310234", "url": "https://genius.com/9310234", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Bad bitch, she a stripper, now she gettin’ spinach", "vault_lines": ["Bad bitch, she a stripper, now she gettin' spinach"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is certainly one to appreciate strippers and their late-night hustle.\n\nThe dollar bills he makes it rain with bear a resemblance to spinach.\n\n\n\nRozay isn’t the only rapper to compare banknotes to hearty vegetables; Future, Big Sean, Wiz Khalifa, and Schoolboy Q are just a handful of others that have nicknamed their profit after produce.", "annotation_id": "9309781", "url": "https://genius.com/9309781", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "You niggas said they wanted war, we started droppin’ that shit Like oh Lord, oh Lord!", "vault_lines": ["Like oh Lord, oh Lord!"], "meaning": "Recent conflicts outside and within the MMG crew, coupled with the negative attention surrounding its members, have caused a ‘war’-like tension and seem to have put a nick in the Untouchable Maybach Empire. However, with the 4th installment of their collab album series on the way, MMG is preparing to fire back.\n\nFurthermore, this line refers to Meek Mill’s “War Pain” diss-track, which he ‘dropped’ as a late response to attacks by his rap-beef nemesis, Drake.", "annotation_id": "9309664", "url": "https://genius.com/9309664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I used to want a quarter bird ’til I got me a brick I used to want that SRT until I hopped in the Benz I used to really want that hoe until she hopped on my dick", "vault_lines": ["I used to really want that hoe until she hopped on my dick"], "meaning": "A ‘quarter bird’ refers to an ounce of cocaine, while a “brick”  may amount to a pound or kilo of product –  both are a visual of Meek’s old hustle.\n\nA Dodge SRT Viper, commonly referred to as a ‘SRT,’ is a relatively expensive sports car, typically priced at almost $90,000.\n\n\n\nThe Mercedes Benz, a classy, more reputable luxury vehicle, is more often found above the $100,000 price range.\n\n\n\nInsinuating the theme of the song, Milly boasts his “dream-chaser” track record of surpassing his goals and achieving even bigger and better things. So often so, that he may even realize he doesn’t ‘really want’ what he was chasing in the first place – as is the case with the women he entertains.", "annotation_id": "9309655", "url": "https://genius.com/9309655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I used to want all that shit, now I got it", "vault_lines": ["I used to want all that shit, now I got it"], "meaning": "Introducing “Make It Work”, Milly recalls a major theme of his “dream-chaser” series: shooting for his goals and achieving so much more.\n\n\n\n“Make It Work” is thus an appeal to doing what it takes to turn pipe dreams into a reality.", "annotation_id": "9309628", "url": "https://genius.com/9309628", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I done prayed the rappers get the Actavis So they can all go back to just sleepin’ on me", "vault_lines": ["I done prayed the rappers get the Actavis", "So they can all go back to just sleepin' on me"], "meaning": "Wale has always been seen as underrated.\nIn contemporary Hip Hop, where artists like Young Thug and Future are dominating the game with their raps about Codeine and Lean obsession, Wale’s more traditional style is falling into the background.\n\n\n\nHe’s saying that he wants his competitors to drink even more Actavis, a brand of codeine, so that they’ll be overcome by drowsiness and he can return to center stage.", "annotation_id": "9308316", "url": "https://genius.com/9308316", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "You niggas know you fuck around, Meek Milly gettin’ you whacked I used to want a pound of weed, I started flippin’ that crack", "vault_lines": ["You niggas know you fuck around, Meek Milly gettin' you whacked", "I used to want a pound of weed, I started flippin' that crack"], "meaning": "Meek says that if you mess with him, you’re in danger of getting whacked, or killed.\n\n\n\nHe goes on to say that, though he wanted to sell weed, selling ‘the white,’ or cocaine, would be far more profitable.\n\nThus, Milly will do whatever it takes to chase his dreams and make a bolder future happen.\nmore!", "annotation_id": "9305439", "url": "https://genius.com/9305439", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Catchin’ feelings when I pull up in it.... rrrk!", "vault_lines": ["Catchin' feelings when I pull up in it.... rrrk!"], "meaning": "Ross is notorious for his taste in high-end, luxury cars.\n\n\n\n\n\nIt’s no surprise that when he appears on the scene “rrrk!”, some of his onlookers would be impressed, and ‘catchin’ [envious] ‘feelings!’", "annotation_id": "9304239", "url": "https://genius.com/9304239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "You niggas said they wanted war, we started droppin’ that shit Like oh Lord, oh Lord!", "vault_lines": ["Like oh Lord, oh Lord!"], "meaning": "Ever since the beef between Meek and Drake began, both artists have been firing subliminals at each other. In the past couple of months, Meek has been the most active, recently releasing a remix of “All The Way Up” on May 25th, 2016.", "annotation_id": "9303783", "url": "https://genius.com/9303783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "She ridin’ waves, I tell your bitch to surfboard Surfboard, surfboard", "vault_lines": ["She ridin' waves, I tell your bitch to surfboard"], "meaning": "Then I fill the tub up halfway then ride it with my surfboard\nSurfboard, surfboard\n\nReferencing Beyoncé and Jay Z’s hit “Drunk In Love,” Meek shows he’s been taking notes (and taking charge in the, uh, bathtub).", "annotation_id": "9303764", "url": "https://genius.com/9303764", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "It’s the 50 millionaire, mothafuckin’ Don Dada", "vault_lines": ["It's the 50 millionaire, mothafuckin' Don Dada"], "meaning": "This a clear shot at Rozay’s longtime enemy, 50 Cent. It’s interesting to note, however, that Ross' net worth is estimated at $35 Million, $15 Million shy of being a “50 millionaire”. 50 Cent’s net worth on the other hand is estimated at $155 Million, despite him filing for bankruptcy in 2015.\n\nRick was quoted in Rolling Stone saying:\n\nAt this point, my relationship with Curtis is really amusing, due to the fact that I’m the biggest L he ever took.\n\n‘Don Dada’ is a Patois term, defined as “The highest ranking boss in any activity; the most respected.”", "annotation_id": "9303717", "url": "https://genius.com/9303717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Keep changin’ on you like late winter", "vault_lines": ["Keep changin' on you like late winter"], "meaning": "“Keep changing on you like late winter”\n\nWale is tired of lame guys who change up on you like the weather during late winter. This sets up the next line “Springing' = late winter”.\n\nIronically, this is first released track off S4 and first track Meek and Wale appear together on since Meek Mill told wale #UNotMMG for the 2nd time.", "annotation_id": "9303713", "url": "https://genius.com/9303713", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I’m in the 6, I’m ridin’ with a plus 4 She a 10, I fuck her and all her friends, pussy nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm in the 6, I'm ridin' with a plus 4", "She a 10, I fuck her and all her friends, pussy nigga"], "meaning": "‘The 6’ is a common moniker for the city of Toronto, made popular in part by Drake, an artist that was born, raised, and came out of the city.\n\n\n\nTensions between Meek Mill and Drake have been under the public eye since Milly’s ghost writing accusations in 2015, and both rappers have taken to the pen with direct and subliminal jabs at each other.\n\nIn this line, Meek is taunting Drake by saying he’s cruising in the 6 god’s territory, and doing so with a dime, or “6 plus 4.” This beautiful woman is presumably Milly’s girlfriend and fellow rapper, Nicki Minaj.", "annotation_id": "9303662", "url": "https://genius.com/9303662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Parkin’ lot, chicken wings, then we skatin’ off", "vault_lines": ["Parkin' lot, chicken wings, then we skatin' off"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is a huge fan of chicken wings. He’s even endorsed chicken wing franchise Wingstop. According to a 2014 Forbes article, Ross owns nine WingStop franchises in the U.S, but when asked  Ross kept quiet in regards to the number of franchises he actually owns.\n\nIn a sit down interview with Forbes, he explained his love for chickens wings, specifically those made by Wingstop:\n\n I just love Wingstop. As you can see, the energy in here is always fun. It’s always youthful. Not only that, you know they got my favorite lemon pepper wings in the world, so it’s just a natural attraction.", "annotation_id": "9303527", "url": "https://genius.com/9303527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "Now follow me, back to back, we in the Wraith, dog", "vault_lines": ["Now follow me, back to back, we in the Wraith, dog"], "meaning": "Rozay makes a reference to Drake’s “Back To Back,” which was a diss track aimed towards Rick’s MMG signee Meek Mill. In the song, Drake rapped about driving in a Rolls Royce Wraith:\n\nI waited four days, nigga, where y'all at?\nI drove here in the Wraith playin' AR-AB\n\nThis wouldn’t be the first time that Ross has made a reference to the song. On “Color Money,” he flips the now famous line “Is that a world tour or your girl’s tour” into a jab towards Drizzy:\n\nColor money got your bitch out on a world tour\nMy lil homie made a million on his girl tour\n\nBack in 2014, Ross braggadociously posted a video of him purchasing a Rolls Royce Wraith.", "annotation_id": "9303519", "url": "https://genius.com/9303519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I took my talents to South Philly, had to get me a sack", "vault_lines": ["I took my talents to South Philly, had to get me a sack"], "meaning": "This bar conflates Lebron James' infamous 2010 decision to play for the Miami Heat with an anecdote from Milly’s past.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VyvavfpEwbI\n\nMeek Mill has always known he had talent in rapping, and after being released from prison for possession of a firearm, he focused all of his attention on the rap game. He dubs his quick rise to fame in the south of Philly as a ‘sack’ in reference to the Eagles, whose stadium resides in the Southern district.", "annotation_id": "9303517", "url": "https://genius.com/9303517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "I daredevil err’day, nigga Like Hell’s Kitchen and faint vision, oh Lord!", "vault_lines": ["Like Hell's Kitchen and faint vision, oh Lord!"], "meaning": "Daredevil is a Marvel superhero operating in Hell’s Kitchen, New York.  As a child he was accidentally blinded by radioactive waste, but this also resulted in his senses being heightened to superhuman levels. His “radar sense” guides him through any danger he may face.\n\nWale is likely not a vigilante by night, so it’s safe to assume he’s taking on the more literal definition of the word. He’s just a daring dude who simply enjoys the thrill of constantly living life on the edge.", "annotation_id": "9303330", "url": "https://genius.com/9303330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Make It Work", "line": "All my niggas on coke, all these bitches on molly Half my niggas do both, you better get yourself some money", "vault_lines": ["All my niggas on coke, all these bitches on molly", "Half my niggas do both, you better get yourself some money"], "meaning": "Everyone is high at this party – both cocaine and ecstasy (molly) are plentiful.\n\n\n\nThese drugs were probably distributed by Ross himself and his crew, since he states half his homies are drug dealers. He said something similar on his song “Hustlin'”:\n\nSee most of my niggas really still deal cocaine", "annotation_id": "9303244", "url": "https://genius.com/9303244", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
