{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mars", "line": "She’s such a centerfold, you other chicks just run along", "vault_lines": ["She's such a centerfold, you other chicks just run along"], "meaning": "A centerfold is one the most prized locations in a magazine because its where 2 pages are bound side by side in a manner unique to those 2 pages. Basically Ricky is just saying that girl is special compared to other girls", "annotation_id": "2061571", "url": "https://genius.com/2061571", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mars", "line": "Kept a paintbrush, studying The Art of War", "vault_lines": ["Kept a paintbrush, studying The Art of War"], "meaning": "The Art of War is an ancient Chinese military treatise attributed to Sun Tzu, a high-ranking military general, strategist and tactician. The text is composed of 13 chapters, each of which is devoted to one aspect of warfare. It is commonly known to be the definitive work on military strategy and tactics of its time. It has been the most famous and influential of China’s Seven Military Classics, and “for the last two thousand years it remained the most important military treatise in Asia, where even the common people knew it by name.” It has had an influence on Eastern and Western military thinking, business tactics, legal strategy and beyond.\n\n\n\nRick Ross hits a nice line comparing the artistic utensil of a paintbrush to Sun Tzu’s “Art of War”.\nWhat an artistic line.", "annotation_id": "2019812", "url": "https://genius.com/2019812", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mars", "line": "My eyes must be clouded, purple haze", "vault_lines": ["My eyes must be clouded, purple haze"], "meaning": "Purple Haze is a strain of cannabis developed by various Dutch seed breeders known for its purple color, abundance of white trichomes and high potency. It is widely regarded as an extinct strain. The vast majority of seed breeders regard purple haze as a myth due to the fact that any cannabis strain can develop purple calyxs in below optimum temperatures. Purple Haze buds are covered in crystals, giving it an almost sugared look mixed with characteristic purple.\n\n\n\nContrary to popular belief Jimi Hendrix’s song “Purple Haze” is not about the cannabis strain but about a dream he reported to have had.", "annotation_id": "2019740", "url": "https://genius.com/2019740", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Mars", "line": "You’re my fallen angel and I’m here to take you home", "vault_lines": ["You're my fallen angel and I'm here to take you home"], "meaning": "Jay Sean states that she is as beautiful as an Angel that fell down from Heaven. The term “Fallen Angel” originates from the Biblical story of a great war in Heaven and the Archangel Michael casting down the angel Lucifer and his accompanying angels from the palace in the sky onto the surface of the Earth.", "annotation_id": "1787821", "url": "https://genius.com/1787821", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
