{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Nasir", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Nas is short for Nasir, Nasir Jones’ first name", "annotation_id": "39155616", "url": "https://genius.com/39155616", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Where all they do is flex (Flex); call it Milli Vanilli (’Nilli)", "vault_lines": ["Where all they do is flex (Flex); call it Milli Vanilli ('Nilli)"], "meaning": "Magic City most likely refers to a well-known strip club in Atlanta huge in the local rap scene. Flexing means you’re probably spending a lot of cash in the club when you don’t really have the funds.\n\nThe truth will eventually catch up like Milli Vanilli, a sham R&B group whose career went downhill when their outrageous lip-syncing became public.", "annotation_id": "30561724", "url": "https://genius.com/30561724", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "And birthdays was the worst days (Worst days) Last week, I made a hundred on a Thursday (Thursday) And Club Liv got me sinnin’ on a church day", "vault_lines": ["And birthdays was the worst days (Worst days)", "Last week, I made a hundred on a Thursday (Thursday)"], "meaning": "In these lines Meek Mill interpolates The Notorious B.I.G.’s “Juicy”:\n\nNo heat, wonder why Christmas missed us\nBirthdays was the worst days\nNow we sip Champagne when we thirsty", "annotation_id": "21517394", "url": "https://genius.com/21517394", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Cuban links equivalent to having suits on", "vault_lines": ["Cuban links equivalent to having suits on"], "meaning": "A “Cuban link” is a style of chain. It also happens to be the style that MMG uses on their chains.\n\n\n\nRozay has Cuban link chains equal to the amount one would pay for a suit. Also when he wears a Cuban link chain he doesn’t really have to dress up. When people wear suits they are asserting power and style, so all Rozay has to do is throw on a chain and the same effect will take place.", "annotation_id": "1236753", "url": "https://genius.com/1236753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "The chorus cinematic. Going back to Cali (Right)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Continuing the song’s Biggie homages, Ross name-drops the legend’s “Going Back to Cali,”, which was itself a tribute to an LL Cool J song of the same name", "annotation_id": "1143615", "url": "https://genius.com/1143615", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Domino effect (Effect), you in that magic city (City)", "vault_lines": ["Domino effect (Effect), you in that magic city (City)"], "meaning": "Domino effect is an expression meaning that if one thing is affected in some way, everything in the surrounding will be affected by that as well, similar to the falling of dominoes.\n\n\n\nMagic City is a TV series aired on the Starz network which is about Ike Evans, (Played by Jeffrey Dean Morgan) owner of one the most glamorous hotels in Miami in the late 1950s.\n\n\n\nIn the series Evans is forced to make a deal with a mob boss which doesn’t work out how he planned it, so everything goes downhill from there.\n\nRoss is saying that being in this rap game is like you’re in the Magic City. One bad move can put your whole career in jeopardy.", "annotation_id": "1143325", "url": "https://genius.com/1143325", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Young street nigga, late 80's suede Bally’s (Ah!)", "vault_lines": ["Young street nigga, late 80's suede Bally's (Ah!)"], "meaning": "Bally is a Swiss high-end shoe brand and it is pretty popular among rappers. Slick Rick is rocking a pair of these on the cover of his debut album.\n\n\n\nJay-Z spit a similar line on Ain’t No Nigga\n\nA pair of suede Ballys", "annotation_id": "1143299", "url": "https://genius.com/1143299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Through the fire, I stood knowing we would reign", "vault_lines": ["Through the fire, I stood knowing we would reign"], "meaning": "After the hell they went through (setbacks, critics, obstacles), they stand on top of the rap game. They knew this would be the case, as we are all instilled with an meritocratic attitude from a young age, meaning that American values are dependent upon hard work being rewarded.\n\nThere’s also some “rain/ reign” wordplay, which is juxtaposed with the fire they’ve come through.", "annotation_id": "1142733", "url": "https://genius.com/1142733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "I made it so I’m chillin’ now, transparent ceiling now", "vault_lines": ["I made it so I'm chillin' now, transparent ceiling now"], "meaning": "My world view changes the more I learn. I learn daily.\n\nWin some Lose some = the magnificent uncertainty … The beauty of life ..", "annotation_id": "1142288", "url": "https://genius.com/1142288", "state": "verified", "votes": 144, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "My liquid money’s a hypnotist to your misses", "vault_lines": ["My liquid money's a hypnotist to your misses"], "meaning": "Money hypnotizing the next man’s girl\n\nA king’s girl attracted to king shit gets entranced by another king’s paper\n\nOr, a chick who wants more. She will see more n the next dude n be his. Corny, but true in some cases.", "annotation_id": "1142250", "url": "https://genius.com/1142250", "state": "verified", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "I’m like an old blues singer living in the bottle Whose wife left him down in the bottom. Writing songs is how we solvin’ the problem", "vault_lines": ["Whose wife left him down in the bottom. Writing songs is how we solvin' the problem"], "meaning": "Booze (“living in the bottle”) has been many a man’s refuge in times of distress.\n\nThese lines might be inspired by Nas’s father, Olu Dara, a blues-inflected jazz musician, but moreover, Olu Dara had a rocky relationship with his wife and Nas’s mother, Anne Jones. Dara was feautured on Nas’s tribute to his mother, “Dance”, from his album God’s Son.\n\nNas might also be speaking about himself as he had a nasty divorce with Kelis, especially since he says “Writin' songs is how we solvin' the problem”. Nas’s latest album, Life Is Good deals with his personal life, including his marriage to Kelis.\n\nMusic is therapy for him. Also note the word play: It´s the relationship that left him at the bottom the bottle/with a empty bottle all drunk and depressed.", "annotation_id": "1142216", "url": "https://genius.com/1142216", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "It was all a dream. On the corner servin’ all them fiends (All them fiends)", "vault_lines": ["It was all a dream. On the corner servin' all them fiends (All them fiends)"], "meaning": "Mill channels his inner Biggie to bring up his dope dealing past. In “Juicy”, Biggie drops the now-famous line:\n\nIt was all a dream\nI used to read Word Up Magazine\n\nWhile Smalls uses his hip-hop idols as a point of reminiscence, Meek Mill uses his past dope dealing.", "annotation_id": "1142165", "url": "https://genius.com/1142165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Through these Maybach curtains, I see how life has changed", "vault_lines": ["Through these Maybach curtains, I see how life has changed"], "meaning": "Sadly, Maybach’s aren’t around anymore, but one of the brand’s most distinctive features–on both the short 57 and the more pimpin' 62–were the sensual curtains that could instantly create a mobile sex room. Mobile privacy–it’s a perk afforded only to the real movers and shakers of the world", "annotation_id": "1142158", "url": "https://genius.com/1142158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Jewels like Rick the Ruler, looking like I ripped the jeweler (Ooh!)", "vault_lines": ["Jewels like Rick the Ruler, looking like I ripped the jeweler (Ooh!)"], "meaning": "Rapper Rick the Ruler or Slick Rick is—in addition to his eye patch and English accent—well-known for wearing a lot of jewelry.", "annotation_id": "1142108", "url": "https://genius.com/1142108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Stevie J all on the mic, he screamin’ out my birthplace", "vault_lines": ["Stevie J all on the mic, he screamin' out my birthplace"], "meaning": "DJ Stevie J, the guy who was rumored to have kissed Lil Wayne (even though he didn’t), is the in-house DJ at Club Liv on Sundays. .\n\n\n\nHe was also the original person singing the hook of the song, back in July 2012 when Maybach Curtains was leaked as a snippet. .", "annotation_id": "1142091", "url": "https://genius.com/1142091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "(Dreamchasers)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The name of Meek’s Dreamchasers mixtape series and label imprint, Dream Chasers Records—launching just four days before the release of Dreams and Nightmare.", "annotation_id": "933504", "url": "https://genius.com/933504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Curtains", "line": "Put down on that Bentley truck, I used to want the Expedition", "vault_lines": ["Put down on that Bentley truck, I used to want the Expedition"], "meaning": "As a dealer, Meek’s dreams were much smaller: a relatively cheap, hood classic Expedition SUV. When he hit it big, he chose the hella expensive Bentley EXP 9 F Design Concept.\n\nFrom this:\n\n\n\nTo this:", "annotation_id": "933017", "url": "https://genius.com/933017", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
