{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Stuffed shells, thanks to crack, I crack crab and lobsters Not all mobsters imposters, gotcha", "vault_lines": ["Stuffed shells, thanks to crack, I crack crab and lobsters", "Not all mobsters imposters, gotcha"], "meaning": "References Notorious B.I.G’s song “I Love The Dough” featuring Jay-Z:\n“Ridin', decidin' cracked crab or lobster Who say mobsters don’t prosper?”", "annotation_id": "17795583", "url": "https://genius.com/17795583", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Realest shit I ever wrote, chillin’ in my Maybach 8-track episodes, been doin’ this since way back Since way back, since way back 8-track episodes, been doin’ this since way back Realest shit I ever wrote, chillin’ in my Maybach 8-track episodes, been doin’ this since way back Since way back, since way back 8-track episodes, been doin’ this since way back", "vault_lines": ["Realest shit I ever wrote, chillin' in my Maybach", "8-track episodes, been doin' this since way back", "Since way back, since way back"], "meaning": "Jay-Z reminisces to writing down his best while sitting in his old school Maybach luxury car.\n\n\n\nShowing he has been wealthy and on top since way back when the cars featured an 8-track cassette radio.\n\n\n\nThis track is a shout out to Rick Ross' music label: Maybach Music Group eponymous with high-end Mercedes models.", "annotation_id": "12765689", "url": "https://genius.com/12765689", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Holdin’ on that MAC-11, Makaveli premonition Waitin’ on my Suge Knight, one nation under God", "vault_lines": ["Holdin' on that MAC-11, Makaveli premonition", "Waitin' on my Suge Knight, one nation under God"], "meaning": "one nation was the unfinished 2Pac concept album before he died\nhttps://genius.com/albums/2pac/One-nation\nMakaveli is 2pac and Suge Knight was his manager, which means that Ross in his early years was trying to find a mentor or manager", "annotation_id": "11968227", "url": "https://genius.com/11968227", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "They pinchin’ pennies, while I’m musclin’ for mills And that muscle be that muzzle, when I stuff it in your grill", "vault_lines": ["They pinchin' pennies, while I'm musclin' for mills", "And that muscle be that muzzle, when I stuff it in your grill"], "meaning": "Ross double entendre about gangsta finesse\n\npinching uses the finger and very few muscles when contrasting pennies to millions.\n\nthe figurative language comes in when the muscle is actually a gun with a muzzle instead of brute force violence", "annotation_id": "11968194", "url": "https://genius.com/11968194", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "The six-deuce long, the curtains are drawn", "vault_lines": ["The six-deuce long, the curtains are drawn"], "meaning": "There’s some jabs on Jay-Z’s lost Maybach 2 verse, where Rick is talking about the 57 here and Jay is talking about the 62\n\nJay likes the “six deuce” because it’s more spacious and tells other rappers to “catch up” to his level with a double entendre to 57’s heinz ketchup\n\nhttps://genius.com/10506466", "annotation_id": "11968077", "url": "https://genius.com/11968077", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "57, yes, yes, good for a D-Boy", "vault_lines": ["57, yes, yes, good for a D-Boy"], "meaning": "There’s some jabs on Jay-Z’s lost Maybach 2 verse, where Rick is talking about the 57 here and Jay is talking about the 62\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maybach_57_and_62\n\nhttps://genius.com/10506466\n\nJay likes the “six deuce” because it’s more spacious and tells other rappers to “catch up” to his level with a double entendre to 57’s heinz ketchup", "annotation_id": "11968047", "url": "https://genius.com/11968047", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Reach my final destination In the lear, closer to Aaliyah,", "vault_lines": ["reach my final destination", "In the lear, closer to Aaliyah,"], "meaning": "Hov is referencing the untimely passing of his close friend Aaliyah, who died in a plane crash  on August 25, 2001. Learjet is a Canadian manufacturer of business jets for civilian and military use. Although the plane she was travelling in was a Cessna 402, Hov’s point about her cause of death is made.\n\nIn the 2000 horror film Final Destination the main character has a premonition of he and his friends being killed in a plane crash. He prevents the accident, only to have Death hunt them down one by one. Hov knows his time will come eventually, and he cannot avoid death. His only hope when he does pass is that he gets to reunite with Aaliyah, who was also known as Baby Girl.\n\nHov would pass this “lear,” a lesson or instruction, down to his newborn daughter in 2012:\n\nSo there you have it, shit happens\nJust make sure the plane you on is bigger than your carry-on baggage", "annotation_id": "11087489", "url": "https://genius.com/11087489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "It’s eat to kill in the field of hip-hop", "vault_lines": ["It's eat to kill in the field of hip-hop"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to The Killing Fields, a number of sites in Cambodia where large numbers of people were killed and buried by the Khmer Rouge regime, during its rule of the country from 1975 to 1979, immediately after the end of the Cambodian Civil War.\n\nIt is a metaphor for the fierce competition and beefs existing within the hip-hop industry, where Ross still manages to “live large”, despite the rivalries.", "annotation_id": "1110494", "url": "https://genius.com/1110494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Certain things your money can’t buy Like being this fly", "vault_lines": ["Certain things your money can't buy", "Like being this fly"], "meaning": "Double Entendre: Jay-Z is saying that you can’t be as fly as him because he has the best gear on and you don’t have the money for that.\n\nHe is also saying that he is fly already without the addition of expensive clothes, therefore you will never be as fly as him.", "annotation_id": "533747", "url": "https://genius.com/533747", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "The partition roof, translucent and humidor", "vault_lines": ["The partition roof, translucent and humidor"], "meaning": "A humidor is a box with constant humidity that is used to store expensive cigars.", "annotation_id": "222359", "url": "https://genius.com/222359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Heh, what is this? (Maybach Music) I like this Maybach Music (Sweet!) Hahahaha", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This female tagline is now used in many of Ross’s songs. Australian supermodel Jessica Gomes is the voice behind the tag.", "annotation_id": "219541", "url": "https://genius.com/219541", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Revenue incredible, it put me on a pedestal Colombia to Mexico, I figured was a better route", "vault_lines": ["Revenue incredible, it put me on a pedestal"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has made a lot of money and has been elevated by his careers because he was able to get drugs from Columbia to the states efficiently.\n\nInterestingly enough, “Freeway” Rick Ross, the rapper’s namesake, made much of his fortune transporting drugs from Colombia to Los Angeles via Mexico during the Contra scandals of the 1980s.", "annotation_id": "112941", "url": "https://genius.com/112941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "But I don’t see the endin’ through these millionaire lenses Just the two M’s on the emblem", "vault_lines": ["But I don't see the endin' through these millionaire lenses", "Just the two M's on the emblem"], "meaning": "Double entendre: Jay refers to the fact that he is a millionaire and the world in which he views has no ending (as far as making money is concerned, that’s why he only sees the Maybach emblem “Two M’s”), and the fact that he’s wearing Louis Vuitton Million sunglasses:\n\n\n\n“Two M’s” is an abbreviation for million. So he sees millions through millionaire lenses.", "annotation_id": "82075", "url": "https://genius.com/82075", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Ace of Spades", "vault_lines": ["Refrigerators, where Ace of Spades"], "meaning": "Jay references Ace of Spades champagne. He’s also talking about the cards he was dealt, he always has a spare ace up his sleeve\n\nJay-Z is not the creator of Armand de Brignac a.k.a. “Ace of Spades”. Although considering he was the one who introduced the champagne to hip-hop and frankly America (“Ace of Spades” first appeared in the “Show Me What You Got” video before it officially launched in America) and the fact that “Ace of Spades” is hugely stockpiled at the New York 40/40 Club, many speculate that Hov is secretly profiting from the brand.", "annotation_id": "70334", "url": "https://genius.com/70334", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "Remind me of Paul McCartney and Mike fightin’ You know, “The Girl Is Mine”", "vault_lines": ["Remind me of Paul McCartney and Mike fightin'", "You know, \"The Girl Is Mine\""], "meaning": "Jay is comparing the white and black parts of the seats to the conflict in “The Girl is Mine”, a song by Beatles legend Paul McCartney (who is white) and Michael Jackson (who is black, or at least he was at the time). The concept of the song is two men arguing over a girl.\n\n“Mike Fighting” is also “Mic Fighting”, as in the beef he had with Nas – see next line. This all ties in very nicely with the M.J./Paul McCartney reference, as Jay & Nas' feud was allegedly over a girl too.\n\n\n\nNot only is it a reference to the song *The Girl Is Mine,“ but also a reference to the real-life feud between Paul McCartney and Michael Jackson over Michael buying the publishing rights to The Beatles' back catalogue.", "annotation_id": "70332", "url": "https://genius.com/70332", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "I’m like G Rap with better transportation On the road to the riches", "vault_lines": ["I'm like G Rap with better transportation", "On the road to the riches,"], "meaning": "Reference to Kool G Rap, an old rapper who is seen by many to be an influence over Jay-Z. G Rap’s first album was called Road to Riches", "annotation_id": "70331", "url": "https://genius.com/70331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "I’m a major player, 40/40's in Vegas at the Palazzo They said it was not so", "vault_lines": ["I'm a major player, 40/40's in Vegas at the Palazzo", "They said it was not so"], "meaning": "The 40/40 Club, a sports bar chain in which Jay-Z is a co-owner, opened a location in the Palazzo in Las Vegas. Too bad Jay didn’t have more time to reflect on these lyrics, because that 40/40 location closed less than a year after opening.", "annotation_id": "70327", "url": "https://genius.com/70327", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music", "line": "(J.U.S.T.I.C.E. League)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Justice League is a producer trio made up of:\n\n\nErik “Rook” Ortiz\nKevin “Colione” Crowe\nKenny “Barto” Bartolomei\n\n\n\nThey produced this song", "annotation_id": "47264", "url": "https://genius.com/47264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
