{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "That’s right, them mils do, like damp clothes", "vault_lines": ["That's right, them mils do, like damp clothes"], "meaning": "Mildew is a thin whitish coating consisting of minute fungal hyphae, growing on plants or damp organic material such as paper or leather.\n\nThis Line is a witty double Entendre lil wayne usually does with his lines. Mills do/Mildew. Usually when damp/ wet clothing are left in closed areas mildew will grow.", "annotation_id": "17707237", "url": "https://genius.com/17707237", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "Benjamin Franklin on X how that cash roll", "vault_lines": ["Benjamin Franklin on X how that cash roll"], "meaning": "“Rolling” is a colloquial term used to describe being under the influence of MDMA aka ecstasy (shortened here to Ex).\n\nAs Benjamin Franklin’s is the face on the hundred dollar bill, Weezy is saying he rolls (spends) money like Ol' Blue Face Franklin tripping on Molly.", "annotation_id": "15684771", "url": "https://genius.com/15684771", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "Hey, realest shit I ever wrote, chillin’ in my Maybach", "vault_lines": ["Hey, realest shit I ever wrote, chillin' in my Maybach"], "meaning": "T-Pain pays homage to the outro of Ross’s first verse on the original “Maybach Music” song.\n\nIt’s Maybach music, the realest shit I wrote, nigga\nBy an ounce, take a toke\nOf this Maybach music, the realest shit I wrote\nBoss!", "annotation_id": "14184490", "url": "https://genius.com/14184490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "I hit the strip club and girls get extra hype You hit the strip club and girls turn extra dyke", "vault_lines": ["I hit the strip club and girls get extra hype", "You hit the strip club and girls turn extra dyke"], "meaning": "Kanye West is one of the biggest name in the music business and therefore, all the girls will go crazy the moment he enters the strip club.\nKanye raps about a someone who is so ugly, that none of the girls in the club would ever find him on bit of attractive and therefore would never have sex with him or even give him a lap dance.", "annotation_id": "13336402", "url": "https://genius.com/13336402", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "With the Grey Poupon", "vault_lines": ["With the Grey Poupon"], "meaning": "Grey Poupon is a brand of gourmet mustard that originated in Dijon, France. It also has a storied history in hip-hop, and is most commonly associated with wealthy white men.", "annotation_id": "13321243", "url": "https://genius.com/13321243", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "The Kurt Cobain", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Wayne was influenced by Nirvana, having said that he related to Cobain and is also a big fan of Nirvana’s “Smells Like Teen Spirit”.\n\n\n\nWayne even photoshopped himself onto Nirvana’s “Nevermind” cover!", "annotation_id": "7683906", "url": "https://genius.com/7683906", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "These made of rhodium", "vault_lines": ["Shades in all shades, these made of rhodium"], "meaning": "Rhodium is a semi-precious metal used in high end jewelry and eyewear.", "annotation_id": "130615", "url": "https://genius.com/130615", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "And we be strapping up like the Navy SEAL do", "vault_lines": ["And we be strapping up like the Navy SEAL do"], "meaning": "The Navy SEALs are an elite section of America’s Navy specially trained in hand to hand combat, so basically Wayne is saying that his crew keeps as many weapons as the Navy SEALs who also have a lot of weapons", "annotation_id": "78633", "url": "https://genius.com/78633", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "I’m on my feet like tough-actin’ Tinactin", "vault_lines": ["I'm on my feet like tough-actin' Tinactin"], "meaning": "Tinactin is a athlete’s foot medication endorsed by John Madden.\n\n\n\nThe expression “on my feet” could mean three things here:\n\n1) Wayne is standing up (Not possible if he’s currently riding in a Maybach).\n\n2) Weezy is self-sufficient. (He earned $18 million in 2009, the year this song was released).\n\nOr 3) Wayne has recovered from a hardship.", "annotation_id": "30044", "url": "https://genius.com/30044", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "Now I got so many horses, bitches call me Polo", "vault_lines": ["Now I got so many horses, bitches call me Polo"], "meaning": "Polo is a sport where you ride around on horses and hit balls with giant mallets. It’s sort of like a medieval drive-by, so Ross maintains his facade of street-cred with this reference to the amount of Horsepower his car has", "annotation_id": "26936", "url": "https://genius.com/26936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "Fresher than Will Smith and Uncle Phil too", "vault_lines": ["Fresher than Will Smith and Uncle Phil too"], "meaning": "Will Smith is the title character in the series ‘The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air’ and James Avery played his fictional uncle Philip “Uncle Phil” Banks.", "annotation_id": "26377", "url": "https://genius.com/26377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music 2", "line": "All-black Maybach, I’m sittin’ in the asshole", "vault_lines": ["All-black Maybach, I'm sittin' in the asshole"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne’s kickin' it in the back seat of his Maybach.\n\nTaken in isolation, the dumbest line he’s ever spat\n\nHowever, he may call it the “asshole” in comparison to the “cockpit”– in which case the line is a bit brilliant", "annotation_id": "26375", "url": "https://genius.com/26375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
