{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Now it’s Black American Express cards", "vault_lines": ["Now it's Black American Express cards"], "meaning": "The Black American Express Card, a status symbol that only a small handful can obtain.\n\nOfficially known as the Centurion® Card from American Express, it is an exclusive, invitation-only charge card.\n\nThere are no hard-and-fast rules on who gets invited, but it reportedly takes at least $500,000 to $1 million in annual spending.", "annotation_id": "32418281", "url": "https://genius.com/32418281", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "And for the record, kid, my final question is: “How your bitch gon’ feel in that when you two pull up next to this?”", "vault_lines": ["And for the record, kid, my final question is:", "\"How your bitch gon' feel in that when you two pull up next to this?\""], "meaning": "How would your girl feel riding along with you in an old, ugly car and you guys just so happen to stop next to T.I. at a red light, and seeing him in his all new, pimped out Maybach?", "annotation_id": "28463635", "url": "https://genius.com/28463635", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Pull bitches from MIA to ATL in style", "vault_lines": ["Pull bitches from MIA to ATL in style"], "meaning": "Tip is referencing both his and Rozay’s home towns. Rick Ross is from Miami, and T.I. is from Atlanta.", "annotation_id": "28463621", "url": "https://genius.com/28463621", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "My bankroll so well-endowed", "vault_lines": ["My bankroll so well-endowed"], "meaning": "To be well-endowed is to have a lot of something. Tip is saying that he has a large bank account, which according to the website CAKnowledge, he is definitely telling the truth. His net worth clocks in at roughly around $60 Million.", "annotation_id": "28463594", "url": "https://genius.com/28463594", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "[Interlude: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The beat changes gradually after the last hook ends, so this track has 2 different beats, one for Jadakiss verse' & T.I.’s verse and one for Ross'.", "annotation_id": "3001690", "url": "https://genius.com/3001690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Ice cream (Ugh),", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Two meanings for ice cream in this situation:\n\n\n“Ice cream” has been refereed to as crack cocaine for a long time in hip hop. This meaning is supplemented by the later part of the line “pipe dreams”, a reference to dreams that burn with the crack pipe.\nActual ice cream, continuing off of the Cold Stone’s line that appears previously. Cold Stones’s produces some dope ass ice cream though, you would be safe calling it crack.", "annotation_id": "2026862", "url": "https://genius.com/2026862", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Still tote chrome, check my chromosomes", "vault_lines": ["Still tote chrome, check my chromosomes"], "meaning": "Clever wordplay here.\n\n“Chrome” is slang for a firearm, most likely a silver one, as they are both metal and have a certain allure to them.\n\n\n\nIn fact, Rozay always has his gun on him that it’s second nature, almost as if it was in his DNA to carry “chrome”. Chromosomes are highly structured pieces of DNA which contain genes, the basic blueprints for a biological being. Genes can dictate behavior, Ross is implying he was born to hold guns, born to be a G.\n\n\n\nAlso, note the assosnance with “tote”, “chrome” and “chromosomes”, repeating the “o” vowel sound.", "annotation_id": "2026838", "url": "https://genius.com/2026838", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Shine brighter than them bitches on the other side", "vault_lines": ["Shine brighter than them bitches on the other side"], "meaning": "Ross was/is at the apex of his career at this point especially compared to his two major foes at this point: 50 & Jeezy, who were struggling to release their albums.\n\nThen #GIFD dropped & it was all over.", "annotation_id": "1315107", "url": "https://genius.com/1315107", "state": "accepted", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Maybach Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It should be noted that this isn’t the famous ad-lib said by Jessica Gomes.", "annotation_id": "1315100", "url": "https://genius.com/1315100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Me and money got a vendetta", "vault_lines": ["Me and money got a vendetta"], "meaning": "He had money problems back in the past. hence the next line if only he had started selling dope earlier…..", "annotation_id": "391204", "url": "https://genius.com/391204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "I came alive like a moth in the summertime (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["I came alive like a moth in the summertime (Ugh)"], "meaning": "Caterpillars metamorphose into moths in the summertime hence their coming alive.\n\n\n\nLet’s pray for winter.", "annotation_id": "200141", "url": "https://genius.com/200141", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Had the bubble crack, but didn’t have a pot to piss in", "vault_lines": ["Had the bubble crack, but didn't have a pot to piss in"], "meaning": "Not having a pot to piss in (nor a window throw it out of) is an expression of one’s dire poverty.\n\nTaken literally, Ross couldn’t piss in his crack pot, because the fiends might detect the urine’s residue and cease to buy their crack from Ross.", "annotation_id": "93721", "url": "https://genius.com/93721", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Pipe dreams Is what they have when I pull up in that light thing (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Is what they have when I pull up in that light thing (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A pipe dream is a fantastic hope or plan that is generally regarded as being nearly impossible to achieve. So when Jada pulls up in his light-colored Maybach, people have pipe dreams about living like him.", "annotation_id": "75143", "url": "https://genius.com/75143", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Tell the ATF I’m ridin’ with another three-eighty", "vault_lines": ["Tell the ATF I'm ridin' with another three-eighty"], "meaning": "The Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives busted Tip for gun possession in 2007.\n\nFuck it though, he’s got a .380 caliber pistol on him anyway.", "annotation_id": "70832", "url": "https://genius.com/70832", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "And in crowds, catch me in Tao On the strip in Vegas", "vault_lines": ["And in crowds, catch me in Tao", "On the strip in Vegas"], "meaning": "TAO is a premier nightclub in Las Vegas where all the celebrities go for a good-ass time\n\n\n\nThere’s a pic of TIP there with Nelly and Jermaine Dupri", "annotation_id": "70831", "url": "https://genius.com/70831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "I’m in the hood like I’m James Evans", "vault_lines": ["I'm in the hood like I'm James Evans"], "meaning": "James Evans was the leading character in the 70’s sitcom Good Times played by john amos about a family living in the projects in the slums of Chicago.", "annotation_id": "65046", "url": "https://genius.com/65046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Chopper in the trunk, forty-five for the belt (Belt)", "vault_lines": ["Chopper in the trunk, forty-five for the belt (Belt)"], "meaning": "Kiss has the chopper in his maybach trunk, a chopper is a slang term for an assault-rifle specifically an AK-47, and his .45 pistol is for his waist line.", "annotation_id": "65041", "url": "https://genius.com/65041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "I’m in the six-deuce, fifty-sevens for the help (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm in the six-deuce, fifty-sevens for the help (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Jada rides in the 62s Maybach hence the six-deuce\n\n\n\nMeanwhile his help, meaning his bodyguards, are rollin' in the 57s.\n\n\n\nMust be a tough job…", "annotation_id": "65040", "url": "https://genius.com/65040", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Fly to NY, meet me at the Waldorf Astorian,", "vault_lines": ["Fly to NY, meet me at the Waldorf"], "meaning": "Waldorf-Astoria is a historic luxury hotel in NYC, and the meet me at the waldorf part is a reference to a popular expression and song “meet me at the hyphen” which is derived from the hyphen in the hotels name.", "annotation_id": "65039", "url": "https://genius.com/65039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Architecture Victorian", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Although it’s a nice rhyme about the Waldorf-Astoria’s Victorian Architecture, the it’s actually built in the Art Deco style.\n\nIt’s safe to assume Tip doesn’t have a Masters in Architecture.", "annotation_id": "65038", "url": "https://genius.com/65038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Hard times, never heard of those", "vault_lines": ["Hard times, never heard of those"], "meaning": "‘Bach here being short for Maybach, but also a play on words because he’s sitting in the spacious back seat.", "annotation_id": "65037", "url": "https://genius.com/65037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Plus, I keep a dope line, similar to Coldstones (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["Plus, I keep a dope line, similar to Coldstones (Ugh)"], "meaning": "Jadakiss uses some wordplay with “dope line” as he spits “dope lines” in his music that may cause a “dope line” to form to buy his CDs at record stores. Also, speaking from the perspective of a drug dealer, he suggests his “dope line” of customers is just as long as the line of customers wanting to buy the good ice cream sold at Cold Stone Creamery.", "annotation_id": "54136", "url": "https://genius.com/54136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Bitch, bite your tongue, this just ain’t a Mercedes", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, bite your tongue, this just ain't a Mercedes"], "meaning": "Some Mercedes-Benzes can be bought for around $30k. Maybachs, however, can easily cost upwards of $400k. So even though Maybach may be made by Mercedes, they just aren’t in the same league.", "annotation_id": "54134", "url": "https://genius.com/54134", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "Ridin’ in the past like you’re drivin’ a DeLorean", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' in the past like you're drivin' a DeLorean"], "meaning": "A DeLorean is the car used in Back To The Future to travel back in time. Basically he’s saying that your car is old", "annotation_id": "52955", "url": "https://genius.com/52955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "That’s my car cost—y’all thought I would fall off? That was just a small loss, we can have a ball-off", "vault_lines": ["That's my car cost—y'all thought I would fall off?", "That was just a small loss, we can have a ball-off"], "meaning": ".380 refers to two things; the caliber of a gun and the price of his Mercedes ($380,000). You thought that because he went to jail he’d become broke and lose his status in the rap game, but prison was just a “small loss” and he’s back as strong as he was before", "annotation_id": "52953", "url": "https://genius.com/52953", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music III", "line": "No denim on my seats, baby, you gon’ need a towel Ride sexy through the city, see me, you will be aroused", "vault_lines": ["Ride sexy through the city, see me, you will be aroused"], "meaning": "With T.I. having white interior in his car, he doesn’t want any denim dye to bleed and cause discoloration on his seats, so he wants the girl to sit on a towel to prevent that. The towel could also be used to soak up any wetness if the girl gets too aroused while riding through the city in the Maybach.", "annotation_id": "52950", "url": "https://genius.com/52950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
