{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "J.U.S.T.I.C.E. League", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song was produced by J.U.S.T.I.C.E. League (stands for Just Undeniably Some of The Illest Composers Ever) who have produced all three previous entries in the maybach music series for Rick Ross.\nHowever J.U.S.T.I.C.E. League  did not the produce the following entry in the Maybach Music series that was featured on Ross’s 2017 album Rather You Than Me.", "annotation_id": "12951727", "url": "https://genius.com/12951727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Niggas get abused like boys at Penn State", "vault_lines": ["Niggas get abused like boys at Penn State"], "meaning": "Former Penn State football coach Jerry Sandusky was arrested and charged with 52 counts of sexual abuse of young boys occurring over a 15-year period.\n\n\n\nCheck this link to hear Rick Ross speak on the Sandusky controversy.\n\nOther rappers have referenced Sandusky, such as Tyler, The Creator (“P”), Lupe Fiasco (“SNDCLSH In Vegas”), Action Bronson (“Steve Wynn”), and Mac Miller (“Onaroll”).", "annotation_id": "2704929", "url": "https://genius.com/2704929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "It takes greatness to recognize greatness", "vault_lines": ["It takes greatness to recognize greatness"], "meaning": "LA. Reid is truly one of the early pioneers for making Hip Hop Global. He’s been instrumental in curating the success of some of the greatest rappers and singers that have graced the world of R&B, Pop, and Rap. A few noteworthy mentions are: Mariah Carey, Avril Lavigne, Paula Abdul, Pink, Rihanna, Kanye West, Toni Braxton, TLC, Usher, Ne-Yo, Rick Ross, Young Jeezy, Ciara, OutKast, Kerli, and Dido.\n\nLA is able to spot talent from a mile away and knows how to nuture and grow it.", "annotation_id": "1844746", "url": "https://genius.com/1844746", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Greatest that ever did it, decided my own fate", "vault_lines": ["Greatest that ever did it, decided my own fate"], "meaning": "Rick makes a bold statement here that also demonstrates his belief in his work.\n\nRoss believes that he’ll be ONE if not the greatest artist in his time that approached rapped. Yes, this may be a bold statement on his part that many people don’t agree with, but it shows how confident he is about his work, which is something that people will respect.", "annotation_id": "1844703", "url": "https://genius.com/1844703", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "(Oh-oh-oh) The good times don’t last long Just rewind the last song (Ooh, ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Just rewind the last song (Ooh, ooh)"], "meaning": "Rick is a soulful rapper and wants to remain relevant for a long time, that’s why he incorporates so many of the older samples in his songs. He’s paying tribute and also extending the shelf life of some of the classics many of us grew up to.\n\nHe’s telling his listeners to Cherish The Day similar to how Sade did.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g13qTy-llok", "annotation_id": "1844684", "url": "https://genius.com/1844684", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "That’s on the Quran, I’ma go and get the chips", "vault_lines": ["That's on the Quran, I'ma go and get the chips"], "meaning": "Rick Ross references God in multiple songs, and also has an album titled God Forgives, I Don’t. Despite the Islamic reference, the Quran being the Holy Book for Muslims, Rozay is a Christian. It is simply used here to continue the rhyme scheme; “Bible” wouldn’t rhyme well with “a bomb.” However, putting it on the Quran is similar to someone swearing on the Bible – you better believe Ross will get his money.", "annotation_id": "1844598", "url": "https://genius.com/1844598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Maybach IV, the allure that I adore", "vault_lines": ["Maybach IV, the allure that I adore"], "meaning": "This is Ross’s fourth rendition of Maybach Music, which has become a popular song that multiple artist have been featured on (Jay-Z, Jadakiss, Kanye, Lil Wayne, etc…), to name a few.\n\nInterestingly, Ross pays tribute and ties the line *the allure I adore** back to the original Maybach Music’s feature Jay-Z, who made a popular song titled “Allure”.", "annotation_id": "1844571", "url": "https://genius.com/1844571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Yeah, such a breath of fresh air", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, such a breath of fresh air"], "meaning": "Ross is encountered a lot of trails through the year from having seizures, dealing with the back lash listeners, succeeding from his label, and the continued beef with 50 Cent, yet he’s still pushing and making great music.\n\nHis perspective remains fresh, hence the breath of fresh air.", "annotation_id": "1844548", "url": "https://genius.com/1844548", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "We all shared some great times (Uh, uh) As I read some great rhymes (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["We all shared some great times (Uh, uh)", "As I read some great rhymes (Ooh)"], "meaning": "Rozay reminds the listener that by enjoying his Maybach Music, that they are sharing in his celebration of life. That is because being a boss less of an economic state than an ontological one. Even when Ross was broke, he was rapping about the finer things.\n\nTiallondra Kemp Ross baby mommy on his hustle:\n\nIt was almost like he was speaking money into reality. He spoke as if the non-existant was already existent.”\n\nDon’t forget that you are a Boss!", "annotation_id": "1358816", "url": "https://genius.com/1358816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Nigga, assets last while memories fade", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, assets last while memories fade"], "meaning": "You’ll forget about good times and bad times eventually, but assets like gold, real estate, stock, etc. will only flourish or maintain value and significance. If cared for correctly of course. A very unfeeling “Money over everything” line from Ross.", "annotation_id": "1161072", "url": "https://genius.com/1161072", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "All the G’s with me, Maybach Eazy-E", "vault_lines": ["All the G's with me, Maybach Eazy-E"], "meaning": "Rumors have surfaced that Rick Ross is in the process of signing Eazy E’s son ,Lil Eazy E, to Maybach Music Group. Further proof? Or just a nod of respect to the NWA front man who was also surrounded by g’s? You decide.\n\nHe is also referring to himself as Maybach Music’s Eazy-E – as both are/were heads of their own labels.", "annotation_id": "1161062", "url": "https://genius.com/1161062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "There’s no finales around here, baby No finales", "vault_lines": ["There's no finales around here, baby"], "meaning": "Ross reiterated this line in an interview with The Breakfast Club, because it was speculated that the 3rd Maybach Music would be the finale, but Rozay is saying there are no finales in his Maybach Music song series. Maybach Music XII coming in 2020.", "annotation_id": "983145", "url": "https://genius.com/983145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Aged like fine wine, ambitions, they never die", "vault_lines": ["Aged like fine wine, ambitions, they never die"], "meaning": "As wine ages it gets better and becomes more sought after. Rick Ross is saying he will age well and live a great life but his ambitions to get money, cars, and everything else will never fade.", "annotation_id": "948625", "url": "https://genius.com/948625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "It takes a boss to know a boss", "vault_lines": ["It takes a boss to know a boss"], "meaning": "Bosses don’t get much bossier than Reid, who is currently the Chairman and CEO of Epic records, and has a long and storied career as a performer, songwriter, and music exec\n\n\n\nReid was also the chairman and CEO of Island Def Jam Music Group from 2004-2011, around the same time Ross got signed to the label.", "annotation_id": "944816", "url": "https://genius.com/944816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "I’m a Mike Tyson typer, typewriter sniper", "vault_lines": ["I'm a Mike Tyson typer, typewriter sniper"], "meaning": "Mike Tyson in his prime had relentless speed, and accuracy like a sniper.  For context, he won his first nineteen fights by knockout\n\nRick parallels his ability to write hard hitting songs and punchlines in the same manner that Iron Mike would throw punches.", "annotation_id": "937479", "url": "https://genius.com/937479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Black chips, gold bottles, ship it out raw", "vault_lines": ["Black chips, gold bottles, ship it out raw"], "meaning": "Black Chips are usually one of the most valuable chips in poker and ‘Gold Bottles’ is most likely a reference to ‘Ace of Spades’ which is a very expensive champagne that comes in a gold bottle.", "annotation_id": "937262", "url": "https://genius.com/937262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "It’s a female strand, you know life’s a bitch", "vault_lines": ["It's a female strand, you know life's a bitch"], "meaning": "“Feminized” strands of marijuana are “the new technologically advanced strains on the market”", "annotation_id": "936995", "url": "https://genius.com/936995", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Quadrupled my net worth and threw in a few incentives", "vault_lines": ["Quadrupled my net worth and threw in a few incentives"], "meaning": "Rick Ross now has a net worth of over 25 Million dollars. He even got some incentives, meaning the rest of the Maybach Music Group (Wale, Meek Mill, and Omarion) to further push up his net-worth.", "annotation_id": "935979", "url": "https://genius.com/935979", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Lil Cease with me, all the cheese with me", "vault_lines": ["Lil Cease with me, all the cheese with me"], "meaning": "Continuing the Biggie references, Lil Cease is a rapper that was being mentored by The Notorious B.I.G. up until the time of his death. Little Caesars is also a chain of pizza joints. The cheese of the pizza “stays with him” either backstage while preparing for a gig, or in his stomach at all times.", "annotation_id": "935704", "url": "https://genius.com/935704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Southpaw, box a nigga off like a outlaw", "vault_lines": ["Southpaw, box a nigga off like a outlaw"], "meaning": "Rozay is suggesting he’s left-handed, and can beat your ass down with no problem using that very hand.\nOutlaws, when trying to corner somebody, use their cars to effectively box in the victim’s car, and run them off the road, into a ditch, or make them stop, leaving them vulnerable to the wiles of the attacker.\n\n\n\nThere’s also a play on words here, as southpaws are most commonly acknowledged in fighting… Specifically boxing.", "annotation_id": "935671", "url": "https://genius.com/935671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "line": "Same way I love to see a ki’ flip", "vault_lines": ["Same way I love to see a ki' flip"], "meaning": "Triple Entendre, “Key” here could mean:\n\n\nA kilogram of cocaine/heroin (or some other drug) being ‘flipped’ (sold)\nIn relation to the last line, key could also be referring to keys in music\nThe keys for a Maybach (which often flip out with the push of a button)", "annotation_id": "933133", "url": "https://genius.com/933133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music IV", "status": "done", "targets": 23, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-maybach-music-iv-lyrics", "genius_title": "Maybach Music IV", "genius_id": 80550, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music V", "line": "And we lie together, cry together And I swear I hope we fucking die together And I’ll be loving you forever You’re all that I need to get by", "vault_lines": ["You're all that I need to get by"], "meaning": "The chorus starts by interpolating the ending of Notorious B.I.G.’s second verse of “Me & My Bitch”:\n\nAnd then we lie together, cry together\nI swear to God I hope we fuckin' die together\n\nAs Biggie’s lyric implies, Katt and her lover are inseparable and heavily involved in each other’s lives.", "annotation_id": "11714115", "url": "https://genius.com/11714115", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music V", "line": "On the phone, she had me listenin’ to Boyz II Men", "vault_lines": ["On the phone, she had me listenin' to Boyz II Men"], "meaning": "Boyz II Men is an American R&B vocal group that consists of 3 members: Nathan Morris, Wanya Morris, and Shawn Stockman.\n\nThe group rose to fame in the 90’s when they released their hit single “End Of The Road” off their debut album Cooleyhighharmony.\n\n\n\nWith over 60 million albums sold worldwide, Boyz II Men is no doubt one of the most truly iconic and successful R&B groups in music history.", "annotation_id": "11561485", "url": "https://genius.com/11561485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music V", "line": "Food stamps now we dinin’ on islands Diced pineapples, now she’s my piña colada", "vault_lines": ["Food stamps now we dinin' on islands", "Diced pineapples, now she's my piña colada"], "meaning": "This alludes to the idea that women who routinely eat pineapples have sweeter vaginal fluids. Ross likens his lover’s fluids to a piña colada, which is typically made with pineapple juice.\n\nRoss also has a song titled “Diced Pineapples” which also features Wale and Drake.", "annotation_id": "11521019", "url": "https://genius.com/11521019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
