{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music VII", "line": "I’m charging, whatever you afford Crack a card or two, you know I’m so employed She go down, whatever for the boy", "vault_lines": ["I'm charging, whatever you afford", "Crack a card or two, you know I'm so employed", "She go down, whatever for the boy"], "meaning": "Don boasts about setting his own high price or standard. He operates at a level of wealth where he dictates the cost, and people will pay whatever they are capable of just to be in his tax bracket or presence.\n\n“Cracking a card” refers to swiping a black card, credit card, or handling heavy finances. Saying “I’m so employed” is a sarcastic or flipped way of saying his full-time “job” is simply being a ultra-rich boss who constantly makes and spends money.\n\nThis speaks to loyalty or submission driven by status. A woman is willing to do whatever is asked (“go down” or go to great lengths) out of attraction or devotion to “the boy\"—the wealthy boss persona holding the spotlight.", "annotation_id": "41051324", "url": "https://genius.com/41051324", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music VII", "line": "I’m charging, whatever you afford Crack a card or two, you know I’m so employed She go down, whatever for the boy", "vault_lines": ["I'm charging, whatever you afford", "Crack a card or two, you know I'm so employed", "She go down, whatever for the boy"], "meaning": "Don boasts about setting his own high price or standard. He operates at a level of wealth where he dictates the cost, and people will pay whatever they are capable of just to be in his tax bracket or presence.\n\n“Cracking a card” refers to swiping a black card, credit card, or handling heavy finances. Saying “I’m so employed” is a sarcastic or flipped way of saying his full-time “job” is simply being a ultra-rich boss who constantly makes and spends money.\n\nThis speaks to loyalty or submission driven by status. A woman is willing to do whatever is asked (“go down” or go to great lengths) out of attraction or devotion to “the boy\"—the wealthy boss persona holding the spotlight.", "annotation_id": "41051322", "url": "https://genius.com/41051322", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music VII", "line": "I’m chargin’, whatever you afford (Sup) Crack a card or two, you know I’m so employed She go down, whatever for the boy", "vault_lines": ["Crack a card or two, you know I'm so employed", "She go down, whatever for the boy"], "meaning": "Don boasts about setting his own high price or standard. He operates at a level of wealth where he dictates the cost, and people will pay whatever they are capable of just to be in his tax bracket or presence.\n\n“Cracking a card” refers to swiping a black card, credit card, or handling heavy finances. Saying “I’m so employed” is a sarcastic or flipped way of saying his full-time “job” is simply being a ultra-rich boss who constantly makes and spends money.\n\nThis speaks to loyalty or submission driven by status. A woman is willing to do whatever is asked (“go down” or go to great lengths) out of attraction or devotion to “the boy\"—the wealthy boss persona holding the spotlight.", "annotation_id": "41051208", "url": "https://genius.com/41051208", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
