{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music VII", "line": "Keep talking about his money, baby, he ain’t really livin’ Bruce Willis, Armageddon, baby, he ain’t really drillin’ (Haha)", "vault_lines": ["Keep talking about his money, baby, he ain't really livin'", "Bruce Willis, Armageddon, baby, he ain't really drillin' (Haha)"], "meaning": "Jeezy suggests the guy who keeps bragging about his wealth isn’t really living the life he says. He references the 1998 sci-fi disaster film Armageddon starring Bruce Willis as a deep-core driller sent to space to destroy an asteroid on a collision course to Earth. They plan to drill a deep hole into the asteroid to blow it up. “Drilling” is often a street term used for violence.", "annotation_id": "40697307", "url": "https://genius.com/40697307", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music VII", "line": "Hello from the other side, motherfucker like Adele", "vault_lines": ["Hello from the other side, motherfucker like Adele"], "meaning": "Reference to British singer-songwriter Adele’s hit song “Hello” released in 2015:\n\nHello from the other side\nI must’ve called a thousand times\nTo tell you I’m sorry for everything that I’ve done\nBut when I call, you never seem to be home", "annotation_id": "40697258", "url": "https://genius.com/40697258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Maybach Music VII", "line": "Rum is Dominican, that’s if we talkin’ preference Best be Guinness book if we talkin’ about records (Yeah) Quintessa 2018, yeah, I’m on that shit We talkin’ 2025, yeah, I own that shit, shut up", "vault_lines": ["Rum is Dominican, that's if we talkin' preference", "Best be Guinness book if we talkin' about records (Yeah)", "Quintessa 2018, yeah, I'm on that shit", "We talkin' 2025, yeah, I own that shit, shut up"], "meaning": "In relation to rapping about his preference of alcoholic beverages, Jeezy mentions rum, guinness (which is the name of the beer company that also owns the record book and also refers to his 2025 record for largest hiphop orchestra recalling back to the “Just know I had ‘em singing \"Trap or Die” in the bow tie (Yeah)“ line), and he mentions his favorite luxury brand of wine (quintessa).", "annotation_id": "40685335", "url": "https://genius.com/40685335", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
