{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "You choose a pussy or pop a bottle, grow half a mill All you wanted was some entertainment All she wanted was some litigation Exploiting a simple penetration", "vault_lines": ["You choose a pussy or pop a bottle, grow half a mill", "All you wanted was some entertainment", "All she wanted was some litigation", "Exploiting a simple penetration"], "meaning": "Ross details a strikingly similar narrative to what Ludacris has been lamenting elsewhere on the record.\n\nChoices always come back to haunt.. A night at the club, and a rendevous with an attractive woman can end in the courts, paying child support for a kid you never planned on having.", "annotation_id": "5116706", "url": "https://genius.com/5116706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Your potentials of having a billion is only real", "vault_lines": ["Your potentials of having a billion is only real"], "meaning": "You know, Dr. Dre just made a billion. It’s possible!", "annotation_id": "5116684", "url": "https://genius.com/5116684", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Imagine being worth a 100 mill", "vault_lines": ["Imagine being worth a 100 mill"], "meaning": "One of Ross' major dreams on 2014 record Mastermind was to be worth $100 million.\n\nThe truth is actually a little less than that...", "annotation_id": "5116681", "url": "https://genius.com/5116681", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Soon all that Gucci don’t fit, now you out of dough One day your pocket’s alright now they all wrong", "vault_lines": ["Soon all that Gucci don't fit, now you out of dough", "One day your pocket's alright now they all wrong"], "meaning": "A rare Ludacris Double Meaning!!\n\nPurchasing Gucci clothing is an expensive habit, which ties back in with the theme of the song.\n\nLudacris spins this in two ways. Firstly, he explains that when you’re hot, and you’re relevant in the game, your money is good and your figure is good, the Gucci fits perfectly over your sculpted frame. However, when you fall off (in both a physical and metaphorical sense), your game is much less tight than it was. All of a sudden, that Gucci doesn’t physically fit, nor does it fit with your image. It becomes worthless.\n\nHe plays on the word “pockets” to mean both the pockets on your expensive clothing not working anymore, and to indicate you no longer have the bank-roll you once did.", "annotation_id": "5116667", "url": "https://genius.com/5116667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "My young students, let me school ya The diamonds ain’t worth half what you bought them for (no)", "vault_lines": ["My young students, let me school ya", "The diamonds ain't worth half what you bought them for (no)"], "meaning": "One of the biggest problems in the jewellery business is consumers being caught out with lower cut products, spending too much money for them.\n\nA lot of rappers have been called out for rocking fake bling, but the case is that a lot of them have been duped in to paying too much for something that is a fake.", "annotation_id": "5116662", "url": "https://genius.com/5116662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "(BLAHHH) Half the industry going bankrupt", "vault_lines": ["Half the industry going bankrupt"], "meaning": "Whilst a lot of rappers are going broke, it’s a stretch to say that half the industry are going bankrupt. Artists like 50 Cent have managed to diversify their revenue streams in order to financially deal with a loss in musical relevancy.\n\nLudacris might be on his high horse about rappers spending all their money, but it must be remembered much of his $25 million net worth has been accrued via his work in the Fast and Furious franchise. It’s all well and good if you are recieving huge cheques for movies to save your money, but for some rappers struggling day to day it isn’t so easy.\n\nJust ask Ja Rule.", "annotation_id": "5116654", "url": "https://genius.com/5116654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "That car you bought depreciated once you drove off No wonder your baby momma wanna knock your nose off", "vault_lines": ["No wonder your baby momma wanna knock your nose off"], "meaning": "Luda’s advice? Lease your cars. As soon as you drive a car off the lot, it depreciates. Within 2 years, your car has lost half its value. Then, a new car comes out, and you want that as well.\n\nHis advice is: why not lease it? Pay a small fee, give it back after a year, and lease the next new thing.", "annotation_id": "5116648", "url": "https://genius.com/5116648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Can’t keep up the payments, they owe a couple hundred thousand Say they making millions, and bills steady pillin’ Diamonds on their neck, they kids’ stomach out here growlin", "vault_lines": ["Can't keep up the payments, they owe a couple hundred thousand", "Say they making millions, and bills steady pillin'", "Diamonds on their neck, they kids' stomach out here growlin"], "meaning": "This is a pet peeve of his. He was incredibly informative on his Breakfast Club interview, in which he explained that one of the saddest things in the hip hop game is rappers who spend all of their money, and end up struggling.\n\nHis advice at the end of the interview was for rappers to live entirely within their means. Not to buy cars, but to lease them. Not to buy private jets. As easy as the money comes, it can go as well.", "annotation_id": "5116642", "url": "https://genius.com/5116642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "What else can anybody do to me? It ain’t new to me when every time I turn around Another money hungry motherfucker suing me", "vault_lines": ["What else can anybody do to me? It ain't new to me when every time I turn around", "Another money hungry motherfucker suing me"], "meaning": "Ludacris has been sued multiple times over things like stolen lyrics and paternity cases. Right now, nothing would surprise him.", "annotation_id": "5116635", "url": "https://genius.com/5116635", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Get your priorities in order nigga You talk about it, but you really can’t afford it nigga", "vault_lines": ["Get your priorities in order nigga", "You talk about it, but you really can't afford it nigga"], "meaning": "This is particularly shot at people getting loans on unecessary luxury things (like a Mercedes Benz) they barely can afford while they should focus on priorities, like their children’s future or spending on something that his value doesn’t depreciate by half in the first year.", "annotation_id": "5018775", "url": "https://genius.com/5018775", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "My biggest gift and my curse More money, more problems tell me what’s worse", "vault_lines": ["My biggest gift and my curse", "More money, more problems tell me what's worse"], "meaning": "Luda references both Biggie: “Mo money, Mo Problems” and Jay Z’s record The Blueprint 2; The Gift & The Curse to illustrate his point about money, and the rap game, being a blessing and a poison at the same time.", "annotation_id": "4705699", "url": "https://genius.com/4705699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Yeah, rappers foreclosin’ on their houses", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, rappers foreclosin' on their houses"], "meaning": "Rappers always spend it when they got it. Sometimes they fall off and can’t continue to pay their expenses and lose it.\n\nDame Dash for instance..", "annotation_id": "4693017", "url": "https://genius.com/4693017", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "It’s driving me crazy, almost as if this shit was planned out", "vault_lines": ["It's driving me crazy, almost as if this shit was planned out"], "meaning": "The fact that Ludacris own family member needed money had to get it from a mistake his dog made. Dogs are not complex as humans so this incident could’ve been intentional. Ludacris has this in the back of his head and it just is making him more mad", "annotation_id": "4598186", "url": "https://genius.com/4598186", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "You see em’ smiling in the club with their drinks up Don’t let that television fool ya Off camera they sweating and stressin", "vault_lines": ["You see em' smiling in the club with their drinks up", "Don't let that television fool ya", "Off camera they sweating and stressin"], "meaning": "Another example of how “Not everything you see on TV is true”. Examples of rappers who seemed very well of and then turned out to be broke", "annotation_id": "4590613", "url": "https://genius.com/4590613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "That I was told to go to school, graduate and get a job But I’m a Hip Hop cash king, rapper from the South And everybody wants the easy way out", "vault_lines": ["That I was told to go to school, graduate and get a job", "But I'm a Hip Hop cash king, rapper from the South", "And everybody wants the easy way out"], "meaning": "Despite not listening to people’s instructions on how to make money, Luda still reigns with his money and success, and because of that everyone wants the “easy way out” (Any of the problems he stated above)", "annotation_id": "4590595", "url": "https://genius.com/4590595", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "And it don’t help that Forbes reports what I’m makin every year", "vault_lines": ["And it don't help that Forbes reports what I'm makin every year"], "meaning": "When people know how much money he’s making, they line him up in their scopes to shake as much money as they can out of him.\nHe’s been on the Forbes list 6 years straight.", "annotation_id": "4590593", "url": "https://genius.com/4590593", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "I’m getting sued by my own family member, all cause my dog bit her And she was the one who walked up and put her hand out, and now she got her handout", "vault_lines": ["I'm getting sued by my own family member, all cause my dog bit her", "And she was the one who walked up and put her hand out, and now she got her handout"], "meaning": "Apparently, one of Ludacris' family members provoked his dog and then was bit. She went on to sue him, despite him being family. All of it for the money.\n\nNote the play on: “Put her hand out, and now she got her handout”, in which she put her hand out (dog bites it) and she gets her handout (money from Luda)", "annotation_id": "4590588", "url": "https://genius.com/4590588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Getting audited by the government, giving up millions to the IRS Or having to take a paternity test from a bitch I never met", "vault_lines": ["Getting audited by the government, giving up millions to the IRS", "Or having to take a paternity test from a bitch I never met"], "meaning": "Getting audited is having everything you’ve spent reviewed thoroughly to ensure you’re not hiding anything from the government such as undeclared bank transfers and income. Giving up millions to the IRS is mainly due to the high tax rich people have to pay, the higher the income, the higher the tax. Tupac has also had ‘paternity problems’, as shown in “Do For Love”. Ludacris is in the same situation.", "annotation_id": "4590558", "url": "https://genius.com/4590558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Now where do I begin? They send you out to reel you back in And its all for the (money)", "vault_lines": ["Now where do I begin? They send you out to reel you back in", "And its all for the (money)"], "meaning": "People help you get up, and reach the level you are at now (Celebrity rapper, actor…) and then they want to reel you back in (hunt you down/fish) because they want what you have.", "annotation_id": "4590556", "url": "https://genius.com/4590556", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "They on the taste for the (money)", "vault_lines": ["They on the taste for the (money)"], "meaning": "Everyone’s there waiting and looking for the money, like a Great White Shark picking up on blood in the sea…", "annotation_id": "4590551", "url": "https://genius.com/4590551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "Cause envy breeds jealousy, jealousy breeds hate", "vault_lines": ["Cause envy breeds jealousy, jealousy breeds hate"], "meaning": "All of these are very powerful emotions, that often lead to people’s darker sides getting the best of them, these feelings push people to do evil things. A very common saying, many rappers often use this line or very similar ones. Jay Z said “They say success breeds envy”. Game said “Go ahead envy me, I’m rap’s MVP”… All of these examples are a reflection of the reality rappers face once they are famous.", "annotation_id": "4590534", "url": "https://genius.com/4590534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money", "line": "The root of all evil deceiving cause even My closest people tryin’ to get me for my (money)", "vault_lines": ["My closest people tryin' to get me for my (money)"], "meaning": "A quote from 1 Timothy 6:10:\n\nFor the love of money is a root of all sorts of evil, and some by longing for it have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves with many griefs.", "annotation_id": "4590530", "url": "https://genius.com/4590530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
