{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Fly nigga, my nigga, Randall Cunningham", "vault_lines": ["Fly nigga, my nigga, Randall Cunningham"], "meaning": "Randall Cunningham was a former NFL quarterback for the Philadelphia Eagles for 11 seasons, from 1989 to 1995. He was known to have revolutionized the quarterback position for being an all-around player. He was fly as he was on the Eagles, but it can also be said he taught people how to “fly” as he was one of the first quarterbacks to move around the field with precision and swiftness.", "annotation_id": "12152714", "url": "https://genius.com/12152714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "And this my Roc-A-Fella flow And you just on hella dope, I’m hella dope", "vault_lines": ["And this my Roc-A-Fella flow", "And you just on hella dope, I'm hella dope"], "meaning": "The-Dream was never signed to Jay Z’s Roc-A-Fella Records, but in 2012 the singer/songwriter posted a picture to Instagram wearing the infamous Roc chain that all artists received when they signed to the defunct label.\n\nhttps://instagram.com/p/HSvhN2Mz_v/\n\nThe picture helped to start rumors that The-Dream had struck a deal with Jay’s Roc Nation, but he explained in an interview with MTV’s “RapFix Live” that he and Jay were just good friends.\n\nWith this verse and flow The-Dream is drawing comparisons to Hov’s storied label while reminding his drug-addicted competition that he’s “hella dope.”", "annotation_id": "7744439", "url": "https://genius.com/7744439", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Atlanta, Miami, Rosé We like 2Pac and Vante", "vault_lines": ["We like 2Pac and Vante"], "meaning": "The-Dream hails from Atlanta and Ross is from Miami. After establishing that they come from different cities, The-Dream points out that they have great musical chemistry like the late 2Pac and Jodeci producer DeVante Swing.\n\nThough ‘Pac collaborated with Jodeci singers K-Ci and JoJo on 1996’s “How Do U Want It” and again on 1997’s “Toss It Up,” DeVante didn’t produce on those tracks.\n\nThat doesn’t mean 2Pac and DeVante didn’t have chemistry though, they collaborated on “No More Pain” from ‘Pac’s classic All Eyez On Me LP.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O2mCW_swjaE", "annotation_id": "7744247", "url": "https://genius.com/7744247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "In the hood, we the Run-DMCs Best quotes and ropes we don’t need Death Row on foul like Cool C", "vault_lines": ["In the hood, we the Run-DMCs", "Best quotes and ropes we don't need", "Death Row on foul like Cool C"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is comparing himself to Run-DMC, a rap trio who many fans and critics regard as the best hip-hop group of all-time. In the 1980’s Run-DMC had some of rap’s best quotes; they were also huge style icons with their black fedoras and gold rope chains. Ross feels he is a 2015 equivalent; lyrically and stylistically.\n\n\n\nThe Cool C line references the 1980s Philadelphia PA rapper who was convicted of first-degree murder in 1996 and sentenced to death by lethal injection. In December 2004, Cool C was granted a stay of execution.", "annotation_id": "7743193", "url": "https://genius.com/7743193", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "No girl, under 10 No whip under a hundred grand Oh yeah, oh yeah Man, I make this money dance", "vault_lines": ["No girl, under 10", "No whip under a hundred grand"], "meaning": "Dream borrows this couplet from Rozay’s verse on Jay Z’s FuckWithMeYouKnowIGotIt:\n\nI don’t bop, I do the money dance\nMy bitch whip cost a hundred grand\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/359022943717691392\n\nDream reworks it to declare that only the finest women and vehicles are worth his cash. Nothing but dimepieces and luxury cars over here.", "annotation_id": "7741818", "url": "https://genius.com/7741818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "I like that ass fat, I can spread it thin", "vault_lines": ["I like that ass fat, I can spread it thin"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to how a nice  ass can be spread out thin. In the music video, you see he makes hand gestures of a nice ass shape and then a spreading motion.", "annotation_id": "7735735", "url": "https://genius.com/7735735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Black with me everywhere I go, he’ll gun you down Full clips, magazines, yeah, the Forbes list", "vault_lines": ["Black with me everywhere I go, he'll gun you down", "Full clips, magazines, yeah, the Forbes list"], "meaning": "Rozay carries his gun around with him and as you can guess the colour is most probably black. On the gun is a bullet carrying compartment called a magazine. A full magazine with the bullets is called a full clip.\n\n\n\nForbes is a business magazine that annually holds a compilation list of the richest individuals and Rick Ross does appear on the magazine a couple of times since he came into the game in 2006. His debut was however marked in 2009.", "annotation_id": "7735564", "url": "https://genius.com/7735564", "state": "accepted", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Top Forbes, poor formal education", "vault_lines": ["Top Forbes, poor formal education"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' tale is one of giving hope to the less fortunate as education is not always the key\nHowever Rick Ross himself was able to acquire formal education and he even had a football scholarship", "annotation_id": "7735470", "url": "https://genius.com/7735470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Two private jets what a nigga’s worth", "vault_lines": ["Two private jets what a nigga's worth"], "meaning": "Ross just mentioned he’s worth 50 million in the previous bar, so he is approximately worth one Dassault Falcon private jet.", "annotation_id": "7735421", "url": "https://genius.com/7735421", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "50 in the bank, diamonds looking flawless This the sway of a rich nigga", "vault_lines": ["50 in the bank, diamonds looking flawless", "This the sway of a rich nigga"], "meaning": "His ways are not of a poor man thus he has the ability to stack 50 stacks in the bank account or more but he simply downsizes this and his diamonds are not fugazy.", "annotation_id": "7735187", "url": "https://genius.com/7735187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Rub my hands when my palms itch", "vault_lines": ["Rub my hands when my palms itch"], "meaning": "Guess birds of a feather fly together…\n\nAn old folklore says that having itchy palms is a sign that money is coming to you.\n\nhttp://complexmagazine.tumblr.com/post/10419063986", "annotation_id": "7735118", "url": "https://genius.com/7735118", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Caution, I’ll approach you with a business mind", "vault_lines": ["Caution, I'll approach you with a business mind"], "meaning": "This is a definite warning by Rick Ross that he has his business mindset always set and thus no time for love or messing around. It’s always about getting money thus even when he has his girl he is still thinking of money to a point she looks just like it.", "annotation_id": "7735056", "url": "https://genius.com/7735056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Pledge allegiance to the flag Where we keep it 100 or get your money back", "vault_lines": ["Pledge allegiance to the flag", "Where we keep it 100 or get your money back"], "meaning": "The love for the country where Rick Ross in his music tales has made himself rich and richer through underhand means until he gave himself the title Hood Billionaire.", "annotation_id": "7734914", "url": "https://genius.com/7734914", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Secret Service wanna see me driving taxis", "vault_lines": ["Secret Service wanna see me driving taxis"], "meaning": "His run-ins with the law even got to his bentley however it wasn’t really the secret service now was it?", "annotation_id": "7734890", "url": "https://genius.com/7734890", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Hug my attorney and then we do the money dance", "vault_lines": ["Hug my attorney and then we do the money dance"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' run-ins with the law didn’t start recently in fact they begun when he stepped in the game When he won this case among many you can bet he will dance the money dance.\n\nJust in case you wanna know how to do it here is how.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YqSqf5CBPRw", "annotation_id": "7734824", "url": "https://genius.com/7734824", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Tip toeing to court, went there for the past week Leaning on my lawyer, pinky looking glassy Charges dropped, these plaintiffs just wanna tax me", "vault_lines": ["Charges dropped, these plaintiffs just wanna tax me"], "meaning": "In the month of June 2015 Rick Ross had double run-ins with the law on separate occassions and this could be just how it turned out behind the doors of the court.", "annotation_id": "7734803", "url": "https://genius.com/7734803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "More Rakim then maybe Master P Thirsty nigga paid in full, I’m tryna buy the beach", "vault_lines": ["More Rakim then maybe Master P", "Thirsty nigga paid in full, I'm tryna buy the beach"], "meaning": "Rozay is very wealthy similar to how Master P, the former CEO of No Limit Records, was in the 90’s. With this wealth he’s able to buy such things like mansions, cars and even a whole beach.\n\nIt’s no coincidence that Rakim is mentioned before stating that he’s “paid in full” as the phrase was also the title of a song and album by Eric B & Rakim.", "annotation_id": "7729969", "url": "https://genius.com/7729969", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Dance", "line": "Funny to see a ghetto nigga so classy Enchanted by women who speak nasty", "vault_lines": ["Enchanted by women who speak nasty"], "meaning": "Ross is a boss nigga..\n\nNot only because he founded the MMG label. Rozay is always with fine suits, diamonds, sunglass – he’s from the ghetto but with that classy style.\n\nRozay love nasty girls so much that he have a song talking about this.", "annotation_id": "7729814", "url": "https://genius.com/7729814", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
