{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Machine", "line": "Making chips off coke and soda like a vending machine", "vault_lines": ["Making chips off coke and soda like a vending machine"], "meaning": "Gucci sets up a metaphor, comparing the way he makes money (chips) off of selling crack cocaine like a vending machine makes money off of selling soda.\n\nIt doesn’t end there, and is becomes a sustained metaphor containing two double entendres:\n\n  \n \"Coke\" refers to the soft drink Coca-Cola as well as cocaine   \n \"Soda\" refers, again, to Coca-Cola, but also baking soda, which is mixed with cocaine to create crack", "annotation_id": "15202542", "url": "https://genius.com/15202542", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Machine", "line": "Sip so much Codeine and Sprite I need a soda machine", "vault_lines": ["Sip so much Codeine and Sprite I need a soda machine"], "meaning": "‘Lean’, or ‘purple drank’ is a popular narcotic drink. It’s a mixture of Codeine (opiate used as a cough medicine) and Sprite. It became popular in the hip hop community in the southern United States in the 1990s, originating in Houston.", "annotation_id": "12140772", "url": "https://genius.com/12140772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Machine", "line": "Screaming please don’t look me puppet like American Me", "vault_lines": ["Screaming please don't look me puppet like American Me"], "meaning": "American Me is a 1992 crime movie, which has a scene where one of the characters, Puppet, is forced to kill his younger brother, Little Puppet. He does this by strangulation, and while he’s strangling him he’s yelling the phrase “don’t look at me!”", "annotation_id": "10705095", "url": "https://genius.com/10705095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Machine", "line": "And it’s placed parallel to the Carbon 15 With the scope, monkey nuts, and the infrared beam", "vault_lines": ["And it's placed parallel to the Carbon 15", "With the scope, monkey nuts, and the infrared beam"], "meaning": "“Monkey nuts” are 100-round drum magazines which can be equipped to rifles and other firearms. Gucci has attached one to his Carbon 15 automatic rifle, which is also fitted with a scope and a red dot sight so he can’t miss.", "annotation_id": "10624373", "url": "https://genius.com/10624373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Machine", "line": "When I say boss I mean that, ya heard me? I’m so fuck what I sold, my toilet seats solid gold You should see my new palace cause that bitch bigger than Lowe’s", "vault_lines": ["When I say boss I mean that, ya heard me?", "I'm so fuck what I sold, my toilet seats solid gold", "You should see my new palace cause that bitch bigger than Lowe's"], "meaning": "Ross is the boss of Maybach Music Group, and the word “boss” is one of his most-used.\n\nHe’s likely referring to his last two albums, Black Market and Hood Billionaire, both of which underperformed commercially by his standards. Regardless, he’s insanely wealthy, and “palace” is no understatement. The brag that it’s bigger than the huge Lowe’s department store warehouses isn’t an exaggeration.", "annotation_id": "10620170", "url": "https://genius.com/10620170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Machine", "line": "Claim I’m laundering money but where the washing machine?", "vault_lines": ["Claim I'm laundering money but where the washing machine?"], "meaning": "Money laundering is the act of taking illicit funds and making them appear legitimate. Gucci refutes claims that he’s using his music to launder illegal money, which drug dealers have done in the past.\n\nLaundromats are often used for laundering money, hence the laundry machine reference.", "annotation_id": "10615531", "url": "https://genius.com/10615531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money Machine", "line": "Fluorescent lamps in my crib, providing light for my seeds", "vault_lines": ["Fluorescent lamps in my crib, providing light for my seeds"], "meaning": "Gucci is growing marijuana in his own home. Florescent lamps are used for indoor growing operations during the vegetative state while the seeds are still young and fragile.", "annotation_id": "10615509", "url": "https://genius.com/10615509", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
