{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money On My Mind (Remix) [Blow]", "line": "I know, but trip And that .40 make a chip Out a potato-head wimp Then, like ranch, I dip", "vault_lines": ["I know, but trip", "And that .40 make a chip", "Out a potato-head wimp", "Then, like ranch, I dip"], "meaning": "If you “trip”, I’ll make chips out of your “potato” head, i.e. shoot you in your Mr. Potatohead-looking face with my 40-caliber gun), and then I’ll “dip” (take off; also a popular accompaniment to potato chips). Ranch is also popular used as a dip when eating appetizers like vegetables.\n\nMr. Potatohead:", "annotation_id": "11508753", "url": "https://genius.com/11508753", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money On My Mind (Remix) [Blow]", "line": "Holla at ya motherfuckin’ boy, J.R Birdman my pa, bitch Ball bred, born rich", "vault_lines": ["Birdman my pa, bitch", "Ball bred, born rich"], "meaning": "Wayne refers to his mentor Birdman as his “pa” and calls himself Birdman Jr. (or just “J.R.”)\n\n\n\nWeezy was not exactly born with a silver spoon in his mouth – although he did become famous at 15 (maybe he doesn’t remember the Poor Days..)", "annotation_id": "11508748", "url": "https://genius.com/11508748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
