{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money and Powder", "line": "Six wheel G wagon, let ’em wrap it with the ribbon", "vault_lines": ["Six wheel G wagon, let 'em wrap it with the ribbon"], "meaning": "Ross got himself the new 6-Wheel Mercedes-Benz G-Class, and had the dealership put a ribbon on it. This emphasised his rich lifestyle, not only his net worth, but this willingness to spend this money.", "annotation_id": "7796948", "url": "https://genius.com/7796948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money and Powder", "line": "All these other niggas broke and trust is more than just a rumor", "vault_lines": ["All these other niggas broke and trust is more than just a rumor"], "meaning": "Rozay is dissing 50 Cent in this line after a long beef between the two of them. 50 Cent declared bankruptcy recently and Ross is confirming that 50  is indeed broke.", "annotation_id": "7765978", "url": "https://genius.com/7765978", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money and Powder", "line": "Chopper make ’em say uhh, pussy boy no limit", "vault_lines": ["Chopper make 'em say uhh, pussy boy no limit"], "meaning": "Rozay will will bring limitless pain to his victims by executing them with a assault rifle like an AK-47.\n\nInterestingly the “uhh” is an onomatopoeia often used in the context of pain. But the phrase “make ‘em say uhh” was popularized in a song of the same name by Master P, who was also head of No Limit Records.", "annotation_id": "7741788", "url": "https://genius.com/7741788", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Money and Powder", "line": "Polo my new hobby", "vault_lines": ["Brand new red Ferrari , Polo my new hobby"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is suggesting that he is so rich that he has picked up the sport of polo as a hobby.  A game known to be played by extremely wealthy people.  It may also be linked to his previous statement about a Ferrari.  Ferrari’s symbol is a horse which is what people ride while playing polo.", "annotation_id": "7738101", "url": "https://genius.com/7738101", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
