{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "BR-80", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "BR-80 is a digital recorder from BOSS the audio gear company. Thinking Rick Ross is called boss, it is no surprising that he uses the “boss” recorder to record his verse.", "annotation_id": "4532491", "url": "https://genius.com/4532491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Jewelers just wanna meet", "vault_lines": [", jewelers just wanna meet"], "meaning": "Since Ross has been walkin' out the jeweler with no mothafuckin' balance, jewelry sellers have been eager to do business with him.", "annotation_id": "4444850", "url": "https://genius.com/4444850", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Fourteen for that tattoo, worth that dollar bill Only one man got the combination to the safe", "vault_lines": ["Only one man got the combination to the safe"], "meaning": "Ross has enough money that he can drop $14,000 on a tattoo, and confidently say it’s “worth it”.\n\n\n\nFun fact: Ross has over 50 tattoos of dollar signs on his body.\n\nHe’s pretty protective of his money, though – he keeps it in a safe that only he has access to.", "annotation_id": "4408298", "url": "https://genius.com/4408298", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Put the pistol to your mouth now show me to the safe", "vault_lines": ["Put the pistol to your mouth now show me to the safe"], "meaning": "At any given time, Rozay will commit armed robbery. His criminal nature isn’t restricted to just drug crimes.", "annotation_id": "4408295", "url": "https://genius.com/4408295", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Schoolin’ the little niggas, kilos all in the campus", "vault_lines": ["Schoolin' the little niggas, kilos all in the campus"], "meaning": "Ross is helping to fund a new generation of gangsters. Well educated, respected, and connected in society. Kind of like the Japanese Yakuza. This may be in reference to the earlier line:\n\nSee me cousin off to college, I see that it costs a lot\n\nPerhaps Rozay’s cousin is going to be moving product for him at some prestigious school. There’s no better way to squeeze top dollar out of your product than to sell it torich kids.", "annotation_id": "4406440", "url": "https://genius.com/4406440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Grammy nominated once, but I’m still movin’ base", "vault_lines": ["Grammy nominated once, but I’m still movin' base"], "meaning": "Even with his success in the music industry, Rick Ross claims to still be in the drug business.\n\nRick Ross’s sole Grammy nomination was for Best Rap/ Sung Collaboration in 2012 for “I’m On One”.", "annotation_id": "4399317", "url": "https://genius.com/4399317", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "We movin’ weight, I’m at a different pace I’m out in Haïti with my lady screamin’ “n’ap boule”", "vault_lines": ["We movin' weight, I'm at a different pace", "I'm out in Haïti with my lady screamin' \"n'ap boule\""], "meaning": "Ross is so efficient at moving coke that he also finds the time to visit the Caribbean with his girlfriend. “N'ap boule” is an Haitian creole saying meaning “we’re doing well” (often in response to “sak pase”, or, “what’s happening).", "annotation_id": "4377595", "url": "https://genius.com/4377595", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Taz Angels just wanna chill", "vault_lines": ["Taz Angels just wanna chill"], "meaning": "The Mastermind is bragging that the gorgeous Taz Angels want to hang out with him.Taz Angels are a group of models.", "annotation_id": "4377397", "url": "https://genius.com/4377397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Ross is a real boss Cause real bosses don’t go to jail, you feel what I’m sayin’? So yeah that’s what I want y’all to know, you know what I mean? As far as like his thinkin’ patterns you know what I mean? You know I admire y’all The way y’all think, you know what I’m sayin’? And I also admire that I was apart of that foundation from day one You know? Y’all was the good homies Y’all took the baton and ran with it The thing is that I was workin’ towards was The empire is what I was workin’ towards And y’all took the baton and ran with it so it’s nothin’ but love man Anythin’ y’all need me to do from behind these walls, I’mma do it You know what I’m sayin’, without no question", "vault_lines": ["Ross is a real boss", "The thing is that I was workin' towards was", "The empire is what I was workin' towards", "And y'all took the baton and ran with it so it's nothin' but love man", "Anythin' y'all need me to do from behind these walls, I'mma do it", "You know what I'm sayin', without no question"], "meaning": "These words are spoken by Kenneth Williams who’s currently serving a life sentence in jail. In the intro he expresses his admiration for a movement and empire he helped start, the Carol City Cartel, one of the biggest organized crime movements.\n\nRick Ross already paid homage to him on “Hustlin'” off his project Port Miami:\n\nWhen they snatched Black, I cried for a hundred nights\nHe got a hundred bodies, serving a hundred lives\n\nThe use of this sample is similar to J Prince’s use of Larry Hoover’s voice on The Resurrection album. Both suggest the connection between the rap game and the drug game.", "annotation_id": "4374743", "url": "https://genius.com/4374743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "We outta state you know my speakers low", "vault_lines": ["I'm movin' base, we outta state you know my speakers low"], "meaning": "When Ross is out of state he has to keep a low profile – because the feds are on the lookout – hence the low speakers in the whip.", "annotation_id": "4360797", "url": "https://genius.com/4360797", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Hoodies come in all flavors, all black if you think you sweet", "vault_lines": ["Hoodies come in all flavors, all black if you think you sweet"], "meaning": "If you think you’re sweet (running shit), than you can dress like Ross; but you’ve gotta be War Ready. Ross wore a black hoodie in his “War Ready” music video proving that it’s his “riding out” clothes, like an executioner", "annotation_id": "4360706", "url": "https://genius.com/4360706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Gave a job to the children you scared to raise", "vault_lines": ["Gave a job to the children you scared to raise"], "meaning": "This line can be read in two ways:\n\n\nHe is speaking to the parents who don’t care about their children and let them wander in the streets until they get caught up in the drug game.\nHe is speaking to the U.S. government, calling them out for providing little to no opportunities for black males.\n\n\n\nIn either cases, Ross is the last hope these males have to earn money and get out of the hood.", "annotation_id": "4360681", "url": "https://genius.com/4360681", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Rolls Royce Corniche, sweepin’ me off my feet", "vault_lines": ["Rolls Royce Corniche, sweepin' me off my feet"], "meaning": "Ross is enamored by the Rolls Royce Corniche, an old 2 door model manufactured and marketed from 1971-1995. While not the most practical car to ride around in, it is a fine choice of style for a HOOD BILLIONAIRE…", "annotation_id": "4360629", "url": "https://genius.com/4360629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "New mob, suit sharp, my suit Farrahkhan In the house of the lord, my niggas bearin’ arms", "vault_lines": ["New mob, suit sharp, my suit Farrahkhan", "In the house of the lord, my niggas bearin' arms"], "meaning": "The Honorable Minister Louis Farrakhan is the leader of the Nation of Islam, whom Ross has shown love for.\n\n\n\nFarrakhan can definitely dress well, and Ross does the same. However, even when they’re worshipping, Ross and his crew have to stay protected so they keep guns under their suits.", "annotation_id": "4360359", "url": "https://genius.com/4360359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Weed man expensive, three trips a week", "vault_lines": ["Weed man expensive, three trips a week"], "meaning": "Ross only smokes the dankest of marijuana, and his strains are probably very expensive.\n\nOf course his is nothing to Ross, in fact he claims to visit his dealer (or dispensary) 3 times a week. He is a man of great taste so he doesn’t mind spending a lot of money for his weed.", "annotation_id": "4354494", "url": "https://genius.com/4354494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Feds stay up the street Know they tailin’ us close so we leak what we wanna leak", "vault_lines": ["feds stay up the street", "Know they tailin' us close so we leak what we wanna leak"], "meaning": "Ross has always prided himself for being a large part of the drug game in his hood. He considers himself a boss, and is a kingpin in his area.\n\nWhere there are drug lords there are usually federal officers trying to arrest these people. Ross has some of those officers watching his house while he is trying to run a successful drug syndicate.\n\n\n\nRoss controls what they know, though – the only information they get is the information he lets them get, so he stays in the clear.", "annotation_id": "4354444", "url": "https://genius.com/4354444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Grammy nominated once, but I’m still movin’ bass", "vault_lines": ["Grammy nominated once, but I'm still movin' bass"], "meaning": "Young nigga won trappin' a grammy, I-I want a Grammy\n\nAt the 2013 Grammy Awards Ross' fifth studio album God Forgives, I Don’t was nominated for best rap album, but even with the award nomination he’s still is slinging drugs.\n\n\n\nRoss was technically Grammy nominated the previous year when DJ Khaled’s song “I’m On One” was nominated for best rap/sung collaboration, Ross was a featured artist on the record.", "annotation_id": "4354406", "url": "https://genius.com/4354406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "Misses just wanna freak,", "vault_lines": ["Misses just wanna freak,"], "meaning": "Ross has a freaky woman that just want to dance. The dance the want to do in particular is called freaking, or grinding.\n\nThis is just another day in the life of the goddamn boss.", "annotation_id": "4354402", "url": "https://genius.com/4354402", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "R-O-C, double M kill anythin’ we touch", "vault_lines": ["R-O-C, double M kill anythin' we touch"], "meaning": "Roc represents Roc Nation, the label own and run by Jay Z. The other label is MMG, which is owned by Rozay himself.\n\nThese are two of the biggest labels in the Hip Hop industry right now and both labels have signed huge artists in the game today. It is obvious that labels this big kill countless tracks on a daily basis.", "annotation_id": "4354338", "url": "https://genius.com/4354338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "You see the plaques on the wall but the yayo still in the spot See my cousin off to college, I see that it costs a lot", "vault_lines": ["You see the plaques on the wall but the yayo still in the spot", "See my cousin off to college, I see that it costs a lot"], "meaning": "The plaques on the wall are probably 10 of the platinum singles Rozay has been awarded, along with countless other awards.\n\nRoss claims that even though he is well off and famous, he still sells yayo. Yayo is another term for cocaine, a drug which Rick Ross is no stranger to. He even claims to have become rich off of cocaine back in his old hood.\n\n\n\nTuition is no laughing matter, if Rozay’s cousin goes to a good college it will probably pull 6 figures.\n\nIt’s worth noting Rick Ross also attended college at Albany State University.", "annotation_id": "4354322", "url": "https://genius.com/4354322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Movin’ Bass", "line": "You see them plaques on a nigga wall And we movin’ bass Got them records jumpin’ off the store uhh And we movin’ bass Copper tried to knock us off And we movin’ bass Haters throwin’ shots through a niggas door And we still movin’ bass", "vault_lines": ["You see them plaques on a nigga wall", "And we movin' bass", "Got them records jumpin' off the store uhh", "Copper tried to knock us off", "Haters throwin' shots through a niggas door", "And we still movin' bass"], "meaning": "Cause I’m richer and prior to this shit was moving free base\n\nHomophones are Jay Z’s signature mark and he uses them here to switch between “bass/base”, creating two separate meanings for the song’s title.\n\nThe first “bass” refers to the bass line of a track; in his almost 20 years long career he released hundreds of tracks and achieved platinum status 15 times.\n\n\n\nThe second meaning refers to freebase, which is a type of cocaine that is cooked up in a frying pan. Many rappers have been mentioning it, including 2 Chainz.\n\nJay Z has always been more or less open about his drug dealing past, particularly involving crack cocaine but the cops never had anything on him.", "annotation_id": "4354319", "url": "https://genius.com/4354319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
