{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Let y’all fiends use the same needle", "vault_lines": ["Let y'all fiends use the same needle"], "meaning": "Double Entendre:\n\n\nRozay is comparing his music to drugs: music fiends, specifically Ross fans, listen to the same songs and thus share the same needle of his message\nHIV/AIDS is so prevalent amongst injection drug users because when a needle is shared, fluids are exchanged between fiends and the dieses passed.", "annotation_id": "1682494", "url": "https://genius.com/1682494", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Watch the words that you speak", "vault_lines": ["Watch the words that you speak"], "meaning": "Rozay is being sardonic here: it is because of words that he said,\n\nI think I’m Big Meech\n\nthat is his life was threatened, perhaps leading to his attempted murder on his January 28th birthday, 2013.\n\nHe plays with this further on his song “Watch your words pussy niggas”.", "annotation_id": "1682381", "url": "https://genius.com/1682381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Must be mad how I’m ballin’ like I’m Nick Saban National champs, look at my rings", "vault_lines": ["Must be mad how I'm ballin' like I'm Nick Saban", "National champs, look at my rings"], "meaning": "Nick Saban is the current head coach of Alabama. He led LSU to the 2003 National Championship as well as Alabama to the title in 2009, and back to back titles in 2011 and 2012.\n\n\n\nNick Saban is one of the NCAA’s most prominent and hated figures. Likewise, Ross is similarly a prominent and hated figure in the rap game – and Ross knows he is hated is due to his success, much like why Saban is so despised.\n\n\n\nSaban is perhaps NCAA’s best recruiter, his recruiting ability is similar to Ross' as well. Recruiting the likes of Julio Jones and Trent Richardson is similar to how Ross recruited Meek Mill and Wale to his empire.", "annotation_id": "1669950", "url": "https://genius.com/1669950", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Call it dirty money, look at all the joy it brings", "vault_lines": ["Call it dirty money, look at all the joy it brings"], "meaning": "Money Ross makes from dealing large amounts of drugs both brings his family the joy of luxurious living as well as allowing him to give back to a world that has been so kind to a Bawse.\n\n\n\nRoss at a Christmas toy giveaway", "annotation_id": "1669894", "url": "https://genius.com/1669894", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Gavin Maloof, Rick Ross, Micky Arison Bitch I’m a fuckin’ boss", "vault_lines": ["Gavin Maloof, Rick Ross, Micky Arison", "Bitch I'm a fuckin' boss"], "meaning": "Rozay establishes himself as a Boss by placing himself in the same company as high-profile billionaire owners, Gavin Maloof and Micky Arison – the owners of his two favorite basketball teams.\n\nGavin Maloof is apart of the Maloof Family, the owners of the Sacramento Kings. Mickey Arison is the CEO of Carnival Corporation, and the owner of the defending NBA champion Miami Heat.\n\nBy placing himself in their company, Ross seems to insinuate he will one day join them as a billionaire himself.", "annotation_id": "1669671", "url": "https://genius.com/1669671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "DeMarcus Cousins, way of doing things", "vault_lines": ["DeMarcus Cousins, way of doing things"], "meaning": "This is Ross' way of saying “We doing big thangs!”\n\nDeMarcus Cousins is the starting center for the Sacramento Kings, and standing at 6 ft 11 inches and 270 lbs, he is quite a big man, much like Ross.\n\n\n\nRoss has stated that the Sacremento Kings are his second favorite team, and Ross and Cousins are known fans of each other. In fact, Ross was seen reppin' Cousins' jersey in the video for his song “Ashamed”.", "annotation_id": "1669600", "url": "https://genius.com/1669600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Charlie Ward, I play for two teams", "vault_lines": ["Charlie Ward, I play for two teams"], "meaning": "Charlie Ward was a standout college football & basketball player for the Florida State Seminoles. He was a Heisman Trophy winner and apart of the FSU college basketball teams that advanced to the Sweet 16. He would go on to play professional basketball for the New York Knicks.\n\n\n\nThe two teams that Ross is referring to is probably referring to is his record labels – Ross is signed to Def Jam as a solo artist, but is also the founding member of his own record label Maybach Music Group, which is distributed under Atlantic Records.", "annotation_id": "1669599", "url": "https://genius.com/1669599", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "I’m a gold nigga", "vault_lines": ["You a half a man, I'm a gold nigga"], "meaning": "Ross has had 4 of his 5 studio albums be certified gold by the RIAA. He has the Midas Touch.", "annotation_id": "1667432", "url": "https://genius.com/1667432", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Killin’ like makin records, niggas wanna sign you", "vault_lines": ["Killin' like makin records, niggas wanna sign you"], "meaning": "When you’re a successful rapper, you create your label and you sign other rappers.\n\nRoss kills features so easily that others want to hire him, and feature him on their track.", "annotation_id": "1667427", "url": "https://genius.com/1667427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Keep your enemies close", "vault_lines": ["Keep your enemies close"], "meaning": "The old saying goes:\n\nKeep your friends close, keep your enemies closer\n\nThe old saying means to know your friends intentions, but even more so, know what your enemies are doing too. If you are aware of what your enemies are doing, then you are able to prepare yourself for their possible attacks. If you’re ahead of the game, you will be able to succeed in life. Basically, know your surroundings.", "annotation_id": "1667426", "url": "https://genius.com/1667426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "See my chain know the clique fatal", "vault_lines": ["See my chain know the clique fatal"], "meaning": "Rozay’s MMG and Carol City Cartel chains let uniformed folks know that his crew is out here killing the Rap Game.\n\n\n\nAlso, Ross plays on the word “clique” similar to the way it is used in the G.O.O.D. Music anthem – when a hater is close enough to the Boss Don to see his chains, they are a point blank shot away from death.", "annotation_id": "1666699", "url": "https://genius.com/1666699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "She know you niggas monkey niggas", "vault_lines": ["She know you niggas monkey niggas"], "meaning": "Ross is telling his haters that their girlfriends think they behave like primates.\n\nThis is not the first time Ross has played on a traditionally racist stereotype. A common derogatory term for blacks is “monkey”, implying that they behave in a sub-human manner.\n\n\n\nWhen a black person calls another black a term used by whites, they are perceived as an “Uncle Tom” type figure, much like Samuel L Jacksons character in Django Unchained. Interestingly, Ross' 100 Black Coffins was featured in the film and on the soundtrack.\n\n\n\n\n\nThis line and the next use alliteration with the letter “M”", "annotation_id": "1666617", "url": "https://genius.com/1666617", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "I’m the flame that the game needed", "vault_lines": ["I'm the flame that the game needed"], "meaning": "When Hustlin' dropped in 2006, the game was set ablaze by Dade County’s finest. Since then, Ross has proven through making beautiful art that he deserved every bit of acclaim for his original smash it and the countless that have followed. Flame is a synonym for gun as well as what Rozay uses to spark his master joints:", "annotation_id": "1666346", "url": "https://genius.com/1666346", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "I had to take the seats out I had to put that Balmain interior in the Maybach, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I had to put that Balmain interior in the Maybach, nigga"], "meaning": "Rozay’s affinity for Maybachs is well known, (see Maybach Music’s I, II, III, & IV), but even what seems to be perfection can be improved upon.\n\nBalmain is a French designer brand known for its high quality clothing. Imagine a Maybach with a leather interior like this jacket:\n\n\n\nThere is no such thing as good enough for Hip Hop’s Biggest Bawse. Complacency is not an option.\n\nThe covert art for the song seems to depict this.", "annotation_id": "1666282", "url": "https://genius.com/1666282", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Hit, hit, go make another hit", "vault_lines": ["Hit, hit, go make another hit"], "meaning": "Ross has mastered the art of bangology, as striving for excellence is how Bosses stay draped in mink:", "annotation_id": "1658957", "url": "https://genius.com/1658957", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Nigga hatin’ on me send his address to my gmail On my twitter bio why the fuck you think it’s up there?", "vault_lines": ["Nigga hatin' on me send his address to my gmail", "On my twitter bio why the fuck you think it's up there?"], "meaning": "Do you know a fuckboi hating on the Bawse? Well then send his home address to BossUpBusiness@gmail.com (Ross' email address, which like the lyric states is posted on his twitter account) so Ross can have his murks take care of him.", "annotation_id": "1657943", "url": "https://genius.com/1657943", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Hundred black caskets, in honor of Boobie", "vault_lines": ["Hundred black caskets, in honor of Boobie"], "meaning": "A double reference to both Ross' song 100 Black Coffins off the Django soundtrack and the alleged murder charge of Boobie Williams – the founder of the Boobie Boys Miami drug cartel & Ross' friend and mentor.", "annotation_id": "1657925", "url": "https://genius.com/1657925", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "Taylor my britches", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Ross' wealth allows him to buy the nicest of clothing, such as tailored pants. Because Ross is so paunchy, he probably wears size XXXXXXL.", "annotation_id": "1654024", "url": "https://genius.com/1654024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "National Champs", "line": "I fucks with no sex offenders", "vault_lines": ["My lil niggas on fire, I fucks with no sex offenders"], "meaning": "A reference to his “misinterpreted” date rape lyric. Ross had recently come under fire for the lyrics, with Reebok being pressured to drop him from their endorsement deal.\n\n\n\nRoss also tweeted an apology the day before this song was released.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/319847608694738945\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/319866665900834816", "annotation_id": "1649998", "url": "https://genius.com/1649998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
