{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Fucking bitches in the PH, not the PJ’s", "vault_lines": ["Fucking bitches in the PH, not the PJ's"], "meaning": "Ab-Soul probably means that he is fucking bitches in the Penthouse instead of the Projects. His living conditions have changed now that he’s making money.", "annotation_id": "29329014", "url": "https://genius.com/29329014", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "(Saudi)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Saudi is a adlib used by [Asaad aka Saudi Money] who is featured on Stigmata.\n\nSoulo shot outs Asaad for having interpolated part of his verse from Block Boy 2.0 on his 2014 project, Flowers II:\n\nUvex when I pulled up and I popped out\nAnd I hopped out, lookin' fresh\nBalmain leather sweats\nStill fuckin' bitches in the jets\nTo impress", "annotation_id": "6381593", "url": "https://genius.com/6381593", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "[Produced by The Kathy]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The beat constantly says Huahh from the Nae Nae song, which more goes along with the title and theme of the album These Days…", "annotation_id": "3927909", "url": "https://genius.com/3927909", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Powder ain’t my name", "vault_lines": ["To move matter with my brain, powder ain't my name"], "meaning": "Powder is a 1995 American fantasy drama film about Jeremy “Powder” Reed, who has an incredible intellect, as well as telepathy and paranormal powers. The film questions the limits of the human mind and body while also displaying society’s capacity for cruelty, and raises hope that humanity will advance to a state of better understanding.\n\nAb-Soul is comparing the main character in this movie to his previous statement of moving matter with his brain.", "annotation_id": "3378401", "url": "https://genius.com/3378401", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "I’m riding round in that nine My car wash at four, my top down at five", "vault_lines": [", I'm riding round in that nine", "My car wash at four, my top down at five"], "meaning": "4, 5, and 9\n\n“I’m riding round in that nine\nMy car wash at four\nMy top down at five”\n\nRoss opens with great wordplay  in his rare guest appearance:\n\n\n9 is his Porsche 911 maybe even the 911 Turbo S Cabriolet\nRick Ross is such a boss he’s also doing math while rapping about his lavish life 4+5=9\n45 and 9 millimeters are guns – Ross is a gun enthusiast, too.", "annotation_id": "3353102", "url": "https://genius.com/3353102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "That white girl in that pot", "vault_lines": ["That white girl in that pot"], "meaning": "I got a a bad bitch in my Chevy\nSelling Miley Cyrus in my brand new Monte Carlo\n\n“White girl” is slang for cocaine, so Rick Ross says he and his crew are cooking cocaine into crack (thus it is in a cooking pot). Ross and his crew will then presumably sell it on the streets.", "annotation_id": "3351735", "url": "https://genius.com/3351735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Something and I pull up And I hop out looking fresh as Zanerobe leather sweats", "vault_lines": ["Something and I pull up", "And I hop out looking fresh as Zanerobe leather sweats"], "meaning": "Zanerobe is a designer clothing label that is known to be the new up and coming brand for denim joggers or sweats.\n\nThis may be a product placement shout out as Ab-Soul’s label TDE did a collaborative collection of clothing with Zanerobe in 2014.\n\n\n\nAlso, an interpolation of Saudi Money FKA Asaad from his track “Block Boy 2.0” from his 2014 project Flowers II.\n\nUvex when I pulled up and I popped out\nAnd I hopped out, lookin' fresh\nBalmain leather sweats\nStill fuckin' bitches in the jets\nTo impress", "annotation_id": "3351518", "url": "https://genius.com/3351518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Balmain bikers, never rode a motorcycle, no denial (no denial) I just got em cause you got it, when you got em, hah?", "vault_lines": ["Balmain bikers, never rode a motorcycle, no denial (no denial)", "I just got em cause you got it, when you got em, hah?"], "meaning": "He’s referring to these Balmain jeans below that cost $1000 +\n\n“Balmain jeans about a stack a pair” – Danny Brown\n\n\n\nHe knows he comes off as a poser because he’s never rode a motorbike (probably due to his poor vision) but he doesn’t care because having the jeans is a statement that you’re rich.\n\nI guess just like Drake, Ab-Soul has never been one for the preservation of money", "annotation_id": "3348243", "url": "https://genius.com/3348243", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "She wanna be a righteous young rich nigga bitch", "vault_lines": ["She wanna be a righteous young rich nigga bitch"], "meaning": "Ab-Soul is the “Righteous, Young, Rich Nigga” that’s being referred to here.\n\nAs he says on Ride Slow, he…\n\nWalks on the dark side, only to shed light where they ain’t no sun\n\nand\n\nRap as if I had 2 left feet, tryna walk a righteous path\"", "annotation_id": "3348237", "url": "https://genius.com/3348237", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Pill popping, peel a nigga shit", "vault_lines": ["Pill popping, peel a nigga shit"], "meaning": "The worldplay here is with the world “pill”\n\nNot only is Soul popping ecstasy pills, Percocets and more but he also rolls with niggas that are ready to shoot\n\n\n\nBanana Clips = the clip of a gun (specifically a curved ammunition magazine). To peel someone means to unload the clip and let it fly\n\n\n\n“Peel a nigga” is also reference to shooting. It’s peeling the scalp back, otherwise known as pushing a cap/hat/wig back – headshots.", "annotation_id": "3348227", "url": "https://genius.com/3348227", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Three bands on my shades", "vault_lines": ["Three bands on my shades"], "meaning": "A band is a slang reference for $1,000. Rick Ross has plenty of money to blow, so he buys sunglasses worth 3 bands – that’s $3,000 for those of you who don’t know math.\n\nHe wasn’t lying with this one either! You can often catch Rick Ross wearing one-of-a-kind shades from the Vintage Frames Company or Cazal Eyewear.", "annotation_id": "3346777", "url": "https://genius.com/3346777", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "I’m a fucking scripture, nigga we bussin’ scripts (pill poppin’)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a fucking scripture, nigga we bussin' scripts (pill poppin')"], "meaning": "I’m on everything except heroin\n\nThroughout this album, Soul mentions religious themes. This time he directly mentions the scriptures. He doesn’t really care for them, but what he does love are prescription drugs. He pops them on the regular – these drugs most likely aren’t prescribed to Soul.", "annotation_id": "3346757", "url": "https://genius.com/3346757", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Are you a lesbian or a librarian? I know you got room for my dic- (shhh) -Tionary in your library then", "vault_lines": ["Are you a lesbian or a librarian?", "I know you got room for my dic- (shhh)"], "meaning": "Soul asks a rhetorical question knowing this girl isn’t a lesbian – she’s going to give her body up to him. Notice the letters dic were cut off the word dictionary and interrupted by a “Shh.” A librarian wouldn’t allow vulgar language like this in her library, but there’s definitely room for his dicktionary inside her library. This a very clever play on the theme of this girl being a librarian.", "annotation_id": "3346659", "url": "https://genius.com/3346659", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "(M-M-M)", "vault_lines": ["Pop a pill then peel your shit, that's T-M-I but that's R-N-"], "meaning": "This is the well know adlib for the members of Maybach Music Group. This adlib, voiced by Jessica Gomes, is used in practically every MMG record.", "annotation_id": "3343994", "url": "https://genius.com/3343994", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Yeah, you know the name, Top Dawg bitch", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you know the name, Top Dawg bitch"], "meaning": "Stevens was signed with small time independent label Streetbeat Entertainment prior to his signing with TDE in 2007.  Soul tells Complex Magazine:\n\n But [while signed to Beatstreet], I had started working with TDE. That deal was for two years, so as soon as that was up, I built a relationship with TDE and became a member of that family.\n\n\n\nAb continues to express his love for his team, even after certain issues with this albums release.  Aside from the substantial pride he has for his label he, as well as others, show a very competive attitude towards his mates.  Ab Soul tells Life + Times:\n\nI’m from LA, where you got to be a cool nigga and you can’t walk around with too much fear in your heart. That’s just how I was brought up. I’ve walked this earth a long time without the media, so I don’t really see the media being an issue for me. I’m not signed to a major label. I’m signed to Top Dawg. It’s a Top Dawg party, so I’m rolling this project out in a similar fashion to how I rolled out my past projects", "annotation_id": "3318607", "url": "https://genius.com/3318607", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "Money, power and respect, powder in my", "vault_lines": ["Money, power and respect, powder in my"], "meaning": "This is a reference to The LOX’s debut album and song “Money, Power, & Respect”.\n\nThis is also a reference to the video game Money. Power. Respect. which followed the life of Tony Montana a.k.a Scarface kingpin.\n\nIt’s the key to life\nMoney, power, and respect, whatchu' need in life\nMoney, power, and respect, you’ll be eatin' right\nMoney, power, and respect, help you sleep at night\nYou’ll see the light, it’s the key to life", "annotation_id": "3314888", "url": "https://genius.com/3314888", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nevermind That", "line": "No cat in this, I volunteered for these Hunger Games (Soul!)", "vault_lines": ["No cat in this, I volunteered for these Hunger Games (Soul!)"], "meaning": "He says he doesn’t have cat in this meaning that he doesn’t have pussy in him, he isn’t a coward, because he’s a top dog (Top Dawg Ent., the label he’s on)\n\nCat in this is a play on words of Katniss (Everdeen) in the popular book “The Hunger Games” in which a couple poeple from each district are chosen to compete in the Hunger Games or, as Katniss did, they volunteer, which is rare.\n\n\n\nHunger Games for Ab-Soul means surviving hunger and coming out on top in a rough environment.\n\nFun Fact: This is Ab’s favorite punchline on the album.\n\nAnother Fun Fact: The ‘HiiiPoWeR’ hand gesture is the same that is used in The Hunger Games.", "annotation_id": "3314628", "url": "https://genius.com/3314628", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
