{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Top down on my fitted, Pittsburgh like Bettis", "vault_lines": ["Top down on my fitted, Pittsburgh like Bettis"], "meaning": "Jerome Bettis is a former halfback for the Pittsburgh Steelers. Ross name drops Bettis to describe what kind of hat he’s wearing – one that reps the Pittsburgh Steelers", "annotation_id": "2890214", "url": "https://genius.com/2890214", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "I don’t play with kids, bitch I play for keeps", "vault_lines": ["I don’t play with kids, bitch I play for keeps"], "meaning": "The phrase, playing for keeps, is said to have originated in the mid 19th century in reference to the game of marbles.  When playing for keeps, each child would bring his/her own collection and if one lost, one would also lose ones marbles to ones opponent. Most kids don’t play for keeps because the stakes are simply too high for them.\n\nKRIT speaks to his confidence in his abilities, stating he will only participate if it is worth his while.", "annotation_id": "2879350", "url": "https://genius.com/2879350", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Diamonds in the back seat will surely crush", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds in the back seat will surely crush"], "meaning": "The rear window of the 1970-1980 Cadillac series was diamond shaped.  It will surely be impressionable.", "annotation_id": "2879335", "url": "https://genius.com/2879335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Doin’ two a days in my Cadillac", "vault_lines": ["Doin' two a days in my Cadillac"], "meaning": "Two-a-days in an athletic term for working out or practicing twice in one day.  KRIT is doing work and still looking good in his (presumably) old school Cadillac.", "annotation_id": "2879276", "url": "https://genius.com/2879276", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "And one last request: bury me in my rings", "vault_lines": ["And one last request: bury me in my rings"], "meaning": "Like many powerful people in ancient times, Ross’s new agenda is to be buried with jewels and other material signs of his success (and with his dawgs!)", "annotation_id": "2878640", "url": "https://genius.com/2878640", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "All I chase is that lettuce", "vault_lines": ["Hatin' niggas so petty, all I chase is that lettuce"], "meaning": "Ross is after money – often referred to as lettuce because of their similar green color", "annotation_id": "2878587", "url": "https://genius.com/2878587", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Takes a lot of shine just to Supernova", "vault_lines": ["Takes a lot of shine just to Supernova"], "meaning": "KRIT plays on the name of the old school Chevy and the supernova explosions that shine bright in the sky, using the wordplay to say that you have to work hard and get big to be able to ball with a car like the Supernova\n\n\n\nKRIT has likened his shine to a supernova before", "annotation_id": "2876533", "url": "https://genius.com/2876533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "If you don’t know I’m with it then you don’t know the shine", "vault_lines": ["If you don’t know I’m with it then you don’t know the shine"], "meaning": "KRIT has had a lot to say about shining in his music, so you should already know what he’s about", "annotation_id": "2876510", "url": "https://genius.com/2876510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "See me on that cover of Rolling Stone’s embellished Diamonds drip from my neck, them tats all on my belly", "vault_lines": ["See me on that cover of Rolling Stone's embellished", "Diamonds drip from my neck, them tats all on my belly"], "meaning": "Referring to Ross’s August 2012 Rolling Stone cover, which was a flamboyant display of Rozay excess.", "annotation_id": "2876498", "url": "https://genius.com/2876498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "He ain’t give you money to give to me bitch? Then what you fuck for?", "vault_lines": ["He ain’t give you money to give to me bitch? Then what you fuck for?"], "meaning": "KRIT is asking (as a pimp) his ho why she would fuck without getting paid. Guess he has to open palm slap the bitch", "annotation_id": "2876496", "url": "https://genius.com/2876496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Smilin’ like I’m William “The Refrigerator” Perry", "vault_lines": ["Smilin' like I’m William \"The Refrigerator\" Perry"], "meaning": "Continuing the reference to big bodied football players, Rozay brings up William “The Refrigerator” Perry, a legendary defensive tackle for the Chicago Bears. After his NFL career ended in 1994, Perry had a smile implant done to replace his missing teeth from his days playing football.\n\nSee the resemblance?", "annotation_id": "2876470", "url": "https://genius.com/2876470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "John Travolta, these subwoofers might blow your face off", "vault_lines": ["John Travolta, these subwoofers might blow your face off"], "meaning": "KRIT’s got his bass playing loud enough to seriously mess with your face.\n\nSo much bass when I pop my tape,\nCan’t feel my face\n\nThe John Travolta reference effects some wordplay with the 1997 Travolta-starrer Face/Off\n\n\n\nThe Travolta reference also extends even further, as Vincent Vega, Travolta’s character in Pulp Fiction, is a hitman (who therefore would literally blow peoples' face off for a living), and in the film does so (albeit unitentionally) in a famous scene (which drives a good third of the movie’s plot).", "annotation_id": "2876423", "url": "https://genius.com/2876423", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "All I had was that dream, Martin Luther my king", "vault_lines": ["All I had was that dream, Martin Luther my king"], "meaning": "A Drug Dealer’s Dream, perhaps?\n\nRicky has come a long way over the past few years, operating his own label, releasing a potentially classic album in MasterMind, and overall, accomplishing success. While these dreams weren’t exactly the same or as powerful as Martin’s, they’re still to be recognized.", "annotation_id": "2876419", "url": "https://genius.com/2876419", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "‘Dem white wall, ‘dem white wall, they was super cold Since a grasshopper all I ever wanted was some triple golds ‘Dem Daytons and that my bass boss", "vault_lines": ["‘Dem white wall, ‘dem white wall, they was super cold", "Since a grasshopper all I ever wanted was some triple golds", "‘Dem Daytons and that my bass boss"], "meaning": "KRIT describes his dream car from childhood: triple gold Dayton Wire Wheels with those sick thin spokes and white casing around them like Macklemore and Q also idolized and a banging sub system\n\n\n\nThese features, along with the woodgrain wheels KRIT mentioned earlier, are characteristic of Southern cars", "annotation_id": "2876373", "url": "https://genius.com/2876373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "All I want is that lemon pepper, but the flavors vary", "vault_lines": ["All I want is that lemon pepper, but the flavors vary"], "meaning": "Wingstop, fat boy need a 10 piece\n\nAs mentioned in this verified annotation from the BAOUS himself, Rozay enjoys his lemon pepper wings from Wingstop, the chicken wing chain where he owns 6 locations.\n\n\n\nEven though he prefers lemon pepper, Wingstop offers an abundance of different flavors. Check out the full wing menu here!", "annotation_id": "2876363", "url": "https://genius.com/2876363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Yeah I got some gators but I need some more", "vault_lines": ["Yeah I got some gators but I need some more"], "meaning": "Seems like KRIT heeded his father’s advice and started his own collection of gator-skin shoes, a clean choice to complete a stunting outfit in KRIT’s South. Still, he wants more, making him hungry to work harder", "annotation_id": "2876304", "url": "https://genius.com/2876304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Flex around me, I might take your bitch and not give her back", "vault_lines": ["Flex around me, I might take your bitch and not give her back"], "meaning": "Looks like KRIT isn’t quite as forgiving as another Southern rapper….", "annotation_id": "2876296", "url": "https://genius.com/2876296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Bitch I got a new agenda", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I got a new agenda"], "meaning": "KRIT’s taking a new approach to his second studio album, Cadillactica, as this will be his first project where a significant portion is produced by someone other than KRIT himself – this may well be the “new agenda” he is referring to here", "annotation_id": "2876272", "url": "https://genius.com/2876272", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "line": "Grippin’ grain ‘till I catch a splinter", "vault_lines": ["Grippin' grain ‘till I catch a splinter"], "meaning": "KRIT loves gripping grain, but if he does it too much, that wooden wheel might leave a splinter in his hand….", "annotation_id": "2876261", "url": "https://genius.com/2876261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Agenda", "status": "done", "targets": 26, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Big-krit-new-agenda-lyrics", "genius_title": "New Agenda", "genius_id": 373898, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Bugatti", "line": ".357, perpetrator stumbles Shots fired, and I fear the worst Gift wrap his ass, December 1st Underneath the tree, can a nigga sleep?", "vault_lines": ["Shots fired, and I fear the worst", "Gift wrap his ass, December 1st", "Underneath the tree, can a nigga sleep?"], "meaning": "Ross’s security system picked up an intruder on his property (maybe the well it, manicured lawn a few lines above), so he has this person shot with a .357 Magnum and wrapped in a body bag, as though the corpse were a present. It’s then buried under a tree.\n\nRoss is gonna turn insomniac with all this gunplay in his front yard.", "annotation_id": "756875", "url": "https://genius.com/756875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Bugatti", "line": "I’m a Harlem nigga, I’m a Ciroc boy", "vault_lines": ["I'm a Harlem nigga, I'm a Ciroc boy"], "meaning": "Young Puff Diddy Dirty Money Daddy pays homage to his hometown of Harlem, NY and informs the listeners for the 1000th time that he owns Ciroc vodka.\n\n\n\nDo note that Diddy ingeniously rhymes “boy” with… “boy”, in the line immediately following this one.", "annotation_id": "676241", "url": "https://genius.com/676241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Bugatti", "line": "So old school, still in my cap and gown", "vault_lines": ["So old school, still in my cap and gown"], "meaning": "If you are old school, or the oldest in your school, you are graduating, while wearing a cap and gown. Ross is old school in the sense that he is an OG.\n\nHowever, given the incident detailed a few lines down, the “cap and gown” probably refers to Ross being in his pajamas during the night.", "annotation_id": "536565", "url": "https://genius.com/536565", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Bugatti", "line": "She wanna feel the rush, I give her sugar hill", "vault_lines": ["She wanna feel the rush, I give her sugar hill"], "meaning": "Double Entendre Alert!\n\nThe rush of being with a guy like Diddy and his lifestyle. While the sugar rush is after consuming a large amount of sugar and for that rush he’ll give her a hill of sugar. Also a shout out to hip-hop legends Sugarhill Gang", "annotation_id": "534926", "url": "https://genius.com/534926", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Bugatti", "line": "One point five for the transport Car got a letter B all on the asshole", "vault_lines": ["One point five for the transport", "Car got a letter B all on the asshole"], "meaning": "Here Ross is rapping about his very expensive and very fast Bugatti Veyron\n\n\n\nNotice the “B” (for Bugatti, duh) on the tail end. And by “transport” Ricky is using his oh so clever lyricism to play with the action of the car and getting the car shipped from overseas.", "annotation_id": "534472", "url": "https://genius.com/534472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Bugatti", "line": "Bought a Vacheron in London, costs a million pounds", "vault_lines": ["Bought a Vacheron in London, costs a million pounds"], "meaning": "Diddy purchased a timepiece made by Swiss luxury watch manufacturer Vacheron Constantin. VC’s do indeed sell for seven figures. At the time of the Rich Forever mixtape’s release, the pound had dropped to a 12-month low versus the dollar, but presuming Diddy acquired the watch sometime during the 2011 calendar year, we can be assured that he paid at least $1.55 million USD. Rick Ross also owns a VC, as stated in “Tears of Joy” from his 2010 Teflon Don album.", "annotation_id": "534449", "url": "https://genius.com/534449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Bugatti", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-new-bugatti-lyrics", "genius_title": "New Bugatti", "genius_id": 63138, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "All my diamonds watchin’, now my watches gettin’ jealous (Haha)", "vault_lines": ["All my diamonds watchin', now my watches gettin' jealous (Haha)"], "meaning": "Ross uses some clever wordplay with watchin'/watches to further flaunt his wealth. He compares the women surrounding him to “diamonds” who are admiring the diamonds in his watches.\n\nDiamond could also be a nod to the diamond shape the bases make on a baseball pitch, continuing the Yankees metaphor in previous lines.\n\n\n\nRoss showcasing some of his flashy jewelry.", "annotation_id": "3391340", "url": "https://genius.com/3391340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Home plate, World Series, how a nigga slidin’ in her (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["Home plate, World Series, how a nigga slidin' in her (Ugh)"], "meaning": "Ross uses baseball analogy and metaphors to boast about his sex life.\n\nIn baseball, the home plate is the final base that a player must touch to score a run. The could also be a nod to the metaphorical relationship bases. The World Series is the annual North American baseball league, Major League Baseball.\n\nSliding is a metaphor for having sex. In baseball, players often slide to reach the home plate in time.\n\n\n\nA player sliding to the home plate in a baseball game.", "annotation_id": "3391277", "url": "https://genius.com/3391277", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "[Produced by Count Justice]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“New Flame” features an elegantly crafted, synth-heavy beat that runs at 95 BPM. Production is handled by up-and-coming producer Count Justice who blends a new age R&B melody with a cushion of clean 808s and drums.", "annotation_id": "3375501", "url": "https://genius.com/3375501", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Smokin’ on a bomb in my autographed LeBron’s", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' on a bomb in my autographed LeBron's"], "meaning": "“A bomb” refers to marijuana, which Ross is smoking in a pair of autographed LeBron James‘ Nike sneakers, such as the LeBron 10 Corks depicted below.", "annotation_id": "3371581", "url": "https://genius.com/3371581", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Babe Ruth ballin’ in a Beamer (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Babe Ruth ballin' in a Beamer (Woo)"], "meaning": "Ross compares himself to Hall of Fame New York Yankees outfielder, Babe Ruth, further continuing the ongoing Yankees metaphor. During his career, Ruth spent 14 years with the Yankees.\n\n“Ballin'” is a term used to indicate success, and is a continuation of the previous line. Ross flaunts his success by mentioning his expensive Beamer, a.k.a a BMW car.\n\n\n\nBabe Ruth batting for the Yankees.", "annotation_id": "3371558", "url": "https://genius.com/3371558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Panamera, Yogi Berra, my two-seater, Derek Jeter", "vault_lines": ["Panamera, Yogi Berra, my two-seater, Derek Jeter"], "meaning": "The Porsche Panamera is a luxury sports car that comes in 4-door and 2-door models. Yogi Berra is a Hall of Fame MLB player best known for his 17-year stint with the New York Yankees. Berra won the World Series 10 times during his career, a feat no other player has matched, and is recognized as one of the best catchers in baseball history.\n\nRoss also shouts out Derek Jeter, a shortstop who spent his entire 20-year career with the Yankees. During his career, Jeter wore the number 2 jersey for the Yankees, which Ross plays on by comparing his two-seater convertible to Jeter. This also ties in with the Panamera reference at the beginning of the bar.\n\n\n\nDerk Jeter playing for the Yankees.", "annotation_id": "2903138", "url": "https://genius.com/2903138", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Come on, just, baby, try a new thing And let’s spark a new flame", "vault_lines": ["Come on, just, baby, try a new thing", "And let's spark a new flame"], "meaning": "Chris encourages his girl to become his lover and be open to starting something new with him.\n\nFlames/fire are often used to describe love because just like love, they are beautiful but sometimes a destructive power. All it takes is one spark to start a new flame—new relationship—but other times, you also have to let it burn.", "annotation_id": "2895920", "url": "https://genius.com/2895920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Collar on my Polo (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Collar on my Polo (Woo)"], "meaning": "Polo Ralph Lauren is Ralph Lauren’s premium, flagship brand, best known for its collared polo shirts. The brand’s popularity is growing in hip-hop thanks to the likes of Pharell Williams and Kanye West.\n\n\n\nPharell and Kanye on stage in Polo shirts.", "annotation_id": "2895872", "url": "https://genius.com/2895872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "There can be one only you, woah-oh (Oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh) And baby, God could never make two, woah, na-na-na (Oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh)", "vault_lines": ["And baby, God could never make two, woah, na-na-na (Oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh)"], "meaning": "Chris is complementing his girl, stating that she’s truly unique and he’ll never find someone else like her. A similar concept can be found in his November 2010 track, “Another You:”\n\nFeel like I just won the lotto, I found a one in a million you (Ooh)\nGod made you from the Earth and he broke the mould\nThere will never be another you", "annotation_id": "2895861", "url": "https://genius.com/2895861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Got more stripes than all these niggas", "vault_lines": ["Got more stripes than all these niggas"], "meaning": "In the military, a solider’s rank is denoted by the number of stripes they have on their uniform. Ross plays on this stating that he has more experience in the rap game than any of his competition.\n\nThis also continues the entended New York Yankees metaphor as the team is famous for their iconic pinstripe jerseys. Ross has figuratively earned more stripes than even the Yankees.\n\n\n\nThe New York Yankees and their pinstripe jerseys.", "annotation_id": "2888634", "url": "https://genius.com/2888634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Baby, I’m a boss, I’m talkin’ George Steinbrenner", "vault_lines": ["Baby, I'm a boss, I'm talkin' George Steinbrenner"], "meaning": "Ross is a self-proclaimed boss, as seen in his February 2008 single, “The Boss.” “Boss” is also one of Ross' signature ad-libs.\n\nGeorge Steinbrenner was an American businessman, best known for owning the New York Yankees.\n\n\n\nGeorge Steinbrenner.", "annotation_id": "2887669", "url": "https://genius.com/2887669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "New Flame", "line": "Who said you can’t find love in the club? ’Cause I wanna tell them they wrong", "vault_lines": ["Who said you can't find love in the club?"], "meaning": "Romance and sexual liaisons sparked within a club aren’t typically associated with longevity and substance. Finding somebody in the club is usually short-term, such as a one night stand, but Chris wants to prove others wrong as he’s found a partner for life in the club. These lyrics also foreshadow Rihanna’s lyrics on Chris' November 2015 track, “Counterfeit.”\n\nThese lyrics could also be a call back to Usher’s February 2008 single, “Love In This Club:”\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cB5e0zHRzHc", "annotation_id": "2886342", "url": "https://genius.com/2886342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
