{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Paid mama’s light bill with them nickel rocks Even kept the phone on with them nickel rocks", "vault_lines": ["Paid mama's light bill with them nickel rocks", "Even kept the phone on with them nickel rocks"], "meaning": "However Illegal most of black urban youth in the ghetto made ends meet buy doing drug sales, or whatever illegal activity that could make money.", "annotation_id": "19543396", "url": "https://genius.com/19543396", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "What you want, code red, you the Feds", "vault_lines": ["What you want, code red, you the Feds"], "meaning": "With code red obviously meaning bad Rick Ross states to someone (possibly inferred that it is someone he may have hanging out with) appears to be working with the Federals trying to find a reason arrest Ross probably posing a suspicious demeanor causing Ross to call him out.", "annotation_id": "6327684", "url": "https://genius.com/6327684", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Duncan owed 5 dollars and he stretched him Over a nickel rock", "vault_lines": ["Duncan owed 5 dollars and he stretched him", "Over a nickel rock"], "meaning": "Junkie owed someone $5 for a Nickel Rock, and he was beaten up badly or possibly killed for not paying his debt of $5 for a Nickel Rock he either took on credit or stole.\n\nThis goes to show how far people will go for even $5 worth of Rock", "annotation_id": "5394081", "url": "https://genius.com/5394081", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Lou started with a nickel rock, started flippin’ plenty blocks", "vault_lines": ["Lou started with a nickel rock, started flippin' plenty blocks"], "meaning": "Lou started his drug dealing career by selling Nickel Rocks, as time went by he sold more drugs and built up a client list and made more money. He first started selling on one block or corner, but as his business grew he went from selling on his one original block or corner to selling on many blocks or corner. Possibly supplying other street dealers on many different blocks.", "annotation_id": "5394062", "url": "https://genius.com/5394062", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Gangsta P got 30 for a nickel rock, repeated offender Should’ve told that nigga stop ’fore they ate him for dinner", "vault_lines": ["Gangsta P got 30 for a nickel rock, repeated offender", "Should've told that nigga stop 'fore they ate him for dinner"], "meaning": "Gangsta P is a repeat offender, and has a long history of being arrested. He committed so much crime in the past and has been arrested so much that when he got arrested with a Nickel Rock the judge ate him for dinner by handing him a 30 year sentence. Boosie wishes he told him to stop before they arrested him, so he wouldn’t have been given much a harsh prison sentence.", "annotation_id": "5394050", "url": "https://genius.com/5394050", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "One nickel rock in my pocket to a half a mill", "vault_lines": ["One nickel rock in my pocket to a half a mill"], "meaning": "Rick Ross started with just 5 dollars worth of crack in his pocket\n\n\n\nand has hustled and grinned his way to the wealth he has today.", "annotation_id": "5161711", "url": "https://genius.com/5161711", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Double M, we get the money that you never will", "vault_lines": ["Double M, we get the money that you never will"], "meaning": "“Double M” stands for Maybach Music, a record label founded by Rozay. This label also includes artists such as Meek Mill and Wale.", "annotation_id": "4735715", "url": "https://genius.com/4735715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Got a 5 dollar sale for these nickel rocks", "vault_lines": ["Got a 5 dollar sale for these nickel rocks"], "meaning": "A nickel rock is any sort of drug rock (most of the time, crack) that is worth five dollars. Hence the five dollar sale Ricky Rozay is having.", "annotation_id": "4735698", "url": "https://genius.com/4735698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Got it all, but the days only nickel rocks", "vault_lines": ["Got it all, but the days only nickel rocks"], "meaning": "Ross uses the concept of a nickel rock (a cheap $5 drug, likely crack cocaine in this case) as a metaphor for his life in that his life is a short yet highly stimulating event.\n\nThis parallels his verse in Benediction where he says:\n\nGold around my neck I’m ballin' for these final minutes, Nothing lasts forever, for these sins I seek repentance", "annotation_id": "4728633", "url": "https://genius.com/4728633", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Got my first pair of Jordans for them nickel rocks Even felt extorted for them nickel rocks", "vault_lines": ["Got my first pair of Jordans for them nickel rocks", "Even felt extorted for them nickel rocks"], "meaning": "With Rozay being able to become somewhat stable financially selling drugs, (in this case, nickel rock) he was able to afford himself some Jordans which usually run at a relatively high price (around $150- $200).\n\n\n\nBesides profiting from nickel rock, Ross found himself dependent/forced by other into distributing and/or taking the drug.", "annotation_id": "4613265", "url": "https://genius.com/4613265", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Started with a nickel rock and got a triple beam", "vault_lines": ["Started with a nickel rock and got a triple beam"], "meaning": "He began selling nickel rock or a street level, single dose. Later graduating to the triple beam where one would weigh out larger quantities of drugs.", "annotation_id": "4502329", "url": "https://genius.com/4502329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Young nigga took an L and he chose to tell All the boys over there, they never took it well", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga took an L and he chose to tell", "All the boys over there, they never took it well"], "meaning": "A kid took an “L” or a “loss” (probably to a cop) and chose to snitch on his dealer to get out of trouble. The dealer’s crew was not okay with this.\n\n\n\nWhen people squeal in the hood, they often seal their fate.", "annotation_id": "4433059", "url": "https://genius.com/4433059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "In the match box I saw my first nickel rock Carol City nigga with his first nickel spot", "vault_lines": ["Carol City nigga with his first nickel spot"], "meaning": "The Matchbox Projects in Carol City (part of Miami), were the 90’s neighbourhood of Ross’s old crew, the Boobie Boys, where he grew up and first dealt with coke and such.\n\nHowever this line could be much deeper as he may have stumbled upon a family member’s stash in a match box.", "annotation_id": "4408279", "url": "https://genius.com/4408279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Seen a man kill his brother for a nickel rock I’m a bad motherfucker with a nickel rock", "vault_lines": ["Seen a man kill his brother for a nickel rock", "I'm a bad motherfucker with a nickel rock"], "meaning": "That is the power that drugs have over the hood. Gangsters will do anything to protect their product – even kill their own kin. Fiends will do anything to get their hands on the product – even if it means doing the same.", "annotation_id": "4360825", "url": "https://genius.com/4360825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "On account of I just want to see my daughter fed Went to the store and I came back with just a loaf of bread", "vault_lines": ["On account of I just want to see my daughter fed", "Went to the store and I came back with just a loaf of bread"], "meaning": "It is very common to explain how someone is in prison or arrested with the phrase on account of… and then stating their crime. Rozay is saying that if he goes to jail, it’s won’t be on account of selling crack-cocaine rocks, in his eyes he’ll be going to jail because he’s trying to provide food for his daughter.\n\nWithout dealing nickel rocks, he can only provide the bare essentials for his family, such as a loaf of bread. However, loaf of bread could  refer to the dough gained from an armed robbery.", "annotation_id": "4302551", "url": "https://genius.com/4302551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Put the pistol in your name and you may get the blame", "vault_lines": ["Put the pistol in your name and you may get the blame"], "meaning": "When one buys a gun, the gun’s serial number is attached to the buyer’s name. This can and will become an issue if said gun is found at a crime scene.\n\nIf the serial number is still visible on the gun and it is found to be anyway involved in a crime, you can bet that whoever’s name is attached to the serial number will be getting asked a few questions, if not blamed for the crime.\n\n\n\nBuying a gun requires a background check and many other prerequisites.", "annotation_id": "4302485", "url": "https://genius.com/4302485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Got my first pussy for a nickel rock Ain’t gon’ lie, that bitch was hot If I had it she would have got a block", "vault_lines": ["Got my first pussy for a nickel rock", "Ain't gon' lie, that bitch was hot", "If I had it she would have got a block"], "meaning": "He traded a nickel rock for his virginity… hope he didn’t catch anything!\n\nThe woman in question was so incredibly sexy that he would have given her a Kilo if he had it!", "annotation_id": "4298572", "url": "https://genius.com/4298572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nickel Rock", "line": "Old shooter on the team, I’m Bernard King", "vault_lines": ["Old shooter on the team, I'm Bernard King"], "meaning": "He refers to legendary NBA small forward Bernard King. King was known for his post game, especially a deadly turnaround. He played till he was 37, even making an all-star game at 35, despite a sequence of crippling knee injuries.\n\n\n\nRozay, 38, is a shooter of a different kind…\n\nHe may also be making an allusion to Bernard King’s historic consecutive 50 point games, or “double nickels”. On a Texas road trip on January 31 and February 1, 1984, King made NBA history by becoming the first player since 1964 to score at least 50 points in consecutive games. King also wore jersey # 55.", "annotation_id": "4296537", "url": "https://genius.com/4296537", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
