{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Run back to a nigga when them shots get to sprayin’", "vault_lines": ["Run back to a nigga when them shots get to sprayin’"], "meaning": "Referring back to the same niggas from the first line. Ross insinuates that they act all independent when they’re caught up in their own fame, but once shit gets real and shots go up he will run back to someone else for help.", "annotation_id": "2583334", "url": "https://genius.com/2583334", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Bitch just bought a house she can’t afford to run her mouth", "vault_lines": ["Bitch just bought a house she can't afford to run her mouth"], "meaning": "This could be a shot at rival 50 Cent, who once purchased Mike Tyson’s home, only to later put it up for sale. Fif has had difficulty selling it.", "annotation_id": "2359175", "url": "https://genius.com/2359175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Ho know we fuckin’, so don’t even ask em", "vault_lines": ["Ho know we fuckin', so don’t even ask em"], "meaning": "This line is reminiscent of his lyric on “U.O.E.N.O.”  which lead to a considerable amount of backlash from just about everyone.\n\n\n\nThis line represents a transformation in Ross’s dealings with women (or at least his rapping about dealings with women): they know they are gonna fuck Ross by the end of the night, he doesn’t even need to ask!", "annotation_id": "2189943", "url": "https://genius.com/2189943", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Ain’t no bottles on your table, pussy boy go get your gwolla", "vault_lines": ["Ain't no bottles on your table, pussy boy go get your gwolla"], "meaning": "While Rozay is balling in the club with Ciroc and has his champagne refrigerated, they don’t have any bottles and are probably to stingy or most likely too poor to buy any.\n\n\n\nGwolla is slang for friend, so perhaps Ross is insinuating that these pussy niggaz can’t ball on his level – they need their homies to pay in order for them to stunt.", "annotation_id": "2182703", "url": "https://genius.com/2182703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "BANG, BANG, BANG, BANG, BANG!", "vault_lines": ["BANG, BANG, BANG, BANG, BANG!"], "meaning": "Gunshot noises are a common feature on southern trap music.\n\nRecently, Ross has made a habit of making gunshot adlibs in songs, such as “50 Plates”, “Lum Lum”, “Rich Porter”, and others.", "annotation_id": "2181200", "url": "https://genius.com/2181200", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Niggas go for self when they caught up in the fame", "vault_lines": ["Niggas go for self when they caught up in the fame"], "meaning": "Ross has denoted that fame and fortune can traumatize a person. And once people starts selling dope and getting money, they will usually change as a person – by becoming extremely self-involved and only looking out for themselves.", "annotation_id": "2180395", "url": "https://genius.com/2180395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Can’t play no games with these niggas Can’t play no games with these niggas Can’t play no games with these bitches Can’t play no games with these bitches Can’t play no games with these niggas, they’re so fake and they phony Can’t play no games with these bitches, they treat me like I’m Tony Can’t play no games with these niggas Can’t play no games with these bitches", "vault_lines": ["Can't play no games with these bitches, they treat me like I'm Tony", "Can't play no games with these bitches"], "meaning": "Rozay & Future aren’t here to play games or joke around, like some other clowns in the rap game. They’re strictly about business, Maybach business. And while other niggaz are wasting their time by taking Instagram selfies and shit, Ross is strictly getting to the money.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/60577690662608896\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/51491687570227200", "annotation_id": "2178865", "url": "https://genius.com/2178865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "No love for these skeezers, we party and fuck ’em Every day is a party so every day we like fuck ‘em", "vault_lines": ["Every day is a party so every day we like fuck ‘em"], "meaning": "A skeezer is synonym for a ratchet ho, a nasty, classless female (think skeevy).  All they’re good for is sex and drugs, and the Boss has no respect for that.\n\nThis is basically Ross' rendition of the famous saying:\n\nWe don’t love them hoes!\n\nRoss and his cohorts fuck bitches whenever they party, and Ross denotes that they party everyday. Ergo, Ross is fucking a different chick every night.", "annotation_id": "2178171", "url": "https://genius.com/2178171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Hundred grand on my watch, you don’t feel me then fuck ’em", "vault_lines": ["Hundred grand on my watch, you don’t feel me then fuck 'em"], "meaning": "Rick Ross spends 100 thousand on a lot of shit.  He pays for it all, of course, with his cut from featuring on songs. Besides the watch, he’s spent that much money on:\n\n\n\nHis chick’s car (also mentioned at the end of this song)\nDonation to Haiti after the devastation there\nA pinky ring", "annotation_id": "2178080", "url": "https://genius.com/2178080", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Feds follow a nigga like it’s a brick at a show", "vault_lines": ["Feds follow a nigga like it’s a brick at a show"], "meaning": "ROZAY TRIPLE ENTENDRE?\n\nMaybe…\n\n\nThe feds constantly follow Rick Ross because they know he’s moving weight – they will even go so far as to attend his shows, in order to bust him.\nEven the feds are such big fans of Rick Ross that they attend his shows, as if they are there to bust him because he has drugs on him.\nRoss could even be insinuating he’s got a police escort to take him to his shows.", "annotation_id": "2178054", "url": "https://genius.com/2178054", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Double M, we poppin’,", "vault_lines": ["Double M, we poppin',"], "meaning": "Reference to Maybach Music Group, the record label Ross founded in 2009 that is home to artists such as Wale, Meek Mill, Gunplay, Stalley, etc\n\nMMG is often thought of one of the hottest rap squads and labels in the game right now, and Ross alludes to that here", "annotation_id": "2177756", "url": "https://genius.com/2177756", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Can’t play no games with these bitches, they treat me like I’m Tony", "vault_lines": ["Can't play no games with these bitches, they treat me like I'm Tony"], "meaning": "They treat Future like he’s Tony Montana the fictional character played by Al Pacino in Scarface. And not the first time he’s made this claim.", "annotation_id": "2177471", "url": "https://genius.com/2177471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Then I got a Porsche, my bitch wanted a Bentley", "vault_lines": ["Then I got a Porsche, my bitch wanted a Bentley"], "meaning": "Ross' girl, Shateria, wanted a Bentley to roll around in. Since Ross is the Boss, he of course obliged and purchased her a whip that cost a couple hundred grand.\n\n\n\nRoss meanwhile decided to go another route & copped a sports car.\n\n\n\nIN HIS 9ELEVEEEENNNNNNNN", "annotation_id": "2177443", "url": "https://genius.com/2177443", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Bow down to the biggest, Belaire I be spilling", "vault_lines": ["Bow down to the biggest, Belaire I be spilling"], "meaning": "As we all know, Rick Ross is the biggest Boss in the game. It’s time for fuckbois to recognize his greatness and bow down to a true rap king.\n\nRecently, Ross inked an endorsement deal with his favorite champagne, Belaire Rose. He even started a Black Bottle Boys faction, consisting of MMG members and DJ’s around the nation.\n\nWhile in Europe, Ross presented Belaire Rose by making a champagne shower in a club in Cannes, France.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-5ZXNg5_ots", "annotation_id": "2177385", "url": "https://genius.com/2177385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Kilo in the kitchen, pussy niggas Merry Christmas", "vault_lines": ["Kilo in the kitchen, pussy niggas Merry Christmas"], "meaning": "Perhaps a callback to an older line, Ross is still whipping work – he’s got kilos of cocaine in the kitchen and handing them out like Santa Claus hands out gifts. Rozay is perhaps referring to Christmas, because of the color white relating to the snow, and the cocaine.\n\n\n\nROZAY CLAUS", "annotation_id": "2177345", "url": "https://genius.com/2177345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "line": "Heard your shit keep flopping and your crib got foreclosed", "vault_lines": ["Heard your shit keep flopping and your crib got foreclosed"], "meaning": "Perhaps a shot at his rival, 50 Cent. 50 has been struggling for over a year now to release his fifth studio album, Street King Immortal, because the album keeps getting pushed back due to his flopping singles. Fif’s house in Farmington, Conneticut has also been put up for sale, and it is being sold for half it’s worth.\n\nMeanwhile, Rozay is living large in his Miami mansion!", "annotation_id": "2177340", "url": "https://genius.com/2177340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Games", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-no-games-lyrics", "genius_title": "No Games", "genius_id": 213197, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "[Outro: Future]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Future’s vocals are only on the SoundCloud version of the song. His vocals were later removed from the single/album version.", "annotation_id": "17747831", "url": "https://genius.com/17747831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Ever since YouTube, niggas been callin’ me the leader of the new school", "vault_lines": ["Ever since YouTube, niggas been callin' me the leader of the new school"], "meaning": "There’s been immense hype over Drake ever since he first began releasing music on the internet (his first mixtape, Room for Improvement, was dropped in 2006). Following his 2009 self-release of So Far Gone, there was a fierce bidding war between labels to sign him.\n\nMore recently, Drake has been integral in assisting the launch of the careers of other new school musicians, such as fellow Torontonian The Weeknd, and ASAP Rocky and Kendrick Lamar, who headlined his 2012 Club Paradise Tour\n\nThis line may be a reference to lyrics from “The Calm” on So Far Gone:\n\nYou can see it in my face or even read it on my palm\nLeader of the new school, it’s proven and it’s known\n\n\n\nLeaders of the New School is also the name of the hip hop group that Busta Rhymes started out in. Drake often praises Native Tongues Posse rappers and their affiliates, so it is possible he is referring to this group.\n\nThis line has also been used by K.dot on Bitch, Don’t Kill My Vibe Remix\n\nLeader of the new school, on my toes like a ballerina. Who knew I’d be Black Swan", "annotation_id": "1681742", "url": "https://genius.com/1681742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Remember sip slow, live fast", "vault_lines": ["Remember sip slow, live fast"], "meaning": "Following the culture of the South and the rappers that sipped lean before Wayne, he stresses taking your time with the drink and enjoy the effects that it has on you. Sipping lean to fast makes you drowsy and will knock you out, which is not an enjoyable experience and there is the possibility of overdosing from it.\n\nWayne also sees the dangers of the drug that is so glorified in the rap industry. With the death of his dear friend Pimp C and many others, along with his recent run in with death (which was rumored to be caused by his lean addiction), he wants people that sip lean to be careful when doing so.\n\nHe isn’t telling those who sip to stop, just to watch yourself when doing so and be reckless in different areas, such as being reckless on a verse. Weezy discusses sipping lean below.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ye_N7pBLsfQ#t=6m45s", "annotation_id": "1681515", "url": "https://genius.com/1681515", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "(Fuck a fake friend! Where your real friends at? Started!)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This specific line was sampled from Drake’s “Started From the Bottom” song.", "annotation_id": "1681054", "url": "https://genius.com/1681054", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "And if we ball, catch us", "vault_lines": ["And if we ball, catch us"], "meaning": "A play on the saying that was administered by Magic and C-Murder in the song Ball ‘Till We Fall where you ball (or make money) until you die. Wayne could be asking his homies that if he is about to die from this money making schemes, please “catch” him before he dies.\n\nWeezy also made this reference in his hook for Duffle Bag Boy.\n\nContinuing from the Goodfellas line, at the climax of the movie, the majority of the characters are either caught by the police or killed by the mafia. Perhaps Wayne is insinuating that if Wayne and his homies are to be in the same boat as the Goodfellas, then Wayne will need some “catching” before he is sent to jail or dies.\n\nAnother meaning is for spectators or average people to make sure to catch Wayne & friends when they ball. This is also a play on the actual physical meaning of the word “ball”, and to “catch” it being one of the most common activities with a ball.", "annotation_id": "1681043", "url": "https://genius.com/1681043", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Dope boy, that’s my dress code", "vault_lines": ["Dope boy, that's my dress code"], "meaning": "Dress the way you live… because Ross makes hella money from dope, he then spends on expensive clothes such as YSL and Hermes.\n\n\n\nAlso, Ross' girlfriend Shateria Moragne-El has her own fashion line, Front Row in which Ross frequently models for.", "annotation_id": "1681017", "url": "https://genius.com/1681017", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Fuck all y’all niggas except my niggas Fuck them other niggas ’Cause I’m down for my niggas", "vault_lines": ["Fuck them other niggas", "'Cause I'm down for my niggas"], "meaning": "Future borrows from C-Murder’s hook on Snoop Dogg’s “Down 4 My Niggas” to express that he’s only concerned with his small circle of friends and people he can trust.\n\nFuck them other niggas ‘cause I’m down for my niggas\nFuck them other niggas 'cause I’m down for my niggas\nFuck them other niggas 'cause I ride for my niggas\nI die for my niggas (What), fuck them other niggas, niggas", "annotation_id": "1680972", "url": "https://genius.com/1680972", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Strip club like e’ry night", "vault_lines": ["Strip club like e'ry night"], "meaning": "Another strip club reference by Rozay.\n\nIn 2011, Rick Ross claimed to have spent a million dollars at King of Diamonds on his birthday (even though Blac Chyna denies it).", "annotation_id": "1680409", "url": "https://genius.com/1680409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Bitch, we good-fellas Boy, all them niggas with you They just pall bearers", "vault_lines": ["Boy, all them niggas with you", "They just pall bearers"], "meaning": "A reference to a Goodfellas a famous movie that was centered around gangsters and killers, it was directed by Martin Scorcese.\n\nWayne and his band of brothers will kill you, so that pall-bearer’s will have to carry you to your grave.", "annotation_id": "1680390", "url": "https://genius.com/1680390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Young Money, stay young I been Cash Money since day one", "vault_lines": ["Young Money, stay young", "I been Cash Money since day one"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has exclusively been on Cash Money Records since he started recording the age of 14.\n\nBack Then:\n\n\n\nNow:", "annotation_id": "1680366", "url": "https://genius.com/1680366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Down in Turks and Caicos", "vault_lines": ["Down in Turks and Caicos"], "meaning": "The Turks and Caicos Islands are a British Overseas Territory consisting of the larger Caicos Islands and smaller Turks Islands. They are known primarily for their tourism.\n\n\n\nThis is also a reference to Drake’s opening lyrics on Rozay’s remix of “Us”.", "annotation_id": "1680323", "url": "https://genius.com/1680323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Money counter go *brrrr* when you sellin’ out the Garden", "vault_lines": ["Money counter go *brrrr* when you sellin' out the Garden"], "meaning": "Ex: Money Counter\nhttp://youtu.be/s9faz0R7ag0\n\nDrake has performed at Madison Square Garden in New York City but he has never has headline a sold out concert at MSG.\n\nIn recent memory, Jay-Z, Run DMC, Bow Wow, and Eminem are the only rappers that have sold out MSG.\n\n\n\nConsidering that the previous line talked about James Harden, this could be a reference to his Houston Rockets teammate Jeremy Lin. When the Knicks were struggling in the middle of the season and Carmelo was injured, Lin emerged and brought some energy to the Garden. The excitement of Linsanity brought people to Madison Square Garden to watch the New York Knicks when there was little to be excited about. As a result of Lin’s breakout season, he was able to move on to the Houston and get a significant pay raise.\n\n\n\nSidenote: Drake could be talking about the MGM Grand Garden Arena in Las Vegas. He went there and sold out during his Club Paradise Tour last May.", "annotation_id": "1680297", "url": "https://genius.com/1680297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Day-one niggas, man, y’all stuck with me, dawg", "vault_lines": ["Day-one niggas, man, y'all stuck with me, dawg"], "meaning": "Noah “40” Shebib, Niko, Oliver, OB and Ryan (From the SFTB video) are common names in his songs, and he regards them as his closest friends because of the fact that they’ve been there since before the money and the fame.\n\nEvery nigga who knew him from day one is always gonna be his dawg cause they stuck with him on the roller coaster. He’s also that type of person, a real nigga who never forgets his brothers. Only severe betrayal without apology/remorse (everyone makes mistakes) might make Drizzy drop your company.\n\nAlso, Drake could be referring to how the rap game has been “stuck” with him from day 1, either because he is the best.", "annotation_id": "1680294", "url": "https://genius.com/1680294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Man, this shit so ill that we had to restart it", "vault_lines": ["Man, this shit so ill that we had to restart it"], "meaning": "This was originally a remix for “Started From The Bottom,” as stated by Drake in an interview with Rap Radar, but was then turned into Khaled’s first single.\n\nNot only have they “restarted” “Started From the Bottom”, Drake is also implying that this song is so good that you’ll also have to keep restarting this one to hear it again.\n\n\n\nThis line and the next few use the same flow as Make Me Proud.\n\nAnother possible explanation would be restarting what these 4 created with the hit “I’m On One.” The forumla for I’m On One and No New Friends is pretty much the same. A DJ Khaled song where….\n\n\nDrake does the hook and raps the first verse\nRick Ross gets Verse 2\nLil Wayne does the 3rd verse\nDJ Khaled does his trademark adlibs", "annotation_id": "1680292", "url": "https://genius.com/1680292", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "All my bitches love me;", "vault_lines": ["All my bitches love me;"], "meaning": "A reference to Lil Wayne’s song, Bitches Love Me in which Drizzy is prominently featured.", "annotation_id": "1680201", "url": "https://genius.com/1680201", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Khaled, that’s my flesh, ho", "vault_lines": ["Khaled, that's my flesh, ho"], "meaning": "DJ Khaled and Rick Ross are like brothers. Khaled was an instrumental part of Ross' initial success in Miami, which led to his major record label deal with Def Jam. At least a quarter of the songs on every Khaled album has a Ross feature on it, including most of the singles such as We Taking Over, I’m So Hood, Out Here Gridin', Fed Up, All I Do Is Win, I’m On One, Take It To The Head, etc.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/273088802791256064\nhttps://twitter.com/djkhaled/status/264597068113391617\n\nCould also be a reference to the 1985 movie, Flesh and Blood, as Ross had mentioned blood in the previous line.", "annotation_id": "1680176", "url": "https://genius.com/1680176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "Birdman go *brrrr* ’cause he know this shit retarded", "vault_lines": ["Birdman go *brrrr* 'cause he know this shit retarded"], "meaning": "Birdman gives one of his signature sounds to show his approval. Check some more out on Rap Board third line down.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k_NsXAoApxY&t=1m43s\n\nThis line also comes back from the money counter line, saying that Birdman’s adlib is similar to the sound a money counter makes.\n\nAlso, this “brrr” is said in a little higher tone than the one above, making it sound more like a Bird(man)", "annotation_id": "1680173", "url": "https://genius.com/1680173", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "No new friends, no new friends No new friends, no, no new (DJ Khaled) Still here with my day-one niggas So you hear me say no new friends No new friends, no new friends, no, no new I still ride with my day-one niggas I don’t really need no new friends No new friends, no new friends, no, no new I stay down from day one, so I say", "vault_lines": ["I don't really need no new friends", "I stay down from day one, so I say"], "meaning": "As he noted in his platinum certified single, Started From The Bottom, Drake still fucks with his friends that were there from day one and doesn’t plan on making any more friends.\n\n\n\nRealistically, the only new friend Drake has made was The Weeknd but they have since had some issues. This song would make sense to target The Weeknd by featuring everyone close to Drake other than him. However, Drake said that he still talks to Abel and that they didn’t exactly have a “parting of ways”, so this might not be a shot at him at all.\n\nBut this mantra is also popular in Chicago, where Fredo Santana doesn’t have time for anyone outside of his familia.", "annotation_id": "1680159", "url": "https://genius.com/1680159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "That’s what yo’ ass really call started from the bottom", "vault_lines": ["That's what yo' ass really call started from the bottom"], "meaning": "DRIZZY TRIPLE ENTENDRE!\n\n\nDrake switched positions to him givin' her ass shots, so he’s starting from HER bottom.\nIt could be taken as the sex starting from the bottom (the floor) then moving up to the bed.\nClearly a reference to his hit Started From the Bottom, as this song was originally deemed the remix.\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso referring to Chris Brown using “Started From The Bottom” as a euphemism to imply Drake was “comin' out the closet” on the former’s verse on Young Jeezy’s R.I.P. (Remix). Drake responds to Chris in this by implying the girl he “started from the bottom” with is Rihanna.", "annotation_id": "1680149", "url": "https://genius.com/1680149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No New Friends", "line": "H-town my second home like I’m James Harden", "vault_lines": ["H-town my second home like I'm James Harden"], "meaning": "Drake has always had ties to Houston – it’s where he first met Lil Wayne – and claims he reps it till the day he dies.\n\nNBA star James Harden was drafted by the Oklahoma City Thunder in 2009 but was then traded to the Houston Rockets, making the team his second home.", "annotation_id": "1680124", "url": "https://genius.com/1680124", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
