{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No U-Turns", "line": "Switch sides? You better stay there You switch sides? You better stay there Switch sides? You better stay Switch sides you better stay there You switch sides? You better stay there Switch sides? You better stay there", "vault_lines": ["Switch sides? You better stay there", "You switch sides? You better stay there", "Switch sides? You better stay"], "meaning": "If you switch sides and start working for the enemy, there’s no coming back. You better stay with them.", "annotation_id": "10477482", "url": "https://genius.com/10477482", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No U-Turns", "line": "Ain’t no U turns on the block It ain’t no U turns on my block Ain’t no U turns on my block Ain’t no U turns on my block It ain’t no U turns on my block It ain’t no U turns on the block Ain’t no U turns on the block It ain’t no U turns on the block It ain’t no U turns on the block", "vault_lines": ["Ain't no U turns on my block", "It ain't no U turns on the block"], "meaning": "A U-Turn is a driving maneuver where the driver change directions on a two-way street using a 180 degree rotation that resembles the letter U.\n\nHere Ross uses the term as a metaphor to describe his views on loyalty within his crew. The  Boss doesn’t allow members of MMG to switch sides in favor of other crews or to change directions.\n\nHe illustrates this further when he raps “Switch sides? You better stay there” later in the song.", "annotation_id": "10427156", "url": "https://genius.com/10427156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No U-Turns", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-no-u-turns-lyrics", "genius_title": "No U-Turns", "genius_id": 2856620, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Worries", "line": "Don’t switch out like Pacquiao, still gon’ put my stacks down Half a mill on Mayweather, I count it down to my crack house", "vault_lines": ["Don't switch out like Pacquiao, still gon' put my stacks down", "Half a mill on Mayweather, I count it down to my crack house"], "meaning": "Ross accuses boxer Manny Pacquiao of backing out of a highly anticipated fight against Floyd “Money” Mayweather. He isn’t too upset though, as he’s going to use his drug money to bet on the match regardless of if it actually happens or not.", "annotation_id": "3297900", "url": "https://genius.com/3297900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Worries", "line": "[Hook: Detail] You can look me in my face (I ain’t got no worries)x3 See the sh-rooms keep me up (I ain’t got no worries)x3 You see money right there, yeah that’s Tunechi right there (turn up) Yeah that’s Mack Maine right there, and we ain’t got no worries You see pussy right there redbone mangos right there See them sh-roomies right there we ain’t got no worries [Verse 2: Lil Wayne] Tunechi in this bitch, e’rybody should be worried Them pussy niggas be purring, bitches be digging me I feel buried And if she make this dick hard, she woke up a sleeping giant Man your bitch speak in tongues every time we speak in private Hope your barber shop open cause we got hair triggers Smoke so much that Smokey the Bear, have to bear with us And that Jeep with the doors off that means that bitch sleek All these bitch think they’re the shit, I sent them up shits creek You see Tunechi right here, give me brain ideas It’s ok if you turn up just don’t turn off my light years All I know is I do it what I’m smoking I grew it These are Blood gang Piru, and all rats gotta die even Stewart On my private jet is my stewardess is your bitch nigga, bitch Nigga I know gold-diggers and ditch-diggers You don’t get dissed, you get disfigured She say sorry I didn’t shave so that pussy a little furry I put that pussy in my face: I ain’t got no worries Tunechi [Hook: Detail]", "vault_lines": ["You can look me in my face (I ain't got no worries)x3", "See the sh-rooms keep me up (I ain't got no worries)x3", "You see money right there, yeah that's Tunechi right there (turn up)", "Yeah that's Mack Maine right there, and we ain't got no worries", "You see pussy right there redbone mangos right there", "See them sh-roomies right there we ain't got no worries", "Tunechi in this bitch, e'rybody should be worried", "Them pussy niggas be purring, bitches be digging me I feel buried", "And if she make this dick hard, she woke up a sleeping giant"], "meaning": "This is all taken from Wayne’s original version of the song, which you can find here.", "annotation_id": "3297876", "url": "https://genius.com/3297876", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No Worries", "line": "I call her Roscoe Dash, she be writing all on my shit", "vault_lines": ["I call her Roscoe Dash, she be writing all on my shit"], "meaning": "Rozay plays on the “write/ride” homophone to reference the incident where Roscoe Dash claimed to have written the hook to Wale’s “Lotus Flower Bomb”. This girl is riding Rozay’s dick like Roscoe claims to be writing hooks.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Roscoedash/status/248865575311405056", "annotation_id": "1126825", "url": "https://genius.com/1126825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
