{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "All the bitches different by the car load", "vault_lines": ["All the bitches different by the car load"], "meaning": "Throwback reference to the late 1980’s-early 1990’s dance hall legend Shabba Ranks.\n\nOne of Shabba’s most popular songs during this time was Trailer Load Of Girls\n\nhttp://www.bing.com/videos/search?q=Shabba+Ranks+Trailer+Load+a+Girls&&view=detail&mid=4D815A4536147171E4DD4D815A4536147171E4DD&FORM=VRDGAR", "annotation_id": "9425717", "url": "https://genius.com/9425717", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "But I smoke the most rappers", "vault_lines": ["But I smoke the most rappers"], "meaning": "Double entendre: He smokes rappers by being better than them. He doesn’t smoke tobacco, but he does smoke blunts, possibly using blunt wraps – “smoke the most wrappers”", "annotation_id": "1508818", "url": "https://genius.com/1508818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "My wrist’s numb", "vault_lines": ["The streets cold, my wrist's numb"], "meaning": "His wrist is numb because there is so much ice on it (which refers back to the cold streets). Ross is probably wearing a nice Vacheron Constantine Watch.", "annotation_id": "1431042", "url": "https://genius.com/1431042", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "Everybody know my name, I’m number one (We are, number one, huh) I’m number one", "vault_lines": ["Everybody know my name, I'm number one (We are, number one, huh)"], "meaning": "A year and a half later, MTV made it official by naming him the #1 hottest MC in the game.", "annotation_id": "1426245", "url": "https://genius.com/1426245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "I got big tips for the waitress (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["I got big tips for the waitress (Huh)"], "meaning": "Huge tips for the waitresses at strip clubs, in fact he spent over one million dollars in King of Diamonds at his 35th birthday party.", "annotation_id": "1426240", "url": "https://genius.com/1426240", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "I’m hot, hollar at me when the summer done (Yeah) Never been where I’m comin’ from, number one", "vault_lines": ["I'm hot, hollar at me when the summer done (Yeah)", "Never been where I'm comin' from, number one"], "meaning": "As of the summer that this song was produced, Trey Songz had only just begun to intermix with a lot of these big name rappers as he would only have songs with rather low-key ones, so he says to all the others, to wait until summer is over, because they have never been to where he is coming from: NUMBA 1.", "annotation_id": "1374128", "url": "https://genius.com/1374128", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "First white two-seater down Fifth Ave (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["First white two-seater down Fifth Ave (Woo)"], "meaning": "Referring to his white Rolls Royce Drop-head Phantom which he was the first to drive down Manhattan’s famous “Fifth Avenue”", "annotation_id": "1374109", "url": "https://genius.com/1374109", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "No. 1", "line": "Here’s a Rose toast to those rappers (Those rappers)", "vault_lines": ["Here's a Rose toast to those rappers (Those rappers)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross loves to drink Rose wine that he’s always bragging about.\n\nTherefore, he buys expensive drinks to rappers that can’t afford them to humilliate them. He also reminds them of his nickname to make it more painful.", "annotation_id": "522820", "url": "https://genius.com/522820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
