{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "[Verse 1: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "HUGE NOTE.\n\nIt’s eerie how similar Ross sounds to BIG throughout the song. Not to mention the beautiful adaptation of Big Poppa’s flow throughout the verse. Example:\n\nGo to bed with a kilo like Casino, Janet Reno, we all got the creed of nino.", "annotation_id": "2882641", "url": "https://genius.com/2882641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Only riders on my rider, murder rate rises", "vault_lines": ["Only riders on my rider, murder rate rises"], "meaning": "Artists typically provide a ‘rider’ to performance venues that lays out hospitality/tech info which includes things like guest lists and security.\nRoss is saying only people who are extremely loyal are allowed to be a part of his travel entourage. And since his entourage is composed of gangsters; the murder rate rises.", "annotation_id": "2862796", "url": "https://genius.com/2862796", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "We kill ‘em and takin’ their bitches", "vault_lines": ["We kill 'em and takin' their bitches"], "meaning": "Continuation of last line,\nMorgue is used for the storage of human corpses awaiting identification.\nMORGUE IS FILLING with snitches because Rozzy kills them and snitches are mostly those who dont have families, so they are stored in a morgue until their relative is found, or he might also be saying that they keep the body in the morgue to check how the murder took place and find the killer.\n\nAs soon as he kills the snitches , the bitches change their   mind and start hanging around with him.\n\n\n\nROSS might also be talking about this quote by Aristotle.\n“If women didn’t exist, all the money in the world would have no meaning”", "annotation_id": "2862105", "url": "https://genius.com/2862105", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Gettin’ high feelin’ like it’s vodou", "vault_lines": ["Gettin' high feelin' like it's vodou"], "meaning": "When Ross smokes is cannabis sativa, he feels as though he is under some sort of mysitcal trance.\n\nRozay has a rich history of using “vodou” to describe different aspects of his BOSS life. They are listed below in chronological order (Port of Miami, God Forgives I Don’t, & Coke Boys 4):\n\n\nSee the vodou priest then the coke gon' come\nNiggas think it’s vodou the way bricks be mulitplyin\nBut my vodou strong enough for 50 niggas", "annotation_id": "2857206", "url": "https://genius.com/2857206", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "If you cut it then you sideways, double up, crime pays", "vault_lines": ["If you cut it then you sideways, double up, crime pays"], "meaning": "White powder drugs can be “cut” or mixed with substances of a similar look and texture to increase profit margins. The fucked up thing is the lower you are down the weight scale, the more it has been cut on its way to you. This is why rappers like Rozay love talking about that pure shit because it means they met papi.\n\nHow many of you niggas really been to papi?\n\nHowever, in War Ready he mentions cutting “that bitch a thousand times”. He could be talking about others in the game or when he was on the come-up getting work that had already been cut.\n\n\n\nCrime pays.", "annotation_id": "2857179", "url": "https://genius.com/2857179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Do you feel me?", "vault_lines": ["do you feel me?"], "meaning": "Ross says this line in the rhythm of a line in Biggie’s second verse on the original.\n\n“Thorough bitches, adapt to any borough bitches\nBe in spots where they were no bitches, you feel me”\n\nRozay paying homage", "annotation_id": "2847048", "url": "https://genius.com/2847048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Still solo, Under Armour still Polo", "vault_lines": ["Still solo, Under Armour still Polo"], "meaning": "Ross isn’t talking literally about Under Armour, but rather referring to bulletproof vests. He’s saying he isn’t scared of what may come to him. Meaning, the only thing between him and a bullet are his fine Ralph Lauren Polo threads.", "annotation_id": "2840614", "url": "https://genius.com/2840614", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "We all we got the creed of Nino", "vault_lines": ["we all we got the creed of Nino"], "meaning": "Refers to Nino Brown of the film New Jack City and his famous quote, “We all we got”", "annotation_id": "2832246", "url": "https://genius.com/2832246", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "[Produced by Diddy]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Interesting that Diddy has sole production credit on this, when he is only one of four credited producers (Stevie J, DJ Enuff and Jiv Poss) on the Biggie song that provides this beat’s source material", "annotation_id": "2825828", "url": "https://genius.com/2825828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "My desire for fine things made me a liar, a shooter", "vault_lines": ["My desire for fine things made me a liar, a shooter"], "meaning": "Money is the root of all evil\n\nRick Ross confesses that he’s had to lie, cheat, steal, and kill to get the nice things he wants. Things like a Maybach…\n\n\n\nor a Rick Ross-shaped pendant.\n\n\n\nHe’s rapped before about how he has to be War Ready, about how he’s trying to evade the feds, so we shouldn’t be surprised that he’s willing to get dishonest and violent to get the nicer things in life.", "annotation_id": "2824255", "url": "https://genius.com/2824255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Black bottles when I’m feelin’ like, you wanna know what winners like", "vault_lines": ["Black bottles when I'm feelin' like, you wanna know what winners like"], "meaning": "Ricky Rozay reverses the sentence here: “You wanna know what winners (are) like?  Black bottles when(ever) I feel like (having one)”.  Basically a winner can have the finest luxuries whenever he wants.\n\nBlack bottles, such Belaire Rosé, one of Rick Ross favorite champagnes, are an example of that luxury.", "annotation_id": "2823032", "url": "https://genius.com/2823032", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Stalkin’ niggas on their IG’s,", "vault_lines": ["Stalkin' niggas on their IG's,"], "meaning": "Rick means “stalking” in two senses – the normal, relatively harmless one, and a more dangerous way, watching their whereabouts and waiting for a time to strike", "annotation_id": "2822976", "url": "https://genius.com/2822976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Go to bed with a kilo like Casino", "vault_lines": ["Go to bed with a kilo like Casino"], "meaning": "1995 Martin Scorsese film starring Joe Pesci and Robert DeNiro", "annotation_id": "2822330", "url": "https://genius.com/2822330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "The truth’ll set you free, son, the truth will set you free", "vault_lines": ["The truth'll set you free, son, the truth will set you free"], "meaning": "This is an old, old phrase form the Bible – John 8:31-32 to be exact.\n\nIn the Christian sense it means to trust in Jesus, which will free you of Earthly worries so you may enter the Kingdom of Heaven.  The phrase has value in a secular sense, too, though.  Those who can see the whole truth in a situation (instead of a clouded vision) will be free to make the best choice possible.\n\nMaybe this line has personal undertones for Rick Ross too, as his rap persona at the beginning was a drug dealer but later he was revealed to be a corrections officer.  The truth in this case sure didn’t hurt Rozay’s career, so in a sense it really did set him free.", "annotation_id": "2822131", "url": "https://genius.com/2822131", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Never really athletic, but I play for keeps,", "vault_lines": ["Never really athletic, but I play for keeps,"], "meaning": "A little bit of word play from THE BOSS. Seeing how Rick Ross is pretty plump and is obviously not very athletic, when he talks about “playing for keeps” he isn’t talking about sports. Instead he means the rap game, other businesses, bitches, etc.\n\nRozay does shoot hoops sometimes, however, and his jumper is pretty wet.\n\n\n\nThe line may be an R.I.P./shout out to L'A Capone.", "annotation_id": "2822089", "url": "https://genius.com/2822089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Janet Reno,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "While most remember Janet Reno for her term as Attorney General under Clinton, Florida residents like Ross clearly recall her 1980s stint as Dade County State Attorney, where she famously cracked down on deadbeat dads.  This crusade made her a hero to many black women, and got her some rap shoutouts unusual for a state official", "annotation_id": "2822087", "url": "https://genius.com/2822087", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "You wanted to fuckin’ walk around these roaches. These niggas is roaches. These niggas is mere motherfuckin’ mortals. I’m tryna push you to supreme bein’. You don’t wanna motherfuckin’... You don’t wanna embrace your destiny, you wanna get by You don’t wanna go into the motherfuckin’ dark where it’s lonely. You can’t handle the motherfuckin’, the pain of the motherfuckin’ not knowin’ when the shit is gonna stop", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Ross has stated that Diddy’s part on the song was “real talk”, and was recorded by a member of Diddy’s REVOLT, not just for the song\n\nRoss says, “What I did next was, Puff talkin' that talk. That was real talk. That wasn’t studio,” Ross said. “Yo. Who exactly he was speaking to, I’m not gonna say his name, but this was real. This was definitely Puff in one of those zones, and the lil homie from Revolt, he captured it.”\n\nhttp://imgur.com/QoUl86f\n\nIt was revealed who Puffy was addressing on King Los' media run on March 20th, 2014 when on Sway In The Morning, he revealed the signee has departed with Diddy and his imprint, Bad Boy. Later that day on MTV’s RapFix Live, he was asked about the quote on the song and explained he was on the receiving end of the words.", "annotation_id": "2822078", "url": "https://genius.com/2822078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Nine lives, SK with the cooler", "vault_lines": ["Nine lives, SK with the cooler"], "meaning": "Having a Gun = Packing heat. A cooler would be something that lowers the heat.\nA SK is a type of gun so a cooler would be a silencer.\n\nBy nine lives he means he is untouchable, which is why he is called the Teflon Don. According to myths, cats have nine lives.\n\n\n\nThis is continuation from the previous line:\n\nfeeling like it’s vodou.\n\nHe fears no death nor those wishing Rozay gets killed becuase he has a gun to protect himself with despite having nine lives.", "annotation_id": "2822039", "url": "https://genius.com/2822039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "“Blast for me” – the last words from my nigga", "vault_lines": ["\"Blast for me\" – the last words from my nigga"], "meaning": "The last words from either a fallen comrade or one about to be incarcerated were to avenge/kill for him in his memory. Keeping with the song’s theme, Rick Ross may also be posing himself, subliminally of course, as Biggie’s reincarnated spirit.", "annotation_id": "2822013", "url": "https://genius.com/2822013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "The narcotics is our product", "vault_lines": ["The narcotics is our product"], "meaning": "“The narcotics is our product” could refer to the fact that people in Ricky’s town sell narcotics or both manufacture (probably synthetic) and sell them.", "annotation_id": "2821976", "url": "https://genius.com/2821976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "The by-product, you walk up on me, I cock it", "vault_lines": ["The by-product, you walk up on me, I cock it"], "meaning": "By-product = an incidental result made by the manufacturing of something else.\n\nIn other words, an unintended result of having sold narcotics (as mentioned in the previous line) is that he has become paranoid and wear of any/everybody.\n\n\n\nBecause Rick Ross is selling illegal drugs he can’t just trust anybody.  He pulls out his weapon of defense and prepares himself in case of a threat.", "annotation_id": "2821964", "url": "https://genius.com/2821964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "I’m from where the streets test you", "vault_lines": ["I'm from where the streets test you"], "meaning": "Ross was raised in Carol City, near Miami.  He payed homage to the area by signing the Carol City Cartel", "annotation_id": "2821915", "url": "https://genius.com/2821915", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Niggas mix business and pleasure", "vault_lines": ["Niggas mix business and pleasure"], "meaning": "Two Meanings:\n\n\nNovice drug dealers are careless and don’t care about the attention they bring to themselves. But Rozay knows better: as Biggie himself said years ago.\nNovice drug dealers get high off their own supply because they haven’t yet learned self control.", "annotation_id": "2821450", "url": "https://genius.com/2821450", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Havin’ sushi down in Nobu", "vault_lines": ["Havin' sushi down in Nobu"], "meaning": "Nobu is a famed Sushi restaurant, with chain stores all around the globe, in places such as London, New York and Dubai.", "annotation_id": "2821398", "url": "https://genius.com/2821398", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Art of war is mental", "vault_lines": ["Hustlers movin' out of rentals, art of war is mental"], "meaning": "This could have two meanings: the personal damages of war or the overarching strategy when fighting a war.\n\nOn one hand, war has an emotional as well as a mental effect on soldiers. Returning from battle, many soldiers suffer from PTSD (post-traumatic stress disorder) or a host of other anxiety disorders that may develop after a person is exposed to one or more traumatic events.\n\nIn another sense, though, war is mental because the general who understands the whole picture and strategizes best will win – according to Sun Tzu’s The Art of War anyway.  Ross is hinting that he’s so trained and skilled in using Sun Tzu’s strategies, he doesn’t need to read from the actual book anymore – he has internalized it and become an unconsciously competent strategist.", "annotation_id": "2821376", "url": "https://genius.com/2821376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Closed the deal with Steven Hill", "vault_lines": ["Like I'm knowin' every heathen will, closed the deal with Steven Hill"], "meaning": "Hill is BET’s President of Music Programming and Specials", "annotation_id": "2821359", "url": "https://genius.com/2821359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Makaveli in the ’Rari, still B-I double G, I, E", "vault_lines": ["Makaveli in the 'Rari, still B-I double G, I, E"], "meaning": "Rick Ross nods his head to two of the greats.\n\n\n\nRoss is boasting that he blasts Tupac’s Makaveli album in his Ferrari.\n\nThe Biggie line refers not just to Ross’s body type, but to the late great BIG, who famously partnered with Diddy on the Bad Boy label.\n\nBiggie spelled out his name in just this way on the track “Going Back to Cali,” which sought to reunite the East and West coasts in the same way that Ross does here.\n\nSpell my name right, B-I, double-G, I-E", "annotation_id": "2821149", "url": "https://genius.com/2821149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "You’re nobody ’til somebody kills you", "vault_lines": ["You're nobody 'til somebody kills you"], "meaning": "This sentiment is a deep one – when you’re alive, people constantly hate and degrade you as a person. When you’re murdered, those same people turn around and pretend like they cared.\n\nThis line is a call back to the original Biggie song, “You’re Nobody (Til Somebody Kills You).”\n\nSimilarities between the two songs:\n\n\nThe beat – this song samples the original beat\nA Diddy intro\n\n\n\nRozay draws a lot of inspiration from Biggie – from fashion to delivery to content. Not to mention weight.", "annotation_id": "2820661", "url": "https://genius.com/2820661", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Strapped like an Afghan soldier, nowhere to go to So it’s bang, no survivors", "vault_lines": ["Strapped like an Afghan soldier, nowhere to go to", "So it's bang, no survivors"], "meaning": "Ross uses some awful imagery of a roadside bombing here to make a very strong point.\n\nAfghan soldiers tote some big weapons, such as machine guns and land-to-air weapons.  But despite all that protection, when a car that’s been loaded down with, let’s say, 75 kg of explosives pulls up next to these soldiers, they have no way to escape their imminent doom.  Stories like this have plagued national news headlines since before the Iraq War.  In fact, one appeared the day before this song was released!\n\nRick is making a parallel between such atrocities and life on the streets in the drug game.  Gets the point across, wouldn’t you say?", "annotation_id": "2820630", "url": "https://genius.com/2820630", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "We Magic City of the networks Cut a nigga cast off,", "vault_lines": ["We Magic City of the networks", "Cut a nigga cast off,"], "meaning": "“Magic City” was a show about 1950s Miami that Rick Ross appeared in for an episode, playing a character called Butterball (see below).  The show was canceled by its network, Starz, abruptly after only two seasons.\n\nThat’s how we get a double entendre with the term “cut a nigga cast off”.  In one sense it means canceling a show, because the actors (cast) are all fired (cut off).  It also is an expression for removing a medical cast after, say, a broken arm is healed.  The irony of this dual meaning is that removal of a medical cast is painless, but a show’s cancelation can hurt those involved a lot, as referenced in the article above.", "annotation_id": "2820437", "url": "https://genius.com/2820437", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Nobody", "line": "Chinchillas on a winter night", "vault_lines": ["Chinchillas on a winter night"], "meaning": "#BRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRR!!!\n\n\n\nChinchilla fur is an extremely soft and expensive material from an adorable animal that is used to make gaudy fur coats.\n\nDon’t let Peta hear this line, Ricky.", "annotation_id": "2820341", "url": "https://genius.com/2820341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
