{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "OG", "line": "We fuck to Oochie Wally, told Jungle I caught a groupie", "vault_lines": ["We fuck to Oochie Wally, told Jungle I caught a groupie"], "meaning": "Nas is referring to the person who cosigned him and his mentor, Nas and the Bravehearts’s 2000 single “Oochie Wally.” Jungle, Nas’s brother was part of the Bravehearts and the single was part of their collaboration project, QB’s Finest. The themes of each song revolve around sex.", "annotation_id": "18527001", "url": "https://genius.com/18527001", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "OG", "line": "Just make ’em wipe me down like I’m Lil Boosie", "vault_lines": ["Just make 'em wipe me down like I'm Lil Boosie"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Boosie who was formerly known as Lil Boosie and his song “Wipe me Down.”", "annotation_id": "18486752", "url": "https://genius.com/18486752", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "OG", "line": "Cuban rope like Richard Porter, I’m just tryna eat like Yogi", "vault_lines": ["Cuban rope like Richard Porter, I'm just tryna eat like Yogi"], "meaning": "Dave is referring to Richard Porter who was a prominent drug dealer during the 80s in Harlem New York where Dave is from. Richard often sported a Cuban rope which is a gold chain ranging from $1,00 to $10,000.", "annotation_id": "18479628", "url": "https://genius.com/18479628", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
