{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Going Donald Trump numbers on the corner", "vault_lines": ["Going Donald Trump numbers on the corner"], "meaning": "Donald Trump, a highly successful business man (and now president of The United States) estimated at a whopping 3.7 billion dollars, is a model to follow for anyone trying to become rich or successful.  By saying he is getting “Donald Trump numbers”, Meek is saying that he knows what it takes to be successful in the hood.", "annotation_id": "11143030", "url": "https://genius.com/11143030", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Kingpin status when I swerve up on the block", "vault_lines": ["Kingpin status when I swerve up on the block"], "meaning": "We all know Rozay is a boss, which is why “kingpin status” fits his character nicely. A drug kingpin is all the way at the top of the food chain within the drug ring, he makes the most money, and he’s the boss.", "annotation_id": "3132872", "url": "https://genius.com/3132872", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "I bought some coke but couldn’t deal with Arizona", "vault_lines": ["I bought some coke but couldn't deal with Arizona"], "meaning": "The cartel often ships Cocaine up to the states by smuggling it from Mexico through Arizona. Meek doesn’t want to deal with the middle man, so he got it straight from the connect to increase his profits.", "annotation_id": "3127539", "url": "https://genius.com/3127539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "But I got stripes like a bengal does", "vault_lines": ["All these niggas on angel bruh, but I got stripes like a bengal does"], "meaning": "In the armed forces or the police – stripes are V shaped bands of material sewn onto a uniform to indicate the rank of corporal or sergeant. To earn your stripes mean that one has to prove one’s diligence and bravery to get promoted and receive the stripe after deserving it. Meek has earned his in the streets, and uses the analogy of a striped Bengal Tiger to show how many he has.", "annotation_id": "3127519", "url": "https://genius.com/3127519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Givenchy all I really play", "vault_lines": ["Givenchy all I really play"], "meaning": "To Play with something is stating sexual implications. Furthermore, one could say that saying “All I really play” could translate into “All I really fuck with”.\n\nGivenchy is an expensive designer brand similar to Gucci, Louis Vuttion, or Versace.\n\nUltimately, Ross is saying he only fucks with the High-end, designer items.\n\n\n\nIn the picture above Ross can be seen rocking the Givenchy Rottweiler T-Shirt.", "annotation_id": "3127359", "url": "https://genius.com/3127359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "I’m on the corner gettin’ cake I’m talkin’ like it’s 88", "vault_lines": ["I'm on the corner gettin' cake", "I'm talkin' like it's 88"], "meaning": "Cake is a slang term for cocaine. Rozay says this in the present tense, and follows up with letting us know the setting of his story.\n\nHe is sharing this story as if it is 1988, back when he was involved in a less legitimate way of acquiring paper.\n\n\n\nNote: “cake” could also be alluding to money.", "annotation_id": "3125471", "url": "https://genius.com/3125471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": ".357 get put in your place", "vault_lines": [".357 get put in your place"], "meaning": "357 is in reference to the .357 Magnum. The .357 is well known to be a rather big and frightening handgun, and with that much firepower, Meek will put you in your place.", "annotation_id": "3125211", "url": "https://genius.com/3125211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "M-m-m-m-a", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The iconic tag for any Maybach Music Group song.", "annotation_id": "3123607", "url": "https://genius.com/3123607", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Been through your hood in a wraith, niggas is jealous, just look at your face", "vault_lines": ["Been through your hood in a wraith, niggas is jealous, just look at your face"], "meaning": "Meek is going through the hood in a $300,000 dollar Rolls Royce Wraith.\n\nIn the first “Inside the Lines” with RZA, he said,\n\nYou would go to a block party with a new leather jacket, a cambo hat, and some adidas you were risking your life…because not everybody had that\n\nMeek is saying that he took that risk and made other’s jealous and furthermore he did it just to see the look in the faces of his peers.", "annotation_id": "3121557", "url": "https://genius.com/3121557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Ugh, Double M, bang!", "vault_lines": ["Ugh, Double M, bang!"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group is Rick Ross' label he founded in 2009. He signed Meek Mill in 2011.", "annotation_id": "3121467", "url": "https://genius.com/3121467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Might pop a perk, go mad long like skrrt", "vault_lines": ["Might pop a perk, go mad long like skrrt"], "meaning": "Perk as in the painkiller percocet, something Meek has referenced multiple times as his “on switch” in sexual situations.\n\nFor example like on the song Tony Montana:\n\nI pop a perk, I fuck yo bitch\n  got you blowing up her phone while she suckin dick\n\n\n\nAlso, while under the influence of Percocet ones sex drive is elongated. The body takes a much longer time to climax, therefore, enabling meek to go mad long.", "annotation_id": "3121449", "url": "https://genius.com/3121449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "I made a million on that corner Going Donald Trump numbers on the corner I made a million on that corner", "vault_lines": ["Going Donald Trump numbers on the corner"], "meaning": "Meek Mill is rolling in dough from selling drugs in the corner.\n\nSo much so that he compares himself to being the Donald Trump of the streets.\n\n\n\nRetrospectively Meek is chillin' bruh", "annotation_id": "3121431", "url": "https://genius.com/3121431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "And my wrist look like the flash on", "vault_lines": ["And my wrist look like the flash on"], "meaning": "Meek is expressing that his watch has so many diamonds and other highly reflective objects in it that is flashing.\n\nComparable to a camera when the flash feature is active.\n\n\n\nIn this picture, Meek is showcasing his iced out Audemar Piguet and Rolex watches.", "annotation_id": "3121264", "url": "https://genius.com/3121264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "I made a million on that corner I mixed perico with baking soda", "vault_lines": ["I made a million on that corner", "I mixed perico with baking soda"], "meaning": "Perico are the fragments of cocaine that fall off the brick in the packing process. These are usually small quantities of cocaine and because of that dealers often cut the product with baking soda, and to be more specific usually arm and hammer.\n\nOther rappers and dealers often refrain from admitting or knowingly adding baking soda to their product to reserve the right to deem their cocaine Pure. Otherwise it is a freebase offset of cocaine known as crack cocaine.\n\nSuch as Gunplay:\n\nWith all this Hannah Montana, without the Arm and Hammer\n\n\n\nIt is apparent that Meek is stating that the way he made a million on that corner is by doing what he had to in order to gain the most money. Selling a cheaper offset of cocaine and maximizing profits.", "annotation_id": "3121227", "url": "https://genius.com/3121227", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Start the Rolls Royce with the angel up", "vault_lines": ["Start the Rolls Royce with the angel up"], "meaning": "The Spirit of ecstasy, the Rolls Royce hood ornament, more commonly known as the Rolls Royce Angel is an iconic instrument that originated with the affair between John Douglas-Scott-Montagu and Eleanor Thornton.\n\nAs the story goes, Montagu, asked Claude Johnson the managing director of Rolls Royce Motor Cars to produce a custom angel like figure resembling his secret love on the hood of his car. The company loved the ornament so much that it became a trademark. Currently, the angel is well renowned as a symbol of wealth and class with a not so secret history.", "annotation_id": "3121194", "url": "https://genius.com/3121194", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "And my clique armed and dangerous, and we’ll flame you up You get smoked mothafucker like angel dust", "vault_lines": ["And my clique armed and dangerous, and we'll flame you up", "You get smoked mothafucker like angel dust"], "meaning": "This line references Biggie Small’s first line, in his song featuring Bone Thugs-n-Harmony called Notorious Thugs\n\nIn notorious thugs first verse, Biggie says:\n\nArmed and dangerous, ain’t too many can bang with us\n\n\n\nMeek lets you know that his crew is full people ready to kill on site in more ways than one. To flame you up is to gun you down, and filling you up with lead. He will smoke you like the drug angel dust, to smoke someone means to shoot them.", "annotation_id": "3121177", "url": "https://genius.com/3121177", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "line": "Them yellow diamonds looking clearer than Corona", "vault_lines": ["Them yellow diamonds looking clearer than Corona"], "meaning": "This displays just how wealthy Meek is:\n\nMeek Mill is so wealthy that he can afford to buy expensive and luxurious yellow tinted diamonds that are so pure, that they are almost as clear as the highly transparent (and yellow colored) Corona beer.", "annotation_id": "3120705", "url": "https://genius.com/3120705", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off The Corner", "status": "done", "targets": 17, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Meek-mill-off-the-corner-lyrics", "genius_title": "Off The Corner", "genius_id": 413169, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off the Boat", "line": "I got put in a rental, and I’m strapped like I’m Boobie Had more guns in the car than the whole state of Missouri", "vault_lines": ["Had more guns in the car than the whole state of Missouri"], "meaning": "Drug dealers normally operate out of rental cars, that way their personal property doesn’t get seized and no evidence can be traced back to them.\n\nKenneth “Boobie” Williams was the leader of the Miami based gang, The Boobie Boys; who were responsible for more than one hundred shootings and thirty five murders. They established drug operations that smuggled over five tons of coke across Florida. In 2000, Kenneth and other members of The Boobie Boys were sentenced to life in prison.\n\nSpeaking in a 2011 statement, Ross talked on how Kenneth inspired him and his music:\n\nThe dude that initially put me into the music game is Boobie. My music touches on his lifestyle. Boobie helped a lot of people in the hood and inspired a lot of positive things [..] The stuff I talk about is real. The dope is real. The gun talk is official.", "annotation_id": "12817548", "url": "https://genius.com/12817548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off the Boat", "line": "Maybach on Monday, Testarossa on Tuesday", "vault_lines": ["Maybach on Monday, Testarossa on Tuesday"], "meaning": "The Mercedes Maybach is an expensive luxury German car manufactured by Mercedes. Ross is known to associate himself with the brand, naming his record label and music series after it. In a 2012 interview with MTV News, he spoke about his thoughts on the brand:\n\nI think, just that level of luxury is just inspiration for people who started, like myself, who just looked and fantasized.\n\nRoss was also pictured in a Maybach on the cover of his 2008 sophomore album Trilla, which photographer Jonathan Mannion commented on in a 2012 interview with Complex:\n\nWe shot him in the Maybach, and it just happened to rain. All the little speckles fit perfectly.\n\n\n\nThe Ferrari Testarossa is a mid-engine sports car which was manufactured by Ferrari between 1984 to 1991. “Testarossa”—which means red head in Italian—was the name given to the car because it’s engine featured two red-colored rocker covers.", "annotation_id": "12817386", "url": "https://genius.com/12817386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off the Boat", "line": "I get it fresh off the boat, I get it ’cross the Atlantic", "vault_lines": ["I get it fresh off the boat, I get it 'cross the Atlantic"], "meaning": "“I get it fresh off the boat”\nHe is probably referring to cigarette speed boats that are used to complete the dope smuggling operation like in the movies Cocaine Cowboys and Bad Boys 2.\n\n“I get it cross the Atlantic”\nHe is essentially bragging that he is major drug dealer who smuggles dope from South America via cargo ships that travel to the U.S. across the Atlantic ocean.\n\nThis couplet is also a reference to Rozay’s debut single, Hustlin':\n\nI’m into distribution, I’m like Atlantic\nI got them mothafuckas flyin' across the Atlantic", "annotation_id": "809749", "url": "https://genius.com/809749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off the Boat", "line": "The R.I.C.O", "vault_lines": ["Now they tapping my phones, wanna give me the R.I.C.O"], "meaning": "RICO is the Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act, a US law often used to prosecute organized crime groups such as the Mafia and drug gangs.", "annotation_id": "554417", "url": "https://genius.com/554417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Off the Boat", "line": "This that her’on flow, I should’ve signed to Atlantic", "vault_lines": ["This that her'on flow, I should've signed to Atlantic"], "meaning": "Atlantic Records, legendary record label co-founded by equally legendary record executive Ahmet Ertegün, has been home to many artists who have had drug/heroin addictions, most famously Ray Charles.", "annotation_id": "532871", "url": "https://genius.com/532871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
