{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "She asked me if I do this every day, I said “Often” Asked how many times she rode the wave, “Not so often” Bitches down to do it either way, often Baby I can make that pussy rain, often Often, often, girl I do this often Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it Often, often, girl I do this often Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it Often", "vault_lines": ["Asked how many times she rode the wave, \"Not so often\"", "Bitches down to do it either way, often", "Baby I can make that pussy rain, often", "Often, often, girl I do this often", "Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it"], "meaning": "Weeknd downplayed the “make that pussy rain” line in an interview with Rolling Stone saying\n\nI mean, no girl has ever actually rained…I don’t want to sound like that guy where sex is not an obstacle. But I’ve had a lot of sex.\n\nFrom “Kiss Land” to “Initiation” to pretty much any of his songs, Abel “often” paints a picture of his sexual experiences.\n\nDespite her lack of sexual experience, this girl’s more than willing to jump at the opportunity of just one night with Abel. This isn’t the first time he’s had a good girl fall prey to his charm.\n\n“Wave,” “rain,” and all things aquatic have an affinity with a drug fuelled sexual experience. From the “surfboard” sex position popularized by Beyonce’s song “Drunk In Love” (which he remixed), to riding the “wave” of a molly/ecstasy induced high, Abel’s telling us he’s great at pleasing her in bed.", "annotation_id": "25055766", "url": "https://genius.com/25055766", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "Oooh, the sun’s risin’ up The night’s almost up The night’s almost done But I see your eyes You wanna go again Girl, I’ll go again Girl, I’ll go again", "vault_lines": ["Oooh, the sun's risin' up", "The night's almost up", "The night's almost done", "But I see your eyes", "You wanna go again", "Girl, I'll go again"], "meaning": "The morning is almost upon them and the girl is still there ready to undertake round 2.\n\nAbel’s really trying to get some, considering he’s already thought about how she’s gonna feel when the sun rises:\n\nBetter slow down\nShe’ll feel it in the morning", "annotation_id": "25055759", "url": "https://genius.com/25055759", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "She asked me if I do this every day, I said “Often” Asked how many times she rode the wave, “Not so often” Bitches down to do it either way, often Baby I can make that pussy rain, often Often, often, girl I do this often Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it Often, often, girl I do this often Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it Often", "vault_lines": ["Asked how many times she rode the wave, \"Not so often\"", "Bitches down to do it either way, often", "Baby I can make that pussy rain, often", "Often, often, girl I do this often", "Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it"], "meaning": "Weeknd downplayed the “make that pussy rain” line in an interview with Rolling Stone saying\n\nI mean, no girl has ever actually rained…I don’t want to sound like that guy where sex is not an obstacle. But I’ve had a lot of sex.\n\nFrom “Kiss Land” to “Initiation” to pretty much any of his songs, Abel “often” paints a picture of his sexual experiences.\n\nDespite her lack of sexual experience, this girl’s more than willing to jump at the opportunity of just one night with Abel. This isn’t the first time he’s had a good girl fall prey to his charm.\n\n“Wave,” “rain,” and all things aquatic have an affinity with a drug fuelled sexual experience. From the “surfboard” sex position popularized by Beyonce’s song “Drunk In Love” (which he remixed), to riding the “wave” of a molly/ecstasy induced high, Abel’s telling us he’s great at pleasing her in bed.", "annotation_id": "25055750", "url": "https://genius.com/25055750", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "She asked me if I do this every day, I said “Often” Asked how many times she rode the wave, “Not so often” Bitches down to do it either way, often Baby I can make that pussy rain, often Often, often, girl I do this often Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it Often, often, girl I do this often Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it Often", "vault_lines": ["Asked how many times she rode the wave, \"Not so often\"", "Bitches down to do it either way, often", "Baby I can make that pussy rain, often", "Often, often, girl I do this often", "Make that pussy pop and do it how I want it"], "meaning": "Weeknd downplayed the “make that pussy rain” line in an interview with Rolling Stone saying\n\nI mean, no girl has ever actually rained…I don’t want to sound like that guy where sex is not an obstacle. But I’ve had a lot of sex.\n\nFrom “Kiss Land” to “Initiation” to pretty much any of his songs, Abel “often” paints a picture of his sexual experiences.\n\nDespite her lack of sexual experience, this girl’s more than willing to jump at the opportunity of just one night with Abel. This isn’t the first time he’s had a good girl fall prey to his charm.\n\n“Wave,” “rain,” and all things aquatic have an affinity with a drug fuelled sexual experience. From the “surfboard” sex position popularized by Beyonce’s song “Drunk In Love” (which he remixed), to riding the “wave” of a molly/ecstasy induced high, Abel’s telling us he’s great at pleasing her in bed.", "annotation_id": "25055724", "url": "https://genius.com/25055724", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "My god white, he in my pocket He get me redder than the devil ’til I go nauseous", "vault_lines": ["My god white, he in my pocket", "He get me redder than the devil 'til I go nauseous"], "meaning": "The white drug is a stimulant that he often enjoys, but his high comes with side effects like a flushed face as red as Satan’s and some nausea.\n\n\n\nThe line “my God white” is layered; there has always been talk among the hip-hop community that Jesus Christ was a man of colour. Abel as a black man is flipping this script, although only as a clever tongue-in-cheek drug reference.", "annotation_id": "25055700", "url": "https://genius.com/25055700", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "In my city I’m a young god That pussy kill be so vicious", "vault_lines": ["In my city I'm a young god", "That pussy kill be so vicious"], "meaning": "Abel is from Scarborough, Ontario—a district of eastern Toronto.\n\nHe is one of the most iconic members of its budding music scene that includes the likes of Drake, Deadmau5, Sean Leon, and Sway Clarke II.\n\n\n\nNot only is he known for being a “god” musically, but he also claims to be renowned in his sexual prowess with the Toronto ladies—ready to “kill the pussy”.", "annotation_id": "25055687", "url": "https://genius.com/25055687", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "You ain’t gonna catch me with them sneak pictures", "vault_lines": ["You ain't gonna catch me with them sneak pictures"], "meaning": "Abel isn’t going to be like other stars and get caught on camera sleeping with girls lowkey. He’s already admitted he isn’t about girls chilling with him just to get pics to take away; if they’re about that, they can go.", "annotation_id": "25055679", "url": "https://genius.com/25055679", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "I usually love sleeping all alone This time around bring your friend with you", "vault_lines": ["This time around bring your friend with you"], "meaning": "Abel is definitely not a man of commitment, and once business is done and his needs are met, he likes having solitude. However tonight he feels like having more fun–a threesome. Two chicks is better than one, right?\n\n\n\nThis opening also serves to parallel the sampled poem, as Abel isn’t feeling the desire for loneliness this time around.", "annotation_id": "25055614", "url": "https://genius.com/25055614", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "[Produced by Ben Billions]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The high pitched vocals heard throughout are sampled from a Turkish song “Ben Sana Vurgunum” by Nükhet Duru.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E0lI5169AYM&t=1s\n\nThe line that repeats is: “Seneler sürer her günüm, Yalnız gitmekten yorgunum.”\n\nThis translates to: “Each day takes years, I’m tired of walking alone.”", "annotation_id": "25055573", "url": "https://genius.com/25055573", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Often (Remix)", "line": "When she climax she make pee pee", "vault_lines": [", when she climax she make pee pee"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nWhen a girl climaxes, the fluid that is discharged is mainly comprised of urine. Therefore, when she climax she make pee pee.", "annotation_id": "19866232", "url": "https://genius.com/19866232", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
