{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oh My Gosh (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yemi-alade-oh-my-gosh-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Oh My Gosh (Remix)", "genius_id": 4542586, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Have the shots of the tequila", "vault_lines": ["We pop bottles, have the shots of the tequila"], "meaning": "“After Shots Of Tequila”  refers to chasing tequila shots with wine, usually sparkling or champagne. Follows the line before that says “put the dutch out, light a cuban up” which is taking the best and hardest plunge first, then chasing it with something more mellow.", "annotation_id": "14395766", "url": "https://genius.com/14395766", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Three man weave, I dump it off to the trailer", "vault_lines": ["Three man weave, I dump it off to the trailer"], "meaning": "The three man weave is a common drill used in basketball practices. It’s designed for a fast break. Kiss is comparing his 3 man smoking rotation to the three man weave in basketball. Also, the trailer in the three man weave is the last person down the court on the weave, so he’s passing the weed to whoever has c’s", "annotation_id": "1856418", "url": "https://genius.com/1856418", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "A scotch in the soda anastasia.com", "vault_lines": ["A scotch in the soda anastasia.com"], "meaning": "A reference to the famous gangster Albert Anastasia who was killed in a bar, which is the meaning behind the “a scotch in the soda…” line.", "annotation_id": "1855545", "url": "https://genius.com/1855545", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "If the pack too loud, dump it off with the sealer", "vault_lines": ["If the pack too loud, dump it off with the sealer"], "meaning": "In marijuana distribution, if the bag you have smells too strong, put it in vacum sealed bags to avoid detection", "annotation_id": "1843904", "url": "https://genius.com/1843904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Therefore I pray I live a hundred years", "vault_lines": ["Therefore I pray I live a hundred years"], "meaning": "After nearly facing death on his 37th birthday, Rick Ross wants to spend the rest of his days enjoying life making the best out of it. A near death experience has given him a new view on life and he would like to be around for the long-haul now.\n\nThis is new outlook is different that many of other references he’s made about life.\n\nOne of many references Bury me a G", "annotation_id": "1843682", "url": "https://genius.com/1843682", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Champagne, spillin’ the opulence", "vault_lines": ["Champagne, spillin' the opulence"], "meaning": "Opulence is having more resources than needed to live in complete luxury", "annotation_id": "1840611", "url": "https://genius.com/1840611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Tired and chartered a plane, oil money the game", "vault_lines": ["Tired and chartered a plane, oil money the game"], "meaning": "Oil Money: The best of the best money. Money coming from people who own oil companies. Typically money from most middle eastern men and referring to their wealth.\n\nRick Ross was tired so instead of flying commercial, he chartered a private plane", "annotation_id": "1840597", "url": "https://genius.com/1840597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Then I took her to Disney World", "vault_lines": ["Got my daughter a Fendi purse then I took her to Disney World"], "meaning": "Ever wondered how the rich and impatient do Disney World?\n\n\n\nAllegedly for a $1,000 a day you can hire a black market tour guide who uses a motorized scooter labelled “Disabled” to skip the queues. Instead of joining the line for the general public, your party will be sent to a different entrance every time with no queue.\n\nWhile some kids wait on line for hours your kid can be on that ride in minutes.\n\nOr you can do like Tom Cruise and pay a few million to shut down a theme park just for your kids for the day.", "annotation_id": "1840593", "url": "https://genius.com/1840593", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "These niggas barely gettin’ tour money", "vault_lines": ["These niggas barely gettin' tour money"], "meaning": "Touring can be lucrative with Jay-Z earning approximately $15 million dollars a year from his 10 year Live Nation deal. However most rappers are lucky to pull in a few million a year from touring.", "annotation_id": "1840520", "url": "https://genius.com/1840520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Pina colada daiquiris Fontaine Bleau on a Tuesday", "vault_lines": ["Pina colada daiquiris Fontaine Bleau on a Tuesday"], "meaning": "The Fontainebleau Miami Beach or the Fontainebleau Hotel is one of the most historically and architecturally significant hotels on Miami Beach.\n\nSo on tuesdays Rick drinks Pina Colada", "annotation_id": "1840512", "url": "https://genius.com/1840512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Room service come to you on a boat,", "vault_lines": ["Room service come to you on a boat,"], "meaning": "Exclusive vacation accommodation in the Maldives doesn’t involve merely a luxury room in a hotel block on dry land. Instead you get your own villa on stilts over the water with a glass bottomed floor so you can watch the tropical fish.\n\n\n\nHuvafen Fushi in the Maldives.\n\nIt’s even possible to hire the entire resort at a cost of a few million per day if you want complete exclusivity and privacy.", "annotation_id": "1840454", "url": "https://genius.com/1840454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Attempted murder, I refuse to exile", "vault_lines": ["Attempted murder, I refuse to exile"], "meaning": "On Rick’s 37th birthday, his Rolls Royce was met with a storm of bullets. Rick walked away untouched from the situation.\n\nBecause of the size of the vehicle not getting touched by a bullet and Rick’s past about lying about being a parole officer, some speculated that the incident was a publicity stunt.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nlQnOFNeEx4", "annotation_id": "1840187", "url": "https://genius.com/1840187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Tip toein’ through the city, Alvin Ailey with a brick", "vault_lines": ["Tip toein' through the city, Alvin Ailey with a brick"], "meaning": "Alvin Ailey, was African American choreographer and actvist. Rick uses tip toein as a play on words to describe how he’s quietly making moves threw the city distributing drugs (bricks).", "annotation_id": "1840130", "url": "https://genius.com/1840130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Giving niggas jobs, living like the mob", "vault_lines": ["Giving niggas jobs, living like the mob"], "meaning": "In the 1800’s when gangs would move into a town, they would take over it to have control of the money moving in and out. It you were on the gangs turf, the gang may require you to pay a portion of the profits that you made, or they would not charge you anything, but use your business to conduct their business whenever they deemed fit.\n\nMob members would also give people jobs that could pay much more than what a typical 9-5 would, but the work would mean you’re indebted to the mob, which means the end result could be bad.\n\nAl Capone was among some of the greatest mob men that there was.", "annotation_id": "1840000", "url": "https://genius.com/1840000", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Mad at every check you deposit, I see it all in their eyes", "vault_lines": ["Mad at every check you deposit, I see it all in their eyes"], "meaning": "Most people aren’t making the amount of money that they’d like to, to be able to enjoy pay day once it comes. Bills generally take the majority of someone’s check, leaving them with little money to spending, making it hard to part ways with a check once you cash it.\n\nLooking at the money that Rick is making compared to the average person, it’s easy to see why someone could be jealous or angry at their money compared to his.", "annotation_id": "1839848", "url": "https://genius.com/1839848", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "When the money is in the circle, the squares can’t touch it", "vault_lines": ["When the money is in the circle, the squares can't touch it"], "meaning": "Jada is referring to having a strong team of people around you circle and keeping the  naysayers and disloyal ones out squares.\n\nThis wordplay addresses the game of shapes that’s used to teach children different sizes and also plays into Rick’s crews last album “Power Circle”\n\nWale had a line similar to this in the song Power Circle", "annotation_id": "1839783", "url": "https://genius.com/1839783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Vacationing on in the Maldives", "vault_lines": ["Nah, vacationing on in the Maldives"], "meaning": "Maldives, officially the Republic of the Maldives and also referred to as the Maldive Islands, is an island nation in the Indian Ocean.\n\n\n\nI feel your choice Jada..", "annotation_id": "1839436", "url": "https://genius.com/1839436", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "It’s going further my nigga It ain’t even being a dope boy my nigga We talking oil money, oil money, ha, yeah", "vault_lines": ["We talking oil money, oil money, ha, yeah"], "meaning": "The most successful drug dealer ever had an estimated net worth of $30 billion (Pablo Escobar).\n\n\n\nExxon Mobil (oil company) has a net worth of $486.429 Billion. Ross is beyond drug dealing money, he’s also using his lyrics to fuel people much like oil does the industrial world.", "annotation_id": "1839270", "url": "https://genius.com/1839270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Put the dutch out, light a Cuban up", "vault_lines": ["You know? Gon' talk that shit for a minute, put the dutch out, light a Cuban up"], "meaning": "Dutch Masters are a brand of cigar. These are typically not purchased for the smoking of the tobacco inside as they are usually split, emptied and filled with the best of the sticky light greens. Jada could be meaning to portray sophistication by saying put out the cheap cigar and light up a classy cuban cigar. OR he could be referencing the dutch as a blunt and by putting out the dutch he means its time to get serious.", "annotation_id": "1837471", "url": "https://genius.com/1837471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Tryna get a grip, but you just can’t clutch it", "vault_lines": ["Tryna get a grip, but you just can't clutch it"], "meaning": "Jada throws a nice play of words between “grip” and “clutch”. The clutch, of course, is the part of a car that transfers power from the engine to the wheel. No clutch, no movement and therefore, your tires won’t grip anything!", "annotation_id": "1837460", "url": "https://genius.com/1837460", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Best head I got in my life, for a Chanel bag", "vault_lines": ["Best head I got in my life, for a Chanel bag"], "meaning": "Jadakiss has enough money to pay girls off for sexual favors by purchasing things like Chanel bags for them. In this particular instance, a girl performed the best head he has received in his life for a Chanel bag.\n\n\n\nA classic Chanel flap bag as of 2013 retails for over $4,000. The prices are put up every year by much more than the rate of inflation.", "annotation_id": "1837454", "url": "https://genius.com/1837454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Classics stay on my feet,", "vault_lines": ["Classics stay on my feet,"], "meaning": "Despite his official split with Reebok earlier in 2013 over U.O.E.N.O controversey, Ricky is still rocking his Reebok classics.\n\nRoss has recently denoted he has no ill feelings towards Reebok and describes his relationship with Reebok has “healthy”. There was even rumors of Ross resigning with Reebok in early May.", "annotation_id": "1837446", "url": "https://genius.com/1837446", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Probably gon’ rang, Gareth Pugh and Belstaff", "vault_lines": ["Probably gon' rang, Gareth Pugh and Belstaff"], "meaning": "Gareth Pugh is an English Fashion designer who currently lives and works in Paris. Belstaff is a British brand founded in Longton, Staffordshire in 1924. They are known for “iconic outerwear and designer fashion with handbags, shoes and accessories to finish the look.”", "annotation_id": "1837034", "url": "https://genius.com/1837034", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "So it’s Club LIV til I’m exed out", "vault_lines": ["So it's Club LIV til I'm exed out"], "meaning": "Club LIV is perhaps the biggest & most exclusive night club in Miami. Rozay has mentioned the club in previous lyrics and is known to party there quite often.\n\nHe’s gonna club til the day he dies. Wordplay on live and exed out/dead.", "annotation_id": "1836851", "url": "https://genius.com/1836851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "line": "Uhh... Mastermind, ha", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The name of Rozay’s upcoming sixth studio album, scheduled for a 2013 release.", "annotation_id": "1836847", "url": "https://genius.com/1836847", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Oil Money Gang", "status": "done", "targets": 25, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-oil-money-gang-lyrics", "genius_title": "Oil Money Gang", "genius_id": 161011, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Diamonds drippin’ on me, she know who the one", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds drippin' on me, she know who the one"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is referring to one of the first singles released from this same album titled “I’m the One,” which featured Justin Bieber, Chance the Rapper, Quavo, and Lil Wayne. This song was very successful topping the Billboard Charts at number 1.", "annotation_id": "12286395", "url": "https://genius.com/12286395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "I walk up to my fate and stare that shit in the face", "vault_lines": ["I walk up to my fate and stare that shit in the face"], "meaning": "Big Sean has made sacrifices during his career, and he knows that some might hurt his career.\n\nRegardless, he knows that he needs to take risks because that’s how life works, even if that risk can be going at Kendrick.\n\nIf this is a shot at Kendrick, this could be Sean talking to Kendrick and telling him that he is ready and not afraid of going against him, even if it might hurt his career, he will accept his fate of going at Kendrick at any cost.", "annotation_id": "12262001", "url": "https://genius.com/12262001", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Top down, JFK, I pray he get impeached", "vault_lines": ["Top down, JFK, I pray he get impeached"], "meaning": "John F. Kennedy was the 35th president of the United States. On November 22, 1963 JFK was assassinated as he rode in a convertible during a motorcade through Dealey Plaza in Dallas, Texas.\n\nRick Ross continues the theme of American presidents when he prays for impeachment. Ross is most likely referring to the 45th president Donald Trump, as he has been outspoken against his campaign. Ross received controversy for his anti-Trump lyrics in his song “Free Enterprise” where he raps about assassinating Trump rather than impeaching him:\n\n“Assassinate Trump like I’m Zimmerman”", "annotation_id": "12255096", "url": "https://genius.com/12255096", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Ayy, DJ Khaled, I’d die for you, my nigga So you already know I’d kill for you, boss (Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, DJ Khaled, I'd die for you, my nigga", "So you already know I'd kill for you, boss (Maybach Music)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross and DJ Khaled are neighbors in Miami and have been friends for decades—Rick Ross appeared on DJ Khaled’s debut single “Holla At Me” way back in 2006.", "annotation_id": "12227772", "url": "https://genius.com/12227772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Aquafina, she drippin’ puddles on a sunny day", "vault_lines": ["Aquafina, she drippin' puddles on a sunny day"], "meaning": "Aquafina is a brand of bottled water beverages  owned by PepsiCo. Rozay compares the brand to a woman’s sex drive—even though it’s a warm day, he still turns her on.", "annotation_id": "12211351", "url": "https://genius.com/12211351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "I just left work to work some more, I’m still a workaholic I done sacrificed it all, paid the dues and costs", "vault_lines": ["I done sacrificed it all, paid the dues and costs"], "meaning": "Sean’s constantly reminding us of his work ethic; for example, on his 2015 track “Blessings,” he dropped similar lines about his commitment to the game:\n\nFuck a vacay, I feel better at work\n\nIn a February 2017 interview with the Breakfast Club, he said:\n\nI put that work in. You not gon’ disrespect me. I’ll hope on any track with anybody, and I will not only stand my own, you gonna know that it’s my verse, and you gonna know I’m in it.\n\nThe second line is a reference to Sean’s February 2017 Migos-assisted song “Sacrifices”:\n\nI done made sacrifices, so many sacrifices\nI done gave up so much free time knowing time ain’t free", "annotation_id": "12210784", "url": "https://genius.com/12210784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Boy, I’m a Caesar, I see shit and seize it", "vault_lines": ["Boy, I'm a Caesar, I see shit and seize it"], "meaning": "Julius Caesar was a Roman general who went on to conquer many civilizations and became one of the most influential rulers in the history of the world. Sean’s proclaiming himself a dominating figure in the rap game; he isn’t afraid to eclipse the competition. This ties into the famous Roman saying “Carpe Diem,” meaning “seize the day.”\n\nAlso, Julius Caesar’s most popular turn of phrase “Veni Vidi Vici” which means, “I came; I saw; I conquered”. This literally represents “see[ing] shit and seiz[ing] it”.\n\n\n\nCaesar is also a a hair style that Big Sean sports, as well as Nas, whose classic track “Ether” is mentioned in the next line.", "annotation_id": "12210739", "url": "https://genius.com/12210739", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Chasin’ a hundred million, baby, my natural ambition, boss", "vault_lines": ["Chasin' a hundred million, baby, my natural ambition, boss"], "meaning": "The acquisition of wealth and chasing mogul status has been a mainstay motif in Rick Ross’s music for years, but he publicly announced his specific goal of reaching $100 million in May of 2017, when Best Seat In the House interviewed him about having allegedly ended the beef between Drake and Meek Mill. Ross added that he and the people around him were trying to “touch nine figures”:\n\nWe wasn’t even discussing anything negative because by the time we get in the room, it’s so much other things going on that it’s already, ‘Let’s get on some money.’ But I had to just make sure we sat down and had some sort of understanding. It’s all about trying to touch nine figures.", "annotation_id": "12208330", "url": "https://genius.com/12208330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "We The Best Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "These are all DJ Khaled’s famous ad-libs. He shouts out his label, We the Best Music, which he founded in 2008.\n\n“DJ Khaled!” is used on most of his tracks since the early 2000s.", "annotation_id": "12208193", "url": "https://genius.com/12208193", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Hundred for the rich forever perspective, never change", "vault_lines": ["Hundred for the rich forever perspective, never change"], "meaning": "Rich Forever is the title of Rozay’s third mixtape, released on January 6, 2012. It’s also his Instagram username.", "annotation_id": "12208166", "url": "https://genius.com/12208166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Yeah, they don’t really fuckin’ feel me Man, but when you really run it they try and clip your Achilles’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they don't really fuckin' feel me", "Man, but when you really run it they try and clip your Achilles'"], "meaning": "Achilles is a warrior from Greek mythology known to be invincible aside from one of his heels; that heel led to his  eventual defeat.\n\n\n\nAn “Achilles heel” in modern language refers to a weakness—Sean is saying that any rapper that finds success in the industry will always have entities trying to take them down.", "annotation_id": "12208023", "url": "https://genius.com/12208023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "I’m on track to a billi’, I got Khaled fuckin’ with me That mean I got the Holy Key and got the key to the city, lil nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm on track to a billi', I got Khaled fuckin' with me", "That mean I got the Holy Key and got the key to the city, lil nigga"], "meaning": "This may be a jab at Kendrick Lamar, who appeared on DJ Khaled’s 2016 song “Holy Key” along with Big Sean and Betty Wright.\n\nBoth Sean and Kendrick own the keys to their respective cities—Detroit and Compton—but Sean believes only one of them has the “Holy Key\"—Khaled’s cosign. While both Sean and Kendrick appeared on Major Key, only Sean appears on Grateful.\n\nThis is also a play on DJ Khaled’s phrase “I got the keys to more success.\"\n\nBig Sean was awarded the Key to Detroit by Mike Duggan, the city mayor.", "annotation_id": "12207985", "url": "https://genius.com/12207985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "And I realized all I ever needed was in me, nigga S on my chest, boy, so shots can’t even pinch me, nigga No substitute for me, but they gon’ still tempt me, nigga God is in me, that’s the only one who can end me, nigga", "vault_lines": ["And I realized all I ever needed was in me, nigga", "S on my chest, boy, so shots can't even pinch me, nigga", "No substitute for me, but they gon' still tempt me, nigga"], "meaning": "On Big Sean’s 2016 track “No More Interviews,” he called out his collaborator Kendrick Lamar, rapping:\n\nAnd I’m just not impressed by you niggas rapping fast\nWho sound like one big asthma attack but trash when I’m rapping it back\nWho you put in your top five and claim they the savior of rap\n\nKendrick responded to the subliminal shots on “The Heart Part 4,” and some would argue he also responded on the chorus of “HUMBLE.,” mimicking Sean’s trademark “lil bitch” ad-lib.\n\nSean compares himself to Superman, whose skin is able to deflect bullets from human guns. Similarly, “shots” from rappers—namely Kendrick—can’t take him down.", "annotation_id": "12207909", "url": "https://genius.com/12207909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Everything", "line": "Roc-A-Fella chain, but you can still get Ether’d", "vault_lines": ["Roc-A-Fella chain, but you can still get Ether'd"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Nas' 2001 diss track “Ether,” which was aimed at JAY-Z, the head of Roc-A-Fella Records. The song is regarded as one of the best disses in rap history, and caused the term “ether” to become synonymous with roasting someone to the point of humiliation. Sean’s warning his competition (potentially Kendrick Lamar in particular) that he won’t hesitate to put them on blast in the same way.\n\nIn February 2017, JAY-Z presented Big Sean with a coveted Roc-A-Fella chain following the release of his album I Decided.  The chain is usually given to those who sign to Roc Nation, but JAY has made it a custom to present the chain to artists he feels have properly established themselves in the rap game.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BQCThwbBov7/", "annotation_id": "12207843", "url": "https://genius.com/12207843", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
