{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Top of the World", "line": "This is mafia music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Here Rick Ross kick starts the song in a typical gangster-rap fashion claiming it’s aimed toward the gangster demographic.\n\nMr. Ross often likes to play the role of a true bonafide  criminal to perpetuate his gangster image (regardless of his law-enforcement history).", "annotation_id": "1895459", "url": "https://genius.com/1895459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "On Top of the World", "line": "Baby mamas I hate ’em They just want you to pay ’em", "vault_lines": ["They just want you to pay 'em"], "meaning": "Rick Ross isn’t a fan of paying child support for the mothers of his children, saying they just take advantage of his money for themselves.", "annotation_id": "1743481", "url": "https://genius.com/1743481", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
