{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One Love", "line": "One, two, three The crew was called DPG And if you wanna go to the tip top Stop the violence in hip-hop", "vault_lines": ["The crew was called DPG", "And if you wanna go to the tip top", "Stop the violence in hip-hop"], "meaning": "A call for peace and unity which is a paraphrase/reference to a lyric from BDP’s stop the violence – also quoted by Blackstar and The Fugees – https://genius.com/Boogie-down-productions-stop-the-violence-lyrics#note-11440798 – on this occasion I would hazard that DPG stands for Dogg Pound Gangstaz", "annotation_id": "17469700", "url": "https://genius.com/17469700", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
