{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One More Shot", "line": "Couple real niggas repping that BCG", "vault_lines": [", couple real niggas repping that BCG"], "meaning": "BCG, which stands for Blue Collar Gang, is one of Stalley’s rap groups, including MMG.", "annotation_id": "4442330", "url": "https://genius.com/4442330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One More Shot", "line": "We just tryna party, I ain’t tryna hurt nobody But my nigga got the hammer on him like a tool kit", "vault_lines": ["We just tryna party, I ain’t tryna hurt nobody", "But my nigga got the hammer on him like a tool kit"], "meaning": "Reference to the YG song I Wanna Party, Stally rather keep the peace. Like the song say:\n\nI just wanna party, I don’t wanna hurt nobody\nBut I’ll beat the fuck out of a nigga, why you bullshittin'?\n\nStally is also letting you know that they’re strapped and ready.", "annotation_id": "4257418", "url": "https://genius.com/4257418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One More Shot", "line": "Party over here, party next door Party on the dance floor, damn little shawty too thick", "vault_lines": ["Party over here, party next door", "Party on the dance floor, damn little shawty too thick"], "meaning": "The festivities are in full ger, party next door could just be a clever way of shouting out the artist PartNextDoor. Stalley is eyeing a fine thick young female as well.", "annotation_id": "4257373", "url": "https://genius.com/4257373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One More Shot", "line": "Got my G’s right, yeah my G’s right Keep sipping like it’s free tonight Got money, power, respect, the keys in life", "vault_lines": ["Got my G's right, yeah my G's right", "Keep sipping like it’s free tonight", "Got money, power, respect, the keys in life"], "meaning": "August’s crew is feeling buzzed, but they still crave for more so they’re ordering drinks like it’s on the house.\n\nInspired by Scarface and keeping the thug theme alive, pne of the most iconic and true quotes by Scarface. Money Rules the World,\nwith money comes the power and essentially that’s the key to life. Then you can really get what you want in the world.\n\nA Double Entendre?\n\n‘'Keys’‘ is slang for kilos of cocaine, which was not only sold by Tony but august as well which you might have heard in his music. So August could be saying that he got money and respect due to the keys being in his life.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c3RFzgOp-5k", "annotation_id": "4257125", "url": "https://genius.com/4257125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One More Shot", "line": "Shot after shot, now we got a whole clip", "vault_lines": ["Shot after shot, now we got a whole clip"], "meaning": "‘'Loading’‘ your body with shots until its full and you’re faded so you can be ready to party or go to war.\n\n\n\nThis is reminiscent of Kendrick Lamar’s bridge\n‘'Swimming Pools’‘ where Kendrick had similar firearm/alcohol metaphor. August is basically saying that they are abusing alcohol while keeping in touch with the thuggish undertones in the theme of this song.", "annotation_id": "4256940", "url": "https://genius.com/4256940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One More Shot", "line": "Parking lot and my top down, never turning my ‘Pac down Me against the world and a bag of weed", "vault_lines": ["Parking lot and my top down, never turning my ‘Pac down", "Me against the world and a bag of weed"], "meaning": "Several references to 2Pac here. The first is that Pac was often portrayed in videos in a parking lot in a convertible (top down). Ross will never turn Pac’s music down, this might be a reference to his death – even though Tupac himself is dead, his music is still alive. Lastly, he makes a reference to Pac’s 3rd studio album, Me Against The World.", "annotation_id": "4125765", "url": "https://genius.com/4125765", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "One More Shot", "line": "Ciroc shots, black bottle Belaire Fresher than the Fresh Prince, hell yeah boy I do this", "vault_lines": ["Ciroc shots, black bottle Belaire", "Fresher than the Fresh Prince, hell yeah boy I do this"], "meaning": "Ciroc is an alcohol brand owned by Diddy, Belaire is the champagne endorsed by Stalley’s boss and labelmate Rick Ross. He also uses a punchline to refer to Will Smith’s iconic show Fresh Prince of Bel Air.", "annotation_id": "4125707", "url": "https://genius.com/4125707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
