{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Options", "line": "And love used to be a vehicle But now there’s too much mileage", "vault_lines": ["But now there's too much mileage"], "meaning": "Luke compares love to a car and saying that  her love use to drive him crazy but he abandoned the vehicle because it had too much mileage meaning there’s too much stress or baggage now.", "annotation_id": "3422455", "url": "https://genius.com/3422455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
