{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Outlawz", "line": "Cause lil’ one when it’s on, they gon’ do ya wrong", "vault_lines": ["'Cause lil' one when it's on, they gon' do ya wrong"], "meaning": "Most rappers that have died have been done wrong including dolph he had no gun on him they fid him dirty caught him lacking the streets will crucify you for gains", "annotation_id": "24729873", "url": "https://genius.com/24729873", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Outlawz", "line": "Mozzarella, now its only tall cheddar Most dope boys been a Paul Bearer", "vault_lines": ["Mozzarella, now its only tall cheddar"], "meaning": "Here, Rick Ross portrays how his purchasing power changed drastically overtime due to the popularity he achieved through his musical career, making a similarity of his quantity of money before and after, to the types of cheese mozzarella and cheddar, with the latter being a slang term used to designate money.\n\nFurthermore, Rick makes a notable nod to the American Funeral Director and was most known as The Undertaker’s manager, Paul Bearer. William Alvin “Bill” Moody was best known for his tenure with the World Wrestling Federation, where he performed under the ring name Paul Bearer.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately, he passed away in 2013. Following an independent event on March 2, 2013, he told friends that he would be seeking treatment for any respiratory problems and treated for a blood clot. Tragically, three days later on, March 5, 2013, Paul Bearer died of a heart attack at the age of 58.", "annotation_id": "24653536", "url": "https://genius.com/24653536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Outlawz", "line": "Maybach Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A reference to Ross’s label Maybach Music Group, which has also signed artists like Meek Mill and Wale.\n\nThis audio clip can be heard on other Ross-assisted tracks, like Drake’s “Lord Knows” and DJ Khaled’s “No New Friends”", "annotation_id": "24425235", "url": "https://genius.com/24425235", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
