{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pacman", "line": "This that Namco yay", "vault_lines": ["This that Namco yay"], "meaning": "The song is called “Pacman,” as Ross and Pill are pack-men, as in they’ve got packs of cocaine. Namco created the class video game, Pacman.", "annotation_id": "376084", "url": "https://genius.com/376084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pacman", "line": "Ground basing, jumping over cars, they Blake Griffin", "vault_lines": ["Ground basing, jumping over cars, they Blake Griffin"], "meaning": "Refference to the NBA Rookie Of The Year notable for his dunks.\n\n\n\nAlso wordplay on basing referring to “base” as cocaine.", "annotation_id": "308445", "url": "https://genius.com/308445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pacman", "line": "All my power pellets turn you bitch niggas to ghosts", "vault_lines": ["All my power pellets turn you bitch niggas to ghosts"], "meaning": "In pacman, when you eat up the lit up pellets, you become the predator and eat all the “ghost” enemies. So Rozay just threw in this sick metaphor about his pellets (bulletts) making people run, and Pacman, the title of the song.", "annotation_id": "248292", "url": "https://genius.com/248292", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
