{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Write my shit so vicious, y’all like snitches, you can’t see the pen", "vault_lines": ["Write my shit so vicious, y'all like snitches, you can't see the pen"], "meaning": "Double Entendre!\n\nWale’s bars that he writes with his pen are so high level that no other rapper can compete with him (see him) in this category.\n\nAlso, pen is short for penitentiary, the prison you are held in after you’re convicted of a serious crime. However, people who snitch do it in order to avoid jail time, meaning that they never end up seeing the pen.", "annotation_id": "20726488", "url": "https://genius.com/20726488", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Nudies and some J6", "vault_lines": [", Nudies and some J6"], "meaning": "Wale paints a picture of what outfit he’s wearing, as he is a fashion icon to many in the rap game.\n\nNudie Jeans are a popular, high quality and expensive denim brand that have been referenced by many rappers including Migos and A$AP Rocky.\n\nJ6 are Jordan 6’s, a popular silhouette of Michael Jordan’s sneakers that were originally released in 1991.\n\n\n\nWale in a pair of 6’s", "annotation_id": "20726444", "url": "https://genius.com/20726444", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Monday night wrestling, I’m so fucking raw", "vault_lines": ["Monday night wrestling, I’m so fucking raw"], "meaning": "WWE, the worlds premier entertainment-wrestling promotion has a show called Monday Night Raw which has been running every Monday night since 1993.\n\nRaw is synonymous with Monday night wrestling, as well as being a term to describe high level rapping.", "annotation_id": "20726408", "url": "https://genius.com/20726408", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Or at the Hilton with Paris", "vault_lines": ["or at the Hilton with Paris"], "meaning": "Paris Hilton, one of the most famous socialites and reality TV stars, is the grand daughter of Conrad Hilton, founder of worldwide chain Hilton Hotels.", "annotation_id": "20726388", "url": "https://genius.com/20726388", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "And be out London with Lauren and tellin Meagan “Good morning”", "vault_lines": ["And be out London with Lauren and tellin Meagan \"Good morning\""], "meaning": "Meek is name dropping a bunch of models/video vixens.\n\nLauren London is an actress and model who gained her first taste of fame starring alongside T.I. in the film ATL, which she followed up with many more prominent roles. Lauren was in a highly publicized relationship with Lil Wayne, sharing a child together, and was also with Nipsey Hussle before his untimely passing.\n\n\n\nMeagan Good is also a model and actress who starred in many movies such as Think Like A Man and Anchorman 2. She has been referenced by many rappers including Drake and A$AP Ferg has a song named after her.", "annotation_id": "20726293", "url": "https://genius.com/20726293", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "I can keep a secret with Vicky", "vault_lines": ["I can keep a secret with Vicky"], "meaning": "A reference to the popular womens clothing and undergarment brand Victoria’s Secret.", "annotation_id": "20726284", "url": "https://genius.com/20726284", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "I am on my Tom Brady, y’all niggas is Eric Crouch", "vault_lines": ["I am on my Tom Brady, y’all niggas is Eric Crouch"], "meaning": "Eric Crouch and Tom Brady were both quarterbacks with very different stories. Crouch won the Heisman his senior year in 2002, but was drafted in the 3rd round as a WR and never played a down in the NFL. Meanwhile, Brady battled from being 7th on Michigan’s QB depth chart his rookie year, was drafted in the 6th round, but went on to be one of the best quarterbacks ever.\n\nWale is saying that you can keep underestimating him. At the end of the day, he’ll have the last laugh.", "annotation_id": "13718871", "url": "https://genius.com/13718871", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "You dreamed of getting cream, best believe I’m John Deere", "vault_lines": ["You dreamed of getting cream, best believe I’m John Deere"], "meaning": "Continuing the last line wale is saying he is Becoming one of the Best MC’s to rise and Making Tons of Millions on his records\n\nHaters are dreaming to see the money wales is absorbing today. John Deere is a tool company that has a green Logo.\n\n“They wish they had as much Money as Wale”\n\nJohn Deere is also known for making lawnmowers and lawnmowers cut green grass\n\nWale made a similar reference in “Power Circle” by MMG", "annotation_id": "920391", "url": "https://genius.com/920391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "She gon wipe me down, I’ma brush her off", "vault_lines": ["She gon wipe me down, I’ma brush her off"], "meaning": "Wipe me Down (a phrase made popular by Lil Boosie) is a way of asserting your flyness. Brushing someone off means to think nothing of them or dismiss them.\n\n\n\nIn this line, Meek is flipping a similar line that his fellow freshman buddy BIG SEAN spit in “Supa Dupa Lemonade”\n\nI'ma dick her down, you gon pick her up", "annotation_id": "380977", "url": "https://genius.com/380977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "My place spacious, smoking aces in Lagos", "vault_lines": ["My place spacious, smoking aces in Lagos"], "meaning": "A reference to the popular film entitled Smokin' Aces\n“Ace” is sland for a joint. It is also slang for about 3.5 grams of weed.\nLagos is the capital city of Nigeria where Ross had been for a few performances just before this song came out.", "annotation_id": "300109", "url": "https://genius.com/300109", "state": "accepted", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Shout out to Lil G, shout out Tre and Mohammad", "vault_lines": ["Shout out to Lil G, shout out Tre and Mohammad"], "meaning": "Besides Maybach Music Group, Wale has a new label called Board Of Administration (BOA) and the people he shout out in this line run the label along side Wale.", "annotation_id": "222426", "url": "https://genius.com/222426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "That BOA shit, we get paid with death over dishonor", "vault_lines": ["That BOA shit, we get paid with death over dishonor"], "meaning": "BOA stands for Board of Administration which is his crew including Black Cobain & Fat Trel.", "annotation_id": "177881", "url": "https://genius.com/177881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "I was tryna bag a brick, you was Nickelodeon", "vault_lines": ["I was tryna bag a brick, you was Nickelodeon"], "meaning": "1) Meek Mill has been messin with Cocaine since he was a child.\nHis classmates were watching ‘Rugrats’ while he was fuckin wit blow.\n\n2) Meek Mill’s current competition is childish and not as serious as him (especially when it comes to coke)\n\n3) He was bagging “bricks,” aka kilograms of coke. You, the competition, were nickel-odeon. Basically, his competition was pushing baby weight, aka nickel bags, aka five-dollar bags for very little profit when compared to the thousands he made off of one brick.", "annotation_id": "169611", "url": "https://genius.com/169611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Fuck your girl, give her back, I’m courteous", "vault_lines": ["Fuck your girl, give her back, I’m courteous"], "meaning": "Meek Mill returns girls like items he has borrowed, which is a courteous thing to do.  There is some sarcasm in this line due to the fact that fucking someone else’s girl is rarely courteous unless you are the Based God", "annotation_id": "140293", "url": "https://genius.com/140293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Armadillo cigars,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "pun meaning cigarillos.\n\n\n\nAlso, much like armadillos, Rozay rolls up his cigars.\nBallin!", "annotation_id": "139261", "url": "https://genius.com/139261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "And I am dead serious, bitch I spit with embalming", "vault_lines": ["And I am dead serious, bitch I spit with embalming"], "meaning": "Embalming fluid is to preserve human remains. So, he is dead serious and spits embalming.", "annotation_id": "122123", "url": "https://genius.com/122123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Hoes, I need a condom for my toast Busting in these niggas", "vault_lines": ["Busting in these niggas"], "meaning": "“Toast”, is a slang term for a gun and “busting in these niggas” means both:\n1. Bustin' a cap in their ass.\n2. Cumming in them.\nWith the latter explaining the usefulness of the condom.", "annotation_id": "107431", "url": "https://genius.com/107431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Whole time, see that fly shit I’ve been on All the girlfriends fall in line from my spinoff That’s game bitch, ain’t shit", "vault_lines": ["Whole time, see that fly shit I’ve been on", "All the girlfriends fall in line from my spinoff", "That's game bitch, ain't shit"], "meaning": "The TV show “The Game” is a spinoff of “Girlfriends”\n\nHe is saying that all his girlfriends obey him because of his “game”\n\nGame – Ability to control females", "annotation_id": "104545", "url": "https://genius.com/104545", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "What the bloodclot? Tommie Frazier, fuck yourself", "vault_lines": ["What the bloodclot? Tommie Frazier, fuck yourself"], "meaning": "Tommy Frazier was an ex-nebraska,led his team to back-to-back consensus national championships in 1994 and 1995\nbut never went to the NFL due to a bloodclot.\n\nBloodclot means “fuck” in a Jamaican slang.\n\nWale is saying you couldn’t make it to the NFL (his level) cause of your/you’re a bloodclot", "annotation_id": "100300", "url": "https://genius.com/100300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "YSL swagger, wrist wear frigid", "vault_lines": ["YSL swagger, wrist wear frigid"], "meaning": "“YSL swagger” – Yves Saint Laurent is an expensive clothing line worn by many rappers.\n\n“Wrist wear frigid” – In the rap game, jewelery is frequently referred to as “Ice”, so basically he’s saying that he has a diamond-studded bracelet.", "annotation_id": "89871", "url": "https://genius.com/89871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Presidential suite and bitch I never use my right to vote", "vault_lines": ["Presidential suite and bitch I never use my right to vote"], "meaning": "Being from D.C., Wale tends to make a lot of political/presidential references. ALSO, since he’s gettin money, he stays at the nicest of rooms at hotels and resorts.\n\n\n\nWale can’t use his right to vote because he lives in DC. Since there is no representation for the district and it’s not a state, no one in DC votes until presidential elections…", "annotation_id": "89867", "url": "https://genius.com/89867", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "God bless you unless you was disrespectful", "vault_lines": ["God bless you unless you was disrespectful"], "meaning": "In the previous lines he mentions “cold”, “achoo!”, so going along with that theme, after you sneeze, it’s rather courteous to say “God Bless You”.", "annotation_id": "89865", "url": "https://genius.com/89865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Where I’m from, it’s cold", "vault_lines": ["Where I’m from, it's cold"], "meaning": "Double meaning. Here Wale is saying that where he’s from (Maryland) it’s cold, which it can get temeperature wise, but also in the sense that the people that hes with are “cold”, slang word for “rough” or “tough”.", "annotation_id": "89863", "url": "https://genius.com/89863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "And niggas get at you like handkerchiefs", "vault_lines": ["and niggas get at you like handkerchiefs"], "meaning": "Continuing with the “cold” theme of the previous line, Wale does not mean “at you” but rather “achoo!”, as the sound you make when sneezing, which is done in handkerchiefs.", "annotation_id": "89861", "url": "https://genius.com/89861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Always on some new shit, CNN", "vault_lines": ["Always on some new shit, CNN"], "meaning": "CNN is the ‘news’ and Wale always comes out with new music.\nHe cleverly says the line in a way that almost sounds like he’s saying ‘news shit’", "annotation_id": "89133", "url": "https://genius.com/89133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
