{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "The .45 for you niggas with nine lives", "vault_lines": ["The .45 for you niggas with nine lives"], "meaning": "The 45 is referring to a gun. Niggas with 9 lives are like CATS, but let’s use the word pussies\n\nClever numberplay from Rozay here. coming 4 or 5 times then calls out ‘45. 4 + 5 = 9, 9 lives.", "annotation_id": "89121", "url": "https://genius.com/89121", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Have a menage with Nicki", "vault_lines": [", have a menage with Nicki"], "meaning": "‘Menage’ referring a menage et trois – which is another word for a threesome. Pronounced the same way as Minaj, as in Nicki Minaj.", "annotation_id": "88645", "url": "https://genius.com/88645", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Word to the homie Ross, I can get that nine piece", "vault_lines": ["Word to the homie Ross, I can get that nine piece"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has a song with T.I. called “9 Piece”\n\nA nine piece refers to a quarter kilo.\n\nKilo = 36 ounces.\n\n¼ of that = 9 oz", "annotation_id": "88641", "url": "https://genius.com/88641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "They say I’m special as Devin Hester on fourth down", "vault_lines": ["They say I'm special as Devin Hester on fourth down"], "meaning": "Devin Hester is a special teams player for the Chicago Bears – punts, of course, happen on fourth downs.  He broke the NFL record for a punt return on Decemeber 2010", "annotation_id": "88432", "url": "https://genius.com/88432", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "I am on my John Lithgow Out of this 3rd Rock, nigga air it out", "vault_lines": ["Out of this 3rd Rock, nigga air it out"], "meaning": "John Lithgow is an actor.  He is in the show “3rd Rock From the Sun”.\n\n\n\nWale is out of this world (The 3rd rock or planet from the Sun)", "annotation_id": "88429", "url": "https://genius.com/88429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Bitch I got a right to brag, bitch I got a right to boast", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I got a right to brag, bitch I got a right to boast"], "meaning": "In “Chillin”, Wale says:\n\nI got the right to be cocky\nGet so much cut disc jockeys jock me", "annotation_id": "88418", "url": "https://genius.com/88418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "Flyest niggas out here, period, no maxi-pad", "vault_lines": ["Flyest niggas out here, period, no maxi-pad"], "meaning": "A Maxi Pad is a product that women put on their vagina while they are menstruating.\n\nNice wordplay with “period”, and “flyest” since  Maxi Pads have wings.\n\nMaxi Pads are used for “periods” and Wale is the flyest nigga out here “period”", "annotation_id": "88408", "url": "https://genius.com/88408", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "line": "General Electric perfected, cooking them O’s", "vault_lines": ["General Electric perfected, cooking them O’s"], "meaning": "GE used to make stoves and stuff like that – nowadays they are basically an undercover investment bank (GE Financial was started to give loans to buy appliances, but like 10 years ago they started playing the “Subprime Game”, thug-style)\n\nAll the more reason for crack dealers to use their appliances!", "annotation_id": "88395", "url": "https://genius.com/88395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pandemonium", "status": "done", "targets": 34, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-pandemonium-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pandemonium", "genius_id": 3110, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "I’m smokin’ in her crib and she prefer I light candles She worried ’bout the scent, while I’m focused on the rent", "vault_lines": ["I'm smokin' in her crib and she prefer I light candles", "She worried 'bout the scent, while I'm focused on the rent"], "meaning": "His new chick doesn’t like when he lights up in the house. But Rockie owns the place so it doesn’t phase him.\n\n\n\nRockie also creates a double entendre with “She prefer I light candles”.\n1. Candles repel the smell of the chronic he’s burning\n2. He also uses this as a reference for sex. When the candles are lit, and the lights go off, you already know whats going down.", "annotation_id": "2599307", "url": "https://genius.com/2599307", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "All she want is me so Sushi feed her ego", "vault_lines": ["Sushi feed her ego"], "meaning": "Rozay uses some food wordplay here, where me so can be read as miso; as in the soup that’s often served at sushi joints.\n\nHe’s also saying that all she wants is Ross, and he’ll take her out on dates to nice sushi restaurants.", "annotation_id": "1742623", "url": "https://genius.com/1742623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
