{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "Flippin falcons got my house bigger than Atlanta", "vault_lines": ["Flippin falcons got my house bigger than Atlanta"], "meaning": "“Falcons” is a slang term for cocaine, and the NFL team in Atlanta is called the Falcons. This line resembles the rise to riches that come from the drug market. The money from Rick Ross' possible selling of drugs allowed him to buy this huge Miami house\n\n\n\nAlthough it being bigger than Atlanta is a bit of an exaggeration, it’s still a huge crib. Perhaps Rozay is referring to the Georgia Dome, the home of the Atlanta Falcons", "annotation_id": "1682945", "url": "https://genius.com/1682945", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "Who signin’ endorsements, Satan or them corporates? Ball so hard they tore shit", "vault_lines": ["Who signin' endorsements, Satan or them corporates?", "Ball so hard they tore shit"], "meaning": "A play on the D-Rose line, Derrick Rose signed an endorsement deal with Adidas, and then tore his ACL in a playoff game https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jo1UlzDeY-o", "annotation_id": "1682938", "url": "https://genius.com/1682938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
