{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "Although they did forget Casey, and he say life changes", "vault_lines": ["Although they did forget Casey, and he say life changes"], "meaning": "Many people felt like Casey Veggies should have been included in the 2013 XXL Freshmen list. Travis Scott, one of the year’s freshman, was quoted saying, “What’s up with Casey Veggies? Why isn’t Casey on this?”\n\nSchoolboy Q, another 2013 freshman, thought the same thing: “For the most part, I think Casey Veggies should’ve had my spot.”\n\nLife Changes is the name of Casey’s 2013 mixtape. Rockie’s mention of the tape then leads into his next three lines about how he will continue to work and eventually get to where he wants to be in the rap game.", "annotation_id": "1682715", "url": "https://genius.com/1682715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "Tracks with Good Charlotte", "vault_lines": ["tracks with Good Charlotte"], "meaning": "Rockie collaborated with The Madden Brothers (of Good Charlotte fame)\n\n\n\non their “BEFORE” The Mixtape Volume 1, resulting in the tracks:\nhttps://soundcloud.com/themaddenbrothers/3-take-me-back-to-teenage AND\nhttps://soundcloud.com/themaddenbrothers/5-the-right-track-so-cold", "annotation_id": "1682586", "url": "https://genius.com/1682586", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "She said I should have been number one on that freshman list I told her it was nothin’ to me, girl don’t stress that shit Plus some of my niggas on it, I respect that shit", "vault_lines": ["I told her it was nothin' to me, girl don't stress that shit", "Plus some of my niggas on it, I respect that shit"], "meaning": "He is referring to XXL’s annual Top 10 Freshmen list. Rockie Fresh didn’t even make it on the list this year, although some people felt he should’ve been number one (according to him at least).\n\nThis is what he had to say about it on Twitter:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rockiefresh/status/316747324477034497", "annotation_id": "1682550", "url": "https://genius.com/1682550", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Panera Bread", "line": "Always been more than a player, I am Thibodeau", "vault_lines": ["Always been more than a player, I am Thibodeau"], "meaning": "#WORDPLAY\nTom Thibodeau is currently the head coach of the Chicago Bulls.\n\n\n\nRockie is explaining that he is not just a player of the game, he’s in fact directing other rappers.", "annotation_id": "1682544", "url": "https://genius.com/1682544", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
