{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "Children havin’ children, but they don’t have a thing", "vault_lines": ["Children havin' children, but they don't have a thing"], "meaning": "Kevin Cossom exposes a social fact: poor people are likely to have more children, meaning that having big families does not make people economically rich in any case.\n\nThis sounds like a classic M.O.B encouragement.", "annotation_id": "15504056", "url": "https://genius.com/15504056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "I’m tryna go where I can’t go Tryna be what I can’t be I wanna teach you what I can’t show We gotta reach what we can’t reach", "vault_lines": ["Tryna be what I can't be", "I wanna teach you what I can't show", "We gotta reach what we can't reach"], "meaning": "As a true hustler, Ross is making everything he can to get to a higher economic status, even though he has come from a long way to where he belongs to now.", "annotation_id": "13516477", "url": "https://genius.com/13516477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "Magic City Where the palm trees and the bright lights look so pretty Don’t lose your soul chasin’ that pot of gold", "vault_lines": ["Don't lose your soul chasin' that pot of gold"], "meaning": "Miami is the Magic City\n\nAs Rick Ross has mentioned before, the luxury and excess of Miami can be pretty but it is important not to forget your roots and lose your soul to the vice filled streets\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aUl3CkPKCJs", "annotation_id": "12134905", "url": "https://genius.com/12134905", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "But I charge ’em just to sell for", "vault_lines": ["But I charge 'em just to sell for"], "meaning": "Wordplay: Rozay is making reference to his new Bellair Rose and other endorsements\n\n\n\nthis can also be considered a selling drugs for other people selling a brick or two and making money on top of the sale", "annotation_id": "2940673", "url": "https://genius.com/2940673", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "But I think it’s time to buy that home", "vault_lines": ["But I think it's time to buy that home"], "meaning": "Rozay has bought Evander Holyfields foreclosed home for 5.8 million dollars in Atlanta, Georgia.\n\n\n\n\n\nIt includes:\n\n\na bowling alley\nhome theater\n350,000 gallon pool\n109 rooms\n\n\n\nThe home cost more than $1 million annually to maintain with an electric bill reportedly costing $17,000 a month.", "annotation_id": "2940617", "url": "https://genius.com/2940617", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "Get to meet Barack, rub elbows", "vault_lines": ["Get to meet Barack, rub elbows"], "meaning": "Rozay wants to meet The President of the USA, Barack Obama and socialise or “rub elbows” with him, like Jay-Z does.", "annotation_id": "2901208", "url": "https://genius.com/2901208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "No charges for the cellphones", "vault_lines": ["No charges for the cellphones"], "meaning": "In Dubai,there are two mobile service operators available which are etisalat and du.Incoming Calls\nin Dubai are free, unless you are abroad and using International Roaming.", "annotation_id": "2881607", "url": "https://genius.com/2881607", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "Like the day she told her dad I was a drug dealer", "vault_lines": ["Like the day she told her dad I was a drug dealer"], "meaning": "Rick Ross values the daughter-mother relationship.  In his 2008 single, “Here I Am,”  Rick Ross mentions, “She used to fight with her moms, ‘til I sat them both down.  Now, she’s tight with her moms.”  Inferring that these quotes are related, it can be assumed that Rick Ross is referencing the moment in which his girlfriend informs her father that she’s been dating a drug dealer, a tough conversation that requires an unconditional love and trust.", "annotation_id": "2877995", "url": "https://genius.com/2877995", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "I kept the G’s, she can count on me", "vault_lines": ["I kept the G's, she can count on me"], "meaning": "Upon request, Rick Ross treats this ambiguous woman to incremental amounts of money.  But Ross doesn’t want her counting his money; he wants her to trust and rely on him.\n\n\n\nThis young man’s doing it wrong.  But assuming these girls don’t pocket all his money while he poses for the camera, he might retain enough money to recover from his foolishness and continue his assent to Mastermind status.", "annotation_id": "2877928", "url": "https://genius.com/2877928", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "We the ones that never got the Pell Grants Fuck FullSail, let your mail stack", "vault_lines": ["We the ones that never got the Pell Grants", "Fuck FullSail, let your mail stack"], "meaning": "Ross and company visualizes a future where Pell Grants aren’t needed. Pell Grants are usually awarded to students as need-based grants to low-income students who are looking to pursue undergraduate studies.\n\nAnother interpretation could be that Ross lives in an environment surrounded by drugs and crime. Pell Grants are not awarded to students with past criminal convictions.\n\nHe dismisses Full Sail, a for-profit university in Florida and instead encourages youngsters to let their inbox stack with offers from other institutions.", "annotation_id": "2876508", "url": "https://genius.com/2876508", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "All this drug dealin’, it’s killin’ our brother, mane", "vault_lines": ["All this drug dealin', it's killin' our brother, mane"], "meaning": "Here, Rick Ross is talking about the whole black population. All the drug dealing done by blacks, “kills” their brother by creating stereotypes.\n\nIt could also be the brothers that die on a daily basis due to the drug dealing.", "annotation_id": "2876068", "url": "https://genius.com/2876068", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paradise Lost", "line": "Magic City Where the palm trees and the bright lights look so pretty", "vault_lines": ["Where the palm trees and the bright lights look so pretty"], "meaning": "This is primarily a metaphor for the music industry but could be interpreted as any industry with deception, where people are lured in by misconceptions and find out the real truth once they’ve arrived.\n\n\n\nMagic City is another name for Miami (and the name of the TV show Rick Ross has appeared on).", "annotation_id": "2854466", "url": "https://genius.com/2854466", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
