{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "These streets all that I know, my block hot like pyro", "vault_lines": ["These streets all that I know, my block hot like pyro"], "meaning": "The street life is all Chinx knows. His simile reflection of the block as hot as pyro paints his neighborhood as a dangerous and high police patrolled area.", "annotation_id": "3899489", "url": "https://genius.com/3899489", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "I keep my hitter with me, that’s my shooter, nigga Only thing I’m scared of is what he’ll do to niggas", "vault_lines": ["I keep my hitter with me, that's my shooter, nigga", "Only thing I'm scared of is what he'll do to niggas"], "meaning": "Threat!!!\n\nKiss cant be caught shooting at hataz -he rolls with shooters who do that for him. He ain’t concerned with none of these itchy trigger finger thugs -his only worry is what his shooters will do to them.", "annotation_id": "3895548", "url": "https://genius.com/3895548", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "All we know is get it so, nigga, if you scared, call 5-0 Finna go bulletproof all of my whips", "vault_lines": ["All we know is get it so, nigga, if you scared, call 5-0", "Finna go bulletproof all of my whips"], "meaning": "The notion all we know is ‘get it’ is like saying ‘by any means necessary’ -motivation talk for a gangster or a hustler in the streets; this usually means gun play will be involved. He’s suggesting you call the cops if you scared.\nMeanwhile he’s about to bulletproof all of his whips.", "annotation_id": "3154415", "url": "https://genius.com/3154415", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "Since they killed Stack front of this building, I relocated my children Hope his shooter step forth and just make his debut appearance", "vault_lines": ["Since they killed Stack front of this building, I relocated my children", "Hope his shooter step forth and just make his debut appearance"], "meaning": "Chinx sends a warning shot to Stack Bundle’s murderer.\n\nSince his friend got shot, paranoia had him relocate his children –he now dares the killer to come out of hiding.\n\n\n\nChinx and Stack Bundles formed the Riot Squad group alongside local rappers Bynoe and Cau2Gs.", "annotation_id": "3154291", "url": "https://genius.com/3154291", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "But my voodoo strong enough for 50 niggas", "vault_lines": ["But my voodoo strong enough for 50 niggas"], "meaning": "Ross uses vodou here to mean that he is protected by the spirits so the bullets from his would be assassins miss their target.\n\nVodou comes from West Africa and found it’s nitch in Carribiean and United States slave culture as a way for slaves to maintain a connection to the motherland while under heavy pressure, in some cases, to convert to Christianity. However, some slave masters allowed their slaves to worship as they pleased.\n\nIn popular culture, voodoo is thought of as the pricking of dolls to make people do stuff, but that is a simplification of a culture with much more deep roots.", "annotation_id": "2857233", "url": "https://genius.com/2857233", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "Daddy gone, I was a lost child, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Daddy gone, I was a lost child, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil Durk had to become the man of his household at a very young age after his father Dontay Banks was sentenced to life in prison in 1994 for his role in distributing crack-cocaine in South Side Chicago.\n\nA then-25-year-old Banks was labeled the ringleader of a criminal enterprise that included associates Robert Shipp, 21; and 25-year-old Mario Dunlap and Alton Mills, according to the Chicago Tribune", "annotation_id": "2759057", "url": "https://genius.com/2759057", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "My Cuban link like Raekwon", "vault_lines": [", my Cuban link like Raekwon"], "meaning": "His connect is Cuban. Connect/link are synonyms.\n\n\n\nOnly Built 4 Cuban Linx… is the title of Raekwon’s debut album.", "annotation_id": "2748598", "url": "https://genius.com/2748598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "Ou paka bat mwen!", "vault_lines": ["Let's get this money nigga, ou paka bat mwen!"], "meaning": "This line is Creole for\n\nYou can’t beat me!\n\n\n\nAlso, notice how Ross repeats this line in his verse later on after the line that mentioned voodoo.", "annotation_id": "2699563", "url": "https://genius.com/2699563", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "I make big money, I drive big cars I got this my nigga, Diddy, what up? Huh Everybody know me, it’s like I’m a movie star!", "vault_lines": ["I make big money, I drive big cars", "I got this my nigga, Diddy, what up? Huh", "Everybody know me, it's like I'm a movie star!"], "meaning": "Willie D’s 1st line from the Geto Boys' “Mind Playing Tricks On Me” http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&v=-M8GszEN9MM#t=79", "annotation_id": "2679557", "url": "https://genius.com/2679557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "Bullets ripping through my door like I was Biggie, nigga (Rest in peace)", "vault_lines": ["Bullets ripping through my door like I was Biggie, nigga"], "meaning": "On January 27th of 2013, Ross was shot at in a drive-by shooting while in his Rolls Royce with his girlfriend (it was his 37th birthday, too). Neither Ross or his partner were harmed, but they ended up crashing against an apartment wall.\n\nHere, he’s comparing this incident with the incident that led to the death of the legendary Notorious B.I.G (aka Biggie Smalls).\n\nRoss' Rolls Royce:\n\n\n\nBiggie’s SUV:", "annotation_id": "2630426", "url": "https://genius.com/2630426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "Real nigga for life (real nigga for life) so paranoid (So paranoid) Connect had hit me, he got shooters in California", "vault_lines": ["Real nigga for life (real nigga for life) so paranoid (So paranoid)", "Connect had hit me, he got shooters in California"], "meaning": "Durk going to be real until he die. His boy rondo is too. Durk is on his toes aware of everything, as he still lives in Chiraq with them savages. He’s got connections with shooters in California – where Chief keef and Glo Gang happen to be currently.", "annotation_id": "2627433", "url": "https://genius.com/2627433", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "They tryna lock up my kind, scared to pick up my line My phone tapped like Avon", "vault_lines": ["They tryna lock up my kind, scared to pick up my line", "My phone tapped like Avon"], "meaning": "He knows being in the drug business is wrong and he starts to become paranoid that the police are constantly aware of what he does.\n\nAvon Barksdale is a character from the TV show The Wire. The line most likely refers to a specific episode in the first season where Avon becomes paranoid about phone lines.", "annotation_id": "2625467", "url": "https://genius.com/2625467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "How many of you niggas really been a papi? (Oh yeah) So callate la boca, baby", "vault_lines": ["How many of you niggas really been a papi? (Oh yeah)", "So callate la boca, baby"], "meaning": "“Papi” would refer to being either the head of a gang or the head of a drug operation.\n\nBeing that “papi” is a Spanish word, Rick gives you a little Spanish lesson. Callate la boca is translated roughly to…\n\nShut the fuck up\n\nOr it could also be translated to…\n\nShut your mouth", "annotation_id": "2625400", "url": "https://genius.com/2625400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "[Chorus: Johnny Maycash]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Only the first four lines of the hook were recited this time.\n\nI be so (I be so) paranoid (paranoid)\nI hear these niggas tryin' to fuck with me\nBut, real shit, I know I got enemies\nI can’t let them niggas into me", "annotation_id": "2625393", "url": "https://genius.com/2625393", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Paranoid (Remix)", "line": "Ay, I-I be the hottest nigga out my city Hit you with some shit you never seen on TV Know a nigga shining, all my diamonds 3D I-I-I hit a lick, I’m worth a couple million Ay, that car net worth 400 thou’, nigga That top drop like Pacquiao, nigga I-I-I hit up K.O.D. and left a hundred in it Hundred on my watch, I’m shining every minute They, they, they caught him on that corner, left a hundred in him Niggas goin’ broke, that’ll never be me That-that paranoia (paranoia) got me watchin’ lawyer (Watchin’ lawyer) Molly water (molly water) tryna wake up sober!", "vault_lines": ["Ay, I-I be the hottest nigga out my city", "Hit you with some shit you never seen on TV"], "meaning": "Same verse as the first verse on the original track.", "annotation_id": "2625385", "url": "https://genius.com/2625385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
