{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Perfectionist", "line": "Ross gon be the quarterback, I’mma run this quarter back", "vault_lines": ["Ross gon be the quarterback, I'mma run this quarter back"], "meaning": "Following up on the position line from the previous bar, Meek states that Ross plays the quarterback position.\n\nIn football, quarterbacks are members of the offensive team and line up directly behind the offensive line. Quarterbacks are the leaders of the offensive team, responsible for calling the play in the huddle. It would make sense for Ross to be the QB of MMG, seeing as QB’s are the leaders of their teams, and Ross is the Maybach Boss. Ross is no stranger to football, as in real life Ross excelled as an offensive lineman.\n\nMeek’s plan is for Ross to purchase a quarter kilo for cheap, and for Meek to re-sell for more profit. Note the ‘quarterback’/‘quarter back’ wordplay here.\n\nRoss is also friends with Miami’s most famous quarterback ever, Dan Marino.", "annotation_id": "1507516", "url": "https://genius.com/1507516", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Perfectionist", "line": "Bricks on Brickell, we got bricks in the Bay", "vault_lines": ["Bricks on Brickell, we got bricks in the Bay"], "meaning": "Brickell is an urban neighborhood in Miami, Florida, United States. A neighborhood of greater Downtown Miami, Brickell is Miami and South Florida’s major financial district.\nBrickell was settled in the modern era in the mid-1800s by early pioneers, growing to become Miami’s “Millionaire’s Row” in the early 1900s after the construction of lavish mansions along Brickell Avenue by Mary Brickell. By the 1970s, office towers, hotels and apartments began replacing the historic mansions.\n\nToday, Brickell has grown to overtake the city’s historic central business district to the north, as one of the largest financial districts in the United States. With a fast growing residential population, Brickell is now one of Miami’s fasting growing neighborhoods. Brickell, along with the CBD, have over 70,000 permanent residents.\n\nDespite being an upscale community, Ross has stashed bricks there as well.", "annotation_id": "729381", "url": "https://genius.com/729381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Perfectionist", "line": "Fuck the competition I bury the cock-a-roaches", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the competition I bury the cock-a-roaches"], "meaning": "“I bury the cockroaches” is a quote from drug kingpin Tony Montana in the movie Scarface.", "annotation_id": "729335", "url": "https://genius.com/729335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Perfectionist", "line": "Double-M G and we 20 million strong", "vault_lines": ["Double-M G and we 20 million strong"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group has a networth of over $20 million.", "annotation_id": "729221", "url": "https://genius.com/729221", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Perfectionist", "line": "Ball like Mayweather, Don King at the register", "vault_lines": ["Ball like Mayweather, Don King at the register"], "meaning": "Don King is an American Boxing promoter that is extremely wealthy.\n\nMayweather is a professional boxer that is undefeated and has won many championships, and is also extremely wealthy. Ross likes to go to Mayweather’s fights.", "annotation_id": "729202", "url": "https://genius.com/729202", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Perfectionist", "line": "Frank Lucas furs at the fight on my cellular", "vault_lines": ["Frank Lucas furs at the fight on my cellular"], "meaning": "Ross is comparing himself to Frank Lucas who was a drug kingpin and was the “King of Heroine”.\n\nHis fur coat cost hundreds of thousands of dollars and that’s what attracted the police to further investigation and led to him being discovered due to his flossing.", "annotation_id": "729182", "url": "https://genius.com/729182", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Perfectionist", "line": "Get the dirty money, clean it all up at the Laundromat", "vault_lines": ["Get the dirty money, clean it all up at the Laundromat"], "meaning": "Dirty money is money that has been obtained by drug dealing or crime, and needs to be cleaned by a front company – an exercise commonly known as money laundering. He is using a play on words by saying he is going to clean it at the laundromat, a place where really poor people go to clean clothes.", "annotation_id": "729166", "url": "https://genius.com/729166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
