{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Phone Tap", "line": "Now you hangin’ out with different people on the weekend Quotin’ different numbers nigga, like I wouldn’t peep it", "vault_lines": ["Now you hangin' out with different people on the weekend", "Quotin' different numbers nigga, like I wouldn't peep it"], "meaning": "Ross is on to his homies' change in behavior. When you participate in any illegal activity its vital to never let your guard down.", "annotation_id": "4547423", "url": "https://genius.com/4547423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Phone Tap", "line": "If you callin’ me, I think your phone tapped", "vault_lines": ["If you callin' me, I think your phone tapped"], "meaning": "If you make phone contact with Ross, your conversation definitely will be eased dropped on (cough NSA cough)", "annotation_id": "4547351", "url": "https://genius.com/4547351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Phone Tap", "line": "I think a nigga phone tapped Wanna give me time for my old raps", "vault_lines": ["Wanna give me time for my old raps"], "meaning": "This is a play on a criminal ‘rap’ which is short for ‘Record of Arrest and Prosecution’.\n\nRoss is suggesting that the police are trying to gather evidence for past crimes that he has committed.\n\nThey can tap a phone in a number of ways, although “audio content wiretaps by law enforcement are relatively rare.”\n\nPotentially, Ross could be referring back to the time when he lost an endorsement deal with Reebok over his old raps. This time, literally meaning his rap lyrics.  The “time” refers her to the money the negative publicity forced him to lose, especially considering the killer sneaker commercials Reebok shot in Ross' backyard were already airing. As the old saying goes, time = money.", "annotation_id": "4547309", "url": "https://genius.com/4547309", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Phone Tap", "line": "My phone tapped Got a feelin’ that my phone tapped", "vault_lines": ["Got a feelin' that my phone tapped"], "meaning": "Rozay has a feeling that his phone is being tracked so that someone can covertly hear or tape his phone calls, most likely the feds or opposing drug dealers. However, if we learned anything from “Goodfellas”, high powered cocaine distributors can get very paranoid.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GeSnzKZvxNE", "annotation_id": "4436990", "url": "https://genius.com/4436990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Phone Tap", "line": "Call me on my sister phone, keep it on some G shit", "vault_lines": ["Call me on my sister phone, keep it on some G shit"], "meaning": "Rozay has his suspicious that his phone may be tapped and his friend has been in on the operation so to prove he really isn’t he insists he calls him on his sisters phone to talk in true privacy .This line also shows how close Rick Ross and his boy were. No many drug dealers would let you have any contact with their families let alone allow you to have their sisters phone number.", "annotation_id": "4407073", "url": "https://genius.com/4407073", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Phone Tap", "line": "Throw a stack in Magic City, make a hater panic", "vault_lines": ["Throw a stack in Magic City, make a hater panic"], "meaning": "A stack is slang for $1000, while Magic City is an Atlanta strip club. People will hate when Ross throws thousands in the strip club.", "annotation_id": "4395489", "url": "https://genius.com/4395489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Phone Tap", "line": "305 nigga, ridin’ in the Chevy", "vault_lines": ["305 nigga, ridin' in the Chevy"], "meaning": "305 is the area code for the city of Miami which is the city Rozay represents. He drives his Chevy around Miami to show off his luxurious ride.", "annotation_id": "4395400", "url": "https://genius.com/4395400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
