{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "Dade County where I came from", "vault_lines": ["Dade County where I came from"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s was raised in Carol City and where he began his rap career, Carol City is located near the edge of Miami-Dade county or more commonly known as Dad County. Ross is referring back to his beginning of his hip hop success and riches.", "annotation_id": "13732836", "url": "https://genius.com/13732836", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "Cocaine on the stovetop (Woah, woah), yayo up, won’t lie", "vault_lines": ["Cocaine on the stovetop (Woah, woah), yayo up, won't lie"], "meaning": "Yayo is slang for crack cocaine, a phrase popularised around the rap and underground community. Cocaine is usually made and cooked on a kitchen stove to purify the substance while forming crack rocks which the user inhales the fumes produced by the rocks.", "annotation_id": "13684493", "url": "https://genius.com/13684493", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "I crashed the Porsche and I crashed the Rover (Brr)", "vault_lines": [", I crashed the Porsche and I crashed the Rover (Brr)"], "meaning": "On May 30th, Lil Pump purchased a yellow Porsche reportedly worth $50K. The very next day, he posted a pic of the dented car on Twitter with the caption\n\nI just crashed the Porsche ouu\n\nhttps://twitter.com/lilpump/status/868923702804594688", "annotation_id": "13425162", "url": "https://genius.com/13425162", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "Bite a bitch ear like Mike Tyson, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I fuck a bitch, I ain't wifin', ooh, bite a bitch ear like Mike Tyson, yeah"], "meaning": "On June 28, 1997, Mike Tyson bit off the left ear of Evander Holyfield in the third round of a extremely notorious boxing match.", "annotation_id": "13145884", "url": "https://genius.com/13145884", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "VVS all on my diamond choker (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["VVS all on my diamond choker (Ooh)"], "meaning": "VVS or very very slightly included diamonds are some of the most expensive you can buy. To the naked eye they are perfect and can go for tens of thousands of dollars. The fact that Lil Pump has many of these on his choker shows his great wealth.", "annotation_id": "13145833", "url": "https://genius.com/13145833", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "Gettin’ out like I’m John Gotti", "vault_lines": ["Bel-Air my new old school, gettin' out like I'm John Gotti"], "meaning": "John Gotti was the leader of the Gambino crime family in New York. At his time, he was an infamous gangster, and died in 2002.", "annotation_id": "12851035", "url": "https://genius.com/12851035", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "And I got water on me like Flapjack (Water, water, water)", "vault_lines": ["Niggas want beef, yeah, we got that, and I got water on me like Flapjack (Water, water, water)"], "meaning": "“Water” is slang for diamonds which Purpp is always wearing. Flapjack is a pirate from the Cartoon Network show, “The Marvelous Misadventures of Flapjack” being a pirate he is obviously always around water.", "annotation_id": "12831117", "url": "https://genius.com/12831117", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pinky Ring", "line": "MAC-11 turned to a Big Mac (Blat, blat, blat)", "vault_lines": ["Ho, I got lean in my backpack (Backpack), MAC-11 turned to a Big Mac (Blat, blat, blat)"], "meaning": "A MAC-11 is a machine gun, and Purpp states that he has added some customization options, likely a scope, laser beam, grip, etc. The line is a play-on-words with the McDonald’s burger the ‘Big Mac’ which is known for being a hefty option on their menu.", "annotation_id": "12811547", "url": "https://genius.com/12811547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
