{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "God forgives and I don’t, only hustlers relate", "vault_lines": ["God forgives and I don't, only hustlers relate"], "meaning": "As a hustler, you should never tolerate being disrespected or walked over at all. i.e forgiveness is only between a man and God.\nTherefore, only real hustlers can understand how being that way is an advantage in the hustle game.", "annotation_id": "18327127", "url": "https://genius.com/18327127", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "Straight Grim Reaper, Air Jordans walkin’ the streets", "vault_lines": ["Straight Grim Reaper, Air Jordans walkin' the streets"], "meaning": "Ross menaces his enemies as the Grim Reaper menaces the lives of the living. This could also be a reference to Ross’s clothing, which could be an all black ensemble.\n\n\n\nAs for the Jordan line, Ross is rocking a coveted pair of Air Jordans as he walks the streets.", "annotation_id": "2052325", "url": "https://genius.com/2052325", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "I guess there ain’t no nice way to tell you niggas it’s game over, huh?", "vault_lines": ["I guess there ain't no nice way to tell you niggas it's game over, huh?"], "meaning": "The ultimate braggadocio – Ross insinuates that the release of this album, GFID, he has essentially ended the rap game, because there is no topping what Ross has just done.", "annotation_id": "2051038", "url": "https://genius.com/2051038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "[Intro]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The song samples The Mad Lads version of “I Forgot to Be Your Lover”, which has also been sampled for songs from MOP, GFK, and AZ. It’s pretty well traveled.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Q2K1gLCAzk#at=92", "annotation_id": "2050837", "url": "https://genius.com/2050837", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "We pirates out here, nigga, just trying to stay afloat", "vault_lines": ["We pirates out here, nigga, just trying to stay afloat"], "meaning": "The song is called “Pirates” because a pirate is a thief of the seas involved in dastardly activities. Like a pirate, Rozay talks about the Machiavellian activities in which a hustler is involved -such as breaking down kilos, importing marijuana, and “putting people to sleep” when necessary — all of which help the proverbial pirate “stay afloat”.\n\nThis is also a metaphor, saying that Rick Ross stays alive and floats above rather than underwater like pirates float on ships.", "annotation_id": "1448597", "url": "https://genius.com/1448597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "Jabar just got twenty-five", "vault_lines": ["Witness bitch niggas tell, Jabar just got twenty-five"], "meaning": "This “Jabar” fellow was previously mentioned on Ross' street single Made Men. He probably got indicted on murder (and was snitched on as referred to on the last line) and thus got 25 to life, the usual sentence for murder.", "annotation_id": "1283633", "url": "https://genius.com/1283633", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "R.I.P. to the legend, 2Pac Shakur with a nine", "vault_lines": ["R.I.P. to the legend, 2Pac Shakur with a nine"], "meaning": "No one can say Rick Ross doesn’t pay homage to the legends that came before him, and here is just another example of him doing just that.\n\nWhile also doing that, he’s saying he’s a thug with his weapons the same way that Tupac Shakur was.\n\nI guess you could say that Tupac’s back whenever Ross holds a .9.", "annotation_id": "1253351", "url": "https://genius.com/1253351", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "Niggas thinkin’ it’s voodoo the way bricks be multiplyin’", "vault_lines": ["Niggas thinkin' it's voodoo the way bricks be multiplyin'"], "meaning": "They cant even belive how much crack ross is stackin.\n\nRumors suggest that Rick Ross is affiliated with the Zoe Pound Gang, therefore he talks about his Haitians. And within this gang, vodou plays a big role because most of them believe in black magic.", "annotation_id": "1048144", "url": "https://genius.com/1048144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "Homicide stay on my mind", "vault_lines": ["Homicide stay on my mind"], "meaning": "The Notorious B.I.G. often mentioned homicide in his music and Ross compares himself to Big in this song as well. He is also saying that he’s thinking about murder and isn’t afraid to commit it. Check out the crime rate in his hometown, Miami.\n\nAlso, he’s saying that homicide is on his mind, because he is getting richer, and more haters come around this time.\nHe is the ‘Christopher Wallace of his time’ meaning that he is the next one in his eyes to be murdered, while being a big rapper in the rap game.\nAlso comparing his skills and succes to Biggie.", "annotation_id": "1048134", "url": "https://genius.com/1048134", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "Blackberry boss, one call, ya put to sleep", "vault_lines": ["Blackberry boss, one call, ya put to sleep"], "meaning": "Blackberry is the only brand of phones that can’t be tapped because they operate using their own servers. Making a call to “put somebody to sleep” would be wise to do with a Blackberry because the police can not hear you doing it which keeps you out of the picture for possible prosecution.", "annotation_id": "935726", "url": "https://genius.com/935726", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pirates", "line": "Associated with death", "vault_lines": ["Affiliated with wealth, associated with death"], "meaning": "Ross would find himself perhaps a bit more “associated with death” than he imagined in February 2012, when a man was found shot dead outside of the rapper’s house", "annotation_id": "933369", "url": "https://genius.com/933369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
