{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "That’s gangsta: Al Capone", "vault_lines": ["That’s gangsta: Al Capone"], "meaning": "Al Capone is an old, Prohibition-era gangster who led a crime syndicate.\n\n\n\nFUN FACT: Al Capone’s physical and mental health deteriorated under the effects of neurosyphilis. Guess he really did “fuck a bitch and [be] gone.”", "annotation_id": "842311", "url": "https://genius.com/842311", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I make that pussy spit like Bone I’m talkin’ ’bout bone, bone, bone bone", "vault_lines": ["I make that pussy spit like Bone", "I'm talkin' 'bout bone, bone, bone bone"], "meaning": "A shout out to the Bone Thugs-n-Harmony, saying he makes girls come like how Bone Thugs rap (VERY fast). “Spitting” is his way of saying “squirting.”\n\n\n\nHe also said “bone” 5 times: one for each member of the group.", "annotation_id": "842299", "url": "https://genius.com/842299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Then beat that pussy like Klitschko", "vault_lines": ["Then beat that pussy like Klitschko"], "meaning": "He beats it up like the boxing Klitschko brothers.\n\n\n\nAlso, Wayne is playing on the sentence, using ‘pussy’ and ‘KLIT(clit)schko’.\n\nFun Fact: Wladimir Klitschko’s partner Hayden Panettiere is much smaller than him, so with that size difference, you can imagine him beating it up.", "annotation_id": "842277", "url": "https://genius.com/842277", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m fuckin’ with French, excuse my French", "vault_lines": ["I'm fuckin' with French, excuse my French"], "meaning": "A play on the phrase “excuse my French” which basically just means “sorry for cursing” (since he just said “fuckin' with French). Excuse My French is also the name of French Montana’s debut album.", "annotation_id": "842265", "url": "https://genius.com/842265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Film it, film it, this bitch want me to film it Ballin’, ballin’ like I play for New England", "vault_lines": ["Film it, film it, this bitch want me to film it", "Ballin', ballin' like I play for New England"], "meaning": "In their 2007 season, the New England Patriots started their season off with some controversy. In Week 2 head coach Bill Belichick and the Patriots were penalized by the NFL for their involvement in the videotaping of opponents' defensive signals from an unauthorized location in their Week 1 game against the New York Jets, referred to in the press as Spygate.\n\nThis line may also be referring to a horny female wanting Rick Ross to video record their sexual encounter.\n\nIronically, the New England Patriots NFL team has the best record in the league since 2001, and is the second most valuable team in the league according to Forbes and in those particular terms, Rozay does his fare share of winning.", "annotation_id": "842260", "url": "https://genius.com/842260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Local club in my city, I fell in love with a stripper", "vault_lines": ["Local club in my city, I fell in love with a stripper"], "meaning": "In January, Ross threw his birthday party at Amnesia in South Beach.\n\nLike T-Pain, he’s in love with a stripperrr", "annotation_id": "842252", "url": "https://genius.com/842252", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m in that white ghost chasin’ Pac-Man Hundred out the lot,", "vault_lines": ["I'm in that white ghost chasin' Pac-Man", "Hundred out the lot,"], "meaning": "Rolls-Royce Phantoms, (in this case a $100.000 one,) have the nickname “Ghosts”, but they actually make a Ghost which is new to the RR lineup. French may be referring to either one.\n\n\n\nIn the arcade game Pac-Man, ghosts chase PacMan around the game. Although there is technically no white ghost, he is referring to the ghosts in general", "annotation_id": "842192", "url": "https://genius.com/842192", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m Young Papi, Champagne", "vault_lines": ["I'm Young Papi, Champagne"], "meaning": "One of Drake’s well known monikers (and Instagram name), especially around the ova circle is “Champagne Papi” which refers to his extensive love for wine and champagne.", "annotation_id": "840125", "url": "https://genius.com/840125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Money comin’, money goin’, ain’t like you could take it with you (Alright)", "vault_lines": ["Money comin', money goin', ain't like you could take it with you (Alright)"], "meaning": "Drake and his crew are making money but spending it too because, like the line from the musical says, you can’t take it with you (when you die)\n\nDrake might be Jewish, but this is also a lesson from the New Testament, 1 Timothy 6:7\n\nFor we brought nothing into this world, and it is certain we can carry nothing out.\n\nPotentially a response to Pusha T, who said in Exodus 23:1 wealth don’t buy health, drake is telling him he would rather spend it he can’t take it with him", "annotation_id": "840094", "url": "https://genius.com/840094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Greystone, twenty bottles that’s all me", "vault_lines": ["Greystone, twenty bottles that's all me"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the extremely popular Greystone Manor nightclub in Hollywood. He is usually there on Sundays as it’s a hip-hop night. Proof: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UXgQ4BFGNH4", "annotation_id": "839759", "url": "https://genius.com/839759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "One of my closest dawgs got three kids and they all three But we always been that type of crew that been good without a plan B, so", "vault_lines": ["One of my closest dawgs got three kids and they all three", "But we always been that type of crew that been good without a plan B, so"], "meaning": "Drake’s crew has never been the type to need a backup plan, while also throwing in the Plan B line relating to his homie and his kids.\n\nNotice the slick homophone of “been good” and “be in good” – as in they get shit done without a back-up plan, the same way they be in “good” (pussy) without the morning-after pill.", "annotation_id": "839720", "url": "https://genius.com/839720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Only thing you got is some years on me Man, fuck you and your time difference", "vault_lines": ["Only thing you got is some years on me", "Man, fuck you and your time difference"], "meaning": "Seems like lines directed at Pusha T, considering Pusha had some words for Drake recently. Also, Pusha is 35, while Drake is 25.\n\nDrake is also referencing Pusha T’s “I Don’t Like” verse, when Pusha says “Dope money, coke money/Hublot, my watch better.”\n\nBut besides Pusha, this is a possible shot at a few rappers older than him or have been/were rapping before him (i.e. DMX, Fabulous, Common, Ludacris). .\n\nNote: Pusha might’ve shot back at Drake with this line from “Blocka”. Both lines use “fuck you and your…”\n\nI ball hard and you bench ride, so fuck you and yo' bassline!", "annotation_id": "839716", "url": "https://genius.com/839716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Gettin cheddar packs like K.D., OKC that’s player shit", "vault_lines": ["Gettin cheddar packs like K.D., OKC that's player shit"], "meaning": "Drake tweeted this line not too long ago.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/209186783970340865\n\nDrizzy gets cheddar (money) like KD which stands for both Kraft Dinner, a brand of macaroni and cheese, and NBA player Kevin Durant. OKC is Durant’s team, Oklahoma City, and also means “Okay, see that’s player shit”.\n\nThe Oklahoma City reference does not come out of the blue.  Drake and his entourage shut down an Oklahoma City night club after massive amounts of marijuana smoke was seen coming out of the VIP section. Drake & Co escaped unscathed, however, the night club owner is suing for damages.\n\nKevin Durant is loving the exposure: https://twitter.com/KDTrey5/status/244635730364731392\n\nIt should also note that calling Kraft Mac and Cheese “KD” is a Canadian thing.\n\nAlso Kevin Durant and Drake had the same net worth at the time.", "annotation_id": "839696", "url": "https://genius.com/839696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "We don’t dress alike, we don’t rap alike I shine different, I rhyme different", "vault_lines": ["We don't dress alike, we don't rap alike", "I shine different, I rhyme different"], "meaning": "Drake has often been accused of stealing the “Supa Dupa flow” style that he used early in his career.", "annotation_id": "839690", "url": "https://genius.com/839690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I hope you pussy niggas hatin’ never make a nickel (Right)", "vault_lines": ["I hope you pussy niggas hatin' never make a nickel (Right)"], "meaning": "Drake is taking a subliminal shot at numerous rappers dissing him right now (Pusha-T, Fabolous, and all others )\n\nAlso many believe that some rappers will create beef with another rapper to promote an album. Drake believes that Common did this with “Sweet” (before they squashed their beef) as he stated on “Stay Schemin”\n\nThis is also a play on the expression ‘I hope you never make a dime’. By saying nickel instead of dime, Drake shows his true dislike of his haters.", "annotation_id": "839682", "url": "https://genius.com/839682", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "OVO, that’s major shit, Toronto with me, that’s mayor shit", "vault_lines": ["OVO, that's major shit, Toronto with me, that's mayor shit"], "meaning": "OVO (Drake’s music group October’s Very Own) is up and rising and becoming a major part of his career.\n\nToronto is his hometown and he will never forget that. Watch out, Rob Ford!", "annotation_id": "839679", "url": "https://genius.com/839679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m about bein’ single, seein’ double, makin’ triple (Right)", "vault_lines": ["I'm about bein' single, seein' double, makin' triple (Right)"], "meaning": "Drake is all about no strings attached relationships (I mean, you only live once right?), getting drunk, and making three times as much money. Single, double, triple. Get it?", "annotation_id": "839673", "url": "https://genius.com/839673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I go by the name Lil Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["I go by the name Lil Tunechi"], "meaning": "One of Lil Waynes many nicknames, ‘@LilTunechi’ is also his Twitter handle. It’s comprised of ‘Tune’ which was a nickname given to Wayne by his grandmother, and ‘chi’ which was added by Wayne to make it sound like ‘Gucci’, the clothing brand.", "annotation_id": "839651", "url": "https://genius.com/839651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
