{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "Ill na na (Uh, uh)", "vault_lines": [", ill na na (Uh, uh)"], "meaning": "This could mean two things.\n\n\nThe verse before this one brings’ up foxy brown so it could be, Ill Na Na the debut studio album by American rapper Foxy Brown. A nickname given to her by rapper Nas & was released on November 19, 1996, by Def Jam Recordings.\nIll na na, u should know that ill means tight and for na na think of the last two letters of vagina.", "annotation_id": "28123567", "url": "https://genius.com/28123567", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "Put that Foxy Brown in his face", "vault_lines": ["Put that Foxy Brown in his face"], "meaning": "https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hip-hop-music/images/5/55/Foxy_Brown.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20150412120002\n\nFoxy Brown is an African American rap musician, model and actress. Her birth name is Inga DeCarlo Fung Marchand. She was born on September 6, 1978 in Brooklyn, New York. As a teenager, she won a talent contest, where she was discovered by the rapper LL Cool J’s production team. They were so impressed by her rapping skills that they signed her on to rap on LL Cool J’s upcoming album “I Shot Ya”.\n\nThis was followed by appearances on several other artists’ songs and albums such as “You’re Makin’ Me High” by Toni Braxton and “Ain’t No Nigga” by Jay-Z.\n\n Her early success led to many labels singling her out and she eventually signed with Def Jam Records. She was also featured on the soundtrack of the 1996 film “The Nutty Professor” starring Eddie Murphy.", "annotation_id": "28123547", "url": "https://genius.com/28123547", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "AMG kit on the Benz (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["AMG kit on the Benz (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "AMG is a type of engine on Mercedes-Benz cars. As a sidenote, AMG Peformance models are usually expensive.", "annotation_id": "7919931", "url": "https://genius.com/7919931", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "Hey, Trey, ain’t ya hear Jhené say (What?) But he gotta eat the booty like groceries (Woop)", "vault_lines": ["Hey, Trey, ain't ya hear Jhené say (What?)", "But he gotta eat the booty like groceries (Woop)"], "meaning": "Trey draws on Jhené’s most memorable line from the original version to tell us he’s not afraid to eat the booty like groceries. Jhené’s vocals from the original are also used here.", "annotation_id": "6775478", "url": "https://genius.com/6775478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "Black bottle in the sky, free Gucci Mane (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Black bottle in the sky, free Gucci Mane (Woo)"], "meaning": "The “Black Bottle Boy” Rozay shouting out his incarcerated homie, Gucci Mane. The Trap God was sentenced to 39 months in prison after pleading guilty to a firearms charge.", "annotation_id": "6510304", "url": "https://genius.com/6510304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "Like oh, I’m here, this is my year I ain’t goin’ back, my old life is done (I ain’t goin’ back)", "vault_lines": ["I ain't goin' back, my old life is done (I ain't goin' back)"], "meaning": "This most definitely is her year. “Me U & Hennessy (Remix)” feat. Lil Wayne peaked at 38 on the Hot R&B/Hip-Hop chart. Already she has been featured on songs with buzzing artist such as Lil Durk, Game, Kid Ink, etc. She was also one of the hand-selected 2015 XXL Freshmen.", "annotation_id": "6374380", "url": "https://genius.com/6374380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "They about to take your phone, just see (Yup) I don’t need no hoes exposin’ me (Nah)", "vault_lines": ["They about to take your phone, just see (Yup)", "I don't need no hoes exposin' me (Nah)"], "meaning": "Often before parties phones are taken as low-profile guests are asked to sign a waiver in order to reduce risk of unwanted exposure.\n\n\n\nChris Brown mentioned such protocol on “Remember Me”\n\nSmoking weed on the plane, that’s the best high\nShe gotta sign the waiver ‘fore I let her fly", "annotation_id": "6372273", "url": "https://genius.com/6372273", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Post to Be (Remix)", "line": "Double M, we throw them alley-oops, that’s all day (Swish)", "vault_lines": ["Double M, we throw them alley-oops, that's all day (Swish)"], "meaning": "Double-M is short for Rick Ross' record label, MMG.\n\n\n\nBecause the label having been dropping fire lately with albums like Ross' “Hood Billionaire” & Wale’s “The Album About Nothing” it is similar to them shooting alley oops in basketball.", "annotation_id": "6372259", "url": "https://genius.com/6372259", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
