{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "I did get a scholarship, but I blew that", "vault_lines": ["I did get a scholarship, but I blew that"], "meaning": "Before his music career, Rick Ross was not only a correctional officer but also attended college for a short amount of time before dropping out.\n\nAfter graduating from Carol City Senior High School, Rozay had attended Albany State University on a football scholarship.", "annotation_id": "12629909", "url": "https://genius.com/12629909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "Had to pull my pants up, go and get ’em brands up", "vault_lines": ["Had to pull my pants up, go and get 'em brands up"], "meaning": "“Pull my pants up” means he’s gotta grow up, get tough, put on his “big boy pants”, and fend for himself.\n\n“Get them brands up” means he’s switching out his old no-name clothing with high-end designer brands: Gucci, Tom Ford, etc. Now that he’s stepped up his game from a nickel rock to a full brick, he’s starting to ball enough to afford the nicer things in life.", "annotation_id": "3194903", "url": "https://genius.com/3194903", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "In the room full of work", "vault_lines": ["In the room full of work"], "meaning": "A load of contraband, usually drugs (often Coke or Weed) they’re going to sell. “Work” is lower-quality stuff so the good stuff can be used themselves.\n\n“Its rainy days if we don’t move all our work”\n- Lil' Flip", "annotation_id": "3194887", "url": "https://genius.com/3194887", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "Thinkin’ ’bout Land Rover, damn near was fucked up", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' 'bout Land Rover, damn near was fucked up"], "meaning": "ran rover was a rapper from miami who ross was close to before he died. he was found in a trunk with another male dead.", "annotation_id": "3039346", "url": "https://genius.com/3039346", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "Fuck football, I’m goin’ down another path", "vault_lines": ["Fuck football, I'm goin' down another path"], "meaning": "Before he came up in the rap game, Rozay went to college at Albany State University, where he played football on a scholarship. Obviously, he chose to abandon football in favor of becoming a crack dealer and an infamous rapper.", "annotation_id": "2526904", "url": "https://genius.com/2526904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "It’s time fo’ me to cash in, laughin’", "vault_lines": ["It's time fo' me to cash in, laughin'"], "meaning": "It is time for him to earn a lot of money,we can say that he is pretty good at cash making as we see by his wealthy lifestyle.\n\n\n\nLaughin' in the end of the line probably means “Laughing to the bank” He is referencing the phrase “laughing all the way to the bank,” as exemplified in the 50 Cent track “Straight to the Bank” where you can hear a “ha ha ha ha” throughout the song.", "annotation_id": "2473099", "url": "https://genius.com/2473099", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "I went and bought a bird", "vault_lines": ["I went and bought a bird"], "meaning": "Typically a street slang measurement term for a kilogram of cocaine. It equals 286 eight balls. A kilogram is also known as a key, bird, chicken, and so forth.", "annotation_id": "1474945", "url": "https://genius.com/1474945", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "Triple C’s", "vault_lines": ["The grenades down the street, you gotta git it how you live (Triple C's)"], "meaning": "He’s referring to the group, the Carol City Cartel or the Triple C’s, in which he’s a member.\n\n It has been referred to in previous introductions from the album including Blow and Cross That Line,", "annotation_id": "1474936", "url": "https://genius.com/1474936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pots and Pans", "line": "Choppa in the crib", "vault_lines": ["Got a 40 in the car, a choppa in the crib"], "meaning": "It was only a few years later when he began to put the choppa in the whip.", "annotation_id": "888859", "url": "https://genius.com/888859", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
