{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "(Yeah, ho)", "vault_lines": ["Your girlfriend down on both knees, she catch more balls than a goalie (Yeah, ho)"], "meaning": "This is a famously used chant from the song “Mafia Niggaz,” from the album When the Smoke Clears… Sixty 6, Sixty 1 by Three 6 Mafia. This is very appropriate, since one of the founding members, Juicy J is one of the producers and founding members.", "annotation_id": "11178012", "url": "https://genius.com/11178012", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Bad chick with me got ass and titties, freaky bitch gon’ fuck the whole team", "vault_lines": ["Bad chick with me got ass and titties, freaky bitch gon' fuck the whole team"], "meaning": "Juicy is only messing with women that show his whole crew love, which means it ain’t no fun if the homies can’t have none.\n\n\n\nAs he rapped on “Sucks On Dick”:\n\nCome on in ho\nI know you wit that train shit, the bitch said for sho'\nPat was hittin from the back like a can of mace\nI was in the front, dick hangin in her face", "annotation_id": "4931394", "url": "https://genius.com/4931394", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "You might need a raincoat", "vault_lines": ["I'll make it flood, shorty, you might need a raincoat"], "meaning": "she’s gonna need a raincoat to withstand the amount of money that Juicy J is flooding the club with!\n\n\n\nHowever, everyone would get disappointed if the strippers wore raincoats, covering their body.", "annotation_id": "2137442", "url": "https://genius.com/2137442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "I go in like a door key", "vault_lines": ["Ziplock bag full of OG, I go in like a door key"], "meaning": "He gets to go into any party without having to wait in line, as if he has a door key for anything.\n\nOr it could be referring to sex, where he puts his “tool” into a girl, being the “key” to her orgasm.", "annotation_id": "2131060", "url": "https://genius.com/2131060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "You niggas shaky like dice", "vault_lines": ["Scared money don't make no money, you niggas shaky like dice"], "meaning": "“Shaky” is a slang for someone who is not skillful. Juicy is playing on the words “shaky” and “shake” as in shaking something, such as dice.", "annotation_id": "2131055", "url": "https://genius.com/2131055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 2: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Surprising to see Ross and Jeezy on the same song, given that they are currently beefing with each other – this lead to shots being fired at an awards ceremony.\n\n\n\nClearly Rihanna’s hustle’s better than both of theirs…", "annotation_id": "1814068", "url": "https://genius.com/1814068", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "[Chorus: Rihanna]", "vault_lines": ["[Chorus: Rihanna & Rick Ross"], "meaning": "Like Juicy reminds us in “Bandz A Make Her Dance\"\nRacks everywhere, they showin' racks, I’m throwing racks\n\nLike TIP reminds us in “Whatever You Like\"\nLong as I got rubberband banks in my pocket… Go get it I’ll buy it\n\nLike Jeezy reminds us in “Supafreak\"\nCan’t hear nothing but the money so she might just think i’m big enough\n\nAnd finally like Rozay reminds us in “Aston Martin Music\"\nI need a new safe cause i’m running out of space", "annotation_id": "1688018", "url": "https://genius.com/1688018", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Surrounded by bad bitches like Riri Got them booty shots, look like Nicki", "vault_lines": ["Got them booty shots, look like Nicki"], "meaning": "Rihanna (Rih-Rih) is the archetypal “bad bitch”, and has been described as such (including by herself) several times before.\n\n\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj also is considered something of a “bad bitch” (and saturates her music with the term). Nicki is also well-known for her massive ass, which Tip also brings reference to.", "annotation_id": "1651456", "url": "https://genius.com/1651456", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Throw it up, throw it up Watch it all fall out Pour it up, pour it up That’s how we ball out Throw it up, throw it up Watch it all fall out Pour it up, pour it up That’s how we ball out", "vault_lines": ["Throw it up, throw it up", "Watch it all fall out", "Pour it up, pour it up", "That's how we ball out"], "meaning": "Just like the 4 southern emcees RiRi chose to include in her song, she’s all about the money.\n\n\n\nLike Juicy reminds us in “Bandz A Make Her Dance”\nRacks everywhere, they showin' racks, I’m throwing racks\n\nLike TIP reminds us in “Whatever You Like”\nLong as I got rubberband banks in my pocket… Go get it I’ll buy it\n\nLike Jeezy reminds us in “Supafreak”\nCan’t hear nothing but the money so she might just think i’m big enough\n\nAnd finally like Rozay reminds us in “Aston Martin Music”\nI need a new safe cause i’m running out of space", "annotation_id": "1643960", "url": "https://genius.com/1643960", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Straight gas nigga, that BP,", "vault_lines": ["Straight gas nigga, that BP,"], "meaning": "Double meaning of “gas” here. He means gas as in ‘go in’ on a track and kill the beat but also as in gasoline, which he clarifies with his reference to BP or British Petroleum.", "annotation_id": "1642676", "url": "https://genius.com/1642676", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "[Intro: Young Jeezy]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Jeezy’s second collaboration with Rihanna, after his featured verse on Hard.\n\nIt’s worth noting Jeezy is very close to Rihanna’s management boss (and mentor) Jay-Z.", "annotation_id": "1640183", "url": "https://genius.com/1640183", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Rick Ross", "vault_lines": ["[Chorus: Rihanna & Rick Ross"], "meaning": "Ross’s second piece of work with Rihanna – after Cake.\n\nHe also says he “gave Rihanna [his] pager” in I Am Your Leader.", "annotation_id": "1640177", "url": "https://genius.com/1640177", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Juicy J pourin’ up codeine, Benz all white, no chlorine", "vault_lines": ["Juicy J pourin' up codeine, Benz all white, no chlorine"], "meaning": "The Trippy King is sippin' on some purple sprite (sprite mixed with cough syrup, which makes you higher than an astronaut), and he possibly doing it in the back of Benz, which is so white, you would think it was bleached with chlorine, which is a chemical element, known for its bleaching ability. Trippy!", "annotation_id": "1635022", "url": "https://genius.com/1635022", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "I’m in the bed with your wife, we poppin’ pills, we goin’ hard", "vault_lines": ["I'm in the bed with your wife, we poppin' pills, we goin' hard"], "meaning": "When Juicy is banging your wife, he pops some Viagra, a pill that makes your dick hard, so that he can perform well (go hard). This double-entendre has also been used by 2 Chainz, in his song “Vi-Agra”.", "annotation_id": "1633751", "url": "https://genius.com/1633751", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Purple all in my Sprite,", "vault_lines": ["Purple all in my Sprite,"], "meaning": "Juicy J’s favorite drink is purple drank, AKA “Dirty Sprite” or “Lean.” This is a mixture of Codeine Promethazine, Sprite (or sometimes Fanta) and purple Jolly Ranchers for added flavor.", "annotation_id": "1633637", "url": "https://genius.com/1633637", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "Peter Luger’s, the better seats", "vault_lines": ["Peter Luger's, the better seats"], "meaning": "The No. 1 steakhouse in New York City for 28 years running. Rick Ross only goes to the best steakhouses with the best steaks because he is the best and makes sure to get the best seat(s) in the restaurant.", "annotation_id": "1605487", "url": "https://genius.com/1605487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "I’m King Tut with my gold chain (Gold chain)", "vault_lines": ["I'm King Tut with my gold chain (Gold chain)"], "meaning": "They’re both shining with all them jewels on\n\n\n\nKing Tut refers to the ancient Egyptian King Tutankhamun who, by Egyptian tradition, was buried with all his valuable gold", "annotation_id": "1602090", "url": "https://genius.com/1602090", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "That Kendrick on them bottles came, poured a Swimming Pool, now we ’bout to dive", "vault_lines": ["That Kendrick on them bottles came, poured a Swimming Pool, now we 'bout to dive"], "meaning": "Reference to the next line and Kendrick Lamar’s Swimming Pools which entertains thoughts of excessive drinking and pouring up pools of liquor.\n\n\n\nJeezy obviously has something similar in mind.", "annotation_id": "1600937", "url": "https://genius.com/1600937", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pour It Up (Remix)", "line": "These bitch niggas be actin’ up, these ho niggas be actin’ foul", "vault_lines": ["These bitch niggas be actin' up, these ho niggas be actin' foul"], "meaning": "Jeezy aims his first subliminal diss at Rick Ross by changing the lyrics to Actin' Up by MMG. He belives that Ross is portraying a lifestyle he has never lived. Rick Ross often claims to be a drug dealer in his raps, although many are skeptical of this claim given the fact that Ross was once a correctional officer in Miami.", "annotation_id": "1600265", "url": "https://genius.com/1600265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
