{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "line": "I’m pouring out my heart to be that nigga in the city Homies in the hood already saying I done did it", "vault_lines": ["I'm pouring out my heart to be that nigga in the city", "Homies in the hood already saying I done did it"], "meaning": "It’s true.  Juvie has been “that nigga” in New Orleans at least since 1991’s classic collaboration with D.J. Jimi, “Bounce (for the Juvenile)”", "annotation_id": "438977", "url": "https://genius.com/438977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "line": "Looking at my bezel and that motherfucker dancing", "vault_lines": ["Looking at my bezel and that motherfucker dancing"], "meaning": "His bezel has so many diamonds in it that they seem to be “dancing” when they glisten in the light", "annotation_id": "437919", "url": "https://genius.com/437919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "line": "Power is something that you develop on the block Pull up on a bad bitch sitting in a drop", "vault_lines": ["Power is something that you develop on the block", "Pull up on a bad bitch sitting in a drop"], "meaning": "Ross’s idol, the fictional Tony Montana, had something to say about this:\n\n In this country, you gotta make the money first. Then when you get the money, you get the power. Then when you get the power, then you get the women", "annotation_id": "437881", "url": "https://genius.com/437881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "line": "Look at me balling, we courtside at the game Twenty for the ticket, ’nother hundred for the chain", "vault_lines": ["Look at me balling, we courtside at the game", "Twenty for the ticket, 'nother hundred for the chain"], "meaning": "Apparently, for once Ross isn’t exaggerating.  Courtside tickets to the NBA finals will cost you in the range of $15-30K.  If he’s at a regular season game, though, he’s getting robbed!", "annotation_id": "437733", "url": "https://genius.com/437733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "line": "Scarface, bitch -- I’m feeling like Brad I’m a underground king like Chad", "vault_lines": ["Scarface, bitch -- I'm feeling like Brad", "I'm a underground king like Chad"], "meaning": "Juvie here compares himself both to the movie’s Scarface (a.k.a. Tony Montana), the Al Pacino-portrayed drug kingpin with tons of money\n\n\n\nas well as the rapper who loved the movie so much he would take its name, Brad “Scarface” Jordan\n\n\n\nIn addition, he name-drops the late rapper and producer Chad “Pimp C” Butler, of the group UGK (short for “Underground Kingz”)\n\n\n\nJuvie isn’t the only rapper who has lately taken to calling himself an underground king", "annotation_id": "437710", "url": "https://genius.com/437710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "line": "Count money, money machines they going ccccccrrrrrrr So that mean a nigga full", "vault_lines": ["Count money, money machines they going ccccccrrrrrrr", "So that mean a nigga full"], "meaning": "Ross' sounds here are reminiscent of Jay-Z’s famous impersonation of a money machine on “I Can’t Get With That”", "annotation_id": "437703", "url": "https://genius.com/437703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "line": "J. Prince, nigga, that’s (power)", "vault_lines": ["J. Prince, nigga, that's (power)"], "meaning": "James Prince is the CEO of Houston’s Rap-a-Lot Records, and has put out legendary albums by the likes of The Geto Boys, Big Mike, Scarface, Z-Ro, and more", "annotation_id": "437671", "url": "https://genius.com/437671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Juvenile-power-lyrics", "genius_title": "Power", "genius_id": 58736, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Oh Lord, this can’t be life, no it can’t be life", "vault_lines": ["Oh Lord, this can't be life, no it can't be life"], "meaning": "A reference to the classic Jay-Z, Beanie Sigel and Scarface track “This Can’t Be Life” from Jay’s “The Dynasty” album", "annotation_id": "29740513", "url": "https://genius.com/29740513", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Seen a pastor tweaking, then sunk his teeth in a rock his demise Later on that evening you heard the grieving of angels that cried See a demon don’t compromise", "vault_lines": ["Seen a pastor tweaking, then sunk his teeth in a rock his demise", "Later on that evening you heard the grieving of angels that cried", "See a demon don't compromise"], "meaning": "Relating to drugs, to “tweak” is to have mindless sporadic movements as a side effect of consuming specific drugs.\n\n In this case, the pastor is tweaking from a “rock” (a slang term used for crack cocaine).\n\nThe imagery that Kendrick paints describes the negative environment of Compton. Even the most righteous fall victim to corruption where he is from.\n\nThis may be a major factor as to why Kendrick denounces pastors, as he’s rapped on the single “Rigamortis”:\n\nI’ll pass the weed to the pastor\nWe all are sinners, won’t you send us to bible study faster?\nYour hypocritesque reaction a blasphemy\n\nHe also stated on “Look Out For Detox”:\n\nThat’s a T-Rex in a V-neck for the rapture\nI’m a factor and your facial\nI will fracture to a fraction\nNo one-half and I hate math\nPastor’s like Eddie long, fucking maricon\n\nHe further elaborates on this imagery by painting the picture of angels grieving for the pastor to come back, but demons don’t make deals and play for keeps. The drugs got the better of said pastor and led to his demise.", "annotation_id": "15587575", "url": "https://genius.com/15587575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "I give her D, I throw up two, I call that shit a safety", "vault_lines": ["I give her D, I throw up two, I call that shit a safety"], "meaning": "Wale doesn’t spend the night with the women he has sex with. The term “give her D” (short for “give her dick”) was popularized by Detroit rapper Big Sean’s line in “Mercy”:\n\nI give her that D ‘cause that’s where I was born and raised in\n\nRather than actually saying goodbye to her, he makes a peace sign with his pointer and index finger, another way of symbolically saying “see you later” or “deuces.”\n\n\n\n“Throwing up two” is also used in football to describe earning 2 points after scoring a safety, which occurs when an offensive player is tackled in their own end zone while in possession of the ball. It’s the least common scoring method in the sport.\n\nA former football player himself, Wale is a huge sports fan and makes it known in his lyrics.", "annotation_id": "14179012", "url": "https://genius.com/14179012", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "So about face if it ain’t business, I get offended", "vault_lines": ["So about face if it ain't business, I get offended"], "meaning": "In military marching drill exercises, “About Face” is where the entire squad, or group of marchers turn around, and walk in the direction they just came from.\n\nKendrick, a businessman himself gets offended if you come to him, and it’s not about business. He’d rather you turn around\nrunning.", "annotation_id": "11478964", "url": "https://genius.com/11478964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Then crank the Lac up", "vault_lines": ["Then crank the Lac up"], "meaning": "To start a Cadillac. Some old cars used to be started via a hand crank on the front of the engine.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D6pLp4tlIw0\n\nNow, cranking a car means turning the key in the ignition.", "annotation_id": "9812497", "url": "https://genius.com/9812497", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "We ain’t never left, acting like we back You should see us now taking pictures acting like we rap", "vault_lines": ["We ain't never left, acting like we back", "You should see us now taking pictures acting like we rap"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5236096119001", "annotation_id": "2926336", "url": "https://genius.com/2926336", "state": "verified", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Now I’m on a power trip", "vault_lines": ["Now I got a power circle, now I'm on a power trip"], "meaning": "A power trip is when someone thinks they are better than everyone else and they can do what they want.\nEx.. Aaron Hernandez thought he was above the law when he “killed” 3 people, obviously he was just on a power trip.", "annotation_id": "1933089", "url": "https://genius.com/1933089", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Stone me, throw me a pile of shit but you won’t pull me out of it", "vault_lines": ["Stone me, throw me a pile of shit but you won't pull me out of it"], "meaning": "More common in the early 1900’s, stoning is a form of capital punishment whereby a group throws stones at a person until death ensues.  Slower than other forms of execution, stoning is a form of execution by torture.\n\n\n\nNo matter what you do to Stalley, even if you throw him into a pile of shit, you won’t help him out because he will get out himself and conquer the situation.", "annotation_id": "1915101", "url": "https://genius.com/1915101", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "When you finish first they hate you worse, startin to see now", "vault_lines": ["When you finish first they hate you worse, startin to see now"], "meaning": "There is an old adage in the rap game (and life) about how once a person comes into power & fame, and begins to get money, hate is surely to follow.\n\nNow that Gunplay is starting to climb to the pinnacle of rap, he understands this old proverb, as he has begun to feel the wrath of MMG haters.", "annotation_id": "1786642", "url": "https://genius.com/1786642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "‘Til the last gavel drop we gon’ have it locked We gon’ have it locked We gon’ have it locked", "vault_lines": ["'Til the last gavel drop we gon' have it locked", "We gon' have it locked"], "meaning": "A clever play on words – Gunplay, no stranger to prison, is comparing the end of the world to a judge sentencing a criminal to life in prison. It is the last gavel drop that prisoner will ever hear, and MMG will continue to release quality music until their last day on this planet.\n\n\n\nMy life more real than my raps", "annotation_id": "1439623", "url": "https://genius.com/1439623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Look at my persona, I dreamed it, woke up and conquered And there was commas after commas, I eat ’em like Benihanas", "vault_lines": ["Look at my persona, I dreamed it, woke up and conquered", "And there was commas after commas, I eat 'em like Benihanas"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5237781216001", "annotation_id": "1135801", "url": "https://genius.com/1135801", "state": "verified", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "[Verse 2: Gunplay]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Gunplay described this verse as putting his best foot forward, as if it was his last verse while being alive. If this was Gunplay’s last verse, this is what he would’ve said. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CD0Z-UJx5QQ&feature=player_embedded", "annotation_id": "1019306", "url": "https://genius.com/1019306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Clique full of real niggas that’ll probably murk you", "vault_lines": ["Clique full of real niggas that'll probably murk you"], "meaning": "Meeks crew, MMG, is full of ‘real niggas’ or being real and true to yourself, but would pull the trigger, or murk you if they need to.", "annotation_id": "977421", "url": "https://genius.com/977421", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "You don’t know nann nigga, nope, uh uh", "vault_lines": ["You don't know nann nigga, nope, uh uh"], "meaning": "You don’t know another nigga like him – he’s truly one of a kind.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference To Trick Daddy’s song “Nann Nigga”, which he later remixed.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rd1pToBnQ2s", "annotation_id": "909360", "url": "https://genius.com/909360", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Shit is crazy when entertainment ain’t entertaining", "vault_lines": ["Shit is crazy when entertainment ain't entertaining"], "meaning": "It’s called entertainment, so why isn’t it entertaining? This is probably referring to played out “reality TV”, weak “beef” in the music industry, etc.", "annotation_id": "880845", "url": "https://genius.com/880845", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "And my inner sanctum need real estate", "vault_lines": ["And my inner sanctum need real estate"], "meaning": "Wale uses inner sanctum to mean his mind. Because he is “out his cabeza” or “out of his mind”, it needs real estate so he can get his mind back by owning the property.", "annotation_id": "873069", "url": "https://genius.com/873069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
