{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Regardless of how it goes down Life goes on, am I right?", "vault_lines": ["Regardless of how it goes down", "Life goes on, am I right?"], "meaning": "Rozay quotes himself, refering to what he said on the title track of his last mixtape Rich Forever.", "annotation_id": "868851", "url": "https://genius.com/868851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "If I fall in the field and ain’t no more air for me Pour some on the ground and put one in the air for me", "vault_lines": ["If I fall in the field and ain't no more air for me", "Pour some on the ground and put one in the air for me"], "meaning": "If Gunplay dies while he’s trapping (you know, in the field of work), he wants his friends & fam to remember him respectfully – by pouring liquor on the ground or, in a less traditional way, smoking one", "annotation_id": "865991", "url": "https://genius.com/865991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "When they day breaks and you earned them stripes And you learned that strike From upstate will adjourn that life and confirm that life It’s good bait for the warden that might get awarded and write", "vault_lines": ["When they day breaks and you earned them stripes", "And you learned that strike", "From upstate will adjourn that life and confirm that life", "It's good bait for the warden that might get awarded and write"], "meaning": "These lines could perhaps be read as a critique of the burgeoning prison-industrial complex. Staying out of jail as a person of color from the hood is also something he’s rapped about before.", "annotation_id": "865405", "url": "https://genius.com/865405", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "And so I walk alone with a cross and a diamond stone I’m a diamond inside the rough that’s too mighty for maricons", "vault_lines": ["And so I walk alone with a cross and a diamond stone", "I'm a diamond inside the rough that's too mighty for maricons"], "meaning": "Rather than relying on the corrupt religious authorities lambasted above, Kendrick is solitary about his religious concerns.  He spoke to MTV about his feelings regarding matters of the spirit:\n\n I wouldn’t say I’m the most religious person, neither were both of my parents. I always do quote-unquote religious songs or whatever you want to call them from the standpoint where I’m trying to find answers. That’s the space I speak from and a lot of people can relate because they feel the same way. [I’m] not a person that’s putting it in your head — “believe this, believe this, believe this.” I’m going through something, I’m a sinner and I’m trying to figure myself out. It never sounds preachy. It sounds like a person who’s really confused by what the world has put upon him", "annotation_id": "865386", "url": "https://genius.com/865386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Look inside the eyes of the last Mohicans survived", "vault_lines": ["Look inside the eyes of the last Mohicans survived"], "meaning": "The Last of the Mohicans is an 1826 novel by James Fennimore Cooper.  One of the novel’s main characters is Natty Bumppo, also known as Hawkeye, a white man who was raised among Native Americans.\n\nKendrick here uses the title of the novel as a nod to the idea of him being the final person of his kind to survive.  Whether he is referring to surviving his Compton youth, his status as an original artist in a trend-driven industry, or something else entirely is unclear.", "annotation_id": "852941", "url": "https://genius.com/852941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Lotta talking, lotta Tweeting, ’til you hear that chopper speaking", "vault_lines": ["Lotta talking, lotta Tweeting, 'til you hear that chopper speaking"], "meaning": "Mill did in fact get into a short-lived Twitter beef with Roscoe Dash over the Drake/Chris Brown brawl", "annotation_id": "852666", "url": "https://genius.com/852666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "I know the priors they running by us when we do crime", "vault_lines": ["I know the priors they running by us when we do crime"], "meaning": "The “priors” here are previous arrests, etc. He could also be talking about the Richard Pryor ‘freebasing incident’ when he accidentally set himself on fire and ran through the streets high on coke.\n\n“Prior” also refers to somebody is the head of a certain religious order, and even sounds like the word “prayer”; so Kendrick is likely to be continuing the religious metaphors.\n\nEven further, this may refer to the Terrelle Pryor scandal, as Pryor was Ohio State’s quarterback, and Kendrick mention OSU two lines later", "annotation_id": "852368", "url": "https://genius.com/852368", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Guess it’s a wrap when your co-defendant make soul music", "vault_lines": ["Guess it's a wrap when your co-defendant make soul music"], "meaning": "Co-defendant= joint suspect in a court case. If MMG were in court he’s saying the case against them wouldn’t go anywhere because of the soul music Meek Mill makes. Even Ricky fucks with soul\n\nIt’s also a play on words here with difference between wrap=rap and soul music, meaning that its a wrap for a suspected criminal if his Co-Defendant starts making soul music= or “singing(snitching)” to the judge/jury, so that he can get a lighter sentence.", "annotation_id": "852226", "url": "https://genius.com/852226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Santeria candles in my sanctuary burn", "vault_lines": ["Santeria candles in my sanctuary burn"], "meaning": "Santería, also known as Regla de Ocha, La Regla Lucumi or Lukumi, is a syncretic religion of West African and Caribbean origin influenced by Roman Catholic Christianity. The use of candles in the Santeria Religion has its roots in the long tradition of Roman Catholic Church candle burning.", "annotation_id": "851784", "url": "https://genius.com/851784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Ricky Madoff everything I deserve", "vault_lines": ["Ricky Madoff everything I deserve"], "meaning": "Rozay, taking a break from his Italian and Gang leader personas, gives himself the alias based on the name of famous Ponzi schemer Bernie Madoff; a pun which Jay-Z made first and Childish Gambino has also used\n\nThis is also a clever wordplay used by Ross both making mention of Bernie Madoff and also stating that he “made off” with the fame, multiple label changes, and starting his on label. He’s stating that he’s a self made millionaire.", "annotation_id": "850364", "url": "https://genius.com/850364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "If Michael Jackson came alive right now He’d ask you to smoke one for him", "vault_lines": ["He'd ask you to smoke one for him"], "meaning": "“To smoke one for him” mean smoke a blunt, joint cig etc. in his honor for a memorial type of deed, for the king of pop as of spillin' alcohol purposely intended for the dead homiez.\n\nWhile MJ may not have smoked cigarettes or marijuana (despite LA authorities finding marijuana in his home shortly after his death), Devo frontman Mark Mothersbaugh claims to have once smoked PCP with the King of Pop:\n\n\n ‘The only time in my life I smoked angel dust was by accident and it was on a double date with Andy Warhol and Michael Jackson,’ laughs Mothersbaugh. ‘We all went to Studio 54 and people were passing drugs all over the place.\n“Michael Jackson had just finished doing the movie The Wiz and still looked like Michael Jackson back then – he had an Afro and he was still black. He passed me a joint and I thought, well OK, we don’t have marijuana in Ohio so I’ll try it.’\n\n Minutes later Mothersbaugh found himself on the dancefloor as pillars of light were swirling around ‘like weedcutters’ knocking people over and cutting them up. He turned to his date in horror, only to hear her say: ‘You didn’t smoke any of that angel dust did you?’\n\n\nThis album also happens to be released on the date after Michael Jackson’s death", "annotation_id": "850352", "url": "https://genius.com/850352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "I’mma earn ’til the last court adjourn", "vault_lines": ["I'mma earn 'til the last court adjourn"], "meaning": "After the end of each case, the judge in court closes by saying: “court is adjourned.” Gunplay is stating that he will have the game on lock, he will keep earnin money til the end of each day, when the LAST case hearing is over.", "annotation_id": "849300", "url": "https://genius.com/849300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "This the circle that’ll murk you, blackout, short circuit", "vault_lines": ["This the circle that'll murk you, blackout, short circuit"], "meaning": "“Circle” refers back to his “round table” reference, around which he and his team MMG sit.\n\nHe’s saying that his team MMG will destroy other teams brutally and easily. If you break up the path of a circuit at any part, you short circuit the whole thing. If one member is taken out of MMG, the whole team blacks out. Ross claims he’ll shoot you, Wale will murk you on a track and well, Meek Mill will take your Rihanna. Just ask these two", "annotation_id": "848046", "url": "https://genius.com/848046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "I’m a billion in five Well a billion cause the limit is the sky and I live on cloud nine", "vault_lines": ["Well a billion cause the limit is the sky and I live on cloud nine"], "meaning": "If “a billion in five” is, as it appears, a poetic way of saying “one in five billion”, then there’s another Kendrick Lamar running around somewhere – the world’s population is currently over seven billion\n\n\n\nAlternately, Kendrick could be talking about making a billion dollars in five years. Making a billion dollars as a rapper might appear impossible to most people, especially in such short time, and that’s why he says “Well, the limit is the sky and I live in cloud nine”", "annotation_id": "847600", "url": "https://genius.com/847600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "At least it do with churches,", "vault_lines": ["At least it do with churches,"], "meaning": "Churches, despite being concerned with spiritual matters, often make congregants donate up to 10% of their worldly earnings, to say nothing of the rise of prosperity gospel, which claims that donating to churches will directly increase one’s wealth", "annotation_id": "847585", "url": "https://genius.com/847585", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Jealousy’s for the weak, you ain’t happy I made it I be feeling like brother Malcolm just out of the Nation", "vault_lines": ["Jealousy's for the weak, you ain't happy I made it", "I be feeling like brother Malcolm just out of the Nation"], "meaning": "If you’re not happy Wale’s successful, you’re jealous and weak\n\nAfter Malcolm X, formerly the group’s most notable minister, was forced out of the Nation of Islam, he and his followers were met with violent resistance and eventual assassination by remaining Nation members.  Manning Marable’s superb biography of Malcolm covers this split in depth", "annotation_id": "847510", "url": "https://genius.com/847510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "I’m at the round table, where your seat at? Where your plate, where your lobster, where your sea bass?", "vault_lines": ["I'm at the round table, where your seat at?", "Where your plate, where your lobster, where your sea bass?"], "meaning": "Or perhaps more to the point, where your crab meats?\n\nThe Round Table was King Arthur’s famed table in the Arthurian legend, around which he and his Knights congregated. Everyone who sat there was known as “great” and legendary, so Gunplay is tauntingly saying that he’s way above you.", "annotation_id": "847026", "url": "https://genius.com/847026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Probably talkin’ bout us, we the only thing to talk about", "vault_lines": ["Probably talkin' bout us, we the only thing to talk about"], "meaning": "Rephrasing what Lil Wayne says in “Swagga Like Us”, which A$AP Rocky also re-phrases in “Palace”.", "annotation_id": "846640", "url": "https://genius.com/846640", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "I know that section eight wanna discontinue my Moms When they heard that Ohio State gave me 30 racks in July", "vault_lines": ["I know that section eight wanna discontinue my Moms", "When they heard that Ohio State gave me 30 racks in July"], "meaning": "His mom apparently still lives in the hood and the landlords find out her son is making $30,000 off one show they want to kick her out the projects because they feel as if she doesnt need low income housing anymore\n\nAlso note that the use of “prior” in the previous line is not accidental.  Ohio State quarterback Terrelle Pryor got in trouble for receiving improper benefits from boosters of the school’s football team", "annotation_id": "846467", "url": "https://genius.com/846467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "They gon’ blitz us but ain’t no way that they gon’ hit us", "vault_lines": ["They gon' blitz us but ain't no way that they gon' hit us"], "meaning": "In football when a team blitzes it means a linebacker is behind the line waiting to lunge at the quarterback quick and easy but there’s no way they’ll get to Wale because you cant hit a quarterback in a scrimmage anyway", "annotation_id": "846415", "url": "https://genius.com/846415", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Cross so heavy crack the tabernacle", "vault_lines": ["Cross so heavy crack the tabernacle"], "meaning": "Referencing his “iced out cross” chain which, as he says, is heavy enough to break the tabernacle, a portable dwelling place for a divine presence.", "annotation_id": "846389", "url": "https://genius.com/846389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "Think you’re Dee Brown, jump if you want", "vault_lines": ["Think you're Dee Brown, jump if you want"], "meaning": "Dee Brown is a former NBA player known for winning the 1992 Dunk Contest with a no look dunk\n\n\n\nThe competition thinks they’re good enough to pull off something like Dee Brown, so he’s inviting them to go for it so he can see them “[come] up short” as stated previously. .", "annotation_id": "846380", "url": "https://genius.com/846380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "The square root of a kilo is me nigga The square root of a kilo is me nigga Do the math, I’m a motherfucking G nigga", "vault_lines": ["Do the math, I'm a motherfucking G nigga"], "meaning": "According to Rozay:\n\n1 kilo = 1 thousand = 1 Grand\n\nSince 1x1=1, the square root of ONE kilo = ONE G.\n\nThe boss didn’t do great in school because the real square root of a kilo is around 31-32 grams.  Good thing his boy Drizzy is good with numbers…\n\nIt also could mean he is at the root of the drug game.", "annotation_id": "846080", "url": "https://genius.com/846080", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "There’s enemies, envy, with green my niggas -- lawnmower", "vault_lines": ["There's enemies, envy, with green my niggas -- lawnmower"], "meaning": "Green is often associated with envy. The envy (green) grows like grass but Wale got niggas that cut that out with a “lawnmower.”", "annotation_id": "846034", "url": "https://genius.com/846034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "My clothes different like quarterbacks at a closed scrimmage", "vault_lines": ["My clothes different like quarterbacks at a closed scrimmage"], "meaning": "Quarterbacks generally wear red jerseys, or ‘redshirt’, so that they aren’t hit at practice. Wale stands out due to the clothes he wears.", "annotation_id": "846029", "url": "https://genius.com/846029", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "May the wind be at your back May the bad be in your past", "vault_lines": ["May the wind be at your back", "May the bad be in your past"], "meaning": "Wale is saying he hopes things come easy for you, and that nothing bad happens to you in your future. A play on a classic old Irish blessing. Wale likely, er, “was inspired by” Drake’s recent use of a similar idea.\n\nThis quote inspired one user enough to get a tattoo of it:", "annotation_id": "846019", "url": "https://genius.com/846019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "I’m out my cabeza", "vault_lines": ["I'm out my cabeza"], "meaning": "‘Cabeza’ means head in Spanish. He means that his head isn’t large enough for the stuff going on inside it- and “I’m out of my head” means I’m going crazy", "annotation_id": "846010", "url": "https://genius.com/846010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "line": "You niggas Spud Webb, coming up short", "vault_lines": ["You niggas Spud Webb, coming up short"], "meaning": "Ross' competition can’t get on his level. They’re “coming up short” like legendary basketball star Spud Webb’s height, 5'7\" to be exact. He must have forgotten that Spud Webb won the 1986 Slam Dunk Contest.\n\n\n\nIncidentally, another rapper previously used almost this exact line, not the only instance of theft on this song.", "annotation_id": "846002", "url": "https://genius.com/846002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Power Circle", "status": "done", "targets": 45, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-power-circle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Power Circle", "genius_id": 77972, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Maybach with the drapes like an apartment in it", "vault_lines": ["Maybach with the drapes like an apartment in it"], "meaning": "His Maybach has curtains that look like drapes.\n\n\n\nPossibly a reference to Meek Mill’s Maybach Curtains, a track on which Ross is featured.", "annotation_id": "30561660", "url": "https://genius.com/30561660", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
