{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "There’s not a better MC than Rick motherfuckin’ Ross", "vault_lines": ["There's not a better MC than Rick motherfuckin' Ross"], "meaning": "This is a subtle reference to Chris Rock being a liar", "annotation_id": "26516885", "url": "https://genius.com/26516885", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "You don’t lie after you say Lord as my witness Did you ever hear OJ say “Lord as my witness?” No, he ain’t go that far, said “I didn’t do it” He hired Johnnie Cochran but he ain’t never say ‘Lord as my witness.’”", "vault_lines": ["No, he ain't go that far, said \"I didn't do it\"", "He hired Johnnie Cochran but he ain't never say 'Lord as my witness.'\""], "meaning": "The 1994 murder trial of OJ Simpson was highly publicised, controversial and divisive amongst the public. Simpson was arrested and charged with the murder of his ex-wife Nicole Brown Simpson and her friend Ron Goldman, but was found not guilty and acquitted in the case of The People of the State of California vs. Orenthal James Simpson. Simpson was represented by a group of lawyers known as “The Dream Team”, which was initially led by Robert Shapiro and subsequently directed by Johnnie Cochran. Cochran was well known for his skill in the courtroom and his prominence as an early advocate for victims of police brutality. Cochran represented a number of celebrities in their numerous trials, including, but not limited to, Diddy, Michael Jackson, Tupac Shakur, Stanley Tookie Williams, Todd Bridges, Jim Brown, Snoop Dogg, Marion Jones and Riddick Bowe. Simpson’s innocence is still a divisive subject amongst the public, with some believing he was guilty and others claiming he was innocent.", "annotation_id": "16898145", "url": "https://genius.com/16898145", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Pot to piss in, not a ribbon, never forgot a Christmas Father figure not around, that’s such a major difference I would play with all my homies’ gifts I understood I didn’t wanna trip", "vault_lines": ["Pot to piss in, not a ribbon, never forgot a Christmas", "Father figure not around, that's such a major difference", "I would play with all my homies' gifts", "I understood I didn't wanna trip"], "meaning": "Rick Ross grew up in extreme poverty with no father. Due to this, his mother struggled to provide for their family on her own and Christmas was just another day for them since she couldnt afford to buy gifts for her kids. At a young age, Ross learned to understand this and accepted that his mother was doing all she could to try and give him a good childhood and Christmas was just something they’d have to live without. As a consolation, Rozay’s friends would feel sorry for him and let him play with their toys on Christmas so he didnt feel entirely left out.", "annotation_id": "16898097", "url": "https://genius.com/16898097", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Amun-Ra sun god combined in one, most prolific", "vault_lines": ["Amun-Ra sun god combined in one, most prolific"], "meaning": "Amun is an Egyptian deity who is known as the king of the Gods. Ra is the Egyptian creator god and god of the sun. According to The Metropolitan Museum of Art:\n\nAs a creator god, Amun is most often identified as Amun-Re (in the typical Egyptian blending of deities, Amun is combined with the main solar deity, Re).\n\n\n\nAligning his commercial success with the gods, Nas asserts his place as one of the most accomplished rappers of all time. In addition to recreating himself as King Tut for the cover of his 2001 album, I Can Nas has expressed his interest in Egypt on previous songs such as ‘Black Zombie’:\n\nWords like God is Greek or Latin\nSo if you study Egypt, you’ll see the truth written by the masters", "annotation_id": "14686854", "url": "https://genius.com/14686854", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "The half moon identifies, the son of God, son of man", "vault_lines": ["The half moon identifies, the son of God, son of man"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nThe half moon and star with a 7 is the symbol for 5% Nation. The moon is a bit hard to see behind the 7 but its there.", "annotation_id": "11524518", "url": "https://genius.com/11524518", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "[Verse 3: Nas]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the 6th time that Rick Ross & Nas have collaborated on each other’s song. The previous 5 being:\n\n\nUsual Suspects\nIt’s a Tower Heist\nTriple Beam Dreams\nAccident Murderers\nOne of Us", "annotation_id": "12934227", "url": "https://genius.com/12934227", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Name ringin’ like DJ Clue on a Friday night", "vault_lines": ["Name ringin' like DJ Clue on a Friday night"], "meaning": "A reference to DJ Clue’s old Friday Night sets that were very popular back in the late 90s/early 2000s.\n\nFabolous and DJ Clue also released a mixtape a few years ago revisiting and paying homage to those sets called “Friday Night Freestyles”", "annotation_id": "11636455", "url": "https://genius.com/11636455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Nation of Islam, they say I might have a few ties", "vault_lines": ["Nation of Islam, they say I might have a few ties"], "meaning": "Very clever line from Young Renzel. Ross has never been one to shy away from having religious undertones in his music, and on this line is letting the listeners know that he has a “ties” with the NOI.\n\n\n\n(Here is Ross with Minister Farrakhan)\n\nAlso, it is play on words as members of the NOI are known to dress in all black with bowties. Him saying he “might have a few ties” could mean that he has a few NOI members at his disposal\n\n\n\nAlso Rick Ross talks about buying real estate in Dubai in the previous line, Dubai is a muslim country so its a play on words when he says “Nation of Islam” and also when he says “might have a few ties” he could be referring the the colleagues that he has in Dubai who he is doing real estate with", "annotation_id": "11636431", "url": "https://genius.com/11636431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Son of Sam", "vault_lines": ["The half moon identifies, the son of God, son of man"], "meaning": "David Richard Berkowitz, also known as the “Son of Sam”, was a serial killer.  He killed 6 people in New York between 1976 and 1977. Sam was Berkowitz' neighbor’s name. In a letter to the police, he described how Sam commanded him to “Go out and kill”. Sam had a demonic dog which Berkowitz claimed needed the blood of pretty young girls.", "annotation_id": "11573291", "url": "https://genius.com/11573291", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Ninth album, Ice Cube, nigga, kill at will", "vault_lines": ["Ninth album, Ice Cube, nigga, kill at will"], "meaning": "Rather You Than Me is the 9th ablum of Rick Ross. He makes a reference to Ice Cube’s Kill At Will EP released on December 18, 1990.", "annotation_id": "11571207", "url": "https://genius.com/11571207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Panama watches, conquer the nonsense, conquerin’ lion", "vault_lines": ["Panama watches, conquer the nonsense, conquerin' lion"], "meaning": "The conquering lion also known as “the Lion of Judah” is a term used to refer the symbol of the Hebrew tribe of Judah, who are the descendants of Judah, the fourth son of Jacob, i.e Israel.\n\nThe lion  was also used to refer to Emperor Haile Selassie of Ethiopia.\n\nThe Lion of Judah also refers to Jesus in as evident in the book of Revelations,  5:5.\n\nThere is both metaphorical and literal interpretations to this.\n\nLiterally Nas refers himself to one that is a winner all day, one who conquers all hate, all nonsense.\n\nMetaphorically, Nas alludes to his roots as Israelite. Remember that in his Album, God’s Son, he says in “Revolutionary Warfare”\n\n We the lost children of Israel in this western world region\".", "annotation_id": "11538490", "url": "https://genius.com/11538490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Crackers wanna kill me for the same thing", "vault_lines": ["Crackers wanna kill me for the same thing"], "meaning": "Ross alludes that his message in his music has the same people who killed Fred Hampton out to do the same to him.", "annotation_id": "11527085", "url": "https://genius.com/11527085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Powers That Be", "line": "Fred Hampton was an angel, may his name ring", "vault_lines": ["Fred Hampton was an angel, may his name ring"], "meaning": "Fred Hampton, was an American activist and revolutionary, chairman of the Illinois chapter of the Black Panther Party (BPP), and deputy chairman of the national BPP.\n\n\n\nRoss shows love and affection for many of our black heroes who helped revolutionize and strengthen the African-American community throughout the album and this is a great person to recognize as a true ANGEL. RIP Mr. Hampton.", "annotation_id": "11527074", "url": "https://genius.com/11527074", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
