{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "I never been in love until I heard a beat", "vault_lines": ["I never been in love until I heard a beat"], "meaning": "His first love is Hip Hop.\n\nAccording to a Rolling Stone interview, when Ross was in grade school, he learned how to rap by memorizing Rakim’s lyrics on Paid in Full\n\n\n\nHe makes a reference to the duo in “10 Jesus Pieces”:\n\nTen chains on Eric B with mob ties/Rakim flows coming from the far side", "annotation_id": "2024104", "url": "https://genius.com/2024104", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
