{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "I was gifted at math, always counted the fastest", "vault_lines": ["I was gifted at math, always counted the fastest"], "meaning": "Gifted at counting money perhaps – Ross admits to sucking at math in a Rolling Stone interview:\n\n “I got through high school on my popularity and shit,” Ross says. “But my grades was never good. I was never good at math.”\n\nThe Boss does know his square roots well however…", "annotation_id": "1305576", "url": "https://genius.com/1305576", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "Went and bought a new crib, week of Wale release", "vault_lines": ["Went and bought a new crib, week of Wale release"], "meaning": "And it was probably a good-sized one.  Wale’s Ambition album, released in November 2011, was the number two album in the country the week of its release, trailing only Justin Bieber’s Christmas record", "annotation_id": "957968", "url": "https://genius.com/957968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "Got my seats on the wood, playas givin’ me dap", "vault_lines": ["Got my seats on the wood, playas givin' me dap"], "meaning": "This line continues Ross' seemingly endless string of references to his courtside NBA seats on this album. He references it so consistently because it happens so often: http://www.worldstarhiphop.com/videos/video.php?v=wshhsq30503U37yo46sG", "annotation_id": "957965", "url": "https://genius.com/957965", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "I made a few mils, ain’t mentionin’ Meek", "vault_lines": ["I made a few mils, ain't mentionin' Meek"], "meaning": "Ross is talking (again) about his mil[lion]s [of dollars], and not about his MMG comrade Meek Mill\n\n\n\nCould also mean he’s made millions of dollars, and he’s not even counting the money that Meek has made (because Meek is signed to him, he surely sees some of the money that Meek makes).", "annotation_id": "942547", "url": "https://genius.com/942547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "She on that Alexander Wang", "vault_lines": ["She on that Alexander Wang"], "meaning": "Not only is Rozay using the name of famous fashion designer, Alexander Wang to describe his and her sexual intimacy, he’s probably suggesting she’s rocking the same designer’s merchandise, too. He’s rich enough to buy it for her.", "annotation_id": "934913", "url": "https://genius.com/934913", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
