{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "Walkin’ on Jewish marble, hand painted the ceilin’ Happy Hanukkah nigga, it’s a wonderful feelin’", "vault_lines": ["Walkin' on Jewish marble, hand painted the ceilin'"], "meaning": "So basically, his house resembles the Sistine Chapel.\n\n\n\nAlso a play on words with “Jewish marble,” since Hanukkah is a Jewish holiday.\n\nHand painted to the ceiling also refers to the act of praying with hands clasped. They literally point to the ceiling.", "annotation_id": "934359", "url": "https://genius.com/934359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Presidential", "line": "I was skippin’ them classes, but I got me a master", "vault_lines": ["I was skippin' them classes, but I got me a master"], "meaning": "Rick Ross attended Albany State University on a football scholarship, but dropped out. He many not have his master’s degree, but he’s mastered the music industry and became a successful rapper and entrepreneur", "annotation_id": "933965", "url": "https://genius.com/933965", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
