{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "Look, night time with my Locs on", "vault_lines": ["Look, night time with my Locs on"], "meaning": "“During the 1970s & 80s, Locs sunglasses were very popular among young people and defined the L.A. look. Influenced by the Hispanic culture in Los Angeles and derive from the Spanish word ‘loco’ (crazy), they were originally worn by cholo’s and later became popular with all gangsters in the L.A. area.” source: https://www.godfathershades.com/pages/locs%C2%AE", "annotation_id": "20007963", "url": "https://genius.com/20007963", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "I’m ridin dirty, my cup leaning, Pimp C inspired my paint", "vault_lines": ["I'm ridin dirty, my cup leaning, Pimp C inspired my paint"], "meaning": "Ridin' dirty is the stereotyping African-Americans and racial profiling by police, usually resulting in police brutality. Typically, law enforcement would insinuate because of the driver’s skin color that they are concealing either a weapon, drugs or some sort of contraband. The term ridin' dirty was most famously coined by Houston rapper Chamillionaire with his 2006 hit single Ridin'.\n\nPimp C, alongside Bun B, was one of the members of legendary Port Arthur, Texas duo Underground Kingz or UGK. Pimp C was one of the individuals who popularized the recreational drug purple drank, which is the combination of promethazine/codeine, usually mixed with Sprite and or other beverages. Unfortunately the iconic rapper passed away on December 5, 2007 in West Hollywood, CA due to the drug combined with a sleeping disorder. Ross is saying that the drug Pimp C popularized inspired him to get the paint job he has on his car.", "annotation_id": "12447510", "url": "https://genius.com/12447510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "I’m strapped down Colin Powell, I hold it down, with these 40 rounds", "vault_lines": ["Colin Powell, I hold it down, with these 40 rounds"], "meaning": "Colin Powell was the U.S. Secretary of State during Bush’s first term and is a retired 4 star general which means he had to be “strapped up” with some high powered rifles whenever he went to war", "annotation_id": "2638220", "url": "https://genius.com/2638220", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "Back to the wall, I was so stoned", "vault_lines": ["Back to the wall, I was so stoned"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n\n\nHad his back to the wall, wall made of stone.\nHad his back to the wall on the street smoking that good and as a result he’s stoned", "annotation_id": "2421037", "url": "https://genius.com/2421037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "Self-made nigga, I was solo", "vault_lines": ["Self-made nigga, I was solo"], "meaning": "He chased his dream by himself, he never had no hand out! It also refers to the fact that he is an independent artist and not signed to a major label since leaving Epic in 2010.\n\nThe line was also retweeted by West Coast MC Ab-Soul\nhttps://twitter.com/abdashsoul/status/209339308295995394", "annotation_id": "1143824", "url": "https://genius.com/1143824", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "I had AR’s, fo-fo’s Alpinas on low pros", "vault_lines": ["I had AR's, fo-fo's Alpinas on low pros"], "meaning": "He had:\n\n\nAn AR-15 gun\nA .44 Magnum gun\nAlpines – those are rims he puts low profile tires on.", "annotation_id": "868597", "url": "https://genius.com/868597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "Black diamonds all on my chain, violence comes with this fame", "vault_lines": ["Black diamonds all on my chain, violence comes with this fame"], "meaning": "Traditional yet ill derived, blood diamonds often come to America and tarnish something that should be immaculate.\nHere it is spoken as if black diamonds is an double entendre to symbolize black on black crime to covet something so organic yet doesn’t regard the worth as a black diamond as a human life but the pinnacle of fame, from a rapper who knows his roots.", "annotation_id": "830217", "url": "https://genius.com/830217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Proud of That", "line": "Try to keep your head above water, they wanna see a nigga capsized", "vault_lines": ["Try to keep your head above water, they wanna see a nigga capsized"], "meaning": "Being above water is essentially make it to survive be amongst all humanities.\nHowever with success envy follows, and not only does his enemies want bad for him but to capsize/drown from success, progress, and ultimately life.", "annotation_id": "830203", "url": "https://genius.com/830203", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
