{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "We The Best Music! Another one DJ Khaled!", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "These are all DJ Khaled’s signature ad-libs. He shouts out his label, We the Best Music, which he founded in 2008.\n\n“Another One” is his way of announcing that he has another smash hit on his hands. “DJ Khaled!” is used on most of his tracks since the early 2000s.", "annotation_id": "12218936", "url": "https://genius.com/12218936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "Went from a robber to the upper upper echelon", "vault_lines": ["Went from a robber to the upper upper echelon"], "meaning": "In a story of “rags to riches,” Gucci has come a long way. Growing up in the rough neighbourhood of Zone 6, Atlanta, Gucci was influenced by the crime-ridden community and turned to stealing at a young age. In a December 2016 interview with Hot 97, Gucci explained how confessing to robbing $50,000 on his song “Lawnmower Man” made him the talk of the town, which gave him a boost at the very beginning of his career, and was the main reason he took to rapping seriously, saying:\n\nThe hype from that just made me like, ‘I’m finna take this serious.’ Everybody saying I’m the truth.\n\n On “Lawnmower Man” he raps:\n\nHit a lick for ‘bout fifty stacks\nNiggas trippin’, talkin' ‘bout Gucci bring the money back\n\nToday, Gucci is part of the upper echelon. In military terms, “upper echelon” refers to the tier of top ranking officials. Gucci is referring to himself as a member of the top of the top in society; an exclusive level very difficult to reach.\n\nThe term “upper echelon” has been adopted by successful rappers like Future in “Diamonds Dancing,” and as the title of Travis Scott’s song, “Upper Echelon.”", "annotation_id": "12214771", "url": "https://genius.com/12214771", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "It’s the Dapper Don going on a trapathon", "vault_lines": ["It's the Dapper Don going on a trapathon"], "meaning": "John Gotti, or the “Dapper Don,” was the last great NYC Italian mob boss. Gotti was head of the Gambino Crime family and known for being untouchable by the law and having expensive clothing. Gotti was frequently shown wearing designer suits on the news.\n\nFuture also has referred to himself as Gotti\n\n\n\nTrap-A-Thon is the title of Gucci Mane’s third album. The title is a play on the term “trapping,” which refers to dealing drugs. With the ending “thon” it seems like a drug dealing competition of great length.", "annotation_id": "12213546", "url": "https://genius.com/12213546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "I rarely post the money, I never pose with guns", "vault_lines": ["I rarely post the money, I never pose with guns"], "meaning": "La Flare rarely shows off his wealth on social media, but after being arrested for the illegal possession of firearms late 2013, then charged and sentenced to 39 months in federal prison in 2014, Gucci is too smart to be seen with any guns especially that he is on parole, and would go back to prison if he was.", "annotation_id": "12212165", "url": "https://genius.com/12212165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "Blowjobs in the SLR’s", "vault_lines": ["Blowjobs in the SLR's"], "meaning": "Mercedes-Benz SLR McLaren is a grand tourer car developed by high-end manufacturers, Mercedes and McLaren that can cost an upwards of $300,000.", "annotation_id": "12210376", "url": "https://genius.com/12210376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "Just to get here, I had to rob a couple Mexicans", "vault_lines": ["Just to get here, I had to rob a couple Mexicans"], "meaning": "Gucci is refering to robbing drugs. Most illegal drugs in the United States come from Mexico. A majority of the time the people who supply local drug dealers are called the “Plug” & are part of a bigger drug dealing chain.\nProduct is made> Smuggled across> given to several distributors (aka the plug)> the “Plug” distributes to small time dealers.\nThey tend to be Mexican most of the time due to family ties & strong brotherly bonds with already existing Cartel members which are obviously Mexican.\nGucci is essentially robbing the plug which means double the product..which means double the money.\nAnyone who listens to a lot of rap music is familiar with the phrase “Rob the plug”", "annotation_id": "12209466", "url": "https://genius.com/12209466", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "I’ma go get that Wraith Jumping out with your bae I just wanna get this paper I’ma do, I’ma do, I’ma do what it takes I’ma go get that cake, I’ma go pull a caper I’ma do, I’ma do, I’ma do what it takes I’ma go get that cake, I’ma go pull a caper I’ma go, I’ma go, I’ma go get that Wraith Jumping out with your bae I just wanna get this paper", "vault_lines": ["I'ma go get that cake, I'ma go pull a caper", "I'ma go, I'ma go, I'ma go get that Wraith"], "meaning": "To “pull a caper” is slang for committing a robbery. Throughout the hook, Kodak talks about his willingness to do anything to get his money up and live lavishly.", "annotation_id": "12209144", "url": "https://genius.com/12209144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "line": "But free Kodak Black, bring Lil’ Kodak back (Kodak) ’Cause they don’t wanna see you move into their cul-de-sac", "vault_lines": ["But free Kodak Black, bring Lil' Kodak back (Kodak)", "'Cause they don't wanna see you move into their cul-de-sac"], "meaning": "Kodak Black has been incarcerated on multiple occasions, having been released from a 90-day stint about two weeks before this song’s release. Gucci is another rapper who has been incarcerated multiple time over the course of his career.\n\nGucci references the arbitrary “they” that has become one of DJ Khaled’s trademarks. Here, Gucci uses “they” to refer to the social establishment and how they don’t want someone like Kodak overcome the economic inequality that he was born into and enter their world and would rather see him in prison. Kodak echoes a similar sentiment on his song “Tunnel Vision.”", "annotation_id": "12208296", "url": "https://genius.com/12208296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pull a Caper", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-khaled-pull-a-caper-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pull a Caper", "genius_id": 3117603, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Pullin on Her Hair", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Marques-houston-pullin-on-her-hair-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pullin on Her Hair", "genius_id": 1069854, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Purple Fentanyl", "line": "David Beckham cologne, carbone for rigatoni", "vault_lines": ["David Beckham cologne, carbone for rigatoni"], "meaning": "In the line Rozay combines two symbols of luxury lifestyle: personal style and high-end dining.\n\nDavid Beckham cologne references Beckham’s fragrance brand, representing grooming, fashion, and a polished image. Carbone refers to the famous New York Italian-American restaurant known for its celebrity clientele and upscale atmosphere, while rigatoni points to one of the restaurant’s signature dishes.", "annotation_id": "40785402", "url": "https://genius.com/40785402", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Purple Fentanyl", "line": "Eddie Murphy’s my homie", "vault_lines": ["My name set in the stone, Eddie Murphy's my homie"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has a longtime connection with Hollywood icon Eddie Murphy. Their connection goes beyond friendship. Ross' massive Georgia estate, known as “The Promise Land,” served as one of the main filming locations for Coming 2 America (2021), starring Murphy in the lead role.\n\nRoss also made a brief appearance in the film. His appearance added another layer to the connection between the rap icon and one of cinema’s most legendary comedic actors.", "annotation_id": "40785338", "url": "https://genius.com/40785338", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Purple Fentanyl", "line": "The Louis, the Gucci, the Prada, Lil Uzi", "vault_lines": ["The Louis, the Gucci, the Prada, Lil Uzi"], "meaning": "In this line, the artist name-drops three major luxury fashion houses Louis Vuitton, Gucci, and Prada. Before referencing Lil Uzi Vert, whose image has become closely tied to high fashion and bold style choices.\n\nLil Uzi is known for constantly switching up his looks, wearing designer pieces, and treating fashion as an extension of his artistic identity. The bar connects luxury brands with hip-hop culture, where designer names often represent status, individuality, and self-expression.", "annotation_id": "40785245", "url": "https://genius.com/40785245", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
