{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push Em Over (50 Cent & Lloyd Banks Diss)", "line": "So that brings me right back to the fuckin monkey", "vault_lines": ["So that brings me right back to the fuckin monkey"], "meaning": "After the awkward Lloyd Banks diss, Rick Ross comes back to dissing 50 Cent.", "annotation_id": "1586061", "url": "https://genius.com/1586061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push Em Over (50 Cent & Lloyd Banks Diss)", "line": "Come out the closet and admit it curly admit it Curly! You’re a dick-sucker", "vault_lines": ["Come out the closet and admit it curly admit it Curly!"], "meaning": "More Rick Ross bullshitting. He assumes that 50 Cent is gay. “Come out the closet” is usually a gay reference.", "annotation_id": "1007003", "url": "https://genius.com/1007003", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push Em Over (50 Cent & Lloyd Banks Diss)", "line": "Never measure a man by his money but by his moves.... monkey", "vault_lines": ["Never measure a man by his money but by his moves.... monkey"], "meaning": "The real meaning of this line is to never judge a man based on the money he has but by the way he lives his life.\n\nAlthough one could point out that 50 not only has more money than Ross (odd because Ross talks about having a lot of money) but that 50 has also made a number of successful investments, whereas Ross hasn’t.", "annotation_id": "1006997", "url": "https://genius.com/1006997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push Em Over (50 Cent & Lloyd Banks Diss)", "line": "Its hard to findout your father was your uncle This snitch infested with incest", "vault_lines": ["Its hard to findout your father was your uncle", "This snitch infested with incest"], "meaning": "According to Rick Ross, 50 Cent’s dad was really his uncle. This is known as incest. However Rick Ross is purely bullshitting as 50 doesn’t even know who his dad is. His Mother has passed away so we will never know the answer.", "annotation_id": "1006983", "url": "https://genius.com/1006983", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push Em Over (50 Cent & Lloyd Banks Diss)", "line": "Lloyd “Blanks” I know you wonder why I ain’t saying nothing bout your bitch ass but I could never acknowledge you, you suck your assistants dick on tape and he licked it, you’re a fucking dick-sucking faggot Niggas homo y’all could Google it. Lloyd Banks your career is over In the south we know you used to suckin dick thats why we don’t fuck with you. We don’t even know you", "vault_lines": ["Niggas homo y'all could Google it. Lloyd Banks your career is over"], "meaning": "Lloyd Banks tried to diss Rick Ross however Rick Ross doesn’t even see him as a Rapper. He then claims that Lloyd Banks has a gay sextape where hes sucking his assistants “thing”.", "annotation_id": "1006950", "url": "https://genius.com/1006950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push Em Over (50 Cent & Lloyd Banks Diss)", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-push-em-over-50-cent-and-lloyd-banks-diss-lyrics", "genius_title": "Push Em Over (50 Cent & Lloyd Banks Diss)", "genius_id": 85470, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "The world is yours, hundred million or more Now I run the streets, they all mine", "vault_lines": ["The world is yours, hundred million or more", "Now I run the streets, they all mine"], "meaning": "“The world is yours” is a recurring motto for Tony Montana in the film Scarface. This song’s beat is also based on something from that film.\n\nhttp://youtu.be/Qt3tOfTxrII?t=8s\n\nRoss embraces Tony’s motto here and expresses the belief that he can control all the streets in the drug trade and earn over $100 million.", "annotation_id": "3372364", "url": "https://genius.com/3372364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "You set your sister straight", "vault_lines": ["You duck your momma house, you set your sister straight"], "meaning": "Another common theme in rap – making sure your loved ones & family (in this case, sister) is living comfortably due to your large checks.", "annotation_id": "1441977", "url": "https://genius.com/1441977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "Bananas in our rifles, no cyphers, I’m just the man to know", "vault_lines": ["Bananas in our rifles, no cyphers, I'm just the man to know"], "meaning": "Banana clips are large capacity magazines for automatic weapons, named after bananas because it’s shape resembles a banana.", "annotation_id": "550276", "url": "https://genius.com/550276", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "Nobody used to speak, now e’rybody wave", "vault_lines": ["Nobody used to speak, now e'rybody wave"], "meaning": "A common theme in rap – back in the day when Ross was a nobody, people didn’t talk to him and they didn’t care for him. Now that he made it, they all wave at him and act like they know him.", "annotation_id": "489380", "url": "https://genius.com/489380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "I bought my first block, broke it down and tore the block apart", "vault_lines": ["I bought my first block, broke it down and tore the block apart"], "meaning": "Double entendre with the word “block”.\n\nThe “first block” he bought was a block of cocaine and he “broke it down”, by cutting it up into smaller portions to sell them. Thus, he took control of/ruined neighborhood (the block).", "annotation_id": "489356", "url": "https://genius.com/489356", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
