{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "You gotta push it to the limit you wanna be paid", "vault_lines": ["You gotta push it to the limit you wanna be paid"], "meaning": "Ricky Rozay pushes EVERYTHING to the limit; his money, his coke selling, his music, and the maximum weight without having a heart attack.", "annotation_id": "488210", "url": "https://genius.com/488210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "I know you see me in that Phantom whiter than veneers", "vault_lines": ["I know you see me in that Phantom whiter than veneers"], "meaning": "Ross has a white Rolls Royce Phantom that is white than a veneer, which is a  thin layer of material placed over a tooth usually to make a tooth appear whiter.", "annotation_id": "488201", "url": "https://genius.com/488201", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "Fresh in my white tee,", "vault_lines": ["Fresh in my white tee,"], "meaning": "A reference to the White Tee single by Dem Franchize Boyz.", "annotation_id": "488190", "url": "https://genius.com/488190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "I’m pushin’ it hard, I’m pushin’ it soft If he pushin’ a line, he pushin’ for Ross", "vault_lines": ["I'm pushin' it hard, I'm pushin' it soft", "If he pushin' a line, he pushin' for Ross"], "meaning": "This ain’t nickels and dimes – Rick does it big. Ross sells both types of coke – the hard rock kind, and the soft snortable kind. Notice the wordplay with opposite words – “soft” and “hard”.\n\nIf there’s a cocaine dealer in your hood, chances are he works for Ross.", "annotation_id": "488182", "url": "https://genius.com/488182", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "Workers were barely paid, no water, we barely bathe", "vault_lines": ["Workers were barely paid, no water, we barely bathe"], "meaning": "The jobs aren’t hiring very much anymore – even the ones that do aren’t giving much past minimum wage.\n\nThis affects the entire community – to the point where Ross & his people can barely cleanse themselves everyday. Showering infrequently is common in the ghettos.", "annotation_id": "488167", "url": "https://genius.com/488167", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "On the boat we hid the work in detergent and soap", "vault_lines": ["On the boat we hid the work in detergent and soap"], "meaning": "Ross is alluding to the fact that he uses detergents and soaps to prevent narcotics dogs from detecting cocaine smuggled into the country on boats.\nHe could also be referencing the fact that he uses detergent and soap packaging/shipping as a front for the boat that his crew uses to transport cocaine.\n\n\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: 3. He’s “cleaning up” his dirty operations by appearance. “Green grass on the lawn, messed up house on the inside”", "annotation_id": "458655", "url": "https://genius.com/458655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "I told you never roll on the soul of a soldier You never know that dishwasher May be the beholder", "vault_lines": ["I told you never roll on the soul of a soldier", "You never know that dishwasher may be the beholder"], "meaning": "Ross is sticking with the Scarface theme here, as Tony Montana began as a dishwasher before becoming a powerful drug lord.\n\nRoss reminds us not to mess with the little guy – the minute he gets more powerful than you, you’re screwed.", "annotation_id": "336354", "url": "https://genius.com/336354", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "I paid dues, my moves done made news", "vault_lines": ["I paid dues, my moves done made news"], "meaning": "He’s paid the cost to be the Boss, and he’s done shit so big, it’s made the news. The move Ross is perhaps referencing is his bidding war and multi-million dollar deal with Def Jam Records.", "annotation_id": "336348", "url": "https://genius.com/336348", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "Push it to the limit", "vault_lines": ["Push it to the limit"], "meaning": "Sampling the song “Scarface (Push It To The Limit)” from the Scarface OST, performed by Paul Engemann\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BhsTmiK7Q2M", "annotation_id": "336342", "url": "https://genius.com/336342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "Tryna survive on 95", "vault_lines": ["Tryna survive on 95"], "meaning": "95 refers to I-95, the main highway on the East Coast of the United States.", "annotation_id": "228594", "url": "https://genius.com/228594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "I’m buildin’ a dream, with elevators in it", "vault_lines": ["I'm buildin' a dream, with elevators in it"], "meaning": "Dream in this context actually refers to a home. When people become successful and can afford it they often build the home they’ve always wanted. The Bawse is going to build a multi-story house that dreams are made of, hence the elevator.", "annotation_id": "215978", "url": "https://genius.com/215978", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Push It", "line": "Port of Miami (Uhh), I’m importin’ the candy (Uhh)", "vault_lines": ["Port of Miami (uhh), I'm importin' the candy (uhh)"], "meaning": "With the opening words of his Port of Miami album, Ross give a shout out to… the Port of Miami. Ross is from Miami-Dade County.\n\nCandy, in this context, refers to drugs (particularly cocaine, since that is what the Port of Miami is known for).\n\n\n\nThis line also fits the Scarface theme of the song, as Tony Montana (Scarface) operates out of Miami as a cocaine kingpin in the film. Ross even chose his rap name after a real-life cocaine kingpin, “Freeway” Rick Ross.\n\nThe “uhh’s” are used as onomatopoeic way of showing that Ross is “pushing it” to the limit. That, or Ross is just using it as a way to feel the beat or start a verse (like most rappers do)…", "annotation_id": "193564", "url": "https://genius.com/193564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
