{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rap Song", "line": "Port of Miami, Trilla, Deeper Than Rap", "vault_lines": ["Port of Miami, Trilla, Deeper Than Rap"], "meaning": "Rick Ross debut, second, and third studio album. Port of Miami, originally titled Career Criminal, the album was renamed, in reference to Miami being a major arrival destination for cocaine shipments to America. Trilla, released on March 11, 2008, by Slip-n-Slide Records, Def Jam South Recordings and Poe Boy Entertainment. Production was handled by The Runners, J. R. Rotem, Drumma Boy, DJ Toomp. Deeper than rap, released on April 21, 2009, by his record label Maybach Music Group and Slip-n-Slide Records; distributed by Def Jam Recordings", "annotation_id": "27383768", "url": "https://genius.com/27383768", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rap Song", "line": "Like Akon, we can stack it all up", "vault_lines": ["Like Akon, we can stack it all up"], "meaning": "This is the beginning of a clever wordplay by Ross, which culminates at the next line.\n\n“Like Akon” – A convict\n\nA convict is “a person found guilty of a crime and sentenced by a court” or “a person serving a sentence in prison”(Wikipedia)\n\n“or do you like a juvie” – Juvenile Delinquent\n\nJuvenile delinquents are minors, usually defined as being between the ages of 10 and 18, who have committed some act that violates the law. (criminal.findlaw.com/juvenile-justice/juvenile-delinquents.html)", "annotation_id": "7767949", "url": "https://genius.com/7767949", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rap Song", "line": "Me and you, yo’ momma and yo’ cousin", "vault_lines": ["Me and you, yo' momma and yo' cousin"], "meaning": "Reference to Outkast’s Elevators (Me & You).", "annotation_id": "2618501", "url": "https://genius.com/2618501", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rap Song", "line": "Go shawty, it’s your birthday We gon’ party like it’s your birthday", "vault_lines": ["Go shawty, it's your birthday", "We gon' party like it's your birthday"], "meaning": "A reference to a line from 50 Cent’s famous “In Da Club”", "annotation_id": "159985", "url": "https://genius.com/159985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rap Song", "line": "Wait, hold up, she got a donk", "vault_lines": ["Wait, hold up, she got a donk, she got a donk"], "meaning": "From Soulja Boy’s song ‘She Got A Donk’.‘Donk’ is a shortened version of the popular rap-term ‘badonkadonk’ butt, meaning a butt that is so big and bouncy that its movement has its own onomatopoeia– ‘badonkadonk’.", "annotation_id": "156643", "url": "https://genius.com/156643", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
