{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "Never lose, like Alexander the Great, biatch", "vault_lines": ["Never lose, like Alexander the Great, biatch"], "meaning": "Alexander the Great was the King of Macedonia from 332–323 BC, who by the age of 30 had created one of the largest empires in history, stretching from Greece to northwestern India.\n\nHe is widely considered to be one of history’s greatest and most successful military commanders, and is said to literally have never lost a battle.", "annotation_id": "24201568", "url": "https://genius.com/24201568", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "Niggas throwing subliminals, act like I don’t hear those I could give you 600 bars, but y’all know that y’all fear those", "vault_lines": ["I could give you 600 bars, but y'all know that y'all fear those"], "meaning": "This is a reference to 300 Bars & Runnin', the Games classic diss track towards 50 Cent.\n\nThe Game also has released other songs with this theme  like ‘200 Bars & Runnin’ and threatens to return with 600 Bars, presumably twice as vicious as its predecessor.", "annotation_id": "24201556", "url": "https://genius.com/24201556", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "Taylor Gang nigga, I ain’t Wiz doe But I got that yellow brick road inside my ear lobes", "vault_lines": ["Taylor Gang nigga, I ain't Wiz doe", "But I got that yellow brick road inside my ear lobes"], "meaning": "Wiz Khalifa is a rapper who owns Taylor Gang Records and can be heard saying it in all of his songs. The Game’s real name is Jayceon Taylor, which really makes him Taylor Gang, and he is also a fan of Converse Chuck Taylor sneakers, as is Wiz.\n\nHe then plays of Wiz Khalifa’s name to talk about his gold earrings, likening them to the ‘Yellow brick road’ from The Wizard of Oz, note the connection of ‘Wiz’.", "annotation_id": "24201539", "url": "https://genius.com/24201539", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "But y’all the Verizon man, I’m just gon’ stand behind y’all", "vault_lines": ["But y'all the Verizon man, I'm just gon' stand behind y'all"], "meaning": "This is a reference to popular Verizon Wireless commercials where a team of support engineers would follow the Verizon Man around while he asks “Can you hear me now?”", "annotation_id": "24201524", "url": "https://genius.com/24201524", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "Ivy Blue is beautiful, me saying that’s unusual That’s just the father in me, don’t think I’m trying to be cool with you", "vault_lines": ["Ivy Blue is beautiful, me saying that's unusual", "That's just the father in me, don't think I'm trying to be cool with you"], "meaning": "In these bars Game is squashing his beef with Jay-Z by being the bigger man and even complimenting his daughter, Blue Ivy. She was born just before this song released.\n\n\n\nThe Game also has an extremely close relationship with his daughter who is only 2 years older than Blue Ivy.\nhttps://genius.com/The-game-california-dream-lyrics", "annotation_id": "24201500", "url": "https://genius.com/24201500", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "But fuck who I was dissing cause I never made a mistake", "vault_lines": ["But fuck who I was dissing cause I never made a mistake"], "meaning": "Game would always say that he has no regrets because he can’t go back and change anything\n\nTo say that is to say when he started off his rap/music career he had his moments when he went overboard against certain Artists just to get known and especially at a time when the west coast was not popping\n\nHowever to him he doesn’t feel like he’s ever made a mistake because it got him where he is at today\n\nSome beef stays on wax meaning on records\nAnd some beef spills out on the street", "annotation_id": "23200481", "url": "https://genius.com/23200481", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "But they should have moved that nigga marrying Gloria Govan", "vault_lines": ["But they should have moved that nigga marrying Gloria Govan"], "meaning": "Game is going at Lakers player Matt Barnes.\n\nGame and Barnes were once cool together until Game’s homie Avante Rose began sending Barnes pictures of himself with Barnes' wife Gloria Govan, claiming to have slept with her.\n\n\n\nUnsurprisingly, Game sided with Rose in the ensuing Twitter beef.", "annotation_id": "691632", "url": "https://genius.com/691632", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "Fuck them Air 1's, I’m too attached to these spikes now Louboutins, hard as croutons", "vault_lines": ["Fuck them Air 1's, I'm too attached to these spikes now", "Louboutins, hard as croutons"], "meaning": "Game may still rock Chuck Taylors but he’s swapped his Air Force 1’s\n\n\n\nfor Spikes – those expensive red-soled shoes by French designer Christian Louboutin.\n\n\n\nGame’s a sneaker head and once dropped $15,000 on a pair of Nikes so the Louboutins probably seem like a bargain.", "annotation_id": "690569", "url": "https://genius.com/690569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "It’s that red bottom boss, nigga", "vault_lines": ["It's that red bottom boss, nigga"], "meaning": "Red bottoms are shoes made by French designer Christian Louboutin.\n\nThe shoes feature an iconic red bottom.\n\n\n\nBy claiming to be the “Red Bottom Boss”, Game (and Rozay) are saying that they can provide their women with these shoes – the finest of the fine, the coolest of the cool.", "annotation_id": "690552", "url": "https://genius.com/690552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "If you see tip drilling, King of Diamonds, tell I got like eight stacks", "vault_lines": ["If you see tip drilling, King of Diamonds, tell I got like eight stacks"], "meaning": "King of Diamonds is a popular strip club in Miami, Florida. The Game really says “tip drilling” in the song instead of “Tip trilling”. If The Game knew any tip drills (girls with a thick body but not so pretty face) in the strip club that night; he would make sure he was there with at least $8,000.", "annotation_id": "684270", "url": "https://genius.com/684270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "Y’all the Verizon man, I’m just gon’ stand behind y’all", "vault_lines": ["Y'all the Verizon man, I'm just gon' stand behind y'all"], "meaning": "Many of Verizon’s ads used to end with a huge crowd of people standing behind the Verizon guy\n\nCleverly, Game follows up his nod to Jay-Z by referencing Roc affiliates – first Rihanna and here Jay’s newest signee, Jay Electronica.", "annotation_id": "683354", "url": "https://genius.com/683354", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "While I get my Duke on, and crossover like Duhon", "vault_lines": ["While I get my Duke on, and crossover like Duhon"], "meaning": "Chris Duhon an ex Duke Alum was the point guard for the Blue Devils from 2000 to 2004.", "annotation_id": "683349", "url": "https://genius.com/683349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "They yellow like Luke on the Lakers, he was traded", "vault_lines": ["They yellow like Luke on the Lakers, he was traded"], "meaning": "Refers to Luke Walton, the former Los Angeles Laker who was traded to the Cleveland Cavaliers after playing his entire career wearing the purple and gold.", "annotation_id": "683347", "url": "https://genius.com/683347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Bottom Boss", "line": "Playing ice hockey, feeling like Gretzky Los Angeles King, and I’m who my city gon’ cheer for", "vault_lines": ["Playing ice hockey, feeling like Gretzky", "Los Angeles King, and I'm who my city gon' cheer for"], "meaning": "Wayne Gretzky is one of the greatest (if not the greatest) hockey players of all time. He played for the Los Angeles Kings for 6 years after being traded from the Edmonton Oilers in a very emotional manner.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o4nE58aXXjU\n\nHis achievements in the NHL are unrivaled.\n\nThe Game is bragging about his jewelry, or “ice” as it is referred to in slang terms. Game is also from the Los Angeles area, and is a known Los Angeles Kings fan.", "annotation_id": "683323", "url": "https://genius.com/683323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
