{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Red Horns", "line": "Eating lemon pepper wings like it’s really lobster", "vault_lines": ["Eating lemon pepper wings like it’s really lobster"], "meaning": "Rick Ross and lemon pepper wings have a long line of history. As of 2018, he owns roughly 25 Wingstop franchises, to which his endorsement is heavily present.\n\nTo express his love for these wings, he’s acknowledged them in countless bars across his discography such as “King of Diamonds” and “Thug Cry.” But one notable song, which happens to speak on the Devil like Red Horns, is “The Devil is a Lie.”\n\nOn the track, he raps:\n\nWingstop, fat boy need a 10 piece", "annotation_id": "21346454", "url": "https://genius.com/21346454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
