{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Revory (Wraith)", "line": "Madame sleepin’ on Egyptian cotton", "vault_lines": ["Madame sleepin' on Egyptian cotton"], "meaning": "The suspected use of homophone in this line gives it two possible meanings, depending on the intended lyric.\n\n\n“Madame sleepin' on Egyptian cotton”\n“Mad I’m sleepin' on Egyptian cotton”\n\n\n\nIn this first interpretation, Ross is referring to a fine mistress of his who is sleeping on his Egyptian-cotton bed sheets (presumably after engaging in some salacious behavior).\n\nThe second interpretation more strongly ties to the previous line, “I’m hearin' how these niggas plottin.” Ross is aware that these devious haters are filled with jealousy and anger over his success (and ability to afford luxurious linens), and so he stays alert to their attempts to diminish him.", "annotation_id": "6317349", "url": "https://genius.com/6317349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
