{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Nigga Lifestyle", "line": "Rap music on the charts like it’s rock and roll", "vault_lines": ["Rap music on the charts like it's rock and roll"], "meaning": "Nielsen Music’s 2018 year-end report stated that for the first time in history, Hip-Hop was the most popular genre in the US.\n\nNumbers-wise, R&B/hip hop totaled a figure of 24.5% of all music consumption in the US – beating Rock to the number one spot, by almost 5%.\n\nIn 2019, rap continues to dominate the charts and and rap artists are breaking records previously held by non-hip-hop artists, such as Drake surpassing The Beatles' record for the second-most Billboard Hot 100 Top 10s, this past June.", "annotation_id": "17796051", "url": "https://genius.com/17796051", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Nigga Lifestyle", "line": "Rich nigga, dirty game, I’m talkin’ Nick Saban", "vault_lines": ["Rich nigga, dirty game, I'm talkin' Nick Saban"], "meaning": "Nick Saban is Head Coach for the NCAA’s University of Alabama Crimson Tide. Saban is the highest paid coach in College Football. Saban is worth an estimated $30-$45 million. Ross is worth an estimated $35 million. NCAA sports are often looked at as a dirty game due to student athletes not being compensated financially whereas coaches are.", "annotation_id": "17783014", "url": "https://genius.com/17783014", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Nigga Lifestyle", "line": "I can’t name a fake nigga that was not exposed How y’all niggas so surprised that Tekashi told? Ain’t a real street nigga ’less you got a code", "vault_lines": ["I can't name a fake nigga that was not exposed", "How y'all niggas so surprised that Tekashi told?", "Ain't a real street nigga 'less you got a code"], "meaning": "Nipsey is alluding to incarcerated New York rapper Tekashi 6ix9ine, who was arrested in November 2018 on nine federal charges, including racketeering, firearms offenses, and narcotics trafficking.\n\n\n\nIn January 2019, Tekashi took a plea deal which required him to cooperate with authorities. Since two of his co-defendants, Anthony “Harv” Ellison and Aljermiah “Nuke” Mack, plead not guilty, he is required to testify against them in court.\n\nWell before the rapper’s arrest, Nipsey expressed his feelings about 6ix9ine in a March 2019 interview with Big Boy’s Neighborhood, saying:\n\nYou can’t even really get on Tekashi, you gotta demand more from the public. You got people reacting to how the public reacting to Tekashi disrespecting them. The public should not even react to clown shit. The public should follow the real niggas, if the real niggas ain’t reactin' so y'all don’t react. Put the dude on goofy time and just let him sit over here doing what he doing till that shit expire, cause it always gonna self-destruct, clearly.\n\nNip is confused as to why people would be surprised at Tekashi bending his knee to the law, considering his criminal past.\n\nRick Ross was also one of the first to diss 6ix9ine after his incarceration, despite previously featuring on a remix of his October 2017 single, “GUMMO.” He referred to Tekashi as a “rat” in November 2018—months before he took a plea deal—on Meek Mill’s “What’s Free”:\n\nScreaming ‘gang gang,’ now you wanna rat\nRacketeering charges caught him on a tap\nLookin' for a bond, lawyers wanna tax\nPurple hair got them faggots on your back", "annotation_id": "17780965", "url": "https://genius.com/17780965", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Nigga Lifestyle", "line": "Court side, goin’ viral when them punches thrown", "vault_lines": ["Court side, goin' viral when them punches thrown"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the Lakers-Rockets fight that unfolded in October 2018, while Nipsey Hussle sat courtside at the game and was seen near the action.\n\nNipsey went viral because fans joked that it appeared as if he was ready to join the melee.", "annotation_id": "17777949", "url": "https://genius.com/17777949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
