{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Off Cocaine", "line": "Fuck a hater, make me throw away another Glock", "vault_lines": ["Fuck a hater, make me throw away another Glock"], "meaning": "This can be a double entendres\nRoss is stating he doesn’t care about a hater\nBut also even if you try to fuck with a hater he will get rid of him. In both terms “fuck a hater”", "annotation_id": "31183686", "url": "https://genius.com/31183686", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Off Cocaine", "line": "Burnin’ butter, got it smellin’ like it’s butterscotch", "vault_lines": ["Burnin' butter, got it smellin' like it's butterscotch"], "meaning": "Ross is using cooking as a metaphor to his drug dealing.\nButter is a name for a certain type of high-quality crack cocaine, and crack generally has a sweet smell when it is lit on fire (burnin') which might be compared to butterscotch scent.", "annotation_id": "2514243", "url": "https://genius.com/2514243", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Off Cocaine", "line": "Chickens put me in position to donate the rice", "vault_lines": ["Chickens put me in position to donate the rice"], "meaning": "The “Chickens” Ross is referring to are actually kilo’s of dope, which he could smuggle into the country in bags of rice, like this…\n\n\n\nRoss justifies his criminal activity by offering the positive affects of making large amounts of untaxed dollars.\n\nRick Ross The Dope Dealer/Philanthropist\n\nWhat a guy.\n\nA 9 to 5 does not have philanthropic flexibility.", "annotation_id": "361305", "url": "https://genius.com/361305", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Off Cocaine", "line": "The last bird flew the coup", "vault_lines": ["The last bird flew the coup"], "meaning": "Birds are bricks of cocaine, and Ross just sold his last brick. A wordplay on birds, since birds also fly.", "annotation_id": "211515", "url": "https://genius.com/211515", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
