{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "I’m hard to kill", "vault_lines": ["I'm hard to kill"], "meaning": "An Attempt To Kill Hip Hop & Rap Star Rick Ross In FORT LAUDERDALE Florida  The predawn gunfire on East Las Olas Boulevard aimed at rap star Rick Ross came from a BMW that pulled up alongside his silver Rolls-Royce, witnesses told police. 5 a.m. Jan. 28. Two witnesses told Fort Lauderdale police three or four men in an older-model, four-door red or maroon BMW sedan opened fire from a passenger window before fleeing north on Southeast 16th Avenue, a police report states The shooting prompted Ross to turn south, where he crashed onto the steps of 311 SE 15th Ave. behind the Floridian restaurant.\n\n\n\nBut According To Rozay It Takes More Than Guns & Bullets To Kill A Boss", "annotation_id": "6320083", "url": "https://genius.com/6320083", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "I bought another Phantom, cash count that at the dealer It took an hour, fast money for us young niggas", "vault_lines": ["I bought another Phantom, cash count that at the dealer", "It took an hour, fast money for us young niggas"], "meaning": "Ross bought a 2014 Rolls Royce Wraith, which he playfully named “Wraithful Edmond”—a reference to Rayful Edmond, who was name-dropped earlier this song. The fact that Ross paid cash for the car emphasizes his wealth as most people must pay off a car with monthly payments, Ross simply paid in one swift payment.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lrds0ju1qNM", "annotation_id": "2566580", "url": "https://genius.com/2566580", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "36 up in the pot like what you cooking nigga?", "vault_lines": ["36 up in the pot like what you cooking nigga?"], "meaning": "36 stands for 36 ounces, and there appears to be 36 ounces in the pot, aka they cooked up a kilo of crack cocaine. 36 ounces= 1 kilogram.", "annotation_id": "2343613", "url": "https://genius.com/2343613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "And I’m fly as Alpo before he drop a statement", "vault_lines": ["And I'm fly as Alpo before he drop a statement"], "meaning": "Alpo Martinez is a notorious drug kingpin who rolled with Rich Porter, but he’s also the very same person who ended up killing him. Like Rich Porter, Alpo was also known for his flashy lifestyle, setting a lot of trends in his time. However, when the Feds caught up with Alpo, he became a government informant (snitch), which is what Meek is referring to by “drop a statement”.", "annotation_id": "2292991", "url": "https://genius.com/2292991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "I knew I started getting money when I got them haters", "vault_lines": ["I knew I started getting money when I got them haters"], "meaning": "An old adage in life is how people will get haters once they start making money. When Meek gained a lot of money, that’s when the haters came and as he got more and more money, more and more haters would appear. Ross has referenced this phenomenon before.", "annotation_id": "2291793", "url": "https://genius.com/2291793", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "You hear that sound? I think it’s Benji, he talkin’ to me", "vault_lines": ["You hear that sound? I think it's Benji, he talkin' to me"], "meaning": "All Meek hears is the Benjamin’s ($100 bills) that he has or is trying to attain talking to him.\n\nThis line is also used in reference to “Intro” from the first Dreamchasers mixtape.", "annotation_id": "2291569", "url": "https://genius.com/2291569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "Fish scale, I love the hustle, I’m ’bout my paper", "vault_lines": ["Fish scale, I love the hustle, I'm 'bout my paper"], "meaning": "Fish Scale is high-quality cocaine, usually right off the key and uncut. It is called fish scale because it’s not grainy like lower quality product that is cut with white powder substances, it’s more flakey like a fish scale.", "annotation_id": "2264968", "url": "https://genius.com/2264968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "Don’t you see a nigga ballin’ like I’m Rayful Edmond?? (No snitching)", "vault_lines": ["Don't you see a nigga ballin' like I'm Rayful Edmond?? (No snitching)"], "meaning": "Rayful Edmond was a notorious drug kingpin who is largely credited with introducing crack cocaine into the Washington D.C. area. Following his conviction, he became a government informant. Ross uses his name to describe how he’s ballin', because Edmond had connections with several Georgetown Hoyas players.\n\nRoss adlibs “no snitching” because like Alpo, Edmond also became a government informant. Ross balls similarly to Rayful, but without the snitching aspect.", "annotation_id": "2263953", "url": "https://genius.com/2263953", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "My DC shooter Fat Trel hold up that Mac-Eleven (Dem Bitches)", "vault_lines": ["My DC shooter Fat Trel hold up that Mac-Eleven (Dem Bitches)"], "meaning": "Ross shouts out his latest Maybach Music signing, the DC-rapper Fat Trel.", "annotation_id": "2261046", "url": "https://genius.com/2261046", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "Feelin’ like I’m Richard Porter, I’m really ballin’", "vault_lines": ["Feelin' like I'm Richard Porter, I'm really ballin'"], "meaning": "Richard Porter was a drug dealer. He was known for his flamboyance which came to life at the youthful age of 12 when he sold his first drug. By the time he was 18, he had an entire garage in Manhattan filled with luxury vehicles he had amassed over the years from his fruitful street pharmaceutical business.", "annotation_id": "2260875", "url": "https://genius.com/2260875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Rich Porter", "line": "My Rollie flooded like New Orleans, just like New Orleans", "vault_lines": ["My Rollie flooded like New Orleans, just like New Orleans"], "meaning": "In 2005, Hurricane Katrina hit the city of New Orleans and flooded most of the city leaving many people homeless. Meek compares his Rolex which is flooded with diamonds, to the flood in Katrina.", "annotation_id": "2256713", "url": "https://genius.com/2256713", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
