{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ridin’ Thru the Ghetto", "line": "Handle mine like a—, I’m in a lime green Lamb’", "vault_lines": ["Handle mine like a—, I'm in a lime green Lamb'"], "meaning": "Rick Ross says here he’s always thinking of the next thing he can do, he keeps his mind active. Whether that’s the next track he can record, the next album he can release, he’s always got his mind set on his game, or else he won’t be as successful as he is right now.\n\nLime green Lamb refers to a Lamborghini, which of course is in a light green color.", "annotation_id": "3417344", "url": "https://genius.com/3417344", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ridin’ Thru the Ghetto", "line": "I just left my mama house and it made me feel good I just paid my mama bills, you would if you could", "vault_lines": ["I just paid my mama bills, you would if you could"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has finally gotten out of his mother’s house and made a living for himself. He feels good that he is now making more than enough money to support himself. He’s making so much money that he pays the bills of the woman who’s helped him and loved him through it all, his mother. He makes a very relatable comment here, saying: ‘you would if you could’. Who wouldn’t, if given the opportunity, pay for their mothers bills after all the struggle she’s endured to raise and support you?", "annotation_id": "3417331", "url": "https://genius.com/3417331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ridin’ Thru the Ghetto", "line": "I’m ridin’ through the ghetto and I’m worth a million dollars I’m ridin’ through the ghetto and I’m worth a million dollars I’m worth a million dollars (Dollars), worth a million dollars (Dollars) I’m worth a million dollars (Dollars), worth a million dollars (Dollars) I’m ridin’ through the ghetto and I’m worth a million dollars I’m ridin’ through the ghetto and I’m worth a million dollars", "vault_lines": ["I'm worth a million dollars (Dollars), worth a million dollars (Dollars)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross continues to brag in the hook. Here he says he rides through the ghetto (possibly his old hood?), and now that he’s making so much money and rising to fame as a rapper he’s worth a lot of money. He may be saying that his net worth is literally 1 million dollars, or he may just be throwing up a random number to impress listeners.\n\n\n\nInterestingly, in 2014 Rick Ross’s net worth was a sum of 35 Million dollars. This song was released in ‘08, which shows just how far Rick Ross has really come.", "annotation_id": "3417310", "url": "https://genius.com/3417310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ridin’ Thru the Ghetto", "line": "Trilla I’m a boss", "vault_lines": ["Got 'bout twenty stacks up in my jeans (I'm a boss)"], "meaning": "Trill is an adjective used in hip-hop culture to describe someone who is considered to be well respected, coming from a combination of the words “true” and “real”. Rozay is bragging and letting everyone know he’s the best in the building.\n\nThe phrase “I’m a boss” is another reminder that he’s the one in charge and running things.\n\n\n\nThis phrase must have been thrown around a lot with Rick Ross, because it caught on with Meek Mill who released the track “Ima Boss” 3 years later, after being signed to MMG.", "annotation_id": "3417296", "url": "https://genius.com/3417296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
