{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "Philly women really chillin’ with me Now I really can’t stop sayin’ jawn", "vault_lines": ["Philly women really chillin' with me", "Now I really can't stop sayin' jawn"], "meaning": "“Jawn” is a prominent term in Philadelphia dialect referring to “any object, place or thing”. Wale has been spending so much time with “philly women” that he has started to adopt their vocabulary.\n\nhttps://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/the-enduring-mystery-of-jawn-philadelphias-allpurpose-noun", "annotation_id": "18892653", "url": "https://genius.com/18892653", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "Mike Amiri put a hole in my jeans", "vault_lines": ["Mike Amiri put a hole in my jeans"], "meaning": "Mike Amiri is a fashion designer who became famous for making clothes for rockstars. One of his “signature” styles are jeans with tears and holes in them.\n\n\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: This could also be a reference to the phrase “A hole in my pocket” which means your broke, so he could be saying that since Mike Amiri jeans are so expensive, that he’s broke after buying them.", "annotation_id": "18892641", "url": "https://genius.com/18892641", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "How many times I gotta tell you that I mob, La Cosa Nostra? (The mob)", "vault_lines": ["How many times I gotta tell you that I mob, La Cosa Nostra? (The mob)"], "meaning": "La Cosa Nostra refers to is the infamous Sicilian mafia, controlled by the Gambino family, whose members called themselves “La Cosa Nostra”.\n\nhttps://www.fbi.gov/investigate/organized-crime/history-of-la-cosa-nostra", "annotation_id": "18892635", "url": "https://genius.com/18892635", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "Black Bo’, rest well (Bo)", "vault_lines": ["Black Bo', rest well (Bo)"], "meaning": "Black Bo was Rick Ross' former manager, until he passed away on December 8, 2017 at the age of 56.\n\nhttps://hiphopdx.com/news/id.45428/title.rick-ross-longtime-manager-black-bo-passes-away", "annotation_id": "18892626", "url": "https://genius.com/18892626", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "Donald said all of us live in huts I tell him, “Dummy, go to Lagos”", "vault_lines": ["Donald said all of us live in huts", "I tell him, \"Dummy, go to Lagos\""], "meaning": "In June of 2017, United States President Donald Trump said Nigerians would not just “go back to their huts” in Africa. This was said out of Trump’s anger for, in his opinion, too many people getting visas to America from other countries.\n\nWith the comment above, Trump is implying that all Nigerians live in “huts,” as Wale points out here. While Wale was born in Washington D.C., both his parents were born in Nigeria.\n\n Mansions Global describes Banana Island (a rich area in the country’s capital, Lagos) as “Nigeria’s answer to Paris’s Seventh Arrondissement, San Diego’s La Jolla, New York City’s Tribeca and Tokyo’s Shibuya and Roppongi”.", "annotation_id": "18315796", "url": "https://genius.com/18315796", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "Stackin’ money like Mayweather", "vault_lines": ["Stackin' money like Mayweather"], "meaning": "“Mayweather” is referring to Floyd Mayweather Jr., who was an American boxer for almost 20 years. He has a perfect 50-0 record, with his last one being in 2017 against Conor McGregor. He has amassed a net worth of over $500 million dollars with reports being as high as $700 million.", "annotation_id": "18302105", "url": "https://genius.com/18302105", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "Can’t H&M us, no", "vault_lines": ["Can't H&M us, no"], "meaning": "In a follow up to the previous line, Wale refers to the retail company H&M, and their controversial 2018 decision to depict a young black child modeling a sweatshirt, with the phrase “Coolest monkey in the jungle.” H&M received tons of backlash from the media, leading to the company removing the image from their website.", "annotation_id": "18222621", "url": "https://genius.com/18222621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "Yeah, BAPE, Folarin, no monkey business", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, BAPE, Folarin, no monkey business"], "meaning": "Monkey Business is defined as shenanigans and the logo of BAPE is an ape. Wale is saying that he owns plenty of BAPE and that isn’t any monkey business.", "annotation_id": "18214980", "url": "https://genius.com/18214980", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "line": "I feel like Carson Wentz I got the wisdom If a nigga sit the bench I got a funny feeling that you niggas fooling Boy, he still the coldest", "vault_lines": ["I feel like Carson Wentz", "I got the wisdom"], "meaning": "Wale likens himself to Philadelphia Eagles Quarterback Carson Wentz who was drafted second overall by the Eagles in the 2016 NFL Draft. Wentz was the leading MVP candidate in 2017 prior to tearing his ACL and LCL against the Los Angeles Rams in Week 14 which rendered him to the bench as he was declared out for the season and playoffs. Despite Wentz’s injury, the Eagles won Super Bowl LII with backup QB Nick Foles replacing Wentz.\n\nWale is saying even if he’s on the bench like Wentz was after his ACL and LCL tear that this is only temporary and that his skillset will shine when he’s back on the NFL field.", "annotation_id": "18214945", "url": "https://genius.com/18214945", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Routine", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Wale-routine-lyrics", "genius_title": "Routine", "genius_id": 3445830, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Royals (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "All I heard was murder, think the house haunted", "vault_lines": ["All I heard was murder, think the house haunted"], "meaning": "Calling back to both the Jay Z track and the previous lyric, Ross continues with the mansion wordplay. “House haunted” is wordplay on its own, referring to haunted houses of course.\n\n“All I heard was murder” is a reference to how Ross “murders” his competition as he gains money and keeps releasing bangers. He’s definitely a force to be reckoned with.\n\nIt could also be playing off of the previous lyric, as his competition literally are dirt poor are desperate to become famous, even murder.", "annotation_id": "3453958", "url": "https://genius.com/3453958", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Royals (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "Label the racketeer, John Grisham with a pen", "vault_lines": ["Label the racketeer, John Grisham with a pen"], "meaning": "Ross is to racketeering as John Grisham (a bestselling author (who is known for his legal thrillers) is to writing (with a pen). Ricky Rozay truly is the Boss.", "annotation_id": "2941076", "url": "https://genius.com/2941076", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Royals (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "Mastermind unfolds like a true crime", "vault_lines": ["Mastermind unfolds like a true crime"], "meaning": "Referencing his sixth studio album, “Mastermind.”\n\n\n\nPeep the tracklist here!", "annotation_id": "2394119", "url": "https://genius.com/2394119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Royals (Rick Ross Remix)", "line": "Double M gold mind for the whole time", "vault_lines": ["Double M gold mind for the whole time"], "meaning": "MMG stands for Maybach Music Group.\n\nAlso, the wordplay with saying gold mind instead of gold mine.\n\nACCEPTED SUGGESTION: He used gold mind instead of gold mine as a reference to his upcoming album, Mastermind.", "annotation_id": "2394105", "url": "https://genius.com/2394105", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
