{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "Me and Yo Gotti fuck the same hoes", "vault_lines": ["Me and Yo Gotti fuck the same hoes"], "meaning": "It is debatable how Ross’s claim to have sex with the same women as Yo Gotti  jives with Gotti’s own words from his song “Law” in which he states: “Don’t fuck no bitch that’s fucking with your dogs, that’s law.”", "annotation_id": "10096913", "url": "https://genius.com/10096913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "He get them turned out up at the absurd house", "vault_lines": ["He get them turned out up at the absurd house"], "meaning": "While Ross owns multiple homes he’s most likely referring to the 54,000 square foot mansion he purchased from Evander Holyfield back in 2014 for $5.8 million.\n\nSitting on 235 acres it’s the largest single family home in Georgia sporting an impressive 109 rooms with 12 bedrooms. Shame to have all that variety of rooms and be stuck with the same hoes.", "annotation_id": "9562665", "url": "https://genius.com/9562665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "They fuck with me but they say their favorite artist is J. Cole", "vault_lines": ["They fuck with me but they say their favorite artist is J. Cole"], "meaning": "Worth to note that J. Cole is the only famous named on the whole song that Rozay doesn’t claim to be eskimo brother with.\n\nMaybe Ross is being just fair, once Cole is now married with his college sweetheart. And as he rapped on “Love Yourz”, he just wanna love what he got.\n\n\n\nDespite that, the hoes who fuck with Rick Ross say that Cole is their favorite artist. Maybe Jermaine’s aptitude to make love lyrics gave him that place.", "annotation_id": "9487033", "url": "https://genius.com/9487033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "Me and Kevin Hart fuckin’ the same hoes I’m ‘bout to shoot a movie usin’ all the same hoes", "vault_lines": ["Me and Kevin Hart fuckin' the same hoes", "I'm 'bout to shoot a movie usin' all the same hoes"], "meaning": "While in the first verse, Rozay ended focusing on rappers/singers, in the second verse, he open up for a wide variety of artists, starting off with the comedian and actor Kevin Hart.\n\nPlaying with the fact that Kevin is an actor, Rozay says he’ll shoot a movie. Which can mean he’ll make a new video for one of his songs using all these same hoes or that he’ll record a sextape while he fuck all these same hoes.\n\nWorth to know that Kevin Hart and Rick Ross already filmed together for the video of Jennifer Hudson’s “Think Like a Man”.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CSE_S8WXQrI\n\nFurthermore, Rozay and Kevin seems to share a close relationship, once Kevin joked with Ross during the 2013 BET Hip-Hop Awards.", "annotation_id": "9484505", "url": "https://genius.com/9484505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "But I put her on her feet in that new Range Rov Me and Mayweather fuck the same hoes Money team, money green, mean Lambo", "vault_lines": ["But I put her on her feet in that new Range Rov", "Me and Mayweather fuck the same hoes"], "meaning": "Since Rozay is talking about having sex in a car, there’s no better celebrity to reference than Floyd Mayweather. The former boxer, whom has a net worth estimated in $400 million, is truly a car enthusiast, owning a personal fleet of high luxury cars. Just to keep it up with the reality of the lyrics, Money does really have a Lamborghini Aventador.\n\n\n\nThe references keep going on when Rozay refers to Floyd’s crew, The Money Team. Rick Ross can even consider himself as part of TMT, once he even went into the ring with Money.", "annotation_id": "9483159", "url": "https://genius.com/9483159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "Me and David Beckham fuckin’ the same hoes Apartment in Tribeca on the third floor", "vault_lines": ["Me and David Beckham fuckin' the same hoes", "Apartment in Tribeca on the third floor"], "meaning": "David Beckham has been known to stay in Tribeca, a swanky neighbourhood in Lower Manhattan. The same is true of Kanye, who has mentioned this recently. This would also lend further credence to the following line which might be a nod to the girl that Ye and Busta may have shared.\n\nHere’s who Beckham is still with – did Ross hit?", "annotation_id": "9478026", "url": "https://genius.com/9478026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "Me and Busta Rhymes, we fuck the same hoes", "vault_lines": ["Me and Busta Rhymes, we fuck the same hoes"], "meaning": "To extend upon this, Ross has also slammed the same hoe as Kanye, and Usher. From Kanye’s “Gold Digger”:\n\nFrom what I heard she got a baby by Busta\nMy best friend say she used to fuck with Usher", "annotation_id": "9472583", "url": "https://genius.com/9472583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "Me and Steve Harvey fuck the same hoes Ms. Universe, they all the same hoes Forget they name nigga, know the saying goes", "vault_lines": ["Me and Steve Harvey fuck the same hoes", "Ms. Universe, they all the same hoes", "Forget they name nigga, know the saying goes"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to Steve Harvey’s accidental announcement of the Miss Universe pageant. At first Miss Colombia, Ariadna Gutiérrez, was called up as the winner, but eventually Miss Philippines, Pia Wurtzbach was given the title.", "annotation_id": "9471397", "url": "https://genius.com/9471397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "line": "I got broads in Atlanta, trappin’ in the Decatur", "vault_lines": ["I got broads in Atlanta, trappin' in the Decatur"], "meaning": "Rozay uses Desiigner’s infamous line from his hit single, “Panda.” Both Rick Ross and Desiigner embrace a lavish lifestyle with women from Atlanta.\n\nI got broads in Atlanta\nTwistin' dope, lean, and the Fanta\n\nDecatur is a city in Georgia, in which Rick Ross owns a crib; it is one of the largest homes in Georgia. It’s no surprise that he would bring a few of his women to his $5.8 million mansion right outside of Atlanta.\n\nTo “trap” means to sell drugs to support oneself. Rozay has spoken about his selling drugs in many songs including Meek’s “Dope Dealer,” “Rich Off Cocaine” and “Drug Dealers Dream”.", "annotation_id": "9470964", "url": "https://genius.com/9470964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Same Hoes", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-same-hoes-lyrics", "genius_title": "Same Hoes", "genius_id": 2554056, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "[Produced by Kanye West, Mustard and Mike Dean]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Mustard explained the collaborative process behind making this beat in an interview with hardknock.tv. Mustard created the original melody, which was much faster:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/A4r_7yci9Gs?t=70\n\nHe then explains:\n\nKanye slowed it all the way down. […]  And then he put the sample on top of it, which made it dope as shit.\n\nApparently even Mustard doesn’t know that Betty Wright’s part is not actually a sample!\n\nMustard went on to say:\n\nI left him 100 beats. I’m sure we gon' do something else. He cool.\n\nPerhaps one of these is what turned into Big Sean’s “I Don’t Fuck with You”, where Mustard and Ye are both co-producers.", "annotation_id": "3040434", "url": "https://genius.com/3040434", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
