{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Lames try to tell me, “Cut the wildin’ out, out”", "vault_lines": ["Lames try to tell me, \"Cut the wildin' out, out\""], "meaning": "As he rapped in “New Slaves”:\n\nI’m ‘bout to wild the fuck out\nI’m going Bobby Boucher\n\n\n\nAlthough people are preferring the old Kanye they still want him to put out albums like Yeezus. Of course that’s a contradiction!", "annotation_id": "2876700", "url": "https://genius.com/2876700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "That’s that Holy water, sanctified refreshments", "vault_lines": ["That's that Holy water, sanctified refreshments"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5236749148001\n\nhttps://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5236749148001", "annotation_id": "2876598", "url": "https://genius.com/2876598", "state": "verified", "votes": 96, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "I walk into the room, you can even hear all the silence", "vault_lines": ["I walk into the room, you can even hear all the silence"], "meaning": "A subtle reference to Kanye’s line in his last collaboration with Rozay on “Devil In a New Dress”.\n\nYou see I always loved that sense of humor\nBut tonight you should have seen how quiet the room was\n\nRozay possesses an aura of awe and “silence” that its tangible—you can also hear the respect for the G in the room.", "annotation_id": "2863716", "url": "https://genius.com/2863716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Okay, all I want’s a hundred million dollars and a bad bitch", "vault_lines": ["Okay, all I want's a hundred million dollars and a bad bitch"], "meaning": "Sean is shooting for the stars! Ambition is key and hard work is extremely important in order to succeed in the music game. As we all know, Sean is a very hard worker and assures us in “10 2 10”:\n\nThat mean I work from 10 to 10\nThen 10 to 10, then 10 again\n\n\n\nLooks like he already has the “bad bitch part” covered, since he was dating actress/singer Ariana Grande when this song was released.\n\n\n\nOpening with this “money and bitches” message is quite the juxtaposition coming off the gospel-inspired lead-ins.", "annotation_id": "2860275", "url": "https://genius.com/2860275", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "God, I’ve been guilty, fornicatin’ from my status", "vault_lines": ["God, I've been guilty, fornicatin' from my status"], "meaning": "Big Sean is talking to God as if he is confessing his sins. Fornication is a term used in the Christian Bible meaning to have sex before marriage. As we can tell from his past lyrics, he has bitches galore, and he is asking God for forgiveness.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Sean’s talked about fornicatin'…\n\n\n\nSean also means that he exploits the fact that he is famous to have sex with females or groupies who throw themselves at him.", "annotation_id": "2860151", "url": "https://genius.com/2860151", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Pass me 30 bottles, champagne procession", "vault_lines": ["Pass me 30 bottles, champagne procession"], "meaning": "When ordering champagne bottles in a club, the bottles move along ceremoniously in orderly succession. This resembles a church procession.\n\nalso note the double entendra in pass/past : “reachin' PAST me” and “PASS me 30 bottles”", "annotation_id": "2853687", "url": "https://genius.com/2853687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Somewhere in Jamaica I’m still holdin’ on my chalice", "vault_lines": ["Somewhere in Jamaica I'm still holdin' on my chalice"], "meaning": "A chalice is a type of goblet, usually associated with royalty. Chalice is a common term in Jamaica referring to a bong.\n\nRick Ross is so large, he has built such an “empire” that he can smoke on his chalice like a king in a nice relaxing spot such as Jamaica.\n\n“Somewhere in Jamaica” may also be a nod to Somewhereinamerica by Jay Z.", "annotation_id": "2850717", "url": "https://genius.com/2850717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "There’s a field with angels movin’ around me I just worship thee, for all he’s done for me It’s a new day, I have been born again I’ve been born again, I’ve been born again In His spirit, and His name, I’m sanctified! Lord I testify, he’s right by my side I believe it be, His word is so clear to me Yeah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["In His spirit, and His name, I'm sanctified!", "Lord I testify, he's right by my side", "I believe it be, His word is so clear to me"], "meaning": "These parts are about being born again, while being baptized into Christianity.\n\n“Feeling his blessings” (in the latter sections) is a metaphor for feeling the holy water wash away his sins. Alternatively this could mean that the holy water is God’s blessing.\n\nThis can be interpreted as a metaphor around Kanye’s and Ross' career: they are back in the game and are blessed by God.", "annotation_id": "2850633", "url": "https://genius.com/2850633", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "[Intro: Betty Wright]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "While Betty Wright has been sampled well over 100 times, this is not one of them. Shortly after the full song became available, MIKE DEAN commented, “no samples  we made that shit!”\n\nMore details about Wright’s part emerged in this New Yorker article from about a month after the song came out. To summarize, Wright got a late-night call from DJ Khaled, who she describes as like a son to her, asking her to come down to the studio that same night. Then:\n\nAfter listening to a demo, Wright recorded the “Sanctified” hook in fifteen minutes, sitting down on a sofa while she sang because she was too exhausted to stand. She assumed that Kanye was going to speed up the sample, as he is known to do with soul melodies, so she performed it slowly, infusing it with an extra intensity so that the final version “wouldn’t sound like Minnie Mouse.” Afterward, Wright was embarrassed about how it sounded, and in the morning she considered asking the engineer to delete her take. When Ross and Puff called to tell her she’d killed it, she was speechless.\n\nSome have speculated that Wright’s portions of the song were originally meant to be sung by fellow ‘70s soul singer Bobby Womack, as he had talked about recording with Ross in a December 2013 interview with Pitchfork. But Ross’s own comments suggest that prior versions were sample-based:\n\nIt actually started as a sample. We did the sample maybe 10 different ways and then we ultimately went with a beautiful lady out of Miami, Ms. Betty Wright. She blessed us.", "annotation_id": "2850622", "url": "https://genius.com/2850622", "state": "accepted", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Rims on my Ferrari, my bitch said that I was childish", "vault_lines": ["Rims on my Ferrari, my bitch said that I was childish"], "meaning": "Ross could be referring to the fact that blowing money on unnecessary expenses and material possessions like rims could be seen as immature and childish. Jay-Z expressed this same sentiment back in 2006:\n\nYoung enough to know the right car to buy\nYet grown enough not to put rims on it\n\nIt doesn’t look like Ross is too concerned with saving his money, however.", "annotation_id": "2850321", "url": "https://genius.com/2850321", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "All I wanted was a hundred million dollars and a bad bitch Now I want two hundred and ménage in my palace", "vault_lines": ["Now I want two hundred and ménage in my palace"], "meaning": "Rozay has expressed before how he wants to hit a net worth of 100 million dollars, all while keeping himself a beautiful woman. However, one must continue to progress—so once Ross hits those goals, he’ll shoot for 200 million and two fine ass women. Note how the number of women doubled which also fulfilled the number of women needed to have a ménage-a-trois.\n\nHe already bought the palace:\n\n\n\nNote: Ross is not referencing Nicki Minaj in this line.", "annotation_id": "2850286", "url": "https://genius.com/2850286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Walkin’ out the jeweler with no mothafuckin’ balance", "vault_lines": ["Walkin' out the jeweler with no mothafuckin' balance"], "meaning": "Rick Ross, known for his extensive expensive jewelry collection, goes to his jeweler and walks out with no money in his pockets. He’s spent it all on exquisite jewelry.\n\n\n\nNote the double entendre here—he has no balance, meaning he can’t walk straight because of all the jewelry.", "annotation_id": "2850098", "url": "https://genius.com/2850098", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Balmain uniform,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Balmain is a fashion house that was founded by Pierre Balmain.\nIt is known for its expensive and stylish clothing. Ross wears Balmain, typically something like this:", "annotation_id": "2849920", "url": "https://genius.com/2849920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "God, I’ve been guilty, fornicatin’ from my status", "vault_lines": ["God, I've been guilty, fornicatin' from my status"], "meaning": "Ye recognizes he has used his fame and social status to fornicate (to have sex) with females in the past. He also recognizes most women are more attracted to his social status than they are to him personally.\n\n\n\nKanye alludes to this in his classic, “Devil in a New Dress”\n\nYou love me for me? Could you be more phony?", "annotation_id": "2849899", "url": "https://genius.com/2849899", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Keys to my success, I get new keys and new address", "vault_lines": ["Keys to my success, I get new keys and new address"], "meaning": "Rick Ross’s alleged drug-dealing past selling kis (kilograms) of cocaine has been part of his key to success, as well as his rap career. Now that he’s paid from slanging drugs and selling records, he can afford the keys to new cars and new houses.\n\nJust last month he spent $10 million on Evander Holyfields’s former mansion, which features 109 rooms.\n\n#Rozay’s livin' the boss’s life!\n\n\n\nRoss spits a similar ki/key pun on Mafia Music II.", "annotation_id": "2849885", "url": "https://genius.com/2849885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "I don’t sweat it, wipe my forehead with a handkerchief", "vault_lines": ["I don't sweat it, wipe my forehead with a handkerchief"], "meaning": "Kanye doesn’t worry about what the media, the public eye or even what the President of the United States thinks of him, he will still call himself a creative genius whenever he wants.\n\nI’m a creative genius and there’s no other way to word it.\n\n\n\nOn the other hand, Kanye puts a lot of work and effort into his passions, whether it be clothing design, business ventures or music.", "annotation_id": "2849873", "url": "https://genius.com/2849873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "So you can gon’ and make up lies, but I’m so sanctified", "vault_lines": ["So you can gon' and make up lies, but I'm so sanctified"], "meaning": "#YOU CAN’T TELL YE NOTHING\nYeezus doesn’t embrace anything you say because you are simply not on his level of holyness, so go ahead and make up rumors but know Ye is never affected.\n\nThe lies Kanye may be referring to are the everlasting Illuminati rumors and speculation that he seems to always be tied too by way of JAY Z. For him to be “sanctified” however, means that he is a holy man.\n\n\n\nKanye has felt Sanctified before,\n\nAnd when I play it at my shows I feel sanctified", "annotation_id": "2849863", "url": "https://genius.com/2849863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Major cult figure, I’m the fresh David Koresh", "vault_lines": ["Major cult figure, I'm the fresh David Koresh"], "meaning": "Ross is implying that he has a religious following, and the power to persuade people like David Koresh.\n\nKoresh was a leader of a religious cult Branch Davidians in Waco, Texas. An FBI raid that was meant to be searching for hoarding weapons ended up being a 51-day standoff and 74 people (including David) led to their fiery death. This sparked a bunch of anti-government sentiment and conspiracy.\n\nHowever to the devout followers of the religion, they believe Koresh was God in the flesh. This moment was one of the 10 stories that defined Generation X.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PbQFB8crxok#t=0m21s", "annotation_id": "2849857", "url": "https://genius.com/2849857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Double M, that be the Army, better yet, the Navy", "vault_lines": ["Double M, that be the Army, better yet, the Navy"], "meaning": "A nod to BG’s banger “Cash Money is an Army”—a line that has been borrowed before by Jay-Z\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAdditionally, the change from Army to Navy in the lyric referenced above alludes to the use of speedboats to move narcotics off the Florida coast. See “Off the Boat”\nFurthermore, MM or double M stands for Maybach Music which is Rick Ross' record label", "annotation_id": "2849853", "url": "https://genius.com/2849853", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "But who the fuck is you reachin’?", "vault_lines": ["But who the fuck is you reachin'?"], "meaning": "This is in reference to radio hosts such as Charlamagne and Sway Calloway. When Charlamagne interviewed Ye' here, he said Kanye’s album was wack and called him a walking contradiction. In Sway’s interview found here, Sway begins to question why Ye doesn’t attempt to empower himself without using major corporations, such as Nike, to manufacture and provide him with other services. Then things begin to turn south in the interview.\n\n\n\nThis line is continuing the 2 lines above. Ye is wondering if Charlamagne and Sway, or any of his critics at all, are creating art that influences people on an international scale, or if they are creating anything worthwhile at all.\n\nHere is a video of Kanye calling out Sway and Charlamagne and going on a rant about all of his critics.", "annotation_id": "2849842", "url": "https://genius.com/2849842", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "God sent me a message, said I’m too aggressive Really!? Me!? Too aggressive!?", "vault_lines": ["God sent me a message, said I'm too aggressive", "Really!? Me!? Too aggressive!?"], "meaning": "Apparently, Kanye just had another talk with Jesus, and he had a very important message for the young God: He may be getting a little too violent in his life.\n\nMany people view Kanye as violent, from his Twitter “rants”, to his attacking of the paparazzi, and not to mention his concert “Visionary Stream of Consciousness™”. Kanye is simply at times misunderstood, but we know he will never surrender. Anyways, just remember, he is not losing his mind, he is using it.\n\n#Kanye will never bow down!!!\n\n\n\nAlso says a lot about how he views himself as Yeezus: he is able to critique God’s messages and find fault in them.\n\nIt’s also perhaps quite ironic that people are saying Kanye is too agressive, because he is definitely responsible for pushing hip-hop out of the gangsta rap that predominated the early 2000s. He got famous off of his “conscious” raps, and perhaps this is indicating that he doesn’t think he fits a “violent” image or public persona.", "annotation_id": "2849831", "url": "https://genius.com/2849831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 234, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "People sayin’, “Ye, we need another Yeezus”", "vault_lines": ["People sayin', \"Ye, we need another Yeezus\""], "meaning": "It’s no secret that Yeezus was met with mixed reviews. On one hand, Yeezus received outstanding ratings from prestigious reviewers and was viewed as essentially an experimental milestone in music as a whole—let alone rap itself—with an intensity that only Ye could pull off.\n\nOn the other side, there’s a mass of people who think that Ye fell off with Yeezus and that his minimalistic style was just a result of apathetic intentions. The latter want Kanye to go back to his less controversial, backpack rapping days and put back on his pink polo. However, Kanye is embracing the former and is going to continue to speak his mind and be a controversial icon, no matter who says he shouldn’t.\n\nThis is a double entendre:\n\n\nPeople want another album Yeezus album.\nA reference to the second coming of Jesus.", "annotation_id": "2849810", "url": "https://genius.com/2849810", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "Niggas be lovin’ the old Ye They sayin’ the new Ye, that nigga be spazzin’ But when Ali turn up and be Ali You can’t ever change that nigga back to Cassius", "vault_lines": ["Niggas be lovin' the old Ye", "They sayin' the new Ye, that nigga be spazzin'", "But when Ali turn up and be Ali", "You can't ever change that nigga back to Cassius"], "meaning": "Cassius Clay, one of the greatest boxers of all time, had secretly followed the Nation of Islam—revealing his newfound faith after winning the heavyweight title in 1964. Elijah Muhammad then gave him the name that we all know to this day—Muhammad Ali.\n\nKanye has had a similar revival in music and overall actions in general, and similar to how Ali will never go back to being Cassius, Ye will never be a mere mortal again—he’s a god.", "annotation_id": "2849809", "url": "https://genius.com/2849809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 158, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "And wash my sins in the blood of Jesus", "vault_lines": ["And wash my sins in the blood of Jesus"], "meaning": "Ahhh, our god Yeezus is back in the booth. While Kanye might have been a bad man in the past, he will be forgiven by washing himself and his sins in the Blood of Jesus. The Jesus mentions have been a staple of Kanye’s work as of recent, and this is a huge statement, even for him. Kanye is definitely on a higher level.\n\nThe Blood of Jesus is another term for red wine, for it’s similar look. In this sense, Kanye could be drowning his mistakes in the bottom of a bottle. Someone might need to hold it for him.\n\nNote the Young Thug-esque flow on this line and the next one", "annotation_id": "2849804", "url": "https://genius.com/2849804", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sanctified", "line": "All I wanted was a hundred million dollars and a bad bitch", "vault_lines": ["All I wanted was a hundred million dollars and a bad bitch"], "meaning": "As you might remember, Kanye’s camp made sure to let Ray J know (during the “I Hit It First” controversy last year) that Kanye hit the $100-million mark first:\n\nRay J is crazy. Kanye don’t condone broke ass, jealous [guys] who be trying to bite off he and Kim’s fame just to stay, wait, just to become relevant. Kanye West and Kim Kardashian will not give Ray J attention. Tell him to call [Kanye] when he gets to the $100-million mark [because] guess what? [Kanye] hit that first.\n\nHe’s now also engaged to Kim Kardashian—so it’s safe to say that he accomplished to get what he wanted to have.", "annotation_id": "2787897", "url": "https://genius.com/2787897", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
