{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Half of my niggas headed to Attica", "vault_lines": ["Half of my niggas headed to Attica"], "meaning": "Attica correctional facility is a prison in Wyoming County, New York. Rozay’s affiliates are street-involved but seem to be less luck than him and are facing extended sentences in prison. He’s the one who made it out and references his luck while also paying homage.", "annotation_id": "28386162", "url": "https://genius.com/28386162", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Santorini Greece, I put it on the map", "vault_lines": ["Santorini Greece, I put it on the map"], "meaning": "Santorini is one of the Cyclades islands in the Aegean Sea. It was devastated by a volcanic eruption in the 16th century BC, forever shaping its rugged landscape. The whitewashed, cubiform houses of its 2 principal towns, Fira and Oia, cling to cliffs above an underwater caldera (crater). They overlook the sea, small islands to the west and beaches made up of black, red and white lava pebbles.\n\nSantorini is renowned for its tradition in wine making and boasts vast vineyards and fine wine varieties. Its boutique wineries are a must as they offer the ultimate ambrosial experience.", "annotation_id": "27926237", "url": "https://genius.com/27926237", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "I know the snipers and I flow the nicest", "vault_lines": ["I know the snipers and I flow the nicest"], "meaning": "Rozay is simply saying that personally he associates with actual killers/hitmen yet he still is one of the nicest rappers in the game.", "annotation_id": "25977357", "url": "https://genius.com/25977357", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Restricted license but I’m so divisive", "vault_lines": ["Restricted license but I'm so divisive"], "meaning": "Rozay is known to have not actually gotten his full drivers license until 2021 at 45 years old. Prior to that he was riding dirty or on restricted terms. https://www.today.com/popculture/rick-ross-explains-why-he-just-got-his-driver-s-t230221", "annotation_id": "25977345", "url": "https://genius.com/25977345", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Room full of cloaks and they countin’ votes Million man march and I’m takin’ notes (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Room full of cloaks and they countin' votes", "Million man march and I'm takin' notes (Huh)"], "meaning": "“Cloak” is another term for overcoat but by saying “they counting votes” in this bar, Ross is making a play on words referencing the “cloakrooms” in Congress where politicians historically went to cajole votes from colleagues.  He’s suggesting that the Milion Man March in Washington, D.C. on October 16, 1995 could, potentially, apply similar political pressure.", "annotation_id": "21904681", "url": "https://genius.com/21904681", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "The bank account done caught the holy ghost (Huh) I say the bank account done caught the holy ghost", "vault_lines": ["The bank account done caught the holy ghost (Huh)", "I say the bank account done caught the holy ghost"], "meaning": "Rozay refers to his 2012 Rich Forever mixtape intro “https://genius.com/Rick-ross-holy-ghost-lyrics%E2%80%9D where he compares his rapid financial success to catching the Holy Ghost!", "annotation_id": "20425241", "url": "https://genius.com/20425241", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Dealin’ yayo, never had my teeth cleaned", "vault_lines": ["Dealin' yayo, never had my teeth cleaned"], "meaning": "Ross being a drug dealer in his past, lived by the ten crack commandments, and rule number 4: “Never get high on your own supply”. As one of the ways cocaine is consumed is by rubbing it on your gum/teeth which leads to teeth decay.\nRoss does not consume his own products hence no dental visits needed.", "annotation_id": "18633166", "url": "https://genius.com/18633166", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Diabetes rampant in my blood line That why fat boy be happy to see the sunshine", "vault_lines": ["That why fat boy be happy to see the sunshine"], "meaning": "Ross is no stranger to health scares.\n\nIn 2011 the rapper faced two seizures which he claimed were caused due to sleep deprivation. Both were experienced while flying and the pilot had to make emergency landings.\n\nI would get two hours of sleep and keep moving… that has to stop\n\nIn March 2018 while building up for the release of his 10th studio-album,  he faced another near death experience when hospitalized for pneumonia and was put of life support.  He thankfully recovered and bounced back later releasing his second single of the year: “Green Gucci Suit”.", "annotation_id": "15385977", "url": "https://genius.com/15385977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Neck rocky, Sylvester Stallone (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Neck rocky, Sylvester Stallone (Woo)"], "meaning": "Sylvester Stallone is an Academy Award-winning actor who is best known for playing boxer Rocky Balboa in the Rocky series'.\n\n\n\nRoss, who has connected with Stallone in the past, uses a double entendre to reference his ‘rocky’ or diamond-filled chains in addition to the movie series.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BfTu3l6lMq9/?taken-by=richforever", "annotation_id": "14686572", "url": "https://genius.com/14686572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Hot pastrami for my Jewish chicks Eight days of Christmas, every day a newer gift", "vault_lines": ["Hot pastrami for my Jewish chicks", "Eight days of Christmas, every day a newer gift"], "meaning": "Pastrami is considered a sandwich meat/cold cut and was introduced to the United States in the late 19th century by Romanian Jews. The meat is very popular in the Jewish community.\n\n\n\nRoss keeps the jewish theme going to the next line as he is likely referring to Chanukah, a Jewish Holiday. Chanukah lasts for Eight days and participants often give and receive a gift for all eight days.", "annotation_id": "12618013", "url": "https://genius.com/12618013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "We in the last days, these racist agendas Blatant double standards because I’m a nigga", "vault_lines": ["We in the last days, these racist agendas", "Blatant double standards because I'm a nigga"], "meaning": "What Rick Ross is referring to is the fact that there is a huge deal of racism towards the black community in USA, we see this all the time with police brutality and the killing of innocent black men/women.\n\nClearly the police in USA show double standards and treat black people with less respect.\n\n\n\nRegarding the “last days” Rick Ross could be referring to the end times aka the day of judgement as we are all equal in the eyes of God.", "annotation_id": "11818194", "url": "https://genius.com/11818194", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Seen a Cuban kilo, I was 15 (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Seen a Cuban kilo, I was 15 (Huh)"], "meaning": "Ross' prepubescent forays into distribution levels of pharmaceuticals is well documented. \n17 I was chargin' niggas 17― Rick Ross (Ft. Jeezy & Tracy T) – War Ready\n\n\nHe also mentions this in a tweet:\nhttps://twitter.com/RickRoss/status/376141899259592704", "annotation_id": "11744439", "url": "https://genius.com/11744439", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "And now it’s boats and the Belaire Rose", "vault_lines": ["And now it's boats and the Belaire Rose"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is part owner of the Belaire champagne brand.\n\n\n\nRoss himself enjoys Belaire Rose and claims it’s his favorite although he reps that Ciroc.\n\nCiroc Boy forever\nBut this Belaire Rosé\nHas to be the world’s finest\n\nRoss also calls himself Rozay which is based of the name of this champagne. They’re are both pronounced the same way.\n\nRozay, that’s my nickname", "annotation_id": "11719957", "url": "https://genius.com/11719957", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Bowlin’ alley in the basement but we still shootin’ dice", "vault_lines": ["Bowlin' alley in the basement but we still shootin' dice"], "meaning": "On October, 11th 2016 during a mansion tour with DJ Khaled, Ross revealed he had an indoor bowling alley in his 235 acre Georgia mansion.", "annotation_id": "11708536", "url": "https://genius.com/11708536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Everywhere you go, bitches throwing rocks, nigga Man, a nigga in a Lamborghini", "vault_lines": ["Man, a nigga in a Lamborghini"], "meaning": "Lot of hate swirled around Ross on several incidents since him releasing ‘Port of Miami’ in 2006.\n\nFrom a long running feud with 50 Cent\n\nTo his affiliations\n\nTo just how real is his rap persona\n\nWhat they do not talk about is his business ventures. From champagne to restaurants to partnerships like the one he had in 2013 with Reebok.\n\nRoss even owns over 12 Wingstop chains.\n\nWhile he might not be at Jay-Z status, it’s hard to not consider that he’s been successful in his business ventures. With success comes opportunities to have what most entrepreneurs already know very well– write-offs. One of the best types of write-offs for those of Rozay status is luxury items like a Lamborghini.", "annotation_id": "11541161", "url": "https://genius.com/11541161", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Fresher than Groovey Lew at a Coogi shoot", "vault_lines": ["Fresher than Groovey Lew at a Coogi shoot"], "meaning": "Rozay shouts out Groovey Lew, a legendary stylist, who used to style The Notorious B.I.G. and the Bad Boy Family.", "annotation_id": "11523354", "url": "https://genius.com/11523354", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Martha Stewart decorated both (Ha) Snoop Dogg donated the smoke", "vault_lines": ["Martha Stewart decorated both (Ha)", "Snoop Dogg donated the smoke"], "meaning": "Martha Stewart and Snoop Dogg have a cooking show together, called Martha and Snoop’s Potluck Dinner Party.  Rick Ross made a special guest appearance on the show, where he flirted with Stewart in order to get her to decorate his 100-room mansion.  Stewart has had a career in home decor since 1990, and Snoop has a reputation as the OG of smoking weed.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/D4198dPBmdw?t=30s", "annotation_id": "11522261", "url": "https://genius.com/11522261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Jesse Jackson on them people payroll (Fuck him)", "vault_lines": ["Jesse Jackson on them people payroll (Fuck him)"], "meaning": "Ross is saying that Jesse Jackson, while known for this civil rights activism, has sold out. Ross also expresses his disdain for politicians in “I Think She Like Me” by saying “fuck a Ben Carson.”", "annotation_id": "11522235", "url": "https://genius.com/11522235", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Mutulu wife reside in Cuba, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Mutulu wife reside in Cuba, nigga"], "meaning": "Mutulu Shakur is the husband of Afeni Shakur and stepfather of Tupac Shakur. He is currently serving 60 years in prison, mainly for a $1.6 million dollar bank robbery and murder.  He assisted with the prison escape of his sister, Assata Shakur, who currently resides in Cuba, under political asylum.\n\nAfeni died in May 2016, but Ross suggests that she is still alive and living with her sister-in-law in Cuba.  A popular conspiracy theory is that Tupac also currently lives in Cuba.", "annotation_id": "11521992", "url": "https://genius.com/11521992", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Santorini Greece", "line": "Art Basel with Lyor I blew 300 with ’em", "vault_lines": ["Art Basel with Lyor I blew 300 with 'em"], "meaning": "Art Basel is a world famous yearly international art fair hosted in three different locations: Hong Kong; Basel, Switzerland; and Miami Beach, Florida. Rozay attended Basel with Lyor Cohen, a legendary music executive with deep roots in hip hop history. After resigning from the positions of chairman and chief executive officer of Warner Music Group, Cohen co-founded 300 Entertainment with Kevin Liles, Roger Gold, and Todd Moscowitz. As a nod to Cohen and his label, Ross claims he dropped $300,000 on artwork showcased at the fair.", "annotation_id": "11521983", "url": "https://genius.com/11521983", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
