{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "Your record label’s left with rigor mortis", "vault_lines": ["Your record label's left with rigor mortis"], "meaning": "Rigor mortis, the third stage of death, is one of the  more recognizable signs of death, caused by chemical changes in the muscles post mortem (after death), which cause the limbs of the corpse to stiffen. Ross uses this to poetically callout other record labels that have since collapsed–all while Ross' label, MMG, continues to be a powerful presence in the rap world.", "annotation_id": "12316538", "url": "https://genius.com/12316538", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "So it better be that Ghost or that double R", "vault_lines": ["So it better be that Ghost or that double R"], "meaning": "A “Ghost” is a type of Rolls Royce, with a retail price starting at $295,000. In saying “double R”, meaning, ‘Rolls Royce’, Ross is making clear that when it comes to automobiles, it’s ultra luxury or nothing.", "annotation_id": "12316499", "url": "https://genius.com/12316499", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "First and one, I got it on the gold line Fully automatic weapons for my O-line", "vault_lines": ["First and one, I got it on the gold line", "Fully automatic weapons for my O-line"], "meaning": "Even though first down from the 1 would actually be first and goal.\n\nIn football, to have the ball on the goal line means you’re about to score. Usually, this means you would run your offense in a goal line set, which has more offensive lineman than a normal set.\n\nRozay takes it a step further and says his offensive line (blockers) all have guns.\n\nEven Eddie Lacy would be able to score with this advantage.", "annotation_id": "8388457", "url": "https://genius.com/8388457", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "Wanna buy the team, they say I need a cosign", "vault_lines": ["Wanna buy the team, they say I need a cosign"], "meaning": "When one’s credit isn’t strong enough to buy something of high value a cosign is usually needed. The cosigner ensures that if the person who’s buying stop paying their bills the cosign could be held responsible for paying.\n\nWhen Rick Ross perhaps tried to buy a team [basketball, football…] But He was told his net worth including assets, cash etc wasn’t enough.", "annotation_id": "8368702", "url": "https://genius.com/8368702", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "They scream our names as we walk the halls (Boss)", "vault_lines": ["They scream our names as we walk the halls (Boss)"], "meaning": "Ross plays a double entendre with this line.\n\nWhile walking back stage, the media and fans alike tend to call him where his response is simply “boss”.\n\nBut on the flip side, a drug boss ever so often visit a crack house/or its likes to see how their product is performing and while walking [the halls] lower workers tend to say “Boss”", "annotation_id": "8368620", "url": "https://genius.com/8368620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "My new freak, she Puerto Rican, trying to reel me in", "vault_lines": ["My new freak, she Puerto Rican, trying to reel me in"], "meaning": "Ross has plenty of success which stems from his business such as this as well as his most famous enterprise the world over.\n\n\n\nWith Success every woman wants to reel in Ross and making him hers, unfortunately he’s taken. However we know now Ross does indeed have fun on the side.", "annotation_id": "8342192", "url": "https://genius.com/8342192", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "Pray to keep the lights on your porch on", "vault_lines": ["Pray to keep the lights on your porch on"], "meaning": "Ross has spoken of lights being cut off before and having to go out and hustle for money to pay for the bill and here he speaks of it once again.\n\nWithout money to pay the bill your lights are cut off and this ends up being the reason to sell drugs when you have no other job.", "annotation_id": "8342160", "url": "https://genius.com/8342160", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "Full metal jacket still a wardrobe", "vault_lines": ["Full metal jacket still a wardrobe"], "meaning": "Full Metal Jacket is a 1987 action movie which details the events of the Vietnamese war according to Stanley Kubrick.\n\n\n\nBeing an army movie, this describes Rick Ross' wardrobe and how war ready Ross is.", "annotation_id": "8342057", "url": "https://genius.com/8342057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "Crack spots block to block, I’ve been a benefactor I don’t think you understand the type of chips I’m after", "vault_lines": ["Crack spots block to block, I've been a benefactor", "I don't think you understand the type of chips I'm after"], "meaning": "Mean double entendre here, he’s clearly talking about trap spots. Deeper than that Ross owns multiple Wingstops believe it’s over 25 at this point. All of which have been very lucrative for him, Ie Crack Spots. Hence the next line of not understanding the chips he’s after. This rap shit is small time. wealth is the goal. setting his kids up for life is the goal.", "annotation_id": "8332974", "url": "https://genius.com/8332974", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Silk Road", "line": "My alma mater is serving fed time", "vault_lines": ["My alma mater is serving fed time"], "meaning": "Instead of going to university and getting an education, Ross committed crimes and did prison time for it. An alma mater is the university one attended, and although prison isn’t a university, Ross may be implying that he gained knowledge through his life of crime and supposed imprisonment.", "annotation_id": "8330012", "url": "https://genius.com/8330012", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
