{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "Every bar I spit classic like Beans throw up rock", "vault_lines": ["Every bar I spit classic like Beans throw up rock"], "meaning": "His bars are classics like back in the early 2000’s when Beanie Sigel threw up the Roc sign.\n\nRoc Nation artists are famous for making a diamond with their hands.", "annotation_id": "2800586", "url": "https://genius.com/2800586", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "Take a hit it feel like Cameron oh And I got it from the Luigi thats my (boy) This kush have you like..", "vault_lines": ["And I got it from the Luigi thats my (boy)", "This kush have you like.."], "meaning": "Game has some bomb kush he got from his homeboy Luigi. Taking a hit of the blunt and he’ll be as high as Wiz Khalifa, whose real name is Cameron Thomaz.\n\nWiz is a certified stoner who even won Stoner of the Year honors. He claims to smoke about a half pound per week, so he’s basically high all of the time.", "annotation_id": "2800552", "url": "https://genius.com/2800552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "Took it from the hood we jetted to Bora Bora Swimming in salt water spend a mill before the chorus Ballin’ out bitch, now my net worth enormous", "vault_lines": ["Took it from the hood we jetted to Bora Bora", "Swimming in salt water spend a mill before the chorus", "Ballin' out bitch, now my net worth enormous"], "meaning": "Started from the bottom, now we’re here\n\nRoss portrays the outlandish life he lives, as he could spend a million dollars before the chorus (which happens to be in about 13 lines) and it wouldn’t matter.\n\nBora Bora is one of the most beautiful places on earth. The destination is popular among rich people, as it’s expensive place to stay.", "annotation_id": "2795442", "url": "https://genius.com/2795442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "Tats on my chest dead homies on my back", "vault_lines": ["Tats on my chest dead homies on my back"], "meaning": "Rozay is known to perform shirtless during concerts, shows, etc, so his many tattoos are visible.\n\n\nOn his chest he has tattoo portraits of dead presidents (George Washington & Abraham Lincoln)\nOn his back, he has a small portrait of Biggie Smalls.", "annotation_id": "2795408", "url": "https://genius.com/2795408", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "First class duffle bags counting cake with your boy All I did was buy a new Mercedes with a spoiler", "vault_lines": ["All I did was buy a new Mercedes with a spoiler"], "meaning": "Rozay has a duffle bag full of cash in his bags. He copped an expensive Mercedes-Benz with some of it.\n\nThe Benz happens to have a spoiler, a spoiler reduces drag so the car burns less fuel. You can find them on many sports cars.", "annotation_id": "2787425", "url": "https://genius.com/2787425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "I got the Franck Muller, Rolex’s Vacheron Constantin in my old Lexus Hublots in that AP, no Peterson", "vault_lines": ["I got the Franck Muller, Rolex's", "Vacheron Constantin in my old Lexus", "Hublots in that AP, no Peterson"], "meaning": "Game reels off a nice long list of high end Swiss watch manufacturers. We already know he is a fan of a nice timepiece, after he tried to name his record label after one of the brands mentioned (and lost the subsequent legal battle with Rolex over the name).\n\n\n\nNot to be confused with MVP running back Adrian Peterson of the Minnesota Vikings.", "annotation_id": "2781041", "url": "https://genius.com/2781041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "Shwag, two stacks for the Bally boots", "vault_lines": ["Shwag, two stacks for the Bally boots"], "meaning": "Damn right Ross has some shwag, Ricky’s Bally’s set him back $2k!", "annotation_id": "2781013", "url": "https://genius.com/2781013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "line": "Purple clouds I can see Aaliyah and Left Eye", "vault_lines": ["Purple clouds I can see Aaliyah and Left Eye"], "meaning": "Aaliyah and Left Eye were both R&B, and singers who died at a very young age. Aaliyah died in a plane crash, and Left Eye died in a car accident.\n\nGame is so high off his kush, that he believes he can actually see both of them in heaven.\n\n\n\nThis is not the first time game mentions the two, in his hit song “Dreams”, the hook goes:\n\nBlushin' in this 40 ounce\nlettin' the ink from my pen bleed\nCause Martin Luther King had a {dream}\nAaliyah had a {dream}, Left Eye had a {dream}", "annotation_id": "2779496", "url": "https://genius.com/2779496", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sing For Me", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Elijah-blake-sing-for-me-lyrics", "genius_title": "Sing For Me", "genius_id": 359710, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Single Again (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 1: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "From a 2008 Rolling Stone interview:\n\nYou did over a hundred guest appearances in the last year and a half. What’s the strangest request you’ve ever got?\nI get some crazy people asking me to do songs. The strangest one was probably Trina’s single, she asked to jump on “Single Again” when clearly [our breakup] was the subject of the song. That was kinda weird, but I did it.", "annotation_id": "8459901", "url": "https://genius.com/8459901", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
