{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "[Intro: Jessica Gomes] (May-May-May) What is this? (May-May-May) Maybach Music I like this Maybach Music, hahahaha", "vault_lines": ["I like this Maybach Music, hahahaha"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group is a record label founded by American rapper Rick Ross in 2008. An imprint of gamma. since 2023, the label was previously an imprint of Def Jam Recordings, Warner Records and Atlantic Records.\n\nThe “Maybach Music” vocal tag heard in many of the label’s recordings is spoken by Australian model Jessica Gomes. She talks about how she went on to say the tagline here.", "annotation_id": "34628476", "url": "https://genius.com/34628476", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "My G, he throwin’ that P-Stone", "vault_lines": ["my G, he throwin' that P-Stone"], "meaning": "The Almighty Black P. Stone Nation is a midwestern gang founded by Jeff Fort in Chicago in the 1950s.\n\n\n\nRoss’s G is throwing up their sign.", "annotation_id": "8050818", "url": "https://genius.com/8050818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Perfect time to relax Nothin’ is perfect other than me and the perfect match", "vault_lines": ["Perfect time to relax", "Nothin' is perfect other than me and the perfect match"], "meaning": "Rozay feels relaxed and at peace with this girl; while he knows that nothing is perfect in the world, he feels they’re perfect together\n\n\n\nThe idea that people can only achieve perfection through a perfect match has been around for millennia. In a famous example, the Greek philosopher Aristophanes argued that men and women were once one combined being, but were cut in half by the Gods. So they would walk around in search of their matching halves in order to make themselves whole again.", "annotation_id": "8044890", "url": "https://genius.com/8044890", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "She’s just perfect in every kinda way But I don’t think I can handle her pain So messed up and I’m too busy just runnin’ my game", "vault_lines": ["So messed up and I'm too busy just runnin' my game"], "meaning": "Actress and model Karrueche Tran is most likely the “she” in this story.\n\n\n\nThey’ve had an on-again, off-again relationship for years, with plenty of messed up behavior on Brown’s side having caused her pain.\n\nMost significantly, he fathered a child with another woman while they were still dating. Since then, he’s tried to win her back, but has generally made things worse—following her home from the club, dissing her in interviews, and yelling at her in public.", "annotation_id": "8044433", "url": "https://genius.com/8044433", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Every picture that you post, leave comments on each one", "vault_lines": ["Every picture that you post, leave comments on each one"], "meaning": "With a few thousand posts and 3.8 million followers, Ricky Rozay is very active on Instagram (“the gram”)\n\nSome funny things have happened in Ross’s Instagram comments: in 2014, people started flooded his Insta with pear emojis after Ross said “shout out to the pear” in an interview about his weight loss.", "annotation_id": "8044320", "url": "https://genius.com/8044320", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Rehab out in Vegas, that made this a murdered sin Sent the bottles to her table, then made love on the jet", "vault_lines": ["Rehab out in Vegas, that made this a murdered sin", "Sent the bottles to her table, then made love on the jet"], "meaning": "Rehab is a popular poolside dayclub in Las Vegas, where Ross has been spotted before—including at Meek Mill’s birthday party in 2013.", "annotation_id": "8044292", "url": "https://genius.com/8044292", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Temporary separations, confessin’ my mistakes She packed her bags and left me home and I’m still hurt You new pussy, but she can’t tell me that it’s real first A lot of lies, apologize, the thirst real When she hear this, thinkin’ to herself, “Damn, this verse real”", "vault_lines": ["Temporary separations, confessin' my mistakes", "She packed her bags and left me home and I'm still hurt"], "meaning": "Ross is telling his new girl about the girl who hurt him before—a classic dating no-no, but one you can get away with when you’re a boss.\n\nRoss has had a bit of a tumultuous dating history, so he could be talking about a lot of people. In 2013, he broke off an engagement with his longtime girlfriend Shateria Moragne-El.\n\nHe’s currently engaged to Lira Mercer (also known as Lira Galore), who’s a relatively new flame—they’d only been dating for a few months before he bought her a ring.\n\n\n\n(Damn, the thirst real)", "annotation_id": "8044234", "url": "https://genius.com/8044234", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Like a thug, I just wanna fuck, that’s every day", "vault_lines": ["Like a thug, I just wanna fuck, that's every day"], "meaning": "“Fuck her like a thug” was a line from Ross’s 2014 song “In Vein”.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qii92JK9qJU\n\nAccording to the Kinsey Institute, it’s actually pretty rare to fuck every day. Even among men with girlfriends, fewer than 10% have sex four or more times a week.", "annotation_id": "8044135", "url": "https://genius.com/8044135", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Temporary thrills, all these women you think I tossed My feelings genuine, disregard what you see on blogs", "vault_lines": ["Temporary thrills, all these women you think I tossed", "My feelings genuine, disregard what you see on blogs"], "meaning": "The blogs have been pretty intense on Ross and women recently—he’s been sued in a rape case by a woman who says she was drugged in his van, and accused of stealing a car from the mother of his child.\n\n\n\nRoss would prefer the woman he’s addressing to ignore these stories.", "annotation_id": "8043836", "url": "https://genius.com/8043836", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Get you a agent, she ballin’ and all she talk is money (Right) Take her shoppin’, baby boy, ain’t no salary caps (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Get you a agent, she ballin' and all she talk is money (Right)", "Take her shoppin', baby boy, ain't no salary caps (Uh)"], "meaning": "Ross compares a girl shopping to an NBA player demanding more money. She’s balling (living rich), and talks money like a baller would have an agent do. The salary cap in the NBA limits the total amount a team can pay its players, and the max salary any player can make—so without a salary cap, she’s running up whatever bill she wants.\n\nRoss is known to do some balling himself:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_w2se32-mao", "annotation_id": "8043694", "url": "https://genius.com/8043694", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Mill in cash on the ‘Gram, they trendin’ Meech home In the D", "vault_lines": ["Mill in cash on the 'Gram, they trendin' Meech home"], "meaning": "Ross compares his fan reception to a homecoming for imprisoned Detroit-based BMF (Black Mafia Family) drug kingpin Big Meech.\n\nRoss previously compared himself to Meech on his 2010 song “B.M.F. (Blowing Money Fast)” \n\n\n\n\nSome rappers took exception to Ross, a former corrections officer, dropping the name of a druglord (Ross already had taken his stage name from Freeway Rick Ross). \n\nYoung Jeezy even released a couple freestyle diss tracks. But Meech praised the song and defended Ross for using his name—Meech’s mother Lucille Flenory did too:\n\nI had no problem with the song. I understand that this is an artist doing his thing, so I had no problem with the song. I felt this was a way of acknowledging Meech and keeping his name out there. Not making him one of the forgotten souls.”", "annotation_id": "8043614", "url": "https://genius.com/8043614", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "They all watch me ’cause the moves I make out they budgets Diamond district, six figures on my shorty nugget", "vault_lines": ["They all watch me 'cause the moves I make out they budgets", "Diamond district, six figures on my shorty nugget"], "meaning": "In September 2015, Ross proposed to his girlfriend Lira Mercer with an 11 carat diamond ring from Rafaello & Co., located in NYC’s Diamond District. The ring set him back $350,000.\n\n\n\nThis move is way out of the budget of an ordinary person. A report from jewelers said the average American husband-to-be spends about $3,500 on a wedding ring, so that would make Ross’s ring a hundred times as much as most people can afford. He’s in the .1%", "annotation_id": "8014670", "url": "https://genius.com/8014670", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "[Produced by Scott Storch]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Scott Storch is notable for his piano work on Dr. Dre’s song “Still D.R.E.”, among a slew of hits in the 90s and early 2000s. While his piano skills have remained top-notch, his career and finances have been in bad shape in recent years. Storch declared bankruptcy in June 2015.\n\nHe told MTV:\n\nIt was the poor decisions I made, that were so poor financially, that caused me to go into this situation where I was forced to change my lifestyle … forced to change a lot of things. [I had] 15 to 20 cars at all times. That’s not smart. I would take one of 15 half-million-dollar cars I owned and go to the mall and spend that much money. Stupid, stupid stuff. It’s like it didn’t make a difference. They were ego investments. I would have been great with three or four cars! I didn’t need a 117-foot boat\"\n\nPost-bankruptcy, he mentioned in interviews that collaborations with Rick Ross and Chris Brown would hopefully alleviate his financial decadence.\n\nThis song is one of those collaborations.", "annotation_id": "7947655", "url": "https://genius.com/7947655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "[Chorus: Chris Brown]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In an interview with The Breakfast Club, Rozay breaks down the track and says the lyrics in this chorus were the basis for his own verses, and set the overall theme of the song.\n\nRoss says this song is intended to appeal to the ladies. The mellow vibe of Scott Storch’s production, mixed with Breezy’s singing, are key elements of this track.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?t=49&v=KesGJBz6f3U", "annotation_id": "7937487", "url": "https://genius.com/7937487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Oh, girl after girl, mistake after mistake", "vault_lines": ["Oh, girl after girl, mistake after mistake"], "meaning": "Brown has had a lot of high-profile girlfriends over the years, along with a lot of disastrous mistakes.\n\nHe dated Rihanna on-and-off from 2007 to 2013, with lots of notorious incidents, including a physical assault in 2009.\n\nThe assault stemmed from an argument around text messages Brown was sending to another woman, rumored to be his manager Tina Davis.\n\n\n\nHe’s had lots of other rumored short-term girlfriends, but the most lasting on-off relationship was with actress and model Karrueche Tran, likely the subject of this song. Their most notorious breakup came after she found out he’d fathered a child with another woman while they were dating.", "annotation_id": "7930728", "url": "https://genius.com/7930728", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Them red bottoms got you walkin’ funny (Ha)", "vault_lines": ["Them red bottoms got you walkin' funny (Ha)"], "meaning": "Red Bottoms are a patented design shoe from Christian Louboutin which seperates them from other shoes because of their blood red soles.\n\n\n\nThe particularly high heels and narrow heels make them hard to walk in—Rozay’s lady is experiencing that difficulty.", "annotation_id": "7929446", "url": "https://genius.com/7929446", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "She get it poppin’, so you better bring battery packs (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["She get it poppin', so you better bring battery packs (Huh)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' girl is about to go on a shopping spree, but she needs his spending power behind her. Rozay uses “battery packs” as a metaphor for credit cards; thanks to him, she can “charge” it all.", "annotation_id": "7927994", "url": "https://genius.com/7927994", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "[Verse 3: Chris Brown]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "You don’t know what you got ‘till it’s gone\n\nChris realizes that one of many reasons of his break up with Karrueche Tran was his lack of compassion. He keeps promising to improve, yet repeatedly makes the same mistakes. In this verse, he expresses regret for that behavior.\n\nShortly before the release, Chris took to Instagram to announce the single.\n\n\n\nHe may have addressed that relationship before. There was speculation that his single Zero, released on September 25, 2015, addressed that breakup—but it expressed a much different sentiment than this song, saying that Brown didn’t care about the woman he was singing to.", "annotation_id": "7927443", "url": "https://genius.com/7927443", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Steppin’ on your heart again, relationship ruined [Pre-Chorus: Chris Brown, Rick Ross] I tried to change, but I’m always out, fuckin’ around in the club (May-May)", "vault_lines": ["Steppin' on your heart again, relationship ruined", "I tried to change, but I'm always out, fuckin' around in the club (May-May)"], "meaning": "As mentioned before, Chris Brown and Tran have had a very tumultuous relationship. In this verse, he takes on the blame for the relationship, acknowledging that his actions were the primary reason that she left him.\n\n\n\nThe club was the setting of a lot of his misdeeds—both his affairs with other women, and a few altercations with Karrueche herself.  He knows he gets in trouble there, but still feels the need to go out and “fuck around.”", "annotation_id": "7927135", "url": "https://genius.com/7927135", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Sorry won’t turn back the clock Baby, I took advantage ’cause I knew you Wouldn’t believe it, so I used you I’m sorry, oh But sorry don’t make it right, I know (May-May-May)", "vault_lines": ["Sorry won't turn back the clock", "Baby, I took advantage 'cause I knew you", "Wouldn't believe it, so I used you", "But sorry don't make it right, I know (May-May-May)"], "meaning": "This is no lie—Chris Brown has had his fair share of trials and tribulations with women. Breezy complains at times that “these hoes ain’t loyal” but at other times expresses remorse. A prime example of this is his interview with SwaysUniverse on April 3, 2013.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y8XDQDgQJM\nAs for Rick Ross, he finds himself in controversy with women from time to time as well.\n\nThe hook serves as a sort of apology to both men’s exes, but with an acknowledgement that an apology can’t undo their wrongs.", "annotation_id": "7926315", "url": "https://genius.com/7926315", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "I tried to change, but they always around pullin’ me down in bed (May-May) Gave you my word, but they were just broken promises (Uh) Broken condoms, lipstick marks and unprotected sex (Uh) I feel like shit, you know I ain’t shit", "vault_lines": ["I tried to change, but they always around pullin' me down in bed (May-May)", "Gave you my word, but they were just broken promises (Uh)", "Broken condoms, lipstick marks and unprotected sex (Uh)", "I feel like shit, you know I ain't shit"], "meaning": "Brown blames the other women for tempting him into his dalliances, but also blames himself for breaking his promises. It’s true that he’s had lots of chances to cheat—it’s also true that he’s often taken them.\n\n\n\nThe “unprotected sex” line is especially significant. He impregnated a woman named Nia Guzman while still dating Karrueche. In October 2015 he made amends with Guzman, and they agreed to “co-parent” their daughter Royalty.", "annotation_id": "7925642", "url": "https://genius.com/7925642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "Life’s short and, baby girl, you deserve a winner Every day the diamonds on you get bigger and bigger Hustle from my heart, so every night I can deliver (Uh) Sayin’ sorry, layin’ up, I’m way up in your liver (Boss)", "vault_lines": ["Life's short and, baby girl, you deserve a winner", "Every day the diamonds on you get bigger and bigger", "Hustle from my heart, so every night I can deliver (Uh)", "Sayin' sorry, layin' up, I'm way up in your liver (Boss)"], "meaning": "Ross wants to give his lady everything, including diamonds, which are often thought of as a girl’s best friend.\n\nRozay is indeed a winner; five of his seven major label albums have landed at No. 1 on the Billboard Hot 100. Not only that, Ross is the head of the highly successful Maybach Music Group record label and he owns 25 Wingstop restaurants.\n\n\n\nAll of these money-making ventures and the “hustle” from Ross' “heart” will ensure that he can give his girl all of the diamonds that she desires—though we’ll assume that he is taking poetic license when he promises to deliver a new jewel “every day.”\n\nThen, at the end of the day, if Ross' girl still isn’t happy, he will plan a night of unmatched passion. It all sounds like make-up sex, as the Boss will apologize while moving his member as deep as humanly possibly.", "annotation_id": "7925205", "url": "https://genius.com/7925205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "I been a boss before I recorded Meek song", "vault_lines": ["I been a boss before I recorded Meek song"], "meaning": "In 2011, Rick Ross appeared on Meek Mill’s “Ima Boss” single, but Rozay first crowned himself the boss way before that.\n\nRoss titled the second single from his 2008 Trilla “The Boss”. Even before that, on Trina’s 2002 single “Told Y'all” a then-unknown Rick rapped: “Y'all niggas wanna fuck wit Ross, Point a mile who really wanna touch the boss.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NEu03bmxiZk&feature=youtu.be&t=2m33s", "annotation_id": "7924816", "url": "https://genius.com/7924816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "line": "We at the crib, she got her legs wrapped around my waist Conversatin’, she lick every tattoo that’s on my face", "vault_lines": ["We at the crib, she got her legs wrapped around my waist", "Conversatin', she lick every tattoo that's on my face"], "meaning": "Rick Ross and his lady are in the throes of passion; here he paints the picture. Though she currently has her legs wrapped around Rozay’s waist, a few years ago this may have been more difficult for the young lady.\n\nIn December 2014, Ross spoke to “Good Morning America” about shedding 85 pounds thanks to some dietary changes and his patented “RossFit” training program.\n\nRoss' lady friend doesn’t stop there, she also licks all the tattoos on his face. He has seven tattoos on his face, including Meek Mill’s Dream Chasers logo, the Miami Heat logo and his own Maybach Music logo.", "annotation_id": "7924720", "url": "https://genius.com/7924720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sorry", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-sorry-lyrics", "genius_title": "Sorry", "genius_id": 2322530, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "Three squares on a row, call it 3rd Bass Get the Gas Face, chopper in your laugh face", "vault_lines": ["Three squares on a row, call it 3rd Bass", "Get the Gas Face, chopper in your laugh face"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the baseball field, where there are four bases. Each of them are square-shaped and connect in a square pattern around the infield. In this sense, Ross is talking about selling three bricks of drugs in a row. Impressive!\n\nAdditionally, Ross is referencing the late-80’s rap group 3rd Bass, known for their hit “Gas Face.”", "annotation_id": "17752159", "url": "https://genius.com/17752159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "Bitch I know Haitians, we speakin Creole", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I know Haitians, we speakin Creole"], "meaning": "Rozay’s plug is from the small island nation of Haiti, and he interacts with him strictly in Haitian Creole (which is a mix of various Niger–Congo languages with French). It’s hard to confirm or deny this because Rozay was found to not actually know the real Noriega.\n\nhttp://nahright.com/2006/02/23/breaking-rick-ross-doesnt-know-noriega/", "annotation_id": "10388842", "url": "https://genius.com/10388842", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "[Intro: Ving Rhames]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Irving Rameses “Ving” Rhames is an African-American actor best known for his roles in  Bringing Out the Dead, Pulp Fiction and the Mission: Impossible series.\n\nHere, Rhames introduces Ludacris.", "annotation_id": "8275658", "url": "https://genius.com/8275658", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "Keep Jewish friends, the newest Benz", "vault_lines": ["Keep Jewish friends, the newest Benz"], "meaning": "Ross is an honorary Jew in hip hop circles. He utilises the link between Jewish people and money here, to show his own wealth, confirmed by his taste in cars.", "annotation_id": "6754851", "url": "https://genius.com/6754851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "And mac-11's that leave you wetter than Michael Phelps! (woo!) But you’ll be swimmin with the fishes", "vault_lines": ["And mac-11's that leave you wetter than Michael Phelps! (woo!)", "But you'll be swimmin with the fishes"], "meaning": "Multiple weapons means multiple threats, and in the hands of Ludacris, deadly enough to have his enemies wetting themselves in fear, an even more potent form of saturation than Michael Phelps' gruelling training regime.\n\nSwimming with the fishes is an idiom for being murdered. Luda flips the “wetness” theme three separate times in these two lines, interlocking it with murder.", "annotation_id": "6754834", "url": "https://genius.com/6754834", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "The MVP of this rap shit", "vault_lines": ["The MVP of this rap shit"], "meaning": "MVP is known in sports such as basketball and football as the Most Valuable Player. Ving Rhames is calling Luda the MVP of hip-hop.\n\nThis term was made popular by one of the finest MCs ever in this classic.", "annotation_id": "6754827", "url": "https://genius.com/6754827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "A true entrepre-negro", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A portmanteau on the words entrepreneur and negro to mean self made, successful, black businessman.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/jayzclassicbars/status/573694943702679553", "annotation_id": "6754823", "url": "https://genius.com/6754823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "He expanded his empire into multiple profitable businesses Including his Thai food restaurant, Straits Internet sites, WeMix.com And my favorite, MyGhetto.com", "vault_lines": ["He expanded his empire into multiple profitable businesses", "Including his Thai food restaurant, Straits"], "meaning": "A list of some of Luda’s businesses outside of rap music.\nAn Asian based bar & restaurant in Atlanta called Straits, now closed.\nTwo music websites,  WeMix.com/MyGhetto.com, both of which have also since shut down.", "annotation_id": "6754821", "url": "https://genius.com/6754821", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "CEO of Disturbing Tha Peace Records", "vault_lines": ["CEO of Disturbing Tha Peace Records"], "meaning": "DTP records was formed by Ludacris, Chaka Zulu and Jeff Dixon back in 2000. It operates under Def Jam and is based in Atlanta, Georgia.", "annotation_id": "6754812", "url": "https://genius.com/6754812", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "We roll like bicycles, icicle flow", "vault_lines": ["We roll like bicycles, icicle flow"], "meaning": "Roll here can refer to a variety of things.\n\n· Rolling weed\n· Rolling in money\n· Rolling as in driving around\n\nHis icicle flow is a more creative way of explaining just how cold his rhyming ability is.", "annotation_id": "6754789", "url": "https://genius.com/6754789", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "Uhh, I’m so sick I wrote this verse in a hospital", "vault_lines": ["Uhh, I'm so sick I wrote this verse in a hospital"], "meaning": "“Sick” implies dopeness. Rappers spend their lives trying to work out clever ways of rapping about just how sick they are. Tity Boi certainly hasn’t unearthed a new method here..", "annotation_id": "6754783", "url": "https://genius.com/6754783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "Bitches catch kudos (you know)", "vault_lines": ["Bitches catch kudos (you know)"], "meaning": "‘Kudos,’ coming from ancient Greek, is a congratulatory statement to someone who’s done a great job. Tity Boi congratulates the bitches for fucking him right, but now it’s time for them to leave.", "annotation_id": "3299075", "url": "https://genius.com/3299075", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "He’s the biggest boss, comin outta the M-I-yayo Straight from the “Port of Miami” To keepin it “Trilla” Involved in many heated acts of violence This goes deeper than rap shit", "vault_lines": ["He's the biggest boss, comin outta the M-I-yayo", "Straight from the \"Port of Miami\"", "To keepin it \"Trilla\"", "Involved in many heated acts of violence", "This goes deeper than rap shit"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is a rapper from the city of Miami, which is known to have a long history of cocaine trafficking; ‘yayo’ is slang for cocaine. Ross himself raps as a cocaine and drug kingpin, which establishes his relationship to the drug.\n\nPort of Miami, Trilla, and Deeper Than Rap are the first three albums by Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "3299056", "url": "https://genius.com/3299056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "Luda! I’m a hustler, BALLER, gangsta, CAP PEELER", "vault_lines": ["Luda! I'm a hustler, BALLER, gangsta, CAP PEELER"], "meaning": "Its no secret Luda’s all of this things. His hustle is on point, and he balls off of his hustle. When someone is referred to as a “Cap Peeler”it means that they kill people. Generally by shooting their heads (caps) in order to cause a peeling affect.\n\nAlso a cap peeler can be one who just shoots guns in general. Plus clips are often shaped like bananas and bananas are peeled.", "annotation_id": "1656082", "url": "https://genius.com/1656082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "I keep my ear to the STREETS like a cocker spaniel", "vault_lines": ["I keep my ear to the STREETS like a cocker spaniel"], "meaning": "The ears of cocker spaniels hang low, sometimes touching the street", "annotation_id": "632744", "url": "https://genius.com/632744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Southern Gangsta", "line": "I got a letter from the government, the other day I opened and read it, it said “We were hustlers”", "vault_lines": ["I got a letter from the government, the other day", "I opened and read it, it said \"We were hustlers\""], "meaning": "This is a slightly altered interpolation of lines from Public Enemy’s “Black Steel in the Hour of Chaos”:\n\nI got a letter from the government the other day\nI opened and read it, it said they were suckers", "annotation_id": "248490", "url": "https://genius.com/248490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
