{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stack On My Belt", "line": "My soldiers real in the field, you WWE", "vault_lines": ["My soldiers real in the field, you WWE"], "meaning": "Wale and his crew are true, and if they say they are going to do something, you best believe they are going to do it.\n\nThe WWE is a professional wrestling organization, which resembles you being an actor, and not real, just like a WWE superstar. Although, many people believe professional wrestling is real (especially young kids).", "annotation_id": "2221092", "url": "https://genius.com/2221092", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stack On My Belt", "line": "Self Made niggas man, you already know", "vault_lines": ["Self Made niggas man, you already know"], "meaning": "This track, and in fact the whole album, features some heavy hitters.  Many of them came up on their own, including two huge names on this track: Rick Ross and Birdman.\n\nBirdman is truly self-made, having co-founded Cash Money Records. In 2013, he has a net worth estimated at $150 million according to Rap Genius contributor and Forbes staff writer Zack O'Malley Greenburg.", "annotation_id": "2220939", "url": "https://genius.com/2220939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stack On My Belt", "line": "Don’t believe y’all Kane stories, I should leave y’all undertaking", "vault_lines": ["Don't believe y'all Kane stories, I should leave y'all undertaking"], "meaning": "Kane and the Undertaker are fictional brothers from WWE. Wale continues to use the WWE wordplay theme in his verse.\n\nCane is another word for cocaine. Wale is saying that their stories about coke are as fake as professional wrestling.", "annotation_id": "2215371", "url": "https://genius.com/2215371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stack On My Belt", "line": "Of course we see ’em punks faking", "vault_lines": ["Of course we see 'em punks faking"], "meaning": "He pronounces “see them punks” as “C M Punks.” CM Punk is a wrestler which references Wale’s previous line about WWE. Of course wrestling is fake so it plays into the reference.", "annotation_id": "2215358", "url": "https://genius.com/2215358", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stack On My Belt", "line": "And when I hit that Heat game, I’m this close to LeBron", "vault_lines": ["And when I hit that Heat game, I'm this close to LeBron"], "meaning": "When Wale is in Miami enjoying the Miami Heat basketball game, he sits courtside, close enough to even trip one of the players.\n\nOf course these seats aren’t cheap, but it shouldn’t be a problem for Wale.", "annotation_id": "2213863", "url": "https://genius.com/2213863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
