{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Star Island", "line": "“Don dada” (Don dada)", "vault_lines": ["Yes, they call me, \"Don dada\" (Don dada)"], "meaning": "The expression “Don Dada” comes from Jamaican slang and is widely used in hip-hop and reggae culture. It means something like “the top boss,” “the leading figure,” or “the one who runs everything.", "annotation_id": "37723756", "url": "https://genius.com/37723756", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Star Island", "line": "The bottles are black (Black)", "vault_lines": ["Kobe and Shaq (Shaq), the bottles are black (Black)"], "meaning": "In his songs, Rick Ross often mentions the champagne brand Luc Belaire, which is distinguished by its black bottles. Rick Ross not only promotes it but also owns a stake in the brand.", "annotation_id": "37723741", "url": "https://genius.com/37723741", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
