{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "State of the Union", "line": "Smell the kilos on me, now we flippin’ burgers", "vault_lines": ["Smell the kilos on me, now we flippin' burgers"], "meaning": "Kilos is slang for kilograms of cocaine. Ross has a past of selling cocaine as a young man growing up in the hood. Now, he no longer sells cocaine; he flips burgers. Ross owns multiple franchises of Wingstop, a fast-food chain. Rick Ross went from selling cocaine to owning franchises of burger-selling chains.", "annotation_id": "33384524", "url": "https://genius.com/33384524", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "State of the Union", "line": "So, I ain’t got to kneel just to stand with you (Uh-uh)", "vault_lines": ["So, I ain’t got to kneel just to stand with you (Uh-uh)"], "meaning": "U.S. national anthem kneeling protests were a set of protests by athletes criticizing the issue of police brutality in the U.S.A. In these protests, athletes kneeled during the national anthem. This lyric is a play on words, as Jim Jones is essentially stating that he does not need to participate in these protests for people to know that he is on their side.", "annotation_id": "26708114", "url": "https://genius.com/26708114", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "State of the Union", "line": "You could build a wall as tall as the sky (To the moon) We all know the coke still go far from the sky", "vault_lines": ["You could build a wall as tall as the sky (To the moon)"], "meaning": "The American President wants to build a  great wall on the Mexican border to control illegal immigrants and drug trafficking. Jimmy says it’s clear that the wall won’t hinder drugs from reaching America, even if it takes the southern cartels dropping consignments from the sky because we all know they work tirelessly.", "annotation_id": "18263750", "url": "https://genius.com/18263750", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "State of the Union", "line": "Pushin’ Phantoms, so they feel I’m preachin’ propaganda", "vault_lines": ["Pushin' Phantoms, so they feel I'm preachin' propaganda"], "meaning": "Pushin' Phantoms, so they feel I’m preachin' propaganda,…meaning because he is driving an expensive car such as a Phantom, he must be pushing the very propaganda that it destroying our communities.", "annotation_id": "17367723", "url": "https://genius.com/17367723", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
