{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Steppin’ Out", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yung-q-steppin-out-lyrics", "genius_title": "Steppin’ Out", "genius_id": 10074332, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Fucking with my niggas, I’ll smoke a zip Redd Eyezz, and I got them Zoes with me", "vault_lines": ["Fucking with my niggas, I'll smoke a zip", "Redd Eyezz, and I got them Zoes with me"], "meaning": "A “zip” is an ounce of marijuana. Future and his boys aren’t light smokers, they go all the way. Getting red eyes is a common side-effect of being high.\n\nA “Zoe” is someone of Haitian descent.", "annotation_id": "8445584", "url": "https://genius.com/8445584", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "10 million dollars cash, fuck a friend", "vault_lines": ["10 million dollars cash, fuck a friend"], "meaning": "Future lives by the “M.O.E. Code” – money over everything – getting money is his main priority while everything else isn’t as important.\n\nAdditionally, he might be showing disgust to the “fake” friends who only come around now that he’s wealthy. He foreshadows this sentiment on “Blow A Bag”:\n\nI know that money can change niggas\nThey don’t look at you like you the same nigga", "annotation_id": "8445575", "url": "https://genius.com/8445575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Riding in a car I barely can pronounce Ordered up a chauffeur, told him “ride me round the whole world” I was on the E-way with that molly and that old girl", "vault_lines": ["Riding in a car I barely can pronounce", "Ordered up a chauffeur, told him \"ride me round the whole world\"", "I was on the E-way with that molly and that old girl"], "meaning": "Perhaps he’s riding in a Pagani Huayra? A Koenigsegg Regara? A Maserati Ghibli? An Alfa Romeo Giulietta? A Rolls-Royce Camargue? Whatever it is, Future can surely afford the most exotic of cars.\n\nThe “E-way” is short for the expressway; he’s on his way to sell drugs. “Molly” is another word for MDMA or Ecstasy, and “that old girl” refers to cocaine. Future’s status is so grand that he’s equipped with chauffeurs even in times when he’s committing illegal activities.", "annotation_id": "8445572", "url": "https://genius.com/8445572", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Oxycontin got her with a body count (sak pase)", "vault_lines": ["Oxycontin got her with a body count (sak pase)"], "meaning": "Oxycontins are opiates designed to ease pain. There’s a high risk that these pills can become addictive, which could lead to people overdosing on them. In that way, they’re “catching bodies,” taking the life of the users.\n\n“Sak Pase” is a Creole greeting roughly translated to “what’s up?”\n\nhttps://twitter.com/1future/status/600394202980159488", "annotation_id": "8445571", "url": "https://genius.com/8445571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Took a shot of Henny, I’ve been going brazy, brazy", "vault_lines": ["Took a shot of Henny, I've been going brazy, brazy"], "meaning": "The alcohol made him go crazy. Bloods typically replace the letter “C” in a word with “B” or “K,” to avoid association with the Crips.\n\nAs Future himself isn’t gang-affiliated, this is likely paying homage to the late A$AP Yams, whose final tweet before he died was “Bodeine Brazy” (a shoutout to the Future’s “Codeine Crazy”).\n\nhttps://twitter.com/ASAPYams/status/556334494048067584\n\nHowever, Future is a part of the FreeBandz crew, which, although is not exclusive to any one gang, is known to have many members of both 9-Tre Bloods as well as II and Sex Money Murder.", "annotation_id": "8445557", "url": "https://genius.com/8445557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Send the boy a bottle, wack ’em in the club over", "vault_lines": ["Send the boy a bottle, wack 'em in the club over"], "meaning": "Pretty mobster-like of Rozay here.\nHe sends over a bottle to you of his preferred choice then when you think he has let his guard down Rozay comes back to hit you with one when the party’s over.\nThat’s when your guard is down and you are thinking Rozay is your friend.\n\nIts could also play to the allusion “fattening the sacrificial lamb” in which the lamb is first fed to become fat then slaughtered after.\nHere Rozay could be simply getting the target drunk then without warning as he leaves the party he is whacked.\n\nWhacking in [mobster glossary] refers to being killed not the cartoon representation of the word.", "annotation_id": "8069283", "url": "https://genius.com/8069283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Slaughter niggas like cattle, killas from overseas", "vault_lines": ["Slaughter niggas like cattle, killas from overseas"], "meaning": "In line with the beef theme Rozay will definitely turn a scene into a slaughterhouse and get to murdering like it’s a normal thing to do.\n\n\n\nAs for his killers, He even gives you a hint just where they might come from", "annotation_id": "8069216", "url": "https://genius.com/8069216", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Not allowed to ride in the coupe if you didn’t suffer with us", "vault_lines": ["Not allowed to ride in the coupe if you didn't suffer with us"], "meaning": "This is a prevalent theme in the rap game which reminds us our “day ones” are pretty much worth riding with us since they have been with us when we didn’t have these things.", "annotation_id": "8067446", "url": "https://genius.com/8067446", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Two way with Jigga nigga show you what this white ‘bout", "vault_lines": ["Two way with Jigga nigga show you what this white ‘bout"], "meaning": "Two powerful men in the music industry according to affluence and how they represent themselves in their music.\nJay-Z:A former drug dealer and Rick Ross:A former police officer who was able to make a living off cocaine rap who all know a thing or two about pushing cocaine can teach you a thing or two about this", "annotation_id": "8067303", "url": "https://genius.com/8067303", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Cut off the phones well protected in my white house", "vault_lines": ["Cut off the phones well protected in my white house"], "meaning": "Rozay is currently under house arrest and while he is here he wants his utmost privacy, however this has not been the case as with his Snapchat that shows the world what is behind the closed doors via his smartphone", "annotation_id": "8067225", "url": "https://genius.com/8067225", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "Fuckin’ two jewish bitches while I got “Black Dollar” bumpin’", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin’ two jewish bitches while I got “Black Dollar” bumpin’"], "meaning": "Not one to follow tradition aye?\n\nRozay here shows his audacious move towards breaking the laws set for Kosher Sex with the two ladies which shows that as he is a bad boy he also attracts the same characteristic of people to him. Guess money makes people do crazy things.\n\nThe allusion to a threesome is something which in the past was available to kings, emperors as well as people in high places as well as those of great affluence and as such when Rick Ross speaks of this he reminds us he is a king as he once told us before", "annotation_id": "8067052", "url": "https://genius.com/8067052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stick Talk (Remix)", "line": "AK-47 bussin’ it got these niggas duckin’", "vault_lines": ["AK-47 bussin’ it got these niggas duckin’"], "meaning": "As with Rick Ross, there is always some war business going on so this is just but a reminder that bullets from the Kalashnikov will have you ducking down when they start getting fired by Ross.\n\n\n\nFun Fact: AK-47 is officially known in the Soviet documentation as Avtomat Kalashnikova. Now you know where the AK abbreviation comes from.", "annotation_id": "8066938", "url": "https://genius.com/8066938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
