{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stop", "line": "It disappeared cos I’m David Blaine", "vault_lines": ["It disappeared cos I'm David Blaine"], "meaning": "David Blaine is an American illusionist and endurance artist. He has traveled internationally performing magic privately for Bill Clinton, George Bush, Donald Rumsfeld, Arnold Schwarzenegger, Henry Kissinger, Bill Gates and Michael Bloomberg.\n\nHe is well known for his magic trick where he disappears.", "annotation_id": "2182404", "url": "https://genius.com/2182404", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stop", "line": "A young Suge Knight but I’m stranded down in Florida", "vault_lines": ["A young Suge Knight but I'm stranded down in Florida"], "meaning": "Marion Hugh Knight Jr, better known as Suge Knight, is the founder and CEO of Black Kapital Records and co-founder and former CEO of Death Row Records. Death Row Records rose to dominate the rap charts after Dr. Dre’s album The Chronic in 1992.", "annotation_id": "2182401", "url": "https://genius.com/2182401", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stop", "line": "Grey rims hit the corner, I’m burning the California", "vault_lines": ["Grey rims hit the corner, I'm burning the California"], "meaning": "He’s burning the wheels of his Ferrari California, a grand touring sports car produced by the Italian manufacturer Ferrari. The phrase could also be perceived as referring to the lighting and smoking of cigarettes wrapped in California-grown marijuana.", "annotation_id": "2182396", "url": "https://genius.com/2182396", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stop", "line": "Leaning on grey juice, it’s better than Grey Goose", "vault_lines": ["Leaning on grey juice, it's better than Grey Goose"], "meaning": "Grey Goose) is a Bacardi-owned vodka produced in France. Among French vodkas, Grey Goose has some competitors, as the French vodkas Monte Carlo and Ice Cube are also now on the market, as well as the German Lumb and Swedish Karlssons brands.", "annotation_id": "2182392", "url": "https://genius.com/2182392", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stop", "line": "But we don’t wear that Bape shit", "vault_lines": ["But we don't wear that Bape shit"], "meaning": "Bape is a Japanese clothing company founded by Nigo in 1993. The company specialises in men’s, women’s and kids' lifestyle and street wear, running nineteen stores in Japan, including Bape Stores, Bape Pirate Stores, Bape Kids Stores and Bap Exclusive Aoyama.", "annotation_id": "2182387", "url": "https://genius.com/2182387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Stop", "line": "From out there, niggas can’t tell it’s Louis Vuitton", "vault_lines": ["From out there, niggas can't tell it's Louis Vuitton"], "meaning": "Louis Vuitton is a French fashion house founded in 1854 by Louis Vuitton. The label’s LV monogram appears on most of its products, ranging from luxury trunks and leather goods to ready-to-wear, shoes, watches, jewellery, accessories, sunglasses, and books.", "annotation_id": "2182384", "url": "https://genius.com/2182384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
