{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Street Life", "line": "My nigga E showed me", "vault_lines": ["My nigga E showed me"], "meaning": "Eazy-E was a popular rapper and friend who was killed early in his life. Real name Eric Lynn Wright, he died March 26, 1995 from AIDS only ten days after announcing to the public that he had them.", "annotation_id": "1474962", "url": "https://genius.com/1474962", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Street Life", "line": "Now a penthouse, you can call me Hi-Top", "vault_lines": ["Now a penthouse, you can call me Hi-Top"], "meaning": "This is a pun, as the penthouse is the top, most expensive apartment or room in an apartment building or hotel. He’s saying he’s at the top of the game, so he’s in the penthouse, and he’s so rich, that he’s in the penthouse.\n\nHi-Tops are expensive shoes with “high tops”, further playing on the fact that’s he’s at the very top.", "annotation_id": "1402861", "url": "https://genius.com/1402861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
