{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Summer Seventeen", "line": "I had to park that purple Lamborghini​ (yummm) And pull that Chevy back out on the cement (huh)", "vault_lines": ["I had to park that purple Lamborghini​ (yummm)", "And pull that Chevy back out on the cement (huh)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is changing vehicles cause he is going from the glamourous Hollywood hills back to the trap.\nIt’s also a reference to the smash hit record, Purple Lamborghini, that he did with Skrillex for the soundtrack of Suicide Squad.", "annotation_id": "26920156", "url": "https://genius.com/26920156", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Summer Seventeen", "line": "I want my niggas rich by summer seventeen (let’s get it) I want my niggas rich by summer seventeen I want my niggas rich by summer seventeen (All my niggas! I’m talking all my niggas!) I want my niggas rich by summer seventeen (Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": ["I want my niggas rich by summer seventeen (let's get it)"], "meaning": "Ross has made it his duty to make sure his team eats alongside him by the summertime of 2017. Just like he stated on “Triple Platinum”:\n\nYou not a boss ‘til everybody at your table ate\n\nHe preached this same sentiment at Birdman on the track “Idols Become Rivals.”\n\nHow the fuck, nigga, you touch half a billion, nigga\nAnd your team starvin', nigga?", "annotation_id": "13440132", "url": "https://genius.com/13440132", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Summer Seventeen", "line": "Put that voodoo on you niggas so that gun’ll jam", "vault_lines": ["Put that voodoo on you niggas so that gun'll jam"], "meaning": "This line is an extension of the previous line dealing with Haitians. Voodoo has deep cultural associations within the Haitian culture. Here Ross implies that his Haitian connections provide him some protection against his enemies.", "annotation_id": "12811058", "url": "https://genius.com/12811058", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Summer Seventeen", "line": "I’m out on bond so I gotta beat it (Lord) Half a million to my lawyer ’cause he undefeated", "vault_lines": ["Half a million to my lawyer 'cause he undefeated"], "meaning": "Unlike bail where the defendant (Ross) pays cash to the court, a bond is a pledge made by a third party (known as a bondsman), who is then responsible for the defendant’s debt.\n\n\n\nThe bondsman has to pay the bail if Ross doesn’t show up to court. He can then overcharge Ross for the inconvenience, and Ross would rather avoid that.\n\nLuckily for Ross, he has one of the best lawyers in the business. He’s willing to drop as much as $500,000 as a retainer so he won’t spend long periods in prison.", "annotation_id": "11714146", "url": "https://genius.com/11714146", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Summer Seventeen", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-summer-seventeen-lyrics", "genius_title": "Summer Seventeen", "genius_id": 3019841, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sun Come Up", "line": "Got more money so we spent more crazy", "vault_lines": ["Got more money so we spent more crazy"], "meaning": "This is the sound that Bloods make to call out to other Bloods to let them know that they are in the area/a greeting to other Bloods", "annotation_id": "2208631", "url": "https://genius.com/2208631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sun Come Up", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-and-birdman-sun-come-up-lyrics", "genius_title": "Sun Come Up", "genius_id": 154620, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "I just wanna let my top down But I’m still runnin’ from the dark cloud It got me prayin’ for some sunshine", "vault_lines": ["I just wanna let my top down", "But I'm still runnin' from the dark cloud", "It got me prayin' for some sunshine"], "meaning": "Ross wants to live worry free but he has a lot of pain that follows him and he prays that it will all just go away\n\nDark Clouds are a sign of gloomy weather and can lead to gloomy attitudes but sunshine symbolizes happiness", "annotation_id": "3014974", "url": "https://genius.com/3014974", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "I’m drinkin’ Cabernet, think of better days", "vault_lines": ["I'm drinkin' Cabernet, think of better days"], "meaning": "Cabernet is one of the most recognized red grape wines, Common is drinking Cabernet thinking about how far he’s come and how he can build on his success", "annotation_id": "3014957", "url": "https://genius.com/3014957", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Used to hold back like a masseuse", "vault_lines": ["Used to hold back like a masseuse"], "meaning": "In the previous lines, Common mentions him holding weapons and losing control sometimes.\n\nIn this line, he talks about him “holding back” or refraining from these violent acts. Just like a masseuse would “hold back,” except in a literal sense.\n\nMasseuse – A woman whose job is to give massages\n\n\n\nCommon has spit a line like this before in a song released back in 1994 on his LP Resurrection, he said:\n\nWhen I’m off that Cognac I can’t hold back like a masseuse", "annotation_id": "3011224", "url": "https://genius.com/3011224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "I hold the MAC that Them panthers and the black cats used to hold", "vault_lines": ["I hold the MAC that", "Them panthers and the black cats used to hold"], "meaning": "Common is holding the same weapon that the notoriously violent Black Panther Party members used to hold. Specifically mentioned was a “MAC,” most likely a MAC-10 or MAC-11.\n\n\n\nWORDPLAY!\n\nCommon is tying this line together very nicely by using the word cat as substitute for “person” or “people” because the majority of black people during the Black Panther Party era were seen as violent or over-aggressive. Which is why’d they’d be holding these weapons. All in all, a black panther is a black cat.\n\nCat – A person, usually male and generally considered or thought to be cool.", "annotation_id": "3011212", "url": "https://genius.com/3011212", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Cover my body with ink, I never cherished the flesh", "vault_lines": ["Cover my body with ink, I never cherished the flesh"], "meaning": "Rick Ross doesn’t really care too much about if his skin is covered in tattoos or not and has never really bought in to the saying, “Your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit.”\n\nSo, he covered his skin with ink (tattoos).", "annotation_id": "3011193", "url": "https://genius.com/3011193", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Nigga lace up your sneakers and go and get some respect", "vault_lines": ["Nigga lace up your sneakers and go and get some respect"], "meaning": "“Lace up your sneakers” or “lace up your boots” is a popular phrase meaning to get ready or prepare yourself for whatever task you’re up against.\n\nYou would lace up your boots when you see The Notorious B.I.G coming through:\n\nSo lace up your boots, cause I’m about to shoot\n\nRozay is simply telling you to get ready to go out and earn your respect.", "annotation_id": "3011186", "url": "https://genius.com/3011186", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "You hold your head to the sky, you put your face in the light Makaveli the Don, I pray I make it tonight", "vault_lines": ["You hold your head to the sky, you put your face in the light", "Makaveli the Don, I pray I make it tonight"], "meaning": "With all the mistakes people make, sometimes we just pray to make it to tomorrow. After all, in Makaveli’s own words:\n\nIf you can make it through the night, there’s a brighter day\n\nRoss is praying to the late 2Pac, aka Makaveli the Don – peep this annotation off one of Pac’s classics for more info on the origins of this name.", "annotation_id": "3011165", "url": "https://genius.com/3011165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "They never said that the odds were fair Now we standin’ in line for that Obamacare", "vault_lines": ["They never said that the odds were fair", "Now we standin' in line for that Obamacare"], "meaning": "Many African Americans are poorer and are lacking health care in proportion to their presence in the American population when compared to Caucasian Americans. Obamacare is a law that allows health care to be more affordable for all Americans. This puts black people more at odds with the white majority who already have health care.", "annotation_id": "3011062", "url": "https://genius.com/3011062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "The fruits of my labor is to produce On Netflix watchin’ Juice I wanna 2pac the people That mean keep ’em regal, at the same time lethal", "vault_lines": ["The fruits of my labor is to produce", "On Netflix watchin' Juice", "I wanna 2pac the people", "That mean keep 'em regal, at the same time lethal"], "meaning": "Common continues to drop some serious wordplay with these bars!\n\nTo “reap the fruits of one’s labor” – a phrase stemming from Pslam 128:2 – means to enjoy the benefits of your hard work. Of course, produce is a synonym for fruit, which is used to make juice.\n\nJuice, however, is also the name of the film 2Pac first starred in and you can watch it on Netflix.\n\n\n\n2Pac is often heralded as one of rap’s greatest artists of all time. However, he also seemed never to stray too far from conflict – hence Com’s reference to being regal and lethal at the same time. This 2Pac reference follows from Ross’s in the first verse.\n\nFun fact: Common’s own show Hell On Wheels also airs on Netflix.", "annotation_id": "3010971", "url": "https://genius.com/3010971", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "The Kendrick Lamar Odom cause I lose control", "vault_lines": ["The Kendrick Lamar Odom cause I lose control"], "meaning": "During the summer of 2013, Kendrick Lamar created a fluster in the rap game when he was featured on Big Sean’s song Control. During his feature, he proclaimed himself as not only the king of the west coast, but of the east coast too. Also, non-subliminally, he named out multiple rappers who are popular right now, and proclaimed that he was going to murder their careers.\n\nFormer NBA player Lamar Odom was recently placed in rehab due to his addiction to crack cocaine for which he couldn’t control.\n\n\n\nTherefore, when Common spits bars he loses total control and takes the game by storm.", "annotation_id": "3010878", "url": "https://genius.com/3010878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Moon walk like Mike Jack, but never backtrack", "vault_lines": ["Moon walk like Mike Jack, but never backtrack"], "meaning": "The moon walk was a dance trademarked by Michael Jackson (Mike Jack).\n\n\n\nCommon is slick like this dance, but he will never retrace someone’s steps (backtrack), because he created his own unique style.\n\nAnother reason why Common is backtracking is because he is always progressing as an artist.", "annotation_id": "3010841", "url": "https://genius.com/3010841", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Dreamin’ of the pussy that I slept on, cat nap", "vault_lines": ["Dreamin' of the pussy that I slept on, cat nap"], "meaning": "Common has been known to be more of a relationship-guy rather than a player. Therefore, he is dreaming of all of the pussy he could’ve gotten up until now.\n\nPussy is slang for a cat.\n\nTherefore, when a cat takes periodical short naps throughout the day, it is referred to as a “catnap”.", "annotation_id": "3010818", "url": "https://genius.com/3010818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Blackstrap molasses in the backpack", "vault_lines": ["Blackstrap molasses in the backpack"], "meaning": "Blackstrap molasses is the dark, syrupy residue that is produced when raw sugar cane is extracted to its maximum.\n\n\n\nPeople who wear backpacks tend to be young.\n\nTherefore, Common is still rapping raw material because he has almost hit his maximum potential. However, don’t be fooled because Common is still youthful due to the backpack that he carries around.\n\n\n\nAfter all, Common IS the black molasses", "annotation_id": "3010727", "url": "https://genius.com/3010727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Hopin’ I reach twenty one, nigga black jack", "vault_lines": ["Hopin' I reach twenty one, nigga black jack"], "meaning": "When Common was younger; he wasn’t sure if he would make it past 21 years old, due to the crime ridden streets.\n\nHowever, since Common lives the life of luxury, the only  21 he has to worry about is the winning number of the popular card game, Blackjack.", "annotation_id": "3010700", "url": "https://genius.com/3010700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "In this maze they called us the black rats Because we trap from the projects, we stack that", "vault_lines": ["In this maze they called us the black rats", "Because we trap from the projects, we stack that"], "meaning": "Building on the Maze reference in the line above, Common says in this puzzled world, African-Americans are considered as the dirty-street rats because they are from the projects.\n\nCommon uses the word “trap” because rats can be caught in them. Also, “trap” is slang for a poor place where drugs are sold.\n\nCommon is referring to cheddar when he says, “we stack that”.\n\nCheddar is slang for money, and a food rats love to feast on.", "annotation_id": "3010668", "url": "https://genius.com/3010668", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Black Panther party, nigga hold up your fist", "vault_lines": ["Black Panther party, nigga hold up your fist"], "meaning": "The Black Panther Party is one of the most prominent figures in black history. They were a revolutionary black power group during the 1960s and 70s. One thing they were known for, was their usage of the raised fist:", "annotation_id": "3010493", "url": "https://genius.com/3010493", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "Born to be poor, chose to be rich", "vault_lines": ["Born to be poor, chose to be rich"], "meaning": "Ross asserts that actions speak louder than destiny. He was handed nothing, and he decided to make something himself.\n\n\n\nHe went from: Growing up in a crime infested city called Carol City, Florida.\n\nTo: Not only being only a rap genius and selling millions of albums, but he is CEO of MMG label, and owner of four businesses called Wingstop.\n\nThat’s not too bad of turnaround..", "annotation_id": "3010489", "url": "https://genius.com/3010489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Sunshine (Remix)", "line": "[Intro: Wale] May the optimism of tomorrow be your foundation for today [Chorus] The spotlight on my fans Sunshine, I can’t tell a lie Want me to say what they just wanna hear now Want me to say what they just wanna hear now [Interlude: Wale (Rick Ross)] I can’t lie I feel quite phenomenal today baby, yeah That new black soul shit, this that new black soul That new black soul Bounce, bounce It’s so soulful at the moment (I’m just happy to be apart of it)", "vault_lines": ["That new black soul", "It's so soulful at the moment"], "meaning": "#Check the OG track from The Gifted and all it’s annotations!", "annotation_id": "3010339", "url": "https://genius.com/3010339", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
