{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "My new deal with Def Jam just set me for life", "vault_lines": ["My new deal with Def Jam just set me for life"], "meaning": "Def Jam Recordings is an American record label focused predominantly on hip hop, pop and urban music, owned by Universal Music Group. Rick Ross is signed to Roc Nation under Def Jam and even has his own record label, Maybach Music under Def Jam.", "annotation_id": "20092447", "url": "https://genius.com/20092447", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "My bitch smilin’ I wanna bet, now we on Fisher Isle", "vault_lines": ["My bitch smilin' I wanna bet, now we on Fisher Isle"], "meaning": "Fisher Island is a wealthy and exclusive location in Miami, Florida. Ross repped the town on his 2011 song, “Ice Cold”:\n\nGet the picture, niggas gettin' richer now\nLivin' next to bitches, out on Fisher Isle\nDown from Oprah, Don King, and Sosa", "annotation_id": "4421092", "url": "https://genius.com/4421092", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "He on swole and that nigga need a telephone In a Range Rover, and a real nigga got it for him", "vault_lines": ["In a Range Rover, and a real nigga got it for him"], "meaning": "The homie is jacked from working out, and is now driving a Range Rover courtesy of Rozay. He might need a cellphone since he’s been released from prison.\n\nRozay is no stranger to showing magnanimity to loyal homies, as indicated by the music video of another song on the Mastermind album, “Thug Cry”.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jEy9ygty4JQ", "annotation_id": "4420954", "url": "https://genius.com/4420954", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Geechi Liberace, I’m rich as a bitch", "vault_lines": ["Geechi Liberace, I'm rich as a bitch"], "meaning": "Liberace was a heavily bejeweled pianist most famous in the 1950s.  A Geechi is a black American originally from the coastal regions of South Carolina.\n\nGeechi people speak a unique dialect that mixes English with west African languages.  Today, Geechi means a person who is “country” or not very sophisticated.  Rick Ross is telling us that he fabulous but not far from his ancestral black roots.\n\n\n\nAlso not the first time he’s called himself this.", "annotation_id": "2898293", "url": "https://genius.com/2898293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Got them gangstas who on my line that’ll blow out your mind Got them gangstas who on my line that’ll blow out your mind Got them gangstas who on my line that’ll blow out your mind Got them gangstas who on my line that’ll blow out your mind", "vault_lines": ["Got them gangstas who on my line that'll blow out your mind"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has connections with gangstas that are loyal to him. They’ll literally blow out your mind if he calls upon them to do so.\n\nAlso worth noting, the deluxe album art of Mastermind features Rick Ross shooting himself in the head with a Desert Eagle  with colorful splashes of his “blood” splattering on the background, which he has said represents his creativity.", "annotation_id": "2878981", "url": "https://genius.com/2878981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Whenever you see the G, it represents God and geometry That’s what the stencil’s for", "vault_lines": ["That's what the stencil's for"], "meaning": "Freemasonry is a large relatively exclusive society with many lodges around the world and that includes many prominent members. It is often accused of being responsible for a New World Order that supposedly controls the governments of the world and media (including many popular musicians, such as Jay Z and Rick Ross himself) behind the scenes by conspiracy theorists.\n\nThe emblem of Freemasonry is a square and a pair of compasses, both tools used in stonemasonry, the original focus of the fraternity. A capital letter “G” is often included between the square and compasses, which is believed to stand for the Great Architect of the Universe, which in turn can refer to “God” as a deity, or to “geometry” which is believed to be the noblest of sciences by freemasons since it is used heavily in architecture and stonemasonry. Both “God” and “geometry” also start with the letter “G”.\n\n\n\nThis is not the first time Rick Ross has touched upon the topic of freemasonry.", "annotation_id": "2862156", "url": "https://genius.com/2862156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Charm city boys get a whole city of brick", "vault_lines": ["Charm city boys get a whole city of brick"], "meaning": "‘Charm City’ is a nickname given to Baltimore in the mid 1970’s with its intended purpose to be promoting the city.  Once again Rozay shows us his wit with this line.\n\n\n\n‘Brick’ is referencing crack cocaine. Researchers have noted that the crack epidemic had a major effect on the city, you can read about that here. Since ‘brick’ is interpreted to mean crack, then Ross means that their is a metric shit ton of crack in Baltimore.", "annotation_id": "2860081", "url": "https://genius.com/2860081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "[Produced by Scott Storch]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "During an interview with XXL Magazine Scott explained how the track came about:\n\n\nEssentially, when I am making the beginnings or nucleus of the tracks, I’m doing most of that stuff on my own in my room. I have certain people that I hear the tracks for. Whether I am making it for them in the beginning or somewhere halfway through, this could go to this person or this would be hot for this person. I think a lot of beatmakers and producers, after making something and realizing, “Oh, this would sound awesome for this person.” Something that we all do. Just trying in your brain [to] visualize them on the track and their patterns and their tones. Who’s going to sound good on what.\n\nI remember when we did this record, we ran it right to him and he immediately felt it. He was like, “That’s mine right there.” He got on the mic immediately and that was when the real joy comes in. You actually get a chance to hear them. And it was sort of tease. We brought it to his house and he jumped on the mic and we listened to him record on it. I mean, he’s real fast. He writes in like, seconds. I watched him in the studio one day writing for other people. He had like three or four different artists for Cash Money that he was writing hooks and did a verse for. Man, it was awesome. He’s a beast with that.\n\nWhat I am getting from it is he made a record that I think will reach not just the dudes. Out of the whole body of music on that album, it’s definitely something where he’s talking about all the fly shit. I think it’s something that the girls will connect to, too. There’s that one and the one he did with The Weeknd, “In Vein,” as far as universal, everybody likes it, type of record. A lot of the stuff on the album is really dark. Amazing, but it’s one of the brighter records on the album.", "annotation_id": "2859516", "url": "https://genius.com/2859516", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "I just met a bitch who never gets jetlag", "vault_lines": ["I just met a bitch who never gets jetlag"], "meaning": "Jet lag is a condition which causes your body clock to be out of sync with the destination time, as it experiences daylight and darkness contrary to the rhythms to which it has grown accustomed.The body’s natural pattern is upset. Jet lag usually occurs when traveling across multiple different time zones.\n\n\n\nRick is referencing a bitch who never experiences JETLAG because she has experience traveling to different parts of the world frequently. This indirectly indicates that she is RICH like RICK. Thus why above he said “hanging with billion dollar niggas, you get to meet billion dollar bitches”.", "annotation_id": "2856462", "url": "https://genius.com/2856462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "And spent 10 thousand dollars on not her best bag You underdig that", "vault_lines": ["And spent 10 thousand dollars on not her best bag"], "meaning": "This line indicates that this billion dollar bitch,  has the financial flexibility and overall swagger to spend $10,000 on a handbag.\n\nA notable characteristic of this billion dollar bitch is that despite the significance of a $10,000 handbag purchase, the handbag will not be the best in her handbag collection- alluding to the swagger-levels associated with these billion dollar bitches.\n\n\n\nThe line suggests that the combination of a developed skill to remain unaffected by jetlag, and a no-limits fashion swagger indicates a supreme level of prestige and talent associated with these women.\n\nThe final line suggests that the average individual is prone to “underdig” the unique characteristics of these unique females, likely because their talents can only be applied while accompanying the global elite.", "annotation_id": "2855148", "url": "https://genius.com/2855148", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "My new bitch out of D.C., call me Ricky the Ruler", "vault_lines": ["My new bitch out of D.C., call me Ricky the Ruler"], "meaning": "“Rick the Ruler” is an epithet for legendary New York rapper Slick Rick. This isn’t the first time Ross has adopted that moniker.", "annotation_id": "2854652", "url": "https://genius.com/2854652", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Gotta gather my concentration while countin’ my stacks", "vault_lines": ["Gotta gather my concentration while countin' my stacks"], "meaning": "Rick Ross seems to be having trouble counting his money! Ross has so much money, that it takes all his concentration to be able to count his millions.\n\nAt the beginning of the song Drug Dealers Dreams, you can hear an automated message saying that Ross has $92,153,183.28 in the bank.\n\nPlease hold while I locate your information. Your checking account available balance is $92,153,183.28. This reflects the most current information available on your account\n\n\n\nHere you can watch Ross go on a 600k spending spree. Rozay has got some next level money!", "annotation_id": "2854476", "url": "https://genius.com/2854476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Big numbers, I’m John Wall, I’m ballin’ tonight", "vault_lines": ["Big numbers, I'm John Wall, I'm ballin' tonight"], "meaning": "John Wall is an NBA player that is labeled by the Wizards as a designated player, signed a five-year contract extension worth approximately $80 million", "annotation_id": "2854178", "url": "https://genius.com/2854178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
