{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Somewhere in Georgia, it’s 109 rooms", "vault_lines": ["Somewhere in Georgia, it's 109 rooms"], "meaning": "Rick Ross recently purchased Evander Holyfield’s 109-Room Mansion in Georgia, just outside Atlanta in Fayetteville County.\n\nAfter the former heavyweight champion had to sell his 45,000-square-foot mansion to a bank for $7.5 million, it went back on the market for $8.2 million. It’s unclear how much Ross paid for the mansion, but the starting price at an auction was $2.5 million.", "annotation_id": "2851201", "url": "https://genius.com/2851201", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "300 horses in this bitch, need a jockey inside", "vault_lines": ["300 horses in this bitch, need a jockey inside"], "meaning": "Ross' car apparently has 300 horsepower, to the point where you could refer to him as a horse jockey.", "annotation_id": "2850345", "url": "https://genius.com/2850345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Supreme", "line": "Tried to murder me while in mine, so that’s how I survived", "vault_lines": ["Tried to murder me while in mine, so that's how I survived"], "meaning": "This refers to the incident where Rick Ross and his girlfriend were the target of a drive by shooting while he was in his Rolls-Royce celebrating his 37th birthday.\n\nFortunately, the drive-by failed, and neither were harmed.", "annotation_id": "2837935", "url": "https://genius.com/2837935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
