{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Swipe Life", "line": "Barack callin’ my name", "vault_lines": ["Barack callin' my name"], "meaning": "President Barack Obama invited Rick Ross and several other rappers, including Nicki Minaj and J. Cole, to talk about his “My Brother’s Keeper” initiative, which aims to keep young minority men out of trouble. During his visit to the White House, Ross' ankle bracelet went off.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BEPOavghvN4/?hl=en", "annotation_id": "9038512", "url": "https://genius.com/9038512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Swipe Life", "line": "My tools all from Afghan Poppy seed residue on my hands", "vault_lines": ["My tools all from Afghan", "Poppy seed residue on my hands"], "meaning": "“My tools all from Afghan” suggests guns. Afghanistan is notorious for the conflict that has raged for over 30 years. Communist rebels in the 80’s, Taliban from the 90’s onwards and US troops in the last decade or so, Afghanistan has been torn apart by war.\n\nThe CIA supported the anti-communist Mujahideen with advanced weapons as part of a cold war proxy war. These along with commonly found Russian arms have made the country rich in spare weaponry.\n\nRoss has got his hands on some guns along with some Afghanistan-grown opium, another thing the country is famous for. He intends to sell this once it is processed into heroin.\n\nIn 2007, 92% of the non-pharmaceutical-grade opiates on the world market originated in Afghanistan.", "annotation_id": "9037112", "url": "https://genius.com/9037112", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
