{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "THIS IS MY YEAR", "line": "Oh, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah", "vault_lines": ["Oh, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah"], "meaning": "Boogie’s melody here is very reminiscent of his 2016 hit “My Shit”", "annotation_id": "23018211", "url": "https://genius.com/23018211", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "THIS IS MY YEAR", "line": "Me and Khaled, we go back, but we ain’t never goin’ back, don’t get confused (We ain’t never going back)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Big Sean and DJ Khaled’s relationship dates all the way back to the early 2010s, with their first collaboration dating to the July 2011 track, “Future.” The two have had much success with each other in the past; a notable track being July 2016’s “Holy Key,” aided by a Kendrick Lamar and a Betty White feature.\n\nThe Detroit native also landed himself on Khaled’s eleventh studio album, Father of Asahd, with the songs “Jealous” and “Thank You.”\n\nSean has touched on their relationship before in the aforementioned “Thank You,” where he raps:\n\nLook, I gotta thank Khaled, who back in 2010 Convinced Ye, Sean should drop “My Last” shit\nIt’s a smash hit, add Chris to it and it’s a classic\nThat’s that rare shit, yeah loyalty everlasting, look\n\nThe rapper plays off his own words, saying that the two artists won’t go back to their pasts. Big Sean has touched on this notion recently in his July 2019 single, “Single Again,” where he raps,\n\nGot me feeling like, “I don’t fuck with you”\nOh nah, nah, that’s the old me\nYou fucking with the new me (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "22980331", "url": "https://genius.com/22980331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "THIS IS MY YEAR", "line": "Redeye", "vault_lines": ["Bought me a Redeye"], "meaning": "Dodge Charger SRT Hellcat", "annotation_id": "22947812", "url": "https://genius.com/22947812", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "THIS IS MY YEAR", "line": "Brightest energy, my soul sing CeCe Winans on the track (Track)", "vault_lines": ["Brightest energy, my soul sing CeCe Winans on the track (Track)"], "meaning": "Big Sean nods to award-winning gospel singer and fellow Detroit native CeCe Winans. Winner of 12 Grammys and 23 GMA Dove Awards for her singing, she is the best-selling female gospel singer of all time.\n\nWith hits like October 1999’s “Alabaster Box,” the November 1995 track “Count on Me,” with Whitney Houston and April 1998’s “Everlasting Love,” CeCe has made gospel music for the past 40 years.\n\nSean compares his upbeat rapping to CeCe’s ability to bring bright energy to a song. During a March 2021 interview with Forbes, talking about her then latest album Believe For It, Winans stated:\n\nI grew up in the church and loved being in worship service with everybody singing and praising the Lord together. It’s uplifting! So, that’s what I wanted to do with this album. With people suffering the way they’ve suffered, a lot of people have lost family members and are still dealing with sickness, I think it’s right on time to really encourage people to believe again.", "annotation_id": "22914602", "url": "https://genius.com/22914602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "THIS IS MY YEAR", "line": "We the Best Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Proclaimed before each track, this serves as DJ Khaled’s producer tag. An imprint of Epic Records, We the Best Music Group is also a record label founded by DJ Khaled in 2008.\n\nBy stating he’s released “another one,” he refers to him having produced yet another hit single.", "annotation_id": "22888331", "url": "https://genius.com/22888331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "THIS IS MY YEAR", "line": "We got Allah with us", "vault_lines": ["We got Allah with us"], "meaning": "is the Arabic word for God in Abrahamic religions. In the English language, the word generally refers to God in Islam", "annotation_id": "22887816", "url": "https://genius.com/22887816", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "THIS IS MY YEAR", "line": "Straight drop dead, Len Bias (That’s right)", "vault_lines": ["Straight drop dead, Len Bias (That's right)"], "meaning": "Len Bias is a former basketball player who played for the University of Maryland from 1982-1986. Bias was drafted second overall in the 1986 NBA Draft by the Boston Celtics. Bias died two days after being drafted at the hands of a cardiac arrhythmia by way of a cocaine overdose.", "annotation_id": "22879997", "url": "https://genius.com/22879997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
