{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Another one DJ Khaled", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "These are DJ Khaled’s trademark slogans that he often proclaims in the intro of his songs since the 2000s.\n\n“Another One” is his way of saying that he has another hit on his hands.", "annotation_id": "17948820", "url": "https://genius.com/17948820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I eat her ice cream, she eat my ice cream cone (Hahaha)", "vault_lines": ["I eat her ice cream, she eat my ice cream cone (Hahaha)"], "meaning": "Wayne uses “ice cream” and “ice cream cone” to represent the female and the male genitalia respectively. On his 2006 song “Feeling Myself,” Wayne also mentions ice cream but uses it to represent cocaine:\n\nFeds hear my cell ring\nPhone, we say ice cream\nHome, we say white", "annotation_id": "17948787", "url": "https://genius.com/17948787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Big fat nigga, all that huffin’ and puffin’", "vault_lines": ["Big fat nigga, all that huffin' and puffin'"], "meaning": "Nicki calling her man a “big fat nigga” means he stacked with cash. This makes sense as Nicki talk about shopping in France in the following lines.\n\nAdditionally, this could be a shoutout to Rick Ross, who is also featured on this song and is famously overweight. Nicki also shouted out him on 2015’s “No Flex Zone (Remix)”:\n\nAss still fat, it’s on Rick Ross", "annotation_id": "17948727", "url": "https://genius.com/17948727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Reputation for G’s, that’s the role of a boss", "vault_lines": ["Reputation for G's, that's the role of a boss"], "meaning": "Ross first called himself a “boss” in 2006 and has since used the term frequently in his music. He even has a 2011 song called “You The Boss” with Nicki Minaj, who is also featured on this song.", "annotation_id": "17948611", "url": "https://genius.com/17948611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Fuck with me, baby, it’s Tunechi, baby", "vault_lines": ["Fuck with me, baby, it's Tunechi, baby"], "meaning": "In a 2010 interview with MTV, Wayne explained the origin of his nickname, Tunechi:\n\nMy nickname is Lil Tune—my grandmother named me that […] We just threw the ‘Chi’ on there. Like Gucci, I say ‘Tunechi!’", "annotation_id": "17941820", "url": "https://genius.com/17941820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Girl, that pussy like medication to patients Got my eyes closed like Asian persuasion", "vault_lines": ["Girl, that pussy like medication to patients", "Got my eyes closed like Asian persuasion"], "meaning": "Wayne implies that sex with his girl is so intense that he ends up falling asleep after he’s done.\n\nIt’s stereotyped that Asians have small eyes due to the epicanthic fold of their upper eyelid—Wayne compares this to his eyes being closed.", "annotation_id": "17941791", "url": "https://genius.com/17941791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I bet you Tunechi make her throw away that silver bullet, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I bet you Tunechi make her throw away that silver bullet, yeah"], "meaning": "A silver bullet is a vibrator—a sex toy that’s used to provide pleasurable sexual stimulation. Wayne notes here that his sex game is pleasurable enough for his girl and that she doesn’t need an alternative.\n\nWayne ends his verse with a sexual allusion as it cuts to Chris Brown singing “Take it to the head”—meaning in Wayne’s case, oral sex.", "annotation_id": "17941716", "url": "https://genius.com/17941716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "With all that pink on, bitch, I’m King Kong", "vault_lines": ["With all that pink on, bitch, I'm King Kong"], "meaning": "King Kong is a fictional monstrous ape that first appeared in the media in 1933, following its debut film that year. He’s one of the most famous movie icons in the world, inspiring numerous sequels, remakes, cartoons, and much more.\n\nWayne also has a 2007 song titled “King Kong,” however in a different context. Here, he’s talking about his ape-like behavior in bed.", "annotation_id": "17941531", "url": "https://genius.com/17941531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Bust a nut, smoke a blunt, now I’m rejuvenated", "vault_lines": ["Bust a nut, smoke a blunt, now I'm rejuvenated"], "meaning": "“Buss a nut” means to ejaculate and “rejuvenated” means to feel fresh and younger.\n\nSex and weed is a common theme in Wayne’s music—he even has a song called “Pussy Money Weed,” which he released in 2007.", "annotation_id": "17941406", "url": "https://genius.com/17941406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I’m killin’ them hoes like Jason", "vault_lines": ["I'm killin' them hoes like Jason"], "meaning": "Jason Voorhees is the main character and antagonist of the American slasher horror film franchise, Friday the 13th. It focuses on Jason, who murders anyone residing at the fictional Camp Crystal Lake as revenge for his drowning as a little boy due to the camp staff’s negligence.", "annotation_id": "17941184", "url": "https://genius.com/17941184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Uh, reputation for tastin’", "vault_lines": ["Uh, reputation for tastin'"], "meaning": "Wayne’s claim isn’t too far fetched—he even has a song called “Pussy Monster,” which is all about the female’s genitalia. It was released in 2008 and is featured on Tha Carter III.\n\nHi, I’m the\nPussy monster, the pussy monster\nThe pussy monster, the pussy monster\nAnd you gotta feed me\nPussy, pussy pussy, pussy pussy", "annotation_id": "17941170", "url": "https://genius.com/17941170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Competition, I don’t see any (Woo-hoo, ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Competition, I don't see any (Woo-hoo, ooh)"], "meaning": "During the late 2000s and early 2010s, other than Nicki, there wasn’t a big female presence in rap. Here, she boasts that her work ethic is no match for another female competitor.\n\nFor example, in 2011, she released her debut album, Pink Friday to massive success, topping the US Billboard charts. It was even nominated for Best Rap Album at the 54th Annual Grammy Awards, which Nicki attended two months before this verse. While she didn’t win, it was still a big deal as Pink Friday became the first female Grammy-nominated rap album since Missy Elliott’s Under Construction in 2004.", "annotation_id": "16892712", "url": "https://genius.com/16892712", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I-I-I ride for him, DMV", "vault_lines": ["I-I-I ride for him, DMV"], "meaning": "DMV is an abbreviation for the Department of Motor Vehicles. It’s a US state-level government agency that manages vehicle registration and driver licensing.\n\nNicki plays on the word “ride,” meaning she’s a ride or die chick. She’ll stand by her man no matter what.", "annotation_id": "16892595", "url": "https://genius.com/16892595", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I got a lot of figures (Yeah), I’m a father figure (Me)", "vault_lines": ["I got a lot of figures (Yeah), I'm a father figure (Me)"], "meaning": "In 2012, Rick Ross' net worth was estimated to be about $15 million. This, in part, came from his restaurant franchise Wingstop—which he first opened in 2011—and the success of his mixtape, Rich Forever and album, God Forgives, I Don’t, which he would later release three months later.\n\nA “father figure” is a person of power or influence who serves as an emotional substitute for a father. Ross is a father himself, who had two kids at the time of this song’s release.", "annotation_id": "16886085", "url": "https://genius.com/16886085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "She know a lot of niggas, don’t know a hotter nigga (Ha!)", "vault_lines": ["She know a lot of niggas, don't know a hotter nigga (Ha!)"], "meaning": "Just 3 months before this verse, Ross released his second mixtape, titled Rich Forever. It became one of the most downloaded hip hop mixtapes of all time and was well-received from critics.\n\nAdditionally, Ross was named the “Hottest MC” of 2011 by MTV.", "annotation_id": "16885997", "url": "https://genius.com/16885997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "She got all them purses, I say in my verses YSL and Hermès and barely scratch the surface (Ugh!)", "vault_lines": ["She got all them purses, I say in my verses", "YSL and Hermès and barely scratch the surface (Ugh!)"], "meaning": "YSL—Yves Saint Laurent—and Hermès are both French luxury fashion houses. YSL purses usually cost thousands of dollars while Hermès'  Birkin handbags can cost up to millions of dollars.\n\n“Barely scratch the surface” could mean buying these expensive items isn’t a big deal for Ross.", "annotation_id": "16885909", "url": "https://genius.com/16885909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "So amazin’ to see, black baguettes in my watch", "vault_lines": ["So amazin' to see, black baguettes in my watch"], "meaning": "A baguette-cut is a square-cut diamond which seemingly resembles the shape of a baguette—a type of French bread.\n\nThey’re often used in rings, earrings, and bracelets but in Ross' case, a watch.\n\n\n\nA Caviar Tourbillon Collection Timepiece invisibly set with Black Baguette Diamonds", "annotation_id": "16885867", "url": "https://genius.com/16885867", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Stamina, GNC", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "GNC is a health company that also sells nutrition products. This line also follows from the previous, implying that, in the sack (and probably in every other aspect), Nicki has great stamina and resilience.", "annotation_id": "14336021", "url": "https://genius.com/14336021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Three letters, CMB", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It’s a word play line. She says CMB as in Cash Money Business (or Billionaires), but it is also the initials of Chris Brown (Christopher Maurice Brown) who sings the hook right after.", "annotation_id": "705707", "url": "https://genius.com/705707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
