{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Do you know what we are gon’ do? We are going to defend ourselves ’Cause Huey P. Newton says that, ”Power Power is the ability to define phenomena and make it act in a desired manner” Power is the ability to define phenomena and make it act in a desired manner Power, if we have the ability to define it, the only next thing to do is get organized, get organized So when a pig walks up to you, or a pig gets to jiving with the people You be so organized, you be learnin’ some tactics, you be learnin’ some revolutionary principles You be having some guns hid out somewhere, you have some proper tactics That when the pig gets to jiving with you The pig is wrong, you whip your guns out on him Blow him away, and then you have the ability In fact, you have made that pig act in a desired manner", "vault_lines": ["Do you know what we are gon' do?", "The pig is wrong, you whip your guns out on him", "Blow him away, and then you have the ability", "In fact, you have made that pig act in a desired manner"], "meaning": "Speech delivered by Bobby Seale at the Kaleidoscope Theater Los Angeles, California – April 16, 1968,Bobby was the chairman of the black panther party.", "annotation_id": "20145093", "url": "https://genius.com/20145093", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Bobby’s still on the rise", "vault_lines": ["Bobby's still on the rise"], "meaning": "Bobby Seale co-founded the African-American revolutionary Party called Black Panther, which has a violent legacy of taking power into their hands. Here Ross is saying the attitude is still very much on the rise.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JN8mNBf56I4\n\nYou can hear one of Bobby’s speeches at the beginning of this song", "annotation_id": "1473916", "url": "https://genius.com/1473916", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "All the dead souls in the field", "vault_lines": ["All the dead souls in the field"], "meaning": "Ross is low key shouting out all of the Africans who died during working in the cotton fields. It could also mean all of the people who have died in the streets. “The Field” and “the streets” are synonyms.\n\n\n\nBloodlines by Toni Scott", "annotation_id": "679650", "url": "https://genius.com/679650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "And I’m still swimmin’ in ice", "vault_lines": ["And I'm still swimmin' in ice"], "meaning": "He owns so many diamonds that he can practically swim in them.\n\nAlso, notice the aquatic imagery. You literally can’t swim in ice because it’s a solid object! It’s liquid form is another story, though.", "annotation_id": "421703", "url": "https://genius.com/421703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Top back, all black, Gretzky puck", "vault_lines": ["Top back, all black, Gretzky puck"], "meaning": "Referring refers to both his convertible’s black color and his own dark skin and shaved head, and compares it to a hockey puck that Wayne Gretzky might hit in a hockey game.", "annotation_id": "251554", "url": "https://genius.com/251554", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Smokin’ a fat spliff in a brand new Benz", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' a fat spliff in a brand new Benz"], "meaning": "Spliffs are cigarettes loaded with both tobacco and marijuana.\n\nNotice the juxtaposition between the spliff, downright criminal, and the German luxury car. Ross practices sophisticated ignorance.\n\nA winner smells of marijuana.", "annotation_id": "251547", "url": "https://genius.com/251547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "To all the loved ones I leave behind At least they can’t see me cry And I ask, when someone wants to be me, why? Thought havin’ everything would ease my mind If you could read my mind My God, I’m scarred, I have tattoo tears of joy", "vault_lines": ["To all the loved ones I leave behind", "At least they can't see me cry", "And I ask, when someone wants to be me, why?", "Thought havin' everything would ease my mind", "If you could read my mind", "My God, I'm scarred, I have tattoo tears of joy"], "meaning": "To all the family and friends that left him after the fame took over, Ross is relieved because they can’t see the pain the success brings. People only see the obvious: the cars, hoes, etc. He wears the tattoo tears for his old friends, although everyone assumes they’re ‘tears of joy’; after all, how could someone with everything have pain?\n\nEven amidst pain, the bravery and resilience that are needed to find happiness are deserving of tattooed tears of joy. Just as a prisoner or gang member get the tattoo, it celebrates survival and the love that Ross/Cee-Lo have for their life and their loved ones. His tears have literally scarred him by forming tattoos on his face.", "annotation_id": "170332", "url": "https://genius.com/170332", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Damn, she might let me fuck", "vault_lines": ["Damn, she might let me fuck"], "meaning": "Ross sarcastically wonders if she’ll have sex with him, showing the commodification of sex.\n\nOn the other hand, Ross could be in pure amazement: “wow, this girl is actually let me going to have sex with her”.", "annotation_id": "119302", "url": "https://genius.com/119302", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "But that bitch Vivica nice", "vault_lines": ["But that bitch Vivica nice"], "meaning": "I agree Ross, Vivica A. Fox is bad!\n\nThis could also be a subliminal shot at 50 cent as she’s his ex-girlfriend.", "annotation_id": "79073", "url": "https://genius.com/79073", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "And we supposed to be shy?", "vault_lines": ["And we supposed to be shy?"], "meaning": "He’s questioning that black men are asked to be modest about owning expensive items and they’re not supposed to stunt when they get things like Rolexes. Jay-Z, once again, has voiced this same view.", "annotation_id": "79067", "url": "https://genius.com/79067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "White man had a problem with mine", "vault_lines": ["White man had a problem with mine"], "meaning": "Perhaps a double entendre.\n\nOn the surface, Ross is saying that white have problems with wealthy blacks, something Jay-Z has noted.\n\nRoss is also saying that whites have a problem with blacks, more generally. Note the phrase “me and mines,” where “mines,” is the speaker’s family or kin.", "annotation_id": "79064", "url": "https://genius.com/79064", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "The revolution’s televised (Alright)", "vault_lines": ["The revolution's televised (Alright)"], "meaning": "A twist on the poem/song “The Revolution Will Not Be Televised,” by Gil Scott-Heron.", "annotation_id": "69309", "url": "https://genius.com/69309", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "I gotta represent for Emmett Till (Emmett Till)", "vault_lines": ["I gotta represent for Emmett Till (Emmett Till)"], "meaning": "Emmett Till was an African American boy, who was murdered at the age of 14 in Money, Mississippi, after reportedly whistling at a white woman at a grocery store.\n\nHis brutal murder has been noted as one of the leading events that motivated the American Civil Rights Movement.\n\nRoss pays homage to the greats of the past.", "annotation_id": "33750", "url": "https://genius.com/33750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "A punch in the face’ll get you 300K Ask Vlad, now he back to makin’ minimum wage Another victim of my criminal ways (Mmm)", "vault_lines": ["A punch in the face'll get you 300K", "Ask Vlad, now he back to makin' minimum wage", "Another victim of my criminal ways (Mmm)"], "meaning": "After VladTV had covered a story on Ross' former career as a corrections officer, Ricky and his entourage were involved in a scuffle with DJ Vlad at the Ozone Awards in Houston, Texas, in 2008.  The altercation resulted in a broken eye socket for DJ Vlad.\n\nVlad filled a $4 million lawsuit against Ricky. A New York Federal Jury awarded DJ Vlad $300,000 in his civil suit, finding Ross liable for his crew breaking Vlad’s eye socket.", "annotation_id": "33748", "url": "https://genius.com/33748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Ice skater lil’ later might let me fuck", "vault_lines": ["Ice skater lil' later might let me fuck"], "meaning": "Ice Skate refers to the ebonics term to skate off: To leave a place with a female your are courting.\n\nIn the conjunction with the previous line, “Top back all black Gretzky puck” Ross plays with the imagery of driving a black top convertible (perhaps a Maybach or a Mercedes which Ross loves to refer to) and gliding smoothly through the streets like a hockey puck with greatness. Gretzky is nickname is “The Great One”.\n\nRoss frequently refers to his rides as smooth. Ross also reference to the black pride movement by having his top all black. Much like Jay-Z’s saying, “All black everything”. Hockey is stereotypically a white sport which Ross juxtaposes with black pride.", "annotation_id": "33048", "url": "https://genius.com/33048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "I wanna take my mama to the Poconos (Goodbye)", "vault_lines": ["I wanna take my mama to the Poconos (Goodbye)"], "meaning": "The Pocono Mountains in Pennsylvania are a peaceful and quiet getaway, so he wants to take his mother for some stress relief.", "annotation_id": "33039", "url": "https://genius.com/33039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Biggie Smalls in the flesh, livin’ life after my death", "vault_lines": ["Biggie Smalls in the flesh, livin' life after my death"], "meaning": "He’s saying he is the Notorious B.I.G. reincarnated.\n\nThis is also a play on big’s last album Life After Death, and their mutual girth.", "annotation_id": "33037", "url": "https://genius.com/33037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Ain’t life a bitch? But you gotta keep her wet Keys open doors, so I gotta keep a set", "vault_lines": ["Ain't life a bitch?", "But you gotta keep her wet", "Keys open doors, so I gotta keep a set"], "meaning": "Ross refers to Nas’s “Life’s A Bitch”\n\n“Ki’s (keys) open doors” is a play on words, a reference to kilos of cocaine and the Clipse song of the same name.\n\nHere, Ross is expressing the financial opportunities (opened doors) that moving cocaine can afford him.\n\nAs Big Sean said:\n\nKi’s open doors, but bricks open windows.", "annotation_id": "33030", "url": "https://genius.com/33030", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Vacheron on my wrist a year ago I didn’t even know the bitches exist Quarter milli’ for the motherfucker No insurance on the motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["Vacheron on my wrist a year ago", "I didn't even know the bitches exist"], "meaning": "Vacheron Constantin watch around his wrist and last year he didn’t know they exist.\n\nThat Ross has no insurance for it implies that he’s still new to being wealthy, and that he’s still of a mindset he had pre-wealth.", "annotation_id": "33027", "url": "https://genius.com/33027", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "Still runnin’ the streets, so I don’t sleep much", "vault_lines": ["Still runnin' the streets, so I don't sleep much"], "meaning": "Getting money, working late in the streets.\n\nRick Ross’s recent seizures in late 2011 were said to be caused by sleep deprivation. According to Ross, the last time he had a full 8-hours of sleep was in 2006.", "annotation_id": "33009", "url": "https://genius.com/33009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "line": "No ID on the track, let the story begin, begin Ha, yeah", "vault_lines": ["No ID on the track, let the story begin, begin"], "meaning": "No I.D. produced this track, and many people who work with him use this line to intro the track. It was also used by Jay-Z on “D.O.A. (Death of Auto-Tune)” and Kanye West on “Big Brother.” .", "annotation_id": "33006", "url": "https://genius.com/33006", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tears of Joy", "status": "done", "targets": 23, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-tears-of-joy-lyrics", "genius_title": "Tears of Joy", "genius_id": 1092, "source": "api"}
