{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Teenage Numbers", "line": "Teenage numbers when we speak about drugs 15, 16, 17 fine 18, 19, 20 too high", "vault_lines": ["Teenage numbers when we speak about drugs"], "meaning": "Here, Mr. Gotti is saying that they use dollar amounts ranging from $13,000 to $19,000 (i.e “teenage numbers”) when they talk about buying kilos of cocaine. Dollar amounts of $15-17,000 per kilo are acceptable (although The lower the better, I’m sure), but kilo amounts above $17,000 are too expensive, as not enough profit will be generated to justify costs after the kilo is broken down for distribution.", "annotation_id": "17517728", "url": "https://genius.com/17517728", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Teenage Numbers", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yo-gotti-teenage-numbers-lyrics", "genius_title": "Teenage Numbers", "genius_id": 201682, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "A true G keeps it raw in his lecture", "vault_lines": ["A true G keeps it raw in his lecture"], "meaning": "You can realize how true somebody is by the way of speech!", "annotation_id": "19871746", "url": "https://genius.com/19871746", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "I could see it in the sparkle ’cause it lackluster", "vault_lines": ["I could see it in the sparkle 'cause it lackluster"], "meaning": "Continuation of the last line in which Ross accuses other rappers of wearing fake diamonds, or “moissanites”. You can tell the difference by how they sparkle.\n\nSome clever wordplay here by Ross because while “lackluster” could certainly be a term to describe fake diamonds, “luster” is also another word for shine or sparkle, so your diamonds are not only “lackluster”, but literally, “lack luster”.", "annotation_id": "14465070", "url": "https://genius.com/14465070", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "[Chorus: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The concept of this song is intentionally ironic — Rozay purposely interpositions religious imagery alongside thug life and money thirst; it’s not because Rick Ross is encouraging immoral behavior — in fact, it’s the opposite.\n\nIt’s the recognition of constant sin and constant forgiveness from the Lord. It’s not a glorification, but it’s the idea that humans can’t forgive anywhere near as much as God, and that God forgives even when people — Rick Ross in particular — pursue these useless materialistic urges. He understands how vapid and pointless all the Jesus Pieces and jewelry is compared to an actual spiritual connection.", "annotation_id": "2159735", "url": "https://genius.com/2159735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Quick to quote a prayer, pull it from the archives", "vault_lines": ["Quick to quote a prayer, pull it from the archives"], "meaning": "Ross, in times of excess & trouble, draws on holy scripture for strength. Evidence of his archival wealth of biblical references and hot lines in general is found in his plethora of mixtapes and successful studio albums.\n\nRozay has referenced prayers before, see “I’m Only Human”.", "annotation_id": "1356048", "url": "https://genius.com/1356048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "I’m his poltergeist, niggas know I’m more than nice", "vault_lines": ["I'm his poltergeist, niggas know I'm more than nice"], "meaning": "A poltergeist is basically a ghost who is known to annoy/bother people. They’re just there to annoy people and be a nuisance. Peeves from the Harry Potter series is a poltergeist, for example.\n\nSo Ross is alluding to the fact he is like a poltergeist to his foes, he’ll bother you because he’s so successful and you’re not – and there’s nothing you can do to really stop him.", "annotation_id": "1230136", "url": "https://genius.com/1230136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "All these jewels on, all Moissanites", "vault_lines": ["All these jewels on, all Moissanites"], "meaning": "Moissanites is a “fake” diamond. it came from the movie “Snatch” when Sol told the guy coming in the store that his diamond was a moissanite aka not authentic.\n\nRoss seems to be accusing his enemies of wearing fake diamonds.", "annotation_id": "1101400", "url": "https://genius.com/1101400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "On trial and they wanna execute me It’s really sad, just the fact they never knew me", "vault_lines": ["On trial and they wanna execute me", "It's really sad, just the fact they never knew me"], "meaning": "Many DA’s and prosecutors want the harshest sentences for rappers and other black entertainers when they are on trial but they usually don’t really know anything about them besides what they hear, read, or see on tv. MMG artist Meek Mill’s The Ride gave us an excellent example of this when he rapped about a similar situation on his cover of Drake’s The Ride.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T8qjxocGA-k", "annotation_id": "963371", "url": "https://genius.com/963371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Reppin’ for your homies when they all gone", "vault_lines": ["Reppin' for your homies when they all gone"], "meaning": "Keeping the memories of those who’ve passed on. Many rappers choose to do this through songs, t-shirts, and various other ways. This is a reference to his fallen comrade, Raymond “P-Nut” Adderly.\n\n\n\n#RIP P-Nut\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/15267195739176960", "annotation_id": "963345", "url": "https://genius.com/963345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Askin’ for a hundred mill as I pray to God", "vault_lines": ["Askin' for a hundred mill as I pray to God"], "meaning": "He’s praying that he’ll see 100 million dollars and with an estimated net worth of 25 million and MMG’s growing success he is well o his way.", "annotation_id": "963333", "url": "https://genius.com/963333", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Niggas claim that they thuggin’ when they dick-ridin’ My niggas rather walk, do they own brick climbin’", "vault_lines": ["Niggas claim that they thuggin' when they dick-ridin'", "My niggas rather walk, do they own brick climbin'"], "meaning": "A lot of dudes claim to be thugs just because a lot of rappers are making that a popular trend.\n\nSince they’re just playing hard because the rappers are they’re technically imitating the rappers dick-riding.\n\nIn contrast, Ross' crew is more about hustling and building their own way to the top – step by step; they’re not riding someone else’s coat-tails.\n\nThis line is a callback to a famous line off his smash single, BMF.", "annotation_id": "963326", "url": "https://genius.com/963326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Ten chains, no luggage, I’m a big timer", "vault_lines": ["Ten chains, no luggage, I'm a big timer"], "meaning": "Big Tymers were always rapping about how much money they had, how much jewelry they owned, how expensive their cars were, and how fly they were.", "annotation_id": "963313", "url": "https://genius.com/963313", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Lil Wodie got it rolled up in a rubber band", "vault_lines": ["Lil Wodie got it rolled up in a rubber band"], "meaning": "A wodie is a term used to refer to a friend or partner. In this case, he’s referencing his manager Gucci Pucci.", "annotation_id": "958068", "url": "https://genius.com/958068", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Ten chains on, Eric B with mob ties Rakim flows, comin’ from the Pharcyde", "vault_lines": ["Ten chains on, Eric B with mob ties", "Rakim flows, comin' from the Pharcyde"], "meaning": "Eric B and Rakim, in addition to their legendary music, were also known for how they dressed, with custom Dapper Dan jackets:\n\n\n\nAs well as giant gold chains:\n\n\n\nRoss also shouts out the classic group The Pharcyde, presumably more for the “Pharcyde”/“far side” homophone than any thematic reason\n\nMany have questioned Rozay’s commitment to Hip Hop as an art and his place in the genre. With this line, Ross shows he is a student of the art-form, listing rappers who he has studied & who have inspired him.", "annotation_id": "958045", "url": "https://genius.com/958045", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Forty dollar tab meanin’ forty grand", "vault_lines": ["Forty dollar tab meanin' forty grand"], "meaning": "If he gets a bill at the club and its for 40 he knows that its really 40,000 because of all the bottles him and his crew bought. Instead of wasting time and writing any more the waiter just says “40.”\n\nSimilar to Jay-z in U Don’t Know (Remix):\n\nSure I do, I tell you the difference between me and them\nThey tryin to get they ones, I’m tryin to get them M’s\n\nAt a certain level in stacking paper you can talk about certain levels of money simply by saying the number in front.\n\nSoon Jay-z will starting talking about “1 B ” as in one billion.\n\nRick Ross is ashamed of his Billion: “Now I’m worth over a billion, I’m ashamed to say ”", "annotation_id": "945772", "url": "https://genius.com/945772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Xolaal sama guys, dundu ben yoon la Dangay dundu sa dundu, gemm Yalla Ligeey, xalis, gnax, amoul nelaw, gnafè Sa life yako dugal, ken du ko jappale Yow ya ray sa bopp ba dee. Moy loolu", "vault_lines": ["Dangay dundu sa dundu, gemm Yalla", "Ligeey, xalis, gnax, amoul nelaw, gnafè", "Sa life yako dugal, ken du ko jappale", "Yow ya ray sa bopp ba dee. Moy loolu"], "meaning": "The firs skit is a man who speaks Wolof, a Senegalese language.\n\nThe translation to English:\n\nWell! People, you only live once. Just live your life, believe in God and work hard. Nobody will help you, you gotta fight to death. That’s all…", "annotation_id": "943012", "url": "https://genius.com/943012", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Mi historia es complicada, pero al final del dia valio la pena, porque ahora estoy trabajando con el jefe Yo vivi en Colombia y vivi muchas cosas, me entiende? Vi muertes...vi muertes...vi cuerpos en las calles, sangrando despues del colegio, con 12, 13 años viendo estas cosas en la calle Y siempre queria venir para aqui otra vez, y me vine, y trabaje porque tenia otra mentalidad. Y cuando llegue aca entendi mi proposito: hacer dinero, ser rico para siempre Dios perdona, yo no", "vault_lines": ["Yo vivi en Colombia y vivi muchas cosas, me entiende?", "Dios perdona, yo no"], "meaning": "The second skit is a man speaking Spanish.\n\nThe translation to English:\n\n\nMy history is complicated, but at the end of the day, it was worth it, because now I’m working with the boss.\n\nI lived in Colombia and I lived a lot of things, you understand me?\n\nI saw deaths……I saw deaths….I saw bodies in the streets, bleeding after school, with 12, 13 years seeing these things in the streets.\n\nAnd I always want to come back here, and I came, and I work because I had a another mentality. And when I arrive here I understood my purpose: make money and be rich forever.\n\nGod Forgives, I Don’t.", "annotation_id": "933381", "url": "https://genius.com/933381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "I’m flyin’ first class as the snakes slither", "vault_lines": ["I'm flyin' first class as the snakes slither"], "meaning": "Ross shitting on his haters: while those fuckbois are struggling to eat, Ross lives lavishly on first class flights.\n\nCould also reference to the 2006 Action Thriller Feature Film, Snakes On A Plane.", "annotation_id": "933192", "url": "https://genius.com/933192", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Went from Benihana to Bimini in Bahamas", "vault_lines": ["Went from Benihana to Bimini in Bahamas"], "meaning": "Benihana is a Florida based chain of Japanese restaurants, Bimini is the western most district of the Bahamas, composed of small islands. He could be referring to the many concerts he has done now withing the Bimini region of the Bahamas\n\nNote the great alliteration with the letter B.", "annotation_id": "933068", "url": "https://genius.com/933068", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Drinkin’ vodka in the memory of my nigga, damn (I miss you P-Nut)", "vault_lines": ["Drinkin' vodka in the memory of my nigga, damn (I miss you P-Nut)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross' best friend, Raymond Adderly (P-Nut), was gunned down in December of 2010 outside of his home.", "annotation_id": "932389", "url": "https://genius.com/932389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "line": "Eight shot, bitch I’m a top shotta", "vault_lines": ["Eight shot, bitch I'm a top shotta"], "meaning": "The reason he says this line with a Jamaican accent is because\na top shotta is a Jamaican term referring to a gangster.\n\nThis could also be a reference to DMX’s song “Top Shotter”, a song made for the movie Belly, which has many scenes based in Jamaica.", "annotation_id": "932019", "url": "https://genius.com/932019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "status": "done", "targets": 20, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-ten-jesus-pieces-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ten Jesus Pieces", "genius_id": 80558, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Thank You", "line": "They say you only get remembered when you got a name 7 others died with Aaliyah on the plane I don’t know nobody else, should them niggas feel the shame", "vault_lines": ["They say you only get remembered when you got a name", "7 others died with Aaliyah on the plane", "I don't know nobody else, should them niggas feel the shame"], "meaning": "Aaliyah was an influential artist/actress who passed away in a plane accident in 2001. Though seven others also died in the accident, we only remember Aaliyah, leading Rocky to the sad truth that “you only get remembered when you got a name.”", "annotation_id": "7932281", "url": "https://genius.com/7932281", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Thank You", "line": "Hating when you sitting in front of God like you, DJ Envy", "vault_lines": ["Hating when you sitting in front of God like you, DJ Envy"], "meaning": "DJ Envy & Charlamagne Tha God are hosts on The Breakfast Club radio show on Power 105.1 When Rockie says “sitting in front of God like you DJ Envy” he’s actually referring to Charlamagne tha “God”", "annotation_id": "7932156", "url": "https://genius.com/7932156", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
