{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Boss", "line": "Ten black Maybachs back to back in a lane", "vault_lines": ["Ten black Maybachs back to back in a lane"], "meaning": "Arguably Rozay’s favorite car. He even named his music label after the car. It only makes sense that he has lots of them in his backyard.", "annotation_id": "7786748", "url": "https://genius.com/7786748", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Boss", "line": "I made a couple million dollars last year dealin’ weight Still in the streets, strapped with them thangs", "vault_lines": ["I made a couple million dollars last year dealin' weight", "Still in the streets, strapped with them thangs"], "meaning": "Ross isn’t talking about his weight here. “Dealing weight” or “pushing weight” is slang for distributing large amounts of narcotics. To be “strapped” is to have a gun on oneself. The boss is making millions off of dealing narcotics in the streets and has a gun for protection…", "annotation_id": "7786609", "url": "https://genius.com/7786609", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Boss", "line": "She like ’em gangsta ’cause", "vault_lines": ["That bitch got 125 on the dash, She like 'em gangsta cause"], "meaning": "Rick Ross claims that he is the best out of everyone who has lived, so far.\n\nBeing a boss means having power. Being a big boss means having a lot of power. Being the biggest boss means that he has the most power, and being the biggest boss that anyone has seen thus far means that nobody has ever had more power than he currently has.\n\nIt may also be an allusion towards Rick Ross' size, since he is overweight, and therefore big. There have been numerous successful obese rappers, but Rick Ross just may be the most obese of them all.", "annotation_id": "345399", "url": "https://genius.com/345399", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Boss", "line": "I’ma make it rain", "vault_lines": ["I'mma make it rain"], "meaning": "To “make it rain” is to throw money around, both literally and figuratively, simply because you have so much of it.", "annotation_id": "116429", "url": "https://genius.com/116429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Boss", "line": "Back to the thuggin’, now I’m sippin’ sizzurp", "vault_lines": ["Back to the thuggin', now I'm sippin' sizzurp"], "meaning": "Sizzurp: Orange soda, cough syrup, and a Jolly Rancher for flavor. A drink popular in the hoods. By saying that he drinks it, Rick Ross is saying that he is still hood.", "annotation_id": "116422", "url": "https://genius.com/116422", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
