{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Dope boys on the goal nigga", "vault_lines": ["Dope boys on the goal nigga"], "meaning": "This is a seemingly obvious line, but “dope” can be taken 2 different ways. He could be using it to refer to themselves as either cool, or as 2 people that use drugs in general. Depending on how you interpret the meaning of “dope”, that could change the meaning of “goal”.\n\nHe’s basically saying, “we’ve got our shit together, we’re cool as shit, and we’re keeping the eyes on our goal(s)” but it could also however refer to their past drug hustling, in which case he may mean they’ve already hit their goals.", "annotation_id": "2689987", "url": "https://genius.com/2689987", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "[Produced by Major Seven, Co-Produced by KE on The Track]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Hey everyone, I’m Major Seven, the producer of Rick Ross feat. Jay-Z new single titled “The Devil Is A Lie” This video shows a little bit of the process I went through for making this beat! Check it out! and definitely comment and tweet me @MajorSeven and let me know what you think, Thanks!\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r-fACEkZ4TQ&feature=youtu.be", "annotation_id": "2656724", "url": "https://genius.com/2656724", "state": "verified", "votes": 102, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "You couldn’t stop me if you tried", "vault_lines": ["You couldn't stop me if you tried"], "meaning": "Rick Ross has cemented himself as an immortal figure in the rap game. Throughout his career, he has hit numerous roadblocks that the average rapper could not comeback from. The obstructions include (but are not limited to):\n\n\nIn 2008, it was reported that Ross, a drug rapper, spent 18 months working as a correctional officer.\nRoss survived his beef with 50 Cent, despite many people believing Fif was ‘destroying’ him for poking fun of his correctional officer past.\nIn 2013, Ross was bombarded with major backlash for what many perceived to be lyrics that promoted date rape.\n\n\n\nRoss conquered all these obstacles and is still one of the biggest names in the game today. It is common knowledge that nobody can hold Rozay back!", "annotation_id": "2617436", "url": "https://genius.com/2617436", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Say a nigga name and the car start", "vault_lines": ["Say a nigga name and the car start"], "meaning": "Earlier in 2013, Ross had to push to start his car. By the end of the year, he’s upgraded to a voice-commanded car: all he has to do is simply has to speak and the car will start itself.\n\nThis line is probably referencing his purchase of the 2014 Rolls Royce Wraith, the most technologically advanced car in the world.\n\nThis could also be referring to the fact that Ross and his goons are ready to ride and show up at your door if you mention his name in a scathing manner.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lrds0ju1qNM", "annotation_id": "2617294", "url": "https://genius.com/2617294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Nigga, let’s get this money nigga, woo, woo Masterminds, R-O-C, double M-G!", "vault_lines": ["Masterminds, R-O-C, double M-G!"], "meaning": "R-O-C refers to Roc-A-Fella Records, a record label founded by King Hov. MMG of course refers to Maybach Music Group, Rozay’s record label.\n\n\n\nThe masterminds of two of the hottest rap labels out have linked up once again to create yet another acclaimed collaboration, which will undoubtedly garner sales and thus, money.", "annotation_id": "2617171", "url": "https://genius.com/2617171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "We gon’ get this forever", "vault_lines": ["We gon' get this forever"], "meaning": "Getting money forever has been a theme for Rick Ross – he named both his Instagram and his acclaimed mixtape after the idea of everlasting wealth.\n\nHowever, in an interview with The Source, Ross spoke on what he truly thinks last forever:\n\nThe art means the most to me. I’m already rich. What ever else I get at this point is a plus. But to me, the art. That’s what lives forever. That’s what 50 years and 100 years from now, they’ll be reading my scrolls of shit I said, shit I tweeted, pictures on my Instagram. That shit is gonna make it in the Hall of Fame for geniuses. That’s what I wanted to do. The art is bigger than the money. […] That’s when the Mastermind title will mean even more.", "annotation_id": "2617078", "url": "https://genius.com/2617078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Masterminds!", "vault_lines": ["Masterminds, R-O-C, double M-G!"], "meaning": "Mastermind is Ross' sixth studio album, slated for an early 2014 release. This track is the album’s second single.\n\nWhile promoting this track, Ross spoke on the title of the album, saying:\n\nIt’s all about coming from wherever you come from and take it wherever you want to go to. And the minute you do that that’s when you can consider yourself a mastermind.\n\nIn an interview with The Source, Ross spoke on his biggest Mastermind Moment:\n\nJust being a real boss. When I say boss, ownership. Being top priority when I go to the table. When I negotiate. Another one of my biggest moves is stepping out of the music. Going into franchises and different things of that nature; Restaurants, steak houses, the things I love to do as a genuine fat boy.", "annotation_id": "2617054", "url": "https://genius.com/2617054", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Double up on that blow, bitch!", "vault_lines": ["Double up on that blow, bitch!"], "meaning": "Ross is all about expanding his cocaine market and profits. Earlier in the song, Ross noted that he’s looking for an increase from his plug, because Ross can sell his blow for twice as much as he bought it. Ergo, Ross wants as much coke from his plug as possible, because he knows he can double up on his revenue.", "annotation_id": "2578579", "url": "https://genius.com/2578579", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Nigga’s stick dirty but his dick clean", "vault_lines": ["Nigga's stick dirty but his dick clean"], "meaning": "This line is a direct reference back to a line of Ross' hook off “MC Hammer”:\n\nMy gun dirty, my brick clean\nI’m riding dirty, my dick clean\n\nRoss uses a clean/dirty wordplay to denote that his penis is scott-free but his gun (stick) isn’t.", "annotation_id": "2578240", "url": "https://genius.com/2578240", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Opposition want me dead or alive", "vault_lines": ["Opposition want me dead or alive"], "meaning": "His haters want him out of the picture, whether he’s dead or just locked up:\n\n\nOpposing drug dealers want him dead or in jail so that they can expand their drug empires into his territory.\nOpposing artists want him dead or in jail so they can get a piece of his sales and so that they can attempt to fill in his place as rap royalty.\n\n\n\nThese lines seem to refer to the attempt on his life on his 37th birthday.", "annotation_id": "2575668", "url": "https://genius.com/2575668", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "6 cribs for the cars in the car lot", "vault_lines": ["6 cribs for the cars in the car lot"], "meaning": "Ross is known for being a car collector, check out GQ’s piece on Boss' car lot.\n\nThis could refer to two things:\n\n\nThe cars in his car lot are worth as much as six mansions.\nRozay’s got so many cars that he needs over six mansions with large garages to hold them all. He’s balling.", "annotation_id": "2574239", "url": "https://genius.com/2574239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "My money goin’ on the deep end", "vault_lines": ["My money goin' on the deep end"], "meaning": "“To go off the deep end” is an idiom referring to jumping into a swimming pool where the water level is over one’s head, so that person needs to be able to swim.\n\nRoss has got so much money that he can fill a swimming pool with cash and swim in the deep end of that money-filled pool.", "annotation_id": "2573988", "url": "https://genius.com/2573988", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Motherfucker cause the devil is a lie", "vault_lines": ["Motherfucker cause the devil is a lie"], "meaning": "Rozay does what he wants and lives how he wants because he has no fear of the Devil. Rozay doesn’t believe the Devil exists so he has nothing to fear for his sinful ways.\n\nRoss is known for being a Christian and doubts the Devil’s existence, but believes God will forgive him for his sins; God Forgives, I Don’t. He places his faith in God, nobody else. He also shows his faith with his multiple Jesus Pieces on the cover of his GFID album.\n\nAlso, notice the wordplay with ‘devil is a lie’ and ‘devil is alive’.", "annotation_id": "2573728", "url": "https://genius.com/2573728", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Big guns and big whips Rich nigga talkin’ big shit", "vault_lines": ["Big guns and big whips", "Rich nigga talkin' big shit"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is known for being a big car collector; he loves cars just as much as he loves pulling out guns when dealing drugs. All the money that he earned through music and hustling lets him have some attitude when talking to other people. He can’t talk about hood stuff anymore; just like Hova said in La Familia:\n\nHead of the family, all my niggas bosses though\nY'all don’t understand we? We talk that shit bosses know", "annotation_id": "2573466", "url": "https://genius.com/2573466", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Club Armani where the cash is", "vault_lines": ["Club Armani where the cash is"], "meaning": "Ross is referring to the Armani Prive, the club fashioned by Giorgio Armani inside the Burj Khalifa in Dubai where Rozay and his frieds blow all their money.", "annotation_id": "2573447", "url": "https://genius.com/2573447", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Bravado", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In reference to the previous line, Jay is bragging about having a whole floor at Barney’s to himself.", "annotation_id": "2573435", "url": "https://genius.com/2573435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "The devil try to hit me with the RICO, them black people", "vault_lines": ["The devil try to hit me with the RICO, them black people"], "meaning": "The Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act is a federal law that keeps an eye on suspicious money activity to tackle ongoing criminal organization.\n\nOn This Life Forever, Jay noted:\n\nFeds still tryna build a case since ‘93. I told them I’m retired, but they like whatever, you know them pigs don’t wanna see you get your life together\n\nAnd on BBC Jay went on like this:\n\nCuban link 5 kilo\nYour life is illegal when your chain can get the RICO\n\nJay Z’s lifestyle is so flashy that he might catch RICO’s attention, even though he stopped selling drugs a long time ago he still acts like he was a drug kingpin with shiny chains and expensive cars.\n\nJay goes onto note that he feels black people are to him as the RICO is to drug dealers; just like unusual wealth activities picked up under the RICO Act, blacks assume something is suspicious by a black man being so rich.", "annotation_id": "2573393", "url": "https://genius.com/2573393", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Jay, I got it, I got it", "vault_lines": ["Jay, I got it, I got it"], "meaning": "A reference to a track on Jay Z’s 2013 album Magna Carta Holy Grail, titled “FuckWithMeYouKnowIGotIt” which Ross features on.\n\nThe track was originally supposed to be on Ross' MasterMind album. Boi-1da spoke on how Jay ended up with record:\n\nThe beat was sent to Rick Ross who intended to use it for his upcoming album, Mastermind. Jay Z was supposed to add a guest verse to it, but when he heard the instrumental, he wanted the track for his album.\n\nIn the end a reprised version of the song without any verses from Jay did end up on Mastermind as one of the bonus tracks on the deluxe edition. It is titled “You Know I Got It (Reprise)” and is the final of the three bonus tracks.", "annotation_id": "2573357", "url": "https://genius.com/2573357", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Bow your head cause it’s time to pay tithes", "vault_lines": ["Bow your head cause it's time to pay tithes"], "meaning": "A tithe is a one-tenth part of something, paid as a contribution to a religious organization or compulsory tax to government. Usually associated with the church, paying tithes keeps up with the underlying religious theme of the song.\n\nRick Ross here declares himself the head of the rap game and other rappers have to pay their tithes to him. He could be using the word tithes to symbolize the respect the other rappers and rap fans in general should be ‘paying’ him.", "annotation_id": "2573308", "url": "https://genius.com/2573308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Black bottle and a bad bitch", "vault_lines": ["Black bottle and a bad bitch"], "meaning": "A reference to Belaire Rose, with whom Maybach Music are in partnership with. Of course, Rozay has to have it with some Diced Pineapples.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MaybachMusicGrp/status/413934507365244928", "annotation_id": "2573268", "url": "https://genius.com/2573268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Curtains in the Maybach bitch peek in", "vault_lines": ["Curtains in the Maybach bitch peek in"], "meaning": "Maybachs are known to have curtains on the windows and all the girls want to peek in to see what celebrity could be hiding behind them.\n\nAlso a reference to both his label, Maybach Music Group, and a track he was featured on, “Maybach Curtains”.", "annotation_id": "2573157", "url": "https://genius.com/2573157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "The hatin’ is flagrant, hit your free throws", "vault_lines": ["The hatin' is flagrant, hit your free throws"], "meaning": "In basketball, a flagrant foul is called due to contact that is deemed excessive or unnecessary. It is a serious personal foul. The team who draws a flagrant foul receives two free throws and possession of the ball.\n\nIn relation to the song, Hov chides his haters: what they do is unnecessary and needs to be backed up with substance and facts, not childish assertions. Specifically, saying Jay-Z is not the King of NY is one thing, but saying Kendrick is is pretty flagrant.", "annotation_id": "2573084", "url": "https://genius.com/2573084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Fuck the game raw when I came in it", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the game raw when I came in it"], "meaning": "Rick Ross started his career by dropping one of the biggest rap records of all time, Hustlin, without warning. Ross rode the success of the single and topped the charts with his debut album, Port of Miami.\n\nFucking the game is a metaphor to say that he owned the rap game as soon as he came in it, which is another sex metaphor.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MaybachMusicGrp/status/413934006007508992", "annotation_id": "2573033", "url": "https://genius.com/2573033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Two mill’ on that I-95", "vault_lines": ["Two mill' on that I-95"], "meaning": "I-95 is the main highway on the East Coast of the United States. It begins just south of downtown Miami (Ross' hometown) and runs primarily through Florida.\n\nTwo mil could refer to three things:\n\n\nA reference to the previous line, meaning that Ross is moving $2 million worth of coke via I-95.\nA reference to transporting $2 million in drug money across the I-95 highway.\nIt could also refer to the price of Ross' car, on the highway. The most expensive car in the world is the Bugatti Veyron, which is valued at $1.7 million, but after taxes, tags, and titles, the car should be well over $2 mill.", "annotation_id": "2573029", "url": "https://genius.com/2573029", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Gettin white money but I’m still black", "vault_lines": ["Gettin white money but I'm still black"], "meaning": "It is stereotyped that the average Black male makes much less money than the average White male, but Jay broke that stereotype. From sports money (Roc Nation Sports Agency), to Cigar money (Cohiba), to alcoholic beverage money (D'usse) – Jay is eatin'.\n\nBit of word play with the ‘white money’; a reference to cocaine-selling past. But tying in with the previous stereotype sentiment, the larger drug cartels are commonly thought to be headed by Latinos but he’s a black man running things thus shattering this stereotype too.", "annotation_id": "2573014", "url": "https://genius.com/2573014", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Went gold 6 times for a gold digger", "vault_lines": ["Went gold 6 times for a gold digger"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is bragging about his RIAA certifications that he’s accrued so far. However, Ross actually has seven gold plaques, not six. He made that music for one goal: to make money, so he could get out of the hood and live an extravagant lifestyle.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MaybachMusicGrp/status/413934445654474752", "annotation_id": "2572994", "url": "https://genius.com/2572994", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "[Verse 3: JAY-Z]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Jay again speaks out against all the Illuminati conspiracies that swirl around him, similar to a previous collaboration he did with Rick Ross, “Free Mason”.\n\n\n\nOn “Heaven”, off his recent album, Magna Carta Holy Grail, he also spoke on this topic. Perhaps these accusations are starting to bother him?", "annotation_id": "2572981", "url": "https://genius.com/2572981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "You know whenever we link up, my nigga They think this shit comes from outer space or something, haha", "vault_lines": ["They think this shit comes from outer space or something, haha"], "meaning": "Rozay and Jay have collaborated together for a number of different tracks together since Jay signed Ross to Def Jam.\n\nRoss knows that a Rozay-Hov collaboration is highly anticipated, their collabs are usually seen as standout tracks.\n\nTheir collaborations include the remix of Rick Ross' “Hustlin'”, Ross' original “Maybach Music”, “Free Mason”, “3 Kings”, and more recently, they came together to make one of the standout tracks on Jay’s latest effort, on the song “FuckWithMeYouKnowIGotIt”.", "annotation_id": "2572944", "url": "https://genius.com/2572944", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Nigga switching lane to lane like Wal-Mart", "vault_lines": ["Nigga switching lane to lane like Wal-Mart"], "meaning": "In Wal-Mart, people switch lanes as they shop to get to each section. Because Wal-Mart carries various products, the stores are usually packed.\n\n\n\nMuch like Wal-Mart, the streets of Miami have much traffic. Similar to Wal-Mart shoppers, Ross switches lanes to work his way around traffic since his car is so fast compared to everyone else’s. Ross could also be switching lane to lane to show off his brilliant car.\n\nThis line could also be referencing that one of Ross' enemies is driving fast and frantically switching lanes to get away from Ross, because of his fear of Rick.", "annotation_id": "2572940", "url": "https://genius.com/2572940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Oh we can’t be a nigga if a nigga rich? Oh we gotta be the devil that’s some nigga shit", "vault_lines": ["Oh we gotta be the devil that's some nigga shit"], "meaning": "When black rappers get rich, people expect them to change their behavior, turning into something that they’re not. Just like Kanye said on Clique (which also featured Jay):\n\n You know white people get money, don’t spend it\nOr maybe they get money, buy a business\nI rather buy 80 gold chains and go ign'ant\nI know Spike Lee gone kill me but let me finish\n\nIf Hova wants to blow a hundred grand on champagne instead of buying stocks, people shouldn’t judge him.\n\nThe second line links back to the gotta be Illuminati if a nigga shine line above and to his track off Reasonable Doubt, D'Evils.\n\nWhen artists start making a lot of money, people start claiming that they’ve sold their soul to the Illuminati and hate on them for no reason. This also happens when poor people make it to the top, all the cats you used to hang out with back in the day get jealous, that’s some nigga shit for real.\n\nThe flow appears to reference another New York artist; A$AP Rocky; specifically the way the latter raps some similar lines on Fuckin' Problems.", "annotation_id": "2572918", "url": "https://genius.com/2572918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Car seats still smelling like 10 ki’s Tell the plug that I’m lookin’ for an increase", "vault_lines": ["Car seats still smelling like 10 ki's", "Tell the plug that I'm lookin' for an increase"], "meaning": "That’s Some Good Coke!\n\nThe Boss just came back from dropping off ten kilograms of cocaine. That much weight can really leave a stench in your car.\n\nBut 10 ki’s just ain’t enough. Ross is telling his plug (also known as his supplier) to up his shipment!\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MaybachMusicGrp/status/413933641023389696\nhttps://twitter.com/MaybachMusicGrp/status/413933855281004544", "annotation_id": "2572913", "url": "https://genius.com/2572913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "You seen what I did to the stop and frisk Brooklyn on the Barney’s like we own the bitch Give the money to the hood, now we all win", "vault_lines": ["You seen what I did to the stop and frisk", "Brooklyn on the Barney's like we own the bitch", "Give the money to the hood, now we all win"], "meaning": "He was under heavy pressure to back out of his collaboration with the luxury store Barneys New York after it was accused of racially profiling two black customers.\n\n\n\nInstead of running away from the problem, leaving all the money he initially intended to donate to The Shawn Carter Foundation, a non-profit charitable organization which his mother runs that grants educational scholarships to those who can’t afford college, he renegotiated the deal to increase the percentages.\n\nAs I previously stated, the collaboration with Barneys has always been about giving and The Shawn Carter Foundation. From this collection, the Foundation will receive not only 25% of sales, it will now receive the additional 75% of Barneys’ sales, totaling 100% of all sales from BNY SCC. Along with 100% of sales from the collaboration, the Foundation will receive an additional 10% of all retail sales from Barneys New York stores nationwide and Barneys.com on November 20th.\n\nRemember: he can’t help the poor if he’s one of them.", "annotation_id": "2572828", "url": "https://genius.com/2572828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Beast Coast, winnin’ at life, nigga, cheat code", "vault_lines": ["Beast Coast, winnin' at life, nigga, cheat code"], "meaning": "After Notorious B.I.G. passed away, the title of “Best MC of NYC” was vacant and Jay Z and Nas battled for it. After 2007, when they stopped fighting, no one else claimed the East Coast crown. Then Control happened:\n\nI’m Makaveli’s offspring, I’m the king of New York\nKing of the Coast, one hand, I juggle them both\n\nEven though Hova wasn’t mentioned in the diss part of Kendrick’s verse, he wants to make a statement and remember everyone that he runs NYC.\n\n\n\nPeople who use cheat codes in videogames have an unfair advantage, that’s the same for Jay, there’s no way someone will be considered bigger than him after all he’s done. He was born with the life cheat code.", "annotation_id": "2572823", "url": "https://genius.com/2572823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Top floor nigga, Burj Khalifa!", "vault_lines": ["Top floor nigga, Burj Khalifa!"], "meaning": "The Burj Khalifa, located in Dubai (which ties into the previous line) is the tallest building in the history of man and stands at 2,722 feet.\n\nWhile visiting Dubai in 2013, Ross visited the building and purchased an apartment in there, marking the first time that World’s Biggest Boss visited the World’s Biggest Building.", "annotation_id": "2572814", "url": "https://genius.com/2572814", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Coulda got blacklist for the crack shit", "vault_lines": ["Coulda got blacklist for the crack shit"], "meaning": "It’s no secret that Jay used to sell cocaine in the 80’s – he had been drug dealing since he was 13 years old. Though he never was convicted of selling drugs, he was given 3 years of probation for a stabbing altercation back in 1999. He could have gotten black listed for his past dealings.\n\nHe talked about this more in Izzo (H.O.V.A.).\n\n\n\n#Peep NYPD’s secret file on him here", "annotation_id": "2572809", "url": "https://genius.com/2572809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Dubai I can do it like a sheikh", "vault_lines": ["Dubai I can do it like a sheikh"], "meaning": "Dubai is a city in the United Arab Emirates that is known for its wealth and excess. Earlier in 2013, Rozay has did it big there. A sheikh is a term of respect in Arabic that means “leader.”\n\nDoing it like a sheikh is probably as big as it can possibly be done, considering many of them are among the richest people in the world. They have made vast fortunes off of the oil and gas industry in the Middle East.\n\nSheikhs are known to be fans of all gold everything. This includes white gold cars, gold-bar dispensing ATMs, and much more.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MaybachMusicGrp/status/413934602114572289", "annotation_id": "2572800", "url": "https://genius.com/2572800", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Talkin’ half a milli’ for the weekend Contract like a nigga play defense", "vault_lines": ["Talkin' half a milli' for the weekend", "Contract like a nigga play defense"], "meaning": "A highly paid NFL defender’s contract would give him around $500K for  every game he plays. Football games are usually played on weekends.\n\nSimilarly, Rick Ross is going to make $500K over a weekend from a either drug deal, a concert, or by completing 5 feature verses (as he noted earlier that he charges $100K for a verse).\n\nIn real life, Ross played high school football and was a standout offensive guard.", "annotation_id": "2572791", "url": "https://genius.com/2572791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "All these niggas claiming king but I’m still that King Hova, Mansa Musa", "vault_lines": ["All these niggas claiming king but I'm still that", "King Hova, Mansa Musa"], "meaning": "A generalized response to anyone naming themselves “King”, eg: Pusha T & Kendrick Lamar, Hov reminds them who the O.G was.\n\nHe compares himself to King Mansa Musa of Mali who was named richest man of all time. After all, he’s got the facts to back up the claim, who else sold 1 million records before their album even drops?", "annotation_id": "2572779", "url": "https://genius.com/2572779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Back to the Benzo when the ends low", "vault_lines": ["Back to the Benzo when the ends low"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n\n\nWhen Ross' connects don’t come through and his coke profits begin to suffer, he is still able to stunt on hoes by riding around in an expensive ass 600 Benz. Going back to the Benzo signifies the street hustle, what made the Enzo possible.\nWhen Ross needs money and his coke supply is running low he switches back to selling Benzodiazepine pills, which is a cheap drug that hustlers usually push when they are strapped for cash.", "annotation_id": "2572754", "url": "https://genius.com/2572754", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Like Mavado, boy I’m that gully", "vault_lines": ["like Mavado, boy I'm that gully"], "meaning": "Reference to DJ Khaled’s artist Mavado, from Kingston, Jamaica.\n\nGully is Jamaican slang for hood. Mavado is also affectionately known as Gully Gad.", "annotation_id": "2572749", "url": "https://genius.com/2572749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "White Jesus in my crock pot I mix the shit with some soda", "vault_lines": ["White Jesus in my crock pot", "I mix the shit with some soda"], "meaning": "Hov uses a common euphemism for cocaine, white Jesus, and describes the process of cooking crack by adding baking soda to pure cocaine.", "annotation_id": "2572744", "url": "https://genius.com/2572744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Double cup, gold wrist", "vault_lines": ["Double cup, gold wrist"], "meaning": "A reference to drinking Purple Drank, as it is typically drunk out of double styrofoam cups to keep the condensation off your hands.\n\n\n\nThe gold on his wrist symbolizes the big and expensive watches he is known for wearing, as we all know Ross is a watch connoisseur.", "annotation_id": "2572722", "url": "https://genius.com/2572722", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Am I down with the devil ’cause my roof come up missin’? Is that Lucifer juice in that two cup he sippin’? That’s D’usse baby welcome to the dark side", "vault_lines": ["Am I down with the devil 'cause my roof come up missin'?", "Is that Lucifer juice in that two cup he sippin'?", "That's D'usse baby welcome to the dark side"], "meaning": "Jay is asking why he can’t be successful without being questioned about it. Is he a mason? Is he Illuminati? Did he sell his soul to the devil? Just because Jay Z is in that drop top Lamborgini Diablo(Spanish word for Devil), doesn’t mean he’s a satanist.\n\n\n\nNothing sinister in his cup either, it’s just D'usse, a dark liquor. Also a possible reference to Jay’s song Lucifer.\n\n\n\nHov also uses a literary technique known as Assonance using the “OO” sound (True, Roof, Lucifer, Juice, Two, D'usse) to enhance his rhyme scheme.", "annotation_id": "2572719", "url": "https://genius.com/2572719", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Getting money ever since I came in it", "vault_lines": ["Getting money ever since I came in it"], "meaning": "Ross has always been hustlin' and getting money since he came into the game – by the time he was 18, he already had $100K in gold, through his crack dealing. Even Ross' debut album, Port of Miami, topped the sales charts its first week out, so he’s been eatin' from the start.\n\n\n\nThis could also be a metaphor, where hip-hop is portrayed as a girl. When guys cum in girls, they get pregnant and the man has to pay child support; the girl gets money ever since the guy came in her, therefore she’s winning. Ross could be making a contrast to further emphasize how much of a winner he is – he came in the girl (a metaphor for hip-hop) and instead of her winning, he’s the one getting paid.", "annotation_id": "2572679", "url": "https://genius.com/2572679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Hazard lights flashing on the four-door Switch the Benzo for the Enzo", "vault_lines": ["Hazard lights flashing on the four-door", "Switch the Benzo for the Enzo"], "meaning": "Ross is known for being a car collector. Rick noted that early in his street career he had a 600 Benz, but now he has made enough money to upgrade to the more expensive Ferrari Enzo.", "annotation_id": "2572649", "url": "https://genius.com/2572649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Devil want these niggas hate they own kind Gotta be Illuminati if a nigga shine", "vault_lines": ["Devil want these niggas hate they own kind", "Gotta be Illuminati if a nigga shine"], "meaning": "Conspiracy theorists screaming Illuminati\n\nWith a line that could possibly finally stop the Illuminati rumors once and for all, Jay-Z finally puts this into perspective. Why can’t a black man be successful without it being part of an “evil” plot though? Why can’t other African-Americans be happy for his success instead of claiming that he got it unfairly?\n\n\n\nThe reference to shining is also a play on words, as the Illuminati are said to be the illuminated ones, the shining ones. the bright ones, etc.", "annotation_id": "2572646", "url": "https://genius.com/2572646", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Is Hova atheist? I never fuck with True Religion", "vault_lines": ["Is Hova atheist? I never fuck with True Religion"], "meaning": "Referring to True Religion jeans and also carrying on the theme of religious topic from the hook, Jay has said many times in interviews that he is not a religious man and does not believe in religions, but he does believe in a God and does not believe in a hell or the Devil.\n\nAnd no, I am not a Christian, though I believe in God\nBut I don’t believe in the devil, my beliefs are odd\n\nDuring an interview with Power 105 in NY he further said “religion is like a personal computer” alluding that it was a personal decision how much one chooses to let others in on their view.\n\n\n\nNotice also how he uses his Hova moniker  in this line, to contrast the True Religion part. This is notable as Jay is somewhat conveying that should God exist, it doesn’t apply to religion. This point of view has been reflected in the above examples.", "annotation_id": "2572638", "url": "https://genius.com/2572638", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "line": "Now I’m black Jesus turn water to wine And all I had to do was turn the stove up", "vault_lines": ["Now I'm black Jesus turn water to wine", "And all I had to do was turn the stove up"], "meaning": "When Jay Z was younger he used to have no money and could only afford water and enough food to survive. This changed when he started dealing and cooking drugs in his hood.\n\nAfter founding Roc-A-Fella records and getting rich, he could afford finer things. Water transformed into wine and cheap plastic cups transformed into holy grails.\n\n\n\nAlso, think for a second about what noise water makes when you boil it for i.e tea…\n\nYes! You got it as well! Clever play on words from Hov as he can make water to wine/whine, just by turning the stove up (to a higher temperature).", "annotation_id": "2572631", "url": "https://genius.com/2572631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Devil Is a Lie", "status": "done", "targets": 56, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-the-devil-is-a-lie-lyrics", "genius_title": "The Devil Is a Lie", "genius_id": 306279, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Game", "line": "There is heaven in winning, and hell in not trying", "vault_lines": ["Thеre is heaven in winning, and hell in not trying"], "meaning": "There is a 100% chance of failure if you don’t try anything in your life. Take a chance on yourself and who knows you  might experience your wildest dreams coming to fruition.", "annotation_id": "28531733", "url": "https://genius.com/28531733", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
