{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Heat fitted, G-5 with the nose up", "vault_lines": ["Heat fitted, G-5 with the nose up"], "meaning": "Ross paints a picture of him wearing a Miami Heat fitted cap (a staple of his wardrobe to represent his home of Miami) while on a G5 or Gulfstream V Jet while it’s taking off.", "annotation_id": "18401149", "url": "https://genius.com/18401149", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Who do whatever I ask of her, dead Siri (Feel me?)", "vault_lines": ["Who do whatever I ask of her, dead Siri (Feel me?)"], "meaning": "Fire double entendre by Fab.\n\nHe’s dead serious about his girl doing whatever he says, and, because she does whatever he wants, he compares her to Siri, the virtual assistant on iPhones who will respond to anything you ask her.", "annotation_id": "18401130", "url": "https://genius.com/18401130", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Like you can get with this (Or) or you can get with that (Huh) I think you get with this (Huh) cause this is where it’s at (Haha)", "vault_lines": ["Like you can get with this (Or) or you can get with that (Huh)", "I think you get with this (Huh) cause this is where it's at (Haha)"], "meaning": "Taken from “The Choice is Yours” by the Black Sheep:\n\nYou can get with this, or you can get with that\nYou can get with this, or you can get with that\nYou can get with this, or you can get with that\nI think you’ll get with this, for this is where it’s at", "annotation_id": "6314380", "url": "https://genius.com/6314380", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Be creative, stop bein’ basic", "vault_lines": ["Be creative, stop bein' basic"], "meaning": "Do something unique, don’t follow in everybody else’s footsteps. Do what you do best and don’t imitate anyone, you are yourself for a reason.", "annotation_id": "2856453", "url": "https://genius.com/2856453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Life’s a game, it’s only how you play it", "vault_lines": ["Life's a game, it's only how you play it"], "meaning": "Life is a strategic game. Make the wrong moves and you’ll deal with bad consequences throughout your life. Make good choices when an opportunity arises and you can become a great person.", "annotation_id": "2856438", "url": "https://genius.com/2856438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Wind through the window blew the candle out No lights, many cold nights", "vault_lines": ["Wind through the window blew the candle out", "No lights, many cold nights"], "meaning": "Being that his parents were poor, they couldn’t afford lighting in his house, so they would use a candle as a siurce of light. The wind from outside blew into his house and extinguished his candles flame.\n\nAs well as a source of light, the candles were also used  as a source of heat, this explaining why the nights were cold.", "annotation_id": "2856427", "url": "https://genius.com/2856427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "I pray I never fumble", "vault_lines": ["I pray I never fumble"], "meaning": "“Fumble” is a metaphor which relates:\n\n\nFumbling in football which is to drop the ball and possibly allow the other team to take it\nAlso symbolizes failure or losing something you once had, in this case Ross not wanting to lose his money/fame/talent", "annotation_id": "2279098", "url": "https://genius.com/2279098", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Yesterday’s home-runs won’t win today’s games, nigga Win today’s games, nigga, uh", "vault_lines": ["Yesterday's home-runs won't win today's games, nigga", "Win today's games, nigga, uh"], "meaning": "While hitting a home run is great and very helpful in winning a game, there’s always a new game to be played in which that previous homer doesn’t count.\n\nIn musical terms, your old “hits” don’t make your current stuff good\n\nEvery day is a new opportunity. You can build on yesterday’s success or put its failures behind and start over again. That’s the way life is, with a new game every day, and that’s the way baseball is – Former MLB great Bob Feller", "annotation_id": "2279093", "url": "https://genius.com/2279093", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Silence is golden, duck tape is silver (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Silence is golden, duck tape is silver (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“Silence is golden” is an idiom that recognizes the importance of quiet and is also a song popularized by the English rock band The Tremeloes\n\nFabolous also includes a threat in this line that duct tape, which unlike the metaphorical “golden silence”, is a silver object that can also bring silence when it’s put over someone’s mouth\n\n\n\nHe also implies that duct tape would be the second best option, as silver symbolizes second place when given out as medals.\n\nFabolous hands out his medals accordingly:\n\n1st Place – Shut the fuck up\n2nd Place – Duct tape over the mouth\n3rd Place – Death?", "annotation_id": "2279085", "url": "https://genius.com/2279085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Keep your two cents to yourself, you might need it later (Word)", "vault_lines": ["Keep your two cents to yourself, you might need it later (Word)"], "meaning": "To give someone your “two cents” is to speak your mind or opinion on the subject.\n\nHowever, Fabolous doesn’t care to hear “broke niggas” speak and thinks you should keep it to yourself as if it were actual money. He thinks they might need that change since they aren’t as rich as he is", "annotation_id": "2279079", "url": "https://genius.com/2279079", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "I be posted like I’m 7’4\"", "vault_lines": ["I be posted like I’m 7’4\""], "meaning": "To be “posted” is to be chilling or hanging in a place.\n\nAlternatively, to post up in basketball is an offensive technique in which you leverage your body in front of the defender so that your back blocks him from intercepting the pass.\n\nThis is a common technique that is more effective when used by a tall and strong player. 7'4\" fits that mold\n\n\n\n7'6\" Yao Ming posting up 6'6\" Kobe Bryant", "annotation_id": "2279058", "url": "https://genius.com/2279058", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "A Carol City rapper facing the music Connected to an alleged robbery and assault Gunplay surrendered at Miami-Dade headquarter The charge armed robbery means he cannot post bond", "vault_lines": ["Connected to an alleged robbery and assault", "Gunplay surrendered at Miami-Dade headquarter", "The charge armed robbery means he cannot post bond"], "meaning": "In April 2012, Gunplay was charged with armed robbery, assault with a deadly weapon, and aggravated assault after pulling a gun on his accountant. He faced life in prison, however the charges were dropped when the victim was unwilling to cooperate with authorities.\n\nCheck the security footage of the crimes:\n\nhttp://youtu.be/cHLHKtPB94Y", "annotation_id": "2251005", "url": "https://genius.com/2251005", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "200 mil’ how I get it, damn I can’t be far", "vault_lines": ["200 mil' how I get it, damn I can't be far"], "meaning": "Rozay is aiming to reach $200 million and feels as though this is within his capacity.\n\nThough his apparent net worth is $28 million, he claims to have $50 million in his songs.\n\n50M’s in the bank, I get me 200, I’m gone", "annotation_id": "2241502", "url": "https://genius.com/2241502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Your bitch gar-B A-G-E", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Your bitch is “garbage” meaning trash. She doesn’t look good.  He just spelled out the last letters to fit the scheme and rhyme the particular flow he was using.", "annotation_id": "2225881", "url": "https://genius.com/2225881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "[Interlude: Kay Foxx] It’s Kay Foxx reporting live", "vault_lines": ["It's Kay Foxx reporting live"], "meaning": "Kay Foxx used to work on 99Jamz in Miami, she hosted “The Takeover” with MMG affiliated DJ Khaled, so it makes a lot of sense to have her on this interlude.", "annotation_id": "2218594", "url": "https://genius.com/2218594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Yeah, my women vary, just give me a young Tahiry", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my women vary, just give me a young Tahiry"], "meaning": "Tahiry is model, known for dating Joe Budden. As bad as they come", "annotation_id": "2217716", "url": "https://genius.com/2217716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Professional shooters, Leon and Mathilda", "vault_lines": ["Professional shooters, Leon and Mathilda"], "meaning": "Léon: The Professional; a movie made in 1994 about a mob hit man who takes in a girl after her family is killed.", "annotation_id": "2217714", "url": "https://genius.com/2217714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Rockie Fresh, and I’m from Chicago (M-M-M-Maybach Music) Where young niggas die every few seconds But we still just wanna be great Americans, yeah", "vault_lines": ["But we still just wanna be great Americans, yeah"], "meaning": "Gang violence continues to take a heavy toll on Chicago. But Rockie wants you to remember that they’re also human beings, they just operates in the environment they’ve been put in, with desires to live a comfortable and successful life.\n\n314 soldiers died in Iraq, 509 died in Chicago\n- Kanye West", "annotation_id": "2217596", "url": "https://genius.com/2217596", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Don’t it sound like I’m dedicated? Joe Flacco deal, nigga with hot flows", "vault_lines": ["Don't it sound like I'm dedicated?", "Joe Flacco deal, nigga with hot flows"], "meaning": "The Super Bowl MVP recently signed his new contract with Baltimore Ravens potentially worth $120.6 millions that makes him the highest-paid player in NFL history.\n\n\n\nBack in April, Ross tweeted this line.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/328313113583697921", "annotation_id": "2217582", "url": "https://genius.com/2217582", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Uh, my car be parked out front of Darby", "vault_lines": ["Uh, my car be parked out front of Darby"], "meaning": "The Darby is fine cuisine in New York, description from their website:\n\nSetting the tone for the ultimate dining experience, The Darby offers a mix of innovative culinary offerings and interactive live performances created by visionary restaurateurs Scott Sartiano and Richie Akiva along with partner Ronnie Madra. The restaurant restores the glamour, charm and exuberance of a bygone era to 244 West 14th Street, located in the legendary Nell’s space.", "annotation_id": "2217475", "url": "https://genius.com/2217475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Great Americans", "line": "Uh, I was born to be another number So was number one,", "vault_lines": ["So was number one,"], "meaning": "Ross, as a young African American from the ghetto, was condemned to be just another statistic from birth, vulnerable to homicide due to gang violence. This sentiment has been expressed by several other rappers, including Kanye and Jay Z and Pusha T.\n\nBut Ross was determined to not be just like others in his position, but rise up and make it to the top – number 1.\n\nHe is, after all, the Bawse.", "annotation_id": "2208686", "url": "https://genius.com/2208686", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
