{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Show", "line": "Don’t know your lady’s cleaners, but I’m in her jeans as much", "vault_lines": ["Don't know your lady's cleaners, but I'm in her jeans as much"], "meaning": "Sometimes when your jeans or any other clothes are dirty you take them to the cleaners, Some dry cleaners will go inside the clothing to clean them thoroughly\n\nto get in a woman’s pants means to engage in intercourse. Wale is saying he doesn’t know who cleans this woman’s pants but he gets inside of them just as much", "annotation_id": "2422387", "url": "https://genius.com/2422387", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Show", "line": "The cars and clothes It’s all for show So let’s start the show Let’s start the show Let’s start the show Let’s start the show", "vault_lines": ["The cars and clothes", "It's all for show", "So let's start the show", "Let's start the show"], "meaning": "Let’s get back to real rap now. Enough with this focus on material possessions (cars and clothes, it’s all for show). As Wale states in the first two lines of the next verse, he’s obviously pretty well off. Not that it ever was just about money, but now more than ever, it’s about integrity and continuing to earn respect.", "annotation_id": "1475995", "url": "https://genius.com/1475995", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
