{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Show", "line": "Never put mama on hold up whenever she call", "vault_lines": ["Never put mama on hold up whenever she call"], "meaning": "Ross has always taken his mother’s calls, no matter how busy he is. In the Rolling Stone story, Ross detailed his good relationship with his mother.", "annotation_id": "1345004", "url": "https://genius.com/1345004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Show", "line": "I came here to eat every way to the bone", "vault_lines": ["I came here to eat every way to the bone"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre.\n\n“Eating” is known to be a metaphor for “working”. Ross has one of (if not the best) work ethic in the rap game, which is why he’s on top of the game.\n\nHowever, Ross also probably means eating in the literally definition.", "annotation_id": "1344996", "url": "https://genius.com/1344996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Show", "line": "Don’t say on the beat what you won’t say in the streets Cause face to face niggas never said it to me", "vault_lines": ["Cause face to face niggas never said it to me"], "meaning": "Ross is saying that the things other rappers say on a song, they won’t repeat and say to his face.\n\nSimilar to what he said on Ali Bomaye.", "annotation_id": "1343913", "url": "https://genius.com/1343913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
