{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Everytime you look around they spinning one of mine", "vault_lines": ["Everytime you look around they spinning one of mine"], "meaning": "No matter where you go, all the DJ’s are playing a Ross record. Namely, BMF, the song that started the feud between these two.", "annotation_id": "1455630", "url": "https://genius.com/1455630", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Self made, you just affiliated", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A line from “B.M.F.”, directed at Young Jeezy. Ross built himself as a rap megastar by himself, while Jeezy rose to fame by being affiliated with the Black Mafia Family.", "annotation_id": "1455625", "url": "https://genius.com/1455625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Bitch I run the south, I’m what you wanna be", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I run the south, I'm what you wanna be"], "meaning": "Ross is claiming to be the best rapper from the South. With all the success he had during the Summer of 2010, it’s hard to argue. Ross is insinuating that Jeezy wishes to be like Ross, as he ends this verse by saying that Jeezy idolizes him.", "annotation_id": "1455603", "url": "https://genius.com/1455603", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "You niggas is petty,", "vault_lines": ["You niggas is petty,"], "meaning": "In 2010, Jeezy’s buzz was dying down fast. He struggled to get a solid release date for his album, TM103. After Jay-Z had departed Def Jam, Rick Ross had become Def Jam’s flagship artist. This lead to Jeezy’s jealousy that ignited the feud between the two artists. Ross addresses Jeezy as pathetic, later on in this song for this.", "annotation_id": "1455579", "url": "https://genius.com/1455579", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Vacheron Don you niggas ain’t ready", "vault_lines": ["Vacheron Don you niggas ain't ready"], "meaning": "Not only is Ross the Teflon Don, but he is the Vacheron Don because of the Vacheron Constantin watch on his wrist.", "annotation_id": "1455571", "url": "https://genius.com/1455571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "You niggas spaghetti Bustin’ yo meatball, nigga you better be ready", "vault_lines": ["Bustin' yo meatball, nigga you better be ready"], "meaning": "Spaghetti is extremely soft, like Jeezy. Ross will bust Jeezy’s head, and they better be ready for war.\n\nAlso, note the spaghetti/meatball rhyme, two foods that are often eaten together.", "annotation_id": "1455568", "url": "https://genius.com/1455568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "The summer’s mine The summer’s mine I’m buying ten bottles bitch and I’m on number nine The summer’s mine The summer’s mine Everytime she see a new whip she know it’s one of mine", "vault_lines": ["Everytime she see a new whip she know it's one of mine"], "meaning": "The summer of 2010 belonged to Ross. It started with the critically acclaimed mixtape, The Albert Anastasia EP which birthed the moniker Ricky Rozay. The tape contained the smash hit “BMF”, which went on to be not only the biggest jam of the summer, but of the year. On July 20th, Ross released his critically acclaimed album, Teflon Don which debuted high on the charts and was certified gold.\n\n\n\nRoss celebrated the success of his summer by purchasing 10 bottles of Rosé and new cars.", "annotation_id": "1455565", "url": "https://genius.com/1455565", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Fuck boi, Fuck boi, Fuck boi, FUCK BOI!!!", "vault_lines": ["Fuck boi, Fuck boi, Fuck boi, FUCK BOI!!!"], "meaning": "The line that almost ended Jeezy’s career. A fuck boi is just about the worst thing you can call someone, it’s a person who is a weak ass pussy that ain’t bout shit. It’s a term that comes from the South. This line is aimed at Jeezy, and after this song dropped Jeezy had a hard time getting his album to drop, and resorted to releasing mixtapes to try to generate buzz.", "annotation_id": "1455553", "url": "https://genius.com/1455553", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "I assassinate and employ them all", "vault_lines": ["I assassinate and employ them all"], "meaning": "He’ll take out Jeezy and then he’ll sign all of CTE to MMG.\n\nRoss could also be saying he will kill, or he’ll employ others to kill for him.", "annotation_id": "1119887", "url": "https://genius.com/1119887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "They used his credit cards just to get they rental cars", "vault_lines": ["They used his credit cards just to get they rental cars"], "meaning": "“They” refers Black Mafia Family. He’s saying that they cared so little about Young Jeezy, that they wasted his money on things that weren’t important.", "annotation_id": "703981", "url": "https://genius.com/703981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Really a water-boy, nigga you entertainment", "vault_lines": ["Really a water-boy, nigga you entertainment"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is saying that Young Jeezy isn’t even a major player in the Black Mafia Family, he’s just Big Meech’s bitch, a rapper who entertains people and claims to be in the gang.", "annotation_id": "703970", "url": "https://genius.com/703970", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Just when I thought I was out..they pull me back in", "vault_lines": ["Just when I thought I was out..they pull me back in"], "meaning": "Famous line from the legendary movie “The Godfather”.\n\n\n\nThis is a reference to his beefs. Just when Ross thought he was done with the 50 Cent beef, Young Jeezy dragged him into another fued.", "annotation_id": "703963", "url": "https://genius.com/703963", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Be honest with yourself I’m who you idolize", "vault_lines": ["Be honest with yourself I'm who you idolize"], "meaning": "Rick Ross and Young Jeezy did a few songs together, and Rick Ross went hard as hell on all of them. Rozay is saying that after Jeezy saw his rapping ability, he was in awe and therefore he idolizes him, he wants to be like Ross.", "annotation_id": "703955", "url": "https://genius.com/703955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "You throwin’ up sets but you really from Cleveland", "vault_lines": ["You throwin' up sets but you really from Cleveland"], "meaning": "There are virtually no well-known gangs that reside in Cleveland. He’s saying that Young Jeezy throws up gang signs when he’s not even from the places that those gangs reside.", "annotation_id": "703944", "url": "https://genius.com/703944", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "See I broke it down like a quarter ki", "vault_lines": ["See I broke it down like a quarter ki"], "meaning": "A ki is the shortened word for kilogram, which is usually the amount of cocaine most rappers always rap about. He’s saying that he broke it down to Young Jeezy and CTE by dissing them  in the previous lines, like a quarter ki, which is a fourth of a kilogram.", "annotation_id": "703935", "url": "https://genius.com/703935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Leave you paraplegic", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Paraplegia is an impairment that disables people’s use of their lower body. It’s usually caused by an injury to the spinal cord. Ross will put you into this state if you mess with him.", "annotation_id": "703931", "url": "https://genius.com/703931", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "Blowin money fast, yellow Maserati", "vault_lines": ["Blowin money fast, yellow Maserati"], "meaning": "“Blowin Money Fast” is the song that ignited the feud between these two. This is another line that shows Jeezy that Rick Ross doesn’t care what he thinks.\n\nAlso, in a more literal sense, Maserati’s cost about 200,000 dollars, and is one of the countless cars Rick Ross raps about. A drug dealer can make about 200,000 dollars in one day, so he’s saying that he blows all of his money by buying a Maserati.\n\nFinally, Rick Ross' music is based off of cocaine-dealing and other drugs. Yellow Maserati is also a type of ecstasy pill. He could be blowing his money buying this.", "annotation_id": "703886", "url": "https://genius.com/703886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "These motherfuckers mad that I’m icey Talking to a pussy nigga yeah I might be", "vault_lines": ["These motherfuckers mad that I'm icey", "Talking to a pussy nigga yeah I might be"], "meaning": "This is the same line that began the second verse in the song “B.M.F.”, the song that pissed Young Jeezy off and therefore provoked Rick Ross to make this song. Using some of the same lines from the song basically shows Jeezy that Ross doesn’t give a fuck what Jeezy thinks.\n\nThis song and all the verbal insults are aimed at Jeezy, who Ross is calling a pussy nigga.", "annotation_id": "702448", "url": "https://genius.com/702448", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "You niggas pathetic,", "vault_lines": ["Vacheron Don you niggas ain't ready"], "meaning": "Ross is saying Young Jeezy is pathetic for being jealous of Rick Ross' success of BMF and the Teflon Don album. The whole beef started because Jeezy was mad that Ross named his song “BMF” a clique which Jeezy was apart of, and was mad that Big Meech even praised the song. Ricky’s become the flagship artist of Def Jam while Jeezy’s become an afterthought. As Ross always says “Jealousy is a female trait”", "annotation_id": "388612", "url": "https://genius.com/388612", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Summer’s Mine", "line": "The summer’s mine, new silver Scaglietti", "vault_lines": ["The summer's mine, new silver Scaglietti"], "meaning": "Silver Scaglietti refers to the new Ferrari Scaglietti that Ricky has just purchased", "annotation_id": "388601", "url": "https://genius.com/388601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
