{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "The Mike Jordan of recording", "vault_lines": ["The Mike Jordan of recording"], "meaning": "Trevor Noah quotes a line from JAY-Z’s hit “Show Me What You Got” declaring that he is the best on the microphone as Jordan was/is the best in the NBA.\n\nLet Hov tell it, he damn near beat Jordan in Around-The-World!", "annotation_id": "24554664", "url": "https://genius.com/24554664", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "It’s the R.O.C. and we runnin’ this rap shit", "vault_lines": ["It's the R.O.C. and we runnin' this rap shit"], "meaning": "Sam Jack is paraphrasing the hook to “Takeover” and although Roc Nation is a major conglomerate in music, it started with Roc-A-Fella Records and for a time, they were runnin' the rap game from at least 1998 to 2004.", "annotation_id": "24554645", "url": "https://genius.com/24554645", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "In the zone like 2-3 and made it look too easy", "vault_lines": ["In the zone like 2-3 and made it look too easy"], "meaning": "Jurnee paraphrases another line from “Show Me What You Got” prior to Trevor Noah’s\n\n“Mami in the zone like the homie two-three\nJordan or James, makes no difference\nWe all ballin' the same”\n\nYou can’t blame her, either, for at least eight years, JAY was on a hot streak like Michael Jordan 90-98 or maybe even LeBron James 10-18… either way, he’s saying he’s him!", "annotation_id": "24554640", "url": "https://genius.com/24554640", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "I’m from the other side where other guys were quick to pull your card [Ed Sheeran] And argue about who’s the best emcee", "vault_lines": ["I'm from the other side where other guys were quick to pull your card", "And argue about who's the best emcee"], "meaning": "Jeymes and Ed starts off the famous quote from JAY-Z hit “Where I’m From” with a conversation piece that some people can still argue to this day", "annotation_id": "24554570", "url": "https://genius.com/24554570", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "The takeover, the break’s over", "vault_lines": ["The takeover, the break's over"], "meaning": "Tyler, who knows a lot about taking over the Hollywood industry independently, quotes the opening line from the infamous Nas diss song “Takeover”", "annotation_id": "24554551", "url": "https://genius.com/24554551", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "If I hit you, I’m brainless [Jermaine Dupri] Now if you get me, you’re famous; what’s a brother to do?", "vault_lines": ["Now if you get me, you're famous; what's a brother to do?"], "meaning": "Rick Ross, an artist who was formerly under JAY-Z’s Def Jam CEO reign and frequent song collaborator & Dupri, who shares hit single “Money Ain’t A Thang” with JAY-Z paraphrases the opening line to Hov’s hood manual “Streets Is Watching”", "annotation_id": "24554504", "url": "https://genius.com/24554504", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "All the way from 4:44 [Queen Latifah] To 40/40s [Jurnee Smollett] Down to 22 Twos", "vault_lines": ["All the way from 4:44"], "meaning": "To connect with the last quote, JAY-Z’s transparency & realism in his lyrics and entrepreneurial success ranges from his Rocawear clothing line, his liquors from Armadale to Ace of Spades and worldwide string of the 40/40 luxury clubs all publicized since his first album and the play on numbers going in reverse shows he knows how to double up on his profit and double down on the competition every time!", "annotation_id": "24554463", "url": "https://genius.com/24554463", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "Congrats, S. Carter: ghostwriter You paid the right price so we just made yo’ hits tighter", "vault_lines": ["Congrats, S. Carter: ghostwriter", "You paid the right price so we just made yo' hits tighter"], "meaning": "Blue Ivy congratulates her father by paraphrasing a line from song “Ride or Die” off the “Vol. 2… Hard Knock Life” album.\n\nJAY-Z had been inducted into the Songwriters' Hall Of Fame (ironic for a man that doesn’t write his own lyrics) for his lyrical works for himself and a few songwriter’s credit for a few others like Dr. Dre whom he wrote “Still D.R.E.” for and that song helped Dr. Dre’s sophomore release “2001” become a massive success.", "annotation_id": "24554336", "url": "https://genius.com/24554336", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "That’s why I’m overcharging ’em for what they did to the Cold Crush", "vault_lines": ["That's why I'm overcharging 'em for what they did to the Cold Crush"], "meaning": "Another quote from the hit “Izzo (H.O.V.A.)” further validating that his Rock & Roll Hall Of Fame induction proves that he and his fellow Hip Hop comrades like those before him such as the Cold Crush Brothers should have been more than just undercompensated for their efforts in pioneering Hip Hop", "annotation_id": "24527801", "url": "https://genius.com/24527801", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "H to the Izzo [H.E.R.] V to the Izzay", "vault_lines": ["H to the Izzo", "V to the Izzay"], "meaning": "The 8th Wonder of the World, the flow of the century, always timeless… HOV!", "annotation_id": "24527785", "url": "https://genius.com/24527785", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "Can’t leave rap alone, the game needs me", "vault_lines": ["Can't leave rap alone, the game needs me"], "meaning": "Another famous quotable from JAY-Z’s first hit single “Izzo (H.O.V.A.)” from the highly acclaimed album “The Blueprint”", "annotation_id": "24527694", "url": "https://genius.com/24527694", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
