{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "No more Big Willie, my game is grown; prefer you call me William", "vault_lines": ["No more Big Willie, my game is grown; prefer you call me William"], "meaning": "A quote from the breakthrough single “Can I Live”, a line that represented the mindset of someone thinking outside the slang status and has a more refined outlook for cordial business\n\nThe evolution of JAY-Z come full circle, perhaps. In his debut album he presented himself as a highly sophisticated crime boss in a suit. Today, he is a highly established entrepreneur in a suit!", "annotation_id": "24527271", "url": "https://genius.com/24527271", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
