{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "I’m from a place where the news cameras never come", "vault_lines": ["I'm from a place where the news cameras never come"], "meaning": "This line condensed from JAY-Z’s song “Where I’m From” is quoted by Lena because like Hov, who’s from Brooklyn, Lena is from Chicago where “news cameras never come” due to it’s high rate of crime", "annotation_id": "24527110", "url": "https://genius.com/24527110", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "They say words are a weapon [Lupita N’yongo] So when I shoot, meet your death in less than eight seconds", "vault_lines": ["They say words are a weapon", "So when I shoot, meet your death in less than eight seconds"], "meaning": "This is paraphrase from JAY-Z’s supposed first solo single “Ain’t No Nigga” featuring Foxy Brown instead replacing the word “sex” with “words”", "annotation_id": "24527065", "url": "https://genius.com/24527065", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
