{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "[Dave Letterman] Allow me to re-introduce myself: my name is Hov, H to the O-V", "vault_lines": ["Allow me to re-introduce myself: my name is Hov, H to the O-V"], "meaning": "It would seem unlikely for Letterman to say this direct quote from JAY-Z’s hit “Public Service Announcement” but besides interviewing him on The Late Show occasionally, he was also a guest on Letterman’s Netflix series “My Next Guest Needs No Introduction With David Letterman”", "annotation_id": "24526973", "url": "https://genius.com/24526973", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "[John Legend] So you can see what was what [SZA] And who was who", "vault_lines": ["So you can see what was what", "And who was who"], "meaning": "These two singers paraphrased the line said by Pain In Da Ass from the album intro of “In My Lifetime, Vol. 1”\n\n“Seems like only yesterday when I got up on that stage\nIn front of that crowd\nAnd showed them who was who, and what was what”", "annotation_id": "24526942", "url": "https://genius.com/24526942", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "[Lin-Manuel Miranda] It’s cool, I’m out for dead presidents to represent me", "vault_lines": ["It's cool, I'm out for dead presidents to represent me"], "meaning": "Lin-Manuel quotes the iconic Nas line from “The World Is Yours” which was the hook from JAY-Z’s single “Dead Presidents”. The irony is that Lin-Manuel got his notoriety for creating and starring in a Hip Hop stage play called “Hamilton”… based on a dead President! Alexander Hamilton is also on the $10 bill so the line only referred to Presidents whose face were on a dollar bill such as George Washington, Abraham Lincoln, Andrew Jackson and Ulysses Grant.", "annotation_id": "24526891", "url": "https://genius.com/24526891", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "Okay! I’m reloaded", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This famous “Scarface” line was an early quote heard before “Brooklyn’s Finest” and the intro to “In My Lifetime, Vol. 1” said by Pain In Da Ass", "annotation_id": "24526795", "url": "https://genius.com/24526795", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "[Rick Ross] When the Remy’s in the system", "vault_lines": ["When the Remy's in the system"], "meaning": "It’s only right that Rick Ross quoted this line which is more relevant from JAY-Z’s smash single “I Just Wanna Love U (Give It 2 Me)” as that song’s opening line was a quote from his close friend and fellow member of the group The Commission the late great Notorious B.I.G.’s song “The World Is Filled…” who Rick Ross also pays homage to in his style of rhymes", "annotation_id": "24526705", "url": "https://genius.com/24526705", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "Know the difference between a 4.0 and a 4.6", "vault_lines": ["To know the difference between a 4.0 and a 4.6"], "meaning": "Basically save up enough money to get that Range Rover with the better engine! Back in 1997, according to JAY-Z’s song “Imaginary Player” it’s in the range between $30,000 to $40,000!\n\nIf you paid close attention to Ahmir’s shirt in the tribute video, it also paid its own homage paraphrasing the song’s closing ad-lib “Yo, your jawn even got leathers?”", "annotation_id": "24526620", "url": "https://genius.com/24526620", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "[DJ Khaled] Beyond reasonable doubt the industry made me wait [Diddy] What’s crazy is I’m still spending money from ’88 [Regina King] Can I live and surprise the game? Think harder [Lenny Kravitz] You know this brother [DJ Premier] JAY-Z [John Legend] Shawn Carter", "vault_lines": ["You know this brother"], "meaning": "These six entertainment juggernauts paid homage to who some would say is the best album in Hov’s discography. Reasonable Doubt was JAY-Z’s debut solo album which was released in 1996 however it was released  under his own record label that was help built from his own funding back in 1988 because other record companies denied his talent. Could you believe that JAY-Z is STILL spending that same money up to his Rock & Roll induction 33 YEARS LATER?\n\nDiddy quoted the infamous ‘88 line from “Dead Presidents II” as Regina King mentioned the classic single “Can I Live?” as well connect the rhymes from the original “Dead Presidents” for Kravitz, Preemo and John Legend to cleanly quote.", "annotation_id": "24526581", "url": "https://genius.com/24526581", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Times And Life of Shawn Carter", "line": "I suggest you all roll with the click, bitch, who you wit’?", "vault_lines": ["So I suggest you all roll with the click, bitch, who you wit'?"], "meaning": "A direct quote from the chorus of the hit single from the “Sprung” soundtrack “Who You Wit”", "annotation_id": "24526276", "url": "https://genius.com/24526276", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
