{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Zenith", "line": "Stress that I be under, blame that on my baby momma", "vault_lines": ["Stress that I be under, blame that on my baby momma"], "meaning": "Ross has had a fair amount of baby momma drama over the years, including child-support court battles, paternity lawsuits, and that time his son’s mother hung out with 50 Cent and told him Ross' secrets", "annotation_id": "866020", "url": "https://genius.com/866020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Zenith", "line": "Shout out Seattle but these rappers, they stealing my thunder", "vault_lines": ["Shout out Seattle but these rappers, they stealing my thunder"], "meaning": "A reference to the NBA’s Seattle Supersonics, who became the Oklahoma City Thunder in 2008", "annotation_id": "865697", "url": "https://genius.com/865697", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Zenith", "line": "Riding in another drop, ain’t talking Enterprise They tryna see me get diabetes from humble pie", "vault_lines": ["Riding in another drop, ain't talking Enterprise", "They tryna see me get diabetes from humble pie"], "meaning": "A pun here on the phrase humble pie, meaning “ to apologize and face humiliation for a serious error” – in this case, being jealous of/underestimating our protagonist", "annotation_id": "865549", "url": "https://genius.com/865549", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Zenith", "line": "I used to look at the future and I couldn’t bear to see Me, my momma and my sister was the bears in the tree Porridge in my bowl, tryna keep hold of my souls", "vault_lines": ["I used to look at the future and I couldn't bear to see", "Me, my momma and my sister was the bears in the tree", "Porridge in my bowl, tryna keep hold of my souls"], "meaning": "Stalley’s use of “bear” in the first line leads into him referencing the fairy tale sometimes known as The Story of the Three Bears", "annotation_id": "865507", "url": "https://genius.com/865507", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Zenith", "line": "Eyes on the sparrow and I’m laid up like a pharaoh", "vault_lines": ["Eyes on the sparrow and I'm laid up like a pharaoh"], "meaning": "“His Eye Is on the Sparrow” is a 1905 song that has become a staple of black church services – despite being by written two white songwriters, lyricist Civilla D. Martin and composer Charles H. Gabriel\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eM_JRAPSwVM\n\nThe “laid up like a pharaoh” line compares Stalley’s material goods to the splendors that Egyptian pharaohs were entombed with", "annotation_id": "865487", "url": "https://genius.com/865487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Zenith", "line": "I ain’t gon’ be slept on forever, tell the Sandman to wake ’em up And help me count this cheddar", "vault_lines": ["I ain't gon' be slept on forever, tell the Sandman to wake 'em up", "And help me count this cheddar"], "meaning": "Stalley puns about being “slept on” as a rapper by mentioning the mythical Sandman who brings children good dreams by sprinkling magical sand into their eyes\n\n\n\nThe character was famously given a goth makeover (and re-named “Dream”) by comic writer Neil Gaiman in his Sandman series", "annotation_id": "865479", "url": "https://genius.com/865479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "The Zenith", "line": "I got that Lee-Roy glow", "vault_lines": ["I got that Lee-Roy glow"], "meaning": "In the Last Dragon Lee-Roy only got “the glow” when he reached the highest level of martial arts and defeated Sho'nuff", "annotation_id": "859009", "url": "https://genius.com/859009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
