{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "You pussy niggas hatin’ on me picked the wrong time", "vault_lines": ["You pussy niggas hatin' on me picked the wrong time"], "meaning": "Even though he is usually nice to people and somehow ignoring his haters, this time he is taken over the edge due to the events in his life.", "annotation_id": "17365984", "url": "https://genius.com/17365984", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "[Verse 3: JAY-Z]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It took me years to get Jay Z on a record, but that particular year I had a condo in New York. It took me a straight year and I made sure I was in New York till I got that verse. I was sick of going back and forth and I thought I had to be close to him to get it.", "annotation_id": "8029408", "url": "https://genius.com/8029408", "state": "verified", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Like you doin’ all this for a reason And what happens most of the time people change", "vault_lines": ["And what happens most of the time people change"], "meaning": "Jigga can’t understand people who accuse him of changing after he became successful and wealthy, like they’re surprised.\nThe mentality of this line is OF COURSE he changed. First of all, you have to be dedicated and talented to climb your way out of the Marcy projects to being a rap legend, a multi-millionare, and on a first name basis with President Barack Obama and Oprah. Of course he changed, that’s what he was grinding so hard for. If he wanted to be stuck on the block playing dominoes or whatever he would have just done that.\n\nJay’s close homie Kanye West expressed a similar thought in “Run This Town”, a track that both ‘Ye and Jigga are featured on. His line,\n\nWhat you think I rap for to push a fuckin' Rav 4?! \"\n\nis saying the same thing. ‘Ye ain’t having it.", "annotation_id": "3137714", "url": "https://genius.com/3137714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Nigga, you ain’t seen it, I’ve been fuckin’ up arenas", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, you ain't seen it, I've been fuckin' up arenas"], "meaning": "Meek has been selling out shows and ripping it up since the summer of 2012 when he dropped Dreamchasers 2, the most downloaded mixtape ever. The MMG Star has recently been selling out shows in advance of his summer album release Dreams Worth More Than Money.\n\n\n\nDrizzy and Meek performing “Amen”.", "annotation_id": "3137243", "url": "https://genius.com/3137243", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "People look at you strange, sayin’ you changed Like you worked that hard to stay the same", "vault_lines": ["Like you worked that hard to stay the same"], "meaning": "Although this is said in an interview context, this is an almost exact quote from one of Hov’s raps – his epic “Grammy Family” freestyle.\n\nThis is also a reference to DJ Khaled’s upcoming eigth studio album entitled “I Changed A Lot.”", "annotation_id": "3135909", "url": "https://genius.com/3135909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "If I feel threatened, I’ma go and get a ladder (Grrt) And climb up your chest, nigga Motherfuck your vest, nigga", "vault_lines": ["If I feel threatened, I'ma go and get a ladder (Grrt)", "And climb up your chest, nigga"], "meaning": "The whole line is simply a clever play on words regarding murder through the metaphor of climbing on a ladder.\n\nMeek let’s everyone know if he feel suspect that you’ll threaten his life he’ll get the “ladder”, which refers to his gun.\n\n\n\nHe is aiming directly at your brain instead of shooting you where your bullet proof vest would be, if he had a red dot on the gun it would “climb” up his chest to his head, which in fact negates all the effects of bullet proof clothing.\n\n\n\nThis also references directly to Jay-Z’s H.A.M verse:\n\nHeadshots nigga, fuck yo vest", "annotation_id": "3134204", "url": "https://genius.com/3134204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Shit startin’ to change, so you startin’ to change, nah They don’t love you no more (They don’t love you no more) They don’t love you no more, nah Should be your favorite, now you’re just hatin’ Shit startin’ to change, you want me to change, nah", "vault_lines": ["Shit startin' to change, so you startin' to change, nah", "They don't love you no more, nah", "Should be your favorite, now you're just hatin'", "Shit startin' to change, you want me to change, nah"], "meaning": "As artists grow from their past roots to their higher status as stars, the people they grew up with in their past begin to claim they have changed. With this change, comes a loss of the love from the people in the past. These are the people who should be lovin you the most but since they perceive “success” as changing you, they ultimately despise your success and begin to claim “they miss the old you”.\n\nThe true premise of this song is as people create themselves into stars, they truly were trying to change from that person in the past and they have changed into the person they have become, so if you choose to hate on them now, you picked the wrong time, because now they are hot and early have changed into very lucrative, well-off people.\n\nCan you blame them though?", "annotation_id": "3134002", "url": "https://genius.com/3134002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "They gon’ talk about you ’til you ain’t got shit (Ahh) Still gon’ talk about you when you got shit", "vault_lines": ["They gon' talk about you 'til you ain't got shit (Ahh)", "Still gon' talk about you when you got shit"], "meaning": "When people see homeless people and lower class people they say how that person is worthless and that they can’t properly contribute to society. They treat these people like they are the scum of society. They don’t deserve all the benefits that the government gives them.\n\n\n\nNow it is the same situation for rich people. People in the middle class always complain about the rich can have anything they want and how it isn’t fair that they are living lavish while they have to work hard for their money.\n\n\n\nMeek Mill is trying to say that it doesn’t matter what side you are on, people will find a way to complain.\n\nHe also may be paying homage to his fellow rapper and friend Fabolous who said the same thing in the chorus of his track “Sacrifices”.", "annotation_id": "3133768", "url": "https://genius.com/3133768", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "X600 as I swerve, Little Haiti", "vault_lines": ["X600 as I swerve, Little Haiti"], "meaning": "Rick Ross leaves away with his modified BMW X6, the X600. He doesn’t care if you still love him, he got his bimmer.\n\n\n\nRoss also shouts out Little Haiti, a poor neighborhood in Miami, Florida. Ross also mentioned it in DJ Khaled’s “I’m So Hood Remix”:\n\nYou fools fugazi, my fools from Haiti\"", "annotation_id": "3133686", "url": "https://genius.com/3133686", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Long line for a limp mink draggin’ (Woo), new bandwagon (Skrrt) Blood drippin’ on me lookin’ like a nigga stabbed him", "vault_lines": ["Long line for a limp mink draggin' (Woo), new bandwagon (Skrrt)", "Blood drippin' on me lookin' like a nigga stabbed him"], "meaning": "Now that Meek Mill and other rappers have started rocking mink coats, a lot of other people are trying to hop on the bandwagon and wear them as well. However, it’s unlikely you’ll get one as fresh as his. Meek Mill’s mink coats are so fresh they practically still have mink blood dripping from them.", "annotation_id": "3133557", "url": "https://genius.com/3133557", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Shit ain’t been the same since I came through in that hot shit", "vault_lines": ["Shit ain't been the same since I came through in that hot shit"], "meaning": "“Hot shit” refers to one of Meek’s many luxurious cars. People around him changed for the worse when they saw the success he attained. Envy at its finest.", "annotation_id": "3133451", "url": "https://genius.com/3133451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "If you say it, guess it’s true though, kudos, I mean but who knows?", "vault_lines": ["If you say it, guess it's true though, kudos, I mean but who knows?"], "meaning": "Sarcasm\n\nHere, HOV is saying that – since his incredibly intelligent doubters said something – it must be true!\nIt should be noted that Jay Z recites this line with his tongue planted firmly in his cheek.\n\n\n\nHe jokingly thanks the hater for their piece of mind, but still leaves the line open with a little closing skepticism.\n\nThis is directly referring to the above quote from the second verse of Drake’s “We Made It”.\n\nIf I said it I meant it, theres no way around it \"", "annotation_id": "3133389", "url": "https://genius.com/3133389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Ou paka bat m’wen, sak pase!", "vault_lines": ["Ou paka bat m'wen, sak pase!"], "meaning": "Creole for:\n\n“You can’t beat me, what’s up?”\n\nHaitian Creole is one of two official languages of The Republic of Haiti, mentioned in the previous line.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Rozay has tried to use Haitian Creole in his music, he uses such a line again on Trae’s “Inkredible”\n\nFrench Montana, also a member of Maybach Music Group, used the phrase in the “Paranoid” remix.", "annotation_id": "3133318", "url": "https://genius.com/3133318", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "I’m bustin’ out the sunroof, nigga, ¡andalé!", "vault_lines": ["I'm bustin' out the sunroof, nigga, ¡andalé!"], "meaning": "“Andalé” is a Spanish word that loosely translates to “come on” or “hey”.\nThe Maybach Laundalet (sounding like “Andale”) is a very expensive and impressive vehicle that sports a sunroof in both the back and front.", "annotation_id": "3133226", "url": "https://genius.com/3133226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Had to shake a couple niggas, everybody won’t make it", "vault_lines": ["Had to shake a couple niggas, everybody won't make it"], "meaning": "He is loyal to all his homies but in the end it’s survival of the fittest. Ross tries his best but he can’t save everyone.\n\nAll Ross can do is hope that he and his team keep eatin' and as of late for him it doesn’t seem like a problem.\n\nAccording to the intro to Drug Dealers Dream  Rick Ross has 92 Million is his checking account.\n\nPlease hold while I locate your information. Your checking account available balance is $92,153,183.28. This reflects the most current information available on your account", "annotation_id": "3133114", "url": "https://genius.com/3133114", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "RRRAAAAHHH", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In the “We Made It Freestyle”, Jay says “don’t make me RRAAHHH ya!” but Drake’s continued jabs made him do it…", "annotation_id": "3133108", "url": "https://genius.com/3133108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Glock .30 in the cockpit (Ha) Sippin’ dirty, conversatin’ with the pilot", "vault_lines": ["Glock .30 in the cockpit (Ha)", "Sippin' dirty, conversatin' with the pilot"], "meaning": "A Glock 30 is a sub-compact pistol used for close quarters. Meek is carrying this gun in his, cockpit, which alludes to the front seat of his car that he’s driving.\n\nSipping Dirty\n\nis a reference to the popular mixed drink often called Dirty Sprite or Lean in which the main ingredients are Promethazine   w/ Codeine syrup and sprite.\n\nThe last part of this bar, come and sail with the pilot, is a metaphor meaning that he wants his companion to get high with him as they are in the cockpit. All of the aeronautical referencing used supports Meek’s interest in getting high.\n\n\n\nNote: as of 4/23/14 the pharmaceutical company Activis has stated that they will not be manufacturing the Promethazine and Codeine cough syrup.", "annotation_id": "3133103", "url": "https://genius.com/3133103", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "I’ve been duckin’ paparazzi with a pop bitch", "vault_lines": ["I've been duckin' paparazzi with a pop bitch"], "meaning": "Paparazzi is a common denominator with celebrities worldwide.\nIf the paparazzi were to see Meek with another famous woman celebrity such as Rihanna, it would attract more attention to himself than usual.\n\nSo he ducks the paparazzi with a popped bitch, (with popped being slang for unattractive in this context).\n\nThis is the opposite of what happened in previous years when Meek, Drake, and Chris Brown were in the media for all potentially having sexual relations with Rihanna.", "annotation_id": "3133099", "url": "https://genius.com/3133099", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Hol’ up, you ain’t got love for me, my nigga?", "vault_lines": ["Hol' up, you ain't got love for me, my nigga?"], "meaning": "Jay Z is acknowledging his haters.\n\nThis could be Jay’s way of alerting Drake to listen up as this is a response to Drizzy’s diss to Jay Z.\n\nThis is also a play off of the title of the song. Jay delivers the line as if it is news to him because he is so raw that he feels as though everyone must recognize it by now.", "annotation_id": "3133087", "url": "https://genius.com/3133087", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Live by the code, it’s the only way to play it", "vault_lines": ["Live by the code, it's the only way to play it"], "meaning": "The code is simple never lie and be loyal. Hustle for the family and you’ll strive with success. By staying with this you’ll “play,” your cards right. Just stick with the code/plan and it will workout in the long run.", "annotation_id": "3133084", "url": "https://genius.com/3133084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "[Skit: JAY-Z]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The whole intro is actually an excerpt from an interview Jay did a while ago, in the interview he was talking about his song “Most Kingz”:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AIYro36Saxk\n\nJump to 0:58\n\nThis skit is absent on streaming sites except for Soundcloud. It also does not appear on the official music video.", "annotation_id": "3133041", "url": "https://genius.com/3133041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Haters wanna ball, let me tighten up my draw string Wrong sport, boy, you know you soft as a lacrosse team", "vault_lines": ["Haters wanna ball, let me tighten up my draw string", "Wrong sport, boy, you know you soft as a lacrosse team"], "meaning": "Continuing jabs at Drake. Notice Hov did this on a Khaled track. In old school hip hop, if you were beefing with someone  a good way to one up them was making a song with someone they frequently collaborated with. Drake’s made many records with Khaled.\n\n\n\nIt’s important to note that Jay said “soft as a lacrosse team” not “soft as lacrosse.” Unlike sports such as basketball and football – whose most popular players often hail from tough, poor to working-class upbringings, lacrosse is largely populated by athletes from relatively privileged socio-economic backgrounds. Hence, the “soft” characterization – while these guys may act tough on the field if you dropped them in the middle of Harlem with nothing but their lacrosse sticks they wouldn’t be so quick to act “hard”.\n\nUnfortunately, this line has been misconstrued to mean that lacrosse itself is a “soft” sport. Jay has been criticized by the media and lacrosse teams for being ignorant.", "annotation_id": "3133028", "url": "https://genius.com/3133028", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Motherfuck your couch,", "vault_lines": ["Motherfuck your vest, nigga"], "meaning": "A classic line from a classic Dave Chappelle skit, from his classic Chapelle’s Show:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3fvfsT3LNNM", "annotation_id": "3133020", "url": "https://genius.com/3133020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "[Verse 1: Meek Mill]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is what Meek had to say about the track before it dropped:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MeekMill/statuses/460912710289743872", "annotation_id": "3133008", "url": "https://genius.com/3133008", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Niggas talkin’ down on the crown Watch them niggas you ’round got you wound", "vault_lines": ["Niggas talkin' down on the crown", "Watch them niggas you 'round got you wound"], "meaning": "It was all good just a week ago, niggas feel theyselves\nAnd that Watch the Throne drop, niggas kill themselves\n\nHov continues to throw jabs at Drake. He plays “crown/watch” referring to Watch The Throne.\n\n\n\nAlso note the wordplay on “watch/wound/round”", "annotation_id": "3133006", "url": "https://genius.com/3133006", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Salute to all the real niggas out there findin’ the loopholes Fuck all these fuck niggas, hate when niggas come up, igh!", "vault_lines": ["Salute to all the real niggas out there findin' the loopholes", "Fuck all these fuck niggas, hate when niggas come up, igh!"], "meaning": "Jay Z has been known to find innovative ways to make his bank account rise throughout the years.\n\nFor example, he made an impressive deal with Samsung to sell one-million copies of his album, Magna Carta Holy Grail, before it was even released. It forced the RIAA to change their rules for platinum certification…\n\n\n\nThey weren’t happy about it though. It’s the kind of opposition Jay has been facing to his entrepreneurial mindset his entire career, whether it be the dismissal from Iceberg Clothing when approached to be a brand ambassador, or the way in which he was ignored by record labels when attempting to record his debut record.", "annotation_id": "3132976", "url": "https://genius.com/3132976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Are you sure? A nigga flip this shit like Jarl Borg", "vault_lines": ["Are you sure? A nigga flip this shit like Jarl Borg"], "meaning": "On the hit TV show, Vikings, Jarl Borg was an ally of Ragnar Lothbrok (a rising star) and betrayed Ragnar by raiding his lands while he was absent. Jay’s flipping the flow just like Jarl Borg flipped sides.\n\n\n\nAnd how did the Vikings deal with Jarl Borg’s treachery? By Blood Eagle, of course.\n\n“Jarl Borg” is pronounced like “Y'all bored”, another reference to the title of the track, calling out people not feeling Hov anymore.", "annotation_id": "3132966", "url": "https://genius.com/3132966", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Hit these bootleg niggas with the Heisman", "vault_lines": ["Hit these bootleg niggas with the Heisman"], "meaning": "Obviously a shot at Johnny Manziel and Drake.\n\n“Draft Day” is a song Drake made to reference his relationship with Johnny, a football player who won the Heisman Trophy in his Freshman year (being the first person to achieve such a feat). In the song, Drake responded to Jay’s comments on the “We Made It Freestyle”. These are Jay’s returning shots to Drizzy.\n\n\n\nJay’s also taking a stance against bootleggers (he’s done it before), literally striking them with the Heisman pose. Metaphorically, he did this with the Samsung MCHG deal.\n\n\n\nKeeping with the football metaphor, a bootleg is when the quarterback rolls out of the pocket to run or throw the ball.\n\n\n\nAnd, of course, the Heisman Trophy is given annually to college football’s best player. Hov’s gonna hit ‘em with it because, well, he’s ballin’.", "annotation_id": "3132951", "url": "https://genius.com/3132951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Tell these crabs in the barrel we eatin’ hella lobster (Igh!)", "vault_lines": ["Tell these crabs in the barrel we eatin' hella lobster (Igh!)"], "meaning": "This line is a nice metaphor about other rappers coming at Jay. In “Murder To Excellence”, Jay Z talks about “putting crabs in a barrel.”\nHov wants us to tell these crabs (the rappers he’s dumped in the barrel to be eaten) that he is too busy eating lobster (considered higher quality than crab) to be bothered eating these lowly rappers.\n\n\n\nThis could also be seen as a shot at Drake eating crab out in Malibu in Nobu. Hov’s on a different level than Drizzy.\n\nDrake also raps on “Draft Day” that he tried raw oysters. Hov may be implying that he is on a higher level by eating lobster, which is considerably more expensive than oyster.", "annotation_id": "3132908", "url": "https://genius.com/3132908", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "People change around you because They startin’ treatin’ you different because of your success", "vault_lines": ["They startin' treatin' you different because of your success"], "meaning": "A common saying rappers state is they try their best to not change even through the money and the fame…but the people around them are the ones who really change due to the fact that their peer is now extremely rich and successful.\n\nThis is also a reference to DJ Khaled’s previous album, Suffering From Success. This album is all about the downsides of becoming famous, and people treating you differently is the no doubt the biggest problem.", "annotation_id": "3132903", "url": "https://genius.com/3132903", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Hopped off the plane, hit the helicopter (Igh!)", "vault_lines": ["Hopped off the plane, hit the helicopter (Igh!)"], "meaning": "Jay is showing off his wealth. Rather than getting off his private jet and taking a car to the next destination he travels by helicopter. His feet never touch the ground because he’s too godly.\n\n\n\nNote Jay continuing to borrow Chance The Rapper’s ad-lib at the end of this line and the following one\nhttps://twitter.com/chancetherapper/status/330103076885241856", "annotation_id": "3132898", "url": "https://genius.com/3132898", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Ever since a nigga hit the top (Uh) Pussy niggas wanna see me in a box (Oh) They don’t love you no more (They don’t love me no more) (Huh) They don’t love you no more DJ Khaled!", "vault_lines": ["Pussy niggas wanna see me in a box (Oh)", "They don't love you no more (They don't love me no more)"], "meaning": "Jealousy and envy are very prominent in todays world, and since money is a very important asset, much of this jealousy comes from money. Ever since French acquired fame, he now has many jealous haters. These haters no longer have love for him and they won’t stop hating until they see him in a coffin.", "annotation_id": "3132895", "url": "https://genius.com/3132895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Got hella options, like a college team", "vault_lines": ["Got hella options, like a college team"], "meaning": "Because Money Ain’t A Thang to Jay-Z, he can do pretty much anything he wants.\n\n\n\nMany college football teams run the option, a style of offense that incorporates many fakes, in which the quarterback runs with the ball, draws in the defense, and either pitches it to a runningback or keeps it himself.\n\n\n\nSo just like those college teams have alot of options in their playbook, Hov’s got options in life.", "annotation_id": "3132892", "url": "https://genius.com/3132892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "I’m with double M, the genius We the motherfuckin’ meanest", "vault_lines": ["We the motherfuckin' meanest"], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group is the label Meek Mill is signed to along with fellow collaborator (and boss) Rick Ross, no one is a great as the untouchable Mayback empire.\n\n\n\nAlso a nice alliteration by Meek here, motherfucking meanest is also a “double M”.", "annotation_id": "3132887", "url": "https://genius.com/3132887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Fuck the NCAA, nigga Let a young nigga get paid, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the NCAA, nigga", "Let a young nigga get paid, nigga"], "meaning": "Can’t a young nigga get money any more?\n\nAlthough college athletes dedicate their lives to their sports, they are not compensated for their efforts because the NCAA argues that athletes are only students engaged in amateur competitions.\n\n However, this broken system has seen significant attempts at reform in past months, as The National Labor Relations Board determined that Northwestern football players were employees of the university, making them eligible to register as a union.\n\n\n\nThis could possibly be Jay’s response to Drake’s subliminals on Draft Day. Jay completely downplays Drake’s college sports theme in the song by sarcastically screaming for the kids to get paid, mocking Drake’s line:\n\nYeah, suits and ties yellin' out, “Pay the guys”\n\nThis may also be a reference to the investigation into whether Jay Z and his Roc Nation Sports broke NCAA rules when Jay hungout with Jadeveon Clowney, the Heisman candidate from South Carolina.", "annotation_id": "3132871", "url": "https://genius.com/3132871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "All eyes on Meek, I’m on my Pac shit", "vault_lines": ["All eyes on Meek, I'm on my Pac shit"], "meaning": "Everyone has their eyes on Meek Mill.\nAll Eyez On Me was the name of 2Pac’s fourth studio album.\n\n\n\nMeek Mill also has 2 songs with Rick Ross about 2Pac called: “2Pac Back”, and another DJ Khaled song called “I Feel Like Pac/I Feel Like Biggie”.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MeekMill/status/460916042714595329", "annotation_id": "3132863", "url": "https://genius.com/3132863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Benz or the Rolls, Mulsanne overrated", "vault_lines": ["Benz or the Rolls, Mulsanne overrated"], "meaning": "You know that your money is on a whole other level when you comfortably can say that a $300,000 Bentley Mulsanne is overrated.\n\n\n\nHe only drives Mercedes-Benz and Rolls-Royce whips.\n\nHis signee and collaborator Meek Mill feels differently, mentioning the Mulsanne regularly in his music:\n\n\n“0 to 100 Remix”\n“Levels”\n“I’m Leanin'”\n“Pound Cake Freestyle”\n“I Feel Like Pac / I Feel Like Biggie”\n“You Don’t Want These Problems”", "annotation_id": "3132861", "url": "https://genius.com/3132861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Love You No More", "line": "Ever meet another nigga like me, my nigga?", "vault_lines": ["Ever meet another nigga like me, my nigga?"], "meaning": "Act like you’ll ever be around mothafuckas like this again\n\nJay-Z is a unique rap artist to say the least and he deserves recignition for this. He’s worked with the best of the best like Notorious B.I.G, had feuds with legends and is married to a superstar wife.\n\n\n\nHe is continuing his rant from the previous line. Recently Jay has had some criticism about his as Drake says “corny” art lyrics.\n\nEven after he addressed this on his We Made It freestyle he is re-establishing his point to emphasise his place as a legend in this rap game.", "annotation_id": "3132858", "url": "https://genius.com/3132858", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
