{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "They Don’t Really Love You", "line": "Come and sit at the table, boy, you better say a prayer", "vault_lines": ["Come and sit at the table, boy, you better say a prayer"], "meaning": "A paraphrase of Psalm 23:5, which reads:\n\nThou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over.\n\nThe true meaning of the verse is debated, but can be seen to describe a host providing a plentiful experience for their guest. Rick Ross considers himself able to provide for others in a similar gracious fashion to such a host, with the “overflowing” cup signifying him possessing more than enough wealth to satisfy any guest of his.", "annotation_id": "30043729", "url": "https://genius.com/30043729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
