{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Me", "line": "Champagne pours, celebrate the cause", "vault_lines": ["Champagne pours, celebrate the cause"], "meaning": "Rick Ross loves champagne. In fact, recently, he put Luc Belaire Rosé on the most wanted list for wine customers. Rozay was also endorsed through them & helped the brand take off in 2013.", "annotation_id": "8640105", "url": "https://genius.com/8640105", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Me", "line": "Maybachs were a dream now it’s all real It’s hard to get sleep layin’ next to five mil", "vault_lines": ["Maybachs were a dream now it's all real", "It's hard to get sleep layin' next to five mil"], "meaning": "Maybach is an ultra high-end German car manufacturer. Their vehicles have an average price tag of $500,000+.\n\nRoss is saying that he used to dream about owning one, but now he has enough money to make this dream a reality. This is good since he can’t sleep anymore (he has to keep an eye on his money).", "annotation_id": "214144", "url": "https://genius.com/214144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Me", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-this-me-lyrics", "genius_title": "This Me", "genius_id": 40257, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "What does death mean to me? I never owned the concept, I was here I’m just a spirit, let’s get one thing clear Everything segues into each other One thing is just an extension of the other, my kid to me", "vault_lines": ["What does death mean to me?", "I never owned the concept, I was here", "I'm just a spirit, let's get one thing clear", "Everything segues into each other", "One thing is just an extension of the other, my kid to me"], "meaning": "These are dope and deep lines which shows the philosophical side of Nas artistry. Death is not something he claims to control or fully understand. He sees himself as a soul, a spirit, existing beyond the idea of endings. Life and death are part of the same flow, seamlessly connected. A karmic cycle.\n\nEverything in his world is linked, each moment or relationship naturally extending into the next. His connection with his child is part of that continuity, a reflection of himself carried forward.", "annotation_id": "37022849", "url": "https://genius.com/37022849", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "A don is one who accept things he cannot change Only thing I accept I cannot change is getting old and dying", "vault_lines": ["Only thing I accept I cannot change is getting old and dying"], "meaning": "Nas is a man grounded in reality and for him, the only things that are in the category of the inevitable are aging and death. Everything else can be challenged, shifted, or controlled, which shows his belief in himself and taking control of things that shape his life.", "annotation_id": "37022800", "url": "https://genius.com/37022800", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "The don of all dons Since y’all wanna call me something, all a sudden Niggas ball and stunting, y’all just started pulling on Havanas Pull ya card, ya spineless, where ya heart? I know where mine is", "vault_lines": ["The don of all dons", "Since y'all wanna call me something, all a sudden", "Niggas ball and stunting, y'all just started pulling on Havanas", "Pull ya card, ya spineless, where ya heart? I know where mine is"], "meaning": "Nas Escobar kicks by calling himself “the don of all dons,” putting himself above everyone else. He mocks rappers who just started showing off wealth, like smoking Havanas, while he’s been living that life for years.\n\nThen he cuts deeper. “Pull ya card, ya spineless, where ya heart?” is him exposing fake toughness. In essence, he’s saying they lack courage and grit, while he knows exactly who he is and what he stands for. He is bout  that life.", "annotation_id": "37020787", "url": "https://genius.com/37020787", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "Natty dread, got no barber", "vault_lines": ["Private jet over water, natty dread, got no barber"], "meaning": "Leaving long hair to its own devices by not brushing or cutting the hair will encourage it to tangle together as it grows, leading to twisted, matted ropes of hair known as dreadlocks.\n\n\n\nWale has dreadlocks, which doesn’t require a barber to maintain.", "annotation_id": "1991332", "url": "https://genius.com/1991332", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "Sometimes I get so fucking paranoid Reminiscing on how them bricks keep going back and forth", "vault_lines": ["Reminiscing on how them bricks keep going back and forth"], "meaning": "Whenever Ross thinks about how he used to sell dope, he gets paranoid, because it is obviously illegal, and Ross' only fear is a dope charge.\n\nEven after Rozay “left the drug game” and ascended to the Mt. Olympus of Hip Hop, the paranoia remains.\n\nI’m talking Dionysus, ambrosia", "annotation_id": "1413099", "url": "https://genius.com/1413099", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "Gold medallion over my son chest He’ll hold it down when I sunset", "vault_lines": ["Gold medallion over my son chest", "He'll hold it down when I sunset"], "meaning": "Nas' son, born in 2009 to his now ex-wife, singer Kelis, is named Knight Jones.  Young Knight with his mother, below:", "annotation_id": "866156", "url": "https://genius.com/866156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "I see Feds, I go that way, that DMV shit taught us When you young and you black, they see you as a target", "vault_lines": ["I see Feds, I go that way, that DMV shit taught us", "When you young and you black, they see you as a target"], "meaning": "DMV is a popular term to describe the DC, Maryland, Virginia area.  The cops in that neck of the woods are, shockingly, hella racist", "annotation_id": "866141", "url": "https://genius.com/866141", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "Follow my actions, came in in ’06 Planted my flag, bitch I’m taking no shit", "vault_lines": ["Follow my actions, came in in '06", "Planted my flag, bitch I'm taking no shit"], "meaning": "Ross' debut album was released in 2006, though he was kicking around for a few years prior as a cameo performer and writer of material for other artists", "annotation_id": "866107", "url": "https://genius.com/866107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "The paper I’m making, I upgraded my fashion Everything tailor-made, flossing’s my passion", "vault_lines": ["The paper I'm making, I upgraded my fashion", "Everything tailor-made, flossing's my passion"], "meaning": "Ross has referred to himself as “fashion conscious” and claims he plans to “dabble in the fashion industry” in the future", "annotation_id": "866106", "url": "https://genius.com/866106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "I toted them toolies", "vault_lines": ["I toted them toolies"], "meaning": "Toolies are guns, and Ross has always been fond of chopper machine guns", "annotation_id": "865165", "url": "https://genius.com/865165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "I wrote the script, I was sipping lean", "vault_lines": ["I wrote the script, I was sipping lean"], "meaning": "‘Lean’ is slang for purple drank, a mix of codiene-laced cough syrup and soda that originated in Houston, Texas", "annotation_id": "864660", "url": "https://genius.com/864660", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "Talking laws of attraction", "vault_lines": ["Fatal mistakes, talking laws of attraction"], "meaning": "The Law of Attraction is a theory that “like attracts like”. It dates back to the early 20th century, but entered mass culture in 2006 with a movie and book called The Secret. The Law is supposedly used to attract wealth and riches into one’s life, though debunkers and skeptics proliferate", "annotation_id": "864326", "url": "https://genius.com/864326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "Adamantly coming at whoever call up for drama Just know that D.C., Philly, Ohio, Miami got us", "vault_lines": ["Just know that D.C., Philly, Ohio, Miami got us"], "meaning": "If you try to pick a fight or start a beef with them they are warning you that DC, Philly, Ohio and Miami got their backs\n\nD.C. for Folarin, Philly for Meek, Ohio for Stalley, and the port of Miami for Rozay – notice Omarion’s hometown, LA, was left out…", "annotation_id": "861418", "url": "https://genius.com/861418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "This thing of ours, oh (Oh) It’s so mafioso (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["This thing of ours, oh (Oh)", "It's so mafioso (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“This thing of ours” is how mafia people refer to the mafia business amongst themselves.  This line (and song) could be a reference to Jay-Z’s “Never Change”", "annotation_id": "861341", "url": "https://genius.com/861341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "This Thing of Ours", "line": "Last thing on my mind was slamming Caddy doors", "vault_lines": ["Last thing on my mind was slamming Caddy doors"], "meaning": "He was so poor at one point, he didn’t even care about getting rich, just pay the bills and survive.\n\nAlso a clever use of the phrase “slamming Cadillac doors”, popularized in the hook of Outkast’s “Elevators”. .", "annotation_id": "859964", "url": "https://genius.com/859964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
