{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "TipToe’N", "line": "I’m tiptoe’n out the bank, hop in the 650", "vault_lines": ["I'm tiptoe'n out the bank, hop in the 650"], "meaning": "Ross is getting in one of the following after leaving the bank:\n\n1.) BMW 650\n\n\n\n2.) Gulfstream G650\n\n\n\n3.) Mercedes Maybach G650 Landaulet\n\n\n\n4.) McLaren 650S", "annotation_id": "12899589", "url": "https://genius.com/12899589", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "TipToe’N", "line": "Just respect a nigga name or die peacefully I don’t fuck with sucka’ niggas, that’s the other side And they still do B&E, that’s on my brotha side", "vault_lines": ["Just respect a nigga name or die peacefully", "I don't fuck with sucka' niggas, that's the other side", "And they still do B&E, that's on my brotha side"], "meaning": "Ross doesn’t have time for lames, he just wants his respect and nothing else. He flexes his connections to the streets as he mentions that he still has family committing specific crimes, such as “B&E” charges, which stand for “breaking and entering” in legal terms.", "annotation_id": "12893821", "url": "https://genius.com/12893821", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "TipToe’N", "line": "When you pull up to the crib you see the waterfalls You would think that I produced TLC Waterfalls", "vault_lines": ["When you pull up to the crib you see the waterfalls", "You would think that I produced TLC Waterfalls"], "meaning": "The waterfalls in his estate serve as a reminder of the wealth that he has accumulated in his career, enough that one may think that Ross played a role in the success of TLC’s Waterfalls. The song Waterfalls was TLC’s biggest hit, spending 6 weeks at the #1 spot on the Billboard Hot 100, as well as receiving Grammy nominations, and winning four MTV Video Music Awards in 1995, including top honors for Video of the Year.\n\nFact: The song was actually produced by the legendary production team Organized Noize.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8WEtxJ4-sh4", "annotation_id": "12893671", "url": "https://genius.com/12893671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
