{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "A perfect 10, I’m watching you through God’s eyes", "vault_lines": ["A perfect 10, I'm watching you through God's eyes"], "meaning": "According to the Bible, God created man in his own perfect image. Genesis 1:26-27 says:\n\n26 And God said, Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth. 27 So God created man in his [own] image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.\n\nRoss likens himself to God, seeing how perfect his girl is, spiritually and beautifully.", "annotation_id": "14937387", "url": "https://genius.com/14937387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "’Cause shawty be the glory, until my dream real", "vault_lines": ["'Cause shawty be the glory, until my dream real"], "meaning": "She or “it” is what he treasures in this life or in the game. This second part of the line can actually determine his thought format of the song. “Until my dream real” which can me dream girl come to life or she is the dream girl until he wakes up to reality. Dream girl can also be substitute md for much more fore which we know wake dose not other brag about females but he do value the rap culture and wants the respect of being the best in people’s mind\n\nhttp://youtu.be/XVXhm_5R41g", "annotation_id": "4534067", "url": "https://genius.com/4534067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "Bonita Applebum (Woo!) - my strawberry letter (Woo!) Love Potion #9 (Woo!) this shit’s a gifted era", "vault_lines": ["Bonita Applebum (Woo!) - my strawberry letter (Woo!)", "Love Potion #9 (Woo!) this shit's a gifted era"], "meaning": "After comparing his ideal woman to money, peacefulness, timelessness, and Godliness, Ross moves on to what he knows best: music. (But especially black music – all of the artist he mentions are African American).\n\nBonita Applebum refers to A Tribe Called Quest song about a girl who is, “38-24-37”\n\n“My strawberry letter” refers to “Strawberry Letter 23”, a song by the Brothers Johnson\n\n“Love Potion #9” is a famous Rock-a-billy song from 1959 by The Clovers (that was later made into a sub-par movie)\n\nBut the time we are in right now will from thenceforth and forever be know as the “Gifted Era” because of the album that this song resides in. Track 11 – officially the most illustrious & gifted track.", "annotation_id": "1922696", "url": "https://genius.com/1922696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "Her emotions at peace, let’s walk the shoreline", "vault_lines": ["Her emotions at peace, let's walk the shoreline"], "meaning": "Another reference Ross' archetype of the perfect woman previously described in “Presidential”\n\nShe a dime but she gotta be a cool bitch\n\nShe is not disturbed by the petty things in life. “Her emotions at peace”, is a much more graceful way of complimenting a woman on her composure and presence than calling her a , “cool bitch”. This is evidence that Ross continues to appreciate as a lyricist like fine wine.\n\n\n\nTaking long walks down the beach is a classic romantic activity.", "annotation_id": "1922669", "url": "https://genius.com/1922669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "Sky-dweller moving counter-clockwise", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Continuing the theme of timelessness, Ross personifies his woman with a beauty and presence so angelic, that time itself stops and takes notice. Beautiful wordplay here from Hip Hop’s Biggest Sweetheart.\n\n\n\nFollowing the previous line, a Sky-Dweller is a Rolex watch. It’s moving back in time or at least it feels like time is slowing down immensely.", "annotation_id": "1922655", "url": "https://genius.com/1922655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "Statuesque as can be, we’re spending more time", "vault_lines": ["Statuesque as can be, we're spending more time"], "meaning": "Her beauty is timeless, like a statue.\n\n\n\nRoss implies that his ideal woman is tall and elegant, illustrious if you will.\n\nThe woman he speaks of can be found chilling in Rozay’s crib throughout the Mastermind album trailer:\nhttp://youtu.be/4su-BDHD3oY?t=1m24s", "annotation_id": "1922639", "url": "https://genius.com/1922639", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "When I look in your soul, all I see is the gold", "vault_lines": ["When I look in your soul, all I see is the gold"], "meaning": "Rozay has made it no mystery that his goal is the gold.\n\nChasin' my money like I’m Oprah, nigga.\n\nIn his ideal woman, he sees someone who can help him reach his goal of a billion dollars. That hustle and intelligence reflect highly of her character. These traits are essential to become Rozay’s First Lady…", "annotation_id": "1922573", "url": "https://genius.com/1922573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "As we plead guilty to this life sentence", "vault_lines": ["As we plead guilty to this life sentence"], "meaning": "Ross is both playing off of the last line, (since their love is wrong and a crime, they’ve already pled guilty and accepted their fate), but introduced the idea of marriage being a life sentence.\n\nIt is interesting how Ross uses a historically negative happening, (life in prison – without parol of course), as a metaphor for the solidarity of their love.", "annotation_id": "1900257", "url": "https://genius.com/1900257", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "Ugh! (Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Just as a drummer of band counts down “1, 2, 3” before the beat drops, Ross prefaces his verse with his adlib as a way of both watermarking the track and preparing himself to rap.", "annotation_id": "1900234", "url": "https://genius.com/1900234", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "M-M-M-Maybach Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Signature MMG drop.\n\n\n\nThis line is similar in the way that is a preposition of sorts like “started” or “yeah” Wale has used this on other songs such as Don’t Hold Your Applause and That Way.", "annotation_id": "1895814", "url": "https://genius.com/1895814", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tired of Dreaming", "line": "If this is wrong, you my co-defendant", "vault_lines": ["If this is wrong, you my co-defendant"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is using this in the legal system to explain if this is an offense, we are in it together pleading guilty.\n\nEven a relationship that is perfect between will still face the trials and tribulations of the outside world. It is a story similar to that of Romeo and Juliet in which differences in society change the outcome of the relationship between two people\n\n\n\nIn any case, Ross and his dream girl abide by traditional marriage vows: for better for worse, for richer for poorer, in sickness and in health, to love and to cherish, till death us do part.", "annotation_id": "1895757", "url": "https://genius.com/1895757", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
