{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Touch’N You", "line": "Smokin’ on that Cali, bumpin’ 2Pac", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' on that Cali, bumpin' 2Pac"], "meaning": "“Cali” is the diminutive for the state of California and is another word to refer to weed. California is known for its tolerance in terms of drug use and has even voted a law for legalization of cannabis in 2016.\n\n2pac is a rapper originally from New York, but has shouted out his love for California and was a major figure in West Coast rap in the 90’s.\nHence the play on words between California and 2pac.", "annotation_id": "22282133", "url": "https://genius.com/22282133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Touch’N You", "line": "In the Galleria all I get is buy me this", "vault_lines": ["In the Galleria all I get is buy me this"], "meaning": "Whenever Rick is with his girl at the mall, he always buys everything for her.", "annotation_id": "18699424", "url": "https://genius.com/18699424", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Touch’N You", "line": "Still can’t get my mind off your body I’m day dreaming ’bout, look how you turn me on baby", "vault_lines": ["Still can’t get my mind off your body", "I’m day dreaming 'bout, look how you turn me on baby"], "meaning": "After the action, Usher still thinks about his girl and what they did to each other. He dreams about her every day and how she turns him on all day.", "annotation_id": "18667675", "url": "https://genius.com/18667675", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Touch’N You", "line": "Been thinking ’bout you all day Right now, it’s about that time", "vault_lines": ["Right now, it's about that time"], "meaning": "Usher has his dreams realized when he’s with his girl", "annotation_id": "18667659", "url": "https://genius.com/18667659", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Touch’N You", "line": "[Intro: Usher]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "There are two versions of this song. One version is ‘Touch'N You,’ the explicit version is ‘Fuckin’ You.'", "annotation_id": "1514740", "url": "https://genius.com/1514740", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Touch’N You", "line": "It’s me against the world now, what’s your phone number?", "vault_lines": ["It’s me against the world now, what’s your phone number?"], "meaning": "This line refers to the 2Pac line above:\n\n\nMe Against the World is the name of 2Pac’s 3rd studio album, containing an eponym track\n“What’s Ya Phone Number”  is a track off of 2Pac’s 4th album, All Eyez on Me.", "annotation_id": "816885", "url": "https://genius.com/816885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Touch’N You", "line": "Conversations on the phone until the break of dawn", "vault_lines": ["Conversations on the phone until the break of dawn"], "meaning": "ACCEPTED COMMENT: This is actually a reference to 2Pac’s song I Get Around where the west coast legend uses the exact same line.", "annotation_id": "797367", "url": "https://genius.com/797367", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
