{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "Love is not found but resides insides me, I manifest this", "vault_lines": ["Love is not found but resides insides me, I manifest this"], "meaning": "You can’t find love on the outside, love is on the inside. Many people think others will make them happy and will be the source of love, but you have to love yourself first. Love is inside you", "annotation_id": "22719795", "url": "https://genius.com/22719795", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "I will replace what I take and have tranquility as my breakfast", "vault_lines": ["I will replace what I take and have tranquility as my breakfast"], "meaning": "Given the song is called tranquillo which is tranquility in spanish, this line has some importance.      If you replace what you take you create balance, and since it is believed that breakfast is the most important meal of the day, by having tranquility as your breakfast you win the day with a great start.", "annotation_id": "22719778", "url": "https://genius.com/22719778", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "Cause he ain’t really livin’ life ’less he’s down to roll the dice Put it all on the line for a couple dollars", "vault_lines": ["Cause he ain't really livin' life 'less he's down to roll the dice", "Put it all on the line for a couple dollars"], "meaning": "Two meanings here: Roll the dice for a couple dollars could mean either craps where you roll dice and players bet on what amount comes up. Winning and “living life”. Its a game of chance.\n\nThe metaphorical meaning is literally putting his life on the line in a game of chance for a couple of dollars.", "annotation_id": "15520458", "url": "https://genius.com/15520458", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "Peace, no material possessions shall cloud my judgement", "vault_lines": ["Peace, no material possessions shall cloud my judgement"], "meaning": "Lupe begins this song with what could be considered a prayer of “Peace”.\n\nPrayer in itself is universally considered direct communication with god, deity or deities, higher power, higher-self, or source.\n\nIn the Oxford Dictionary, prayer is defined as a “solemn request of help or an expression of thanks” however, since Lupe is a practiced Muslim, his use of the word “Peace” can be a simplification of the Islamic practice of using the salutation or greeting expressed as, “Peace be upon you” and in reply, “Upon you, peace”.\n\n\n\nFurthermore, Lupe provides to listeners an affirmation or declaration that materialism whether physical or otherwise will never reduce his ability of discernment.\n\nIn the eastern spiritual tradition of Buddhism, attaining Nirvana (peace and enlightenment) would be through the removal of all earthly attachments and material possessions.", "annotation_id": "14876523", "url": "https://genius.com/14876523", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "I will pursue felicity, find value in simplicity Altruism and empathy will be the first thing extended to my enemy Clarity will be the trademark of my friendships Just invest in my business and appreciative of the rarity of my existence", "vault_lines": ["I will pursue felicity, find value in simplicity", "Altruism and empathy will be the first thing extended to my enemy", "Clarity will be the trademark of my friendships", "Just invest in my business and appreciative of the rarity of my existence"], "meaning": "A recurring theme throughout this first verse is Lupe’s desire to better manage his time by directing his attention and efforts to meaningful pursuits. “Felicity” in this context means an intense happiness or sense of joy. In saying that he will pursue felicity, Lupe is literally saying he will chase his own happiness by finding value in the simple things in life.\n\nLupe goes on to mention altruism and empathy – topics generally associated with having a selfless concern for the well-being of others – as things he extends to his enemies. This reiterates the fact that Lupe has turned over a new leaf and is actively looking to better the world around him, starting by improving his relationships with those he considers his enemies.\n\nGiven his new sense of self, Lupe now has a greater level of clarity regarding what he wants to do with his life. This in turn has lead to him applying the same sense of clarity to all his friendships like a trademark.", "annotation_id": "11313621", "url": "https://genius.com/11313621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "White folk pass your Face dyin’ in the grass cause they wouldn’t call the, law Cause your hoodie’s black and they think you’re sellin’ crack Maybe so, you don’t give a fuck in a rut nigga ’Til those in the street got you stuck nigga, what nigga? Buck buck nigga", "vault_lines": ["Face dyin' in the grass cause they wouldn't call the, law", "Cause your hoodie's black and they think you're sellin' crack", "Maybe so, you don't give a fuck in a rut nigga", "'Til those in the street got you stuck nigga, what nigga?"], "meaning": "K.R.I.T believes that many white people within our modern society still view their self as being higher up in society than the average black male. Furthermore, these same people may sometimes even go on to stereotype a young black male as a drug dealer, simply due to the fact that they’re standing on the street and wearing a hoodie. The combination of this stereotyping and the ideology that the white man is superior could even go as far as to cause the aforementioned white people to ignore the man they stereotyped, even if he was laying on the ground and dying right in front of their eyes.\n\nHowever, K.R.I.T then goes on to state that these men who are being stereotyped for selling drugs really don’t care because the truth is that sometimes they actually are — when living in a low income area where no jobs are available, sometimes illegal activities seem like the only option. However, even though these men may not care about being stereotyped, chances are they’re going to care when rivals from their hood got them stuck (come after them violently with the intent to harm) and force them to buck up (be ready to fight).", "annotation_id": "11299217", "url": "https://genius.com/11299217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "Chasin’ woodgrain and the leather", "vault_lines": ["Chasin' woodgrain and the leather"], "meaning": "Many nice cars have their interior created with a combination of wood grain and leather. A lot of young people chase the dream of being able to purchase a car like this when they grow up.\n\nPictured below is a Bentley with this interior", "annotation_id": "11294634", "url": "https://genius.com/11294634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "And wisely regulate time I do have Cause what is defeat? But just the evidence of my haste Lack of preparedness, in my waste, so I wait", "vault_lines": ["Cause what is defeat? But just the evidence of my haste"], "meaning": "Time is a precious commodity – a very limited one, at that. Lupe is advocating for people to start managing their time better, directing their attention and efforts to meaningful pursuits. By better regulating the time you have and refraining from wasting it, you will not be forced to be hasty in formulating/executing your plans.\n\nAdditionally, Lupe uses a play on words with Defeat/‘Da Feet – a double entendre referring both to how feet can leave a literal trail of footprints as evidence of haste and that a defeat can be caused by mental haste/hasty planning. This aforementioned mental haste can be seen as a lack of preparedness and a deciding factor in defeat.\n\nConsequently, Lupe will take his time and wait to reach whatever goals he may have in mind.", "annotation_id": "11294573", "url": "https://genius.com/11294573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "[Verse 3: Big K.R.I.T.]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Prior to the release of this song, Lupe tweeted that K.R.I.T ‘renegaded’ him and Ross on this album. Thus, this set up very high expectations for the following verse by K.R.I.T https://twitter.com/lupefiasco/status/776851278160801792", "annotation_id": "11248430", "url": "https://genius.com/11248430", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "‘Cause I got chillin’ by the million, tranquillo by the kilo Nigga, nigga, what, and I got kilos by the speedboat And I ain’t talkin’ ’bout them drugs I’m talkin’ ’bout that love For myself and all my niggas All my bitches and all my thugs, what’s up? ‘Cause I got chillin’ by the million, tranquillo by the kilo Nigga, nigga, what, and I got kilos by the speedboat And I ain’t talkin’ ’bout that work I’m talkin’ ’bout that worth Of myself and all my niggas Every diamond came out the dirt, nigga", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I got chillin' by the million, tranquillo by the kilo", "Nigga, nigga, what, and I got kilos by the speedboat", "And I ain't talkin' 'bout them drugs"], "meaning": "Throughout Hip-Hop, and even in some of Lupe’s past music, a subject that seems to come up consistently when talking about cocaine is its smuggling by the kilo across coastal waters. However, in the case of this song, Lupe is using this lyrical norm and flipping it onto a more positive spectrum.\n\nWhen translating from Spanish to English, tranquilo can become any variation of calm/quiet/peaceful.  On his metaphorical boat, Lupe isn’t bringing in work — or drugs. Rather, he’s smuggling in tranquilo — or peace and love — and distributing it to the people just like the criminals distribute their cocaine to the people.\n\nHe then goes on to quickly say that everyone can eventually achieve this tranquilo state, making a reference to the classic idiom, “A diamond in the rough”, which basically describes someone who has hidden exceptional characteristics and/or future potential, but currently lacks the final touches that would allow them to achieve this state.", "annotation_id": "11237305", "url": "https://genius.com/11237305", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "line": "As I reach, in an ethereal direction to provide my substance", "vault_lines": ["As I reach, in an ethereal direction to provide my substance"], "meaning": "Ethereal is something airy and insubstantial, such as a ghostly figure at the top of the stairs. It might also be something delicate and light, like a translucent fabric, or a singer’s delicate voice.\nEthereal comes from the Greek word for ether, which is a drug that makes you feel light headed and, in larger doses, causes you to lose consciousness. An ethereal substance or sound is one that carries the feeling of ether––something you might see in a vision, that might strike you as heavenly or supernatural.\nlove lu", "annotation_id": "8824205", "url": "https://genius.com/8824205", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tranquillo", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lupe-fiasco-tranquillo-lyrics", "genius_title": "Tranquillo", "genius_id": 2438502, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Boomin", "line": "When I hit a lick it I bought a wingstop (Twenty of em) I sprinkle lemon pepper", "vault_lines": ["When I hit a lick it I bought a wingstop (Twenty of em)", "I sprinkle lemon pepper"], "meaning": "Ross is the proud owner of multiple Wingstop franchises across the nation. He’s mentioned many times how his favorite flavor is lemon pepper.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5sPHiu9A6Eo", "annotation_id": "902741", "url": "https://genius.com/902741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
