{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Had to kill the watch, nigga -- time served", "vault_lines": ["Had to kill the watch, nigga -- time served"], "meaning": "Double entendre and a wordplay here. He could be referring to watch as the time piece, or a term for a period in prison.: because he just killed it, he had to serve time.\n\n#Get it?", "annotation_id": "2116870", "url": "https://genius.com/2116870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Coke Boys in this bitch, move 11 hundred", "vault_lines": ["Coke Boys in this bitch, move 11 hundred"], "meaning": "Coke Boys are a rap group that consists of French Montana, Chinx Drugz, Cheeze, Flip, Droop Pop & Charlie Rock. Birdman is on French’s trap so he’s hanging with their crew.", "annotation_id": "1894615", "url": "https://genius.com/1894615", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Right side turn wheel; talk kush, we burn fields", "vault_lines": ["Right side turn wheel; talk kush, we burn fields"], "meaning": "French is refering to the right-hand drive cars he owns. In the U.S Most cars are left-hand drive  saying he has foreign cars imported(foreign-foreign cars)- probably an Aston Martin from England, or perhaps a Lambo.\n\n\n\nHe then goes on to warn fools not to talk about how much they weed they smoke around him, because the amount of weed he and his guys smoke is equivalent to a whole field of dope!", "annotation_id": "1882013", "url": "https://genius.com/1882013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House", "line": "I’m a boss, motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["I'm a boss, motherfucker"], "meaning": "One of Ross' nicknames is “The Boss” and has had numerous boss-titled songs through his career, including Meek Mill’s I’m A Boss which Ross uses as an into when performing at concerts.", "annotation_id": "1794713", "url": "https://genius.com/1794713", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House", "line": "On the salt, motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["On the salt, motherfucker"], "meaning": "“The salt” refers to bath salts, which is the street name for a family of designer drugs often containing substituted cathinones, which have effects similar to amphetamine and cocaine.\n\nRoss also once mentioned that he is known as The Bath Salt Boss.", "annotation_id": "1792488", "url": "https://genius.com/1792488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House", "line": "I talk money, some say I speak foreign (HUH)", "vault_lines": ["I talk money, some say I speak foreign (HUH)"], "meaning": "All Rick Ross talks about is money – cuz that’s all he knows. He speaks about money a lot, but to some broke people it sounds like a different language cuz they ain’t ever heard the numbers he deals with.", "annotation_id": "1792449", "url": "https://genius.com/1792449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
