{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "line": "Who the fuck that is peeking in my window? Fuck boys know I keep that extendo (GuWop)", "vault_lines": ["Who the fuck that is peeking in my window?", "Fuck boys know I keep that extendo (GuWop)"], "meaning": "This isn’t an exaggeration, Gucci killed an assailant in self defence in 2005 after they attacked him at his home.\n\nIt’s also a reference to “Cell Therapy” by Goodie Mob:\n\nWho’s that peeking in my window\nPOW nobody now\n\nAn “extendo” is slang for a semi-automatic rifle or pistol magazine with an extended clip.", "annotation_id": "2053932", "url": "https://genius.com/2053932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "line": "Trap house, trap house, trap house, trap Trap house, trap house, trap house, trap Trap house, trap house, trap house, trap house Trap house, trap house, trap house, trap Trap house, trap, trap house, trap Trappin’ off a pack, know I trap house trap Trap house, trap, trap house, trap (Maybach Music) Trappin’ off a pack, know I trap house trap", "vault_lines": ["Trap house, trap house, trap house, trap", "Trap house, trap house, trap house, trap house", "Trap house, trap, trap house, trap", "Trappin' off a pack, know I trap house trap"], "meaning": "A Trap House is slang for a house (most often abandoned) where drugs are cooked, later to be sold.", "annotation_id": "1947024", "url": "https://genius.com/1947024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "line": "I use to trap out all the bandos Abandoned homes with boarded windows", "vault_lines": ["I use to trap out all the bandos", "Abandoned homes with boarded windows"], "meaning": "Bandos are an abbreviation for “abandoned” homes\" which are vacant houses, typically with boarded up windows so no one can get inside.", "annotation_id": "1868911", "url": "https://genius.com/1868911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "line": "Now, GuWop, they call me El Chapo, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Now, GuWop, they call me El Chapo, nigga"], "meaning": "Gucci Man reportedly was going to change his rap name to GuWop for reasons unknown, probably the same reason he got an ice cream cone tattoo.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/gucci1017/statuses/308582762649120769\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHe later changed his mind due to fan feedback.\n\n\n\nEl Chapo is a Mexican drug lord whose real name is Joaquín Archivaldo Guzmán Loera. He is the leader of the Sinaloa Cartel, a criminal organization named after the Mexican Pacific coast state of Sinaloa where it was initially formed.", "annotation_id": "1868908", "url": "https://genius.com/1868908", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "line": "I’m riding ’round with my lieutenant", "vault_lines": ["I'm riding 'round with my lieutenant"], "meaning": "He’s riding with his main shooter and is prepared to keep it 100 if niggas run up on him again", "annotation_id": "1810744", "url": "https://genius.com/1810744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "line": "Trap House III, got a K with me And three young niggas that stay with me", "vault_lines": ["Trap House III, got a K with me", "And three young niggas that stay with me"], "meaning": "Gucci Mane is in his trap house with a kilo of coke and three shooters to hold shit down in case of trouble\n\n\n\nThe “K” could also stand for AK 47’s, which his shooters are using.", "annotation_id": "1810715", "url": "https://genius.com/1810715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "line": "Guaranteed I make this money stack, nigga I’m trying to make this money fast, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Guaranteed I make this money stack, nigga"], "meaning": "Cocaine is running at $24,000-$27,000 in the United States, which is easy to see why Gucci is able to have stacks of cash after a quick business transaction.", "annotation_id": "1810697", "url": "https://genius.com/1810697", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap House 3", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gucci-mane-trap-house-3-lyrics", "genius_title": "Trap House 3", "genius_id": 156120, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Double M, no longer that Buick Regal money", "vault_lines": ["Double M, no longer that Buick Regal money"], "meaning": "Rozay plays on car brands here.\nFirst “Double M” as the Maybach (Which is also the name of his Label) a High-end luxury car and the “Buick Regal” which is relatively not.\nIn relation with money, Ross proclaims He’s reaching heights in His money making Business and no longer living on puny paychecks", "annotation_id": "12906115", "url": "https://genius.com/12906115", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "I pray you play by the rules", "vault_lines": ["I pray you play by the rules"], "meaning": "Ross prays that young niggas will play by the rules of the game. Or rules of life. No second guessing, no snitching, no back-talk, and let niggas know that you’re loyal.\n\nQuoted from The Wire. By D'Angelo Barksdale", "annotation_id": "4658923", "url": "https://genius.com/4658923", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "I speak for dope boys every track I’m on Until this day, my people never rat or told Posted twenty in, I’m talkin’ fed pen", "vault_lines": ["I speak for dope boys every track I'm on", "Until this day, my people never rat or told", "Posted twenty in, I'm talkin' fed pen"], "meaning": "On every song Ross is featured on, he’s representing drug dealers – since he used to be a drug dealer too, he can relate to them. As a drug dealer, nobody has ever snitched on Ross. These drug dealers that have refused to snitch on Ross, are currently serving 20 years in the Federal Penitentiary.", "annotation_id": "4658732", "url": "https://genius.com/4658732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Dudes can’t appreciate, you know what I’m saying, talent and wealth, you know what I mean, as far as like mental wealth, you know what I mean? When you see when you the fool", "vault_lines": ["I appreciate the love"], "meaning": "Throughout this album, the real Bobbie Williams, the drug kingpin serving time in prison talks through a prison phone. Bobbie Williams continues what he was saying at the end of the previous track, “Phone Tap,” and the very beginning of this track.\n\nBobbie Williams is saying that years ago, he’s always been telling niggas, that niggas with high stature in the hood, that niggas are going to hold shit against you. And Bobbie is saying that he fights everyday for Maybach Music Group. Every time he gets letter from Rick Ross, whether it favors the courts or not, Bobbie appreciate the letters he gets from Rick Ross cuz Ross and MMG is what motivates Bobbie to carry out his long term sentence (or his life-term sentence.) That’s real love", "annotation_id": "4658705", "url": "https://genius.com/4658705", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "I be strapped on stage, fuck the award show ’Cause I’ll shoot this bitch up and only God knows", "vault_lines": ["I be strapped on stage, fuck the award show", "'Cause I'll shoot this bitch up and only God knows"], "meaning": "Yo Gotti is saying he keeps himself strapped at all times so he can be ready for any enemies that try to do great harm or even to end Yo Gotti’s life. Whether it’s niggas he has beef with, niggas who’s playa hating cux of his rich lifestyle as a rapper and as a well known candidate out on the streets. or if to try to rob Yo Gotti of his money, drugs and jewelry.\n\nSo when dangers comes to Gotti he’ll be prepared and he will shoot the bitch (calling his enemies which are niggas, calling them bitch ass niggas.) and when he kills you, no one else will know but him and God", "annotation_id": "4658246", "url": "https://genius.com/4658246", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Ten million dollars later, I’m a blessin’, nigga (Hood Billionaire) How a nigga rich, but still stressin’, nigga? Glock 40, Smith & Wesson, nigga Streets’ll never ever stop testin’ niggas (Never)", "vault_lines": ["Ten million dollars later, I'm a blessin', nigga (Hood Billionaire)", "How a nigga rich, but still stressin', nigga?", "Glock 40, Smith & Wesson, nigga"], "meaning": "Even though all of Yo Gotti’s dreams have come true and he feels blessed for earning all this money, he still has problems in his life. As the late Biggie put it: Mo' Money Mo' Problems. The streets haven’t changed for him, it’s still full of danger like it’s always been – Gotti still carries his weapons (Glock 40 and Smith & Wesson) for this reason.", "annotation_id": "4658066", "url": "https://genius.com/4658066", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Art of hustle, nigga Rules, laws, strategy", "vault_lines": ["Art of hustle, nigga"], "meaning": "Life is nothing but a hustle. A hustle to get ahead of things. Whether it’s a legitimate business or illegal activity. Everything in life is not for free, so you got to “hustle,” our way to the top to get where you need to get to in life.\n\nAlso Yo Gotti is saying there’s three things in life people hustle for. Rules, Laws and Strategies. It’s like what Jay Z said, “You can’t knock the hustle.”", "annotation_id": "4658046", "url": "https://genius.com/4658046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "[Intro: Yo Gotti & Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Yo Gotti is explaining that he lives in a world (when he says jungle, he could also be referring to the hood he was lived and grew up in.) that it’s survival of the fittest. A world that is filled with positivity and negativity. A place where you have to fight for your rights and to fight to stay alive.", "annotation_id": "4658019", "url": "https://genius.com/4658019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "We flipped pies to franchisin’ Dominoes", "vault_lines": ["We flipped pies to franchisin' Dominoes"], "meaning": "Comparing making pizzas at Domino’s to owning the company itself. Especially Ross can relate to this since he owes his own record label, Maybach Music Group.", "annotation_id": "4589964", "url": "https://genius.com/4589964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "I’m in a jungle (M—) Lions, tigers and gorillas and shit, nigga (Hood Billionaire) It’s a lot of monkey-ass niggas out here too", "vault_lines": ["It's a lot of monkey-ass niggas out here too"], "meaning": "Lions, and tigers, and gorillas oh my! A line up similar to the frightening creatures mentioned in “The Wizard of Oz”. The monkeys could be a reference to the flying monkeys of “Wizard of Oz”; the witches goons.", "annotation_id": "4454166", "url": "https://genius.com/4454166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "I’ll be back when they quit livin’ through phones When niggas put the ’Gram down and pick the grams up You got follows, but no dollars, man, that shit ain’t addin’ up", "vault_lines": ["I'll be back when they quit livin' through phones", "When niggas put the 'Gram down and pick the grams up", "You got follows, but no dollars, man, that shit ain't addin' up"], "meaning": "Referring to people living their lives online, more worried about what’s going on there, like getting ‘likes’ and ‘followers’, instead of what’s going on in the real world. Gotti has no respect for people trying harder to get followers than money.\n\nGram refers to Instagram and a ‘gram’ is a unit of measurement used to weigh drugs.", "annotation_id": "4400258", "url": "https://genius.com/4400258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Niggas crossin’ over like they Allen Iverson", "vault_lines": ["Niggas crossin' over like they Allen Iverson"], "meaning": "In basketball, a crossover is a move in which the player with the ball switches from one hand to the other and jukes out his defender to drive to the basket or take a quick jump shot. Allen Iverson had one of the sickest crossovers in the game.\n\nInstead of basketball, Gotti’s referring to a spiritual crossover when one dies.", "annotation_id": "4400210", "url": "https://genius.com/4400210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Fuck that iPhone 6, they be trackin’ niggas I’m ’bout to get a beeper, fade to black on niggas", "vault_lines": ["I'm 'bout to get a beeper, fade to black on niggas"], "meaning": "Yo Gotti wants to keep his drug deals on the low so he won’t be able to be tracked. The iPhone 6 (and other older models) have an app called Find My iPhone which allows iPhone owners find their iPhone if it ever gets lost or stolen. Yo Gotti is keeping it simple by just getting a beeper so he can avoid being tracked by the authorities.\n\n\n\nThis is also a reference to the previous track on Hood Billionaire, “Phone Tap”", "annotation_id": "4394371", "url": "https://genius.com/4394371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Niggas ridin’ gold rims and they mama poor And they kill a family member for that envelope’", "vault_lines": ["Niggas ridin' gold rims and they mama poor", "And they kill a family member for that envelope'"], "meaning": "People in the hood have priorities backwards and would rather floss their cash than make sure their family is taken care of, according to Ross. They spend money on themselves, like buying gold rims, instead of using that money to financially provide for their mother. They are even willing to kill their family members for money.", "annotation_id": "4378625", "url": "https://genius.com/4378625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Still losin’ weight with the south on my back, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Still losin' weight with the south on my back, nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is one of the bigger names popping out of the South/Florida area right now. He is continuing to grow his brand while giving himself a new image with his “RossFit” workout plan.\n\n\n\nThere’s nothing wrong with getting rich and dropping a few pounds in the process, even DJ Khaled is on board", "annotation_id": "4375336", "url": "https://genius.com/4375336", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "I’m the Lionel Richie to these Commodores", "vault_lines": ["I'm the Lionel Richie to these Commodores"], "meaning": "Rick is so essential to other people’s success much like Lionel Ritchie played a crucial part in the success of the musical group “Commodores”.", "annotation_id": "4375315", "url": "https://genius.com/4375315", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "line": "Amongst my boys, I’m W.E.B. Du Bois Souls of black folk, to hustle wasn’t a choice", "vault_lines": ["Amongst my boys, I'm W.E.B. Du Bois", "Souls of black folk, to hustle wasn't a choice"], "meaning": "Ross is using African-American sociologist and civil rights activist W.E.B. Du Bois to draw a comparison to the black people hustling to conquer the ghetto struggle.\n\n\n\nThough slavery and racial prejudice have been largely overcome, their devastating impact still holds black communities in a crushing grip. Every nigga slanging ‘caine is continuing the fight against racial injustice but as the battle has changed severely, so have the war tactics.\n\n‘The Souls of Black Folk’ is Du Bois’s groundbreaking sociological book on his personal experiences as an African-American.", "annotation_id": "4375056", "url": "https://genius.com/4375056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Luv", "status": "done", "targets": 17, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-trap-luv-lyrics", "genius_title": "Trap Luv", "genius_id": 579995, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Just like Omar and Khloe", "vault_lines": [", just like Omar and Khloe"], "meaning": "Probably talking about 2 millionaires referring to Lamar Odom and Khloe Kardashian, a famous celebrity couple at the time.", "annotation_id": "30546287", "url": "https://genius.com/30546287", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Fuck around, call the Fed on me Chk-chk, boom boom boom your head, homie, reds", "vault_lines": ["Fuck around, call the Fed on me", "Chk-chk, boom boom boom your head, homie, reds"], "meaning": "Thugger states that if you call the police (feds) on him he’ll pump your guts full of lead.\n\n\n\nHe also does a gun cocking sound to add effect and reds means the blood on the head when the person is shot.", "annotation_id": "15536207", "url": "https://genius.com/15536207", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "See the look on my face (Woo!) like Carol City won state", "vault_lines": ["See the look on my face (Woo!) like Carol City won state"], "meaning": "Carol City is a lower middle class area city in Miami-Dade County, Florida. The city was originally known as Coral City(as in the stuff in the ocean)then permanently chaged to Carol City in 2003. Carol City is now being recognised due to the fact that there are up and coming hip hop stars who riginate from this area, an example being Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "13402463", "url": "https://genius.com/13402463", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "I was tryna bet the whole map out in Vegas, out the trap", "vault_lines": ["I was tryna bet the whole map out in Vegas, out the trap"], "meaning": "Young Thug is a known gambling addict. Even though his brother was killed from his gambling issues, that was not enough to stop him. His sisters try their best for Young Thug to go anywhere except for Vegas:\n\nThey spent the day playing dice, and by midnight Thug had lost all the money he’d made and more. This was fairly typical. “I done lost a million kazillion dollars gambling,” he says, spacing out for a moment before adding, “My dad is a gambler.”", "annotation_id": "12859123", "url": "https://genius.com/12859123", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "When it come to bitches I’m Gucci I’m the wrong one to rob", "vault_lines": ["I'm the wrong one to rob"], "meaning": "In 2005, Gucci Mane was charged with murder after a group of thugs attempted to rob him at the home of a female acquaintance in Decatur, Georgia. Gucci is unable to comment on what happened, but all evidence points to him killing one of his attempted robbers.", "annotation_id": "12779293", "url": "https://genius.com/12779293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "In the label I’m Russ", "vault_lines": ["In the label I'm Russ"], "meaning": "Russell Simmons is a successful owner of Def Jam Recording, so Ross is comparing himself to the Russell Simmons of Maybach music (Ross' Label).", "annotation_id": "11549459", "url": "https://genius.com/11549459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "All she want is good dick and advice", "vault_lines": ["Adios, do 120, all she want is good dick and advice"], "meaning": "The woman that Wale is with desires to have sexual loving and empathetic care. He is certainly an artist who has displayed his affection for females several times in tracks such as “Diary” and “Lotus Flower Bomb”.\n\nThis line is also a saying which is further explained in “DNA”—a track that appears on his 5th studio album Shine.", "annotation_id": "11749235", "url": "https://genius.com/11749235", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Nigga run base, base in the trap", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga slave in the trap, nigga run base, base in the trap"], "meaning": "“Run” means to sell/peddle drugs.  Base is short for freebase (cocaine heated to produce vapors for inhalation or smoked as crack)", "annotation_id": "11627204", "url": "https://genius.com/11627204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "You came down for the packs, I sent you right back loaded", "vault_lines": ["You came down for the packs, I sent you right back loaded"], "meaning": "“Packs” usually refers to a bag of drugs, as Rick Ross was on house arrest at the time, he couldn’t go meet you for the drug deal. This meant that you had to come down to him for the drugs, and he sends you back all filled up with the product.", "annotation_id": "11581404", "url": "https://genius.com/11581404", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "In the trap I’m Rick Ross", "vault_lines": [", in the trap I'm Rick Ross"], "meaning": "“Freeway” Rick Ross is an American drug kingpin, convicted of running a multi-billion dollar drug empire.\n\nIn 2010, the former drug lord filed a lawsuit against Rick Ross, worth $10 million, for copyright infringement after the Miami-based rapper profited off his name and image as a ruthless criminal. The lawsuit was subsequently  dismissed after a short trial and Rozay was able to escape without paying a dime.", "annotation_id": "11558020", "url": "https://genius.com/11558020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Double M, Goldman Sachs", "vault_lines": ["Double M, Goldman Sachs"], "meaning": "“Double M” means MM, or the abbreviation for millions of dollars ($50MM). It is also a reference to Ross' record label Maybach Music Group (MMG). Notable MMG signees include Meek Mill, Wale, and Omarion\n\nGoldman Sachs is the world’s most prestigious investment bank, known for massive wealth and reputation.", "annotation_id": "11546098", "url": "https://genius.com/11546098", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Nigga, watch your babies in the trap", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, watch your babies in the trap"], "meaning": "Thug is warning people to watch their backs while in the trap and to keep a close eye on their work – a baby can be slang for any substantial amount of cocaine or marijuana.", "annotation_id": "11544315", "url": "https://genius.com/11544315", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Double M the Empire", "vault_lines": ["Famous here but I'm humble, Double M the Empire"], "meaning": "MMG (Maybach Music Group) aka Double M is a record label imprint founded by American rapper Rick Ross. The label is home to a huge empire of well-known rappers such as Meek Mill, Wale, Omarion, Gunplay and Torch, among others. It was even the label of former member French Montana until May 5, 2016 when his joint contract with Interscope and MMG ended.", "annotation_id": "11544282", "url": "https://genius.com/11544282", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Draco got a lot of lead on it, you dead", "vault_lines": ["Draco got a lot of lead on it, you dead"], "meaning": "Draco Pistol. These are imported Romanian built AK 47 pistols in 7.62x39 semi auto caliber, Matte black finish, new units. Barrel has integral front sight & gas tube.\nThus, combined with relative abundance and low cost, these factors resulted in the extensive use of lead in construction, plumbing, batteries, bullets and shot, weights, solders, pewters, fusible alloys, and radiation shielding. In the late 19th century, lead was recognized as poisonous.", "annotation_id": "11541168", "url": "https://genius.com/11541168", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "In the jungle I’m Nas", "vault_lines": [", in the jungle I'm Nas"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is paying homage to one of Queensbridge’s very own, Nas.\n\n“The Jungle” is a nickname for Queensbridge, New York, stating that in the jungle, he’s respected at the same level Nas is.   Jungle is also the name of Nas' younger brother.\n\nRick Ross and Nas have been linked for over a decade, and both have a high level of respect for one another.", "annotation_id": "11522131", "url": "https://genius.com/11522131", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Renzel got me all day, I’m Kyrie, he LeBron James Tired niggas say Folarin ain’t top, I been SportsCenter erryday", "vault_lines": ["Renzel got me all day, I'm Kyrie, he LeBron James", "Tired niggas say Folarin ain't top, I been SportsCenter erryday"], "meaning": "Wale compares the dynamic duo of Kyrie Irving and LeBron James of the Cleveland Cavaliers to himself and Rick Ross. Rick Ross signed Wale to his MMG label in 2011. Ross explained in an interview that Wale impressed him not only musically, but his ability to hustle.\n\nWale is also explaining that he is tired of people not referring to him as a top 10 rapper, comparing it to SportsCenter’s Top 10 list, in which Kyrie and LeBron usually make.\n\nWale wrote the theme song for ESPN’s First Take. Meaning he’s literally on ESPN every day.​", "annotation_id": "11519085", "url": "https://genius.com/11519085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "I ain’t nothin’ like them trap guys, I mean I kinda do bag dimes", "vault_lines": ["I ain't nothin' like them trap guys, I mean I kinda do bag dimes"], "meaning": "Wale says he’s not like the “trap guys”, but he does  “bag dimes”. This is a double reference, as “trap guys” are typically those slangin' drugs and wale references how they sell “dime bags” (usually $10 for a gram of weed), whereas Wale “bags dimes” – in the sense that he gets with girls who are dimes (dime piece) – a perfect 10.", "annotation_id": "11519079", "url": "https://genius.com/11519079", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Answer the door with the Woolie, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I'm 'bout to get this shit movin', yeah, answer the door with the Woolie, yeah"], "meaning": "When Young Thug aka Jeffery answers the door he does so with a Woolie in hand. A woolie is slang for a gun.\n\n\n\n“Consider our street soldiers, run with the wooly”", "annotation_id": "11501486", "url": "https://genius.com/11501486", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Then I earnt the Lombardi", "vault_lines": ["Then I earnt the Lombardi"], "meaning": "The Vince Lombardi Trophy is the trophy awarded each year to the winning team of the National Football League’s championship game, the Super Bowl.\n\nIt was first awarded January 15, 1967 – Going to the Green Bay Packers after defeating the Kansas City Chiefs", "annotation_id": "11501431", "url": "https://genius.com/11501431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Beep, beep I’m sittin’ at the red light My ankle monitor beepin’", "vault_lines": ["My ankle monitor beepin'"], "meaning": "In 2015 Ricky Rozay was placed on house arrest after allegedly pistol-whipping his groundskeeper. While on house arrest Ross was forced to wear an ankle monitor, keeping track of his every move.\n\nRoss stopped by Meek Mill’s place to show off both of their ankle monitors since they were both on house arrest at the same time for completely different charges.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BDD106SS2IU/", "annotation_id": "11501348", "url": "https://genius.com/11501348", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Stand at the stove ’til you’re woozy, woozy", "vault_lines": ["Stand at the stove 'til you're woozy, woozy"], "meaning": "In reference to the process of “cooking crack” on a stove top, Thug is saying keep stirring or whipping the product in the pot until the fumes from said product (and/or possibly your rapid stirring motion) disorient you or make you woozy enough to stop.", "annotation_id": "11498897", "url": "https://genius.com/11498897", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Trap Trap Trap", "line": "Bitch, I’m richer than Tom Cruise, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Move, move, move, bitch, I'm richer than Tom Cruise, yeah"], "meaning": "Young Thug claims to have assessed more wealth than one of Hollywood’s most successful actors, Tom Cruise. Although Thugger is sitting on a net worth of $6 Million, it’s nothing compared to Tom’s estimated $480 Million.", "annotation_id": "11482612", "url": "https://genius.com/11482612", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
