{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "Copped my Makaveli CD and I listened and I learned", "vault_lines": ["Copped my Makaveli CD and I listened and I learned"], "meaning": "Many rappers such as Kendrick Lamar and J.Cole have openly shown their love and influenced by [Tupac Shakur]. In this case, Meek Mill also  learned a lot of things from the late Tupac’s album: Makaveli The Don Killuminati – The Seven Day Theory.", "annotation_id": "8413795", "url": "https://genius.com/8413795", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "I’m screaming, “Free my nigga Hearn”", "vault_lines": ["And let it burn, I'm screaming, \"Free my nigga Hearn\""], "meaning": "At this time rapper Earl Sweatshirt was “locked up” in a boarding school in indonesia by his mother due to the fact that he was getting high too frequently.", "annotation_id": "8413740", "url": "https://genius.com/8413740", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "Ugh! 2Pac back, I’m two Glocks strapped", "vault_lines": ["Ugh! 2Pac back, I'm two Glocks strapped"], "meaning": "In 2008, he was arrested on a gun charge and was sentenced to eight months in jail..Be careful with your toys,Meek.\n\nAlso a reference to Pac’s song “2 Glocks”", "annotation_id": "1051908", "url": "https://genius.com/1051908", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "But don’t ever get it twisted, it’s Meek Mill, we spittin’ facts (Meek Milly!)", "vault_lines": ["But don't ever get it twisted, it's Meek Mill, we spittin' facts (Meek Milly!)"], "meaning": "Although the track is called “Tupacs Back”, Meek is letting you know this is his story and he’s not trying to be 2Pac. He’s just referring to their similar upbringing and events that happened to the both of them.", "annotation_id": "679675", "url": "https://genius.com/679675", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "Plotting on this new 7, I can picture me rolling", "vault_lines": ["Plotting on this new 7, I can picture me rolling"], "meaning": "Making plans to buy a BMW 7-series. Meek can already imagine himself in it. Big rims, status, wealth.\n\n\n\nReference to the 2Pac song “Picture Me Rollin'”", "annotation_id": "273502", "url": "https://genius.com/273502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "Riding on my muh’fuckin’ enemies!", "vault_lines": ["Riding on my muh'fuckin' enemies!"], "meaning": "This is a reference to 2Pac’s song “When We Ride On Our Enemies”", "annotation_id": "232496", "url": "https://genius.com/232496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "I need a brand new Mercedes", "vault_lines": ["But I'm stacking my paper, I need a brand new Mercedes"], "meaning": "Another “Picture Me Rollin” reference, specifically to the Benz mentioned in the previous line", "annotation_id": "232485", "url": "https://genius.com/232485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": ".40 kick like it’s soccer, bullets hitting the goal", "vault_lines": [".40 kick like it's soccer, bullets hitting the goal"], "meaning": "A 40mm gun has kick (the force that pushes the gun backwards when you shoot it), but Meek Millz also plays on the fact that you “kick” a soccer ball.\n\n\n\nHe means .40 caliber, unless he’s firing off a grenade launcher!", "annotation_id": "229489", "url": "https://genius.com/229489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "I’m dreaming spitting with Pac (Pac!) and cyphers with B.I.G (B.I.G!)", "vault_lines": ["I'm dreaming spitting with Pac (Pac!) and cyphers with B.I.G (B.I.G!)"], "meaning": "A cypher is a circle of people formed for community freestyle rap. One emcee will spit for an undetermined period of time, after which he or she will yield the floor to the next freestyler. Mill dreams of participating in a cypher with gangster rap legends Tupac and the Notorious B.I.G.", "annotation_id": "222377", "url": "https://genius.com/222377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "Mommy a soldier", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Meek’s mother had to look after Meek when he was young because his father died. In keeping with the Pac-referencing theme of this song, 2Pac’s mother was a “soldier” for the black panthers, she was released out of prison just a few weeks before Pac was born.", "annotation_id": "210884", "url": "https://genius.com/210884", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "It’s a recession on the work, I’m screaming, “Who got crack?”", "vault_lines": ["It's a recession on the work, I'm screaming, \"Who got crack?\""], "meaning": "An analogy for today’s economy. If something is in a recession it is in a decline. “Work” (drugs) is hard to find now because like every other business, the drug business is in a recession as well. It has been shown statistically from history that when the country has a high unemployment rate (from recession) that people go cheap, hence crack cocaine instead of the more expensive cocaine", "annotation_id": "188838", "url": "https://genius.com/188838", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "Bitch, I’m like John Wall ’cause I just give ’em and go", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm like John Wall 'cause I just give 'em and go"], "meaning": "John Wall is a basketball player for the Washington Wizards.\n\n\n\nMeek Millz plays off of the fact that John Wall is a basketball player, referencing a “give and go,” which is a popular play in basketball.", "annotation_id": "187678", "url": "https://genius.com/187678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "2Pac back, 2Pac back That’s all these bitches screaming that 2Pac back", "vault_lines": ["2Pac back, 2Pac back", "That's all these bitches screaming that 2Pac back"], "meaning": "2Pac was one of the realest rappers in history; Meek & Ross believe 2Pac’s realness to be reincarnated through their music", "annotation_id": "187667", "url": "https://genius.com/187667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "Riding brand new rims, but them bitches is stolen", "vault_lines": ["Riding brand new rims, but them bitches is stolen"], "meaning": "Rims are expensive and easy to remove\n\n\n\nContinuing the “Picture Me Rollin'” references, Ross conflicts with the original song, as Pac talked of “flossin' a Benz on rims that isn’t stolen.”", "annotation_id": "187553", "url": "https://genius.com/187553", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "line": "All eyes on me, better picture me rollin’", "vault_lines": ["All eyes on me, better picture me rollin'"], "meaning": "Allusion to Picture Me Rollin, one of the finest tracks from 2Pac’s All Eyez On Me", "annotation_id": "187551", "url": "https://genius.com/187551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Tupac Back", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Meek-mill-tupac-back-lyrics", "genius_title": "Tupac Back", "genius_id": 6298, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "And I put ’em on paper, oh that’s what this shit do? Oh, that’s how you nigga rock? I be wrong, I get you dropped I get you wet, nigga turn ya back Know where I live, I lay you flat, nigga, that’s a fact Put it on my kids, you niggas rats, and I’m comin’ back Look what you did, made me do that, got you niggas clapped These pussy niggas...", "vault_lines": ["And I put 'em on paper, oh that's what this shit do?", "Oh, that's how you nigga rock? I be wrong, I get you dropped", "I get you wet, nigga turn ya back"], "meaning": "Meek, now going all out in his verse is letting his feelings out about the people who turned their backs and turned him down. Now that Meek is living the life, he doesn’t care about them.\n\nMeek also calls these “these niggas” weak, emphasising the point he stated before about the hard life he has come from.\n\nThis could also be seen as a diss towards Drake, after their previous altercations and beef.", "annotation_id": "7734371", "url": "https://genius.com/7734371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "I knew a nigga 10 years, it’s a deadly game Man can win those cracker canes, shawty said my name Shit ain’t the same, there’s somethin’ missin’ There’s somethin’ different Either ya ass get pimped or you’re doin’ the pimpin’", "vault_lines": ["I knew a nigga 10 years, it's a deadly game", "Man can win those cracker canes, shawty said my name", "Shit ain't the same, there's somethin' missin'"], "meaning": "Slab has come far in his music career, from when he started to now. In the start of his career, he was getting “pimped”, or getting destroyed, but now that he’s successful, he’s “pimpin'” and has everything.", "annotation_id": "7734366", "url": "https://genius.com/7734366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "Fucked up my set, my bottom bitch, she turned her back She want rum and rocky with me, she was chasin’ sack Pussy hoe, she turned her back, that’s how she felt Collect call from Rice Street, that bitch, she run herself", "vault_lines": ["Fucked up my set, my bottom bitch, she turned her back", "She want rum and rocky with me, she was chasin' sack", "Pussy hoe, she turned her back, that's how she felt", "Collect call from Rice Street, that bitch, she run herself"], "meaning": "Even people that Slab was in a relationship with have turned their back on him. This particular girl used to be close with Slab but now, he doesn’t need her any more.", "annotation_id": "7734364", "url": "https://genius.com/7734364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "You could pay a nigga’s rent, have a nigga back Even pay a nigga bond what kind of shit is that?", "vault_lines": ["You could pay a nigga's rent, have a nigga back", "Even pay a nigga bond what kind of shit is that?"], "meaning": "The people he has been talking about in this verse could have helped him at least a bit when he was poor and now he doesn’t need their help.", "annotation_id": "7734363", "url": "https://genius.com/7734363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "He said “been workin’ lockin’ up that shit, it won’t come back” I told that nigga “man, there ain’t no need to call me that”", "vault_lines": ["He said \"been workin' lockin' up that shit, it won't come back\"", "I told that nigga \"man, there ain't no need to call me that\""], "meaning": "He’s had many instances in the past where other people have been talking shit on him, but look where he is now, on a track with Rozay and Meek, doing what he does best, rapping.", "annotation_id": "7734360", "url": "https://genius.com/7734360", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "Man, it’s funny how a nigga act", "vault_lines": ["Man, it's funny how a nigga act"], "meaning": "Gucci Mane starts off his verse talking about the way his haters act once he has become prosperous and successful.", "annotation_id": "7734354", "url": "https://genius.com/7734354", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "When I was broke man these bitches wouldn’t call me back", "vault_lines": ["When I was broke man these bitches wouldn't call me back"], "meaning": "Gucci mane grew up poor and ended up getting turned down a lot by the ladies. Once he got money & fame though, those same women changed up quick and started pursuing him now.", "annotation_id": "7733459", "url": "https://genius.com/7733459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "You stole a stack but bitch man, I would take the whole sack “Say Gucci Mane, you the man, why you doin’ that?”", "vault_lines": ["\"Say Gucci Mane, you the man, why you doin' that?\""], "meaning": "Women only want Gucci Mane because he has a lot of money. They don’t want to have sex with him too, they’re just there for his money.", "annotation_id": "7733448", "url": "https://genius.com/7733448", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "A Mastermind", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rozay is a mastermind, because he got out of where he was, and came to where he is now.\n\nMastermind is also his sixth studio album.", "annotation_id": "7733402", "url": "https://genius.com/7733402", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "I took the shirt off my back and put it on your back Then you turned your back, oh what kind of shit is that? Burr!", "vault_lines": ["I took the shirt off my back and put it on your back", "Then you turned your back, oh what kind of shit is that?"], "meaning": "Gucci has helped other people with their hip hop careers, through the metaphor of their shared interest as his shirt. But what did they do? Stabbed him in the back.", "annotation_id": "7733288", "url": "https://genius.com/7733288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "But then ’em niggas wanna front", "vault_lines": ["But then 'em niggas wanna front"], "meaning": "This alludes to the idea that no one dares to front him, because he is so successful with his music, and because he is quite scary and big.", "annotation_id": "7732811", "url": "https://genius.com/7732811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "You know, going through the things you go through Make you who you are But when the closest ones to you turn they back on you It’s such a painful feeling", "vault_lines": ["It's such a painful feeling"], "meaning": "Rick’s intro paints the picture of the song, and starts on the idea of people turning their backs on him, even the people that he loves.", "annotation_id": "7732809", "url": "https://genius.com/7732809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "All my niggas turned they back, they turned they back Even my people turned they back, they turned they back Even my cousin turned they back, he turned his back But now I’m back, now I’m back Even my bitch, she turned her back, she turned her back But now I’m back bitch, where you at? Now where you at?", "vault_lines": ["All my niggas turned they back, they turned they back", "Even my people turned they back, they turned they back", "Even my cousin turned they back, he turned his back", "But now I'm back, now I'm back"], "meaning": "Great punchline by Ross, questions the people who left him, as he is back again.", "annotation_id": "7732803", "url": "https://genius.com/7732803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "Slab!", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Slab’s ad lib. Get ready to start hearing this more often as he gets more famous.", "annotation_id": "7732735", "url": "https://genius.com/7732735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "Niggas turned they back on me, tried to fuck my bitch too", "vault_lines": ["Niggas turned they back on me, tried to fuck my bitch too"], "meaning": "Meek’s haters are jealous of him and Nicki. Because of his relationship with Nicki, once friends have turned on him.", "annotation_id": "7732672", "url": "https://genius.com/7732672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "Man I ain’t see it comin’, all the shit we been through And they ain’t see it comin’ neither, last time I spinned through Hard-top bent blue, every time I dipped through", "vault_lines": ["Man I ain't see it comin', all the shit we been through", "And they ain't see it comin' neither, last time I spinned through", "Hard-top bent blue, every time I dipped through"], "meaning": "Meek, as well as others, did not see his rise to fame from a battle rapper back in his Philly days.\n\nHe also proved everyone wrong by making it all the way to where he is.", "annotation_id": "7732666", "url": "https://genius.com/7732666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "They triple crossed me, left me for dead They blowin’ racks, I’m fucked up, I owe these chicos bread I’m in the red, I took a loss, had to crawl back My own niggas crossed me out, now what you call that?", "vault_lines": ["They triple crossed me, left me for dead", "They blowin' racks, I'm fucked up, I owe these chicos bread"], "meaning": "Whole Slab is in a similar situation as Rick Ross, people walked out on him and now that he’s becoming more and more successful.\n\nAt the moment, Slab is not with a music label, and he alludes to other labels ‘triple-crossing’ him and not having trust in him, but see where he is now, rapping with Rosé and Meek.\n\nSlab has put so much time and money into his career that he went in debt, but he is crawling back and beginning to get his name out in the rap game.", "annotation_id": "7732652", "url": "https://genius.com/7732652", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "Okay, hoes turnin’ back, niggas did too I was sellin’ crack, my niggas did too", "vault_lines": ["Okay, hoes turnin' back, niggas did too", "I was sellin' crack, my niggas did too"], "meaning": "Meek Mill grew up in Philly, the streets. Mill had to hustle to gain a living, expressing his struggle. Basically he doesn’t fuck with fake niggas.", "annotation_id": "7732643", "url": "https://genius.com/7732643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "They blowin’ stacks, they blowin’ stacks", "vault_lines": ["They blowin' stacks, they blowin' stacks"], "meaning": "Watching MMG rise to fame, others in the hip hop industry and haters of his art are getting angered by how he became so famous. Such as the phrase “blowin' stacks”.\n\n\n\n‘Blowing stacks’ may also refer to spending a lot money at one time. But, in this track and its context may not be relevant.", "annotation_id": "7732583", "url": "https://genius.com/7732583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "They turned they back, turned they back But then ’em niggas wanna front They blowin’ stacks, they blowin’ stacks They turn they back, turn they back But then ’em niggas wanna front They blowin’ stacks, they blowin’ stacks They turned they back, turned they back Watch a nigga fall down They turned they back, turned they back", "vault_lines": ["They blowin' stacks, they blowin' stacks", "They turn they back, turn they back", "Watch a nigga fall down"], "meaning": "Rick Ross mentions the people that forgot about him and “turned they backs” on him after he started to fall.\n\nNow, that he is about to release this album, those people and haters are coming back to him because he’s becoming more and more well known and successful.", "annotation_id": "7732561", "url": "https://genius.com/7732561", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Turn Ya Back", "line": "Like he got shit bad, but really that is just a knack You know a bitch that called police on you and took her back?", "vault_lines": ["Like he got shit bad, but really that is just a knack", "You know a bitch that called police on you and took her back?"], "meaning": "Mane he talks about all the fake people in his life and how they are faking all the problems they have, even though they have never experienced the hardships of his own life.", "annotation_id": "7732552", "url": "https://genius.com/7732552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
