{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "That nigga sold you that re-rock, you ain’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["That nigga sold you that re-rock, you ain't even know it"], "meaning": "the act of re-rocking cocaine back into rock form after cutting it with a cutting agent…\n\ni bet y'all ain’t even know it…", "annotation_id": "25663709", "url": "https://genius.com/25663709", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Poor high-class niggas", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is something Future has also said in “Upper Echeleon” from Dirty Sprite. Perhaps a slogan, something like Freeband Gang.\n\nPo is a southern pronuncian of “poor” – basically, Future used to be a poor guy, but now is a wealthy high class guy (as depicted by his braggadocio rhymes) – but still has the mindset of a nigga in the ghetto, ergo he is a poor high class nigga.", "annotation_id": "1816996", "url": "https://genius.com/1816996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "This a thousand dollar pair of shoes, you don’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["This a thousand dollar pair of shoes, you don't even know it"], "meaning": "Future is referring to his Chanel Running Shoes.\n\nHe performed at the Boardwalk Hall in Atlantic City for Power 99′s FM Spring Fest concert earlier this year rocking these kicks.\n\nThey were released in the beginning of the year starting at $795 and ranging in price to $950.", "annotation_id": "1816975", "url": "https://genius.com/1816975", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "If it ain’t P.J., no Rosé for me, hostess, don’t even pour it", "vault_lines": ["If it ain't P.J., no Rosé for me, hostess, don’t even pour it"], "meaning": "Basically saying he drinks “Perrier-Jouët Rose'.” The price of the bottles range from $150-$300. This price depends on the year it was bottled as well as the type of bottle it is.", "annotation_id": "1812034", "url": "https://genius.com/1812034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "[Produced By: Childish Major & Don Cannon]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The sound in the intro and throughout the whole track is actually a sound from a program called Omnisphere.  I can’t give out the name, but its not a horn, totally a synth.", "annotation_id": "1742765", "url": "https://genius.com/1742765", "state": "verified", "votes": 97, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Got a bag of bitches I play with, on cloud nine in my spaceship", "vault_lines": ["Got a bag of bitches I play with, on cloud nine in my spaceship"], "meaning": "Double meaning here. Ross is saying he has a bunch of women he uses for fun and also his bag of bitches could be different strains of weed and we all know Mary Jane is a fine lady. Cloud 9 can mean anything from being in love to being high.\n\nA spaceship refers to a brand new car with all the electronics.\n\nAlso, cloud 9 and spaceship tie in together in that spaceships take you very high up, maybe high enough to reach cloud 9.", "annotation_id": "1703816", "url": "https://genius.com/1703816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "We came up from nothin’, you don’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["We came up from nothin', you don’t even know it"], "meaning": "Despite rapping about living a lavish life, Future and many of his rap associates began life in poverty.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9pdbtxFxq2s\n\nAlso echoes the recent Started From The Bottom sentiments of his buddy Drake", "annotation_id": "1673976", "url": "https://genius.com/1673976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Specks on Tom Ford", "vault_lines": ["Specks on Tom Ford"], "meaning": "Rocko wears high class shades made by Tom Ford.", "annotation_id": "1673929", "url": "https://genius.com/1673929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Then you gon know it, damn, who shot you? They don’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["Then you gon know it, damn, who shot you? They don’t even know it"], "meaning": "This line goes along with the line above. When Rocko shoots you, hopefully for him there wont be any witnesses around to give the police information about the shooting.\n\nA slight allusion to the The Notorious B.I.G. song “Who Shot Ya?”.\n\nAn artful line!", "annotation_id": "1648101", "url": "https://genius.com/1648101", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Lil’ high glow, no no, we don’t do Moët", "vault_lines": ["lil' high glow, no no, we don’t do Moët"], "meaning": "Moët & Chandon or Moët is a french winery and co-owner of the luxury goods company Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton. Rocko might not like it, but Nas surely does.\n\nIt is not as fancy as Dom P, after all, which is produced by Moet & Chandon.\n\nMoët typically retails for around $50 for a 4-glass bottle (or up to $200 a bottle at clubs) while Dom wholesales for $190 or so a bottle and can reach dizzying prices at clubs.", "annotation_id": "1643131", "url": "https://genius.com/1643131", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Got a hundred rounds in this AR, you ain’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["Got a hundred rounds in this AR, you ain't even know it"], "meaning": "The Colt AR-15 is a lightweight, 5.56 mm, magazine-fed, semi-automatic rifle, with a rotating-lock bolt, actuated by direct impingement gas operation or long/short stroke piston operation. It is manufactured with the extensive use of aluminum alloys and synthetic materials.\n\n\n\nMost definitely not a standard clip. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k3zjqMq59tI", "annotation_id": "1641426", "url": "https://genius.com/1641426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "This a million dollar watch, nigga, you don’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["This a million dollar watch, nigga, you don't even know it"], "meaning": "Future’s got on a watch that clocks in at 7 digits. Still, its not as nice as Jay-Z’s 5 million dollar watch….", "annotation_id": "1637799", "url": "https://genius.com/1637799", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "[Chorus: Future]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Well, this hook and his verse probably wasn’t the smartest decision in his music career since his baby mama is accusing him of lying about his income and therefore paying much less in child support then he should. She is coming after you, you don’t even know it. Or hol' up wait a minute (word to Meek Mill) you actually do know it. Good luck in court!", "annotation_id": "1635017", "url": "https://genius.com/1635017", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Sip Dom Peri’,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A reference to Dom Pérignon an expensive French champagne.", "annotation_id": "1633650", "url": "https://genius.com/1633650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Boats all in my yard,", "vault_lines": ["Boats all in my yard,"], "meaning": "Ross owns an oceanside Miami mansion and thus his boats are truly in his yard. Ross is also the founder of the Yacht Club.\n\n\n\nIt’s also common for the less affluent people of Florida (especially residents of Polk County) to keep their boats in their yards since it’s expensive to keep them at a dock or bay.", "annotation_id": "1633634", "url": "https://genius.com/1633634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Your main nigga bout to turn his back, you ain’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["Your main nigga bout to turn his back, you ain't even know it"], "meaning": "Your friends are not loyal to you as Ross' friends are to him. He implies that your friends are bound to turn their back on you some day – the worst part is you never saw it coming. Did you know it? I bet not\n\n\n\nThis is highlighted in Ross' “Box Chevy” music video, where a man who plots to kill Ross is turned on by his own accomplice.", "annotation_id": "1633613", "url": "https://genius.com/1633613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Lemon pepper my wings", "vault_lines": ["lemon pepper my wings"], "meaning": "Ross makes another “Lemon Pepper” seasoning reference, as he is an avid Wingstop fan & owner.", "annotation_id": "1630651", "url": "https://genius.com/1630651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "I’d die over these Reeboks, you ain’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["I'd die over these Reeboks, you ain't even know it"], "meaning": "Ross was endorsed by Reebok, though ironically, after this song, he was dropped from their deal. Even more ironically, the line that got him dropped from the endorsement occurs right after this one.\n\n\n\nAfter getting dropped, Ross thanked them for their endorsement.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/322781079322894336\n\nIt was reported that Ross would lose an estimated between $3.5 and $5 million from the fallout.", "annotation_id": "1629190", "url": "https://genius.com/1629190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 73, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "You don’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["You don't even know it"], "meaning": "“U.O.E.N.O” is onomatopoeia for “you don’t even know.”  It’s somewhere between an abbreviation and an acronym\n\nHint: Say it out loud, quickly.", "annotation_id": "1566349", "url": "https://genius.com/1566349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Hawks game, fuckin’ floor it, TV seat, front row it", "vault_lines": ["Hawks game, fuckin' floor it, TV seat, front row it"], "meaning": "Rocko is an avid basketball spectator and fan of the Atlanta Hawks, and is sitting courtside at their games – the best seats in the house.", "annotation_id": "1566303", "url": "https://genius.com/1566303", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Rocko Da Don CEO it, ain’t gotta rap and you know it", "vault_lines": ["Rocko Da Don CEO it, ain’t gotta rap and you know it"], "meaning": "Rocko is also a businessman, therefore he doesn’t have to rap to pay the bills, because he already has money coming in from him being the founder of A1 Records\n\n\n\nAlso note that there is a noticeable pause after this line, with enough time to add another rhyme. The pause emphasizes the fact that Rocko “ain’t gotta rap”.", "annotation_id": "1554925", "url": "https://genius.com/1554925", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "U.O.E.N.O", "line": "Put Molly all in her champagne, she ain’t even know it I took her home and I enjoyed that, she ain’t even know it", "vault_lines": ["Put Molly all in her champagne, she ain’t even know it", "I took her home and I enjoyed that, she ain't even know it"], "meaning": "Ross' infamous “date rape” lyric that has gotten the rapper in a bit of controversy. It has prompted a petition calling for him to apologize for the lyric, as well as Reebok being pressured to drop the Miami native from their endorsement deal.\n\nAfter increasing backlash in response to the lyric, Ross attempted to clarify the lyrics, saying he was misinterpreted:\n\nI want to make sure this is clear, that woman is the most precious gift known to man, you understand? It was a misunderstanding with a lyric, a misinterpretation where the term rape wasn’t used. I would never use the term rape. As far as my camp, hip hop don’t condone that. The streets don’t condone that. Nobody condones that. So I wanted to reach out to all the queens that’s on my timeline, all the sexy ladies, the beautiful ladies that have been reaching out to me with the misunderstanding. We don’t condone rape and I’m not with that.\n\nRoss also made an additional statement to Funkmaster Flex.\n\nOn April 4, 2013 after a “Drop Rick Ross” petition from Reebok was started by UltraViolet, a woman’s rights group, Rick tweeted an apology reiterating the fact that he does not condone rape.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/319847608694738945\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/319866665900834816\n\nOn April 11, Reebok dropped Ross from their endorsement deal. UltraViolet, the women’s rights group that propelled the DRR campaign reacted to the news as well.\n\nThe day after being dropped from Reebok, Ross once again issued another apology:\n\nBefore I am an artist, I am a father, a son, and a brother to some of the most cherished women in the world. So for me to suggest in any way that harm and violation be brought to a woman is one of my biggest mistakes and regrets. As an artist, one of the most liberating things is being able to paint pictures with my words. But with that comes a great responsibility. And most recently, my choice of words was not only offensive, it does not reflect my true heart. And for this, I apologize. To every woman that has felt the sting of abuse, I apologize. I recognize that as an artist I have a voice and with that, the power of influence. To the young men who listen to my music, please know that using a substance to rob a woman of her right to make a choice is not only a crime, it’s wrong and I do not encourage it. To my fans, I also apologize if I have disappointed you. I can only hope that this sparks a healthy dialogue and that I can contribute to it.", "annotation_id": "1553426", "url": "https://genius.com/1553426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 523, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
