{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "VSVSVS (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/24hrs-vsvsvs-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "VSVSVS (Remix)", "genius_id": 3029199, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vacheron", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-vacheron-lyrics", "genius_title": "Vacheron", "genius_id": 7598853, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "line": "Valentina, baby I only need one moment of time To make you feel a way From the first time I looked in your eyes I knew that I would find a way To make you mine", "vault_lines": ["To make you feel a way", "From the first time I looked in your eyes", "I knew that I would find a way", "To make you mine"], "meaning": "This isn’t the first time we have seen this lyrical pattern before. In Daniel Caesar’s Get You, he uses these similar lines:\n\nEvery time I look into your eyes, I see it\nYou’re all I need\n\nIn Get You, these lines were to express Daniel Caesar’s sexual relationship with his lover.\n\nHe is seen doing the same thing in “Valentina”, expressing his sexual relations and differentiating it from just a sexual interaction; instead, it’s also layered with intimacy and trust. Something he is experiencing with Valentina. During their time of intimacy, Daniel Caesar realizes that he has found a way to make Valentina his lover, which is through sexual pleasure.", "annotation_id": "38388058", "url": "https://genius.com/38388058", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "line": "Give me a break, I know that you want me too (Give me a break)", "vault_lines": ["Give me a break, I know that you want me too (Give me a break)"], "meaning": "Daniel knows that, despite her being in a relationship, she wants Daniel because of the way he makes her feel. He wants her to “give him a break” because he knows that’s what she wants; she’s just bound by a relationship with another lover. The relationship feels like an anchor to her life, but she can’t get with Daniel because of the other aspects that come with him, like his mental baggage.", "annotation_id": "38388043", "url": "https://genius.com/38388043", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "line": "I know it’s late, and I know you got a man (I know it’s late) Please understand, baby, he won’t (Baby, he won’t) Love you like I do (Like I do)", "vault_lines": ["I know it's late, and I know you got a man (I know it's late)", "Please understand, baby, he won't (Baby, he won't)", "Love you like I do (Like I do)"], "meaning": "Daniel is the “other man,” or the side piece, in her relationship; in other words, she’s having an affair. Despite that, Daniel knows that her ‘main man’ won’t make her feel the way he does, especially sexually. However, Daniel stated that he would never go through this again. In an interview, Daniel said:\n\nUhh, I have [been a side piece] but I’ll never do it again… Even if you can be with a girl who’s being unfaithful with her man, you shouldn’t, because it jades your whole world. And there’s nothing scarier than the lies she tells. I’ll never do it again.", "annotation_id": "38388019", "url": "https://genius.com/38388019", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "line": "[Verse 1: Daniel Caesar]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The verse of the song was written by his brother Zachary Simmonds. According to Daniel in an interview, he brought him the beat and a little snippet of the verse written. Daniel loved it, and after that, he ran with it, released it as a single, and it ended up on the project, NEVER ENOUGH.\n\nI never do this, but one day [my brother] sent me a beat he made himself and the first verse or the chorus, and then it just happened.", "annotation_id": "38388012", "url": "https://genius.com/38388012", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "line": "[Verse 2: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross is a known rapper from the south-east (Florida) which he mentions later in the song. Despite being a more “gangsta” rapper, having ties with Cash Money Record Label (though never official!!! Which is important) by having connections with Birdman and Lil Wayne- Its a really heartfelt verse he is spitting.", "annotation_id": "30382816", "url": "https://genius.com/30382816", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "line": "Makin’ love like it’s war when it’s really peace", "vault_lines": ["Makin' love like it's war when it's really peace"], "meaning": "When people have sex, they tend to do or say kinky stuff. By this example, Rick Ross potentially smacks his lover’s ass or perhaps badmouths her by calling her “bitch, slut” etc.\nBut its all merely words, that are covered by his love to this person", "annotation_id": "28785594", "url": "https://genius.com/28785594", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "line": "You’re loyal it’s cool, I understand (I understand) And I respect it", "vault_lines": ["You're loyal it's cool, I understand (I understand)", "And I respect it"], "meaning": "Daniel has fallen victim to being cheated on in his past relationships; this respect he feels for loyalty is because he knows that’s what she should morally do — go back to her partner. Daniel being the second man in her relationship shows how his views on love have shifted and his past has scarred his view on relationships.\n\nThe ideas of disloyalty in a relationship has been seen before in Daniel’s past music, like on Freudian.\n\nThere are times I think about that fateful day\nI threw your love away\n— “Neu Roses (Transgressor’s Song)”\n​​​\nI never asked for much only that you stay true\nNeed I remind you all the things I do for you?\n— “Hold Me Down”", "annotation_id": "28238806", "url": "https://genius.com/28238806", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valentina (Bonus)", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Daniel-caesar-valentina-bonus-lyrics", "genius_title": "Valentina (Bonus)", "genius_id": 9001103, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Lord knows when I see this monkey, I’ma be the devil Beat him ’cause I’m clever, beat him at whatever You never was a G, nigga, unit mean together", "vault_lines": ["Lord knows when I see this monkey, I'ma be the devil", "Beat him 'cause I'm clever, beat him at whatever"], "meaning": "As he does numerous times on the album (Deeper Than Rap), Rick Ross takes a shot at rival artist 50 Cent. He refers to him as a monkey and does a play on words with 50’s group name “G-Unit”.", "annotation_id": "27034644", "url": "https://genius.com/27034644", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "New York unified, down south love that When we got to shine, “Motherfuckers, where the love at?”", "vault_lines": ["New York unified, down south love that", "When we got to shine, \"Motherfuckers, where the love at?\""], "meaning": "Ross refers to the shift of hip-hop relevancy from New York to the South in the mid-2000s. He talks on the fact that southern based artists showed nothing but love and respect for New York artists when it was their time, but the respect was not returned when the South took the spotlight.", "annotation_id": "27034606", "url": "https://genius.com/27034606", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Both chains reminiscin’ to them nooses", "vault_lines": ["Both chains reminiscin' to them nooses"], "meaning": "He is thinking back when slave owners use to hang black people with ropes(nooses).", "annotation_id": "16549928", "url": "https://genius.com/16549928", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Not the one just to jump to conclusions", "vault_lines": ["Not the one just to jump to conclusions"], "meaning": "Picking up from the previous line, it could be implied that Rick Ross is using sarcasm to state he would rather not get into the speculations of Trick Daddy’s illness.", "annotation_id": "2223989", "url": "https://genius.com/2223989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Keep it triller", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Popularized by Ross himself, “trilla” comes from the root word “trill”, a combination of “true” and “real”. Ross' sophomore album is entitled Trilla, and he has confirmed that it is a play on the notorious Michael Jackson album Thriller.", "annotation_id": "1120969", "url": "https://genius.com/1120969", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Took me forty minutes to walk there to buy it", "vault_lines": ["We could build our own world (Took me forty minutes to walk there to buy it"], "meaning": "He’s come a long way from being a fan, buying records, to a force in hip-hop, selling records and signing other artists.\n\nHip Hop critiques question Ross' commitment & realness in the genre, but the Biggest Boss is a student of the music and respects it greatly. He references his influences throughout his discogrophy.", "annotation_id": "1120966", "url": "https://genius.com/1120966", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "David or Goliath, hate me or admire", "vault_lines": ["David or Goliath, hate me or admire"], "meaning": "There are many opinions bout Rozay and they’re very different.\n\nThis is another Bible annotation about the story of where David (future kKing of Israel, not king at time if incident) knocked out and defeated Goliath who was a giant (abnormally tall).", "annotation_id": "672381", "url": "https://genius.com/672381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "When your phone off, there’s only one to call on", "vault_lines": ["When your phone off, there's only one to call on"], "meaning": "This is probably one of the best metaphors ever. No phone to call no one. Not ya mother, brother, sister etc. But you can always call on jesus . The almighty man upstairs.", "annotation_id": "672339", "url": "https://genius.com/672339", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "And now I sign artists", "vault_lines": ["This ain't how life goes (And now I sign artists"], "meaning": "A continuation to the story from above. How he always prayed for just a chance to get signed, but now not only did he get signed, he is the person that does the signing.\n\nThe Untouchable Maybach Music Empire.", "annotation_id": "541966", "url": "https://genius.com/541966", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Very first line, he called Trick Daddy stupid Say he got AIDS, tellin’ people that it’s lupus", "vault_lines": ["Very first line, he called Trick Daddy stupid", "Say he got AIDS, tellin' people that it's lupus"], "meaning": "A shot at Trick Daddy that is never fully defined, Trick was diagnosed with Lupus but Ross maybe implying that he had AIDS instead", "annotation_id": "389454", "url": "https://genius.com/389454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "That’s what The Bible says", "vault_lines": ["I'd give up everything (That's what The Bible says"], "meaning": "Matthew 5:5 is the fifth verse of the fifth chapter of the Gospel of Matthew in the New Testament: Blessed are the gentle,\nfor they shall inherit the earth.", "annotation_id": "298847", "url": "https://genius.com/298847", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "The world’s so cold, hope you got a lil’ sweater", "vault_lines": ["The world's so cold, hope you got a lil' sweater"], "meaning": "This is world play on the saying “the world’s a cold place” so Ross says you should put on your metaphorical sweater and battle through it.", "annotation_id": "282385", "url": "https://genius.com/282385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Will I get to heaven? Turn to Psalm 27", "vault_lines": ["Will I get to heaven? Turn to Psalm 27"], "meaning": "The LORD is my light and my salvation—\nwhom shall I fear?\nThe LORD is the stronghold of my life—\n   of whom shall I be afraid?\n\n2 When the wicked advance against me\nto devour[a] me,\nit is my enemies and my foes\nwho will stumble and fall.\n3 Though an army besiege me,\nmy heart will not fear;\nthough war break out against me,\n   even then I will be confident.\n\n4 One thing I ask from the LORD,\nthis only do I seek:\nthat I may dwell in the house of the LORD\nall the days of my life,\nto gaze on the beauty of the LORD\nand to seek him in his temple.\n5 For in the day of trouble\nhe will keep me safe in his dwelling;\nhe will hide me in the shelter of his sacred tent\n   and set me high upon a rock.\n\n6 Then my head will be exalted\nabove the enemies who surround me;\nat his sacred tent I will sacrifice with shouts of joy;\n   I will sing and make music to the LORD.\n\n7 Hear my voice when I call, LORD;\nbe merciful to me and answer me.\n8 My heart says of you, “Seek his face!”\nYour face, LORD, I will seek.\n9 Do not hide your face from me,\ndo not turn your servant away in anger;\nyou have been my helper.\nDo not reject me or forsake me,\nGod my Savior.\n10 Though my father and mother forsake me,\nthe LORD will receive me.\n11 Teach me your way, LORD;\nlead me in a straight path\nbecause of my oppressors.\n12 Do not turn me over to the desire of my foes,\nfor false witnesses rise up against me,\n   spouting malicious accusations.\n\n13 I remain confident of this:\nI will see the goodness of the LORD\nin the land of the living.\n14 Wait for the LORD;\nbe strong and take heart\n   and wait for the LORD.\n\nRoss has cited this as his favorite Bible chapter, in particular verses 1 and 2 (he even has verse 1 tattooed on him).", "annotation_id": "282383", "url": "https://genius.com/282383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "From that very day, I carried on the three C’s", "vault_lines": ["From that very day, I carried on the three C's"], "meaning": "Rozay is the founding member of the Miami-based crew The Carol City Cartel, along with Gunplay and Torch.", "annotation_id": "282361", "url": "https://genius.com/282361", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Young nigga, fifteen with three seeds", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga, fifteen with three seeds"], "meaning": "A seed is a euphemism for children.\n\nRoss is not speaking about himself – a few lines later he says he has 2 kids. Rather, he observed a 15 year old kid with 3 kids of his own, which inspired him to hustle even harder.\n\nHis thought process:\nIf a meer child has to take care of 3 kids, then what is stopping me from taking over music? Music is easy compared to that. Shit is real life. Ain’t no joke.", "annotation_id": "282358", "url": "https://genius.com/282358", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Valley of Death", "line": "Nigga never had a gun and badge", "vault_lines": [", nigga never had a gun and badge"], "meaning": "Even as a corrections officer, he did not not have a gun & badge.\n\n\n\nRoss is saying that even though he was a corrections officer, he was not out on the streets putting hard working hustlers away.", "annotation_id": "282294", "url": "https://genius.com/282294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
