{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Never golfin’ with the Trumps and I give you my word Back to comin’ out the trunk, chargin’ 20 a bird", "vault_lines": ["Back to comin' out the trunk, chargin' 20 a bird"], "meaning": "Continuing from the previous lines, Ross is saying that you’ll never catch him working with Donald Trump or any of his family members. He goes on to say that he’d go back to slanging drugs before he did that. Possibly suggesting that Kanye is really only supporting Trump to help his own money situation.", "annotation_id": "27435516", "url": "https://genius.com/27435516", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Testify on your right hand, put ’em in a Camel Clutch", "vault_lines": ["Testify on your right hand, put 'em in a Camel Clutch"], "meaning": "A camel clutch is a wrestling move that is very painful. If you testify, or snitch, Ross will catch you in  a choke like this.\n\nhttps://static.wikia.nocookie.net/prowrestling/images/d/d5/Tajiri_camel_clutch.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/666?cb=20160413074008", "annotation_id": "24054076", "url": "https://genius.com/24054076", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Hundred miles and runnin’, I pray it never run it’s course", "vault_lines": ["Hundred miles and runnin', I pray it never run it's course"], "meaning": "100 Miles and Runnin' is a highly successful album by NWA. This album came out when Ross was 14 years old and probably had a big impact on him.\n\nLike it did for NWA and many other rappers before him, Ross hopes that his career stays ‘100 miles and runnin’ forever.", "annotation_id": "24054069", "url": "https://genius.com/24054069", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Benny Medina, yeah, it’s J-Lo (Hola)", "vault_lines": ["Phone ringin', Benny Medina, yeah, it's J-Lo (Hola)"], "meaning": "Benny Medina is a record executive who is long time manager of Jennifer Lopez", "annotation_id": "24054029", "url": "https://genius.com/24054029", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Givenchy poster boy, Naomi tryna get up on me", "vault_lines": ["Givenchy poster boy, Naomi tryna get up on me"], "meaning": "Naomi Campbell is a runway model who has done multiple shows and been the face of campaigns for luxury designer Givenchy.\n\n\n\nRoss is a lover of designer clothes, especially since losing weight, and has worn and rapped about Givenchy plenty throughout the years.", "annotation_id": "24054003", "url": "https://genius.com/24054003", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Restaurants, I bought me fifty and they do they thing", "vault_lines": ["Restaurants, I bought me fifty and they do they thing"], "meaning": "Ross is a big time investor, and one of his most popular and well known investments is in the franchise Wing Stop, of which he reportedly owns “more than 25 locations.” He also owns a few Checkers franchises, and frequently raps about his love for both of the restaurants.", "annotation_id": "24053976", "url": "https://genius.com/24053976", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Dozen lawyers on the team, I’d rather keep ’em close Bill Cosby dead in prison, I could see the quotes Headlines when them white boys get to pay a fine Never rapin’ women, keep it on some player time", "vault_lines": ["Dozen lawyers on the team, I'd rather keep 'em close", "Bill Cosby dead in prison, I could see the quotes", "Headlines when them white boys get to pay a fine", "Never rapin' women, keep it on some player time"], "meaning": "In 2014, beloved comedian Bill Cosby was accused of sexual assault by a large number of women, with incidents going all the way back to the 1960’s. Although Cosby’s conviction was later overturned in 2021, Ross keeps his lawyers close because he doesn’t want to be the victim of something similar,  potentially decades after the allegations.\n\nThe second part of the line is most likely a reference to Brock Turner, who was a white student-athlete at Stanford University accused of rape in 2015. Although he was found guilty of 3 felony accounts of rape, he was only sentenced to 6 months in jail, and was released after only 3 months for good behavior. Ross is pointing out that because of his skin color Brock got off easy, and if it had been an African American the punishment would have been more severe.\n\n\n\nLastly, Ross clarifies that he doesn’t partake in these activities, because in 2013 he lost sponsors like Reebok for a controversial line about date rape. On Ross' verse from Rocko’s hit song, U.O.E.N.O,  he said:\n\nPut molly all in her champagne, she ain’t even know it\nI took her home and I enjoyed that, she ain’t even know it\n\nHe has since apologized many times for the wording  of the line and the misunderstanding it caused.\nhttps://twitter.com/RickRoss/status/319847608694738945?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E319847608694738945%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgenius.com%2FRocko-uoeno-lyrics", "annotation_id": "24053877", "url": "https://genius.com/24053877", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Went from battle raps to now we wearin’ M.A.G.A. hats", "vault_lines": ["Went from battle raps to now we wearin' M.A.G.A. hats"], "meaning": "This line goes in conjunction with the one before it about Kanye West.\n\nIn Kanye’s song featuring Rick Ross, Devil In A New Dress, Ross mentions rapping in cyphers with Kanye all the way back in 2002, before either of them had made it.\n\nHad cyphers with Yeezy before his mouth wired\n\nIn 2018, Kanye controversially wore a Make America Great Again (MAGA) hat on Saturday Night Live, in support of then President Donald Trump. Although the segment didn’t make the show, Kanye continued to be outspoken about his political beliefs and support for Trump.", "annotation_id": "24053798", "url": "https://genius.com/24053798", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
