{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "In Hawaii, Zion got me livin’, fuck the Coast", "vault_lines": ["In Hawaii, Zion got me livin', fuck the Coast"], "meaning": "The actual line is:\nIn Hawaii, Kanye got me livin’, fuck the coast\n\nThis refers to when Kanye flew Ross to Hawaii to work on his magnum opus, My Beautiful Dark Twisted Fantasy, to contribute to Monster and Devil in a New Dress – which many still consider to be Rick Ross’ best verse", "annotation_id": "17819079", "url": "https://genius.com/17819079", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "For my B-day, Dr. Dre gave me another watch", "vault_lines": ["For my B-day, Dr. Dre gave me another watch"], "meaning": "This is a reference to his 2012 birthday when hip-hop mogul Dr. Dre gifted Ross a $100,000 diamond-encrusted Hublot watch.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iq9e_uvmkHY", "annotation_id": "17812946", "url": "https://genius.com/17812946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "I’ma pull out the Vacheron", "vault_lines": ["I'ma pull out the Vacheron"], "meaning": "Vacheron Constantin is a luxury Swiss manufacture of prestige watches and a brand of the Richemont group. It employs around 1,100 people worldwide, most of whom are based in the manufacturing plants in Geneva and Vallée de Joux. It is an active member of the Federation of the Swiss Watch Industry\n\nhttps://s3.amazonaws.com/filepicker-images-rapgenius/f6XDaTuQqSuRPnj0nX7C_duckduckgo", "annotation_id": "17792744", "url": "https://genius.com/17792744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "I’ma pull out the Vacheron", "vault_lines": ["I'ma pull out the Vacheron"], "meaning": "Vacheron Constantin SA is a Swiss luxury watch and clock manufacturer founded in 1755. Since 1996, it has been a subsidiary of the Swiss Richemont Group. Vacheron Constantin is one of the oldest watch manufacturers in the world with an uninterrupted watchmaking history since its founding.", "annotation_id": "17788823", "url": "https://genius.com/17788823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Yo, watchin’ Kanye interview, feel like I wanna cry For every innocent brother charged with a homicide", "vault_lines": ["For every innocent brother charged with a homicide"], "meaning": "This is referring to the instantly controversial interview between TMZ and fellow rapper Kanye West. In the interview, West said that he felt like slavery was a choice, and that the slaves could have easily risen up and overtaken their owners. Needless to say, this did not sit well with the public, and many people voiced their strong disagreements with Kanye’s statements and their concern for his mental health, which has always been an issue.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1LIGh91mloA\n\nSlavery is a very touchy subject, and so is the active racism against young African-American men who are charged with crimes. Both involve discriminating against blacks, which Ross is calling for a change about. He feels that Kanye West’s comments about slavery show that we as Americans have barely progressed mindset-wise since the times of slavery.", "annotation_id": "17783209", "url": "https://genius.com/17783209", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Eatin’ with my dawgs, we just a different pedigree", "vault_lines": ["Eatin' with my dawgs, we just a different pedigree"], "meaning": "This is a double-entendre as Pedigree is both a renown brand of dog food and pedigree is the definition of those from a select class- generally one of higher class and status.", "annotation_id": "17782948", "url": "https://genius.com/17782948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Thurman Thomas, every step I take is footwork", "vault_lines": ["Thurman Thomas, every step I take is footwork"], "meaning": "Ross likens himself to former NFL Running back Thurman Thomas who played in the NFL from 1988 to 2000 for the Buffalo Bills and Miami Dolphins. Thomas ran for 12,074 yards, was named to the Pro Bowl 5x and was named NFL MVP in 1991. While Thomas made strides on the football field by running the ball Ross is taking steps outside of football to further build his empire.", "annotation_id": "17782902", "url": "https://genius.com/17782902", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "I’m the Kim Dotcom up in K.O.D", "vault_lines": ["I'm the Kim Dotcom up in K.O.D"], "meaning": "Kim Dotcom is a German and Finnish entrepreneur who is best known for being the founder of the now defunct MegaUpload.Com. Dotcom, born Kim Schmitz changed his last name to Dotcom in 2005. Dotcom is worth an estimated $200 million.\n\nRick Ross is worth an estimated $35 million and juxtaposes himself to Dotcom when he is present at popular Miami Gentlemen’s Club King of Diamonds which is frequently shortened to simply K.O.D.", "annotation_id": "17782853", "url": "https://genius.com/17782853", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Junior Seau, concussion, suicidal every season", "vault_lines": ["Junior Seau, concussion, suicidal every season"], "meaning": "Junior Seau is a former NFL Linebacker who played in the NFL from the 1990 season until the 2009 season for the San Diego Chargers, Miami Dolphins and New England Patriots. Seau was highly successful during his NFL career having and was named an NFL Pro Bowl selection 12x and was inducted into the Pro Football Hall of Fame in 2015.\n\nSeau committed suicide on May 2, 2012 via a gunshot to the chest. In January 2013, it was revealed that Seau’s brain had shown signs of CTE.", "annotation_id": "17782782", "url": "https://genius.com/17782782", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Vegas Residency", "line": "Black Bo, you know we miss you", "vault_lines": ["Black Bo, you know we miss you"], "meaning": "Nadrian Lateef “Black Bo” James was Rick Ross' longtime manager, who passed away in late 2017.\n\nHe is commemorated in an icy pendant on the cover of Port of Miami 2.", "annotation_id": "17778000", "url": "https://genius.com/17778000", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
