{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Veteran’s Day", "line": "Cash money is the Army, Veterans day", "vault_lines": ["Cash money is the Army, Veterans day"], "meaning": "Cash Money records takes a lot of inspiration from the Armed Forces, hence “Veterans Day”!\n\nIt’s a common comparison for him to make:\n\nCash Money is the Army, Navy Seal me in here\n\n(from “Fly In”)\n\nThe phrase originates from B.G.’s song of the same name.", "annotation_id": "53972", "url": "https://genius.com/53972", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
