{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "WE OFF THAT", "line": "Lock my CEO up, now it’s back to coka", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Waka is signed to Bricksquad Records, owned by chronic jail patron Gucci Mane. Back in 2008, Gucci was jailed for six months after violating probation. In the meantime, Flocka’s promotional machine and label support suffered. Instead of waiting for a lucky day, Waka took it back to the hood and returned to dealing, insuring a cash flow no matter what.", "annotation_id": "1498736", "url": "https://genius.com/1498736", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "WE OFF THAT", "line": "Pictures of Christopher on my wall all in my condo", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Diddy was responsible for the success (and possibly the exploitation) of Notorious B.I.G. As head of Bad Boy Records, Diddy organized the marketing scheme that eventually landed Biggie as one of the gods of rap and was often involved in the more shady sides of the business.\n\nPaying homage to his legendary friend and one-time source of revenue, Diddy still keeps pictures of Biggie on his walls in every house he owns.", "annotation_id": "1498724", "url": "https://genius.com/1498724", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "WE OFF THAT", "line": "Mad Decent will blow your head", "vault_lines": ["Mad Decent will blow your head"], "meaning": "Daniel Disaster (Heroes+Villains) is a member of Mad Decent, the record label started by Diplo and famous for electronic, trap, dubstep, and world music.", "annotation_id": "1498720", "url": "https://genius.com/1498720", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "WE OFF THAT", "line": "You either die a hero Or live long enough to watch yourself become the villain", "vault_lines": ["Or live long enough to watch yourself become the villain"], "meaning": "A direct sample from The Dark Night and a perfect phrase for producer Heroes+Villains!\n\nOnce a hero gathers power and changes all bad to good, he is the only one left to be considered “evil.” Thus, even the best become villains if they do not give up power, corrupting themselves absolutely.\n\nhttp://youtu.be/sWTBscL90q8?t=1m17s", "annotation_id": "1498712", "url": "https://genius.com/1498712", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
