{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Waist So Skinny", "line": "Fresh out the salon And I just got my hair done Niggas trynna holla at me But I told em’ move along Cause my waist so skinny", "vault_lines": ["Cause my waist so skinny"], "meaning": "Fresh can symbolise the feeling you get when you have a inflated self confidence from getting your hair done as she continues to say “out the Salon”. “Cuz my waist so skinny” can sybolise an inflated self confidence from the idealized female role of beauty. Cause my waist so skinny can also refer to how she has not eaten in a long time which can refer to the “started from the bottom” theme which is prominent in todays rap.", "annotation_id": "3105199", "url": "https://genius.com/3105199", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
