{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Watcha Gon’ Do?", "line": "Heckler Koch, M-1's and nine millis Stories like a motherfucker (That’s right)", "vault_lines": ["Heckler Koch, M-1's and nine millis", "Stories like a motherfucker (That's right)"], "meaning": "Besides the obvious gun references…\nhttps://hk-usa.com\n\n…this is when the verse starts to describe the scene in the club both Biggie and the “williest” are in…which could invoke the lyrics in Big Poppa– “mad question asking', blunt passin', music blastin'”", "annotation_id": "14913636", "url": "https://genius.com/14913636", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Watcha Gon’ Do?", "line": "Rolling blunts with the williest of the willy", "vault_lines": ["'Gator trunks, bitch (Bitch), rolling blunts with the williest of the willy"], "meaning": "The term “willy” was used to describe the “best of the best” as well as the most important or highest ranking faction of the day….Biggie is reinforcing his “I’m really living it” theme by ensuring you know he’s a part of that group.\n\nhttps://goo.gl/images/gE7Ws9", "annotation_id": "14913584", "url": "https://genius.com/14913584", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Watcha Gon’ Do?", "line": "Niggas talking it but ain’t living it Crystal pops, I’m sipping it, mob hats and lizard shit", "vault_lines": ["Niggas talking it but ain't living it", "Crystal pops, I'm sipping it, mob hats and lizard shit"], "meaning": "Biggie is comparing those that talk like they have money and live large, but actually don’t live that lifestyle day to day…unlike B.I.G, who sips expensive champagne whenever available,\n\nhttps://goo.gl/images/tHm4Fg\n\nand also has the money to flaunt expensive clothes and accessories, including a reference to “mob hats”, reinforcing his mafia-themed lyrics and style from that day.\n\nhttps://goo.gl/images/e7qGwu", "annotation_id": "14913559", "url": "https://genius.com/14913559", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Watcha Gon’ Do?", "line": "I tell ’em watch close, nigga, jot notes If you use my approach, you could dock boats", "vault_lines": ["If you use my approach, you could dock boats"], "meaning": "Puff invites others to observe how he does things and lives his life, brining up how he’s had enough financial success to own a SuperYacht, “Oasis”, which he purchased for $72 million from Eric Smidt, the chairman of Google.\n\nAccording to TheRichest.com, Puff has the second-highest net worth of any rapper ($820 million), following only Dr. Dre ($830 million).", "annotation_id": "12593299", "url": "https://genius.com/12593299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
