{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "[Interlude: Nas & Wiz Khalifa] Ayo Wiz, come meet me out in Vegas Them new releases coming out at 12 AM Look, we gotta stay fresh playboy, yeah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Ayo Wiz, come meet me out in Vegas", "Them new releases coming out at 12 AM", "Look, we gotta stay fresh playboy, yeah, yeah"], "meaning": "12 AM Run is Nas sneaker store in Las Vegas that oppened up in April 2014.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=40G9-xVPWH8", "annotation_id": "4048387", "url": "https://genius.com/4048387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "[Produced by Sledgren, Ricky P, and RMB Justize]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Wiz turned this into a real remix by changing the beat. The original boisterous, trap-heavy beat driven by the matching, thunderous drums is slowed down. Making it more relaxed and mellow.", "annotation_id": "3389409", "url": "https://genius.com/3389409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "The warden just caught his case, he was looking forward to vote", "vault_lines": ["The warden just caught his case, he was looking forward to vote"], "meaning": "If you are a convicted felon, you cannot vote. The warden caught his first case, which means he ran into trouble with the law. He apparently committed a felony, because he can no longer vote.\n\nTies to the previous and the next line  about democracy you should count yor blessing for being able to vote.", "annotation_id": "3388812", "url": "https://genius.com/3388812", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Bitch, we dem boyz, nigga, we the Beatles", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, we dem boyz, nigga, we the Beatles"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is comparing himself and his crew to the Beatles, an English rock band formed in 1960. The Beatles had a large following and were very popular among young and old people alike, and have left a lasting legacy on music that will most likely be here forever. Rick Ross is saying that he and his crew (whether that be MMG or Q, Nas, and Wiz) are as influential and legendary as the Beatles.", "annotation_id": "3388803", "url": "https://genius.com/3388803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Keys to my estate,", "vault_lines": ["Keys to my estate,"], "meaning": "Here Wiz just throws in that instead of an average house, he has an estate.", "annotation_id": "3388549", "url": "https://genius.com/3388549", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Put the cheese inside a safe", "vault_lines": ["put the cheese inside a safe"], "meaning": "He refers to money as “cheese”, and he locks it up in a safe, most likely found in the house mentioned before.", "annotation_id": "3388519", "url": "https://genius.com/3388519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "And just recent, nigga, my teeth is nickel, got disco-ball glow, uh", "vault_lines": ["And just recent, nigga, my teeth is nickel, got disco-ball glow, uh"], "meaning": "Q just got a new grill, and it shines like a disco ball, A$AP Ferg shows his off here:", "annotation_id": "3388495", "url": "https://genius.com/3388495", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "They hate to see you flourish, so I draw the curtains", "vault_lines": ["They hate to see you flourish, so I draw the curtains"], "meaning": "People from Rozay’s side of town hate seeing him succeed, so Ricky closes the curtains on them so they can’t see him or his money. Also, Rick Ross & Nas both featured on a hit track called “Maybach Curtains” so this could be a reference to that song.\n\nThis could also mean that when the haters see Ross drive by in his Maybach, he closes the curtain so they don’t know it’s his, hiding the fact that he is the successful person driving the expensive car.", "annotation_id": "3388064", "url": "https://genius.com/3388064", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "On that poor side of town, grinding to pay our bills", "vault_lines": ["On that poor side of town, grinding to pay our bills"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is from Miami Gardens, Florida. The area is notorious for crime and poverty. Over 20% of residents are below the poverty line. Rick Ross was supposedly used  be a part of that statistic.", "annotation_id": "3388056", "url": "https://genius.com/3388056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Paranoid as a child, blessed to be a dreamer", "vault_lines": ["Paranoid as a child, blessed to be a dreamer"], "meaning": "I saw momma praying as she wait on results\nIt was hot in the kitchen can I wait on the porch\n\nRick Ross has explained to us the struggles of his childhood several times. One can even go as far as saying his mother had finical problems because of his appetite. That could have made him paranoid, as he would not know where his next meal would come from. Maybe it was also because of his mother’s health problems and violence he saw during his childhood.\n\nRoss takes a page from other artist like J. Cole and the iconic Kanye West and examines his inner dreamer. As a child, you may coop with your lack of psychical belongs with your imagination.", "annotation_id": "3387727", "url": "https://genius.com/3387727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "I never give a rat a pass, it’s the fattest ass that attracts me", "vault_lines": ["I never give a rat a pass, it's the fattest ass that attracts me"], "meaning": "Double Entendre…\n\n\n\n\nA “rat” is a snitch. A taboo that Nas won´t tolerate. As well as we know Nas to be an ass magnet…\nHe never passes on hood rats cause those fat asses attracts him.", "annotation_id": "3387713", "url": "https://genius.com/3387713", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "How do I define Nasty? Ghastly, explain Esco Plain and simple, with a redbone in the Benzo sippin’ XO", "vault_lines": ["How do I define Nasty? Ghastly, explain Esco", "Plain and simple, with a redbone in the Benzo sippin' XO"], "meaning": "For the youngsters who are just getting introduced to Nas through this banger he´ll explain who he is.\n\n\n\nStarting off with two reference to his alias: Nasty Nas and Nas Escobar. Nasty is the horrifying rap especially early on before Illmatic with his shock rhymes. While Escobar is more materialistic driving expensive cars and sipping fancy drinks.", "annotation_id": "3387660", "url": "https://genius.com/3387660", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "1-8-7, no appeal, get it how you live", "vault_lines": ["1-8-7, no appeal, get it how you live"], "meaning": "187 is slang for murder, taken from Section 187 of the California Penal Code.\n\nIt’s referenced in many rap songs, and was notably the original title of a Tyga x Rick Ross joint before being dubbed as “Dope” instead.", "annotation_id": "3387652", "url": "https://genius.com/3387652", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "From Figueroa to the airport to them Iceland hoes Head to London then to Paris, double sold-out shows Then I fell asleep in my Saint-Laurent and woke up to stunt more", "vault_lines": ["Head to London then to Paris, double sold-out shows", "Then I fell asleep in my Saint-Laurent and woke up to stunt more"], "meaning": "Q is touring all over the world now that he’s made it.\n\n\n\nHe went from the street life to the living lavish. Figueroa Street is the poor and violent street he grew up on and became a gangsta. Now his career allows him to explore the more amazing sights; sporting designer clothes like Saint-Laurent in Paris.\n\n\n\n5th & 6th of May, 2014, he made two performances in Paris at Le Bataclan concert hall. That was during (european) Oxymoron Tour. Same situation in London.", "annotation_id": "3387602", "url": "https://genius.com/3387602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Hold up, hol’ up, hol’ up, this game we play, you can’t control us Hol’ up, hol’ up, they knew us ’cause the way we pulled up", "vault_lines": ["Hold up, hol' up, hol' up, this game we play, you can't control us", "Hol' up, hol' up, they knew us 'cause the way we pulled up"], "meaning": "The Game – having sex, doing drugs, lookin' fresh, and getting money; and Q lives by the\nPMW (Pussy, Money, Weed) motto:\n\nBorn stunna nigga, turn night to bright\nHigh as a kite in my Nike Flights\nMade 30 Racks it was just a flight\nFlew a bitch out too, it was just a night\nShorty got the booty make a nigga say, “Whoa”\n\n\n\nAs well as the street life.\n\n\n\nAlso, reference to how a game controller allows the player to control a video game.", "annotation_id": "3387585", "url": "https://genius.com/3387585", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "First-round draft pick, hittas stay in the field", "vault_lines": ["First-round draft pick, hittas stay in the field"], "meaning": "When players are coming from college, sports organizations have a “draft” where the teams draft college players onto their teams. As there are multiple rounds, a first round draft pick would mean the player that is very important. Thus, Rozay  is a very important person.\n\n\n\n\n\n“Hittas stay in the field:”\n\n\nFootball players are meant to hit each other during games.\nIn slang terms: “Killers stay on the streets.”", "annotation_id": "3387575", "url": "https://genius.com/3387575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "From the Don to God’s Son, the Project Prophet, the live one", "vault_lines": ["From the Don to God's Son, the Project Prophet, the live one"], "meaning": "Nas has gone through many phaces. From The Don in his mafioso rap on It Was Written to being God´s Son. As well as the project prophet he was on Nastradamus. This transformation he has attributed to being confused as a youngster and set out to get the answers – as he later did.\n\nReference to his song “The Don” and his nickname and album Gods Son.", "annotation_id": "3387574", "url": "https://genius.com/3387574", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "The father of Destiny, Knight’s pops, Will’s man", "vault_lines": ["The father of Destiny, Knight's pops, Will's man"], "meaning": "Here Nas refers to some people who are very important in his life:\n\n\nDestiny – Destiny, (pictured below), is Nas' first born child. She is the love of his life and he even made a song about her called “Daughters”.\nKnight – Knight is Nas' son who is in the custody of his ex-wife, Kelis.\nWill – This refers to Ill Will, one of Nas' homies when he was growing up in Queensbridge. Unfortunately, Ill Will was murdered when they were just teenagers, leading Nas to name his legendary debut album Illmatic after him.", "annotation_id": "3387573", "url": "https://genius.com/3387573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "I’m 20 in, still outside, don’t ask for it", "vault_lines": ["I'm 20 in, still outside, don't ask for it"], "meaning": "20th Year Anniversary Of Illmatic\n\n\n\nBut even 20 years in the game he is still an outsider and has proclaimed himself the most mainstream underground artist. Note the contrast off in and outside.", "annotation_id": "3387567", "url": "https://genius.com/3387567", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Mass Appeal, HSTRY, Henny sippers, let’s get it nigga", "vault_lines": ["Mass Appeal, HSTRY, Henny sippers, let's get it nigga"], "meaning": "Getting That Money!\n\n\n\nThese are all Nas busniess ventures: Owning Mass Appeal, collaborating with HSTRY clothing line and partnership with Hennessy and has been working with their “Wild Rabbit” campaign.\n\nAs well as they represent what Nas is. Has the mass appeal, the history in the game and has been sipping Hennessy for years.", "annotation_id": "3387539", "url": "https://genius.com/3387539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Take another selfie, watch my lawyer beat the case", "vault_lines": ["Take another selfie, watch my lawyer beat the case"], "meaning": "While Wiz was in prison he made a joke of the legal system by tweeting out selfies of himself from his cell. He did this because he knew that he had the best lawyers money can buy and that they’ll make sure he’s free long before he suffers any consequences.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/wizkhalifa/statuses/470541572094705665", "annotation_id": "3387526", "url": "https://genius.com/3387526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Democracy be the dope, community in the choke", "vault_lines": ["Democracy be the dope, community in the choke"], "meaning": "Rick Ross could be referring to the way that the appearance of democracy can be used to keep a community appeased and docile, when in fact in the United States the Electoral College pretty much determines presidencies. Also, the US similarly ‘deals’ out democracy to the middle east, well-seeming political intentions often disguising imperialism and business interests.", "annotation_id": "3387520", "url": "https://genius.com/3387520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Fresh up out a cell to the seats of private planes", "vault_lines": ["Fresh up out a cell to the seats of private planes"], "meaning": "This refers to when Wiz Khalifa was arrested for possession of Marijuana. After he was arrested, all he had to do was post bail and he was released from his cell – free to board a private jet and resume the tour he was doing at the time.", "annotation_id": "3387512", "url": "https://genius.com/3387512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Hold up, hol’ up, Wiz on joints, my woods be rolled up", "vault_lines": ["Hold up, hol' up, Wiz on joints, my woods be rolled up"], "meaning": "Everybody knows that Wiz Khalifa ain’t fucking with blunts, and only smokes papers. He hates blunts, and he never smokes them, even though he did that in the past. It’s reversed for Q because he only smokes his weed rolled in Backwood blunts with his special technique.\n\nNow not only that he is smoking papers, but he also signed a deal with RAW Rolling Papers company for a new line of smoking accessories.", "annotation_id": "3387510", "url": "https://genius.com/3387510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Niggas throwin’ shots but I’mma dodge ’em all, you can’t touch this Don’t believe if my name involved in some punk shit, uh, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Niggas throwin' shots but I'mma dodge 'em all, you can't touch this", "Don't believe if my name involved in some punk shit, uh, yeah"], "meaning": "Being the gangsta Q is, he’s used to handling guns every now and then. He may have to duck literal bullets or criticism, but no matter what he keeps his distance from the bullshit.\n\nNiggas banged on me, but they should’ve shot me\nSee, I hit the corner then spot him, got him\n\n\n\nFun Fact: At the time the track was released Q left a performance with Nas and was later targeted by shooters, in which he was unharmed.", "annotation_id": "3387499", "url": "https://genius.com/3387499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "Jungle’s brother, girl, I house you like the Jungle Brothers Understand", "vault_lines": ["Jungle's brother, girl, I house you like the Jungle Brothers"], "meaning": "Jungle is Nas' little brother and the Jungle Brothers were an important hip-hop group early its development. Note the homophone.\n\nThe Jungle Brothers' first big single was named I’ll House You, so Nas is going to give this girl a place to stay just like in the song.", "annotation_id": "3387497", "url": "https://genius.com/3387497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "I shine before ya’ll time I been outside when T La Rock invented rhymes", "vault_lines": [", I shine before ya'll time", "I been outside when T La Rock invented rhymes"], "meaning": "T La Rock is known for being one of the first ever rappers and has been active in the rap industry since the 1970s.\n\nHe alone probably didn’t ‘invent’ hip-hop, but he was huge in its foundation, he even released the very first Def Jam record way back in 1984 (titled: It’s Yours), when Nas was 11.\n\nNas probably used to play outside while bumping that track on a boombox! Either way this is proof that Nas was shining long before any of these new rappers were even born", "annotation_id": "3387484", "url": "https://genius.com/3387484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Dem Boyz (Remix)", "line": "That half moon is that Nas cut", "vault_lines": ["That parched up from here on, that half moon is that Nas cut"], "meaning": "Here Nas acknowledges his famous half-moon haircut – over the years he’s adopted having a half moon shape carved into his hair every time he goes to the barber.", "annotation_id": "3387475", "url": "https://genius.com/3387475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
