{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "Cryin’ in the dark, nigga, we gon’ make it Countin’ cash 6 days, nigga, we gon’ make it", "vault_lines": ["Cryin' in the dark, nigga, we gon' make it", "Countin' cash 6 days, nigga, we gon' make it"], "meaning": "Paints a vivid picture of Ross' life then versus now. He used to cry in the dark and now he counts cash for 6 days straight.\n\nBOSS!", "annotation_id": "7843193", "url": "https://genius.com/7843193", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "And a lot of people talk you’ve never seen talk When your man testify, that’s a coin toss", "vault_lines": ["And a lot of people talk you've never seen talk", "When your man testify, that's a coin toss"], "meaning": "Coins have two sides, heads or tails, and you have a 50% chance of getting either outcome. In this case Rick Ross compares how much people lie in court to get out of trouble.", "annotation_id": "7745341", "url": "https://genius.com/7745341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "Never trust niggas, hit ’em with a moonwalk Billie Jean, Billie Jean, oh Billie Jean", "vault_lines": ["Never trust niggas, hit 'em with a moonwalk", "Billie Jean, Billie Jean, oh Billie Jean"], "meaning": "In a theme repeated many times across the game including Rick Ross' archenemy, Rick Ross echoes this again but uses a more reverent approach to it giving obeisance to one of the musical greats Micheal Jackson and his famous dancing style the moonwalk.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I0MQF2u6SLA\n\nThe direction of a moonwalk is reverse which shows that when you are meet a “nigga you don’t trust” you simply “hit em with a moonwalk” or go the other way.", "annotation_id": "7740002", "url": "https://genius.com/7740002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "I seen a lot of niggas fall, still standin’ tall", "vault_lines": ["I seen a lot of niggas fall, still standin' tall"], "meaning": "Rick Ross may be addressing the fact that in America and in the world a black man is always subjected to bad situations  which even culminate in death, however he is blessed to still be alive and standing tall.", "annotation_id": "7739932", "url": "https://genius.com/7739932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "Still holdin’ on my pistol, nigga we gon’ make it", "vault_lines": ["Still holdin' on my pistol, nigga we gon' make it"], "meaning": "In a world Rick Ross has always painted in his music as a drug infested playground with a bloody fight for power, Rick Ross keeps his gun for protection, despite his enormous wealth.", "annotation_id": "7739929", "url": "https://genius.com/7739929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "No power in December, nigga we gon’ make it Stove open, I remember, nigga we gon’ make it These the words mama whispered, we gon’ make it", "vault_lines": ["No power in December, nigga we gon' make it", "Stove open, I remember, nigga we gon' make it", "These the words mama whispered, we gon' make it"], "meaning": "Rozay throws in a little anecdote, talking about his life and how he was brought up in Mississippi, while keeping his message of hope.", "annotation_id": "7739532", "url": "https://genius.com/7739532", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "Demonstrators jumping on police cars, setting some on fire, the city in rubbles, rubber bullet shooting chaos. Looters robbing stores in broad daylight They sayin’ we animals and we actin’ like we ready to go ’head If you don’t bring him to justice, if you don’t bring him to town square, you’re gonna see all these people in your motherfuckin’ neighborhood", "vault_lines": ["They sayin' we animals and we actin' like we ready to go 'head"], "meaning": "The song ends the same way it started, with a spoken outro. The first part is a news broadcast, and the second parts are interviews of people at the time of the protests.\n\nThe outro backs up Rozay’s suggestions of racism in society.\n\nEven though Ross gives this hopeful message throughout the song, saying that there will be an end to the racism, it could be suggesting that there might not be an end, unless justice is served.", "annotation_id": "7739447", "url": "https://genius.com/7739447", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "He called his mom, guess he figured she would post his bond Times have changed and she really runnin’ low on funds Hung up the phone, in the cell still in his Foams Reekin’ of the weed, that’s all his money blown", "vault_lines": ["Times have changed and she really runnin' low on funds", "Hung up the phone, in the cell still in his Foams", "Reekin' of the weed, that's all his money blown"], "meaning": "He is now in jail, asking his mom for bail who is financially unstable for whatever reason, which is a common theme in hip hop at the moment.", "annotation_id": "7739411", "url": "https://genius.com/7739411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "Lil homies livin’ like it’s no tomorrow Caught a charge smokin’ large in a stolen car", "vault_lines": ["Caught a charge smokin' large in a stolen car"], "meaning": "Through the song, Ross tells a story of someone who gets in trouble and is always caught up with bad things, not caring what he does. But as the song suggests, there is a hopeful ending and he is “gon' make it”.\n\nHe starts his story here, telling how he got into trouble – by stealing a car and smoking in it.", "annotation_id": "7739394", "url": "https://genius.com/7739394", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "They say we just a bunch of thugs, don’t stand for nothin’ Disgrace to our race, don’t belong in public It was us against the world from the first day Let us bow our heads, may we all pray Throwin’ bricks at the man, we gon’ make it Genocide not in the plans, we gon’ make it Pray my son understands, we gon’ make it Know God holdin’ our hands, we gon’ make it", "vault_lines": ["They say we just a bunch of thugs, don't stand for nothin'", "Disgrace to our race, don't belong in public", "It was us against the world from the first day"], "meaning": "Rozay is talking about the Baltimore riots throughout the song, there is dark imagery of the riots. He talks about the racism that occurred and still occurs now.\n\nThere is a hopeful message in the song, though. “We gon' make it”, illustrates this idea of hope and that the institutional racism that is prevalent will soon end.", "annotation_id": "7739363", "url": "https://genius.com/7739363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "line": "Breaking news from Baltimore, a city on edge since the death of a suspect while in police custody, his spine nearly severed. Tonight those tensions fueling violent protests now. Dramatic images coming in at this hour. You can see some people there on the streets throwing rocks and bricks at police officers", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The song, about the Baltimore riots earlier this year, has an introduction from a real television broadcast from the riots.\n\nIt paints the dark picture for the rest of the song, despite the hopeful title and message.", "annotation_id": "7739348", "url": "https://genius.com/7739348", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Gon Make It", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-we-gon-make-it-lyrics", "genius_title": "We Gon Make It", "genius_id": 2296340, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Shinin’", "line": "I done fucked every dime up in diamonds", "vault_lines": ["I done fucked every dime up in diamonds"], "meaning": "In excessive Miami fashion, Ross smashed each dancer at King of Diamonds, formerly known as Diamonds. Whereas the common man drools over these women, a boss like Rozay has a whole lot of dancers. A common joke in Miami but not so much a stretch.", "annotation_id": "3968629", "url": "https://genius.com/3968629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Shinin’", "line": "I got ten keys on my wrist so have you the D.E.A. tell ’em that", "vault_lines": ["I got ten keys on my wrist so have you the D.E.A. tell 'em that"], "meaning": "Wordplay with Key:\n\nRick Ross got rich through selling keys of cocaine in the drug game, and he used that money to buy expensive jewelry (or keys). So, he is dissing the DEA because they were never able to catch him.", "annotation_id": "2869253", "url": "https://genius.com/2869253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Shinin’", "line": "Maybach Music, nigga I am the CEO and we are sucker free, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I am the CEO and we are sucker free, nigga"], "meaning": "At this point, Ross had just formed the Maybach Music Group imprint, but the only artists signed were the Triple C’s (himself, Gunplay, and Torch).", "annotation_id": "1407057", "url": "https://genius.com/1407057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Shinin’", "line": "Kanye and these hoes tellin’ me nothin’", "vault_lines": ["Kanye and these hoes tellin' me nothin'"], "meaning": "A reference to his homie Kanye West’s single off of his 2007 album, “Can’t Tell Me Nothing”.", "annotation_id": "816180", "url": "https://genius.com/816180", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
