{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "I love brain, I need a leech", "vault_lines": ["I love brain, I need a leech"], "meaning": "I love brain refers to oral sex, leeches are known for sucking blood out of people. Tunechi is saying he needs some to slurp up the meat.", "annotation_id": "30976638", "url": "https://genius.com/30976638", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "And I like my Sprite Easter pink", "vault_lines": ["And I like my Sprite Easter pink"], "meaning": "He’s saying he likes his Sprite with cough syrup in it, otherwise known as “lean”, and the cough syrup gives it a purple or pinkish hue or looking “Easter pink”.", "annotation_id": "29716723", "url": "https://genius.com/29716723", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Touch and I will bust your medulla", "vault_lines": ["Touch and I will bust your medulla"], "meaning": "This could be a light play on words referencing the Busta Rhymes song ‘Touch It’.\n\nThe case for this is strengthened by Wayne again referencing ‘Touch It' on his freestyle/remix of this very song of Da Drought 3", "annotation_id": "26073949", "url": "https://genius.com/26073949", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "That’s a bullethole, it is not a tumor", "vault_lines": ["That's a bullethole, it is not a tumor"], "meaning": "This is a reference to a line from Arnold Schwarzenegger in Kindergarten Cop (1990) when he snaps at a kid who suggested his headache could be a tumor, yelling “It’s not a tumah!” However, Lil Wayne is saying his victim’s head is hurting from a gunshot, not a tumor.", "annotation_id": "24666230", "url": "https://genius.com/24666230", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Been a G in the game, now my son on the throne", "vault_lines": ["Been a G in the game, now my son on the throne"], "meaning": "Birdman was already a well established MC (rapper and record executive) in the rap game for over a decade at the time We Takin’ Over was released\n\nIt all started in 1991 when Birdman and his brother  “Slim” cofounded Cash Money Records now acclaimed  one of the most successful labels in hip-hop history. Cash Money has fostered many of todays gamut of rappers as well as the artist of this track DJ Khaled himself.\n\nBirdman discovered and signed then protégé Lil Wayne at the tender age of 12 making Wayne the youngest member signed to Cash Money Records. Birdman took Wayne under the wing and they formed a tight parental like bond due to the absence of Wayne’s biological father and recent passing of Wayne’s step-father who he was close too and saw as his father figure. Wayne and Birdman  call each other father and son and even so far to duo on a track called Like Father Like Son.\n\n\n\nLike a King Baby passes the throne to his heir not only is this a nod to Wayne opening the next verse but also recognition cause that same year this track We Takin’ Over dropped in 07 Wayne became President of Cash Money Records and CEO of Young Money.", "annotation_id": "24082542", "url": "https://genius.com/24082542", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Cash rule everything around me", "vault_lines": ["Cash rule everything around me"], "meaning": "C.R.E.A.M.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PBwAxmrE194", "annotation_id": "20191598", "url": "https://genius.com/20191598", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Get shot up like Shyne, that’s on my neck I’m big like Diddy; damn it, I’m with it", "vault_lines": ["Get shot up like Shyne, that's on my neck", "I'm big like Diddy; damn it, I'm with it"], "meaning": "This is a reference to when Shyne and Diddy were allegedly involved in a club shooting.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-h__rlTXhyI", "annotation_id": "19177379", "url": "https://genius.com/19177379", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Twelve years down and I’m finally free", "vault_lines": ["Twelve years down and I'm finally free"], "meaning": "At the time the song came out, Joey had finally gotten his release from Atlantic Records, making him free to do his thing independently.  (the first product of said freedom was 2006’s Me, Myself & I which spawned the megahit Make It Rain (Remix).", "annotation_id": "7927794", "url": "https://genius.com/7927794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Jacksonville, Tallahassee, Memphis, Tenn; holla at me", "vault_lines": ["Jacksonville, Tallahassee, Memphis, Tenn; holla at me"], "meaning": "Jacksonville & Tallahasse are cities located in Flordia while Memphis is a city located in Tennessee.\n\nSince T.I. is from the dirty south, you would expect him calling out states and cities from the south.\n\n\n\nHe also makes a reference to DJ Khaled’s debut single “Holla at Me”.", "annotation_id": "3165977", "url": "https://genius.com/3165977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "I’m the man out in Dallas, better ask Khaled", "vault_lines": ["I'm the man out in Dallas, better ask Khaled"], "meaning": "Being the President of Def Jam South, Khaled is the one who would be in charge of Dallas in the corporate marketing hierarchy", "annotation_id": "17838", "url": "https://genius.com/17838", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Started in Atlanta then I spread out with it South Carolina, Alabama, Mississippi On to North Carolina, Philadelphia and Virginia From down in Miami where it warm in the winter", "vault_lines": ["On to North Carolina, Philadelphia and Virginia", "From down in Miami where it warm in the winter"], "meaning": "This song is something of an anthem for Southern rappers, and Atlanta-based T.I. is one of the biggest of the “Southern Trap style”.\n\nThe whole song is an anthem about Southern rappers like T.I., Miami-based Rick Ross, and New Orleans-born Lil Wayne taking over the rap game. Hence, the listing of southern states.\n\n\n\nNotice that Philadelphia is not a state, nor is it even a part of a southern state.", "annotation_id": "10390", "url": "https://genius.com/10390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Might get shot on the porch of your fortress", "vault_lines": ["Might get shot on the porch of your fortress"], "meaning": "Could be a reference to Gianni Versace being shot on the porch of his Miami mansion (“fortress”) by crazed killer Andrew Cunanan in 1997. Or could be a general threat. But again, RICK ROSS WAS A CORRECTIONAL OFFICER so don’t be too scared in Miami", "annotation_id": "10059", "url": "https://genius.com/10059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Be in H-Town, Southside, Cloverland, daddy", "vault_lines": ["Be in H-Town, Southside, Cloverland, daddy"], "meaning": "“H-Town” is Houston, and Southside is the southern half of the city, where Houston’s rap scene is centered. Cloverland is a neighborhood on the Southside, home to many rappers like Lil' Flip", "annotation_id": "10030", "url": "https://genius.com/10030", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Feelin’ like Pac, all eyes on me", "vault_lines": ["Feelin' like Pac, all eyes on me"], "meaning": "All Eyez On Me was 2Pac’s best album and last one released while he was (officially) alive. A bit arrogant from Joe, but ties in nicely with Rick Ross’s Biggie reference from the previous verse", "annotation_id": "6830", "url": "https://genius.com/6830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "I’m YSL, Versace", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "YSL (Yves St. Laurent) and Versace are expensive fashion designers, so this follows from the previous line where he was bragging about his money", "annotation_id": "6827", "url": "https://genius.com/6827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "I am the little big kahuna, y’dig?", "vault_lines": ["I am the little big kahuna, y'dig?"], "meaning": "A kahuna is a Hawaiian priest, sorcerer, magician, wizard, minister, or expert in any profession.  Wayne has also called himself “Young Tune, the big kahuna” on “The Mobb”\n\nThis is a shout-out to Birdman (the big kahuna) / play on Wayne’s name", "annotation_id": "6822", "url": "https://genius.com/6822", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "I stay on track like a box of Pumas", "vault_lines": ["I stay on track like a box of Pumas"], "meaning": "Puma shoes have become associated with running thanks to their partnership with Usain Bolt.\n\nIt’s also a clever simile: Pumas are a popular running shoe so therefore literally staying on track, similar to Wayne, either staying on the track (song) or how he has his life in order, contrary to the rumors. And it stays in the same rhyme scheme of the previous two lines.", "annotation_id": "6821", "url": "https://genius.com/6821", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "We Takin’ Over", "line": "Ah, I am the beast Feed me rappers or feed me beats", "vault_lines": ["Ah, I am the beast", "Feed me rappers or feed me beats"], "meaning": "He’s not asking for beets, he’s got an all-consuming need to be given beats to make music on.  This song came out at the height of Wayne’s prolific output on mixtapes, so this line perfectly reflected Wayne’s seemingly devouring appetite for making music.\n\nAlso, Wayne is the self-proclaimed “Best Rapper Alive” – beast could allude to best.", "annotation_id": "6816", "url": "https://genius.com/6816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
