{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Put to sleep by the pillowcase killer", "vault_lines": ["Put to sleep by the pillowcase killer"], "meaning": "In line with the previous line he’s calling out the “pussy niggas” in reference to Christopher Hubbart who was a notorious rapist named the “Pillowcase Rapist” that would put a pillow case over his victims heads to silence their screams.\nSo this could mean that Rozay a pillows over his victims face before he puts them to sleep to silence their screams.", "annotation_id": "3421828", "url": "https://genius.com/3421828", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "I’m an artist and my niggas are the realest", "vault_lines": ["I'm an artist and my niggas are the realest"], "meaning": "Double Entendre:\n\n\nRoss alludes to himself as a hip-hop artist and claims his crew’s realness is unparalleled.\nRealism was a form of art popularized by Gustave Courbet in the late 1800’s that attempted to represent familiar and everyday people and situations in an accurate, unidealized manner. Rozay is claiming he is an artist, and his crew are the Realists.", "annotation_id": "2983856", "url": "https://genius.com/2983856", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Full magazine, bitch, shoot for the stars", "vault_lines": ["Full magazine, bitch, shoot for the stars"], "meaning": "A magazine, in this case, is where bullets are held within a gun. His magazine is full and he tells his bitch to shoot for the stars in the sky.\n\nThis also could mean that since the bitch is with Rozay she’s clearly got everything she needs, in a metaphorical sense, “a full magazine,” and since she does have this advantage she should “shoot for the stars” or set high goals for herself.\n\n\n\nThis could back-fire on Rozay though, ask Drake:\n\nI don’t think I’m conscious of making\nMonsters outta the women I sponsor ‘til it all goes bad", "annotation_id": "2918679", "url": "https://genius.com/2918679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Bordeaux Polo, smoke a ton of weed", "vault_lines": ["Bordeaux Polo, smoke a ton of weed"], "meaning": "Bordeaux is a region of France that produces wine, so Rozay is referring to the color of his Polo shirt as a wine color. And he smokes a ton of weed.", "annotation_id": "2918665", "url": "https://genius.com/2918665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Pullin’ niggas’ cards, givin’ shooters bonuses", "vault_lines": ["Pullin' niggas' cards, givin' shooters bonuses"], "meaning": "Ross used a similar line on “Bugatti”\n\nI got shooters out the D league, signing bonus\nHit that man from 30 feet", "annotation_id": "2909790", "url": "https://genius.com/2909790", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "We the Knights of the Templar", "vault_lines": ["We the Knights of the Templar"], "meaning": "The Knights Templar was a secret society active from 1119-1312. Although they are officially defunct, some modern people claim to be members.\n\nRoss is comparing the nobility and royalty of his MMG crew to the nobility and royalty of the Knights Templar faction.", "annotation_id": "2877453", "url": "https://genius.com/2877453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Snatch a nigga chain just to post it on the blog", "vault_lines": ["Snatch a nigga chain just to post it on the blog"], "meaning": "This was a trend in the middle to late 2000’s where gang members or celebrities would steal rappers chains and pendants and post them up on blogs to rank on em. Most popular one was Yung Berg’s Transformer chain being stolen, twice even…", "annotation_id": "2872957", "url": "https://genius.com/2872957", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Stackin’ money to the sky, gettin’ rich, haaaan Stackin’ bricks to the sky, this is it, haaaan", "vault_lines": ["Stackin' money to the sky, gettin' rich, haaaan", "Stackin' bricks to the sky, this is it, haaaan"], "meaning": "French is stacking his money to the ceiling. He most likely got all this money from pushing coke (as evident in the next line). Along with the money, he is stacking bricks, or kilos of drugs sky high.\n\n\n\nFrench is also recreating Camp Lo’s infamous “Luchini” listen to the hook. “This is it – what?! / Luchini fallin' from the sky, let’s get rich- what?!”. Montana uses the same melody to pay homage to a hip-hop classic.", "annotation_id": "2860410", "url": "https://genius.com/2860410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "[Produced by Reefa]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "During an interview with XXL Magazine Reefa explained how the track came about:\n\n\nI’m just in the era from the 90s, the early 2000s, the whole New York era, the feel good music. Me and Ross had a relationship before. And we still have a relationship. I was in the studio with French. I played French the joint, he laid a hook to it, and he ended up sending it to Ross. Ross was like, we going to keep it for the album. Before that I did the “Ice Cold” beat on God Forgives, I Don’t. It’s almost like the same kind of drum patterns or same kind of sound I’m trying to really push out with my whole ATM Company.\n\nI just caught a vibe, I played the melody, and I have a producer on my team his name is stats, he laid all the color around it and we just went from there. I had the drums going for a while but I just wanted it to knock the right way. People ain’t really hitting their head. It ain’t that mood no more.; that whole 90s kind of mood. So I kind of wanted to bring a little bit of that back with a current sound. When I’m messing with Ross or whoever, I try to give them something that everybody else wouldn’t do. I tip my hat off to Ross and French, they know what they’re doing. It wasn’t pressure or whatever, it was a real collaboration. A real song put together from start to finish\n\nMe and Ross, we’re in a great space. I knew it was crazy from just the beat. When I heard the hook, the hook took it to a crazy other level. I knew it was one of those types of joints when I first did it, that it was gong to be crazy and something that special.", "annotation_id": "2859506", "url": "https://genius.com/2859506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "No room for nonsense, you under new ownership", "vault_lines": ["No room for nonsense, you under new ownership"], "meaning": "Ross displayed his no nonsense style of management when he took over TMZ, (renaming it MMZ), changed the name of TMZ head man Harvey to Hervis and changed the cameraman’s name to Clevis, all in a mastermind effort to promote Self Made 3.\n\nYou think you clever, so it’s Clevis.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WXc4pcWrg6E", "annotation_id": "2857675", "url": "https://genius.com/2857675", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "[Chorus: French Montana]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The hook is another nod to the 90s, this time in the form of the Bronx, NY based duo Camp Lo’s break out single “Luchini (This Is It)” which cadence is borrowed from\n\n\n\nFrench Montana performs another hook on this album, on Nobody, which is itself another salute to the 90s (it’s basically a remake of The Notorious B.I.G.’s You’re Nobody (Til Somebody Kills You)).", "annotation_id": "2855989", "url": "https://genius.com/2855989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Shame on a nigga who tried to run game on a nigga", "vault_lines": ["Shame on a nigga who tried to run game on a nigga"], "meaning": "A reference to ‘’Shame On A Nigga‘’ by Wu-Tang Clan.", "annotation_id": "2851074", "url": "https://genius.com/2851074", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Face, gut, buck 50, got two pistols", "vault_lines": ["Face, gut, buck 50, got two pistols"], "meaning": "Buck 50 refers to cutting somebody with a knife or a box cutter, typically in the face, but Ross is taking it one step further and doing it in someone’s stomach.\n\nContinuing with the Wu-Tang references in this song, this line is a reference to Ghostface’s song Buck 50.", "annotation_id": "2850377", "url": "https://genius.com/2850377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "What a Shame", "line": "Def Jam see me as a threat now", "vault_lines": ["Def Jam see me as a threat now"], "meaning": "The higher-ups at record label Def Jam are now becoming worried that mogul Rick Ross may leave and essentially pull a “Jay Z” and start his own recording empire from scratch! Keep ballin' Rozay!", "annotation_id": "2840568", "url": "https://genius.com/2840568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
