{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Whatever", "line": "My grandma seen me buy my first Polo sweater", "vault_lines": ["My grandma seen me buy my first Polo sweater"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nIt also means his grandma seen him when he got his hands dirty trapping chicken..\nRemember My Collection when he said “I used to sell dope at my grandma house as a rude child”", "annotation_id": "12367288", "url": "https://genius.com/12367288", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Whatever", "line": "I, got my hand flooded, I, bought the whole projects", "vault_lines": ["I, got my hand flooded, I, bought the whole projects"], "meaning": "His hand is flooded, meaning he has diamonds on it. A lot of them. Diamonds = ice = water = flooded.\n\nSince he could afford all these diamonds, he could definitely buy all of the projects, so he says he did.", "annotation_id": "13050099", "url": "https://genius.com/13050099", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Whatever", "line": "Work, no acrobatics Work, no calisthenics", "vault_lines": ["You gon' need a ladder (Ladder), work, no acrobatics"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is using ‘work’ here in reference to drugs, commonly with crack/cocaine.\n\n2 Chainz was arrested for felony cocaine possession when he was 15.", "annotation_id": "12210955", "url": "https://genius.com/12210955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Whatever", "line": "Smoking like Calvin Broadus, blueberry with the big homie", "vault_lines": ["Smoking like Calvin Broadus, blueberry with the big homie"], "meaning": "Calvin Broadus Jr is Snoop Dogg’s government name. Ross shouts him out here, mentioning that they smoke together.\n\nThe two have collaborated before on “Quintessential” and recently, Ross spoke out in support of Snoop over the latter’s music video and comments mocking Donald Trump.", "annotation_id": "12208427", "url": "https://genius.com/12208427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
