{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "When You Feel This", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Stafford-brothers-when-you-feel-this-lyrics", "genius_title": "When You Feel This", "genius_id": 2172808, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "line": "I’mma big boss and I never took a loss, see I need that I might of took a loss but it wasn’t like that (Ross)", "vault_lines": ["I'mma big boss and I never took a loss, see I need that", "I might of took a loss but it wasn't like that (Ross)"], "meaning": "As a boss, Ross does not lose the money, work, or to the competition. However, there are moments in the boss life where a loss needs to be took.\n\nTake for example when he lost an endorsement deal with Reebok, or when he lost weight by getting more sleep.", "annotation_id": "3048478", "url": "https://genius.com/3048478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "line": "Shoot through Macon, see what’s shakin’, my shit white as miss Vanna", "vault_lines": ["Shoot through Macon, see what’s shakin', my shit white as miss Vanna"], "meaning": "Macon is a city on the way to Atlanta when traveling from Savannah.\n\nHis cocaine is as white as actress Vanna White", "annotation_id": "1119625", "url": "https://genius.com/1119625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "line": "Triple beam on the dresser", "vault_lines": ["Triple beam on the dresser"], "meaning": "A scale for calculating the weight of drugs.", "annotation_id": "1119619", "url": "https://genius.com/1119619", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "line": "You gotta cross the tracks", "vault_lines": ["You gotta cross the tracks"], "meaning": "The phrase “on the other side of the tracks” means crossing over from a place of high moral and social standing to one where crimes are oft committed & ruffians roam. Ross beleives that you can find him on both sides – as seen in his love of luxury cars & passion for rapping about drug dealing.\n\n\n\nCombined, they create:", "annotation_id": "1119603", "url": "https://genius.com/1119603", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "line": "Homicide for the cash ride around gunnin’ mass Summer time Son of Sam", "vault_lines": ["Homicide for the cash ride around gunnin' mass", "Summer time Son of Sam"], "meaning": "The Son of Sam, aka Dave Berkowitz committed 6 murders during the summer of 1977 in NYC.\n\n\n\nIt is ironic that Ross would suggest that he commits “homicide for the cash” & then reference a serial killer who killed because he claimed that he was commanded to kill by a demon that possessed his neighbor’s dog.\n#Rozay!", "annotation_id": "1119587", "url": "https://genius.com/1119587", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "line": "Slap Bush with my cash, all these taxes and his gas", "vault_lines": ["Slap Bush with my cash, all these taxes and his gas"], "meaning": "President Bush (supposedly) went to war with Iraq to secure oil pipelines for US interests. Ross wants to slap Bush with his cash because George Bush has his priorites messed up. Fighting forgein wars when black people suffer. Rappers agree, George Bush does not care about black people.", "annotation_id": "921577", "url": "https://genius.com/921577", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "line": "I’mma get mine you can call me uncle Sam", "vault_lines": ["I'mma get mine you can call me uncle Sam"], "meaning": "Uncle Sam (initials U.S.) is a common national personification of the American government. The government will always get its money, this is a reference to the earlier line about the IRS", "annotation_id": "921574", "url": "https://genius.com/921574", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-where-my-money-i-need-that-lyrics", "genius_title": "Where My Money (I Need That)", "genius_id": 40240, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "line": "The double M nigga", "vault_lines": ["The double M nigga"], "meaning": "‘Double M’ is a slang of MMG, which is the acronym of Maybach Music Group – a record label imprint owned by Rick Ross.", "annotation_id": "21100717", "url": "https://genius.com/21100717", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "line": "Niggas desire to fit in, I was invited", "vault_lines": ["Niggas desire to fit in, I was invited"], "meaning": "Ross makes it clear, that where most men and women would love to fit in, he gets invited to those same places.", "annotation_id": "21080844", "url": "https://genius.com/21080844", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "line": "Big dough when you thought of my block", "vault_lines": ["Big dough when you thought of my block"], "meaning": "Benny’s block did $20K a day when he was in the streets", "annotation_id": "21080834", "url": "https://genius.com/21080834", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "line": "When you a dope boy, this the life that your bitch inherit", "vault_lines": ["When you a dope boy, this the life that your bitch inherit"], "meaning": "Separating family and the drugs is extremely difficult, which often leads to family ending up carrying the burden of your actions in the streets. In this case, it’s the woman he’s involved with.\n\n“India” (feat. El Camino) also by Benny, is a prime example of this line being expanded in a song and giving stories of how women end up “inheriting” this life.", "annotation_id": "21080812", "url": "https://genius.com/21080812", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "line": "It’s on my wrist and as well as my hip, it’s cold metal", "vault_lines": ["It's on my wrist and as well as my hip, it's cold metal"], "meaning": "The jewelry on Benny’s wrist and and the weapon on his waist are both products of cold metal.", "annotation_id": "21080798", "url": "https://genius.com/21080798", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "line": "I buy her expensive shit and she forget to wear it", "vault_lines": ["I buy her expensive shit and she forget to wear it"], "meaning": "[My girl] India has grown and expanded with me. We started a hair company, we sell luxury wigs and luxury hair products. When I said that, I was talking about her because sometimes she’s chasing these new levels with me. She might have a $4,000 purse she might not be accustomed to wearing. She probably don’t want to wear that type of sh-t to go back home and make people feel uncomfortable. This is not her saying this, this is me. But sometimes she don’t wear shit because she could be forgetting we’re becoming different people and it’s okay that we’re successful.", "annotation_id": "21077048", "url": "https://genius.com/21077048", "state": "verified", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "line": "Hospital stays, laid up, related to asthma", "vault_lines": ["Hospital stays, laid up, related to asthma"], "meaning": "I been in and out of the hospital all year. Two, three times a year in the emergency room because of my asthma. That’s what I’ve been dealing with for 25 years. I never spoke about that [before], but I just spoke about that because that was on my mind. That’s something that I dealt with all my life and it’s been a struggle.\n\nI got to control my breathing, I got to be careful, I got to make sure I wear my mask, I got to make sure I’m taking my medicine. Running the streets and being in and out of prison, it’s probably something I haven’t done the best of. But being older, that’s something that I take care of. Asthmatics, they know how this shit is.", "annotation_id": "21077042", "url": "https://genius.com/21077042", "state": "verified", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Would I Go", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Benny-the-butcher-where-would-i-go-lyrics", "genius_title": "Where Would I Go", "genius_id": 6055666, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Gas rolling up in the blunt, Amoco", "vault_lines": ["Gas rolling up in the blunt, Amoco"], "meaning": "The Amoco Corporation, originally Standard Oil, was a global chain of gas and petrol stations that merged with BP in 1998. But the gas Future refers to is weed, which we know Nayvadius likes to smoke.", "annotation_id": "8639617", "url": "https://genius.com/8639617", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Put a pic with me on the gram now you popping", "vault_lines": ["Put a pic with me on the gram now you popping"], "meaning": "As Future’s songs rule the airwaves and his popularity rises, a simple picture with him on Instagram could boost your whole career. But such a favor isn’t intended for fake friends. This concept is even a skit on Future’s 56 Nights mixtape. A ‘fan’ wanting a picture with Future’s DJ, Esco, eventually gets punished by some mafia-like characters for flexing.\n\nDrake said something similar on the “Sh!t (Remix)”:\n\nAnd if a nigga say my name, he the hot shit\nBut if I say the nigga name, he still the hot shit", "annotation_id": "8639614", "url": "https://genius.com/8639614", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Where your ass at? We keep that fully loaded contracts", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass at? We keep that fully loaded contracts"], "meaning": "Contracts refer to two things in this case. Firstly, it is seen as weak in hip hop to lease, or rent vehicles rather than buying them outright. Future and his crew buy everything they own.\n\n\n\nSecondly, these fully loaded contracts are contract killers, or shooters. Future has real shooters on his team, so when these fake friends come around after he’s blown up looking for a hand out, he has individuals willing to take them out for him.", "annotation_id": "8639611", "url": "https://genius.com/8639611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?"], "meaning": "Hi-Tech pharmaceuticals produces cough syrup with Promethazine and Codeine similar to Actavis. Like so many other “lean sippers” Future prefers Actavis over Hi-Tech. Actavis was pulled from stores for a bit, but Hi-Tech was still distributing the syrup. Hi-Tech’s also the cheaper brand—you’re only drinking it if you can’t afford or can’t access the good stuff—it’s tough times.", "annotation_id": "8639607", "url": "https://genius.com/8639607", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Fuck where you was at, I had the 6 on my shoulders", "vault_lines": ["Fuck where you was at, I had the 6 on my shoulders"], "meaning": "Drake has discovered or given a crucial co-sign to many Toronto artists in the last few years. To name a notable few: The Weeknd, PARTYNEXTDOOR, and Majid Jordan.\n\nThe area code of Toronto is 416, the “6”. Drake told The Fader, “Toronto is the reason I do this.”\n\nHis tattoo of the 6 isn’t quite on his shoulder, but it’s close.", "annotation_id": "8445495", "url": "https://genius.com/8445495", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Now your ass around because we’re paying back dues Where were you? When all the dogs needed help", "vault_lines": ["Now your ass around because we’re paying back dues", "Where were you? When all the dogs needed help"], "meaning": "People keep showing up out of nowhere to be part of Drake’s squad now that he is famous. They want to benefit from being friends with him without having been there when times were hard.\n\n\n\nDrake is known for treating his friends and family very well, paying for everything from lawyers to houses, so it’s worth a shot.\n\nI got people talkin’ down, man, like I give a fuck\nI bought this one a purse, I bought this one a truck\nI bought this one a house, I bought this one a mall\nI keep buyin’ shit, just make sure you keep track of it all", "annotation_id": "8445480", "url": "https://genius.com/8445480", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?"], "meaning": "There were some who knew what was up as soon as Drake started dropping mixtapes like Room For Improvement and Comeback Season, but whoever Drake’s talking to wasn’t one of them. Maybe he learned when Lil Wayne joined the cause, but maybe not even then.", "annotation_id": "8445479", "url": "https://genius.com/8445479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Where your ass was at when all they’d ask was what’s the hold up?", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at when all they'd ask was what's the hold up?"], "meaning": "You won’t feel me til you want it so bad you tell yourself you’re in it\nAnd tell the world around you that your paperwork is finished\nAnd steal your mother’s debit cards so you maintain an image\n\nEveryone wants to be part of the crew now that Drake’s famous; where were they during the Ride?", "annotation_id": "8445478", "url": "https://genius.com/8445478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Man, where your ass was at when we took the city over?", "vault_lines": ["Man, where your ass was at when we took the city over?"], "meaning": "Drake asks his ‘friends’ where they were when he was starting from the bottom and grinding in Toronto. It took years for Drake to rise up and become the 6 God, but the people around now didn’t want to put the work in.", "annotation_id": "8445477", "url": "https://genius.com/8445477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Jackie Chan moves got game in the choke", "vault_lines": ["Jackie Chan moves got game in the choke"], "meaning": "The moves that Future makes to keep the rap game on lockdown and in the palms of his hands are similar to the lethal moves of legendary Chinese martial artist and actor Jackie Chan.\n\n\n\nI wonder who has a better karate chop…", "annotation_id": "8445470", "url": "https://genius.com/8445470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the stove? Had to struggle to get where I’m at and sell dope", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the stove?", "Had to struggle to get where I'm at and sell dope"], "meaning": "Future had to cook crack cocaine and sell dope to get to where he is. He’s not the only rapper to take this path, giving their career a kick-start with their drug money.\n\nIt continues a trend in modern music where an artist calls out “new” friends, who weren’t around when they were involved in the struggle, but all of a sudden come up with their hands out.", "annotation_id": "8445469", "url": "https://genius.com/8445469", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Running through the pussy like a nigga going jogging", "vault_lines": ["Running through the pussy like a nigga going jogging"], "meaning": "Men burn an average of 100 calories during sex, but running was found to burn twice as many calories per minute. Either way, Future’s getting his exercise in.", "annotation_id": "8445463", "url": "https://genius.com/8445463", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Had to rent that on the dick ass jocking", "vault_lines": ["Had to rent that on the dick ass jocking"], "meaning": "Future has a fine female in his bedroom and is currently showing her what Rich $ex feels like.\n\nShe is squirming around in pleasure with movements similar to those of a dancer trying to bring about rain.\n\nIt’s safe to assume that Future’s skills in bed probably granted her wish.", "annotation_id": "8445460", "url": "https://genius.com/8445460", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Where your ass was at dog, when niggas wouldn’t feed me? Where your ass was at dog, when bitches didn’t need me? Where your ass was at dog, when niggas tried to run off? Where your ass was at dog? You made me pull this gun out", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at dog, when niggas wouldn’t feed me?", "Where your ass was at dog, when bitches didn’t need me?", "Where your ass was at dog, when niggas tried to run off?"], "meaning": "This song has the no new friends theme running through it. Future is addressing all of these new people around him, asking them where were they when he needed them the most, when he wasn’t as famous as he is now, when he didn’t have enough money to support himself and used to pick gang fights where bodies would come sliding. Instead of being there for him, his so called friends switched sides and ran off.\n\nFuture doesn’t need such fakes in his life—he’s down with his true friends.", "annotation_id": "8445446", "url": "https://genius.com/8445446", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Kid dynamite, this why they call me the bomb", "vault_lines": ["Kid dynamite, this why they call me the bomb"], "meaning": "Kid Dynamite refers to Mike Tyson. The reason for Mike Tyson having the nickname was because of his explosive life in and out of the ring. Controversies followed him everywhere with outbursts being the order of the day. With a rap sheet this long, Kid Dynamite as a name suits the man. More on this here.\n\nRick Ross could be drawing a likely perpendicular between him and Mike and from his past this could be right.\n\nBeats by Rick Ross\nBeats by Mike\n\nAlso the two have charming flair. This could be why Rick Ross speaks of him being called the bomb.", "annotation_id": "8319803", "url": "https://genius.com/8319803", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "In the mall I make her smile like Arsenio Hall Front or back I fuck her raw while accepting my calls", "vault_lines": ["In the mall I make her smile like Arsenio Hall", "Front or back I fuck her raw while accepting my calls"], "meaning": "Arsenio Hall is a renowned comedian and current talk show host for his own show Arsenio Hall Show\nOne of his most notable traits is his banana smile which Rick Ross here refers to when he takes his girl to the mall to buy stuff like this\n\n\n\nWhen it comes back to the house after this field trip to the mall Ross get a free pass to go in her without any condom and can even pick business calls while sexing. The business calls maybe could be on this", "annotation_id": "8319759", "url": "https://genius.com/8319759", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Where Ya At (Remix)", "line": "Early morning on the balcony in my Versace briefs, nigga Ocean splashes against the stones", "vault_lines": ["Ocean splashes against the stones"], "meaning": "This intro picks up from the “30 for 30 freestyle” in which Ross requests for the preparation of the beach house after being freed from house arrest.", "annotation_id": "8319734", "url": "https://genius.com/8319734", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
