{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "White Girl (Remix)", "line": "And two grand flat get ya four and a baby", "vault_lines": ["And two grand flat get ya four and a baby"], "meaning": "For $2,000 you can have 4 ½ oz of coke!\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: This is also recycled from Jeezy’s last line in the first verse of “Trap Star”, which gives props to him for the collaboration.", "annotation_id": "91744", "url": "https://genius.com/91744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "White Girl (Remix)", "line": "I got that off white, call it Nelly Furtado", "vault_lines": ["I got that off white, call it Nelly Furtado"], "meaning": "Off-white drugs, possibly heroin, nick-named Nelly furtado because it is above average and off-white, like Nelly who is Portuguese and Canadian.", "annotation_id": "91345", "url": "https://genius.com/91345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
