{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wild One", "line": "Pat Riley of rap, all my niggas got rings", "vault_lines": ["Pat Riley of rap, all my niggas got rings"], "meaning": "The President of the NBA’s Miami Heat, Pat Riley is no stranger to winning rings (championships). Riley’s won as an NBA player (1972 with the Los Angeles Lakers), as an NBA Assistant Coach (1980 with the Lakers), as an NBA Head Coach (1982, 1985, 1987 and 1988 with the Lakers and 2006 with the Heat) and as the President of the Heat in 2006, 2012 and 2013. In 2006, Riley served as both Head Coach and President of the Heat when he took over mid-season for Coach Stan Van Gundy who resigned.\n\nRick Ross is saying his team, MMG wins at a high rate just as Pat Riley does. Ross is a Miami Heat fan and even has the team’s logo tattooed on his face!", "annotation_id": "12610320", "url": "https://genius.com/12610320", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
