{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wing Stop (Remix)", "line": "Years ago Pimpin’ Curly we know we ethered him", "vault_lines": ["Years ago Pimpin’ Curly we know we ethered him"], "meaning": "Pimpin' Curly is the made-up character that 50 Cent played in his short comedy series of the same name\n\n\n\n\n\n“Ether” is the name of Nas’s diss track towards Jay-Z in which majority of people declared that Nas had won the beef after it. Rick Ro$$ claims to have ended 50 Cent just as badly with his diss tracks 6 years prior when he started beefing with 50 Cent.\n\nRick Ro$$ had also previously made this claim 6 years ago in his song “Jumping Out The Window”\n\nFuck 50 Cent, I ether that boy\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cmtc5YDrFbw&t=15s", "annotation_id": "31326012", "url": "https://genius.com/31326012", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wing Stop (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Philthy-rich-wing-stop-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Wing Stop (Remix)", "genius_id": 2256036, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wit It", "line": "How that boy a sinner with a closet full of Christians Red underneath and my receipt look like a scripture", "vault_lines": ["How that boy a sinner with a closet full of Christians", "Red underneath and my receipt look like a scripture"], "meaning": "A play on the name of French footwear designer Christian Louboutin – who pioneered that staple of Rozay’s wardrobe, red bottoms.\n\n\n\n“Red underneath” refers to the red-lacquered soles; and to the red letter edition of the Bible, which Rozay’s receipt very much resembles after paying for the aforementioned footwear. (Again, a play on the name “Christian”.)", "annotation_id": "2932278", "url": "https://genius.com/2932278", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
