{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "World’s Finest", "line": "Put a bullet in a bully, nigga, good night", "vault_lines": ["Put a bullet in a bully, nigga, good night"], "meaning": "Rozay doesn’t like bullies. Don’t be a bully. He will kill you or pay for a hit on you.. after all, he is wealthy.\nhttps://instagram.com/p/7bloQRhvOP/?taken-by=richforever", "annotation_id": "7843229", "url": "https://genius.com/7843229", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "World’s Finest", "line": "Count a half a milli, do the Diddy bop", "vault_lines": ["Count a half a milli, do the Diddy bop"], "meaning": "The Diddy bop is a dance move made by Diddy when he was still known as Puff Daddy and has been seen as a dance move used by many, including Chris Brown, Bobby Shmurda and NFL players using it for their touchdown celebration. It has also been the inspiration for many other popular dance moves such as the “Nae Nae”, the “Stanky Leg” and the “Dougie”.", "annotation_id": "7751967", "url": "https://genius.com/7751967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "World’s Finest", "line": "Niggas goin’ through pain I ain’t show up to school ‘cause I was goin’ through things Now I’m gettin’ this money, feel like I’m goin’ through change", "vault_lines": ["Niggas goin' through pain", "I ain't show up to school 'cause I was goin' through things", "Now I'm gettin' this money, feel like I'm goin' through change"], "meaning": "Continuing on from before, Meek talks more about his life growing up and the pain he went through to get to where he is now.", "annotation_id": "7745410", "url": "https://genius.com/7745410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "World’s Finest", "line": "You ain’t come where I come from, niggas on xannys Mommy on crack, how we gon’ feed the family? Might as well start sellin’ it, everybody inhalin’ it", "vault_lines": ["You ain't come where I come from, niggas on xannys", "Mommy on crack, how we gon' feed the family?", "Might as well start sellin' it, everybody inhalin' it"], "meaning": "Meek Mill is talking about him growing up in Philly and the hard lifestyle he came out of. His mom was addicted to crack, not providing the best example, but he and his family needed to eat so they started selling it to help.", "annotation_id": "7745333", "url": "https://genius.com/7745333", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "World’s Finest", "line": "Yeah baby, show you all the finer things Cuban links and diamond rings You know you’ve got designer dreams (Get it, get money) Everything’s expensive, nothing’s too good Champagne with the movie stars Black Maybach in my garage Rolexes and Audemars Everything’s expensive, nothing’s too good", "vault_lines": ["Yeah baby, show you all the finer things", "Cuban links and diamond rings", "You know you've got designer dreams", "Everything's expensive, nothing's too good", "Champagne with the movie stars", "Black Maybach in my garage"], "meaning": "Black Dollar is all about how successful Rick Ross has become and him indulging in his affluence, this song is no different.\n\nThe hook is extending this, showing he has a rich lifestyle, talking about the expensive things he owns.", "annotation_id": "7745318", "url": "https://genius.com/7745318", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "World’s Finest", "line": "Fuck niggas, fuck bitches, they all phony When I was broke, they wasn’t ’round and they all on me", "vault_lines": ["Fuck niggas, fuck bitches, they all phony", "When I was broke, they wasn't 'round and they all on me"], "meaning": "Meek is aware of gold diggers and other individuals that try to profit of his new found success; of course he is not down with such people. It seems like he hasn’t changed at all:\n\nFuck bitches, get money, get money and fuck bitches\nYou know that I’m a G, I’m a G\nGet money, get money and fuck bitches\nYou know it’s MOB", "annotation_id": "7742093", "url": "https://genius.com/7742093", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "World’s Finest", "line": "My cigar lit up like I’m Suge Knight", "vault_lines": ["My cigar lit up like I'm Suge Knight"], "meaning": "Suge Knight, is the former CEO of Deathrow Records and is often spotted smoking a cuban cigar. Ross can identify with Suge’s cigar obsession since he’s also making music for cigars.", "annotation_id": "7741794", "url": "https://genius.com/7741794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
