{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wuzzup", "line": "Finally made it to the majors, stealin’ bases of course", "vault_lines": ["Finally made it to the majors, stealin' bases of course"], "meaning": "Ross made it to the top of the dope game by robbing drug dealers of high quality freebase cocaine. This line is a brilliant metaphor comparing baseball and the dope game.", "annotation_id": "4924394", "url": "https://genius.com/4924394", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wuzzup", "line": "48 Laws flawed, my dawgs above the law", "vault_lines": ["48 Laws flawed, my dawgs above the law"], "meaning": "Ross references The 48 Laws Of Power by Robert Greene (who is dissed in the following line), a book that is highly popular with prison inmates and celebrities.", "annotation_id": "4924388", "url": "https://genius.com/4924388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wuzzup", "line": "Couple dollars on my neck, DGK on my sweats", "vault_lines": ["Couple dollars on my neck, DGK on my sweats"], "meaning": "DGK (which stands for Dirty Ghetto Kids) is a skateboard clothing brand started by pro skater Stevie Williams.\n\nRoss has often worn DGK clothing in several Instagram posts, and may hold some sort of stock in the company.", "annotation_id": "4912100", "url": "https://genius.com/4912100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wuzzup", "line": "Teddy Bridgewater run the trap just like a faucet", "vault_lines": ["Teddy Bridgewater run the trap just like a faucet"], "meaning": "Rozay shouts out the Minnesota Vikings franchise QB, Teddy Bridgewater. Like Ross, Teddy is a Miami native. Bridgewater was a 2014 first round pick, and was the most impressive rookie QB of 2014.\n\nRoss plays on the “water” part of Teddy’s last name by saying he “runs the trap just like a faucet”.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/rickyrozay/status/464615758803533825\nhttps://twitter.com/teddyb_h2o/status/563436420283781123", "annotation_id": "4502453", "url": "https://genius.com/4502453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wuzzup", "line": "Duck-tape Robert Greene, make him read the Qu’ran", "vault_lines": ["Duck-tape Robert Greene, make him read the Qu'ran"], "meaning": "Robert Greene is a well-acclaimed author of five bestsellers, one of which found its way onto Kendrick Lamar’s Section 80 album artwork, another that inspired 50 Cent to meet with Greene, and another that was subsequently written by both Greene and 50 Cent, called “The 50th Law”:\n\n\n\nThe book is based off his previous writings, particularly “The 48 Laws of Power.” Both Greene and 50 Cent agree that the philosophy/psychology found in Greene’s books and discussed technically by society’s intellects is and has been applied intuitively by urban gangs and drug dealers.\n\nGiven Ross' beef with 50 Cent, here he is suggesting that he’s going duck tape Greene and make him read the Qu'ran, another instance of Ross' love for the Abrahamic religions.\n\nWith this line he implies that all of the wisdom and philosophy found in street culture that Greene/50 seek to put in academic terms can be found in religious scriptures and proverbs popular in the ghetto.", "annotation_id": "4432221", "url": "https://genius.com/4432221", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wuzzup", "line": "Cartier frames, Belaire on my breath", "vault_lines": ["Cartier frames, Belaire on my breath"], "meaning": "It is very rare that you will see Ross without a pair of sick shades on, today he’s repping Cartier, which has a line of luxury glasses.\n\n\n\nThe black bottle boy is known to drink Luc Belaire, the sparkling rosé from France.", "annotation_id": "4428761", "url": "https://genius.com/4428761", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Wuzzup", "line": "Photoshoot fresh, four cubans layin’ on my chest", "vault_lines": ["Photoshoot fresh, four cubans layin' on my chest"], "meaning": "The boss is looking fly, just finishing up a photoshoot in which he had four Cuban link chains around his neck and on his chest.", "annotation_id": "4428736", "url": "https://genius.com/4428736", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
