{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "YRB", "line": "Kilo after kilo, blow my winnings out in Reno (Boss)", "vault_lines": ["Kilo after kilo, blow my winnings out in Reno (Boss)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross is interpolating his own lyrics from “Fuck Em,” the opening track on his classic Rich Forever mixtape:\n\n“C-note after C-note, put the remix on my kilo.”\n\nThe song was another Rick Ross/2 Chainz collaboration.\n\nhttps://genius.com/Rick-ross-fuck-em-lyrics", "annotation_id": "22792999", "url": "https://genius.com/22792999", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "YRB", "line": "Can’t walk a day in these shoes, these don’t come in your size", "vault_lines": ["Can't walk a day in these shoes, these don't come in your size"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is saying that no one else can do what he’s done. In other words, no one will be able to continue his legacy. This might also play into the fact that 2 Chainz is very tall, and probably has a large shoe size.", "annotation_id": "21764037", "url": "https://genius.com/21764037", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
