{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "I’m the greedy genius, no reference to the ugly clothes (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I'm the greedy genius, no reference to the ugly clothes (Woo)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross likens himself to being a greedy genius along with not being a fan of the company Greedy Genius. Greedy Genius is a footwear and apparel company that produces merchandise which is bright and colorful.", "annotation_id": "20544867", "url": "https://genius.com/20544867", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "I’m cruisin’ in the gulf, I think you’re so deaf Janet was in control because the ho left", "vault_lines": ["I'm cruisin' in the gulf, I think you're so deaf", "Janet was in control because the ho left"], "meaning": "This is a play on words.\n\nJanet Jackson was in a relationship with So So Def founder Jermaine Dupri at one point.\n\nAlso, Janet Jackson released an album called Control back in 1986.", "annotation_id": "11282110", "url": "https://genius.com/11282110", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "He not bigger than Biggie (Boss), bitch, I’m bigger than you", "vault_lines": ["He not bigger than Biggie (Boss), bitch, I'm bigger than you"], "meaning": "A little double entendre action from The Boss. Haters claim that Ross is not bigger than Biggie in terms of weight or fame. Ross' response to this is well I’m definitely bigger than you in all facets of life.\n\nRozay is 6'0 and weighed around 300-350 lbs when this song came out. Although now it looks like he is trying to slim down for summertime & his health’s sake.\n\n\n\nBig Poppa was 6'2 395 lbs at the time of his death", "annotation_id": "2938390", "url": "https://genius.com/2938390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "Maybach Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group is a record label imprint founded by Rick Ross in 2009.\n\nMagazeen is a reggae artist that signed to MMG in 2010.\n\n\n\nThe Maybach Music voice over is commonly used by the artists under the label.", "annotation_id": "2922404", "url": "https://genius.com/2922404", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "She no speaky no Engly, maybe Fat Joe could teach her (Ha)", "vault_lines": ["She no speaky no Engly, maybe Fat Joe could teach her (Ha)"], "meaning": "The girl is from Puerto Rico, like Fat Joe, a fellow rapper.\nSpeakay No Englay, (Speak No English) in a Spanish way, the language people speak in Puerto Rico.", "annotation_id": "2869419", "url": "https://genius.com/2869419", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "My talk is priceless, baby", "vault_lines": ["All the girls dem welcome (My talk is priceless, baby"], "meaning": "When a price is put on something that is priceless, like the Rothko painting White Center (1950), people will pay any amount. In this case $81,100,000.\n\n\n\nFortunately for you all you have to do is shell out anywhere from $7.99 for a copy of Deeper Than Rap to $26.99 for the deluxe t-shirt edition of God Forgives, I Don’t", "annotation_id": "1362480", "url": "https://genius.com/1362480", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "I still hustle for dope, but no more me scuffin’ my soles", "vault_lines": ["I still hustle for dope, but no more me scuffin' my soles"], "meaning": "Instead of blow, Ross hustles music. Making excellent albums and expanding his Maybach & Wingstop Empires constitute his new grind.\n\n\n\n17th Century Chinese nobles grew out their fingernails to show that they did not have to perform manual labor for their livelihood. For Ross, his crisp shoes lack the abrasions that come with a difficult life.", "annotation_id": "1306343", "url": "https://genius.com/1306343", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yacht Club", "line": "Kill all the middlemen, I’m the militant Gilligan", "vault_lines": ["Kill all the middlemen, I'm the militant Gilligan"], "meaning": "This is possibly my favorite line by Rick Ross, mostly due to its superb assonance but also to its gleefully menacing absurdity. Ross is frustrated by “middlemen” taking up an unnecessary position in his line of business and making money off of something he could do himself, so in keeping with the nautical theme of the song he compares himself to this guy\n\n\n\n due to his island theme and resolves to kill them all, whether figuratively (by eliminating their purpose) or literally.", "annotation_id": "217031", "url": "https://genius.com/217031", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
