{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "For dinero, ocho cinco, catch me a body nigga", "vault_lines": ["For dinero, ocho cinco, catch me a body nigga"], "meaning": "Chad Ochocinco is willing to kill Rozay’s enemies for money, or Ross could have 85 assassins at his beck and call. Although, the real Spanish form of “85” is “ochenta y cinco.”\n\nFurthermore, Ross and Ochocinco are very good friends.\nSee", "annotation_id": "538710", "url": "https://genius.com/538710", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "Dead presidents all on my body, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Dead presidents all on my body, nigga"], "meaning": "Generally when rappers talk about dead presidents they’re referring to money, which obviously has dead presidents on it (and Alexander Hamilton, but that’s a technicality). So here, Rick Ross is claiming to have a lot of money on him\n\nBut he loves money so much he actually has tattoo portraits of dead presidents on his body. See Washington and Lincoln below:", "annotation_id": "538707", "url": "https://genius.com/538707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "I’m whippin’ cake up like I’m Jacob, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm whippin' cake up like I'm Jacob, nigga"], "meaning": "He’s making money like “Jacob the Jeweler”, jeweler to the stars who was also embroiled in a money laundering scandal involving the Black Mafia Family. He probably bought the watch mentioned in the next line from Jacob\n(also note the subtle, but classy, “cake up/Jacob” internal rhyme)", "annotation_id": "538705", "url": "https://genius.com/538705", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "Study your plays in my office, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Study your plays in my office, nigga"], "meaning": "Continuing the reference to the Dolphins above, he’s studying your playbook like an offensive coordinator to scheme ways to defeat you. He’s plotting to kill you or at least take away your clientele in the drug game", "annotation_id": "538703", "url": "https://genius.com/538703", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "Go cash a check just like a dolphin, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Go cash a check just like a dolphin, nigga"], "meaning": "Rick Ross implies that – just like a Miami Dolphin player – (a so-so NFL team) you only go to work to get a paycheck – a boring 9-to-5 job with limited financial upside if you will.\n\nRoss is making so much money that an average NFL player making half-a-mil/year (top 1% earners in the US) is poor compared to him.\n\nHe’s could also be talking about Dolphin Cash payday loans. Either way you’re not cut out for a life of crime.", "annotation_id": "538702", "url": "https://genius.com/538702", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "Club LIV is your coffin nigga", "vault_lines": ["Club LIV is your coffin nigga"], "meaning": "Club LIV is a very exclusive Miami club. Just don’t act a fool or Ross will lay you down there\n\n\n\nAlso, an ironic play on the club’s name being pronounced like the word “live”. Similar to Lil' Wayne’s “Leave ‘em dead in the living room” line from the “9 Piece Remix”", "annotation_id": "538185", "url": "https://genius.com/538185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "The time is now fuck all the waitin’, nigga I can’t hold back all these Haitian niggas", "vault_lines": ["The time is now fuck all the waitin', nigga", "I can't hold back all these Haitian niggas"], "meaning": "Ross claims to run with the infamous Zoe Pound Haitian gang members, who are known to be ruthless and impatient when handling business.", "annotation_id": "536575", "url": "https://genius.com/536575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Yella Diamonds", "line": "My dope be shinin’ like it’s yella diamonds My dope be shinin’ like it’s yella diamonds", "vault_lines": ["My dope be shinin' like it's yella diamonds"], "meaning": "Pure cocaine can be mixed with other things like baking soda so the seller can keep as much of the real product he can. Rick Ross' crack (the mixture) is yellow like “yella” diamonds", "annotation_id": "531225", "url": "https://genius.com/531225", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
