{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You A Lie Remix", "line": "These flashing lights is blinding (Damn) go get them a visor", "vault_lines": ["These flashing lights is blinding (Damn) go get them a visor"], "meaning": "Rockie’s letting his haters see his fame. Also a little wordplay because you use a visor to protect you from the sun, or in this case, flashing lights of a camera. In addition, he could be referencing Kanye West’s song, Flashing Lights.", "annotation_id": "1313027", "url": "https://genius.com/1313027", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You A Lie Remix", "line": "Flooded like Melpomene", "vault_lines": ["My Jesus piece yellow, flooded like Melpomene"], "meaning": "Potential double meaning.\nHis Jesus piece is a chain with the face of Jesus flooded with diamonds.\n\n\n\nMelpomene is a project in New Orleans which Rick Ross may been thinking got flooded during Hurricane Katrina. However, it was one of the projects that was not flooded.", "annotation_id": "1153124", "url": "https://genius.com/1153124", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You A Lie Remix", "line": "Definition of swagging, all off of my passion", "vault_lines": ["Definition of swagging, all off of my passion"], "meaning": "Rockie Fresh is known for being fly. This is where he got the name “Fresh” from. Since Rockie is making so much money off his passion (music) he can swag-out even more.", "annotation_id": "1122578", "url": "https://genius.com/1122578", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You A Lie Remix", "line": "I dropped out of college and made more dough than my teachers (Tell ’em)", "vault_lines": ["I dropped out of college and made more dough than my teachers (Tell 'em)"], "meaning": "Rockie dropped out of college to pursue his rap career. Most people probably questioned his decision, but now he makes more money than most college graduates.", "annotation_id": "1122574", "url": "https://genius.com/1122574", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
