{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You Can Tell How I Walk", "line": "Who fuckin’ with fat boy, I traffic my body weight", "vault_lines": ["Who fuckin' with fat boy, I traffic my body weight"], "meaning": "This is not the first time Rozay refers to his noticable body weight in his lyrics, “The Devil Is A Lie” and in “Monster”\n\nMoving weight is a slang term for transporting drugs. Here, he is saying the dope he moves is as heavy as him, which is…. very heavy.", "annotation_id": "4205549", "url": "https://genius.com/4205549", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
