{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Your Love (Remix)", "line": "Still blowin’ money fast, Boston George", "vault_lines": ["Still blowin' money fast, Boston George"], "meaning": "What’s a Rick Ross verse without some vicious name-dropping?\nHere it’s the turn of George Jung, a.k.a. Boston George, the subject of the movie Blow\n\n\n\nJust in case, Jung is on the right, Depp on the left\n\nGive credit to Rozay for linking the Jung and blowin references through BMF.", "annotation_id": "672544", "url": "https://genius.com/672544", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Your Love (Remix)", "line": "If I bought another Coupe, you niggas couldn’t stand it", "vault_lines": ["If I bought another Coupe, you niggas couldn't stand it"], "meaning": "We know how much the Bawse loves his cars so much he gives them well-thought names!", "annotation_id": "672369", "url": "https://genius.com/672369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Your Love (Remix)", "line": "Smokin’ on a jet, they bill your card with the fine", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' on a jet, they bill your card with the fine"], "meaning": "Ricky, Ricky, can’t you see the light on?\n\n\n\nSmoking during U.S. domestic airline flights was banned since 1990 (a bit earlier in California) and on all international flights entering/leaving the U.S. since 2000 – a detailed timeline is here.\nOf course, it wasn’t always that way\n\n\n\nAnd there was even an unsuccessful attempt to create a smoking-allowed airline. Although technically you can be charged with a felony, you usually get a $5000 fine if caught smoking, which for Officer Ricky is peanuts. Though I doubt he pays the fine with his card, as he’s always carrying big wads of cash.\n\nHowever, private jets are not covered by the federal ban, and companies chartering jets allow it on selected aircraft. So, Rozay, if you really make as much money as you say, just buy your own plane, pay the extra so you can smoke on your rental, or ask Weezy to lend you one of his.", "annotation_id": "672239", "url": "https://genius.com/672239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "Your Love (Remix)", "line": "Blew a milli in a club, next day we made five", "vault_lines": ["Blew a milli in a club, next day we made five"], "meaning": "A reference to A Milli\n\nWell, we know Rozay loves flaunting his money. After all, he did rake in $6 million in 2011 and made the Forbes list for the third year in a row, at # 17… Not bad for a correctional-officer-turned-rapper\n\n\n\nthat goes by the name of a former real kingpin\n\n\n\nand names his songs/mixtapes/albums after other bad guys\n\n\n\nbecause he’s such a badass\n\n\n\nand seems to have an innate ability to polarize hip-hop fans. Just read the exchange in the comment section in this blog post.\n\nBut the real money-maker in this song is Diddy, as he brought $35 mil to his vault bringing his net worth up to half a Billion.\n\n\n\nWho said vodka is not a good business?\n\nOf course Diddy would be worth twice as much if he was as good a rapper as he is a businessman.", "annotation_id": "672066", "url": "https://genius.com/672066", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
