{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "Niggas fake, they hate candy paint and all the paper that your partner make", "vault_lines": ["Niggas fake, they hate candy paint and all the paper that your partner make"], "meaning": "He’s talking about that people who were talking negative about the South, Saying that they’re being bitches and hating on what the south got including the money that Southern Rappers make.", "annotation_id": "17630591", "url": "https://genius.com/17630591", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "Mississippi’s my home, ’til I’m die and I’m gone I know I put it on my back, held that bitch up alone", "vault_lines": ["Mississippi's my home, 'til I'm die and I'm gone", "I know I put it on my back, held that bitch up alone"], "meaning": "David Banner was born in Brookhaven, Mississippi and some time later he moved with his family to Jackson, Mississippi where he was raised.\nHe reps his state hard, being the best known rapper from there – it’s hardly to tell some other MCs name originated from there – hence put it on his back and held it alone line. But, he also literally put it on his back…", "annotation_id": "14596832", "url": "https://genius.com/14596832", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
