{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "You’re everything I knew", "vault_lines": ["You're everything I knew"], "meaning": "The sample is from 1993’s “Cry For You” by Jodeci:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Iznvc-eqKpU", "annotation_id": "6542958", "url": "https://genius.com/6542958", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "It’s the South, ain’t nothin’ above it and that’s why I love it, mayne!", "vault_lines": ["It's the South, ain't nothin' above it and that's why I love it, mayne!"], "meaning": "A clever turn of phrase, since, geographically at least, there is a lot above the South:\n\n\n\nYet Bun is metaphorically asserting the region’s superiority, in which case there ain’t nothing gonna top it.", "annotation_id": "1720703", "url": "https://genius.com/1720703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "I’m a G, that’s a genius, best to just respect my thuggin’, mayne", "vault_lines": ["I'm a G, that's a genius, best to just respect my thuggin', mayne"], "meaning": "The OG RAP GENIUS, Bun B is both a gangster and an intellectual, as evidenced by his tenure as “Professor Trill” at Rice University, co-teaching the course Religion and Hip-Hop.", "annotation_id": "1720636", "url": "https://genius.com/1720636", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "Look at these seats they gator made", "vault_lines": ["Haterade they Gatorade, look at these seats they gator made"], "meaning": "On the one hand, a punning rhyme with “gatorade,” which is also “gator made,” since it was developed as a sports drink by researchers at the University of Florida to replenish and refresh their Gator teams.\n\nIn addition, a boast, similar to Rich Boy’s line “Gator skin seats / call me Dundee,” about possessing the finest vehicular upholstery.", "annotation_id": "1720571", "url": "https://genius.com/1720571", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "Yellow stones all in my shit, yellowbones all on my dick", "vault_lines": ["Yellow stones all in my shit, yellowbones all on my dick"], "meaning": "Yellow diamonds all on Rick Ross’s chain, and yellow bones are sucking his dick. A yellow bone is a light skinned black woman. Rozay also could be referencing his song ‘Yella Diamonds’", "annotation_id": "1283672", "url": "https://genius.com/1283672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "You’re Everything", "line": "R.I.P. to my Uncle Chad, UGK, you can’t fuck wit’ that", "vault_lines": ["R.I.P. to my Uncle Chad, UGK, you can't fuck wit' that"], "meaning": "Tribute to the late Pimp C, who died in December 2007.\nYou can’t fuck with what Bun B and Pimp C did for the Southern music with UGK. Respect.", "annotation_id": "640832", "url": "https://genius.com/640832", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
