{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "glo_up", "line": "I’d rather be dying than be going broke", "vault_lines": ["I'd rather be dying than be going broke"], "meaning": "Here, blackbear is revising a popular idiom–\"get rich or die trying\" (A movie has even been made using the phrase for the title, “Get Rich or Die Tryin'”. On past tracks, blackbear has expressed his particular focus on money, so much so that he made a whole track dedicated to the topic titled “Money”.\n\nIt’s about the money\nWonder why I do the things I do\nPeople changing everyday for the money\nIt’s for the money, it’s for the money…", "annotation_id": "13168415", "url": "https://genius.com/13168415", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "glo_up", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Blackbear-glo-up-lyrics", "genius_title": "glo_up", "genius_id": 3314273, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "’06", "line": "Picture me rolling, nigga, like Pac in the ’90s, ho (90's, ho)", "vault_lines": ["Picture me rolling, nigga, like Pac in the '90s, ho (90's, ho)"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to legendary West Coast rapper 2Pac’s 1996 track “Picture Me Rollin'.” In the song, Pac talks about getting out of jail and rolling through the streets in his Mercedes-Benz sportscar to prove that he’s out for good.\n\nJeezy compares himself to 2Pac, similarly telling his listeners that he’s unstoppable in a way.", "annotation_id": "17944381", "url": "https://genius.com/17944381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Rick Ross", "song": "’06", "line": "Jeezy for president, make America snow again (Yeah) Make America snow again (Snow)", "vault_lines": ["Jeezy for president, make America snow again (Yeah)", "Make America snow again (Snow)"], "meaning": "Jeezy makes a flip on America’s 45th president, Donald Trump’s famous slogan “Make America Great Again”–combining it with his snowman persona–where snow refers to him having been a cocaine dealer. Cocaine is often referred to as snow, due to their similar white powdery appearance.\n\nJeezy also has merchandise for sale with this flipped slogan on his website, including hoodies and caps.", "annotation_id": "17880574", "url": "https://genius.com/17880574", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
